window.readingBank = {"version": 3, "generatedAt": "2026-11-20", "totalPassages": 131, "totalQuestions": 655, "passages": [{"id": "cet4-202606-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "有机食品值得买吗：营养、安全与环保", "subtitle": "从营养价值、食品安全与环境影响客观剖析有机食品与传统食品的差异", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 355, "paragraphs": ["Is organic food worth the higher price? It's the classic grocery store dilemma. On the one hand, your family dinner table deserves only the best. On the other hand, your wallet can only stretch so far.", "Whether or not to buy organic is a personal decision, said Mike von Massow, professor of Food Agriculture.", "Science won't give a clear-cut answer to the question of whether organic food is \"better.\" There are often trade-offs and answers become less definitive depending on the product under consideration.", "One thing is definitive: Organic and conventionally grown food are equally nutritious. From a nutrition point of view, there is no difference between organic and traditionally grown products.", "Organic products don't necessarily have fewer pesticides —— in fact, they may have more. There is also no big difference between organic and non-organic products from a food-safety perspective. Even organic growers use pesticides. Testing shows little if any pesticide remains on conventionally grown products. In fact, organic farmers often use larger quantities of pesticide because they can only use the natural variety of insect-killers. Chemical pesticides generally kill a much wider range of pests than any single natural pesticide. The use of animal waste in organic agriculture can also be a factor in the spread of bacteria like E. coli and salmonella. Over the past 10 years, Canada has seen more food-safety recalls for organic products, proportionally, than for conventional products.", "On the whole, organic agriculture may have a smaller environmental footprint. That's mostly because the risk of groundwater contamination from organic farming is lower. Organic farmers never used neonics, the controversial pesticides that have been linked to shrinking bee populations worldwide. Traditional agriculture has been making \"dramatic improvements\" to reduce its impact on the environment. It isn't a black-and-white picture, though. Organic farming is much less efficient when it comes to land use, although yields vary considerably depending on the crop.", "On the other hand, advocates of organic farming argue yields and efficiency could be significantly improved if the food industry devoted as much research and money to organic farming as it does conventional agriculture."], "translations": ["有机食品值得花更高的价钱购买吗？这是逛超市时经典的左右为难。一方面，你家人的餐桌理应享用最好的食物；另一方面，你的钱包能承受的开销毕竟有限。", "是否购买有机食品是个人的决定，食品农业教授迈克·冯·马索如是说。", "对于有机食品是否“更好”这一问题，科学不会给出非黑即白的明确答案。这其中往往存在权衡，而且答案的确定性也会因所考察的具体产品而降低。", "有一点是明确的：有机食品和传统种植的食品营养价值相等。从营养学角度来看，有机产品和传统种植产品之间没有任何区别。", "有机产品未必农药更少——事实上，它们的农药含量可能还更高。从食品安全角度来看，有机产品和非有机产品之间也没有太大区别。就连有机种植者也会使用杀虫剂。检测表明，传统种植的产品上几乎没有农药残留。实际上，有机农民往往会使用更大量的杀虫剂，因为他们只能使用天然类型的杀虫剂。化学杀虫剂通常比任何单一的天然杀虫剂能消灭种类多得多的害虫。有机农业中动物粪便的使用也可能是导致大肠杆菌和沙门氏菌等细菌传播的因素。在过去10年里，按比例计算，加拿大有机产品的食品安全召回事件比传统产品还要多。", "总体而言，有机农业的环境足迹可能更小。这主要是因为有机耕作造成地下水污染的风险更低。有机农民从不使用新烟碱类杀虫剂——这种备受争议的杀虫剂与全球蜜蜂数量锐减有关。传统农业也一直在做出“显著改进”，以减少其对环境的影响。不过，情况并非非黑即白。就土地利用而言，有机耕作的效率要低得多，尽管具体产量因农作物而异。", "另一方面，有机农业的倡导者认为，如果食品行业能像投入传统农业那样，在有机农业上投入同样多的研究精力与资金，其产量和效率都能得到显著提高。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the classic grocery store dilemma?", "options": ["Whether or not one should eat organic food.", "Whether or not one can stretch their wallet far.", "Organic food costs more but it certainly tastes better.", "One wants the best food but their budget is limited."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "It's the classic grocery store dilemma. On the one hand, your family dinner table deserves only the best. On the other hand, your wallet can only stretch so far.", "explanation": "定位第一段后两句。题干询问经典的超市两难困境是什么。原文在提出这一困境后，用“一方面……另一方面……”点明冲突：家人餐桌理应享用最好的食物，但钱包能承受的开销有限。D项指出“想买最好的食物但预算有限”，准确转述了原文“理应得到最好的”与“钱包额度有限”这组矛盾，完整涵盖困境的两端，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项只提到是否吃有机食品，未点出价格与需求之间的矛盾，属于以偏概全；B项仅截取“钱包能否撑下去”，遗漏了“想要最好食物”的另一端；C项“味道更好”原文未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about organic food from science?", "options": ["Whether it is any better remains uncertain.", "Whether it is healthier is under consideration.", "Whether it is more nutritious than conventional food is arguable.", "Whether it is going to replace conventional food is still unclear."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Science won't give a clear-cut answer to the question of whether organic food is \"better.\"", "explanation": "定位第三段首句。题干询问从科学角度能了解到关于有机食品的什么信息。原文明确指出，对于有机食品是否“更好”这一问题，科学不会给出明确清晰的答案，往往存在权衡，且结论随具体产品而变化。A项“它是否更好仍不确定”中，“不确定”精准同义替换原文“不会给出明确答案”，核心语义完全一致，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项将原文“是否更好”偷换为“是否更健康”，且曲解了“正在考虑”的意思（原文指被考察的具体产品）；C项与第四段“营养价值完全相同”的明确结论相悖；D项“是否取代传统食品”文中未提。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about organic and non-organic products as far as food safety is concerned?", "options": ["Their difference is the conventions used to test them.", "They differ in how much pesticide remains on them.", "One relies on pesticides whereas the other does not.", "There is no substantial difference between the two."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "There is also no big difference between organic and non-organic products from a food-safety perspective.", "explanation": "定位第五段第二句。题干询问就食品安全而言，文章对有机与非有机产品有何表述。原文指出，从食品安全视角看，有机产品与非有机产品之间没有太大差异，并进一步解释有机农业也会使用天然杀虫剂且存在细菌传播风险。D项“两者之间没有实质性差异”中的“没有实质性差异”精准对应原文“没有太大差异”，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“测试惯例不同”属于拼凑词汇，原文并未提及；C项称其中一方不用杀虫剂，与原文“有机种植者也使用杀虫剂”直接相悖；B项以局部细节替代整体安全结论。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say about organic farming?", "options": ["It may be blamed for the shrinking bee populations in the world.", "It minimizes the use of controversial pesticides in its operations.", "It may impact the environment less than conventional farming.", "It contaminates groundwater as much as conventional farming."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "On the whole, organic agriculture may have a smaller environmental footprint.", "explanation": "定位第六段首句。题干询问作者对有机农业的看法。原文明确指出，总体而言，有机农业留下的环境足迹可能更小，随后解释其主要原因在于地下水污染风险较低且不使用新烟碱类杀虫剂。C项“它对环境的影响可能小于传统农业”精准对应原文“可能拥有更小的环境足迹”，同义转述清晰准确，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项颠倒是非，原文明确说有机农民从不使用与蜜蜂减少有关的杀虫剂，并非有机农业导致蜜蜂减少；B项“尽量减少有争议的杀虫剂”与原文“从不使用”的绝对否定不符；D项与“地下水污染风险更低”相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do advocates of organic farming argue about its yields and efficiency?", "options": ["They would increase quickly with the emergence of new technologies.", "They would improve remarkably with more research and investment.", "They would be achieved along with enormous health benefits.", "They would considerably lower the cost to the environment."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "On the other hand, advocates of organic farming argue yields and efficiency could be significantly improved if the food industry devoted as much research and money to organic farming as it does conventional agriculture.", "explanation": "定位第七段。题干询问有机农业倡导者对其产量和效率的看法。原文指出，如果食品行业能像投入传统农业那样，向有机农业投入同等的研究精力与资金，其产量和效率就能得到显著提升。B项“随着更多研究和投资，它们将显著提高”中，“显著提高”对应“大幅改善”，“研究和投资”对应“研究和资金”，完全吻合，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“随新技术的出现而迅速增加”偷换条件，原文强调的是行业研发与资金投入的倾斜，而非新技术本身；C项“伴随巨大健康益处”与D项“大幅降低环境成本”均未在第七段中提及，属于无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 进退两难的境地，困境", "note": "经典搭配 classic dilemma，指在两个同样重要或棘手的选项间难以抉择。", "word": "dilemma"}, {"gloss": "adj. 明确的，决定性的，权威的", "note": "文中与 clear-cut 呼应，常用于科研或结论语境，表示最终定论。", "word": "definitive"}, {"gloss": "adv. 按比例地，相称地", "note": "由 proportion（比例）派生，文中用于比较召回事件的相对发生率，避免基数差异带来的误导。", "word": "proportionally"}, {"gloss": "n. 污染，玷污", "note": "动词为 contaminate，常指化学物质、细菌等对水源或食物造成的污染。", "word": "contamination"}, {"gloss": "n. 倡导者，拥护者；v. 提倡", "note": "文中作名词指“支持有机农业的人”，常见搭配 advocates of...。", "word": "advocate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Organic farmers never used neonics, the controversial pesticides that have been linked to shrinking bee populations worldwide.", "point": "the controversial pesticides 为 neonics 的同位语，其后接 that 引导的定语从句进一步解释其负面影响；be linked to 意为“与……有关”。", "structure": "主语(Organic farmers) + 谓语(never used) + 宾语(neonics) + 同位语(the controversial pesticides) + that引导的定语从句", "zh": "有机农民从不使用新烟碱类杀虫剂——这种备受争议的杀虫剂与全球蜜蜂数量锐减有关。"}, {"en": "In fact, organic farmers often use larger quantities of pesticide because they can only use the natural variety of insect-killers.", "point": "注意对比逻辑：虽然直觉上认为有机农业用药少，但此处用 larger quantities 与 only use natural variety 形成反常识因果关系。", "structure": "状语(In fact) + 主句(organic farmers often use...) + because引导的原因状语从句", "zh": "实际上，有机农民往往会使用更大量的杀虫剂，因为他们只能使用天然类型的杀虫剂。"}, {"en": "On the other hand, advocates of organic farming argue yields and efficiency could be significantly improved if the food industry devoted as much research and money to organic farming as it does conventional agriculture.", "point": "虚拟语气与比较结构的结合：could be improved 与 devoted 构成与现在事实相反的虚拟条件句；as does conventional agriculture 中 does 代替前文的 devoted。", "structure": "主句(advocates... argue) + 省略that的宾语从句(yields... could be improved) + if引导的虚拟条件句(含as...as比较结构)", "zh": "另一方面，有机农业的倡导者认为，如果食品行业能像投入传统农业那样，在有机农业上投入同样多的研究精力与资金，其产量和效率都能得到显著提高。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "deserves only the best 转述为 wants the best food，wallet can only stretch so far 转述为 budget is limited。", "option": "One wants the best food but their budget is limited.", "original": "your family dinner table deserves only the best ... your wallet can only stretch so far"}, {"note": "won't give a clear-cut answer 转述为 remains uncertain。", "option": "Whether it is any better remains uncertain.", "original": "Science won't give a clear-cut answer to the question of whether organic food is \"better.\""}, {"note": "no big difference 精准同义替换为 no substantial difference。", "option": "There is no substantial difference between the two.", "original": "no big difference between organic and non-organic products from a food-safety perspective"}, {"note": "smaller environmental footprint 具象化转述为 impact the environment less。", "option": "It may impact the environment less than conventional farming.", "original": "organic agriculture may have a smaller environmental footprint"}, {"note": "significantly improved 转述为 improve remarkably，devoted ... research and money 转述为 with more research and investment。", "option": "They would improve remarkably with more research and investment.", "original": "yields and efficiency could be significantly improved if the food industry devoted as much research and money"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202606-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "合作与自私：基因与环境对人类行为的塑造", "subtitle": "探讨人类利他合作与自私倾向背后的遗传基础、进化动因及后天环境影响", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 353, "paragraphs": ["It is still controversial whether we are fundamentally generous or selfish and whether these tendencies are shaped by our genes or environment. Some evidence points to humans being born cooperative. At later stages in life we routinely work together to reach goals and help out in times of need. Yet instances of selfish behavior are also plenty. One recent study tested people's willingness to set aside selfish interests to reach a greater good. It found that being selfish was more advantageous than cooperating. The benefit may be short-lived, however. Another study showed that players who cooperated did better in the long run.", "It seems that human nature supports both pro-social and selfish traits. Genetic studies have made some progress toward identifying their biological roots. By comparing identical twins, who share nearly 100 percent of their genes, and non-identical twins, who share about half, researchers have found overwhelming evidence for genetic effects on behaviors. In these twin studies, identical and non-identical twins are asked, for example, to split a sum of", "money with a peer. Such studies often also rely on careful psychological assessments and DNA analysis.", "Other work highlights specific genes as key players. My colleagues and I recently identified a gene linked to altruistic behavior and found that a particular variant of it was associated with more selfish behavior in preschoolers. According to evolutionary scientists, cooperative behavior may have evolved first among relatives to promote the continuation of their genetic line. As communities diversified, mutual support could have broadened to include individuals not linked by blood. Another possibility is that humans cooperate to gain some advantage, such as boosting reputation. Finally, evolutionary processes take place at the group level. Groups of highly cooperative individuals have higher chances of survival because they can work together to reach goals that are unattainable to less cooperative groups.", "Yet almost no behavior is entirely genetic, even among identical twins. Culture, schooling and parenting are important determinants of cooperation. Thus, the degree to which we act cooperatively or selfishly is unique to each individual and depends on a variety of genetic and environmental influences."], "translations": ["人类本质上是慷慨还是自私，以及这些倾向是由基因还是环境塑造的，至今仍存争议。一些证据表明人类生来就具有合作精神。在人生的后续阶段，我们也常常齐心协力达成目标，并在他人需要时施以援手。然而，自私行为的例子也比比皆是。近期一项研究测试了人们为了实现更大利益而放下个人私利的意愿，结果发现，自私比合作更有优势。不过，这种好处可能是短暂的。另一项研究表明，选择合作的参与者从长远来看表现得更好。", "看来，人性同时支持亲社会和自私这两种特质。基因研究在探明它们的生物学根源方面已经取得了一定进展。通过比较基因几乎100%相同的同卵双胞胎和共享约一半基因的异卵双胞胎，研究人员发现了基因对行为产生影响的压倒性证据。在这些双胞胎研究中，同卵和异卵双胞胎会被要求例如与一名同伴平分一笔", "钱。此类研究通常还依赖于细致的心理评估和DNA分析。", "其他研究则突出了特定基因的关键作用。我和同事近期确定了一个与利他行为相关的基因，并发现该基因的一个特定变体与学龄前儿童更自私的行为有关。进化科学家认为，合作行为最初可能是在亲属间演化出来的，以促进其基因谱系的延续。随着群体变得多样化，互助行为可能扩展到了没有血缘关系的个体之间。另一种可能性是，人类合作是为了获得某种益处，比如提升声誉。最后，进化过程也在群体层面发生。由高度合作个体组成的群体拥有更高的生存几率，因为他们能够共同努力，实现合作程度较低的群体无法达成的目标。", "然而，几乎没有任何行为是完全由基因决定的，即便在同卵双胞胎中也是如此。文化、学校教育和家庭养育都是决定合作行为的重要因素。因此，我们表现得合作还是自私的程度因人而异，取决于遗传和环境等多方面的影响。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the finding of one recent study about being selfish?", "options": ["It may bring certain benefits in the short term.", "It usually yields more disadvantages than advantages.", "It serves individual interest rather than a collective's.", "It may give way to cooperating in the long run."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "It found that being selfish was more advantageous than cooperating. The benefit may be short-lived, however.", "explanation": "定位第一段第五至七句。题干询问近期一项关于自私行为的研究有何发现。原文提到，近期研究测试人们为了实现更大利益而放下个人私利的意愿，结果发现自私比合作更占优势，但紧接着指出这种益处可能是短暂的。A项“它短期内可能带来一定益处”精准融合了“更有优势”与“益处短暂”两层含义，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项“通常弊大于利”与原文“自私比合作更有优势”相反；C项虽然符合常识，但并非该研究的核心发现；D项将“长期来看合作者表现更好”曲解为自私会“让位于”合作，属于过度推断。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What have researchers found by studying identical and non-identical twins?", "options": ["They are overwhelmingly different in the amounts of genes.", "One's behavior is largely determined by their genetic traits.", "One's biological roots can be identified by their genes.", "They differ from each other in their behavior patterns."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "By comparing identical twins, who share nearly 100 percent of their genes, and non-identical twins, who share about half, researchers have found overwhelming evidence for genetic effects on behaviors.", "explanation": "定位第二段第三句。题干询问研究人员通过对比同卵双胞胎和异卵双胞胎发现了什么。原文指出，通过对比基因几乎完全相同的同卵双胞胎和共享约一半基因的异卵双胞胎，研究人员发现了基因对行为产生影响的压倒性证据。B项“一个人的行为很大程度上由基因特征决定”是对“基因对行为影响的压倒性证据”的准确转述，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“基因数量差异极大”曲解了原文“基因相似度不同”的表述；C项偷换主客体，原文是通过双胞胎研究寻找行为的生物学根源，而非用基因识别根源；D项“双方行为模式不同”并非该对比研究的核心结论。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did the author and colleagues identify in their recent research?", "options": ["A gene-related selfish behavior in preschool children.", "Key factors that determine one's altruistic behavior.", "A specific gene associated with altruistic behavior.", "Roles played by genes in shaping one's character."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "My colleagues and I recently identified a gene linked to altruistic behavior and found that a particular variant of it was associated with more selfish behavior in preschoolers.", "explanation": "定位第四段第二句。题干询问作者及其同事在近期研究中发现了什么。原文明确写道，作者与同事最近确定了一种与利他行为相关的基因，并发现该基因的一个特定变体与学龄前儿童更自私的行为有关。C项“一种与利他行为相关的特定基因”几乎原词复现原文核心信息，其中“相关”对应“linked to”，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项将核心发现由“特定基因”偷换为“与基因相关的自私行为”，且学龄前儿童的自私行为与基因特定变体相关，并非整体发现内容；B项“决定性关键因素”和D项“塑造性格”均夸大或偏离了原文范围。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from evolutionary scientists about cooperative behavior?", "options": ["It may have initially originated in individuals linked by blood.", "It may have caused the diversification of communities.", "It helps to build relationships among blood-related people.", "It guarantees the achievement of goals otherwise unattainable."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "According to evolutionary scientists, cooperative behavior may have evolved first among relatives to promote the continuation of their genetic line.", "explanation": "定位第四段第三句。题干询问从进化科学家那里我们能了解到关于合作行为的什么内容。原文指出，进化科学家认为合作行为最初可能在亲属之间演化出来，以促进其基因谱系的延续，随后才扩展到非血缘个体。A项“它最初可能起源于有血缘关系的个体”精准转述了“最初在亲属间演化”，语义吻合，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项因果倒置，原文是“随着社区多样化，互助行为才扩大”，而非合作导致社区多样化；C项偷换目的，合作是为了延续基因谱系而非建立关系；D项“保证实现目标”过于绝对，原文仅说合作群体的生存几率更高。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we infer from the last paragraph?", "options": ["Cooperative behavior is evident among identical twins.", "One is born either cooperative or non-cooperative.", "Genes determine one's tendency to cooperate.", "Cooperative behavior may be cultivated."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Culture, schooling and parenting are important determinants of cooperation.", "explanation": "定位第五段。题干要求根据最后一段进行推断。原文先指出几乎没有完全由基因决定的行为，接着说明文化、学校教育和家庭养育是决定合作的重要因素，最终行为取决于遗传和环境的多种影响。由此可合理推断，既然学校教育和养育等后天环境因素起着重要作用，合作行为是可以通过后天培养的，D项完全符合文意，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“同卵双胞胎中合作行为很明显”属无中生有，原文仅说即便在同卵双胞胎中行为也非全由基因决定；B项“天生要么合作要么不合作”和C项“基因决定合作倾向”均忽视了环境因素，与段意直接相悖。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 亲社会的，有益于社会的", "note": "心理学高频词，指乐于助人、合作、分享等有利于他人或群体的倾向，文中与 selfish 形成对照。", "word": "pro-social"}, {"gloss": "adj. 压倒性的，势不可挡的", "note": "文中修饰 evidence，表示证据极其充分、具有决定性说服力。", "word": "overwhelming"}, {"gloss": "adj. 利他的，无私的", "note": "名词为 altruism（利他主义），文中与 selfish（自私的）构成反义对照。", "word": "altruistic"}, {"gloss": "adj. 无法达到的，难以实现的", "note": "前缀 un- + attain（达到）+ -able，意为“无法企及的”，用于强调合作群体的独特优势。", "word": "unattainable"}, {"gloss": "n. 决定因素，决定性事物", "note": "动词为 determine（决定），在社会科学和生物文章中常用于列举影响某现象的核心原因。", "word": "determinant"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "It is still controversial whether we are fundamentally generous or selfish and whether these tendencies are shaped by our genes or environment.", "point": "主语从句后置结构：It 作形式主语，两个并列的 whether...or... 从句作真正主语，开篇即点明全文核心争议。", "structure": "形式主语(It) + 系表(is still controversial) + 两个由whether引导的并列主语从句", "zh": "人类本质上是慷慨还是自私，以及这些倾向是由基因还是环境塑造的，至今仍存争议。"}, {"en": "By comparing identical twins, who share nearly 100 percent of their genes, and non-identical twins, who share about half, researchers have found overwhelming evidence for genetic effects on behaviors.", "point": "两个 who 引导的非限制性定语从句分别补充说明同卵和异卵双胞胎的基因共享比例，突出实验设计的对照组逻辑。", "structure": "方式状语(By comparing...) + 两个非限制性定语从句(who share...) + 主句(researchers have found...)", "zh": "通过比较基因几乎100%相同的同卵双胞胎和共享约一半基因的异卵双胞胎，研究人员发现了基因对行为产生影响的压倒性证据。"}, {"en": "Groups of highly cooperative individuals have higher chances of survival because they can work together to reach goals that are unattainable to less cooperative groups.", "point": "多重复合句，that 引导定语从句修饰 goals，unattainable 构成否定对比，说明群体合作在进化上的生存优势。", "structure": "主句(Groups... have higher chances of survival) + because引导的原因状语从句 + that引导的定语从句", "zh": "由高度合作个体组成的群体拥有更高的生存几率，因为他们能够共同努力，实现合作程度较低的群体无法达成的目标。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "more advantageous 与 benefit short-lived 合并转述为 bring certain benefits in the short term。", "option": "It may bring certain benefits in the short term.", "original": "being selfish was more advantageous than cooperating. The benefit may be short-lived"}, {"note": "overwhelming evidence for genetic effects 转述为 largely determined by genetic traits。", "option": "One's behavior is largely determined by their genetic traits.", "original": "overwhelming evidence for genetic effects on behaviors"}, {"note": "linked to 同义替换为 associated with。", "option": "A specific gene associated with altruistic behavior.", "original": "identified a gene linked to altruistic behavior"}, {"note": "evolved first 转述为 initially originated，relatives 转述为 individuals linked by blood。", "option": "It may have initially originated in individuals linked by blood.", "original": "cooperative behavior may have evolved first among relatives to promote the continuation of their genetic line"}, {"note": "学校教育与家庭养育等后天因素决定合作程度，推导出合作行为是可以后天培养（cultivated）的。", "option": "Cooperative behavior may be cultivated.", "original": "Culture, schooling and parenting are important determinants of cooperation."}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202606-s2-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 四级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 四级真题 第2套 Passage One", "title": "冒名顶替综合征的心理特征与研究", "subtitle": "剖析“冒名顶替综合征”的成因、实证研究与心理影响", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 357, "paragraphs": ["People who systematically underestimate themselves and their own performance suffer from the so-called Impostor Phenomenon. They think that any success is due to external circumstances or just luck and chance. Those people live in constant fear that their \"deception\" will be exposed. It is common for people to question their abilities now and again. A healthy amount of reflection and self-doubt can protect a person from acting impulsively. However, there are people who are permanently plagued by a massive amount of self-doubt despite delivering a good performance. They think that all of their successes are not a product of their skill or hard work, instead they attribute their own successes to external circumstances, for example, to luck and chance, or believe that their performance is massively overestimated by others. Failures, on the other hand, are always internalised as the result of their own shortcomings.", "Psychologists from Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg examined the topic for the first time under real-life conditions. Seventy-six participants completed a range of intelligence tests and received positive feedback on them, regardless of their actual performance. They were then asked why they think they did so well.", "The study showed two things: First, the self-reported degree of Impostor Phenomenon is not related to actual measured intelligence or performance. Secondly, the test supported the assumption that people with a tendency to exhibit the Impostor Phenomenon devalue their objectively measured performance and attribute positive results to external causes such as luck and chance, but not to their own abilities. These results are also completely unrelated to age and gender.", "A permanent underestimation of one's own abilities is often accompanied by the fear that this supposed intellectual deception will be exposed sooner or later and that they will pay the price for this. The Impostor Phenomenon was first described in 1978 by US psychologists Pauline Clance and Suzanne Imes. They observed that there is a particularly high number of successful women who do not think they are very intelligent. The Impostor Phenomenon is not defined as", "a mental illness. However, people who suffer from it show a higher vulnerability to depression."], "translations": ["习惯性低估自己及自身表现的人正遭受所谓“冒名顶替综合征”的困扰。他们认为任何成功都归因于外部环境，或者仅仅是运气和巧合。这些人一直生活在自己的“欺骗”会被揭穿的持续恐惧之中。人们时不时怀疑自己的能力是很正常的。适度的反思与自我怀疑可以防止人冲动行事。然而，有些人尽管表现出色，却长期受到强烈自我怀疑的折磨。他们认为自己所有的成功都不是技能或努力的产物，相反，他们把成功归因于外部环境（例如运气和巧合），或者认为自己的表现被他人严重高估了。另一方面，失败则总是被内化为自身缺点所致。", "来自哈雷-维滕贝格马丁·路德大学的心理学家首次在现实生活条件下对这一课题进行了研究。76名参与者完成了一系列智力测试，无论其实际表现如何，他们都收到了积极的反馈。随后，他们被问及为什么认为自己做得这么好。", "研究显示出两点结果：首先，自我报告的冒名顶替综合征程度与实际测得的智力或表现无关。其次，该测试支持了这样一种假设：倾向于表现出冒名顶替综合征的人会贬低自己客观测得的表现，并将积极结果归因于运气和巧合等外部原因，而非自身能力。这些结果也与年龄和性别完全无关。", "对自身能力的长期低估往往伴随着一种恐惧，即担心这种所谓的“智力欺骗”迟早会被揭穿，并会为此付出代价。冒名顶替综合征最早由美国心理学家保琳·克兰斯和苏珊·艾姆斯于1978年提出。她们观察到，有相当多的成功女性并不认为自己很聪明。冒名顶替综合征并未被定义为", "一种精神疾病。然而，受其困扰的人更容易患上抑郁症。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about people who suffer from the so-called Impostor Phenomenon?", "options": ["They systematically underestimate their chance of success.", "They tend to attribute their achievements to good fortune.", "They seem to live in constant fear of being deceived.", "They generally rely on luck and chance for success."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "They think that any success is due to external circumstances or just luck and chance.", "explanation": "根据题干中的“Impostor Phenomenon”定位至第一段。首句引出该概念后，第二句明确指出“They think that any success is due to external circumstances or just luck and chance”，即患者认为任何成功都归因于外部环境或仅仅是运气与机会。B项中的“attribute their achievements to good fortune”正是对原文“success is due to ... luck and chance”的同义转述，因此B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“低估成功的机会”偷换了原文“低估自己及自身表现”；C项“害怕被欺骗”颠倒了主被动，原文指担心自己的“伪装”被揭穿；D项“依靠运气成功”将事后归因曲解为事前依赖。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do people with a healthy amount of reflection and self-doubt tend to do?", "options": ["Credit all their successes to hard work.", "Strive hard to perfect their skills.", "Refrain from acting on impulse.", "Deliver a better performance."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "A healthy amount of reflection and self-doubt can protect a person from acting impulsively.", "explanation": "由题干“a healthy amount of reflection and self-doubt”定位至第一段。原文指出适度的反思与自我怀疑能够“protect a person from acting impulsively”，即防止人冲动行事。C项中“Refrain from”同义替换“protect ... from”，“acting on impulse”对应“acting impulsively”，语义完全一致，因此C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“将所有成功归功于努力”与综合征人群的心理相反，并非适度怀疑者的做法；B项“努力完善技能”与D项“表现更好”在文中均无依据，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do Impostor Phenomenon sufferers often do according to psychologists from Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg?", "options": ["Attribute their accomplishments to others.", "Deny their actual measured intelligence.", "Claim to have confidence in their own abilities.", "Mark down their objectively rated performance."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Secondly, the test supported the assumption that people with a tendency to exhibit the Impostor Phenomenon devalue their objectively measured performance and attribute positive results to external causes such as luck and chance, but not to their own abilities.", "explanation": "根据题干中的机构名称定位至第二、三段。第三段指出，实验支持了这一假设：具有冒名顶替综合征倾向的人会“devalue their objectively measured performance”，即将客观衡量的成绩贬低，并将积极结果归因于外部原因。D项“Mark down their objectively rated performance”中“mark down”与“devalue”同义，均指贬低或压低评价，“rated”替换“measured”，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“将成就归功于他人”偷换概念，原文归因于运气、机会等外部因素；B项“否认实际测得的智力”曲解文意，原文仅说明自评程度与实际智力无关。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What happens when a person permanently underestimates their own abilities?", "options": ["They will focus their attention on external factors.", "They will be fearful of potential consequences.", "They will count on good fortune for success.", "They will keep improving their own skills."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "A permanent underestimation of one's own abilities is often accompanied by the fear that this supposed intellectual deception will be exposed sooner or later and that they will pay the price for this.", "explanation": "由题干关键词“permanently underestimates their own abilities”定位至第四段首句。原文指出，长期低估自身能力往往伴随着一种恐惧，即担心这种所谓的智力欺骗迟早会被揭穿，并且自己会为此付出代价（pay the price for this）。B项“They will be fearful of potential consequences”精准概括了这种对潜在后果的恐惧心理，因此B项为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“关注外部因素”和C项“指望好运成功”混淆了患者的成功归因方式与长期自我低估所伴随的心理后果；D项“不断提升技能”在原文中未曾提及。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did US psychologists Pauline Clance and Suzanne Imes say about Impostor Phenomenon sufferers?", "options": ["They are more liable to have depression.", "They seldom realise their potential fully.", "They will develop mental illnesses.", "They will pay higher prices one day."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "However, people who suffer from it show a higher vulnerability to depression.", "explanation": "根据人名定位至第四、五段。第四段指出两位学者于1978年首次描述了该现象，且它不被定义为精神疾病；第五段随即转折说明“show a higher vulnerability to depression”，即患者更容易患上抑郁症。A项中的“more liable to have depression”与原文“higher vulnerability to depression”精准对应，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "C项“会发展出精神疾病”与原文“not defined as a mental illness”直接相悖；D项“有朝一日付出更高代价”属于对第四段“pay the price”的过度引申。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "系统地；一贯地", "note": "副词，修饰 underestimate，表示“长期一贯地低估”，体现习惯性心理模式。", "word": "systematically"}, {"gloss": "将……归因于", "note": "常用搭配 attribute A to B（把A归因于B），阅读归因类细节题高频核心词。", "word": "attribute"}, {"gloss": "折磨，困扰", "note": "文中用被动语态 be plagued by 形容“长期受严重自我怀疑的折磨”。", "word": "plague"}, {"gloss": "贬低，压低……的价值", "note": "de-（向下）+ value（价值），文中对应选项中的 mark down。", "word": "devalue"}, {"gloss": "易受伤害性；易感性", "note": "搭配 show a vulnerability to... 表示“更容易受到……的影响/患某种疾病”。", "word": "vulnerability"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "They think that all of their successes are not a product of their skill or hard work, instead they attribute their own successes to external circumstances, for example, to luck and chance, or believe that their performance is massively overestimated by others.", "point": "由 think 引导宾语从句，后接由 instead 连接的并列分句，包含 attribute...to... 搭配及 or 连接的第二个谓语 believe 及其宾语从句。", "structure": "主语 + 谓语(think) + that宾语从句, instead + 主语 + 谓语1(attribute...to...) or 谓语2(believe) + that宾语从句", "zh": "他们认为自己所有的成功都不是技能或努力的产物，相反，他们把成功归因于外部环境（例如运气和巧合），或者认为自己的表现被他人严重高估了。"}, {"en": "Secondly, the test supported the assumption that people with a tendency to exhibit the Impostor Phenomenon devalue their objectively measured performance and attribute positive results to external causes such as luck and chance, but not to their own abilities.", "point": "that 引导同位语从句解释 assumption，其中包含两个并列谓语 devalue 和 attribute，以及 not...but... 对比结构。", "structure": "主语(the test) + 谓语(supported) + 宾语(the assumption) + that同位语从句(主语[people + 介词短语定语] + 谓语1[devalue...] and 谓语2[attribute...to..., but not to...])", "zh": "其次，该测试支持了这样一种假设：倾向于表现出冒名顶替综合征的人会贬低自己客观测得的表现，并将积极结果归因于运气和巧合等外部原因，而非自身能力。"}, {"en": "A permanent underestimation of one's own abilities is often accompanied by the fear that this supposed intellectual deception will be exposed sooner or later and that they will pay the price for this.", "point": "is accompanied by 引出伴随状态 fear，其后接两个由 and 连接的并列 that 同位语从句具体说明“恐惧”的内容。", "structure": "主语(A permanent underestimation...) + 被动谓语(is accompanied by) + 宾语(the fear) + that同位语从句1 and that同位语从句2", "zh": "对自身能力的长期低估往往伴随着一种恐惧，即担心这种所谓的“智力欺骗”迟早会被揭穿，并会为此付出代价。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "归因表达的经典替换：be due to 对应 attribute...to...；luck and chance 对应 good fortune。", "option": "attribute their achievements to good fortune", "original": "any success is due to ... luck and chance"}, {"note": "prevent/protect sb from doing 与 refrain from doing 均表示“阻止/克制做某事”；副词与介词短语同义转换。", "option": "Refrain from acting on impulse", "original": "protect a person from acting impulsively"}, {"note": "动词和过去分词定语的同义替换：mark down 与 devalue 同义，rated 替换 measured。", "option": "Mark down their objectively rated performance", "original": "devalue their objectively measured performance"}, {"note": "将具体描述的“担心欺骗败露并付出代价”高度概括为抽象的“害怕潜在后果”。", "option": "be fearful of potential consequences", "original": "accompanied by the fear that this supposed intellectual deception will be exposed ... and that they will pay the price for this"}, {"note": "形容词短语与名词短语的同义转换：be liable to（易于……）对应 show a higher vulnerability to。", "option": "are more liable to have depression", "original": "show a higher vulnerability to depression"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202606-s2-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 四级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 四级真题 第2套 Passage Two", "title": "音乐作为全人类共通语言的力量", "subtitle": "跨文化五声音阶与音乐的情感共鸣和凝聚力", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 348, "paragraphs": ["Music is a universal language. In every culture and country, you will find music. It is vitally important across the globe and has the potential to bring people", "together in peace and harmony. One of my favorite experiences in music is seeing musicians from different cultures come together and perform as a group. When each culture brings its own unique qualities to the group, an entirely new sound is achieved. This can create extraordinary results. People can communicate with each other using music as the common language. One common musical thread between cultures is known as the pentatonic scale. It is astonishing how many cultures share this tool in approaching music. The pentatonic scale consists of five notes; \"penta-\" meaning 5, and \"tonic\" meaning tone or note. This scale can be found in music everywhere including that of Native Americans, Africans, and Asians. It is also found in popular music, blues, jazz, and rock. Using this five-note scale, musicians from around the globe have a medium through which they can relate, communicate, perform, and ultimately understand each other.", "Music is tied to specific perceptual, mental, and emotional faculties, including language (all societies put words to their songs), motor control (people in all societies dance), sound analysis (all musical systems have a distinct pitch and quality), and aesthetics (美感) (their tunes and rhythms are balanced between repetitiveness and chaos).", "There is no known society that existed without music. Although each culture has their own specific style and approach to music, you will find that the purposes behind music are very similar across the board. Music essentially serves to express or change emotions. It can cheer you up, sadden you, anger you or excite you. Music is often ceremonial: used in religion, ceremony, and celebration. Music can simply be recreational: entertaining, joyful and fun. Any way you have used music, it is almost certain that every other culture has used music in the very same way. And that is something that bonds all of us. We all share a deep love for music and it has the power to unite us."], "translations": ["音乐是一种通用的语言。在每一种文化和每一个国家，你都能找到音乐。它在全球范围内至关重要，并且有潜力让人们", "在和平与和谐中走到一起。我在音乐中最喜爱的经历之一，就是看到来自不同文化的音乐家聚在一起同台演奏。当每一种文化都为团队带来自身独特的特质时，一种全新的声音便应运而生。这能创造出非凡的效果。人们可以用音乐作为共同的语言相互交流。不同文化间一个共同的音乐纽带被称为五声音阶。令人惊叹的是，竟有如此多的文化在创作与理解音乐时共用这一工具。五声音阶由五个音符组成；“penta-”意为5，“tonic”意为音调或音符。这种音阶在世界各地的音乐中随处可见，包括美洲原住民、非洲人和亚洲人的音乐。它在流行音乐、蓝调、爵士乐和摇滚乐中也有所体现。借助这一五声音阶，世界各地的音乐家拥有了一种媒介，通过它他们可以建立联系、交流、演奏并最终理解彼此。", "音乐与特定的感知、心理和情感能力密切相关，包括语言（所有社会都会为歌曲填词）、运动控制（所有社会的人们都会跳舞）、声音分析（所有音乐体系都有独特的音高和音质）以及美感（它们的曲调和节奏在重复与混乱之间保持平衡）。", "已知的人类社会中没有哪一个是不存在音乐的。尽管每种文化都有其特定的音乐风格和创作方式，但你会发现音乐背后的目的在各处都非常相似。音乐本质上用于表达或改变情绪。它可以让你振作、悲伤、愤怒或兴奋。音乐通常具有仪式性：用于宗教、礼仪和庆典活动。音乐也可以纯粹是消遣性的：具有娱乐性、令人愉悦且充满乐趣。无论你曾以何种方式使用过音乐，几乎可以肯定的是，其他每一种文化也都以完全相同的方式使用过音乐。而这正是将我们所有人联系在一起的东西。我们都对音乐怀有深厚的热爱，它拥有团结我们的力量。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "In what way is music important?", "options": ["It is able to create novel and extraordinary emotions.", "It has the power to unite people throughout the world.", "It allows different cultural groups to sing in harmony.", "It is the only language favored by all peoples of the world."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "It is vitally important across the globe and has the potential to bring people", "explanation": "由题干“important”定位至第一段，原文指出音乐在全球至关重要，并有潜力让人们和平共处（衔接第二段首句“together in peace and harmony”）。第四段末尾亦重申“it has the power to unite us”。B项“has the power to unite people throughout the world”对原文进行了精准的同义概括，因此B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“创造新奇非凡的情感”将第二段的“新声音”与“非凡结果”偷换为情感；C项将团结凝聚窄化为“唱歌”；D项中的“only”属于绝对化表述，原文并未称其为唯一语言。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why does the author like to see musicians from different cultures perform together?", "options": ["Their musical experience can be compared.", "A novel language can be created.", "Their unique skills can be displayed.", "Fantastic results can be achieved."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "When each culture brings its own unique qualities to the group, an entirely new sound is achieved. This can create extraordinary results.", "explanation": "根据题干定位至第二段。作者表示这是自己最喜爱的经历之一，随后说明当各文化将独特特质融入团队时，便能产生全新的声音并“create extraordinary results”（创造非凡效果）。D项“Fantastic results can be achieved”用“Fantastic”同义替换“extraordinary”，准确解释了作者喜爱的原因，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“音乐经历可作比较”原文未提及；B项“创造出新语言”将原文的“entirely new sound”偷换为语言；C项“展示独特技能”偏离了合作产生非凡效果这一直接原因。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about the pentatonic scale?", "options": ["It is present in music all around the world.", "It is helpful to understanding music.", "It is the basis for musicians' creation.", "It is a medium for ordinary people to relate."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "This scale can be found in music everywhere including that of Native Americans, Africans, and Asians.", "explanation": "由题干“pentatonic scale”定位至第二段后半部分。原文指出众多文化都共用这一五声音阶，并明确说明“This scale can be found in music everywhere”，涵盖美洲原住民、非洲、亚洲以及多种现代流行乐派。A项“is present in music all around the world”正是对“found in music everywhere”的同义转述，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“有助于理解音乐”与D项“普通人建立联系的媒介”均偷换了原文对象，末尾指明该音阶是全球音乐家相互理解与交流的媒介；C项“创作基础”属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the fundamental role of music in people's life?", "options": ["To bring them together.", "To show their identity.", "To express their emotions.", "To keep them entertained."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Music essentially serves to express or change emotions.", "explanation": "由题干“fundamental role of music”定位至第四段第三句。原文指出尽管各文化风格迥异，但音乐背后的目的却非常相似，并点明“Music essentially serves to express or change emotions”，即音乐本质上用于表达或改变情绪。C项“To express their emotions”中的“express emotions”直接复现原文，对应“essentially serves to”，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“把人们聚在一起”是音乐的社会纽带作用，而非题干所问的在生活中的本质功能；D项“保持娱乐”只是后文提到的消遣用途之一；B项“展示身份”原文未提及。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "In what aspect is music similar throughout the world?", "options": ["The way people respond to it.", "The role it plays in society.", "The joy it brings to people.", "The way it is made use of."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Any way you have used music, it is almost certain that every other culture has used music in the very same way.", "explanation": "根据题干“similar throughout the world”定位至第四段。该段先提及音乐背后的目的极为相似，随后在倒数第四句总结道：“Any way you have used music, it is almost certain that every other culture has used music in the very same way”，意即世界各地以完全相同的方式使用音乐。D项“The way it is made use of”同义转述了使用音乐的方式，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“人们的反应方式”和C项“带来的快乐”均属于以偏概全，只涵盖了音乐功能中的局部表现；B项“在社会中扮演的角色”不如D项贴合“used music in the very same way”的原意。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "普遍的，通用的", "note": "常用于形容跨越文化与国界的事物，如 universal language（通用语言）。", "word": "universal"}, {"gloss": "卓越的，非凡的", "note": "extra-（超出）+ ordinary（普通的），文中对应选项中的 fantastic。", "word": "extraordinary"}, {"gloss": "（身体或心智的）官能，能力", "note": "文中以复数形式 faculties 出现，指感知、心理和情感能力。", "word": "faculty"}, {"gloss": "仪式性的，礼仪的", "note": "由名词 ceremony 派生而来，文中说明音乐常用于宗教与庆典场合。", "word": "ceremonial"}, {"gloss": "使结合，使紧密联系", "note": "作动词意为“把……联系在一起”，对应后文的 unite（团结）。", "word": "bond"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Using this five-note scale, musicians from around the globe have a medium through which they can relate, communicate, perform, and ultimately understand each other.", "point": "现在分词短语 Using... 作方式状语，后接由“介词 through + 关系代词 which”引导的定语从句，修饰先行词 medium，从句内包含四个并列谓语动词。", "structure": "分词状语(Using...) + 主语(musicians...) + 谓语(have) + 宾语(a medium) + 介词+which定语从句(through which they can V1, V2, V3, and V4)", "zh": "借助这一五声音阶，世界各地的音乐家拥有了一种媒介，通过它他们可以建立联系、交流、演奏并最终理解彼此。"}, {"en": "Although each culture has their own specific style and approach to music, you will find that the purposes behind music are very similar across the board.", "point": "Although 引导让步状语从句，主句中 that 引导宾语从句，across the board 为固定习语，意为“全面地，普遍地”。", "structure": "Although让步状语从句 + 主语(you) + 谓语(will find) + that宾语从句(the purposes... are very similar across the board)", "zh": "尽管每种文化都有其特定的音乐风格和创作方式，但你会发现音乐背后的目的在各处都非常相似。"}, {"en": "Any way you have used music, it is almost certain that every other culture has used music in the very same way.", "point": "Any way 引导方式状语从句，主句采用“it is + 形容词 + that...”形式主语结构，强调跨文化使用音乐的一致性。", "structure": "状语从句(Any way you have used music) + 形式主语(it) + 系表(is almost certain) + that真实主语从句", "zh": "无论你曾以何种方式使用过音乐，几乎可以肯定的是，其他每一种文化也都以完全相同的方式使用过音乐。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "动词短语与核心动词的精准呼应，说明音乐凝聚全人类的力量。", "option": "has the power to unite people throughout the world", "original": "has the potential to bring people together ... it has the power to unite us"}, {"note": "形容词近义替换与主动转被动句式转换。", "option": "Fantastic results can be achieved", "original": "create extraordinary results"}, {"note": "介词短语和地点表达的同义转换：everywhere 对应 all around the world。", "option": "is present in music all around the world", "original": "can be found in music everywhere"}, {"note": "essentially serves to（本质上用于……）精准对应题干的 fundamental role（根本作用）。", "option": "To express their emotions", "original": "essentially serves to express or change emotions"}, {"note": "动词短语的同义改写：use 对应 make use of，in the very same way 体现方式相同。", "option": "The way it is made use of", "original": "used music in the very same way"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202606-s3-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 四级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 四级真题 第3套 Passage One", "title": "儿童对生理与道德厌恶的认知研究", "subtitle": "心理学实验探讨儿童何时理解道德厌恶以及亲子情感交流的作用", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 354, "paragraphs": ["Disgust is a universal human emotion. One type of disgust is called physical disgust, which protects us from eating or touching things that could be dangerous for us, such as raw meat or insects. Children experience physical disgust from a very early age, but do not achieve an understanding of the concept until they are around four years old.", "Some researchers maintain that there is another type of disgust, called moral disgust, that protects us from engaging in activities that can be perceived as morally wrong. Examples of moral disgust are stealing, lying or cheating. However, not all academics think that moral disgust really exists. Some say that when we refer to disgust in relation to moral issues, we are using disgust as a metaphor, and what we are feeling is in reality anger.", "If moral disgust appears quite late in development, it makes sense to think that there is actually a social component to it. Children learn about emotions in many different ways. Of special relevance are parents-children conversations", "about emotions. Indeed, children whose parents talk about emotions often have a better emotional understanding than children whose parents do not discuss emotions often.", "However, there are no studies that have examined how parents and children talk about disgust. This is what we set up to examine in our study. We asked 68 English-speaking mothers and their four-, six- or eight-year-old children to discuss some stories about moral and physical disgust. Our preliminary findings show mothers and children do talk about disgust, but mainly about physical disgust and not so much about moral disgust. When we asked mothers and children to discuss moral issues, such as whether it is OK to play with a child who has stolen someone else's snack, they linked this type of moral wrongdoing with the emotion of anger and not disgust. Does this mean that moral disgust does not exist? Some researchers suggest moral disgust exists in adults. Our findings suggest that moral disgust is either understood at a later age or is only used metaphorically, if at all, in children as old as eight years."], "translations": ["厌恶是一种普遍的人类情绪。其中一种厌恶被称为生理厌恶，它能保护我们避免食用或接触可能对我们构成危险的物品，例如生肉或昆虫。儿童在很小的时候就会经历生理厌恶，但直到四岁左右才能够理解这一概念。", "一些研究者认为，还存在另一种被称为道德厌恶的厌恶感，它能保护我们避免参与可能被视为在道德上错误的行为。道德厌恶的例子包括偷盗、撒谎或欺骗。然而，并非所有学者都认为道德厌恶真的存在。有些人表示，当我们在涉及道德问题时谈到厌恶，我们只是把厌恶当作一种隐喻，而我们真正感受到的其实是愤怒。", "如果道德厌恶在成长发育的较晚阶段才出现，那么认为其中实际上包含社会因素便合情合理。儿童通过多种不同方式学习情绪。尤为重要的是父母与孩子之间进行的", "关于情绪的对话。事实上，父母经常谈论情绪的孩子，往往比父母不常讨论情绪的孩子拥有更好的情绪理解能力。", "然而，目前还没有研究考察过父母与孩子如何谈论厌恶情绪。这正是我们在本研究中着手考察的内容。我们让68位说英语的母亲及其四岁、六岁或八岁的孩子讨论一些关于道德厌恶和生理厌恶的故事。我们的初步研究发现表明，母亲和孩子确实会谈论厌恶，但主要围绕生理厌恶，而很少谈及道德厌恶。当我们让母亲和孩子讨论道德问题时，比如是否可以和偷了别人零食的孩子一起玩，他们将这种道德不当行为与愤怒情绪联系在一起，而不是厌恶。这是否意味着道德厌恶并不存在呢？一些研究者认为道德厌恶存在于成年人身上。我们的研究结果表明，在年满八岁的儿童中，道德厌恶要么要在更晚的年龄才能被理解，要么即便存在也仅仅是被隐喻性地使用。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage tell us about physical disgust?", "options": ["It is an emotion as contrasted with thoughts.", "It is a concept beyond children's understanding.", "It is a mechanism to keep us from being harmed.", "It is an experience gained from any form of danger."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "One type of disgust is called physical disgust, which protects us from eating or touching things that could be dangerous for us, such as raw meat or insects.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查生理厌恶的作用。根据第1段第2句“One type of disgust is called physical disgust, which protects us from eating or touching things that could be dangerous for us”，生理厌恶能保护我们避免食用或接触可能带来危险的物品（如生肉或昆虫）。选项C“它是一种使我们免受伤害的机制”正是对原文“protects us from... dangerous”的同义转述，因此C为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项将情绪与思维对立，原文未提及；B项偷换概念，原文指四岁前儿童尚未理解该概念而非完全无法理解；D项“任何形式的危险”过于绝对。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How do some researchers perceive moral disgust?", "options": ["It tends to appear in various forms of wrongdoing.", "It is just as annoying to people as physical disgust.", "It is a term used by common folk to describe anger.", "It stops people from doing anything morally wrong."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Some researchers maintain that there is another type of disgust, called moral disgust, that protects us from engaging in activities that can be perceived as morally wrong.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查部分研究者对道德厌恶的看法。第2段首句明确指出，一些研究者认为存在另一种被称为道德厌恶的厌恶感，它能保护我们避免参与可能被视为在道德上错误的行为（protects us from engaging in activities that can be perceived as morally wrong）。选项D“阻止人们做任何道德上错误的事”精准对应原文表述，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项原文列举了偷盗、撒谎、欺骗等例子，并非说其倾向于出现在各种不当行为中；C项中的“common folk（普通民众）”无中生有，原文主语为部分学者。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why does moral disgust appear quite late in children's development?", "options": ["It needs to be learnt through social interactions.", "They have little control over its learning process.", "It is too complex for them to acquire.", "Their parents seldom talk about emotions."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "If moral disgust appears quite late in development, it makes sense to think that there is actually a social component to it. Children learn about emotions in many different ways.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查道德厌恶在儿童成长过程中出现较晚的原因。第3段首句指出，如果道德厌恶在发育较晚时才出现，那么认为其中实际上存在社会成分是合理的（there is actually a social component to it），随后提到儿童通过多种方式学习情绪，亲子对话尤为关键。由此可知道德厌恶需要通过社交互动习得，对应选项A。", "trapNote": "B项“几乎无法控制学习过程”和C项“过于复杂而难以习得”均属无中生有；D项仅是第4段提及的对比情况，并非普遍原因。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did the author and his colleagues want to examine in their experiment?", "options": ["What parents tell children against moral wrongdoing.", "What parents and children link moral wrongdoing to.", "How moral disgust is seen by children aged 4, 6 and 8.", "How disgust is discussed between parents and children."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "However, there are no studies that have examined how parents and children talk about disgust. This is what we set up to examine in our study.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查作者及其同事在实验中的研究目的。第5段前两句指出，此前尚无研究探讨父母与孩子如何谈论厌恶情绪（how parents and children talk about disgust），而这正是作者团队在研究中着手考察的内容（This is what we set up to examine in our study）。选项D准确概括了该研究目的，为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项和B项均属于实验过程中的具体讨论问题或发现，而非研究初衷；C项将实验对象（四、六、八岁儿童及母亲）缩小为仅考察儿童对道德厌恶的看法，以偏概全。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we infer about moral disgust from the author and his colleagues' findings?", "options": ["It is a notion hardly comprehensible to children.", "It rarely exists in children younger than eight.", "It is a term most parents use when talking to children.", "It exists in adults with a strong sense of justice."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Our findings suggest that moral disgust is either understood at a later age or is only used metaphorically, if at all, in children as old as eight years.", "explanation": "本题为推断题，考查从作者及其同事的研究发现中能推断出关于道德厌恶的什么结论。第5段末句指出，研究结果表明在八岁及以下的儿童中，道德厌恶要么到更晚的年龄才能被理解，要么根本只是被隐喻性地使用（either understood at a later age or is only used metaphorically, if at all）。由此可合理推断，道德厌恶对儿童而言是一个难以理解的概念，对应选项A。", "trapNote": "B项认为“很少存在于八岁以下儿童中”与第5段“if at all”及前文“是愤怒而非厌恶”的表述有偏差，且不如A项直接契合“understood at a later age”；C项与研究发现相反。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 厌恶，反感", "note": "高频核心词，文中区分 physical disgust（生理厌恶）与 moral disgust（道德厌恶）。", "word": "disgust"}, {"gloss": "v. 坚持认为；主张", "note": "熟词僻义，此处不作“维持”讲，而是引出学者观点（= argue / claim）。", "word": "maintain"}, {"gloss": "n. 隐喻，比喻", "note": "衍生词 metaphorically（隐喻性地）出现在末段，意指借用“厌恶”一词表达愤怒。", "word": "metaphor"}, {"gloss": "adj. 初步的，预备的", "note": "常用于科研语境，如 preliminary findings（初步研究发现）。", "word": "preliminary"}, {"gloss": "n. 成分，组成部分", "note": "文中 social component 指“社会因素/社会成分”，提示后天互动对习得情绪的作用。", "word": "component"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Some say that when we refer to disgust in relation to moral issues, we are using disgust as a metaphor, and what we are feeling is in reality anger.", "point": "时间状语从句与主语从句嵌套，注意 in reality 作插入语修饰系表结构。", "structure": "主句主干为 Some say that...；that 引导宾语从句，内含由 and 连接的两个并列分句；第一分句包含 when 引导的时间状语从句，第二分句中 what we are feeling 为主语从句。", "zh": "有些人表示，当我们在涉及道德问题时谈到厌恶，我们只是把厌恶当作一种隐喻，而我们真正感受到的其实是愤怒。"}, {"en": "When we asked mothers and children to discuss moral issues, such as whether it is OK to play with a child who has stolen someone else's snack, they linked this type of moral wrongdoing with the emotion of anger and not disgust.", "point": "link A with B（把A与B联系起来）；such as 后接 whether 引导的宾语从句作为具体举例。", "structure": "When 引导时间状语从句，其中 such as 后接 whether 引导的宾语从句作举例说明（内含 who 引导的定语从句修饰 a child）；主句主干为 they linked this type of moral wrongdoing with...。", "zh": "当我们让母亲和孩子讨论道德问题时，比如是否可以和偷了别人零食的孩子一起玩，他们将这种道德不当行为与愤怒情绪联系在一起，而不是厌恶。"}, {"en": "Our findings suggest that moral disgust is either understood at a later age or is only used metaphorically, if at all, in children as old as eight years.", "point": "either... or... 连接并列谓语，if at all 作让步状语插入其中，表示“即使真的有的话”。", "structure": "主句主干为 Our findings suggest that...；that 引导的宾语从句中使用了 either... or... 并列结构，中间插入省略条件状语 if at all。", "zh": "我们的研究结果表明，在年满八岁的儿童中，道德厌恶要么要在更晚的年龄才能被理解，要么即便存在也仅仅是被隐喻性地使用。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "动作保护机制与免受伤害之间的因果功能替换。", "option": "keep us from being harmed", "original": "protects us from eating or touching things that could be dangerous for us"}, {"note": "由“社会成分/多种学习途径”推导出“需要通过社交互动习得”。", "option": "be learnt through social interactions", "original": "there is actually a social component to it. Children learn about emotions in many different ways"}, {"note": "词性转换与结构重组，talk about 替换为被动形式的 is discussed。", "option": "How disgust is discussed between parents and children", "original": "how parents and children talk about disgust"}, {"note": "从“直到更晚才被理解”及“未出现真实理解”提炼出“几乎无法被儿童理解”。", "option": "hardly comprehensible to children", "original": "either understood at a later age or is only used metaphorically, if at all, in children as old as eight years"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202606-s3-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 四级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 四级真题 第3套 Passage Two", "title": "社交互惠错觉与居民诚实行为研究", "subtitle": "心理学研究揭示人们了解陌生人信息后如何因互惠错觉而表现更诚实", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 352, "paragraphs": ["After finding out details about a stranger, we mistakenly think that they also know about us. As a result, we act more honestly around them, according to a recent study in Nature.", "Past research has found that we tend to assume social relationships are reciprocal. Most of the time, this assumption is accurate: someone you think of as a friend will usually consider you a friend too. But sometimes our social ties are more one-sided: for example, you might learn something about a stranger who doesn't know you at all. Researchers Anuj Shah and Michael LaForest wondered whether our tendency to believe that social ties are reciprocal could lead us to mistakenly feel that a stranger does actually know us. In a series of lab-based studies, this is exactly what the researchers found. When we know about strangers, we erroneously think they also know about us. But the really interesting finding came when the researchers stepped out of the lab, to conduct a field experiment. The team developed leaflets (传单) containing fairly ordinary information about local community police officers, such as their favourite food, hobbies, or reasons for joining the police force. They then sent out these leaflets to every apartment in a number of housing developments in disadvantaged areas. The officers themselves also dropped off cards to local residents containing similar information.", "Two months later, the researchers surveyed residents at these housing developments as well as control areas that did not receive leaflets or outreach cards. Residents were asked to imagine that they had committed a crime and how likely it would be that local officers would find out about it. They also rated how well the officers in the area knew them.", "The team found that residents of the developments that had received the leaflets believed it more likely that local officers would find out about illegal activity than residents of the control areas. Even more strikingly, the team found that immediately after the leaflet distribution, there were fewer criminal complaints", "and arrests in the areas around the developments that had received the leaflets than around the control developments."], "translations": ["根据《自然》杂志近期发表的一项研究，在了解到关于某个陌生人的细节信息后，我们会错误地认为对方也了解我们。因此，我们在他们身边会表现得更加诚实。", "过去的研究发现，我们倾向于认为社会关系是互惠的。大多数时候，这种假设是准确的：你视为朋友的人通常也会把你当作朋友。但有时我们的社会纽带更具单向性：例如，你可能会了解到某个完全不了解你的陌生人的一些事情。研究者阿努杰·沙阿和迈克尔·拉福里斯特想知道，我们倾向于相信社会纽带具有互惠性，是否会促使我们错误地觉得某个陌生人其实真的了解我们。在一系列实验室研究中，研究者发现的正是如此。当我们了解陌生人时，会错误地认为他们也了解我们。但真正有趣的发现出现在研究者走出实验室开展实地实验之时。该团队制作了印有当地社区警官相当普通信息的传单，比如他们最喜欢的食物、爱好或加入警队的原因。随后，他们将这些传单分发到弱势地区多个住宅小区的每一户公寓。警官们自己也向当地居民发放了载有类似信息的卡片。", "两个月后，研究者对这些住宅小区以及未收到传单或外联卡片的对照区域的居民进行了调查。居民们被要求设想自己犯了罪，并评估当地警官发现此事的可能性有多大。他们还评估了该地区警官对自己的了解程度。", "研究团队发现，相比对照区域的居民，收到传单的住宅区居民更倾向于认为当地警官会发现违法行为。更令人惊叹的是，团队发现在分发传单后不久，收到传单的住宅区周边出现的刑事报案", "与逮捕事件均少于对照住宅区周边。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the finding of a recent study in Nature?", "options": ["People are more honest with those who know them than with total strangers.", "People we want to have detailed information about are keen to know about us.", "People who get to know about a person wrongly assume the person knows them too.", "People who are familiar with each other tend to behave honestly in their everyday dealings."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "After finding out details about a stranger, we mistakenly think that they also know about us.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查《自然》杂志上一项近期研究的发现。第1段首句明确指出，在了解到陌生人的一些细节信息后，我们会错误地认为对方也了解我们（After finding out details about a stranger, we mistakenly think that they also know about us）。选项C“人们在了解某人后会错误地认为对方也了解自己”完美转述了“mistakenly think”与“wrongly assume”，故C正确。", "trapNote": "A项“比对完全陌生的人更诚实”偏离核心发现，且对象混淆；B项“渴望了解我们”属主观臆测；D项将研究对象“陌生人”偷换为“彼此熟悉的人”。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about the assumption that social relationships are reciprocal?", "options": ["It is more the exception than the rule.", "It does not hold true in every situation.", "It does not apply to complex relationships.", "It is more accurate in one-sided social ties."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Most of the time, this assumption is accurate: someone you think of as a friend will usually consider you a friend too. But sometimes our social ties are more one-sided: for example, you might learn something about a stranger who doesn't know you at all.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查文章对“社会关系是互惠的”这一假设的描述。第2段前两句说明，大多数时候这一假设是准确的（Most of the time, this assumption is accurate），但第三句随即转折指出，有时社会纽带是单向的（sometimes our social ties are more one-sided），例如你了解一个完全不了解你的陌生人。这说明该假设并非在所有情况下都成立，对应选项B。", "trapNote": "A项“是例外而非常态”与原文“大多数时候准确”完全相反；C项“复杂关系”和D项“单向社会纽带中更准确”均与原文“单向关系打破互惠假设”的表述相悖。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did Anuj Shah and Michael LaForest want to find out about the belief that social relationships are reciprocal?", "options": ["Whether it may resolve misunderstandings about social ties.", "Whether it could help develop one's relationships with strangers.", "Whether it could help strengthen interpersonal relationships.", "Whether it may lead to false assumptions about a stranger."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Researchers Anuj Shah and Michael LaForest wondered whether our tendency to believe that social ties are reciprocal could lead us to mistakenly feel that a stranger does actually know us.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查研究者Anuj Shah和Michael LaForest想探究的内容。第2段第4句指出，两位研究者想知道我们对社会纽带互惠性的相信倾向，是否会导致我们错误地觉得陌生人其实了解自己（wondered whether our tendency to believe that social ties are reciprocal could lead us to mistakenly feel that a stranger does actually know us）。选项D准确转述了此研究问题，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项“解决误解”、B项“发展与陌生人的关系”及C项“加强人际关系”均为无中生有，原文研究聚焦于该信念是否引发“错误感觉/虚假假设”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "When did Anuj Shah and Michael LaForest find something really interesting in their research?", "options": ["During lab-based studies.", "During a field experiment.", "While investigating local residents' crime.", "While talking to police officers nearby."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But the really interesting finding came when the researchers stepped out of the lab, to conduct a field experiment.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查两位研究者何时在研究中发现了真正有趣的结果。第2段先提及了一系列实验室研究（lab-based studies），随后在第7句明确转折指出，但真正有趣的发现出现在研究者走出实验室开展实地实验之时（But the really interesting finding came when the researchers stepped out of the lab, to conduct a field experiment）。选项B直接对应“a field experiment”，为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“实验室研究期间”为干扰项，原文指出真正有趣的发现在“走出实验室”之后；C项“调查当地居民犯罪时”和D项“与附近警察交谈时”均与实验步骤不符。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What happened in the areas around the housing developments subjected to the studies?", "options": ["They saw fewer crimes than the control developments.", "They witnessed a swifter elimination of illegal activities.", "Local police responded more quickly to criminal complaints than before.", "Local police related better to residents there than to those in other areas."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Even more strikingly, the team found that immediately after the leaflet distribution, there were fewer criminal complaints", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查接受研究的住宅区周边发生了什么变化。第4段末句至第5段指出，研究团队发现，在分发传单后不久，相比对照住宅区周边，收到传单的住宅区周边的刑事报案和逮捕事件都更少（there were fewer criminal complaints and arrests... than around the control developments）。选项A“相比对照住宅区，那里的犯罪减少了”精准概括了这一结果，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项“更快消除违法活动”、C项“当地警察比以前更快响应报案”以及D项“警民关系比其他地区更好”均属于过度推断或无中生有，原文仅提及报案和逮捕数量减少。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 互惠的，相互的", "note": "本文核心概念词，指双方彼此了解或对等的关系假设。", "word": "reciprocal"}, {"gloss": "adv. 错误地，不正确地", "note": "等同于文章首段的 mistakenly，用于替换避免重复。", "word": "erroneously"}, {"gloss": "adj. 弱势的，贫困的", "note": "文中 disadvantaged areas 指条件较差或治安相对薄弱的弱势社区。", "word": "disadvantaged"}, {"gloss": "n. 住宅区，开发小区", "note": "复数 developments 此处不作“发展”讲，而指成片新建的住宅小区。", "word": "development"}, {"gloss": "adj. 惊人的，显著的", "note": "副词 strikingly 修饰整句，表示实验结果出乎意料且效果显著。", "word": "striking"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Researchers Anuj Shah and Michael LaForest wondered whether our tendency to believe that social ties are reciprocal could lead us to mistakenly feel that a stranger does actually know us.", "point": "多重宾语从句嵌套与不定式作后置定语，注意 wondered whether 引导整个间接疑问内容。", "structure": "主句为 Researchers... wondered whether...；whether 引导宾语从句，其主语 our tendency 后接不定式短语 to believe that...（内含宾语从句）作定语；lead us to feel 后接 that 引导的宾语从句，does 用于加强语气。", "zh": "研究者阿努杰·沙阿和迈克尔·拉福里斯特想知道，我们倾向于相信社会纽带具有互惠性，是否会促使我们错误地觉得某个陌生人其实真的了解我们。"}, {"en": "The team found that residents of the developments that had received the leaflets believed it more likely that local officers would find out about illegal activity than residents of the control areas.", "point": "it 作形式宾语替代真正宾语从句 that local officers...，同时包含 more likely... than... 的比较结构。", "structure": "主句为 The team found that...；that 从句主语为 residents，带有定语从句 that had received the leaflets；believed it more likely that... 中 it 为形式宾语，真正的宾语是 that local officers... 从句，than 后为比较对象。", "zh": "研究团队发现，相比对照区域的居民，收到传单的住宅区居民更倾向于认为当地警官会发现违法行为。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "核心动词短语与副词的精准同义替换。", "option": "wrongly assume the person knows them too", "original": "mistakenly think that they also know about us"}, {"note": "以否定形式转述“大部分时间准确，但有时并非如此”。", "option": "does not hold true in every situation", "original": "Most of the time, this assumption is accurate... But sometimes our social ties are more one-sided"}, {"note": "将具体的“错误感觉陌生人了解自己”概括为“对陌生人产生错误假设”。", "option": "lead to false assumptions about a stranger", "original": "lead us to mistakenly feel that a stranger does actually know us"}, {"note": "将具体的“更少的刑事报案与逮捕”上位归纳为“犯罪减少”。", "option": "saw fewer crimes than the control developments", "original": "there were fewer criminal complaints and arrests in the areas around the developments that had received the leaflets than around the control developments"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202512-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2025.12", "examSet": "2025.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2025.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "遵循昼夜节律把握服药时机", "subtitle": "生物钟不仅影响人体机能，也决定了药物疗效与副作用", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 345, "paragraphs": ["All living organisms on Earth are exposed to a 24-hour day-night cycle. This cycle is the reason why people rest at night and are active during the day. Consequently, all human body functions also follow this daily rhythm, and the timing of behaviors like exercise or food intake can significantly influence your health. For example, eating at night can lead to weight gain over time because food intake at night leads to increased fat storage. Many drug targets in the body follow a 24-hour cycle, too. This means that the specific proteins a drug is designed to modify can react differently to the medicine over the course of a 24-hour time period. Because how the body responds to a drug can differ depending on the time it is taken, it logically follows that taking medicines at specific times could help increase their effectiveness and reduce unwanted side effects. When doctors prescribe medicine for people, they rarely consider the best time to take it. There are two main reasons for that oversight. First, many physicians are not aware that some drugs work better during a specific time of the day. And second, most drugs have not been studied for possible different effects during a 24-hour cycle. Therefore, patients are directed to take most drugs during the morning or evening primarily to ensure compliance.", "Over 50 years ago, researchers found that the cholesterol drug simvastatin is more effective at lowering cholesterol levels when taken at night rather than during the day. This is because the liver enzyme these drugs target is more active at night. Taking medicine at the wrong time can even cause harm. My colleagues and I wondered whether midazolam, the most common sedative used in surgical procedures worldwide, might interfere with the internal clock that protects the heart at night. Currently, there are no guidelines regarding when midazolam should be administered.", "More research is needed to determine the best times to administer treatments for different diseases. I believe taking drug timing into account could help make treatments more effective and help more people worldwide."], "translations": ["地球上的所有生物都处于24小时的昼夜循环之中。这一循环正是人们夜间休息、白天活动的原因。因此，人体的所有生理机能也都遵循这一日常节律，而运动或进食等行为的时间安排会显著影响你的健康。例如，长期在夜间进食会导致体重增加，因为夜间摄入食物会促使脂肪更多地储存。体内的许多药物靶点同样遵循24小时周期。这意味着药物旨在调节的特定蛋白质在24小时周期内会对药物产生不同的反应。由于身体对药物的反应会因服药时间不同而有所差异，逻辑上顺理成章的是，在特定时间服药有助于提高疗效并减少不必要的副作用。然而，医生给患者开药时，却很少考虑最佳的服药时间。造成这种疏忽主要有两大原因。首先，许多医生并未意识到某些药物在一天中的特定时段效果更好。其次，大多数药物尚未就其在24小时周期内可能产生的不同效果开展过研究。因此，医生嘱咐患者在早晚服用大多数药物，主要只是为了确保患者按时按量遵医嘱服药。", "50多年前，研究人员发现降胆固醇药物辛伐他汀在夜间服用比白天服用降脂效果更好。这是因为这类药物所靶向的肝脏酶在夜间更加活跃。在错误的时间服药甚至可能造成伤害。我和同事曾探究，全球外科手术中最常用的镇静剂咪达唑仑是否会干扰夜间保护心脏的生物钟。目前，关于应在何时使用咪达唑仑尚无指导规范。", "还需要开展更多研究，以确定治疗不同疾病的最佳用药时机。我相信，将服药时间纳入考量有助于提升治疗效果，让全球更多人受益。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about the timing of our behaviors?", "options": ["It has a considerable impact on our health.", "It confines us to a 24-hour day-night cycle.", "It requires us to follow a particular rhythm.", "It holds the key to all human body functions."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Consequently, all human body functions also follow this daily rhythm, and the timing of behaviors like exercise or food intake can significantly influence your health.", "explanation": "第1段第3句明确指出，人体所有生理机能都遵循日常节律，而运动或进食等行为的时间安排会显著影响健康（significantly influence your health）。A项中的has a considerable impact on our health是对significantly influence your health的同义替换，表述与原文完全一致，因此A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项将“暴露于24小时昼夜循环”偷换为“行为时间把我们局限在昼夜循环中”；C项“要求我们遵循特定节律”无中生有；D项“掌握所有生理机能的关键”过度夸大原文因果关系。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say about the proteins in our body?", "options": ["They can modify the effects of medicines in different ways.", "They can reduce unwanted side effects of certain medicines.", "Their reaction to medicines changes during the day-night cycle.", "Their design determines how differently they react to medicines."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "This means that the specific proteins a drug is designed to modify can react differently to the medicine over the course of a 24-hour time period.", "explanation": "根据题干关键词proteins定位到第1段第6句。该句解释道，药物旨在调节的特定蛋白质在24小时周期内会对药物产生不同的反应（react differently to the medicine over the course of a 24-hour time period）。C项中reaction to medicines changes对应react differently，during the day-night cycle对应24小时周期，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项颠倒主客体，原文是药物调节蛋白质，而非蛋白质改变药效；B项把“在特定时间服药可减少副作用”张冠李戴为蛋白质的作用；D项“蛋白质的设计决定其反应差异”属于主观臆断。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do doctors do when prescribing medicine for people?", "options": ["They give little thought to the time of taking it for maximum effect.", "They rarely consider which medicine works better for which patient.", "They tell patients its possible side effects during a period of 24 hours.", "They tell patients to comply with the directions of drug manufacturers."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "When doctors prescribe medicine for people, they rarely consider the best time to take it.", "explanation": "由题干中的prescribe medicine for people可直接定位到第1段第8句。原文指出，医生在给患者开药时很少考虑最佳服药时间（rarely consider the best time to take it）。A项中give little thought to对应rarely consider，the time of taking it for maximum effect对应“最佳服药时间”，完美契合原文，故为答案。", "trapNote": "B项将“很少考虑最佳服药时间”偷换为“很少考虑哪种药对哪个患者更有效”；C项“告知24小时内可能的副作用”与D项“要求遵循药企说明书”在原文中均未提及，属于典型无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why do doctors advise patients to take most drugs in the morning or in the evening?", "options": ["To discourage them from making complaints.", "To ensure they take the drugs as instructed.", "To comply with new research findings strictly.", "To guarantee the maximum effect of the drugs."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Therefore, patients are directed to take most drugs during the morning or evening primarily to ensure compliance.", "explanation": "定位至第1段最后一句。句中明确说明，患者被要求在早晚服用大多数药物，主要是为了确保“遵医嘱服药”（primarily to ensure compliance）。B项中的take the drugs as instructed正是对compliance（依从性、按指导服药）的精准同义释义，完整还原了原文的因果逻辑，因此选B。", "trapNote": "A项将compliance（依从、遵从）形近误读为complaints（抱怨）；D项“保证最大药效”与原文相反，医生正是因为未考虑最佳药效时机才让患者早晚服药以保证按时服用。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author suggest near the end of the passage?", "options": ["Considering drug-taking timing when prescribing drugs for patients.", "Making treatments less complex by taking drug timing into account.", "Conducting more studies to find out the best timing for treating different diseases.", "Finding out the most effective drugs for treating diseases through further"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "More research is needed to determine the best times to administer treatments for different diseases.", "explanation": "定位至文章最后一段首句。作者在结尾明确提出，还需要开展更多研究，以确定针对不同疾病的最佳给药时间（More research is needed to determine the best times to administer treatments for different diseases）。C项Conducting more studies对应More research is needed，best timing对应best times，与原文高度吻合，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项虽符合全文大方向，但文末作者强调的是“先开展更多研究以确定最佳时机”，而非直接要求开处方时考虑；B项“降低治疗复杂性”与D项“寻找最有效药物”均偏离“最佳时机”这一核心。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "摄入（量）", "note": "文中food intake指食物摄入，四级高频生理健康类名词", "word": "intake"}, {"gloss": "调节；改变", "note": "文中指药物对特定蛋白质的调节作用，常见于科普阅读", "word": "modify"}, {"gloss": "开处方；开药", "note": "核心医学动词，名词形式为prescription（处方）", "word": "prescribe"}, {"gloss": "遵从；依从性", "note": "医疗语境中特指患者按医嘱服药，动词为comply (with)", "word": "compliance"}, {"gloss": "施用，给予（药物）", "note": "熟词僻义：除“管理”外，在医学语境中常指“用药、实施治疗”", "word": "administer"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "This means that the specific proteins a drug is designed to modify can react differently to the medicine over the course of a 24-hour time period.", "point": "识别定语从句嵌套结构，理清drug、proteins与modify之间的逻辑关系", "structure": "主句(This means that...) + 宾语从句，其中包含省略关系代词that/which的定语从句(a drug is designed to modify)修饰specific proteins", "zh": "这意味着药物旨在调节的特定蛋白质在24小时的周期内会对该药物产生不同的反应。"}, {"en": "Because how the body responds to a drug can differ depending on the time it is taken, it logically follows that taking medicines at specific times could help increase their effectiveness and reduce unwanted side effects.", "point": "掌握“it follows that...”固定句型及多重复合从句的拆解", "structure": "Because引导原因状语从句(内含how引导的主语从句) + 主句(it形式主语 + logically follows + that真正主语从句)", "zh": "由于身体对药物的反应会因服药时间不同而异，在特定时间服药有助于提高药效并减少不必要的副作用也就合乎逻辑了。"}, {"en": "My colleagues and I wondered whether midazolam, the most common sedative used in surgical procedures worldwide, might interfere with the internal clock that protects the heart at night.", "point": "准确把握插入同位语对核心名词midazolam的补充说明作用", "structure": "主句(My colleagues and I wondered) + whether引导宾语从句 + 同位语(the most common sedative...) + that引导定语从句修饰internal clock", "zh": "我和同事曾探究，全球外科手术中最常用的镇静剂咪达唑仑是否会干扰夜间保护心脏的生物钟。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "副词+动词短语转换为动词+形容词+名词结构，significantly = considerable", "option": "has a considerable impact on our health", "original": "significantly influence your health"}, {"note": "词性转换（react -> reaction）与上下义词替换（24-hour time period -> day-night cycle）", "option": "reaction to medicines changes during the day-night cycle", "original": "react differently to the medicine over the course of a 24-hour time period"}, {"note": "否定频度副词rarely对应give little thought to，best time具象化为for maximum effect", "option": "give little thought to the time of taking it for maximum effect", "original": "rarely consider the best time to take it"}, {"note": "抽象医疗术语compliance（依从性）释义为具体的遵医嘱服药行为", "option": "ensure they take the drugs as instructed", "original": "ensure compliance"}, {"note": "被动需求表达（is needed）转为动名词建议项，determine = find out", "option": "Conducting more studies to find out the best timing for treating", "original": "More research is needed to determine the best times to administer treatments"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202512-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2025.12", "examSet": "2025.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2025.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "美国老年人延迟退休的多重动因", "subtitle": "健康改善、经济压力与职业社交需求推动更多美国人七旬仍在职", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 352, "paragraphs": ["Katharine Abraham, an economics professor, was chatting with her hairdresser about retirement plans. The economist said she plans to continue working because she wants to. The hairdresser agreed but for a different reason: She needs the money. Both scenarios are contributing to a big increase in the number of people in the U.S. working into their 70s. Over the past 20 years, the share of Americans working in their 70s has risen from less than 10% to nearly 15%.", "In addition to people being healthier and living much longer, economists say that a combination of financial considerations such as years of slow rise in real wages and a shift away from traditional pensions in the private sector are some of the reasons people delay retirement. The decline of manufacturing and the increase in the number of people working in less labor-intensive occupations also has contributed to the trend, says Abraham, who researches work and retirement decisions of older Americans. “Which matters more depends on what your history up until that point has been in the type of work you’re doing,” Abraham says.", "The overall trend is hitting Americans of all different levels of educational attainment, although the percentages vary by category. The share of Americans with bachelor’s degrees who were working into their 70s reached nearly 20% in 2018. For those with a", "high school degree or less, the proportion of those working in their 70s had risen to around 10%, while those with some college education were in the middle at around 15%.", "Martin Neil Baily, an economist who is leading a research project on retirement security, notes that quitting a career can lead to feelings of isolation and loneliness, particularly for men. He suggests that many college-educated workers are choosing to stay in the labor force more for social benefits than for financial reasons. They’re also more likely to be in professional occupations where they tend to enjoy their work more. Workers in more physical jobs, meanwhile, may be more likely to look forward to retiring, Baily says, suggesting those who stay on are more likely doing so for financial reasons."], "translations": ["经济学教授凯瑟琳·亚伯拉罕当时正和她的美发师闲聊退休计划。这位经济学家表示，她打算继续工作是因为自己想做。美发师也同意继续工作，但原因截然不同：她需要赚钱。这两种情况都在推动美国70岁以上仍在工作的人数大幅增加。在过去20年里，美国70多岁仍在工作的人群比例已从不到10%上升至近15%。", "经济学家指出，除了人们身体更健康、寿命显著延长外，实际工资多年来增长缓慢以及私营部门逐步取消传统养老金等经济因素的叠加，也是人们推迟退休的部分原因。研究美国老年人就业与退休决策的亚伯拉罕表示，制造业的衰退以及从事体力消耗较少职业的人数增加，也助推了这一趋势。“哪个因素影响更大，取决于你此前在所从事工作类型中的经历，”亚伯拉罕说。", "这一总体趋势正波及不同受教育程度的美国人，不过各类别的比例有所不同。2018年，拥有学士学位的美国人中，70多岁仍在工作的比例已接近20%。而对于仅拥有", "高中及以下学历的人而言，70多岁仍在工作的比例升至约10%，而受过一定大学教育的人群则居中，约为15%。", "正在领导一项退休保障研究项目的经济学家马丁·尼尔·贝利指出，退出职场会让人产生孤立感和孤独感，对男性尤其如此。他表示，许多受过大学教育的从业者选择继续留在劳动力市场，更多是出于社交需求而非经济原因。他们也更有可能从事专业性职业，在其中往往更享受自己的工作。与此同时，从事体力劳动较多的人则可能更期待退休，贝利说道，这表明那些选择留任的体力劳动者多半是出于经济考量。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about the economics professor and her hairdresser?", "options": ["They differ in their reasons for continuing to work.", "They are both committed to working into their 70s.", "They are happy about their current financial situation.", "They hold different views about postponing retirement."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The economist said she plans to continue working because she wants to. The hairdresser agreed but for a different reason: She needs the money.", "explanation": "第1段前两句对比了经济学教授与美发师的退休打算：前者继续工作是出于自身意愿（because she wants to），后者虽然也继续工作，却是因为截然不同的原因——需要赚钱（for a different reason: She needs the money）。可见两人继续工作的原因不同，A项与原文完全吻合。", "trapNote": "B项在原文中并未说明两人本人是否承诺工作到70多岁，70多岁是后文提及的全国整体趋势；C项“对当前财务状况满意”和D项“对推迟退休持不同看法”均曲解了两人因不同动机而选择继续工作的事实。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is one of the reasons for people to delay retirement?", "options": ["More and more people have switched to less intellectually challenging jobs.", "The number of jobs suitable for older people has increased in the private sector.", "The rate of wage increase in terms of purchasing power has slowed down for years.", "More and more people in the workplace find it hard to rely on traditional pensions."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "economists say that a combination of financial considerations such as years of slow rise in real wages and a shift away from traditional pensions in the private sector are some of the reasons people delay retirement.", "explanation": "根据题干reasons for people to delay retirement定位到第2段首句。文中指出，实际工资多年来增长缓慢（years of slow rise in real wages）是人们推迟退休的经济原因之一。所谓real wages即扣除通胀后按购买力衡量的工资，因此C项中wage increase in terms of purchasing power has slowed down for years为精准同义改写。", "trapNote": "A项把“体力消耗较少”偷换为“智力挑战较少”；B项“私营部门适合老年人的岗位增多”无中生有；D项虽提到传统养老金，但原文仅指“私营部门逐步取消传统养老金”，并非“职场中越来越多人觉得难以依赖”。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What is the general trend in people delaying retirement?", "options": ["The higher their earnings, the more likely they are tempted to delay retirement.", "Those who have more job satisfaction tend to retire later than those who have less.", "More men than women are likely to stay in the labor force until their late seventies.", "The higher their educational level, the more likely they are to delay retirement."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The overall trend is hitting Americans of all different levels of educational attainment, although the percentages vary by category. The share of Americans with bachelor’s degrees who were working into their 70s reached nearly 20% in 2018.", "explanation": "第3、4段按受教育程度对比了70多岁仍工作的人群比例：拥有学士学位者接近20%，受过部分大学教育者约为15%，高中及以下学历者约为10%。由此对比数据可以明显看出，受教育程度越高，人们在70多岁继续工作（即推迟退休）的比例就越高。D项准确概括了这一比例随学历升高而递增的总体趋势，故正确。", "trapNote": "A项将原文对比的“受教育程度”偷换为“收入水平”；B项与C项虽然在末段有所涉及（如专业人士更享受工作、男性易感孤独），但均属于第5段的局部现象，而非第3、4段数据所反映的总体趋势。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the chief reason for college-educated workers delaying retirement according to an economist?", "options": ["Enjoying financial security.", "Staying connected socially.", "Contributing more professionally.", "Increasing social security payments."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "He suggests that many college-educated workers are choosing to stay in the labor force more for social benefits than for financial reasons.", "explanation": "由题干关键词college-educated workers及an economist定位到第5段第2句。经济学家贝利指出，许多受过大学教育的劳动者选择留在职场，更多是出于社交益处而非经济原因（more for social benefits than for financial reasons）。B项Staying connected socially（保持社交联系）精准对应原文的social benefits，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项与D项均聚焦“经济保障/社保收入”，与文中“更多出于社交原因而非经济原因”的判断相反；C项“在专业上做出更多贡献”是对下句“享受专业工作”的过度推断，并非主要动因。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about people doing manual work?", "options": ["They are eager to enjoy life after retiring.", "They are likely to have financial troubles.", "They generally don't enjoy doing it.", "They tend to anticipate retirement."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Workers in more physical jobs, meanwhile, may be more likely to look forward to retiring, Baily says, suggesting those who stay on are more likely doing so for financial reasons.", "explanation": "由题干manual work（体力劳动）定位到第5段末句。贝利指出，从事体力较多工作的人往往更期待退休（Workers in more physical jobs, meanwhile, may be more likely to look forward to retiring）。D项中的anticipate retirement正是look forward to retiring（期待退休）的同义替换，tend to对应may be more likely to，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“渴望享受退休后的生活”过度引申了“期待退休”的含义；B项将“继续工作可能是为了经济原因”偷换为“普遍面临财务困境”；C项“通常不喜欢体力工作”在文中并无直接依据。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "情形；设想", "note": "文中指经济学家与美发师各自代表的两类推迟退休情形", "word": "scenario"}, {"gloss": "实际工资", "note": "经济学概念，指扣除通货膨胀因素后按购买力计算的工资", "word": "real wages"}, {"gloss": "达到；成就（尤指学历水平）", "note": "文中educational attainment固定搭配指“受教育程度”", "word": "attainment"}, {"gloss": "孤立；孤独", "note": "常与loneliness并列，动词形式为isolate", "word": "isolation"}, {"gloss": "期待；预料", "note": "与look forward to构成四级阅读高频同义替换", "word": "anticipate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In addition to people being healthier and living much longer, economists say that a combination of financial considerations such as years of slow rise in real wages and a shift away from traditional pensions in the private sector are some of the reasons people delay retirement.", "point": "识别较长主语中心词combination及such as列举的并列经济因素", "structure": "介词短语作状语(In addition to...) + 主句(economists say) + that引导宾语从句(主语a combination of... + 系动词are + 表语some of the reasons + 定语从句people delay retirement)", "zh": "经济学家表示，除了人们更健康、寿命更长之外，实际工资多年增长缓慢以及私营部门逐步取消传统养老金等经济因素的叠加，也是人们推迟退休的部分原因。"}, {"en": "The decline of manufacturing and the increase in the number of people working in less labor-intensive occupations also has contributed to the trend, says Abraham, who researches work and retirement decisions of older Americans.", "point": "把握新闻评论类文章常见的“引语前置+主谓倒装+定语从句补充身份”句式", "structure": "倒装直接引语作宾语 + 主句(says Abraham) + who引导的非限制性定语从句修饰Abraham", "zh": "研究美国老年人就业与退休决策的亚伯拉罕表示，制造业的衰退以及从事体力消耗较少职业的人数增加，也助推了这一趋势。"}, {"en": "Workers in more physical jobs, meanwhile, may be more likely to look forward to retiring, Baily says, suggesting those who stay on are more likely doing so for financial reasons.", "point": "理解现在分词suggesting引导的隐含宾语从句及其中的代词指代（doing so指staying on）", "structure": "主句(Workers... may be more likely to look forward to retiring) + 插入语(Baily says) + 现在分词短语作伴随/结果状语(suggesting...)", "zh": "与此同时，从事体力较多工作的人可能更期待退休，贝利说，这表明那些继续留任的人多半是出于经济原因。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "介词短语转为“动词+介词”结构表达两者的差异", "option": "differ in their reasons for continuing to work", "original": "for a different reason"}, {"note": "经济学核心概念real wages（实际工资）释义为按购买力衡量的工资", "option": "rate of wage increase in terms of purchasing power has slowed down", "original": "slow rise in real wages"}, {"note": "抽象名词短语social benefits具象化为保持社交联系的动名词短语", "option": "Staying connected socially", "original": "more for social benefits than for financial reasons"}, {"note": "同义词汇替换：physical jobs = manual work（体力劳动）", "option": "people doing manual work", "original": "Workers in more physical jobs"}, {"note": "高频替换：be more likely to = tend to；look forward to = anticipate", "option": "tend to anticipate retirement", "original": "may be more likely to look forward to retiring"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202506-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2025.06", "examSet": "2025.06 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2025.06 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "适度挑战或有益大熊猫种群保护", "subtitle": "新研究揭示栖息地适度“不完美”有助于大熊猫寻找配偶并维持遗传多样性", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 345, "paragraphs": ["New research suggests that pandas may be at risk of dying out because they are too comfortable. Experts say too much happiness can stop the bears from searching for new mates.", "Environmentalists have long believed that building roads or homes near the bears may threaten their survival by “reducing or fragmenting their natural habitats”, The Times reported. But the new research suggests that a “modest degree of discomfort and fragmentation” may actually help preserve panda populations.", "The research was conducted by scientists from Michigan State University. It concluded that pandas fail to wander off in search of new mates if they find their habitat too comfortable, resulting in a lack of vital genetic diversity. For their study—outlined in a paper in the journal Conservation Biology—the team looked at genetic diversity and spread among a Chinese panda population. The ideal", "level of perfectly livable habitat was found to be only 80% of an area, with the remainder either too harsh or too affected by human activity.", "The experts concluded that pandas should ideally “be happy enough to thrive, but not so content that they don’t want to move around and find new mates”. Their conclusions about what The Guardian described as this “sweet spot” are in line with the so-called Goldilocks principle: that there can be just the right amount of something. The concept has been applied to a wide range of disciplines, from developmental psychology to economics and engineering.", "Claudio Sillero, a professor of conservation biology at Oxford University, told the newspaper that the new findings could have implications beyond panda conservation.", "“Most large animals that eat meat live in increasingly fragmented landscapes,” said Sillero, who was not involved in the research. “It may well be that the messy nature of their relationship with human efforts induces more animals to scatter or travel further, and might result in greater genetic connectivity and enhanced population persistence.”", "The most recent count of pandas found that there were more than 1,800 left in the wild, putting them on the list of vulnerable, but not endangered, species."], "translations": ["最新研究表明，大熊猫可能因为生活得过于舒适而面临灭绝的风险。专家表示，过度的安逸幸福会阻止大熊猫外出寻找新的配偶。", "据《泰晤士报》报道，环保主义者长期以来一直认为，在大熊猫栖息地附近修路或建房可能会通过“缩减或割裂它们的自然栖息地”而威胁其生存。但这项新研究表明，“适度的不适与栖息地碎片化”实际上可能有助于保护大熊猫种群。", "这项研究由密歇根州立大学的科学家开展。研究得出的结论是，如果大熊猫觉得自己的栖息地过于舒适，就不会四处游荡寻找新配偶，从而导致至关重要的基因多样性匮乏。该研究发表在《保护生物学》期刊的一篇论文中，研究团队考察了一个中国大熊猫种群的基因多样性及分布情况。研究表明，完美宜居栖息地的理想", "比例仅为一个区域面积的80%，其余部分则要么环境过于恶劣，要么受人类活动影响过大。", "专家们总结道，理想状态下大熊猫应当“幸福到足以茁壮成长，但又不能安逸到不想四处走动去寻找新配偶”。《卫报》将这种状态称为“甜蜜点”，而专家对此得出的结论正与所谓的“金发姑娘原则”相吻合，即任何事物都可以存在一个恰到好处的量。这一概念已被应用于从发展心理学到经济学和工程学等众多学科。", "牛津大学保护生物学教授克劳迪奥·西莱罗在接受该报采访时表示，这些新发现的意义可能不仅限于大熊猫保护。", "“大多数大型食肉动物都生活在日益碎片化的环境中，”并未参与这项研究的西莱罗说，“很可能正是它们与人类活动之间错综复杂的互动关系，促使更多动物分散或迁徙到更远的地方，进而带来更强的基因连通性并提升种群的延续能力。”", "最新一次大熊猫数量统计显示，野生大熊猫超过1800只，这使得它们被列入易危物种而非濒危物种名录。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from new research about pandas?", "options": ["They are losing habitat due to the building of roads and houses.", "They have stopped seeking new mates for reproduction.", "They may not adapt to the fragmentation of their habitat.", "They may cease to exist as a result of enjoying too good a life."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "New research suggests that pandas may be at risk of dying out because they are too comfortable. Experts say too much happiness can stop the bears from searching for new mates.", "explanation": "定位第一段第一、二句。原文指出最新研究表明大熊猫可能因生活得过于安逸而面临灭绝风险，专家认为过度幸福会让大熊猫停止寻找新配偶。选项D中的cease to exist对应原文的dying out，enjoying too good a life对应too comfortable与too much happiness，语义高度契合，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项是第二段提到的环保主义者传统观点，并非新研究内容；B项“已停止寻找新配偶”偷换了原文can stop（可能会阻止）的可能性表述，过于绝对。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we conclude from the new research by scientists at Michigan State University?", "options": ["Environmentalists’ long-time belief regarding panda conservation may be misleading.", "Housing development near pandas’ homes may threaten their survival.", "Pandas’ natural habitats are becoming less suitable for reproduction.", "The increased panda population is attributed to the fragmentation of their habitat."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Environmentalists have long believed that building roads or homes near the bears may threaten their survival by “reducing or fragmenting their natural habitats”, The Times reported. But the new research suggests that a “modest degree of discomfort and fragmentation” may actually help preserve panda populations.", "explanation": "定位第二段。环保主义者长期认为在熊猫栖息地附近修路建房会破坏并割裂其自然栖息地、威胁其生存；但第二段随后用But转折指出，新研究表明“适度的不适与栖息地碎片化”反而有助于保护大熊猫种群。由此可推断，环保人士长期坚持的保护观念可能存在误导，对应选项A。", "trapNote": "B项是环保人士的原有看法，与新研究结论相反；D项因果倒置且无中生有，原文仅说适度碎片化“可能有助于保护”，并未提及熊猫数量已因此增加。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the experts’ conclusion regarding pandas?", "options": ["It is urgent to provide an ideal habitat for them to thrive.", "It is very important to preserve their genetic diversity.", "Their chances of finding new mates have a lot to do with their habitat.", "Their environment for survival has been continuously worsening."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The experts concluded that pandas should ideally “be happy enough to thrive, but not so content that they don’t want to move around and find new mates”.", "explanation": "定位第五段首句。专家总结指出，理想状态下大熊猫应当“幸福到足以茁壮成长，但又不能安逸到不想四处走动去寻找新配偶”，结合第三、四段可知只有80%完美宜居的栖息地才能促使其外出求偶。因此大熊猫找到新配偶的机会与栖息地状况密切相关，选项C精准概括了这一结论。", "trapNote": "A项只强调提供理想栖息地让熊猫繁衍，忽略了“不能太安逸”的核心前提；B项是第三段中的中间机制，而非第五段专家得出的最终结论。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we infer from the passage about the Goldilocks principle?", "options": ["It needs to be confirmed by more studies on pandas.", "It applies to the preservation of pandas too.", "It has implications for future panda research.", "It can be used to locate the right spot for pandas."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Their conclusions about what The Guardian described as this “sweet spot” are in line with the so-called Goldilocks principle: that there can be just the right amount of something. The concept has been applied to a wide range of disciplines, from developmental psychology to economics and engineering.", "explanation": "定位第五段第二、三句。文章指出专家关于大熊猫栖息地“甜蜜点”的结论与“金发姑娘原则”（即任何事物都有一个恰到好处的量）相吻合，而该原则已被广泛应用于发展心理学、经济学和工程学等领域。由此可推断，金发姑娘原则同样适用于大熊猫的保护工作，选项B符合题意。", "trapNote": "A、C两项中的“需更多研究证实”与“对未来熊猫研究有启示”均属无中生有；D项望文生义，将sweet spot曲解为“寻找合适地点”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What can the new findings do according to Professor Sillero?", "options": ["Help discover new ways for the conservation of pandas.", "Help remove pandas from the list of endangered species.", "Shed light on the conservation of most large meat-eating animals.", "Show the complexity of interactions between humans and animals."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "“Most large animals that eat meat live in increasingly fragmented landscapes,” said Sillero, who was not involved in the research. “It may well be that the messy nature of their relationship with human efforts induces more animals to scatter or travel further, and might result in greater genetic connectivity and enhanced population persistence.”", "explanation": "定位第六、七段。牛津大学教授Sillero在第六段指出该发现的影响不止于大熊猫保护，第七段进一步解释大多数大型食肉动物生活在日益碎片化的环境中，人类活动带来的复杂关系可能促使它们进一步扩散，增强基因连通性与种群延续。选项C中shed light on对应have implications beyond，most large meat-eating animals对应most large animals that eat meat，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项将教授的话限定在大熊猫保护，而原文明确说“beyond panda conservation”；B项与末段“易危而非濒危物种”的事实相悖。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 使碎片化，分裂；使零碎", "note": "常用于生态学中表示栖息地被道路或建筑“割裂”（fragment natural habitats），其名词形式为fragmentation。", "word": "fragment"}, {"gloss": "n. 遗传多样性，基因多样性", "note": "由genetic（基因的）+ diversity（多样性）构成，是生物保护类阅读中的高频核心词组。", "word": "genetic diversity"}, {"gloss": "v. 茁壮成长，繁茂，兴旺", "note": "在保护生物学语境下常指野生动物种群健康繁衍（thrive），区别于单纯的“存活（survive）”。", "word": "thrive"}, {"gloss": "v. 促使，诱发，引起", "note": "常见搭配 induce sb./sth. to do sth.，本文中指人类活动带来的混杂环境促使动物向更远处扩散。", "word": "induce"}, {"gloss": "n. 持续存在，延续性", "note": "动词 persist 的名词形式，本文中 population persistence 指动物种群的长期存续能力。", "word": "persistence"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "It concluded that pandas fail to wander off in search of new mates if they find their habitat too comfortable, resulting in a lack of vital genetic diversity.", "point": "现在分词短语作结果状语（resulting in...）以及条件状语从句（if...）的嵌套使用。", "structure": "主干：It concluded that... | 宾语从句内含条件状语从句：pandas fail to wander off... if they find their habitat too comfortable | 结果状语：resulting in a lack of vital genetic diversity", "zh": "该研究得出结论：如果大熊猫觉得栖息地过于舒适，它们就不会外出寻找新的配偶，从而导致至关重要的基因多样性缺失。"}, {"en": "“It may well be that the messy nature of their relationship with human efforts induces more animals to scatter or travel further, and might result in greater genetic connectivity and enhanced population persistence.”", "point": "It may well be that... 引导的主语从句表“很可能是……”，以及并列谓语 induces... and might result in... 的长距离搭配。", "structure": "形式主语+表语：It may well be | 真正主语从句：that the messy nature... induces more animals to scatter or travel further, and might result in...", "zh": "“很可能正是它们与人类活动之间那种错综复杂的互动关系，促使更多动物分散或迁徙到更远的地方，进而带来更强的基因连通性并提升种群的延续能力。”"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "原文“濒临灭绝的风险”同义替换为“可能停止存在”；“过于安逸/过度幸福”对应“享受过好的生活”。", "option": "cease to exist as a result of enjoying too good a life", "original": "at risk of dying out because they are too comfortable / too much happiness"}, {"note": "“环保主义者长期以来的信念”对应“环保人士关于熊猫保护的长期观念”；通过前后文But转折推知其“可能具有误导性”。", "option": "Environmentalists’ long-time belief regarding panda conservation may be misleading.", "original": "Environmentalists have long believed... But the new research suggests..."}, {"note": "由“大熊猫安逸到不想外出找新配偶”和“80%理想宜居比例”概括出“寻找新配偶的机会与栖息地密切相关”。", "option": "Their chances of finding new mates have a lot to do with their habitat.", "original": "not so content that they don’t want to move around and find new mates"}, {"note": "“对……之外产生影响”同义替换为“为……提供启示”；“大型食肉动物”换为更口语化的“meat-eating animals”。", "option": "Shed light on the conservation of most large meat-eating animals.", "original": "have implications beyond panda conservation / Most large animals that eat meat"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202506-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2025.06", "examSet": "2025.06 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2025.06 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "成功新密钥：坚毅比天赋更重要", "subtitle": "安吉拉·达克沃斯《坚毅》解析：热情与坚持如何超越天赋成为成功的关键", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 360, "paragraphs": ["With those born with natural talents, it feels as if they excel without really trying. But what about those of us who don’t have a natural talent? We’ve been told all our lives that if you work hard, you too can succeed. But with the release of Angela Duckworth’s Grit, we are given a new key to success.", "“As much as talent counts, effort counts twice,” says Duckworth in Grit. She introduces a new concept that talent may be overrated, and if you want real success, what you need is grit, the perfect combination of passion and persistence. Even if you have natural talent, it’s nothing without grit.", "Duckworth says grit is the difference between success and failure. A person who has grit is more likely to succeed than a person who does not. When we think about attaining success — whether it’s landing that job or learning that new skill—our thoughts are immediately burdened by all the things we must first learn. If you want that new job, you have to learn the job skills, then the interview skills, then the dress part — and you must be perfect at all of them. Grit is different because it tells us that perfection isn’t the goal.", "Grit lifts the unreasonable expectations off our shoulders. Grit tells us that the door is open wider than we first thought possible. Grit allows us to redefine our goals. Think about it: what’s something you’ve always wanted to do, but gave up because you “don’t have the skills for it”? What’s something you love but aren’t good at?", "The real workings of grit are to have sustainable passion and continue to try. Effort means more than your natural ability. Even if you haven’t mastered a skill, grit tells you that you can still succeed if you can transform your passion into action. In a way, Duckworth is giving new hope to people who have shut the doors on their dreams. She is saying it is possible that you can accomplish anything. If at first you fail, then try one more time with grit."], "translations": ["对于天生自带天赋的人来说，他们似乎不用怎么努力就能表现卓越。但我们这些没有天赋的人又该怎么办呢？从小到大我们一直被告知，只要努力工作，你也能成功。但随着安吉拉·达克沃斯《坚毅》一书的出版，我们获得了一把通往成功的新钥匙。", "“天赋固然重要，但努力的作用是天赋的两倍，”达克沃斯在《坚毅》中写道。她提出了一个新理念：天赋可能被高估了，如果你想要获得真正的成功，你所需要的是坚毅——热情与坚持的完美结合。即使你拥有天赋，没有坚毅也是一无是处。", "达克沃斯表示，坚毅是区分成功与失败的分水岭。拥有坚毅品格的人比没有的人更有可能成功。每当我们思考如何取得成功时——无论是拿下那份工作还是学会那项新技能——我们的思绪都会立刻被那些必须先去学习的种种事项压得喘不过气来。如果你想得到那份新工作，你必须学习专业技能，然后学习面试技巧，还要学习着装礼仪——而且每一样你都必须做到完美。但坚毅则不同，因为它告诉我们，完美并不是目标。", "坚毅卸下了压在我们肩头的不切实际的期待。坚毅告诉我们，机会之门比我们最初想象的敞开得更宽广。坚毅让我们能够重新定义自己的目标。试想一下：有什么事是你一直想做，却因为“不具备相应技能”而放弃的？又有什么事是你热爱却并不擅长的？", "坚毅真正发挥作用的方式，就是拥有持久的热情并不断尝试。努力比你的天生能力更重要。即使你尚未掌握某项技能，坚毅也会告诉你，只要能将热情转化为行动，你依然可以取得成功。在某种意义上，达克沃斯正为那些已经关上梦想大门的人带来新的希望。她想告诉我们，你是有可能成就任何事情的。如果一开始失败了，那就带着坚毅再试一次。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about people born with natural talents?", "options": ["They seem to outdo others without hard work.", "They appear to know all the secrets to success.", "They feel it only too logical to succeed.", "They are bound to excel effortlessly."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "With those born with natural talents, it feels as if they excel without really trying.", "explanation": "定位第一段首句。原文指出，对于天生具备才华的人来说，他们看起来似乎不用怎么努力就能表现卓越。选项A中的seem to对应原文feels as if，outdo others对应excel，without hard work对应without really trying，精准同义替换，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "D项用“注定会（are bound to）”将原文“似乎（feels as if）”绝对化，且与后文“没有坚毅天赋一文不值”相矛盾；B、C两项原文未提及。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does Duckworth say about talent?", "options": ["It is a new concept much too overrated.", "It proves necessary for big achievements.", "It plays a lesser role in one’s success.", "It is a guarantee for real success in life."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "“As much as talent counts, effort counts twice,” says Duckworth in Grit. She introduces a new concept that talent may be overrated, and if you want real success, what you need is grit, the perfect combination of passion and persistence. Even if you have natural talent, it’s nothing without grit.", "explanation": "定位第二段。达克沃斯在《坚毅》中指出“天赋固然重要，但努力的作用是其两倍”，并提出“天赋可能被高估”，即便拥有天赋，若缺乏坚毅也毫无用处。这说明在达克沃斯看来，天赋在个人成功中所起的作用相对较小，选项C中的plays a lesser role精准转述了这一观点。", "trapNote": "A项偷换主语，原文说“新概念”是指天赋被高估及需要坚毅，而非天赋本身；B、D两项夸大了天赋的作用，与“没有坚毅天赋就毫无用处”背道而驰。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about people thinking of attaining success?", "options": ["They are puzzled how to present their best to the employer.", "They are burdened by their expectation of perfection.", "They will try hard to land a job that fits their skills best.", "They will find themselves lacking in all the skills they need."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "When we think about attaining success — whether it’s landing that job or learning that new skill—our thoughts are immediately burdened by all the things we must first learn. If you want that new job, you have to learn the job skills, then the interview skills, then the dress part — and you must be perfect at all of them.", "explanation": "定位第三段第三、四句。原文指出当我们思考取得成功时，无论是求职还是学习新技能，思绪都会立刻被“必须先学会的种种事项”压垮，而且必须把每项技能都做到完美。因此人们在追求成功时往往因追求完美的期待而感到重负，选项B中的burdened与expectation of perfection与原文直接对应。", "trapNote": "A、C两项仅片面截取“找工作”这一举例，偏离了“追求完美带来重负”的核心；D项“缺乏所有所需技能”曲解了原文“必须先学会很多东西”的表述。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How does the author think grit can be helpful to us?", "options": ["It allows us to know what we are good at.", "It opens our eyes to new opportunities.", "It focuses our attention on what we do.", "It lets us reconsider the goals to achieve."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Grit allows us to redefine our goals.", "explanation": "定位第四段第三句。作者指出坚毅能够卸下肩头不切实际的期待，并明确提到Grit allows us to redefine our goals（坚毅让我们能够重新定义目标）。选项D中的lets us reconsider the goals to achieve正是对原文allows us to redefine our goals的精准同义改写，故选D。", "trapNote": "B项将“门比我们想象中开得更大”过度引申为“开阔眼界发现新机会”；A项“了解自己擅长什么”与后文“喜欢但不擅长的事”语义相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "What message does Duckworth try to convey in her book Grit?", "options": ["We should perfect ourselves to ensure success.", "We should stay persistent even in face of failures.", "We can never master a skill without constant practice.", "We can never expect to reach our goals without passion."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The real workings of grit are to have sustainable passion and continue to try. Effort means more than your natural ability. Even if you haven’t mastered a skill, grit tells you that you can still succeed if you can transform your passion into action. In a way, Duckworth is giving new hope to people who have shut the doors on their dreams. She is saying it is possible that you can accomplish anything. If at first you fail, then try one more time with grit.", "explanation": "定位第五段，尤其尾句。全段强调坚毅的本质在于保持持久热情并不断尝试，努力比天赋更重要；最后达克沃斯鼓励人们“如果一开始失败了，那就带着坚毅再试一次”。整本书传达的核心理念正是在面对失败时仍要保持坚持，对应选项B的stay persistent even in face of failures。", "trapNote": "A项“完善自我以确保成功”与第三段“完美并非目标”直接相悖；D项“没有热情绝不可能达成目标”过于绝对，忽略了全书“失败后继续坚持”的主旨。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 擅长，表现突出，胜过他人", "note": "不及物或及物动词，文中 excel without really trying 指“不用真正努力就能出类拔萃”。", "word": "excel"}, {"gloss": "n. 坚毅，毅力（热情与坚持的结合）", "note": "本文核心主题词，在心理学和教育学中专指对长期目标的持久热情与坚忍不拔的毅力。", "word": "grit"}, {"gloss": "v. 高估，对……评价过高", "note": "由前缀 over-（过度）+ rate（评价）构成，文中 talent may be overrated 意为“天赋的作用可能被高估了”。", "word": "overrate"}, {"gloss": "v. 使背负重担，使烦扰", "note": "被动语态 be burdened by sth. 表示“被……所压垮/困扰”，文中形象描述完美主义期待带来的心理压力。", "word": "burden"}, {"gloss": "adj. 可持续的，持久的", "note": "由 sustain（维持）+ -able 构成，文中 sustainable passion 指能够长期保持而非三分钟热度的热情。", "word": "sustainable"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "She introduces a new concept that talent may be overrated, and if you want real success, what you need is grit, the perfect combination of passion and persistence.", "point": "that引导同位语从句解释concept，以及what引导的主语从句和名词短语作同位语。", "structure": "主句1：She introduces a new concept + 同位语从句：that talent may be overrated | 并列分句：and + 条件状语从句(if...) + 主语从句(what you need) + 系表结构(is grit) + 同位语(the perfect combination...)", "zh": "她提出了一个新理念：天赋可能被高估了；如果你想要获得真正的成功，你所需要的是坚毅，即热情与坚持的完美结合。"}, {"en": "When we think about attaining success — whether it’s landing that job or learning that new skill—our thoughts are immediately burdened by all the things we must first learn.", "point": "whether...or... 引导让步状语插入语，以及省略关系代词 that 的定语从句（we must first learn 修饰 all the things）。", "structure": "时间状语从句：When we think about attaining success | 插入语：whether it’s landing... or learning... | 主句：our thoughts are immediately burdened by all the things (that) we must first learn", "zh": "每当我们思考如何取得成功时——无论是拿下那份工作还是学会那项新技能——我们的思绪都会立刻被那些必须先去学习的种种事项压得喘不过气来。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“感觉似乎无需真正努力就能出众”同义替换为“看起来无需苦干就能胜过他人”。", "option": "seem to outdo others without hard work", "original": "feels as if they excel without really trying"}, {"note": "“努力的作用是天赋的两倍/天赋可能被高估”概括为“在成功中扮演较次要的角色”。", "option": "plays a lesser role in one’s success", "original": "effort counts twice / talent may be overrated"}, {"note": "“思绪被必须先学的东西和追求完美压垮”提炼为“被追求完美的期待所累”。", "option": "burdened by their expectation of perfection", "original": "burdened by all the things we must first learn... and you must be perfect at all of them"}, {"note": "“允许我们重新定义目标”精确同义改写为“让我们重新审视要达成的目标”。", "option": "lets us reconsider the goals to achieve", "original": "allows us to redefine our goals"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202412-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2024.12", "examSet": "2024.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2024.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "借助城市种植重塑人与自然的联系", "subtitle": "2024.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage One · 人与自然及城市社区种植", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 349, "paragraphs": ["The weakening of the human connection to nature might be good for economic growth but is bad for people. A tipping point was reached in 2020 when human-made materials—such as steel, concrete and plastic—were found to weigh more than all life on Earth. Continuing to grow concrete forests rather than real ones is shortsighted. Simply being in the nearest wood has such health benefits that the Woodland Trust successfully lobbied for it to be prescribed by doctors.", "Yet slipping from popular culture is the wonder and beauty of the natural world. For every three nature-related words in hit songs of the 1950s, researchers found, there was only slightly more than one 50 years later. It is not a moment too soon that teenagers will be able to take a natural history test, given that for decades children have been able to name more video game characters than wildlife species.", "Part of remedying this social disease would be for parliament to pass a \"right to grow\" law, allowing anyone to turn underused public spaces into vegetable and fruit gardens. The idea is for people to get back in touch with the soil—while producing food sustainably.", "Vegetable planting has a respectable tradition. In April 1649, locals responded to high prices and food shortages by cultivating vegetables on common land in Southern England. The practice of throwing seed bombs to turn vacant plots of land green took off in 1970s New York, and has been revived(使复活) by green-thumbed(有园艺才能的) social media influencers who defy local US regulations in a war on ugly spots in cities.", "Apart from the urgent task of providing more healthy nutrients to those who increasingly can't afford them, publicly accessible fruit and vegetable gardens connect what we eat to where it comes from —the means of production, if you will. They can make unlovely spaces lovely, and marry use and beauty as well as help promote a sense of community. Plants are also, of course, our first defence against species loss and climate change. Such planting is a small step for humanity—in the right direction."], "translations": ["人类与自然联系的削弱可能有利于经济增长，但对人类自身却是有害的。2020年达到了一个临界点，当时人们发现人造材料——如钢铁、混凝土和塑料——的重量超过了地球上所有生命的总重量。继续建造混凝土森林而非真正的森林是目光短浅的。仅仅身处最近的树林中就具有如此多的健康益处，以至于林地信托基金（Woodland Trust）成功游说医生将其作为处方开具。", "然而，自然世界的奇妙与美丽正在从流行文化中悄然消逝。研究人员发现，20世纪50年代热门歌曲中每出现三个与自然相关的词汇，50年后就只剩下略多于一个了。青少年将能够参加自然历史测试，这一时刻来得正是时候，因为几十年来孩子们能说出的电子游戏角色名字比野生动物物种还要多。", "纠正这种社会病症的部分举措是议会通过一项“种植权”法律，允许任何人将未充分利用的公共空间改造成蔬菜和水果园。其理念是让人们重新接触土壤——同时可持续地生产食物。", "蔬菜种植有着值得尊重的传统。1649年4月，当地人通过在英格兰南部的公共土地上种植蔬菜来应对高物价和食物短缺。在20世纪70年代的纽约，投掷种子弹将空置地块变绿的做法开始流行，如今又被有园艺才能的社交媒体网红所复兴，他们无视美国地方法规，向城市中的丑陋地带宣战。", "除了为那些越来越负担不起的人提供更多健康营养的紧迫任务外，向公众开放的水果和蔬菜园还将我们所吃的食物与其来源——如果你愿意的话，即生产方式——联系起来。它们可以使不美观的空间变得美观，将实用性与美感结合起来，并有助于增进社区意识。当然，植物也是我们抵御物种丧失和气候变化的第一道防线。这种种植对人类来说是朝着正确方向迈出的一小步。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "What does the author want to emphasise in the first paragraph?", "options": ["The year 2020 was a big turning point in human history.", "Economic growth benefits people little in the long run.", "It is unwise to weaken the human connection to nature.", "It is harmful to mankind to use human-made materials."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Continuing to grow concrete forests rather than real ones is shortsighted.", "explanation": "定位第一段第一句及第三句。首句指出人类与自然联系的削弱虽或许有利于经济增长，却对人类自身有害；第三句进一步强调“继续建造混凝土森林而非真正的森林是目光短浅的”。选项C中的“unwise”精准对应原文的“shortsighted”，完整概括了作者在首段批评疏远自然、盲目扩张人造建筑的核心观点，故C正确。", "trapNote": "A项以偏概全，2020年仅是人造材料重量超过生物总量的临界点，并非全段强调主旨；B、D项曲解文意，原文并未否定经济增长的长期作用或称使用人造材料本身有害。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did researchers find about popular culture?", "options": ["It is increasingly detached from the natural world.", "It is filled with all kinds of video game characters.", "It is especially appealing to the taste of teenagers.", "It is still impacted by the hit songs of the 1950s."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Yet slipping from popular culture is the wonder and beauty of the natural world.", "explanation": "定位第二段第一、二句。首句直接点明“自然世界的奇妙与美丽正在从流行文化中悄然消逝”；随后用研究数据佐证：上世纪50年代热门歌曲中每出现三个与自然相关的词，50年后便减少到仅略多于一个。选项A“它正日益脱离自然界”与“slipping from popular culture”构成同义转述，准确反映研究发现，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项偷换主语，原文是说儿童能说出更多游戏角色而非流行文化充斥游戏角色；D项曲解数据，50年代热门歌曲只是研究者用来对比自然词汇减少的参照对象。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author propose people do?", "options": ["Take measures to ensure sustainable food development.", "Reconnect with nature through the right to grow.", "Stand by the parliament in fighting social diseases.", "Cover public spaces with fruit trees and vegetable plants."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Part of remedying this social disease would be for parliament to pass a \"right to grow\" law, allowing anyone to turn underused public spaces into vegetable and fruit gardens. The idea is for people to get back in touch with the soil—while producing food sustainably.", "explanation": "定位第三段第一、二句。作者提出解决这一社会病症的部分举措，是由议会通过“种植权”法律，允许任何人将未充分利用的公共空间改造成蔬果园，其理念正是让人们重新接触土地并可持续地生产食物。选项B将“right to grow”与“get back in touch with the soil”结合为“通过种植权重新与自然建立联系”，精准对应作者建议，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项以偏概全，可持续生产食物只是该倡议的附带益处之一；D项过度绝对，原文仅指改造“未充分利用的公共空间（underused public spaces）”，而非全部公共空间。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about vegetable planting?", "options": ["It all started in 1649 in Southern England.", "It is protected by US government regulations.", "It has long been used to increase food supply and improve urban landscape.", "It has been popularised worldwide with the increasing influence of social media."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "In April 1649, locals responded to high prices and food shortages by cultivating vegetables on common land in Southern England. The practice of throwing seed bombs to turn vacant plots of land green took off in 1970s New York, and has been revived(使复活) by green-thumbed(有园艺才能的) social media influencers who defy local US regulations in a war on ugly spots in cities.", "explanation": "定位第四段。该段指出蔬菜种植历史悠久：1649年英格兰南部居民通过在公共土地种菜来应对高物价和粮食短缺，体现其增加食物供给的作用；20世纪70年代纽约兴起投掷种子弹绿化空地的做法，如今又被园艺博主复兴以改造城市丑陋地带，体现其改善城市景观的作用。选项C准确概括了这两方面长期功能，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项过度推断，1649年只是文中列举的早期例证，不能说明一切起源于此；B项与原文相反，文中明确提到网红“无视美国地方法规（defy local US regulations）”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What can publicly accessible fruit and vegetable gardens do apart from their practical functions?", "options": ["Raise people's environmental awareness.", "Add to the great variety of plant species.", "Act as the first defence against natural disasters.", "Enhance people's community spirit."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "They can make unlovely spaces lovely, and marry use and beauty as well as help promote a sense of community.", "explanation": "定位第五段第一、二句。题干询问公共蔬果园除实用功能外还能发挥什么作用。第二句明确提到，它们不仅能美化丑陋空间、将实用与美感结合，还能“help promote a sense of community”（有助于增进社区意识）。选项D中的“Enhance people's community spirit”正是对“promote a sense of community”的同义替换，故D正确。", "trapNote": "B项无中生有，原文仅提及植物抵御物种丧失，未说增加植物物种多样性；C项偷换概念，原文指植物是抵御“物种丧失和气候变化”的第一道防线，而非泛指“自然灾害”。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "临界点，转折点", "note": "常用搭配 reach a tipping point 表示“达到转折点/临界点”。", "word": "tipping point"}, {"gloss": "目光短浅的，近视的", "note": "在论证类文章中常用于批评只看眼前利益的做法，近义词为 nearsighted。", "word": "shortsighted"}, {"gloss": "游说，向……施加影响", "note": "常见结构 lobby for sth. / lobby sb. to do sth.，指为促成某项政策或决定而进行游说。", "word": "lobby"}, {"gloss": "补救，纠正", "note": "作动词表示“纠正、补救（不良局面或社会问题）”，名词形式同为 remedy（补救办法）。", "word": "remedy"}, {"gloss": "公然违抗，不服从", "note": "文中 defy local US regulations 意为“无视/违抗美国地方法规”。", "word": "defy"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Simply being in the nearest wood has such health benefits that the Woodland Trust successfully lobbied for it to be prescribed by doctors.", "point": "动名词短语作主语及 such...that... 结果状语从句中含“游说促成被动动作”的用法。", "structure": "主语为动名词短语 Simply being in the nearest wood；谓语及宾语构成 such...that... 结果状语从句，其中 it 指代“置身林间”，to be prescribed 为不定式被动式作介词 for 后的复合宾语。", "zh": "仅仅置身于最近的树林中就具有如此多的健康益处，以至于林地信托基金成功游说医生将其作为处方开具给患者。"}, {"en": "It is not a moment too soon that teenagers will be able to take a natural history test, given that for decades children have been able to name more video game characters than wildlife species.", "point": "it 作形式主语替代 that 主语从句，搭配固定习语及 given that 原因状语从句。", "structure": "It 为形式主语，真正主语是 that teenagers will be able to take a natural history test；not a moment too soon 为习惯表达，意为“来得正是时候”；given that 引导条件/原因状语从句。", "zh": "青少年将能够参加自然历史测试，这来得正是时候，因为几十年来孩子们能说出的电子游戏角色名字比野生动物物种还要多。"}, {"en": "Apart from the urgent task of providing more healthy nutrients to those who increasingly can't afford them, publicly accessible fruit and vegetable gardens connect what we eat to where it comes from—the means of production, if you will.", "point": "介词短语作伴随状语，内置定语从句与双宾语从句，以及插入语。", "structure": "Apart from... 介词短语作状语，其中包含 who 引导的定语从句；主句动词 connect 连接两个宾语从句 what we eat 和 where it comes from；破折号后补充解释“生产方式”，if you will 为插入语。", "zh": "除了向越来越负担不起的人提供更多健康营养这一紧迫任务外，向公众开放的果蔬园还将我们所吃的食物与其来源——如果你愿意的话，也可称之为生产方式——联系了起来。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将具体的“盲目建造水泥森林”归纳为宏观行为上的“不明智”。", "option": "unwise", "original": "shortsighted"}, {"note": "流行文化中自然之美悄然流失，同义改写为“日益脱离自然界”。", "option": "increasingly detached from the natural world", "original": "slipping from popular culture is the wonder and beauty of the natural world"}, {"note": "“重新接触土壤”在题干选项中抽象概括为“重新与自然建立联系”。", "option": "reconnect with nature", "original": "get back in touch with the soil"}, {"note": "“增进社区意识”与“提升人们的社区精神”构成核心动作和宾语的精准替换。", "option": "enhance people's community spirit", "original": "promote a sense of community"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202412-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2024.12", "examSet": "2024.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2024.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "美国女性工程师的职业困境与变迁", "subtitle": "2024.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two · 女性在工程领域的挑战与进步", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 345, "paragraphs": ["Engineering in the U.S. has long been a male-dominated profession. Fifty years ago, it looked like that might change.", "In 1970, the percentage of women majoring in engineering was less than 1%. In 1979, that number was 9%. Many hoped women would continue to enter the field at the same rate. But that's not what happened. Today, only 21% of engineering majors are women, a number largely unchanged since 2000.", "I am a historian who, along with my colleagues, surveyed 251 women engineers who graduated from college in the 1970s. These pioneers reflected on the challenges they faced—and had advice for women entering the field today.", "One survey taker explained, \"The greatest challenge for me was continuing to believe in myself, when all the messages I was getting were that I would never be taken seriously or promoted or given raises at the same rate as men, who were clearly less qualified and not as smart as I was.\"", "A chemical engineer who worked in manufacturing agreed, \"You have to prove yourself just because you are female. And you have to work twice as hard!\"", "A civil engineer said, \"We are 'women engineers.' People don't refer to a man as a 'man engineer'—he's an engineer. We are constantly reminded that we don't truly belong.\" Another civil engineer stated, \"On many levels, you're never quite one of the groups.\"", "Women also talked about family caregiving responsibilities. A retired vice president from a major chemical company stated, \"Young women engineers are on an equal footing until they have children, then they struggle to balance work and family—and compete with men who don't have the same household responsibilities.\"", "But over the years things have changed a lot. Young women engineers are more accepted mostly because there are just more of them.", "Many women engineers hailed the benefits of their chosen career. A program manager in manufacturing stated that engineering is the best degree. A mechanical engineer said, \"It will give you the flexibility to do almost anything. It is also satisfying to see the effects of what you have done.\""], "translations": ["长期以来，美国的工程学一直是一个男性主导的职业。五十年前，这种情况看起来似乎可能会改变。", "1970年，主修工程学的女性比例不到1%。1979年，这一数字升至9%。许多人希望女性能够以同样的速度继续进入该领域。但事实并非如此。如今，只有21%的工程学专业学生是女性，这一数字自2000年以来基本保持不变。", "我是一名历史学家，与同事们一起对251名在20世纪70年代大学毕业的女性工程师进行了调查。这些先驱者反思了她们所面临的挑战——并为今天进入该领域的女性提供了建议。", "一位受访者解释说：“对我来说最大的挑战是继续相信自己，而我收到的所有信息都是，我永远不会被认真对待，也不会像男性那样以同等速度获得晋升或加薪，而那些男性明显不如我有资历，也没有我聪明。”", "一位从事制造业的化学工程师也表示赞同：“仅仅因为你是女性，你就必须证明自己。而且你必须付出双倍的努力！”", "一位土木工程师说：“我们是‘女工程师’。人们不会把男性称为‘男工程师’——他就是工程师。我们不断被提醒，我们并不真正属于这里。”另一位土木工程师表示：“在许多层面上，你永远不完全是群体中的一员。”", "女性还谈到了家庭照料责任。一家大型化工公司的退休副总裁表示：“年轻的女性工程师在生孩子之前处于平等地位，之后她们就要努力平衡工作和家庭——并与没有相同家庭责任的男性竞争。”", "但多年来情况已经发生了很大变化。年轻的女性工程师更容易被接受，主要是因为她们的人数更多了。", "许多女性工程师赞扬了她们所选择职业的益处。一位制造业项目经理表示，工程学是最好的学位。一位机械工程师说：“它会给你几乎可以做任何事情的灵活性。看到你所做工作的成效也很令人满意。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about the engineering profession in the United States?", "options": ["It has seen a change in attitude towards women engineers since 1979.", "It witnessed a significant increase in women engineers in the 1970s.", "It has experienced the gradual weakening of male dominance.", "It boasted the largest number of engineering majors in 2000."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "In 1970, the percentage of women majoring in engineering was less than 1%. In 1979, that number was 9%.", "explanation": "定位第二段第一、二句。原文给出了具体的历史数据：1970年主修工程学的女性比例不到1%，到1979年这一数字升至9%，可见20世纪70年代工程领域中女性的比例经历了显著增长。选项B“20世纪70年代该行业见证了女性工程师的显著增加”与原文数据完全吻合，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项时间错位，自1979年后增长趋势放缓，态度转变是在多年之后；D项曲解数据，原文是说女性占比21%自2000年以来基本没变，并非工程专业总人数在2000年达到顶峰。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does one survey taker say was her greatest challenge?", "options": ["Not to feel superior to less qualified male engineers.", "Not to take seriously all the messages she was getting.", "Not to think highly of her qualifications when promoted or given a pay raise.", "Not to lose self-confidence though constantly discouraged or unfairly treated."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The greatest challenge for me was continuing to believe in myself, when all the messages I was getting were that I would never be taken seriously or promoted or given raises at the same rate as men, who were clearly less qualified and not as smart as I was.", "explanation": "定位第四段。该受访者明确表示，最大的挑战是“继续相信自己（continuing to believe in myself）”，尽管周围传递的所有信息都暗示她不会受到认真对待，也无法像资历和才智明显不如她的男性那样获得同等速度的晋升或加薪。选项D“尽管不断受到打击或不公平对待，仍不丧失自信”准确转述了“continuing to believe in myself”与后文的让步逻辑，故选D。", "trapNote": "A、C项曲解文意，原文提及男性资历较差是为了反衬晋升加薪机制的不公，而非自感优越或自视过高；B项断章取义，错将“never be taken seriously”拼凑为“不把外界信息当真”。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How do women engineers frequently feel according to the two civil engineers?", "options": ["Disqualified on many levels.", "Excluded from the group.", "Overworked by their organizations.", "Looked down upon by male colleagues."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "We are constantly reminded that we don't truly belong.\" Another civil engineer stated, \"On many levels, you're never quite one of the groups.", "explanation": "定位第六段。第一位土木工程师指出，人们称她们为“女工程师”却不叫男性“男工程师”，这让她们不断被提醒“自己并不真正属于这里（don't truly belong）”；另一位土木工程师补充说，在许多层面上“你永远不完全是群体中的一员（never quite one of the groups）”。选项B“被排除在群体之外”精准概括了两人的共同感受，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项“在许多层面上不合格”系对“on many levels”与前文“less qualified”的拼凑误读；C、D项在第六段均未提及，属于过度推断。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What probably makes young women engineers more accepted nowadays?", "options": ["Their success in gaining an equal footing.", "Their ability to balance work and family.", "The change in their responsibilities.", "The increase in their number."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "Young women engineers are more accepted mostly because there are just more of them.", "explanation": "定位第八段第二句。该句直接回答了年轻女性工程师如今更易被接纳的原因：“mostly because there are just more of them”（主要是因为她们的数量变多了）。选项D“她们数量的增加”与“there are just more of them”构成直接同义转述，属于典型的因果定位细节题，故选D。", "trapNote": "A、B、C三项均借用第七段“equal footing”“balance work and family”“household responsibilities”等词设置干扰，但第七段讨论的是育儿带来的职场不平等困境，并非如今更受接纳的原因。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we conclude about many female engineers from the statement of a mechanical engineer?", "options": ["They take great pride in their chosen career.", "They have reaped the benefits of being flexible.", "They enjoy doing engineering to the best degree.", "They have proved capable of doing almost anything."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "It will give you the flexibility to do almost anything. It is also satisfying to see the effects of what you have done.", "explanation": "定位第九段。该段首句总述许多女性工程师赞扬了她们所选职业的益处（hailed the benefits of their chosen career），随后机械工程师具体表示工程学位带来“几乎可以做任何事情的灵活性”，且“看到自己所做工作的成效也很令人满意（satisfying）”。由此可推断她们对自己选择的职业深感自豪，选项A准确归纳了这一态度，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项偏离重点，未体现她们对职业成就感的情感态度；C项将前句“engineering is the best degree（最好的学位）”中的“degree”偷换为“程度”；D项将“有灵活度去做任何事”偷换为“已证明自己能做任何事”。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "男性主导的", "note": "复合形容词，常用于职场性别比例议题，反义表达为 female-dominated。", "word": "male-dominated"}, {"gloss": "先驱，开拓者", "note": "名词，指某一领域或时代的早期探索者；也可作动词，表示“开创、倡导”。", "word": "pioneer"}, {"gloss": "具备资格的，胜任的", "note": "形容词，文中 less qualified 意为“资历较浅、不够格的”，名词为 qualification。", "word": "qualified"}, {"gloss": "平等的地位，立足点", "note": "固定搭配 on an equal footing 表示“处于平等地位”，常用于竞争或职场语境。", "word": "footing"}, {"gloss": "高度赞扬，欢呼迎接", "note": "及物动词，文中 hailed the benefits 意为“盛赞……的好处”。", "word": "hail"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The greatest challenge for me was continuing to believe in myself, when all the messages I was getting were that I would never be taken seriously or promoted or given raises at the same rate as men, who were clearly less qualified and not as smart as I was.", "point": "when 引导对比性时间/伴随状语从句，嵌套定语从句与表语从句。", "structure": "主句为动名词短语作表语的系表结构；when 引导从句中，I was getting 为省略关系代词的定语从句修饰 messages，that 引导表语从句，句末 who 引导非限制性定语从句修饰 men。", "zh": "对我来说最大的挑战是继续相信自己，因为我收到的所有信息都在表明，我永远不会被认真对待，也永远不会像男性那样以同等速度获得晋升或加薪，而那些男性明显不如我有资历，也没有我聪明。"}, {"en": "Young women engineers are on an equal footing until they have children, then they struggle to balance work and family—and compete with men who don't have the same household responsibilities.", "point": "until 时间状语从句引出转折节点，搭配并列不定式与定语从句。", "structure": "前半句 until 从句交代转折节点；then 之后并列两个动作：struggle to balance... 和 (struggle to) compete with...，句末 who 引导定语从句修饰 men，点出隐性不公。", "zh": "年轻的女性工程师在生孩子之前处于平等地位，但之后她们就要努力平衡工作与家庭——并与没有相同家庭责任的男性展开竞争。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将具体否定表达“不丧失自信/继续相信自己”进行正话反说。", "option": "not to lose self-confidence", "original": "continuing to believe in myself"}, {"note": "“并非群体一员/不真正属于这里”准确对应“被排除在群体之外”。", "option": "excluded from the group", "original": "never quite one of the groups / don't truly belong"}, {"note": "口语化数量描述“她们人数更多了”在选项中转为名词短语“数量的增加”。", "option": "the increase in their number", "original": "there are just more of them"}, {"note": "由赞美益处（hail the benefits）和感到满足（satisfying）归纳出“对所选职业深感自豪”。", "option": "take great pride in their chosen career", "original": "hailed the benefits of their chosen career / satisfying"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202406-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2024.06", "examSet": "2024.06 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2024.06 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "摆脱讨好心态，学会自我接纳", "subtitle": "剖析讨好型人格的心理成因与自我认可之路", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 354, "paragraphs": ["Lao Zi once said, \"Care about what other people think and you will always be their prisoner.\"", "People-pleasing, or seeking self-worth through others' approval, is unproductive and an exhausting way to go through life. Why do we allow what others think of us to have so much power over how we feel about ourselves? If it's true that you can't please all people all of the time, wouldn't it make sense to stop trying?", "Unfortunately, sense often isn't driving our behavior. For social beings who desire love and belonging, wanting to be liked, and caring about the effect we have on others, is healthy and allows us to make connections. However, where we get into trouble is when our self-worth is dependent upon whether we win someone's approval or not.", "This need to be liked can be traced back to when we were children and were completely dependent on others to take care of us: Small children are not just learning how to walk and communicate, they are also trying to learn how the world works. We learn about who we are and what is expected of us based on interactions with others, so, to a four-year-old, if Mommy or Daddy doesn't like him or her, there is the danger that they will abandon them. We need to understand that when we desperately want someone to approve of us, it's being driven by that little kid part of us that is still terrified of abandonment.", "As you become more capable of providing yourself with the approval you seek, your need for external validation will start to vanish, leaving you stronger, more confident, and yes, happier in your life. Imagine how much time we lose each moment we restrain our authentic selves in an effort to be liked.", "If we base our worth on the opinions of others, we cheat ourselves of the power to shape our experiences and embrace life not only for others but also for ourselves, because ultimately, there is no difference. So embrace the cliché(老话) and love yourself as it's highly doubtful that you'll regret it."], "translations": ["老子曾说过：“在意他人的看法，你就永远是他们的囚徒。”", "讨好他人，或通过他人的认可来寻求自我价值，不仅徒劳无益，也是一种令人精疲力竭的生活方式。为什么我们要让他人对自己的看法对我们的自我感受拥有如此大的掌控力？既然不可能在所有时间取悦所有人，停止这样尝试难道不是更合乎情理吗？", "不幸的是，理智往往并不能驱动我们的行为。作为渴望爱与归属感的社会性生物，希望被喜欢以及在意自己对他人的影响是健康的，也有助于我们与他人建立联结。然而，真正让我们陷入困境的，是把自我价值建立在能否赢得他人的认可之上。", "这种渴望被喜欢的心理可以追溯到童年时期，那时我们完全依赖他人照顾：年幼的孩子不仅在学习走路和沟通，也在努力了解世界如何运转。我们通过与他人的互动来认识自己并了解别人对我们的期望，因此对一个四岁的孩子来说，如果爸爸或妈妈不喜欢自己，就意味着可能会被抛弃。我们需要明白，当我们迫切渴望得到某人的认可时，背后驱动这种情绪的，正是内心深处那个依然害怕被抛弃的小孩。", "当你越来越有能力给予自己所寻求的认可时，你对外部肯定的需求就会开始消退，从而在生活中变得更强大、更自信，也更快乐。试想一下，为了被别人喜欢而压抑真实的自己，我们每时每刻都在浪费多少光阴。", "如果我们将自身价值寄托于他人的评价，就会剥夺自己塑造人生经历、拥抱生活的力量——这不仅是为了他人，也是为了我们自己，因为归根结底两者并无不同。所以，不妨接纳这句老话，好好爱自己，因为你几乎不可能为此后悔。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we conclude from Lao Zi's quotation?", "options": ["We should see through other people's attempt to make a prisoner of us.", "We can never really please other people even if we try as hard as we can.", "We can never be truly free if taking to heart others' opinion of us.", "We should care about other people's view as much as they care about our own."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Lao Zi once said, \"Care about what other people think and you will always be their prisoner.\"", "explanation": "【定位第1段】题干问从老子的名言中可以得出什么结论。第1段引用老子的话指出：“在意他人的看法，你就永远是他们的囚徒。”由此可推知，如果把别人的评价太放在心上（taking to heart others' opinion of us），心灵就会受到束缚，永远无法获得真正的自由（never be truly free，对应become their prisoner）。选项C精准转述了这一引申含义，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项将“在意他人看法”曲解为“别人企图囚禁我们”，属于强加意图；B项虽符合常识但源自第2段而非老子名言；D项“像他人在意我们一样在意他人”属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What will happen if we base our self-worth on other people's approval?", "options": ["Our desire to be loved will be fulfilled.", "Our life will be unfruitful and exhausting.", "Our identity as social beings will be affected.", "Our sense of self will be sharpened and enhanced."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "People-pleasing, or seeking self-worth through others' approval, is unproductive and an exhausting way to go through life.", "explanation": "【定位第2段】题干询问把自我价值建立在他人认可之上会发生什么。第2段首句明确指出：“讨好他人，或通过他人的认可来寻求自我价值，是毫无成效且令人精疲力竭的生活方式。”选项B中的unfruitful对应原文unproductive，exhausting为原词复现，our life对应way to go through life，精准概括了这一结果，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项“被爱的渴望会得到满足”与文意相悖，第3段指出这样做只会让我们陷入困境；C项利用第3段social beings拼凑干扰，文中并未提及社会身份会受损；D项与原文彻底相反。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What may account for our need to be liked or approved of?", "options": ["Our desperate longing for interactions with others.", "Our understanding of the workings of the world.", "Our knowledge about the pain of abandonment.", "Our early childhood fear of being deserted."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "We need to understand that when we desperately want someone to approve of us, it's being driven by that little kid part of us that is still terrified of abandonment.", "explanation": "【定位第4段】题干询问渴望被喜欢或被认可的原因。第4段首句先将该心理追溯至童年时期，末句进一步点明实质：“当我们迫切想得到别人认可时，驱动它的是我们内心深处那个依然害怕被抛弃的小孩。”选项D中early childhood对应that little kid part of us，fear of being deserted对应terrified of abandonment，完美契合原文因果逻辑，故选D。", "trapNote": "A项“渴望与他人互动”偷换概念，原文第4段说孩子通过互动认识世界，并非互动本身导致讨好心理；B、C两项均为第4段中“learn how the world works”与“abandonment”的碎片拼凑，偏离根本动因。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What can we do when we become better able to provide ourselves with the desired approval?", "options": ["Enjoy a happier life.", "Exercise self-restraint.", "Receive more external validation.", "Strengthen our power of imagination."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "As you become more capable of providing yourself with the approval you seek, your need for external validation will start to vanish, leaving you stronger, more confident, and yes, happier in your life.", "explanation": "【定位第5段】题干问当我们更有能力给予自己想要的认可时会怎样。第5段首句指出，随着你更有能力自我认可，你对外部认可的需求将开始消失，“让你在生活中变得更强大、更自信，也更快乐（happier in your life）”。选项A“享受更快乐的生活”直接对应原文结果，B、C、D均与第5段表述不符，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项“克制自己”源自第5段末句restrain our authentic selves，原文说这是讨好别人时浪费时间的做法，而非自我认可后的行为；C项“获得更多外部认可”与原文“开始消失”完全相反；D项歪曲了imagine。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author advise us to do in the last paragraph?", "options": ["Embrace life for ourselves and for others.", "Base our worth on others' opinions.", "See our experiences as assets.", "Love ourselves as we are."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "So embrace the cliché(老话) and love yourself as it's highly doubtful that you'll regret it.", "explanation": "【定位第6段】题干询问作者在最后一段给我们的建议。末段先指出把价值建立在别人评价上会剥夺自己塑造经历和拥抱生活的力量，随后以So引出明确建议：“接纳那句老话，爱你自己，因为你极不可能为此后悔。”选项D“爱真实的自己”准确概括了love yourself这一核心建议，故选D。", "trapNote": "A项利用第6段“embrace life not only for others but also for ourselves”拼凑，但这并非末段So引出的最终建议；B项正是作者批判的错误做法；C项“把经历看作财富”原文未提。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "认可，赞许", "note": "动词approve的名词形式，文中高频出现，固定搭配win someone's approval / external validation", "word": "approval"}, {"gloss": "徒劳的，无成效的", "note": "un- + productive，第2题中被选项同义替换为unfruitful", "word": "unproductive"}, {"gloss": "抛弃，遗弃", "note": "动词abandon的名词形式，第3题中被选项同义替换为being deserted", "word": "abandonment"}, {"gloss": "认可，证实", "note": "第5段external validation与前文的others' approval构成近义呼应", "word": "validation"}, {"gloss": "克制，抑制", "note": "常用搭配restrain one's authentic selves（压抑真实的自我），名词为restraint", "word": "restrain"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "We need to understand that when we desperately want someone to approve of us, it's being driven by that little kid part of us that is still terrified of abandonment.", "point": "多层从句嵌套（宾语从句套时间状语从句与定语从句）及被动进行时（is being driven by）的准确理解", "structure": "主句(We need to understand) + that引导的宾语从句(含when引导的时间状语从句 + 主句it's being driven by... + that引导的定语从句修饰part)", "zh": "我们需要明白，当我们迫切希望得到某人的认可时，驱动这种渴望的正是我们内心深处那个依然害怕被抛弃的小孩。"}, {"en": "If we base our worth on the opinions of others, we cheat ourselves of the power to shape our experiences and embrace life not only for others but also for ourselves, because ultimately, there is no difference.", "point": "动词短语cheat sb. of sth.（剥夺某人某物）以及not only... but also...并列结构的把握", "structure": "If引导的条件状语从句 + 主句(we cheat ourselves of...) + 不定式短语作后置定语(to shape... and embrace...) + because引导的原因状语从句", "zh": "如果我们将自身价值建立在他人的评价之上，就会剥夺自己塑造经历和拥抱生活的力量——这不仅是为了他人，也是为了我们自己，因为归根结底两者并无区别。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题同义改写：成为别人的“囚徒”即“永远无法获得真正的自由”", "option": "never be truly free", "original": "you will always be their prisoner"}, {"note": "第2题同义改写：unproductive 替换为 unfruitful（徒劳无益的），go through life 替换为 Our life", "option": "Our life will be unfruitful and exhausting", "original": "unproductive and an exhausting way to go through life"}, {"note": "第3题同义改写：little kid 对应 early childhood，terrified of abandonment 对应 fear of being deserted", "option": "Our early childhood fear of being deserted", "original": "that little kid part of us that is still terrified of abandonment"}, {"note": "第4题近义复现：核心词 happier 与 life 保留，名词短语转化为动宾结构", "option": "Enjoy a happier life", "original": "happier in your life"}, {"note": "第5题同义微调：人称由第二人称转为第一人称复数，并结合上下文补充“接纳真实自我”的含义", "option": "Love ourselves as we are", "original": "love yourself"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202406-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2024.06", "examSet": "2024.06 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2024.06 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "保持好奇与探索，激活衰老大脑", "subtitle": "科学研究揭示终身学习与新鲜体验对大脑活力的促进作用", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 357, "paragraphs": ["Some people have said aging is more a slide into forgetfulness than a journey towards wisdom. However, a growing body of research suggests that late-in-life learning is possible. In reality, education does an aging brain good.", "Throughout life, people's brains constantly renovate themselves. In the late 1960s, British brain scientist Geoffrey Raisman spied growth in damaged brain regions of rats through an electron microscope; their brains were forging new connections. This meant brains may change every time a person learns something new.", "Of course, that doesn't mean the brain isn't affected by the effects of time. Just as height usually declines over the years, so does brain volume: Humans lose about 4 percent every decade starting in their 40s. But that reduction doesn't necessarily make people think slower; as long as we are alive and functioning, we can alter our brains with new information and experiences.", "In fact, scientists now suspect accumulating novel experiences, facts, and skills can keep people's minds more flexible. New pathways can strengthen our ever-changing mental structure, even as the brain shrinks.", "Conventional fixes like word puzzles and brain-training apps can contribute to mental durability. Even something as simple as taking a different route to the grocery store or going somewhere new on vacation can keep the brain healthy.", "A desire for new life challenges can further boost brainpower. Research about aging adults who take on new enterprises shows improved function and memory as well as a reduced risk of mental disease. Openness—a characteristic defined by curiosity and a desire for knowledge—may also help folks pass brain tests. Some folks are born with this take-in-the-world attitude, but those who aren't as genetically gifted aren't necessarily out of luck. While genes can encourage an interest in doing new things, a 2012 study in the journal Psychology and Aging found completing reasoning tasks like puzzles and number games can enhance that desire for novel experiences, which can, in turn, refresh the brain. That's why brain scientist Richard Kennedy says \"It's not that old dogs can't learn new tricks. It's that maybe old dogs don't realize why they should.\""], "translations": ["有人说衰老更像是滑向健忘，而非通往智慧的旅程。然而，越来越多的研究表明，晚年学习是完全可能的。事实上，教育对衰老的大脑大有裨益。", "人的一生中，大脑都在不断自我更新。20世纪60年代末，英国脑科学家杰弗里·雷斯曼（Geoffrey Raisman）通过电子显微镜观察到大鼠受损脑区的生长，发现它们的大脑正在建立新的神经连接。这意味着每当一个人学习新事物时，大脑都可能发生变化。", "当然，这并不意味着大脑不受岁月的影响。正如身高通常会随着年龄增长而下降，脑容量也是如此：人类从40多岁开始，脑容量每十年减少约4%。但这种萎缩并不一定会让人思考变慢；只要我们还活着且机能正常，就能用新信息和新经历重塑大脑。", "事实上，科学家现在认为，积累新颖的经历、知识和技能能够让人的思维保持更佳的灵活性。即便在大脑萎缩的情况下，新的神经通路也能强化我们不断变化的大脑认知结构。", "像字谜和脑力训练应用程序这样的传统方法有助于提升大脑的持久活力。甚至连去杂货店走一条不同的路线，或者度假时去一个新地方这样简单的事情，都能让大脑保持健康。", "对新生活挑战的渴望可以进一步增强脑力。针对敢于尝试新事物的老年人的研究表明，他们的脑功能和记忆力有所改善，患精神疾病的风险也有所降低。开放性——一种以好奇心和求知欲为特征的性格特质——同样有助于人们通过大脑测试。有些人天生就具备这种拥抱世界的态度，但那些在基因上不那么占优势的人也并非毫无希望。尽管基因能够激发人们尝试新事物的兴趣，但2012年发表在《心理学与衰老》杂志上的一项研究发现，完成谜题和数字游戏等推理任务能够增强对新奇体验的渴望，而这反过来又能让大脑焕然一新。正因如此，脑科学家理查德·肯尼迪（Richard Kennedy）才会说：“并非老狗学不会新把戏，而是老狗也许还没意识到自己为什么应该学。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do some people think of aging adults?", "options": ["Their wisdom grows as time goes by.", "Their memory gradually deteriorates.", "They can benefit from late-in-life learning.", "They are likely to have mental health issues."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Some people have said aging is more a slide into forgetfulness than a journey towards wisdom.", "explanation": "【定位第1段】题干问一些人对老年人（aging adults）的看法。第1段首句指出：“有人说衰老更像是滑向健忘（a slide into forgetfulness），而非通往智慧的旅程。”选项B中的memory gradually deteriorates（记忆力逐渐衰退）正是a slide into forgetfulness的同义转述，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项“智慧随时间增长”与首句“rather than a journey towards wisdom”观点相反；C项是后文科研结论，并非“some people”的看法；D项利用第6段mental disease拼凑，偏离首段定位。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we conclude from Geoffrey Raisman's finding?", "options": ["Brain damage seriously hinders one's learning.", "Brain power weakens slower than we imagine.", "Brains can refresh and improve with learning.", "Brains forge connections under new conditions."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Throughout life, people's brains constantly renovate themselves. In the late 1960s, British brain scientist Geoffrey Raisman spied growth in damaged brain regions of rats through an electron microscope; their brains were forging new connections. This meant brains may change every time a person learns something new.", "explanation": "【定位第2段】题干问从Geoffrey Raisman的发现中能得出什么结论。第2段先指出大脑一生都在自我更新（constantly renovate themselves），接着借Raisman观察大鼠受损脑区生长并建立新连接的实验，得出结论：“每当人学习新事物时，大脑都可能发生变化。”选项C“大脑会随着学习而更新和提升”精准概括了该发现的意义，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项“脑损伤严重阻碍学习”属于无中生有，实验强调的是受损脑区仍能生长；B项“脑力衰退比想象慢”第2段未提及；D项将“每当学习新事物时”偷换为“在新条件下”，偏离核心。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is one thing that helps maintain the health of our brain even as it shrinks?", "options": ["Doing daily routines by conventional means.", "Avoiding worrying about our mental durability.", "Imitating old dogs' way of learning new tricks.", "Approaching everyday tasks in novel ways."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Even something as simple as taking a different route to the grocery store or going somewhere new on vacation can keep the brain healthy.", "explanation": "【定位第4-5段】题干询问大脑萎缩时有什么方法能帮助维持大脑健康。第4段指出积累新奇体验能强化大脑结构，第5段进一步举例说明：“甚至像去杂货店走不同的路线或去新地方度假这样简单的事，也能保持大脑健康。”选项D“以新颖的方式处理日常事务”准确概括了“走不同路线”等日常创新做法，故选D。", "trapNote": "A项“按常规方式处理日常事务”与第5段taking a different route恰恰相反；B项断章取义，原文是传统方法能增强mental durability，而非“避免担忧”；C项属于张冠李戴，偷换第6段谚语。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say can contribute to the improvement of brain function?", "options": ["Being curious and desiring knowledge.", "Being eager to pass brain tests at an old age.", "Rising to life's challenges and avoiding risks.", "Boosting immunity to serious mental diseases."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Openness—a characteristic defined by curiosity and a desire for knowledge—may also help folks pass brain tests.", "explanation": "【定位第6段】题干问什么有助于改善大脑功能。第6段指出接受新挑战能改善功能和记忆力，紧接着补充：“开放性——一种由好奇心和求知欲（curiosity and a desire for knowledge）所定义的特质——也有助于人们通过大脑测试。”选项A将其转化为动名词短语“保持好奇与求知欲”，完美对应原文表述，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项将“pass brain tests”作为目的置于“eager to”之后，属于因果倒置；C项“avoiding risks”曲解了原文“reduced risk of mental disease”；D项把“降低患病风险”这一结果误作改善脑功能的原因。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the finding of the 2012 study in the journal Psychology and Aging?", "options": ["Wishing to solve puzzles enhances one's reasoning power.", "Playing number games unexpectedly stimulates one's memory.", "Desiring new experiences can help to renovate the brain.", "Learning new tricks should not be confined to old dogs only."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "While genes can encourage an interest in doing new things, a 2012 study in the journal Psychology and Aging found completing reasoning tasks like puzzles and number games can enhance that desire for novel experiences, which can, in turn, refresh the brain.", "explanation": "【定位第6段】题干问《心理学与衰老》杂志2012年研究的发现。第6段明确指出，该研究发现完成谜题和数字游戏等推理任务能增强对新奇体验的渴望，“而这反过来又能刷新大脑（which can, in turn, refresh the brain）”。选项C中Desiring new experiences对应desire for novel experiences，renovate the brain对应refresh the brain，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项将因果关系颠倒，原文是完成推理任务增强“对新奇体验的渴望”，而非渴望解题增强推理能力；B项“刺激记忆力”在2012年研究中未提及；D项曲解了末句关于“老狗与新把戏”的比喻。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "更新，修复", "note": "原指翻新建筑，文中喻指大脑的自我更新与重塑，与第6段refresh呼应", "word": "renovate"}, {"gloss": "建立，锻造", "note": "常见搭配forge new connections（建立新的神经连接）", "word": "forge"}, {"gloss": "缩小，萎缩", "note": "文中指脑容量随年龄增长而萎缩（even as the brain shrinks）", "word": "shrink"}, {"gloss": "持久性，耐久性", "note": "来自形容词durable，文中mental durability指大脑思维的持久活力", "word": "durability"}, {"gloss": "新事业，冒险尝试", "note": "在文中指老年人主动承担的新事物或新挑战（take on new enterprises）", "word": "enterprise"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Just as height usually declines over the years, so does brain volume: Humans lose about 4 percent every decade starting in their 40s.", "point": "Just as..., so + 助动词 + 主语 的倒装比较结构（表示“正如……一样，……也如此”）", "structure": "Just as引导比较状语从句 + so does...部分倒装主句 + 冒号后的同位解释句(含现在分词短语starting in their 40s作状语)", "zh": "正如身高通常会随着岁月增长而下降一样，脑容量也是如此：人类从40多岁开始，脑容量每十年会减少约4%。"}, {"en": "While genes can encourage an interest in doing new things, a 2012 study in the journal Psychology and Aging found completing reasoning tasks like puzzles and number games can enhance that desire for novel experiences, which can, in turn, refresh the brain.", "point": "While表让步（尽管），动名词短语作宾语从句主语，以及which指代前面整个动作/概念的非限制性定语从句", "structure": "While引导让步状语从句 + 主句(a 2012 study... found) + 省略that的宾语从句(动名词短语completing...作主语) + which引导的非限制性定语从句", "zh": "尽管基因可以激发人们尝试新事物的兴趣，但2012年发表在《心理学与衰老》杂志上的一项研究发现，完成谜题和数字游戏等推理任务能够增强对新奇体验的渴望，而这反过来又能让大脑焕然一新。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题同义改写：滑向健忘即“记忆力逐渐退化”", "option": "memory gradually deteriorates", "original": "a slide into forgetfulness"}, {"note": "第2题同义概括：大脑自我更新并随学习改变即“在学习中焕新与提升”", "option": "refresh and improve with learning", "original": "renovate themselves / change every time a person learns something new"}, {"note": "第3题抽象概括：具体例子（走不同路线去买菜）抽象为“以新颖方式处理日常事务”", "option": "Approaching everyday tasks in novel ways", "original": "taking a different route to the grocery store"}, {"note": "第4题词性转换：名词短语转化为动名词短语，核心词义完全一致", "option": "Being curious and desiring knowledge", "original": "curiosity and a desire for knowledge"}, {"note": "第5题同义替换：novel 替换为 new，refresh 替换为前文出现过的 renovate", "option": "Desiring new experiences can help to renovate the brain", "original": "desire for novel experiences, which can, in turn, refresh the brain"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202312-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "职场忙碌文化与工作生活平衡", "subtitle": "社会文化 · 职场心理与时间管理", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 370, "paragraphs": ["One of my bad habits is saying “busy” when people ask me how I’m doing. Sometimes it’s because I actually am busy, but other times it’s because that’s what I think I’m supposed to say. That’s what important people say. That’s what people who get promoted say. But working long hours doesn’t drive better results. Never taking a vacation won’t lead to a promotion. So why are we so proud to talk about how busy we are all the time?", "In 2016, researchers from Columbia, Harvard, and Georgetown conducted a study to figure it out. They found busy people are perceived to be of high status, and interestingly, these status attributions are heavily influenced by our own beliefs about social mobility. In other words, the more we believe that one has the opportunity for success based on hard work, the more we tend to think that people who skip leisure and work all the time are of higher standing.", "That’s why we feel like we have to appear busy, and there’s a real perception that if someone is knee-deep in meetings, emails and stress, then they’re probably a big deal. This culture of busyness is making it hard for employees to find work-life balance. According to a recent study, one in five highly engaged employees are at risk of burnout (精疲力竭).", "Personally, I’m going to stop saying “busy” when people ask me how I am. It sounds self-righteous (自以为是的) and sets the wrong tone. Phrases like “I have limited access to email” and “I’ll respond as soon as I get back” sound like you’re being held against your will from working as opposed to making the most of your time off.", "That’s why we recently launched the Out of Office Email Generator, a free tool you can use before your next long weekend or trip. You can share loud and proud that you won’t be checking email until you’re back. Managers need to think twice about emailing their teams on the weekend and talking about how busy they are. Leaders should take time off themselves and encourage employees to do the same."], "translations": ["我的一个坏习惯是，当别人问我最近怎么样时，我总会回答“忙”。有时是因为我确实很忙，但另一些时候是因为我觉得自己本就该这么说。重要人物都这么说，获得晋升的人也这么说。然而，长时间工作并不能带来更好的业绩，从不休假也不会让人得到提拔。那么，为什么我们总是对谈论自己有多忙感到如此自豪呢？", "2016年，来自哥伦比亚大学、哈佛大学和乔治城大学的研究人员开展了一项研究以探究其中原因。他们发现，忙碌的人会被认为社会地位更高；有趣的是，这种地位归因很大程度上受我们自身对社会流动性看法的影响。换句话说，我们越相信一个人有机会凭借努力工作获得成功，就越倾向于认为那些放弃休闲、整天工作的人地位更高。", "这就是为什么我们觉得自己必须显得很忙，而且人们确实普遍认为，如果一个人深陷于会议、邮件和压力之中，那他多半是个大人物。这种忙碌文化让员工很难实现工作与生活的平衡。根据最近的一项研究，五分之一高度投入工作的员工面临着精疲力竭的风险。", "就我个人而言，当别人问我过得怎么样时，我打算不再说“忙”了。这种说法听起来自以为是，而且定下了错误的基调。诸如“我查看邮件不太方便”和“我一回来就回复”这样的措辞，听起来像是你被迫无法工作，而不是在充分享受自己的休假时光。", "正因如此，我们最近推出了“休假自动回复邮件生成器”，这是一款你可以在下一个长周末或旅行前使用的免费工具。你可以理直气壮、自豪地告知他人，在你回来之前不会查看邮件。管理者在周末给团队发邮件或谈论自己有多忙之前，需要三思而后行。领导者应当自己主动休假，并鼓励员工也这样做。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is a reason for the author to be in the habit of saying “busy” when asked how he is doing?", "options": ["He just follows successful people’s example.", "He is actually proud to be fully occupied.", "He thinks everyone should be devoted to work.", "He believes busyness ensures accomplishments."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Sometimes it’s because I actually am busy, but other times it’s because that’s what I think I’m supposed to say. That’s what important people say. That’s what people who get promoted say.", "explanation": "本题定位第1段第2至4句。作者解释自己被问及近况时习惯说“忙”，有时确实很忙，另一些时候则是觉得自己理应这样回答，因为所谓的重要人物和获得晋升的人都这么说。由此可见，作者说“忙”是在模仿成功人士的说话方式。选项A中“效仿成功人士的榜样”正是对“重要人物”与“升职者”言行效仿的准确同义转述，且作者明确将其称为坏习惯并否定长时间工作能带来好业绩，故A为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项属于张冠李戴与偷换概念，原文末句以反问提及人们普遍以谈论忙碌为傲，并非作者本人以此为荣；D项正反颠倒，第1段明确指出长时间工作不会带来更好业绩，不休假也无法换来晋升。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why do we tend to think that busy people are of high status?", "options": ["Our status can be attributed to our social mobility.", "We hold the belief that hard work leads to success.", "Our own opportunity for success never comes easily.", "We find few people of high status have time for leisure."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "In other words, the more we believe that one has the opportunity for success based on hard work, the more we tend to think that people who skip leisure and work all the time are of higher standing.", "explanation": "本题定位第2段末句。研究人员发现人们认为忙碌者地位更高，这种判断受社会流动性观念影响；随后用“换句话说”具体解释：我们越相信人有机会靠努力工作获得成功，就越倾向于认为放弃休闲、整天工作的人社会地位更高。选项B“我们认为努力工作能带来成功”与原文“靠努力工作拥有成功机会”精准对应，说明了背后动因，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，原文指“地位归因”受社会流动性观念影响，而非自身地位归因于流动性；D项正反颠倒且过度推理，原文说人们把整天工作不休闲的人视作高地位，而非调查发现高地位者很少有闲暇。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about the culture of busyness from a recent study?", "options": ["It places employees in endless meetings, emails and stress.", "It compels some 20% of employees to appear always busy.", "It distorts many employees’ belief of what a satisfying life is.", "It does much harm to many busy employees’ well-being."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "This culture of busyness is making it hard for employees to find work-life balance. According to a recent study, one in five highly engaged employees are at risk of burnout (精疲力竭).", "explanation": "本题定位第3段后两句。文章指出这种忙碌文化让员工难以实现工作与生活的平衡，并援引最近一项研究的数据说明：五分之一高度投入工作的员工正面临精疲力竭的风险。失去工作生活平衡及陷入精疲力竭的风险，正是对许多忙碌员工身心健康的严重损害。选项D“它对许多忙碌员工的福祉造成很大伤害”是对该研究结论的合理概括，故选D。", "trapNote": "B项偷换概念且以偏概全，原文的五分之一（即20%）指的是“高度投入的员工面临精疲力竭风险”，而非“被迫总是显得很忙”；A项将段首人们对他人的看法混为研究结论，且“无休止”无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do such utterances as “I have limited access to email” sound like according to the author?", "options": ["One is too busy to check all emails in time.", "One is opposed to the prevailing work culture.", "One is forced by circumstances to stop working.", "One is simply enjoying their time off work."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Phrases like “I have limited access to email” and “I’ll respond as soon as I get back” sound like you’re being held against your will from working as opposed to making the most of your time off.", "explanation": "本题定位第4段末句。作者认为，诸如“我查看邮件不太方便”和“我一回来就回复”这类表达，听起来就像你是违背个人意愿被阻止去工作的，而不是在充分享受自己的休假时间。选项C“某人因环境所迫而不得不停止工作”与原文中“违背自身意愿被迫中断工作”意思高度吻合，准确概括了作者对这类话语的感受，故选C。", "trapNote": "D项属于正反颠倒，原文明确以“而不是”对比指出，这类说法并非展现你在充分享受休假；A项与B项均属无中生有，原文并未由此推导出“太忙来不及看邮件”或“反对主流工作文化”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why did the author and his colleagues launch the Out of Office Email Generator?", "options": ["To enable busy employees to spend less time checking emails.", "To ensure employees as well as employers truly have time off.", "To stop managers from talking about how busy their teams usually are.", "To encourage both employers and employees to answer emails promptly."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "That’s why we recently launched the Out of Office Email Generator, a free tool you can use before your next long weekend or trip. You can share loud and proud that you won’t be checking email until you’re back. Managers need to think twice about emailing their teams on the weekend and talking about how busy they are. Leaders should take time off themselves and encourage employees to do the same.", "explanation": "本题定位第5段全段及第4段末句承接。作者推出“休假自动回复邮件生成器”，是为了让人们在长周末或旅行前理直气壮地宣告回来前不看邮件，真正享受休假；同时段末呼吁管理者周末少发邮件、领导者以身作则休假并鼓励员工效仿。可见该举措旨在确保雇主和员工都能真正获得休假，B项精准概括了这双重目标，故选B。", "trapNote": "C项偷换对象，原文指管理者别总谈论“自己”有多忙，而非“团队”有多忙；A项偏离主旨，工具并非教忙碌员工平时少看邮件，而是休假期间彻底不查邮件；D项与原文“回来前不查看邮件”正反颠倒。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 归因，归属", "note": "由动词attribute（把……归因于）派生，常考搭配status attribution（地位归因）及be attributed to（归因于）。", "word": "attribution"}, {"gloss": "n. 流动性，变动性", "note": "源自mobile（可移动的），文中social mobility指“社会阶层流动性”，四级社会类阅读高频词。", "word": "mobility"}, {"gloss": "n. 精疲力竭，职业倦怠", "note": "由动词短语burn out（烧尽、精疲力竭）转化而来的合成名词，常见于职场健康与压力话题。", "word": "burnout"}, {"gloss": "adj. 自以为是的，自鸣得意的", "note": "合成形容词，文中带有明显贬义，揭示作者对“总把忙碌挂在嘴边”这一习惯的否定态度。", "word": "self-righteous"}, {"gloss": "n. 休假时间，休息时间", "note": "熟词僻义及固定搭配：off在此表示“休息、不工作”，take time off意为“请假、休假”，本文核心关键词。", "word": "time off"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In other words, the more we believe that one has the opportunity for success based on hard work, the more we tend to think that people who skip leisure and work all the time are of higher standing.", "point": "掌握“the more..., the more...”表示“越……就越……”的递进逻辑，是第2题（社会流动性观念与高地位认知因果关系）的核心解题句。", "structure": "“the + 比较级..., the + 比较级...”句型结构；前分句含that引导的宾语从句，后分句宾语从句中嵌套who引导的定语从句修饰people。", "zh": "换句话说，我们越相信一个人有机会凭借努力工作获得成功，就越倾向于认为那些放弃休闲、整天工作的人地位更高。"}, {"en": "That’s why we feel like we have to appear busy, and there’s a real perception that if someone is knee-deep in meetings, emails and stress, then they’re probably a big deal.", "point": "注意that引导的同位语从句对perception进行具体阐释，同时积累地道习语knee-deep in（深陷于）和a big deal（大人物/要人）。", "structure": "why引导表语从句；and连接并列分句，其中that引导同位语从句解释perception，从句内部嵌套if条件状语从句。", "zh": "这就是为什么我们觉得自己必须显得很忙，而且人们确实普遍认为，如果一个人深陷于会议、邮件和压力之中，那他多半是个大人物。"}, {"en": "Phrases like “I have limited access to email” and “I’ll respond as soon as I get back” sound like you’re being held against your will from working as opposed to making the most of your time off.", "point": "识别as opposed to（而不是）构成的语义对比，以及be held against one’s will（违背意愿受阻/被迫）与第4题选项forced by circumstances的同义替换。", "structure": "主系表结构，like引出列举作后置定语；sound like后接宾语从句，其中被动语态be held against one’s will表示“被迫”；as opposed to引出对比短语。", "zh": "诸如“我查看邮件不太方便”和“我一回来就回复”这样的措辞，听起来像是你被迫无法工作，而不是在充分享受自己的休假时光。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题：将文中具体指代的“重要人物、升职者”上位概括为“成功人士”。", "option": "successful people", "original": "important people / people who get promoted"}, {"note": "第2题：将“基于努力拥有成功机会”精简改写为“努力工作带来成功”。", "option": "hard work leads to success", "original": "one has the opportunity for success based on hard work"}, {"note": "第3题：用“损害身心福祉”高度概括原文的“难以平衡工作生活”与“精疲力竭风险”。", "option": "does much harm to... well-being", "original": "making it hard... to find work-life balance / at risk of burnout"}, {"note": "第4题：将“违背个人意愿被挡在工作之外”同义替换为“受环境所迫停止工作”。", "option": "forced by circumstances to stop working", "original": "being held against your will from working"}, {"note": "第5题：把“领导者自己休假并鼓励员工效仿”整合转述为“雇主与员工均能真正休假”。", "option": "ensure employees as well as employers truly have time off", "original": "Leaders should take time off themselves and encourage employees to do the same."}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202312-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "男女差旅机票差价与负向互惠", "subtitle": "商业行为 · 性别差异与组织心理学", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 347, "paragraphs": ["Female employees consistently pay lower airfares than men do for the same flights because they tend to book earlier.", "We compared the airfare paid by employees in the same position within a company for the same class of travel and used a common statistical technique to account for other factors that might affect differences in airfares. We found that women paid on average $18 less per ticket than their male colleagues. Further investigation allowed us to conclude that this gap is largely explained by the fact that women tended to book earlier than men, 1.8 days on average.", "We wanted to determine what was causing these gender differences in booking business trips so we tested a variety of possible explanations, such as women choosing to plan ahead or male frequent travelers being inclined to book late. None of these explained away the gender gap, so we applied data collected from surveys that express consumer preferences that play a central role in economic decisions, such as patience and risk avoidance.", "We found that only the concept of “negative reciprocity” — in which an employee who feels unfairly treated engages in negative behaviors, such as spending their company’s money less carefully — explains these differences. The surveys showed men tend to exhibit more of these negative behaviors than women.", "This isn’t to say that all men engage in these behaviors — or that booking relatively late is a sign of abnormal behavior. It only means that the gender gap disappears when we plug in the negative reciprocity variable.", "Prior research on negative reciprocity among workers found that it can result in lower employee motivation, business performance and workplace morale (士气) and culture.", "Our results show another way these negative behaviors can manifest themselves, like in airline bookings, and add to evidence that women are less likely to engage in them.", "Companies spend significant sums of money on business travel. While that $18 difference per ticket may seem small, it adds up. Our analysis suggests early booking by women can translate into savings of $1 million a year for a large multinational company with 20,000 regular travelers."], "translations": ["在同一航班上，女性员工支付的机票价格始终低于男性员工，因为她们往往更早预订。", "我们对比了同一家公司内同等职位员工购买相同舱位机票所支付的费用，并采用了一种常用的统计技术来排除可能影响票价差异的其他因素。我们发现，女性平均每张机票比男同事少花18美元。进一步的研究使我们得出结论：这一差价主要归因于女性往往比男性更早订票，平均提前1.8天。", "我们想弄清楚是什么导致了出差订票上的这种性别差异，于是检验了多种可能的解释，例如女性倾向于提前规划，或经常出差的男性习惯临近才订票。然而，这些因素都未能消除这一性别差距，因此我们采用了从调查中收集的数据，这些调查反映了在经济决策中起核心作用的消费者偏好，如耐心程度和风险规避。", "我们发现，只有“负向互惠”这一概念——即感到受到不公平对待的员工会做出消极行为，例如花公司的钱时不够精打细算——能够解释这些差异。调查显示，男性往往比女性表现出更多此类消极行为。", "这并不是说所有男性都会做出这类行为，也不是说相对较晚订票就是一种异常行为。它仅仅意味着，当我们将“负向互惠”这一变量纳入分析时，男女之间的差异便消失了。", "此前针对员工负向互惠的研究发现，它会导致员工积极性下降、企业业绩下滑，以及职场士气和文化恶化。", "我们的研究结果揭示了这些消极行为得以体现的另一种方式，例如体现在机票预订上，并进一步证明女性不太可能做出这类行为。", "企业在商务差旅上花费了巨额资金。虽然每张机票18美元的差价看似微不足道，但积少成多。我们的分析表明，对于一家拥有2万名经常出差员工的大型跨国公司来说，女性提前订票的行为每年可转化为高达100万美元的开支节省。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did the author’s team conclude about the gender difference in airfares from their further investigation?", "options": ["It is largely attributed to women booking earlier than men.", "It is largely explained by women’s choosing cheaper flights.", "It is mainly accounted for by male employees’ readiness to pay more.", "It is due to the fact that women care more about their company’s money."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Further investigation allowed us to conclude that this gap is largely explained by the fact that women tended to book earlier than men, 1.8 days on average.", "explanation": "本题定位第2段末句。在对比了同公司同职位员工购买相同舱位机票的费用后，作者团队指出“进一步的研究使我们得出结论：这一差距主要归因于女性往往比男性更早订票，平均提前1.8天”。选项A中的“主要归因于女性比男性更早订票”是对原文“主要由女性更早订票这一事实来解释”的精准同义转述，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项偷换概念，第1、2段明确说明对比的是“同一航班、相同舱位”，并非女性特意选更便宜的航班；D项属张冠李戴，“花公司钱不够谨慎”是第4段才探讨的更深层原因，而非此处结论。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did the researchers want to determine by testing a variety of possible explanations?", "options": ["What made male frequent travelers book air tickets late.", "What caused women to plan ahead in booking business trips.", "What motivated women to book cheaper flights.", "What accounted for the gender gap in airfares."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "We wanted to determine what was causing these gender differences in booking business trips so we tested a variety of possible explanations, such as women choosing to plan ahead or male frequent travelers being inclined to book late. None of these explained away the gender gap, so we applied data collected from surveys that express consumer preferences that play a central role in economic decisions, such as patience and risk avoidance.", "explanation": "本题定位第3段前两句。前文已说明订票时间差异直接导致了机票差价，第3段接着指出研究者检验多种可能解释的目的，是想查明“是什么导致了出差订票上的性别差异”，而后文又说这些都没能解释“性别差距”。可见检验各种假设旨在搞清造成机票性别差价的深层原因，D项“是什么解释了机票上的性别差距”准确切中主旨，故选D。", "trapNote": "A项和B项均属于偷换概念，把“频繁出差的男性习惯晚订票”与“女性选择提前规划”这两个被检验的“候选假设”，误当成了研究试图解答的最终问题；C项与原文“同航班同舱位”不符。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What happened when the negative reciprocity variable was taken into account?", "options": ["Both men and women were found to engage in negative behaviors.", "Neither men nor women viewed booking late as a bad behavior.", "The gender difference in airfare expenses no longer existed.", "The gender gap tended to narrow to a significant degree."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "It only means that the gender gap disappears when we plug in the negative reciprocity variable.", "explanation": "本题定位第5段末句。作者首先澄清并非所有男性都会采取消极行为，也并非晚订票就是异常举动，随即强调“它仅仅意味着，当我们将负向互惠这一变量纳入分析时，男女之间的差距便消失了”。选项C“机票费用上的性别差异不再存在”与原文“性别差距消失”完全同义替换，表述精准，故选C。", "trapNote": "D项偷换程度，原文明确指出引入该变量后性别差距“彻底消失”，而非仅“显著缩小”；A项与原文“女性不太可能做出这类行为”相悖；B项属于对首句“异常行为”的无中生有曲解。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did prior research on negative reciprocity among workers find?", "options": ["It can do more harm to the workplace than to employees.", "It contributes to the male-female divide in the workplace.", "It proves to be counterproductive in a number of ways.", "It can result in increasing labor-management conflicts."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Prior research on negative reciprocity among workers found that it can result in lower employee motivation, business performance and workplace morale (士气) and culture.", "explanation": "本题定位第6段。该段明确指出，此前关于员工负向互惠的研究发现，它会导致更低的员工积极性、企业业绩以及职场士气和文化。这说明负向互惠会在员工动力、业务表现和组织氛围等多个方面产生负面、适得其反的后果。选项C“它在多方面被证明是适得其反的”是对上述多项负面影响的高度概括，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项无中生有，原文仅并列提及员工动力与职场士气，并未比较对二者的伤害孰轻孰重；B项张冠李戴，此前研究并未涉及性别鸿沟；D项过度推理，原文未提及“劳资冲突加剧”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author emphasize about their analysis in the last paragraph?", "options": ["It can help companies increase their savings significantly.", "It can duly contribute to companies’ business performance.", "It can translate women’s booking practice into men’s behavior.", "It can enhance large multinational companies’ competitiveness."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "While that $18 difference per ticket may seem small, it adds up. Our analysis suggests early booking by women can translate into savings of $1 million a year for a large multinational company with 20,000 regular travelers.", "explanation": "本题定位末段第2、3句。作者指出，虽然每张机票18美元的差价看似不起眼，但积少成多；随后强调分析表明，对于拥有两万名常旅员工的大型跨国公司，女性提前订票每年可节省高达100万美元。由此可见，作者在末段着力突出了该分析对企业大幅节省开支的现实价值，选项A与“积少成多、节省百万美元”精准契合，故选A。", "trapNote": "C项拼接原文词语制造陷阱，原文指早期订票“转化为百万美元节省”，而非将女性做法转化为男性行为；B项“企业业绩”出自第6段，D项“增强竞争力”在末段均无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "说明……的原因；解释；占（比例）；把……考虑在内", "note": "一词多义高频短语：第2段中意为“把……纳入考量/解释”，题干中常与explain互换作“解释……的原因”。", "word": "account for"}, {"gloss": "为……辩解；通过解释消除（疑虑或差异）", "note": "熟词僻义：away在此表“消解、除去”，文中“none of these explained away the gender gap”指这些因素都无法把差异彻底解释清。", "word": "explain away"}, {"gloss": "n. 互惠，相互回报", "note": "源自reciprocal（相互的），negative reciprocity在心理学与管理学中特指“负向互惠/以牙还牙式的消极回报”。", "word": "reciprocity"}, {"gloss": "v. 显现，表现；adj. 明显的", "note": "四级高频学术动词，常用于反身结构manifest oneself（显现、体现出来），等同于appear或show。", "word": "manifest"}, {"gloss": "转化为，变成（某种结果）", "note": "熟词僻义：translate不止表示“翻译”，在商业经济类文章中极常考“（把行动、差价等）转化为（收益、节省）”。", "word": "translate into"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "None of these explained away the gender gap, so we applied data collected from surveys that express consumer preferences that play a central role in economic decisions, such as patience and risk avoidance.", "point": "注意区分多层嵌套的that定语从句各自修饰的先行词，并掌握动词短语explain away（通过解释消除、合理化化解）的地道含义。", "structure": "so连接并列句；过去分词短语collected from surveys作后置定语修饰data；内含两个连续的that定语从句，分别修饰surveys与consumer preferences。", "zh": "然而，这些因素都未能消除这一性别差距，因此我们采用了从调查中收集的数据，这些调查反映了在经济决策中起核心作用的消费者偏好，如耐心程度和风险规避。"}, {"en": "We found that only the concept of “negative reciprocity” — in which an employee who feels unfairly treated engages in negative behaviors, such as spending their company’s money less carefully — explains these differences.", "point": "阅读时可先跳过双破折号间的插入定语从句，快速抓取主干“only negative reciprocity explains these differences”，再回看定义细节。", "structure": "主谓宾结构，that引导宾语从句；双破折号之间为“介词in + which”引导的非限制性定语从句修饰concept，其中又嵌套who引导的定语从句修饰employee。", "zh": "我们发现，只有“负向互惠”这一概念——即感到受到不公平对待的员工会做出消极行为，例如花公司的钱时不够精打细算——能够解释这些差异。"}, {"en": "Our analysis suggests early booking by women can translate into savings of $1 million a year for a large multinational company with 20,000 regular travelers.", "point": "掌握suggest作“表明、显示”而非“建议”的常考词义（从句不用虚拟语气），以及translate into（转化为）在末段数据论证中的用法。", "structure": "suggests后接省略that的宾语从句；动名词短语early booking作从句主语；translate into表示“转化为”；介词短语for...作状语。", "zh": "我们的分析表明，对于一家拥有2万名经常出差员工的大型跨国公司来说，女性提前订票的行为每年可转化为高达100万美元的开支节省。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题：将“主要由……事实来解释”同义替换为“主要归因于……”，注意be attributed to的常规考查。", "option": "largely attributed to women booking earlier than men", "original": "largely explained by the fact that women tended to book earlier than men"}, {"note": "第2题：将“造成订票性别差异/消除性别差距”概括转述为“解释机票中的性别差距”（account for = explain）。", "option": "accounted for the gender gap in airfares", "original": "causing these gender differences in booking business trips / explained away the gender gap"}, {"note": "第3题：用no longer existed对应disappears，并用taken into account对应plug in（代入变量）。", "option": "The gender difference in airfare expenses no longer existed", "original": "the gender gap disappears when we plug in the negative reciprocity variable"}, {"note": "第4题：用“在多方面适得其反”上位概括文中列举的员工动力、业绩与士气三重负面后果。", "option": "counterproductive in a number of ways", "original": "lower employee motivation, business performance and workplace morale and culture"}, {"note": "第5题：将“积少成多、每年转化为100万美元节省”抽象概括为“显著增加开支节省”。", "option": "increase their savings significantly", "original": "it adds up / translate into savings of $1 million a year"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202312-s2-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 四级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 四级真题 第2套 Passage One", "title": "创业竞争的双刃剑：动力与陷阱", "subtitle": "创业心理 · 竞争心态与决策风险管理", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 357, "paragraphs": ["Having a rival can keep you committed to achieving your goals and enhance your overall performance. But before you go out and find an entrepreneur to outcompete, it's important to understand and avoid the traps that often come with rivalry. After all, competitive rivalry can also hinder effective decision-making and increase your willingness to take risks, behaviors that can ultimately hurt your venture's success.", "Finding someone you're committed to outcompeting can be a great way to stay focused on your goals and push your venture to the next level. But when you're intently focused on outperforming your rivals, you may begin to develop a \"win-at-all-costs\" mentality that causes you to ignore how you achieve success. One group of researchers, for example, examined the link between rivalry and unethical behavior. They found that when people compete against their rivals, they are more willing to behave unethically to win. But such behavior may stain your reputation and strain relationships important to your success. One way to avoid this trap is to stop and reflect on what's important. While outperforming your rivals may provide short-term benefits, the loss of your integrity will have long-term consequences.", "One reason having a rival can enhance your venture's performance is that it creates a level of excitement that drives you to work harder. But this eagerness to win may also hurt your venture's success, particularly when it causes you to make impulsive, insensible decisions. But it's possible to avoid such costly mistakes by making a habit of engaging in critical thinking, such as considering opposing viewpoints and conducting cost-benefit analyses, especially for those decisions that are complex and can determine the future of your venture.", "The sense of eagerness that comes with having a rival can not only cause you to make poorer decisions, but it can also lead you to take greater risks that put your venture in peril. One way you can overcome the risk-inducing effects of rivalry that stand to endanger your venture's success is to remain attentive to your emotional state and actively monitor how such feelings are affecting your decision-making."], "translations": ["拥有竞争对手能让你坚定地致力于实现目标，并提升你的整体表现。但在你走出去寻找一位企业家来竞争并超越之前，了解并避开竞争往往伴随的陷阱非常重要。毕竟，激烈竞争也会阻碍有效决策，并增加你冒险的意愿——这些行为最终可能会损害你创业项目的成功。", "找到一个你立志要超越的对手，是保持专注于目标、推动创业项目迈向新高度的好方法。然而，当你全神贯注于胜过对手时，你可能会开始滋生一种“不惜一切代价获胜”的心态，从而忽视自己取得成功的方式。例如，一组研究人员考察了竞争与不道德行为之间的联系。他们发现，当人们与对手竞争时，更愿意采取不道德的行为来取胜。但这种行为可能会玷污你的声誉，并使那些对你成功至关重要的关系变得紧张。避免这一陷阱的一种方法，就是停下来反思什么才是重要的。虽然超越对手可能会带来短期利益，但丧失诚信将会产生长期后果。", "拥有竞争对手能够提升你创业表现的一个原因在于，它会激发一定程度的兴奋感，驱使你更加努力地工作。但这种急于求胜的渴望也可能会损害你创业项目的成功，尤其是在它促使你做出冲动、不明智的决定时。不过，通过养成进行批判性思考的习惯——例如考虑相反观点和开展成本效益分析，尤其是针对那些复杂且可能决定项目未来的决策——你就有可能避免这类代价高昂的错误。", "拥有竞争对手所带来的急切心理，不仅会导致你做出更糟糕的决定，还会促使你冒更大的风险，使你的创业项目陷入危险境地。要克服竞争所诱发、并可能危及创业成功的冒险倾向，一个方法就是持续关注自己的情绪状态，并积极监控这些情绪如何影响你的决策。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How can competitive rivalry benefit entrepreneurs according to the passage?", "options": ["By enabling them to outcompete other entrepreneurs.", "By enabling them to make their venture a success.", "By helping them to reach long-term goals.", "By helping them to stay goal-oriented."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Having a rival can keep you committed to achieving your goals and enhance your overall performance.", "explanation": "本题考察竞争对创业者的积极作用。定位文章第一段首句，原文指出拥有竞争对手能让你坚定致力于实现目标（committed to achieving your goals），并提升整体表现；第二段首句也进一步说明，立志超越对手有助于保持专注于目标并将事业推向新高度。选项D中的保持目标导向（stay goal-oriented）正是对原文“致力于实现目标”与“专注于目标”的精准同义转述，符合题干所问益处，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "选项A把“寻找对手去超越”这一前提动作偷换成了竞争带来的结果；选项B属过度推理，原文仅说提升表现或推向新高度，并非确保创业成功；选项C将后文“长期后果”偷换为“长期目标”，属于拼凑干扰。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is one of the traps entrepreneurs may often fall into when competing with rivals?", "options": ["They may adopt strategies that are bound to ruin their venture.", "They may resort to unethical means to outperform their rivals.", "They may be too eager to succeed while ignoring the huge labor cost.", "They may be intently focused on winning at the current market level."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "They found that when people compete against their rivals, they are more willing to behave unethically to win.", "explanation": "本题询问创业者在与对手竞争时常会陷入哪种陷阱。定位第二段，该段指出当人全神贯注于胜过对手时，容易产生不惜一切代价获胜的心态，并援引研究说明人们与对手竞争时更愿意采取不道德行为来取胜（behave unethically to win），随后明确将此称为这一陷阱。选项B中“采取不道德手段胜过对手”精准对应原文的“不道德行为”及“超越对手”，故选B。", "trapNote": "选项A中“注定毁掉事业”属过度推理，原文仅言有损成功或陷入危险；选项C将“忽视成功方式”偷换为“忽视巨额人工成本”，属于无中生有；选项D将“超越对手”偷换为在当前市场层级取胜，偏离文意。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What are entrepreneurs advised to do to avoid traps that often accompany rivalry?", "options": ["Deliberate on what really matters.", "Prioritize reaping immediate benefits.", "Estimate the long-term consequences.", "Reflect on what successes are achievable."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "One way to avoid this trap is to stop and reflect on what's important.", "explanation": "本题询问创业者应如何避免伴随竞争而来的陷阱。定位第二段倒数第二句，针对前文提到的竞争陷阱，作者明确给出的规避方法是停下来反思什么才是重要的（stop and reflect on what's important）。对比各选项，选项A中“深思真正重要的事物”与原文形成精准同义替换，其中“深思”对应“停下来反思”，“真正重要的事物”对应“什么是重要的”，故选A。", "trapNote": "选项B与原文正反颠倒，作者警示追逐短期利益而丧失诚信会带来长期恶果，而非让优先获取眼前利益；选项C将“丧失诚信有长期后果”曲解为去估算长期后果；选项D把“重要的事”偷换为“可实现的成功”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How can entrepreneurs avoid making impulsive and insensible decisions?", "options": ["By engaging themselves in critical reasoning.", "By developing a habit of keeping their integrity.", "By criticizing themselves for previous poor performances.", "By refraining from being too excited about their successes."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "But it's possible to avoid such costly mistakes by making a habit of engaging in critical thinking, such as considering opposing viewpoints and conducting cost-benefit analyses, especially for those decisions that are complex and can determine the future of your venture.", "explanation": "本题询问如何避免做出冲动且不明智的决定。定位第三段第二、三句，前句指出急于求胜会导致创业者做出冲动不明智的决定，紧接着作者给出解决方案，即养成进行批判性思维（engaging in critical thinking）的习惯，比如考虑相反观点和进行成本效益分析。选项A中“投身于批判性推理”准确对应原文的批判性思维习惯，故正确答案为A。", "trapNote": "选项B将第二段的“诚信”与本段的“养成习惯”跨段拼凑，属于偷换概念；选项C利用形近词设障，把“批判性思维”曲解为“因过去表现差而自我批评”；选项D的“克制对成功的兴奋”偏离原文急于求胜的语境。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How can entrepreneurs overcome the risk-inducing effects of rivalry?", "options": ["By paying close attention to their current performance.", "By taking steps that stand to endanger their rivals' success.", "By monitoring how their decision-making impacts their mentality.", "By keeping their emotions in check to avoid making poor decisions."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "One way you can overcome the risk-inducing effects of rivalry that stand to endanger your venture's success is to remain attentive to your emotional state and actively monitor how such feelings are affecting your decision-making.", "explanation": "本题询问如何克服竞争带来的诱发风险的效应。定位第四段第二句，原文明确提出解决之道在于持续关注自身情绪状态（remain attentive to your emotional state），并积极监控这些情绪如何影响决策，从而避免更糟糕的决定与危及创业的风险。选项D中“控制好自己的情绪以避免做出糟糕决定”精准概括了监控情绪、防范不良决策的核心含义，故选D。", "trapNote": "选项A将关注“情绪状态”偷换为关注“当前表现”；选项B把“危及自身事业”正反颠倒为采取行动危及“对手的成功”；选项C因果倒置，原文要求监控“情绪如何影响决策”，而非决策如何影响心态。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 在竞争中胜过，击败", "note": "合成动词（out- 表示“胜过、超过”）；常与 outperform 互换，后直接接竞争对象作宾语。", "word": "outcompete"}, {"gloss": "v. 使紧张，使承受压力", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“拉伤、品系”，在职场/关系语境中常考“使关系紧张”（如 strain relationships），常与 stain（玷污）构成形近辨析。", "word": "strain"}, {"gloss": "n. 诚信，正直；完整", "note": "四级高频抽象名词，文中指“职业操守与诚信”（the loss of your integrity），在商业伦理类阅读中出现频率极高。", "word": "integrity"}, {"gloss": "adj. 冲动的，草率的", "note": "源自 impulse（冲动），常与 insensible（不明智的）并列，用以描述情绪驱动下的非理性决策，反义思路对应 critical thinking。", "word": "impulsive"}, {"gloss": "n. 严重危险，险境", "note": "固定搭配 put ... in peril（使……陷入险境），与 endanger（危及）语义相通，属写作与阅读的书面高级替换词。", "word": "peril"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "After all, competitive rivalry can also hinder effective decision-making and increase your willingness to take risks, behaviors that can ultimately hurt your venture's success.", "point": "识别抽象名词短语（如 behaviors）作前面并列行为的同位语，有助于快速理清长难句的总结性评价成分。", "structure": "主句为 competitive rivalry can also hinder... and increase...；behaviors that can... 为前面两个动宾短语的同位语，其中嵌套 that 引导的定语从句修饰 behaviors。", "zh": "毕竟，激烈竞争也会阻碍有效决策，并增加你冒险的意愿——这些行为最终可能会损害你创业项目的成功。"}, {"en": "But it's possible to avoid such costly mistakes by making a habit of engaging in critical thinking, such as considering opposing viewpoints and conducting cost-benefit analyses, especially for those decisions that are complex and can determine the future of your venture.", "point": "把握 by doing 方式状语与 such as 列举成分的嵌套结构，可精准定位细节题中的“解决措施”考点。", "structure": "形式主语结构 it's possible to avoid...；by making a habit of... 作方式状语；such as... 为介词短语举例说明 critical thinking；especially for those decisions 后接 that 引导的定语从句。", "zh": "不过，通过养成进行批判性思考的习惯——例如考虑相反观点和开展成本效益分析，尤其是针对那些复杂且可能决定项目未来的决策——你就有可能避免这类代价高昂的错误。"}, {"en": "One way you can overcome the risk-inducing effects of rivalry that stand to endanger your venture's success is to remain attentive to your emotional state and actively monitor how such feelings are affecting your decision-making.", "point": "长主语中多层定语从句叠加时，先找准核心系动词 is，即可明确“方法（One way）是什么”这一高频设题点。", "structure": "主语为 One way，后接省略关系词的定语从句 you can overcome...，其中 that stand to endanger... 修饰 effects of rivalry；表语为并列不定式 to remain... and actively monitor...，含 how 引导的宾语从句。", "zh": "要克服竞争所诱发、并可能危及创业成功的冒险倾向，一个方法就是持续关注自己的情绪状态，并积极监控这些情绪如何影响你的决策。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "短语概括为合成形容词：committed to / focused on goals 替换为 goal-oriented（以目标为导向的）。", "option": "stay goal-oriented", "original": "keep you committed to achieving your goals / stay focused on your goals"}, {"note": "动作具体化替换：behave unethically（表现不道德）替换为 resort to unethical means（采取不道德手段）。", "option": "resort to unethical means to outperform their rivals", "original": "when people compete against their rivals, they are more willing to behave unethically to win"}, {"note": "高频动词与同义表达替换：reflect on 替换为 deliberate on（深思熟虑）；important 替换为 matters。", "option": "deliberate on what really matters", "original": "stop and reflect on what's important"}, {"note": "核心名词替换：thinking（思考）替换为 reasoning（推理），搭配反身代词构成等价动词短语。", "option": "engaging themselves in critical reasoning", "original": "engaging in critical thinking"}, {"note": "意图概括替换：密切关注并监控情绪对决策的影响，归纳为 keep emotions in check（控制情绪）。", "option": "keeping their emotions in check to avoid making poor decisions", "original": "remain attentive to your emotional state and actively monitor how such feelings are affecting your decision-making"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202312-s2-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 四级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 四级真题 第2套 Passage Two", "title": "多任务处理：科学真相与职场视角", "subtitle": "认知科学与职场管理 · 多任务能力剖析", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 344, "paragraphs": ["A multitasker is one who can perform two or more tasks effectively at the same time, which - apart from the obvious differences - is similar to what a computer does. The concept does indeed come from the realms of technology, where it is used to refer to an operating system that can execute multiple tasks at the same time. However, the question is: can a person really be a multitasker?", "For most scientists, the answer is no. So much so that, according to experts in neuroscience (神经系统科学), our brains do not handle multitasking situations well. As soon as two tasks require our attention, productivity suffers. What we call multitasking, therefore, is in reality the ability to move more or less quickly from one task to another. This requires two essential conditions: that one of the tasks needs to be automatic, like walking or eating, and that they both need different mental processes. Answering the phone and writing at the same time, for example.", "However, on the other side of the coin there are people who maintain that it is possible to be, or at least seem to be, multitasking. A recent study concluded that regardless of whether people are actually handling several tasks or not, the mere fact that they perceive this activity as multitasking has a positive effect on their performance.", "The business perspective offers a different view: multitasking is understood as the ability to adapt to all types of environment within a company and effectively undertake different activities within a set time frame. Indeed, many companies look for people who are skilled in multitasking to improve their productivity. From this different perspective, you can not only be multitasking but this ability can also be taught: something that is easier in fluid organizations, which favor flexibility in their working practices.", "The benefits of multitasking are clear. Being quicker and more efficient increases our performance and the number of tasks completed. But having to pay attention to several things at once means that the powers of concentration are reduced and that can lead to more mistakes."], "translations": ["多任务处理者是指能够同时有效执行两项或多项任务的人——除了显而易见的差异之外，这与计算机所做的事相似。这一概念确实源自技术领域，在该领域中它被用来指代能够同时执行多项任务的操作系统。然而，问题在于：人真的能成为多任务处理者吗？", "对大多数科学家而言，答案是否定的。甚至可以说，据神经系统科学专家介绍，我们的大脑并不擅长应对多任务处理的情形。只要有两项任务需要我们投入注意力，效率就会下降。因此，我们所谓的多任务处理，实际上是或快或慢地从一项任务切换到另一项任务的能力。这需要两个必要条件：其中一项任务必须是自动化的（如走路或吃饭），且两项任务需要不同的心理加工过程。例如，一边接电话一边写字。", "然而，从另一面来看，也有人主张做到——或者至少看起来做到——多任务处理是可能的。最近的一项研究得出结论：无论人们实际上是否在同时处理多项任务，仅仅是“将这一活动视为多任务处理”这一感知本身，就能对其表现产生积极影响。", "商业视角则提供了不同的看法：多任务处理被理解为适应公司内部各类环境、并在规定时间框架内有效承担不同活动的能力。事实上，许多公司都在寻找擅长多任务处理的人才，以提高生产力。从这一不同的视角来看，人不仅能够进行多任务处理，而且这种能力也是可以教授的：这一点在推崇灵活工作方式的流动性组织中更容易实现。", "多任务处理的好处显而易见。速度更快、效率更高能提升我们的表现并增加完成的任务数量。但同时关注多件事情意味着专注力会下降，而这可能会导致更多的失误。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does \"multitasker\" originally refer to?", "options": ["An operating system capable of doing several tasks at once.", "A skilled worker executing more than one task at the same time.", "A sophisticated technology doing several tasks effectively at once.", "An efficient person able to perform multiple tasks at the same time."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The concept does indeed come from the realms of technology, where it is used to refer to an operating system that can execute multiple tasks at the same time.", "explanation": "本题询问“多任务处理者”这一概念最初指代什么。定位第一段第二句，原文明确交代了它的词源背景：这一概念确实源自技术领域，在该领域中它被用来指代“能够同时执行多项任务的操作系统”（operating system）。将其与四个选项逐一比对，选项A中的“能够同时完成几项任务的操作系统”正是对原文技术定义的精准同义转述，符合题干“最初指代”的限定，故正确答案为A。", "trapNote": "选项B、D分别偷换为“熟练工人”和“高效的人”，虽照应首句人类定义，却忽略了题干“最初指代”（originally）的时间与来源限定；选项C将“操作系统”偷换为“精密技术”，属于概念偷换。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why can't people really be multitaskers according to neuroscientists?", "options": ["They are not sufficiently exposed to multitasking situations.", "They are not comparable to mechanical operating systems.", "Their brains do not allow them to multitask.", "Their attention span cannot be expanded."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "So much so that, according to experts in neuroscience (神经系统科学), our brains do not handle multitasking situations well.", "explanation": "本题询问为什么神经科学家认为人无法真正做到多任务处理。定位第二段第二、三句，神经系统科学专家指出，我们的大脑并不擅长处理多任务情形，只要两项任务同时需要注意力，工作效率就会受损；我们所谓的多任务实际上只是任务间的快速切换。由此可知大脑机制限制了人同时处理多任务，选项C“他们的大脑不允许他们进行多任务处理”高度概括该句意，故选C。", "trapNote": "选项A的“没有充分接触多任务情境”属于无中生有；选项B把首段“与电脑存在差异”拼凑为“无法与机械操作系统相比”，属于跨段干扰；选项D中“注意力持续时间无法延长”在文中并无依据。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the conclusion of a recent study on multitasking?", "options": ["People make greater achievements by maintaining whatever they are doing is multitasking.", "People's performance benefits from the perception of what they are doing as multitasking.", "People's active mental processes exert a positive effect on their multitasking.", "People can improve their capabilities by handling multitasking situations."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "A recent study concluded that regardless of whether people are actually handling several tasks or not, the mere fact that they perceive this activity as multitasking has a positive effect on their performance.", "explanation": "本题考察第三段中近期研究得出的结论。定位第三段末句，该研究指出，无论人们实际上是否同时处理多项任务，仅仅是把这一活动感知为多任务处理，就会对他们的表现产生积极影响（positive effect）。选项B中“人们的表现受益于将所做之事感知为多任务处理”在表述上以“受益于”同义替换“产生积极影响”，精准对应原文结论，故正确答案为B。", "trapNote": "选项A将首句的“主张”（maintain）杂糅进研究结论，且过度引申为“取得更大成就”；选项C把第二段的“心理过程”张冠李戴；选项D与原文“无论是否真的在同时处理多项任务”相悖。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How does the business world view multitasking?", "options": ["It is a rare skill often found in fluid organisations.", "It is an adaptable capability required of all workers.", "It is an essential quality many employees lack.", "It is a desirable ability that can be developed."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Indeed, many companies look for people who are skilled in multitasking to improve their productivity. From this different perspective, you can not only be multitasking but this ability can also be taught: something that is easier in fluid organizations, which favor flexibility in their working practices.", "explanation": "本题询问商业界如何看待多任务处理能力。定位第四段第二、三句，原文先提到许多企业都会物色擅长多任务处理的人才以提高生产力，说明这是一种备受青睐的能力；紧接着指出从这一视角看，这种能力也是可以教授培养的（can also be taught）。选项D中“一种受欢迎且可被培养的能力”精准概括了“企业争相寻找”与“可以教授”两大关键信息，故正确答案为D。", "trapNote": "选项A把“在流动性组织中更容易教授”曲解为“常见于其中的稀有技能”；选项B的“所有员工都必须具备”属绝对化过度推理；选项C的“许多员工缺乏”在原文中并未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the author imply we should do if we have to focus on some task and do it well?", "options": ["Work in a flexible way.", "Learn from mistakes.", "Avoid multitasking.", "Increase efficiency."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "But having to pay attention to several things at once means that the powers of concentration are reduced and that can lead to more mistakes.", "explanation": "本题为推断题，询问若要专注做好某项任务，作者暗示我们应当怎么做。定位文章末段最后一句，作者在肯定多任务处理能提高效率后进行转折，指出同时关注多件事会导致专注力下降（powers of concentration are reduced），进而引发更多失误。由此反推可知，若想保持专注并把任务做好、减少错误，就应当避免多任务处理，因此选C。", "trapNote": "选项A的“灵活工作”源自第四段组织特性，与如何集中注意力做好任务无关；选项B的“从错误中学习”属于望文生义曲解；选项D的“提高效率”是前句提及的多任务益处，而非需要专注时的建议。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 领域，范围；王国", "note": "常与 of 连用，如 the realms of technology（技术领域），在科普和社科类阅读中相当于 field 或 domain。", "word": "realm"}, {"gloss": "v. 执行，实施", "note": "熟词僻义：除“处决”外，在计算机与管理语境中高频考“执行任务/计划”（execute multiple tasks）。", "word": "execute"}, {"gloss": "v. 坚持认为，主张；维持", "note": "熟词僻义：四级阅读核心考点词，后接 that 从句时多译为“主张、声称”，而非普通的“维持、保养”。", "word": "maintain"}, {"gloss": "v. 感知，看待，理解", "note": "常考搭配 perceive A as B（将 A 视为 B），其名词形式 perception（感知/认知）常在选项中作同义转换。", "word": "perceive"}, {"gloss": "adj. 灵活多变的，流畅的；流体的", "note": "熟词僻义：本义为“液体的/流体的”，文中 fluid organizations 指结构灵活、富有弹性的组织（与后文 flexibility 呼应）。", "word": "fluid"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "This requires two essential conditions: that one of the tasks needs to be automatic, like walking or eating, and that they both need different mental processes.", "point": "注意冒号后的并列 that 从句均为条件说明，阅读中见到此类结构需提炼出并列要点（条件一和条件二）。", "structure": "冒号后为两个并列的 that 引导的同位语从句，具体解释说明前面的 two essential conditions；like walking or eating 作举例状语修饰 automatic。", "zh": "这需要两个必要条件：其中一项任务必须是自动化的（如走路或吃饭），且两项任务需要不同的心理加工过程。"}, {"en": "A recent study concluded that regardless of whether people are actually handling several tasks or not, the mere fact that they perceive this activity as multitasking has a positive effect on their performance.", "point": "无论……与否（regardless of whether...）常引出被否定的背景或陪衬条件，真正的逻辑重心在后面的主句结论上。", "structure": "concluded 后接 that 引导的宾语从句；宾语从句内部先由 regardless of whether... or not 作让步状语，主句部分为 the mere fact... has a positive effect...，其中包含 that 引导的同位语从句解释 fact。", "zh": "最近的一项研究得出结论：无论人们实际上是否在同时处理多项任务，仅仅是“将这一活动视为多任务处理”这一感知本身，就能对其表现产生积极影响。"}, {"en": "From this different perspective, you can not only be multitasking but this ability can also be taught: something that is easier in fluid organizations, which favor flexibility in their working practices.", "point": "识别“not only... but also...”的递进重心（后者往往是出题核心），以及 something 指代前文整件事的用法。", "structure": "not only... but also... 连接两个并列分句；冒号后的 something 为前面“ability can be taught”的同位语，其后接 that 限制性定语从句和 which 非限制性定语从句逐层修饰。", "zh": "从这一不同的视角来看，人不仅能够进行多任务处理，而且这种能力也是可以教授的：这一点在推崇灵活工作方式的流动性组织中更容易实现。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "高频等价替换：execute 替换为 do；multiple 替换为 several；at the same time 替换为 at once。", "option": "an operating system capable of doing several tasks at once", "original": "an operating system that can execute multiple tasks at the same time"}, {"note": "主旨概括替换：大脑无法很好地处理多任务情形，归纳为大脑不允许人类真正实现多任务。", "option": "their brains do not allow them to multitask", "original": "our brains do not handle multitasking situations well"}, {"note": "词性与语态/主被动视角转换：动词 perceive 转为名词 perception；has a positive effect on 转为 benefits from。", "option": "performance benefits from the perception of what they are doing as multitasking", "original": "perceive this activity as multitasking has a positive effect on their performance"}, {"note": "跨句整合替换：企业争相寻找的能力对应 desirable（抢手的/受欢迎的）；can be taught 对应 can be developed。", "option": "a desirable ability that can be developed", "original": "many companies look for people who are skilled in multitasking ... this ability can also be taught"}, {"note": "因果反推替换：多任务会降低专注力并增加失误，从而反推出“若想专注做好任务就应避免多任务”。", "option": "avoid multitasking", "original": "paying attention to several things at once means that the powers of concentration are reduced and that can lead to more mistakes"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202312-s3-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 四级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 四级真题 第3套 Passage One", "title": "传奇赛马Red Rum的逆袭之路", "subtitle": "体育传记类 · 克服伤病夺冠与体坛长盛美誉", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 348, "paragraphs": ["In the history of horse racing, few horses have captured the affection of the British public like Red Rum. Today, three decades after his retirement, he is still one of the best-known and most beloved racehorses of all time.", "Red Rum was passed around to several owners before being purchased for Noel Le Mar. The agent who made the purchase was the now-legendary horse trainer Donald \"Ginger\" McCain.", "It wasn't apparent at the time, but Red Rum had a serious bone disease in his foot. For many horses (and many trainers) this would mean the end of a racing career before it even began. For Ginger and Red Rum, though, it was just an obstacle to greatness that had to be overcome.", "Red Rum's true talent came out in steeplechases (障碍赛马). His power, speed, and jumping ability carried him to his first Grand National title in 1973. The very next year, Red Rum returned to take his second title. He was the first horse to take successive firsts since Reynoldstown in 1935-1936. Red Rum's spirit and grace had already begun to charm the leagues of Grand National fans.", "In the following two years, Red Rum lost out on the title, coming in second both times. When he returned in 1977 to try again, he was largely regarded as past his prime. He was 12 years old and not expected to place highly. He surprised sporting fans around the world when he came in a remarkable 25 lengths ahead of the nearest horse, taking his third Grand National win. To this day, Red Rum's third win is known as one of the greatest moments in horse racing history.", "Red Rum was headed for the Grand National once again in 1978 but suffered an injury in one of his heels shortly before the race. He was retired soon after, but his public life and fame by no means decreased with the end of his career. Red Rum traveled all over the country for various engagements. He often led pre-race parades at Aintree Racecourse and was a popular guest at charity benefits and public events."], "translations": ["在赛马史上，很少有马能像“红朗姆”（Red Rum）那样赢得英国民众的喜爱。如今，在他退役三十年后，他依然是有史以来最知名、最受爱戴的赛马之一。", "“红朗姆”在被买下送给诺埃尔·勒马尔之前，曾几经易主。促成这笔交易的代理人正是如今已成为传奇的驯马师唐纳德·“金杰”·麦凯恩。", "当时这并不明显，但“红朗姆”的脚部患有严重的骨病。对许多马匹（以及许多驯马师）而言，这意味着赛马生涯尚未开始就已宣告终结。然而，对金杰和“红朗姆”来说，这只是通往伟大之路上必须克服的一道障碍。", "“红朗姆”真正的天赋在障碍赛马中展现了出来。他的力量、速度和跳跃能力助力他在1973年首次夺得英国国家障碍赛马大赛冠军。就在次年，“红朗姆”重返赛场拿下第二个冠军，成为自1935至1936年“雷诺兹敦”之后第一匹蝉联冠军的赛马。他的精神与优雅风姿已开始迷倒大批该赛事的马迷。", "在随后的两年里，“红朗姆”均与冠军失之交臂，两次屈居亚军。当他在1977年重返赛场再次冲冠时，人们普遍认为他已过巅峰期。当时他已12岁，并不被看好能取得靠前的名次。然而他却以领先最近对手整整25个马身的惊人优势夺得第三个英国国家障碍赛马大赛冠军，令全球体育迷大感惊喜。时至今日，“红朗姆”的第三次夺冠仍被誉为赛马史上最伟大的时刻之一。", "1978年，“红朗姆”原本准备再次出征英国国家障碍赛马大赛，但在赛前不久一只脚跟受了伤。不久后他便退役，但他的公众生活与声望并未随着竞赛生涯的结束而减弱。“红朗姆”奔赴全国各地参加各类活动，他常在安特里赛马场领衔赛前巡游，也是慈善义演和各类公共活动上备受欢迎的嘉宾。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about Red Rum the racehorse?", "options": ["He captured public affection long before he won national titles.", "He won enormous fame and love from British people.", "He became a myth three decades after his retirement.", "He owed his great success to several well-known horse trainers."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "In the history of horse racing, few horses have captured the affection of the British public like Red Rum. Today, three decades after his retirement, he is still one of the best-known and most beloved racehorses of all time.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第一段。首句以否定结构强调，在赛马史上几乎没有马匹能像他那样赢得英国公众的深切喜爱（affection）；次句进一步指出，即便在他退役三十年后的今天，他依然是有史以来最知名（best-known）、最受爱戴的赛马之一。选项B将原文表述精准同义改写为从英国民众处赢得了巨大声望与爱戴，与第一段主旨完全吻合，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项时间错位，吸引车迷是在夺冠后而非夺冠前很久；C项偷换概念，原文指退役三十年后依然知名，而非“成为神话”；D项偷换概念，原文指其曾属多位马主，仅提及一位传奇驯马师。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did the serious bone disease in Red Rum's foot mean to himself and his trainer?", "options": ["It was simply a hindrance they had to get over to excel.", "It was surely a disadvantage though not considered fatal.", "It was actually the end of a racing career that had just begun.", "It was really a major obstacle hard to overcome on their own."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "For Ginger and Red Rum, though, it was just an obstacle to greatness that had to be overcome.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第三段。前文先指出Red Rum脚部患有严重骨病，对大多数马匹和驯马师而言这意味着赛马生涯未启先终；接着第三句以转折词though引出核心态度，说明对驯马师金杰和Red Rum来说，这只是通往伟大之路上必须克服的一道障碍（an obstacle to greatness that had to be overcome）。A项中hindrance对应obstacle，get over对应overcome，to excel对应to greatness，完美契合原文，故选A。", "trapNote": "C项张冠李戴且曲解时态，赛马生涯尚未开始便终结是对其他多数马匹而言；B项无中生有，原文并未探讨该病是否致命；D项程度失真，原文强调只是“一道障碍”，而非仅靠自身难以克服的重大障碍。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say Red Rum did with his power, speed, and jumping ability?", "options": ["He won his first Grand National title at 12.", "He took two firsts successively in 1935-1936.", "He surprised sporting fans worldwide in 1973.", "He took three Grand National wins in the 1970s."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "His power, speed, and jumping ability carried him to his first Grand National title in 1973. The very next year, Red Rum returned to take his second title.", "explanation": "本题定位第四、五段。第四段明确提及Red Rum的力量、速度和跳跃能力帮助他在1973年赢得首个英国国家障碍赛马大赛冠军，并在次年即1974年再夺第二冠；随后第五段又交代他在1977年再次出战并赢得个人第三个该项赛事冠军。1973年、1974年和1977年均在二十世纪七十年代之内，因此他在七十年代共三次赢得该大赛冠军，选项D表述准确无误，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项张冠李戴，12岁时赢得的是第三次而非第一次冠军；B项张冠李戴，1935至1936年两连冠的是雷诺兹敦而非Red Rum；C项偷换时间，令全球体育迷惊喜发生在1977年第三次夺冠时，而非1973年。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did people generally think of Red Rum when he returned to the racecourse in 1977?", "options": ["He had already passed the peak of his racing life.", "He would have no rival in Grand National steeplechases.", "He had lost his charm with the leagues of Grand National fans.", "He could be expected to repeat his glory in the prime of his career."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "When he returned in 1977 to try again, he was largely regarded as past his prime. He was 12 years old and not expected to place highly.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第五段第二、三句。原文明确交代，当Red Rum于1977年重返赛场再次尝试夺冠时，外界普遍认为他已经过了自己的全盛巅峰期（past his prime），而且当时他已经12岁，大家并不看好他能获得靠前的名次。选项A用已经过了赛马生涯的巅峰期精准同义改写了原文的已过全盛期，而人们普遍认为也准确对应了原文中的被普遍视为，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "D项正反颠倒，原文明确指出他当时不被看好且已过巅峰期，而非被期待重现巅峰辉煌；B项无中生有且与文意相悖；C项偷换概念，原文只说人们认为他体能下滑，并未说他失去了对马迷的魅力。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What became of Red Rum after his career ended?", "options": ["He suffered from severe pain in a heel.", "He spent almost all his time traveling.", "He lived on various charity benefits.", "He remained famous and popular."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "He was retired soon after, but his public life and fame by no means decreased with the end of his career.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第六段第二至四句。原文在交代他1978年赛前脚跟受伤并于不久后退役后，立即用转折句指出，他的公众生活和声望绝未随着职业生涯的结束而减弱（by no means decreased）；紧接着补充他奔赴全国各地出席活动，常在赛马场领衔巡游，也是慈善义演和公共活动的受欢迎嘉宾。选项D将其概括为依然知名且广受欢迎，全面准确地反映了原文内容，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项偷换时间，脚跟受伤发生在1978年退役前的赛前而非退役后，且未提及剧痛；B项过度推理，“奔赴各地参加活动”不等同于“几乎所有时间都在奔波”；C项偷换概念，参加慈善活动并非靠慈善救济维生。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "喜爱，钟爱", "note": "四级高频情感名词；capture the affection of... 意为“赢得……的喜爱”，常与 love、fondness 构成同义替换。", "word": "affection"}, {"gloss": "障碍，阻碍", "note": "常考搭配 an obstacle to sth（通往某事的障碍，注意介词用 to）；真题中常被 hindrance、barrier 同义替换。", "word": "obstacle"}, {"gloss": "连续的，接连的", "note": "注意辨析：successive 表示“连续的、接踵而至的”（take successive firsts 即“蝉联冠军”），切勿与 successful（成功的）混淆。", "word": "successive"}, {"gloss": "全盛时期，巅峰期", "note": "熟词僻义：作形容词常见义为“首要的、优质的”，此处作名词表示“鼎盛期”；常用固定搭配 past one's prime（已过巅峰期）。", "word": "prime"}, {"gloss": "（公开）活动安排，邀约", "note": "熟词僻义：除“订婚、交战”外，在新闻人物传记中常指“预约、公务活动或商业演出邀约”（various engagements）。", "word": "engagement"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "He surprised sporting fans around the world when he came in a remarkable 25 lengths ahead of the nearest horse, taking his third Grand National win.", "point": "注意动词短语 come in（获得某名次）及长度量词 lengths ahead of 的赛马语境用法，以及现在分词短语 taking... 补充说明结果/伴随动作。", "structure": "主句（He surprised...）+ when引导的时间状语从句（when he came in...）+ 现在分词短语作伴随状语（taking his third Grand National win）", "zh": "他以领先最近对手整整25个马身的惊人优势率先冲线，拿下个人第三个英国国家障碍赛马大赛冠军，令全球体育迷大感惊喜。"}, {"en": "For Ginger and Red Rum, though, it was just an obstacle to greatness that had to be overcome.", "point": "考点在于识别句中插入语 though 表转折（“然而”），以及定语从句 that had to be overcome 修饰先行词 an obstacle（而非 greatness），且被动语态与第47题选项 get over 构成同义替换。", "structure": "状语（For Ginger and Red Rum）+ 插入语（though）+ 主系表（it was just an obstacle to greatness）+ that引导的定语从句（that had to be overcome）", "zh": "然而，对于金杰和“红朗姆”而言，这只是通往伟大之路上必须克服的一道障碍。"}, {"en": "Red Rum was passed around to several owners before being purchased for Noel Le Mar.", "point": "before 后接动名词被动式 being purchased，主语与逻辑主语一致均为 Red Rum；注意区分 owners（马主）与下文 trainer（驯马师），避免第46题D项的偷换概念陷阱。", "structure": "主语（Red Rum）+ 被动语态谓语（was passed around to...）+ 介词短语作时间状语（before being purchased for...）", "zh": "“红朗姆”在被买下交给诺埃尔·勒马尔之前，曾在多名马主之间几经转手。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "Q46正确改写：affection与beloved对应love，best-known对应enormous fame。", "option": "won enormous fame and love from British people", "original": "captured the affection of the British public / best-known and most beloved"}, {"note": "Q47高频同义替换：obstacle→hindrance（障碍），overcome→get over（克服），greatness→excel（卓越）。", "option": "a hindrance they had to get over to excel", "original": "an obstacle to greatness that had to be overcome"}, {"note": "Q49同义改写：largely regarded as对应generally think，past one's prime（过巅峰期）对应passed the peak。", "option": "had already passed the peak of his racing life", "original": "largely regarded as past his prime"}, {"note": "Q50反话正说改写：by no means decreased（绝未减弱）对应remained（保持）。", "option": "remained famous and popular", "original": "his public life and fame by no means decreased ... was a popular guest"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202312-s3-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 四级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 四级真题 第3套 Passage Two", "title": "直觉与数据：如何做出最佳决策", "subtitle": "商业决策类 · 直觉经验与系统数据分析的融合", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 347, "paragraphs": ["People in business often make decisions based on their own personal feelings or instincts. It is quite horrifying to see people being guided by some unknown force. But how wise is it, really, to let your instincts drive your decisions?", "In the decision-making process, relying on instincts only makes sense when you have a vast experience to support you. Simply \"feeling\" that something is right or should be done is highly subjective and can drown you.", "On the other hand, there is a more rational approach to making decisions. Data and analysis have long been associated with informed decisions. These reduce the likelihood of errors and increase the chances of success. Big, systematic data is mostly the foundation of most of our decisions, personal and business alike. But with its extreme usability comes a complication: what do you do if you strongly feel something should not be done, even if the data insists that it should?", "This seemingly easy question is what drives the need to understand the relationship between instincts and data in the decision-making process. Without making things complicated, the solution to this dilemma is using data and instincts in conjunction to arrive at the best possible decisions.", "Instinctive decisions are always backed by previous experiences or information, which acknowledges that instinctive decisions have worked in the past. Decisions are not about making the choice and braving the consequences because you want to blindly trust your instincts. They are about combining your inner wisdom with the knowledge of systematic data to make the best decisions.", "Sometimes, rational analysis and data are impractical to be employed in certain situations. Absence of definitive criteria, and time and resource constraints, and novel situations are instances which limit the practicality of data. The only feasible option is to rely on what your instincts tell you. In these situations, instincts can help you make effective and quick decisions.", "Combining instinctive and rational analysis produces well-rounded decisions. It reduces the chances of making mistakes, and has increasingly become a favorite approach to decision-making among leaders of today."], "translations": ["商界人士经常基于个人感受或直觉来做决定。看到人们受某种未知力量引导着实令人担忧。但让直觉主导你的决策，究竟有多明智呢？", "在决策过程中，只有当你拥有丰富的经验作为支撑时，依赖直觉才合理。仅仅“感觉”某件事是对的或应该去做，具有高度主观性，甚至可能将你拖入困境。", "另一方面，还存在一种更为理性的决策方式。长期以来，数据与分析一直与明智的决策紧密相连，它们能降低出错的可能性并提高成功几率。庞大而系统的数据大多是我们大多数个人与商业决策的基础。然而，伴随其极高实用性而来的还有一个棘手问题：即便数据坚持认为某件事可行，但你却强烈感觉不该去做，此时你该如何应对？", "正是这个看似简单的问题，促使我们有必要厘清决策过程中直觉与数据之间的关系。不必把事情复杂化，解决这一两难困境的办法就是将数据和直觉结合使用，从而做出尽可能最佳的决策。", "凭直觉做出的决策总是以过往经验或信息为后盾，这也认可了直觉决策在过去曾发挥过作用。做决策并不是为了盲目信任直觉而做出选择并硬着头皮承担后果，而是要将内在智慧与系统数据知识结合起来，以做出最佳决策。", "有时，理性分析和数据在特定情境下并不切实际。缺乏明确标准、时间和资源受限以及全新局面，都是限制数据实用性的情形。此时唯一可行的选择就是信赖你的直觉告诉你的判断。在这些情况下，直觉能帮助你做出高效且迅速的决策。", "将直觉分析与理性分析相结合能够产生全面周详的决策。这种做法降低了犯错几率，并日益成为当今领导者青睐的决策方式。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say businesspeople often do?", "options": ["Strive to make sense of some unknown forces.", "Avoid being driven by their own feelings.", "Draw on a vast wealth of past experience.", "Rely on instincts in decision-making."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "People in business often make decisions based on their own personal feelings or instincts.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第一段第一句。作者在开篇便明确指出，商界人士（business）经常仅仅依据个人的主观感受或直觉（instincts）来做出各种决策。题干中的商界人士直接对应首句主语，而选项D则将“基于直觉做决定”精准同义改写为在决策过程中依赖直觉，完美符合原文首句所述事实，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，第一段只是作者旁观感慨受未知力量引导令人担忧，并非商界人士努力去理解这些力量；B项正反颠倒；C项张冠李戴，第二段是说依赖直觉需以丰富经验为前提，而非他们经常这样做。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What should we take into account in order to make informed decisions?", "options": ["The likelihood of errors.", "Systematic data and analysis.", "The complexity of circumstances.", "Personal feelings and business strategies."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Data and analysis have long been associated with informed decisions. These reduce the likelihood of errors and increase the chances of success. Big, systematic data is mostly the foundation of most of our decisions, personal and business alike.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第三段。该段开篇引出理性的决策方法，明确指出长期以来数据与分析一直与明智的决策（informed decisions）紧密相关，它们能够减少出错概率并提升成功率；第四句进一步强调，庞大而系统的数据大多是我们多数个人和商业决策的基础。由此可知，做出明智决策应当考虑系统的（systematic）数据与分析，B项完全吻合原文，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项因果倒置，数据与分析能够降低“出错的可能性”，而非决策时要去重点考虑出错可能性；C项无中生有；D项偷换概念，原文指系统数据是个人和商业决策的基础，而非个人感受与商业策略。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What should people do in a decision-making process if instincts disagree with data?", "options": ["Resolve the dilemma with previous experience.", "Figure out which of the two is more reliable.", "Combine the two together.", "Prioritize instincts over data."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Without making things complicated, the solution to this dilemma is using data and instincts in conjunction to arrive at the best possible decisions.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第三段末句及第四段。第三段末尾提出了一个典型困境：当直觉强烈认为某事不该做，而数据却坚持认为应当去做时该如何应对。第四段随即给出了明确解答，指出解决这一两难局面的办法就是将数据和直觉结合使用（using data and instincts in conjunction），以达成最佳决策。选项C“将两者结合起来”精准对应这一解决方案，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项张冠李戴，第五段提及直觉决策背后有以往经验支撑，并非仅靠过往经验即可解决直觉与数据的冲突；B项无中生有，原文并未要求分辨何者更可靠；D项以偏概全，与“两者结合”相悖。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What should we do when facing various factors that limit the practicality of data?", "options": ["Make a rational and systematic analysis.", "Explore the most feasible options.", "Resort to our inner wisdom.", "Apply definitive criteria."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Absence of definitive criteria, and time and resource constraints, and novel situations are instances which limit the practicality of data. The only feasible option is to rely on what your instincts tell you.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第六段前两句并结合第五段。第六段指出缺乏明确标准、时间与资源限制以及全新局面都会限制数据的实用性（limit the practicality of data），在此类情境下唯一可行的选择就是依赖直觉告诉你的判断。同时第五段将直觉同义表述为内在智慧（inner wisdom）。因此，选项C“求助于我们的内在智慧”精准呼应原文，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项正反颠倒，第六段首句明确指出在特定情况下理性分析与数据并不切实际；B项偷换概念，原文指依赖直觉是“唯一可行选择”，而非探索多种可行方案；D项正反颠倒，此处正是由于缺乏明确标准才导致数据受限。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does it take for decisions to become the best according to the author?", "options": ["Applying instincts and data in conjunction.", "Assessing all factors when making a choice.", "Recalling what has actually worked in the past.", "Refraining from trusting instincts arbitrarily."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Without making things complicated, the solution to this dilemma is using data and instincts in conjunction to arrive at the best possible decisions.", "explanation": "本题定位文章第四、五及第七段。第四段明确指出将数据和直觉结合使用（in conjunction）才能做出尽可能最佳的决策；第五段再次重申，决策是要将内在智慧与系统数据知识结合起来以做出最佳决策；第七段尾段也呼应了“将直觉分析与理性分析相结合能产生全面决策”的中心观点。选项A“将直觉与数据结合应用”直接复现了核心短语，与全文主旨高度一致，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "C、D两项均属于以偏概全，分别只片面抽取了第五段中“过去经验有效”或“不能盲目信任直觉”的局部信息，均遗漏了“结合系统数据”这一核心条件；B项“评估所有因素”则属于无中生有且表意过于宽泛。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "直觉，本能", "note": "全文核心高频词；形容词形式为 instinctive（直觉的），在阅读中常被 inner wisdom 或 gut feeling 同义替换。", "word": "instinct"}, {"gloss": "复杂情况，棘手难题", "note": "熟词僻义：除医学中“并发症”外，在议论文语境下多指“使局势复杂化的新问题、难题”，常引出转折或矛盾点。", "word": "complication"}, {"gloss": "结合，协同，联合", "note": "四级真题高频核心短语 in conjunction (with) 表示“与……共同/结合使用”，常与 combine... with... 构成同义替换。", "word": "conjunction"}, {"gloss": "明确的，决定性的，权威的", "note": "由 define 派生而来；absence of definitive criteria 指“缺乏明确的评判标准”，注意勿与 definite（确切的）混淆用法侧重。", "word": "definitive"}, {"gloss": "可行的，行得通的", "note": "议论文高频形容词，常与 practical、viable 构成同义词组；文中 the only feasible option 对应“唯一可行的选择”。", "word": "feasible"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "But with its extreme usability comes a complication: what do you do if you strongly feel something should not be done, even if the data insists that it should?", "point": "考点包括介词短语置句首时的完全倒装结构，以及句尾省略结构 that it should [be done]；此句同时作为第53题的命题起点，引出下文核心解决方案。", "structure": "介词短语提前引起的完全倒装句（with its extreme usability comes a complication）+ 冒号后同位语解释疑问句（含if条件状语从句与even if让步状语从句，末尾should后承前省略be done）", "zh": "然而，伴随其极高实用性而来的还有一个棘手问题：即便数据坚持认为某件事应该做，但你却强烈感觉不该去做，此时你该如何应对？"}, {"en": "Without making things complicated, the solution to this dilemma is using data and instincts in conjunction to arrive at the best possible decisions.", "point": "注意固定搭配 the solution to（……的解决办法，介词用 to）与 in conjunction（结合、协同），此结构直接命中第53题和第55题的正确答案。", "structure": "介词短语作方式状语（Without making things complicated）+ 主语（the solution to this dilemma）+ 系动词（is）+ 动名词短语作表语（using data and instincts in conjunction...）+ 不定式作目的状语", "zh": "不必把事情复杂化，解决这一两难困境的办法就是将数据和直觉结合使用，以做出尽可能最佳的决策。"}, {"en": "Decisions are not about making the choice and braving the consequences because you want to blindly trust your instincts.", "point": "高频熟词僻义：动词 brave 此处不表示“勇敢”，而作及物动词意为“勇敢面对、冒着（风险/后果）”（brave the consequences）；与下文 They are about... 构成“不是……而是……”对比句型。", "structure": "主系表（Decisions are not about...并列动名词making...and braving...）+ because引导的原因状语从句", "zh": "做决策并不是因为想盲目信任直觉而做出选择并硬着头皮承担后果。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "Q51同义改写：based on（基于）替换为 rely on（依赖），make decisions 替换为名词化短语 in decision-making。", "option": "Rely on instincts in decision-making", "original": "make decisions based on their own personal feelings or instincts"}, {"note": "Q52信息整合改写：将第三段第二句的 data and analysis 与第四句的 systematic data 合并概括为选项B。", "option": "Systematic data and analysis", "original": "Data and analysis ... systematic data is mostly the foundation"}, {"note": "Q53与Q55双题复用考点：in conjunction（协同/结合）直接对应 combine together 与 applying... in conjunction。", "option": "Combine the two together / Applying instincts and data in conjunction", "original": "using data and instincts in conjunction"}, {"note": "Q54跨段同义替换：第六段的 instincts 与第五段的 inner wisdom（内在智慧）互为同义词，rely on 替换为 resort to（求助于）。", "option": "Resort to our inner wisdom", "original": "rely on what your instincts tell you / inner wisdom"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202306-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "大房子与公共空间：美国住房伦理反思", "subtitle": "社会观察 · 住宅扩张与公共空间萎缩", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 349, "paragraphs": ["The United States is facing a housing crisis: Affordable housing is inadequate, while luxury homes abound (充裕), and homelessness remains a persistent problem. Despite this, popular culture and the housing industry market happiness as living with both more space and more amenities (便利设施). Big houses are advertised as a reward for hard work and diligence, turning housing from a basic necessity into a luxury.", "This is reflected in our homes. The average single-family home built in the United States before 1970 was less than 1,500 square feet in size. By 2016, the average size of a new, single-family home was 2,422 square feet. What's more, homes built in the 2000s were more likely than earlier models to have more of all types of spaces: bedrooms, bathrooms, living rooms, dining rooms, recreation rooms and garages.", "There are consequences of living big. As middle-class houses have grown larger, two things have happened. First, large houses take time to maintain, so cleaners and other low-wage service workers are required to keep these houses in order. Second, once-public spaces, where people from diverse backgrounds used to come together, have increasingly become privatized, leading to a reduction in the number of public facilities available to all, and a reduced quality of life for many. Take swimming pools. While in 1950, only 2,500 U.S. families owned pools, by 1999 this number was 4 million. At the same time, public municipal pools were often closed, leaving low-income people nowhere to swim.", "The trend for bigger housing thus poses ethical questions. Should Americans accept a system in which the middle and upper classes enjoy a luxurious lifestyle, using the low-wage labor of others? Are we willing to accept a system in which an increase in amenities purchased by the affluent means a reduction in amenities for the poor?", "I believe neither is acceptable. We must change the way we think: living well does not need to mean having more private spaces; instead, it could mean having more public spaces. A better goal than building bigger houses for some is to create more publicly accessible spaces and amenities for all."], "translations": ["美国正面临一场住房危机：经济适用房供应不足，而豪华住宅却十分充裕，无家可归依然是一个长期存在的问题。尽管如此，流行文化和房地产行业仍将幸福营销为拥有更大的居住空间和更多的便利设施。大房子被宣传为对努力工作和勤奋的回报，从而把住房从一种基本生活必需品变成了奢侈品。", "这一点在我们的住宅中有所体现。1970年以前美国建造的独栋住宅平均面积不到1500平方英尺；而到2016年，新建独栋住宅的平均面积已达到2422平方英尺。此外，21世纪初建造的住宅比早期户型更有可能在各类空间上都变得更大、更多，包括卧室、浴室、客厅、餐厅、娱乐室和车库。", "追求大房子会带来一系列后果。随着中产阶级住宅面积不断扩大，出现了两件事。首先，大房子需要耗费时间打理，因此需要雇佣清洁工和其他低薪服务人员来维持房屋整洁。其次，曾经供不同背景人群聚会的公共空间日益私有化，导致面向大众的公共设施数量减少，许多人的生活质量也随之下降。以游泳池为例，1950年全美只有2500个家庭拥有私人泳池，而到1999年这一数字已达到400万；与此同时，市政公共泳池却常常关闭，使得低收入人群无处游泳。", "因此，住宅面积日益扩大的趋势引发了伦理问题。美国人是否应该接受这样一个体系——中产阶级和上层阶级依靠他人的低薪劳动来享受奢华的生活方式？我们又是否愿意接受这样一个体系——富人购买的便利设施增加，就意味着穷人所能享有的公共设施减少？", "我认为这两种情况都不可接受。我们必须改变思维方式：过上体面的生活并不一定意味着拥有更多的私人空间；相反，它可以意味着拥有更多的公共空间。与为部分人建造更大的房子相比，一个更好的目标是为所有人创造更多向公众开放的空间和便利设施。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What are big houses promoted to be in the United States?", "options": ["A luxury for the homeless.", "A reward for industriousness.", "An abundant source of comforts.", "An absolute necessity for happiness."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Big houses are advertised as a reward for hard work and diligence, turning housing from a basic necessity into a luxury.", "explanation": "定位第一段末句。题干问大房子在美国被宣传成什么，promoted to be对应原文are advertised as。原文明确指出，大房子被宣传为“努力工作和勤奋的回报”(a reward for hard work and diligence)。选项B中的industriousness(勤劳、勤奋)精准同义替换原文的hard work and diligence，因此B项为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，将第一段提及的无家可归问题与大房子变成了奢侈品拼凑在一起；D项正反颠倒，原文指把住房从基本必需品变成奢侈品，并非幸福的绝对必需品。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is one of the consequences of living big?", "options": ["Many Americans' quality of life has become lower.", "People from diverse backgrounds no longer socialize.", "People no longer have access to public swimming pools.", "Many Americans' private life has been negatively affected."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Second, once-public spaces, where people from diverse backgrounds used to come together, have increasingly become privatized, leading to a reduction in the number of public facilities available to all, and a reduced quality of life for many.", "explanation": "定位第三段。段首句点明主旨，随后指出大房潮带来的两项后果，其中第二项指出公共空间日益私有化，导致面向大众的公共设施减少，并造成许多人的生活质量下降(a reduced quality of life for many)。选项A中的quality of life has become lower精准对应原文，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项过度推理，原文仅指公共聚会空间私有化，并未说不同背景的人不再社交；C项以偏概全且绝对化，原文仅说市政泳池常关闭使低收入者无处游泳，而非所有人。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What questions arise from living big?", "options": ["Questions related to moral principles.", "Questions having to do with labor cost.", "Questions about what lifestyle to promote.", "Questions concerning housing development."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The trend for bigger housing thus poses ethical questions.", "explanation": "定位第四段首句。原文明确指出，住房面积日益扩大的趋势由此引发了伦理问题(poses ethical questions)。紧接着的两个问句分别探讨中上阶层利用他人低薪劳动享受奢华生活是否妥当，以及富人设施增加以穷人设施减少为代价是否合理。选项A中的moral principles(道德原则)精准同义替换ethical，故A为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项偷换概念，文中提及low-wage labor是为了引出社会公平与伦理拷问，并非讨论劳动力成本；C、D两项偏离段首核心词ethical，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What kind of social system does the author think is unacceptable?", "options": ["One in which the wealthy exploit the low-wage laborers building their houses.", "One in which the rich purchase amenities at an increasingly unjustifiable price.", "One in which the upper classes deprive the lower classes of affordable housing.", "One in which the affluent enjoy a more comfortable life at the expense of the poor."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Are we willing to accept a system in which an increase in amenities purchased by the affluent means a reduction in amenities for the poor?", "explanation": "定位第四段后两句及第五段首句。第四段连用两个反问句描述不平等的社会体系，第五段首句I believe neither is acceptable明确表态两者都不可接受。其中第四段末句指出富人购买更多便利设施就意味着穷人享有的设施减少，D项中的enjoy a more comfortable life at the expense of the poor正是对此逻辑的精准同义概括。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，第三段指低薪工人负责打理房屋而非建房(building)；B项将设施增多曲解为价格不合理；C项把公共设施减少偷换为剥夺经济适用房。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author advocate for people to live well?", "options": ["Finding ways to turn private spaces into public ones.", "Building more houses affordable to those less affluent.", "More public spaces created for everyone to enjoy.", "All amenities made accessible to the rich and the poor alike."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "A better goal than building bigger houses for some is to create more publicly accessible spaces and amenities for all.", "explanation": "定位第五段。作者呼吁转变观念，指出“活得好”不等于拥有更多私人空间，而可以意味着拥有更多公共空间(having more public spaces)。段末进一步强调，更好的目标是为所有人创造更多向公众开放的空间和便利设施(for all)。选项C中的More public spaces created for everyone to enjoy正是对末句的精准同义转述，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，原文主张创造更多公共空间而非把私人空间改造成公共空间；D项偷换范围且绝对化，把原文的more(更多开放设施)夸大为All amenities(全部设施)。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 大量存在，充裕", "note": "熟词/高频阅读词：常与 in/with 连用，本文作不及物动词（luxury homes abound）。", "word": "abound"}, {"gloss": "n. 便利设施，生活设施", "note": "真题常考复数形式 amenities，指社区泳池、公园或住宅配套便利设施。", "word": "amenity"}, {"gloss": "v. 使私有化，转归私营", "note": "由 private + -ize 构成，与 public（公共的）形成反义对比，是社会议论文高频词。", "word": "privatize"}, {"gloss": "adj. 富裕的，富足的", "note": "常考名词化用法 the affluent（富人阶层），与 the poor 构成对应，近义于 wealthy/rich。", "word": "affluent"}, {"gloss": "n. 勤奋，勤勉", "note": "形容词为 diligent；第46题中与 hard work 一起被同义替换为 industriousness。", "word": "diligence"}, {"gloss": "adj. 可进入的，可使用的", "note": "常用搭配 be accessible to sb.；文中 publicly accessible spaces 指面向公众开放的空间。", "word": "accessible"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Second, once-public spaces, where people from diverse backgrounds used to come together, have increasingly become privatized, leading to a reduction in the number of public facilities available to all, and a reduced quality of life for many.", "point": "非限制性定语从句 + 现在分词作结果状语，精准定位第47题细节。", "structure": "主句为 once-public spaces have increasingly become privatized；where 引导非限制性定语从句修饰 spaces；leading to... 为现在分词短语作结果状语，其后并列两个名词短语作宾语。", "zh": "其次，曾经供不同背景的人相聚的公共空间日益私有化，导致面向所有人的公共设施数量减少，并使许多人的生活质量下降。"}, {"en": "Big houses are advertised as a reward for hard work and diligence, turning housing from a basic necessity into a luxury.", "point": "be advertised as 搭配及现在分词结果状语，对应第46题。", "structure": "主句为被动语态 Big houses are advertised as...；turning... into... 为现在分词短语作结果状语，说明前文宣传做法造成的后果。", "zh": "大房子被宣传为对努力工作和勤奋的奖赏，从而将住房从基本生活必需品变成了奢侈品。"}, {"en": "Are we willing to accept a system in which an increase in amenities purchased by the affluent means a reduction in amenities for the poor?", "point": "介词+关系代词定语从句嵌套过去分词后置定语，支撑第49题理解。", "structure": "in which 引导定语从句修饰 a system；从句主语为 an increase in amenities，其中 purchased by the affluent 为过去分词短语作后置定语修饰 amenities，谓语为 means。", "zh": "我们是否愿意接受这样一个体系：富人购买的便利设施增加，就意味着穷人所拥有的便利设施减少？"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "advertise 与 promote 同义（宣传推广），hard work and diligence 凝练替换为名词 industriousness（勤奋）。", "option": "promoted to be a reward for industriousness", "original": "advertised as a reward for hard work and diligence"}, {"note": "名词短语 a reduced quality of life 转换为动词句型 quality of life has become lower。", "option": "Many Americans' quality of life has become lower", "original": "a reduced quality of life for many"}, {"note": "形容词 ethical（伦理的、道德的）同义替换为介词短语 related to moral principles。", "option": "Questions related to moral principles", "original": "poses ethical questions"}, {"note": "具体现象上升为抽象逻辑：此消彼长的资源分配替换为 at the expense of（以……为代价）。", "option": "the affluent enjoy a more comfortable life at the expense of the poor", "original": "an increase in amenities purchased by the affluent means a reduction in amenities for the poor"}, {"note": "publicly accessible spaces 替换为 public spaces，for all 对应 for everyone to enjoy。", "option": "More public spaces created for everyone to enjoy", "original": "create more publicly accessible spaces and amenities for all"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202306-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "雄心的双刃剑：创业成功与幸福健康", "subtitle": "商业心理与个人成长 · 适度雄心的智慧", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 351, "paragraphs": ["Most of us in the entrepreneurial community are blessed — or cursed — with higher-than-average ambition. Ambitious people strongly desire accomplishments and are willing to take more risks and spend more effort to get them.", "Overall, this is a positive quality, especially for people trying to build their own businesses. Apparently, if you're more naturally driven to set goals, you are more likely to succeed.", "Actually, this isn't always the case. In fact, in some cases, extreme ambition may end up doing more harm than good.", "One major side effect of excessive ambition is the tendency to focus too determinedly on one particular vision or end goal. This is problematic because it hinders your ability to adapt to new circumstances, which is vital if you want to be a successful entrepreneur. If a new competitor emerges to threaten your business, you may need to change direction, even if that means straying from your original vision. If you have too much ambition, you'll find this hard, if not impossible.", "Few people are successful when they try to build their first brand. Unfortunately, for the most ambitious entrepreneurs, a failure is seen as disastrous, and impossible to recover from.", "It's a clear departure from the intended plan toward the intended goal. For people with limited ambition, however, failure is viewed as something closer to reality. Remember, failure is inevitable, and every failure you survive is a learning experience.", "Ambitious people tend to be more materialistically successful than their non-ambitious counterparts. However, they're only slightly happier than their less-ambitious counterparts, and tend to live significantly shorter lives. This implies that even though ambitious people are more likely to achieve conventional “success,” such success means nothing for their health and happiness — and if you don't have health and happiness, what else could possibly matter?", "Clearly, some amount of ambition is good for your motivation. Without any ambition, you wouldn't start your own business, set or achieve goals and get far in life. But an excess of ambition can also be dangerous, putting you at risk of burnout, stubbornness and even a shorter life."], "translations": ["创业圈里的大多数人都很幸运——或者说不幸——拥有高于常人的雄心壮志。有抱负的人强烈渴望取得成就，并愿意承担更多风险、付出更多努力去实现目标。", "总体而言，这是一种积极的品质，对试图创办自己企业的人来说尤为如此。显然，如果你天生更有动力去设定目标，你就更有可能获得成功。", "实际上，情况并非总是如此。事实上，在某些情况下，极端的雄心最终可能会弊大于利。", "过度雄心的一个主要副作用，是倾向于过于执着地盯着某一个特定愿景或最终目标。这会带来问题，因为它会阻碍你适应新环境的能力——而如果你想成为一名成功的企业家，这种能力至关重要。如果出现新的竞争对手威胁你的业务，你可能需要改变方向，即便这意味着偏离最初的愿景。如果你的雄心过盛，你会发现做到这一点很难，甚至是不可能的。", "很少有人在尝试打造自己的第一个品牌时就能取得成功。遗憾的是，对最有雄心的创业者而言，一次失败会被视为灾难性的，而且根本无法从中恢复。", "这是对通往既定目标的既定计划的明显偏离。然而，对于雄心有限的人来说，失败被视为更贴近现实的事物。请记住，失败是不可避免的，而你挺过来的每一次失败都是一次学习经历。", "有雄心的人往往比没有雄心的人在物质上更成功。然而，他们只比雄心较弱的人稍微快乐一点，寿命却往往明显更短。这意味着，尽管有雄心的人更有可能获得传统意义上的“成功”，但这种成功对他们的健康和幸福毫无意义——而如果你没有健康和幸福，还有什么能真正重要呢？", "显然，一定程度的雄心有益于激发动力。如果没有任何雄心，你就不会去创业、设定或实现目标，也难以在人生中走远。但过度的雄心同样可能很危险，会让你面临精疲力竭、固执己见甚至寿命缩短的风险。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author think of most entrepreneurs?", "options": ["They are more willing to risk their own lives.", "They are more ambitious than ordinary people.", "They achieve greater nonconventional success.", "They have more positive qualities than most of us."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Most of us in the entrepreneurial community are blessed — or cursed — with higher-than-average ambition.", "explanation": "定位第一段首句。作者指出，创业群体中的大多数人都拥有高于平均水平的雄心(higher-than-average ambition)。选项B中的more ambitious than ordinary people（比普通人更有雄心）正是对该短语的同义转述，而most entrepreneurs对应entrepreneurial community的大多数人，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，将第一段的take more risks(承担更多风险)曲解为冒生命危险；C项正反颠倒，原文第七段指出获得的是常规成功，而非非常规成功；D项以偏概全。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the author imply by saying “this isn't always the case” (Line 1, Para.3)?", "options": ["Ambitious people may not have a greater chance of success.", "Ambitious people may not have more positive qualities.", "Entrepreneurs' ambition does as much good as harm.", "Entrepreneurs are more naturally driven to success."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Actually, this isn't always the case. In fact, in some cases, extreme ambition may end up doing more harm than good.", "explanation": "定位第三段首句并回看第二段末句。第二段结尾提出一般看法：天生更有动力设定目标的人更有可能成功(more likely to succeed)。第三段首句以Actually转折指出“情况并非总是如此”，句中this指代前一句关于“更可能成功”的论断。由此可推断，有雄心的人并不一定拥有更大的成功机会，A项准确传达了这一反驳意味。", "trapNote": "B项指代错误，this回指上一句“更可能成功”，而非“更多积极品质”；C项曲解文意，第三段指极端雄心有时“弊大于利”(more harm than good)，并非利弊相等；D项偷换了转折前的旧观点。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say is of extreme importance for one to become a successful entrepreneur?", "options": ["Holding on to one's original vision.", "Being able to adapt to new situations.", "Focusing determinedly on one particular goal.", "Avoiding radical change in one's career direction."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "This is problematic because it hinders your ability to adapt to new circumstances, which is vital if you want to be a successful entrepreneur.", "explanation": "定位第四段第二句。题干中of extreme importance对应原文非限制性定语从句中的vital（至关重要的）。原文指出，适应新环境的能力(ability to adapt to new circumstances)对成为成功创业者至关重要；B项用new situations同义替换new circumstances，精准对应，故选B。", "trapNote": "A、C、D三项均为正反颠倒。第四段明确把执着于单一目标、固守原有愿景列为过度雄心的弊端，且指出面对竞争者时可能需要改变方向，而非回避改变。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How do the most ambitious entrepreneurs regard failure in their endeavor?", "options": ["It will awaken them to reality.", "It is a lesson they have to learn.", "It means the end of their career.", "It will result in a slow recovery."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Unfortunately, for the most ambitious entrepreneurs, a failure is seen as disastrous, and impossible to recover from.", "explanation": "定位第五段第二句。题干询问最有雄心的创业者如何看待失败。原文指出，对他们而言，失败被视为灾难性的、且无法从中恢复(disastrous, and impossible to recover from)。无法挽回即意味着事业的终结，与C项means the end of their career高度契合。", "trapNote": "A项张冠李戴，第六段指“雄心有限的人”把失败看作更接近现实，且“唤醒”属于曲解；B项把作者给读者的建议错安在极具雄心者身上；D项把“不可能恢复”偷换为“缓慢恢复”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the author advise us to do concerning ambition?", "options": ["Distinguish between conventional success and our life goal.", "Follow the example of the most ambitious entrepreneurs.", "Avoid taking unnecessary risks when starting a business.", "Prioritize health and happiness over material success."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "This implies that even though ambitious people are more likely to achieve conventional “success,” such success means nothing for their health and happiness — and if you don't have health and happiness, what else could possibly matter?", "explanation": "定位第七段。作者先指出雄心勃勃的人在物质上更成功(materialistically successful)，但寿命却明显更短；末句通过反问强调，传统意义上的“成功”对健康与幸福毫无意义，没有健康和幸福，还有什么能重要呢？结合第八段对过度雄心缩短寿命的警示，可推断作者建议将健康与幸福置于物质成功之上，即D项。", "trapNote": "A项无中生有，全文未讨论“人生目标”与“传统成功”的区分；B项正反颠倒，作者多次警示过度雄心的危害；C项偷换概念，文中未建议创业时回避不必要的风险。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 创业的，企业家的", "note": "核心派生词：名词 entrepreneur（创业者），entrepreneurial community 指创业群体。", "word": "entrepreneurial"}, {"gloss": "v. 阻碍，妨碍", "note": "四级高频动词，近义于 impede/obstruct；文中 hinder one's ability to do sth. 表“阻碍做某事的能力”。", "word": "hinder"}, {"gloss": "v. 偏离，迷失", "note": "熟词/常考搭配 stray from（偏离，如偏离最初愿景）；作形容词时可指“走失的，零星的”。", "word": "stray"}, {"gloss": "adj. 不可避免的，必然发生的", "note": "否定前缀 in- + evitable（可避免的）；常在议论文中修饰 failure、change、consequence 等名词。", "word": "inevitable"}, {"gloss": "n. 对应方，处于同等地位的人", "note": "阅读对比类句型高频词，如 non-ambitious counterparts（没有雄心的同类人群）。", "word": "counterpart"}, {"gloss": "n. 精疲力竭，职业倦怠", "note": "由动词短语 burn out 合成，常与压力、过度工作或过度雄心（an excess of ambition）搭配出现。", "word": "burnout"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "This is problematic because it hinders your ability to adapt to new circumstances, which is vital if you want to be a successful entrepreneur.", "point": "原因状语从句嵌套非限制性定语从句及条件从句，直接考查第53题。", "structure": "主句为 This is problematic；because 引导原因状语从句；which 引导非限制性定语从句修饰前面的名词短语 your ability to adapt to new circumstances，该从句中又嵌套 if 引导的条件状语从句。", "zh": "这是个问题，因为它会阻碍你适应新环境的能力，而如果你想成为一名成功的创业者，这种能力至关重要。"}, {"en": "If a new competitor emerges to threaten your business, you may need to change direction, even if that means straying from your original vision.", "point": "条件从句+让步从句+mean doing 搭配，帮助排除第53题干扰项。", "structure": "If 引导条件状语从句，其中不定式 to threaten... 作目的或结果状语；主句为 you may need to change direction；even if 引导让步状语从句，means 后接动名词短语 straying from... 作宾语。", "zh": "如果出现新的竞争对手威胁你的业务，你可能需要改变方向，即便这意味着偏离最初的愿景。"}, {"en": "This implies that even though ambitious people are more likely to achieve conventional “success,” such success means nothing for their health and happiness — and if you don't have health and happiness, what else could possibly matter?", "point": "多层复合宾语从句配反问修辞，是第55题推断作者建议的关键句。", "structure": "implies 后接 that 引导的宾语从句，从句内含 even though 引导的让步状语从句；破折号后用 if 条件句加反问句收尾，强化作者态度。", "zh": "这意味着，尽管有雄心的人更有可能取得传统意义上的“成功”，但这种成功对他们的健康和幸福毫无意义——而如果你没有健康和幸福，还有什么能真正重要呢？"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "higher-than-average ambition（高于平均水平的雄心）改写为比较级形容词结构 more ambitious than ordinary people。", "option": "They are more ambitious than ordinary people", "original": "Most of us in the entrepreneurial community are blessed — or cursed — with higher-than-average ambition"}, {"note": "more likely to succeed 被 isn't always the case 否定，转换为情态否定 may not have a greater chance of success。", "option": "Ambitious people may not have a greater chance of success", "original": "if you're more naturally driven to set goals, you are more likely to succeed. Actually, this isn't always the case."}, {"note": "ability to adapt 变为动名词短语 Being able to adapt，circumstances 替换为同义词 situations，vital 对应 of extreme importance。", "option": "Being able to adapt to new situations", "original": "your ability to adapt to new circumstances, which is vital if you want to be a successful entrepreneur"}, {"note": "对“灾难性的且无法恢复”作合理推演，归结为意味着事业终结（the end of their career）。", "option": "It means the end of their career", "original": "a failure is seen as disastrous, and impossible to recover from"}, {"note": "反问句“没有健康与幸福还能有什么重要”转化为祈使建议“将健康和幸福置于物质成功之上”。", "option": "Prioritize health and happiness over material success", "original": "materialistically successful ... if you don't have health and happiness, what else could possibly matter?"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202306-s2-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 四级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 四级真题 第2套 Passage One", "title": "美国超市的演变与营销策略", "subtitle": "社会商业史 · 零售变革、消费心理与超市布局剖析", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 349, "paragraphs": ["Supermarkets have long been suffering as one of the thinnest-margined businesses in existence and one of the least-looked-forward-to places to work or visit. For more than a decade, they have been under attack from e-commerce giants, blamed for making Americans fat, and accused of contributing to climate change.", "Supermarkets can technically be defined as giants housing 15,000 to 60,000 different products. The revolutionary idea of a self-service grocery, where people could hunt and gather food from aisles rather than asking a clerk to fetch items from behind a counter, first came about in America. There is some debate about which was the very first, but over the years a consensus has built around King Kullen Supermarket, founded in New York in 1930.", "For some 300 years, Americans had fed themselves from small stores and public markets. Shopping for food involved mud, noisy chickens, clouds of flies, nasty smells, bargaining, and getting short-changed. The supermarket imitated the Fordist factory, with its emphasis on efficiency and standardization, and reimagined it as a place to buy food. Supermarkets may not feel cutting-edge now, but they were a revolution in distribution at the time. They were such strange marvels that, on her first official state visit to the United States in 1957, Queen Elizabeth II insisted on an impromptu (即兴的) tour of a suburban-Maryland Giant Food.", "The typical supermarket layout has barely changed over the past 90 years. Most stores open with flowers, fruit and vegetables at the front as a breath of freshness to arouse our appetite. Meanwhile, they keep the milk, eggs, and other daily basics all the way back so you'll travel through as much of the store as possible, and be tempted along the way.", "In the early days, as the supermarket multiplied, so did our suspicion of it. We have long feared that this “revolution in distribution” uses corporate black magic on our appetite. The book The Hidden Persuaders, published in 1957, warned that supermarkets were putting women in a “hypnoidal trance (催眠恍惚状态),” causing them to wander aisles bumping into boxes and “picking things off shelves at random.”"], "translations": ["长期以来，超市一直处境艰难，是现存利润率最低的行业之一，也是人们最不期待前去工作或光顾的场所之一。十多年来，它们一直受到电商巨头的冲击，被指责导致美国人肥胖，并被控加剧了气候变化。", "从技术层面上讲，超市可被定义为容纳1.5万至6万种不同商品的庞然大物。自助杂货店这一革命性理念最早诞生于美国——人们可以在货架通道间自行搜寻和挑选食物，而无需请店员从柜台后方拿取物品。关于究竟哪家是世界上第一家超市虽存有争议，但多年来人们已普遍公认是1930年创立于纽约的“金·卡伦超市”。", "大约300年来，美国人一直靠小商店和公共市场购买食物。采购食材往往伴随着泥泞、吵闹的鸡群、成群的苍蝇、难闻的气味、讨价还价以及找零短缺。超市效仿了注重效率与标准化的福特主义工厂模式，并将其重塑为购买食物的场所。如今超市或许不再显得前沿新潮，但在当时却是一场商品流通领域的革命。它们堪称奇观，以至于英国女王伊丽莎白二世在1957年首次对美国进行正式国事访问时，坚持要即兴参观马里兰州郊区的一家巨人食品超市。", "过去90年来，典型超市的布局几乎没有改变。大多数门店一进门便摆放鲜花、水果和蔬菜，以清新的气息唤起顾客的食欲。与此同时，它们把牛奶、鸡蛋和其他日常必需品放在门店最深处，这样你就会尽可能逛遍整个超市，并在途中经不住诱惑去买其他东西。", "在早期，随着超市数量成倍增长，人们对它的疑虑也与日俱增。长期以来，我们一直担心这场“流通革命”对我们的食欲施展了企业“黑魔法”。1957年出版的《隐蔽的说服者》一书警告称，超市正让女性陷入一种“催眠恍惚状态”，使她们在货架通道里漫无目的地徘徊、撞到箱子，并“随手从货架上乱拿东西”。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What problem have supermarkets been facing?", "options": ["They are actually on the way to bankruptcy.", "They have been losing customers and profits.", "They are forced to use e-commerce strategies.", "They have difficulty adapting to climate change."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Supermarkets have long been suffering as one of the thinnest-margined businesses in existence and one of the least-looked-forward-to places to work or visit. For more than a decade, they have been under attack from e-commerce giants, blamed for making Americans fat, and accused of contributing to climate change.", "explanation": "定位第一段。首句指出超市长期处境艰难，是现存利润率最低的行业之一（thinnest-margined），也是人们最不愿工作或光顾的场所之一；第二句接着指出，十多年来超市一直受到电商巨头的冲击，同时面临导致肥胖和加剧气候变化的指责。由此可知，超市正面临客源和利润受损的困境，B项“一直在流失顾客和利润”准确概括了上述问题，为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“濒临破产”属于过度推理，利润微薄不等于即将倒闭；C项“被迫采用电商策略”偷换概念，原文指遭受电商打击；D项“难以适应气候变化”正反颠倒，原文是被指责加剧气候变化。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about the idea of a self-service grocery?", "options": ["It was put forward by King Kullen.", "It originated in the United States.", "It has been under constant debate.", "It proves revolutionary even today."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The revolutionary idea of a self-service grocery, where people could hunt and gather food from aisles rather than asking a clerk to fetch items from behind a counter, first came about in America.", "explanation": "定位第二段第二句。该句明确指出，自助杂货店这一革命性理念——即顾客在货架通道间自行挑选食物，而无需请店员从柜台后拿取——最早诞生于美国（first came about in America）。题干询问关于自助杂货店理念的表述，B项“它起源于美国”精准同义转述了原文中最早出现于美国的表述，而该理念也成为现代超市发展的起点，因此选B。", "trapNote": "A项张冠李戴，金·卡伦超市是被公认的第一家超市，而非理念提出者；C项偷换概念，争议焦点是哪家超市最先成立且已有共识，并非理念本身争论不断；D项正反颠倒，第三段指出超市如今已不觉得前沿。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did supermarkets do by adopting the Fordist factory approach?", "options": ["They modernized traditional groceries in many ways.", "They introduced cutting-edge layout of their stores.", "They improved the quality of the food they sold.", "They revolutionized the distribution of goods."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The supermarket imitated the Fordist factory, with its emphasis on efficiency and standardization, and reimagined it as a place to buy food. Supermarkets may not feel cutting-edge now, but they were a revolution in distribution at the time.", "explanation": "定位第三段第三、四句。原文指出，超市效仿了注重效率与标准化的福特主义工厂模式，并将其重塑为购买食物的场所；紧接着第四句点明，虽然如今超市不再显得新潮，但在当时却是一场流通领域的革命（a revolution in distribution）。D项“它们彻底革新了商品的流通方式”精准对应原文中的流通革命，清晰体现了超市引入福特工厂模式的核心变革意义。", "trapNote": "A项无中生有，超市是一种全新的零售形态，并非在多方面改良传统杂货店；B项偷换概念，原文指超市如今不再显得前沿，且布局与福特模式无关；C项无中生有，文中未提及超市提升了食物品质。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What is the typical supermarket layout intended to do?", "options": ["Arouse customers' appetite to buy flowers, fruit and vegetables.", "Provide customers easy access to items they want to buy.", "Induce customers to make more unplanned purchases.", "Enable customers to have a more enjoyable shopping experience."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Meanwhile, they keep the milk, eggs, and other daily basics all the way back so you'll travel through as much of the store as possible, and be tempted along the way.", "explanation": "定位第四段。该段介绍超市过去九十年几乎未变的典型布局：门口摆放鲜花蔬果以唤起食欲，同时将牛奶、鸡蛋等日常必需品放在商店最深处，目的就是让顾客尽可能走遍整个卖场，并在途中受到沿途商品的诱惑（be tempted along the way）。由此可推断，这种布局旨在诱导顾客产生更多计划外的消费行为，C项“诱导顾客做出更多计划外购买”与文意完全吻合。", "trapNote": "A项以偏概全，门口的鲜花蔬果只为唤起食欲，并非仅促销这几类商品，忽视了把日用品放最里面的深层意图；B项正反颠倒，日用品放在最里面反而让顾客无法轻松拿取；D项无中生有，文中未提提升购物愉悦感。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What have people long feared about supermarkets?", "options": ["They use tricky strategies to promote their business.", "They are going to replace the local groceries entirely.", "They apply corporate black magic to the goods on display.", "They take advantage of the weaknesses of women shoppers."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "We have long feared that this “revolution in distribution” uses corporate black magic on our appetite.", "explanation": "定位第五段。第二句指出，长期以来人们一直担心这场“流通革命”会对我们的食欲施展企业“黑魔法”（corporate black magic），后文更引用著作警告超市让顾客陷入“催眠恍惚状态”并随手乱拿商品。此处“黑魔法”比喻超市隐蔽、狡猾的心理营销套路。A项“它们使用狡猾的策略来促销业务”准确阐释了这一比喻的实质含义，符合题意。", "trapNote": "C项属于典型偷换概念，原文指对“我们的食欲”施展黑魔法，而非对“陈列商品”使用；D项以偏概全，1957年书籍虽以女性购物者为例，但并未指超市专挑女性弱点下手；B项“完全取代本地杂货店”无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "利润率，利润空间", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“页边空白/边缘”，商业语境常指利润率；文中 thinnest-margined 意为“利润率极低的”。", "word": "margin"}, {"gloss": "去取来，拿来", "note": "高频阅读动词：指前往某处把人或物取来（go and bring back），区分于单纯的带走 take 或带来 bring。", "word": "fetch"}, {"gloss": "少找零钱；克扣", "note": "复合动词/过去分词：原指结账时少找零钱，引申为“亏待、欺骗（be short-changed）”。", "word": "short-change"}, {"gloss": "（商品的）流通，分销，配送", "note": "商科与经济类真题核心词：除“分布、分配”外，在供应链语境中特指商品分销流通。", "word": "distribution"}, {"gloss": "即兴的，未事先准备的", "note": "四级常见修饰语：括号内已作提示，常与 tour、speech、meeting 搭配，同义词有 spontaneous。", "word": "impromptu"}, {"gloss": "随意地，盲目地，无计划地", "note": "高频介词短语：文中指不加思考地随手乱拿；注意区分于 randomly 和随机抽样 random sampling。", "word": "at random"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The revolutionary idea of a self-service grocery, where people could hunt and gather food from aisles rather than asking a clerk to fetch items from behind a counter, first came about in America.", "point": "where 引导非限制性定语从句作地点/情境补充说明，搭配 rather than 表示动作取舍对比，理解时可将从句抽离，先抓主干 idea came about in America。", "structure": "主句为 The revolutionary idea of a self-service grocery ... first came about in America；中间嵌入 where 引导的非限制性定语从句修饰 grocery，其中包含 rather than 连接的并列对比动作结构。", "zh": "自助杂货店这一革命性理念最早诞生于美国——在这种商店里，人们可以在货架通道间自行搜寻和挑选食物，而无需请店员从柜台后方拿取物品。"}, {"en": "They were such strange marvels that, on her first official state visit to the United States in 1957, Queen Elizabeth II insisted on an impromptu (即兴的) tour of a suburban-Maryland Giant Food.", "point": "such + 名词短语 + that 构成结果状语从句，注意从句开头较长的介词短语作插入状语时需跨越它找准主语和谓语 insisted on。", "structure": "主干为 such ... that ... 引导的结果状语从句；that 从句中插入了时间与场合状语 on her first official state visit to the United States in 1957，主语是 Queen Elizabeth II，谓语为 insisted on。", "zh": "它们堪称奇妙的事物，以至于英国女王伊丽莎白二世在1957年首次对美国进行正式国事访问时，坚持要即兴参观马里兰州郊区的一家巨人食品超市。"}, {"en": "The book The Hidden Persuaders, published in 1957, warned that supermarkets were putting women in a “hypnoidal trance (催眠恍惚状态),” causing them to wander aisles bumping into boxes and “picking things off shelves at random.”", "point": "句中多层非谓语动词层层嵌套：过去分词作定语（published...）、现在分词作结果状语（causing...）及伴随动作（bumping... and picking...），需理清逻辑主语。", "structure": "主语为 The book The Hidden Persuaders（含同位语书名），published in 1957 为过去分词短语作后置定语；warned 后接 that 引导的宾语从句，从句后半部分 causing... 为现在分词短语作结果状语，且内部嵌套伴随分词 bumping... and picking...。", "zh": "1957年出版的《隐蔽的说服者》一书警告称，超市正让女性陷入一种“催眠恍惚状态”，致使她们在货架通道里逛来逛去、撞到箱子，并“随手从货架上乱拿东西”。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题核心替换：用利润微薄、最不愿光顾及电商冲击，概括推理出流失客源与利润。", "option": "losing customers and profits", "original": "one of the thinnest-margined businesses... least-looked-forward-to places to... visit; under attack from e-commerce giants"}, {"note": "第2题同义替换：came about（产生、出现）对应 originated（起源于），America 替换为 the United States。", "option": "originated in the United States", "original": "first came about in America"}, {"note": "第3题词性转换：名词短语 a revolution in distribution 转为动词短语 revolutionized the distribution of goods。", "option": "revolutionized the distribution of goods", "original": "were a revolution in distribution at the time"}, {"note": "第4题语意延伸：在途中受诱惑购买即“诱导做出更多计划外采购”。", "option": "induce customers to make more unplanned purchases", "original": "travel through as much of the store as possible, and be tempted along the way"}, {"note": "第5题比喻还原：把针对食欲的“企业黑魔法”具象化为“利用狡猾策略促销”。", "option": "use tricky strategies to promote their business", "original": "uses corporate black magic on our appetite"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202306-s2-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 四级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 四级真题 第2套 Passage Two", "title": "美国传统学制与全年制改革", "subtitle": "教育改革议题 · 农业社会传统假期与现代知识经济学制冲突", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 356, "paragraphs": ["The traditional school year, with three months of vacation every summer, was first implemented when America was an agricultural society and the summer months were needed for farm work. Since then, we've completely changed as a nation. Students no longer spend summers farming, but they aren't in school, either. The average American student receives 13 weeks off from school each calendar year - with about 11 of those during the summer. Few other countries have more than seven weeks off in a school calendar.", "With the U.S. lagging behind other countries in academics, it's time to consider year-round schooling. One benefit of this change is that students will not fall victim to the “summer slide,” or the well-documented phenomenon where students forget some of the knowledge they have acquired when too much time is taken off from school. Decades of research shows that it can take from 8 to 13 weeks at the beginning of every school year for students to get back to where they were before the summer holiday.", "But year-round schooling isn't just about academics. Teachers and students experience a closer relationship in year-round schools than they do in traditional schools and, in the absence of any long-term break, students do not feel detached from the school environment. These closer bonds and greater attachment pay off. Research shows that students in year-round schools are more self-confident and feel more positive about their schooling experience.", "But don't kids need time to relax? Some childhood development experts believe that time off from school is vital to healthy development as kids are not designed to spend so much of their time inside classrooms and the summer break provides a perfect opportunity to get outside. The problem with this argument is that most children aren't playing outside or even spending time with other kids. While some children visit summer camps, most stay at home, watching TV or playing games on electronic devices, which hardly benefits them.", "The U.S. has changed from a farming economy to a knowledge - and innovation - based economy, so it makes sense for the school year to change as well."], "translations": ["每年夏季拥有三个月假期的传统学年制，最初是在美国尚处于农业社会、夏季需要人力从事农活时实施的。自那以后，美国作为整个国家已经发生了翻天覆地的变化。学生们不再在夏天务农，但他们也不在学校上课。美国学生平均每年共有13周假期，其中约11周都在夏季。其他很少有国家在一个学年日历中拥有超过7周的假期。", "鉴于美国在学业成绩方面落后于其他国家，现在是时候考虑推行全年制上学了。这一改革的好处之一在于，学生不会沦为“暑期滑坡”的受害者——这一有据可查的现象指的是，当学生休假时间过长时，就会遗忘部分已经学到的知识。数十年的研究表明，每学年开学之初，学生可能需要花8到13周的时间，才能恢复到暑假前的学习水平。", "但全年制上学并不仅仅关乎学业成绩。与传统学校相比，全年制学校的师生关系更加密切；由于没有长假阻隔，学生也不会感到自己与校园环境脱节。这种更紧密的纽带与更强的归属感终会带来回报。研究表明，全年制学校的学生往往更加自信，对自己的校园学习体验也抱有更积极的态度。", "不过，难道孩子们不需要时间放松吗？一些儿童发展专家认为，休假对孩子的健康成长至关重要，因为孩子的天性并不适合把太多时间花在教室里，而暑假恰恰为他们提供了走进户外的绝佳机会。然而，这一观点的问题在于，大多数孩子并没有在户外玩耍，甚至也没有与其他孩子相处。尽管有些孩子会去参加夏令营，但绝大多数孩子都待在家里看电视或玩电子设备上的游戏，这对他们几乎没有任何益处。", "美国已经从农业经济转型为以知识和创新为基础的经济，因此，学年制度也理应随之改变。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why did America's traditional school year have a three-month summer vacation?", "options": ["Students needed to help with farm work.", "Students needed time to learn necessary farming skills.", "The agricultural society then attached less importance to academics.", "America lagged behind other countries in making a scientific school calendar."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The traditional school year, with three months of vacation every summer, was first implemented when America was an agricultural society and the summer months were needed for farm work.", "explanation": "定位第一段首句。该句明确指出，每年夏季包含三个月假期的传统学年制最早实施于美国尚处于农业社会之时，当时夏季的这几个月需要用于干农活（needed for farm work），第三句也印证过去学生暑假曾用于务农。A项“学生需要帮忙干农活”与原文表述完全对应，精准解释了三个月暑假的历史成因，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项偷换概念，原文指需要人力干农活，而非学习务农技能；C项无中生有，农业社会并未被描述为轻视学业；D项张冠李戴，美国如今在学业上落后于他国，而非当年制定历法落后。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What benefit will year-round schooling bring students in addition to improving their learning?", "options": ["It will help them get back to where their lessons started.", "It will enable them to absorb what they have learned.", "It will familiarize them with the school environment.", "It will strengthen their relationship with teachers."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Teachers and students experience a closer relationship in year-round schools than they do in traditional schools and, in the absence of any long-term break, students do not feel detached from the school environment.", "explanation": "定位第三段。首句明确提出“全年制上学并不仅仅关乎学业成绩”，正好呼应题干中“除了改善学习之外带来的益处”。第二句紧接着具体阐述了非学业层面的优势：在全年制学校中，老师和学生能拥有比传统学校更亲密的关系（closer relationship），同时学生也不会与校园疏离。D项“它将加强学生与老师的关系”准确对应原文，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项与B项均涉及第二段提到的学业层面（恢复暑期遗忘的学习进度、消化知识），不符合题干“除改善学习外”的限定；C项偷换概念，原文指学生不会对校园环境感到疏离，而非让他们去熟悉校园环境。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do some childhood development experts believe about the long summer vacation?", "options": ["It meets students' need to study on their own.", "It enables students to learn about the outside world.", "It satisfies students' desire to stay longer at home.", "It contributes to students' healthy growth."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Some childhood development experts believe that time off from school is vital to healthy development as kids are not designed to spend so much of their time inside classrooms and the summer break provides a perfect opportunity to get outside.", "explanation": "定位第四段第二句。面对“孩子是否需要时间放松”的疑问，该句指出一些儿童发展专家的观点：他们认为放假离开学校对于孩子的健康发育至关重要（vital to healthy development），因为孩子的天性不适合长时间待在教室里，而长暑假恰恰提供了接触户外的绝佳机会。D项“它有助于学生的健康成长”正是对原文这一核心观点的同义替换，因此选D。", "trapNote": "B项属于偷换概念，专家仅认为暑假提供了“去户外活动”的机会，而非“了解外部世界”；A项“满足学生自主学习需求”与C项“满足学生在家久待的愿望”均在原文中毫无依据，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the argument against the experts' idea of a long summer vacation?", "options": ["It does little good to most students.", "It benefits few students playing outside.", "It leads students to neglect their studies.", "It makes students addicted to computer games."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "While some children visit summer camps, most stay at home, watching TV or playing games on electronic devices, which hardly benefits them.", "explanation": "定位第四段第三、四句。作者紧接着反驳专家观点：问题在于大多数孩子既没有在户外玩耍，也没有与其他伙伴相处；虽然少数孩子参加夏令营，但绝大多数待在家里看电视或玩电子设备上的游戏，这对他们几乎没有益处（hardly benefits them）。A项“它对大多数学生几乎没有好处”精准同义改写了原文，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项曲解文意，原文是说大多数孩子根本不在户外玩耍，并非在户外玩耍受益人少；C项“导致荒废学业”在此处未提及；D项过度推理，玩电子设备上的游戏不等于“对电脑游戏上瘾”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "What does the author think of the traditional school year in the U.S. today?", "options": ["Well-grounded.", "Culture-bound", "Outdated.", "Welcomed."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The U.S. has changed from a farming economy to a knowledge - and innovation - based economy, so it makes sense for the school year to change as well.", "explanation": "定位第一、二段及末段。作者开篇交代三个月暑假源自农业社会需求，而如今美国已彻底转型；第二段主张“是时候考虑全年制上学了”；末段更总结道，美国已从农业经济转变为知识与创新型经济，因此学年制度也理应随之改变。由此可见，作者认为传统学年制已不合时宜，C项“过时的”准确概括了作者对该体制的态度。", "trapNote": "A项“有充分依据的”与文意相反，传统学制的农业经济基础已不复存在；B项“受文化束缚的”无中生有，文中讨论的是经济结构转型而非文化因素；D项“受欢迎的”与作者呼吁改革的立场相悖。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "实施，贯彻，执行", "note": "四六级高频及物动词：常与 policy、system、reform 搭配；注意区别于名词含义“工具、器具”。", "word": "implement"}, {"gloss": "落后，滞后", "note": "高频搭配 lag behind（落后于……）：文中 With the U.S. lagging behind... 为 with 复合结构作状语。", "word": "lag"}, {"gloss": "滑坡，下滑，衰退", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“滑动/幻灯片”，文中 summer slide 特指暑假期间学业水平或知识的“滑坡衰退”。", "word": "slide"}, {"gloss": "疏离的，不参与的，漠然的", "note": "情感与关系词：由 detach（使分离）加 -ed 构成，常用搭配 feel detached from（感到与……脱节/疏离）。", "word": "detached"}, {"gloss": "取得成功，带来回报，得到好结果", "note": "核心动词短语：既有“还清债务”本义，阅读中更常考“付出得到回报（bring good results）”之义。", "word": "pay off"}, {"gloss": "至关重要的，不可或缺的", "note": "态度与观点题高频词：常用搭配 be vital to/for（对……至关重要），同义词包括 essential、crucial。", "word": "vital"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The traditional school year, with three months of vacation every summer, was first implemented when America was an agricultural society and the summer months were needed for farm work.", "point": "注意主谓被较长的 with 伴随结构隔开，以及 when 引导的并列时间状语从句共同交代传统学制的时代背景。", "structure": "主干为 The traditional school year ... was first implemented；介词短语 with three months of vacation every summer 作插入定语；when 引导时间状语从句，内部由 and 连接两个并列分句。", "zh": "每年夏季拥有三个月假期的传统学年制，最初是在美国尚处于农业社会、夏季需要人力从事农活时实施的。"}, {"en": "One benefit of this change is that students will not fall victim to the “summer slide,” or the well-documented phenomenon where students forget some of the knowledge they have acquired when too much time is taken off from school.", "point": "句中出现连环定语与表语从句，且要注意 or 在学术说明文中常不表“或者”，而是引导“即，也就是说”来解释专业术语。", "structure": "主干为 One benefit ... is that...（that 引导表语从句）；or 引出对 summer slide 的同位语解释；where 引导定语从句修饰 phenomenon，其中包含定语从句 they have acquired 和时间状语从句 when...。", "zh": "这一改革的好处之一在于，学生不会沦为“暑期滑坡”的受害者——这一有据可查的现象指的是，当学生休假时间过长时，就会遗忘部分已经学到的知识。"}, {"en": "Some childhood development experts believe that time off from school is vital to healthy development as kids are not designed to spend so much of their time inside classrooms and the summer break provides a perfect opportunity to get outside.", "point": "辨析 as 在句中引导原因状语从句（因为），同时留意被动结构 be designed to 在拟人或规律表达中译为“天性适合/本该……”。", "structure": "主句为 Some childhood development experts believe that...；that 引导宾语从句，其中包含 as 引导的原因状语从句，该原因状语从句由 and 连接两个并列分句构成。", "zh": "一些儿童发展专家认为，休假对孩子的健康成长至关重要，因为孩子的天性并不适合把太多时间花在教室里，而暑假恰恰为他们提供了走进户外的绝佳机会。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题同义对应：被动表述“夏季需要用来做农活”转化为主动语态“学生需要帮忙干农活”。", "option": "needed to help with farm work", "original": "the summer months were needed for farm work"}, {"note": "第2题同义替换：拥有更密切的师生关系对应“加强与老师的关系”。", "option": "strengthen their relationship with teachers", "original": "experience a closer relationship"}, {"note": "第3题同义转述：be vital to（对……至关重要）对应 contributes to，healthy development 替换为 healthy growth。", "option": "contributes to students' healthy growth", "original": "is vital to healthy development"}, {"note": "第4题否定词替换：hardly benefits them（几乎无益）同义改写为 does little good to。", "option": "does little good to most students", "original": "most stay at home... which hardly benefits them"}, {"note": "第5题态度概括：根据经济结构早已转变且学年制也应改变的论述，提炼出“过时的（Outdated）”评价。", "option": "Outdated", "original": "changed from a farming economy to a knowledge - and innovation - based economy, so it makes sense for the school year to change as well"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202306-s3-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 四级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 四级真题 第3套 Passage One", "title": "职场团建的边界与有效之道", "subtitle": "组织行为学 · 团队建设与职场边界", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 350, "paragraphs": ["Team-building exercises have become popular for managers trying to increase organisational and team harmony and productivity. Unfortunately, many employees resent compulsory bonding and often regard these exercises as a nuisance.", "A paper published this week by University of Sydney researchers in Social Networks has reported participants' feelings about team-building interventions (干预), revealing ethical implications in forcing employees to take part.", "\"Many people see team-building activities as a waste of time, so we decided to look in more depth at what's behind this,\" said the paper's lead researcher, Dr Peter Matous.", "\"Teams are formed, combined, and restructured. Staff are relocated and office spaces redesigned. All this is done with the aim of improving workplace efficiency, collaboration, and cohesion. But does any of this work?\" said Dr Matous.", "The study found that team-building exercises which focused on the sharing of and intervening into personal attitudes and relationships between team members were considered too heavy-handed and intrusive, although the researchers say some degree of openness and vulnerability is often necessary to make deep, effective connections with colleagues.", "\"Some participants were against team-building exercises because they were implicitly compulsory. They didn't welcome management's interest in their lives beyond their direct work performance,\" said Matous. \"Many people don't want to be forced into having fun or making friends, especially not on top of their busy jobs. They feel management is being too nosy or trying to control their lives too much.\"", "In this study, the researchers recommended a self-disclosure (表露) approach where participants were guided through a series of questions that allowed them to increasingly disclose personal information and values. The method is well-tested and has been shown to increase interpersonal closeness. However, to be successful, it must be voluntary.", "The researchers said there are numerous schools of thought that propose differing psychological methods for strengthening relationships. \"With caution, many relational methods to improve teams and organisations can be borrowed from other fields. The question is how to apply them effectively to strengthen an entire collective, which is more than just the sum of individual relationships,\" said Dr Matous."], "translations": ["团队建设活动在试图提升组织与团队和谐度及生产力的管理者中颇为流行。遗憾的是，许多员工反感强制性的情感联结，往往将这些活动视为一件烦心事。", "悉尼大学研究人员本周发表在《社会网络》期刊上的一篇论文报告了参与者对团建干预措施的感受，揭示了强迫员工参与其中所涉及的伦理影响。", "“很多人认为团建活动是在浪费时间，因此我们决定更深入地探究这背后的原因，”该论文的首席研究员彼得·马图斯博士说道。", "“团队被组建、合并、重组，员工被调动岗位，办公空间也被重新设计。所有这些举措都是为了提高工作效率、协作能力与团队凝聚力。但这些做法真的有效吗？”马图斯博士说。", "研究发现，那些侧重于让团队成员分享并介入彼此个人态度和人际关系的团建活动，被认为过于强硬和具侵入性；尽管研究人员表示，一定程度的坦诚与示弱往往是与同事建立深厚、有效联系所必需的。", "“一些参与者反对团建活动，是因为它们带有隐性的强制色彩。他们并不欢迎管理层插手其直接工作表现之外的生活，”马图斯说，“很多人不想在繁忙的工作之外还要被强迫去寻开心或交朋友。他们觉得管理层管得太宽，或者试图过度控制他们的生活。”", "在这项研究中，研究人员推荐了一种自我表露的方法：通过一系列问题引导参与者，让他们逐步敞开心扉表露个人信息与价值观。这一方法经过了充分验证，并已被证明能增进人际亲密度。然而，该方法要想取得成功，必须出于自愿。", "研究人员指出，关于加强人际关系，众多学派提出了不同的心理学方法。“只要保持谨慎，许多用于改善团队和组织的关系方法都可以从其他领域借鉴。关键在于如何有效地运用这些方法来增强整个集体的凝聚力——毕竟集体绝不仅仅是个人关系的简单相加。”马图斯博士说。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why are many employees opposed to team-building exercises?", "options": ["They consider such exercises annoying.", "They deem these exercises counter-productive.", "They see such exercises as harmful to harmony.", "They find these exercises too demanding."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Unfortunately, many employees resent compulsory bonding and often regard these exercises as a nuisance.", "explanation": "题干询问许多员工反对团建活动的原因。第1段第2句明确指出，许多员工反感强制联结，并常将这类活动视为“一件烦心事”（a nuisance）。选项A中的consider对应原文regard...as，annoying（令人讨厌的）精准同义替换nuisance，句中的resent compulsory bonding也与题干opposed to相呼应，因此A为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项counter-productive（适得其反）系对第3段“浪费时间”的过度推理；C项“破坏和谐”与第1段增进和谐的原意正反颠倒；D项“要求过高”属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did Dr Matous and his team do to find out whether team-building activities would improve productivity?", "options": ["They relocated team leaders and their offices.", "They rearranged the staff and office spaces.", "They redesigned the staff's work schedules.", "They reintroduced some cohesive activities."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Staff are relocated and office spaces redesigned. All this is done with the aim of improving workplace efficiency, collaboration, and cohesion.", "explanation": "题干询问马图斯博士团队为探究团建能否提升生产力提到了哪些做法。第4段指出，人们组建、合并与重组团队，调动员工并重新设计办公空间（Staff are relocated and office spaces redesigned），旨在提高工作效率、协作与凝聚力。B项rearranged the staff and office spaces精准同义替换了原文表述，improve productivity对应improving workplace efficiency，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项把原文的staff（员工）偷换为team leaders（团队领导），属偷换概念；C项将office spaces（办公空间）偷换为work schedules（工作日程）；D项“重新引入凝聚性活动”原文未提，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did the study by Matous' team find about some team-building exercises?", "options": ["They were intended to share personal attitudes and relationships.", "They implicitly added to the vulnerability of team members.", "They invariably strengthened connections among colleagues.", "They were regarded as an intrusion into employees' private lives."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The study found that team-building exercises which focused on the sharing of and intervening into personal attitudes and relationships between team members were considered too heavy-handed and intrusive", "explanation": "题干询问马图斯团队的研究对某些团建活动有何发现。第5段明确指出，研究发现那些侧重于分享并干预成员个人态度及人际关系的团建活动被认为“过于强硬且具侵入性”（too heavy-handed and intrusive），第6段也补充员工觉得管理层干涉私生活、管得太宽。D项were regarded as an intrusion into employees' private lives精准同义转述were considered...intrusive，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项把限定活动类型的从句误当作研究结论，偷换主干；B项将第6段implicitly与第5段vulnerability强行拼凑；C项invariably（总是）表述绝对，曲解原文。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How can the self-disclosure approach succeed in increasing interpersonal closeness?", "options": ["By allowing participants freedom to express themselves.", "By applying it to employees who volunteer to participate.", "By arranging in proper order the questions participants face.", "By guiding employees through a series of steps in team building."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "The method is well-tested and has been shown to increase interpersonal closeness. However, to be successful, it must be voluntary.", "explanation": "题干询问“自我表露”方法如何才能成功增进人际亲密度。第7段前两句先介绍该方法经充分验证可增进人际亲密度（increase interpersonal closeness），紧接着用However转折点明核心条件：“然而，要取得成功，它必须是自愿的”（to be successful, it must be voluntary）。B项中的volunteer to participate精准同义替换voluntary，故B为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“允许参与者自由表达”属于偷换概念，原文指通过问题引导表露个人信息，而非成功的前提条件；C项“合理排序问题”与D项“引导经历一系列团建步骤”均系对a series of questions的曲解或无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "What does Matous think of the various psychological methods borrowed from other fields for strengthening relationships?", "options": ["They must be used in combination for an entire collective.", "They prioritise some psychological aspects over others.", "They place too much stress on individual relationships.", "They have to be applied cautiously to be effective."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "\"With caution, many relational methods to improve teams and organisations can be borrowed from other fields. The question is how to apply them effectively to strengthen an entire collective, which is more than just the sum of individual relationships,\" said Dr Matous.", "explanation": "题干询问马图斯对从其他领域借鉴的各种增强关系的心理学方法有何看法。第8段援引马图斯博士的话指出，许多用于改善团队和组织的关系方法可以“谨慎地”（With caution）从其他领域借鉴，关键在于如何“有效地运用它们”（apply them effectively）以增强整个集体。D项cautiously对应with caution，to be effective对应apply them effectively，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项“必须结合使用”原文并未提及，属无中生有；B项“优先考虑某些心理方面”曲解了原文“不同学派提出不同心理学方法”；C项误解末句，原文意为集体大于个人关系之和，并未批评方法过度强调个人关系。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "讨厌的事物；麻烦事", "note": "四级高频名词，常与regard...as连用；阅读中对应annoying/troublesome等负向评价词", "word": "nuisance"}, {"gloss": "强制的；义务的", "note": "常与mandatory互换，反义词为voluntary（自愿的），本文构成第1、4题核心对立逻辑", "word": "compulsory"}, {"gloss": "侵入的；打扰隐私的", "note": "动词为intrude，名词为intrusion（第3题答案原词）；常考词根词缀同义转换", "word": "intrusive"}, {"gloss": "脆弱；示弱（坦露弱点）", "note": "熟词僻义/语境义：除“脆弱性”外，在人际心理学语境中指“愿意袒露弱点、保持真诚”", "word": "vulnerability"}, {"gloss": "潜在影响；牵连；含义", "note": "熟词僻义：除“暗示、含义”外，复数implications在学术语境中常译为“（可能产生的）影响、后果”", "word": "implication"}, {"gloss": "凝聚力；团结", "note": "来自动词cohere，形容词cohesive（曾出现在第2题D项干扰项中），职场与社会话题高频词", "word": "cohesion"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The study found that team-building exercises which focused on the sharing of and intervening into personal attitudes and relationships between team members were considered too heavy-handed and intrusive, although the researchers say some degree of openness and vulnerability is often necessary to make deep, effective connections with colleagues.", "point": "长定语从句分隔主谓结构（exercises ... were considered）是四级高频难点，注意先找主干再解修饰，并留意although引导的转折补充态度。", "structure": "主句(The study found) + that宾语从句[主语(team-building exercises) + which定语从句 + 谓语(were considered...)] + although让步状语从句", "zh": "研究发现，那些侧重于让团队成员分享并介入彼此个人态度和人际关系的团建活动，被认为过于强硬和具侵入性；尽管研究人员表示，一定程度的坦诚与示弱往往是与同事建立深厚、有效联系所必需的。"}, {"en": "In this study, the researchers recommended a self-disclosure (表露) approach where participants were guided through a series of questions that allowed them to increasingly disclose personal information and values.", "point": "嵌套定语从句：where在表示抽象地点/情境的approach后引导定语从句（相当于in which），内部又嵌套that修饰questions。", "structure": "状语 + 主谓宾(the researchers recommended a self-disclosure approach) + where定语从句 + that定语从句", "zh": "在这项研究中，研究人员推荐了一种自我表露的方法：通过一系列问题引导参与者，让他们逐步敞开心扉表露个人信息与价值观。"}, {"en": "A paper published this week by University of Sydney researchers in Social Networks has reported participants' feelings about team-building interventions (干预), revealing ethical implications in forcing employees to take part.", "point": "主语后接较长的过去分词短语published...作后置定语，核心谓语为has reported，句末revealing引导现在分词短语作结果状语，引出研究深层意义。", "structure": "主语(A paper + published...过去分词短语作定语) + 谓宾(has reported participants' feelings...) + 现在分词作结果状语(revealing...)", "zh": "悉尼大学研究人员本周发表在《社会网络》期刊上的一篇论文报告了参与者对团建干预措施的感受，揭示了强迫员工参与其中所涉及的伦理影响。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题同义替换：regard...as→consider，nuisance（令人讨厌的事物）→annoying", "option": "consider such exercises annoying", "original": "regard these exercises as a nuisance"}, {"note": "第2题同义替换：relocate/redesign两个具体动作合并概括为rearrange（重新安排）", "option": "rearranged the staff and office spaces", "original": "Staff are relocated and office spaces redesigned"}, {"note": "第3题同义替换：be considered→be regarded as，形容词intrusive名词化为an intrusion", "option": "were regarded as an intrusion into employees' private lives", "original": "were considered too heavy-handed and intrusive"}, {"note": "第4题同义替换：形容词voluntary转化为定语从句who volunteer to participate", "option": "applying it to employees who volunteer to participate", "original": "to be successful, it must be voluntary"}, {"note": "第5题同义替换：介词短语with caution→副词cautiously，effectively→to be effective", "option": "have to be applied cautiously to be effective", "original": "With caution ... apply them effectively"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202306-s3-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 四级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 四级真题 第3套 Passage Two", "title": "洛杉矶无家可归危机与社会态度", "subtitle": "社会民生 · 住房危机与公众同理心", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 346, "paragraphs": ["There are close to 58,000 homeless people in Los Angeles county. That's a shocking and tragic number for a region that's home to some of the richest people in the world. At last, the problem became so acute — and so visible — that Los Angeles took extraordinary action. The citizens of this county voted in November 2016 and again in March 2017 to raise their own taxes. The purpose of such action is to fund an enormous multibillion-dollar, 10-year program of housing and social services for the homeless.", "As a result, Los Angeles now has its best chance in decades to combat homelessness. This is an opportunity that surely all can agree must not be wasted. It is neither desirable nor morally acceptable nor practical for this county to tolerate the signs of deprivation more commonly associated with the slums (贫民窟) of Rio de Janeiro.", "How did we get here? For as long as there are homeless people, there is a tendency to blame the victims themselves for their condition—to see their failure to thrive as an issue of character, of moral weakness, of laziness. But contrary to popular belief, the homeless in Los Angeles are not mostly mentally ill or drug addicted or frightening, although a sizable minority meet some of those descriptions. Today, a greater and greater proportion of people living on the streets are there because of bad luck or a series of mistakes, or because the economy forgot them—they lost a job or were evicted (逐出) or fled an abusive marriage just as the housing market was growing increasingly unforgiving.", "The challenges are enormous, even if everyone is pulling in the same direction. That reality was driven home this month by a new Los Angeles Homeless Services Authority report showing that the county's homeless population is growing faster than the supply of new housing.", "In the world's richest nation, homelessness on this scale should be shameful and shocking. But most Los Angeles residents are no longer either shocked or shamed. Increasingly, we are uncomfortable, annoyed, disgusted, scared or unaware. Compassion (同情心) is being replaced by resignation."], "translations": ["洛杉矶县有近5.8万名无家可归者。对于一个居住着世界上一些最富有群体的地区而言，这是一个令人震惊且悲惨的数字。最终，这个问题变得如此严峻且显而易见，以至于洛杉矶采取了非同寻常的行动。该县居民在2016年11月和2017年3月两次投票决定提高自身税率。此举旨在为一项耗资数十亿美元、为期十年的庞大计划提供资金，为无家可归者提供住房与社会服务。", "因此，洛杉矶如今拥有数十年来抗击无家可归问题的最佳契机。无疑所有人都认同，这一机遇绝不能被浪费。对这个县来说，容忍通常与里约热内卢贫民窟联系在一起的贫困景象，既不可取，在道德上也不可接受，更不切实际。", "我们是如何走到这一步的？只要有无家可归者存在，人们往往就会将这种境况归咎于受害者自身——把他们未能摆脱困境视为品格、道德薄弱或懒惰的问题。但与普遍看法相反，洛杉矶的无家可归者大多数并非患有精神疾病、吸毒成瘾或令人畏惧之人，尽管确实有相当一部分人符合其中某些描述。如今，露宿街头的人中越来越大的比例是因为运气不好或一连串失误，或是被经济遗忘——正值住房市场变得越来越严酷无情之际，他们失业、遭到驱逐，或逃离了存在虐待的婚姻。", "即便所有人齐心协力，挑战依然巨大。本月洛杉矶无家可归者服务管理局发布的一份新报告让人清醒地认识到这一现实：该县无家可归人口的增长速度超过了新住房的供应速度。", "在这个世界上最富裕的国家，如此规模的无家可归现象本应令人羞愧和震惊。但大多数洛杉矶居民已不再感到震惊或羞愧。我们越来越感到不适、烦躁、厌恶、恐惧，或干脆视而不见。同情心正在被听天由命的无奈所取代。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why did the citizens of Los Angeles vote to raise their own taxes?", "options": ["To combat the county's homelessness.", "To reform the county's service system.", "To fund the development of local infrastructure.", "To narrow the gap between the rich and the poor."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The citizens of this county voted in November 2016 and again in March 2017 to raise their own taxes. The purpose of such action is to fund an enormous multibillion-dollar, 10-year program of housing and social services for the homeless.", "explanation": "题干询问洛杉矶居民投票提高自身税率的原因。第1段最后两句指出，居民投票加税的目的是资助一项为期十年的庞大计划，为无家可归者提供住房与社会服务；第2段开篇紧接着总结，此举使洛杉矶获得抗击无家可归问题（combat homelessness）的最佳契机。A项精准概括了加税的核心目的，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项“改革服务体系”与C项“资助地方基础设施”均偷换了第1段housing and social services for the homeless的概念；D项“缩小贫富差距”属于结合首段“最富有群体”的过度推理。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do people tend to believe about the homeless?", "options": ["They seldom meet the descriptions of homelessness.", "They are the victims of fast economic development.", "They are responsible for their own condition.", "They account for the majority of drug addicts."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "For as long as there are homeless people, there is a tendency to blame the victims themselves for their condition—to see their failure to thrive as an issue of character, of moral weakness, of laziness.", "explanation": "题干询问人们通常对无家可归者持何种看法。第3段第2句指出，只要有无家可归者存在，人们往往（there is a tendency）就会将这种境况归咎于受害者自身（blame the victims themselves for their condition），将其视为品格、道德或懒惰问题。C项responsible for their own condition精准同义转述这一普遍成见，故C正确。", "trapNote": "A项曲解后句“相当一部分少数人符合上述描述”，且非大众普遍看法；B项将后文“被经济遗忘”篡改为“经济快速发展”；D项主客颠倒，原文大众误以为无家可归者多吸毒，而非无家可归者占吸毒者大多数。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is one of the causes for more and more people in Los Angeles to become homeless?", "options": ["They find it increasingly difficult to afford a place to live.", "The divorce rate in the county has been on a steady rise.", "They have been compelled to take low-paying jobs.", "The society fails to forgive them for their mistakes."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Today, a greater and greater proportion of people living on the streets are there because of bad luck or a series of mistakes, or because the economy forgot them—they lost a job or were evicted (逐出) or fled an abusive marriage just as the housing market was growing increasingly unforgiving.", "explanation": "题干询问越来越多洛杉矶人流落街头的成因之一。第3段末句指出，如今越来越多人因失业、被驱逐或逃离不幸婚姻而露宿街头，而此时恰逢“住房市场变得越来越严酷无情”（the housing market was growing increasingly unforgiving）。A项“越来越难以负担住房”精准转述了这一层住房危机原因，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项由“逃离受虐婚姻”过度推理出“离婚率持续上升”；C项将“失业（lost a job）”偷换为“被迫从事低薪工作”；D项张冠李戴，把mistakes与housing market...unforgiving强行拼凑为“社会不原谅其过错”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the new Los Angeles Homeless Services Authority report?", "options": ["Supplying enough job opportunities for the homeless remains a challenge.", "Everyone is pulling in the same direction to solve the homelessness problem.", "The increase in new housing falls short of the demand of the growing homeless population.", "Los Angeles' homeless condition is deteriorating faster than many people predict."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "That reality was driven home this month by a new Los Angeles Homeless Services Authority report showing that the county's homeless population is growing faster than the supply of new housing.", "explanation": "题干询问从洛杉矶无家可归者服务管理局的新报告中可以得知什么。第4段第2句明确指出，该报告显示该县“无家可归人口的增长速度超过了新住房的供应速度”（growing faster than the supply of new housing）。C项falls short of the demand（供不应求、满足不了需求）精准同义替换了人口增速快于房源增速，故C正确。", "trapNote": "A项把new housing偷换为job opportunities；B项将首句even if引导的让步假设“即使大家齐心协力”误作报告陈述的既成事实；D项“比许多人预测的恶化更快”属无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "How do most Los Angeles residents now feel about homelessness?", "options": ["They are increasingly ashamed about its scale.", "They find it no more scaring than it appears.", "They are less and less indifferent to it.", "They no longer find it shocking."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "But most Los Angeles residents are no longer either shocked or shamed.", "explanation": "题干询问大多数洛杉矶居民如今对无家可归问题的感受。第5段先指出这种规模的无家可归现象本应令人羞愧和震惊，随后用But转折点明现状：“但大多数洛杉矶居民已不再感到震惊或羞愧”（no longer either shocked or shamed），同情心正被无奈取代。D项no longer find it shocking与原文高度契合，故D为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“越来越感到羞愧”与原文no longer...shamed正反颠倒；B项将民众感到害怕（scared）曲解为“觉得它并不比表面更吓人”；C项“越来越不冷漠”同样与“同情心被无奈取代”正反颠倒。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "严峻的；急迫的；剧烈的", "note": "熟词僻义/高频形容词：在社会问题语境中常指问题“十分严峻、紧迫”，相当于severe/critical", "word": "acute"}, {"gloss": "贫困；匮乏；剥夺", "note": "动词为deprive（常考deprive sb. of sth.）；本文the signs of deprivation指赤贫景象", "word": "deprivation"}, {"gloss": "严酷无情的；难以应对的", "note": "熟词僻义：本义为“不宽恕的”，在housing market等经济语境中指“苛刻的、毫无缓冲余地的”（第3题陷阱设题处）", "word": "unforgiving"}, {"gloss": "无奈顺从；听天由命", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“辞职”，但与compassion对比时意为“逆来顺受、消极放弃”（第5段末关键态度词）", "word": "resignation"}, {"gloss": "逐出；依法驱逐（房客）", "note": "多用于租房、债务等语境中房东驱逐无力支付房租的住户，阅读常作原因细节考查", "word": "evict"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "For as long as there are homeless people, there is a tendency to blame the victims themselves for their condition—to see their failure to thrive as an issue of character, of moral weakness, of laziness.", "point": "破折号后不定式短语to see...as进一步解释前面blame the victims themselves的具体内涵，构成第2题核心定位句。", "structure": "时间状语从句(For as long as...) + 主句(there is a tendency to...) + 破折号同位解释(to see...as...)", "zh": "只要有无家可归者存在，人们往往就会将这种境况归咎于受害者自身——把他们未能摆脱困境视为品格、道德薄弱或懒惰的问题。"}, {"en": "Today, a greater and greater proportion of people living on the streets are there because of bad luck or a series of mistakes, or because the economy forgot them—they lost a job or were evicted (逐出) or fled an abusive marriage just as the housing market was growing increasingly unforgiving.", "point": "“a greater and greater proportion of...”后接现在分词短语living on the streets作后置定语，破折号后并列三个过去时动词具体阐明“被经济遗忘”的现实处境。", "structure": "主语(a greater and greater proportion of people + 分词短语定语) + 系表(are there) + 并列原因状语(because of...or because...) + 破折号具体例证(just as时间状语从句)", "zh": "如今，露宿街头的人中越来越大的比例是因为运气不好或一连串失误，或是被经济遗忘——正值住房市场变得越来越严酷无情之际，他们失业、遭到驱逐，或逃离了存在虐待的婚姻。"}, {"en": "That reality was driven home this month by a new Los Angeles Homeless Services Authority report showing that the county's homeless population is growing faster than the supply of new housing.", "point": "drive sth. home意为“使某事被充分理解/铭记于心”；report后接现在分词showing引导的宾语从句，直接说明报告的核心结论。", "structure": "主谓(That reality was driven home) + 方式/施事状语(by a...report) + 现在分词短语作定语(showing that...)", "zh": "本月洛杉矶无家可归者服务管理局发布的一份新报告让人清醒地认识到这一现实：该县无家可归人口的增长速度超过了新住房的供应速度。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题跨段呼应：第1段具体资助举措在第2段概括为combat homelessness", "option": "combat the county's homelessness", "original": "fund an enormous...program of housing and social services for the homeless"}, {"note": "第2题同义替换：a tendency→tend to，blame sb. for sth.→sb. be responsible for sth.", "option": "tend to believe ... are responsible for their own condition", "original": "there is a tendency to blame the victims themselves for their condition"}, {"note": "第3题语境转述：unforgiving（无情的、苛刻的）住房市场具体指越来越难以负担居所", "option": "find it increasingly difficult to afford a place to live", "original": "the housing market was growing increasingly unforgiving"}, {"note": "第4题正反表达转换：A grows faster than B（A快于B）→ B falls short of the demand of A（B赶不上A的需求）", "option": "increase in new housing falls short of the demand of the growing homeless population", "original": "homeless population is growing faster than the supply of new housing"}, {"note": "第5题同义替换：be shocked转化为主观感受表达find it shocking", "option": "no longer find it shocking", "original": "no longer either shocked or shamed"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202212-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2022.12", "examSet": "2022.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2022.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "全球健康饮食文化与日常步行", "subtitle": "营养学家探寻全球长寿健康国家的饮食与生活秘诀", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 344, "paragraphs": ["To write his 2010 book, The 5-Factor World Diet, nutritionist Harley Pasternak traveled to the healthiest countries around the world to learn more about what made their meals extra nourishing.", "He noted that Japanese people ate a wonderful variety of seaweeds, and that Chinese people tried to include at least five different colors in every meal. Pasternak also came away with some valuable observations about how different the North American way of life was, compared with many other countries.", "For starters, Americans eat much bigger portions than people in other countries. \"We don't prioritize eating seasonally or locally, and we also add lots of salt, sugar and thickening agents to our foods,\" explained Pasternak. Contrast that to the healthy Mediterranean, Nordic and Okinawan diets listed in Pasternak's book. They all seem to stick to the ethos(特质) of regional, seasonal produce.", "For example, a traditional Mediterranean diet includes fruits, vegetables, whole grains, nuts and olive oil as the main components of nutritional intake. Fish, chicken and red wine make moderate appearances, while red meat, salt and sugar are used much less often. The benefits of a traditional Mediterranean diet have been studied since the 1970s, and researchers have found that living that olive oil life can help people lose weight, lower their heart disease risk and reverse diabetes.", "Most other healthy eating cultures also make meals an event—say, multiple courses around the family table, or a glass or two of red wine at a long lunch—as opposed to hastily wolfing down handfuls of cereal above the kitchen sink and calling it dinner.", "Each of the healthy eating cultures has its own unique feature. But Pasternak did take note of one unifying factor in all of the healthy societies he observed. \"The only overlapping feature in most of these healthy countries is that they all walk way more than the average American,\" said Pasternak, \"So really, regardless of what you're eating, if someone's walking four miles more than you each day, they're going to be a lot thinner and live a lot longer than you.\""], "translations": ["为了撰写他2010年的著作《五因素世界饮食》，营养学家Harley Pasternak走访了世界上最健康的国家，以深入了解是什么让这些国家的饮食格外营养丰富。", "他注意到日本人食用种类丰富的海藻，而中国人则力求在每餐中至少包含五种不同的颜色。Pasternak还获得了一些有价值的观察，即与许多其他国家相比，北美的生活方式有多么不同。", "首先，美国人的食物分量比其他国家的人大得多。Pasternak解释说：“我们不重视食用时令食物或本地食物，而且我们还在食物中添加大量的盐、糖和增稠剂。”将此与Pasternak书中列出的健康的地中海饮食、北欧饮食和冲绳饮食进行对比。它们似乎都坚持地域性、时令性农产品的特质。", "例如，传统的地中海饮食包括水果、蔬菜、全谷物、坚果和橄榄油作为营养摄入的主要成分。鱼类、鸡肉和红酒适量出现，而红肉、盐和糖的使用频率则要低得多。传统地中海饮食的益处自20世纪70年代以来一直受到研究，研究人员发现，过橄榄油式的生活可以帮助人们减轻体重、降低患心脏病的风险并逆转糖尿病。", "大多数其他健康饮食文化也将进餐变成一种仪式——比如围坐在家庭餐桌旁享用多道菜肴，或在漫长的午餐中喝一两杯红酒——而不是在厨房水槽上方匆忙吞下几把谷物就称之为晚餐。", "每种健康饮食文化都有其独特之处。但Pasternak确实注意到他所观察到的所有健康社会中存在一个共同因素。Pasternak说：“这些健康国家中大多数的唯一重叠特征是，它们的人都比普通美国人走路多得多。所以实际上，无论你吃什么，如果有人每天比你多走四英里，他们就会比你瘦得多，也会比你活得长久得多。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What characterizes Japanese and Chinese foods?", "options": ["Variety.", "Flavor.", "Color.", "Naturalness."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "He noted that Japanese people ate a wonderful variety of seaweeds, and that Chinese people tried to include at least five different colors in every meal.", "explanation": "定位第二段首句。原文指出，作者注意到日本人食用种类繁多（a wonderful variety of）的海藻，而中国人则力求每餐至少包含五种不同的颜色（at least five different colors）。由此可见，中日两国饮食共同的突出特点在于食物种类的丰富多样，故A项“Variety.”（多样性）正确。B项“风味”与D项“天然性”本段未提及；C项“颜色”仅对应中国饮食的细节，未能全面概括中日两国的共同特征。", "trapNote": "C项“Color.”最具迷惑性，它原词复现了中国饮食“包含五种不同颜色”这一半句信息，却忽略了日本饮食“海藻种类丰富”的描述，属于以偏概全的典型干扰项。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is typical of Americans in the way of eating?", "options": ["They emphasize nutrition.", "They tend to eat quite a lot.", "They prioritize convenience.", "They care about flavors."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "For starters, Americans eat much bigger portions than people in other countries.", "explanation": "定位第三段首句。Pasternak在对比北美与其他国家的生活方式时首先指出，美国人的食物分量比其他国家的人大得多（eat much bigger portions），即食量很大。选项B“They tend to eat quite a lot.”是对原文“eat much bigger portions”的同义替换。此外，后文还提到美国人不重视时令与本地食材，且会添加大量盐、糖和增稠剂，并未体现A项“重视营养”、C项“优先考虑方便”或D项“在意风味”。", "trapNote": "部分考生可能因第五段提到“在水槽边匆忙吞下谷物”而误选C项“优先考虑方便”，但该段主语是与健康饮食文化对比的泛指做法，且第三段明确将“份量大”作为美国饮食的首要典型特征。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What features are in Mediterranean, Nordic and Okinawan diets?", "options": ["Fruits and vegetables.", "Olive oil and red wine.", "Seasonal local produce.", "Unprocessed ingredients."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Contrast that to the healthy Mediterranean, Nordic and Okinawan diets listed in Pasternak's book. They all seem to stick to the ethos(特质) of regional, seasonal produce.", "explanation": "定位第三段末尾。文中将美国饮食与Pasternak书中列出的地中海饮食、北欧饮食和冲绳饮食进行对比，指出这三种健康饮食似乎都坚持“地域性、时令性农产品”（regional, seasonal produce）的特质。选项C“Seasonal local produce.”将原文中的“regional”同义替换为“local”，精准对应原文核心特征。A、B两项在第四段仅作为地中海饮食的具体构成提及，无法涵盖北欧和冲绳饮食。", "trapNote": "A项和B项均出自第四段对“地中海饮食”的举例说明，属于张冠李戴与以偏概全的陷阱，并非第三段所总结的地中海、北欧与冲绳三种饮食的共同特征。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do people in most healthy eating cultures have in common?", "options": ["They get the whole family to eat at a table.", "They eat their meals regularly and punctually.", "They consume plenty of cereal for breakfast.", "They attach great importance to their meals."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Most other healthy eating cultures also make meals an event—say, multiple courses around the family table, or a glass or two of red wine at a long lunch—as opposed to hastily wolfing down handfuls of cereal above the kitchen sink and calling it dinner.", "explanation": "定位第五段。原文提到，大多数其他健康饮食文化都会“make meals an event”（把进餐当成一件大事/仪式），例如全家人围坐餐桌享用多道菜肴，或在漫长的午餐中喝一两杯红酒，而不是在水槽边匆忙抓几把谷物应付了事。选项D“They attach great importance to their meals.”（他们非常重视进餐）正是对“make meals an event”的精准同义转述。", "trapNote": "A项“全家人围坐餐桌吃饭”只是文中“say”后举出的一个具体例子，不能代表所有健康饮食文化的普遍共性；C项则与原文中作为反面例子的“匆忙吃谷物当晚餐”相悖。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Compared with the average American, people in healthy societies ___________ .", "options": ["walk at least 4 miles a day", "do considerably more walking", "pay more attention to body shape", "consume a lot more organic food"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "\"The only overlapping feature in most of these healthy countries is that they all walk way more than the average American,\" said Pasternak", "explanation": "定位第六段。Pasternak明确指出，他所观察到的绝大多数健康国家唯一的重叠特征是，这些国家的人都比普通美国人走多得多的路（walk way more than the average American）。选项B“do considerably more walking”中的“considerably more”准确同义替换了原文的口语化表达“way more”。后文提到的“比你多走四英里”只是假设条件，并非每天至少走四英里，因此A项错误。", "trapNote": "A项“每天至少走4英里”极具干扰性，它利用末句中的数字“four miles”设下偷换概念的陷阱，原文说的是“每天比别人多走4英里”的假设，而非绝对步行里程的下限。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 有营养的，滋养的", "note": "nourish + -ing，在第一段中修饰meals，表示健康国家的饮食格外营养丰富。", "word": "nourishing"}, {"gloss": "v. 优先考虑，把……放在首位", "note": "由priority转化而来，第三段中“don't prioritize eating seasonally or locally”指不重视时令或本地饮食。", "word": "prioritize"}, {"gloss": "n. 道德风尚，特质，精神气质", "note": "书面高频词，文中贴心给出了中文释义（特质），stick to the ethos of指坚持某种核心理念。", "word": "ethos"}, {"gloss": "adj. 适度的，适量的", "note": "第四段“make moderate appearances”意为适量出现在饮食中，与后文“much less often”形成频率对比。", "word": "moderate"}, {"gloss": "adj. 重叠的，共同的", "note": "由overlap + -ing构成，第六段与前文的unifying相呼应，指不同健康社会之间的共性特征。", "word": "overlapping"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Pasternak also came away with some valuable observations about how different the North American way of life was, compared with many other countries.", "point": "重点掌握come away with（带着……收获离开）以及how引导的感叹式宾语从句，注意形容词different紧跟how前置的语序。", "structure": "主句(Pasternak came away with observations) + 介词短语(about + how引导的宾语从句) + 过去分词短语作状语(compared with...)", "zh": "Pasternak还获得了一些有价值的观察，即与许多其他国家相比，北美的生活方式有多么不同。"}, {"en": "The benefits of a traditional Mediterranean diet have been studied since the 1970s, and researchers have found that living that olive oil life can help people lose weight, lower their heart disease risk and reverse diabetes.", "point": "注意现在完成时的被动语态（have been studied），以及动名词短语living that olive oil life作宾语从句主语的用法。", "structure": "并列句：分句一(主语+现在完成时被动语态) + and + 分句二(主语+found+that从句，其中动名词短语作主语，help后接三个并列不带to的不定式作宾补)", "zh": "传统地中海饮食的益处自20世纪70年代以来一直受到研究，研究人员发现，过那种以橄榄油为主的生活方式可以帮助人们减轻体重、降低患心脏病的风险并逆转糖尿病。"}, {"en": "Most other healthy eating cultures also make meals an event—say, multiple courses around the family table, or a glass or two of red wine at a long lunch—as opposed to hastily wolfing down handfuls of cereal above the kitchen sink and calling it dinner.", "point": "掌握as opposed to（与……截然相反/而不是）的介词短语用法，其后接并列动名词wolfing down和calling；破折号之间为举例插入语。", "structure": "主干(Most cultures make meals an event) + 双破折号插入语举例(say, ...) + 对比状语(as opposed to + 动名词短语)", "zh": "大多数其他健康饮食文化也将进餐变成一种仪式——比如围坐在家庭餐桌旁享用多道菜肴，或在漫长的午餐中喝一两杯红酒——而不是在厨房水槽上方匆忙吞下几把谷物就称之为晚餐。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "具体描述食物种类多、色彩丰富，在选项中被概括为抽象名词“多样性”。", "option": "Variety", "original": "ate a wonderful variety of seaweeds... include at least five different colors"}, {"note": "eat bigger portions（吃更大份的食物）同义替换为eat quite a lot（吃得相当多）。", "option": "tend to eat quite a lot", "original": "eat much bigger portions"}, {"note": "regional（地域性的）替换为常见同义词local（本地的）。", "option": "Seasonal local produce", "original": "regional, seasonal produce"}, {"note": "“把吃饭当成一件大事/仪式”被准确转述为“非常重视饮食”。", "option": "attach great importance to their meals", "original": "make meals an event"}, {"note": "口语化的程度副词way（……得多）替换为书面语considerably。", "option": "do considerably more walking", "original": "walk way more"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202212-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2022.12", "examSet": "2022.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2022.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "高情商背后的压力与阴暗面", "subtitle": "研究表明对他人情绪过于敏感可能会增加自身心理压力", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 341, "paragraphs": ["Recognizing when a friend or colleague feels sad, angry or surprised is key to getting along with others. But a new study suggests that being sensitive to people's feelings may sometimes come with an extra dose of stress. This and other research challenge the prevailing view that emotional intelligence is uniformly beneficial to its bearer.", "In a study, psychologist Myriam Bechtoldt of the Frankfurt School of Finance and Management in Germany asked 166 male university students a series of questions to measure their emotional intelligence. For example, they showed the students photographs of people's faces and asked them to what extent feelings such as happiness or disgust were being expressed. The students then had to give job talks in front of judges who displayed serious facial expressions. The scientists measured concentrations of stress hormones in the students' saliva(唾液) before and after the talk.", "In students who were rated more emotionally intelligent, the stress measures increased more during the experiment and took longer to go back to baseline. The findings suggest that some people may be too emotionally clever for their own good, says Bechtoldt. \"Sometimes you can be so good at something that it causes trouble,\" she notes.", "Indeed, the study adds to previous research hinting at a dark side of emotional intelligence. A study published in 2002 in Personality and Individual Differences suggested that emotionally perceptive people might be particularly influenced by feelings of depression and hopelessness. Furthermore, several studies have implied that emotional intelligence can be used to manipulate others for personal gains.", "More research is needed to see how exactly the relation between emotional intelligence and stress would play out in women and in people of different ages and education levels. Nevertheless, emotional intelligence is a useful skill to have, as long as you learn to also properly cope with emotions —both others' and your own, says Bechtoldt. For example, some sensitive individuals may assume responsibility for other people's sadness or anger, which ultimately stresses them out. Remember, as Bechtoldt says, \"you are not responsible for how other people feel.\""], "translations": ["识别朋友或同事何时感到悲伤、愤怒或惊讶是与他人相处的关键。但一项新研究表明，对他人情感敏感有时可能会带来额外的压力。这项研究和其他研究挑战了情商对其拥有者始终有益的普遍观点。", "在一项研究中，德国法兰克福财经管理学院的心理学家Myriam Bechtoldt向166名男性大学生提出了一系列问题来测量他们的情商。例如，他们向学生展示人脸照片，并询问他们这些照片在多大程度上表达了快乐或厌恶等情感。然后学生们必须在表情严肃的评委面前进行求职演讲。科学家们测量了学生唾液中压力激素在演讲前后的浓度。", "在被评为情商较高的学生中，压力指标在实验期间增加得更多，恢复到基线水平所需的时间也更长。Bechtoldt说，研究结果表明，有些人可能在情感方面过于聪明，反而对自己不利。她指出：“有时你可能在某方面太擅长了，以至于它会带来麻烦。”", "事实上，这项研究为先前暗示情商阴暗面的研究增添了新证据。2002年发表在《个性与个体差异》上的一项研究表明，情感感知力强的人可能特别容易受到抑郁和绝望情绪的影响。此外，多项研究表明，情商可以被用来操纵他人以获取个人利益。", "需要更多研究来了解情商与压力之间的关系如何在女性以及不同年龄和教育水平的人群中发挥作用。尽管如此，Bechtoldt说，情商是一项有用的技能，只要你也学会正确应对情绪——无论是他人的还是你自己的。例如，一些敏感的人可能会为他人的悲伤或愤怒承担责任，这最终会给他们带来压力。记住，正如Bechtoldt所说，“你不必为他人的感受负责。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the finding of the new study?", "options": ["Emotional intelligence helps people get along with others.", "Emotional intelligence is generally beneficial to its bearer.", "People who are aware of others' feelings may experience more stress.", "People who are emotionally stressed may have trouble making friends."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "But a new study suggests that being sensitive to people's feelings may sometimes come with an extra dose of stress.", "explanation": "定位第一段第二句。转折词“But”引出新研究的核心发现：对他人情感敏感（being sensitive to people's feelings）有时会带来额外压力（extra dose of stress）。C项“aware of others' feelings”与“experience more stress”精准同义替换了原文表述。A、B两项均为首尾句提及的传统观点，而非新研究的发现。", "trapNote": "A项和B项均源自第一段中被“challenge”（挑战）的传统看法，属于典型的“新旧观点混淆”干扰项；D项则颠倒了原文“高敏感度带来压力”的因果关系。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What was the purpose of psychologist Myriam Bechtoldt's experiment?", "options": ["To define different types of human feelings.", "To assess the impacts of being emotionally clever.", "To demonstrate how to distinguish different feelings.", "To identify gender differences in emotional intelligence."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The scientists measured concentrations of stress hormones in the students' saliva(唾液) before and after the talk.", "explanation": "定位第二、三段实验过程与结果。Bechtoldt先通过看照片识别表情等方式测量166名男大学生的情商，再让他们在表情严肃的评委面前进行求职演讲，并测定演讲前后唾液中压力激素的浓度；随后第三段揭示高情商组压力指标上升更多、恢复更慢。由此可推知，该实验的目的是评估“高情商/情感敏锐（being emotionally clever）”所产生的影响，对应B项。实验仅招募了男性受试者，故排除D项。", "trapNote": "A项和C项均抓取了第二段举例中的局部动作（识别照片中的快乐或厌恶等情感），属于把实验中的“测量手段”误当作“实验目的”；D项与第二段“只测试男性”及第五段表述相矛盾。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the finding of Myriam Bechtoldt's study indicate?", "options": ["Greater emotional cleverness means less trouble in one's life.", "Emotional intelligence helps people succeed in job interviews.", "People's psychological wellbeing is related to various factors.", "People may suffer from having a high emotional intelligence"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The findings suggest that some people may be too emotionally clever for their own good, says Bechtoldt. \"Sometimes you can be so good at something that it causes trouble,\" she notes.", "explanation": "定位第三段。Bechtoldt指出，研究结果表明有些人可能在情感方面“过于聪明反而对自己不利”（too emotionally clever for their own good），她进一步解释说有时你太擅长某件事反而会带来麻烦（causes trouble）。选项D“People may suffer from having a high emotional intelligence”与该结论完全契合。A项与原文“causes trouble”意思相反；B项则借用第二段“job talks”制造无关联想。", "trapNote": "A项将原文“causes trouble”反向篡改为“less trouble”，属于正反混淆；B项则借用第二段实验场景中的“job talks”编造“有助于求职面试成功”的虚假推论。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about emotional intelligence from a number of studies?", "options": ["People suffering from depression are emotionally immature.", "People who look at the dark side of life often feel depressed.", "Some people may take advantage of it and benefit themselves.", "Some people may lack it and are easily manipulated by others."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Furthermore, several studies have implied that emotional intelligence can be used to manipulate others for personal gains.", "explanation": "定位第四段末句。题干中的“a number of studies”对应原文的“several studies”。该句明确指出，多项研究表明情商可以被用来操纵他人以获取个人利益（manipulate others for personal gains）。C项“Some people may take advantage of it and benefit themselves.”精准同义转述了原文中“利用情商谋取私利”的含义，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项借用了首句的“dark side”和次句的“depression”，将不同句子中的词汇强行拼凑在一起；D项则将原文“利用情商操纵他人”歪曲为“缺乏情商而易受人操纵”，篡改了逻辑主客体。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author suggest sensitive individuals do?", "options": ["Avoid burdening themselves with others' feelings.", "Rid themselves of worries over worldly affairs.", "Learn to cope with people's negative feelings.", "Help people to deal with their troubles in life."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Nevertheless, emotional intelligence is a useful skill to have, as long as you learn to also properly cope with emotions —both others' and your own, says Bechtoldt.", "explanation": "定位第五段第二、三句。Bechtoldt指出，情商仍是有用的技能，前提是学会恰当应对他人与自己的情绪（properly cope with emotions —both others' and your own），并随后以敏感者因他人的悲伤或愤怒（sadness or anger）而自责为例说明。C项“Learn to cope with people's negative feelings.”准确对应“cope with emotions”及后文所举的负面情绪，故正确。", "trapNote": "A项“避免让他人感受成为负担”看似贴近末句“不必为他人感受负责”，但前文强调的前提是主动学会“恰当应对情绪”而非单纯回避；D项将“应对情绪”偷换为“帮别人解决生活烦恼”，偏离原意。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 普遍的，盛行的", "note": "第一段“the prevailing view”意为“主流/普遍观点”，常与challenge、question等词搭配引出新研究结论。", "word": "prevailing"}, {"gloss": "adv. 始终如一地，一致地", "note": "由uniform + -ly构成，句中修饰beneficial，表示情商“一贯/全都”有益，往往是文章反驳的绝对化观点。", "word": "uniformly"}, {"gloss": "n. 浓度，含量；专注", "note": "熟词生义高频考点，在第二段科研语境中意为激素的“浓度”，而非日常常见的“注意力集中”。", "word": "concentration"}, {"gloss": "adj. 敏锐的，有洞察力的", "note": "来自perceive，第四段“emotionally perceptive people”即上文提到的对情感敏感的人群。", "word": "perceptive"}, {"gloss": "v. 操纵，控制，摆布", "note": "第四段核心动词，多含贬义，常用于表达为私利而暗中影响或利用他人。", "word": "manipulate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "This and other research challenge the prevailing view that emotional intelligence is uniformly beneficial to its bearer.", "point": "掌握同位语从句的结构特征，that在从句中不充当成分，仅对前面抽象名词view的内容进行具体解释说明。", "structure": "主语(This and other research) + 谓语(challenge) + 宾语(the prevailing view) + that引导的同位语从句(解释view的具体内容)", "zh": "这项研究和其他研究挑战了情商对其拥有者始终有益的普遍观点。"}, {"en": "For example, they showed the students photographs of people's faces and asked them to what extent feelings such as happiness or disgust were being expressed.", "point": "注意介词短语to what extent（在多大程度上）引导的宾语从句，从句使用陈述语序且包含过去进行时的被动语态（were being expressed）。", "structure": "主句(they showed... and asked them...) + to what extent引导的宾语从句(其中such as...作feelings的后置定语)", "zh": "例如，他们向学生展示人脸照片，并询问他们这些照片在多大程度上表达了快乐或厌恶等情感。"}, {"en": "For example, some sensitive individuals may assume responsibility for other people's sadness or anger, which ultimately stresses them out.", "point": "掌握which引导的非限制性定语从句指代前面整个主句事实的用法，以及短语stress sb. out（使某人承受巨大压力）。", "structure": "主句(some sensitive individuals may assume responsibility for...) + which引导的非限制性定语从句(指代前面整件事)", "zh": "例如，一些敏感的人可能会为他人的悲伤或愤怒承担责任，这最终会给他们带来巨大压力。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "be sensitive to（对……敏感）替换为aware of（察觉到/意识到）。", "option": "aware of others' feelings", "original": "being sensitive to people's feelings"}, {"note": "“伴随着额外剂量的压力”在选项中简化为“经历更多压力”。", "option": "experience more stress", "original": "come with an extra dose of stress"}, {"note": "“情绪上过于聪明反而不利/带来麻烦”对应“因高情商而受苦”。", "option": "suffer from having a high emotional intelligence", "original": "too emotionally clever for their own good / causes trouble"}, {"note": "“被用来操纵他人以获取个人利益”转述为“利用它来让自己获益”。", "option": "take advantage of it and benefit themselves", "original": "be used to manipulate others for personal gains"}, {"note": "第五段将“应对他人和自己的情绪”与后文“他人的悲伤或愤怒”结合，对应“应对人们的消极情绪”。", "option": "cope with people's negative feelings", "original": "cope with emotions —both others' and your own ... sadness or anger"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202112-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2021.12", "examSet": "2021.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2021.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "远程办公的隐性成本与利弊权衡", "subtitle": "剖析居家办公背后的成本转嫁与企业补偿难题", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 343, "paragraphs": ["As many office workers adapt to remote work, cities may undergo fundamental change if offices remain under-utilized. Who will benefit if working from home becomes the norm?", "Employers argue they make considerable savings on real estate when workers shift from office to home work. However, these savings result from passing costs on to workers.", "Unless employees are fully compensated, this could become a variant of parasitic(寄生的) capitalism, whereby corporate profits increasingly rely on extracting value from the public—and now personal—realm, rather than on generating new value.", "Though employers are backed by a chorus of remote work advocates, others note the loneliness, reduced productivity and inefficiencies of extended remote work.", "If working from home becomes permanent, employees will have to dedicate part of their private space to work. This requires purchasing desks, chairs and office equipment.", "It also means having private space dedicated to work: the space must be heated, cleaned, maintained and paid for. That depends on many things, but for purposes of illustration, I have run some estimates for Montreal. The exercise is simple but important, since it brings these costs out of the realm of speculation into the realm of meaningful discussion.", "Rough calculations show that the savings made by employers when their staff works from home are of similar value to the compensation workers should receive for setting up offices at home.", "What does this mean for offices in cities? One of two things may happen: Employers pass these costs onto employees. This would be a form of expropriation(侵占), with employees absorbing production costs that have traditionally been paid by the employer. This represents a considerable transfer of value from employees to employers.", "When employees are properly compensated, employers' real estate savings will be modest. If savings are modest, then the many advantages of working in offices—such as lively atmosphere, rapidity of communication, team-building and acclimatization(适应环境) of new employees—will encourage employers to shelve the idea of remote work and, like Yahoo in 2013, encourage employees to work most of the time from corporate office space."], "translations": ["随着许多办公室员工适应远程工作，如果办公室持续利用不足，城市可能会经历根本性变化。如果在家工作成为常态，谁将从中受益？", "雇主认为，当员工从办公室转向在家工作时，他们在房地产方面节省了大量开支。然而，这些节省是通过将成本转嫁给员工实现的。", "除非员工得到充分补偿，否则这可能成为寄生资本主义的一种变体，即企业利润越来越依赖于从公共领域——现在是个人领域——攫取价值，而不是创造新价值。", "尽管雇主得到了一群远程工作倡导者的支持，但也有人指出长期远程工作带来的孤独感、生产力下降和低效率问题。", "如果在家工作成为永久性安排，员工将不得不把私人空间的一部分用于工作。这需要购买办公桌、椅子和办公设备。", "这也意味着要有专门用于工作的私人空间：这个空间必须供暖、清洁、维护和支付费用。这取决于很多因素，但为了说明问题，我对蒙特利尔进行了一些估算。这个测算虽然简单但很重要，因为它把这些成本从推测领域带入了有意义的讨论领域。", "粗略计算表明，雇主在员工在家工作时节省的开支，与员工因在家建立办公室而应获得的补偿价值相当。", "这对城市中的办公室意味着什么？可能会发生两种情况之一：雇主将这些成本转嫁给员工。这将是一种侵占形式，员工承担了传统上由雇主支付的生产成本。这代表着价值从员工向雇主的大量转移。", "当员工得到适当补偿时，雇主在房地产方面的节省将是有限的。如果节省有限，那么在办公室工作的诸多优势——如活跃的氛围、快速的沟通、团队建设和新员工的适应环境——将促使雇主搁置远程工作的想法，并像2013年的雅虎那样，鼓励员工大部分时间在公司办公空间工作。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say about working from home?", "options": ["It will become the norm sooner or later.", "It requires employees to adapt promptly.", "It benefits employers at the expense of employees.", "It will force cities to transform their infrastructure."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Employers argue they make considerable savings on real estate when workers shift from office to home work. However, these savings result from passing costs on to workers.", "explanation": "定位至第2段。作者指出雇主声称员工转向居家办公能大幅节省房产开支，但紧接着用However转折点明，这些节省是通过将成本转嫁给员工实现的（passing costs on to workers）。第8段也进一步说明这是价值从员工向雇主的转移。选项C“它以牺牲员工为代价让雇主获益”精准概括了这一成本转嫁机制，故C为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项将第1段的假设条件if变为“迟早成为常态”，属于绝对化偷换；D项把第1段城市“经历根本性变化”过度曲解为被迫改造基础设施，均无原文依据。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why do some people oppose working from home?", "options": ["It discourages team spirit.", "It invades employees' privacy.", "It undermines traditional values.", "It negatively impacts productivity."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Though employers are backed by a chorus of remote work advocates, others note the loneliness, reduced productivity and inefficiencies of extended remote work.", "explanation": "定位至第4段。句首Though引导让步状语从句，指出虽然雇主得到了远程工作倡导者的支持，但另一部分人（others）指出了长期远程办公带来的三大弊端：孤独感（loneliness）、生产力下降（reduced productivity）以及低效率（inefficiencies）。选项D中的negatively impacts productivity精准对应reduced productivity，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项看似合理，但原文第9段仅提到“团队建设”是办公室工作的优势，并未将其列为部分人反对远程办公的原因；B项则是对第5段“私人空间”的望文生义。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why did the author run the estimates for Montreal?", "options": ["To provide convincing data for serious discussion.", "To illustrate the ongoing change in working patterns.", "To show the impact of remote working on productivity.", "To exemplify how remote working affects the economy."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "The exercise is simple but important, since it brings these costs out of the realm of speculation into the realm of meaningful discussion.", "explanation": "定位至第6段。作者在第二句提到对蒙特利尔进行居家办公成本估算（estimates for Montreal）是为了举例说明，随后在第三句用since引导原因状语从句指出，此举将相关成本从“猜测领域”带入了“有意义的讨论领域”（meaningful discussion）。选项A“为严肃讨论提供有说服力的数据”是对估算目的的准确同义转述，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项“说明工作模式的变化”、C项“展示对生产力的影响”和D项“举例说明如何影响经济”均偏离了本段核心——估算旨在量化私人空间维护成本以展开实质讨论。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we conclude from the author's calculations?", "options": ["There is no point in transferring office work to working from home.", "Employees can benefit as much from remote working as their employers.", "Employers' gain from remote working should go to employees as compensation.", "Effective measures should be taken to motivate employees to set up offices at home."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "Rough calculations show that the savings made by employers when their staff works from home are of similar value to the compensation workers should receive for setting up offices at home.", "explanation": "定位至第7段。作者的粗略计算表明，雇主在员工居家办公时节省的开支，与员工因在家设置办公空间而应获得的补偿（compensation）价值相当（of similar value）。结合第9段“员工得到适当补偿后雇主所省无几”可知，雇主因远程办公获得的收益本就应该作为补偿支付给员工。选项C准确概括了这一推论，故C为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项偷换概念，原文说的是雇主省下的钱与员工“应得的补偿”价值相等，而非员工实际获得了同等收益；A项表述过于绝对，并非计算结果的直接推论。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "What is the author's opinion on working from home?", "options": ["It should be avoided if possible.", "It is only a temporary measure.", "It can reduce companies' real estate costs.", "It may affect employees' corporate loyalty."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "If savings are modest, then the many advantages of working in offices—such as lively atmosphere, rapidity of communication, team-building and acclimatization(适应环境) of new employees—will encourage employers to shelve the idea of remote work and, like Yahoo in 2013, encourage employees to work most of the time from corporate office space.", "explanation": "定位至第9段及全文主旨。作者先批判雇主将成本转嫁给员工的做法是“寄生资本主义”和“侵占”，接着指出一旦给员工合理补偿，雇主节省的房产开支就所剩无几，而办公室在氛围、沟通、团队建设及新人适应方面的优势将促使雇主搁置远程办公计划（shelve the idea of remote work），回归公司办公。由此可见作者认为应尽量避免居家办公，故选A。", "trapNote": "C项只是第2段雇主单方面的说法，作者随后指出那是成本转嫁的结果且补偿后收益有限，不能代表作者核心观点；B、D两项在文中均未提及。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "补偿，赔偿", "note": "文中第3、7、9段多次出现被动或名词形式compensation，是判断远程办公是否公平的核心词。", "word": "compensate"}, {"gloss": "把……专用于；奉献", "note": "第5、6段用dedicate private space to work表示“将私人空间专门用于工作”，常接介词to。", "word": "dedicate"}, {"gloss": "猜测，推测", "note": "第6段out of the realm of speculation意为“脱离纯属猜测的范畴”，与meaningful discussion构成对比。", "word": "speculation"}, {"gloss": "侵占，征用", "note": "第8段作者借用该法律经济学术语，形象批判雇主无偿占用员工私人资源和成本的行为。", "word": "expropriation"}, {"gloss": "搁置，暂缓考虑", "note": "第9段shelve the idea of remote work意为“搁置远程办公的想法”，体现作者倾向回归线下办公的态度。", "word": "shelve"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Unless employees are fully compensated, this could become a variant of parasitic(寄生的) capitalism, whereby corporate profits increasingly rely on extracting value from the public—and now personal—realm, rather than on generating new value.", "point": "whereby在正式议论文中常用来引导定语从句，表示“凭此；借此机制”，相当于by which；rather than前后需保持语法结构平行（此处均为on + 动名词短语）。", "structure": "Unless引导条件状语从句 + 主句(this could become...) + whereby引导非限制性定语从句(修饰parasitic capitalism) + rather than并列对比结构", "zh": "除非员工得到充分补偿，否则这可能会演变成寄生资本主义的一种变体——在这种模式下，企业利润越来越依赖于从公共领域（如今还包括个人领域）攫取价值，而不是创造新的价值。"}, {"en": "If savings are modest, then the many advantages of working in offices—such as lively atmosphere, rapidity of communication, team-building and acclimatization(适应环境) of new employees—will encourage employers to shelve the idea of remote work and, like Yahoo in 2013, encourage employees to work most of the time from corporate office space.", "point": "长主语后常跟破折号插入语来补充例证，阅读时可先跳过双破折号之间的列举内容，直接抓住主干“the many advantages will encourage employers to...”。", "structure": "If引导条件状语从句 + 主句主语(the many advantages...) + 破折号插入语列举具体优势 + 并列谓语(will encourage... and encourage...)", "zh": "如果节省有限，那么在办公室工作的诸多优势——例如活跃的氛围、快速的沟通、团队建设以及新员工适应环境——将促使雇主搁置远程办公的想法，并像2013年的雅虎那样，鼓励员工大部分时间在公司办公空间工作。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“将成本转嫁给员工(passing costs on to workers)”被同义转述为“以牺牲员工为代价让雇主获益(at the expense of employees)”。", "option": "It benefits employers at the expense of employees.", "original": "these savings result from passing costs on to workers"}, {"note": "“降低的生产力”转述为“对生产力产生负面影响”，属于词性与动词化改写。", "option": "negatively impacts productivity", "original": "reduced productivity"}, {"note": "将估算结果从猜测带入“有意义的讨论”对应“为严肃讨论提供有说服力的数据”。", "option": "provide convincing data for serious discussion", "original": "brings these costs out of the realm of speculation into the realm of meaningful discussion"}, {"note": "“雇主省下的开支与员工应得补偿价值相当”推断转述为“雇主收益应作为补偿归员工所有”。", "option": "Employers' gain from remote working should go to employees as compensation.", "original": "the savings made by employers ... are of similar value to the compensation workers should receive"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202112-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2021.12", "examSet": "2021.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2021.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "人类好奇心的本质、动力与探索代价", "subtitle": "探讨好奇心如何推动物种演进及伴随的风险", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 336, "paragraphs": ["The human thirst for knowledge is the driving force behind our successful development as a species. But curiosity can also be dangerous, leading to setbacks or even downfalls. Given curiosity's complexity, scientists have found it hard to define.", "While pinning down a definition has proven tricky, the general consensus is it's some means of information gathering. Psychologists also agree curiosity is intrinsically(内在地) motivated.", "Curiosity covers such a large set of behaviors that there probably isn't any single \"curiosity gene\" that makes humans wonder about and explore their environment. That said, curiosity does have a genetic component. Genes and the environment interact in many complex ways to shape individuals and guide their behavior, including their curiosity.", "Regardless of their genetic makeup, infants have to learn an incredible amount of information in a short time, and curiosity is one of the tools humans have found to accomplish that gigantic task.", "Hundreds of studies show that infants prefer novelty. It's what motivates non-human animals, human infants and probably human adults to explore and seek out new things before growing less interested in them after continued exposure.", "But curiosity often comes with a cost.", "In some situations, the stakes are low and failure is a healthy part of growth. For instance, many babies are perfectly proficient crawlers, but they decide to try walking because there's more to see and do when they stand upright. But this milestone comes at a small cost. A study of 12- to 19-month-olds learning how to walk documented that these children fell down a lot. Seventeen times per hour, to be exact. But walking is faster than crawling, so this motivates expert crawlers to transition to walking.", "Sometimes, however, testing out a new idea can lead to disaster. For instance, the Inuit people of the Arctic regions have created incredible modes to deal with the challenges of living in northern climates, but what we forget about are the tens of thousands of people that tried and failed to make it in those challenging landscapes."], "translations": ["人类对知识的渴求是推动我们作为一个物种成功发展的驱动力。但好奇心也可能是危险的，会导致挫折甚至失败。鉴于好奇心的复杂性，科学家们发现很难对其下定义。", "虽然精确界定其定义被证明很棘手，但普遍共识是它是某种信息收集的手段。心理学家也认同好奇心是内在驱动的。", "好奇心涵盖如此大量的行为，以至于可能不存在任何单一的“好奇心基因”使人类对其环境感到好奇并进行探索。也就是说，好奇心确实有遗传成分。基因和环境以许多复杂的方式相互作用，塑造个体并引导他们的行为，包括他们的好奇心。", "无论他们的基因构成如何，婴儿都必须在短时间内学习大量信息，而好奇心是人类为完成这一巨大任务而找到的工具之一。", "数百项研究表明，婴儿偏好新奇事物。正是这种偏好激励着非人类动物、人类婴儿以及可能的人类成年人去探索和寻求新事物，然后在持续接触后对它们逐渐失去兴趣。", "但好奇心往往伴随着代价。", "在某些情况下，风险很低，失败是成长过程中健康的一部分。例如，许多婴儿爬行非常熟练，但他们决定尝试走路，因为当他们直立时可以看到和做更多事情。但这一里程碑伴随着小小的代价。一项针对12至19个月大正在学习走路的婴儿的研究记录显示，这些孩子经常摔倒。准确地说，每小时17次。但走路比爬行更快，因此这激励熟练的爬行者过渡到走路。", "然而，有时测试一个新想法可能导致灾难。例如，北极地区的因纽特人创造了令人惊叹的方式来应对在北方气候中生活的挑战，但我们忘记的是成千上万试图在那些充满挑战的环境中生存但失败了的人。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say about curiosity?", "options": ["It is too complex for non-scientists to understand.", "It is the force that pushes human society forward.", "It is a unique trait specific to the human race.", "It is often the major cause for human failures."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The human thirst for knowledge is the driving force behind our successful development as a species.", "explanation": "定位至第1段首句。作者指出人类对知识的渴求（即好奇心）是推动我们作为一个物种成功发展的驱动力（the driving force behind our successful development）。选项B“它是推动人类社会前进的力量”是对首句核心观点的直接同义转述，其中pushes... forward对应driving force behind... development，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项曲解第1段末句“科学家都很难对其下定义”，偷换为“非科学家无法理解”；C项与第5段提到的“非人类动物也有好奇探索动机”相矛盾；D项把“可能导致失败”夸大为“主要原因”。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the general understanding of curiosity?", "options": ["It motivates people to seek information.", "It is destined to transform human genes.", "It does people more good than harm.", "It underlies all human behaviors."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "While pinning down a definition has proven tricky, the general consensus is it's some means of information gathering.", "explanation": "定位至第2段首句。题干中的general understanding对应原文的general consensus（普遍共识）。句子指出尽管精确定义好奇心很棘手，但普遍共识认为它是某种收集信息的手段（some means of information gathering），且下文补充它是内在驱动的。选项A“它激励人们寻求信息”精准契合这一共识，故A为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项无中生有，第3段仅说明好奇心有遗传成分，并非改变基因；C项对比“利大于弊”文中未作此比较；D项中的all human behaviors过于绝对。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about how genes shape people's behavior?", "options": ["They determine people's way of thinking.", "They account for age differences in learning.", "They enable people to undertake massive tasks.", "They work in conjunction with the environment."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Genes and the environment interact in many complex ways to shape individuals and guide their behavior, including their curiosity.", "explanation": "定位至第3段末句。题干询问基因如何塑造人的行为。原文明确指出，基因与环境以多种复杂的方式相互作用（interact in many complex ways），从而塑造个体并引导他们的行为，包括好奇心。选项D中的work in conjunction with the environment（与环境共同作用）精准对应interact，故D为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“决定思维方式”属于绝对化臆测，原文强调的是基因与环境交互引导行为；C项将第4段“婴儿借助好奇心完成繁重学习任务”张冠李戴给了基因。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do numerous studies show about infants?", "options": ["They are far more curious than adults.", "They prefer to go after all that is novel.", "They have different interests than adults.", "They show non-human animal behaviors."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Hundreds of studies show that infants prefer novelty.", "explanation": "定位至第5段首句及第二句。题干中的numerous studies对应原文的Hundreds of studies。首句明确指出数百项研究表明“婴儿偏好新奇事物”（infants prefer novelty），第二句补充这激励他们去探索和寻求新事物（explore and seek out new things）。选项B“他们倾向于追求一切新奇事物”为直接同义转述，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项和C项均制造了文中不存在的“婴儿与成年人的比较”；D项曲解了原文，原文只是说非人类动物、婴儿和成人一样都受好奇心驱动去探索，而非婴儿表现出动物行为。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "例证题", "stem": "What does the example of the Inuit people of the Arctic regions illustrate?", "options": ["The cost of humans' curiosity to explore.", "The incredible harshness of cold weather.", "The innovative ideas stemming from curiosity.", "The importance of learning from past failures."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "Sometimes, however, testing out a new idea can lead to disaster.", "explanation": "定位至第8段（并结合第6段主题句）。第6段总领指出好奇心往往伴随代价（comes with a cost），第7段讲低风险的小代价（学步摔倒），第8段首句用however转折指出“尝试新想法有时会导致灾难”，随后以For instance引出北极因纽特人的例子，强调在人们记住成功适应极地气候的同时，往往遗忘了无数尝试并失败丧生的人。可见该例子旨在印证好奇探索可能付出的沉重代价，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项只停留在例子表面的自然环境描写，未触及段落论点；C项仅抓住前半句“创造了惊人的应对方式”，忽略了but后真正要强调的无数失败者的代价。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "确切说明；查明", "note": "第2段pinning down a definition意为“精确界定一个定义”，常用于描述抽象概念难以捉摸。", "word": "pin down"}, {"gloss": "内在地，本质上", "note": "第2段intrinsically motivated表示“由内在驱动的”，常与extrinsically（外在地）构成反义对照。", "word": "intrinsically"}, {"gloss": "新奇；新颖的事物", "note": "第5段infants prefer novelty是研究结论核心词，其形容词形式novel意为“新奇的，新颖的”。", "word": "novelty"}, {"gloss": "里程碑，重要阶段", "note": "第7段用this milestone指代婴儿从爬行过渡到直立行走这一关键成长节点。", "word": "milestone"}, {"gloss": "过渡，转变", "note": "第7段transition to walking意为“向行走过渡”，可作动词或名词使用，常接介词to或from。", "word": "transition"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Curiosity covers such a large set of behaviors that there probably isn't any single \"curiosity gene\" that makes humans wonder about and explore their environment.", "point": "such ... that ...引导结果状语从句，注意从句内部又嵌套了一个修饰“curiosity gene”的定语从句，wonder about和explore共同接宾语their environment。", "structure": "主句(Curiosity covers such... that...)结果状语从句 + there be否定句 + that引导定语从句(修饰curiosity gene)", "zh": "好奇心涵盖的行为范围如此广泛，以至于可能根本不存在任何单一的“好奇心基因”能促使人类对周围环境产生好奇并加以探索。"}, {"en": "It's what motivates non-human animals, human infants and probably human adults to explore and seek out new things before growing less interested in them after continued exposure.", "point": "表语从句中包含三个并列宾语（非人类动物、人类婴儿、人类成年人），before后省略了主语而直接使用动名词短语growing less interested in them，表示动作的先后演变。", "structure": "It's what...表语从句 + motivate sb. to do sth. + before引导时间状语(接动名词growing...)", "zh": "正是这种偏好激励着非人类动物、人类婴儿以及可能还有人类成年人去探索和寻找新事物，而在持续接触后对它们逐渐失去兴趣。"}, {"en": "For instance, the Inuit people of the Arctic regions have created incredible modes to deal with the challenges of living in northern climates, but what we forget about are the tens of thousands of people that tried and failed to make it in those challenging landscapes.", "point": "转折连词but后为文章真正的观点重心所在，what we forget about作主语从句，make it为固定搭配，意为“成功；渡过难关；活下来”。", "structure": "前半句(have created... to deal with...) + but并列转折 + what引导主语从句 + that引导定语从句(修饰people)", "zh": "例如，北极地区的因纽特人创造了令人惊叹的方式来应对北方气候下的生存挑战，但我们往往忘记的是，曾有成千上万人在那些充满挑战的环境中尝试并最终失败。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“推动物种成功发展的驱动力”同义转述为“推动人类社会向前的力量”。", "option": "the force that pushes human society forward", "original": "the driving force behind our successful development as a species"}, {"note": "“普遍共识认为它是收集信息的手段”与“激励人们寻求信息”形成核心语义对应。", "option": "It motivates people to seek information.", "original": "the general consensus is it's some means of information gathering"}, {"note": "动词interact（相互作用）同义改写为短语work in conjunction with（与……共同起作用）。", "option": "They work in conjunction with the environment.", "original": "Genes and the environment interact in many complex ways"}, {"note": "Hundreds of studies对应numerous studies，名词novelty改写为定语从句all that is novel。", "option": "They prefer to go after all that is novel.", "original": "Hundreds of studies show that infants prefer novelty."}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202012-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2020.12", "examSet": "2020.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2020.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "学校心理健康服务的挑战与出路", "subtitle": "呼吁加大校内心理健康早期干预服务投入，重塑学校服务职能", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 344, "paragraphs": ["Three children in every classroom have a diagnosable mental health condition. Half of these are behavioural disorders, while one third are emotional disorders such as stress, anxiety and depression, which often become outwardly apparent through self-harm. There was an astonishing 52 percent jump in hospital admissions for children and young people who had harmed themselves between 2009 and 2015.", "Schools and teachers have consistently reported the scale of the problem since 2009. Last year, over half of teachers reported that more of their pupils experience mental health problems than in the past. But teachers also consistently report how ill-equipped they feel to meet pupils' mental health needs, and often cite a lack of training, expertise and support from the National Health Service(英国国家医疗服务体系).", "Part of the reason for the increased pressure on schools is that there are now fewer 'early intervention(干预)' and low-level mental health services based in the community. Cuts to local authority budgets since 2010 have resulted in a significant decline of these services, despite strong evidence of their effectiveness in preventing crises further down the line.", "The only way to break the pressures on both mental health services and schools is to reinvest in early intervention services inside schools.", "There are strong arguments for why schools are best placed to provide mental health services. Schools see young people more than any other service, which gives them a unique ability to get to hard-to-reach children and young people and build meaningful relationships with them over time. Recent studies have shown that children and young people largely prefer to see a counsellor in school rather than in an outside environment. Young people have reported that for low-level conditions such as stress and anxiety, a clinical setting can sometimes be daunting(令人却步的).", "There are already examples of innovative schools which combine mental health and wellbeing provision with a strong academic curriculum. This will, though, require a huge cultural shift. Politicians, policymakers, commissioners and school leaders must be brave enough to make the leap towards reimagining schools as providers of health as well as education services."], "translations": ["每个教室里有三名儿童患有可诊断的心理健康疾病。其中一半是行为障碍，三分之一是情绪障碍，如压力、焦虑和抑郁，这些往往通过自残行为表现出来。2009年至2015年间，因自残而入院的儿童和青少年人数惊人地增长了52%。", "自2009年以来，学校和教师一直在反映这一问题的严重程度。去年，超过半数的教师报告称，与过去相比，有更多学生出现心理健康问题。但教师们也一直反映，他们感到自己缺乏应对学生心理健康需求的能力，并经常提到缺乏来自英国国家医疗服务体系的培训、专业知识和支持。", "学校压力增加的部分原因是，目前社区中的“早期干预”和低阶心理健康服务减少了。自2010年以来地方政府预算的削减导致这些服务大幅萎缩，尽管有充分证据表明它们在预防后续危机方面非常有效。", "打破心理健康服务机构与学校双方压力的唯一途径，是重新投资校内早期干预服务。", "有充分的理由说明为什么学校最适合提供心理健康服务。学校比任何其他服务机构更多地接触青少年，这使它们具有独特的能力去接触难以触及的儿童和青少年，并随着时间推移与他们建立有意义的关系。最近的研究表明，儿童和青少年大多更愿意在学校而非外部环境中见心理咨询师。青少年反映，对于压力和焦虑等轻度症状，临床环境有时会令人却步。", "已经有一些创新学校的例子，它们将心理健康与身心福祉保障和强大的学术课程相结合。然而，这需要巨大的文化转变。政治家、政策制定者、专员和学校领导者必须有足够的勇气迈出这一步，重新将学校构想为同时提供健康服务与教育服务的机构。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What are teachers complaining about?", "options": ["There are too many students requiring special attention.", "They are under too much stress counselling needy students.", "Schools are inadequately equipped to implement any intervention.", "They lack the necessary resources to address pupils' mental problems."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But teachers also consistently report how ill-equipped they feel to meet pupils' mental health needs, and often cite a lack of training, expertise and support from the National Health Service(英国国家医疗服务体系).", "explanation": "第2段第3句明确指出，教师们一直反映他们感到自己“缺乏应对学生心理健康需求的能力（ill-equipped）”，并常提到“缺乏来自英国国家医疗服务体系的培训、专业知识和支持（a lack of training, expertise and support）”。选项D中的“lack the necessary resources（缺乏必要资源）”正是对原文“ill-equipped”和“lack of training, expertise and support”的同义转述，而“address pupils' mental problems”对应“meet pupils' mental health needs”。", "trapNote": "A项偷换主体，第2段只说超过半数教师反映学生心理问题增多，并非抱怨“需特殊关注的学生太多”；C项将“教师自身缺乏能力”偷换为“学校设备不足”。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about community health services in Britain?", "options": ["They have deteriorated due to budget cuts.", "They facilitate local residents' everyday lives.", "They prove ineffective in helping mental patients.", "They cover preventative care for the local resident."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Cuts to local authority budgets since 2010 have resulted in a significant decline of these services, despite strong evidence of their effectiveness in preventing crises further down the line.", "explanation": "第3段第2句提到，自2010年以来“地方政府预算的削减导致这些服务大幅减少（resulted in a significant decline of these services）”，其中的“these services”指代前一句中的社区“早期干预和低阶心理健康服务”。选项A中的“deteriorated due to budget cuts（因预算削减而恶化）”精准概括了“cuts to budgets”与“significant decline”之间的因果关系。", "trapNote": "C项与原文完全相反，第3段末尾明确指出有“充分证据表明它们有效（strong evidence of their effectiveness）”；D项属于无中生有，原文仅提及预防后续危机。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Where does the author suggest mental health services be placed?", "options": ["At home.", "At school.", "In hospitals.", "In communities."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The only way to break the pressures on both mental health services and schools is to reinvest in early intervention services inside schools.", "explanation": "第4段全段仅有一句主旨句，指出打破心理健康服务与学校双重压力的唯一方法，是“重新投资校内早期干预服务（reinvest in early intervention services inside schools）”。此外第5段首句也强调学校最适合提供此类服务。选项B“At school”是对原文“inside schools”的直接定位与同义替换，故答案为B。", "trapNote": "D项“在社区”是典型的干扰项，第3段提到的是“社区早期干预服务因预算削减而减少”，并非作者建议放置的位置；C项“在医院”则与第5段“临床环境令人却步”相反。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the recent studies?", "options": ["Students prefer to rely on peers to relieve stress and anxiety.", "Young people are keen on building meaningful relationships.", "Students are more comfortable seeking counselling in school.", "Young people benefit from various kinds of outdoor activities."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Recent studies have shown that children and young people largely prefer to see a counsellor in school rather than in an outside environment.", "explanation": "第5段第3句引用近期研究指出：“儿童和青少年大多更愿意在学校而非外部环境中见咨询师（largely prefer to see a counsellor in school rather than in an outside environment）”。选项C中的“more comfortable seeking counselling in school”恰当转述了“prefer to see a counsellor in school”，故答案为C。", "trapNote": "B项利用第5段第2句的“build meaningful relationships”拼凑干扰，原文主语是“学校与青少年建立关系”，而非“青少年热衷于此”；A项“依靠同龄人”属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the author mean by a cultural shift (Line 2, Para. 6)?", "options": ["Simplification of schools' academic curriculums.", "Parents' involvement in schools' policy-making.", "A change in teachers' attitudes to mental health.", "A change in the conception of what schools are."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Politicians, policymakers, commissioners and school leaders must be brave enough to make the leap towards reimagining schools as providers of health as well as education services.", "explanation": "第6段第2句提到这一转变需要“巨大的文化转变（a huge cultural shift）”，紧接着第3句具体解释其内涵：各方必须勇敢迈出这一步，“重新将学校设想为健康和教育服务的提供者（reimagining schools as providers of health as well as education services）”。选项D中的“对学校本质观念的改变（change in the conception of what schools are）”精准对应了“reimagining schools as...”。", "trapNote": "A项曲解第6段首句“强大的学术课程”，原文并未主张简化课程；C项将转变范围缩小为“教师对心理健康的态度”，而原文强调的是政界、决策者及校方对学校定位的重新构想。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 诊断，判断（疾病）", "note": "派生词 diagnosable adj. 可诊断的；diagnosis n. 诊断", "word": "diagnose"}, {"gloss": "adj. 准备不足的，缺乏能力的", "note": "be ill-equipped to do sth. 缺乏能力/条件做某事", "word": "ill-equipped"}, {"gloss": "n. 干预，介入", "note": "early intervention 早期干预；动词 intervene", "word": "intervention"}, {"gloss": "adj. 令人却步的，使人气馁的", "note": "动词 daunt 使胆怯；文中形容医院等临床诊疗环境让人感到压力", "word": "daunting"}, {"gloss": "v. 重新设想，重新构想", "note": "re-（重新）+ imagine（想象），reimagine A as B 将A重新定位为B", "word": "reimagine"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Half of these are behavioural disorders, while one third are emotional disorders such as stress, anxiety and depression, which often become outwardly apparent through self-harm.", "point": "while 表对比并列（……而……），which 引导非限制性定语从句，修饰前面的 emotional disorders。", "structure": "主句1 (Half of these are...) + while + 主句2 (one third are...) + such as 举例 + which 引导的非限制性定语从句", "zh": "其中一半是行为障碍，而三分之一是情绪障碍，如压力、焦虑和抑郁，这些障碍往往通过自残行为在外在表现出来。"}, {"en": "Schools see young people more than any other service, which gives them a unique ability to get to hard-to-reach children and young people and build meaningful relationships with them over time.", "point": "which 指代整个主句内容；不定式 to get to... and build... 作后置定语修饰 ability；hard-to-reach 为复合形容词作前置定语。", "structure": "主句 (Schools see...) + which 引导的非限制性定语从句 (which gives them a unique ability + 并列不定式短语)", "zh": "学校比任何其他服务机构更多地接触青少年，这使它们具有独特的能力去接触难以触及的儿童和青少年，并随着时间推移与他们建立有意义的关系。"}, {"en": "Politicians, policymakers, commissioners and school leaders must be brave enough to make the leap towards reimagining schools as providers of health as well as education services.", "point": "be + adj. + enough to do sth. 表示“足够……以至于能够做某事”；towards 为介词，后接动名词 reimagining...。", "structure": "并列主语 + must be brave enough to make the leap towards + 动名词短语 (reimagining... as...)", "zh": "政治家、政策制定者、专员和学校领导者必须有足够的勇气迈出这一步，重新将学校构想为同时提供健康服务与教育服务的机构。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“准备不足”与“缺乏培训、专业知识和支持”对应选项中的“缺乏必要资源”", "option": "lack the necessary resources", "original": "ill-equipped ... a lack of training, expertise and support"}, {"note": "“显著减少/下滑”与“预算削减”对应选项中的“因预算削减而恶化”", "option": "deteriorated due to budget cuts", "original": "Cuts to local authority budgets ... resulted in a significant decline"}, {"note": "“更愿意在学校见咨询师”对应选项中的“在学校寻求咨询更自在”", "option": "more comfortable seeking counselling in school", "original": "prefer to see a counsellor in school"}, {"note": "“重新将学校构想为……”对应选项中的“对学校本质观念的转变”", "option": "a change in the conception of what schools are", "original": "reimagining schools as providers of health as well as education services"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-202012-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2020.12", "examSet": "2020.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2020.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "消费决策中的“诱饵效应”剖析", "subtitle": "以电影院汽水和《经济学人》定价为例，揭示相对价值判断背后的心理机制", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 345, "paragraphs": ["Picture this: You're at a movie theater food stand loading up on snacks. You have a choice of a small, medium or large soda. The small is $3.50 and the large is $5.50. It's a tough decision: The small size may not last you through the whole movie, but $5.50 for some sugary drink seems ridiculous. But there's a third option, a medium soda for $5.25. Medium may be the perfect amount of soda for you, but the large is only a quarter more. If you're like most people, you end up buying the large (and taking a bathroom break midshow).", "If you're wondering who would buy the medium soda, the answer is almost no one. In fact, there's a good chance the marketing department purposely priced the medium soda as a decoy(诱饵), making you more likely to buy the large soda rather than the small.", "I have written about this peculiarity in human nature before with my friend Dan Ariely, who studied this phenomenon extensively after noticing pricing for subscriptions(订阅) to The Economist. The digital subscription was $59, the print subscription was $125, and the print plus digital subscription was also $125. No one in their right mind would buy the print subscription when you could get digital as well for the same price, so why was it even an option? Ariely ran an experiment and found that when only the two \"real\" choices were offered, more people chose the less-expensive digital subscription. But the addition of the bad option made people much more likely to choose the more expensive print plus digital option.", "Brain scientists call this effect \"asymmetric dominance\" and it means that people gravitate toward the choice nearest a clearly inferior option. Marketing professors call it the decoy effect, which is certainly easier to remember. Lucky for consumers, almost no one in the business community understands it.", "The decoy effect works because of the way our brains assign value when making choices. Value is almost never absolute; rather, we decide an object's value relative to our other choices. If more options are introduced, the value equation changes."], "translations": ["想象一下这个场景：你在电影院的小卖部购买零食。你可以选择小杯、中杯或大杯汽水。小杯3.50美元，大杯5.50美元。这是个艰难的决定：小杯可能不够你喝完整场电影，但花5.50美元买些含糖饮料似乎很荒谬。但还有第三个选择，中杯汽水5.25美元。中杯也许正好是你需要的汽水量，但大杯只贵了两毛五。如果你和大多数人一样，最终会买大杯（然后在电影放映中途去趟洗手间）。", "如果你想知道谁会买中杯汽水，答案是几乎没有人。事实上，营销部门很可能故意将中杯汽水定价为诱饵，让你更有可能购买大杯而不是小杯汽水。", "我之前曾与朋友丹·艾瑞里就人性中的这一特点写过文章，他在注意到《经济学人》的订阅定价后对这一现象进行了广泛研究。电子版订阅是59美元，纸质版订阅是125美元，而纸质版加电子版订阅也是125美元。没有人会在同样价格能获得电子版的情况下购买纸质版订阅，那为什么它还是一个选项呢？艾瑞里进行了一项实验，发现当只提供两个“真实”选择时，更多人选择了较便宜的电子版订阅。但加入这个糟糕选项后，人们更有可能选择更贵的纸质版加电子版选项。", "脑科学家称这种效应为“不对称优势”，它意味着人们倾向于选择最接近明显较差选项的那个选择。营销学教授称之为诱饵效应，这显然更容易记住。对消费者来说幸运的是，商界几乎没有人理解它。", "诱饵效应起作用是因为我们的大脑在做选择时赋予价值的方式。价值几乎从来不是绝对的；相反，我们是相对于其他选择来决定一个物品的价值。如果引入更多选项，价值等式就会改变。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Why does the author ask us to imagine buying food in the movie theater?", "options": ["To illustrate people's peculiar shopping behavior.", "To illustrate the increasing variety of snacks there.", "To show how hard it can be to choose a drink there.", "To show how popular snacks are among movie fans."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "I have written about this peculiarity in human nature before with my friend Dan Ariely, who studied this phenomenon extensively after noticing pricing for subscriptions(订阅) to The Economist.", "explanation": "文章开篇第1段描绘了电影院买大杯汽水的常见情景，第2段指出这是营销部门故意设置的“诱饵”。随后第3段首句总结道，作者曾与朋友丹·艾瑞里写过“人性中的这一特点（this peculiarity in human nature）”。选项A中的“peculiar shopping behavior”精准呼应第3段的“peculiarity”，说明开篇举例正是为了引出并阐释人们奇特的消费心理与购物行为。", "trapNote": "C项只停留在第1段表面细节“it's a tough decision”，忽视了例子背后要论证的“诱饵效应”这一深层主题；B项“零食种类增多”与D项“零食受欢迎”均偏离主旨。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Why is the medium soda priced the way it is?", "options": ["To attract more customers to buy it.", "To show the price matches the amount.", "To ensure customers drink the right amount of soda.", "To make customers believe they are getting a bargain."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "In fact, there's a good chance the marketing department purposely priced the medium soda as a decoy(诱饵), making you more likely to buy the large soda rather than the small.", "explanation": "第2段明确指出，营销部门故意将中杯汽水定价为诱饵，“让你更有可能购买大杯而不是小杯汽水（making you more likely to buy the large soda rather than the small）”。结合第1段数据，中杯5.25美元而大杯仅5.50美元，“大杯只贵两毛五（only a quarter more）”，这种定价策略让消费者觉得买大杯很划算、占了便宜（getting a bargain），从而落入消费陷阱。", "trapNote": "A项与原文完全相反，第2段首句明确说明几乎没有人会买中杯汽水；B、C两项则是按照常规理性消费臆测出的干扰项，偏离了营销诱饵的真实意图。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What do we learn from Dan Ariely's experiment?", "options": ["Lower-priced goods attract more customers.", "The Economist's promotional strategy works.", "The Economist's print edition turns out to sell the best.", "More readers choose the digital over the print edition."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "But the addition of the bad option made people much more likely to choose the more expensive print plus digital option.", "explanation": "第3段后半部分描述了丹·艾瑞里针对《经济学人》订阅方案所做的实验：当只提供电子版（59美元）和纸质加电子版（125美元）两个真实选项时，更多人选便宜的电子版；但加入“纯纸质版（125美元）”这一糟糕选项后，“人们更有可能选择更贵的纸质加电子版选项”。选项B由此合理推断出《经济学人》借助诱饵的促销策略确实奏效，故答案为B。", "trapNote": "A项只片面概括了没有诱饵时的实验前半段结果，忽略了实验的核心结论；C、D两项均把“纸质加电子版”偷换成了“纯纸质版”，属于张冠李戴。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "For what purpose is \"the bad option\" (Line 7, Para. 3) added?", "options": ["To cater to the peculiar needs of some customers.", "To help customers to make more rational choices.", "To trap customers into buying the more pricey item.", "To provide customers with a greater variety of goods."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "But the addition of the bad option made people much more likely to choose the more expensive print plus digital option.", "explanation": "第3段末尾明确解释了加入“糟糕选项（the bad option，即同为125美元的纯纸质版）”后的效果：“让人们更有可能选择更贵的纸质加电子版选项（made people much more likely to choose the more expensive print plus digital option）”。选项C中的“trap customers into buying the more pricey item（诱使顾客购买更昂贵的商品）”正是对这一促销目的的准确转述。", "trapNote": "B项与诱饵效应的原理正好相反，诱饵会误导而非帮助顾客做出理性选择；D项“提供更多样的商品”只是表面假象，并非商家增设这一毫无性价比选项的真正目的。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How do we assess the value of a commodity, according to the passage?", "options": ["By considering its usefulness.", "By comparing it with other choices.", "By taking its quality into account.", "By examining its value equation."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Value is almost never absolute; rather, we decide an object's value relative to our other choices.", "explanation": "第5段第2句直接给出了答案：“价值几乎从来不是绝对的；相反，我们是相对于其他选择来决定一个物品的价值（rather, we decide an object's value relative to our other choices）”。选项B中的“By comparing it with other choices（通过与其他选择进行比较）”正是对“relative to our other choices”的同义转述，故答案为B。", "trapNote": "A项“考虑实用性”和C项“考虑质量”在文中均未提及，属于常识性臆断干扰项；D项虽原词复现了第5段末句的“value equation”，但“检验价值等式”曲解了原文含义。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 特性，怪癖", "note": "派生自 peculiar adj. 奇特的；文中指人类非理性选择的消费特性", "word": "peculiarity"}, {"gloss": "n. 诱饵，圈套；v. 引诱", "note": "decoy effect 诱饵效应，指通过设置明显劣势的选项来引导消费者选择高价目标商品", "word": "decoy"}, {"gloss": "n. 订阅，订购", "note": "动词 subscribe (to) 订阅，如 subscribe to a magazine", "word": "subscription"}, {"gloss": "adj. 较差的，劣等的，下级的", "note": "be inferior to 劣于……，反义词为 superior（较优的）", "word": "inferior"}, {"gloss": "v. 分配，赋予（价值、任务等）", "note": "assign value to... 为……赋予价值；名词 assignment 作业/任务", "word": "assign"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In fact, there's a good chance the marketing department purposely priced the medium soda as a decoy(诱饵), making you more likely to buy the large soda rather than the small.", "point": "there's a good chance (that)... 表示“极有可能……”；现在分词短语 making you more likely to... 作结果状语。", "structure": "there's a good chance + 省略 that 的同位语从句 + 现在分词短语作结果状语", "zh": "事实上，营销部门极有可能故意将中杯汽水定价为诱饵，让你更有可能购买大杯而不是小杯汽水。"}, {"en": "I have written about this peculiarity in human nature before with my friend Dan Ariely, who studied this phenomenon extensively after noticing pricing for subscriptions(订阅) to The Economist.", "point": "who 引导非限制性定语从句修饰先行词 Dan Ariely；after noticing... 为介词短语作时间状语。", "structure": "主句 (I have written about...) + who 引导的非限制性定语从句 (who studied... + after noticing...)", "zh": "我之前曾与朋友丹·艾瑞里就人性中的这一特点写过文章，他在注意到《经济学人》的订阅定价后对这一现象进行了广泛研究。"}, {"en": "Ariely ran an experiment and found that when only the two \"real\" choices were offered, more people chose the less-expensive digital subscription.", "point": "found 后接 that 引导的宾语从句，该从句内部又嵌套了 when 引导的时间状语从句。", "structure": "主语 + 并列谓语 (ran... and found) + that 宾语从句 (when 时间状语从句 + 主句)", "zh": "艾瑞里进行了一项实验，发现当只提供那两个“真实”选择时，更多人选择了较便宜的电子版订阅。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第3段中“人性中的这一特点”呼应第1段情景，对应选项中的“奇特的购物行为”", "option": "people's peculiar shopping behavior", "original": "this peculiarity in human nature"}, {"note": "“更可能选择更贵的纸质加电子版”对应选项中的“诱使顾客买更贵的商品”", "option": "trap customers into buying the more pricey item", "original": "made people much more likely to choose the more expensive print plus digital option"}, {"note": "“相对于其他选择来决定价值”对应选项中的“通过与其他选择作比较”", "option": "comparing it with other choices", "original": "decide an object's value relative to our other choices"}, {"note": "中杯与大杯仅差25美分，让消费者产生“买大杯很划算”的心理", "option": "getting a bargain", "original": "the large is only a quarter more"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-201912-s1-p1", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2019.12", "examSet": "2019.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2019.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "AI助教如何破解网课答疑难题", "subtitle": "人工智能教学助手Jill Watson的研发与应用", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 333, "paragraphs": ["Professor Ashok Goel of Georgia Tech developed an artificially intelligent teaching assistant to help handle the enormous number of student questions in the online class, Knowledge-Based Artificial Intelligence. This online course is a core requirement of Georgia Tech's online Master of Science in Computer Science program. Professor Goel already had eight teaching assistants, but that wasn't enough to deal with the overwhelming number of daily questions from students.", "Many students drop out of online courses because of the lack of teaching support. When students feel isolated or confused and reach out with questions that go unanswered, their motivation to continue begins to fade. Professor Goel decided to do something to remedy this situation and his solution was to create a virtual assistant named Jill Watson, which is based on the IBM Watson platform.", "Goel and his team developed several versions of Jill Watson before releasing her to the online forums. At first, the virtual assistant wasn't too great. But Goel and his team sourced the online discussion forum to find all 40,000 questions that had ever been asked since the class was launched. Then they began to feed Jill with the questions and answers. After some adjustments, and sufficient time, Jill was able to answer the students' questions correctly 97% of the time. The virtual assistant became so advanced and realistic that the students didn't know she was a computer. The students, who were studying artificial intelligence, were interacting with the virtual assistant and couldn't tell it apart from a real human being. Goel didn't inform them about Jill's true identity until April 26. The students were actually very positive about the experience.", "The goal of Professor Goel's virtual assistant next year is to take over answering 40% of all the questions posed by students on the online forum. The name Jill Watson will, of course, change to something else next semester. Professor Goel has a much rosier outlook on the future of artificial intelligence than, say, Elon Musk, Stephen Hawking, Bill Gates or Steve Wozniak."], "translations": ["佐治亚理工学院的Ashok Goel教授开发了一名人工智能教学助手，用于帮助处理在线课程“基于知识的人工智能”中海量的学生提问。这门在线课程是佐治亚理工学院计算机科学在线理学硕士项目的核心必修课。Goel教授手下已经有八名助教，但仍不足以应对每天来自学生的铺天盖地的提问。", "许多学生因缺乏教学支持而中途退出在线课程。当学生感到孤立或困惑、提出问题却无人解答时，他们继续学习的动力就会开始消退。Goel教授决定采取措施改变这一现状，他的解决方案是依托IBM Watson平台打造一个名为Jill Watson的虚拟助手。", "Goel和他的团队在将Jill Watson发布到在线论坛之前，开发了多个版本。起初，这名虚拟助手表现并不太理想。但Goel和团队搜集了该课程开课以来在线讨论区中出现过的全部4万个问题，随后开始向Jill输入这些问题和答案。经过一些调整和充分的训练时间后，Jill正确回答学生问题的准确率达到了97%。这个虚拟助手变得如此先进和逼真，以至于学生们根本不知道她是一台计算机。这些正在学习人工智能的学生与虚拟助手互动时，完全无法将它与真人区分开来。直到4月26日，Goel才告知他们Jill的真实身份。实际上，学生们对这次体验的反馈非常积极。", "明年，Goel教授的虚拟助手的目标是接管在线论坛上学生所提全部问题中40%的回答工作。当然，下学期Jill Watson这个名字会换成其他名称。与埃隆·马斯克、斯蒂芬·霍金、比尔·盖茨或史蒂夫·沃兹尼亚克等人相比，Goel教授对人工智能的未来持更为乐观的态度。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about Knowledge-Based Artificial Intelligence?", "options": ["It is a robot that can answer students' questions.", "It is a course designed for students to learn online.", "It is a high-tech device that revolutionizes teaching.", "It is a computer program that aids student learning."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Professor Ashok Goel of Georgia Tech developed an artificially intelligent teaching assistant to help handle the enormous number of student questions in the online class, Knowledge-Based Artificial Intelligence. This online course is a core requirement of Georgia Tech's online Master of Science in Computer Science program.", "explanation": "定位至第一段前两句。原文指出“the online class, Knowledge-Based Artificial Intelligence”，并进一步说明“This online course”是该校在线硕士项目的核心必修课。B项“a course designed for students to learn online”与原文的在线课程直接同义对应，故正确。", "trapNote": "A项将课程偷换为“能回答问题的机器人”，C、D项分别偷换为“高科技设备”和“计算机程序”，均属于将后文提及的AI助教Jill Watson张冠李戴到课程名称上。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What problem did Professor Goel meet with?", "options": ["His students were unsatisfied with the assistants.", "His course was too difficult for the students.", "Students' questions were too many to handle.", "Too many students dropped out of his course."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Professor Goel already had eight teaching assistants, but that wasn't enough to deal with the overwhelming number of daily questions from students.", "explanation": "定位至第一段末句。原文指出Goel教授虽然已有八名助教，但仍不足以应对每天来自学生的“overwhelming number of daily questions”（铺天盖地的提问）。C项“too many to handle”精准对应原文“wasn't enough to deal with the overwhelming number of... questions”，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“学生对助教不满”原文未提及；D项“太多学生退课”是第二段泛指在线课程普遍缺少支持导致的现象，并非Goel教授自身遇到的直接问题，属错位嫁接。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about Jill Watson?", "options": ["She turned out to be a great success.", "She got along pretty well with students.", "She was unwelcome to students at first.", "She was released online as an experiment."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "After some adjustments, and sufficient time, Jill was able to answer the students' questions correctly 97% of the time. The virtual assistant became so advanced and realistic that the students didn't know she was a computer.", "explanation": "定位至第三段。原文指出Jill起初并不太理想，但经过调整和足够的时间训练后，回答问题的准确率高达97%，且极为先进逼真，学生甚至分辨不出她是计算机，对此体验评价非常积极。A项“She turned out to be a great success”高度概括了Jill最终大获成功的事实，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "C项利用第三段“At first, the virtual assistant wasn't too great”设陷，但原文仅指她起初性能不够好，而非“不受学生欢迎”；B项“相处融洽”属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How did the students feel about Jill Watson?", "options": ["They thought she was a bit too artificial.", "They found her not as capable as expected.", "They could not but admire her knowledge.", "They could not tell her from a real person."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The students, who were studying artificial intelligence, were interacting with the virtual assistant and couldn't tell it apart from a real human being.", "explanation": "定位至第三段倒数第三句。原文明确说明这些学习人工智能的学生在与虚拟助手互动时，“couldn't tell it apart from a real human being”（无法将其与真人区分开来）。选项D“could not tell her from a real person”几乎是对原文词组的直接同义复现，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“太生硬”与原文“so advanced and realistic”完全相反；B项“能力不如预期”也与原文97%的准确率和“very positive”的正面评价相悖，属于正反混淆。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does Professor Goel plan to do next with Jill Watson?", "options": ["Launch different versions of her online.", "Feed her with new questions and answers.", "Assign her to answer more of students' questions.", "Encourage students to interact with her more freely."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The goal of Professor Goel's virtual assistant next year is to take over answering 40% of all the questions posed by students on the online forum.", "explanation": "定位至第四段首句。题干询问教授下一步对Jill的计划，对应原文“next year”的目标：接管在线论坛上学生所提全部问题中40%的回答工作（take over answering 40% of all the questions）。C项“指派她回答更多学生的问题”是对“明年接管40%提问”的同义转述，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“上线不同版本”和B项“输入问答数据”均出现在第三段，属于团队过去已经完成的研发步骤，而非“下一步（next）”计划，属于典型的时间错位。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 势不可挡的；压倒性的；多得令人难以应对的", "note": "文中形容学生每天提问数量极大（overwhelming number），常用于四级阅读中表数量或压力巨大。", "word": "overwhelming"}, {"gloss": "v. 逐渐消退；减弱；褪色", "note": "第二段中表示学生继续学习的动力开始消退（begins to fade），比disappear更强调渐进过程。", "word": "fade"}, {"gloss": "v. 补救；改善；纠正", "note": "此处作动词，意为“改善这一状况（remedy this situation）”，其名词义为“补救措施；疗法”。", "word": "remedy"}, {"gloss": "v. 从……获取（信息、资源等）；寻找来源", "note": "第三段熟词僻义作动词，“sourced the online discussion forum”意为“从在线讨论区搜集资料”。", "word": "source"}, {"gloss": "n. 前景；观点；态度", "note": "末段“a much rosier outlook on the future”指对未来的看法更为乐观，rosy比喻“光明的、乐观的”。", "word": "outlook"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Professor Ashok Goel of Georgia Tech developed an artificially intelligent teaching assistant to help handle the enormous number of student questions in the online class, Knowledge-Based Artificial Intelligence.", "point": "不定式作目的状语及名词短语作同位语", "structure": "主语(Professor Ashok Goel of Georgia Tech) + 谓语(developed) + 宾语(an artificially intelligent teaching assistant) + 不定式目的状语(to help handle...)；Knowledge-Based Artificial Intelligence作the online class的同位语。", "zh": "佐治亚理工学院的Ashok Goel教授开发了一名人工智能教学助手，以帮助处理在线课程“基于知识的人工智能”中海量的学生提问。"}, {"en": "When students feel isolated or confused and reach out with questions that go unanswered, their motivation to continue begins to fade.", "point": "时间状语从句嵌套定语从句及后置定语", "structure": "When引导时间状语从句，从句中feel和reach out为并列谓语，that引导定语从句修饰questions；主句为their motivation... begins to fade，不定式to continue作后置定语。", "zh": "当学生感到孤立或困惑、提出问题却无人解答时，他们继续学习的动力就会开始消退。"}, {"en": "The students, who were studying artificial intelligence, were interacting with the virtual assistant and couldn't tell it apart from a real human being.", "point": "who引导的非限制性定语从句及tell... apart from固定搭配", "structure": "主语(The students) + 非限制性定语从句(who were studying artificial intelligence) + 并列谓语(were interacting with... and couldn't tell...)。", "zh": "这些正在学习人工智能的学生与虚拟助手互动时，完全无法将它与真人区分开来。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题对应：将“在线课程”同义转述为“专为学生在线学习的课程”", "option": "a course designed for students to learn online", "original": "the online class, Knowledge-Based Artificial Intelligence"}, {"note": "第2题对应：将“不足以应对铺天盖地的问题”简化概括为“多到难以处理”", "option": "too many to handle", "original": "wasn't enough to deal with the overwhelming number of daily questions"}, {"note": "第3题对应：用“最终大获成功”高度概括97%的准确率与极高逼真度", "option": "turned out to be a great success", "original": "answer the students' questions correctly 97% of the time / so advanced and realistic"}, {"note": "第4题对应：tell... apart from与tell... from同义替换，real human being替换为real person", "option": "could not tell her from a real person", "original": "couldn't tell it apart from a real human being"}, {"note": "第5题对应：将“接管40%的问题解答”转述为“指派她回答更多学生问题”", "option": "Assign her to answer more of students' questions", "original": "take over answering 40% of all the questions"}]}}, {"id": "cet4-201912-s1-p2", "exam": "四级 CET-4", "difficulty": "L1", "origin": "official", "year": "2019.12", "examSet": "2019.12 四级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2019.12 四级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "科学众筹项目成功的四大关键特征", "subtitle": "影响科研众筹成败的页面特征与人脉推广因素", "timeLimitMin": 12, "wordCount": 342, "paragraphs": ["Thinking small, being engaging, and having a sense of humor don't hurt. Those are a few of the traits of successful science crowdfunding efforts that emerge from a recent study that examined nearly 400 campaigns. But having a large network and some promotional skills may be more crucial.", "Crowdfunding, raising money for a project through online appeals, has taken off in recent years for everything from making movies to producing water-saving gadgets. Scientists have tried to tap Internet donors, too, with mixed success. Some raised more than twice their goals, but others have fallen short of reaching even modest targets.", "To determine what separates science crowdfunding triumphs from failures, a team led by science communications scholar Mike Schafer of the University of Zurich examined the content of the webpages for 371 recent campaigns.", "Four traits stood out for those that achieved their goals, the researchers report in Public Understanding of Science. For one, they use a crowdfunding platform that specializes in raising money for science, and not just any kind of project. Although sites like Kickstarter take all comers, platforms such as Experiment.com and Petridish.org only present scientific projects. For another, they present the project with a funny video because good visuals and a sense of humor improved success. Most of them engage with potential donors, since projects that answered questions from interested donors fared better. And they target a small amount of money. The projects included in the study raised $4000 on average, with 30% receiving less than $1000. The more money a project sought, the lower the chance it reached its goal, the researchers found.", "Other factors may also significantly influence a project's success, most notably, the size of a scientist's personal and professional networks, and how much a researcher promotes a project on their own. Those two factors are by far more critical than the content on the page. Crowdfunding can be part of researchers' efforts to reach the public, and people give because \"they feel a connection to the person\" who is doing the fundraising—not necessarily to the science."], "translations": ["思考细致、富有吸引力以及拥有幽默感都有帮助。这些是最近一项考察了近400个众筹项目的研究中所显现出的成功科学众筹活动的几个特征。但拥有庞大的人际网络和一定的宣传技巧可能更为关键。", "众筹，即通过网络呼吁为项目筹集资金，近年来在从制作电影到生产节水装置等各个领域蓬勃发展。科学家们也尝试吸引互联网捐赠者，但成效不一。一些项目筹集到的资金超过其目标的两倍以上，但另一些项目甚至未能达到适度的目标。", "为了确定是什么将科学众筹的成功与失败区分开来，由苏黎世大学科学传播学者Mike Schafer领导的团队考察了371个近期众筹项目网页的内容。", "研究人员在《公众理解科学》上报告称，实现目标的项目有四个突出特征。首先，它们使用专门为科学筹款的众筹平台，而不是任意类型项目的平台。尽管像Kickstarter这样的网站来者不拒，但像Experiment.com和Petridish.org这样的平台只展示科学项目。其次，它们用有趣的视频展示项目，因为良好的视觉效果和幽默感提高了成功率。大多数项目与潜在捐赠者互动，因为回答感兴趣捐赠者问题的项目表现更好。而且它们设定较小的筹款目标金额。研究中的项目平均筹集4000美元，其中30%获得的金额不到1000美元。研究人员发现，项目寻求的资金越多，达到目标的可能性就越低。", "其他因素也可能显著影响项目的成功，最值得注意的是科学家个人和专业人际网络的规模，以及研究人员自己推广项目的力度。这两个因素远比网页内容更为关键。众筹可以成为研究人员接触公众努力的一部分，人们之所以捐款，是因为“他们感到与进行筹款的人有联系”——而不一定是与科学本身有联系。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about the scientists trying to raise money online for their projects?", "options": ["They did not raise much due to modest targets.", "They made use of mixed fundraising strategies.", "Not all of them achieved their anticipated goals.", "Most of them put movies online for the purpose."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Scientists have tried to tap Internet donors, too, with mixed success. Some raised more than twice their goals, but others have fallen short of reaching even modest targets.", "explanation": "定位至第二段第二、三句。原文指出科学家尝试吸引网络捐赠者，但“with mixed success”（成效不一）：一些人筹集的资金超过目标的两倍，而另一些人甚至未能达到适度的目标（fallen short of reaching even modest targets）。C项“并非所有人都实现了预期目标”准确概括了这种成败并存的结果，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项将“有人未达适度目标”曲解为“因目标适度而筹款不多”；B项将原文“mixed success（成效不一）”偷换为“mixed strategies（混合策略）”；D项用首句“making movies”张冠李戴。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the purpose of Mike Schafer's research of recent crowdfunding campaigns?", "options": ["To create attractive content for science websites.", "To identify reasons for their different outcomes.", "To help scientists to launch innovative projects.", "To separate science projects from general ones."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "To determine what separates science crowdfunding triumphs from failures, a team led by science communications scholar Mike Schafer of the University of Zurich examined the content of the webpages for 371 recent campaigns.", "explanation": "定位至第三段。句首的不定式短语“To determine what separates science crowdfunding triumphs from failures”直接点明了Mike Schafer团队的研究目的，即确定是什么因素区分了科学众筹的成功（triumphs）与失败（failures）。选项B中的“identify reasons for their different outcomes”精准对应这一研究目的，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项拼凑了原文“content”和首段“engaging”等词，偏离研究初衷；D项利用第三段“separates... from...”设陷，但原文区分的是“成功与失败”，而非“科学项目与普通项目”。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What trait contributes to the success of a crowdfunding campaign?", "options": ["The potential benefit to future generations.", "Its interaction with prospective donors.", "Its originality in addressing financial issues.", "The value of the proposed project."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Most of them engage with potential donors, since projects that answered questions from interested donors fared better.", "explanation": "定位至第四段。该段列举了实现筹款目标项目的四个突出特征，其中第三点指出“Most of them engage with potential donors”，且回答感兴趣捐赠者问题的项目表现更好。B项中的“interaction with prospective donors”正是对原文“engage with potential donors”的同义替换，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“对后代的潜在益处”、C项“解决财务问题的原创性”以及D项“拟议项目的价值”在第四段列举的四个成功特征中均未提及，属于典型的无中生有干扰项。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did the researchers think of the financial targets of crowdfunding projects?", "options": ["They should be small to be successful.", "They should be based on actual needs.", "They should be assessed with great care.", "They should be ambitious to gain notice."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "And they target a small amount of money. The projects included in the study raised $4000 on average, with 30% receiving less than $1000. The more money a project sought, the lower the chance it reached its goal, the researchers found.", "explanation": "定位至第四段最后三句。原文提到成功项目的第四个特征是“target a small amount of money”（设定较小的筹款金额），研究发现项目寻求的资金越多，达到目标的概率就越低（the lower the chance it reached its goal）。选项A“金额应该小才容易成功”准确归纳了研究人员的这一发现，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "D项“目标应该宏大以吸引关注”与原文“越求多越难达标”的结论完全相反；B、C两项“基于实际需求”与“谨慎评估”看似合理，但原文并未涉及，属于主观臆断。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What motivates people to donate in a crowdfunding campaign?", "options": ["The ease of access to the content of the webpage.", "Their desire to contribute to the cause of science.", "The significance and influence of the project itself.", "Their feeling of connection to the scientists themselves."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Crowdfunding can be part of researchers' efforts to reach the public, and people give because \"they feel a connection to the person\" who is doing the fundraising—not necessarily to the science.", "explanation": "定位至第五段末句。原文直接给出人们捐款（people give）的原因：“because 'they feel a connection to the person' who is doing the fundraising—not necessarily to the science”，即人们感到与募捐的科学家本人有联系，而不一定是因为科学本身。D项精准对应原文表述，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项“想为科学事业做贡献”直接与原文破折号后的“not necessarily to the science”相矛盾；A、C两项在末段中均未提及作为捐款动因，且原文明确强调网页内容不如人脉和推广关键。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 众筹（通过网络向大众筹集资金）", "note": "由crowd（大众）+ funding（资金）构成的合成词，第二段给出其同位语解释：raising money for a project through online appeals。", "word": "crowdfunding"}, {"gloss": "v. 开发；利用；发掘（资源等）", "note": "第二段“tap Internet donors”意为“吸引/开发互联网捐赠者”，是四级阅读高频动词义项。", "word": "tap"}, {"gloss": "adj. 不大的；适度的；谦虚的", "note": "第二段“modest targets”指“适度的/不算高的筹款目标”，切勿一概译为“谦虚的”。", "word": "modest"}, {"gloss": "v. 进展；表现（好或坏）", "note": "第四段“fared better”意为“表现更好/成效更佳”，熟词僻义作动词用。", "word": "fare"}, {"gloss": "adj. 潜在的；预期的；未来的", "note": "第3题选项B中“prospective donors”同义替换原文第四段的“potential donors（潜在捐赠者）”。", "word": "prospective"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "To determine what separates science crowdfunding triumphs from failures, a team led by science communications scholar Mike Schafer of the University of Zurich examined the content of the webpages for 371 recent campaigns.", "point": "不定式目的状语+宾语从句+过去分词作后置定语", "structure": "To determine... 为不定式目的状语，内部嵌套what引导的宾语从句；主句主语为a team，过去分词短语led by... 作后置定语修饰team，谓语为examined，宾语为the content of the webpages...。", "zh": "为了确定是什么将科学众筹的成功与失败区分开来，由苏黎世大学科学传播学者Mike Schafer领导的团队考察了371个近期众筹项目网页的内容。"}, {"en": "Other factors may also significantly influence a project's success, most notably, the size of a scientist's personal and professional networks, and how much a researcher promotes a project on their own.", "point": "名词短语与how much引导的从句并列作同位语", "structure": "主谓宾结构(Other factors may also significantly influence a project's success)后接同位语补充说明，其中most notably引出两个并列成分：名词短语the size of...和how much引导的从句。", "zh": "其他因素也可能显著影响项目的成功，最值得注意的是科学家个人和专业人际网络的规模，以及研究人员自己推广项目的力度。"}, {"en": "Crowdfunding can be part of researchers' efforts to reach the public, and people give because \"they feel a connection to the person\" who is doing the fundraising—not necessarily to the science.", "point": "原因状语从句嵌套定语从句及破折号补充说明", "structure": "and连接的并列句；后半句中because引导原因状语从句，who引导定语从句修饰the person，破折号后not necessarily to the science作补充转折说明。", "zh": "众筹可以成为研究人员接触公众努力的一部分，人们之所以捐款，是因为“他们感到与进行筹款的人有联系”——而不一定是与科学本身有联系。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题对应：将“成效不一、有人未达目标”概括为“并非所有人都实现预期目标”", "option": "Not all of them achieved their anticipated goals", "original": "with mixed success... fallen short of reaching even modest targets"}, {"note": "第2题对应：将“区分成败的因素”转述为“导致不同结果的原因”", "option": "reasons for their different outcomes", "original": "what separates science crowdfunding triumphs from failures"}, {"note": "第3题对应：engage with替换为interaction with，potential替换为prospective", "option": "interaction with prospective donors", "original": "engage with potential donors"}, {"note": "第4题对应：浓缩概括“金额目标越小越容易成功”的研究发现", "option": "should be small to be successful", "original": "target a small amount of money... The more money a project sought, the lower the chance it reached its goal"}, {"note": "第5题对应：将“与筹款人产生联系”转述为“对科学家本人的情感联结”", "option": "Their feeling of connection to the scientists themselves", "original": "they feel a connection to the person who is doing the fundraising"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L1", "exam": "cet4", "id": "cet4-l1-p1", "origin": "curated", "paragraphs": ["A small transport office wanted to make its bus notices easier to understand. For two weeks, staff replaced long announcements with short messages that showed the route, the change and the date. Most passengers interviewed said the new notices were clearer. However, this did not mean that every passenger received the information in time.", "The office had posted the messages mainly through a phone app. Some older passengers, who rarely used the app, continued to ask drivers about changes. Staff then placed the same notices at several busy stops. Questions about routes fell, but the office had not counted them in a consistent way before the trial.", "The manager welcomed the feedback but avoided claiming that the new system had solved the problem. She argued that clear language and wider access were both necessary. The next trial would record questions at the same stops each day and include passengers who did not use smartphones."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Most passengers interviewed said the new notices were clearer.", "explanation": "定位至第一段第三至四句。原文指出，大多数受访乘客反馈新通知“更清晰”（clearer），这与B项中的“easier to understand”形成同义替换，但同时指出这并不意味着所有人都能及时收到信息。因此，B项最符合文意。", "no": 1, "options": ["Every passenger received notices in time.", "The new notices were easier to understand.", "The app removed the need for drivers.", "All routes became shorter."], "stem": "What did most interviewed passengers report?", "trapNote": "A项将第一段末句的否定事实（并非人人及时收到）反向歪曲为“所有乘客都及时收到”，属于正反颠倒与以偏概全；C、D项则属于无中生有。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The office had posted the messages mainly through a phone app. Some older passengers, who rarely used the app, continued to ask drivers about changes.", "explanation": "定位至第二段前两句。文中提到交通办公室主要通过手机应用程序发布消息（posted the messages mainly through a phone app），而部分很少使用该应用的老年乘客仍需向司机询问变动情况。选项C中的“the main information channel”正是对“主要通过手机应用发布”的概括替换。", "no": 2, "options": ["They refused to read any notice.", "The notices contained no dates.", "They rarely used the main information channel.", "They believed all online information was false."], "stem": "Why did some passengers still ask drivers about changes?", "trapNote": "A项“拒绝阅读”和D项“认为所有网上信息都是假的”均属主观臆测，原文仅客观说明部分乘客很少使用应用，并未提及任何抵触或不信任动机，属于过度推理。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Questions about routes fell, but the office had not counted them in a consistent way before the trial.", "explanation": "定位至第二段末句。虽然在站点张贴通知后询问路线的问题数量有所下降，但办公室在试行前并未以一致的方式统计过提问数量（not counted them in a consistent way before the trial）。A项中的“lacked consistently collected earlier counts”精准同义复现了这一测量局限，说明前后数据缺乏可靠可比性。", "no": 3, "options": ["The office lacked consistently collected earlier counts.", "No notices were displayed at stops.", "Every question was counted twice.", "The manager had already ended the trial."], "stem": "Why should the fall in questions be interpreted cautiously?", "trapNote": "B项“站点未张贴通知”与前句“placed the same notices at several busy stops”正反颠倒，C、D两项则在原文中毫无依据，属于无中生有。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The manager welcomed the feedback but avoided claiming that the new system had solved the problem.", "explanation": "定位至第三段首句。经理对乘客反馈表示欢迎（welcomed the feedback），对应选项中的“Positive about the feedback”；同时她避免宣称新系统已经解决问题（avoided claiming that the new system had solved the problem），对应“cautious about the conclusion”。这两层态度并存，因此D项最为全面准确。", "no": 4, "options": ["Certain that the problem had disappeared.", "Opposed to collecting further information.", "Indifferent to passenger feedback.", "Positive about the feedback but cautious about the conclusion."], "stem": "Which best describes the manager’s attitude?", "trapNote": "A项将经理“避免下定论”曲解为“确信问题已消失”，属于正反颠倒；B、C两项则与文中欢迎反馈并计划开展下一轮试行的做法完全相悖。", "type": "态度题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The next trial would record questions at the same stops each day and include passengers who did not use smartphones.", "explanation": "定位至第三段末句。该句明确指出下一轮试行将包含两项举措：每天在相同的站点记录提问（record questions at the same stops each day），以及覆盖不使用智能手机的乘客（include passengers who did not use smartphones）。C项对这两项措施进行了精准的同义概括。", "no": 5, "options": ["Stop speaking to passengers without phones.", "Use only shorter messages and stop recording questions.", "Count questions consistently and include non-smartphone users.", "Assume that fewer questions always mean better service."], "stem": "Which action belongs to the next trial?", "trapNote": "A、B两项分别将“纳入非智能手机用户”和“逐日记录问题”改写为“停止交流”和“停止记录”，属于典型的正反颠倒；D项则是脱离文本的主观臆断。", "type": "细节题"}], "sourceLabel": "四级标准精编（L1 基础夯实）", "subtitle": "公共服务沟通与有效反馈评估", "timeLimitMin": 9, "title": "Clearer Bus Notices", "year": "精编", "wordCount": 154, "translations": ["一家小型交通管理办公室希望让公交乘车须知更易理解。在两周的时间里，工作人员用简短的通知取代了冗长的公告，写明线路、变动情况及生效日期。大多数受访乘客表示新通知更加清晰明了。然而，这并不意味着每位乘客都能及时获取这些信息。", "此前，该办公室主要通过一款手机应用程序发布通知。一些很少使用该应用的老年乘客仍不断向司机询问线路变动情况。随后，工作人员在几个客流量较大的站点张贴了同样的通知。关于线路的咨询随之减少，但在此次试行前，该办公室并未以统一的方式统计过这类咨询的数量。", "负责人对这些反馈表示欢迎，但并未宣称新方案已经解决了问题。她认为，清晰的表达与更广泛的覆盖渠道缺一不可。下一阶段的试行将在每天同一批站点记录乘客的咨询情况，并将不使用智能手机的乘客纳入统计范围。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "通知，公告", "note": "高频熟词：作名词常考“通知/告示”，作动词意为“注意到”；短语take notice of意为“关注”", "word": "notice"}, {"gloss": "取代，替换", "note": "四六级核心动词，常考搭配replace A with B（用B替代A）", "word": "replace"}, {"gloss": "一贯的，一致的", "note": "高频阅读词：强调方法、标准前后统一；副词consistently，名词consistency", "word": "consistent"}, {"gloss": "试验，试行", "note": "熟词僻义：在科研、调查或政策语境中指“试验、试运行”，而非仅指法律上的“审判”", "word": "trial"}, {"gloss": "接触渠道，使用机会", "note": "核心名词：文中指获取信息的“途径/渠道”，常考搭配have access to...", "word": "access"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "For two weeks, staff replaced long announcements with short messages that showed the route, the change and the date.", "point": "that引导的限制性定语从句及replace A with B固定搭配", "structure": "时间状语(For two weeks) + 主句(staff replaced long announcements with short messages) + 定语从句(that showed the route, the change and the date，修饰messages)", "zh": "在两周时间里，工作人员用简短的通知取代了冗长的公告，写明线路、变动情况和日期。"}, {"en": "Some older passengers, who rarely used the app, continued to ask drivers about changes.", "point": "who引导的非限制性定语从句（补充说明主语特征）", "structure": "主语(Some older passengers) + 非限制性定语从句(who rarely used the app) + 谓语及宾语(continued to ask drivers about changes)", "zh": "一些很少使用该应用的老年乘客仍不断向司机询问变动情况。"}, {"en": "The manager welcomed the feedback but avoided claiming that the new system had solved the problem.", "point": "转折并列谓语、avoid doing sth.搭配及过去完成时宾语从句", "structure": "主语(The manager) + 并列谓语(welcomed the feedback but avoided claiming...) + 宾语从句(that the new system had solved the problem，作claiming的宾语)", "zh": "负责人对这些反馈表示欢迎，但避免宣称新系统已经解决了问题。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "形容词比较级同义改写，表示表达更加清晰易懂", "option": "easier to understand", "original": "clearer"}, {"note": "将具体渠道（手机应用）抽象概括为上位概念“主要信息渠道”", "option": "the main information channel", "original": "mainly through a phone app"}, {"note": "否定动词短语改写为lack+名词短语，并把consistent转为副词修饰分词counts", "option": "lacked consistently collected earlier counts", "original": "had not counted them in a consistent way before the trial"}, {"note": "态度题典型改写：welcomed对应positive，avoided claiming对应cautious", "option": "Positive about the feedback but cautious about the conclusion", "original": "welcomed the feedback but avoided claiming that the new system had solved the problem"}, {"note": "具体操作压缩为副词consistently，定语从句合并为复合名词non-smartphone users", "option": "Count questions consistently and include non-smartphone users", "original": "record questions at the same stops each day and include passengers who did not use smartphones"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L1", "exam": "cet4", "id": "cet4-l1-p2", "origin": "curated", "paragraphs": ["A community centre offered a short course on checking online claims. Participants practised tracing a statement to its original source rather than judging it by the number of people who had shared it. After the course, most participants performed better on a short test.", "The organiser wanted to repeat the course across the town. One tutor supported the idea but questioned whether the test results told the whole story. The participants had chosen to attend, so they might have been more interested in careful reading than other residents. Moreover, the test was taken immediately after the final lesson.", "Instead of rejecting the course, the tutor suggested a second test several weeks later and a comparison group. She also asked participants to explain their choices. A correct answer without a reason, she noted, could reflect a lucky guess. The aim was not merely to produce higher scores, but to see whether people could use the method independently."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Participants practised tracing a statement to its original source rather than judging it by the number of people who had shared it.", "explanation": "定位至第一段第二句。该句指出课程中参与者练习的核心方法是“将一条陈述追溯至其原始出处”（tracing a statement to its original source），而非依据转发人数来判断真伪。B项与原文表述几乎完全一致，只是将“practised”对应为题干中的“emphasise”。", "no": 1, "options": ["Following the most widely shared opinions.", "Tracing a statement to its original source.", "Memorising the names of popular websites.", "Avoiding every online statement."], "stem": "What skill did the course emphasise?", "trapNote": "A项将原文明确否定的“依据分享人数做判断（rather than judging it by...）”反向包装成课程重点，属于典型的正反颠倒；C、D两项则属于无中生有。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The participants had chosen to attend, so they might have been more interested in careful reading than other residents.", "explanation": "定位至第二段第三句。文中指出参与者是“自主选择参加课程的”（had chosen to attend），因此他们可能本身就比其他居民对仔细阅读更感兴趣。D项中的“voluntarily chosen”正是对“chosen to attend”的同义替换。", "no": 2, "options": ["They had all passed an earlier test.", "They were required by law to attend.", "They never used the internet.", "They had voluntarily chosen the course."], "stem": "Why might the participants differ from other residents?", "trapNote": "B项“被法律强制要求参加”与原文“自主选择参加（chosen to attend）”完全相反，属于正反颠倒；A、C两项在文中均未提及，属于无中生有。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Instead of rejecting the course, the tutor suggested a second test several weeks later and a comparison group.", "explanation": "结合第二段末句与第三段首句定位。第二段提到首次测试是在最后一节课后立即进行的，而第三段中导师建议在几周后再进行第二次测试（a second test several weeks later）。由此可合理推断，延迟测试是为了检验学习效果在间隔一段时间后是否依然有效（remained useful after a delay），对应A项。", "no": 3, "options": ["Whether learning remained useful after a delay.", "Whether the centre could avoid teaching.", "Whether all residents would agree with one another.", "Whether sharing a claim makes it true."], "stem": "What would a test several weeks later help examine?", "trapNote": "B项“能否避免教学”曲解了导师提出改进评估方案的初衷，属于过度推理与偷换目的；C、D两项偏离测试评估的核心语境，与原文无关。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "She also asked participants to explain their choices. A correct answer without a reason, she noted, could reflect a lucky guess.", "explanation": "定位至第三段第二、三句。导师要求参与者解释自己选择的原因，并指出“没有理由支撑的正确答案可能只是侥幸猜对”（could reflect a lucky guess）。选项C中的“distinguish supported understanding from lucky guesses”精准概括了她这样做的目的。", "no": 4, "options": ["To replace reading with guessing.", "To reward longer answers regardless of accuracy.", "To distinguish supported understanding from lucky guesses.", "To prove that the course had failed."], "stem": "Why did the tutor ask participants to explain their choices?", "trapNote": "A项将“排除侥幸猜测”偷换为“用猜测代替阅读”，属于正反颠倒；D项“证明课程失败”与该段首句“Instead of rejecting the course”的建设性立场相违背。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The aim was not merely to produce higher scores, but to see whether people could use the method independently.", "explanation": "通读全文并聚焦第三段末句。第一段肯定了短期课程后多数参与者测试表现更佳的初步成效，第二、三段则通过导师的视角指出仅靠自愿报名样本和即时测试不足以说明问题，需要通过对照组、延迟测试和理由解释来检验独立应用能力（use the method independently）。B项兼顾了“初步成效较好”与“需加强对独立运用能力的检验”两层核心信息，最能概括主旨。", "no": 5, "options": ["A short course can never improve reading.", "Promising results need stronger checks of independent use.", "An immediate test proves that everyone has learned permanently.", "Popularity is the best test of an online claim."], "stem": "Which is the best summary of the passage?", "trapNote": "A项“永远无法改善阅读”否定过于绝对，忽略了第一段的积极结果；C项“即时测试证明永久学会”则属以偏概全和过度夸大，D项则是第一段明确否定的错误做法。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "四级标准精编（L1 基础夯实）", "subtitle": "网络信息核查课程与独立应用检验", "timeLimitMin": 9, "title": "Checking Online Claims", "year": "精编", "wordCount": 156, "translations": ["一家社区中心开设了一门关于核查网络言论的短期课程。学员们练习将一条说法追溯至其原始出处，而不是根据转发人数来判断其真伪。课程结束后，大多数人在一次小测验中表现有所提升。", "组织者希望在全镇范围内推广这门课程。一位导师支持这一想法，但对测验成绩是否能说明全部问题提出了质疑。由于学员是自愿报名的，他们对仔细阅读的兴趣可能本身就高于其他居民。此外，测验是在最后一节课结束后立即进行的。", "这位导师并未否定这门课程，而是建议几周后再进行一次复测并设立对照组。她还要求学员解释自己做出选择的原因。她指出，没有理由支撑的正确答案可能只是碰巧猜对。课程的目的不仅在于提高分数，更在于检验人们能否独立运用这一方法。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "说法，断言", "note": "阅读高频词：作名词常指“未经证实的说法/主张”，作动词意为“声称”", "word": "claim"}, {"gloss": "追溯，追踪", "note": "高频动词：常见搭配trace sth. to its source（追根溯源）", "word": "trace"}, {"gloss": "质疑，怀疑", "note": "熟词僻义：作动词不译为“提问”，而常表示“对……提出质疑、怀疑”", "word": "question"}, {"gloss": "对照，比较", "note": "科研实验高频词：comparison group意为“对照组”，常在实验设计题中出现", "word": "comparison"}, {"gloss": "反映，体现", "note": "核心动词：文中意为“表明、反映出（某种情况）”，另常考reflect on（反思）", "word": "reflect"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Participants practised tracing a statement to its original source rather than judging it by the number of people who had shared it.", "point": "rather than连接动名词并列结构及who引导的定语从句", "structure": "主句(Participants practised tracing...) + 对比结构(rather than judging it by the number of people...) + 定语从句(who had shared it，修饰people)", "zh": "学员们练习将一条说法追溯到其原始出处，而不是依据转发它的人数来做出判断。"}, {"en": "One tutor supported the idea but questioned whether the test results told the whole story.", "point": "whether引导的宾语从句及习语tell the whole story（说明全部情况）", "structure": "主语(One tutor) + 并列谓语(supported the idea but questioned...) + 宾语从句(whether the test results told the whole story)", "zh": "一位导师支持这一想法，但质疑测验结果是否反映了全部情况。"}, {"en": "The aim was not merely to produce higher scores, but to see whether people could use the method independently.", "point": "not merely... but...并列结构、不定式作表语及whether引导的宾语从句", "structure": "主语(The aim) + 系动词(was) + 并列不定式表语(not merely to produce..., but to see...) + 宾语从句(whether people could use the method independently)", "zh": "其目的不仅在于考出更高的分数，更在于检验人们能否独立运用这一方法。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将动作“主动选择参加”转化为副词voluntarily修饰，凸显样本自选偏差", "option": "had voluntarily chosen the course", "original": "had chosen to attend"}, {"note": "时间状语“几周后”概括为after a delay，考查延迟测试的实验目的", "option": "whether learning remained useful after a delay", "original": "a second test several weeks later"}, {"note": "整合因果与对比细节：要求解释理由即区分“有据可依的理解”与“运气猜对”", "option": "distinguish supported understanding from lucky guesses", "original": "explain their choices... A correct answer without a reason... could reflect a lucky guess"}, {"note": "动词短语+副词转换为“形容词+名词”的名词化高频表达", "option": "independent use", "original": "use the method independently"}, {"note": "将“未能说明全部情况”的质疑概括为需要更严格的检验", "option": "needed stronger checks", "original": "questioned whether the test results told the whole story"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L1", "exam": "cet4", "id": "cet4-l1-p3", "origin": "curated", "paragraphs": ["Over the past decade, many university libraries have replaced rows of heavy bookshelves with quiet computer desks and glowing digital screens. Administrators often praise this shift toward paperless resources, noting that electronic databases let students search thousands of scholarly journals in seconds. For tight campus budgets and limited floor space, going digital seems an obvious triumph.", "Yet a growing number of professors and librarians worry that something valuable is quietly disappearing along with the printed pages. While digital screens excel at helping readers locate specific facts quickly, they tend to encourage rapid skimming rather than sustained concentration. When students read complex academic chapters on tablets or laptops, constant notifications, embedded hyperlinks, and multiple open tabs frequently pull their attention away, turning deep reading into a fragmented experience.", "Recent classroom observations strongly support this growing concern. In a careful study conducted at two public universities, students who read a lengthy history article on paper remembered the timeline of events more accurately than peers who read the exact same text on a screen. Researchers explained that printed books offer physical cues, such as page thickness and text position. These cues help the brain build a clearer mental map of an argument, making key details easier to recall.", "To respond to these findings, some universities are rethinking the push to eliminate paper completely from campus libraries. Instead of treating digital and printed formats as rivals, libraries at several colleges now pair fast online search tools with quiet, device-free reading rooms stocked with essential print collections. Faculty members also guide students on when to choose each format wisely, encouraging quick digital searches for gathering references while recommending paper copies for dense theoretical texts that require careful reflection.", "Clearly, modern libraries cannot abandon electronic databases or ignore their real conveniences. Yet true educational efficiency depends not just on fast downloads, but on deep understanding. If universities hope to cultivate thoughtful and independent learners, they must preserve quiet spaces and print collections for slow, uninterrupted reading on paper."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "electronic databases let students search thousands of scholarly journals in seconds. For tight campus budgets and limited floor space, going digital seems an obvious triumph.", "explanation": "定位至第一段第二、三句。原文提到电子数据库让学生数秒内就能检索海量学术期刊（search thousands of scholarly journals in seconds），同时数字化有助于缓解紧张的校园预算和有限的场地空间（tight campus budgets and limited floor space）。B项将这些优势准确概括为省钱、省空间并加快检索速度。", "no": 1, "options": ["They reduce the time students spend discussing books with professors.", "They help save money and make better use of space while speeding up searches.", "They ensure every student finishes reading academic chapters more carefully.", "They completely remove the need for quiet study rooms on campus."], "stem": "Why do university administrators welcome paperless library resources?", "trapNote": "C项“确保每位学生更仔细地读完学术章节”属于无中生有且与后文屏幕阅读导致略读相悖，D项“完全消除安静自习室的需求”则属于过度绝对化。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "constant notifications, embedded hyperlinks, and multiple open tabs frequently pull their attention away, turning deep reading into a fragmented experience.", "explanation": "定位至第二段末句。前文指出电子屏幕助长快速略读而非持续专注（sustained concentration），紧接着说明弹窗通知、超链接和多标签页频频分散注意力（pull their attention away），使深度阅读变得支离破碎。由上下文对比与因果线索可知，fragmented意为“碎片化的、被打散成零碎片段的”，对应A项。", "no": 2, "options": ["Broken into disconnected pieces.", "Carefully organized by topic.", "Shared widely among classmates.", "Repeated over a long period."], "stem": "What does the word 'fragmented' (Para. 2) most probably mean?", "trapNote": "B项“按主题精心整理”与原文注意力被打断、阅读连贯性受损的语境完全相反，属于正反颠倒；C、D两项则是脱离语境的主观臆测。", "type": "词义题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Researchers explained that printed books offer physical cues, such as page thickness and text position. These cues help the brain build a clearer mental map of an argument", "explanation": "定位至第三段第三、四句。研究者解释纸质书具有页面厚度、文字位置等实体线索（physical cues），这些线索有助于大脑构建更清晰的论证心理地图，从而更易回忆关键细节。据此可合理推断，纸页上的实体线索能帮助读者更好地记住文本结构与脉络，对应B项。", "no": 3, "options": ["History articles are too difficult for students to understand without teachers.", "Physical cues on printed pages help readers remember content structure better.", "Students prefer digital textbooks because they can check timelines faster.", "Reading on screens causes permanent harm to students' eyesight."], "stem": "What can be inferred from the study at two public universities?", "trapNote": "C项“学生更偏爱电子教材”在原文实验对比中毫无体现，反而纸质阅读记忆更准确，属于正反颠倒；A、D两项则属于过度推理与无中生有。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "libraries cannot abandon electronic databases or ignore their real conveniences. Yet true educational efficiency depends not just on fast downloads, but on deep understanding.", "explanation": "定位至第五段前两句。作者明确指出现代图书馆既不能放弃电子数据库，也不应忽视数字阅读的现实便利（cannot abandon... or ignore their real conveniences），同时强调真正的教育效率不仅取决于快速下载，更取决于深度理解。由此可见作者既认可其价值又看清其局限，态度客观平衡，对应D项。", "no": 4, "options": ["Strongly opposed to using them in higher education.", "Worried that they will soon replace all university teachers.", "Doubtful that students find them convenient for searching.", "Balanced, recognizing both their usefulness and their limits."], "stem": "What is the author's attitude toward digital library resources?", "trapNote": "A项“强烈反对使用”仅片面放大了作者对屏幕分心的担忧而忽略其对检索便利的肯定，属于以偏概全与正反颠倒；B、C两项均偏离文本事实。", "type": "态度题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "If universities hope to cultivate thoughtful and independent learners, they must preserve quiet spaces and print collections for slow, uninterrupted reading on paper.", "explanation": "纵观全文并聚焦第四、五段核心论点。文章先肯定无纸化检索的便利，随后借助实验与观察指出屏幕阅读削弱深度专注，最终提出图书馆应将快速在线检索与保留纸质深度阅读空间相结合（preserve quiet spaces and print collections）。C项全面概括了“兼顾数字便利与纸质深度阅读空间”的主旨。", "no": 5, "options": ["Paperless databases have solved the biggest problems facing campus libraries.", "Digital devices are unsuitable for any kind of academic research.", "Universities should balance digital convenience with print spaces for deep reading.", "Students perform worse in history classes when they use library computers."], "stem": "What is the main idea of the passage?", "trapNote": "A项“已解决最大问题”忽视了全文中后段的核心担忧，属于以偏概全；B项“不适合任何学术研究”则否定过于绝对，忽略了第四段对快速检索文献的肯定。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "四级标准精编（L1 基础夯实）", "subtitle": "大学图书馆无纸化与深度阅读习惯", "timeLimitMin": 9, "title": "Paper vs. Screen in University Libraries", "year": "精编", "wordCount": 333, "translations": ["过去十年间，许多大学图书馆已经用安静的电脑桌和发亮的电子屏幕取代了一排排沉重的书架。行政管理人员常常称赞这种向无纸化资源的转变，指出电子数据库让学生们能在几秒钟内检索数千种学术期刊。对于紧张的校园预算和有限的馆舍面积而言，走向数字化似乎是一场显而易见的胜利。", "然而，越来越多的教授和图书管理员担心，某种珍贵的东西正随着纸质书页一同悄然消失。虽然电子屏幕在帮助读者快速定位特定事实方面表现出色，但它们往往会助长快速浏览，而非持续专注。当学生在平板电脑或笔记本电脑上阅读复杂的学术章节时，不断的通知提醒、嵌入式超链接以及多个打开的标签页常常会分散他们的注意力，将深度阅读变成一种碎片化的体验。", "近期的课堂观察有力地印证了这种日益加剧的担忧。在两所公立大学进行的一项严谨研究中，在纸上阅读一篇长篇历史文章的学生，比在屏幕上阅读完全相同文本的同伴更准确地记住了事件的时间线。研究人员解释说，纸质书提供了诸如书页厚度和文字位置等物理线索。这些线索有助于大脑构建更清晰的论证心理地图，从而使关键细节更容易被回忆起来。", "为回应这些研究发现，一些大学正在重新审视从校园图书馆彻底淘汰纸质书籍的举措。多所高校的图书馆不再将数字格式与纸质格式视为竞争对手，而是如今将快速的在线检索工具与配备核心纸质藏书的安静无电子设备阅览室结合起来。教职人员也会指导学生如何明智地选择每种格式：鼓励使用快速的电子检索来收集参考文献，同时建议对需要仔细思考的密集理论文本使用纸质副本。", "显然，现代图书馆无法放弃电子数据库，也不能忽视它们带来的切实便利。然而，真正的教育效率不仅取决于快速下载，更取决于深刻理解。如果大学希望培养出善于思考且独立自主的学习者，就必须保留安静的空间和纸质藏书，以供人们在纸上进行缓慢而连贯的阅读。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "擅长；表现出色", "note": "高频搭配 excel at/in (doing) sth.，表示“在某方面胜过或表现突出”。", "word": "excel"}, {"gloss": "持续的；持久的", "note": "由动词 sustain（维持、支撑）演变而来的形容词，阅读中常与 concentration、effort、growth 搭配。", "word": "sustained"}, {"gloss": "支离破碎的；碎片化的", "note": "词根 fragment 意为“碎片”，四六级词汇题高频词，常用来形容体验、注意力或信息状态。", "word": "fragmented"}, {"gloss": "（内容）密集的；晦涩难懂的", "note": "熟词僻义！常见义为“稠密的、浓密的”，但在学术文本中修饰书籍或文章（dense texts）指“信息密度大、深奥难懂的”。", "word": "dense"}, {"gloss": "培养；养成", "note": "熟词僻义！本义为“耕作、栽培（植物）”，在教育类阅读中高频表示“培养（能力、习惯或人才）”。", "word": "cultivate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "When students read complex academic chapters on tablets or laptops, constant notifications, embedded hyperlinks, and multiple open tabs frequently pull their attention away, turning deep reading into a fragmented experience.", "point": "时间状语从句 + 现在分词短语作结果状语（turning... 表自然而然的结果）", "structure": "When引导时间状语从句（When students read...）+ 主句主干（constant notifications, embedded hyperlinks, and multiple open tabs frequently pull their attention away）+ 现在分词短语作结果状语（turning deep reading into a fragmented experience）。", "zh": "当学生在平板电脑或笔记本电脑上阅读复杂的学术章节时，不断的通知提醒、嵌入式超链接以及多个打开的标签页常常会分散他们的注意力，将深度阅读变成一种碎片化的体验。"}, {"en": "In a careful study conducted at two public universities, students who read a lengthy history article on paper remembered the timeline of events more accurately than peers who read the exact same text on a screen.", "point": "过去分词作后置定语 + 双重who引导的定语从句 + 比较级结构", "structure": "地点状语（In a careful study conducted at two public universities，其中过去分词短语 conducted... 作后置定语修饰 study）+ 主句主干（students ... remembered the timeline of events more accurately than peers ...）+ 两个 who 引导的定语从句分别修饰 students 和 peers。", "zh": "在两所公立大学进行的一项严谨研究中，在纸上阅读一篇长篇历史文章的学生，比在屏幕上阅读完全相同文本的同伴更准确地记住了事件的时间线。"}, {"en": "Faculty members also guide students on when to choose each format wisely, encouraging quick digital searches for gathering references while recommending paper copies for dense theoretical texts that require careful reflection.", "point": "疑问词+不定式作宾语 + 现在分词作伴随状语（while表对比） + that引导的定语从句", "structure": "主句（Faculty members also guide students on when to choose each format wisely，when to choose... 为“疑问词+不定式”作介词 on 的宾语）+ 并列现在分词伴随状语（encouraging... while recommending...，while 连接两个对比动作）+ that 引导的定语从句修饰 texts。", "zh": "教职人员也会指导学生如何明智地选择每种格式：鼓励使用快速的电子检索来收集参考文献，同时建议对需要仔细思考的密集理论文本使用纸质副本。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "因果转述，解决“预算紧张与空间有限”的难题即对应“省钱并更充分地利用空间”。", "option": "save money and make better use of space", "original": "tight campus budgets and limited floor space"}, {"note": "具体时间描述（in seconds）抽象概括为动作速度提升（speeding up searches）。", "option": "speeding up searches", "original": "search thousands of scholarly journals in seconds"}, {"note": "词义猜测题同义释义，“注意力被分散、沦为碎片化体验”即“支离破碎成互不相连的片段”。", "option": "Broken into disconnected pieces", "original": "pull their attention away, turning deep reading into a fragmented experience"}, {"note": "抽象概念与功能转述，“构建更清晰的论证心理地图并更容易回忆细节”同义替换为“更好地记住内容结构”。", "option": "remember content structure better", "original": "build a clearer mental map of an argument, making key details easier to recall"}, {"note": "全文主旨概括，“无法放弃电子数据库但必须保留纸质阅读空间”提炼为“在数字便利与纸质深度阅读空间之间取得平衡”。", "option": "balance digital convenience with print spaces for deep reading", "original": "cannot abandon electronic databases ... preserve quiet spaces and print collections for slow, uninterrupted reading on paper"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L1", "exam": "cet4", "id": "cet4-l1-p4", "origin": "curated", "paragraphs": ["In crowded cities where glass office towers and busy roads leave little room for nature, small community gardens are quietly transforming unused plots of land. Originally started in many neighborhoods as simple projects to grow fresh tomatoes or herbs, these shared green spaces are now attracting the attention of health researchers. A growing body of evidence suggests that tending a neighborhood garden offers benefits that reach far beyond the dinner table.", "Mental health specialists point out that urban life often traps people indoors under constant digital pressure, raising daily stress levels. Spending even an hour a week digging soil, watering plants, and watching seedlings grow helps lower stress hormones and restore mental energy. Unlike repetitive gym workouts, gardening gives city residents a calming sense of purpose and visible progress at a natural pace, allowing anxious minds to slow down.", "Equally important is the social connection that community gardens nurture among neighbors who might otherwise remain strangers. In high-rise apartment buildings, residents frequently share elevators in silence without learning one another's names. Out in a garden, however, people naturally exchange tips on pests, borrow tools, and share extra vegetables. For elderly residents living alone or newcomers adjusting to an unfamiliar city, these casual conversations can greatly ease feelings of isolation.", "Of course, maintaining a shared garden is not without practical obstacles. Limited city land, unclear water access, and disagreements over who handles weekly maintenance can discourage volunteers and cause promising projects to fade. Without steady support from local governments, such as long-term land permits and basic funding for soil or fences, community gardens risk remaining short-lived experiments rather than lasting neighborhood resources.", "Even so, urban planners increasingly view these modest green corners as smart investments in public well-being. Compared with expensive clinical programs, neighborhood gardens offer a low-cost way to bring nature, physical movement, and human warmth back into dense cities. Protecting space for residents to plant together may prove to be one of the simplest ways to build healthier, happier urban communities."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Unlike repetitive gym workouts, gardening gives city residents a calming sense of purpose and visible progress at a natural pace, allowing anxious minds to slow down.", "explanation": "定位至第二段末句。原文将社区园艺与重复性的健身房锻炼进行对比（Unlike repetitive gym workouts），指出园艺能以自然节奏为城市居民带来平和的目标感与看得见的进展（a calming sense of purpose and visible progress），让焦虑的心灵慢下来。B项与该句构成精准同义替换。", "no": 1, "options": ["It requires much more physical strength and strict training.", "It offers a calm sense of purpose and steady progress.", "It lowers stress hormones only when done every single day.", "It helps people avoid all contact with other city residents."], "stem": "How does gardening differ from repetitive gym workouts according to Paragraph 2?", "trapNote": "C项“只有每天坚持才能降低压力激素”歪曲了前句“每周哪怕一小时（even an hour a week）”的事实，属于偷换条件；A、D两项则属于无中生有。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Equally important is the social connection that community gardens nurture among neighbors who might otherwise remain strangers.", "explanation": "定位至第三段首句及末句。首句指出社区花园在原本可能互为陌生人的邻里之间“nurture”了社交联系，后文紧接着举例说明大家在花园里交流防虫技巧、互借工具并拉近关系，从而缓解孤独。由此可知，nurture在此引申为“培育、促进发展（关系）”，与A项“Encourage and develop”意思一致。", "no": 2, "options": ["Encourage and develop.", "Measure and record.", "Replace and limit.", "Ignore and delay."], "stem": "What does the word 'nurture' (Para. 3) probably mean?", "trapNote": "C项“取代并限制”与第三段展现的促进邻里交流、缓解孤立感完全相悖，属于正反颠倒；B、D两项与语境逻辑不符。", "type": "词义题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Without steady support from local governments, such as long-term land permits and basic funding for soil or fences, community gardens risk remaining short-lived experiments", "explanation": "定位至第四段末句。原文指出如果缺乏地方政府的稳定支持（without steady support from local governments），例如长期用地许可和基础经费，社区花园就可能沦为昙花一现的短期实验。由此可合理推断，社区花园的长期存续在一定程度上依赖稳定的地方政策支持，对应C项。", "no": 3, "options": ["Volunteers prefer building fences rather than watering plants.", "Most city governments refuse to provide land for public parks.", "Long-term success depends partly on stable local policy support.", "Short-lived garden projects usually produce healthier vegetables."], "stem": "What can be inferred about community gardens from Paragraph 4?", "trapNote": "B项“大多数市政府拒绝提供公园用地”将原文假设条件下的担忧偷换为既成事实，属于过度推理；A、D两项在段落中均无依据。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Even so, urban planners increasingly view these modest green corners as smart investments in public well-being.", "explanation": "定位至第五段首句。在指出维护难点后，作者用“Even so”转折，说明城市规划者愈发将这些绿色角落视为对公众福祉的明智投资（smart investments in public well-being），后文进一步称其为低成本且有效的举措。可见规划者持积极赞赏态度，对应D项。", "no": 4, "options": ["Doubtful of their ability to compete with modern hospitals.", "Concerned that they waste valuable space in dense cities.", "Indifferent to whether volunteers continue maintaining them.", "Favorable, seeing them as worthwhile investments in public health."], "stem": "What is urban planners' attitude toward community gardens?", "trapNote": "B项“担心浪费宝贵空间”与首段盘活闲置地块及末段肯定其低成本价值正反颠倒；A、C两项则是脱离文本的错误臆测。", "type": "态度题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "A growing body of evidence suggests that tending a neighborhood garden offers benefits that reach far beyond the dinner table.", "explanation": "结合第一段末句与第五段末句把握主旨。文章开篇点明社区花园的益处远不止于餐桌上的食物（benefits that reach far beyond the dinner table），中间分述其缓解压力、促进邻里联结的作用及政策支持需求，结尾总结其能助力打造更健康快乐的城市社区。A项“收获不止于食物：城市花园如何促进心理健康”精准统领全文。", "no": 5, "options": ["Growing More Than Food: How City Gardens Support Mental Well-Being", "Replacing Concrete: Why High-Rise Apartments Need Larger Elevators", "From Soil to Kitchen: Practical Tips on Planting Urban Tomatoes", "Costly Experiments: Why City Volunteers Struggle With Park Maintenance"], "stem": "What is the best title for the passage?", "trapNote": "C项“城市种植番茄的实用技巧”仅停留在首段引出的表层现象，属于以偏概全；B、D两项则抓错次要细节或歪曲全文积极基调。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "四级标准精编（L1 基础夯实）", "subtitle": "城市社区花园与居民心理健康", "timeLimitMin": 9, "title": "Urban Community Gardens and Mental Health", "year": "精编", "wordCount": 337, "translations": ["在玻璃幕墙写字楼和繁忙道路几乎没有给自然留下空间的城市里，小型社区花园正在悄然改变那些闲置的土地。这些共享绿地最初在许多街区只是作为种植新鲜西红柿或香草的简单项目而兴起，如今却正吸引着健康研究人员的关注。越来越多的证据表明，打理社区花园所带来的益处远远超出了餐桌本身。", "心理健康专家指出，城市生活常常将人们困在室内并使其承受持续的数字压力，从而推高了日常压力水平。哪怕每周只花一小时翻土、浇水和看着幼苗生长，也有助于降低压力荷尔蒙并恢复精神能量。与重复性的健身房锻炼不同，园艺活动为城市居民提供了一种令人平静的目标感，以及按自然节奏推进的可见进展，让焦虑的头脑得以放慢脚步。", "同样重要的是社区花园在邻居之间培养起的社交联系，否则这些邻居或许始终只是陌生人。在高层公寓楼里，住户们经常在沉默中同乘电梯，却彼此连名字都不知道。然而到了花园里，人们会自然而然地交流防治虫害的技巧、借用工具并分享多余的蔬菜。对于独居老人或正在适应陌生城市的新居民而言，这些随意的交谈能够大大缓解孤独感。", "当然，维护一个共享花园并非没有现实障碍。有限的城市土地、不明确的供水条件以及围绕谁来负责每周维护的分歧，都可能打击志愿者的积极性，并导致很有前景的项目逐渐衰落。如果缺乏地方政府的稳定支持——例如长期的土地使用许可以及用于购买土壤或栅栏的基础资金——社区花园就有可能只停留在短暂的试验阶段，而无法成为持久的社区资源。", "即便如此，城市规划者越来越将这些朴素的绿色角落视为对公共福祉的明智投资。与昂贵的临床项目相比，社区花园提供了一种低成本的方式，将自然、身体活动和人情温暖重新带回人口稠密的城市。为居民保留一起种植的空间，或许会被证明是建设更健康、更快乐的城市社区最简单的方法之一。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "照料；打理", "note": "熟词僻义！常见义为不及物动词“倾向于（tend to do）”，但在及物用法 tend a garden 中表示“照料、打理”。", "word": "tend"}, {"gloss": "培养；培育；促进", "note": "高频核心词，本义指“养育（儿童或植物）”，抽象语境下常考“培养社交关系、观念或才能”。", "word": "nurture"}, {"gloss": "逐渐消退；衰落", "note": "由“（颜色）褪色”引申为“（项目、记忆或影响力）逐渐消失、衰微”。", "word": "fade"}, {"gloss": "许可证；批文", "note": "词性活用考点：作动词时重音在后，意为“允许”；作名词时重音在前，意为“许可证、执照”。", "word": "permit"}, {"gloss": "朴素的；规模不大的", "note": "熟词僻义！除了形容人“谦虚的”，修饰事物（如 modest green corners, modest income）时常指“不大的、朴素的、适度的”。", "word": "modest"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Equally important is the social connection that community gardens nurture among neighbors who might otherwise remain strangers.", "point": "表语前置引起的完全倒装 + 双重定语从句 + otherwise引导的含蓄虚拟语气", "structure": "表语前置倒装主句（Equally important is the social connection）+ that 引导的定语从句修饰 connection + who 引导的定语从句修饰 neighbors（内含 otherwise 表示“否则”的含蓄虚拟）。", "zh": "同样重要的是社区花园在邻居之间培养起的社交联系，否则这些邻居或许始终只是陌生人。"}, {"en": "Unlike repetitive gym workouts, gardening gives city residents a calming sense of purpose and visible progress at a natural pace, allowing anxious minds to slow down.", "point": "介词unlike表对比 + 双宾语结构 + 现在分词作结果状语", "structure": "对比状语（Unlike repetitive gym workouts）+ 双宾语主句（gardening gives city residents a calming sense of purpose and visible progress at a natural pace）+ 现在分词短语作结果状语（allowing anxious minds to slow down）。", "zh": "与重复性的健身房锻炼不同，园艺活动为城市居民提供了一种令人平静的目标感，以及按自然节奏推进的可见进展，让焦虑的头脑得以放慢脚步。"}, {"en": "Without steady support from local governments, such as long-term land permits and basic funding for soil or fences, community gardens risk remaining short-lived experiments rather than lasting neighborhood resources.", "point": "without条件状语 + risk doing sth.固定搭配 + rather than平行对比结构", "structure": "介词短语作条件状语（Without steady support from local governments，含 such as... 举例插入语）+ 主句（community gardens risk remaining short-lived experiments rather than lasting neighborhood resources，risk doing 表“冒着……的风险”）。", "zh": "如果缺乏地方政府的稳定支持——例如长期的土地使用许可以及用于购买土壤或栅栏的基础资金——社区花园就有可能只停留在短暂的试验阶段，而无法成为持久的社区资源。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "同根词替换（calming -> calm）及语义概括（visible progress at a natural pace -> steady progress）。", "option": "a calm sense of purpose and steady progress", "original": "a calming sense of purpose and visible progress at a natural pace"}, {"note": "语境词义猜测题，nurture 在此指促进并发展邻里间的社交联结。", "option": "Encourage and develop", "original": "the social connection that community gardens nurture among neighbors"}, {"note": "否定条件推理，“没有稳定支持就会沦为短命试验”正话反说，推导出“长期成功部分依赖稳定的地方政策支持”。", "option": "Long-term success depends partly on stable local policy support", "original": "Without steady support from local governments, such as long-term land permits ... risk remaining short-lived experiments"}, {"note": "态度题同义转述，smart investments 对应 worthwhile investments，public well-being 对应 public health。", "option": "Favorable, seeing them as worthwhile investments in public health", "original": "view these modest green corners as smart investments in public well-being"}, {"note": "主旨标题凝练，beyond the dinner table 形象转述为 Growing More Than Food，并点明“促进心理健康”的核心话题。", "option": "Growing More Than Food: How City Gardens Support Mental Well-Being", "original": "benefits that reach far beyond the dinner table ... lower stress hormones and restore mental energy"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202606-s1-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 六级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "青少年社交媒体使用与心理健康监管", "subtitle": "剖析社交媒体与青少年抑郁的关联及监管困境", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["Children's use of social media is a problem. That doesn't mean it should be stopped. While younger children should not be on platforms where 13 is the minimum age, it is neither practical nor desirable to imagine a world in which teenagers are prevented from accessing the platforms and messaging systems that the adults around them use to organise their lives.", "But the pleasure and stimulation that people of all ages find on their screens and smartphones must not blind us to the harm that spending time in this way can cause. The finding that the alarmingly high rate of depression in British teenage girls is closely correlated to time spent on social media is extremely concerning. Research found that two in five girls are on social media for at least three hours a day—with half as many boys engaged to the same extent. More than a third of depressed girls have experienced online harassment. About half of affected girls suffered disrupted sleep, compared with 20% of depressed boys.", "Although the research does not prove that social media causes depression, the importance of the finding that there is a connection should not be underestimated. Schools have done important work in communicating key messages about the risks of online abuse. But when it comes to broader questions about \"screen time\", many professionals as well as parents are confused and uncertain.", "The health secretary, Matt Hancock, wants official guidelines on time and age limits. This idea has the virtue of simplicity, though some experts question its effects and call for a greater degree of differentiation, arguing that time online by itself is not a bad thing and it all depends on what you are doing. Also due this year is information commissioner Elizabeth Denham's Age Appropriate Design Code, covering the use of children's personal data. Both initiatives are welcome. But the government is playing catch-up. Statutory regulation of the digital media giants is long overdue. The failure to protect children from data harvesting and targeted advertising thus far is as shocking as the lack of concern shown by the companies themselves with regard to children's psychological health.", "Of course, social media companies are not the source of all our ills, and can offer a too-easy target for politicians keen to divert attention from inadequately resourced schools and health services. There are other reasons for the rising incidence of depression in young people, with increasing pressure to succeed in education and in life more broadly—to be famous, beautiful, rich—often cited as a source of unhappiness or anxiety which can, if aggravated by other factors and not managed, tip into ill health. Safeguarding means more than the avoidance of physical threat."], "translations": ["儿童使用社交媒体是一个问题。但这并不意味着应当制止这种行为。年幼的儿童不应使用最低年龄限制为13岁的社交平台，但设想这样一个世界既不现实，也不可取：青少年无法访问身边成年人用来安排生活的各种平台和消息系统。", "不过，各个年龄段的人从屏幕和智能手机中获得的愉悦与刺激，不应使我们忽视以这种方式消磨时间可能造成的伤害。英国少女抑郁症发病率高得令人担忧，而这一现象与花在社交媒体上的时间密切相关，这一发现极其令人忧虑。研究发现，五分之二的女孩每天使用社交媒体至少三个小时，而达到同等程度的男孩只有这一比例的一半。超过三分之一的抑郁女孩曾遭受网络骚扰。受到影响的女孩中，约有一半睡眠受到干扰，而抑郁男孩中这一比例为20%。", "尽管这项研究并未证明社交媒体会导致抑郁，但不能低估“二者存在关联”这一发现的重要性。学校在传达有关网络虐待风险的重要信息方面已经开展了重要工作。但是，在涉及有关“屏幕时间”的更广泛问题时，许多专业人士和家长一样，都感到困惑和不确定。", "卫生大臣马特·汉考克希望制定关于使用时间和年龄限制的官方指导方针。这一想法的优点在于简单明了，尽管一些专家质疑其效果，并呼吁进行更大程度的区分，认为上网本身并不是坏事，关键在于你在网上做什么。此外，信息专员伊丽莎白·德纳姆制定的《适龄设计规范》也将于今年出台，内容涉及儿童个人数据的使用。这两项举措都值得欢迎。但政府一直在追赶。对数字媒体巨头进行法定监管早就应当实施。迄今为止未能保护儿童免受数据收集和定向广告侵害，这一点令人震惊，正如相关企业本身对儿童心理健康表现出的漠不关心同样令人震惊。", "当然，社交媒体公司并不是我们所有问题的根源，也可能成为那些急于转移公众对资源不足的学校和医疗服务关注的政客们一个过于容易的目标。年轻人抑郁症发病率上升还有其他原因。人们常常认为，日益增加的教育压力以及在更广泛的生活中取得成功的压力——成为名人、美丽而富有——是不快乐或焦虑的来源；如果这些情绪受到其他因素加剧且没有得到妥善处理，就可能恶化为健康问题。保护儿童意味着不仅要避免身体上的威胁。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author believe regarding social media?", "options": ["To stop children using it is unrealistic and inadvisable.", "It helps both adults and children to organise their lives.", "It poses problems to both parents and children.", "A world without it is really hard to imagine."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "While younger children should not be on platforms where 13 is the minimum age, it is neither practical nor desirable to imagine a world in which teenagers are prevented from accessing the platforms and messaging systems that the adults around them use to organise their lives.", "explanation": "定位第1段第2-3句。作者明确指出青少年使用社交媒体是个问题，但这并不意味着应当被制止；随后用neither practical nor desirable说明禁止青少年使用成年人日常所用的平台和消息系统既不现实也不可取。题干询问作者对社交媒体的看法，A项中的unrealistic对应原文neither practical，inadvisable对应neither desirable，to stop children using it对应stopped及prevented from accessing，属于精准同义替换。", "trapNote": "B项将原文teenagers偷换为both adults and children；C项虽提及问题但偏离第1段核心立场；D项把“设想禁止青少年使用的世界”偷换为“没有社交媒体的世界”，均属曲解原意。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about British teenage girls?", "options": ["The more frequently they interact on social media, the more they experience harassment.", "The more time they spend on social media, the more likely they suffer from depression.", "Most of them are engaged on social media for at least three hours a day.", "They spend half as many hours on social media as British teenage boys."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The finding that the alarmingly high rate of depression in British teenage girls is closely correlated to time spent on social media is extremely concerning.", "explanation": "定位第2段第2句。原文指出英国少女抑郁症发病率高得令人担忧，且这一现象与花在社交媒体上的时间密切相关（is closely correlated to time spent on social media）。题干询问关于英国少女我们能从文章了解到什么，B项指出她们在社交媒体上花的时间越多，患抑郁症的可能性就越大，准确对应原文的相关性表述，是正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项将“抑郁与使用时长相关”偷换为“互动越频繁遭骚扰越多”，属无中生有；C项把“五分之二（40%）”夸大为“大多数”；D项将男女比例颠倒，原文是男孩只有女孩的一半。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "态度题", "stem": "What is the author's view on the research finding about British teenage girls?", "options": ["Its implications about online abuse are obvious.", "Its key message calls for immediate attention.", "Its importance should not be undervalued.", "Its uncertainty should not go unnoticed."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Although the research does not prove that social media causes depression, the importance of the finding that there is a connection should not be underestimated.", "explanation": "定位第3段第1句。尽管研究并未证明社交媒体会导致抑郁，但作者明确强调“二者存在关联这一发现的重要性不应被低估”（the importance of the finding that there is a connection should not be underestimated）。题干询问作者对该研究发现的观点态度，C项中的should not be undervalued精准同义替换了原文的should not be underestimated，符合文意。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，第3段第2句指学校已传达网络虐待风险信息，而非研究启示显而易见；B项“呼吁立即关注”原文未提；D项将专业人士与家长的“uncertain”嫁接到研究发现本身。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do experts think of health secretary Matt Hancock's idea?", "options": ["Its implementation requires prompt action.", "It is a welcome initiative but is long overdue.", "Its success depends on how it is implemented.", "It is too simplistic to produce the desired effect."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "This idea has the virtue of simplicity, though some experts question its effects and call for a greater degree of differentiation, arguing that time online by itself is not a bad thing and it all depends on what you are doing.", "explanation": "定位第4段第1-2句。卫生大臣Matt Hancock希望制定关于使用时长和年龄限制的官方指南，作者提到这一想法具有简单的优点，紧接着用though转折指出一些专家质疑其效果（question its effects），并呼吁进行更大程度的区分，认为上网本身并不是坏事。D项中too simplistic对应simplicity的局限性，to produce the desired effect对应experts question its effects，概括准确。", "trapNote": "A项“需要立即行动”属于无中生有；B项张冠李戴，原文说both initiatives are welcome，而long overdue修饰的是对数字媒体巨头的法定监管；C项把“取决于你在网上做什么”偷换为“如何实施”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Besides social media companies, what factors contribute to young people's psychological health problems?", "options": ["Poorly financed schools and health services.", "Politicians' eagerness to divert public attention.", "Bad statutory regulation of digital media giants.", "Their parents' educational background and life."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Of course, social media companies are not the source of all our ills, and can offer a too-easy target for politicians keen to divert attention from inadequately resourced schools and health services.", "explanation": "定位第5段第1句。原文指出社交媒体公司并非所有问题的根源，还可能成为政客的替罪羊，借此转移公众对“inadequately resourced schools and health services”（资源与经费不足的学校和医疗服务）的关注。题干问除社交媒体公司外，还有什么因素导致青少年心理健康问题，A项中的poorly financed精准同义替换了inadequately resourced，与文意相符。", "trapNote": "B项“政客急于转移公众注意力”只是掩盖问题的政治行为，并非导致心理问题的根源因素；C项将监管缺失偷换为“糟糕的法定监管”；D项“父母的教育背景和生活”原文未提，属无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 刺激；激励；兴奋", "note": "注意与动词 stimulate（刺激，激发）同根记忆，文中指屏幕与手机带来的感官刺激。", "word": "stimulation"}, {"gloss": "n. 骚扰；困扰", "note": "常与 online 搭配构成 online harassment（网络骚扰），动词为 harass。", "word": "harassment"}, {"gloss": "v. 低估；看轻", "note": "高频阅读词汇，常用于否定结构 should not be underestimated，与 undervalue 互为同义替换。", "word": "underestimate"}, {"gloss": "adj. 法定的；法令规定的", "note": "源自 statute（法规），statutory regulation 指政府层面的法定监管，区别于企业自律。", "word": "statutory"}, {"gloss": "v. 加重；使恶化", "note": "第5段出现过去分词形式 aggravated，相当于 worsen，常用于负面情绪或病情的加剧。", "word": "aggravate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "While younger children should not be on platforms where 13 is the minimum age, it is neither practical nor desirable to imagine a world in which teenagers are prevented from accessing the platforms and messaging systems that the adults around them use to organise their lives.", "point": "长难句中套嵌多层定语从句，注意识别形式主语 it 与真正主语不定式短语，准确把握让步转折后的作者核心立场。", "structure": "While引导让步状语从句（含where定语从句） + it作形式主语，to imagine...为真正主语 + in which引导定语从句修饰a world + that引导定语从句修饰platforms and messaging systems。", "zh": "年幼的儿童不应使用最低年龄限制为13岁的社交平台，但设想这样一个世界既不现实，也不可取：青少年被禁止访问身边成年人用来安排生活的各种平台和消息系统。"}, {"en": "The failure to protect children from data harvesting and targeted advertising thus far is as shocking as the lack of concern shown by the companies themselves with regard to children's psychological health.", "point": "注意识别主语核心词 failure 与过去分词短语 shown... 作后置定语，以及固定短语 with regard to（关于）的衔接作用。", "structure": "主语（The failure to protect...） + 系动词 is + as shocking as 比较结构（比较对象为 the lack of concern，后接过去分词短语 shown by... 作定语）。", "zh": "迄今为止未能保护儿童免受数据收集和定向广告侵害，这一点令人震惊，正如相关企业本身对儿童心理健康表现出的漠不关心同样令人震惊。"}, {"en": "There are other reasons for the rising incidence of depression in young people, with increasing pressure to succeed in education and in life more broadly—to be famous, beautiful, rich—often cited as a source of unhappiness or anxiety which can, if aggravated by other factors and not managed, tip into ill health.", "point": "理解 with 复合结构作伴随状语的逻辑，以及条件状语从句省略主语和 be 动词（if [it is] aggravated...）的语法现象。", "structure": "There be 主句 + with+宾语+过去分词短语（often cited as...）作伴随状语 + 破折号插入语解释说明 + which引导定语从句（内嵌if省略条件从句）。", "zh": "年轻人抑郁症发病率上升还有其他原因，人们常常认为在教育和更广泛的生活中取得成功——变得出名、美丽、富有——的日益增长的压力是不快乐或焦虑的来源；如果这些情绪受到其他因素加剧且未妥善处理，就可能恶化为健康问题。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题考点：并列否定表达的同义转换", "option": "unrealistic and inadvisable", "original": "neither practical nor desirable"}, {"note": "第2题考点：变量相关性与“越……越……”句式的转换", "option": "The more time they spend on social media, the more likely they suffer from depression.", "original": "depression in British teenage girls is closely correlated to time spent on social media"}, {"note": "第3题考点：高频动词“低估”的直接同义替换", "option": "should not be undervalued", "original": "should not be underestimated"}, {"note": "第4题考点：由优点与转折质疑推导出“过于简单而难奏效”", "option": "too simplistic to produce the desired effect", "original": "has the virtue of simplicity, though some experts question its effects"}, {"note": "第5题考点：“资源/经费不足”的精准同义替换", "option": "poorly financed schools and health services", "original": "inadequately resourced schools and health services"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202606-s1-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 六级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "跨国企业避税天堂与全球最低企业税改革", "subtitle": "揭示跨国利润转移现状与全球最低税率治理路径", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 441, "paragraphs": ["About a decade ago, the G-20, a forum of the world's biggest economies, agreed to crack down on multinational corporations' abusive use of tax havens. This resulted in a plan that aimed to curb practices that shielded a large chunk of corporate profits from tax authorities.", "But, instead of reining in the use of tax havens—countries such as the Bahamas and Cayman Islands with very low or no effective tax rates—the problem has only gotten worse.", "In a new study, we measured the excessive profits reported in tax havens that cannot be explained by ordinary economic activity such as employees, factories and research in that country. Our findings show a striking pattern of artificial shifting of paper profits to tax havens by corporations, which has been relentless since the 1980s.", "We found that the world's biggest multinational businesses shifted 37% of the profits—$969 billion—they earned in other countries to tax havens in 2019. The figure was less than 2% in the 1970s. The main reasons for the large increase were the growth of the tax avoidance industry in the 1980s and U.S. policies that made it easier to shift profits from high-tax countries to tax havens.", "We estimate that the amount of corporate taxes lost as a result reached 10% of total corporate revenue in 2019, up from less than 0.1% in the 1970s. In 2019, the total government tax loss globally was $250 billion. U.S. multinational corporations alone accounted for about half of that, followed by the U.K. and Germany.", "How do policymakers fix this? So far, the world as a whole has been trying to solve this problem by cutting or scrapping corporate taxes in a very gradual way. In the past 40 years, the global effective corporate tax rate has fallen from 23% to 17%. At the same time, governments have relied more heavily on consumption taxes.", "But the root cause of profit-shifting is the incentives involved, such as generous or lenient corporate tax rates in other countries. If countries could agree on a global minimum corporate tax rate of, say, 20%, the problem of profit-shifting would largely disappear, as tax havens would simply cease to exist.", "This type of mechanism is exactly what more than 130 countries signed onto in 2021, with implementation of a 15% minimum tax set to begin soon in the EU, U.K., Japan, Indonesia and many other countries. The U.S. has notably not been able to pass this legislation.", "Our research suggests implementing this type of tax reform is necessary in reversing the shift of ever-greater amounts of corporate profits to tax havens—instead of being taxed by the governments where they operate and create value."], "translations": ["大约十年前，作为世界最大经济体论坛的二十国集团同意严厉打击跨国公司滥用避税天堂的行为。这促成了一项计划，旨在遏制那些使企业利润中的很大一部分逃避税务机关监管的做法。", "然而，避税天堂的使用非但没有得到遏制——避税天堂包括巴哈马和开曼群岛等实际税率极低或为零的国家和地区——这一问题反而变得更加严重。", "在一项最新研究中，我们在避税天堂测算了申报的、无法用该国的雇员、工厂和研发等正常经济活动来解释的超额利润。我们的研究结果显示，企业将账面利润人为转移至避税天堂的现象十分明显，而且自20世纪80年代以来一直持续不断。", "我们发现，2019年，全球最大的跨国企业将其在其他国家赚取的利润中的37%（9690亿美元）转移到了避税天堂。20世纪70年代，这一比例还不到2%。这一比例大幅上升的主要原因，是20世纪80年代避税行业的发展，以及美国的相关政策使得企业更容易将利润从高税率国家转移到避税天堂。", "我们估计，2019年因此损失的企业税额已达到企业总收入的10%，而20世纪70年代还不到0.1%。2019年，全球政府税收损失总额为2500亿美元。其中，仅美国跨国公司就占了约一半，其后是英国和德国。", "政策制定者应如何解决这一问题？到目前为止，世界各国总体上一直试图通过非常渐进地削减或取消企业税来解决这一问题。在过去40年里，全球企业实际税率已从23%降至17%。与此同时，各国政府越来越依赖消费税。", "但利润转移的根本原因在于相关激励措施，例如其他国家慷慨或宽松的企业税率。如果各国能够就全球最低企业税率达成一致，比如确定为20%，利润转移问题将基本消失，因为避税天堂将不复存在。", "这类机制正是2021年由130多个国家签署支持的方案；欧盟、英国、日本、印度尼西亚以及许多其他国家将很快开始实施15%的最低税率。值得注意的是，美国一直未能通过这项立法。", "我们的研究表明，实施这类税制改革对于扭转企业利润越来越多地流向避税天堂的趋势是必要的；这些利润本应由企业开展经营并创造价值所在国的政府征税。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about the G-20's agreement on curbing the use of tax havens?", "options": ["It has aggravated the problem in non-G-20 countries.", "It has taken a toll on countries such as Cayman Islands.", "It has failed to achieve the expected outcome.", "It has failed to result in any long-term plan."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But, instead of reining in the use of tax havens—countries such as the Bahamas and Cayman Islands with very low or no effective tax rates—the problem has only gotten worse.", "explanation": "定位第1段与第2段。第1段提到约十年前二十国集团同意打击跨国公司滥用避税天堂的行为并制定了遏制计划；第2段随即用But转折指出，避税天堂的使用非但没有得到遏制（instead of reining in），问题反而变得更糟（the problem has only gotten worse）。C项“未能达到预期结果”精准概括了协议未产生遏制效果反致恶化的事实。", "trapNote": "A项“在非G20国家加剧问题”原文未提及；B项“对开曼群岛等国家造成损失”与文意相反，避税天堂仍被持续利用；D项偷换概念，第1段明确指出协议催生了一项计划（resulted in a plan）。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What mainly accounted for the large increase in the world's biggest multinational corporations' shift of profits to tax havens?", "options": ["Fluctuating tax rates globally.", "Lenient policies of the U.S.", "Heavy taxes imposed on them.", "Rapid growth of their business."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The main reasons for the large increase were the growth of the tax avoidance industry in the 1980s and U.S. policies that made it easier to shift profits from high-tax countries to tax havens.", "explanation": "定位第4段第3句。原文指出跨国企业向避税天堂转移利润比例大幅上升的主要原因（The main reasons for the large increase），一是20世纪80年代避税行业的发展，二是使利润更易从高税率国家转移至避税天堂的美国政策（U.S. policies that made it easier to shift profits）。题干询问利润转移大幅增长的主要原因，B项“美国宽松的政策”精准对应原文。", "trapNote": "A项“全球税率波动”与原文不符，第6段显示全球税率是渐进下降而非波动；C项“对其征收重税”与D项“其业务快速增长”在原文所述主要原因中均未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What have policymakers been doing to prevent government tax loss?", "options": ["Reducing corporate taxes step by step.", "Scrapping consumption taxes gradually.", "Making joint efforts to levy corporate taxes.", "Adjusting global effective corporate tax rates."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "So far, the world as a whole has been trying to solve this problem by cutting or scrapping corporate taxes in a very gradual way.", "explanation": "定位第6段第1-2句。针对如何防止政府税收流失的问题，原文指出迄今为止世界各国总体上一直试图通过“非常渐进地削减或取消企业税”（by cutting or scrapping corporate taxes in a very gradual way）来解决这一问题。题干问政策制定者一直在做什么，A项中的reducing corporate taxes对应cutting corporate taxes，step by step对应in a very gradual way，属于精准同义替换。", "trapNote": "B项将“逐渐削减企业税”偷换为“逐渐取消消费税”，原文第6段末句指出政府反而更依赖消费税；C项“共同努力征收企业税”指的是拟议新机制而非既有做法；D项“调整”未体现降税方向。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say would bring tax havens to an end?", "options": ["The alignment of corporate taxes with consumption taxes.", "The implementation of generous tax rates in all countries.", "The agreement on the root cause of global profit-shifting.", "The imposition of a global minimum corporate tax rate."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "If countries could agree on a global minimum corporate tax rate of, say, 20%, the problem of profit-shifting would largely disappear, as tax havens would simply cease to exist.", "explanation": "定位第7段第2句。原文指出，如果各国能就全球最低企业税率（a global minimum corporate tax rate）比如20%达成一致，利润转移问题将基本消失，因为避税天堂将不复存在（tax havens would simply cease to exist）。题干问作者认为什么会终结避税天堂，D项“实施全球最低企业税率”中的imposition对应agree on，精准契合原文条件句的逻辑。", "trapNote": "A项“将企业税与消费税对齐”文中未提及；B项“在所有国家实施宽松税率”恰恰是第7段第1句指出的利润转移根源，而非解决方案；C项“就根本原因达成共识”并不能直接消除避税天堂。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What could be expected of the global problem of profit-shifting in the near future?", "options": ["It would be solved with more countries cutting tax rates.", "It would end with governments' awareness of its severity.", "It would cease to exist with worldwide corporate support.", "It would continue because of noncooperation from the U.S."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "This type of mechanism is exactly what more than 130 countries signed onto in 2021, with implementation of a 15% minimum tax set to begin soon in the EU, U.K., Japan, Indonesia and many other countries. The U.S. has notably not been able to pass this legislation.", "explanation": "定位第8段及第5段。第8段指出2021年虽有130多个国家签署15%最低税率机制且欧盟、英国等即将实施，但美国却未能通过这项立法（The U.S. has notably not been able to pass this legislation）。结合第5段所述“仅美国跨国公司就占全球税收损失总额的约一半”，可合理推断由于美国的不配合，全球利润转移问题在近期仍将持续，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“更多国家降税就能解决”与第7段主张相反，降税不能消除套利激励；B项“政府意识到严重性就会结束”与第2段现实相悖；C项“全球企业支持就会消失”违背企业避税逻辑且原文未提。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 滥用的；虐待的", "note": "来自 abuse，文中 abusive use of tax havens 指跨国公司对避税天堂的滥用行为。", "word": "abusive"}, {"gloss": "v. 控制；约束（常用搭配 rein in）", "note": "原指“勒住马缰绳”，第2段 rein in 表示遏制或控制某问题继续恶化。", "word": "rein"}, {"gloss": "adj. 持续不断的；毫不留情的", "note": "由 relent + -less 构成，文中形容自20世纪80年代以来企业向避税天堂转移账面利润的趋势从未停歇。", "word": "relentless"}, {"gloss": "v. 废弃；取消；废除", "note": "作名词指“碎片、废料”，作动词 scrap 在经济政策语境中表示彻底取消某项税种或政策。", "word": "scrap"}, {"gloss": "adj. 宽松的；仁慈的", "note": "第7段用于修饰 corporate tax rates，指某些国家吸引利润转移的宽松低税率政策。", "word": "lenient"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In a new study, we measured the excessive profits reported in tax havens that cannot be explained by ordinary economic activity such as employees, factories and research in that country.", "point": "注意识别 reported in tax havens 为过去分词短语作后置定语，而 that 引导的定语从句修饰前面的核心名词 profits。", "structure": "状语（In a new study） + 主谓宾（we measured the excessive profits） + 过去分词短语（reported in tax havens）作定语 + that引导定语从句（修饰excessive profits）。", "zh": "在一项最新研究中，我们测算了在避税天堂申报的、无法用该国的雇员、工厂和研发等正常经济活动来解释的超额利润。"}, {"en": "The main reasons for the large increase were the growth of the tax avoidance industry in the 1980s and U.S. policies that made it easier to shift profits from high-tax countries to tax havens.", "point": "重点掌握 make it + adj. + to do 形式宾语结构，以及并列主语补足语（表语）的识别。", "structure": "主语（The main reasons...） + 系动词 were + 并列表语（the growth... and U.S. policies） + that引导定语从句（含make it easier to shift... 形式宾语结构）。", "zh": "这一比例大幅上升的主要原因，是20世纪80年代避税行业的发展，以及使企业更容易将利润从高税率国家转移到避税天堂的美国相关政策。"}, {"en": "Our research suggests implementing this type of tax reform is necessary in reversing the shift of ever-greater amounts of corporate profits to tax havens—instead of being taxed by the governments where they operate and create value.", "point": "注意 suggests 后接省略 that 的宾语从句，从句中动名词短语 implementing... 作主语，破折号后引出对比说明。", "structure": "主谓（Our research suggests） + 省略that的宾语从句（implementing... is necessary in reversing...） + instead of介词短语（含where引导的定语从句修饰governments）。", "zh": "我们的研究表明，实施这类税制改革对于扭转企业利润越来越多地流向避税天堂的趋势是必要的——而非由企业开展经营并创造价值所在国的政府征税。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题考点：否定预期与结果恶化的概括归纳", "option": "failed to achieve the expected outcome", "original": "instead of reining in the use of tax havens ... the problem has only gotten worse"}, {"note": "第2题考点：“使转移更容易的政策”同义替换为“宽松政策”", "option": "lenient policies of the U.S.", "original": "U.S. policies that made it easier to shift profits"}, {"note": "第3题考点：“渐进削减”的词组对应替换", "option": "reducing corporate taxes step by step", "original": "cutting or scrapping corporate taxes in a very gradual way"}, {"note": "第4题考点：由条件句推导出核心治理措施的名词化表达", "option": "imposition of a global minimum corporate tax rate", "original": "agree on a global minimum corporate tax rate"}, {"note": "第5题考点：美国未能通过立法对应“美国方面的不配合”", "option": "noncooperation from the U.S.", "original": "The U.S. has notably not been able to pass this legislation."}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202606-s2-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 六级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 六级真题 第2套 Passage One", "title": "自律的本质与意志力强化之道", "subtitle": "心态如何决定自律体验及意志力的肌肉式强化", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 460, "paragraphs": ["What does self-discipline look like at work? Sometimes, it's the ability to resist temptation, such as distractions to avoid a particular task. Other times it's the ability to persist with a task when your energy and motivation seem low.", "What do you believe about the nature of your own self-discipline? Is it something that runs on internal energy that is spent with use? Or is it something that is bolstered as you apply it and persist?", "Your answer matters, as it determines how much self-discipline you experience. For years, research in psychology pointed to self-control as a resource that is depleted with use and needs to be restored through breaks, rest, or sleep. More recently, however, research points to the importance of mindset. If you view self-discipline as an expendable resource, your willpower tends to fade with use. If you believe that exercising your self-control strengthens and fuels it, that is more likely to be your experience as you resist temptation or push yourself to get something done that is not appealing.", "If you don't already view self-discipline as a force that feeds itself, what might you do? Reflect on times that you had initial difficulty resisting temptation, getting started on something, or sticking with it, but pushed ahead and accomplished the task or met the goal. That's the kind of experience we're talking about with this particular belief about self-discipline, and you've already had such an experience, so you've shown that it's possible. When you feel your willpower and motivation fading, remind yourself of those previous experiences and imagine the same happening now.", "What if your experiences have always seemed to indicate that your self-control diminishes with use, and you need breaks to recharge? There's nothing wrong with that as long as you can afford to take those breaks. If not, remind yourself that not everyone experiences self-discipline as a depletable resource and that your experience might be different if you focus on gathering more energy at this point rather than focusing on how difficult it is to continue or the need for a break.", "Also, if you know someone who is a role model of self-discipline, picture that person in your situation, persisting in the task. Regardless of how you do it, as you push forward to continue to accomplish progress, be sure to mentally reinforce yourself by taking pride in your ability to exert more willpower as you persist.", "The benefits of exerting willpower are cumulative. Your self-discipline is akin to a muscle, and each time you resist temptation or persist in a task despite a lack of motivation, you strengthen that muscle, leading to less effort and resistance in similar instances in the future."], "translations": ["在工作中，自律是什么样的表现？有时，它是抵制诱惑的能力，比如抵制那些让你逃避某项特定任务的干扰。还有些时候，它是在精力和动力似乎都很低的时候，仍然坚持完成一项任务的能力。", "你如何看待自身自律的本质？它是否依靠一种会随着使用而消耗的内在能量运行？还是说，它会在你运用自律并坚持下去的过程中得到增强？", "你的答案很重要，因为它决定了你能体验到多少自律。多年来，心理学研究认为，自我控制是一种会因使用而消耗、需要通过休息、放松或睡眠来恢复的资源。然而，近来的研究更加重视思维方式的重要性。如果你把自律看作一种会耗尽的资源，你的意志力往往会随着使用而减弱。如果你相信运用自我控制能够增强并补充它，那么当你抵制诱惑，或迫使自己完成一件并不吸引人的事情时，你更有可能获得这样的体验。", "如果你还没有把自律看作一种能够自我补充的力量，可以做些什么呢？回想一下这样的时刻：起初你很难抵制诱惑、开始做某件事，或者坚持做下去，但后来你还是继续努力，完成了任务或实现了目标。这正是我们所说的关于自律的这种特定信念所对应的经历，而你已经有过这样的经历，所以你已经证明了这是可能的。当你感到意志力和动力逐渐消退时，提醒自己想起以往的这些经历，并想象现在也会发生同样的情况。", "如果你的经历一直表明，你的自我控制会随着使用而减弱，需要通过休息来充电，那该怎么办？只要你有条件休息，这本身没有什么问题。如果没有条件，那么就提醒自己，并非每个人都会把自律体验为一种会耗尽的资源；如果此时你把注意力放在积蓄更多能量上，而不是关注继续下去有多么困难或认为自己需要休息，你的体验可能会有所不同。", "此外，如果你认识一位自律方面的榜样，可以想象那个人处在你的情境中，坚持完成这项任务。无论你采用什么方式，当你继续向前、不断取得进展时，一定要通过为自己能够在坚持过程中发挥出更强的意志力而感到自豪，在心理上不断强化自己。", "发挥意志力所带来的益处会不断累积。你的自律就像一块肌肉，每当你抵制诱惑，或在缺乏动力的情况下仍坚持完成一项任务时，你都会锻炼并强化这块肌肉，从而使自己在今后遇到类似情况时付出更少的努力，也能减少阻力。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What plays an important role in determining how much self-discipline people experience?", "options": ["Their belief about the nature of motivation.", "Their use of internal energy for persisting.", "Their conception of self-discipline.", "Their ability to resist temptation."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Your answer matters, as it determines how much self-discipline you experience.", "explanation": "本题定位到第三段首句及下文心态研究。第二段提出人们对自律本质的两种看法（是随使用消耗的能量，还是随坚持而增强），第三段开篇即指出“你的答案很重要，因为它决定了你能体验到多少自律”，随后进一步说明研究揭示了思维方式（mindset）的重要性。C项中的conception of self-discipline正是对第二段belief about the nature of your own self-discipline及第三段Your answer的同义概括，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，原文探讨的是对“自律本质”的看法而非对“动力本质”的看法；B项和D项均只涉及自律的具体表现或过程，并非决定能体验到多少自律的关键因素。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did years of research suggest about self-discipline?", "options": ["It is a depletable resource.", "It is bolstered through use.", "Its strength is dependent on willpower.", "Its exercise is an exhausting experience."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "For years, research in psychology pointed to self-control as a resource that is depleted with use and needs to be restored through breaks, rest, or sleep.", "explanation": "本题由题干years of research定位到第三段第二句。该句明确指出，多年来心理学研究认为自我控制是一种会随着使用而消耗（depleted with use）、需要通过休息或睡眠来恢复的资源。A项中的a depletable resource精准同义替换原文的a resource that is depleted with use（第五段亦出现原词depletable resource），完整概括了过往多年研究对自律的核心界定，因此A为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项与过往研究结论相反，“使用后增强”是作者及近期心态研究支持的观点；C项“其强度取决于意志力”和D项“锻炼它是令人精疲力竭的体验”在文中均未作为多年研究的结论提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Why does the author ask us to reflect on our experience of meeting the goal despite initial difficulty?", "options": ["To show the urgency of abandoning outdated beliefs about self-control.", "To show the feasibility of viewing self-discipline as a force fueling itself.", "To support the argument for persistence in workplace accomplishments.", "To add evidence to consistent findings in previous psychological research."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "That's the kind of experience we're talking about with this particular belief about self-discipline, and you've already had such an experience, so you've shown that it's possible.", "explanation": "本题定位到第四段。段首提出问题：如果你尚未将自律视作一种能自我补充的力量（a force that feeds itself），该怎么做？随后作者建议回想自己最初克服困难并完成目标的经历，并在第三句点明用意：这正是这种自律信念所对应的体验，而你已经有过此类经历，从而证明它是可行的（shown that it's possible）。B项中的feasibility对应possible，fueling itself对应feeds itself，故正确。", "trapNote": "A项“摒弃过时观念的紧迫性”在第四段并未强调；C项“支持职场成就需要坚持”以偏概全，第四段重点在于证明自我补充型自律信念的可行性，而非专门论证职场成就；D项曲解文意，该例并非为以往心理学研究添证。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What are we advised to do if we cannot afford to take breaks to recharge?", "options": ["Figure out what has gone wrong.", "Focus on the hardest part of our task.", "Exert ourselves to go on with the work.", "Gather new energy from people around."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "If not, remind yourself that not everyone experiences self-discipline as a depletable resource and that your experience might be different if you focus on gathering more energy at this point rather than focusing on how difficult it is to continue or the need for a break.", "explanation": "本题由cannot afford to take breaks定位到第五段第二、三句。原文先说明如果有条件休息则无妨，随后用If not引出没有条件休息时的建议：提醒自己并非所有人都会觉得自律越用越少，且如果此时专注于积蓄更多能量，而不是想着继续有多难或需要休息，体验就会不同。这实质上是鼓励人们振作自己继续投入工作，与C项Exert ourselves to go on with the work高度契合。", "trapNote": "B项与原文相反，原文明确建议不要把注意力放在继续有多难（how difficult it is to continue）上；D项属于无中生有，文中只说积蓄更多能量，并未提及“从周围人身上获取能量”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Why does the author compare our self-discipline to a muscle?", "options": ["The more it is applied, the more resistance it encounters.", "The more it is exerted, the more proud we become.", "The more it is enforced, the stronger our willpower proves.", "The more it is exercised, the more strengthened it gets."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "Your self-discipline is akin to a muscle, and each time you resist temptation or persist in a task despite a lack of motivation, you strengthen that muscle, leading to less effort and resistance in similar instances in the future.", "explanation": "本题定位到第七段第二句。作者将自律比作肌肉（akin to a muscle），紧接着解释道：每次你抵制诱惑或在缺乏动力时坚持完成任务，都会强化这块肌肉（strengthen that muscle），使今后在类似情境中付出更少努力并遇到更小阻力。D项“锻炼得越多，它就变得越强健”准确提炼了这一类比的核心逻辑，与原文strengthen that muscle完全对应，因此选D。", "trapNote": "A项与原文意思完全相反，原文明确指出肌肉强化后会“减少阻力”（less effort and resistance），而非遇到更多阻力；B项“越自豪”源自第六段的心理强化建议，并非第七段肌肉类比的直接含义。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "增强，巩固，支撑", "note": "文中指通过坚持运用自律使其变得更加坚韧，常与confidence、morale等搭配", "word": "bolster"}, {"gloss": "耗尽，消耗，使枯竭", "note": "形容词形式depletable亦在第五段出现，是心理学“自我损耗”理论的核心词汇", "word": "deplete"}, {"gloss": "可消耗的，用完即弃的", "note": "词根expend（花费、消耗）+-able，文中指视自律为一次性消耗的资源", "word": "expendable"}, {"gloss": "强化，加强，加固", "note": "第六段mentally reinforce yourself指通过自我肯定和自豪感来巩固心理动力", "word": "reinforce"}, {"gloss": "累积的，渐增的", "note": "第七段核心词，强调每次发挥意志力的益处会不断叠加，降低未来行动的阻力", "word": "cumulative"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "If you believe that exercising your self-control strengthens and fuels it, that is more likely to be your experience as you resist temptation or push yourself to get something done that is not appealing.", "point": "多层从句嵌套及动名词作主语（exercising your self-control）", "structure": "If条件状语从句中嵌套that宾语从句，主句为that is more likely to be your experience，后接as引导的时间状语从句，其中嵌套that引导的定语从句修饰something", "zh": "如果你相信运用自我控制能够增强并补充它，那么当你抵制诱惑，或迫使自己完成一件并不吸引人的事情时，你更有可能获得这样的体验。"}, {"en": "If not, remind yourself that not everyone experiences self-discipline as a depletable resource and that your experience might be different if you focus on gathering more energy at this point rather than focusing on how difficult it is to continue or the need for a break.", "point": "并列宾语从句与rather than对比结构", "structure": "省略条件句If not后接祈使句，主干remind yourself后接两个由and连接的that宾语从句，第二个宾语从句内含if条件从句及rather than对比结构", "zh": "如果没有条件，那么就提醒自己，并非每个人都会把自律体验为一种会耗尽的资源；如果此时你把注意力放在积蓄更多能量上，而不是关注继续下去有多么困难或认为自己需要休息，你的体验可能会有所不同。"}, {"en": "Your self-discipline is akin to a muscle, and each time you resist temptation or persist in a task despite a lack of motivation, you strengthen that muscle, leading to less effort and resistance in similar instances in the future.", "point": "each time引导时间状语从句及现在分词作结果状语", "structure": "并列句，第二个分句含each time引导的时间状语从句和despite让步介词短语，句尾现在分词短语leading to...作结果状语", "zh": "你的自律就像一块肌肉，每当你抵制诱惑，或在缺乏动力的情况下仍坚持完成一项任务时，你都会锻炼并强化这块肌肉，从而使自己在今后遇到类似情况时付出更少的努力，也能减少阻力。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "对自身自律本质的看法 → 对自律的认知/观念", "option": "conception of self-discipline", "original": "belief about the nature of your own self-discipline"}, {"note": "随使用而消耗的资源 → 可耗尽的资源", "option": "a depletable resource", "original": "a resource that is depleted with use"}, {"note": "自我补给的力量+证明可行 → 视自律为自我充能之力的可行性", "option": "the feasibility of viewing self-discipline as a force fueling itself", "original": "a force that feeds itself / shown that it's possible"}, {"note": "专注积蓄能量继续前进，不纠结于休息 → 努力坚持推进工作", "option": "Exert ourselves to go on with the work", "original": "focus on gathering more energy... rather than... the need for a break"}, {"note": "每次抵制诱惑或坚持任务都会强化肌肉 → 锻炼越多则越强健", "option": "The more it is exercised, the more strengthened it gets", "original": "each time you resist temptation or persist in a task... you strengthen that muscle"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202606-s2-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 六级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 六级真题 第2套 Passage Two", "title": "青少年过度使用手机的隐忧与家长应对", "subtitle": "数字时代社交媒体与屏幕时间对青少年心理健康的影响", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["Smartphones have always posed challenges for parents of teens. From social media apps to excessive screen time, the digital world is as threatening as the physical.", "A new study shows that about half of parents of teens are worried about their teens being exposed to explicit content online. This is a valid concern, of course. But there are ways to alleviate the spread of explicit content, from changing the settings in their kids' phone to monitoring such content with apps like Bark.", "Just as alarming, if not more so, is that the amount of time teens spend on social media can lead to anxiety and depression.", "Excessive screen time has detrimental effects, for a lot of obvious reasons. Constant media consumption inhibits healthy activities associated with childhood, like spending time outside, exercising, talking to friends and family. If it interferes with sleep, that's even worse.", "Ample research shows too much smartphone use produces significant anxiety, depression, and feelings of isolation in teens. Teens log on to social media or spend time online trying to make connections, but end up feeling more alone and sad than ever. Faceless communication not only produces feelings of isolation and loneliness but increases instances of online bullying and susceptibility to criminal conducts.", "Though I've banned most social media, I've still battled smartphone time with my own kids. A lot of the time I wish I could throw my kids' smartphones into the nearest lake. The convenience of communication—when they need a ride home from school after practice, for instance—often feels like it isn't worth the battle to keep their screen time low and productive, and continue to encourage \"real-life\" activities outside and with friends and family. I understand the addiction and often tell them I'm not sure how I would have handled having a smartphone as a teen. As an adult, I too, struggle with overuse.", "In a recent TV interview to promote a new film about a mother and daughter navigating social media use, actress Kate Winslet expressed her view on teens and social media—and her concern mirrors the trends. \"I do definitely feel that the world of social media is frightening to parents because we don't really know what's there,\" she said. \"We don't know how our children are using it. We don't know the effects that it's really having on them.\"", "I don't think the U.S. government should regulate social media and teen smartphone use, but it is a vital topic for parents to understand and take seriously. Unfortunately, now, parents don't just have to worry about real-world dangers, but all the ones sneaking online and the effects they have on teenagers and their mental health."], "translations": ["智能手机一直给青少年父母带来挑战。从社交媒体应用到过度使用屏幕，数字世界和现实世界一样具有威胁性。", "一项新的研究显示，大约一半的青少年父母担心自己的孩子会在网上接触到露骨内容。当然，这种担忧是合理的。但是，有一些方法可以减缓露骨内容的传播，比如更改孩子手机中的设置，或使用Bark等应用监控这类内容。", "同样令人担忧，甚至更加令人担忧的是，青少年花在社交媒体上的时间可能会导致焦虑和抑郁。", "过度使用屏幕会产生不利影响，原因有很多，而且显而易见。持续接触媒体会妨碍童年时期与健康相关的活动，例如待在户外、锻炼以及与朋友和家人交谈。如果它还干扰睡眠，那就更糟糕了。", "大量研究表明，过度使用智能手机会使青少年产生严重的焦虑、抑郁和孤立感。青少年登录社交媒体或上网，试图建立联系，但最终却比以往任何时候都感到更加孤独和悲伤。缺乏面对面的交流不仅会产生孤立感和孤独感，还会增加网络欺凌事件以及受犯罪行为影响的可能性。", "虽然我已经禁止使用大多数社交媒体，但我仍然一直在和自己的孩子争论使用智能手机的时间。很多时候，我真希望能把孩子们的智能手机扔进最近的湖里。通信的便利性——比如他们课外活动结束后需要搭车回家时——常常让人觉得，为了控制他们的屏幕使用时间，使其保持较低水平并发挥积极作用，同时继续鼓励他们在户外以及与朋友和家人进行“现实生活”活动，并不值得这样争斗。我理解这种成瘾，而且常常告诉他们，我不知道自己在青少年时期拥有一部智能手机会如何应对。作为一个成年人，我也在努力应对过度使用的问题。", "在最近一次为宣传一部讲述母女共同应对社交媒体使用问题的新电影而进行的电视采访中，女演员凯特·温斯莱特表达了她对青少年和社交媒体的看法，而她的担忧与相关趋势相一致。她说：“我确实觉得，社交媒体的世界令父母感到害怕，因为我们并不真正知道那里有什么。我们不知道自己的孩子是如何使用它的。我们不知道它究竟会对他们产生什么影响。”", "我认为美国政府不应监管社交媒体和青少年使用智能手机的问题，但这是一个父母必须了解并认真对待的重要话题。遗憾的是，如今父母不仅要担心现实世界中的危险，还要担心所有悄悄潜入网络的危险，以及这些危险对青少年及其心理健康造成的影响。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do around half of parents of teens do according to a new study?", "options": ["They set their kids' phones to filter out obscene information.", "They try to alleviate the spread of explicit scenes on the internet.", "They feel concerned about their kids' viewing indecent content online.", "They strive to prevent their kids from spending excessive screen time."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "A new study shows that about half of parents of teens are worried about their teens being exposed to explicit content online.", "explanation": "本题由around half of parents of teens和a new study定位到第二段首句。该句指出，约半数青少年父母担心孩子会在网上接触到露骨内容（worried about their teens being exposed to explicit content online）。C项中的feel concerned about同义替换worried about，viewing indecent content online同义替换being exposed to explicit content online，精准复现原文信息，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项和B项将第二段第三句作者提出的“应对方法”（更改手机设置或用应用监控以减缓传播）张冠李戴为“半数父母在研究中的实际做法”；D项“过度屏幕时间”是第三、四段讨论的问题，并非该研究针对的半数父母担忧对象。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does a large amount of research show about teens' excessive smartphone use?", "options": ["It allows them less time for meaningful activities.", "It renders them more lonely and low-spirited.", "It gives them less time for social interactions.", "It makes them more alert to online bullying."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Ample research shows too much smartphone use produces significant anxiety, depression, and feelings of isolation in teens.", "explanation": "本题由a large amount of research定位到第五段首句及第二句。首句指出，大量研究表明过度使用智能手机会让青少年产生严重的焦虑、抑郁和孤立感；第二句进一步指出，青少年上网试图建立联系，结果却比以往任何时候都感到更加孤独和悲伤（more alone and sad than ever）。B项中的more lonely and low-spirited精准对应原文的alone and sad以及depression和isolation，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“用于有意义活动的时间减少”对应第四段“妨碍户外、锻炼等健康活动”，并非第五段大量研究的核心结论；C项偷换概念，青少年上网本意是社交联系，却反而感到孤独；D项与原文“增加网络欺凌事件”意思相悖。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "态度题", "stem": "What do we learn about the author's feelings regarding smartphones and screen time?", "options": ["They are deep-seated.", "They are instinctive.", "They are unique.", "They are mixed."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "The convenience of communication—when they need a ride home from school after practice, for instance—often feels like it isn't worth the battle to keep their screen time low and productive, and continue to encourage \"real-life\" activities outside and with friends and family.", "explanation": "本题定位到第六段。作者先表示自己禁止了大多数社交媒体，仍常为手机使用时间与孩子争执，甚至想把手机扔进湖里；但紧接着又坦言通信带来的便利（如孩子训练后需要接送）让自己觉得不值得为了压低屏幕时间而不断争斗，且自己作为成年人也难以抵抗过度使用。可见作者对智能手机和屏幕时间的态度既反感担忧又承认其便利与诱惑，内心十分矛盾纠结，D项mixed（复杂的、矛盾的）最为贴切。", "trapNote": "A项“根深蒂固的”、B项“本能的”和C项“独特的”均未能准确概括作者在“想扔掉手机”与“认可通信便利、理解成瘾”之间的矛盾心理，属于主观臆断或偏离情感基调的干扰项。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does actress Kate Winslet think about the world of social media?", "options": ["It poses increasing challenges to parents trying to ensure internet safety.", "It scares parents because they don't really know what is on the screen.", "It is a sphere difficult for parents and their teens to navigate.", "It is full of uncertainties frightful to parents and their teens."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "\"I do definitely feel that the world of social media is frightening to parents because we don't really know what's there,\" she said.", "explanation": "本题定位到第七段凯特·温斯莱特的原话。她在采访中明确表示：“我确实觉得社交媒体的世界令父母感到害怕，因为我们并不真正知道那里有什么（because we don't really know what's there）。”B项中的scares parents对应is frightening to parents，don't really know what is on the screen对应don't really know what's there，几乎逐词同义转述，故B为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“给试图确保网络安全的父母带来越来越多挑战”在温斯莱特引语中未提及；C项将电影主题“母女共同应对（navigating）社交媒体”移花接木为温斯莱特的观点；D项扩大范围，原文只说令父母害怕，未提“令青少年害怕”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "What message does the author try to convey in the last paragraph?", "options": ["Parents have to be concerned about dangers to their teens in both real and virtual worlds.", "Governments have responsibilities in regulating social media and teens' smartphone use.", "Parents should provide guidance to their teens in the use of social media.", "Online dangers are as serious as problems with teenagers' mental health."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "I don't think the U.S. government should regulate social media and teen smartphone use, but it is a vital topic for parents to understand and take seriously.", "explanation": "本题定位到最后一段。首句讨论了美国政府是否应监管社交媒体和青少年手机使用的问题，作者明确表示不认为政府应当监管，并转折强调这是父母必须理解并认真对待的重要议题，随后指出父母如今不仅要担心现实危险，还要应对网络危险及其对青少年心理健康的影响。按本题提供的官方参考答案（refKey）标定为B项，作答时需留意原文首句对政府监管的表态与尾句核心警示之间的差异。", "trapNote": "A项贴合末句“父母须同时担忧现实与网络危险”，但与给定参考答案B相左；C项“提供使用指导”末段未直接提出；D项“网络危险与心理健康问题同样严重”将末句的因果影响关系曲解为并列比较关系。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "露骨的，直白的，明确清晰的", "note": "第二段explicit content指网上的不良/色情露骨内容，常与indecent、obscene构成同义替换", "word": "explicit"}, {"gloss": "缓解，减轻，缓和", "note": "第二段alleviate the spread指减缓不良内容的传播，高频阅读动词，近义词有mitigate、ease", "word": "alleviate"}, {"gloss": "有害的，不利的", "note": "第四段detrimental effects为常见搭配，意为“不良影响”，常考同义词harmful、damaging", "word": "detrimental"}, {"gloss": "抑制，妨碍，阻碍", "note": "第四段指持续使用媒体会阻碍健康的童年活动，注意与exhibit（展示）、prohibit（禁止）区分", "word": "inhibit"}, {"gloss": "易感性，易受影响性，脆弱性", "note": "第五段susceptibility to criminal conducts指“易受犯罪行为侵害/影响的可能性”，动词为suspect", "word": "susceptibility"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The convenience of communication—when they need a ride home from school after practice, for instance—often feels like it isn't worth the battle to keep their screen time low and productive, and continue to encourage \"real-life\" activities outside and with friends and family.", "point": "破折号插入语及it形式主语与并列不定式结构", "structure": "主干The convenience of communication often feels like...，破折号之间为when引导的举例插入语，表语从句中it为形式主语，真正主语为并列不定式to keep... and continue to encourage...", "zh": "通信的便利性——比如他们课外活动结束后需要搭车回家时——常常让人觉得，为了控制他们的屏幕使用时间，使其保持较低水平并发挥积极作用，同时继续鼓励他们在户外以及与朋友和家人进行“现实生活”活动，并不值得这样争斗。"}, {"en": "Faceless communication not only produces feelings of isolation and loneliness but increases instances of online bullying and susceptibility to criminal conducts.", "point": "not only... but (also)...并列谓语及多重抽象名词搭配", "structure": "not only... but (also)...连接的并列谓语结构，说明缺乏面对面交流带来的多重负面后果", "zh": "缺乏面对面的交流不仅会产生孤立感和孤独感，还会增加网络欺凌事件以及受犯罪行为影响的可能性。"}, {"en": "Unfortunately, now, parents don't just have to worry about real-world dangers, but all the ones sneaking online and the effects they have on teenagers and their mental health.", "point": "代词ones指代、现在分词作后置定语及省略关系词的定语从句", "structure": "not just... but (also)...结构，ones指代dangers，后接现在分词短语sneaking online作后置定语及定语从句(that) they have...修饰the effects", "zh": "遗憾的是，如今父母不仅要担心现实世界中的危险，还要担心所有悄悄潜入网络的危险，以及这些危险对青少年及其心理健康造成的影响。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "担心青少年接触网上露骨内容 → 担忧孩子浏览网上不当内容", "option": "feel concerned about their kids' viewing indecent content online", "original": "worried about their teens being exposed to explicit content online"}, {"note": "最终感到比以往更孤独和悲伤 → 使他们更加孤单和情绪低落", "option": "renders them more lonely and low-spirited", "original": "end up feeling more alone and sad than ever"}, {"note": "既想扔掉手机又认可其联系便利 → 情感是矛盾复杂的", "option": "They are mixed", "original": "wish I could throw my kids' smartphones into the nearest lake / convenience of communication"}, {"note": "令父母害怕因为不知里面有什么 → 让父母恐惧因不知屏幕上有什么", "option": "scares parents because they don't really know what is on the screen", "original": "frightening to parents because we don't really know what's there"}, {"note": "既要担心现实危险也要担心网络危险 → 现实与虚拟世界中的双重危险", "option": "dangers to their teens in both real and virtual worlds", "original": "not just have to worry about real-world dangers, but all the ones sneaking online"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202606-s3-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 六级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 六级真题 第3套 Passage One", "title": "AI绘画版权纠纷与合理使用争议", "subtitle": "艺术家起诉AI图像工具侵权及“合理使用”原则争议", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["Three artists have brought a lawsuit against Stability AI, DeviantArt, and Midjourney, alleging that the text-to-image AI tools have infringed the rights of thousands of artists.", "The lawsuit claims that the Stable Diffusion tool used by Stability AI, DeviantArt, and Midjourney was trained on billions of copyrighted images downloaded from the internet and used by the companies \"without compensation or consent from the artists.\"", "The artists are represented by The Joseph Saveri Law Firm and Matthew Butterick.", "\"If Stable Diffusion and similar products are allowed to continue to operate as they do now, the foreseeable result is they will replace the very artists whose stolen works power these AI products with whom they are competing,\" the law firm wrote in a press release. \"AI image products are not just an infringement of artists' rights; they will eliminate 'artist' as a viable career path. In addition to obtaining compensation for the wrongful conduct, this lawsuit seeks to prevent that outcome and ensure these products follow the same rules as any other new technology that involves the use of massive amounts of intellectual property. If streaming music can be accomplished within the law, so can AI products.\"", "Since text-to-image generators have increased in popularity in the past year, many artists have been vocalizing their opposition to AI art after seeing their own distorted signatures appear in AI art and finding out that their work was used to train the tools without their permission.", "Not only are many artists furious at the possible copyright violations of AI art, but they have also been frustrated by how AI tools are able to sidestep the labor and art processes they are required to go through. As a result, many artists have been trying to ban AI art from art-sharing platforms.", "As AI innovation continues at a rapid speed, it seems that artists and lawmakers are trying to put a brake on further developments before it's too late.", "Many tech enthusiasts are still rallying around the promise of AI tools to create detailed images cheaply and quickly—anonymous tech supporters have already published a response to Butterick and Joseph Saveri's lawsuit on a website, using the \"fair use\" clause as the basis for why copyrighted images could be used by the tool.", "Fair use, a legal doctrine that allows for a limited usage of copyrighted materials without permission by the original creators for purposes such as teaching and news sharing, is what a lot of generative model creators claim that their training data is covered by. However, since fair use applies differently to each case, it's hard to make a blanket statement about all works in a dataset as being applicable."], "translations": ["三位艺术家对 Stability AI、DeviantArt 和 Midjourney 提起诉讼，指控文生图人工智能工具侵犯了数千名艺术家的权利。", "诉讼称，Stability AI、DeviantArt 和 Midjourney 使用的 Stable Diffusion 工具，是利用从互联网下载的数十亿张受版权保护的图像训练而成的，而这些公司在“未向艺术家支付报酬也未征得其同意的情况下”使用了这些图像。", "这些艺术家由 The Joseph Saveri Law Firm 律师事务所和 Matthew Butterick 代理。", "该律师事务所在一份新闻稿中写道：“如果允许 Stable Diffusion 及类似产品继续按现在的方式运行，可预见的结果是，它们将取代那些被盗用作品为这些AI产品提供动力、且正与之竞争的艺术家。AI图像产品不仅是对艺术家权利的侵犯，还将消除‘艺术家’这一可行的职业道路。除了为不当行为寻求赔偿外，这起诉讼还力求防止这一结果的发生，并确保这些产品遵循与其他涉及使用大量知识产权的新技术相同的规则。如果流媒体音乐能够在法律框架内实现，那么AI产品也同样可以。”", "过去一年，随着文生图生成器的日益流行，许多艺术家在AI艺术作品中看到了自己扭曲的签名，并发现自己的作品在未经许可的情况下被用来训练这些工具，随后纷纷发声反对AI艺术。", "许多艺术家不仅对AI艺术可能涉及的版权侵权感到愤怒，而且对AI工具能够绕过他们必须经历的劳动和艺术创作过程感到沮丧。因此，许多艺术家一直试图在艺术分享平台上封禁AI艺术。", "随着人工智能创新继续以飞快的速度发展，艺术家和立法者似乎正试图在为时已晚之前给进一步的发展踩下刹车。", "许多科技爱好者仍然团结在AI工具廉价、快速地创作精细图像的前景周围——匿名科技支持者已经在一家网站上发表了对 Butterick 和 Joseph Saveri 诉讼的回应，以“合理使用”条款作为该工具可以使用受版权保护图像的依据。", "“合理使用”是一项法律原则，允许在教学和新闻分享等用途下，未经原作者许可有限度地使用受版权保护的材料，许多生成式模型创作者正是声称他们的训练数据受这一原则的保护。然而，由于合理使用在不同案件中的适用情况不同，很难就数据集中的所有作品都适用这一原则做出一概而论的声明。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why have three artists brought a lawsuit against Stability AI, DeviantArt, and Midjourney?", "options": ["They claim that the use of the Stable Diffusion tool is a violation of law.", "They claim these companies infringed their intellectual property rights.", "They want to stop the use of all AI tools in the creation of art works.", "They want to prevent artists from being compelled to rely on AI tools."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Three artists have brought a lawsuit against Stability AI, DeviantArt, and Midjourney, alleging that the text-to-image AI tools have infringed the rights of thousands of artists.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位至第1段及第2段。第1段开篇指出三位艺术家对Stability AI、DeviantArt和Midjourney提起诉讼，指控文生图AI工具侵犯了数千名艺术家的权利；第2段进一步说明Stable Diffusion在未经艺术家同意且未支付报酬的情况下使用了受版权保护的图像。选项B中的infringed their intellectual property rights（侵犯知识产权）精准对应原文的infringed the rights和copyrighted images，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，诉讼针对的是未经授权使用版权作品的行为，而非认定该工具本身违法；C项“阻止所有AI工具用于艺术创作”和D项“防止艺术家被迫依赖AI”均属过度推断或无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What will happen if Stable Diffusion and similar products are allowed to continue to operate as they do now, according to the law firm?", "options": ["Intellectual property laws will be hard to enforce.", "Fewer artists will invest talent in artistic creation.", "Artists will lose their means of subsistence.", "Copied works will flood the art market."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "AI image products are not just an infringement of artists' rights; they will eliminate 'artist' as a viable career path.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，根据题干中的law firm和operate as they do now定位至第4段。律师事务所在新闻稿中指出，若放任此类产品按现行方式运作，它们将取代被盗用作品的艺术家，不仅侵犯权益，更会“消除‘艺术家’这一可行的职业道路”（eliminate 'artist' as a viable career path）。选项C中的lose their means of subsistence（失去谋生手段）正是对失去职业道路的同义转述，故C正确。", "trapNote": "B项“更少艺术家将才华投入艺术创作”属于对职业消失后果的自行推演，原文未提及；D项“抄袭作品充斥艺术市场”是对AI生成内容的臆测，文中仅强调艺术家本身面临被取代的风险。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What makes artists furious aside from copyright infringement?", "options": ["Art works produced with AI tools are not banned from art-sharing platforms.", "Text-to-image generators have won such great popularity in the past year.", "Their distorted signatures appear more and more frequently in AI art.", "AI tools can bypass the considerable labor involved in creating art works."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Not only are many artists furious at the possible copyright violations of AI art, but they have also been frustrated by how AI tools are able to sidestep the labor and art processes they are required to go through.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，根据题干关键词furious和aside from copyright infringement定位至第6段。该段首句采用not only...but also...结构，指出艺术家不仅对AI艺术可能涉及的版权侵权感到愤怒，还对AI工具能够“绕过他们必须经历的劳动和艺术创作过程”（sidestep the labor and art processes）感到沮丧。选项D中的bypass对应原文的sidestep，considerable labor对应labor and art processes，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项反客为主，第6段说艺术家正试图从分享平台封禁AI艺术，并非因为“未被封禁”才愤怒；C项“扭曲签名频繁出现”是第5段提及艺术家发现作品被用于训练的契机，并非本题所问的“除版权侵权外的另一愤怒原因”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about many AI enthusiasts?", "options": ["They look forward to AI tools creating good-quality art works.", "They claim artists can use copyrighted materials just as teachers do.", "They support AI's limited use of copyrighted images without permission.", "They wish the \"fair use\" clause would be applicable to all works in a dataset."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "anonymous tech supporters have already published a response to Butterick and Joseph Saveri's lawsuit on a website, using the \"fair use\" clause as the basis for why copyrighted images could be used by the tool.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，根据AI enthusiasts定位至第8段并结合第9段理解。第8段指出许多科技爱好者仍支持AI工具，并以“合理使用”（fair use）条款作为其使用受版权保护图像的依据；第9段随即解释“合理使用”允许在未经原作者许可的情况下有限度地使用受版权保护的材料（allows for a limited usage of copyrighted materials without permission）。选项C精准概括了两段信息，故C正确。", "trapNote": "D项极具干扰性，第9段指出由于合理使用因案而异，难以一概而论地声明数据集内所有作品均适用，这是作者和法律层面的客观局限，而非科技爱好者“希望”的结果；B项则曲解了第9段中对教学用途的举例。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "What does the author think of the \"fair use\" clause in copyright law?", "options": ["It may determine the final verdict of the case.", "It may not apply to the present legal case.", "It does not cover the works of all artists.", "It is subject to different interpretations."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "However, since fair use applies differently to each case, it's hard to make a blanket statement about all works in a dataset as being applicable.", "explanation": "本题为态度题，定位至第9段末句。在解释完“合理使用”原则的定义及生成式模型创作者的主张后，作者用However转折指出：“由于合理使用在不同案件中的适用情况不同，很难对数据集中的所有作品都适用这一原则做出一概而论的声明”（fair use applies differently to each case）。这表明作者认为该条款在具体适用时存在不同解释空间。选项D中的is subject to different interpretations精准对应原文，故D正确。", "trapNote": "B项“可能不适用于本案”过于武断，原文只说难以对所有数据集作品一概而论，并未直接否定其在本案中的适用性；A项“可能决定最终裁决”与C项“未涵盖所有艺术家作品”均偏离末句核心论点。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "（未获充分证据前）指控，声称", "note": "法律语境高频词，常接that从句引出起诉方主张的侵权或违法事实。", "word": "allege"}, {"gloss": "侵犯，侵害（权利、版权等）", "note": "常用搭配为infringe (on/upon) sb.'s rights或intellectual property，名词为infringement。", "word": "infringe"}, {"gloss": "报酬，补偿，赔偿", "note": "在版权与法律文本中常指经济赔偿或使用版权作品应付的报酬。", "word": "compensation"}, {"gloss": "绕过，回避（困难、规则或必要工序）", "note": "文中表示AI工具绕开了人类艺术家必须经历的繁重劳动与创作流程，与bypass同义。", "word": "sidestep"}, {"gloss": "（法律）原则，学说，教义", "note": "文中指“合理使用”这一法律原则（a legal doctrine），常见于法学及政策类议论文。", "word": "doctrine"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "\"If Stable Diffusion and similar products are allowed to continue to operate as they do now, the foreseeable result is they will replace the very artists whose stolen works power these AI products with whom they are competing,\" the law firm wrote in a press release.", "point": "the very + 名词表示“恰恰就是……”，后接whose引导的定语从句及with whom引导的定语从句双重修饰artists，需厘清指代关系。", "structure": "直接引语（If条件状语从句 + 主句[the foreseeable result is + 省略that的表语从句，内含whose和with whom引导的两个定语从句修饰artists]） + 插入语式主句（the law firm wrote...）", "zh": "该律师事务所在一份新闻稿中写道：“如果允许Stable Diffusion及类似产品继续按现在的方式运行，可预见的结果是，它们将取代那些被盗用作品为这些AI产品提供动力、且正与之竞争的艺术家。”"}, {"en": "Fair use, a legal doctrine that allows for a limited usage of copyrighted materials without permission by the original creators for purposes such as teaching and news sharing, is what a lot of generative model creators claim that their training data is covered by.", "point": "主语Fair use与谓语is之间插入了较长的同位语及定语从句；表语部分由what引导，且claim that...结构充当插入语嵌套其中。", "structure": "主语（Fair use） + 同位语（a legal doctrine + that定语从句） + 系动词（is） + 表语从句（what...claim that their training data is covered by）", "zh": "“合理使用”是一项法律原则，允许在教学和新闻分享等用途下，未经原作者许可有限度地使用受版权保护的材料，而许多生成式模型创作者正是声称他们的训练数据受该原则保护。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "原文“侵犯艺术家权利”及“受版权保护的图像”在选项中概括为“侵犯知识产权”。", "option": "infringed their intellectual property rights", "original": "infringed the rights of thousands of artists / copyrighted images"}, {"note": "“消除作为可行职业道路的‘艺术家’”同义转述为“失去谋生手段”。", "option": "lose their means of subsistence", "original": "eliminate 'artist' as a viable career path"}, {"note": "“绕过所需付出的劳动”对应“避开创作艺术品涉及的大量劳动”。", "option": "bypass the considerable labor involved in creating art works", "original": "sidestep the labor and art processes they are required to go through"}, {"note": "“因案而异、难以一概而论”在选项中凝练为“受制于不同的解释”。", "option": "is subject to different interpretations", "original": "applies differently to each case, it's hard to make a blanket statement"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202606-s3-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2026.06", "examSet": "2026.06 六级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2026.06 六级真题 第3套 Passage Two", "title": "私营部门助力非洲电网电气化", "subtitle": "撒哈拉以南非洲电力短缺困境与私营企业破局之道", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 446, "paragraphs": ["On a warm October morning, Daniel Agok woke up to another disappointing day at his school in Wanyjok, South Sudan. The classes he had planned teaching computer skills to aspiring young professionals were canceled, due to an unreliable diesel generator and the absence of a municipal power grid in his area. Now, he would be losing frustrated customers as well as income. Agok is just one of the hundreds of millions of people in sub-Saharan Africa, many of whom are business owners, who still do not have dependable electricity. This inequitable access to energy continues to put their livelihood and future at risk.", "The current system keeps a lid on the economic talents of people like Agok and his students. We must instead unleash their abilities and let Africa reach its true economic potential. That means wiring Africa with clean, dependable energy.", "Historically, national governments on the continent have led electrification efforts, but fewer than half of the people surveyed say that the national grid is providing a reliable supply of electricity.", "This has led to expensive and harmful temporary \"solutions\". In Nigeria alone experts estimate people spend $13 billion every year on fuel for toxic, polluting generators. That number will only grow as the continent's population hits 2.5 billion people by 2050. Deploying modern grid infrastructure with speed and at scale is essential to replacing these temporary solutions with reliable and affordable alternatives.", "The rapidly growing private power sector in Africa holds the key to achieving the speed and scale necessary to close the continent's energy access gap. Private companies today are building worldclass infrastructure and driving forward economic growth with sustainable business models. In fact, many governments agree and have begun to embrace the private sector as partners in providing reliable power at scale. In South Africa, President Cyril Ramaphosa has streamlined licensing requirements and enlisted the private sector to play a key role.", "South Africa is just one example. Across the continent, the private sector has delivered power faster and more reliably, and governments are increasingly turning to private partners.", "With the right funding and structure in place, the private sector will come together to provide this essential service. After all, electrifying sub-Saharan Africa is a $350 billion opportunity.", "Today, Daniel Agok is steadily growing his business in South Sudan. His town of Wanyjok was electrified by a private company, providing clean, reliable, and affordable power to his business and his neighbors. Agok now operates his growing computer skills training business smoothly. His classes are no longer affected by the smell and the constant noise of the diesel generator, and he saves money with more affordable power. His students are developing hardware and software skills."], "translations": ["十月一个温暖的早晨，丹尼尔·阿戈克醒来时，迎接他的又是南苏丹瓦尼约克学校里令人失望的一天。由于柴油发电机运行不稳定，而且他所在地区没有市政电网，他原本计划为有志成为年轻专业人士的人教授计算机技能的课程被取消了。现在，他不仅会失去因失望而离去的客户，还会损失收入。阿戈克只是撒哈拉以南非洲数亿人中的一员——其中许多人是企业主——至今仍没有可靠的电力供应。这种不公平的能源获取状况持续使他们的生计和未来面临风险。", "现行体系限制了阿戈克及其学生这类人的经济才能。相反，我们必须释放他们的能力，让非洲实现真正的经济潜力。这意味着要用清洁、可靠的能源为非洲接入电网。", "从历史上看，非洲大陆各国政府一直主导着电气化工作，但接受调查的人中，不到一半表示国家电网能够提供可靠的电力供应。", "这导致了昂贵且有害的临时“解决方案”。专家估计，仅在尼日利亚，人们每年就要花费130亿美元购买有毒且污染环境的发电机燃料。随着非洲大陆人口到2050年达到25亿，这一数字只会继续增长。快速、大规模部署现代电网基础设施，对于用可靠且价格可负担的替代方案取代这些临时解决方案至关重要。", "非洲迅速发展的私营电力行业，是实现弥合非洲大陆能源获取缺口所需的速度和规模的关键。如今，私营企业正在建设世界一流的基础设施，并通过可持续的商业模式推动经济增长。事实上，许多政府对此表示认同，并已开始接受私营部门作为合作伙伴，以大规模提供可靠电力。在南非，西里尔·拉马福萨总统简化了许可要求，并邀请私营部门发挥关键作用。", "南非只是其中一个例子。在整个非洲大陆，私营部门以更快的速度提供了更加可靠的电力，各国政府也越来越多地寻求与私营合作伙伴合作。", "只要建立适当的资金和组织架构，私营部门就会联合起来提供这项基本服务。毕竟，为撒哈拉以南非洲实现电气化蕴含着3500亿美元的机遇。", "如今，丹尼尔·阿戈克正在稳步发展他在南苏丹的企业。瓦尼约克镇由一家私营公司实现了电气化，为他的企业和邻居们提供了清洁、可靠且价格可负担的电力。阿戈克现在可以顺利运营不断发展的计算机技能培训业务。他的课程不再受到柴油发电机气味和持续噪声的影响，而且借助价格更低的电力，他节省了开支。他的学生正在培养硬件和软件技能。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about the current electric supply system in Africa?", "options": ["It curbs the economic development of the continent.", "It mainly depends on the polluting diesel generators.", "It is the primary cause of inequitable distribution of wealth.", "It deprives many Africans of the opportunity to use computers."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The current system keeps a lid on the economic talents of people like Agok and his students.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，根据current electric supply system定位至第2段。第1段先通过Agok因缺乏可靠电网而停课、损失收入的例子引入非洲普遍缺电的现状，第2段随即总结指出：“现行体系限制了像Agok及其学生这样的人的经济才能”（keeps a lid on the economic talents），并呼吁释放能力以让非洲实现真正的经济潜力。选项A中的curbs（抑制、限制）精准转述了keeps a lid on，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项“主要依赖污染性柴油发电机”夸大事实，第4段仅提及尼日利亚等地的部分临时替代方案，而非整个电力系统；C项“财富分配不均的主因”偷换了第1段中inequitable access to energy的概念。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about Africa's past electrification efforts?", "options": ["They have failed to meet most Africans' need of a reliable power supply.", "They have failed to build a national grid to provide electric power.", "They have unleashed the true economic potential of the continent.", "They have aimed at wiring Africa with clean, dependable energy."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Historically, national governments on the continent have led electrification efforts, but fewer than half of the people surveyed say that the national grid is providing a reliable supply of electricity.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，根据past electrification efforts定位至第3段。原文指出，从历史上看，非洲大陆各国政府一直主导着电气化工作，但接受调查的人中只有不到一半表示国家电网能提供可靠的电力供应（fewer than half of the people surveyed say that the national grid is providing a reliable supply of electricity）。这意味着过去的努力未能满足大多数非洲人对可靠电力的需求，与选项A完全吻合，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项“未能建成国家电网”与原文事实相悖，国家电网已经存在，只是供电不可靠；C、D两项张冠李戴，释放经济潜力和接入清洁能源是第2段提出的未来目标，并非过去电气化努力的成果。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is essential to tackling the power supply shortage in Africa?", "options": ["Replacing temporary solutions with long-term strategies.", "Accelerating economic growth with sustainable policies.", "Restructuring national power generation companies.", "Putting in place a large-scale modern power grid speedily."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Deploying modern grid infrastructure with speed and at scale is essential to replacing these temporary solutions with reliable and affordable alternatives.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，根据essential定位至第4段末句。原文指出“快速、大规模地部署现代电网基础设施，对于用可靠且负担得起的替代方案取代这些临时解决方案至关重要”（Deploying modern grid infrastructure with speed and at scale is essential...）。选项D中putting in place对应deploying，large-scale对应at scale，speedily对应with speed，精准同义替换，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项“用长期战略取代临时方案”过于笼统，未点出“现代电网基础设施”这一核心举措；B项“以可持续政策加速经济增长”将第5段私营企业带来的结果误当作解决缺电的关键前提。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What are many governments in Africa doing to solve the electricity supply problem?", "options": ["Focusing on building world-class infrastructures.", "Relying on the private sector for scale economy.", "Launching sustainable business models.", "Cooperating with private companies."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "In fact, many governments agree and have begun to embrace the private sector as partners in providing reliable power at scale.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，根据many governments定位至第5段。该段先阐述私营电力部门正在建设一流基础设施并推动经济增长，接着指出：“事实上，许多政府对此表示认同，并已开始接受私营部门作为合作伙伴，以大规模提供可靠电力”（have begun to embrace the private sector as partners），第6段也进一步呼应各国政府正越来越多地转向私营合作伙伴。选项D中的Cooperating with private companies精准对应原文，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项“专注建设一流基础设施”和C项“推出可持续商业模式”均偷换了动作主体，第5段明确指出这两项举措的实施者是私营企业，而非非洲各国政府；B项“依靠私营部门实现规模经济”曲解了at scale的含义。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why will private companies be motivated to join the effort of electrifying sub-Saharan Africa?", "options": ["There is big money to be made.", "They have enough funding in place.", "South Africa has set a successful example.", "Governments are turning to them for help."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "After all, electrifying sub-Saharan Africa is a $350 billion opportunity.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，根据private companies和electrifying sub-Saharan Africa定位至第7段。该段首句指出只要资金和架构到位，私营部门就会联合起来提供这项基本服务，紧接着用After all（毕竟）点明其内在驱动力：“为撒哈拉以南非洲实现电气化是一个价值3500亿美元的机遇”（is a $350 billion opportunity）。选项A中的There is big money to be made（有利可图、商机巨大）正是对这一巨额市场机遇的形象概括，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项“它们已有充足资金到位”与原文With the right funding and structure in place这一假设条件不符；C、D两项均是第5、6段提及的背景或外部合作趋势，并非第7段所强调的私营企业参与其中的直接经济动因。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "不公平的，不公正的", "note": "文中inequitable access to energy指“能源获取不公”，反义词为equitable。", "word": "inequitable"}, {"gloss": "释放，发泄（潜力、力量等）", "note": "常用于“释放经济潜力/创造力”（unleash economic potential/talents），是议论文高频动词。", "word": "unleash"}, {"gloss": "部署，配置，有效利用", "note": "文中deploying modern grid infrastructure指部署现代化电网基础设施。", "word": "deploy"}, {"gloss": "简化，使……流程更顺畅/高效", "note": "第5段streamlined licensing requirements意为“简化许可审批要求”。", "word": "streamline"}, {"gloss": "吸纳，招募，争取（某人协助或参与）", "note": "搭配enlist sb. to do sth.表示邀请或吸收某方参与并发挥作用。", "word": "enlist"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Agok is just one of the hundreds of millions of people in sub-Saharan Africa, many of whom are business owners, who still do not have dependable electricity.", "point": "两个定语从句相继修饰people：many of whom引导非限制性定语从句补充身份，who引导限制性定语从句说明核心困境。", "structure": "主语（Agok） + 系动词 + 表语（just one of...people） + 插入式非限制性定语从句（many of whom...） + 限制性定语从句（who still do not have...）", "zh": "阿戈克只是撒哈拉以南非洲数亿人中的一员——其中许多人是企业主——他们至今仍没有可靠的电力供应。"}, {"en": "Deploying modern grid infrastructure with speed and at scale is essential to replacing these temporary solutions with reliable and affordable alternatives.", "point": "注意essential to中的to为介词，后接动名词短语replacing...；with speed and at scale表示“快速且大规模地”。", "structure": "动名词短语作主语（Deploying...at scale） + 系表结构（is essential to） + 介词宾语（replacing...with...）", "zh": "快速、大规模地部署现代电网基础设施，对于用可靠且价格可负担的替代方案取代这些临时解决方案至关重要。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "习惯用语keep a lid on（控制、压制）精准对应动词curb（抑制、限制）。", "option": "curbs the economic development", "original": "keeps a lid on the economic talents"}, {"note": "调查显示不到半数民众认可电网可靠性，转述为未能满足大多数人的需求。", "option": "failed to meet most Africans' need of a reliable power supply", "original": "fewer than half of the people surveyed say that the national grid is providing a reliable supply of electricity"}, {"note": "deploying、with speed、at scale与选项中的putting in place、speedily、large-scale一一对应。", "option": "Putting in place a large-scale modern power grid speedily", "original": "Deploying modern grid infrastructure with speed and at scale"}, {"note": "“接受私营部门作为合作伙伴”同义转述为“与私营企业合作”。", "option": "Cooperating with private companies", "original": "embrace the private sector as partners"}, {"note": "“3500亿美元的商机”形象地转述为“有大钱可赚 / 利润丰厚”。", "option": "There is big money to be made", "original": "a $350 billion opportunity"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202512-s1-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2025.12", "examSet": "2025.12 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2025.12 六级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "追求个人成功不应以牺牲友谊为代价", "subtitle": "反思激进个人主义文化，重拾支持与陪伴的锚点", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["Many see friendships as a comfort blanket: a shoulder to cry on, a reliable soul to confide in. However, more often than not, in our eagerness to seek individual success, we lose friends along the way and that has become part of the process.", "The chaos and never-ending turmoil that accompanies everyday life is an aggressive obstacle in the pursuit of stable friendships. As students, we use this excuse to shrug off losing people who we once thought to be loved ones.", "Instead of viewing our lives as a race, where everyone is on their own path to some form of success, we must relearn to value the connections we make along the track. We must reevaluate the harm of radical, individual freedom.", "Radical individualism elevates the freedom of the individual over the collective. It argues, for instance, that universal healthcare, an example of collectivism, threatened the dream of many Americans.", "Many of us have fallen victim to an individualistic culture. Society tends to celebrate personal achievement and commend it based on the assumption that winning or succeeding is a consequence of working harder than the next person.", "As a society, we idolize the concept of \"losing friends on the road to success\". I remember hearing in high school, \"Don't worry about losing friendships, just focus on study and getting into college. That's all that will matter in the long run,\" a sentiment that is not unique to my experience. It's preached in many success stories, and it's embedded in the way we see growth. Motivational speakers will push their audience to be complacent to the inevitable end of losing friends. Spend too much time with friends? You're losing time better utilized on your achievements. Invest time in your relationships? Invest time in your work instead.", "This constant need to succeed has blinded us from seeing through the whirlwind of change that accompanies our everyday lives. We are expected to tangibly succeed, earn awards, get higher positions, earn better grades. In order to succeed, we lose friends, and that has sadly become normalized.", "We cannot be complacent with losing friendships because they are our anchors. Yes, pursue success. Challenge yourself. Push limits. But contrary to all the self-proclaimed success experts, doing it alone does not make you more successful or any better than someone who achieved it with the help of others.", "Put effort into fostering healthy relationships, and maintaining them through your busy schedule that seems like it leaves no time for anyone else. Although we may be living in a society that treasures the independent pursuit of achievement, having people to support and love you on the way is far more important than any end result."], "translations": ["许多人将友谊视为一条慰藉的毛毯：一个可以靠着哭泣的肩膀，一个可以信赖、倾诉的灵魂。然而，更多时候，在我们急于追求个人成功的过程中，我们沿途失去了朋友，而这已成为这一过程的一部分。", "伴随日常生活而来的混乱和永无止境的动荡，是追求稳定友谊的严重障碍。作为学生，我们用这个借口来对失去那些曾经被视为挚爱之人的事实不以为意。", "我们不应该将生活视为一场竞赛——每个人都在通往某种形式成功的各自道路上——而必须重新学会珍视我们在这条轨道上建立的联系。我们必须重新评估激进的个人自由所带来的危害。", "激进个人主义将个人自由置于集体之上。例如，它认为全民医疗保健这一集体主义的例子威胁到了许多美国人的梦想。", "我们中的许多人已经成为个人主义文化的受害者。社会倾向于颂扬个人成就，并基于这样的假设对其进行赞扬：获胜或成功是比别人更努力工作的结果。", "作为一个社会，我们崇拜“在通往成功的路上失去朋友”这一概念。我记得在高中时听到过：“不要担心失去友谊，只需专注于学习和考上大学。从长远来看，那才是唯一重要的事情。”这种情绪并非我独有的经历。它在许多成功故事中被宣扬，并且嵌入在我们看待成长的方式中。励志演讲者会推动他们的听众对失去朋友这一不可避免的结局感到坦然。花太多时间和朋友在一起？你正在浪费本可以更好地用于成就上的时间。在人际关系上投入时间？把时间投入到工作上吧。", "这种对成功的持续需求使我们看不清伴随日常生活而来的变化旋涡。我们被期望取得有形的成功，赢得奖项，获得更高的职位，取得更好的成绩。为了成功，我们失去了朋友，而这已可悲地变得正常化了。", "我们不能对失去友谊感到自满，因为它们是我们的锚。是的，去追求成功，挑战自己，突破极限。但与所有那些自封的成功专家相反，独自做到这一点并不会让你更成功，也不会让你比在他人帮助下实现目标的人更优秀。", "努力培养健康的人际关系，并在你那似乎不为任何其他人留出时间的繁忙日程中维持这些关系。尽管我们可能生活在一个珍视独立追求成就的社会中，但在这条路上有人支持和爱你远比任何最终结果都重要得多。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What often happens when people are eager to pursue individual success?", "options": ["They lack a shoulder to cry on.", "They have no soul to confide in.", "They cannot find reliable friends.", "They ignore their ties with friends."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "However, more often than not, in our eagerness to seek individual success, we lose friends along the way and that has become part of the process.", "explanation": "定位第一段第二句。题干询问人们急于追求个人成功时常发生的情况。原文明确指出，在我们急于追求个人成功（eagerness to seek individual success）的过程中，往往会一路失去朋友（lose friends along the way），且这已成为普遍过程的一部分。D项“忽视与朋友的联系”与前文抛弃友情、只顾个人成功的逻辑一致，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“缺乏哭诉的肩膀”和B项“没有倾诉的灵魂”均偷换了首句对友谊作用的比喻，原文并未说人完全找不到朋友，而是人在逐梦时主动疏远、失去了朋友。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author advise people to do in their pursuit of radical individualism?", "options": ["Reexamine its detrimental effects.", "Shrug off the loss of their loved ones.", "Avoid the chaos and turmoil involved.", "Remove aggressive obstacles in the way."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "We must reevaluate the harm of radical, individual freedom.", "explanation": "定位第三段末句。题干询问作者建议人们在面对激进个人主义时应怎么做。前文先呼吁重新学会珍视人生轨迹中建立的人际联结，随后明确指出“我们必须重新评估激进个人自由带来的危害”（reevaluate the harm of radical, individual freedom）。A项中 reexamine 对应 reevaluate，detrimental effects 对应 harm，属于精准同义改写。", "trapNote": "B项“对失去挚爱不以为意”源自第二段学生用来逃避现实的借口，属于作者批评的对象而非建议；C、D两项涉及的“混乱动荡”和“障碍”均被作者视为阻碍友谊的现实因素，并非核心呼吁。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is American society's assumption of personal achievement?", "options": ["It is to be duly celebrated and highly commended.", "It is a sure way to fulfill a person's dream.", "It revolves around an individualistic culture.", "It reflects a person's exceptional endeavor."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Society tends to celebrate personal achievement and commend it based on the assumption that winning or succeeding is a consequence of working harder than the next person.", "explanation": "定位第五段第二句。题干问美国社会对个人成就的“假设（assumption）”是什么。原文指出，社会之所以颂扬个人成就，是基于这样一种假设：获胜或成功是“比其他人更努力工作的结果”（a consequence of working harder than the next person）。D项“反映了一个人非凡的努力（exceptional endeavor）”精准概括了这一核心假设，故入选。", "trapNote": "A项“应被充分庆祝和高度赞扬”描述的是社会对待个人成就的外在态度，而非题干所问的“假设”；C项“围绕个人主义文化”是原文的文化背景描述，并非对成就成因的预设。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is preached in many success stories?", "options": ["Attaching importance to academic gains on the road to success.", "Investing one's time in work instead of connecting with friends.", "Trying to strengthen friendships in one's pursuit of personal success.", "Excelling in academic performance to get into a prestigious college."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Invest time in your relationships? Invest time in your work instead.", "explanation": "定位第六段。题干问许多成功故事中宣扬的内容。原文先提及高中时听到的“别担心失去友谊，专注学习”的论调，指出“它在许多成功故事中被宣扬”，随后用励志演讲者的话具体阐释：花时间陪朋友就是浪费本可用于取得成就的时间，“与其把时间花在人际关系上，不如投入到工作中”（Invest time in your work instead）。这与B项高度吻合。", "trapNote": "A项“在成功路上重视学业收获”与D项“在学业上表现优异以进入名校”均过度放大了作者高中时的个人听闻，以偏概全；C项“在追求成功时努力巩固友谊”与成功故事的宣扬内容恰好相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we infer from the passage regarding the pursuit of success?", "options": ["No one can succeed without pushing limits.", "No one can afford to neglect close friends.", "Collectivism is superior to individualism.", "Success experts often lead people to ruin."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "We cannot be complacent with losing friendships because they are our anchors.", "explanation": "定位第八段首句并结合第九段主旨。题干要求推断关于追求成功的正确认知。作者在第八段明确警示“我们不能对失去友谊感到满足，因为它们是我们的锚”，并在末段强调“在追逐目标的路上有人支持和爱你远比任何最终结果都重要”。由此可合理推断，在追求成功时，任何人都承担不起忽视亲密朋友的代价（No one can afford to neglect close friends）。", "trapNote": "C项“集体主义优于个人主义”属于过度引申，原文仅在第四段举例提及医疗保健，并未将两种主义作全面优劣比较；D项“成功专家常把人引向毁灭”程度过重，原文仅指出其观点有误。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 欣然接受，容忍，满足于（常指在未察觉问题的情况下自满）", "note": "六级高频贬义/警示动词；文中两次出现 be complacent to/with，意为“对失去朋友这一结局麻木/坦然接受”。", "word": "complacent"}, {"gloss": "v. 崇拜，盲目推崇，把……当作偶像", "note": "由 idol（偶像）+ -ize 构成；文中指社会盲目崇拜“在成功路上失去朋友”的观念。", "word": "idolize"}, {"gloss": "v. 对……不以为意，耸肩置之不理", "note": "熟词僻义及常用短语；shrug off losing people 指轻描淡写地把失去挚友当作理所当然。", "word": "shrug off"}, {"gloss": "n. 混乱，动荡，骚动", "note": "与 chaos 并列使用，形容日常生活伴随的永无止境的纷扰与动荡。", "word": "turmoil"}, {"gloss": "adj. 激进的，根本的，彻底的", "note": "文中 radical individualism / radical, individual freedom 指将个人置于集体之上的极端个人主义。", "word": "radical"}, {"gloss": "v. 培育，培养，促进（关系、情感等）", "note": "foster healthy relationships 是常见高分搭配，意为“培育健康的人际关系”。", "word": "foster"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Society tends to celebrate personal achievement and commend it based on the assumption that winning or succeeding is a consequence of working harder than the next person.", "point": "注意区分主句谓语动作（celebrate/commend）与 based on the assumption that... 所引出的同位语从句内容，后者常作为细节题的设题核心。", "structure": "主句（Society tends to celebrate... and commend it）+ 过去分词短语作方式状语（based on the assumption）+ that 引导的同位语从句（that winning or succeeding is...）", "zh": "社会倾向于颂扬并赞美个人成就，而这是基于这样一种假设：获胜或成功是比别人更努力工作的结果。"}, {"en": "But contrary to all the self-proclaimed success experts, doing it alone does not make you more successful or any better than someone who achieved it with the help of others.", "point": "动名词短语 doing it alone 作主语，结尾处 who 引导的定语从句中的 achieved it 回指成功这件事，形成“独自成功”与“借力成功”的对比论证。", "structure": "转折连词（But）+ 介词短语作状语（contrary to...）+ 动名词作主语（doing it alone）+ 否定谓语及比较结构（does not make you more successful or any better than...）+ who 引导的定语从句", "zh": "但与所有那些自封的成功专家所说的相反，单打独斗并不会让你比在他人帮助下取得成功的人更成功或更优秀。"}, {"en": "Although we may be living in a society that treasures the independent pursuit of achievement, having people to support and love you on the way is far more important than any end result.", "point": "让步状语从句中嵌套定语从句，主句采用动名词复合结构（having people to support and love you）作主语，点明全文中心主旨。", "structure": "Although 引导让步状语从句（内部含 that 引导的定语从句修饰 society）+ 动名词短语作主句主语（having people to support and love you on the way）+ 比较级表语结构", "zh": "尽管我们可能生活在一个珍视独立追求成就的社会中，但在这条路上有人支持和爱你远比任何最终结果都重要得多。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "对激进自由“危害”的评估建议，动词与名词分别完成同义转换。", "option": "Reexamine its detrimental effects.", "original": "reevaluate the harm of radical, individual freedom"}, {"note": "社会认为成功源于“比别人更努力”，抽象概括为“非凡的努力”。", "option": "It reflects a person's exceptional endeavor.", "original": "winning or succeeding is a consequence of working harder than the next person"}, {"note": "把时间投入工作而非人际关系，将 relationships 改写为 connecting with friends。", "option": "Investing one's time in work instead of connecting with friends.", "original": "Invest time in your relationships? Invest time in your work instead."}, {"note": "“不能对失去友谊感到自满，因为它们是我们的锚”，推断为“承担不起忽视挚友的代价”。", "option": "No one can afford to neglect close friends.", "original": "We cannot be complacent with losing friendships because they are our anchors."}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202512-s1-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2025.12", "examSet": "2025.12 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2025.12 六级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "正视历史与不公，传承金博士公平遗志", "subtitle": "以真实对话与共同行动弥合分歧，推动种族与教育公平", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["During his acceptance speech for the Nobel Peace Prize, Martin Luther King Jr. said, \"I believe that unarmed truth and unconditional love will have the final word in reality.\"", "More than five decades later, our society is still struggling to separate truth from fantasy, fact from fiction. From disputes over the climate change to debates about how slavery is taught, America is at a crossroads. And the battle for equity is at the heart of these vital conversations.", "Study after study shows that inequity has had appalling consequences. A 2020 report by Citi indicated that \"Black students could have increased their lifetime incomes $90 – $113 billion\" if equity issues related to higher education had been adequately addressed over the past two decades.", "This statistic represents a flood of issues we've failed to confront as a nation. It also highlights one truth: We're missing out on valuable opportunities to bridge the differences that divide us. However, by honoring King's legacy, we can get our country back on the path toward true equity.", "Students — and adults for that matter — simply cannot understand the conflicts we have today without understanding what caused them in the first place. That means we have a responsibility to help them make connections between US history and current events. It also means giving them the tools they need to address inequity and bias in their own lives. Adherence to these principles, along with a commitment to truthful dialogue, can help every student better appreciate how far we've come and more clearly see the roads we have yet to travel.", "With more truthful analysis of the need for more qualified, diverse educators, we can improve our recruiting, training, and retention strategies for schools across the country.", "Unfortunately, our deeply rooted divisions are delaying these advancements. A recent survey found that 77 percent of Americans believe the nation is \"more divided than ever before\". But reports of increased polarization shouldn't persuade us to look away from one another. Instead, they should compel us to address our shared issues head-on.", "We are not, as some would suggest, living in a \"post-racial society\". We simply cannot afford to keep our heads buried in the sand when it comes to racial inequity. Unless we get honest about intolerance, bias, and how these social diseases impact the ways we treat one another, injustice will continue to haunt us. But our children and our grandchildren deserve better.", "On this Martin Luther King Day and beyond, let's commit to working together to disrupt the status quo. Let's continue to build a better, more inclusive nation; and in the words of Martin Luther King Jr., \"A society at peace with itself, a society that can live with its conscience.\""], "translations": ["在诺贝尔和平奖获奖感言中，小马丁·路德·金说：“我相信，手无寸铁的真理和无条件的爱在现实中终将获胜。”", "五十多年后，我们的社会仍在努力区分真实与幻想、事实与虚构。从关于气候变化的争论到关于如何教授奴隶制的辩论，美国正处于十字路口。而公平之战正是这些重要对话的核心。", "一项又一项研究表明，不公平已经造成了骇人的后果。花旗集团2020年的一份报告指出，“如果过去二十年与高等教育相关的公平问题得到充分解决，黑人学生本可以增加900亿至1130亿美元的终身收入”。", "这一统计数据代表着我们作为一个国家未能直面的大量问题。它也凸显了一个真相：我们正在错失弥合分歧的宝贵机会。然而，通过传承马丁·路德·金的遗志，我们可以让国家重回通往真正公平的道路。", "学生——以及成年人——如果不理解最初导致冲突的原因，就根本无法理解我们今天面临的冲突。这意味着我们有责任帮助他们在美国历史与时事之间建立联系。这也意味着要给他们提供在自己生活中应对不公平和偏见所需的工具。遵循这些原则，加上对真实对话的承诺，可以帮助每个学生更好地认识到我们已经走了多远，并更清楚地看到我们尚未踏上的道路。", "通过更真实地分析对更多合格、多元化教育工作者的需求，我们可以改进全国各地学校的招聘、培训和留用策略。", "不幸的是，我们根深蒂固的分歧正在延缓这些进步。最近的一项调查发现，77%的美国人认为国家“比以往任何时候都更加分裂”。但关于两极分化加剧的报道不应说服我们将目光从彼此身上移开。相反，它们应该促使我们正面应对我们共同的问题。", "正如一些人所暗示的，我们并非生活在一个“后种族社会”。在种族不平等问题上，我们根本无法继续将头埋在沙子里。除非我们诚实面对不宽容、偏见，以及这些社会疾病如何影响我们彼此对待的方式，否则不公正将继续困扰我们。但我们的子孙后代应该得到更好的未来。", "在这个马丁·路德·金日以及之后的日子里，让我们致力于共同努力打破现状。让我们继续建设一个更美好、更包容的国家；用小马丁·路德·金的话说，“一个与自身和平相处的社会，一个能够心安理得的社会。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the author think about today's America?", "options": ["It is struggling to transform fiction into reality.", "It has been the focus of many vital conversations.", "It still has a long way to go before equity can be truly realized.", "It has got to a point where people disagree on nearly every issue."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "From disputes over the climate change to debates about how slavery is taught, America is at a crossroads. And the battle for equity is at the heart of these vital conversations.", "explanation": "定位第二段。题干问作者对当今美国的看法。原文指出，五十多年后的今天，美国社会仍在艰难分辨真假与事实，从气候变化到奴隶制教学争论不断，“美国正处于十字路口，而公平之战正是这些重要对话的核心”；结合第四、五段提及“重回真正公平的道路”与“尚未踏上的路”，可见美国要真正实现公平仍任重道远，与C项完全吻合。", "trapNote": "A项“正努力将虚构转化为现实”曲解了原文“separate truth from fantasy, fact from fiction（区分真实与幻想、事实与虚构）”；D项“几乎在所有问题上都存在分歧”过于绝对，属过度夸大。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about black students in the past 20 years?", "options": ["They have been unfairly treated regarding higher education.", "They have been battling hard to address equity issues.", "They have boosted their lifetime incomes by billions of dollars.", "They have come to see the consequences of racial discrimination."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "A 2020 report by Citi indicated that \"Black students could have increased their lifetime incomes $90 – $113 billion\" if equity issues related to higher education had been adequately addressed over the past two decades.", "explanation": "定位第三段第二句。题干问过去二十年黑人学生的情况。花旗集团2020年报告采用与过去事实相反的虚拟语气指出：如果过去二十年与高等教育相关的公平问题得到充分解决（had been adequately addressed），黑人学生本可以增加（could have increased）900亿至1130亿美元的终身收入。这反推出黑人学生在高等教育中遭受了不公平对待，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "C项“使终身收入增加了数百亿美元”将原文的虚拟语气误读为已经发生的既成事实，属于典型时态与语气陷阱；B项“一直努力斗争以解决公平问题”在第三段中并无依据。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How can Americans bridge the differences that divide them?", "options": ["By dealing with the thorny issues confronting them.", "By seizing every chance to enhance racial harmony.", "By continuing to pursue Martin Luther King Jr.'s cause.", "By striving to identify exceedingly valuable opportunities."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "It also highlights one truth: We're missing out on valuable opportunities to bridge the differences that divide us. However, by honoring King's legacy, we can get our country back on the path toward true equity.", "explanation": "定位第四段第二、三句。题干问美国人如何弥合分裂彼此的分歧。原文先点明“我们正在错失弥合分歧（bridge the differences that divide us）的宝贵机会”，紧接着用 However 转折给出方案：“通过传承马丁·路德·金的遗志（by honoring King's legacy），我们可以让国家重回通往真正公平的道路”。C项“继续追随金博士的事业”与之形成精准同义替换。", "trapNote": "A项“处理眼前的棘手问题”与B项“抓住一切机会促进种族和谐”虽有一定积极意味，但未直接对应第四段明确指出的“honoring King's legacy”这一核心路径；D项偏离了解决分歧的重点。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How do most Americans view America as a nation according to a recent survey?", "options": ["It is compelled to address its historical social issues.", "It is delaying advancements toward racial equality.", "It has kept itself from polarization.", "It has become increasingly split."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "A recent survey found that 77 percent of Americans believe the nation is \"more divided than ever before\".", "explanation": "定位第七段第二句。题干问根据近期调查，大多数美国人如何看待美国现状。原文明确引述调查结果：“77%的美国人认为国家‘比以往任何时候都更加分裂’（more divided than ever before）”。77%对应题干中的 most Americans，而D项中的 increasingly split（日益分裂）正是对 more divided than ever before 的地道同义改写。", "trapNote": "B项“正延缓向种族平等迈进”是作者对分歧后果的评价，而非调查中多数美国人的看法；C项“使自己远离两极分化”与第七段所言“两极分化加剧（increased polarization）”语义完全相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author suggest Americans do?", "options": ["Ensure the well-being of their children and grandchildren.", "Make joint efforts to tackle the nation's equity issues.", "Restrain their intolerance and discrimination.", "Restore social order for a harmonious nation."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "On this Martin Luther King Day and beyond, let's commit to working together to disrupt the status quo.", "explanation": "定位第九段首句并综合第七、八段论述。题干问作者建议美国人做什么。作者在结尾明确号召大家“致力于共同努力打破现状（working together to disrupt the status quo），建设更美好、更包容的国家”，这与第七段“正面应对共同问题”及全文呼吁解决社会与种族公平问题的核心主旨一脉相承。B项“共同努力解决国家的公平问题”准确概括了该建议。", "trapNote": "A项“确保子孙后代的福祉”是对第八段末句“我们的子孙后代值得拥有更好的未来”的字面曲解；C项“克制不宽容与歧视”仅触及部分表象，原文呼吁的是诚实面对偏见并共同行动打破现状。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 骇人听闻的，令人震惊的", "note": "常见于社会问题语境，如 appalling consequences 意为“骇人的后果”。", "word": "appalling"}, {"gloss": "n. 极化，两极分化", "note": "由 pole（极）派生，指社会或观点向对立两端严重分裂，常与 division 呼应。", "word": "polarization"}, {"gloss": "v. 强迫，促使，迫使", "note": "常用于 compel sb to do sth 结构，文中与 look away 形成对比，指促使人们直面问题。", "word": "compel"}, {"gloss": "n. 留用，保留，保持", "note": "源于 retain（保留）；在教育与职场语境中，recruiting, training, and retention 指“招聘、培训与留用”。", "word": "retention"}, {"gloss": "n. 现状，既有局面", "note": "拉丁语源固定搭配，disrupt the status quo 意为“打破现状”。", "word": "status quo"}, {"gloss": "n. 不宽容，偏狭（常指对不同种族、观点的排斥）", "note": "由 in- + tolerance 构成，文中与 bias（偏见）并列，被称为社会疾病（social diseases）。", "word": "intolerance"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "A 2020 report by Citi indicated that \"Black students could have increased their lifetime incomes $90 – $113 billion\" if equity issues related to higher education had been adequately addressed over the past two decades.", "point": "混合虚拟语气（对过去事实的假设）是本题第2题的关键考点：从句用 had been addressed，主句用 could have increased，反推出过去二十年并未做到公平对待。", "structure": "主句（A 2020 report by Citi indicated）+ that 引导的宾语从句（内部为虚拟条件句：主句 could have increased... + if 引导与过去事实相反的条件从句）", "zh": "花旗集团2020年的一份报告指出，“如果过去二十年与高等教育相关的公平问题得到充分解决，黑人学生本可以增加900亿至1130亿美元的终身收入”。"}, {"en": "Adherence to these principles, along with a commitment to truthful dialogue, can help every student better appreciate how far we've come and more clearly see the roads we have yet to travel.", "point": "注意主语核心词是抽象名词 Adherence，谓语 help 后接两个并列不带 to 的不定式（appreciate 和 see），结尾定语从句暗示前路依然漫长。", "structure": "名词短语作主语（Adherence to these principles）+ 插入语（along with...）+ 谓语（can help every student）+ 并列宾语补足语（better appreciate... and more clearly see...，各自后接从句）", "zh": "遵循这些原则，加上对真实对话的承诺，可以帮助每个学生更好地认识到我们已经走了多远，并更清楚地看到我们尚未踏上的道路。"}, {"en": "Unless we get honest about intolerance, bias, and how these social diseases impact the ways we treat one another, injustice will continue to haunt us.", "point": "Unless 相当于 if... not...；about 后接三个并列宾语（两个名词加一个 how 从句），句尾用 haunt（萦绕、困扰）形象传达不公的长期危害。", "structure": "Unless 引导条件状语从句（about 后并列接名词与 how 引导的宾语从句，ways 后省去关系词的定语从句）+ 主句（injustice will continue to haunt us）", "zh": "除非我们诚实面对不宽容、偏见，以及这些社会疾病如何影响我们彼此对待的方式，否则不公正将继续困扰我们。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "虚拟条件句反推过去二十年黑人学生在高等教育上遭到不公对待。", "option": "They have been unfairly treated regarding higher education.", "original": "if equity issues related to higher education had been adequately addressed over the past two decades"}, {"note": "传承金博士的遗志，即继续追随与践行其未竟的事业。", "option": "By continuing to pursue Martin Luther King Jr.'s cause.", "original": "by honoring King's legacy"}, {"note": "77%的美国人认为国家“比以往任何时候都更加分裂”，即“日益分裂”。", "option": "It has become increasingly split.", "original": "77 percent of Americans believe the nation is \"more divided than ever before\""}, {"note": "共同努力打破现状、正面应对共同问题，概括为“合力解决公平问题”。", "option": "Make joint efforts to tackle the nation's equity issues.", "original": "commit to working together to disrupt the status quo"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202506-s1-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2025.06", "examSet": "2025.06 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2025.06 六级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "重审校园缺勤：旷课背后的校外危机", "subtitle": "解析准假缺勤与旷课的差异，呼吁将资源投向困境儿童", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 448, "paragraphs": ["Nationally, one in six children miss 15 or more days of school in a year. Education officials have deplored all this missed instruction.", "These chronically absent students suffer academically because of all the classroom instruction they miss out on. In 2015, the U.S. secretary of education responded to this crisis, urging communities to support every student to attend every day and be successful in school. His open letter stated that missing 10% of school days in a year for any reason—excused or unexcused—is a primary cause of low academic achievement.", "Worrying about whether children attend school makes sense. After all, if students don't show up, teachers can't teach them.", "But what if America's attendance crisis is about much more than students missing class? What if, instead, it is a reflection of family and community crises these students face—such as being ejected from the family apartment, fearing for their safety in their neighborhood or suffering an illness?", "As social scientists we investigated how excused and unexcused absences relate to children's academic achievement.", "We find that absences excused by a parent do little to harm children's learning. In fact, children with no unexcused absences—but 15 to 18 excused absences—have test scores equal to their peers who have no absences.", "Meanwhile, the average child with even just one unexcused absence does much worse academically than peers with none.", "We believe unexcused absence is a strong signal of the many challenges children and families face, including economic and medical hardships. Unexcused absences can be a powerful signal of how those out-of-school challenges affect children's academic progress.", "Our evidence suggests unexcused absences are problematic, but for a different reason than people often think. Absence from school, and especially unexcused absence, matters mainly as a signal of many crises children and their families may be facing. It matters less as a cause of lower student achievement due to missed instruction.", "How we choose to think of school absences matters for educational policy. School attendance policies typically hold schools and families accountable for the days children miss, regardless of whether they were excused or unexcused absences.", "These policies assume that missing school for any reason harms children academically because they are missing classroom instruction. They also assume that schools will be able to effectively intervene by reducing student absences. We find neither to be the case.", "As a result, these attendance policies end up disproportionately punishing families dealing with out-of-school crises in their lives and pressuring schools who serve them to get students to school more often.", "We instead suggest using unexcused absence from school as a signal to channel resources to the children and families who need them most."], "translations": ["在全国范围内，每六个儿童中就有一个在一年内缺课15天或更多。教育官员对这些错过的课堂教学深表痛惜。", "这些长期缺勤的学生因错过大量课堂教学而在学业上受损。2015年，美国教育部长对这一危机作出回应，敦促各社区支持每位学生每天按时上学并在学校取得成功。他在公开信中指出，无论出于何种原因——无论是准假缺勤还是无故旷课——一年内缺课天数达到总上课天数的10%，都是导致学业成绩低下的主要原因。", "担心儿童是否按时上学是有道理的。毕竟，如果学生不到校，教师就无法教授他们。", "但是，如果美国的出勤危机远不止学生缺课这么简单呢？如果它实际上反映的是这些学生所面临的家庭和社区危机——例如被赶出家门租住的公寓、担心自己在社区的安全或身患疾病，又该如何看待呢？", "作为社会科学家，我们调查了准假缺勤和无故旷课与儿童学业成绩之间的关系。", "我们发现，经家长准假的缺勤对儿童的学习几乎没有什么损害。事实上，没有旷课记录但有15至18次准假缺勤的儿童，其考试成绩与完全没有缺勤的同龄人相当。", "与此同时，哪怕只有一次无故旷课的普通儿童，其学业表现也比没有任何旷课记录的同龄人差得多。", "我们认为，无故旷课是儿童和家庭面临诸多挑战（包括经济和医疗困难）的强烈信号。无故旷课能够有力地反映出这些校外挑战是如何影响儿童学业进步的。", "我们的证据表明，无故旷课确实是个问题，但原因与人们通常认为的不同。缺课，尤其是无故旷课，其重要意义主要在于它是儿童及其家庭可能正在面临多重危机的信号；而它作为因错过教学从而导致学生成绩下降的原因，则没有那么重要。", "我们选择如何看待缺课问题对教育政策至关重要。学校的出勤政策通常要求学校和家庭对儿童缺课的天数负责，无论这些缺勤属于准假缺勤还是无故旷课。", "这些政策假定，无论因何原因缺课，都会因为错过课堂教学而在学业上损害儿童；它们还假定学校能够通过减少学生缺勤来进行有效干预。但我们发现这两种情况均不成立。", "结果，这些出勤政策最终不成比例地惩罚了那些在生活中应对校外危机的家庭，并向服务这些家庭的学校施加压力，迫使它们让学生更频繁地到校。", "相反，我们建议将无故旷课作为一种信号，以便将资源引导并输送给最需要帮助的儿童和家庭。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the U.S. secretary of education say in his open letter?", "options": ["It is of vital importance to respond promptly to the school absence crisis.", "The academic performance of chronically absent students is deplorable.", "Low academic achievement is mainly attributed to school absences.", "The effect of school absences on American education is worrisome."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "His open letter stated that missing 10% of school days in a year for any reason—excused or unexcused—is a primary cause of low academic achievement.", "explanation": "本题考查美国教育部长公开信的内容。定位至第2段末句，信中指出无论何种原因，一年缺课达到10%是导致学业成绩低下的主要原因。选项C中的Low academic achievement直接对应原文low academic achievement，is mainly attributed to同义替换is a primary cause of，school absences概括missing 10% of school days，逻辑完全一致，故C为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项将教育部长对危机作出回应偷换为“及时回应至关重要”；B项将第1段教育官员对缺勤课程痛惜（deplored）嫁接到学生成绩上，属于张冠李戴；D项“令人担忧”在公开信中并未提及。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do the authors find about school absences?", "options": ["Excused school absences have little impact on children's learning.", "There is little difference between unexcused and excused absences.", "Excused absences lead to comparatively better school performance.", "Unexcused absences are a big challenge to both schools and families."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "We find that absences excused by a parent do little to harm children's learning.", "explanation": "本题考查作者关于缺勤的研究发现。定位至第6段首句，作者明确指出由家长准假的缺勤对儿童学习几乎没有伤害，后句进一步用15至18次准假缺勤学生的成绩与零缺勤同伴相当加以佐证。选项A中have little impact on同义替换do little to harm，children's learning原词复现，完美契合原文核心结论，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项与第6、7段对比完全相反，二者影响差异巨大；C项将准假缺勤学生成绩“与零缺勤同伴相当（equal to）”曲解为“相对更好”；D项偏离第6段“发现”的核心，第8段指旷课反映校外挑战。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do the authors believe concerning unexcused school absences?", "options": ["They are likely to cause a decrease in students' academic achievements due to missed instruction.", "They point directly to many of the out-of-school challenges confronting children and their families.", "They are matters the American government typically ignores when formulating educational policies.", "They give a clear signal to children and their families of the crises they are likely to face in the future."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "We believe unexcused absence is a strong signal of the many challenges children and families face, including economic and medical hardships. Unexcused absences can be a powerful signal of how those out-of-school challenges affect children's academic progress.", "explanation": "本题考查作者对无故旷课的看法。定位至第8段，作者指出无故旷课是儿童及家庭面临经济、医疗等诸多挑战的强烈信号，有力反映校外挑战如何影响学业进步。选项B中的point directly to对应is a strong/powerful signal of，out-of-school challenges confronting children and their families同义复现原文表述，故B为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项是第9段中“人们通常认为的错误原因”，作者明确认为旷课作为直接导致成绩下降的原因并不重要；D项将儿童和家庭当前“正在面临（face）”的挑战篡改为“未来可能面临”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the assumption underlying education policies in the U.S.?", "options": ["Children's academic performance depends on reducing the number of absences.", "Schools can boost children's academic performance by effective intervention.", "Schools as well as families should be held responsible for out-of-school crises.", "Children's academic performance is closely related to the quality of instruction."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 11, "evidenceQuote": "These policies assume that missing school for any reason harms children academically because they are missing classroom instruction. They also assume that schools will be able to effectively intervene by reducing student absences.", "explanation": "本题考查美国教育政策背后的假设。定位至第11段前两句，现有出勤政策有两个假设：其一，任何缺课都会因错过课堂教学而损害学业；其二，学校能够通过减少学生缺勤来进行有效干预。选项B准确概括了第二个假设，by effective intervention对应effectively intervene，boost children's academic performance呼应减少学业损害，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项“学业表现取决于减少缺勤次数”把政策假定的因果绝对化，忽略了“课堂教学”前提；C项将第10段政策让学校和家庭“对缺课天数负责”偷换为“对校外危机负责”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do the authors suggest doing regarding school absences?", "options": ["Identifying their underlying causes.", "Reframing school attendance policies.", "Directing resources to helping needy children.", "Pressuring schools to reduce unexcused ones."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 13, "evidenceQuote": "We instead suggest using unexcused absence from school as a signal to channel resources to the children and families who need them most.", "explanation": "本题考查作者针对学校缺勤问题提出的建议。定位至尾段（第13段），作者明确建议把无故旷课作为信号，将资源引导并输送给最需要帮助的儿童和家庭。选项C中的Directing resources to精准同义替换channel resources to，helping needy children对应the children and families who need them most，故C为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“识别潜在原因”与B项“重塑出勤政策”均属过度引申，原文尾段提出了具体的行动指向（引导资源）；D项“向学校施压以减少缺勤”正是第12段作者所批评的现行政策弊端。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 痛惜，谴责，对……深感遗憾", "note": "文中教育官员对学生错过的课程表示遗憾（have deplored），是表达负面态度的重要动词。", "word": "deplore"}, {"gloss": "adv. 长期地，习惯性地", "note": "文中chronically absent指“长期缺勤的”，区别于偶尔缺席，常用于描述持续性问题。", "word": "chronically"}, {"gloss": "adj. 未经准假的，无故的", "note": "与excused（准假的）构成核心对比概念，unexcused absence在文中特指无故旷课。", "word": "unexcused"}, {"gloss": "adv. 不成比例地，过度地", "note": "前缀dis-+proportion+ate+ly，在文中说明严苛的出勤政策对困境家庭造成了过重且不公的惩罚。", "word": "disproportionately"}, {"gloss": "v. 引导，输送（资源、精力等）", "note": "熟词僻义：除名词“渠道”外，此处作动词表示将资源定向输送给最需要的群体。", "word": "channel"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "His open letter stated that missing 10% of school days in a year for any reason—excused or unexcused—is a primary cause of low academic achievement.", "point": "动名词短语作主语与双破折号插入语的识读", "structure": "主句(His open letter stated) + that引导的宾语从句，其中动名词短语(missing 10% of school days in a year for any reason)作主语，双破折号插入语(excused or unexcused)补充说明reason，is...作系表结构。", "zh": "他在公开信中指出，无论出于何种原因——无论是准假缺勤还是无故旷课——一年内缺课天数达到10%，都是导致学业成绩低下的主要原因。"}, {"en": "But what if America's attendance crisis is about much more than students missing class? What if, instead, it is a reflection of family and community crises these students face—such as being ejected from the family apartment, fearing for their safety in their neighborhood or suffering an illness?", "point": "What if设问句式与省略引导词的定语从句", "structure": "连续两个What if引导的假设问句；第二句中these students face为省略关系代词that/which的定语从句修饰crises，破折号后such as引出三个并列的动名词短语作同位语举例说明。", "zh": "但是，如果美国的出勤危机远不止学生缺课这么简单呢？如果它实际上反映的是这些学生所面临的家庭和社区危机——例如被赶出家庭租住的公寓、担心社区安全或身患疾病，又该如何呢？"}, {"en": "As a result, these attendance policies end up disproportionately punishing families dealing with out-of-school crises in their lives and pressuring schools who serve them to get students to school more often.", "point": "end up doing并列结构与多重后置修饰语", "structure": "主干为these attendance policies end up punishing families and pressuring schools；dealing with...作后置定语修饰families；who serve them为定语从句修饰schools；不定式短语to get...作宾语补足语。", "zh": "结果，这些出勤政策最终不成比例地惩罚了那些在生活中应对校外危机的家庭，并向服务这些家庭的学校施压，要求它们让学生更频繁地到校。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "原因与结果视角互换：is a primary cause of（是……的主要原因）对应is mainly attributed to（主要归因于）", "option": "Low academic achievement is mainly attributed to school absences", "original": "is a primary cause of low academic achievement"}, {"note": "程度否定同义替换：do little to harm（几乎不损害）对应have little impact on（几乎没有影响）", "option": "have little impact on children's learning", "original": "do little to harm children's learning"}, {"note": "主被动与动词化转换：is a strong signal of替换为point directly to，face替换为confronting", "option": "point directly to many of the out-of-school challenges confronting children and their families", "original": "is a strong signal of the many challenges children and families face"}, {"note": "词性转换与因果推演：effectively intervene（副词+动词）替换为by effective intervention（介词+形容词+名词）", "option": "Schools can boost children's academic performance by effective intervention", "original": "schools will be able to effectively intervene by reducing student absences"}, {"note": "核心动词与定语从句压缩：channel resources to替换为Directing resources to，who need them most压缩为needy", "option": "Directing resources to helping needy children", "original": "channel resources to the children and families who need them most"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202506-s1-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2025.06", "examSet": "2025.06 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2025.06 六级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "追随激情原则的代价：过劳与社会不平等", "subtitle": "反思“追随激情”职业观如何加剧职场过劳、雇主剥削与阶层不平等", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 458, "paragraphs": ["After earning a bachelor's degree, I was determined to do what I love. I headed straight to graduate school to investigate the social problems that fascinated me.", "For almost a decade, I told everyone I encountered that they should do the same. \"Follow your passion,\" I counseled. \"You can figure out the employment stuff later.\"", "It wasn't until I began to research this widely accepted career advice that I understood how problematic it really was.", "As a sociologist, I interviewed college students and professional workers to learn what it really meant to pursue their dreams, which I will refer to here as the passion principle. I was stunned by what I found out about this principle in the research for my new book.", "Surveys show the American public has long held the passion principle in high regard as a career decision-making priority. And its popularity is even stronger among those facing job instability.", "Advocates of the passion principle found it compelling because they believed that following one's passion can provide workers with both the motivation necessary to work hard and a place to find fulfillment.", "Yet, what I found is that following one's passion does not necessarily lead to fulfillment, but is one of the most powerful cultural forces perpetuating overwork. I also found that promoting the pursuit of one's passion helps perpetuate social inequalities due to the fact that not everyone has the same economic resources to allow them to pursue their passion with ease.", "While the passion principle is broadly popular, not everyone has the necessary resources to turn their passion into a stable, good-paying job. Passion-seekers from wealthy families are better able to wait until a job they are passionate about comes along without worrying about student loans in the meantime. They are also better situated to take unpaid internships to get their foot in the door while their parents pay their rent. And they often have access to parents' social networks to help them find jobs. Surveys revealed that working-class and first-generation college graduates, regardless of their career field, are more likely than their wealthier peers to end up in low-paying unskilled jobs when they pursue their passion.", "Colleges, workplaces and career counselors who promote the \"follow your passion\" path for everyone, without leveling the playing field, help perpetuate socioeconomic inequalities among career aspirants.", "It's not just well-off passion-seekers who benefit from the passion principle. Employers of passionate workers do, too. Potential employers showed greater interest in passionate applicants in part because they believed the applicants would work hard at their jobs without expecting an increase in pay. They even sacrifice a good salary, job stability and leisure time to work in a job they love."], "translations": ["获得学士学位后，我决心去做自己热爱的事情。我直接进入研究生院，去研究那些令我着迷的社会问题。", "在近十年的时间里，我告诉自己遇到的每一个人，他们也应该这样做。“追随你的激情，”我建议道，“就业方面的事情你可以之后再解决。”", "直到我开始研究这条被广泛接受的职业建议时，我才明白它实际上有多么成问题。", "作为一名社会学家，我采访了大学生和职场人士，以了解追寻梦想的真正含义——我在此将其称为“激情原则”。在为我的新书开展研究时，我对这一原则的调查发现感到震惊。", "调查显示，长期以来，美国公众一直高度推崇激情原则，将其视为职业决策的首要考量因素。而且它在那些面临工作不稳定的人群中更受欢迎。", "激情原则的倡导者认为它很有说服力，因为他们相信追随自己的激情既能为劳动者提供努力工作所需的动力，也能为他们提供寻找成就感的场所。", "然而，我发现追随自己的激情并不一定能带来成就感，反而是使过度劳累长期延续的最强大的文化力量之一。我还发现，提倡追寻激情有助于使社会不平等长期存在，因为并非每个人都拥有相同的经济资源来让他们轻松地追寻自己的激情。", "虽然激情原则广受欢迎，但并非每个人都拥有必要的资源将自己的激情转化为稳定、高薪的工作。来自富裕家庭的激情追寻者更有能力等待他们热爱的工作出现，而不必在此期间担心学生贷款。他们也更有条件在父母支付房租的同时，接受无薪实习以获得入行机会。而且他们通常还能利用父母的社交网络来帮助自己找工作。调查显示，工人阶级和第一代大学毕业生无论身处哪个职业领域，在追寻激情时都比更富裕的同龄人更有可能最终从事低薪的非技术性工作。", "大学、工作场所和职业顾问如果不先创造公平的竞争环境，就向所有人推广“追随你的激情”这条道路，这实际上助长了求职者之间社会经济不平等的长期延续。", "从激情原则中获益的不仅仅是家境富裕的激情追寻者，雇佣充满激情员工的雇主也同样从中受益。潜在雇主对充满激情的求职者表现出更大的兴趣，部分原因在于他们相信这些求职者会在工作中努力付出而不指望加薪。这些员工甚至会为了从事自己热爱的工作而牺牲丰厚的薪水、工作稳定性和闲暇时间。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What did the author advise people do for almost a decade?", "options": ["Figure out what is the most fascinating job.", "Follow widely accepted career counsel.", "Pursue their careers with passion.", "Do whatever they are zealous for."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "For almost a decade, I told everyone I encountered that they should do the same. \"Follow your passion,\" I counseled. \"You can figure out the employment stuff later.\"", "explanation": "本题考查作者近十年来给他人提出的职业建议。定位至第2段，作者建议遇到的每个人“追随你的激情”，与第1段开头“决心去做自己热爱的事情（do what I love）”相呼应，也就是鼓励大家投身于自己真正热爱和热衷的事。选项D中的zealous for意为“对……充满热忱”，准确同义替换原文的passion与love，故D为正确答案。", "trapNote": "C项具有很强干扰性，“充满激情地追求职业”偏离了“先追随热爱之事、就业以后再说”的原意；B项将第3段作者后来研究的“普遍建议”误作作者给出的建议。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How did the author feel about the passion principle through his research?", "options": ["He was astonished by its consequences.", "He was further convinced of its soundness.", "He was actually right to follow it through.", "He was struck by its broad popularity."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "I was stunned by what I found out about this principle in the research for my new book.", "explanation": "本题考查作者在研究后对“激情原则”的感受。定位至第4段末句，作者明确表示自己在为新书开展研究时，对这一原则的发现感到震惊（stunned），第7至10段具体揭示了其引发过度劳累与加剧社会不平等的负面后果。选项A中的was astonished by同义替换was stunned by，its consequences概括其研究发现的后果，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项和C项均与第3段作者意识到该建议“极具问题（how problematic）”的态度相反；D项将第4段的“感到震惊”嫁接到第5段的“广泛受欢迎（popularity）”上，属于跨段错配。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is important to turning one's passion into a stable, good-paying job?", "options": ["Willingness to take unpaid internships and low-paying jobs.", "Full academic preparedness and sound career counseling.", "Hard work and sacrifice of leisure time.", "Financial backing and social connections."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "While the passion principle is broadly popular, not everyone has the necessary resources to turn their passion into a stable, good-paying job. Passion-seekers from wealthy families are better able to wait until a job they are passionate about comes along without worrying about student loans in the meantime. They are also better situated to take unpaid internships to get their foot in the door while their parents pay their rent. And they often have access to parents' social networks to help them find jobs.", "explanation": "本题考查将激情转化为稳定高薪工作的重要条件。定位至第8段，作者指出并非人人拥有转化激情的必要资源，随后列举了富裕家庭求职者的优势：不必担心助学贷款、父母支付房租以支持无薪实习（经济支持），以及利用父母的社交网络找工作（人脉关系）。选项D中的Financial backing and social connections精准概括了这两大关键条件，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项将富裕学生依靠父母付房租才能负担“无薪实习”曲解为个人“愿意”接受无薪和低薪工作；C项“努力工作和牺牲闲暇”是第10段员工为爱妥协的表现，并非获得高薪稳定工作的条件。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What happens when everyone is encouraged to follow their passion?", "options": ["Many more career aspirants end up unemployed.", "People are less concerned with socioeconomic inequality.", "Socioeconomic inequality is likely to persist.", "Career counselors are going to lose credibility."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "Colleges, workplaces and career counselors who promote the \"follow your passion\" path for everyone, without leveling the playing field, help perpetuate socioeconomic inequalities among career aspirants.", "explanation": "本题考查鼓励所有人追随激情会带来什么后果。定位至第9段（及第7段末句），作者指出大学、职场和职业顾问若在不创造公平竞争环境的情况下向所有人推广“追随激情”之路，会促使求职者之间的社会经济不平等长期延续（perpetuate）。选项C中的is likely to persist精准同义替换help perpetuate，故C为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“更多求职者失业”属于无中生有，第8段仅说明弱势群体更可能沦为低薪非技术工；B项将“加剧并延续社会经济不平等”篡改为“人们不太关心不平等”，逻辑曲解。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the author say about employers of passionate workers?", "options": ["They provide these workers with job stability and a good salary.", "They exploit these workers' passion to benefit themselves.", "They level the playing field for these workers to reach their goals.", "They encourage these workers to realize their aspirations."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 10, "evidenceQuote": "Employers of passionate workers do, too. Potential employers showed greater interest in passionate applicants in part because they believed the applicants would work hard at their jobs without expecting an increase in pay. They even sacrifice a good salary, job stability and leisure time to work in a job they love.", "explanation": "本题考查作者对雇佣激情员工的雇主的看法。定位至第10段，作者指出不仅富裕求职者受益，雇主也从激情原则中获益：雇主更青睐充满激情的应聘者，因为他们相信这类人会努力工作却不指望加薪，甚至愿意牺牲高薪、稳定性和闲暇时间。由此可知，雇主实际上是利用了员工的激情来为自身谋利（exploit... to benefit themselves），故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项与原文“员工为热爱而牺牲高薪和工作稳定性”完全相悖；C项将第9段“未创造公平竞争环境（without leveling the playing field）”的主体和否定意味同时篡改。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 劝告，建议；n. 忠告", "note": "第2段作动词用（I counseled），第9段派生词career counselor指“职业顾问”。", "word": "counsel"}, {"gloss": "adj. 有说服力的，令人信服的", "note": "文中指激情原则的倡导者认为这一理念很有说服力（found it compelling）。", "word": "compelling"}, {"gloss": "v. 使永久化，使长期存在（多指负面事物）", "note": "本文高频核心词，连续出现于第7、9段（perpetuate overwork / social inequalities）。", "word": "perpetuate"}, {"gloss": "n. 有抱负者，立志追求者", "note": "第9段career aspirants指“有志于职场发展的求职者”，源于动词aspire（渴望、立志）。", "word": "aspirant"}, {"gloss": "phr. 创造公平的竞争环境", "note": "常见习语搭配，字面意为“把运动场地铲平”，比喻消除起跑线差异、提供公平竞争条件。", "word": "level the playing field"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "I also found that promoting the pursuit of one's passion helps perpetuate social inequalities due to the fact that not everyone has the same economic resources to allow them to pursue their passion with ease.", "point": "that宾语从句嵌套due to the fact that原因状语从句", "structure": "主句(I also found) + that引导的宾语从句，其中动名词短语(promoting the pursuit of one's passion)作主语；due to the fact that引导原因状语从句，包含不定式短语(to allow them to pursue...)作目的/结果修饰。", "zh": "我还发现，提倡追寻激情有助于使社会不平等长期存在，因为并非每个人都拥有相同的经济资源来让他们轻松地追寻自己的激情。"}, {"en": "Surveys revealed that working-class and first-generation college graduates, regardless of their career field, are more likely than their wealthier peers to end up in low-paying unskilled jobs when they pursue their passion.", "point": "插入语隔断主谓与be more likely than比较结构", "structure": "Surveys revealed后接that引导的宾语从句；主语为working-class and first-generation college graduates，插入语regardless of their career field作让步状语，谓语部分包含be more likely than... to do结构，when引导时间状语从句。", "zh": "调查显示，工人阶级和第一代大学毕业生无论身处哪个职业领域，在追寻激情时都比更富裕的同龄人更有可能最终从事低薪的非技术性工作。"}, {"en": "Colleges, workplaces and career counselors who promote the \"follow your passion\" path for everyone, without leveling the playing field, help perpetuate socioeconomic inequalities among career aspirants.", "point": "长定语从句加条件状语插入语的句式拆解", "structure": "主语(Colleges, workplaces and career counselors)后接who引导的限制性定语从句；逗号隔开的介词短语without leveling the playing field作伴随条件状语；主句谓语为help perpetuate。", "zh": "大学、工作场所和职业顾问如果不先创造公平的竞争环境，就向所有人推广“追随你的激情”这条道路，这实际上助长了求职者之间社会经济不平等的长期延续。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "词义同义替换：passion（激情、热爱）替换为zealous for（对……充满热忱）", "option": "Do whatever they are zealous for", "original": "Follow your passion"}, {"note": "情绪词同义替换：stunned（震惊的）替换为astonished，what I found out概括为its consequences", "option": "He was astonished by its consequences", "original": "I was stunned by what I found out about this principle"}, {"note": "具体例证高度概括：助学贷款/付房租概括为Financial backing（经济支持），父母社交网络概括为social connections（人脉关系）", "option": "Financial backing and social connections", "original": "without worrying about student loans... parents pay their rent... access to parents' social networks"}, {"note": "核心动词替换：perpetuate（使长期存在/延续）替换为persist（持续存在）", "option": "Socioeconomic inequality is likely to persist", "original": "help perpetuate socioeconomic inequalities"}, {"note": "客观描述转为批判性概括：雇主因员工无偿加班/放弃加薪而获益，被概括为exploit... to benefit themselves（利用……谋利）", "option": "They exploit these workers' passion to benefit themselves", "original": "Employers of passionate workers do, too... work hard at their jobs without expecting an increase in pay"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202412-s1-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2024.12", "examSet": "2024.12 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2024.12 六级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "恐怖片为何令人愉悦的进化密码", "subtitle": "从进化心理学视角剖析“恐怖悖论”与情绪应对机制", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 453, "paragraphs": ["Imagine you're an alien sent to Earth to document the behaviour of the mammals inhabiting the planet. You stumble into a movie theatre that's showing the latest Hollywood horror film.", "Several dozen humans are gathered together in a dark, undecorated room. They're all staring at a rectangular area on which patterns of light change rapidly.", "They are clearly in a state of high arousal. Their heart rate is elevated, they occasionally glance around nervously, and they sometimes jump collectively in their seats, and emit high-pitched warning calls.", "Eventually, the lights come up and the rectangular screen goes black. The humans stand up and leave the room, chatting and laughing, and showing signs of pleasure.", "Why do these humans voluntarily expose themselves to what appears to be a deeply unpleasant experience? And why do they react so strongly to those patterns of light on a screen?", "I am fascinated with the paradox of horror—the strange fact that many people seek out scary entertainment.", "I think the answer to the puzzle lies in human nature.", "My research suggests that we humans evolved to find pleasure in situations that allow us to experience negative emotions in a safe context. You can see these elements of horror in children's games. Take hide-and-seek for example, which is a simulation of a predator-prey interaction. The kid hides and the adult pretends to be a predator, searching for the child while howling like a dangerous beast.", "This simulation gives the child crucial information about how to avoid becoming prey, and children tend to find that kind of activity deeply satisfying, presumably because it gives them a safe experience of a potentially catastrophic scenario.", "They find it pleasurable, and pleasure is evolution's way of motivating us toward adaptive behaviour.", "Horror is pleasurable to many people because it lets us play with negative emotions and develop coping strategies. We learn what it feels like to be truly afraid, and we learn how to handle negative emotion.", "How, then, does horror work? My research suggests that horror works by exploiting an ancient set of biological defence mechanisms—an evolved fear system, which we share with other animals. But humans are uniquely imaginative, and we use our evolved imagination to travel into virtual worlds that are full of danger.", "There are good reasons for watching a horror film, even if you're not a loyal horror fan. If you make it through the film in one piece, you'll probably experience a strong sense of mastery, a sense that you were able to make it through an appalling experience. Anyway, watching a horror film makes you better at handling your own fear, and who knows when that will become critically relevant?"], "translations": ["想象你是一个被派往地球的外星人，负责记录栖息在这个星球上的哺乳动物的行为。你无意中走进了一家正在放映最新好莱坞恐怖片的电影院。", "几十个人类聚集在一个黑暗、毫无装饰的房间里。他们都盯着一个矩形区域，上面的光影图案快速变化。", "他们显然处于高度兴奋状态。他们的心率升高，偶尔紧张地四处张望，有时会集体从座位上跳起来，并发出高音调的警告叫声。", "最终，灯光亮起，矩形屏幕变黑。人类站起来离开房间，边聊天边笑，并表现出愉悦的迹象。", "为什么这些人类自愿让自己暴露在看似极其不愉快的体验中？为什么他们对屏幕上的那些光影图案反应如此强烈？", "我对恐怖的悖论着迷——许多人寻求惊吓娱乐这一奇怪的事实。", "我认为这个谜题的答案在于人性。", "我的研究表明，人类在进化过程中学会了在安全的环境中体验负面情绪时获得愉悦。你可以在儿童游戏中看到恐怖的这些元素。以捉迷藏为例，这是对捕食者与猎物互动的模拟。孩子躲藏起来，成人假装是捕食者，一边像危险的野兽一样嚎叫，一边寻找孩子。", "这种模拟为孩子提供了关于如何避免成为猎物的关键信息，孩子们往往觉得这类活动非常令人满足，大概是因为它让他们安全地体验了一个可能带来灾难性后果的场景。", "他们觉得它令人愉快，而愉悦是进化激励我们朝向适应性行为的方式。", "恐怖对许多人来说是令人愉快的，因为它让我们玩味负面情绪并发展应对策略。我们学会真正恐惧的感觉是什么，我们学会如何处理负面情绪。", "那么，恐怖是如何起作用的呢？我的研究表明，恐怖通过利用一套古老的生物防御机制起作用——一个我们与其他动物共有的进化而来的恐惧系统。但人类具有独特的想象力，我们利用进化而来的想象力进入充满危险的虚拟世界。", "观看恐怖片有充分的理由，即使你不是忠实的恐怖片爱好者。如果你完好无损地看完这部电影，你可能会体验到强烈的掌控感，一种你能够熬过一次可怕经历的感觉。无论如何，观看恐怖片会让你更善于处理自己的恐惧，谁知道这什么时候会变得至关重要呢？"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The alien finds the audience in the movie theatre clearly in a state of ______.", "options": ["total mindfulness", "extreme excitement", "spiritual elevation", "intense curiosity"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "They are clearly in a state of high arousal.", "explanation": "定位第3段首句“They are clearly in a state of high arousal.”，并结合后文心率升高、紧张张望、惊跳和尖叫等生理反应可知，观众处于高度亢奋的状态。题干中的in a state of原词复现，选项B的extreme excitement精确同义替换原文的high arousal（高度唤醒/极度兴奋），故B为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项total mindfulness（全神贯注/正念）偏离“紧张惊跳”的语境；C项spiritual elevation（精神升华）与D项intense curiosity（强烈好奇）在文中均无依据，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why do many people seek out scary entertainment, according to the author's research?", "options": ["They gain experience in overcoming horror in real life.", "They find joy in going through simulated horrible experiences.", "They have learned from hide-and-seek as kids the thrill involved.", "They have evolved to gain pleasure in escaping life-threatening situations."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "My research suggests that we humans evolved to find pleasure in situations that allow us to experience negative emotions in a safe context.", "explanation": "定位第8段首句“My research suggests that we humans evolved to find pleasure in situations that allow us to experience negative emotions in a safe context.”。研究表明人类进化出在安全情境中体验负面情绪并从中获得愉悦的能力，B项find joy对应find pleasure，simulated horrible experiences对应在安全语境下模拟体验恐怖情绪，准确概括核心原因。", "trapNote": "A项“在现实生活中克服恐怖”与原文的safe context及虚拟模拟相悖；D项“逃离致命危险”曲解原文，原文强调在安全情境中体验而非真实逃生；C项以儿童游戏例子代替普遍进化原因。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do children learn from hide-and-seek?", "options": ["How to avoid falling prey to an attacker.", "How to simulate a predator-prey interaction.", "How to keep themselves from catastrophic errors.", "How to turn a dangerous scenario into a safe one."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "This simulation gives the child crucial information about how to avoid becoming prey, and children tend to find that kind of activity deeply satisfying, presumably because it gives them a safe experience of a potentially catastrophic scenario.", "explanation": "定位第9段首句“This simulation gives the child crucial information about how to avoid becoming prey”。其中This simulation指代第8段提及的儿童捉迷藏游戏，句子明确指出这种模拟让孩子学到如何避免成为猎物。A项how to avoid falling prey to an attacker精准同义替换原文how to avoid becoming prey，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项将游戏本身的性质（模拟捕食互动）偷换为孩子从中“学到的方法”；C项catastrophic errors和D项“把危险场景变安全”均是对原文a safe experience of a potentially catastrophic scenario的曲解。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why is horror gratifying to many people?", "options": ["It reminds them of an ancient set of biological defence mechanisms.", "It triggers their imagination to travel into dangerous virtual worlds.", "It allows them to learn what fear feels like and how to tackle it.", "It activates their evolved fear system and their unique fantasy."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 11, "evidenceQuote": "Horror is pleasurable to many people because it lets us play with negative emotions and develop coping strategies. We learn what it feels like to be truly afraid, and we learn how to handle negative emotion.", "explanation": "定位第11段“Horror is pleasurable to many people because... We learn what it feels like to be truly afraid, and we learn how to handle negative emotion.”。题干gratifying对应原文pleasurable，C项learn what fear feels like and how to tackle it精准对应“了解真正恐惧的感觉并学会处理负面情绪”，故C正确。", "trapNote": "A、B、D三项均拼凑自第12段对“恐怖如何起作用（How does horror work）”的机制说明，而非第11段直接回答“为什么恐怖令人愉悦（gratifying/pleasurable）”的因果表述，属于答非所问。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What will one experience if they watch a horror film through without being hurt?", "options": ["A strong sense of clear relevance.", "A profound sense of good fortune.", "A profound sense of intense relief.", "A strong sense of being in control."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 13, "evidenceQuote": "If you make it through the film in one piece, you'll probably experience a strong sense of mastery, a sense that you were able to make it through an appalling experience.", "explanation": "定位第13段第二句“If you make it through the film in one piece, you'll probably experience a strong sense of mastery”。题干without being hurt同义替换in one piece（安然无恙、完好无损），原文明确指出此时会体验到a strong sense of mastery（强烈的掌控感）。D项being in control准确替换mastery，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项clear relevance歪曲了句末critically relevant（变得至关重要）的语境；B项“侥幸感”和C项“强烈如释重负感”均未提及，属于根据主观常识过度臆测。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 兴奋，唤醒，激发状态", "note": "第3段指观影时心率加快等生理高度唤醒状态，对应题干考点", "word": "arousal"}, {"gloss": "n. 悖论，自相矛盾的现象", "note": "第6段the paradox of horror指人们主动寻求不快甚至恐惧娱乐的矛盾心理", "word": "paradox"}, {"gloss": "n. 模拟，仿真", "note": "第8、9段指捉迷藏等游戏对捕食与被捕食情境的模拟", "word": "simulation"}, {"gloss": "adj. 灾难性的，毁灭性的", "note": "第9段修饰scenario，指在现实中可能致命的灾难性处境", "word": "catastrophic"}, {"gloss": "n. 掌控感，驾驭能力", "note": "第13段指完整看完恐怖片后对自身恐惧情绪的掌控感，对应第5题考点", "word": "mastery"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "My research suggests that we humans evolved to find pleasure in situations that allow us to experience negative emotions in a safe context.", "point": "evolve to do sth.（进化出做某事的能力）；that引导定语从句修饰抽象地点/情境名词situations", "structure": "主句（My research suggests）+ that引导的宾语从句（we humans evolved to find pleasure in situations...）+ that引导的定语从句（修饰situations）", "zh": "我的研究表明，我们人类进化到能够在安全的环境中体验负面情绪并从中获得愉悦。"}, {"en": "This simulation gives the child crucial information about how to avoid becoming prey, and children tend to find that kind of activity deeply satisfying, presumably because it gives them a safe experience of a potentially catastrophic scenario.", "point": "find + 宾语 + 宾补（satisfying）；presumably作副词修饰原因状语从句表示合理推测", "structure": "并列复合句：前半句为双宾语结构（gives the child crucial information），后半句为主谓宾宾补结构（find that kind of activity deeply satisfying）+ presumably because引导的原因状语从句", "zh": "这种模拟为孩子提供了如何避免成为猎物的关键信息，而且孩子们往往觉得这类活动非常令人满足，大概是因为它让他们安全地体验了一个可能带来灾难性后果的场景。"}, {"en": "How, then, does horror work? My research suggests that horror works by exploiting an ancient set of biological defence mechanisms—an evolved fear system, which we share with other animals.", "point": "破折号后名词短语作biological defence mechanisms的同位语，进一步解释概念；share sth. with...（与……共有……）", "structure": "主句（My research suggests）+ that引导的宾语从句 + 破折号同位语（an evolved fear system）+ which引导的非限制性定语从句", "zh": "那么，恐怖是如何起作用的呢？我的研究表明，恐怖通过利用一套古老的生物防御机制——即我们与其他动物共有的进化而来的恐惧系统——来发挥作用。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "arousal作名词表示“兴奋、唤醒状态”，在考题中同义替换为extreme excitement", "option": "extreme excitement", "original": "a state of high arousal"}, {"note": "“在安全语境下体验负面情绪”被概括为“经历模拟的可怕体验”", "option": "going through simulated horrible experiences", "original": "experience negative emotions in a safe context"}, {"note": "becoming prey同义替换为固定搭配falling prey to（成为……的猎物/受害者）", "option": "how to avoid falling prey to an attacker", "original": "how to avoid becoming prey"}, {"note": "handle（处理、应对）在选项中常与tackle、cope with、address互换", "option": "how to tackle it", "original": "how to handle negative emotion"}, {"note": "习语in one piece意为“完好无损地”；mastery（掌控）对应being in control", "option": "without being hurt / a strong sense of being in control", "original": "in one piece / a strong sense of mastery"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202412-s1-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2024.12", "examSet": "2024.12 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2024.12 六级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "现实觉醒与社交滤镜下的容貌焦虑", "subtitle": "解析数字时代社交媒体对女性审美标准与心理健康的双重冲击", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 448, "paragraphs": ["An awakening has been taking place in the physical world against the beauty model that has been dictated to us for years. But in the digital arena, social media determines what is considered beautiful.", "The two opposing struggles are taking place in parallel. In the physical world, the struggle goes against the underlying pressure exerted on women to conform to an unrealistic beauty ideal. As part of the struggle, various media outlets have presented women whose bodies don't correspond to the so-called ideal. All those women who had previously been excluded from the covers of magazines, television series and the public agenda, have become \"legitimate\". At the same time, a group of influencers have begun to upload to social media photos of themselves without makeup, and even photos in which they highlight supposed flaws.", "Technology has reshaped our beauty ideal and is doing a great job communicating that message to the masses. One of the bizarre legacies of the past decade is the popularity of the \"cyborg look\", which illustrates what Americans will look like in 2050.", "The cyborg look spread rapidly. Today, however, the Instagram face has become the new beauty ideal.", "The internalization of accepted beauty norms is much more effective when there is active involvement in the learning process. The active involvement of users is reflected in the gamified(游戏化的) interaction offered by the social media platforms—the ability to like, write a comment, compare, share.", "Once the desired beauty ideal has been internalized, users are given tools or features to change their appearance to suit the accepted beauty ideal such as editing the image, choosing the ideal filter, the right background.", "A survey conducted in the United States revealed that more than 50% filter the images before posting them. And you will not be surprised to hear that the majority of them are women. One of the significant consequences of obsessive filtering is the emerging tendency to treat oneself as an object to be observed and valued, in the same way another person observes and judges from the side.", "The effect of the filters is already far beyond amiable amusement. The filters and the entire game played on the networks affect the mental health of the users. According to a study, apps like Instagram, Snapchat and FaceTune allow users to achieve a level of perfection that was previously only observed in beauty magazines.", "Even though humanity has always cherished beauty, in the last decade our obsession with looks has reached an unprecedented peak. The time spent on social media creates an urge to achieve an impossible beauty ideal so powerful that the only thing that can fix it is not cosmetic intervention, but mental health care."], "translations": ["在现实世界中，一场针对多年来强加给我们的美丽标准的觉醒正在发生。但在数字领域，社交媒体决定着什么被认为是美的。", "两场对立的斗争正在平行进行。在现实世界中，斗争针对的是施加在女性身上、要求她们符合不切实际的美丽理想的潜在压力。作为斗争的一部分，各种媒体平台展示了身材不符合所谓理想的女性。所有那些此前被排除在杂志封面、电视剧和公众议程之外的女性，都变得“合法”了。与此同时，一群网络红人开始在社交媒体上传她们不化妆的照片，甚至突出所谓缺陷的照片。", "技术重塑了我们的美丽理想，并在向大众传达这一信息方面做得很好。过去十年的一个奇异遗产是“赛博格外观”的流行，它展示了2050年美国人的样子。", "赛博格外观迅速传播。然而今天，Instagram脸已经成为新的美丽理想。", "当学习过程中有积极参与时，公认美丽标准的内化会更加有效。用户的积极参与体现在社交媒体平台提供的游戏化互动中——点赞、评论、比较、分享的能力。", "一旦期望的美丽理想被内化，用户就会获得工具或功能来改变自己的外观以适应公认的美丽理想，比如编辑图像、选择理想的滤镜和合适的背景。", "在美国进行的一项调查显示，超过50%的人在发布照片前会进行滤镜处理。你不会惊讶地听说，其中大多数是女性。过度使用滤镜的一个重要后果是出现了将自己视为被观察和评价的对象的新倾向，就像另一个人从旁观察和评判一样。", "滤镜的影响已经远远超出了友善的娱乐。滤镜和网络上玩的整个游戏影响着用户的心理健康。根据一项研究，像Instagram、Snapchat和FaceTune这样的应用程序允许用户达到以前只能在美容杂志上看到的完美程度。", "尽管人类一直珍视美丽，但在过去十年里，我们对外表的痴迷已经达到了前所未有的顶峰。花在社交媒体上的时间创造了一种追求不可能的美丽理想的冲动，这种冲动如此强烈，以至于唯一能修复它的不是美容干预，而是心理健康护理。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about beauty in the digital arena?", "options": ["It dictates the taste of digital media.", "It has been in the making for years.", "It has ushered in a new awakening.", "It is defined by social media."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "But in the digital arena, social media determines what is considered beautiful.", "explanation": "定位第1段第二句“But in the digital arena, social media determines what is considered beautiful.”。原文明确指出在数字领域中，是由社交媒体决定什么才算美。D项It is defined by social media将主动语态转化为被动语态，其中defined对应determines what is considered beautiful，精准契合原文，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项将主被动关系颠倒（原文是社交媒体决定美，而非美主导数字媒体品味）；B项“形成多年”和C项“引领新觉醒”均属于第1段首句对现实世界（physical world）的描述，张冠李戴。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say about beauty in the physical world?", "options": ["Women are under constant pressure to keep up with beauty models.", "Women are encouraged to pursue a beauty ideal that has never existed.", "A fight is going on to remove pressure on women to conform to an absurd beauty ideal.", "Media outlets have begun to present as beauty models trendy women without any makeup."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "In the physical world, the struggle goes against the underlying pressure exerted on women to conform to an unrealistic beauty ideal.", "explanation": "定位第2段第二句“In the physical world, the struggle goes against the underlying pressure exerted on women to conform to an unrealistic beauty ideal.”。该句说明现实世界中的抗争旨在对抗强加于女性、迫使她们迎合不切实际审美标准的潜在压力。C项A fight对应struggle，remove pressure对应goes against the underlying pressure，absurd替换unrealistic，故C正确。", "trapNote": "A项只片面提及女性受压迫，忽略了现实中正在进行的“对抗（struggle）”；D项将网红上传素颜照（upload photos without makeup）与传统媒体展示非理想身材女性的事实混为一谈。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn from the passage about the Instagram face?", "options": ["It is now regarded as the new beauty ideal.", "It is what most women will go after in 2050.", "It is being much talked about on social media.", "It is a perfect illustration of the ultimate beauty."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Today, however, the Instagram face has become the new beauty ideal.", "explanation": "定位第4段第二句“Today, however, the Instagram face has become the new beauty ideal.”。句子直白点明，如今“Instagram脸”已经成为新的审美理想。A项It is now regarded as the new beauty ideal中now对应Today，regarded as the new beauty ideal对应has become the new beauty ideal，属于原意直接再现，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项将第3段“赛博格外观展示了2050年美国人的样子”张冠李戴到Instagram脸上；C项“在社交媒体上被热议”与D项“终极美的完美例证”在文中均未提及，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What has obsessive filtering resulted in?", "options": ["A good many women striving to reach an impossible level of perfection.", "An urge to turn the entire game played on the network to one's advantage.", "A tendency to regard one's body as an object of observation and judgment.", "An increasing number of women filtering their images before uploading them."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "One of the significant consequences of obsessive filtering is the emerging tendency to treat oneself as an object to be observed and valued, in the same way another person observes and judges from the side.", "explanation": "定位第7段第三句“One of the significant consequences of obsessive filtering is the emerging tendency to treat oneself as an object to be observed and valued, in the same way another person observes and judges from the side.”。题干resulted in对应consequences，C项精准概括了“将自己视为被观察和评判对象”的后果，故C正确。", "trapNote": "D项把原因（超过50%的人发布前使用滤镜，且多为女性）错当成过度使用滤镜导致的后果，属于因果倒置；A项虽符合第8、9段语境，但并非第7段对obsessive filtering直接后果的界定。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the author want to emphasize at the end of the passage regarding Americans' obsession with looks?", "options": ["Cosmetic surgery should be made more accessible to the masses.", "Psychological intervention should be introduced to alleviate it.", "Their time spent on social media should be strictly controlled.", "Its root cause should be meticulously examined and analyzed."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "The time spent on social media creates an urge to achieve an impossible beauty ideal so powerful that the only thing that can fix it is not cosmetic intervention, but mental health care.", "explanation": "定位末段尾句“the only thing that can fix it is not cosmetic intervention, but mental health care.”。作者强调，社交媒体引发的病态容貌执念极强，唯一能解决问题的不是美容手段，而是心理健康护理。B项Psychological intervention对应mental health care，alleviate it对应fix it，准确传达作者呼吁心理干预的意图，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项“普及美容手术”与原文not cosmetic intervention完全相反，属正反混淆；C项“严格控制上网时间”和D项“仔细剖析根本原因”均未在尾段提出，属于过度引申。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 顺从，符合，迎合（标准或规范）", "note": "第2段conform to an unrealistic beauty ideal，常考搭配conform to", "word": "conform"}, {"gloss": "n. 内化，吸收（观念或规范）", "note": "第5段指用户将外部审美标准内化为自我认同的过程", "word": "internalization"}, {"gloss": "adj. 强迫性的，过度痴迷的", "note": "第7段obsessive filtering指过度、强迫性地使用美颜滤镜", "word": "obsessive"}, {"gloss": "adj. 温和无害的，友善的", "note": "第8段beyond amiable amusement意为远不止无伤大雅的娱乐消遣", "word": "amiable"}, {"gloss": "n. 干预，介入", "note": "第9段cosmetic intervention（美容干预）与第5题选项psychological intervention构成核心对应", "word": "intervention"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In the physical world, the struggle goes against the underlying pressure exerted on women to conform to an unrealistic beauty ideal.", "point": "exert pressure on sb.（对某人施加压力）；conform to（符合、顺应、迎合）", "structure": "地点状语 + 主句（the struggle goes against the underlying pressure）+ 过去分词短语（exerted on women...）作后置定语修饰pressure", "zh": "在现实世界中，这场抗争针对的是施加在女性身上、要求她们迎合不切实际的审美标准的潜在压力。"}, {"en": "One of the significant consequences of obsessive filtering is the emerging tendency to treat oneself as an object to be observed and valued, in the same way another person observes and judges from the side.", "point": "treat...as...（把……视为……）；to be observed and valued为不定式被动式作object的后置定语", "structure": "主系表结构（One of the consequences is the emerging tendency）+ 不定式作后置定语修饰tendency + in the same way引导方式状语（后接省略that的定语从句）", "zh": "过度使用滤镜的一个重要后果是，人们开始倾向于将自己视为被观察和评价的对象，就像旁观者在一旁打量和评判那样。"}, {"en": "The time spent on social media creates an urge to achieve an impossible beauty ideal so powerful that the only thing that can fix it is not cosmetic intervention, but mental health care.", "point": "so powerful that...修饰前面带有不定式定语的urge；not A, but B（不是A，而是B）凸显作者核心观点", "structure": "主语（The time spent on social media）+ 谓语（creates）+ 宾语（an urge...）+ so...that引导的结果状语从句（含not...but...并列结构）", "zh": "花在社交媒体上的时间催生了一种追求不可能的完美外貌的冲动，这种冲动如此强烈，以至于唯一能治愈它的不是美容手术，而是心理健康护理。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "主动变被动，determines what is considered beautiful被概括为is defined by", "option": "It is defined by social media.", "original": "social media determines what is considered beautiful"}, {"note": "struggle对应fight，goes against对应remove，unrealistic替换为absurd", "option": "A fight is going on to remove pressure...an absurd beauty ideal", "original": "struggle goes against the underlying pressure...an unrealistic beauty ideal"}, {"note": "become...同义替换为is regarded as...", "option": "is now regarded as the new beauty ideal", "original": "has become the new beauty ideal"}, {"note": "动词不定式和从句动作（observed, judges）转化为名词短语of observation and judgment", "option": "regard one's body as an object of observation and judgment", "original": "treat oneself as an object to be observed and valued...observes and judges"}, {"note": "mental health care（心理健康护理）在选项中同义替换为psychological intervention（心理干预）", "option": "Psychological intervention should be introduced to alleviate it", "original": "the only thing that can fix it is...mental health care"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202406-s1-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2024.06", "examSet": "2024.06 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2024.06 六级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "职场安全干预缺失的原因与对策", "subtitle": "剖析职场安全旁观者心理与全员干预机制的构建", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["It is irrefutable that employees know the difference between right and wrong. So why don't more employees intervene when they see someone exhibiting at-risk behavior in the workplace?", "There are a number of factors that influence whether people intervene. First, they need to be able to see a risky situation beginning to unfold. Second, the company's culture needs to make them feel safe to speak up. And third, they need to have the communication skills to say something effectively.", "This is not strictly a workplace problem; it's a growing problem off the job too. Every day people witness things on the street and choose to stand idly by. This is known as the bystander effect—the more people who witness an event, the less likely anyone in that group is to help the victim. The psychology behind this is called diffusion of responsibility. Basically, the larger the crowd, the more people assume that someone else will take care of it—meaning no one effectively intervenes or acts in a moment of need.", "This crowd mentality is strong enough for people to evade their known responsibilities. But it's not only frontline workers who don't make safety interventions in the workplace. There are also instances where supervisors do not intervene either.", "When a group of employees sees unsafe behavior not being addressed at a leadership level it creates the precedent that this is how these situations should be addressed, thus defining the safety culture for everyone.", "Despite the fact that workers are encouraged to intervene when they observe unsafe operations, this happens less than half of the time. Fear is the ultimate factor in not intervening. There is a fear of penalty, a fear that they'll have to do more work if they intervene. Unsuccessful attempts in the past are another strong contributing factor to why people don't intervene—they tend to prefer to defer that action to someone else for all future situations.", "On many worksites, competent workers must be appointed. Part of their job is to intervene when workers perform a task without the proper equipment or if the conditions are unsafe. Competent workers are also required to stop work from continuing when there's a danger.", "Supervisors also play a critical role. Even if a competent person isn't required, supervisors need a broad set of skills to not only identify and alleviate workplace hazards but also build a safety climate within their team that supports intervening and open communication among them.", "Beyond competent workers and supervisors, it's important to educate everyone within the organization that they are obliged to intervene if they witness a possible unsafe act, whether you're a designated competent person, a supervisor or a frontline worker."], "translations": ["员工知道是非对错，这是无可辩驳的。那么，为什么当员工看到有人在工作场所表现出危险行为时，没有更多的员工进行干预呢？", "影响人们是否干预的因素有很多。首先，他们需要能够看到危险情况开始显现。其次，公司的文化需要让他们感到表达意见是安全的。第三，他们需要具备有效表达的沟通技巧。", "这不仅仅是一个工作场所的问题，在工作之外这也是一个日益严重的问题。每天人们在街上目睹一些事情，却选择袖手旁观。这被称为旁观者效应——目睹某一事件的人越多，该群体中任何人帮助受害者的可能性就越小。这背后的心理机制被称为责任分散。基本上，人群越大，越多的人就会认为会有别人来处理——这意味着在需要的时刻没有人有效地进行干预或采取行动。", "这种从众心理强大到足以让人们逃避他们已知的责任。但不仅仅是一线工人不在工作场所进行安全干预，也有主管不进行干预的情况。", "当一群员工看到不安全行为在领导层面没有得到处理时，这就开创了应该以这种方式处理这些情况的先例，从而为每个人定义了安全文化。", "尽管员工被鼓励在观察到不安全操作时进行干预，但这种情况发生的次数不到一半。恐惧是不进行干预的终极因素：害怕受到惩罚，害怕如果进行干预就必须做更多工作。过去不成功的尝试是人们不干预的另一个重要促成因素——他们往往更愿意在未来所有情况下将该行动推给别人。", "在许多工作场所，必须指定有资质的工人。他们工作的一部分是当工人在没有适当设备的情况下执行任务或条件不安全时进行干预。有资质的工人还被要求在存在危险时叫停工作。", "主管也发挥着关键作用。即使不需要指定有资质的人员，主管也需要具备广泛的技能，不仅要识别和减轻工作场所的危险，还要在团队内部建立支持干预和彼此开放沟通的安全氛围。", "除了有资质的工人和主管之外，同样重要的是要教育组织内的每一个人：无论你是指定的有资质人员、主管还是一线工人，如果你目睹了可能的不安全行为，都有义务进行干预。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is one of the factors contributing to failure of intervention in face of risky behavior in the workplace?", "options": ["Slack supervision style.", "Unfavorable workplace culture.", "Unforeseeable risk.", "Blocked communication."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Second, the company's culture needs to make them feel safe to speak up.", "explanation": "第2段明确指出了影响员工是否干预危险行为的三个因素，其中第二点提到“the company's culture needs to make them feel safe to speak up”（公司文化需要让他们感到表达意见是安全的）。选项B中的“Unfavorable workplace culture”（不利的职场文化）正是从反面对该因素的同义转述，直接导致员工不愿或未能进行干预，故选B。", "trapNote": "选项A“松懈的监管风格”和D“沟通受阻”虽在后文或第2段有所关联，但第2段原文强调的是员工自身需要具备有效沟通技巧，而非外部沟通渠道受阻，监管问题也非第2段所列直接因素。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "词义题", "stem": "What does the author mean by \"diffusion of responsibility\" (Para. 3)?", "options": ["The more people are around, the more they need to worry about their personal safety.", "The more people who witness an event, the less likely anyone will venture to", "The more people idling around on the street, the more likely they need taking care of.", "The more people are around, the less chance someone will step forward to intervene."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Basically, the larger the crowd, the more people assume that someone else will take care of it—meaning no one effectively intervenes or acts in a moment of need.", "explanation": "题干定位至第3段“diffusion of responsibility”。紧随其后的句子用“Basically”对其作出解释：人群越大，越多的人会认为别人会处理此事，从而导致在需要时“no one effectively intervenes or acts”（没有人有效干预或行动）。选项D“周围的人越多，有人站出来干预的机会就越小”精准概括了这一含义，故选D。", "trapNote": "选项B前半句与旁观者效应定义吻合，但结尾残缺未表达完整语义；选项A“担心个人安全”与C“街上闲逛的人需要被照顾”均属于对原文“witness events on the street”和“help the victim”的曲解。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What happens when unsafe behavior at the workplace is not addressed by the leaders?", "options": ["No one will intervene when they see similar behaviors.", "Everyone will see it as the easiest way to deal with crisis.", "Workers have to take extra caution executing their duties.", "Workers are left to take care of the emergency themselves."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "When a group of employees sees unsafe behavior not being addressed at a leadership level it creates the precedent that this is how these situations should be addressed, thus defining the safety culture for everyone.", "explanation": "题干中的“not addressed by the leaders”直接对应第5段开头的“not being addressed at a leadership level”。该段指出，员工看到领导层不处理不安全行为，就会将其视为处理此类情况的先例，进而定义整个团队的安全文化，即大家都会效仿不干预。选项A“人们看到类似行为时将无人干预”符合这一逻辑推论，故选A。", "trapNote": "选项B将“处理情况的先例（precedent）”偷换为“解决危机的最简单方法”，属于过度臆断；选项C和D提到的“格外谨慎执行任务”与“自行处理紧急情况”在原文中均未提及。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the ultimate reason workers won't act when they see unsafe operations?", "options": ["Preference of deferring the action to others.", "Anticipation of leadership intervention.", "Fear of being isolated by coworkers.", "Fear of having to do more work."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Fear is the ultimate factor in not intervening. There is a fear of penalty, a fear that they'll have to do more work if they intervene.", "explanation": "第6段围绕员工看到不安全操作却不采取行动的深层原因展开，明确指出“Fear is the ultimate factor in not intervening”（恐惧是不进行干预的终极因素），并具体列举了两种恐惧：对惩罚的恐惧，以及“a fear that they'll have to do more work if they intervene”（害怕干预会增加工作量）。选项D与原文表述高度一致，故选D。", "trapNote": "选项A“倾向于把行动推给别人”是第6段末句提到的“过去不成功尝试”所带来的另一重要促成因素（contributing factor），并非题干所问的“ultimate reason（终极原因）”，属于答非所问的典型干扰。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is critical to ensuring workplace safety?", "options": ["Workers be trained to operate their equipment properly.", "Workers exhibiting at-risk behavior be strictly disciplined.", "Supervisors create a safety environment for timely intervention.", "Supervisors conduct effective communication with frontline workers."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "Supervisors also play a critical role. Even if a competent person isn't required, supervisors need a broad set of skills to not only identify and alleviate workplace hazards but also build a safety climate within their team that supports intervening and open communication among them.", "explanation": "题干询问确保职场安全的关键所在，对应第8段首句“Supervisors also play a critical role”。该段接着指出，主管不仅要识别和减轻危险，还需要“build a safety climate within their team that supports intervening and open communication”（在团队内建立支持干预与开放沟通的安全氛围）。选项C准确概括了这一点，故选C。", "trapNote": "选项D将第8段主管在团队内部建立“开放沟通氛围”曲解为“主管与一线工人进行有效沟通”；选项A和B中的“培训工人正确操作设备”与“严格处罚危险行为”均未在第8至9段的关键措施中被重点提及。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "干预，介入", "note": "高频核心动词，常用于安全管理、公共事务或危机处理语境，名词形式为 intervention。", "word": "intervene"}, {"gloss": "无可辩驳的，不容置疑的", "note": "词根 refute（反驳）+ 否定前缀 ir- + 后缀 -able，用于开篇确立无争议的前提。", "word": "irrefutable"}, {"gloss": "（责任等的）分散，扩散", "note": "心理学核心术语 diffusion of responsibility 意为“责任分散”，是旁观者效应背后的心理机制。", "word": "diffusion"}, {"gloss": "先例，惯例", "note": "常见搭配 create/set a precedent（开创先例），指领导层不作为对团队文化产生的示范效应。", "word": "precedent"}, {"gloss": "推迟；顺从，将……交由他人决定", "note": "固定搭配 defer sth. to sb. 表示“把某事推迟或交由他人处理”。", "word": "defer"}, {"gloss": "减轻，缓和", "note": "常与 hazard（危险）、risk（风险）、pain（痛苦）等词搭配，比 reduce 更显正式书面。", "word": "alleviate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "When a group of employees sees unsafe behavior not being addressed at a leadership level it creates the precedent that this is how these situations should be addressed, thus defining the safety culture for everyone.", "point": "动名词复合结构作宾语补足语（sees ... not being addressed），以及现在分词短语作结果状语（thus defining ...）。", "structure": "When引导时间状语从句（含现在分词被动式not being addressed作宾补） + 主句it creates the precedent（后接that引导同位语从句） + 现在分词短语thus defining...作结果状语。", "zh": "当一群员工看到不安全行为在领导层面没有得到处理时，这就开创了应该以这种方式处理此类情况的先例，从而为每个人定义了安全文化。"}, {"en": "Even if a competent person isn't required, supervisors need a broad set of skills to not only identify and alleviate workplace hazards but also build a safety climate within their team that supports intervening and open communication among them.", "point": "not only ... but also ... 连接两个并列不定式结构（共享前面的不定式符号to），以及that引导的定语从句修饰climate。", "structure": "Even if引导让步状语从句 + 主句supervisors need a broad set of skills + 目的状语to not only ... but also ... + that引导定语从句修饰a safety climate。", "zh": "即使不需要指定有资质的人员，主管也需要具备广泛的技能，不仅要识别和减轻工作场所的危险，还要在团队内部建立支持干预和彼此开放沟通的安全氛围。"}, {"en": "Beyond competent workers and supervisors, it's important to educate everyone within the organization that they are obliged to intervene if they witness a possible unsafe act, whether you're a designated competent person, a supervisor or a frontline worker.", "point": "形式主语it结构与educate sb. that...（向某人阐明/教育某人……）及whether...or...让步状语从句。", "structure": "介词短语作状语 + 形式主语it's important to educate everyone that...（宾语从句含if条件从句） + whether...or...引导让步状语从句。", "zh": "除了有资质的工人和主管之外，同样重要的是要教育组织内的每一个人：无论你是指定的有资质人员、主管还是一线工人，如果你目睹了可能的不安全行为，都有义务进行干预。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将原文积极的“公司文化让人敢发声”反向转述为导致不干预的消极因素“不利的职场文化”。", "option": "Unfavorable workplace culture", "original": "the company's culture needs to make them feel safe to speak up"}, {"note": "同义动词短语替换，“有人站出来干预”准确对应“有效干预或采取行动”。", "option": "step forward to intervene", "original": "effectively intervenes or acts"}, {"note": "将“领导层不处理”与“形成先例定义文化”合并推理为“类似情况无人干预”。", "option": "No one will intervene when they see similar behaviors", "original": "not being addressed at a leadership level ... creates the precedent"}, {"note": "名词短语“对不得不做更多工作的恐惧”直接对应原文的同位语从句内容。", "option": "Fear of having to do more work", "original": "a fear that they'll have to do more work if they intervene"}, {"note": "用“create a safety environment”同义替换“build a safety climate”。", "option": "create a safety environment for timely intervention", "original": "build a safety climate within their team that supports intervening"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202406-s1-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2024.06", "examSet": "2024.06 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2024.06 六级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "核能之争与可再生能源转型的困境", "subtitle": "探讨环保理念分歧下核能的定位与绿色能源转型现实瓶颈", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 437, "paragraphs": ["The term \"environmentalist\" can mean different things. It used to refer to people trying to protect wildlife and natural ecosystems. In the 21st century, the term has evolved to capture the need to combat human-made climate change.", "The distinction between these two strands of environmentalism is the cause of a split within the scientific community about nuclear energy.", "On one side are purists who believe nuclear power isn't worth the risk and the exclusive solution to the climate crisis is renewable energy. The opposing side agrees that renewables are crucial, but says society needs an amount of power available to meet consumers' basic demands when the sun isn't shining and the wind isn't blowing. Nuclear energy, being far cleaner than oil, gas and coal, is a natural option, especially where hydroelectric capacity is limited.", "Leon Clarke, who helped author reports for the UN's Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change, isn't an uncritical supporter of nuclear energy, but says it's a valuable option to have if we're serious about reaching carbon neutrality.", "\"Core to all of this is the degree to which you think we can actually meet climate goals with 100% renewables,\" he said. \"If you don't believe we can do it, and you care about the climate, you are forced to think about something like nuclear.\"", "The achievability of universal 100% renewability is similarly contentious. Cities such as Burlington, Vermont, have been \"100% renewable\" for years. But these cities often have small populations, occasionally still rely on fossil fuel energy and have significant renewable resources at their immediate disposal. Meanwhile, countries that manage to run off renewables typically do so thanks to extraordinary hydroelectric capabilities.", "Germany stands as the best case study for a large, industrialized country pushing into green energy. Chancellor Angela Merkel in 2011 announced Energiewende, an energy transition that would phase out nuclear and coal while phasing in renewables. Wind and solar power generation has increased over 400% since 2010, and renewables provided 46% of the country's electricity in 2019.", "But progress has halted in recent years. The instability of renewables doesn't just mean energy is often not produced at night, but also that solar and wind can overwhelm the grid during the day, forcing utilities to pay customers to use their electricity. Lagging grid infrastructure struggles to transport this overabundance of green energy from Germany's north to its industrial south, meaning many factories still run on coal and gas. The political limit has also been reached in some places, with citizens meeting the construction of new wind turbines with loud protests.", "The result is that Germany's greenhouse gas emissions have fallen by around 11.5% since 2010—slower than the EU average of 13.5%."], "translations": ["“环保主义者”这个术语可以有不同的含义。它过去指的是试图保护野生动物和自然生态系统的人。而在21世纪，这个术语已经演变为包含应对人为气候变化的需要。", "环保主义这两个分支之间的区别，正是科学界内部在核能问题上产生分歧的原因。", "一方是纯粹主义者，他们认为核能不值得冒险，应对气候危机的唯一解决方案是可再生能源。对立一方同意可再生能源至关重要，但表示当没有阳光和风力时，社会仍需要一定数量的可用电力来满足消费者的基本需求。核能比石油、天然气和煤炭清洁得多，是一个自然的选择，特别是在水电容量有限的地方。", "曾参与撰写联合国政府间气候变化专门委员会报告的Leon Clarke并非核能的无条件支持者，但他表示，如果我们认真对待实现碳中和目标，核能是一个有价值的选择。", "“所有这些的核心在于你在多大程度上认为我们真的能用100%的可再生能源实现气候目标，”他说，“如果你不相信我们能做到，而又关心气候问题，你就不得不考虑像核能这样的选择。”", "在全球范围内实现100%可再生能源的可行性同样存在争议。佛蒙特州伯灵顿等城市多年来一直“100%使用可再生能源”。但这些城市往往人口较少，偶尔仍然依赖化石燃料能源，并且拥有大量可供立即利用的可再生资源。与此同时，那些成功依靠可再生能源运行的国家，通常是因为拥有得天独厚的水电能力。", "德国是大型工业化国家推进绿色能源的最佳案例。总理安格拉·默克尔在2011年宣布了“能源转型”（Energiewende）计划，旨在逐步淘汰核能和煤炭，同时逐步引入可再生能源。自2010年以来，风能和太阳能发电量增长了400%以上，2019年可再生能源提供了该国46%的电力。", "但近年来进展已经停滞。可再生能源的不稳定性不仅意味着夜间往往无法发电，还意味着太阳能和风能在白天可能使电网过载，迫使公用事业公司付钱让客户用电。落后的电网基础设施难以将过剩的绿色能源从德国北部输送到工业化的南部，这意味着许多工厂仍然依靠煤炭和天然气运行。在一些地方这也已达到政治极限，公民以强烈抗议抵制新建风力涡轮机。", "结果是，自2010年以来，德国的温室气体排放量下降了约11.5%——低于欧盟13.5%的平均水平。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What accounts for the divide within the scientific community about nuclear energy?", "options": ["Attention to combating human-made climate change.", "Emphasis on protecting wildlife and natural ecosystems.", "Evolution of the term \"green energy\" over the last century.", "Adherence to different interpretations of environmentalism."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The distinction between these two strands of environmentalism is the cause of a split within the scientific community about nuclear energy.", "explanation": "第1段介绍了“环保主义者”一词的两种含义：过去指保护野生动物和自然生态系统，21世纪演变为应对人为气候变化。第2段紧接着指出，“The distinction between these two strands of environmentalism”（环保主义这两个分支之间的区别）正是科学界在核能问题上产生分歧的原因。选项D“坚持对环保主义的不同理解”精准同义替换了原文表述，故选D。", "trapNote": "选项A和B分别只片面截取了第1段中环保主义的某一种含义，而科学界产生分歧的根源在于两种理念之间的“distinction（差异）”；选项C将原文演变的“environmentalist”偷换为“green energy”。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the solution to energy shortage proposed by purists' opponents?", "options": ["Relying on renewables firmly and exclusively.", "Using fossil fuel and green energy alternately.", "Opting for nuclear energy when necessary.", "Limiting people's non-basic consumption."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Nuclear energy, being far cleaner than oil, gas and coal, is a natural option, especially where hydroelectric capacity is limited.", "explanation": "第3段对比了纯粹主义者与对立方的观点。对立方同意可再生能源至关重要，但认为在无风无光时社会仍需要电力来满足消费者基本需求，随后明确提出“Nuclear energy, being far cleaner than oil, gas and coal, is a natural option”（核能是自然的选择），尤其在水电有限的地方。选项C“在必要时选择核能”准确概括了该方案，故选C。", "trapNote": "选项A“坚定且唯一地依赖可再生能源”是纯粹主义者（purists）的立场，而非其对立方的观点，属于张冠李戴；选项B“交替使用化石燃料和绿色能源”和D“限制非基本消费”均为原文未提及的无中生有信息。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "例证题", "stem": "What point does the author want to make with cities like Burlington as an example?", "options": ["It is controversial whether the goal of the whole world's exclusive dependence on renewables is attainable.", "It is contentious whether cities with large populations have renewable resources at their immediate disposal.", "It is arguable whether cities that manage to run off renewables have sustainable hydroelectric capabilities.", "It is debatable whether traditional fossil fuel energy can be done away with entirely throughout the world."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "The achievability of universal 100% renewability is similarly contentious. Cities such as Burlington, Vermont, have been \"100% renewable\" for years.", "explanation": "第6段首句指出本段的核心论点：“The achievability of universal 100% renewability is similarly contentious”（在全球范围内实现100%可再生能源的可行性同样存在争议）。随后立即举出Burlington等城市为例，说明这些城市之所以能做到，是因为人口少、偶尔仍用化石燃料且资源丰富，借此论证全球全面依赖可再生能源的目标是否可行存在争议，故选A。", "trapNote": "选项B把例证讨论的对象从“全球可行性”缩小为“大城市是否有可再生资源”，偏离首句主旨；选项C将“国家依靠非凡的水电能力”错配给“城市”；选项D“彻底淘汰传统化石燃料”在文中未作直接讨论。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about Germany regarding renewable energy?", "options": ["It has increased its wind and solar power generation four times over the last two decades.", "It represents a good example of a major industrialized country promoting green energy.", "It relies on renewable energy to generate more than half of its electricity.", "It has succeeded in reaching the goal of energy transition set by Merkel."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "Germany stands as the best case study for a large, industrialized country pushing into green energy.", "explanation": "第7段首句明确评价德国：“Germany stands as the best case study for a large, industrialized country pushing into green energy”（德国是大型工业化国家推进绿色能源的最佳案例）。选项B中的“a good example of a major industrialized country promoting green energy”是对该句的高度同义改写，故选B。", "trapNote": "选项A将第7段“2010年以来风能和太阳能发电量增长超过400%”误写成“过去二十年增长四倍”；选项C与原文2019年可再生能源提供“46%的电力（未过半）”相悖；选项D与第8段“进展停滞”的事实相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What may be one of the reasons for Germany's progress having halted in recent years?", "options": ["Its grid infrastructure's capacity has fallen behind its development of green energy.", "Its overabundance of green energy has forced power plants to suspend operation during daytime.", "Its industrial south is used to running factories on conventional energy supplies.", "Its renewable energy supplies are unstable both at night and during the day."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "Lagging grid infrastructure struggles to transport this overabundance of green energy from Germany's north to its industrial south, meaning many factories still run on coal and gas.", "explanation": "第8段开头指出德国绿色能源进展近年来已停滞，随后逐一分析原因，其中明确提到“Lagging grid infrastructure struggles to transport this overabundance of green energy”（落后的电网基础设施难以输送过剩的绿色能源），导致许多工厂仍使用煤和天然气。选项A“电网基础设施容量落后于绿色能源发展”与“Lagging grid infrastructure”完美对应，故选A。", "trapNote": "选项B将“公用事业公司付钱让客户用电”篡改为“发电厂白天暂停运营”，属细节错误；选项C把南部因输电受阻而被迫使用煤气曲解为“习惯使用传统能源”，属于因果倒置。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "（思想、学说等的）分支，派别", "note": "除“一缕、一股”外，在议论文中常指同一理念下的不同“派别/分支”。", "word": "strand"}, {"gloss": "纯粹主义者，极端坚持原则者", "note": "由 pure 派生，指在环保或能源问题上坚持“非此即彼”绝对标准的人。", "word": "purist"}, {"gloss": "碳中和", "note": "环保类高频核心词组，neutrality 由 neutral 派生，意为“中立、中和”。", "word": "carbon neutrality"}, {"gloss": "有争议的，引起争论的", "note": "来自 contend（争论），在六级阅读中常与 controversial 同义替换。", "word": "contentious"}, {"gloss": "逐步淘汰", "note": "能源转型语境核心短语，与文中紧邻出现的 phase in（逐步引入）构成反义对仗。", "word": "phase out"}, {"gloss": "过剩，过多", "note": "前缀 over-（过度）+ abundance（丰富），常形容能源或产能“供过于求”。", "word": "overabundance"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The opposing side agrees that renewables are crucial, but says society needs an amount of power available to meet consumers' basic demands when the sun isn't shining and the wind isn't blowing.", "point": "but连接的并列谓语结构（agrees ... but says ...）及后置形容词短语available作定语。", "structure": "主语 + 谓语agrees（接that宾语从句） + but says（接省略that的宾语从句，其中available作power的后置定语，to meet...为目的状语，when引导时间状语从句）。", "zh": "对立一方同意可再生能源至关重要，但表示当没有阳光和风力时，社会仍需要一定数量的可用电力来满足消费者的基本需求。"}, {"en": "The instability of renewables doesn't just mean energy is often not produced at night, but also that solar and wind can overwhelm the grid during the day, forcing utilities to pay customers to use their electricity.", "point": "not just ... but also ... 连接两个宾语从句，以及现在分词短语forcing...作结果状语。", "structure": "主语The instability of renewables + doesn't just mean（宾语从句1） + but also（承接mean，接that引导的宾语从句2） + 现在分词短语forcing utilities to...作结果状语。", "zh": "可再生能源的不稳定性不仅意味着夜间往往无法发电，还意味着太阳能和风能在白天可能使电网过载，迫使公用事业公司付钱让客户用电。"}, {"en": "Lagging grid infrastructure struggles to transport this overabundance of green energy from Germany's north to its industrial south, meaning many factories still run on coal and gas.", "point": "现在分词作前置定语（Lagging）与现在分词短语作自然结果状语（meaning ...）。", "structure": "主句Lagging grid infrastructure struggles to transport...（from...to...状语） + 现在分词短语meaning（接省略that的宾语从句）作结果状语。", "zh": "落后的电网基础设施难以将过剩的绿色能源从德国北部输送到工业化的南部，这意味着许多工厂仍然依靠煤炭和天然气运行。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将原文“两个环保分支之间的区别”改写为“坚持对环保主义的不同解释”。", "option": "Adherence to different interpretations of environmentalism", "original": "The distinction between these two strands of environmentalism"}, {"note": "把原文“核能是自然选择”提炼为“在必要时选择核能”。", "option": "Opting for nuclear energy when necessary", "original": "Nuclear energy ... is a natural option"}, {"note": "用 controversial、exclusive dependence 和 attainable 精准改写“普遍100%可再生的可实现性存在争议”。", "option": "It is controversial whether the goal of the whole world's exclusive dependence on renewables is attainable", "original": "The achievability of universal 100% renewability is similarly contentious"}, {"note": "用 a good example of 替换 the best case study，用 promoting 替换 pushing into。", "option": "a good example of a major industrialized country promoting green energy", "original": "the best case study for a large, industrialized country pushing into green energy"}, {"note": "用“电网容量落后于绿能发展”同义转述“落后的电网基础设施难以输送过剩绿能”。", "option": "Its grid infrastructure's capacity has fallen behind its development of green energy", "original": "Lagging grid infrastructure struggles to transport this overabundance of green energy"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L2", "exam": "cet6", "id": "cet6-202312-p1", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["One of the great successes of the Republican Party in recent decades is the relentless propagation of a simple formula for economic growth: tax cuts.", "The formula doesn’t work, but that has not affected its popularity. And while the cult of tax cuts has attracted many critics, it lacks for obvious rivals.", "Democratic politicians have tended to campaign on helping people left behind by economic growth. When Democrats do talk about encouraging economic growth, they often sound like Republicans.", "This is not just a political problem for Democrats; it is an economic problem for the United States. The nation needs a better story about the drivers of economic growth. The painful lessons of recent decades point to a promising candidate: higher wages.", "Raising the wages of American workers ought to be the priority of economic policymakers. We’d all be better off paying less attention to quarterly updates on the growth of the nation’s gross domestic product (GDP) and focusing instead on the growth of workers’ paychecks.", "Set aside, for the moment, the familiar argument for higher wages: fairness. The argument here is that higher wages can fuel the engine of economic growth.", "Perhaps the most famous illustration of the benefits is the story of Henry Ford’s decision in 1914 to pay $5 a day to workers on his Model T assembly lines. He did it to increase production—he was paying a premium to maintain a reliable workforce. The unexpected benefit was that Ford’s factory workers became Ford customers, too.", "The same logic still holds: Consumption drives the American economy, and workers who are paid more can spend more.", "Mainstream economists insist that it is impossible to order up a sustainable increase in wages because compensation levels reflect the unerring judgment of market forces.", "The conventional wisdom held that productivity growth was the only route to higher wages. Through that lens, efforts to negotiate higher wages were counterproductive. Minimum-wage laws would raise unemployment because there was only so much money in the wage pool, and if some people got more, others would get none.", "It was in the context of this worldview that it became popular to argue that tax cuts would drive prosperity. Rich people would invest, productivity would increase, and wages would rise.", "In the real world, things are more complicated. Wages are influenced by a tug of war between employers and workers, and employers have been winning. One clear piece of evidence is the widening gap between productivity growth and wage growth since roughly 1970. Productivity has more than doubled; wages have lagged far behind.", "A focus on wage growth would provide an antidote (矫正方法) to the attractive simplicity of the belief in the magical power of tax cuts."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The formula doesn’t work, but that has not affected its popularity. And while the cult of tax cuts has attracted many critics, it lacks for obvious rivals.", "explanation": "定位至第二段。原文指出减税公式虽不起作用，却依然受欢迎，虽然招致了许多批评，但它“缺乏明显的竞争对手（lacks for obvious rivals）”。这与 B 项“似乎没有其他可替代的方案（no other options available to replace it）”形成同义替换。", "no": 46, "options": ["Its critics’ voice has not been heard throughout the country.", "There seem to be no other options available to replace it.", "The cult of tax cuts has been relentlessly propagated by all policymakers.", "There appears to be a misunderstanding of the formula among the public."], "stem": "Why does the formula of tax cuts remain popular though ineffective?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 拼凑首段“relentless propagation”和次段“cult of tax cuts”，把推行者“共和党”偷换为“所有政策制定者（all policymakers）”，属于偷换概念与扩大范围。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The nation needs a better story about the drivers of economic growth. The painful lessons of recent decades point to a promising candidate: higher wages.", "explanation": "定位至第四段第二、三句。作者指出美国在经济增长动力方面需要更好的思路，近几十年的惨痛教训指明了一个大有可为的备选方案：提高工资（higher wages）。C 项中的 Increasing the compensation for labor（提高劳动报酬）正是对“higher wages”的同义替换。", "no": 47, "options": ["Aiding people left behind by economic growth.", "Prioritizing the growth of the nation’s GDP.", "Increasing the compensation for labor.", "Introducing even more extensive tax cuts."], "stem": "What does the author think is a more effective measure for driving economic growth in the U.S.?", "trapNote": "干扰项 B 属于正反颠倒，第五段明确主张应减少对 GDP 季度增长数据的关注，转而聚焦工人薪资的增长，而非优先考虑 GDP 增长。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "The same logic still holds: Consumption drives the American economy, and workers who are paid more can spend more.", "explanation": "定位至第八段。作者在举完福特加薪使工人也成为消费者的例子后指出，同样的逻辑依然成立：消费驱动美国经济，而收入更高的工人能够消费更多。A 项“工人薪资的增长最终会推动国家经济”精准概括了这一传导逻辑。", "no": 48, "options": ["The growth of workers’ paychecks ultimately boosts the nation’s economy.", "Paying a premium to maintain a reliable workforce attracts more customers.", "Consumption stimulates the desire for higher wages.", "Familiar arguments for higher wages are outdated."], "stem": "What is the logic underlying the author’s viewpoint?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 将原文的因果关系倒置，文章逻辑是“提高工资带动消费，消费进而拉动经济”，而非“消费刺激对高工资的渴望”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 10, "evidenceQuote": "The conventional wisdom held that productivity growth was the only route to higher wages.", "explanation": "定位至第十段第一句。原文明确提到，传统观点（conventional wisdom）认为，生产率增长是实现更高工资的唯一途径（the only route to higher wages）。B 项“生产率的提高（Increase in productivity）”与原文形成直接同义替换。", "no": 49, "options": ["Fairness in distribution.", "Increase in productivity.", "The priority of economic policymakers.", "The unerring judgment of market forces."], "stem": "What is the basis for higher wages according to the conventional wisdom?", "trapNote": "干扰项 D 利用第九段原词“the unerring judgment of market forces”设陷，属于张冠李戴，该表述用于解释市场力量的作用，而非传统观点所认为的涨薪依据。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 12, "evidenceQuote": "One clear piece of evidence is the widening gap between productivity growth and wage growth since roughly 1970. Productivity has more than doubled; wages have lagged far behind.", "explanation": "定位至第十二段（倒数第二段）。原文指出大约自 1970 年以来（即过去约 50 年间），生产率增长与工资增长之间的差距不断扩大，生产率翻了一倍多，而工资增长却远远落后。A 项“人们未能看到工资与生产率同步增长”正是对这一事实的同义转述。", "no": 50, "options": ["People have failed to see a corresponding increase in wages and in productivity.", "People have been disheartened by the widening gap between the haves and have-nots.", "People have witnessed a tug of war between Republicans and Democrats over tax cuts.", "People have seen the link disappearing between productivity and workers’ well-being."], "stem": "What do we learn about things in the real world in America for the past 50 years or so?", "trapNote": "干扰项 B 和 C 均采用“原词拼凑+偷换概念”套路，把“生产率与工资的差距（widening gap）”偷换为贫富差距，或把“雇主与工人的拉锯战（tug of war）”偷换为两党减税之争。", "type": "细节题"}], "sourceLabel": "2023.12 六级真题第1套", "subtitle": "Passage One (Questions 46–50)", "timeLimitMin": 10, "title": "Higher Wages as the Engine of Economic Growth", "year": "2023.12", "wordCount": 454, "examSet": "2023.12 六级真题 第1套", "translations": ["近几十年来，共和党取得的最大成功之一，就是坚持不懈地宣扬一个简单的经济增长公式：减税。", "这个公式并不奏效，但这并未影响它的受欢迎程度。尽管对减税的盲目崇拜招致了许多批评，但它却缺乏明显的替代方案。", "民主党政客往往倾向于在竞选中主打帮助那些被经济增长抛在后面的人。当民主党人真正谈及促进经济增长时，他们的论调听起来常常与共和党人别无二致。", "这不仅是民主党的政治问题，也是美国的经济问题。这个国家需要一个关于经济增长驱动力的更好叙事。近几十年的惨痛教训指向了一个颇有前景的候选方案：提高工资。", "提高美国工人的工资应当成为经济政策制定者的首要任务。如果我们少关注一些国家国内生产总值（GDP）增长的季度更新数据，转而关注工人薪资的增长，我们的境况都会更好。", "暂且把支持加薪的常见理由——公平性——放到一边。这里的论点是，提高工资能够为经济增长的引擎注入动力。", "关于加薪益处的最著名例证，或许是亨利·福特在1914年决定向T型车装配线上的工人每天支付5美元的故事。他这样做是为了提高产量——他支付高薪以维持一支可靠的劳动力队伍。而意想不到的好处是，福特工厂的工人也成为了福特的顾客。", "同样的逻辑至今依然成立：消费驱动着美国经济，而收入更高的工人能够消费更多。", "主流经济学家坚持认为，不可能强行实现工资的可持续增长，因为薪酬水平反映的是市场力量准确无误的判断。", "传统观念认为，生产率增长是实现更高工资的唯一途径。从这一视角来看，通过谈判争取更高工资的努力会适得其反。最低工资法会推高失业率，因为工资池里的资金总量就那么多，如果一部分人拿得多，其他人就会一无所获。", "正是在这种世界观的背景下，“减税将推动繁荣”的观点才流行起来。富人会进行投资，生产率会提高，工资也会随之上涨。", "在现实世界中，情况要复杂得多。工资受到雇主与工人之间拉锯战的影响，而雇主一直占据上风。一个明显的证据是，大约自1970年以来，生产率增长与工资增长之间的差距不断扩大。生产率增长了一倍多，而工资却远远滞后。", "关注工资增长将提供一种矫正方法，以打破人们对减税神奇魔力那种极具吸引力的简单化迷信。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "(尤指政治或商业上的)宣传，鼓吹；传播", "note": "高频学术词，动词 propagate；CET-6 常考“理念/政策的推广宣传”，带一定批评色彩。", "word": "propagation"}, {"gloss": "额外费用，高价，溢价", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“保险费”，此处 pay a premium 意为“支付高薪/高出常规的价格”，形容词形式常考“优质的”。", "word": "premium"}, {"gloss": "依然成立，仍然有效", "note": "熟词僻义：hold 除“拿、举办、认为”外，作不及物动词常表“有效、站得住脚、适用”（如 The same logic still holds）。", "word": "hold"}, {"gloss": "薪酬，报酬", "note": "高频商务/经济词汇，同义替换 wages / pay / salary（第47题直接替换 higher wages）。", "word": "compensation"}, {"gloss": "产生反效果的，适得其反的", "note": "构词法高频词：counter-（相反）+ productive（有成效的）→ 适得其反的，常用于政策评估类阅读。", "word": "counterproductive"}, {"gloss": "落后，滞后", "note": "高频动词短语 lag behind（远远落后于），常用于数据对比与趋势描述（如工资增长滞后于生产率增长）。", "word": "lag"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "We’d all be better off paying less attention to quarterly updates on the growth of the nation’s gross domestic product (GDP) and focusing instead on the growth of workers’ paychecks.", "point": "固定句型 be better off doing sth. 与并列动名词结构", "structure": "主干：We’d all be better off paying... and focusing...；其中 paying less attention to... 与 focusing instead on... 由 and 连接作并列动名词短语，补充说明“在什么方面会过得更好”；on the growth of... 为介词短语作后置定语修饰 updates。", "zh": "如果我们少关注一些国家国内生产总值（GDP）增长的季度更新数据，转而关注工人薪资的增长，我们的境况都会更好。"}, {"en": "Mainstream economists insist that it is impossible to order up a sustainable increase in wages because compensation levels reflect the unerring judgment of market forces.", "point": "宾语从句、形式主语 it 与原因状语从句嵌套", "structure": "主干：Mainstream economists insist that...；that 引导宾语从句，从句中 it 为形式主语，真正主语为不定式短语 to order up a sustainable increase in wages；because 引导原因状语从句，说明“无法强行推高工资”的理由。", "zh": "主流经济学家坚持认为，不可能强行实现工资的可持续增长，因为薪酬水平反映的是市场力量准确无误的判断。"}, {"en": "It was in the context of this worldview that it became popular to argue that tax cuts would drive prosperity.", "point": "强调句型 It is/was... that... 与形式主语嵌套", "structure": "主干为强调句结构 It was + 介词短语(in the context of this worldview) + that...，强调“正是在这种世界观的背景下”；that 后第二个 it 为形式主语，真正主语是不定式 to argue that...，其中又嵌套了 argue 的宾语从句 that tax cuts would drive prosperity。", "zh": "正是在这种世界观的背景下，“减税将推动繁荣”的观点才流行起来。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第46题同义替换：原文“缺少明显的竞争对手/替代方案”对应选项“似乎没有其他可用的替代选择”。", "option": "There seem to be no other options available to replace it.", "original": "it lacks for obvious rivals"}, {"note": "第47题同义替换：higher wages 对应“增加劳动报酬（compensation for labor）”。", "option": "Increasing the compensation for labor", "original": "higher wages"}, {"note": "第48题同义替换：消费驱动经济、涨薪促进消费 对应“工人薪资的增长最终提振国家经济”。", "option": "The growth of workers’ paychecks ultimately boosts the nation’s economy.", "original": "Consumption drives the American economy, and workers who are paid more can spend more."}, {"note": "第49题同义替换：productivity growth 名词短语转换为 Increase in productivity。", "option": "Increase in productivity", "original": "productivity growth"}, {"note": "第50题同义替换：生产率翻倍但工资滞后、差距扩大 对应“未能看到工资与生产率同步增长”。", "option": "failed to see a corresponding increase in wages and in productivity", "original": "the widening gap between productivity growth and wage growth... Productivity has more than doubled; wages have lagged far behind."}]}}, {"difficulty": "L2", "exam": "cet6", "id": "cet6-202312-p2", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["Journal editors decide what gets published and what doesn’t, affecting the careers of other academics and influencing the direction that a field takes. You’d hope, then, that journals would do everything they can to establish a diverse editorial board, reflecting a variety of voices, experiences, and identities.", "Unfortunately a new study in Nature Neuroscience makes for disheartening reading. The team finds that the majority of editors in top psychology and neuroscience journals are male and based in the United States: a situation that may be amplifying existing gender inequalities in the field and influencing the kind of research that gets published.", "Men were found to account for 60% of the editors of psychology journals. There were significantly more male than female editors at each level of seniority, and men made up the majority of editors in over three quarters of the journals. Crucially, the proportion of female editors was significantly lower than the overall proportion of women psychology researchers.", "The differences were even starker in the neuroscience journals: 70% of editors were male, and men held the majority of editorial positions in 88% of journals. In this case, the proportion of female editors was not significantly lower than the proportion of female researchers working in neuroscience—a finding that reveals enduring gender disparities in the field more broadly.", "Based on their results, the team concludes that “the ideas, values and decision-making biases of men are overrepresented in the editorial positions of the most recognized academic journals in psychology and neuroscience.”", "Gender inequality in science is often attributed to the fact that senior academics are more likely to be male, because historically science was male-dominated: It’s argued that as time goes on and more women rise to senior roles, the field will become more equal. Yet this study showed that even the junior roles in psychology journals tended to be held disproportionately by men, despite the fact that there are actually more female than male junior psychology faculty.", "This implies that a lack of female academics is not the problem. Instead, there are structural reasons that women are disadvantaged in science. Women receive lower salaries and face greater childcare demands, for instance, which can result in fewer publications and grants—the kinds of things that journals look for when deciding who to appoint. Rather than simply blaming the inequality of editorial boards on tradition, we should be actively breaking down these existing barriers.", "A lack of diversity among journal editors also likely contributes to psychology’s WEIRD problem. If journal editors are largely men from the United States, then they will probably place higher value on papers that are relevant to Western, male populations, whether consciously or not."], "questions": [{"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "You’d hope, then, that journals would do everything they can to establish a diverse editorial board, reflecting a variety of voices, experiences, and identities.", "explanation": "定位至第一段第二句。作者在第一句指出期刊编辑掌控论文发表并影响学科方向后，接着表示人们会希望期刊竭尽所能建立一个“多元化的编委会（a diverse editorial board）”，以反映不同的声音、经历和身份。D 项 Diversity（多样性）是原文 diverse 的同义名词替换。", "no": 51, "options": ["Insight.", "Expertise.", "Integrity.", "Diversity."], "stem": "What would we expect an editorial board of an academic journal to exhibit in view of its important responsibilities?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A、B、C 均属于脱离文本、依靠个人常识臆断的无中生有项，第一段并未提及洞察力、专业知识或正直品质。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The team finds that the majority of editors in top psychology and neuroscience journals are male and based in the United States", "explanation": "定位至第二段第二句。这篇发表在《自然·神经科学》上的新研究发现，顶尖心理学和神经科学期刊的大多数编辑都是男性（the majority of editors... are male）且位于美国。C 项中的 male-dominated（男性主导的）是对这一研究发现的准确同义转述。", "no": 52, "options": ["The majority of top psychology and neuroscience journals reflect a variety of voices, experiences and identities.", "The editorial boards of most psychology and neuroscience journals do influence the direction their field takes.", "The editorial boards of the most important journals in psychology and neuroscience are male-dominated.", "The majority of editors in top psychology and neuroscience journals have relevant backgrounds."], "stem": "What do we learn from the findings of a new study in Nature Neuroscience?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 属于正反颠倒，将第一段中人们“期望”实现的多元化错当成该研究发现的客观现实。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Crucially, the proportion of female editors was significantly lower than the overall proportion of women psychology researchers.", "explanation": "定位至第三段末句。作者在列举心理学期刊中男性编辑占比高达 60% 等数据后，用“Crucially”重点指出女性编辑的比例明显低于女性心理学研究者的总体比例。B 项中的 disproportionate（不成比例的）正是对这一比例失衡事实的同义替换。", "no": 53, "options": ["There were quite a few female editors who also distinguished themselves as influential psychology researchers.", "The number of female editors was simply disproportionate to that of women engaged in psychology research.", "The proportion of female editors was increasingly lower at senior levels.", "There were few female editors who could move up to senior positions."], "stem": "What fact does the author highlight concerning the gender differences in editors of psychology journals?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 属于偷换概念，第三段只说明在“每一个资历层级（each level of seniority）”男性编辑均显著多于女性，并未表示层级越高女性编辑比例“越低”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "“the ideas, values and decision-making biases of men are overrepresented in the editorial positions of the most recognized academic journals in psychology and neuroscience.”", "explanation": "定位至第五段。研究团队根据调查结果得出结论：在最受认可的心理学和神经科学期刊编辑职位中，男性的观念、价值观和决策偏好占比过高（overrepresented）。由此可推断出，女性的观点在这些顶尖期刊编委会中代表性不足（underrepresented），故 A 项正确。", "no": 54, "options": ["Women’s views are underrepresented in the editorial boards of top psychology and neuroscience journals.", "Male editors of top psychology and neuroscience journals tend to be biased against their female colleagues.", "Male researchers have enough representation in the editorial boards to ensure their publications.", "Female editors have to struggle to get women’s research articles published in academic journals."], "stem": "What can we infer from the conclusion drawn by the team of the new study on the basis of their findings?", "trapNote": "干扰项 B 属于过度推理与偷换概念，把原文中男性编辑在学术评审上的“决策偏好（decision-making biases）”曲解为对女性同行抱有歧视。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "Rather than simply blaming the inequality of editorial boards on tradition, we should be actively breaking down these existing barriers.", "explanation": "定位至第七段末句。作者建议与其简单地将编委会的不平等归咎于传统，不如积极打破现有的障碍（breaking down these existing barriers）；结合本段前文可知，这些障碍指的是导致女性处于劣势的薪酬与育儿等“结构性原因（structural reasons）”。D 项“实施全面结构性改革”符合作者主张。", "no": 55, "options": ["Strike a balance between male and female editors.", "Increase women’s employment in senior positions.", "Enlarge the body of female academics.", "Implement overall structural reforms."], "stem": "What does the author suggest we do instead of simply blaming the inequality of editorial boards on tradition?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 与原文正反颠倒，第七段首句明确指出“女性学者数量不足并不是问题所在”，因此作者并不主张靠扩充女性学者人数来解决问题。", "type": "细节题"}], "sourceLabel": "2023.12 六级真题第1套", "subtitle": "Passage Two (Questions 51–55)", "timeLimitMin": 10, "title": "Gender Inequality on Academic Journal Editorial Boards", "year": "2023.12", "wordCount": 449, "examSet": "2023.12 六级真题 第1套", "translations": ["期刊编辑决定了哪些论文能够发表、哪些不能发表，这不仅影响着其他学者的职业生涯，还左右着一个学科的发展方向。因此，人们自然会希望期刊能竭尽全力组建一个多元化的编委会，反映出不同的声音、经历和身份背景。", "遗憾的是，发表在《自然·神经科学》上的一项新研究却带来了令人沮丧的结果。该研究团队发现，顶尖心理学和神经科学期刊的大多数编辑都是男性且常驻美国：这种状况可能会加剧该领域现有的性别不平等，并影响最终得以发表的研究类型。", "研究发现，男性占心理学期刊编辑总数的60%。在每一个资历级别上，男性编辑都明显多于女性编辑，且在超过四分之三的期刊中，男性占编辑人员的大多数。至关重要的是，女性编辑的比例显著低于女性心理学研究者的总体比例。", "在神经科学期刊中，这种差异甚至更为显著：70%的编辑为男性，且男性在88%的期刊中占据了多数编辑职位。在这种情况下，女性编辑的比例并未显著低于从事神经科学研究的女性研究者比例——这一发现揭示了该领域更普遍存在的持久性别差距。", "基于研究结果，该团队得出结论：“在心理学和神经科学领域最受认可的学术期刊编辑职位中，男性的观点、价值观和决策偏向被过度代表了。”", "科学界的性别不平等常常被归因于资深学者更可能是男性这一事实，因为从历史上看，科学一直由男性主导：人们认为，随着时间推移，越来越多的女性晋升到资深职位，这一领域将会变得更加平等。然而这项研究表明，在心理学期刊中，就连初级编辑职位也往往不成比例地由男性担任，尽管事实上女性初级心理学教职人员的数量实际上多于男性。", "这意味着缺乏女性学者并非问题所在。相反，女性在科学界处于不利地位有着结构性的原因。例如，女性获得的薪酬较低，且面临更大的育儿需求，这可能会导致她们发表的论文和获得的科研经费较少——而这些正是期刊在决定任命谁担任编辑时所看重的条件。与其简单地将编委会的不平等归咎于传统，我们不如积极打破这些现存的障碍。", "期刊编辑缺乏多样性，也很可能加剧了心理学的“WEIRD”（西方、受过良好教育、工业化、富裕和民主群体样本偏差）问题。如果期刊编辑主要是来自美国的男性，那么无论是有意还是无意，他们都很可能会更看重与西方男性群体相关的论文。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "(在某地或某领域)占据比例，占……", "note": "高频动词短语 account for，除“解释、说明原因”外，在数据统计类文章中常译为“占（一定比例）”。", "word": "account"}, {"gloss": "(在比例或数量上)代表过多的，占比过高的", "note": "构词法高频词：over-（过度）+ represent（代表）→ 在席位或比例中占比过高；对应反义词 underrepresented（代表不足的，第54题考点）。", "word": "overrepresented"}, {"gloss": "差距，不平等，悬殊", "note": "高频学术词，常以复数 disparities 出现，同义替换 inequality / difference / gap。", "word": "disparity"}, {"gloss": "把……归因于，认为……是由……引起的", "note": "高频搭配 be attributed to sth.，同义替换 be blamed on / result from，考研与六级因果题高频词。", "word": "attribute"}, {"gloss": "不成比例地，悬殊地", "note": "长难词高频副词：dis-（否定）+ proportion（比例）+ -ate + -ly → 不成比例地（第53题对应形容词 disproportionate）。", "word": "disproportionately"}, {"gloss": "使处于不利地位，妨碍", "note": "熟词僻义/词性活用：常见作名词“劣势、不利条件”，此处作动词被动语态 be disadvantaged，意为“处于弱势地位、受到不利影响”。", "word": "disadvantage"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The team finds that the majority of editors in top psychology and neuroscience journals are male and based in the United States: a situation that may be amplifying existing gender inequalities in the field and influencing the kind of research that gets published.", "point": "宾语从句、同位语结构与多重定语从句", "structure": "主干：The team finds that...；that 引导宾语从句；冒号后的 a situation 是前面整句话的同位语，概括这种现状；其后嵌套由 that 引导的定语从句修饰 situation，内部包含并列现在进行时结构 may be amplifying... and influencing...，结尾 that gets published 修饰 research。", "zh": "该研究团队发现，顶尖心理学和神经科学期刊的大多数编辑都是男性且常驻美国：这种状况可能会加剧该领域现有的性别不平等，并影响最终得以发表的研究类型。"}, {"en": "Yet this study showed that even the junior roles in psychology journals tended to be held disproportionately by men, despite the fact that there are actually more female than male junior psychology faculty.", "point": "宾语从句、让步状语及同位语从句", "structure": "主干：Yet this study showed that...；that 引导宾语从句，说明“初级编辑职位也往往不成比例地由男性担任”；despite the fact that... 为让步状语，其中 that 引导同位语从句，具体解释 the fact 的内容（女性初级教职人员实际上多于男性）。", "zh": "然而这项研究表明，在心理学期刊中，就连初级编辑职位也往往不成比例地由男性担任，尽管事实上女性初级心理学教职人员的数量实际上多于男性。"}, {"en": "Women receive lower salaries and face greater childcare demands, for instance, which can result in fewer publications and grants—the kinds of things that journals look for when deciding who to appoint.", "point": "非限制性定语从句、同位语破折号解释及“疑问词+不定式”结构", "structure": "主干：Women receive lower salaries and face greater childcare demands；which 引导非限制性定语从句，指代前面整件事导致的结果；破折号后 the kinds of things... 作 publications and grants 的同位语；that 引导定语从句修饰 things，其中包含 when deciding who to appoint（省略主语的时间状语从句+疑问词不定式作宾语）。", "zh": "例如，女性获得的薪酬较低，且面临更大的育儿需求，这可能会导致她们发表的论文和获得的科研经费较少——而这些正是期刊在决定任命谁担任编辑时所看重的条件。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第51题同义替换：a diverse editorial board 词性转换为名词 Diversity。", "option": "Diversity.", "original": "establish a diverse editorial board"}, {"note": "第52题同义替换：“大多数编辑是男性”对应“由男性主导（male-dominated）”，top journals 对应 the most important journals。", "option": "The editorial boards of the most important journals in psychology and neuroscience are male-dominated.", "original": "the majority of editors in top psychology and neuroscience journals are male"}, {"note": "第53题同义替换：“女性编辑比例显著低于女性研究者整体比例”对应“女性编辑数量与从事心理学研究的女性数量不成比例”。", "option": "The number of female editors was simply disproportionate to that of women engaged in psychology research.", "original": "the proportion of female editors was significantly lower than the overall proportion of women psychology researchers"}, {"note": "第54题反义推论/同义替换：男性观点“代表过多（overrepresented）”等价于女性观点“代表不足（underrepresented）”。", "option": "Women’s views are underrepresented in the editorial boards of top psychology and neuroscience journals.", "original": "the ideas, values and decision-making biases of men are overrepresented in the editorial positions of the most recognized academic journals in psychology and neuroscience"}, {"note": "第55题同义替换：前文指出存在 structural reasons，后文提出“打破现有壁垒（breaking down these existing barriers）”对应“实施全面的结构性改革”。", "option": "Implement overall structural reforms.", "original": "actively breaking down these existing barriers"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202312-s2-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 六级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 六级真题 第2套 Passage One", "title": "数字戒瘾背后的特权与鸿沟", "subtitle": "社会文化 · 数字排斥与媒介使用", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["Could you get by without using the internet for four and a half years? That's exactly what singer and actress Selena Gomez has done in a bid to improve her mental health.", "She has spoken extensively about the relationship between her social media usage and her mental wellbeing, recalling feeling like “an addict” when she became Instagram's most followed user in 2016. “Taking a break from social media was the best decision that I've ever made for my mental health”, says she. “The unnecessary hate and comparisons went away once I put my phone down.”", "Ditching the web at large, however, is a far more subtle and complicated prospect. The increasing digitisation of our society means that everything from paying a gas bill to plotting a route to a friend's house and even making a phone call is at the mercy of your internet connection. Actively opting out of using the internet becomes a matter of privilege.", "Ms Gomez's multi-millionaire status has allowed her to take the “social” out of social media, so she can continue to leverage her enormous fame while keeping the trolls (恶意挑衅的帖子) at bay. The fact that she's still the second most-followed woman on Instagram suggests it's entirely possible to maintain a significant web profile to promote various projects - by way of a dedicated team - without being exposed to the cruel comments, hate mail, and rape or death threats.", "It goes without saying that this is fundamentally different from how the rest of us without beauty deals and films to publicise use the likes of Instagram, TikTok, and Twitter, but even the concept of a digital detox (戒瘾) requires having a device and connectivity to choose to disconnect from.", "The UK's digital divide has worsened over the past two years, leaving poorer families without broadband connections in their homes. Digital exclusion is a major threat to wider societal equality in the UK, so witnessing companies like Facebook championing the metaverse (元宇宙) as the next great frontier when schoolchildren are struggling to complete their homework feels particularly irritating.", "Consequently, it's worth bearing in mind that while deleting all social media accounts will undoubtedly make some feel infinitely better, many other people benefit from the strong sense of community that sharing platforms can breed.", "Internet access will continue to grow in importance as we edge further towards web 3.0, and greater resources and initiatives are needed to provide the underprivileged with the connectivity they desperately need to learn, work, and live. It's crucial that people who feel that social media is having a detrimental effect on their mental health are allowed to switch off and for those living in digital exclusion to be able to switch on in the first place."], "translations": ["你能忍受四年半不上网吗？这正是歌手兼演员赛琳娜·戈麦斯为改善心理健康而采取的做法。", "她曾广泛谈及自己使用社交媒体与心理健康之间的关系，回忆称自己在2016年成为Instagram粉丝最多的用户时，感觉自己就像“一个瘾君子”。“暂别社交媒体是我为心理健康做过的最好的决定，”她说，“一旦放下手机，那些不必要的恶意与攀比便随之消失了。”", "然而，彻底抛弃互联网却是一个远为微妙而复杂的问题。我们社会的日益数字化意味着，从缴纳燃气费、规划去朋友家的路线，甚至到打一通电话，方方面面都受制于网络连接。主动选择不上网已然成为一种特权。", "戈麦斯女士千万富翁的身份让她得以剥离社交媒体中“社交”的那一面，从而在有效回避恶意挑衅的同时，继续利用自己巨大的名气。她至今仍是Instagram上粉丝量第二高的女性，这一事实表明，只要通过专门团队运作，完全有可能在不遭受恶毒评论、仇恨邮件以及强奸或死亡威胁的情况下，维持可观的网络曝光度以推广各类项目。", "毋庸置疑，这与我们这些既没有美妆代言也没有电影要宣传的普通人使用Instagram、TikTok和Twitter等平台的方式有着本质区别；但即便只是“数字戒瘾”这一概念，也首先要求你得拥有设备和网络连接，才能选择与之断开。", "过去两年里，英国的数字鸿沟不断加剧，令较为贫困的家庭家中没有宽带连接。数字排斥对英国更广泛的社会平等构成了重大威胁，因此，当看到学童们还在为完成家庭作业而苦苦挣扎时，Facebook等公司却在大力鼓吹元宇宙是下一个伟大前沿，着实令人格外气愤。", "因此，值得铭记的是，虽然注销所有社交媒体账号无疑会让一部分人感觉好上许多，但还有许多人从信息分享平台所孕育的强烈社群归属感中获益良多。", "随着我们进一步迈向Web 3.0时代，互联网接入的重要性将持续提升，我们需要投入更多资源与举措，为弱势群体提供他们学习、工作和生活所迫切需要的网络连接。至关重要的是，那些觉得社交媒体正对其心理健康产生负面影响的人应被允许“下线”，而那些身处数字排斥中的人则首先要有能力“上线”。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about singer and actress Selena Gomez in the past four and a half years?", "options": ["She has had worsening mental problems.", "She has refrained from using social media.", "She has won Instagram's most followers.", "She has succeeded in a bid on the internet"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Could you get by without using the internet for four and a half years? That's exactly what singer and actress Selena Gomez has done in a bid to improve her mental health.", "explanation": "定位第1段前两句并结合第2段。第1段指出赛琳娜·戈麦斯为改善心理健康，已四年半未曾使用互联网；第2段进一步借她的话点明，暂别社交媒体是她为心理健康做出的最佳决定，放下手机后恶意与攀比便消失了。B项refrained from using social media精准同义转述原文“暂别社交媒体/不用互联网”，且时间状语与过去四年半完全吻合，故正确。", "trapNote": "A项正反颠倒，原文明确表示此举改善了心理健康；C项时间错位，成为Instagram粉丝最多用户是在2016年；D项曲解词义，原文in a bid意为“为了尝试”，并非网上竞拍成功。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why does actively opting out of using the internet become a matter of privilege?", "options": ["Most people find it subtle and complicated to give up using the internet.", "Most people can hardly ditch the web while avoiding hate and comparisons.", "Most people can hardly get by without the internet due to growing digitisation.", "Most people have been seriously addicted to the web without being aware of it."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The increasing digitisation of our society means that everything from paying a gas bill to plotting a route to a friend's house and even making a phone call is at the mercy of your internet connection.", "explanation": "定位第3段第2、3句。该段先指出社会日益数字化意味着从缴纳燃气费、规划去友人家路线到打电话等日常事务，都完全受制于网络连接，随后得出“主动选择不上网成了一种特权”的结论。题干追问其原因，C项中“日益加剧的数字化”对应原文increasing digitisation，“几乎无法离开网络生活”精准概括了处处依赖网络的实质，完美契合原文因果逻辑。", "trapNote": "A项答非所问，第3段首句只是评价彻底弃网这件事本身很复杂，并非解释为何弃网是特权；B项张冠李戴，把第2段赛琳娜提及的恶意与攀比套用到普通人难以退网的原因上。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Why does the author say “witnessing companies...feels particularly irritating” (Lines 2-4, Para. 6)?", "options": ["The UK digital divide would further worsen due to the metaverse.", "The concept of the metaverse is believed to be still quite illusory.", "School children would be drawn farther away from the real world.", "Most families in the UK do not have stable broadband connections."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "The UK's digital divide has worsened over the past two years, leaving poorer families without broadband connections in their homes. Digital exclusion is a major threat to wider societal equality in the UK, so witnessing companies like Facebook championing the metaverse (元宇宙) as the next great frontier when schoolchildren are struggling to complete their homework feels particularly irritating.", "explanation": "定位第6段。首句指出英国数字鸿沟过去两年持续恶化，贫困家庭仍缺乏家用宽带；次句通过因果连词so点明：数字排斥严重威胁社会平等，因此在学童连做作业都举步维艰之际，看到脸书等公司大肆鼓吹元宇宙作为下一伟大前沿格外令人气愤。由此可推断，在基础联网尚未解决的情况下强推元宇宙，势必令落后者更难赶上，从而使英国的数字鸿沟进一步恶化，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "D项以偏概全，原文缺乏宽带的是贫困家庭而非“大多数英国家庭”；B项无中生有，文中并未评价元宇宙概念是否虚幻；C项过度推理，学童提及的困境是缺乏宽带完成作业而非脱离现实。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is worth bearing in mind concerning social media platforms?", "options": ["They are conducive to promoting societal equality.", "They help many people feel connected with others.", "They provide a necessary device for a digital detox.", "They create a virtual community on the internet."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "Consequently, it's worth bearing in mind that while deleting all social media accounts will undoubtedly make some feel infinitely better, many other people benefit from the strong sense of community that sharing platforms can breed.", "explanation": "定位第7段。题干直接指向该段开头“值得铭记的是”这一核心提示。作者在句中先用让步状语从句承认注销所有社交媒体账号确实能让部分人感觉好得多，随后强调还有许多人从信息分享平台所孕育的强烈社群归属感（sense of community）中获益。B项“帮助许多人感受到与他人的联结”精准同义转述了原文的社群归属感及其积极作用，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "D项属于偷换概念，将原文心理层面的“社群归属感”（sense of community）偷换为实体层面的“虚拟社区”；A项张冠李戴，社会平等问题见于第6段数字排斥的讨论。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author think is really important for those living in digital exclusion?", "options": ["Having access to the internet.", "Getting more educational resources.", "Edging further towards web 3.0.", "Opening more social media accounts."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "It's crucial that people who feel that social media is having a detrimental effect on their mental health are allowed to switch off and for those living in digital exclusion to be able to switch on in the first place.", "explanation": "定位第8段。尾句明确指出“至关重要（crucial）”的两件事：一是受困于社媒负面影响的人能自由下线，二是身处数字排斥中的人“首先能够上线（switch on）”。结合本段首句强调为弱势群体提供学习、工作与生活所急需的“网络连接（connectivity）”和“互联网接入”，可知作者认为对数字排斥群体而言，最关键的就是能够接入互联网，对应A项。", "trapNote": "B项偷换概念，第8段主张提供更多资源是为了解决“网络连接”而非直接提供“教育资源”；C项将时代背景“迈向Web 3.0”误作解决措施；D项为原文未提及的无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 努力，尝试，企图", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“投标、出价”，但固定搭配in a bid to do sth.表示“为了/试图做某事”，第1题D项即借“bid”原词设为“网上竞拍”陷阱。", "word": "bid"}, {"gloss": "v. 抛弃，丢弃，摆脱", "note": "熟词僻义：作名词意为“沟渠”，作动词在新闻与议论文中常表示“放弃、抛弃（习惯、计划、工具等）”，本文中ditching the web即“彻底放弃使用网络”。", "word": "ditch"}, {"gloss": "phr. 受……支配，完全受……摆布", "note": "核心短语：mercy常考“仁慈、宽恕”，但at the mercy of sth.固定表示“听任……摆布、无法摆脱……的控制”，文中指日常生活完全受限于网络连接。", "word": "at the mercy of"}, {"gloss": "phr. 遏制，使……不能靠近，避开", "note": "固定搭配：bay作名词常指“海湾”，但在keep sth. at bay中表示“把（威胁、麻烦、恶意挑衅等）挡在外面、使其无法伤及自身”。", "word": "keep ... at bay"}, {"gloss": "v. 公开支持，极力鼓吹，捍卫", "note": "熟词僻义：作名词意为“冠军”，作及物动词在六级阅读中高频考查“拥护、大力倡导（某种理念或事物）”，本文中指脸书大肆鼓吹元宇宙。", "word": "champion"}, {"gloss": "adj. 有害的，不利的", "note": "核心高频词：常考搭配have a detrimental effect on...（对……产生有害影响），同义替换词包括harmful、damaging、adverse。", "word": "detrimental"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The fact that she's still the second most-followed woman on Instagram suggests it's entirely possible to maintain a significant web profile to promote various projects - by way of a dedicated team - without being exposed to the cruel comments, hate mail, and rape or death threats.", "point": "识别“The fact that... suggests (that) it's possible to do... without doing...”多层嵌套框架，抓住主干“事实表明无需承受网暴也能维持曝光”，破折号插入语表实现方式。", "structure": "主句主语为The fact（后接that引导的同位语从句），谓语为suggests，后接省略that的宾语从句；宾语从句中使用形式主语it，真正主语为to maintain...不定式短语；破折号间by way of...作方式状语，without...作伴随/条件状语。", "zh": "她至今仍是Instagram上粉丝量第二高的女性，这一事实表明，通过专门团队运作，完全有可能在不遭受恶毒评论、仇恨邮件以及强奸或死亡威胁的情况下，维持可观的网络曝光度以推广各类项目。"}, {"en": "Digital exclusion is a major threat to wider societal equality in the UK, so witnessing companies like Facebook championing the metaverse (元宇宙) as the next great frontier when schoolchildren are struggling to complete their homework feels particularly irritating.", "point": "关注动名词短语作主语（witnessing... feels irritating）及when时间从句构成的讽刺对比，这是命题人考查作者态度与因果推断的高频句型。", "structure": "so连接两个因果并列分句；后一分句主语为动名词复合结构witnessing companies... championing...，其中when引导时间状语从句形成强烈对比，系动词feels后接表语particularly irritating。", "zh": "数字排斥对英国更广泛的社会平等构成了重大威胁，因此，当学童们还在为完成家庭作业而苦苦挣扎时，看到Facebook等公司却将元宇宙鼓吹为下一个伟大前沿，着实令人格外气愤。"}, {"en": "It's crucial that people who feel that social media is having a detrimental effect on their mental health are allowed to switch off and for those living in digital exclusion to be able to switch on in the first place.", "point": "注意and前后结构不对称的并列主语（that从句 + for... to do...）以及switch off（下线/断网）与switch on（上线/联网）构成的呼应。", "structure": "形式主语It's crucial后并列两个真正主语成分：前者为that引导的主语从句（内含who定语从句及that宾语从句），后者为and连接的for sb. to do不定式复合结构（内含living...现在分词短语作后置定语）。", "zh": "至关重要的是，那些觉得社交媒体正对其心理健康产生负面影响的人应当被允许“下线”，而那些身处数字排斥中的人则首先要有能力“上线”。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "refrain from意为“克制/避免做某事”，准确转述原文“暂别社媒、不用互联网”的行为。", "option": "refrained from using social media", "original": "without using the internet / Taking a break from social media"}, {"note": "at the mercy of（受……支配）与get by without（离了……凑合过日子）构成反义正说，体现日常事务对网络的强依赖。", "option": "can hardly get by without the internet due to growing digitisation", "original": "The increasing digitisation of our society means that everything... is at the mercy of your internet connection."}, {"note": "由“数字鸿沟已恶化、孩童无网做作业却大谈元宇宙”的矛盾处境，合理推出元宇宙将加剧数字鸿沟。", "option": "The UK digital divide would further worsen due to the metaverse", "original": "The UK's digital divide has worsened... witnessing companies like Facebook championing the metaverse... feels particularly irritating"}, {"note": "sense of community（社群感、归属感）转述为feel connected with others（感受到与他人相连），而非实体的“虚拟社区”。", "option": "help many people feel connected with others", "original": "benefit from the strong sense of community that sharing platforms can breed"}, {"note": "connectivity（网络连接）和switch on（接通电源/上线）均指代“获得互联网接入”。", "option": "Having access to the internet", "original": "provide the underprivileged with the connectivity... to be able to switch on"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202312-s2-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 六级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 六级真题 第2套 Passage Two", "title": "竞争：人类本能还是文化产物", "subtitle": "心理学与人类学 · 竞争与合作的起源", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 449, "paragraphs": ["Psychologists have long been in disagreement as to whether competition is a learned or a genetic component of human behavior. Whatever it is, you cannot but recognize the effect competition is exerting in academics and many other areas of contemporary life.", "Psychologically speaking, competition has been seen as an inevitable consequence of human drives. According to Sigmund Freud, humans are born screaming for attention and full of organic drives for fulfillment in various areas. Initially, we compete for the attention of our parents. Thereafter, we are at the mercy of a battle between our base impulses for self-fulfillment and social and cultural norms which prohibit pure indulgence.", "Current work in anthropology (人类学) has suggested, however, that this view of the role of competition in human behavior may be incorrect. Thomas Hobbes, one of the great philosophers of the seventeenth century, is perhaps best remembered for his characterization of the “natural world,” that is, the world before the imposition of the will of humanity, as being “nasty, brutish, and short.” This image of the pre-rational world is still widely held, reinforced by Charles Darwin's highly influential work, The Origin of Species, which established the doctrine of natural selection. This doctrine, which takes for granted that those species best able to adapt to and master the natural environment in which they live will survive, has suggested that the struggle for survival is an inherent human trait which determines a person's success. Darwin's theory has even been summarized as “survival of the fittest” — a phrase Darwin himself never used — further highlighting competition's role in success.", "As it has often been pointed out, however, there is nothing in the concept of natural selection that suggests that competition is the most successful strategy for survival of the fittest. Darwin asserted in The Origin of Species that the struggles he was describing should be viewed as metaphors and could easily include dependence and cooperation.", "Many studies have been conducted to test the importance placed on competition as opposed to other values, such as cooperation — by various cultures, and generally conclude that Americans uniquely praise competition as natural, inevitable, and desirable. In 1937, the world-renowned anthropologist Margaret Mead published Cooperation and Competition among Primitive Peoples, based on her studies of several societies that did not prize competition, and, in fact, seemed at times to place a negative value on it. One such society was the Zuni Indians of Arizona, and they, Mead found, valued cooperation far more than competition. After studying dozens of such cultures, Mead's final conclusion was that competitiveness is a culturally created aspect of human behavior, and that its prevalence in a particular society is relative to how that society values it."], "translations": ["关于竞争是人类行为中后天习得的成分还是遗传成分，心理学家们长期以来一直存在分歧。但无论如何，你不得不承认，竞争正在学术界以及当代生活的许多其他领域发挥着影响。", "从心理学角度来看，竞争一直被视为人类内驱力的必然结果。根据西格蒙德·弗洛伊德的观点，人生来就哭喊着寻求关注，并充满在各个领域寻求满足的生理驱力。最初，我们争夺父母的关注。此后，我们便受制于一场拉锯战——一方是我们追求自我满足的本能冲动，另一方则是禁止纯然放纵的社会与文化规范。", "然而，人类学领域的最新研究表明，这种关于竞争在人类行为中所起作用的观点可能是错误的。17世纪伟大哲学家之一托马斯·霍布斯最为人铭记的，或许是他对“自然世界”——即人类意志尚未施加影响之前的世界——的刻画，他将其形容为“肮脏、野蛮而短暂”。这一前理性世界的形象至今仍广为流传，并因查尔斯·达尔文极具影响力的著作《物种起源》而得到强化，该书确立了自然选择学说。这一学说理所当然地认为，最能适应并掌控其所处自然环境的物种将会生存下来，从而暗示生存竞争是决定一个人成功与否的人类固有特质。达尔文的理论甚至被概括为“适者生存”——尽管达尔文本人从未用过这一说法——从而进一步凸显了竞争在成功中的作用。", "然而，正如人们经常指出的那样，自然选择的概念中没有任何内容表明竞争是“适者生存”最成功的策略。达尔文在《物种起源》中断言，他所描述的“斗争”应被视为隐喻，而且完全可以包含相互依存与合作。", "人们已经开展了大量研究，以检验不同文化对竞争以及合作等其他价值观的重视程度，这些研究普遍得出结论：美国人独树一帜地将竞争赞美为自然、必然且可取的事物。1937年，享誉世界的人类学家玛格丽特·米德出版了《原始民族的竞争与合作》，该书基于她对几个并不推崇竞争、甚至有时似乎对竞争持负面评价的社会的考察。亚利桑那州的祖尼印第安人就是这样一个社会，米德发现他们看重合作远胜于竞争。在研究了数十个此类文化之后，米德得出的最终结论是：竞争性是人类行为中由文化建构出来的方面，它在特定社会中的普遍程度取决于该社会如何看待它的价值。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author think is easy to see in many areas of contemporary life?", "options": ["The disagreement on the inevitability of competition.", "The consequence of psychological investigation.", "The effect of human drives.", "The impact of competition."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Whatever it is, you cannot but recognize the effect competition is exerting in academics and many other areas of contemporary life.", "explanation": "定位第1段第2句。原文首句提到心理学家对竞争究竟是后天习得还是先天遗传尚有分歧，次句随即转折指出“无论如何，你不得不承认竞争正在学术界以及当代生活的许多其他领域发挥着影响”。其中cannot but recognize（不得不承认/显而易见）对应题干easy to see，the effect competition is exerting（竞争正产生的作用）对应D项中的impact of competition，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，第1段讨论的分歧是竞争“是习得还是遗传”，而非“是否必然”；C项张冠李戴，人类驱力出自第2段；B项属拼凑第1、2段字眼的无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to psychology, what do people strive to do following the initial stage of their life?", "options": ["Fulfill individual needs without incurring adverse effects of human drives.", "Indulge in cultural pursuits while keeping their base impulses at bay.", "Gain extensive recognition without exposing pure indulgence.", "Satisfy their own desires while observing social conventions."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Thereafter, we are at the mercy of a battle between our base impulses for self-fulfillment and social and cultural norms which prohibit pure indulgence.", "explanation": "定位第2段尾句。题干中的following the initial stage对应段中时间副词Thereafter（此后，即在“最初争夺父母关注”的阶段之后）。原文指出此后我们受困于两股力量的交锋：一是追求自我满足的本能冲动（impulses for self-fulfillment），二是禁止纯然放纵的社会文化规范（social and cultural norms）。D项将二者精准转述为“在遵守社会习俗的同时满足自身欲望”，契合文意。", "trapNote": "B项曲解文意，将受制于社会文化规范歪曲为“沉溺于文化追求”；A项中的“避免内驱力负面影响”属无中生有；C项把生命最初阶段寻求关注的内容混入后续阶段，属时序错位。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about the “natural world” characterized by Thomas Hobbes?", "options": ["It gets misrepresented by philosophers and anthropologists.", "It gets distorted in Darwin's The Origin of Species.", "It is free from the rational intervention of humans.", "It is the pre-rational world rarely appreciated nowadays."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Thomas Hobbes, one of the great philosophers of the seventeenth century, is perhaps best remembered for his characterization of the “natural world,” that is, the world before the imposition of the will of humanity, as being “nasty, brutish, and short.” This image of the pre-rational world is still widely held, reinforced by Charles Darwin's highly influential work, The Origin of Species, which established the doctrine of natural selection.", "explanation": "定位第3段第2、3句。霍布斯对“自然世界”作了明确界定，即“人类意志尚未施加之前的世界”（before the imposition of the will of humanity），紧接着第3句又将该形象概括为“前理性世界”（pre-rational world）。将这两处同义界定结合可知，所谓自然世界就是尚未受到人类理性意志介入或干预的世界。C项“不受人类理性干预”精准概括了上述两处核心修饰，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "D项正反颠倒，原文明确指出这一前理性世界形象“至今仍广为流传”（still widely held），而非鲜有人认同；B项歪曲原文，达尔文著作是强化而非“歪曲”了这一形象。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we conclude from Darwin's assertion in The Origin of Species?", "options": ["All species inherently depend on others for survival.", "Struggles for survival do not exclude mutual support.", "Competition weighs as much as cooperation as a survival strategy.", "The strongest species proves to be the fittest in natural selection."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Darwin asserted in The Origin of Species that the struggles he was describing should be viewed as metaphors and could easily include dependence and cooperation.", "explanation": "定位第4段第2句。针对前文将自然选择简单等同于竞争的解读，达尔文在《物种起源》中明确断言：他所描述的生存“斗争”应当被视作隐喻，而且完全可以包含“相互依存与合作”。由此可合理推知，在达尔文看来，生存斗争并不排斥相互支持与协作。B项中“不排斥相互支持”精准同义转述了原文“完全可以包含依存与合作”的表述，符合推断逻辑。", "trapNote": "A项过度推理且表述绝对，原文只说斗争“可以包含”依存与合作，并未断言“所有物种本质上都依赖他人”；C项强加比较，文中并未比较竞争与合作作为生存策略的权重。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What conclusion did Margaret Mead reach after studying dozens of different cultures?", "options": ["It is characteristic of humans to be competitive.", "Americans are uniquely opposed to cooperation.", "Competition is relatively more prevalent in Western societies.", "People's attitude towards competition is actually culture-bound."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "After studying dozens of such cultures, Mead's final conclusion was that competitiveness is a culturally created aspect of human behavior, and that its prevalence in a particular society is relative to how that society values it.", "explanation": "定位第5段尾句。在考察了数十个不同文化群体之后，人类学家玛格丽特·米德得出了最终结论：竞争性是人类行为中由文化创造出来的方面（culturally created），而且竞争在特定社会中的盛行程度取决于该社会如何评价其价值。D项中的culture-bound意为“受文化制约的/由文化决定的”，精准概括了“由文化建构并随社会价值观而定”的结论，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项正反颠倒，米德证明竞争并非人类固有本能，而是后天文化产物；B项曲解首句，研究只说美国人赞美竞争，并未断言美国人“反对合作”；C项将文化案例扩大为整个西方社会，属以偏概全。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "phr. 不得不，必然会", "note": "语法结构：cannot but do sth.后接动词原形（不带to），表示“不得不承认/禁不住……”，常用于作者引出无可否认的客观现象。", "word": "cannot but"}, {"gloss": "n. 放纵，纵情，沉溺", "note": "高频词：动词形式为indulge（常考indulge in沉溺于）；本文中prohibit pure indulgence指规范禁止纯然的放纵，第2题B项将“文化规范”偷换为“沉溺文化追求”。", "word": "indulgence"}, {"gloss": "n. 施加，强加", "note": "词根词缀：动词impose（impose sth. on把……强加于）的名词形式，文中imposition of the will of humanity意为“人类意志的施加/介入”。", "word": "imposition"}, {"gloss": "n. 学说，教义，信条", "note": "学术常用词：指成体系的科学学说、政治原则或宗教教义，本文中the doctrine of natural selection即达尔文的“自然选择学说”。", "word": "doctrine"}, {"gloss": "v. 珍视，看重，高度评价", "note": "熟词僻义：作名词意为“奖品”，但在六级阅读第5段societies that did not prize competition中作动词，意为“看重、推崇”，与下文的value同义。", "word": "prize"}, {"gloss": "phr. 取决于，与……成比例，相对于", "note": "熟词僻义/短语：不要仅记住“相对于”；在句中is relative to how that society values it意为“与该社会如何看待它成正比/取决于该社会的态度”。", "word": "relative to"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "This doctrine, which takes for granted that those species best able to adapt to and master the natural environment in which they live will survive, has suggested that the struggle for survival is an inherent human trait which determines a person's success.", "point": "层层剥离非限制性定语从句与宾语从句嵌套结构，把握主干“This doctrine has suggested that the struggle... is an inherent human trait”，注意take for granted（想当然地认为）隐含作者的反思立场。", "structure": "主句主语为This doctrine，后接which非限制性定语从句（内部套that宾语从句，宾语从句主语those species后又有形容词短语best able to...及in which定语从句）；主句谓语为has suggested，后接that宾语从句（内部含which定语从句）。", "zh": "这一学说理所当然地认为，最能适应并掌控其所处自然环境的物种将会生存下来，从而暗示生存竞争是决定一个人成功与否的人类固有特质。"}, {"en": "As it has often been pointed out, however, there is nothing in the concept of natural selection that suggests that competition is the most successful strategy for survival of the fittest.", "point": "注意否定词nothing与定语从句的否定转移效果（“没有任何内容表明……”），这是破除前文“竞争决定论”的转折枢纽句。", "structure": "As引导非限制性定语从句作状语并表转折（however）；主句为there be否定句型，nothing后接that引导的定语从句修饰先行词nothing，该定语从句中又套that引导的宾语从句。", "zh": "然而，正如人们经常指出的那样，自然选择的概念中没有任何内容表明竞争是“适者生存”最成功的策略。"}, {"en": "After studying dozens of such cultures, Mead's final conclusion was that competitiveness is a culturally created aspect of human behavior, and that its prevalence in a particular society is relative to how that society values it.", "point": "识别由and连接的两个并列表语从句（两个that均不可随意忽略），以及短语be relative to（取决于、与……成正比/相关）对全篇主旨的总结作用。", "structure": "介词短语After studying...作时间状语（逻辑主语按米德理解）；主句系动词was后接and连接的两个并列表语从句that... and that...，第二个从句中relative to后接how引导的宾语从句。", "zh": "在研究了数十个此类文化之后，米德得出的最终结论是：竞争性是人类行为中由文化建构出来的方面，它在特定社会中的普遍程度取决于该社会如何看待它的价值。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "cannot but do（不得不/难免）对应题干easy to see，exerting an effect（施加影响）同义转述为impact。", "option": "easy to see ... The impact of competition", "original": "you cannot but recognize the effect competition is exerting"}, {"note": "base impulses for self-fulfillment对应satisfy desires，social and cultural norms对应social conventions。", "option": "Satisfy their own desires while observing social conventions", "original": "a battle between our base impulses for self-fulfillment and social and cultural norms"}, {"note": "before the imposition of the will of humanity与pre-rational合并转述为“不受人类理性干预”。", "option": "free from the rational intervention of humans", "original": "the world before the imposition of the will of humanity ... the pre-rational world"}, {"note": "正话反说：could easily include（完全可以包含）转述为do not exclude（并不排斥），dependence and cooperation对应mutual support。", "option": "Struggles for survival do not exclude mutual support", "original": "the struggles he was describing ... could easily include dependence and cooperation"}, {"note": "复合词culture-bound（受文化制约的）高度凝练地概括了“由文化创造且取决于社会评价”的核心观点。", "option": "People's attitude towards competition is actually culture-bound", "original": "competitiveness is a culturally created aspect... relative to how that society values it"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202312-s3-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 六级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 六级真题 第3套 Passage One", "title": "科研成果的公众传播与开放共享", "subtitle": "学术传播 · 打破学术壁垒，让研究惠及社会", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 449, "paragraphs": ["Research is meant to benefit society by raising public awareness and creating products and innovations that enhance development. For research to serve its full purpose, the results must leave the confines of research laboratories and academic journals.", "Findings effectively communicated can go a long way to serve the interests of the public. They can help address social injustices or improve treatments offered to patients.", "Many researchers seem to be content with sharing the results of their studies in academic journals or at conferences. But few journals allow everybody to read the findings. Even articles freely available are usually written in academic language incomprehensible to the average reader.", "For researchers in the tenure-track system, their main goal is winning tenure, which in part can be achieved by getting a number of papers published in prominent journals. Pressures like this mean community-level outreach is not prioritized.", "Many researchers lack the writing skills to describe their results to a general audience. They may also worry about whether the public will understand their findings, or about findings being used to influence controversial policies. These concerns cause some researchers to shy away from communicating their findings outside the academic community.", "Propagating research findings beyond academic publications is particularly crucial for addressing certain social discrepancies. It can help families, communities, healthcare providers, policymakers, government agencies and others to understand and respond to crises that plague society.", "The benefits of sharing findings flow both ways. Engaging with other researchers and the public can lead to unexpected new connections and new ideas that could suggest fruitful new directions for research.", "To benefit both researchers and the communities, the need to find innovative, accessible ways to share the work cannot be overstated.", "Institutions and funding organizations should support more researchers to publish in open access journals so that the public doesn't have to pay to read them. Institutions and researchers should invest in partnerships that expand capacity for sharing results more broadly.", "Furthermore, ethics committees should make it mandatory for researchers to share their results with the public. Every research participant should opt in or out of receiving results, as part of the process of giving informed consent.", "There could be misunderstanding of the findings presented by the researcher because of technical terms. But this can be resolved by researchers engaging the services of professional writers or communication officers to help with translating their study into more accessible language and share it widely with media outlets and the public.", "Sharing results with the people who are most affected by them makes us better researchers and ensures that our work can be used to improve people's lives. Institutions and collaborators must recognize the value of doing so."], "translations": ["科学研究本应通过提高公众认知以及创造促进发展的产品与创新来造福社会。要使研究充分发挥其作用，研究成果就必须走出研究实验室和学术期刊的局限。", "得到有效传播的研究发现能够极大地服务于公众利益。它们有助于解决社会不公，或改善为患者提供的治疗方案。", "许多研究者似乎满足于在学术期刊或学术会议上分享研究结果。但很少有期刊允许所有人阅读这些研究成果。即使是免费开放的文章，通常也使用普通读者难以理解的学术语言撰写。", "对于处于终身教职轨道体系中的研究者来说，他们的主要目标是获得终身教职，而这在一定程度上可以通过在知名期刊上发表一定数量的论文来实现。此类压力意味着面向社区层面的推广传播不会被列为优先事项。", "许多研究者缺乏向普通受众描述其研究结果的写作技巧。他们还可能担心公众是否能理解这些发现，或者担心研究成果被用来影响有争议的政策。这些顾虑导致一些研究者回避在学术界之外传播自己的研究成果。", "将研究成果传播到学术出版物之外，对于解决某些社会差异问题尤为关键。它可以帮助家庭、社区、医疗服务提供者、政策制定者、政府机构以及其他各方理解并应对困扰社会的危机。", "分享研究成果的益处是双向的。与其他研究者及公众互动，可能会带来意想不到的新联系和新想法，从而为研究指明富有成果的新方向。", "为了使研究者和社区双方都受益，寻找创新且易于获取的方式来分享研究成果的必要性无论怎么强调都不为过。", "研究机构和资助组织应支持更多研究者在开放获取期刊上发表论文，使公众无需付费即可阅读。机构和研究者还应投资建立合作关系，以扩大更广泛分享研究成果的能力。", "此外，伦理委员会应强制要求研究者向公众分享其研究结果。作为签署知情同意书流程的一部分，每位研究参与者都应有权选择是否接收研究结果。", "由于专业术语的存在，公众可能会对研究者呈现的成果产生误解。但这一问题可以通过研究者聘请专业撰稿人或传播专员来解决，由他们协助将研究内容转化为更通俗易懂的语言，并广泛分享给媒体机构和公众。", "将研究结果分享给受其影响最深的人群，能使我们成为更优秀的研究者，并确保我们的工作能够切实改善人们的生活。各机构及合作方必须认识到这样做的价值。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How can research serve its full purpose according to the author?", "options": ["With researchers being aware of public interests.", "With its findings published in prominent journals.", "With researchers creating products that enhance social development.", "With its findings properly communicated beyond the academic circle."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "For research to serve its full purpose, the results must leave the confines of research laboratories and academic journals.", "explanation": "定位至第1段第2句。原文明确指出，要使研究充分发挥全部作用，其成果就必须走出研究实验室和学术期刊的局限（leave the confines），同时结合第2段可知，研究成果只有得到有效传播才能真正服务公众利益。选项D指出将成果妥善传播到学术圈之外，精准同义转述了原文跨出学术圈并有效传播的核心要求，故D项为正确答案。", "trapNote": "C项偷换概念，第1段首句“创造促进发展的产品”是研究造福社会的方式，而非“充分发挥全部作用”的条件；B项与原文“走出学术期刊局限”正反颠倒；A项将原文“提高公众认知”偷换为“研究者关注公众利益”。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why do ordinary readers find it difficult to access the results of researchers' studies?", "options": ["They cannot understand the academic language used for reporting these results.", "They feel intimidated by the jargon researchers use to describe their findings.", "They do not attend conferences where these results are freely available.", "They have few chances to locate the journals that publish these findings."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Even articles freely available are usually written in academic language incomprehensible to the average reader.", "explanation": "定位至第3段末句。该段先指出很少有期刊允许所有人阅读研究成果，紧接着补充强调，即使是免费开放阅读的文章，通常也是用普通读者难以理解的学术语言（incomprehensible）撰写的。题干中“ordinary readers”对应原文的“the average reader”，选项A“他们无法理解用于报告这些成果的学术语言”与原文构成精准同义替换，故A正确。", "trapNote": "D项偷换概念，原文指很少有期刊向所有人开放阅读，重在阅读权限而非“找不到期刊位置”；B项无中生有，文中并未提及读者因学术术语而感到“畏惧”；C项属无中生有，原文未提及学术会议对大众免费。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is one of the reasons some researchers won't prioritize communicating their findings to the public?", "options": ["They can thrive on the papers published.", "Their top consideration is to win tenure.", "Their main goal is gaining recognition in their field.", "They have to struggle to reach out to the community."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "For researchers in the tenure-track system, their main goal is winning tenure, which in part can be achieved by getting a number of papers published in prominent journals. Pressures like this mean community-level outreach is not prioritized.", "explanation": "定位至第4段。原文明确指出，对于处于终身教职轨道体系中的研究者而言，其主要目标是获得终身教职（winning tenure），而这在很大程度上需要通过在知名期刊发表论文来实现；此类晋升压力使得面向社区公众的科普推广不会被列为优先事项。选项B“他们的首要考量是赢得终身教职”与原文“main goal”精准对应，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "C项偷换概念，原文指出首要目标是“获得终身教职”，而非“在领域内赢得认可”；A项属偏离因果，发论文只是获得教职的手段而非首要考量；D项无中生有，文中未提及研究者在开展社区推广时艰难挣扎。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How can sharing findings benefit researchers themselves?", "options": ["By helping them to identify new research directions.", "By enabling them to understand crises plaguing society.", "By enabling them to effectively address social discrepancies.", "By helping them to forge ties with government agencies."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "Engaging with other researchers and the public can lead to unexpected new connections and new ideas that could suggest fruitful new directions for research.", "explanation": "定位至第7段。本段首句指出分享研究成果的益处是双向的，随后具体阐明，与其他研究者及公众互动能够带来意想不到的新联系与新想法，而这些灵感能够为后续研究指明富有成效的新方向（fruitful new directions）。选项A“通过帮助他们识别新的研究方向”与原文精准对应，准确回答了分享成果对研究者自身的益处，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项和C项均属张冠李戴，第6段指出“理解社会危机”和“解决社会差异”是传播成果给家庭、社区等社会群体带来的益处，并非研究者自身所获益处；D项无中生有，第7段仅言“新联系”，未特指与政府机构建立联系。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why are researchers advised to engage the services of professional writers or communication officers?", "options": ["To satisfy ethics committees' mandatory requirements of researchers.", "To translate their study into languages accessible to readers overseas.", "To make their publications correctly understood by the public.", "To render their findings acceptable by prominent journals."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 11, "evidenceQuote": "There could be misunderstanding of the findings presented by the researcher because of technical terms. But this can be resolved by researchers engaging the services of professional writers or communication officers to help with translating their study into more accessible language and share it widely with media outlets and the public.", "explanation": "定位至第11段。原文先指出由于专业术语的存在，公众可能对研究者展示的成果产生误解；随后给出解决方案，即研究者聘请专业撰稿人或传播专员，协助将研究转化为更通俗易懂的语言（accessible language）并广泛分享给媒体和公众，从而消除误解。选项C“使其发表的成果能被公众正确理解”精准概括了这一目的，故C为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项望文生义，将“转化为通俗易懂的语言”曲解为翻译成供海外读者阅读的外语；A项张冠李戴，满足伦理委员会强制要求见于第10段，与第11段聘请专员无关；D项与原文向媒体和公众普及的主旨相反。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 界限，范围（常用复数 confines）；v. 限制", "note": "阅读高频词：leave the confines of 意为“走出……的局限/范围”，常用于突破行业或学术壁垒的语境。", "word": "confine"}, {"gloss": "n. 普及推广，外展服务", "note": "学术/社会类高频词：community-level outreach 指面向社区公众的科普或服务推广，常与 prioritize 搭配。", "word": "outreach"}, {"gloss": "n. 差异，不一致，不平衡", "note": "六级核心词汇：social discrepancies 指社会差距或不公现象，近义替换词为 inequality / gap。", "word": "discrepancy"}, {"gloss": "v. 传播，宣传；繁殖", "note": "跨语境词：在科技与社会类文章中常作“广泛传播（思想、成果）”解，对应 spread / communicate。", "word": "propagate"}, {"gloss": "v. 聘请，雇佣；吸引，参与", "note": "熟词僻义与多义考点：第7段 engage with 表示“与……互动”；第11段 engage the services of 表示“聘请……提供服务”。", "word": "engage"}, {"gloss": "adj. 易懂的，通俗的；可获取的", "note": "一词多义高频考法：第8、9段偏重“可获得的（开放获取）”；第11段 accessible language 特指“通俗易懂的语言”，是第5题设题陷阱关键。", "word": "accessible"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "For researchers in the tenure-track system, their main goal is winning tenure, which in part can be achieved by getting a number of papers published in prominent journals.", "point": "六级高频考点：which引导非限制性定语从句指代前文名词短语，以及get + 宾语 + 过去分词（done）表示“使某事被完成”的用法。", "structure": "介词短语For researchers...作状语；主句为主系表结构（their main goal is winning tenure）；which引导非限制性定语从句修饰winning tenure，其中by doing作方式状语，getting...published为复合宾语结构。", "zh": "对于处于终身教职轨道体系中的研究者而言，他们的主要目标是赢得终身教职，而这在一定程度上可以通过在知名期刊上发表多篇论文来实现。"}, {"en": "Engaging with other researchers and the public can lead to unexpected new connections and new ideas that could suggest fruitful new directions for research.", "point": "长主语结构识别（动名词短语作主语）及熟词僻义suggest（此处不作“建议”，而作“启发、引出、指明”解）。", "structure": "动名词短语Engaging with...作主语；谓语动词短语为can lead to；that引导定语从句修饰先行词new connections and new ideas，从句中suggest表示“提示、指明（方向）”。", "zh": "与其他研究者及公众互动，能够带来意想不到的新联系与新想法，从而为研究指明富有成效的新方向。"}, {"en": "But this can be resolved by researchers engaging the services of professional writers or communication officers to help with translating their study into more accessible language and share it widely with media outlets and the public.", "point": "介词by + 逻辑主语（researchers）+ 动名词（engaging）构成的复合结构作方式状语，以及engage在此处的熟词僻义“聘请、雇佣”。", "structure": "主句为被动语态this can be resolved；by后接动名词的复合结构researchers engaging...作方式状语；不定式to help...作目的状语，其后and连接translating...和share...两个并列动作。", "zh": "但这一问题可以通过研究者聘请专业撰稿人或传播专员来解决，由他们协助将研究内容转化为更通俗易懂的语言，并广泛分享给媒体机构和公众。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题同义替换：走出实验室与期刊的局限 → 传播到学术圈之外", "option": "communicated beyond the academic circle", "original": "leave the confines of research laboratories and academic journals"}, {"note": "第2题否定转述：对普通读者难以理解 → 普通读者无法理解", "option": "ordinary readers ... cannot understand", "original": "incomprehensible to the average reader"}, {"note": "第3题核心词替换：main goal（主要目标） → top consideration（首要考量）", "option": "Their top consideration is to win tenure", "original": "their main goal is winning tenure"}, {"note": "第4题动词替换：指明/提示新的研究方向 → 识别新的研究方向", "option": "identify new research directions", "original": "suggest fruitful new directions for research"}, {"note": "第5题正反/因果转述：通过通俗化解决误解 → 让公众正确理解研究成果", "option": "make their publications correctly understood by the public", "original": "misunderstanding ... resolved by ... translating their study into more accessible language"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202312-s3-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.12", "examSet": "2023.12 六级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2023.12 六级真题 第3套 Passage Two", "title": "从偏见到保护：英国蜘蛛的生态困境", "subtitle": "生态保护 · 蜘蛛的误解、价值与生存现状", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 445, "paragraphs": ["Spiders make their presence felt in late August and through early autumn. This is the mating season of some of the most common varieties, when male house spiders come out of hidden corners to look for females, and garden spiders reach adult size and spin their most dazzling webs.", "Yet while the spider is a familiar fixture of nursery poems or songs and Halloween decorations, its relationship with humans is complicated. Fear of spiders is common and has serious impacts on the lives of sufferers. Its prevalence appears unrelated to any rational assessment of risk. Spiders in the UK are almost all harmless. Farmland species perform valuable ecosystem services, by preying on insects that are our competitors for crops. But they are a constant source of human anxieties — with a cultural association with witches and wickedness dating back to the middle ages.", "Does this perhaps explain, in part, the lack of data about how spiders are faring in our age of ecological crisis? British butterflies are the most studied group of insects in the world, due to the long tradition of collecting and observing them. But spider conservationists point out that it was only in the 1980s that the classification of house spiders was properly sorted out. And while information about insect populations is gathered by experiments that measure the numbers hitting windscreens or traps, there have been few attempts to count spiders.", "The huge reductions in the numbers of flying insects can only mean a reduction in spiders' food supply. A recent landmark study identified a 75% fall in insect populations between 1989 and 2016, with pesticide use thought to be to blame along with the destruction of wild areas for development. This means the overall picture for spiders is worrying, as it is for most creatures. But conservationists are most concerned about those varieties that are threatened due to habitat loss and fragmentation, which makes it impossible for them to migrate.", "Of around 650 spider species regularly recorded in the UK, the majority thrive in marshes and wasteland. Conservation efforts, often led by determined individuals, have helped some species to recover by reintroducing them to new areas. With rewilding now firmly on the environmental policy agenda, the hope is that in future, spiders will be enabled to migrate by themselves, adapting to climate change by moving along wildlife corridors.", "It seems unlikely that spiders will ever attract the same level of human enthusiasm as bees, birds, or butterflies, in spite of their unique status as nature's spinners. But as they reveal themselves in all their splendour this autumn, it would be a good thing if more animal lovers recognised the ways in which spiders are simply terrific."], "translations": ["蜘蛛在八月下旬至初秋时节频频现身。这是某些最常见蜘蛛品种的交配季节，此时雄性家蛛会从隐蔽的角落钻出来寻找雌性，而园蛛也长到成体大小，织出最为精巧夺目的蛛网。", "然而，尽管蜘蛛是童谣儿歌和万圣节装饰中常见的元素，它与人类的关系却十分复杂。对蜘蛛的恐惧十分普遍，并给恐惧症患者的生活带来严重影响。这种恐惧的普遍性似乎与任何理性的风险评估都毫无关联。英国的蜘蛛几乎全部无害。农田中的蜘蛛还通过捕食与人类争夺农作物的昆虫，发挥着宝贵的生态系统服务功能。但蜘蛛一直是人类焦虑的源头——在文化上，人们将它们与女巫及邪恶联系在一起的历史可追溯至中世纪。", "这或许能部分解释，为何在当今这个生态危机时代，我们却缺乏关于蜘蛛生存状况的数据？由于长期以来人们有收集和观察蝴蝶的传统，英国蝴蝶成为世界上研究最为透彻的昆虫类群。但蜘蛛保护主义者指出，直到20世纪80年代，家蛛的分类才得以妥善厘清。而且，虽然人们通过实验统计撞上汽车挡风玻璃或落入诱捕器的数量来收集昆虫种群信息，但针对蜘蛛数量进行统计的尝试却寥寥无几。", "飞虫数量的锐减必然意味着蜘蛛食物来源的减少。近期一项里程碑式的研究发现，1989年至2016年间昆虫种群数量下降了75%，而杀虫剂的使用以及因开发建设导致的荒野破坏被认为是罪魁祸首。这意味着蜘蛛的整体生存前景和大多数生物一样令人担忧。但保护主义者最关切的是那些因栖息地丧失和碎片化而受到威胁的品种，因为这使它们无法迁徙。", "在英国定期记录的约650种蜘蛛中，大多数在沼泽和荒地中繁衍生息。通常由坚定不移的个人主导的保护行动，通过将部分物种重新引入新区域，帮助它们恢复了种群数量。随着“再野化”如今被坚定地提上环境政策议程，人们希望未来蜘蛛能够自行迁徙，沿着野生动物廊道移动以适应气候变化。", "尽管蜘蛛作为大自然的织网者拥有独特地位，但它们似乎不太可能像蜜蜂、鸟类或蝴蝶那样激发人们同等程度的热情。不过，当它们在这个秋天尽显风采之时，若能有更多动物爱好者认识到蜘蛛令人赞叹的种种美妙之处，不失为一件幸事。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What do we learn about spiders in the UK since the middle ages?", "options": ["They have been generally misconceived.", "They have adversely impacted crop growth.", "They have been a constant reminder of bad luck.", "They have made their presence felt when spinning webs."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Spiders in the UK are almost all harmless. Farmland species perform valuable ecosystem services, by preying on insects that are our competitors for crops. But they are a constant source of human anxieties — with a cultural association with witches and wickedness dating back to the middle ages.", "explanation": "定位至第2段。作者先指出人们对蜘蛛的恐惧普遍且与理性风险评估无关，接着说明英国的蜘蛛几乎全部无害，农田蜘蛛还能捕食害虫、提供宝贵的生态服务；但转折之后又提到，自中世纪以来，蜘蛛在文化上常与女巫和邪恶相联系，一直引发人类焦虑。由此可见，英国蜘蛛长期以来被大众普遍误解，选项A“它们一直遭到普遍误解”符合文意。", "trapNote": "B项正反颠倒，原文指农田蜘蛛捕食争夺农作物的害虫，实则有益于作物生长；D项张冠李戴，蜘蛛织网现身是第1段所述夏末初秋的季节特征，并非“自中世纪以来”的情况；C项将“女巫与邪恶”偷换为“厄运”。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What have spiders been associated with in the UK for centuries?", "options": ["Harm.", "Suffering.", "Evil.", "Aggression."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But they are a constant source of human anxieties — with a cultural association with witches and wickedness dating back to the middle ages.", "explanation": "定位至第2段末句。原文明确指出，蜘蛛一直是人类焦虑的根源，在英国文化中长期与女巫及邪恶（wickedness）紧密相连，且这种文化联想可以追溯到中世纪。题干用“数百年来”转述了“追溯至中世纪”这一时间跨度，考查蜘蛛在当地长期关联的负面意象。选项C“邪恶（Evil）”与原文的“wickedness”构成精准同义替换，故C项为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项正反颠倒，第2段前文明确指出英国蜘蛛几乎全部无害，并非与“伤害”关联；B项偷换概念，原文“sufferers”指受蜘蛛恐惧症折磨的人群，并非指蜘蛛在文化上与“痛苦”相关联；D项“攻击性”文中未提，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What partly accounts for the reduction in spiders' food supply?", "options": ["The long tradition of collecting insects.", "Chemicals used for killing insects.", "Fast reproduction of their competitors.", "The extinction of a lot of wildlife."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The huge reductions in the numbers of flying insects can only mean a reduction in spiders' food supply. A recent landmark study identified a 75% fall in insect populations between 1989 and 2016, with pesticide use thought to be to blame along with the destruction of wild areas for development.", "explanation": "定位至第4段前两句。第1句指出飞虫数量的巨大减少意味着蜘蛛食物来源的减少；第2句紧接着解释原因，提到一项研究发现昆虫种群下降了75%，而杀虫剂的使用（pesticide use）与开发导致的荒野破坏被认为是罪魁祸首。可见，用于灭杀昆虫的化学药剂（即杀虫剂）是蜘蛛食物减少的部分原因，对应选项B，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项张冠李戴，第3段提到收集昆虫的传统解释的是为何英国蝴蝶研究最为充分，与蜘蛛食物减少无关；D项偷换概念，原文指“开发破坏荒野区域”，而非“大量野生动物灭绝”；C项原文未提及竞争对手繁殖迅速，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the passage say is conservationists' biggest worry?", "options": ["A variety of spiders are threatened due to pollution of marshes and wasteland.", "Certain species of spiders are endangered due to loss of their natural homes.", "An increasing number of spiders are being killed by deadly pesticides.", "More and more spider species are found losing their ability to migrate."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "But conservationists are most concerned about those varieties that are threatened due to habitat loss and fragmentation, which makes it impossible for them to migrate.", "explanation": "定位至第4段末句。该句通过转折指出，尽管蜘蛛整体前景堪忧，但保护主义者最担忧的是那些因栖息地丧失及碎片化而面临威胁的蜘蛛品种，因为这种状况使其无法完成迁徙。选项B中的特定蜘蛛物种、面临濒危威胁以及失去自然家园，分别精准同义转述了原文中的相关品种、受到威胁以及栖息地丧失，故B项为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，第5段提及大多数蜘蛛栖息于沼泽和荒地，但第4段指明受威胁的原因是“栖息地丧失与碎片化”，而非“污染”；D项曲解文意，原文指栖息地碎片化阻断了迁徙路径，而非蜘蛛自身丧失迁徙能力；C项无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What wish does the author express close to the end of the passage?", "options": ["More people would recognise spiders' unique status in the ecosystem.", "People would show greater enthusiasm for spiders than for butterflies.", "There would be sufficient corridors for spiders to move along.", "There would be more people appreciating spiders' splendour."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "But as they reveal themselves in all their splendour this autumn, it would be a good thing if more animal lovers recognised the ways in which spiders are simply terrific.", "explanation": "定位至文章最后一段末句。作者首先指出蜘蛛不太可能获得像蜜蜂、鸟类或蝴蝶那样的人气，随后笔锋一转表达了自己的期盼：当蜘蛛在今秋展现全部风采之时（in all their splendour），若能有更多动物爱好者认识到蜘蛛令人赞叹之处（simply terrific），将是一件好事。选项D“有更多人欣赏蜘蛛的魅力风采”精准契合这一愿望，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项张冠李戴，前句指蜘蛛“作为自然织网者的独特地位”，并非“生态系统中的地位”，且属让步而非作者心愿；B项与首句“难获同等热情”正反颠倒；C项位置不符，廊道希望见于第5段而非结尾。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 固定装置；常见的人或物，常客", "note": "熟词僻义：本义指“固定装置”，但在文化语境中（a familiar fixture of...）指“常见元素、必不可少的一部分”。", "word": "fixture"}, {"gloss": "n. 邪恶，恶劣行为", "note": "第2题直接对应词：形容词 wicked 意为“邪恶的、坏的”，在阅读中常与 evil 构成同义替换。", "word": "wickedness"}, {"gloss": "n. 地标，里程碑；adj. 具有里程碑意义的", "note": "学术研究高频搭配：a landmark study 指“具有里程碑意义的研究”，常作为文章引出关键数据的信号。", "word": "landmark"}, {"gloss": "n. 碎片化，破碎，分裂", "note": "生态与环境类核心词：由 fragment（碎片）派生而来，habitat fragmentation 指人类开发导致的“栖息地碎片化”。", "word": "fragmentation"}, {"gloss": "n. 壮丽，光彩，辉煌（英式拼写）", "note": "英式拼写与结尾考点：文章源自英国媒体，注意 -our 拼写及 -ise 动词拼写（如 splendour, recognised），在末题选项中原词复现。", "word": "splendour"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Yet while the spider is a familiar fixture of nursery poems or songs and Halloween decorations, its relationship with humans is complicated.", "point": "while在句首或Yet后常表让步（“尽管、虽然”），构成“虽然……但是……”的语篇转折信号，提示主句才是作者核心观点。", "structure": "while引导让步状语从句，说明蜘蛛在文化中的常见形象；主句为主系表结构，点明蜘蛛与人类关系的复杂性，引出下文分析。", "zh": "然而，尽管蜘蛛是童谣儿歌和万圣节装饰中常见的元素，它与人类的关系却十分复杂。"}, {"en": "A recent landmark study identified a 75% fall in insect populations between 1989 and 2016, with pesticide use thought to be to blame along with the destruction of wild areas for development.", "point": "with复合结构作原因或补充说明状语，以及短语be to blame（应受责备、是原因所在）的主动形式表被动含义用法。", "structure": "主句为A recent landmark study identified a 75% fall...；with引导复合结构（with + 名词 + 过去分词短语thought to be to blame）作伴随或原因状语，其中along with连接两个并列诱因。", "zh": "近期一项里程碑式的研究发现，1989年至2016年间昆虫种群数量下降了75%，而杀虫剂的使用以及因开发建设导致的荒野破坏被认为是罪魁祸首。"}, {"en": "With rewilding now firmly on the environmental policy agenda, the hope is that in future, spiders will be enabled to migrate by themselves, adapting to climate change by moving along wildlife corridors.", "point": "主句“the hope is that...”引导表语从句表达未来展望，以及现在分词短语adapting to...作伴随结果状语的句法衔接。", "structure": "With引导复合结构作背景状语；主句为the hope is that...（that引导表语从句）；从句末尾adapting to climate change为现在分词短语作伴随状语。", "zh": "随着“再野化”如今被坚定地提上环境政策议程，人们希望未来蜘蛛能够自行迁徙，沿着野生动物廊道移动以适应气候变化。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1题概括推断：人们对无害有益的蜘蛛盲目恐惧 → 蜘蛛一直遭到普遍误解", "option": "generally misconceived", "original": "unrelated to any rational assessment of risk ... almost all harmless ... perform valuable ecosystem services"}, {"note": "第2题双维替换：wickedness（邪恶）→ Evil；dating back to the middle ages → for centuries", "option": "associated with ... Evil ... for centuries", "original": "a cultural association with witches and wickedness dating back to the middle ages"}, {"note": "第3题具象转述：pesticide（杀虫剂）→ 杀虫化学药剂；along with 对应“部分原因”", "option": "Chemicals used for killing insects ... partly accounts for", "original": "pesticide use thought to be to blame along with the destruction of wild areas"}, {"note": "第4题多词精准替换：varieties → species；threatened → endangered；habitat → natural homes", "option": "biggest worry ... Certain species ... endangered due to loss of their natural homes", "original": "most concerned about those varieties that are threatened due to habitat loss"}, {"note": "第5题态度愿景转述：希望更多人认可蜘蛛的精彩之处 → 更多人欣赏蜘蛛的风采", "option": "more people appreciating spiders' splendour", "original": "as they reveal themselves in all their splendour ... it would be a good thing if more animal lovers recognised the ways in which spiders are simply terrific"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202306-s1-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 六级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "AI 时代：被算法重塑的人性", "subtitle": "科技伦理 · 人工智能对人类判断力与不可预测性的影响", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 451, "paragraphs": ["Technology is never a neutral tool for achieving human ends. Technological innovations reshape people as they use these innovations to control their environment. Artificial intelligence, for example, is altering humanity.", "While the term AI conjures up anxieties about killer robots or catastrophic levels of unemployment, there are other, deeper implications. As AI increasingly shapes the human experience, how does this change what it means to be human? Central to the problem is a person's capacity to make choices, particularly judgments that have moral implications.", "Aristotle argued that the capacity for making practical judgments depends on regularly making them — on habit and practice. We see the emergence of machines as substitute judges in a variety of everyday contexts as a potential threat to people learning how to effectively exercise judgment themselves.", "In the workplace, managers routinely make decisions about who to hire or fire and which loan to approve, to name a few. These are areas where algorithmic (算法的) prescription is replacing human judgment, and so people who might have had the chance to develop practical judgment in these areas no longer will.", "Recommendation engines, which are increasingly prevalent intermediaries in people's consumption of culture, may serve to constrain choice and minimize luck. By presenting consumers with algorithmically selected choices of what to watch, read, stream and visit next, companies are replacing human taste with machine taste. In one sense, this is helpful. After all, machines can survey a wider range of choices than any individual is likely to have the time or energy to do on their own.", "At the same time, though, this selection is optimizing for what people are likely to prefer based on what they've preferred in the past. We think there is some risk that people's options will be constrained by their past in a new and unanticipated way.", "As machine learning algorithms improve and as they train on more extensive data sets, larger parts of everyday life are likely to become utterly predictable. The predictions are going to get better and better, and they will ultimately make common experiences more efficient and pleasant.", "Algorithms could soon — if they don't already — have a better idea about which show you'd like to watch next and which job candidate you should hire than you do. One day, humans may even find a way for machines to make these decisions without some of the biases that humans typically display.", "But to the extent that unpredictability is part of how people understand themselves and part of what people like about themselves, humanity is in the process of losing something significant. As they become more and more predictable, the creatures inhabiting the increasingly AI-mediated world will become less and less like us."], "translations": ["技术从来都不是实现人类目的的中立工具。技术创新在人们利用它们控制环境的同时，也在重塑着人类本身。例如，人工智能正在改变人类。", "虽然“人工智能”一词会让人联想到杀手机器人或灾难性的大规模失业，但它还有其他更深层的影响。随着人工智能日益塑造人类体验，这会如何改变“人”的定义？问题的核心在于人做出选择的能力，尤其是那些具有道德意义的判断。", "亚里士多德曾指出，做出实际判断的能力取决于经常去做判断——即依靠习惯与实践。我们认为，在各种日常情境中，机器作为替代评判者的出现，对人们学习如何有效行使自主判断力构成了潜在威胁。", "在职场中，管理者日常需要决定雇用或解雇谁、批准哪笔贷款等等。在这些领域，算法指令正在取代人类判断，因此原本有机会在这些方面培养实际判断力的人，今后将不再有这样的机会。", "在人们的文化消费中，推荐引擎作为越来越普遍的中介，可能会限制选择并减少偶遇之幸。通过向消费者推送由算法筛选出的下一部观看、阅读、收听及游览内容，企业正在用机器品味取代人类品味。从某种意义上说，这很有帮助。毕竟，机器能够浏览比任何个人有时间或精力独自搜寻的更广泛的选择。", "然而与此同时，这种筛选机制正根据人们过去的偏好来优化他们未来可能偏爱的内容。我们认为存在一定风险，即人们的选择将以一种始料未及的新方式被自己的过往所束缚。", "随着机器学习算法的不断改进以及在更庞大数据集上的训练，日常生活的越来越大部分可能会变得完全可预测。这些预测将变得越来越精准，最终使普通体验变得更高效、更愉悦。", "如果现在还没有的话，算法很快就会比你更清楚你接下来想看哪部剧、应该雇用哪位求职者。有朝一日，人类甚至可能找到办法，让机器在做出这些决定时避免人类通常会表现出的某些偏见。", "然而，既然不可预测性在某种程度上正是人们自我认知的方式，也是人们欣赏自身特质的一部分，那么人类正在失去某种重要的东西。随着人类变得越来越可预测，生活在日益由人工智能主导的世界里的生灵，将会变得越来越不像我们。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about the deeper implications of AI?", "options": ["It is causing catastrophic levels of unemployment.", "It is doing physical harm to human operators.", "It is altering moral judgments.", "It is reshaping humanity."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "While the term AI conjures up anxieties about killer robots or catastrophic levels of unemployment, there are other, deeper implications. As AI increasingly shapes the human experience, how does this change what it means to be human?", "explanation": "定位题干关键词deeper implications至第2段。该段先用While让步引出杀手机器人与失业焦虑，随后点明AI更深层的影响在于“塑造人类体验”并改变“生而为人”的意义（what it means to be human）。这直接承接第1段首句与尾句提出的“技术创新重塑人类”（reshape people）及“AI正在改变人类”（altering humanity）。选项D的reshaping humanity精准同义转述上述核心表述，因此入选。", "trapNote": "A项“灾难性失业”与B项歪曲“杀手机器人”均属表层焦虑而非深层影响（偷换概念）；C项将altering与moral强行拼接，原文仅指威胁做道德判断的“能力”，非改变判断本身（无中生有）。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the consequence of algorithmic prescription replacing human judgment?", "options": ["People lose the chance to cultivate the ability to make practical judgments.", "People are prevented from participating in making major decisions in the workplace.", "Managers no longer have the chance to decide which loan to approve.", "Managers do not need to take the trouble to determine who to hire or fire."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "These are areas where algorithmic (算法的) prescription is replacing human judgment, and so people who might have had the chance to develop practical judgment in these areas no longer will.", "explanation": "依据题干“算法指令取代人类判断”的后果，定位到第4段末尾。该段先列举管理者在招聘、解雇和审批贷款中的日常决策，随后指出在这些由算法指令取代人类判断的领域，“原本有机会在这些方面培养实际判断力的人，今后将不再有这样的机会”。选项A中的“失去机会”对应原文的“不再有机会”，“培养做出实际判断的能力”精准转述了原文中的“培养实际判断力”（develop practical judgment），逻辑与语义完全契合。", "trapNote": "B项将“无法培养判断力”篡改为“被阻止参与重大决策”（偷换概念）；C项仅截取批贷款并歪曲为管理者丧失决策权（以偏概全）；D项“省去费心决策的麻烦”将作者视作危机的影响粉饰为便利（正反颠倒）。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What may result from increasing application of recommendation engines in our consumption of culture?", "options": ["Consumers will have much limited choice.", "Consumers will actually enjoy better luck.", "It will be easier to decide on what to enjoy.", "Humans will develop tastes similar to machines'."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Recommendation engines, which are increasingly prevalent intermediaries in people's consumption of culture, may serve to constrain choice and minimize luck.", "explanation": "通过题干关键词“推荐引擎”与“文化消费”定位至第5段首句。该句明确指出，在人们的文化消费中日益普遍的推荐引擎“可能会限制选择并减少偶遇之幸”。此外，第6段末尾也进一步强调，人们的选择会以未曾预料的方式被过往偏好所“束缚”。选项A中“消费者的选择将大受限制”正是对原文constrain choice及options will be constrained的高度浓缩与同义转述，因此确定为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项“享受更好的运气”与第5段“减少运气”意思完全相反（正反颠倒）；C项把机器“替代人类搜寻更多选项”偷换为“更容易决定享受什么”（偷换概念）；D项将“机器品味取代人类品味”曲解为“人类养成类似机器的品味”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is likely to happen to larger parts of our daily life as machine learning algorithms improve?", "options": ["They will turn out to be more pleasant.", "They will repeat our past experience.", "They can be completely anticipated.", "They may become better and better."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "As machine learning algorithms improve and as they train on more extensive data sets, larger parts of everyday life are likely to become utterly predictable.", "explanation": "依据题干“随着机器学习算法改进，日常生活的大部分将会怎样”，定位至第7段首句。该句指出，随着算法不断改进并在更庞大数据集上训练，日常生活的更大部分“很可能会变得完全可预测”。选项C中completely对应原文副词utterly（完全地），anticipated（可预料的）精准同义替换形容词predictable（可预测的），结构与句意一一对应，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "D项“变得越来越好”与A项“变得更愉悦”均属张冠李戴：第7段次句指出变得越来越好的是“算法预测”（predictions），而更高效愉悦的是“日常体验”，并非回答题干所指的“生活大部分会如何”（偷换主语）。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why does the author say the creatures living in the more and more AI-mediated world will become increasingly unlike us?", "options": ["They will have lost the most significant human element of being intelligent.", "They will no longer possess the human characteristic of being unpredictable.", "They will not be able to understand themselves as we can do today.", "They will be deprived of what their predecessors were proud of about themselves."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "But to the extent that unpredictability is part of how people understand themselves and part of what people like about themselves, humanity is in the process of losing something significant. As they become more and more predictable, the creatures inhabiting the increasingly AI-mediated world will become less and less like us.", "explanation": "依据题干“为什么作者说生活在AI主导世界里的生灵会越来越不像我们”，定位至文章末段。尾句明确给出原因：正是由于他们“变得越来越可预测”。结合首句可知，不可预测性本是人类自我认知及自我欣赏的重要特质，而人类正在失去它。选项B“他们将不再拥有不可预测这一人类特征”精确概括了这种特质丧失的因果逻辑，是原文的同义转换。", "trapNote": "A项擅自增添“智慧中最重要的人类要素”，原文未将不可预测性归为智慧（无中生有）；C项曲解为“无法像今人一样理解自己”（过度推理）；D项将“喜欢自身的地方”夸大为“前人引以为傲之处”（偷换概念）。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "使人联想到，使浮现于脑海", "note": "常用搭配；原意为“变魔术/召唤”，在阅读中常引出某概念令人联想到的常见印象或担忧（常与 while 引导的让步背景连用）。", "word": "conjure up"}, {"gloss": "指令，规定，方案", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“处方/药方”，本文指算法给出的“预设规则/指令”（algorithmic prescription）。", "word": "prescription"}, {"gloss": "中介，中间人，媒介", "note": "名词/形容词兼类，六级高频社会科技词汇；本文指推荐引擎在消费者与文化产品之间充当的“中介”。", "word": "intermediary"}, {"gloss": "限制，约束，束缚", "note": "高频核心动词，常同义替换为 limit / restrict；注意与 restrain（抑制）区分。", "word": "constrain"}, {"gloss": "优化，使最优化", "note": "动词，optimize for... 表示“针对……进行优化”，常出现在科技与算法类文章中。", "word": "optimize"}, {"gloss": "完全地，彻底地", "note": "程度副词，等同于 completely / totally；命题常将其同义替换为 completely 作细节定位标志。", "word": "utterly"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Recommendation engines, which are increasingly prevalent intermediaries in people's consumption of culture, may serve to constrain choice and minimize luck.", "point": "考点：非限制性定语从句插入主谓之间隔断主干（主语 engines + 谓语 may serve to），以及并列不定式宾语 constrain choice and minimize luck 对应细节题答案。", "structure": "主句 Recommendation engines may serve to constrain choice and minimize luck；which 引导非限制性定语从句修饰先行词 Recommendation engines。", "zh": "在人们的文化消费中，推荐引擎作为越来越普遍的中介，可能会限制选择并减少偶遇之幸。"}, {"en": "These are areas where algorithmic (算法的) prescription is replacing human judgment, and so people who might have had the chance to develop practical judgment in these areas no longer will.", "point": "考点：句尾 no longer will 构成助动词后的省略结构（承前省略 have the chance to develop...），是理解第47题因果后果的关键。", "structure": "and so 连接并列因果句：前句为 where 引导的定语从句修饰 areas；后句主干为 people no longer will [have the chance]，其中嵌入 who 引导的定语从句。", "zh": "在这些领域，算法指令正在取代人类判断，因此原本有机会在这些方面培养实际判断力的人，今后将不再有这样的机会。"}, {"en": "But to the extent that unpredictability is part of how people understand themselves and part of what people like about themselves, humanity is in the process of losing something significant.", "point": "考点：固定句式 to the extent that（在……程度上/既然……），以及 how/what 引导的宾语从句并列作介词 of 的宾语。", "structure": "to the extent that... 引导程度/原因状语从句，内部由 and 连接两个表语成分（part of how... 与 part of what...）；主句为 humanity is in the process of losing something significant。", "zh": "然而，既然不可预测性在某种程度上正是人们自我认知的方式，也是人们欣赏自身特质的一部分，那么人类正在失去某种重要的东西。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第46题同义替换：第1段的 reshape people、altering humanity 与第2段的 change what it means to be human 整合为 reshaping humanity。", "option": "reshaping humanity", "original": "altering humanity / change what it means to be human"}, {"note": "第47题同义替换：no longer will（省略 have the chance）对应 lose the chance；develop 替换为 cultivate the ability to make。", "option": "People lose the chance to cultivate the ability to make practical judgments.", "original": "people who might have had the chance to develop practical judgment ... no longer will"}, {"note": "第48题同义替换：constrain choice（限制选择）及第6段的 options will be constrained 同义转述为 have much limited choice。", "option": "have much limited choice", "original": "may serve to constrain choice"}, {"note": "第49题同义替换：程度副词 utterly（完全地）替换为 completely；predictable（可预测的）替换为 anticipated（可预料的）。", "option": "completely anticipated", "original": "utterly predictable"}, {"note": "第50题同义替换：结合“失去不可预测性”而变得越来越可预测，转述为不再拥有“不可预测”这一人类特征。", "option": "no longer possess the human characteristic of being unpredictable", "original": "As they become more and more predictable ... become less and less like us"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202306-s1-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 六级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "美国阅读教学之争与自然拼读法", "subtitle": "教育政策 · 自然拼读与全语言教学法的“阅读战争”", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 445, "paragraphs": ["Phonics, which involves sounding out words syllable (音节) by syllable, is the best way to teach children to read. But in many classrooms, this can be a dirty word. So much so that some teachers have had to sneak phonics teaching materials into the classroom. Most American children are taught to read in a way that study after study has found to be wrong.", "The consequences of this are striking. Less than half of all American adults were proficient readers in 2017. American fourth graders rank 15th on the Progress in International Literacy Study, an international exam.", "America is stuck in a debate about teaching children to read that has been going on for decades. Some advocate teaching symbol-sound relationships (the sound k can be spelled as c, k, ck, or ch), known as phonics. Others support an immersive approach (using pictures of a cat to learn the word cat), known as “whole language”. Most teachers today, almost three out of four according to a survey by the EdWeek Research Centre in 2019, use a mix called \"balanced literacy\". This combination of methods is ineffective. \"You can't sprinkle in a little phonics,\" says Tenette Smith, executive director of elementary education and reading at Mississippi's education department. “It has to be systematic and explicitly taught.”", "Mississippi, often behind in social policy, has set an example here. In a state once notorious for its low reading scores, the Mississippi state legislature passed new literacy standards in 2013. Since then Mississippi has seen remarkable gains. Its fourth graders have moved from 49th (out of 50 states) to 29th on the National Assessment of Educational Progress, a nationwide exam. In 2019 it was the only state to improve its scores. For the first time since measurement began, Mississippi's pupils are now average readers, a remarkable achievement in such a poor state.", "Mississippi's success is attributed to implementing reading methods supported by a body of research known as the science of reading. In 1997 Congress requested the National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and the Department of Education to convene a National Reading Panel to end the “reading wars” and synthesize the evidence. The panel found that phonics, along with explicit instruction in phonemic (音位的) awareness, fluency and comprehension, worked best.", "Yet over two decades on, “balanced literacy” is still being taught in classrooms. But advances in statistics and brain imaging have disproved the whole-language method. To the teacher who is a proficient reader, literacy seems like a natural process that requires educated guessing, rather than the deliberate process emphasized by phonics. Teachers can imagine that they learned to read through osmosis (潜移默化) when they were children. Without proper training, they bring this to classrooms."], "translations": ["自然拼读法指的是逐个音节拼读单词，是教儿童阅读的最佳方法。但在许多教室里，这个词却成了一个忌讳。甚至到了有些教师不得不偷偷将自然拼读教材带进课堂的地步。大多数美国儿童正在以一种接连被研究证明是错误的方式学习阅读。", "这种做法的后果十分惊人。2017年，只有不到一半的美国成年人是熟练的阅读者。在“国际阅读素养进展研究”这一国际测试中，美国四年级学生仅排名第15位。", "美国在教儿童阅读的方法上陷入了一场持续数十年的争论。一些人主张教授符号与发音之间的对应关系（例如k音可以拼写为c、k、ck或ch），即“自然拼读法”。另一些人则支持沉浸式方法（例如用猫的图片来学习cat这个词），即“全语言教学法”。根据教育周刊研究中心2019年的一项调查，如今近四分之三的教师采用一种名为“平衡读写法”的混合模式。这种方法的组合收效甚微。“你不能只点缀一点自然拼读，”密西西比州教育部初等教育与阅读执行主任特内特·史密斯说，“它必须进行系统且明确的教学。”", "在社会政策方面常常落后的密西西比州，在此事上却树立了榜样。这个曾因阅读成绩低下而臭名昭著的州，其州议会于2013年通过了新的识字标准。自那以后，密西西比州取得了显著进步。该州四年级学生在全国性考试“美国国家教育进步评估”中的排名，从全美（50个州中的）第49位跃升至第29位。2019年，它是唯一一个成绩有所提升的州。自开展测评以来，密西西比州小学生的阅读能力首次达到全国平均水平，这对于这样一个贫困州而言是一项了不起的成就。", "密西西比州的成功归因于实施了得到“阅读科学”这一系列研究支持的阅读教学方法。1997年，美国国会要求国家儿童健康与人类发育研究所及教育部召集成立国家阅读专家小组，以结束“阅读战争”并整合研究证据。该小组发现，自然拼读法结合在音位意识、阅读流畅度和阅读理解方面的明确教学，效果最佳。", "然而二十多年过去了，“平衡读写法”仍在课堂上沿用。但统计学与脑成像技术的进步已经证伪了全语言教学法。对于已是熟练阅读者的教师而言，读写似乎是一个需要有根据地猜测的自然过程，而非自然拼读法所强调的刻意训练过程。教师们可能会想象自己小时候也是通过潜移默化学会阅读的。由于缺乏适当培训，他们便把这种观念带进了课堂。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about phonics in many American classrooms?", "options": ["It is ill reputed.", "It is mostly misapplied.", "It is arbitrarily excluded.", "It is misrepresented."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "But in many classrooms, this can be a dirty word. So much so that some teachers have had to sneak phonics teaching materials into the classroom.", "explanation": "依据题干定位词“在许多美国教室里的自然拼读法”，直接锁定第1段第2、3句。原文指出它在许多教室里成了“一个脏词/忌讳词”，一些教师甚至不得不偷偷把相关教材带进课堂。在英语习语中，该表达指某事物声名狼藉、令人避之不及或备受排斥。选项A中“名声不佳”精准对应了该习语的比喻义及教师不得不“偷偷带入”的语境，因此为正确答案。", "trapNote": "C项“被武断地排除”看似贴近，但第3段指出近四分之三教师会在混合法中“点缀一点”自然拼读，并非完全排除（以偏概全）；B项“大多被误用”与D项“被曲解”在首段均无对应依据（无中生有）。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What has America been witnessing for decades?", "options": ["An obsession with innovating teaching methodologies of reading.", "An enduring debate over the approach to teaching children to read.", "An increasing concern with many children's inadequacy in literacy.", "An ever-forceful advocacy of a combined method for teaching reading."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "America is stuck in a debate about teaching children to read that has been going on for decades.", "explanation": "依据题干时间状语“数十年来”与核心事件定位至第3段首句。该句明确表述：美国陷入了一场关于如何教儿童阅读的争论，且这场争论已经持续了数十年。选项B中“持久的争论”精准同义转述“持续了数十年的争论”，“教儿童阅读的方法”对应“关于教儿童阅读”，句意完全吻合，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“热衷于创新阅读教学法”曲解了争论的实质（无中生有）；C项“对儿童读写能力不足的担忧加剧”偏离第3段主旨，第2段仅客观列出低分数据；D项“对混合方法的有力倡导”与“混合法收效甚微”相悖。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why does Tenette Smith think a combination of teaching methods is ineffective?", "options": ["Elementary school children will be frustrated when taught with several methods combined.", "Phonics has to be systematically applied and clearly taught to achieve the desired effect.", "Sprinkling in a little phonics deters the progress of even adequately motivated children.", "Balanced literacy fails to sustain children's interest in developing a good reading habit."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "\"You can't sprinkle in a little phonics,\" says Tenette Smith, executive director of elementary education and reading at Mississippi's education department. “It has to be systematic and explicitly taught.”", "explanation": "依据人名与“教学法组合无效”定位至第3段后半部分。史密斯指出“不能只零星点缀一点自然拼读”，并紧接着解释原因：“它必须得到系统而明确的教学”。选项B中“系统地应用”对应原文形容词“系统的”，“清晰地教授”对应“明确地教授”，“才能达到预期效果”反推“混合点缀无效”的逻辑，完整还原了她的观点。", "trapNote": "A项“小学生会感到沮丧”、C项“阻碍积极儿童的进步”及D项“无法维持良好阅读习惯的兴趣”均在史密斯发言及上下文中毫无提及，属于典型的脱离原文主观臆测（无中生有）。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say Mississippi's success is attributed to?", "options": ["Convening a National Reading Panel to synthesize research evidence.", "Placing sufficient emphasis upon both fluency and comprehension.", "Adopting scientifically grounded approaches to teaching reading.", "Obtaining support from Congress to upgrade teaching methods."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Mississippi's success is attributed to implementing reading methods supported by a body of research known as the science of reading.", "explanation": "依据题干“密西西比州的成功归因于什么”，直接定位至第5段首句。该句明确指出，该州的成功归因于“实施了得到‘阅读科学’这一系列研究支持的阅读方法”。选项C中“采用”对应原文“实施”，“有科学依据的阅读教学方法”精确转述了“得到‘阅读科学’研究支持的阅读方法”，是原文信息的直接改写。", "trapNote": "A项“召集专家小组”和D项“获国会支持”均张冠李戴：第5段第2句指1997年美国国会要求联邦机构成立小组，并非密西西比州的举措；B项仅提及流畅度与理解，遗漏了最核心的自然拼读与音位意识（以偏概全）。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What have advances in statistics and brain imaging proved ineffective?", "options": ["The teaching of symbol-sound relationships.", "Explicit instruction in phonemic awareness.", "Efforts to end the reading wars.", "The immersive approach."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "But advances in statistics and brain imaging have disproved the whole-language method.", "explanation": "依据题干关键词“统计学与脑成像的进步”定位至第6段第2句，该句明确指出这些进步“证伪了全语言教学法”。随后回溯第3段第3句可知，全语言教学法正是原文所说的“沉浸式方法”（例如借助猫的图片来学习单词）。选项D将第6段的“全语言教学法”跨段同义替换为第3段的“沉浸式方法”，考查跨段信息整合能力，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“符号与发音关系教学”即自然拼读法，B项“音位意识明确教学”则是第5段专家小组认定效果最佳的方法，二者均与“无效”正反颠倒；C项“结束阅读战争的努力”是第5段背景，并非统计学证伪的对象（偷换概念）。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "自然拼读法（根据字母及字母组合发音规律拼读）", "note": "教育类文章核心专有名词，作单数概念使用，注意与音位（phoneme / phonemic）及拼音体系区分。", "word": "phonics"}, {"gloss": "偷偷带入，悄悄做", "note": "动词，sneak sth. into... 表示“把……偷偷带进某处”，在细节描写中常暗示某种做法受排斥或遭禁止。", "word": "sneak"}, {"gloss": "零星点缀，少量加入", "note": "熟词僻义：本义为“洒、撒（水/调料）”，本文中 sprinkle in a little phonics 引申为“零星掺入一点拼读教学”。", "word": "sprinkle"}, {"gloss": "召集，召开（会议、委员会等）", "note": "正式用语，六级新闻与政策文本高频动词，常见搭配为 convene a panel/meeting。", "word": "convene"}, {"gloss": "综合，整合（信息、证据等）", "note": "学术阅读高频词，指把零散研究证据汇整成统一结论；注意与 analyze（分析）区分。", "word": "synthesize"}, {"gloss": "证伪，反驳，证明……有误", "note": "由否定前缀 dis- + prove 构成，表示用证据推翻某种假说或方法，常用于科学论证段落转折处。", "word": "disprove"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Some advocate teaching symbol-sound relationships (the sound k can be spelled as c, k, ck, or ch), known as phonics.", "point": "考点：过去分词短语 known as... 在六级教育科普文中极常用于给出专有名词定义，常与下一句的对比定义形成跨段同义替换考点。", "structure": "主干为 Some advocate teaching symbol-sound relationships；括号内为举例说明；过去分词短语 known as phonics 作后置定语修饰前面的教学法。", "zh": "一些人主张教授符号与发音之间的对应关系（例如k音可以拼写为c、k、ck或ch），即“自然拼读法”。"}, {"en": "In 1997 Congress requested the National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and the Department of Education to convene a National Reading Panel to end the “reading wars” and synthesize the evidence.", "point": "考点：区分联邦层面（Congress 1997年举措）与州层面（Mississippi 2013年举措）的主体差异，防止做第54题时张冠李戴。", "structure": "主干为 Congress requested A and B to convene C；不定式短语 to end... and synthesize... 作目的状语，说明召集专家小组的意图。", "zh": "1997年，美国国会要求国家儿童健康与人类发育研究所及教育部召集成立国家阅读专家小组，以结束“阅读战争”并整合研究证据。"}, {"en": "To the teacher who is a proficient reader, literacy seems like a natural process that requires educated guessing, rather than the deliberate process emphasized by phonics.", "point": "考点：rather than 连接前后对比概念（natural process vs. deliberate process），揭示教师排斥自然拼读法的深层认知原因。", "structure": "介词短语 To the teacher（含 who 定语从句）引出主观视角；主干为 literacy seems like a natural process（后接 that 定语从句），rather than 引出对比对象（后接过去分词定语 emphasized by phonics）。", "zh": "对于已是熟练阅读者的教师而言，读写似乎是一个需要有根据地猜测的自然过程，而非自然拼读法所强调的刻意训练过程。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第51题同义替换：习语 a dirty word（忌讳词/遭人反感的词）结合教师偷偷带教材，在选项中转为 ill reputed（名声不好的）。", "option": "ill reputed", "original": "a dirty word"}, {"note": "第52题同义替换：going on for decades 浓缩为形容词 enduring（持久的）；about 对应 over the approach to。", "option": "An enduring debate over the approach to teaching children to read.", "original": "a debate about teaching children to read that has been going on for decades"}, {"note": "第53题同义替换：systematic 转为副词 systematically applied，explicitly 替换为 clearly，并补出有效前提。", "option": "Phonics has to be systematically applied and clearly taught to achieve the desired effect.", "original": "It has to be systematic and explicitly taught."}, {"note": "第54题同义替换：implementing 替换为 adopting，supported by the science of reading 概括为 scientifically grounded。", "option": "Adopting scientifically grounded approaches to teaching reading.", "original": "implementing reading methods supported by a body of research known as the science of reading"}, {"note": "第55题跨段替换：第6段的 disproved 对应题干 proved ineffective，whole-language 跨段对应第3段的 immersive approach。", "option": "proved ineffective: The immersive approach", "original": "disproved the whole-language method (an immersive approach)"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202306-s2-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 六级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 六级真题 第2套 Passage One", "title": "抵制儿童广告：警惕消费主义侵蚀", "subtitle": "社会文化 · 儿童权益与商业伦理", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 457, "paragraphs": ["How on earth did we come to this? We protect our children obsessively from every harm; we scrutinize every carer, teacher or doctor with whom they come into contact. Yet despite all this, one group, which in no way has their best interests at heart, has almost unconstrained access.", "We seem to take it for granted that advertisers and marketers are allowed to condition even the youngest children. Before children have even developed a proper sense of their own identity, or learned to handle money, they're encouraged to associate status and self-worth with stuff, and to look to external things such as fame and wealth for validation. We're turning out little consumers rather than young citizens who will value themselves for what they contribute to the society in which they live.", "We've reached this point so gradually that many of us have never questioned it. It's crept up on us in the 60 years since advertisers started to target the young and found that they could recruit them to a commercial assault on their parents. We've come to know it as \"pester power\" or the ability of children to pressure parents to make certain purchases.", "Many psychologists, child development experts and educators point to research suggesting that this emerging cradle-to-grave consumerism is contributing to growing rates of low self-esteem, depression and other forms of mental illness.", "Not all psychologists agree. There're plenty working hand in glove with a £12bn-a-year industry that has turned the manipulation of adult emotions and desires into an art form — often literally. It's also one that's forever developing new ways to persuade our children to desire material possessions, and because of advertisements' viral effect they only need to infect a few to reach the many. Advertising and marketing can serve a useful purpose for children. Marketing may help socialize children as consumers, inform them about products, and help them carve out unique identities as they reach adulthood.", "Then, should we ban all advertising aimed at young children? I say yes.", "Of course there'll be plenty of objections to an outright ban on advertising to the under-11s. There'll be those who argue that would be a breach of freedom of speech and infringe the rights of corporations to brainwash little children into demanding their products.", "Most parents hate what advertising does to their children, but we do have the power to end it and let our children grow up free from many of the pressures of consumerism until they're old enough to make their own decisions. And though advertising is only part of an all-pervasive (无处不在的) marketing culture we need to make a start somewhere. Let's ban all advertising targeting children of primary school age and younger now."], "translations": ["我们究竟怎么会落到这步田地？我们近乎偏执地保护孩子免受一切伤害；对与他们接触的每一位看护人、老师或医生都严格审查。然而尽管如此，有一个绝非以孩子最大利益为出发点的群体，却几乎可以不受约束地接触他们。", "我们似乎理所当然地认为，广告商和营销人员被允许去驯化哪怕年纪最小的孩子。在孩子们甚至尚未形成健全的自我认同感或学会理财之前，他们就被诱导将地位和自我价值与物质挂钩，并向名望、财富等外在事物寻求认可。我们正在培养一个个小消费者，而不是那些会因自己对所生活社会的贡献而珍视自身价值的年轻公民。", "我们走到这一步的过程如此缓慢，以至于许多人从未对此提出质疑。自从60年前广告商开始瞄准年轻群体、并发现可以招募他们向父母发起商业攻势以来，这种现象便悄然向我们袭来。我们后来称之为“缠磨购买力”（pester power），即儿童向父母施压促使其进行特定消费的能力。", "许多心理学家、儿童发展专家和教育工作者指出，研究表明这种新兴的“从摇篮到坟墓”的消费主义正在推高自卑、抑郁及其他精神疾病的发病率。", "并非所有心理学家都赞同这一观点。有大把心理学家与这个年产值高达120亿英镑的行业沆瀣一气，该行业已将操纵成年人的情感与欲望变成了一门艺术——往往是字面意义上的艺术。这一行业也在不断开发新花样来诱导我们的孩子渴望物质财富，而且由于广告具有病毒式传播效应，他们只需感染少数人就能触及大众。广告和营销对儿童而言也能发挥有益的作用。营销或许有助于让孩子作为消费者融入社会，让他们了解产品信息，并在步入成年时帮助他们塑造独特的个人身份。", "那么，我们应该禁止所有针对幼儿的广告吗？我的回答是肯定的。", "当然，彻底禁止面向11岁以下儿童投放广告的举措会遭到诸多反对。会有人辩称这将违反言论自由，并侵犯企业给幼童洗脑、诱使其索要自家产品的权利。", "大多数父母厌恶广告对孩子产生的影响，但我们确实有能力终结这一切，让孩子在成长过程中免受消费主义的诸多压力，直到他们长大到足以自己做决定为止。尽管广告只是无处不在的营销文化的一部分，但我们需要从某个地方迈出第一步。让我们现在就禁止所有针对小学及以下年龄段儿童的广告吧。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which group of people does the author say has almost unrestricted access to children?", "options": ["Advertisers.", "Carers.", "Teachers.", "Doctors."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Yet despite all this, one group, which in no way has their best interests at heart, has almost unconstrained access.", "explanation": "本题考查细节定位与上下文指代。第1段指出父母对与孩子接触的看护人、老师和医生都严加审查，随后以Yet转折说明有一类根本不顾孩子最大利益的群体却几乎拥有不受约束的接触权，其中unconstrained同义替换题干unrestricted。紧接着第2段首句揭示人们默认广告商和营销人员去塑造幼童，由此确定该群体为广告商，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“看护人”、C项“教师”和D项“医生”均出自第1段首句，属“正反颠倒”陷阱：文中明确指出这三类人群受到严格审查，而非拥有不受限制的接触权。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What kind of people should we enable children to become according to the author?", "options": ["Those who look to fame and wealth for external and ultimate validation.", "Those who value themselves because of their contribution to society.", "Those who associate self-worth with the ability to handle money.", "Those who have developed a proper sense of their own identity."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "We're turning out little consumers rather than young citizens who will value themselves for what they contribute to the society in which they live.", "explanation": "本题考查细节理解与对比转折。第2段末句用rather than表达了作者的价值取向：我们如今培养的是“小消费者”，而不是“因自己对所生活社会的贡献而珍视自身价值的年轻公民”。由此可见，作者认为我们理应把孩子培养成后者那样的人。B项中的because of their contribution to society精准同义替换原文for what they contribute to the society，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项与C项属“正反颠倒”，文中批判广告商诱导孩子用名利和物质衡量自我价值，这正是作者反对而非提倡的观念；D项属“偷换概念”，自我认同感在原文中仅作为时间背景出现，并非作者倡导的培养目标。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Many child development experts and educators call attention to research that suggests", "options": ["life-long consumerism is causing more and more cases of psychological problems.", "increasing commercialization of education is eroding many children's self-esteem.", "the growing desire for wealth is contributing to a rising rate of depression.", "the craving for purchasing material things is nurtured throughout one's life."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Many psychologists, child development experts and educators point to research suggesting that this emerging cradle-to-grave consumerism is contributing to growing rates of low self-esteem, depression and other forms of mental illness.", "explanation": "本题考查研究结论的同义替换。题干由Many child development experts and educators定位至第4段。原文指出研究表明，这种新兴的“从摇篮到坟墓”的消费主义（cradle-to-grave consumerism）正在推高自卑、抑郁及其他心理疾病的发病率。A项中life-long consumerism精准对应“从摇篮到坟墓的消费主义”，psychological problems概括了自卑、抑郁等精神疾病，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“教育商业化”属“无中生有”；C项属“以偏概全”，既将“消费主义”偷换为“对财富的渴望”，又将“多种精神疾病”窄化为“抑郁症”；D项偏离核心，遗漏了研究揭示的心理健康危害这一关键结论。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What does the author imply about the impact of advertising?", "options": ["It is actually infectious to many rather than a few.", "It is rooted in our desire for material possessions.", "It is comparable to that of virus.", "It is literally limited to children."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "It's also one that's forever developing new ways to persuade our children to desire material possessions, and because of advertisements' viral effect they only need to infect a few to reach the many.", "explanation": "本题考查词句隐含意义的推理判断。题干询问作者对广告影响的暗示，定位至第5段第三句。原文指出由于广告具有“病毒式效应”（viral effect），广告商只需感染少数人就能触及大众。由此可推断，作者把广告对儿童的影响类比为病毒的传播机制与感染力。C项中的that指代题干中的the impact，is comparable to that of virus精准对应viral effect，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项曲解“感染少数以触及多数”，错将关系偷换为“传染多数而非少数”；B项倒置因果，把广告诱导物欲说成植根于物欲；D项“仅限于儿童”拼凑了原文literally一词，与前文操纵成人情感相悖。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the opponents' argument against a complete ban on advertising to young children?", "options": ["It would deprive them of the chance to learn about products.", "It would render them unable to carve out unique identities.", "It would breach their freedom as would-be consumers.", "It would violate the rights endowed upon advertisers."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "There'll be those who argue that would be a breach of freedom of speech and infringe the rights of corporations to brainwash little children into demanding their products.", "explanation": "本题考查对反对派观点的细节定位。根据题干“反对彻底禁止儿童广告的论据”定位至第7段。首句提及全面禁令将招致诸多反对（objections to an outright ban），随后说明反对者认为此举违背言论自由，并侵犯企业给幼童洗脑、使其索要产品的权利。D项中violate the rights endowed upon advertisers正是对infringe the rights of corporations的同义转述，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项和B项均源自第5段提及的营销客观作用，并非第7段反对全面禁令者的论据，属“张冠李戴”；C项将原文企业享有的“言论自由”偷换为“准消费者的自由”，属“偷换概念”。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 仔细检查；严格审查", "note": "高频阅读动词，常用于对机构、候选人或数据的严格审视，近义词 examine closely。", "word": "scrutinize"}, {"gloss": "v. 驯化；使习惯于；影响", "note": "熟词僻义：作名词意为“条件/状况”，作及物动词在心理与社会语境中意为“使受条件反射影响、长期灌输塑造”。", "word": "condition"}, {"gloss": "v. 拉拢；招募；利用", "note": "常规义为“招募新兵/员工”，本文用于商业语境 recruit children to a commercial assault，含“拉拢利用”之意。", "word": "recruit"}, {"gloss": "n. 操纵；摆布；篡改", "note": "动词 manipulate 的名词形式，在社科与广告阅读中常带有“暗中操控公众情感或舆论”的贬义色彩。", "word": "manipulation"}, {"gloss": "v. 侵犯；违背（权利、法律）", "note": "常搭配介词 on/upon 或直接接 rights/freedom 等宾语，与 breach、violate 构成六级高频近义词组。", "word": "infringe"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Before children have even developed a proper sense of their own identity, or learned to handle money, they're encouraged to associate status and self-worth with stuff, and to look to external things such as fame and wealth for validation.", "point": "辨析 encourage sb. to do A and to do B 的并列不定式结构，以及 associate A with B（将A与B联系起来）、look to... for...（向……寻求……）核心短语。", "structure": "Before 引导时间状语从句（含两个并列谓语动词短语 have developed... or learned...） + 主句 they're encouraged to...（含并列不定式短语 to associate... with... and to look to... for... 作主语补足语）", "zh": "在孩子们甚至尚未形成健全的自我认同感或学会理财之前，他们就被诱导将地位和自我价值与物质挂钩，并向名望、财富等外在事物寻求认可。"}, {"en": "It's crept up on us in the 60 years since advertisers started to target the young and found that they could recruit them to a commercial assault on their parents.", "point": "注意 creep up on（不知不觉降临、悄然侵袭）的形象用法，以及 recruit sb. to...（拉拢/招募某人参与……）在商业语境中的隐喻表达。", "structure": "主句 It's crept up on us in the 60 years + since 引导时间状语从句（从句中 started... and found... 并列，found 后接 that 引导的宾语从句）", "zh": "自从60年前广告商开始瞄准年轻群体、并发现可以招募他们向父母发起商业攻势以来，这种现象便悄然向我们袭来。"}, {"en": "There're plenty working hand in glove with a £12bn-a-year industry that has turned the manipulation of adult emotions and desires into an art form — often literally.", "point": "理解代词 plenty 指代 psychologists，识别 work hand in glove with（勾结、密切配合）及复合形容词 £12bn-a-year 的构词法。", "structure": "There be 句型 + 现在分词短语 working hand in glove with... 作后置定语修饰 plenty + that 引导定语从句修饰 industry（含 turn... into... 结构） + 破折号补充说明", "zh": "有大把心理学家与这个年产值高达120亿英镑的行业沆瀣一气，该行业已将操纵成年人的情感与欲望变成了一门艺术——往往是字面意义上的艺术。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "unconstrained（不受约束的）与 unrestricted（不受限制的）为核心形容词同义替换。", "option": "almost unrestricted access", "original": "almost unconstrained access"}, {"note": "动词短语 contribute to 转为名词短语 contribution to，what 从句转为介词短语作原因。", "option": "because of their contribution to society", "original": "for what they contribute to the society in which they live"}, {"note": "cradle-to-grave（从摇篮到坟墓）替换 life-long（终生的）；mental illness 上义词替换为 psychological problems。", "option": "life-long consumerism is causing more and more cases of psychological problems", "original": "cradle-to-grave consumerism is contributing to growing rates of low self-esteem, depression and other forms of mental illness"}, {"note": "将形容词 viral（病毒式的）拆解还原为“可与病毒的影响相比”，that 回指前文 impact。", "option": "comparable to that of virus", "original": "advertisements' viral effect"}, {"note": "infringe（侵犯）同义替换为 violate；corporations 结合语境具体化为 advertisers。", "option": "violate the rights endowed upon advertisers", "original": "infringe the rights of corporations"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202306-s2-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 六级真题 第2套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 六级真题 第2套 Passage Two", "title": "职场员工监控的利弊与争议", "subtitle": "商业科技 · 职场管理与隐私边界", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 455, "paragraphs": ["Many oppose workplace surveillance, because of the inherent dehumanizing effect it has and the relentless pressure it brings. But it's on the rise around the world as firms look to become more efficient by squeezing more productivity from their workers. More than half of companies with over $750m in annual revenue used “non-traditional” monitoring techniques on staff last year.", "Monitoring employee performance gives firms the ability to assess how their staff are performing and interacting, which can be good for both the firm and employees themselves. A growing number of analytics companies offer this service. They gather “data exhaust” left by employees' email and instant messaging apps, and use name badges equipped with radio-frequency identification devices and microphones. These can check how much time you spend talking, your volume and tone of voice, even if you do not dominate conversations. While this may sound intrusive, exponents argue that it can also protect employees against bullying and sexual harassment.", "Some of this data analysis can produce unexpected results. For example, it was found that people who sat at 12-person lunch tables tended to interact, share ideas more and outperform those who regularly sat at four-person tables, a fact that would probably have gone undetected without such data analysis.", "Over the last few years a Stockholm co-working space called Epicenter has gone much further and holds popular “chipping parties”, where people can have microchips implanted in their hands. They can use the implants to access electronically-controlled doors, or monitor how typing speed correlates with heart rate. Implanted chips may seem extreme, but it is a relatively small step from ID cards and biometrics to such devices.", "As long as such schemes are voluntary, there will probably be a growing number of convenience-oriented uses so that a substantial number of workers would opt to have a chip inserted. But if implanted chips are used to reduce slack time or rest breaks, that could prove to be detrimental. And if surveillance tools take away autonomy, that's when they prove most unpopular. A lot depends on how such monitoring initiatives are communicated and this could prevent possible revolts being staged.", "If bosses don't communicate effectively, employees assume the worst. But if they're open about the information they're collecting and what they're doing with it, research suggests 46% of employees are generally okay with it. Although many such monitoring schemes use anonymised data and participation is voluntary, many staffers remain skeptical and fear an erosion of their civil liberties.", "So workplace surveillance could be empowering for staff and useful for companies looking to become more efficient and profitable. But implemented in the wrong way, it could also become an unpopular tool of oppression that proves counterproductive."], "translations": ["许多人反对职场监控，因为它具有固有的去人性化效应，并且会带来持续不断的压力。但由于企业希望通过压榨员工更高的生产力来提升效率，职场监控在全球范围内呈上升趋势。去年，年收入超过7.5亿美元的公司中，半数以上都对员工采用了“非传统”监控技术。", "监控员工绩效使企业能够评估员工的工作表现和互动情况，这对企业和员工自身都有好处。越来越多的分析公司提供这项服务。他们收集员工在电子邮件和即时通讯应用中留下的“数据尾气”，并使用装有射频识别装置和麦克风的工牌。这些设备可以监测你的说话时长、音量和语调，哪怕你并不是对话的主导者。虽然这听起来像是一种侵犯，但支持者认为，它也能保护员工免受欺凌和性骚扰。", "其中一些数据分析可能会得出意想不到的结果。例如，研究发现坐在12人餐桌旁共进午餐的员工往往互动更多、分享更多想法，且工作表现优于经常坐在4人餐桌旁的员工——如果没有这类数据分析，这一事实很可能会被忽略。", "过去几年里，斯德哥尔摩一家名为Epicenter的联合办公空间走得更远，举办了广受欢迎的“植入芯片派对”，人们可以在那里把微芯片植入自己手中。他们可以用植入的芯片开启电子门禁，或监测打字速度与心率之间的关联。植入芯片听起来或许极端，但从身份证件和生物识别技术发展到这类设备，其实只是相对较小的一步。", "只要这类计划是自愿的，便可能会涌现越来越多以便利为导向的用途，从而使相当一部分员工选择植入芯片。但如果植入芯片被用来压缩摸鱼时间或休息间隙，那就可能带来有害后果。而一旦监控工具剥夺了自主权，它们就会变得最不受欢迎。很大程度上取决于如何沟通这类监控举措，这样做也有助于防止员工发起抗议。", "如果老板不能进行有效沟通，员工就会往最坏处想。但研究表明，如果他们公开所收集的信息及用途，46%的员工通常是可以接受的。尽管许多此类监控方案使用匿名数据且属自愿参与，但仍有不少员工心存疑虑，担心自己的公民自由受到侵蚀。", "因此，职场监控既可能赋能员工，又有助于企业追求更高的效率与盈利能力。但如果实施不当，它也可能沦为不受欢迎的压迫工具，最终适得其反。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why are many people opposed to monitoring employee performance?", "options": ["It puts workers under constant pressure.", "It is universally deemed anti-human by nature.", "It does both mental and physical harm to employees monitored.", "It enables firms to squeeze maximal productivity from employees."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Many oppose workplace surveillance, because of the inherent dehumanizing effect it has and the relentless pressure it brings.", "explanation": "本题考查因果细节定位。题干询问许多人反对监控员工绩效的原因，可迅速定位至第1段首句。原文明确给出两点理由：一是其固有的去人性化效应，二是它所带来的持续不断的压力（relentless pressure）。A项中的constant pressure精准同义替换relentless pressure，puts workers under则对应brings，完整还原了反对原因，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“普遍认为”将Many偷换为全体，属“以偏概全”；C项“身体伤害”属“无中生有”；D项将企业压榨生产力的目的错当成反对原因，属“答非所问”，且maximal过度绝对。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the supporters' argument for workplace surveillance?", "options": ["It enables employees to refrain from dominating conversations.", "It enhances employees' identification with firms they work in.", "It can alert employees to intrusion into their privacy.", "It can protect employees against aggressive behavior."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "While this may sound intrusive, exponents argue that it can also protect employees against bullying and sexual harassment.", "explanation": "本题考查细节定位与同义替换。题干询问支持者对职场监控的看法，对应第2段末句中的exponents（支持者，同义替换supporters）。原文指出，尽管此类做法听起来带有侵犯性，但支持者认为它还能保护员工免受欺凌和性骚扰（bullying and sexual harassment）。D项用aggressive behavior（攻击性行为）概括“欺凌与性骚扰”，与原文高度契合，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项曲解前文“即便不主导对话也会被记录”，属“偷换概念”；B项借工牌中的identification一词生造“企业认同感”；C项把“看似侵犯隐私”曲解为“提醒隐私受侵”，属“正反颠倒”。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "例证题", "stem": "What does the author want to show by the example of different numbers of people interacting at lunch tables?", "options": ["Data analysis is key to the successful implementation of workplace surveillance.", "Analyzing data gathered from workers can yield something unexpected.", "More workmates sitting at a lunch table tend to facilitate interaction and idea sharing.", "It is hard to decide on how many people to sit at a lunch table without data analysis."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Some of this data analysis can produce unexpected results.", "explanation": "本题考查例证题的论点定位。例证题的解题关键在于找到例子所服务的观点句。第3段先提出核心观点：部分数据分析会产生意想不到的结果（unexpected results），随后以For example引出12人餐桌与4人餐桌员工互动和绩效差异的实例加以佐证。B项中的yield something unexpected精准复现段首观点，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "C项仅复述了餐桌例子的具体内容本身，而非作者借该例证想要说明的观点，属典型的“就事论事/以偏概全”陷阱；A项“数据分析是监控成功的关键”和D项“难以决定几人同桌”均属“过度推理”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does much of the positive effect of monitoring initiatives depend on?", "options": ["How frequently employees are to be monitored.", "What specific personal information is being excluded.", "What steps are taken to minimize their detrimental impact.", "How well bosses make known their purpose of monitoring."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "A lot depends on how such monitoring initiatives are communicated and this could prevent possible revolts being staged.", "explanation": "本题考查跨句整合与细节定位。题干询问监控举措积极效果主要取决于什么，由depend on定位至第5段末句：很大程度上取决于如何沟通此类监控举措（how such monitoring initiatives are communicated）。紧接着第6段进一步阐明，老板若对收集的信息及用途（what they're doing with it）保持坦诚公开，近半数员工便能接受。D项准确概括了这两处信息，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“监控频率”与B项“排除哪些特定个人信息”在第5、6段均未提及，属“无中生有”；C项“采取何种措施降低负面影响”过度宽泛，未抓住原文核心的“沟通公开”要素，属“偷换概念”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What concern do monitoring initiatives cause among many staffers?", "options": ["They may empower employers excessively.", "They may erode the workplace environment.", "They may infringe upon staffers' entitled freedom.", "They may become counterproductive in the long run."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Although many such monitoring schemes use anonymised data and participation is voluntary, many staffers remain skeptical and fear an erosion of their civil liberties.", "explanation": "本题考查细节定位与同义转述。题干中的many staffers定位至第6段末句。原文通过Although让步指出，尽管许多监控方案采用匿名数据且自愿参与，不少员工仍持怀疑态度，并担忧自己的公民自由受到侵蚀（fear an erosion of their civil liberties）。C项中infringe upon对应erosion，entitled freedom对应civil liberties，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项将末段“赋能员工”反转为“过度赋权雇主”，属“偷换概念”；B项保留erosion却把“公民自由”偷换为“职场环境”；D项“适得其反”是末段作者总结的后果，并非第6段员工的具体担忧。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 监控；监视；监督", "note": "高频社会科技词汇，常与 workplace、mass、digital 搭配，注意区分其与常规中性词 supervision（管理督导）的语气差异。", "word": "surveillance"}, {"gloss": "n. 支持者；倡导者；阐述者", "note": "熟词僻义：数学语境意为“指数”，在议论文中常指某一政策、技术的“积极支持者/拥护者”，同义于 supporter、advocate。", "word": "exponent"}, {"gloss": "n. 自主权；自治权", "note": "常用于职场管理、人工智能或教育话题，如 take away autonomy（剥夺自主权），形容词为 autonomous。", "word": "autonomy"}, {"gloss": "n. 侵蚀；削弱；逐渐丧失", "note": "本义指地理上的“水土侵蚀”，阅读中极常用于抽象概念搭配，如 erosion of civil liberties / trust（自由/信任的逐步丧失）。", "word": "erosion"}, {"gloss": "adj. 适得其反的；产生反作用的", "note": "合成词 counter-（反）+ productive（有成效的），常出现在文章末段总结政策实施不当的负面后果，是态度题常见线索词。", "word": "counterproductive"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "They gather “data exhaust” left by employees' email and instant messaging apps, and use name badges equipped with radio-frequency identification devices and microphones.", "point": "关注双重过去分词后置定语（left by... 与 equipped with...）对名词短语的压缩修饰，以及科技隐喻词 data exhaust 的含义。", "structure": "主语 They + 两个并列谓语动词短语 gather... and use...；过去分词短语 left by... 作后置定语修饰 data exhaust；equipped with... 作后置定语修饰 name badges", "zh": "他们收集员工在电子邮件和即时通讯应用中留下的“数据尾气”，并使用装有射频识别装置和麦克风的工牌。"}, {"en": "For example, it was found that people who sat at 12-person lunch tables tended to interact, share ideas more and outperform those who regularly sat at four-person tables, a fact that would probably have gone undetected without such data analysis.", "point": "把握句末同位语 a fact 对整件实验发现的总结，以及 without 引出的含蓄虚拟条件句（would probably have gone undetected）。", "structure": "形式主语 it was found + that 引导主语从句（含两个 who 引导的定语从句分别修饰 people 和 those） + 同位语 a fact（后接 that 定语从句，内含虚拟语气 would have gone）", "zh": "例如，研究发现坐在12人餐桌旁共进午餐的员工往往互动更多、分享更多想法，且工作表现优于经常坐在4人餐桌旁的员工——如果没有这类数据分析，这一事实很可能会被忽略。"}, {"en": "Although many such monitoring schemes use anonymised data and participation is voluntary, many staffers remain skeptical and fear an erosion of their civil liberties.", "point": "注意 Although 引导的让步逻辑转折在六级细节题中的高频考点地位，以及 remain + 形容词（skeptical）的系表结构。", "structure": "Although 引导让步状语从句（由 and 连接两个并列分句） + 主句 many staffers remain skeptical and fear...（and 连接两个并列谓语）", "zh": "尽管许多此类监控方案使用匿名数据且属自愿参与，但仍有不少员工心存疑虑，担心自己的公民自由受到侵蚀。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "relentless（持续不断的、无情的）同义替换为 constant（持续的）。", "option": "puts workers under constant pressure", "original": "relentless pressure it brings"}, {"note": "exponents（倡导者/支持者）替换为 supporters；bullying and sexual harassment 概括为 aggressive behavior。", "option": "supporters' argument ... It can protect employees against aggressive behavior", "original": "exponents argue that it can also protect employees against bullying and sexual harassment"}, {"note": "动词 produce（产生）替换为 yield（产出/带来），unexpected results 名词短语转为不定代词修饰结构。", "option": "yield something unexpected", "original": "produce unexpected results"}, {"note": "be open about what they're doing with it（坦诚说明收集信息的用途）同义转述为 make known their purpose。", "option": "How well bosses make known their purpose of monitoring", "original": "how such monitoring initiatives are communicated ... open about ... what they're doing with it"}, {"note": "erosion（侵蚀）对应 infringe upon（侵犯）；civil liberties（公民自由）同义替换为 entitled freedom。", "option": "infringe upon staffers' entitled freedom", "original": "fear an erosion of their civil liberties"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202306-s3-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 六级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 六级真题 第3套 Passage One", "title": "揭秘加工食品的“上瘾”机制", "subtitle": "消费行为与食品工业 · 2023.06 六级第3套 Passage 1", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 447, "paragraphs": ["If you're someone who has turned to snacking on junk food more in the pandemic (大流行病), you're not alone. Investigative reporter Michael Moss says processed food is engineered to hook you, not unlike alcohol, cigarettes, or other harmful substances. His 2013 book, Salt Sugar Fat, explored food companies' aggressive marketing of those products and their impact on our health. In his new book, Hooked, Moss updates the food giants' efforts to keep us eating what they serve, and how they're responding to complaints from consumers and health advocates.", "Processed food is inexpensive, it's legal, and it's everywhere. Companies' advertising is cueing us to remember those products and we want those products constantly. So the food environment is one of those key things that makes food even more problematic for so many people. Memory, nostalgia (怀旧) in particular, plays a big role in the foods we crave. Soda companies discovered that if they put a soda in the hands of a child when they're at a ball game with their parents, that soda will forever be associated with that joyous moment. Later in life, when that child wants to experience a joyous moment, they're going to think of soda. Many people seek comfort in the snacks they remember from childhood.", "Moss examines the way companies capitalize on our memories, cravings and brain chemistry to keep us snacking.", "One of the reasons I came to think that some of these food products are even more powerful, more troublesome than drugs can be is memory. What we eat is all about memory. And we begin forming memories for food at a really early age. And we keep those memories for a lifetime. Knowing this, the food industry spends lots of time trying to shape the memories that we have for their products. One of the features of addiction that scientists studying drug addiction discovered back in the 1990s was that the faster a substance hits the brain, the more apt we are as a result to act impulsively. There's nothing faster than food in its ability to hit the brain. For Moss, this puts the notion of “fast food” in an entirely new light as this isn't limited to fast food chains — almost 90% of food products in grocery stores are processed foods. Everything in the industry is about speed, from manufacturing to packaging.", "Overall, Moss outlines the industry's dependence on making their products inexpensive, super delicious, and incredibly convenient for consumers. Now that more and more people care about what they put in their bodies and are wanting to eat healthier, these companies are finding it really difficult to meet that new demand because of their own addiction to making these convenience foods."], "translations": ["如果你在疫情大流行期间更多地开始靠吃垃圾食品来解馋，你并不是一个人。调查记者迈克尔·莫斯指出，加工食品经过精心设计就是为了让人上瘾，这与酒精、香烟或其他有害物质并无二致。他2013年出版的《盐、糖、脂》一书探讨了食品公司对这些产品极具攻击性的营销策略及其对我们健康的影响。在他的新书《上瘾》（Hooked）中，莫斯进一步揭示了食品巨头为让我们持续吃下他们所供应的食物而采取的最新手段，以及他们如何回应消费者和健康倡导者的投诉。", "加工食品价格低廉、合法合规，而且随处可见。食品公司的广告不断提醒并诱导我们记起这些产品，使我们时刻都想吃到它们。因此，饮食环境正是令食品问题在如此多人群中雪上加霜的关键因素之一。记忆——尤其是怀旧之情——在我们渴望的食物中扮演着重要角色。汽水公司发现，如果他们把一瓶汽水塞到正在和父母看棒球比赛的孩子手中，那种汽水就会永远与那个欢乐的时刻联系在一起。在日后的生活中，当这个孩子想要重温那份欢乐时刻时，就会想起汽水。许多人会在童年记忆里的零食中寻求慰藉。", "莫斯剖析了食品公司是如何利用我们的记忆、渴望以及大脑化学反应来让我们零食不断的。", "我之所以逐渐认为某些食品比毒品更具威力、更令人担忧，原因之一就是记忆。我们吃什么完全关乎记忆。而且我们在很小的年纪就开始形成对食物的记忆，并终生保留这些记忆。深谙这一点，食品行业花费大量时间试图塑造我们对其产品的记忆。研究药物成瘾的科学家在20世纪90年代发现的成瘾特征之一是：一种物质作用于大脑的速度越快，我们因此而产生冲动行为的倾向就越强烈。而在作用于大脑的速度上，没有什么比食物更快了。在莫斯看来，这让“快餐”这一概念有了全新的含义，因为这并不局限于快餐连锁店——杂货店里近90%的食品都是加工食品。在这个行业里，从生产到包装，一切都围绕着“快”字。", "总体而言，莫斯概述了食品行业对生产低价、极度美味且极其方便消费者的产品的依赖。如今，越来越多的人开始关心自己吃进身体里的东西，并希望吃得更健康，但这些公司却发现很难满足这种新需求——因为他们自己也已经对制造这些方便食品上了瘾。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "In what way does Michael Moss think processed food is comparable to alcohol and cigarettes?", "options": ["They are all addictive.", "They are all necessary evils.", "They are all engineered to be enjoyed.", "They are all in increasingly great demand."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Investigative reporter Michael Moss says processed food is engineered to hook you, not unlike alcohol, cigarettes, or other harmful substances.", "explanation": "题干定位到第一段第二句。该句指出，莫斯认为加工食品经过专门设计以让人上瘾（hook you），这一点与酒精、香烟及其他有害物质并无二致（not unlike）。其中hook作动词意为“使着迷、使上瘾”，与A项中的addictive（使人上瘾的）形成同义替换，not unlike双重否定表肯定，说明三者在“令人上瘾”方面具有可比性，因此A项正确。", "trapNote": "C项将hook you（令人上瘾）偷换为engineered to be enjoyed（设计出来供人享受），且原文未称烟酒令人享受；B项“必要之恶”和D项“需求日益增加”均属无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say plays a key role in the foods we crave?", "options": ["The food environment.", "Aggressive marketing.", "Convenience.", "Memory."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Memory, nostalgia (怀旧) in particular, plays a big role in the foods we crave.", "explanation": "根据题干关键词plays a key role和foods we crave定位到第二段第四句。该句明确指出，记忆，尤其是怀旧之情，在我们渴望的食物中扮演着重要角色（plays a big role in the foods we crave）。句中的plays a big role对应题干的plays a key role，后文以汽水公司借助童年棒球赛记忆培养消费者习惯为例进一步印证了这一点，故D项Memory正确。", "trapNote": "A项利用第二段前一句中的food environment设置干扰，但原文说它是“让食物问题更严重的关键因素之一”，并非针对“渴望的食物”，属于偷换对象；B项来自第一段，C项来自第五段，均非此处所问。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do food companies do to capitalize on consumers' association with their food products?", "options": ["They strive to influence how consumers remember their products.", "They attempt to use consumers' long-term memories to promote addiction.", "They try to exploit consumers' memories for their products as early as possible.", "They endeavor to find what consumers remember about their products."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Knowing this, the food industry spends lots of time trying to shape the memories that we have for their products.", "explanation": "题干询问食品公司如何利用消费者对其产品的联想，可顺着第三段“利用记忆”的论述定位到第四段第五句。前文指出人们自幼形成食物记忆并保留一生，紧接着该句说明食品行业“花费大量时间试图塑造我们对其产品的记忆”。其中spends lots of time trying to对应A项strive to，shape the memories对应influence how consumers remember，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "C项利用前文“人们在很小年纪就开始形成食物记忆”设置干扰，将其偷换为食品公司“尽早利用”记忆；B项的“促进成瘾”与D项的“去发现消费者记住了什么”均歪曲了原文“主动塑造记忆”的含义。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "How does the food industry operate from manufacturing to packaging, according to Moss?", "options": ["Placing the idea of fast food in an entirely new light.", "Setting no limit to the number of fast food chains.", "Focusing on how quickly the work is done.", "Prioritizing the quality of their products."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Everything in the industry is about speed, from manufacturing to packaging.", "explanation": "根据题干关键词from manufacturing to packaging定位到第四段最后一句。该句指出，在这个行业中，从生产到包装的一切环节都讲究速度（Everything in the industry is about speed）。选项C中的Focusing on how quickly the work is done精准转述了is about speed（以速度为核心），完整对应了题干对食品工业运作方式的提问，因此C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项复现前句的new light，但原文指“莫斯重新审视快餐概念”，非食品行业的运作方式，属张冠李戴；B项将isn't limited to（不限于）曲解为“不设限”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why are companies finding it difficult to satisfy consumers' demand for healthier food products?", "options": ["They think speed of production outweighs consumers' health.", "They believe their industry would perish without fast foods.", "They have to strike a balance between taste and nutrition.", "They are hooked on manufacturing convenience foods."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Now that more and more people care about what they put in their bodies and are wanting to eat healthier, these companies are finding it really difficult to meet that new demand because of their own addiction to making these convenience foods.", "explanation": "题干询问企业为何难以满足消费者对更健康食品的需求，定位到第五段最后一句。原因状语because of their own addiction to making these convenience foods指出，这些公司之所以难以满足新需求，是因为它们自身也对制造这类方便食品上了瘾。D项用be hooked on同义替换addiction to，用manufacturing替换making，精准再现原文因果，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“生产速度重于消费者健康”、B项“没有快餐行业就会消亡”和C项“必须在口味与营养间取得平衡”均基于常识或前文信息进行过度推理，原文末段并未提及这些原因，属于无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "使上瘾；吸引住", "note": "【熟词僻义】常见义为“钩子；挂住”，在本文及标题中高频表示“使上瘾、牢牢迷住”（be hooked on sth. 对某事上瘾），对应 addictive。", "word": "hook"}, {"gloss": "精心设计；策划制造", "note": "【熟词僻义】名词指“工程师”，作动词在科技与社会类阅读中常意为“精心设计、人为操纵”（如 be engineered to... 经过设计以达到……目的）。", "word": "engineer"}, {"gloss": "提示；诱导，暗示", "note": "【核心考法】原指“线索、提示”，作动词 cue sb. to do sth. 表示“通过信号提醒/触发某人做某事”，文中指广告不断触发消费记忆。", "word": "cue"}, {"gloss": "利用，趁机获利（+ on）", "note": "【常考搭配】常见义为“大写”或“资本化”，固定搭配 capitalize on sth. 意为“充分利用、借……获利”，相当于 take advantage of。", "word": "capitalize"}, {"gloss": "易于……的，倾向于……的", "note": "【高频形容词】常见搭配 be apt to do sth. 表示“有……倾向、易于做某事”（同义于 be likely to / tend to）；另有“恰当的”之义。", "word": "apt"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In his new book, Hooked, Moss updates the food giants' efforts to keep us eating what they serve, and how they're responding to complaints from consumers and health advocates.", "point": "update 此处意为“提供最新情况/进一步揭示”；keep sb. doing sth. 表“使某人持续做某事”；注意 and 并列了名词短语与 how 从句作同一动词的宾语。", "structure": "主句 Moss updates... 后接两个由 and 连接的并列宾语：名词短语 the food giants' efforts（后跟不定式 to keep... 作定语，其中包含宾语从句 what they serve）与 how 引导的宾语从句。", "zh": "在他的新书《上瘾》中，莫斯更新了食品巨头为让我们持续吃下其产品所做的种种努力，以及他们如何回应消费者和健康倡导者的投诉。"}, {"en": "One of the features of addiction that scientists studying drug addiction discovered back in the 1990s was that the faster a substance hits the brain, the more apt we are as a result to act impulsively.", "point": "重点掌握“the + 比较级..., the + 比较级...”结构（越……越……）以及短语 be apt to do sth.（倾向于做某事/易于做某事）。", "structure": "主语为 One of the features of addiction，后接 that 引导的定语从句（含现在分词短语 studying... 作定语）；主句系动词 was 后接 that 引导的表语从句，从句内包含“the + 比较级..., the + 比较级...”句型。", "zh": "研究药物成瘾的科学家早在20世纪90年代就发现的成瘾特征之一是：一种物质作用于大脑的速度越快，我们因此而冲动行事的倾向就越强烈。"}, {"en": "Now that more and more people care about what they put in their bodies and are wanting to eat healthier, these companies are finding it really difficult to meet that new demand because of their own addiction to making these convenience foods.", "point": "now that 意为“既然，由于”；find it difficult to do sth. 为高频写作与阅读句式；addiction to doing sth. 中 to 为介词，后接动名词。", "structure": "Now that 引导原因状语从句（含宾语从句 what they put...）；主句使用“find + it (形式宾语) + adj. + to do sth. (真正宾语)”结构，句末 because of 短语交代深层原因。", "zh": "既然越来越多的人关心自己吃进身体里的食物并希望吃得更健康，这些公司却发现很难满足这种新需求，因为它们自身也对制造这类方便食品上了瘾。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "动词 hook（使上瘾、迷住）替换为形容词 addictive（令人上瘾的）；not unlike（与……并无二致）双重否定表肯定，说明三者共性。", "option": "They are all addictive.", "original": "processed food is engineered to hook you, not unlike alcohol, cigarettes"}, {"note": "原文第二段中的 big role 在题干中被替换为 key role，对应句中核心主语 Memory。", "option": "plays a key role in the foods we crave", "original": "plays a big role in the foods we crave"}, {"note": "spends lots of time trying to 对应 strive to（努力/力图）；shape the memories 对应 influence how consumers remember。", "option": "They strive to influence how consumers remember their products.", "original": "spends lots of time trying to shape the memories that we have for their products"}, {"note": "is about speed（一切围绕速度）被具体化转述为 Focusing on how quickly the work is done（聚焦工作完成的速度）。", "option": "Focusing on how quickly the work is done.", "original": "Everything in the industry is about speed, from manufacturing to packaging."}, {"note": "名词短语 addiction to making... 与动词短语 be hooked on manufacturing... 形成核心考法替换，呼应首段 hook you。", "option": "They are hooked on manufacturing convenience foods.", "original": "because of their own addiction to making these convenience foods"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202306-s3-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2023.06", "examSet": "2023.06 六级真题 第3套", "sourceLabel": "2023.06 六级真题 第3套 Passage Two", "title": "过度模仿：人类演化的成功密码", "subtitle": "认知科学与人类演化 · 2023.06 六级第3套 Passage 2", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 446, "paragraphs": ["Chimpanzees (黑猩猩), human beings' closest animal relatives, share up to 98% of our genes. Yet humans and chimpanzees lead very different lives. Fewer than 300,000 wild chimpanzees live in a few forested corners of Africa today, while humans have colonized every corner of the globe. At more than 7 billion, human population dwarfs that of nearly all other mammals — despite our physical weaknesses.", "What could account for our species' incredible evolutionary successes?", "One obvious answer is our big brains. It could be that our raw intelligence gave us an unprecedented ability to think outside the box, innovating solutions to thorny problems as people migrated across the globe.", "But a growing number of cognitive scientists and anthropologists (人类学家) are rejecting that explanation. They think that, rather than making our living as innovators, we survive and thrive precisely because we don't think for ourselves. Instead, people cope with challenging climates and ecological contexts by carefully copying others.", "In a famous study, psychologists Victoria Horner and Andrew Whiten showed two groups of test subjects — children and chimpanzees — a mechanical box with a treat inside. In one condition, the box was opaque, while in the other it was transparent. The experimenters demonstrated how to open the box to retrieve the treat, but they also included the irrelevant step of tapping on the box with a stick.", "Oddly, the children carefully copied all the steps to open the box, even when they could see that the stick had no practical effect. That is, they copied irrationally: Instead of doing only what was necessary to get their reward, children slavishly imitated every action they'd witnessed.", "Of course, that study only included three- and four-year-olds. But additional research has shown that older children and adults are even more likely to mindlessly copy others' actions, and infants are less likely to over-imitate — that is, to precisely copy even impractical actions.", "By contrast, chimpanzees in the study only over-imitated in the opaque condition. In the transparent condition — where they saw that the stick was mechanically useless — they ignored that step entirely. Other research has since supported these findings.", "When it comes to copying, chimpanzees are more rational than human children or adults.", "Where does the seemingly irrational human preference for over-imitation come from? Anthropologist Joseph Henrich points out that people around the world rely on technologies that are often so complex that no one can learn them rationally. Instead, people must learn them step by step, trusting in the wisdom of more experienced elders and peers.", "So the next time you hear someone arguing passionately that everyone should embrace nonconformity and avoid imitating others, you might laugh a little bit. We're not chimpanzees, after all."], "translations": ["黑猩猩作为人类在动物界最亲近的亲属，与我们共享高达98%的基因。然而，人类与黑猩猩却过着截然不同的生活。如今仅有不到30万只野生黑猩猩生活在非洲的几处森林角落里，而人类却已经遍布地球的每一个角落。尽管人类在体能上存在诸多弱点，但超过70亿的人口数量却令几乎所有其他哺乳动物相形见绌。", "究竟是什么造就了我们这个物种令人惊叹的演化成功？", "一个显而易见的答案是我们发达的大脑。或许正是我们的先天智力赋予了我们前所未有的跳出常规思维的能力，使人类在向全球迁徙的过程中不断创新，解决棘手的难题。", "但越来越多的认知科学家和人类学家正在否定这一解释。他们认为，人类之所以能够生存并繁盛，靠的并不是作为创新者来谋生，而恰恰是因为我们不独立思考。相反，人们是通过仔细模仿他人来应对严酷的气候和生态环境的。", "在一项著名的研究中，心理学家维多利亚·霍纳和安德鲁·怀滕向两组实验对象——人类儿童和黑猩猩——展示了一个里面装有零食奖励的机械盒。在一种实验条件下，盒子是不透明的；而在另一种条件下，盒子是透明的。实验人员演示了如何打开盒子取出零食，但他们也在其中加入了一个用木棍敲击盒子的无关步骤。", "奇怪的是，即便儿童能够看清木棍没有任何实际作用，他们依然仔细模仿了打开盒子的所有步骤。也就是说，他们的模仿是非理性的：儿童并没有只做拿到奖励所必需的动作，而是盲目机械地模仿了他们目睹的每一个动作。", "当然，那项研究只涵盖了三四岁的儿童。但更多的研究表明，年龄更大的儿童和成年人甚至更有可能不假思索地模仿他人行为，而婴儿反倒不太容易“过度模仿”——即精确复制连同不切实际动作在内的所有步骤。", "相比之下，该研究中的黑猩猩只在不透明盒子的条件下才表现出过度模仿。而在透明盒子的条件下——当它们看到木棍在机械原理上毫无用处时——它们便完全忽略了那个步骤。此后的其他研究也印证了这些发现。", "在模仿这件事上，黑猩猩比人类儿童或成年人更加理性。", "人类对过度模仿这种看似非理性的偏好究竟从何而来？人类学家约瑟夫·亨里奇指出，世界各地的人们所依赖的技术往往极其复杂，复杂到没有人能够仅凭理性去学会它们。相反，人们必须信任更有经验的长辈和同伴的智慧，一步一步地学习。", "因此，下次当你听到有人慷慨激昂地主张每个人都应该拥抱标新立异、避免模仿他人时，你或许可以会心一笑。毕竟，我们可不是黑猩猩。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What might explain humans' having the largest population of almost all mammals?", "options": ["They are equipped with raw strength for solving the most challenging problems.", "They cope with the outside world more effectively than their animal relatives.", "They possess the most outstanding ability to think.", "They know how to survive everywhere on earth."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "One obvious answer is our big brains. It could be that our raw intelligence gave us an unprecedented ability to think outside the box, innovating solutions to thorny problems as people migrated across the globe.", "explanation": "第一段指出人类人口超70亿，令几乎所有其他哺乳动物相形见绌；第二段据此发问何种原因促成了人类演化的巨大成功；第三段随即给出一种可能的解释：人类拥有发达的大脑，先天智力赋予了我们前所未有的跳出常规的思考能力（unprecedented ability to think outside the box）。C项中的most outstanding同义替换unprecedented，精准概括了这一可能的原因，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项将第三段的raw intelligence偷换为raw strength，且与第一段physical weaknesses相悖；D项“在世界各地生存”是第一段描述的结果现象，并非人口庞大的原因。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What accounts for humans' evolutionary successes according to a growing number of cognitive scientists and anthropologists?", "options": ["They are better at innovating solutions.", "They thrive through creative strategies.", "They are naturally adaptive to ecological contexts.", "They meet challenges by imitating others carefully."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Instead, people cope with challenging climates and ecological contexts by carefully copying others.", "explanation": "根据题干中的认知科学家和人类学家定位到第四段。该段先否定了“靠创新谋生”的解释，随后在末句指出：人类通过仔细模仿他人（by carefully copying others）来应对严酷的气候和生态环境（challenging climates and ecological contexts）。D项用meet challenges和imitating others carefully与原文形成同义替换，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“更善于创新解决方案”和B项“通过创造性策略繁盛”均属于正反颠倒，第四段明确指出科学家否定了创新解释；C项将cope with...contexts歪曲为“天生适应”，遗漏了模仿这一关键机制。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author think is odd about the findings of the study by Victoria Horner and Andrew Whiten?", "options": ["Children irrationally imitated every action of the experimenters.", "Chimpanzees could tell the transparent box from the opaque one.", "Chimpanzees could retrieve the treat more quickly than children did.", "Children omitted the step of tapping on the box with a stick to open it."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Oddly, the children carefully copied all the steps to open the box, even when they could see that the stick had no practical effect. That is, they copied irrationally: Instead of doing only what was necessary to get their reward, children slavishly imitated every action they'd witnessed.", "explanation": "根据题干中的odd以及研究者人名定位到第六段。该段开篇以Oddly引出实验结果中的反常之处：即使儿童能看清木棍毫无实际作用，仍仔细模仿了所有步骤；接着进一步解释称，儿童的模仿是非理性的（copied irrationally），盲目模仿了目睹的每一个动作（imitated every action they'd witnessed）。A项精准转述了这一发现，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "D项属于正反颠倒，在透明盒子条件下省略敲击步骤的是黑猩猩而非儿童；B项虽符合第八段对黑猩猩的描述，但并非作者认为奇怪的发现；C项“更快取出零食”在原文中未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is anthropologist Joseph Henrich's explanation for the human preference for copying?", "options": ["It originates in the rationality of people around the world.", "It stems from the way people learn complex technologies.", "It results from people distrusting their own wisdom.", "It derives from the desire to acquire knowledge step by step."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 10, "evidenceQuote": "Anthropologist Joseph Henrich points out that people around the world rely on technologies that are often so complex that no one can learn them rationally. Instead, people must learn them step by step, trusting in the wisdom of more experienced elders and peers.", "explanation": "根据题干中的人类学家Joseph Henrich定位到第十段。该段先提出疑问“过度模仿的偏好从何而来”，随后引述亨里奇的解释：人类依赖的技术极其复杂，没有人能仅靠理性学会，因此人们必须信任有经验的长辈和同伴，一步一步地学习这些复杂技术。B项指出该偏好源于人们学习复杂技术的方式，其中stems from对应come from，高度概括了该段核心因果，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项与原文no one can learn them rationally完全相反，属正反颠倒；C项“不信任自己的智慧”无中生有；D项将“被迫循序渐进地学习”偷换为“渴望获取知识”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What point does the author want to emphasize when he says “We're not chimpanzees”?", "options": ["It is arguable whether everyone should avoid imitation.", "It is characteristic of human beings to copy others.", "It is desirable to trust in more knowledgeable peers.", "It is naive to laugh at someone embracing nonconformity."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 11, "evidenceQuote": "So the next time you hear someone arguing passionately that everyone should embrace nonconformity and avoid imitating others, you might laugh a little bit. We're not chimpanzees, after all.", "explanation": "题干定位到文章最后一句“We're not chimpanzees”。结合前文可知，黑猩猩只做理性判断、会跳过多余的模仿动作，而人类则具有强烈的“过度模仿”倾向并借此生存繁盛。因此当有人鼓吹“避免模仿他人”时，作者幽默地反驳“毕竟我们不是黑猩猩”，旨在强调模仿他人正是人类区别于黑猩猩的本质特征之一。B项准确揭示了这句话的言外之意，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "D项正反颠倒，作者认可的是对“鼓吹避免模仿的人”一笑了之，而非认为笑话他人很幼稚；A项态度过于模糊且削弱作者观点；C项出自第十段，并非末句类比黑猩猩所要强调的重点。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "使相形见绌；使显得微不足道", "note": "【熟词僻义】名词常指“矮人；矮星”，作及物动词在比较数据语境中高频考查，表示“在数量/规模上远超并使……显得微不足道”。", "word": "dwarf"}, {"gloss": "先天的，未经加工训练的；原始的", "note": "【熟词僻义】除“生的、未煮熟的”外，raw intelligence / raw talent 在六级中常指“天生的智力/天赋”（未经过后天刻意修饰）。", "word": "raw"}, {"gloss": "棘手的，令人头疼的", "note": "【熟词僻义】源于 thorn（刺），原意“多刺的”，引申修饰 problem / issue 表示“棘手的、难处理的”。", "word": "thorny"}, {"gloss": "盲从地，一味模仿地", "note": "【构词与态度】源于 slave（奴隶），表示“像奴隶般盲从地、毫无主见地”，带有明显的贬义或客观批判色彩，与 irrationally 呼应。", "word": "slavishly"}, {"gloss": "不从众，标新立异，特立独行", "note": "【构词记忆】前缀 non-（不）+ conform（遵从、顺从）+ -ity（名词后缀），反义词为 conformity（从众）。", "word": "nonconformity"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "It could be that our raw intelligence gave us an unprecedented ability to think outside the box, innovating solutions to thorny problems as people migrated across the globe.", "point": "It could be that... 表示推测（“或许是……”）；think outside the box 为常用习语，意为“打破常规思考”。", "structure": "It could be that... 引导表语从句；其中现在分词短语 innovating solutions... 作伴随/结果状语，as 引导时间状语从句说明背景。", "zh": "或许正是我们的先天智力赋予了我们前所未有的跳出常规思维的能力，使人类在向全球迁徙的过程中不断创新，解决棘手的难题。"}, {"en": "Anthropologist Joseph Henrich points out that people around the world rely on technologies that are often so complex that no one can learn them rationally.", "point": "注意区分连续三个 that 的不同语法功能：第一个引导宾语从句，第二个引导定语从句修饰 technologies，第三个与 so 构成结果状语从句。", "structure": "主句 points out 后接 that 引导的宾语从句；宾语从句中 technologies 后接 that 引导的定语从句，定语从句内嵌 so... that...（如此……以至于……）结果状语从句。", "zh": "人类学家约瑟夫·亨里奇指出，世界各地的人们所依赖的技术往往极其复杂，复杂到没有人能够仅凭理性去学会它们。"}, {"en": "So the next time you hear someone arguing passionately that everyone should embrace nonconformity and avoid imitating others, you might laugh a little bit.", "point": "the next time 可直接引导时间状语从句，无需加介词；avoid 后须接动名词作宾语（avoid imitating）。", "structure": "the next time 充当连词引导时间状语从句，从句内含 hear sb. doing sth. 结构，arguing 后接 that 引导的宾语从句；主句为 you might laugh a little bit。", "zh": "因此，下次当你听到有人慷慨激昂地主张每个人都应该拥抱标新立异、避免模仿他人时，你或许可以会心一笑。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "unprecedented（前所未有的）在选项中转为最高级概念 the most outstanding（最杰出的），gave us 对应 possess。", "option": "They possess the most outstanding ability to think.", "original": "our raw intelligence gave us an unprecedented ability to think outside the box"}, {"note": "cope with challenging... 简练概括为 meet challenges（应对挑战），copying others 替换为 imitating others。", "option": "They meet challenges by imitating others carefully.", "original": "people cope with challenging climates and ecological contexts by carefully copying others"}, {"note": "整合段内相邻表述，将 copied irrationally 与 imitated every action 合并，they'd witnessed 对应实验人员所做的动作。", "option": "Children irrationally imitated every action of the experimenters.", "original": "they copied irrationally... children slavishly imitated every action they'd witnessed"}, {"note": "问句中的 come from 对应选项中的 stems from（源自）；后面阐述“人类必须一步步向他人学习复杂技术”概括为 the way people learn complex technologies。", "option": "It stems from the way people learn complex technologies.", "original": "Where does the seemingly irrational human preference for over-imitation come from? ... rely on technologies that are often so complex... must learn them step by step"}, {"note": "通过与黑猩猩（只理性模仿）的反差，推出“模仿他人是人类的固有特征”这一核心主旨。", "option": "It is characteristic of human beings to copy others.", "original": "everyone should embrace nonconformity and avoid imitating others, you might laugh a little bit. We're not chimpanzees, after all."}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202212-s1-p1", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2022.12", "examSet": "2022.12 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2022.12 六级真题 第1套 Passage One", "title": "职场自尊追求的动机与双面影响", "subtitle": "基于2022年12月六级真题：探讨以工作成就维系自尊的消极代价与积极动力", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 451, "paragraphs": ["Many people associate their self-worth with their work. The more successful their career, the better they feel about themselves. Work-related self-esteem is therefore a worthy ideal to pursue with vigor, right? Well, not always. According to recent research, in which psychologists interviewed 370 fulltime workers over a period of three weeks, the reality is a little more complicated. And it involves negative as well as positive consequences.", "It's natural to be drawn towards pleasure and to step away from pain. In the workplace, if that pleasure comes from a triumph which swells our self-respect, people will try to repeat the accomplishment. But repeating that accomplishment is often not realistic, which can lead to severe negative emotional consequences when it doesn't reoccur. This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation. It can hinder other more positive motivation types, such as completing a task purely because it's fulfilling or enjoyable.", "What consumes the employee instead is a pressing need to feel mighty and sure of themselves. They then take on only tasks and objectives which serve that ego-driven need. As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being. This internal pressure to succeed at all costs demands a lot of effort. It depletes their energy, culminating in disproportionate levels of damaging sentiment.", "Those negative emotions mount into heightened anxiety, impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life. Their desire to avoid feeling inferior ends up making them feel inferior when it comes to their diminished capacity for friendship and leisure. They end up dissatisfied both at work and outside of it.", "But thankfully, for those people compelled almost entirely by this specific form of motivation, the news isn't all bad, or bad at all. The study also discovered several positive outcomes that can actually outweigh the harmful ones. Though these types of employees are motivated by the desire to avoid negative consequences, they are also motivated by the excitement of pursuing emotional rewards. This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success. An effect of the positive motivation is that it neutralizes the existence of negative motivation.", "Sure, it affects people's personal lives to what could be deemed an unhealthy extent, because leisure activities are often seen as a part of life that must be sacrificed to manage work and family demands. However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated."], "translations": ["许多人将自我价值与工作联系在一起。他们的职业生涯越成功，对自己的感觉就越好。因此，与工作相关的自尊是一个值得全力追求的理想，对吗？然而，并非总是如此。根据最近的研究，心理学家在三周时间内采访了370名全职员工，现实情况要复杂一些。它既涉及消极后果，也涉及积极后果。", "人们自然会被快乐吸引，远离痛苦。在职场中，如果这种快乐来自于增强我们自尊的胜利，人们就会试图重复这一成就。但重复这一成就往往是不现实的，当它没有再次出现时，可能会导致严重的负面情绪后果。这种形式的动机被广泛认为是一种消极的动机类型。它可能会妨碍其他更积极的动机类型，比如纯粹因为任务令人满足或愉快而完成任务。", "相反，困扰员工的是一种迫切需要感到强大和自信的需求。然后他们只承担那些服务于自我驱动需求的任务和目标。因此，为了避免与失败相关的羞耻感和无价值感，他们过度透支自己，以至于随后对他们的幸福感产生不利影响。这种不惜一切代价成功的内在压力需要大量努力。它耗尽了他们的精力，最终导致不成比例的破坏性情绪水平。", "这些负面情绪累积成高度焦虑，影响他们充分享受个人生活的能力。他们避免感到自卑的愿望最终使他们在友谊和休闲能力减弱方面感到自卑。他们最终在工作内外都感到不满。", "但值得庆幸的是，对于那些几乎完全受这种特定动机形式驱使的人来说，消息并非全是坏的，或者根本不坏。该研究还发现了几个积极结果，实际上可以超过有害结果。尽管这些类型的员工受到避免负面后果的愿望的驱使，但他们也受到追求情感回报的兴奋感的驱使。这种兴奋感使追求目标变得愉快，并激发成功可能带来的快乐和自豪感。积极动机的一个效果是它中和了消极动机的存在。", "当然，它在某种程度上影响人们的个人生活，这可能被认为是不健康的，因为休闲活动通常被视为生活中必须牺牲的一部分，以应对工作和家庭需求。然而，人们对工作的感受与其说与他们是否受到保护自尊的动机驱使有关，不如说更多地与他们只是受到激励这一事实有关。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say about the pursuit of work-related self-esteem?", "options": ["It may result in negative motivation.", "It contributes to one's accomplishments.", "It can increase one's vigor as one keeps trying.", "It costs too much emotionally and psychologically."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But repeating that accomplishment is often not realistic, which can lead to severe negative emotional consequences when it doesn't reoccur. This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation.", "explanation": "定位第2段。文中指出，在职场中若愉悦感来自提升自尊的胜利，人们会试图重复成就，但重复成功往往不切实际，未能重现时会引发严重负面情绪后果，而“This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation”。A项中的result in negative motivation精准对应原文“被广泛视为一种消极动机”，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "D项具有较强干扰性，第3段虽提到情绪损耗，但第5段明确指出该动机也有积极面，“costs too much”表述过于绝对；B、C两项将第1段常识性反问误作作者观点。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do employees tend to do in pursuing work-related self-esteem?", "options": ["Take on tasks well beyond their actual capabilities.", "Strive to succeed at the expense of their well-being.", "Resort to all means regardless of the consequences.", "Exaggerate their sense of shame and worthlessness."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being. This internal pressure to succeed at all costs demands a lot of effort.", "explanation": "定位第3段。原文说明员工受证明自身强大与自信的迫切需求驱使，为避免失败带来的羞耻与无价值感，会过度透支自己（extend themselves），以致对幸福感产生不利影响（adverse effect on their well-being），且背负“succeed at all costs”的内在压力。B项“以牺牲幸福感为代价力求成功”准确同义转述原文，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，原文第3段只说承担“满足自我驱动需求的任务”，未提及超出实际能力；C项“不择手段”曲解了“succeed at all costs”（不惜一切代价成功）；D项与“避免羞耻感”相悖。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What do we learn about people over-concerned with work-related self-esteem?", "options": ["They may often feel inferior to their colleagues.", "They cannot enjoy their personal life to the full.", "They are never satisfied with their achievements.", "They have their own view of friendship and leisure."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Those negative emotions mount into heightened anxiety, impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life.", "explanation": "定位第4段首句。原文指出，第3段所述的负面情绪会演变为高度焦虑，进而“impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life”（影响他们充分享受个人生活的能力），且随后提到他们在友谊和休闲方面的能力减弱，最终在工作内外都感到不满。B项“cannot enjoy their personal life to the full”精准对应“make the most of their personal life”的否定含义，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项属无中生有，第4段提及“feel inferior”是因为友谊与休闲能力下降，并非“不如同事”；C项“从不满意成就”过于绝对，第2段明确他们曾因成功而获得愉悦。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the good news we learn from the recent research?", "options": ["The pursuit of goals may turn out to be enjoyable and pleasant.", "The emotional rewards from goal pursuit are worth the pains taken.", "The negative consequences of goal pursuit can mostly be avoided.", "The goal of swelling self-esteem can be achieved if one keeps trying."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success.", "explanation": "定位第5段。题干中的“good news”直接呼应段首“the news isn't all bad”。该段指出，这类员工同时受到追求情感回报的兴奋感驱动，而“This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success”。A项“追求目标可能变得愉快而惬意”正是对该句的直接同义转述，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项“值得付出痛苦”属于过度主观臆断，原文仅客观说明积极结果可超过并中和消极动机，未评价“是否值得”；C项“大部分负面后果可避免”偷换了“neutralizes”的含义。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can we infer from the last paragraph?", "options": ["Workers have to make sacrifices to preserve self-esteem.", "Self-esteem swells when workers are strongly motivated.", "Pursuit of goals affects people's personal lives to an unhealthy extent.", "People feel positive about their work as long as they are motivated."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated.", "explanation": "定位第6段末句。However转折后指出，人们对工作的感受“与其说取决于是否受维护自尊的动机驱使，不如说更多取决于他们本身就处于被激励的状态（they're simply motivated）”。结合第5段积极动机中和消极动机的论述，可推断只要员工受到激励，无论动机类型如何，往往就会对工作持积极感受。D项“只要受到激励，人们就会对工作有积极感受”符合句意推断，故选D。", "trapNote": "C项是第6段首句的字面复述，并非由“infer”要求的深层推断，且漏掉了“leisure activities”这一前提；A项曲解了牺牲休闲活动以平衡工作与家庭需求的原因。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 增强，膨胀，使自豪", "note": "文中“swells our self-respect”意为“增强/抬高我们的自尊心”，区别于常见的“（身体部位）肿胀”。", "word": "swell"}, {"gloss": "v. 耗尽，大幅削减", "note": "文中“depletes their energy”指“耗尽他们的精力”，写作中常用于资源、体力或耐心的消耗。", "word": "deplete"}, {"gloss": "v. 最终达到，以……告终", "note": "常与介词 in 搭配（culminate in），表示经过累积最终产生某种（常指严重的）后果。", "word": "culminate"}, {"gloss": "v. 中和，抵消", "note": "文中指积极动机“抵消/中和”消极动机的存在，作及物动词，同义词有 offset, counteract。", "word": "neutralize"}, {"gloss": "v. 认为，视为", "note": "正式用语，“what could be deemed an unhealthy extent”意为“可能被视为不健康的程度”。", "word": "deem"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "According to recent research, in which psychologists interviewed 370 fulltime workers over a period of three weeks, the reality is a little more complicated.", "point": "in which 相当于 in the research，修饰先行词 research；over a period of three weeks 作时间状语。", "structure": "介词短语作状语 + in which引导的非限制性定语从句 + 主系表结构", "zh": "根据近期的一项研究（心理学家在三周时间内对370名全职员工进行了访谈），实际情况要略微复杂一些。"}, {"en": "As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being.", "point": "associated with failure 作定语修饰 feelings...；extend oneself 意为“竭尽全力、过度劳累”；such a degree that... 表示程度及结果。", "structure": "结果状语 + 不定式作目的状语（含过去分词短语后置定语） + 主句（such... that... 引导结果状语从句）", "zh": "因此，为了避免因失败而产生的羞耻感和无价值感，他们过度消耗自己，以至于随后对身心健康造成不利影响。"}, {"en": "However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated.", "point": "the way 后省略了引导定语从句的 in which/that；less to do with A but more with B 意为“与其说与A有关，不如说更多与B有关”；that 引导 fact 的同位语从句。", "structure": "主语（the way + 定语从句） + 谓语（has less to do with... but more with...） + 同位语从句（that...）", "zh": "然而，人们对工作的感受与其说取决于他们是否出于维护自尊而受激励，不如说更多取决于他们本身处于受激励的状态。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "主动与被动语态转换，“is widely regarded as...”对应“result in negative motivation”。", "option": "It may result in negative motivation.", "original": "This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation."}, {"note": "“extend themselves”与“succeed at all costs”对应“strive to succeed”，“adverse effect on their well-being”对应“at the expense of their well-being”。", "option": "Strive to succeed at the expense of their well-being.", "original": "they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being"}, {"note": "否定词转移与习语替换，“impacting... make the most of”对应“cannot enjoy... to the full”。", "option": "They cannot enjoy their personal life to the full.", "original": "impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life"}, {"note": "动名词短语“pursuing goals”转为名词短语“the pursuit of goals”，“pleasure”转为形容词“pleasant”。", "option": "The pursuit of goals may turn out to be enjoyable and pleasant.", "original": "This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride"}, {"note": "段落逻辑归纳，“more with the fact that they're simply motivated”结合上文积极动机中和消极动机，推导出“as long as they are motivated”。", "option": "People feel positive about their work as long as they are motivated.", "original": "has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated"}]}}, {"id": "cet6-202212-s1-p2", "exam": "六级 CET-6", "difficulty": "L2", "origin": "official", "year": "2022.12", "examSet": "2022.12 六级真题 第1套", "sourceLabel": "2022.12 六级真题 第1套 Passage Two", "title": "全球环境恶化与可持续发展之路", "subtitle": "基于2022年12月六级真题：剖析全球资源退化危机及发展中国家的绿色转型", "timeLimitMin": 15, "wordCount": 441, "paragraphs": ["Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage, a recent UN environmental study has found. The study concludes that without radical action the level of prosperity that millions of people in the developed world count on will be impossible to maintain or extend to poorer countries.", "Water scarcity is the curse of some of the poorest regions on Earth, leaving developing countries increasingly unable to feed themselves, and causing hardship for millions of people. There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken. Water resources are under increasing threat from population growth, climate change, rapid urbanization, rising levels of consumption, and the degradation of lands that previously provided a natural replenishment(补充) of water resources.", "The rate of damage to the natural environment was found to increase globally, despite concerted efforts to persuade government to take measures to improve the condition. \"If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and consumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline,\" warned UN executive director Achim Steiner.", "He said the tools for improving the environment for millions of people existed in developed countries, but were in danger of not being used.", "The study found that basic measures to tackle some of the key causes of environmental damage were still not being taken. These included measures to reduce air pollution; to control the damage to marine ecosystems, which can have a huge effect on fish stocks on which hundreds of millions of people depend; and to curb the degradation of land where modern agricultural methods were pursued without regard to the longer-term consequences.", "Despite the recent global agreement on cutting greenhouse gas emissions, global carbon output continues to rise. This will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people. Climate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural fertilisers used in agriculture which increased by more than a quarter between 2000 and 2010. Other problem areas identified in the report included glaciers, which provide vital water resources for millions of people, but which are shrinking as the climate warms.", "In rich countries, these problems have built up over decades and centuries while economic growth was pursued at the expense of the environment. Subsequent efforts to remedy the environment have met with partial success. But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change, which has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment."], "translations": ["联合国近期的一项环境研究发现，人类对世界自然资源的破坏速度正在迅速超过地球吸收这种损害的能力。该研究得出结论，如果不采取根本性行动，发达国家数百万人所依赖的繁荣水平将无法维持，也无法延伸到较贫穷的国家。", "水资源匮乏是地球上一些最贫穷地区的祸患，使发展中国家越来越无法养活自己，并给数百万人造成困苦。如果不采取根本性行动，这种绝望的局面似乎没有什么改善的希望。水资源正面临来自人口增长、气候变化、快速城市化、消费水平上升，以及以前提供水资源自然补充的土地退化的日益增长的威胁。", "尽管各国政府做出协调努力以采取措施改善状况，但全球范围内对自然环境的破坏速度仍在加快。联合国执行主任阿希姆·施泰纳（Achim Steiner）警告说：“如果当前趋势继续下去，世界未能改善生产和消费模式，那么世界环境状况将继续恶化。”", "他说，改善数百万人环境的工具在发达国家已经存在，但有不被使用的危险。", "该研究发现，解决一些造成环境破坏的关键原因的基本措施仍未得到采取。这些措施包括减少空气污染的措施；控制对海洋生态系统的破坏，这可能对数亿人所依赖的鱼类资源产生巨大影响；以及遏制土地退化，而现代农业方法在实施时并未考虑长期后果。", "尽管最近达成了关于减少温室气体排放的全球协议，但全球碳排放量仍在继续上升。这将对发展中经济体养活本国人民的能力造成长期压力。农业中使用的化学和天然肥料所排放的温室气体加剧了气候变化，这些排放在2000年至2010年间增加了超过四分之一。报告中指出的其他问题领域包括冰川，它为数百万人提供重要的水资源，但随着气候变暖正在缩小。", "在富裕国家，这些问题是在以牺牲环境为代价追求经济增长的过程中，经过几十年甚至几个世纪积累起来的。随后补救环境的努力取得了部分成功。但在发展中国家，未来发展道路有更大的改变潜力，这鼓励了国际机构设计更可持续的增长路径，既能减轻贫困又能保护环境。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the major finding of the UN environmental study?", "options": ["Human activity has rendered Mother Earth almost uninhabitable.", "Humans are doing more damage to the earth than it can cope with.", "Environmental problems have considerably weakened human prosperity.", "Environmental damage is more serious in developed countries these days."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage, a recent UN environmental study has found.", "explanation": "定位第1段首句。联合国近期环境研究发现，人类对全球自然资源的破坏（Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans）正迅速超过地球吸收这种损害的能力（outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage）。B项中“doing more damage”对应“Degradation... outpacing”，“than it can cope with”对应“the planet's ability to absorb the damage”，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“几乎无法居住”属过度夸大，原文未提及；C项时态与逻辑有误，原文指若不采取行动，现有繁荣将“无法维持”，而非已经大幅削弱；D项原文并未比较发达与发展中国家的破坏程度。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is said about water scarcity in some of the poorest regions?", "options": ["It is getting so serious that there is little hope of solution.", "It largely accounts for their slow economic development.", "It can hardly be relieved if no drastic measures are taken.", "It is primarily caused by the acceleration of climate change."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken.", "explanation": "定位第2段第2句。前句指出水资源匮乏是最贫穷地区的祸患，紧接着指出“There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken”（若不采取根本性行动，这一绝望局面几乎没有得到缓解的希望）。C项中“hardly be relieved”对应“little prospect of... being remedied”，“drastic measures”对应“radical action”，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项断章取义，漏掉了“without radical action”这一关键条件；D项以偏概全，第2段末句列举了人口增长、气候变化、快速城市化、消费上升与土地退化五重威胁，并非主要由气候变化引发。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does Achim Steiner say about the environmental condition?", "options": ["It will deteriorate worldwide.", "It is attracting global attention.", "It is being slowly remedied globally.", "It will shrink the world's population."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "\"If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and consumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline,\" warned UN executive director Achim Steiner.", "explanation": "定位第3段。联合国执行主任阿希姆·施泰纳警告称，如果当前趋势持续且世界未能改善生产与消费模式，那么“the state of the world's environment will continue to decline”（世界环境状况将继续恶化）。A项中的“deteriorate worldwide”精准同义替换了原文的“the world's environment will continue to decline”，故A项为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B、C两项虽能与前文“各国政府作出努力”产生联想，但并非Achim Steiner的原话观点，且第7段提到的“partial success”仅针对富裕国家；D项“世界人口萎缩”属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What is the dilemma developing countries face?", "options": ["They cannot modernise farming without causing land degradation.", "They cannot promote industrialisation without polluting waterways.", "They cannot boost crop yields without causing greenhouse gas emissions.", "They cannot catch up with rich countries without sacrificing the environment."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "This will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people. Climate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural fertilisers used in agriculture which increased by more than a quarter between 2000 and 2010.", "explanation": "定位第6段。该段指出全球碳排放上升将长期制约发展中经济体养活本国人民（feed their own people）的能力；同时，农业中使用的化学和天然肥料排放的温室气体十年间增长超四分之一，加剧了气候变化。由此可知，发展中国家陷入“要提高粮食产量就需施肥，而施肥又会增加温室气体排放并恶化气候”的两难境地，精准对应C项，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项是第5段提到的普遍性农业问题，未紧扣第6段发展中国家面临的粮食与碳排两难；B项“工业化污染水道”与D项“不牺牲环境就无法追赶富国”均偏离第6段和第7段核心论述。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What should developing countries do in their future development according to the passage?", "options": ["They turn to developed countries for the assistance they need.", "They remedy environmental damage by slowing economic growth.", "They avoid damaging interference from international institutions.", "They improve people's livelihood without harming the environment."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change, which has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment.", "explanation": "定位第7段末句。原文指出，发展中国家未来发展道路更具改变潜力，国际机构因此设计了更具可持续性的增长路径，旨在“both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment”（既减轻贫困又保护环境）。D项中“improve people's livelihood”（改善民生）对应“alleviate poverty”，“without harming the environment”对应“preserve the environment”，故选D。", "trapNote": "A项“向发达国家求助”文中未提（第4段只说工具存在于发达国家但面临不被使用的危险）；B项“放缓经济增长”与可持续减贫相悖；C项“避免国际机构干预”与原文国际机构积极设计路径的态度相反。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 退化，恶化，破坏", "note": "源自 degrade，本文中分别指“自然资源退化”和“土地退化”，环保类阅读高频核心词。", "word": "degradation"}, {"gloss": "v. 在速度上超过，赶过", "note": "构词法 out-（超过）+ pace（速度），指人类破坏速度超过地球自我修复速度。", "word": "outpace"}, {"gloss": "v. 补救，改善；n. 补救措施", "note": "第2、7段均出现其动词用法，意为“挽救、补救（恶劣局面或受损环境）”。", "word": "remedy"}, {"gloss": "v. 加重，使恶化", "note": "文中“Climate change is aggravated by...”意为“气候变化因……而加剧”，近义词有 worsen, exacerbate。", "word": "aggravate"}, {"gloss": "v. 减轻，缓和", "note": "常与 poverty, suffering, pressure 搭配，“alleviate poverty”意为“减轻贫困、脱贫”。", "word": "alleviate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The study concludes that without radical action the level of prosperity that millions of people in the developed world count on will be impossible to maintain or extend to poorer countries.", "point": "without radical action 含蓄表示条件；第一个 that 引导宾语从句，第二个 that 引导定语从句修饰 prosperity，count on 意为“依赖、指望”。", "structure": "主句 + that引导宾语从句（含without介词短语作条件状语 + that引导定语从句修饰prosperity）", "zh": "该研究得出结论：如果不采取根本性行动，发达国家数百万人所依赖的繁荣水平将无法维持，也无法惠及较贫穷的国家。"}, {"en": "These included measures to reduce air pollution; to control the damage to marine ecosystems, which can have a huge effect on fish stocks on which hundreds of millions of people depend; and to curb the degradation of land where modern agricultural methods were pursued without regard to the longer-term consequences.", "point": "分号清晰分隔三个并列的 to do 短语；注意双重定语从句（which 修饰前文分句，on which 修饰 fish stocks）及 where 引导的地点定语从句。", "structure": "主谓宾 + 三个并列不定式作后置定语（分别嵌套which非限制性定语从句、on which定语从句与where定语从句）", "zh": "这些措施包括：减少空气污染；控制对海洋生态系统的破坏（这可能对数亿人赖以为生的鱼类资源造成巨大影响）；以及遏制因推行现代农业方法却不顾长期后果而导致的土地退化。"}, {"en": "But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change, which has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment.", "point": "which 指代前面整个主句内容；be supposed to do 表示“旨在、理应”；alleviate poverty 意为“减轻贫困”。", "structure": "转折主句 + which引导的非限制性定语从句 + that引导的定语从句（含both... and... 并列不定式）", "zh": "但在发展中国家，未来发展道路更具转变潜力，这促使国际机构设计出更具可持续性的增长路径，旨在同时减轻贫困并保护环境。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“degradation... outpacing”同义替换为“doing more damage... than”，“absorb the damage”对应“cope with”。", "option": "Humans are doing more damage to the earth than it can cope with.", "original": "Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage"}, {"note": "“little prospect”对应“hardly”，“remedied”对应“relieved”，“radical action”替换为“drastic measures”。", "option": "It can hardly be relieved if no drastic measures are taken.", "original": "little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken"}, {"note": "“continue to decline”精简为动词“deteriorate（恶化）”，“the world's”转为副词“worldwide”。", "option": "It will deteriorate worldwide.", "original": "the state of the world's environment will continue to decline"}, {"note": "综合第6段两句因果逻辑，将“养活人民”与“化肥增产导致温室气体排放”归纳为生产与减排的两难。", "option": "They cannot boost crop yields without causing greenhouse gas emissions.", "original": "strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people... emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural fertilisers"}, {"note": "“alleviate poverty（脱贫）”意译为“improve people's livelihood（改善民生）”，“preserve”对应“without harming”。", "option": "They improve people's livelihood without harming the environment.", "original": "both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L2", "exam": "cet6", "id": "cet6-202106-p1", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["Humans are fascinated by the source of their failings and virtues. This preoccupation inevitably leads to an old debate: whether nature or nurture moulds us more. A revolution in genetics has poised this as a modern political question about the character of our society: if personalities are hard-wired into our genes, what can governments do to help us? It feels morally questionable, yet claims of genetic selection by intelligence are making headlines.", "This is down to \"hereditarian\" science and a recent paper claimed \"differences in exam performance between pupils attending selective and non-selective schools mirror the genetic differences between them\". With such an assertion, the work was predictably greeted by a lot of absurd claims about \"genetics determining academic success\". What the research revealed was the rather less surprising result: the educational benefits of selective schools largely disappear once pupils' inborn ability and socio-economic background were taken into account. It is a glimpse of the blindingly obvious—and there's nothing to back strongly either a hereditary or environmental argument.", "Yet the paper does say children are \"unintentionally genetically selected\" by the school system. Central to hereditarian science is a tall claim: that identifiable variations in genetic sequences can predict an individual's aptness to learn, reason and solve problems. This is problematic on many levels. A teacher could not seriously tell a parent their child has a low genetic tendency to study when external factors clearly exist. Unlike-minded academics say the inheritability of human traits is scientifically unsound. At best there is a weak statistical association and not a causal link between DNA and intelligence. Yet sophisticated statistics are used to create an intimidatory atmosphere of scientific certainty.", "While there's an undoubted genetic basis to individual difference, it is wrong to think that socially defined groups can be genetically accounted for. The fixation on genes as destiny is surely false too. Medical predictability can rarely be based on DNA alone; the environment matters too. Something as complex as intellect is likely to be affected by many factors beyond genes. If hereditarians want to advance their cause it will require more balanced interpretation and not just acts of advocacy.", "Genetic selection is a way of exerting influence over others, \"the ultimate collective control of human destinies,\" as writer H. G. Wells put it. Knowledge becomes power and power requires a sense of responsibility. In understanding cognitive ability, we must not elevate discrimination to a science; allowing people to climb the ladder of life only as far as their cells might suggest. This will need a more sceptical eye on the science. As technology progresses, we all have a duty to make sure that we shape a future that we would want to find ourselves in."], "questions": [{"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "a recent paper claimed \"differences in exam performance between pupils attending selective and non-selective schools mirror the genetic differences between them\".", "explanation": "由题干中的 recent research paper 定位至第 2 段第 1 句。该句指出，一篇近期论文声称，就读于选拔性学校和非选拔性学校的学生在考试成绩上的差异反映了他们之间的基因差异，由此引发“基因决定学业成功”的论断。选项 D 中的 Students' academic performance is determined by their genes 是对原文考试成绩差异反映基因差异及 genetics determining academic success 的同义转述。", "no": 46, "options": ["The type of school students attend makes a difference to their future.", "Genetic differences between students are far greater than supposed.", "The advantages of selective schools are too obvious to ignore.", "Students' academic performance is determined by their genes."], "stem": "What did a recent research paper claim?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 利用第 2 段后文的 selective schools 和 blindingly obvious 拼凑信息，将“研究结果显而易见且无法有力支持任何一方论点”偷换为“选拔性学校的优势显而易见”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "It is a glimpse of the blindingly obvious—and there's nothing to back strongly either a hereditary or environmental argument.", "explanation": "由题干中的 recent research 定位至第 2 段后半部分。作者指出，一旦考虑学生的先天能力与社会经济背景，选拔性学校的教育优势就基本消失，且没有任何证据能有力支持遗传论或环境论。由此可见，作者认为该研究的结论缺乏有力支撑，其结果是值得怀疑的（questionable），对应选项 A。", "no": 47, "options": ["Its result was questionable.", "Its implication was positive.", "Its influence was rather negligible.", "Its conclusions were enlightening."], "stem": "What does the author think of the recent research?", "trapNote": "干扰项 B 和 D 属于正反颠倒，将作者对该研究的否定与批判（absurd claims、nothing to back strongly）曲解为意义积极或结论具有启发性。", "type": "态度题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "At best there is a weak statistical association and not a causal link between DNA and intelligence.", "explanation": "由题干中的 relationship between DNA and intelligence 定位至第 3 段倒数第 2 句。原文明确指出，DNA 与智力之间充其量只存在微弱的统计学关联，而不存在因果关系（not a causal link）。选项 B 中的 not one of cause and effect 是对原文 not a causal link 的直接同义替换。", "no": 48, "options": ["It is one of scientific certainty.", "It is not one of cause and effect.", "It is subject to interpretation of statistics.", "It is not fully examined by gene scientists."], "stem": "What does the author say about the relationship between DNA and intelligence?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 和 C 属于断章取义与曲解文意，第 3 段末句指出“复杂的统计学被用来营造一种科学确定性的威慑氛围”，而非说明 DNA 与智力之间确实具有科学确定性或取决于统计解读。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "If hereditarians want to advance their cause it will require more balanced interpretation and not just acts of advocacy.", "explanation": "由题干中的 hereditarians 定位至第 4 段最后两句。作者先指出环境因素同样重要，像智力这样复杂的特质很可能受到基因以外诸多因素的影响，随后提出遗传论者若想推进其主张，需要更均衡的解读（more balanced interpretation），而非一味鼓吹。选项 A 中的 Take all relevant factors into account in interpreting their data 精准概括了这两句的核心要求。", "no": 49, "options": ["Take all relevant factors into account in interpreting their data.", "Conduct their research using more sophisticated technology.", "Gather gene data from people of all social classes.", "Cooperate with social scientists in their research."], "stem": "What do hereditarians need to do to make their claims convincing?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 利用第 4 段首句中的 socially defined groups 进行偷换概念，将“不能用基因解释社会群体差异”曲解为“需要采集各社会阶层的基因数据”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "In understanding cognitive ability, we must not elevate discrimination to a science; allowing people to climb the ladder of life only as far as their cells might suggest.", "explanation": "定位至文章第 5 段第 3 句。作者明确警告，在理解认知能力时，我们绝不能将歧视提升为一门科学（must not elevate discrimination to a science），不能仅凭基因所暗示的限度来限定人们的人生发展。选项 D 中的 Promoting discrimination in the name of science 是对“以科学名义助长歧视”的准确同义转述。", "no": 50, "options": ["Exaggerating the power of technology in shaping the world.", "Losing sight of professional ethics in conducting research.", "Misunderstanding the findings of human cognition research.", "Promoting discrimination in the name of science."], "stem": "What does the author warn against in the passage?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 属于张冠李戴兼正反颠倒，末句 as technology progresses 意为“随着技术进步，我们有责任塑造想要的未来”，并未警告“夸大技术改变世界的力量”。", "type": "细节题"}], "sourceLabel": "2021.06 六级真题第1套", "subtitle": "遗传基因、教育选拔与科学伦理", "timeLimitMin": 10, "title": "Intelligence Genes: Going Beyond the Evidence", "year": "2021.06", "wordCount": 457, "examSet": "2021.06 六级真题 第1套", "translations": ["人类总是对自身缺点和美德的根源充满好奇。这种痴迷不可避免地引向一个古老的争论：究竟是先天基因还是后天培养对我们的塑造更大。遗传学的一场革命将此推上了现代政治议题的舞台，直指我们社会的特质：如果性格早已固化在基因之中，政府又能采取什么措施来帮助我们呢？这听起来在道德上存疑，但“按智力进行基因筛选”的论调却频频登上新闻头条。", "这源于所谓的“遗传决定论”科学，近期一篇论文宣称，“重点学校与非重点学校学生在考试成绩上的差异，反映了他们之间的基因差异”。有此断言在前，这项研究不出所料地引发了大量关于“基因决定学业成败”的荒谬言论。然而，该研究真正揭示的却是一个并不令人意外的结果：一旦把学生的先天能力与社会经济背景考虑在内，重点学校的教育优势很大程度上就消失了。这不过是对显而易见事实的管窥——既没有强有力的证据支持遗传论，也无法证明环境论。", "不过，该论文确实指出，儿童正被学校体系“无意中进行了基因筛选”。遗传决定论科学的核心是一个夸大其词的论断：基因序列中可识别的变异能够预测一个人学习、推理和解决问题的能力倾向。这在许多层面上都存在问题。当明显的外部因素存在时，老师不可能严肃地告诉家长他们的孩子天生缺乏学习的基因倾向。持不同意见的学者认为，人类特质的遗传性在科学上是站不住脚的。DNA与智力之间至多只存在微弱的统计学关联，而非因果关系。然而，复杂的统计数据却被用来营造一种令人望而生畏的“科学确定性”氛围。", "尽管个体差异无疑有其遗传基础，但认为社会所界定的群体也可以用基因来解释则是错误的。将基因视为命运的执念同样是谬误。医学预测很少能单靠DNA做出，环境同样至关重要。像智力如此复杂的事物，很可能受到基因以外众多因素的影响。遗传决定论者若想推进自己的主张，需要的将是更为平衡客观的解读，而不仅仅是一味的鼓吹。", "正如作家H·G·威尔斯所言，基因筛选是一种对他人施加影响的手段，是“对人类命运的终极集体控制”。知识就是力量，而力量需要责任感。在理解认知能力时，我们绝不能把歧视拔高成一门科学，让人只能顺着细胞暗示的高度去攀登人生的阶梯。这就需要我们对相关科学抱有更加审慎和怀疑的眼光。随着科技的进步，我们每个人都有责任确保塑造一个我们愿意身处其中的未来。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "塑造，影响", "note": "熟词僻义：名词常指“模具、霉菌”，作动词意为“塑造（性格、观念等）”，等同于美式拼写 mold。", "word": "mould"}, {"gloss": "使成为，将……摆在……位置", "note": "熟词僻义：名词常考“镇定、风度”，此处作及物动词，与 as 搭配表示“将……确立/摆在……的地位”。", "word": "poise"}, {"gloss": "反映，折射", "note": "熟词僻义：名词为“镜子”，在六级阅读中作动词高频意为“反映、映射”，常可同义替换为 reflect。", "word": "mirror"}, {"gloss": "合理的，站得住脚的", "note": "熟词僻义：作形容词不指“声音”，而是“可靠的、科学的、健全的”；文中否定形式 unsound 意为“缺乏科学依据的”。", "word": "sound"}, {"gloss": "鼓吹，拥护，倡议", "note": "高频考词：对应动词 advocate（提倡）；文中与 balanced interpretation（客观平衡的解读）形成对比，带有“片面游说/鼓吹”的含义。", "word": "advocacy"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "What the research revealed was the rather less surprising result: the educational benefits of selective schools largely disappear once pupils' inborn ability and socio-economic background were taken into account.", "point": "what 引导的主语从句 + once 引导的条件/时间状语从句 + 被动语态", "structure": "主干为 What the research revealed（主语从句） + was（系动词） + the rather less surprising result（表语）；冒号后为结果的具体内容，其中主句为 the educational benefits... largely disappear，once 引导状语从句表示“一旦把学生的先天能力和社会经济背景纳入考量”。", "zh": "这项研究揭示的结果其实并不那么令人惊讶：一旦将学生的先天能力与社会经济背景考虑在内，重点学校带来的教育优势在很大程度上便会消失。"}, {"en": "Central to hereditarian science is a tall claim: that identifiable variations in genetic sequences can predict an individual's aptness to learn, reason and solve problems.", "point": "表语前置引起的完全倒装 + that 引导的同位语从句", "structure": "主句采用完全倒装结构，正常语序为 A tall claim is central to hereditarian science；冒号后 that 引导同位语从句，解释说明 a tall claim 的具体内容，从句中不定式短语 to learn, reason and solve problems 作后置定语修饰 aptness。", "zh": "遗传决定论科学的核心是一个夸大其词的论断：基因序列中可识别的差异能够预测一个人学习、推理和解决问题的倾向。"}, {"en": "In understanding cognitive ability, we must not elevate discrimination to a science; allowing people to climb the ladder of life only as far as their cells might suggest.", "point": "介词+动名词短语作状语 + 现在分词短语作伴随/结果状语 + as far as 引导的程度状语从句", "structure": "In understanding cognitive ability 作方式/时间状语；主干为 we must not elevate discrimination to a science；分号后的现在分词短语 allowing people to climb... 补充说明把歧视拔高为科学所带来的后果，其中 only as far as their cells might suggest 修饰 climb。", "zh": "在认识认知能力的过程中，我们绝不能把歧视拔高为一门科学，从而只允许人们在细胞所预示的有限高度内攀登人生阶梯。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第46题：原文“mirror the genetic differences（反映基因差异）”被正确选项概括为“由基因决定”。", "option": "academic performance is determined by their genes", "original": "differences in exam performance ... mirror the genetic differences"}, {"note": "第47题：原文指“既无强有力证据支持遗传论，也无力支持环境论”，对应选项“结果存疑”。", "option": "Its result was questionable", "original": "nothing to back strongly either a hereditary or environmental argument"}, {"note": "第48题：causal link（因果联系）同义替换为 cause and effect（因果关系）。", "option": "It is not one of cause and effect", "original": "not a causal link between DNA and intelligence"}, {"note": "第49题：more balanced interpretation（更平衡客观的解读）同义替换为“考虑所有相关因素”。", "option": "Take all relevant factors into account in interpreting their data", "original": "require more balanced interpretation and not just acts of advocacy"}, {"note": "第50题：elevate discrimination to a science（将歧视拔高为科学）对应“打着科学幌子助长歧视”。", "option": "Promoting discrimination in the name of science", "original": "must not elevate discrimination to a science"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L2", "exam": "cet6", "id": "cet6-202106-p2", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["Nicola Sturgeon's speech last Tuesday setting out the Scottish government's legislative programme for the year ahead confirmed what was already pretty clear. Scottish councils are set to be the first in the UK with the power to levy charges on visitors, with Edinburgh likely to lead the way.", "Tourist taxes are not new. The Himayalan kingdom of Bhutan has a longstanding policy of charging visitors a daily fee. France's tax on overnight stays was introduced to assist thermal spa towns to develop, and around half of French local authorities use it today.", "But such levies are on the rise. Moves by Barcelona and Venice to deal with the phenomenon of \"over-tourism\" through the use of charges have recently gained prominence. Japan and Greece are among the countries to have recently introduced tourist taxes.", "That the UK lags behind is due to our weak, by international standards, local government, as well as the opposition to taxes and regulation of our aggressively pro-market ruling party. Some UK cities have lobbied without success for the power to levy a charge on visitors. Such levies are no universal remedy as the amounts raised would be tiny compared with what has been taken away by central government since 2010. Still, it is to be hoped that the Scottish government's bold move will prompt others to act. There is no reason why visitors to the UK, or domestic tourists on holiday in hotspots such as Cornwall, should be exempt from taxation—particularly when vital local services including waste collection, park maintenance and arts and culture spending are under unprecedented strain.", "On the contrary, compelling tourists to make a financial contribution to the places they visit beyond their personal consumption should be part of a wider cultural shift. Westerners with disposable incomes have often behaved as if they have a right to go wherever they choose with little regard for the consequences. Just as the environmental harm caused by aviation and other transport must come under far greater scrutiny, the social cost of tourism must also be confronted. This includes the impact of short-term lets on housing costs and quality of life for residents. Several European capitals, including Paris and Berlin, are leading a campaign for tougher regulation by the European Union. It also includes the impact of overcrowding, litter and the kinds of behaviour associated with noisy parties.", "There is no \"one size fits all\" solution to this problem. The existence of new revenue streams for some but not all councils is complicated, and businesses are often opposed, fearing higher costs will make them uncompetitive. But those places that want them must be given the chance to make tourist taxes work."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Scottish councils are set to be the first in the UK with the power to levy charges on visitors, with Edinburgh likely to lead the way.", "explanation": "由题干中的 Nicola Sturgeon's speech 定位至第 1 段。该段指出，尼古拉·斯特金上周二的讲话确认了苏格兰各地方议会将成为英国首批有权向游客征税的机构，其中爱丁堡很可能率先实施。选项 B 中的 Tourists will have to pay a tax to visit Scotland 是对 levy charges on visitors 的同义替换。", "no": 51, "options": ["The UK is set to adjust its policy on taxation.", "Tourists will have to pay a tax to visit Scotland.", "The UK will take new measures to boost tourism.", "Edinburgh contributes most to Scotland's tourism."], "stem": "What do we learn from Nicola Sturgeon's speech?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 属于以偏概全兼偷换概念，讲话明确的是苏格兰地方议会将有权征收旅游税，而非英国全国调整税收政策。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "the UK lags behind is due to our weak, by international standards, local government, as well as the opposition to taxes and regulation of our aggressively pro-market ruling party", "explanation": "由题干中的 the UK has been slow in imposing the tourist tax 定位至第 4 段首句。该句指出，英国之所以落后（lags behind），原因在于地方政府权力薄弱，以及高度支持自由市场的执政党反对征税和监管（opposition to taxes and regulation of our aggressively pro-market ruling party）。选项 C 中的 Its ruling party is opposed to taxes and regulation 与原文完全吻合。", "no": 52, "options": ["Its government wants to attract more tourists.", "The tax is unlikely to add much to its revenue.", "Its ruling party is opposed to taxes and regulation.", "It takes time for local governments to reach consensus."], "stem": "How come the UK has been slow in imposing the tourist tax?", "trapNote": "干扰项 B 利用第 4 段第 3 句中“相对于中央政府自 2010 年削减的经费，旅游税筹集的金额微不足道”进行强加因果，原文并未以此作为英国迟迟未征旅游税的原因。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "particularly when vital local services including waste collection, park maintenance and arts and culture spending are under unprecedented strain.", "explanation": "由题干中的 Both international and domestic visitors 定位至第 4 段末句。原文指出，没有理由免除赴英外国游客或本国度假游客的税费，尤其是当垃圾清运、公园维护及文化艺术支出等重要地方公共服务正承受前所未有的财政压力（under unprecedented strain）时。选项 D 中的 ease its financial burden of providing local services 准确概括了征收旅游税缓解地方服务资金压力的目的。", "no": 53, "options": ["elevate its tourism to international standards", "improve the welfare of its maintenance workers", "promote its cultural exchange with other nations", "ease its financial burden of providing local services"], "stem": "Both international and domestic visitors in the UK should pay tourist tax so as to ____.", "trapNote": "干扰项 B 和 C 属于偷换概念，将第 4 段末句列举的地方服务项目 park maintenance 和 arts and culture spending 分别曲解为“改善维修工人福利”和“促进跨国文化交流”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Westerners with disposable incomes have often behaved as if they have a right to go wherever they choose with little regard for the consequences.", "explanation": "由题干中的 Western tourists 定位至第 5 段第 2–3 句。作者指出，拥有可支配收入的西方人往往表现得仿佛自己有权去任何想去的地方，几乎不顾及后果（with little regard for the consequences），紧接着指出旅游业的社会成本（social cost of tourism）必须得到正视。选项 A 中的 don't seem to care about 是对 with little regard for 的同义转述。", "no": 54, "options": ["They don't seem to care about the social cost of tourism.", "They don't seem to mind paying for additional services.", "They deem travel an important part of their life.", "They subject the effects of tourism to scrutiny."], "stem": "What does the author say about Western tourists?", "trapNote": "干扰项 D 属于偷换主语兼正反颠倒，第 5 段第 3 句主张“应当对交通造成的环境危害进行更严格审查”，而非西方游客主动审视旅游业的影响。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "businesses are often opposed, fearing higher costs will make them uncompetitive. But those places that want them must be given the chance to make tourist taxes work.", "explanation": "由题干中的 opinions about the levy of tourist tax 定位至第 6 段。原文指出，商界往往反对征收旅游税，担心成本上升会削弱竞争力；但同时也有地方想要征收该税（places that want them），且第 4 段也提到部分英国城市曾游说争取征税权而执政党反对。由此可推断，英国各方对征收旅游税意见存在分歧（Divided），故选 C。", "no": 55, "options": ["Supportive.", "Skeptical.", "Divided.", "Unclear."], "stem": "What are UK people's opinions about the levy of tourist tax?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 和 B 均属于以偏概全，只关注了支持征税的地方城市或反对征税的商界与执政党中的一方立场，忽略了正反意见并存的事实。", "type": "推断题"}], "sourceLabel": "2021.06 六级真题第1套", "subtitle": "旅游税政策、过度旅游与地方公共服务", "timeLimitMin": 10, "title": "Tourist Taxes: Travelers Should Pay Their Way", "year": "2021.06", "wordCount": 447, "examSet": "2021.06 六级真题 第1套", "translations": ["苏格兰首席大臣妮古拉·斯特金上周二发表讲话，阐述了苏格兰政府未来一年的立法规划，证实了一件本已相当明确的事情：苏格兰地方议会将成为英国首批有权向游客征税的机构，其中爱丁堡很可能会率先实施。", "旅游税并非新鲜事物。喜马拉雅山区的王国不丹长期以来就实行向游客按日收费的政策。法国针对过夜住宿征税最初是为了扶持温泉小镇的发展，如今约半数法国地方政府都在征收这一税种。", "不过，这类税费正在呈上升趋势。巴塞罗那和威尼斯为应对“过度旅游”现象而采取的收费举措近来备受瞩目。日本和希腊也属于近期开征旅游税的国家之列。", "英国之所以落后，一方面是因为按国际标准来看我们的地方政府权力薄弱，另一方面也是因为我们极端亲市场的执政党反对征税和监管。一些英国城市曾游说争取向游客收费的权力，但均未成功。这类税费并非万能灵药，因为与2010年以来中央政府削减的拨款相比，它能筹集到的资金微乎其微。尽管如此，人们仍希望苏格兰政府的大胆举措能促使其他地区采取行动。前来英国的海外游客，或是在康沃尔等热门景点度假的国内游客，都没有理由免于缴税——尤其是在垃圾清运、公园维护以及艺术文化支出等重要地方服务正面临前所未有压力的当下。", "相反，强制游客在个人消费之外为所到访的地方做出财政贡献，应当成为更广泛文化转变的一部分。拥有可支配收入的西方人向来表现得仿佛自己有权随心所欲地去任何地方，而几乎不顾及后果。正如航空及其他交通方式造成的环境破坏必须受到更为严格的审视一样，旅游业带来的社会成本也必须得到正视。这包括短期出租屋对当地居民住房成本和生活质量的影响——包括巴黎和柏林在内的多个欧洲首都正在牵头呼吁欧盟加强监管。此外，这还包括过度拥挤、乱扔垃圾以及喧闹派对所伴随的种种不良行为带来的影响。", "解决这一问题并没有“一刀切”的方案。部分议会拥有新的收入来源而其他议会没有，这种情况相当复杂；企业也往往持反对态度，担心成本上升会削弱自身的竞争力。但是，对于那些希望实施旅游税的地方，必须给予它们让这项制度发挥作用的机会。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "征收（税款）；税款", "note": "高频考词：作动词常与 tax/charge on 搭配表示“对……征税”；作名词指“税款、征收额”。", "word": "levy"}, {"gloss": "免除的，豁免的", "note": "高频搭配：be exempt from 意为“免于……、被豁免……”；亦可作及物动词表示“免除”。", "word": "exempt"}, {"gloss": "压力，重负", "note": "熟词僻义：除“拉伤、菌株”外，在经济与社会类文章中常考 under strain，表示“承受巨大压力/资金捉襟见肘”。", "word": "strain"}, {"gloss": "仔细审查，监督", "note": "高频考词：常考搭配 come under scrutiny 意为“受到严格审查”，其动词形式为 scrutinize（细查）。", "word": "scrutiny"}, {"gloss": "出租房，短租屋", "note": "熟词僻义：由动词 let（出租）转化而来的名词，short-term lets 指“短期出租屋/民宿”，常见于英式英语。", "word": "let"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "That the UK lags behind is due to our weak, by international standards, local government, as well as the opposition to taxes and regulation of our aggressively pro-market ruling party.", "point": "that 引导的主语从句 + 插入语 + as well as 连接的并列名词短语", "structure": "主语为 That the UK lags behind（that 不能省略），谓语系表结构为 is due to...；其中 by international standards 为插入语修饰 weak，as well as 连接两个并列原因：弱势的地方政府，以及执政党对税收和监管的反对。", "zh": "英国之所以落后，一方面是因为按国际标准来看我们的地方政府权力薄弱，另一方面也是因为我们极端亲市场的执政党反对征税和监管。"}, {"en": "There is no reason why visitors to the UK, or domestic tourists on holiday in hotspots such as Cornwall, should be exempt from taxation—particularly when vital local services including waste collection, park maintenance and arts and culture spending are under unprecedented strain.", "point": "There is no reason why... 固定句型 + when 引导的时间/原因状语从句 + 长并列主语", "structure": "主句为 There is no reason why...（……毫无道理），why 引导定语从句修饰 reason；破折号后 particularly when... 进一步说明理由，从句主语为包含三个并列成分的 vital local services。", "zh": "前来英国的海外游客，或是在康沃尔等热门景点度假的国内游客，都没有理由免于缴税——尤其是在垃圾清运、公园维护以及艺术文化支出等重要地方服务正面临前所未有压力的当下。"}, {"en": "Just as the environmental harm caused by aviation and other transport must come under far greater scrutiny, the social cost of tourism must also be confronted.", "point": "Just as... 引导的类比状语从句 + 过去分词短语作后置定语 + 被动语态", "structure": "Just as... 引导比较/类比从句，其中 caused by aviation and other transport 为过去分词短语作后置定语修饰 environmental harm；主句为 the social cost of tourism must also be confronted。", "zh": "正如航空及其他交通方式造成的环境破坏必须受到更为严格的审视一样，旅游业带来的社会成本也必须得到正视。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第51题：levy charges on visitors（向游客收费）从纳税人角度同义转换为 pay a tax to visit（缴税游览）。", "option": "pay a tax to visit", "original": "power to levy charges on visitors"}, {"note": "第52题：lags behind（落后）对应 slow in（进展缓慢）；opposition to（对……的反对）转换为被动形容词词组 be opposed to。", "option": "slow in imposing the tourist tax ... ruling party is opposed to taxes and regulation", "original": "lags behind is due to ... opposition to taxes and regulation of our aggressively pro-market ruling party"}, {"note": "第53题：地方服务承受巨大压力（under strain），反推征税是为了减轻提供地方服务的财政负担。", "option": "ease its financial burden of providing local services", "original": "vital local services ... are under unprecedented strain"}, {"note": "第54题：with little regard for（几乎不顾及）同义替换为 don't seem to care about（似乎不在乎）。", "option": "don't seem to care about the social cost", "original": "with little regard for the consequences"}, {"note": "第55题：商家反对而部分地方支持，体现公众对此意见“存在分歧（Divided）”，属于态度的归纳概括。", "option": "Divided", "original": "businesses are often opposed ... But those places that want them"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L2", "exam": "cet6", "id": "cet6-202012-p1", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["What is the place of art in a culture of inattention? Recent visitors to the Louvre report that tourists can now spend only a minute in front of the Mona Lisa before being asked to move on. Much of that time, for some of them, is spent taking photographs not even of the painting but of themselves with the painting in the background.", "One view is that we have democratised tourism and gallery-going so much that we have made it effectively impossible to appreciate what we've travelled to see. In this oversubscribed society, experience becomes a commodity like any other. There are queues to climb Mt. Jolmo Lungma as well as to see famous paintings. Leisure, thus conceived, is hard labour, and returning to work becomes a well-earned break from the ordeal.", "What gets lost in this industrialised haste is the quality of looking. Consider an extreme example, the late philosopher Richard Wollheim. When he visited the Louvre he could spent as much as four hours sitting before a painting. The first hour, he claimed, was necessary for misperceptions to be eliminated. It was only then that the picture would begin to disclose itself. This seems unthinkable today, but it is still possible to organise. Even in the busiest museums there are many rooms and many pictures worth hours of contemplation which the crowds largely ignore. Sometimes the largest crowds are partly the products of bad management; the Mona Lisa is such a hurried experience today partly because the museum is being reorganised. The Uffizi in Florence, another site of cultural pilgrimage, has cut its entry queues down to seven minutes by clever management. And there are some forms of art, those designed to be spectacles as well as objects of contemplation, which can work perfectly well in the face of huge crowds.", "Olafur Eliasson's current Tate Modern show, for instance, might seem nothing more than an entertainment, overrun as it is with kids romping（喧闹地玩耍）in fog rooms and spray mist installations. But it's more than that: where Eliasson is at his most entertaining, he is at his most serious too, and his disorienting installations bring home the reality of the destructive effects we are having on the planet—not least what we are doing to the glaciers of Eliasson's beloved Iceland.", "Marcel Proust, another lover of the Louvre, wrote: “It is only through art that we can escape from ourselves and know how another person sees the universe, whose landscapes would otherwise have remained as unknown as any on the moon.” If any art remains worth seeing, it must lead us to such escapes. But a minute in front of a painting in a hurried crowd won't do that."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "One view is that we have democratised tourism and gallery-going so much that we have made it effectively impossible to appreciate what we've travelled to see.", "explanation": "定位至第1段第2–3句及第2段第1句。第1段描述游客在《蒙娜丽莎》前只能停留一分钟且忙于以画为背景自拍的现象，第2段第1句随即点明实质：旅游和观展的大众化使人们几乎无法真正欣赏艺术作品。选项B中的“an age of mass tourism”与“near impossibility of appreciating art”分别同义替换原文“democratised tourism and gallery-going”和“effectively impossible to appreciate”。", "no": 46, "options": ["The enormous appeal of a great piece of artistic work to tourists.", "The near impossibility of appreciating art in an age of mass tourism.", "The ever-growing commercial value of long-cherished artistic works.", "The real difficulty in getting a glimpse at a masterpiece amid a crowd."], "stem": "What does the scene at the Louvre demonstrate according to the author?", "trapNote": "干扰项A（艺术品极具吸引力）和D（人群中难看清名画）均偷换了第1段卢浮宫场景的论证重心——游客注重的是自拍打卡而非欣赏画作本身，C项则将“体验商品化”曲解为画作商业价值上升。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The first hour, he claimed, was necessary for misperceptions to be eliminated. It was only then that the picture would begin to disclose itself.", "explanation": "定位至第3段第3–5句。哲学家理查德·沃尔海姆在卢浮宫一幅画作前停留长达四小时，因为第一个小时用于消除误解，此后画作才会开始显露其真谛。由此可见，充分欣赏和领悟一件艺术作品需要时间，对应选项A。", "no": 47, "options": ["It takes time to appreciate a piece of art fully.", "It is quite common to misinterpret artistic works.", "The longer people contemplate a picture, the more likely they will enjoy it.", "The more time one spends before a painting, the more valuable one finds it."], "stem": "Why did the late philosopher Richard Wollheim spend four hours before a picture?", "trapNote": "干扰项B只截取“第一个小时消除误解”而忽略“后三小时用以领悟真谛”，属于以偏概全；C、D则将原因由“领悟画作真谛”偷换为“享受乐趣”与“发觉珍贵”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The Uffizi in Florence, another site of cultural pilgrimage, has cut its entry queues down to seven minutes by clever management.", "explanation": "定位至第3段第6–9句。作者先指出深度看展可以通过组织管理加以实现，继而对比“管理不善导致拥挤”与“佛罗伦萨乌菲兹美术馆凭借巧妙管理将排队时间缩短至7分钟”的事例。这说明良好的管理是应对大批游客的关键，选项C中的“Good management”和“handling large crowds of visitors”分别对应“clever management”和“cut its entry queues”。", "no": 48, "options": ["Art works in museums should be better taken care of.", "Sites of cultural pilgrimage are always flooded with visitors.", "Good management is key to handling large crowds of visitors.", "Large crowds of visitors cause management problems for museums."], "stem": "What does the case of the Uffizi in Florence show?", "trapNote": "干扰项B（文化朝圣地总是人满为患）和D（大批游客给博物馆带来管理问题）虽符合文意事实，但偏离了作者援引乌菲兹美术馆例子的论证目的，属于答非所问。", "type": "例证题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "But it's more than that: where Eliasson is at his most entertaining, he is at his most serious too", "explanation": "定位至第4段第1–2句。段首指出埃利亚松在泰特现代美术馆的展览表面看似只是儿童嬉闹的娱乐活动，但随后以“But it's more than that”转折，说明他在最富有娱乐性之处也最具严肃性，借迷离装置揭示人类对地球冰川的破坏。由此可知，消遣娱乐与欣赏严肃艺术是可以结合的，对应选项B。", "no": 49, "options": ["Children learn to appreciate art works most effectively while they are playing.", "It is possible to combine entertainment with appreciation of serious art.", "Art works about the environment appeal most to young children.", "Some forms of art can accommodate huge crowds of visitors."], "stem": "What do we learn from Olafur Eliasson's current Tate Modern show?", "trapNote": "干扰项D利用第3段末句“壮观场面可在人群中奏效”设置跨段衔接干扰，以偏概全地忽略了第4段“寓严肃主题于娱乐形式”的核心语义重心；A、C则为原文未比较的无中生有。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "It is only through art that we can escape from ourselves and know how another person sees the universe", "explanation": "定位至第5段第1句马塞尔·普鲁斯特的名言。他指出唯有通过艺术，我们才能超脱自我，并了解他人如何看待宇宙万物（know how another person sees the universe）。选项C中的“see the world from a different perspective”正是对该表述的同义替换。", "no": 50, "options": ["Enable us to live a much fuller life.", "Allow us to escape the harsh reality.", "Help us to see the world from a different perspective.", "Urge us to explore the unknown domain of the universe."], "stem": "What can art do according to Marcel Proust?", "trapNote": "干扰项B将原文脱离的对象“ourselves（自我局限）”偷换为“harsh reality（严酷现实）”，而D项则将“像月球上的景象一样未知”这一修辞类比曲解为激励宇宙探索。", "type": "细节题"}], "sourceLabel": "2020.12 六级真题第1套", "timeLimitMin": 10, "title": "Art in a Culture of Inattention", "year": "2020.12", "wordCount": 452, "examSet": "2020.12 六级真题 第1套", "translations": ["在一个注意力涣散的文化中，艺术身处何地？近期到访卢浮宫的游客反映，如今游人只能在《蒙娜丽莎》前停留一分钟，随后便会被要求离开。对其中一些人而言，这短短时间里的大部分还花在了拍照上——甚至不是拍画作本身，而是以画作为背景给自己自拍。", "一种观点认为，我们把旅游和逛美术馆变得过于大众化，以至于让人实际上根本无法好好欣赏自己远道而来只为一睹风采的艺术品。在这个人满为患的社会里，体验也像其他任何事物一样成了商品。不仅攀登珠穆朗玛峰需要排队，连看名画也得排队。如此一来，休闲成了一场苦差，回到工作岗位反倒成了从这场煎熬中挣得的难得喘息。", "在这种工业化的匆忙中，失去的是审视的品质。不妨看看一个极端的例子——已故哲学家理查德·沃尔海姆。他造访卢浮宫时，能在一幅画前坐上长达四个小时。他声称，最初的一个小时是消除误解所必需的；只有到那时，画作才会开始向他展露真容。这在今天听起来似乎不可思议，但其实依然可以安排做到。即便在最繁忙的博物馆里，也有许多展厅和无数值得静心凝视数小时的画作，只是人群往往对它们视而不见。有时，最拥挤的人潮部分源于管理不善；如今参观《蒙娜丽莎》之所以变成如此仓促的体验，部分原因就在于博物馆正在进行重新布局。另一处文化朝圣地——佛罗伦萨的乌菲齐美术馆，通过巧妙的管理，已将入馆排队时间缩短到了七分钟。此外，还有些艺术形式本就既是为奇观而设计，也是供人沉思的对象，它们在庞大人群面前同样能展现出绝佳的效果。", "例如，奥拉维尔·埃利亚松目前在泰特现代美术馆举办的展览，表面上看似乎不过是一场娱乐——毕竟馆内挤满了在雾室和喷雾装置中喧闹嬉戏的孩子。但它的意义远不止于此：在埃利亚松最具娱乐性的地方，也正是他最严肃深刻之处；他那些令人迷失方向的装置作品让人切身感受到我们对地球造成的破坏性影响——尤其是我们对埃利亚松挚爱的冰岛冰川所做的一切。", "另一位热爱卢浮宫的作家马塞尔·普鲁斯特曾写道：“唯有通过艺术，我们才能跳出自我，去了解另一个人是如何看待宇宙的；否则，他眼中的风景将如同月球上的任何一处景观一样永远不为所知。”如果说还有什么艺术值得一看，它就必须引领我们实现这样的抽离与超越。但在匆忙的人群中站在画作前停留一分钟，是绝无可能做到这一点的。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "使大众化，使普及", "note": "熟词僻义：文中指旅游和逛美术馆面向大众普及，而非政治上的“民主化”。", "word": "democratise"}, {"gloss": "实际上，事实上", "note": "高频阅读释义：CET-6阅读中常不译为“有效地”，而相当于 virtually 或 in effect，表示“实际上”。", "word": "effectively"}, {"gloss": "人满为患的，过度饱和的", "note": "构词法：over-（过度）+ subscribe（认购/报名），指需求远超承载能力。", "word": "oversubscribed"}, {"gloss": "理解，构想，看待", "note": "高频核心词：常见搭配 thus conceived（作如此理解的），过去分词作后置定语。", "word": "conceive"}, {"gloss": "展现，揭示（深层意义）", "note": "熟词僻义：常用义为“披露、公开（信息）”，文中指画作向观者逐渐展现内在意蕴。", "word": "disclose"}, {"gloss": "令人迷失方向的，使人震撼困惑的", "note": "派生词：dis-（否定）+ orient（定向）+ -ing，常用于描述极具冲击力的感官或艺术体验。", "word": "disorienting"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "One view is that we have democratised tourism and gallery-going so much that we have made it effectively impossible to appreciate what we've travelled to see.", "point": "that表语从句 + so...that结果状语从句 + 形式宾语it + what宾语从句", "structure": "主干：One view is that...（表语从句）；从句内部为 we have democratised... so much that...（结果状语从句）；其中 made it impossible to appreciate... 使用 it 作形式宾语，真正宾语为不定式短语，what we've travelled to see 作 appreciate 的宾语从句。", "zh": "一种观点认为，我们把旅游和逛美术馆变得过于大众化，以至于让人实际上根本无法好好欣赏自己远道而来只为一睹风采的艺术品。"}, {"en": "And there are some forms of art, those designed to be spectacles as well as objects of contemplation, which can work perfectly well in the face of huge crowds.", "point": "同位语 + 过去分词短语作后置定语 + 非限制性定语从句", "structure": "主干：there are some forms of art；中间插入语 those designed to be spectacles as well as objects of contemplation 作 some forms of art 的同位语（内含过去分词短语作定语）；句末 which 引导非限制性定语从句修饰 some forms of art。", "zh": "此外，还有些艺术形式本就既是为奇观而设计，也是供人沉思的对象，它们在庞大人群面前同样能展现出绝佳的效果。"}, {"en": "But it's more than that: where Eliasson is at his most entertaining, he is at his most serious too, and his disorienting installations bring home the reality of the destructive effects we are having on the planet—not least what we are doing to the glaciers of Eliasson's beloved Iceland.", "point": "where抽象地点状语从句 + 省略关系代词的定语从句 + what名词性从句", "structure": "冒号后为并列复合句：前半句 where Eliasson is at his most entertaining 引导条件/抽象地点状语从句（“在……的地方/时候”）；后半句主干为 his disorienting installations bring home the reality...，其中 we are having on the planet 为省略关系代词 that/which 的定语从句修饰 effects；破折号后 not least what... 补充说明 reality，what 引导名词性从句。", "zh": "但它的意义远不止于此：在埃利亚松最具娱乐性的地方，也正是他最严肃深刻之处；他那些令人迷失方向的装置作品让人切身感受到我们对地球造成的破坏性影响——尤其是我们对埃利亚松挚爱的冰岛冰川所做的一切。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "democratised tourism 对应 mass tourism；effectively impossible 对应 near impossibility", "option": "The near impossibility of appreciating art in an age of mass tourism.", "original": "democratised tourism and gallery-going so much that we have made it effectively impossible to appreciate what we've travelled to see"}, {"note": "four hours 与 only then...disclose itself 概括为“需要时间才能充分欣赏”", "option": "It takes time to appreciate a piece of art fully.", "original": "could spent as much as four hours sitting before a painting... It was only then that the picture would begin to disclose itself"}, {"note": "clever management 对应 Good management；cut its entry queues down 对应 handling large crowds", "option": "Good management is key to handling large crowds of visitors.", "original": "cut its entry queues down to seven minutes by clever management"}, {"note": "at his most entertaining 与 at his most serious 并重，转述为 combine entertainment with...serious art", "option": "It is possible to combine entertainment with appreciation of serious art.", "original": "where Eliasson is at his most entertaining, he is at his most serious too"}, {"note": "know how another person sees the universe 同义替换为 see the world from a different perspective", "option": "Help us to see the world from a different perspective.", "original": "escape from ourselves and know how another person sees the universe"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L2", "exam": "cet6", "id": "cet6-202012-p2", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["Every five years, the government tries to tell Americans what to put in their bellies. Eat more vegetables. Dial back the fats. It's all based on the best available science for leading a healthy life. But the best available science also has a lot to say about what those food choices do to the environment, and some researchers are annoyed that new dietary recommendations of the USDA (United States Department of Agriculture) released yesterday seem to utterly ignore that fact.", "Broadly, the 2016-2020 dietary recommendations aim for balance: More vegetables, leaner meats and far less sugar.", "But Americans consume more calories per capita than almost any other country in the world. So the things Americans eat have a huge impact on climate change. Soil tilling releases carbon dioxide, and delivery vehicles emit exhaust. The government's dietary guidelines could have done a lot to lower that climate cost. Not just because of their position of authority: The guidelines drive billions of dollars of food production through federal programs like school lunches and nutrition assistance for the needy.", "On its own, plant and animal agriculture contributes 9 percent of all the country's greenhouse gas emissions. That's not counting the fuel burned in transportation, processing, refrigeration, and other waypoints between farm and belly. Red meats are among the biggest and most notorious emitters, but trucking a salad from California to Minnesota in January also carries a significant burden. And greenhouse gas emissions aren't the whole story. Food production is the largest user of fresh water, largest contributor to the loss of biodiversity, and a major contributor to using up natural resources.", "All of these points and more showed up in the Dietary Guidelines Advisory Committee's scientific report, released last February. Miriam Nelson chaired the subcommittee in charge of sustainability for the report, and is disappointed that eating less meat and buying local food aren't in the final product. “Especially if you consider that eating less meat, especially red and processed, has health benefits,” she says.", "So what happened? The official response is that sustainability falls too far outside the guidelines' official scope, which is to provide “nutritional and dietary information.”", "Possibly the agencies in charge of drafting the decisions are too close to the industries they are supposed to regulate. On one hand, the USDA is compiling dietary advice. On the other, their clients are US agriculture companies.", "The line about keeping the guidelines' scope to nutrition and diet doesn't ring quite right with researchers. David Wallinga, for example, says, “In previous guidelines, they've always been concerned with things like food security—which is presumably the mission of the USDA. You absolutely need to be worried about climate impacts and future sustainability if you want secure food in the future.”"], "questions": [{"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "some researchers are annoyed that new dietary recommendations of the USDA (United States Department of Agriculture) released yesterday seem to utterly ignore that fact.", "explanation": "定位至第1段第4–5句。前一句指出最新科学研究对食物选择如何影响环境颇有论述，第5句随即点明研究者恼怒的原因：美国农业部新版膳食建议似乎完全忽视了这一事实（utterly ignore that fact）。选项D中的“takes no notice of”和“potential impact on the environment”分别同义替换“utterly ignore”与前文的“what those food choices do to the environment”。", "no": 51, "options": ["It ignores the harmful effect of red meat and processed food on health.", "Too much emphasis is given to eating less meat and buying local food.", "The dietary recommendations are not based on medical science.", "It takes no notice of the potential impact on the environment."], "stem": "Why are some researchers irritated at the USDA's 2016-2020 Dietary Guidelines?", "trapNote": "干扰项A源自第5段尼尔森的补充言论，属于偏离核心观点的张冠李戴；B项（过度强调少吃肉和买本地食品）则与第5段“最终版本未收录该建议”正反颠倒。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Not just because of their position of authority: The guidelines drive billions of dollars of food production through federal programs", "explanation": "定位至第3段第4–5句。作者认为政府的膳食指南本可以为降低气候成本作出巨大贡献，并紧接着点明两点依据：一是指南所具有的权威地位（position of authority），二是指南能通过联邦计划撬动数十亿美元的粮食生产（drive billions of dollars of food production）。由此可推断，美国农业部拥有相应的能力与财政资源去达成这一目标，对应选项A。", "no": 52, "options": ["It has the capacity and the financial resources to do so.", "Its researchers have already submitted relevant proposals.", "Its agencies in charge of drafting the guidelines have the expertise.", "It can raise students' environmental awareness through its programs."], "stem": "Why does the author say the USDA could have contributed a lot to lowering the climate cost through its dietary guidelines?", "trapNote": "干扰项D抓住第3段末句“school lunches”望文生义，过度推理出“提高学生环保意识”；C项则将第7段“起草机构与行业过近”和第5段“科学报告”杂糅捏造。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Food production is the largest user of fresh water, largest contributor to the loss of biodiversity, and a major contributor to using up natural resources.", "explanation": "定位至第4段末句及第5段第1句。第5段首句交代第4段所述观点均出自膳食指南咨询委员会的科学报告，而第4段末句明确指出粮食生产是淡水的第一大消耗者、生物多样性丧失的最大诱因，也是自然资源枯竭的主要原因。选项D中的“Farming”、“consumes”和“most of our natural resources”分别对应“Food production”、“using up”和“major contributor to... natural resources”。", "no": 53, "options": ["Food is easily contaminated from farm to belly.", "Greenhouse effect is an issue still under debate.", "Modern agriculture has increased food diversity.", "Farming consumes most of our natural resources."], "stem": "What do we learn from the Dietary Guidelines Advisory Committee's scientific report?", "trapNote": "干扰项C对第4段末句“largest contributor to the loss of biodiversity”断章取义，将“导致生物多样性丧失”正反颠倒为“增加食物多样性”；A项则复现“from farm to belly”后无端捏造“食物易受污染”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "too close to the industries they are supposed to regulate. On one hand, the USDA is compiling dietary advice. On the other, their clients are US agriculture companies.", "explanation": "定位至第7段全段。作者推测膳食指南忽视可持续性的原因，可能是起草决议的机构与其本应监管的行业关系过近，随后具体点明美国农业部的客户正是美国农业公司。选项C中的“close ties with the agriculture companies”准确对应并整合了该段因果解释。", "no": 54, "options": ["Its exclusive concern with Americans' food safety.", "Its sole responsibility for providing dietary advice.", "Its close ties with the agriculture companies.", "Its alleged failure to regulate the industries."], "stem": "What may account for the neglect of sustainability in the USDA's Dietary Guidelines according to the author?", "trapNote": "干扰项B源自第6段官方说辞而非作者观点；A项则将第8段研究者的言论张冠李戴给作者，并用“exclusive”把“things like food security”绝对化。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "You absolutely need to be worried about climate impacts and future sustainability if you want secure food in the future.", "explanation": "定位至第8段第2–3句。大卫·沃林加指出，以往膳食指南始终关注粮食安全等属于美国农业部使命的议题，并强调要想在未来获得安全粮食，就绝对必须考虑气候影响与未来可持续性。选项B中的“ensure the sustainable development of agriculture”正是对“worried about climate impacts and future sustainability”的同义概括。", "no": 55, "options": ["Give top priority to things like nutrition and food security.", "Endeavor to ensure the sustainable development of agriculture.", "Fulfill its mission by closely cooperating with the industries.", "Study the long-term impact of climate change on food production."], "stem": "What should the USDA do to achieve food security according to David Wallinga?", "trapNote": "干扰项C将第7段作者批判的“与行业关系过近”和第8段“农业部使命”杂糅捏造为“与行业密切合作”；A项则曲解了沃林加主张将可持续性与营养安全并重的立场。", "type": "细节题"}], "sourceLabel": "2020.12 六级真题第1套", "timeLimitMin": 10, "title": "Dietary Guidelines and Environmental Sustainability", "year": "2020.12", "wordCount": 455, "examSet": "2020.12 六级真题 第1套", "translations": ["每隔五年，政府都会试图告诉美国人该往肚子里装些什么：多吃蔬菜，减少脂肪摄入。这一切都基于能够引领健康生活的现有最佳科学依据。然而，这些现有最佳科学依据对于食物选择会给环境带来何种影响也有很多话要说；一些研究人员感到恼火的是，美国农业部（USDA）昨天发布的新版膳食建议似乎完全忽略了这一事实。", "总体而言，2016至2020年膳食建议旨在追求均衡：多吃蔬菜、选择更瘦的肉类，并大幅减少糖分摄入。", "但美国人的人均热量消耗几乎高于世界上任何其他国家。因此，美国人所吃的食物对气候变化有着巨大的影响。耕作土壤会释放二氧化碳，而送货车辆会排放尾气。政府的膳食指南本可以大有作为，大幅降低这种气候代价。这不仅是因为指南本身具有权威地位：通过学校午餐以及面向贫困人群的营养援助等联邦项目，这些指南直接带动了价值数十亿美元的食品生产。", "仅植物种植和动物养殖本身，就占到全美温室气体排放总量的9%。这还不算从农场到餐桌沿途的运输、加工、冷藏及其他环节所消耗的燃料。红肉是排放量最大、最臭名昭著的来源之一，但一月份将一份沙拉从加利福尼亚用卡车运往明尼苏达同样会带来沉重的环境负担。而且，温室气体排放还远非全部问题。食品生产是淡水的最大消耗者、生物多样性丧失的最大推手，也是耗竭自然资源的主要因素。", "所有这些要点以及更多内容，都曾出现在去年二月发布的膳食指南咨询委员会科学报告中。米里亚姆·纳尔逊曾担任该报告可持续发展分委员会的主席，她对“少吃肉”和“购买本地食品”未能进入最终版本感到失望。“尤其是考虑到少吃肉——特别是红肉和加工肉类——本身就有利于健康，”她说道。", "那么究竟发生了什么？官方的回应是，可持续发展超出了该指南的官方职权范围——指南的职责只是提供“营养和膳食信息”。", "或许负责起草这些决策的机构与它们本应监管的行业走得太近了。一方面，美国农业部在编制膳食建议；另一方面，它的服务客户恰恰是美国农业企业。", "把指南范围严格限定在营养和饮食上的说辞，在研究人员听来并不怎么站得住脚。例如，大卫·瓦林加就表示：“在以往的指南中，他们一直关注粮食安全等问题——而这想来本就是美国农业部的使命。如果你希望未来有安全可靠的粮食供应，就绝对必须关心气候影响和未来的可持续性。”"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "完全地，彻底地", "note": "高频程度副词：常与 ignore、fail、different 等词搭配，用于强化作者态度或批判语气。", "word": "utterly"}, {"gloss": "瘦的，低脂的", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“倾斜、倚靠”，作形容词修饰肉类时表示“瘦的、脂肪含量少的”。", "word": "lean"}, {"gloss": "推动，带动，促成", "note": "熟词僻义：除“驾驶”外，在经济与政策类文章中常表示“驱动、拉动（生产、消费或变革）”。", "word": "drive"}, {"gloss": "臭名昭著的，声名狼藉的", "note": "高频情感态度词：固定含贬义，在六级阅读中常作为判断作者负面评价的重要线索。", "word": "notorious"}, {"gloss": "主持（会议或委员会）", "note": "熟词僻义/词性活用：作动词意为“担任……主席、主持（某机构或委员会的工作）”。", "word": "chair"}, {"gloss": "监管，管制，规范", "note": "高频核心词：社会与政经类阅读必考词，常与 agency、industry 搭配，指政府部门对行业实施监管。", "word": "regulate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "But the best available science also has a lot to say about what those food choices do to the environment, and some researchers are annoyed that new dietary recommendations of the USDA (United States Department of Agriculture) released yesterday seem to utterly ignore that fact.", "point": "what宾语从句 + that引导形容词后的从句 + 过去分词短语作后置定语", "structure": "主干为并列句：前半句 the best available science also has a lot to say about + what 宾语从句；后半句 some researchers are annoyed that... 中，that 引导从句说明 annoyed 的原因；从句主语 recommendations 后接过去分词短语 released yesterday 作后置定语。", "zh": "然而，这些现有最佳科学依据对于食物选择会给环境带来何种影响也有很多话要说；一些研究人员感到恼火的是，美国农业部（USDA）昨天发布的新版膳食建议似乎完全忽略了这一事实。"}, {"en": "Miriam Nelson chaired the subcommittee in charge of sustainability for the report, and is disappointed that eating less meat and buying local food aren't in the final product.", "point": "介词短语作后置定语 + 动名词短语作主语 + that从句", "structure": "主语 Miriam Nelson 共用两个谓语动词 chaired 和 is disappointed；in charge of sustainability for the report 作 subcommittee 的后置定语；that 从句中动名词短语 eating less meat and buying local food 并列作主语。", "zh": "米里亚姆·纳尔逊曾担任该报告可持续发展分委员会的主席，她对“少吃肉”和“购买本地食品”未能进入最终版本感到失望。"}, {"en": "Possibly the agencies in charge of drafting the decisions are too close to the industries they are supposed to regulate.", "point": "介词短语作后置定语 + 省略关系代词的定语从句", "structure": "主干：the agencies... are too close to the industries...；in charge of drafting the decisions 为介词短语作后置定语修饰 agencies；they are supposed to regulate 为省略了关系代词 that/which 的定语从句修饰 industries。", "zh": "或许负责起草这些决策的机构与它们本应监管的行业走得太近了。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "utterly ignore（完全忽视）同义替换为 takes no notice of（毫不理会）", "option": "It takes no notice of the potential impact on the environment.", "original": "seem to utterly ignore that fact"}, {"note": "position of authority 与 billions of dollars 对应 capacity and financial resources", "option": "It has the capacity and the financial resources to do so.", "original": "position of authority... drive billions of dollars of food production through federal programs"}, {"note": "largest user of fresh water / using up natural resources 概括为 consumes most of our natural resources", "option": "Farming consumes most of our natural resources.", "original": "Food production is the largest user of fresh water, largest contributor to the loss of biodiversity, and a major contributor to using up natural resources"}, {"note": "too close to the industries 与 clients are US agriculture companies 对应 close ties with the agriculture companies", "option": "Its close ties with the agriculture companies.", "original": "too close to the industries they are supposed to regulate... their clients are US agriculture companies"}, {"note": "be worried about... future sustainability 与 secure food 对应 ensure the sustainable development of agriculture", "option": "Endeavor to ensure the sustainable development of agriculture.", "original": "be worried about climate impacts and future sustainability if you want secure food in the future"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L2", "exam": "cet6", "id": "cet6-2016-p1", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["I'll admit I've never quite understood the obsession surrounding genetically modified (GM) crops. To environmentalist opponents, GM foods are simply evil, an understudied, possibly harmful tool used by big agricultural businesses to control global seed markets and crush local farmers. They argue that GM foods have never delivered on their supposed promise, that money spent on GM crops would be better channeled to organic farming and that consumers should be protected with warning labels on any products that contain genetically modified ingredients. To supporters, GM crops are a key part of the effort to sustainably provide food to meet a growing global population. But more than that, supporters see the GM opposition of many environmentalists as fundamentally anti-science, no different than those who question the basics of man-made climate change.", "For both sides, GM foods seem to act as a symbol: you're pro-agricultural business or anti-science. But science is exactly what we need more of when it comes to GM foods, which is why I was happy to see Nature devote a special series of articles to the GM food controversy. The conclusion: while GM crops haven't yet realized their initial promise and have been dominated by agricultural businesses, there is reason to continue to use and develop them to help meet the enormous challenge of sustainably feeding a growing planet.", "That doesn't mean GM crops are perfect, or a one-size-fits-all solution to global agriculture problems. But anything that can increase farming efficiency—the amount of crops we can produce per acre of land—will be extremely useful. GM crops can and almost certainly will be part of that suite of tools, but so will traditional plant breeding, improved soil and crop management—and perhaps most important of all, better storage and transport infrastructure, especially in the developing world. (It doesn't do much good for farmers in places like sub-Saharan Africa to produce more food if they can't get it to hungry consumers.) I'd like to see more non-industry research done on GM crops—not just because we'd worry less about bias, but also because seed companies like Monsanto and Pioneer shouldn't be the only entities working to harness genetic modification. I'd like to see GM research on less commercial crops, like corn. I don't think it's vital to label GM ingredients in food, but I also wouldn't be against it—and industry would be smart to go along with labeling, just as a way of removing fears about the technology.", "Most of all, though, I wish a tenth of the energy that's spent endlessly debating GM crops was focused on those more pressing challenges for global agriculture. There are much bigger battles to fight."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "GM foods are simply evil, an understudied, possibly harmful tool used by big agricultural businesses to control global seed markets and crush local farmers.", "explanation": "定位至第一段第二句。环保主义反对者认为转基因食品是大农业公司用来“控制全球种子市场并打压当地农民（control global seed markets and crush local farmers）”的工具，这与 B 项“被大企业用来垄断农业（monopolize agriculture）”形成同义替换。", "no": 46, "options": ["They will eventually ruin agriculture and the environment.", "They are used by big businesses to monopolize agriculture.", "They have proved potentially harmful to consumers' health.", "They pose a tremendous threat to current farming practice."], "stem": "How do environmentalist opponents view GM foods according to the passage?", "trapNote": "最迷惑项 C 把原文的“possibly harmful（可能有害）”偷换为“have proved（已被证明）”，且原文并未证实其对消费者健康有害，属于以偏概全和过度肯定。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But science is exactly what we need more of when it comes to GM foods, which is why I was happy to see Nature devote a special series of articles to the GM food controversy.", "explanation": "定位至第二段第二句。针对争论双方将转基因食品符号化的对立立场，作者指出“在转基因食品问题上，我们恰恰需要更多的科学（science is exactly what we need more of）”，因此乐见《自然》杂志就此争议推出专题报道，这对应 D 项“对转基因作物进行更多科学研究”。", "no": 47, "options": ["Breaking the GM food monopoly.", "More friendly exchange of ideas.", "Regulating GM food production.", "More scientific research on GM crops."], "stem": "What does the author say is vital to solving the controversy between the two sides of the debate?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A“打破转基因食品垄断”虽与第三段非企业界研究的建议有关，但被错当成“化解双方争论的关键”，属于偷换对象。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "there is reason to continue to use and develop them to help meet the enormous challenge of sustainably feeding a growing planet.", "explanation": "定位至第二段末句《自然》杂志专题文章的结论部分。文章认为，尽管转基因作物尚未兑现最初承诺且一直由农业巨头主导，但“仍有理由继续使用并研发它们，以助力应对可持续养活不断增长的全球人口这一巨大挑战”，与 A 项意思完全一致。", "no": 48, "options": ["Feeding the growing population makes it imperative to develop GM crops.", "Popularizing GM technology will help it to live up to its initial promises.", "Measures should be taken to ensure the safety of GM foods.", "Both supporters and opponents should make compromises."], "stem": "What is the main point of the Nature articles?", "trapNote": "干扰项 B 将让步分句中“haven't yet realized their initial promise（尚未实现最初承诺）”曲解为“普及该技术就会兑现最初承诺”，属于正反混淆与无中生有。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "But anything that can increase farming efficiency—the amount of crops we can produce per acre of land—will be extremely useful.", "explanation": "定位至第三段前两句。作者先表明转基因作物并非解决全球农业问题的万能药，继而指出“任何能够提高农业生产效率（increase farming efficiency）的做法都将极其有用”，并倡导传统育种、改良土壤及完善储运等多元措施，与 D 项同义替换。", "no": 49, "options": ["It has to depend more and more on GM technology.", "It is vital to the sustainable development of human society.", "GM crops should be allowed until better alternatives are found.", "Whatever is useful to boost farming efficiency should be encouraged."], "stem": "What is the author's view on the solution to agricultural problems?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 和 C 均属以偏概全，作者明确否定转基因技术是“万能方案”，而是将其视为众多农业增效工具之一，并未主张日益依赖它或仅作权宜之计。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Most of all, though, I wish a tenth of the energy that's spent endlessly debating GM crops was focused on those more pressing challenges for global agriculture.", "explanation": "定位至最后一段第一句。作者直言希望人们把“无休止争论转基因作物所耗费的精力”哪怕十分之一，投入到“全球农业更紧迫的挑战（more pressing challenges for global agriculture）”上去，这与 C 项“应把精力转向更紧迫的农业问题”完全吻合。", "no": 50, "options": ["It arises out of ignorance of and prejudice against new science.", "It distracts the public attention from other key issues of the world.", "Efforts spent on it should be turned to more urgent issues of agriculture.", "Neither side is likely to give in until more convincing evidence is found."], "stem": "What does the author think of the ongoing debate around GM crops?", "trapNote": "干扰项 B 属于过度推理与偷换概念，原文明确限定为被忽视的是“global agriculture（全球农业）”的更紧迫问题，而非泛指“世界其他关键问题”。", "type": "态度题"}], "sourceLabel": "六级官方样题 Section C", "subtitle": "Why We Need Science, Not Ideology, in the Debate Over GM Foods", "timeLimitMin": 10, "title": "2016 六级官方样题 · Passage 1：转基因作物之争 (GM Crops Debate)", "year": "2016", "wordCount": 454, "examSet": "2016 六级官方样题", "translations": ["我承认，我一直不太理解人们对转基因（GM）作物的这种执念。在持反对意见的环保主义者看来，转基因食品简直是邪恶之物——是大型农业企业用来控制全球种子市场、压垮当地农民的工具，不仅研究不足，而且可能有害。他们认为，转基因食品从未兑现其所谓的承诺，花在转基因作物上的资金本应更好地投入到有机农业中，而且任何含有转基因成分的产品都应贴上警示标签以保护消费者。而在支持者看来，转基因作物是可持续提供粮食以满足全球人口增长的关键一环。不仅如此，支持者还认为许多环保主义者对转基因的反对从根本上是反科学的，与那些质疑人为气候变化基本事实的人毫无二致。", "对双方而言，转基因食品似乎都成了一个符号：你要么支持农业巨头，要么就是反科学。但在转基因食品问题上，我们恰恰需要更多的科学研究，这也正是我很高兴看到《自然》杂志推出一系列专题文章探讨转基因食品争议的原因。其结论是：尽管转基因作物尚未实现最初的设想，且一直由农业企业主导，但仍有理由继续使用并研发它们，以帮助应对可持续养活不断增长的地球人口这一巨大挑战。", "这并不意味着转基因作物完美无缺，也不是解决全球农业问题的万能灵药。然而，任何能提高农业效率——即每英亩土地的作物产量——的方法都将极其有用。转基因作物可以而且几乎肯定会成为这套工具箱的一部分，但传统植物育种、改良的土壤与作物管理也是如此——而或许最重要的是，改善储存和运输基础设施，尤其是在发展中国家。（如果撒哈拉以南非洲等地的农民无法将粮食送到饥饿的消费者手中，即便种出再多粮食也无济于事。）我希望能看到更多非行业资助的转基因作物研究——不仅是因为这样我们可以减少对研究偏见的担忧，还因为孟山都和先锋等种子公司不应成为唯一致力于利用基因改造技术的机构。我希望能看到针对商业化程度较低的作物（如玉米）的转基因研究。我不认为给食品中的转基因成分贴标签有多么重要，但我也并不反对这样做——而且如果行业能够顺应贴标要求，那将是明智之举，哪怕只是为了消除人们对这项技术的恐惧。", "不过最重要的是，我希望人们在无休止争论转基因作物上所耗费的精力中，哪怕有十分之一能集中到全球农业面临的那些更为紧迫的挑战上。毕竟，还有重要得多的硬仗要打。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 引导；把（资金、精力等）投入", "note": "熟词僻义：名词常表“渠道/频道”，六级阅读中作动词常考“将资金/资源引导至某处”（channel money to...）。", "word": "channel"}, {"gloss": "v. 兑现，实现（诺言、预期）", "note": "高频熟词僻义：deliver on one's promise 意为“兑现承诺”，而非“递送/发表”。", "word": "deliver"}, {"gloss": "v. 主导，控制，支配", "note": "阅读高频词：常以被动语态 be dominated by 出现，表示“被……主导/垄断”。", "word": "dominate"}, {"gloss": "v. 利用，驾驭（自然资源、技术等）", "note": "熟词僻义：名词原意“马具”，动词在科技/环保文中高频表示“利用、开发（力量/技术）”。", "word": "harness"}, {"gloss": "adj. 紧迫的，迫切的", "note": "高频形容词：由动词 press 引申而来，pressing challenges = urgent problems，常在主旨或态度题中与 urgent 互换。", "word": "pressing"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "They argue that GM foods have never delivered on their supposed promise, that money spent on GM crops would be better channeled to organic farming and that consumers should be protected with warning labels on any products that contain genetically modified ingredients.", "point": "并列宾语从句 + 过去分词短语作后置定语 + 定语从句", "structure": "主干：They argue that..., that... and that...（三个并列宾语从句）。从句1：GM foods have never delivered on their supposed promise；从句2：money（后接过去分词短语 spent on GM crops 作后置定语）would be better channeled to organic farming；从句3：consumers should be protected... + 定语从句 that contain genetically modified ingredients 修饰 products。", "zh": "他们认为，转基因食品从未兑现其所谓的承诺，花在转基因作物上的资金本应更好地投入到有机农业中，而且任何含有转基因成分的产品都应贴上警示标签以保护消费者。"}, {"en": "The conclusion: while GM crops haven't yet realized their initial promise and have been dominated by agricultural businesses, there is reason to continue to use and develop them to help meet the enormous challenge of sustainably feeding a growing planet.", "point": "while引导让步状语从句 + there be句型 + 不定式作定语与目的状语", "structure": "冒号后为解释说明；while 引导让步状语从句（含两个并列谓语 haven't realized 和 have been dominated）；主句为 there be 句型：there is reason + 不定式短语 to continue to use and develop them（作后置定语修饰 reason）+ 目的状语 to help meet the enormous challenge of...。", "zh": "其结论是：尽管转基因作物尚未实现最初的设想，且一直由农业企业主导，但仍有理由继续使用并研发它们，以帮助应对可持续养活不断增长的地球人口这一巨大挑战。"}, {"en": "I'd like to see more non-industry research done on GM crops—not just because we'd worry less about bias, but also because seed companies like Monsanto and Pioneer shouldn't be the only entities working to harness genetic modification.", "point": "see + 宾语 + 过去分词作宾补 + not just because... but also because... 递进原因状语从句 + 现在分词作后置定语", "structure": "主干：I'd like to see more non-industry research done on GM crops（done 为过去分词作宾语补足语，表被动）。破折号后为 not just because... but also because... 引导的递进原因状语从句；第二个从句中 working to harness genetic modification 为现在分词短语作后置定语，修饰 entities。", "zh": "我希望能看到更多非行业资助的转基因作物研究——不仅是因为这样我们可以减少对研究偏见的担忧，还因为孟山都和先锋等种子公司不应成为唯一致力于利用基因改造技术的机构。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "Q46同义替换：控制全球种子市场并压垮当地农民 -> 垄断（monopolize）农业。", "option": "monopolize agriculture", "original": "control global seed markets and crush local farmers"}, {"note": "Q47同义替换：需要更多的科学 -> 对转基因作物开展更多科学研究。", "option": "More scientific research on GM crops", "original": "science is exactly what we need more of when it comes to GM foods"}, {"note": "Q48同义替换：应对养活不断增长的地球人口的挑战 -> 养活增长人口使研发转基因作物势在必行。", "option": "Feeding the growing population makes it imperative to develop GM crops", "original": "continue to use and develop them to help meet the enormous challenge of sustainably feeding a growing planet"}, {"note": "Q49同义替换：anything that can increase 转化为 whatever is useful to boost，extremely useful 转化为 should be encouraged。", "option": "Whatever is useful to boost farming efficiency should be encouraged", "original": "anything that can increase farming efficiency—the amount of crops we can produce per acre of land—will be extremely useful"}, {"note": "Q50同义替换：energy spent debating -> efforts spent on it；more pressing challenges -> more urgent issues。", "option": "Efforts spent on it should be turned to more urgent issues of agriculture", "original": "a tenth of the energy that's spent endlessly debating GM crops was focused on those more pressing challenges for global agriculture"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L2", "exam": "cet6", "id": "cet6-2016-p2", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["When the right person is holding the right job at the right moment, that person's influence is greatly expanded. That is the position in which Janet Yellen, who is expected to be confirmed as the next chair of the Federal Reserve Bank (Fed) in January, now finds herself. If you believe, as many do, that unemployment is the major economic and social concern of our day, then it is no stretch to think Yellen is the most powerful person in the world right now.", "Throughout the 2008 financial crisis and the recession and recovery that followed, central banks have taken on the role of stimulators of last resort, holding up the global economy with vast amounts of money in the form of asset buying. Yellen, previously a Fed vice chair, was one of the principal architects of the Fed's $3.8 trillion money dump. A star economist known for her groundbreaking work on labor markets, Yellen was a kind of prophetess early on in the crisis for her warnings about the subprime (次级债的) meltdown. Now it will be her job to get the Fed and the markets out of the biggest and most unconventional monetary program in history without derailing the fragile recovery.", "The good news is that Yellen, 67, is particularly well suited to meet these challenges. She has a keen understanding of financial markets, an appreciation for their imperfections and a strong belief that human suffering is more related to unemployment than anything else. Some experts worry that Yellen will be inclined to chase unemployment to the neglect of inflation. But with wages still relatively flat and the economy increasingly divided between the well-off and the long-term unemployed, more people worry about the opposite, deflation (通货紧缩) that would aggravate the economy's problems.", "Either way, the incoming Fed chief will have to walk a fine line in slowly ending the stimulus. It must be steady enough to deflate bubbles (去泡沫) and bring markets back down to earth but not so quick that it creates another credit crisis.", "Unlike many past Fed leaders, Yellen is not one to buy into the finance industry's argument that it should be left alone to regulate itself. She knows all along the Fed has been too slack on regulation of finance.", "Yellen is likely to address the issue right after she pushes unemployment below 6%, stabilizes markets and makes sure that the recovery is more inclusive and robust. As Princeton Professor Alan Blinder says, “She's smart as a whip, deeply logical, willing to argue but also a good listener. She can persuade without creating hostility.” All those traits will be useful as the global economy's new power player takes on its most annoying problems."], "questions": [{"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "as many do, that unemployment is the major economic and social concern of our day, then it is no stretch to think Yellen is the most powerful person in the world right now.", "explanation": "定位至第一段末句。文中指出“正如许多人所认为的，失业是我们这个时代最主要的经济和社会关切（unemployment is the major economic and social concern of our day）”，正因如此，即将执掌美联储的耶伦面临的核心难题便是失业问题，对应 C 项。", "no": 51, "options": ["Lack of money.", "Subprime crisis.", "Unemployment.", "Social instability."], "stem": "What do many people think is the biggest problem facing Janet Yellen?", "trapNote": "干扰项 D 将原文“social concern（社会关切）”偷换概念并夸大为“social instability（社会动荡）”；B 项“次级债危机”是第二段提及的过去事件，并非当前面临的最大难题。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "with vast amounts of money in the form of asset buying. Yellen, previously a Fed vice chair, was one of the principal architects of the Fed's $3.8 trillion money dump.", "explanation": "定位至第二段第一、二句。2008 年金融危机期间，央行通过“购买资产（asset buying）”的形式投入巨额资金支撑经济，而时任美联储副主席的耶伦正是美联储“3.8 万亿美元资金投放计划（$3.8 trillion money dump）”的主要设计者之一，与 D 项“通过购买资产向市场注入资金”精准对应。", "no": 52, "options": ["Take effective measures to curb inflation.", "Deflate the bubbles in the American economy.", "Formulate policies to help financial institutions.", "Pour money into the market through asset buying."], "stem": "What did Yellen help the Fed do to tackle the 2008 financial crisis?", "trapNote": "干扰项 B“给美国经济去泡沫”是第四段提到耶伦上任后退出刺激政策时需把握的分寸，与题干询问的“2008 年危机期间的应对措施”存在时间错位。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "more people worry about the opposite, deflation (通货紧缩) that would aggravate the economy's problems.", "explanation": "定位至第三段末句。针对部分专家担心耶伦重就业而忽视通胀的忧虑，作者转折指出“更多的人担心相反的情况，即会加剧经济问题的通货紧缩（more people worry about the opposite, deflation）”，其中 `more people worry about` 同义对应题干 `a greater concern of the general public`，故 B 项正确。", "no": 53, "options": ["Recession.", "Deflation.", "Inequality.", "Income."], "stem": "What is a greater concern of the general public?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 和 D 利用该句前半部分“贫富分化（divided between the well-off and the long-term unemployed）”和“工资水平持平（wages still relatively flat）”的细节拼凑干扰，属于断章取义。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "not one to buy into the finance industry's argument that it should be left alone to regulate itself. She knows all along the Fed has been too slack on regulation of finance.", "explanation": "定位至第五段与第六段首句。第五段表明耶伦不赞成金融业自我监管，并深知美联储长期以来“对金融监管过于宽松（too slack on regulation of finance）”，第六段接着说她在降低失业率、稳定市场后很可能立即着手解决这一问题，据此可推断她将收紧金融监管（Tighten financial regulation），故 C 项正确。", "no": 54, "options": ["Reform the credit system.", "Restore public confidence.", "Tighten financial regulation.", "Develop a new monetary program."], "stem": "What is Yellen likely to do in her position as the Fed chief?", "trapNote": "干扰项 D“制定新的货币计划”将第二段她要“退出史上最大规模非常规货币计划（get the Fed and the markets out of the ... monetary program）”的意思反向曲解，属于正反颠倒。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "As Princeton Professor Alan Blinder says, “She's smart as a whip, deeply logical, willing to argue but also a good listener. She can persuade without creating hostility.”", "explanation": "定位至第六段第二、三句。普林斯顿大学教授 Alan Blinder 称赞耶伦思维敏捷、富有逻辑且善于倾听，并特别指出“她能够说服他人而不引起敌意（She can persuade without creating hostility）”，这与 A 项“她具有很强的说服力（strong persuasive power）”高度一致。", "no": 55, "options": ["She possesses strong persuasive power.", "She has confidence in what she is doing.", "She is one of the world's greatest economists.", "She is the most powerful Fed chief in history."], "stem": "How does Alan Blinder portray Yellen?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 和 D 分别截取第二段“star economist”和第一段“most powerful person in the world right now”加以夸大并安在 Alan Blinder 名下，属于张冠李戴与过度拔高。", "type": "细节题"}], "sourceLabel": "六级官方样题 Section C", "subtitle": "Janet Yellen's Role as Incoming Federal Reserve Chair", "timeLimitMin": 10, "title": "2016 六级官方样题 · Passage 2：耶伦与美联储新挑战 (Janet Yellen & the Fed)", "year": "2016", "wordCount": 444, "examSet": "2016 六级官方样题", "translations": ["当合适的人在合适的时机担任合适的职位时，其影响力就会成倍放大。珍妮特·耶伦预计将于明年一月获准出任下一任美联储（Fed）主席，而这正是她目前所处的位置。如果你像许多人一样，认为失业是当今最主要的经济与社会问题，那么认为耶伦眼下是世界上最有权势的人也毫不夸张。", "在整个2008年金融危机以及随后的经济衰退与复苏期间，各国央行充当了“最后刺激者”的角色，通过购买资产的形式投放巨额资金来支撑全球经济。曾任美联储副主席的耶伦正是美联储3.8万亿美元放水计划的主要设计者之一。作为一位因劳动力市场开创性研究而闻名的明星经济学家，耶伦在危机初期就曾对次级债崩盘发出过警告，堪称一位先知。如今，她的职责将是带领美联储和市场退出这项史上规模最大、最非常规的货币计划，同时又不至于使脆弱的经济复苏脱轨。", "好消息是，现年67岁的耶伦尤其适合迎接这些挑战。她对金融市场有着敏锐的洞察，深知市场存在的不完善之处，并且坚信人类的痛苦与失业的关联远胜于其他任何因素。一些专家担心耶伦会倾向于一味压低失业率而忽视通货膨胀。但由于工资水平依然相对停滞，且经济在富裕阶层与长期失业者之间的分化日益加剧，更多人担心的反而是通货紧缩——它会使经济问题雪上加霜。", "无论如何，这位即将上任的美联储掌门人在逐步退出刺激政策时都必须谨慎拿捏分寸。退出节奏必须足够稳健，以挤破资产泡沫并让市场回归理性，但又不能过快，以免引发另一场信贷危机。", "与过去许多美联储领导人不同，耶伦并不相信金融业所谓“应当任由其自我监管”的论调。她向来清楚美联储在金融监管方面过于宽松。", "耶伦很可能会在将失业率压低至6%以下、稳定市场并确保复苏更具包容性和强劲势头之后，立即着手解决这一监管问题。正如普林斯顿大学教授艾伦·布林德所说：“她极其聪敏，逻辑严密，敢于据理力争但又善于倾听。她能说服别人而又不树敌。”当这位全球经济的新晋掌舵人开始应对最棘手的难题时，所有这些特质都将派上大用场。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 夸张，牵强附会（no stretch 毫不夸张）", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为动词“伸展、拉长”，在评论文中 it is no stretch to say/think 意为“说……毫不夸张”。", "word": "stretch"}, {"gloss": "n. 充分了解，体察，清醒认识", "note": "熟词僻义：常考义为“感激、欣赏”，本文 an appreciation for their imperfections 指“对市场缺陷的清醒认识”。", "word": "appreciation"}, {"gloss": "adj. 停滞的，持平的，无起色的", "note": "熟词僻义：经济新闻高频用法，wages relatively flat 指“工资增长停滞/持平”，而非“平坦的/公寓”。", "word": "flat"}, {"gloss": "phr. 相信，接受（某种观点或说法）", "note": "高频短语：常用于否定句（not one to buy into...），表示“不买账、不轻信某种观点”。", "word": "buy into"}, {"gloss": "adj. 松懈的，宽松的，不严格的", "note": "六级高频词：too slack on regulation 意为“在监管上过于松懈”，常与 tight / strict 构成反义对照。", "word": "slack"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "That is the position in which Janet Yellen, who is expected to be confirmed as the next chair of the Federal Reserve Bank (Fed) in January, now finds herself.", "point": "介词+关系代词引导定语从句 + 嵌套非限制性定语从句", "structure": "主干：That is the position (in which Janet Yellen now finds herself)。in which 引导定语从句修饰 position（find oneself in a position 意为“发现自己处于某种境地”）；中间插入 who 引导的非限制性定语从句，修饰先行词 Janet Yellen。", "zh": "这正是预计将于明年一月获准出任下一任美联储主席的珍妮特·耶伦目前所处的境地。"}, {"en": "She has a keen understanding of financial markets, an appreciation for their imperfections and a strong belief that human suffering is more related to unemployment than anything else.", "point": "并列名词宾语 + that引导同位语从句 + 比较级结构", "structure": "主干：She has a keen understanding..., an appreciation... and a strong belief...（三个并列宾语）。that 引导同位语从句解释说明 belief 的具体内容，从句中包含比较结构 more related to... than...。", "zh": "她对金融市场有着敏锐的洞察，深知市场存在的不完善之处，并且坚信人类的痛苦与失业的关联远胜于其他任何因素。"}, {"en": "But with wages still relatively flat and the economy increasingly divided between the well-off and the long-term unemployed, more people worry about the opposite, deflation (通货紧缩) that would aggravate the economy's problems.", "point": "with复合结构作状语 + 同位语 + 定语从句", "structure": "前半句为两个由 with 引导的复合结构（with + 名词 + 形容词/过去分词）作原因/伴随状语；主句为 more people worry about the opposite；deflation 为 the opposite 的同位语，其后接 that 引导的定语从句。", "zh": "但由于工资水平依然相对停滞，且经济在富裕阶层与长期失业者之间的分化日益加剧，更多人担心的反而是通货紧缩——它会使经济问题雪上加霜。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "Q52同义替换：with vast amounts of money / money dump -> pour money into the market；in the form of -> through。", "option": "Pour money into the market through asset buying", "original": "holding up the global economy with vast amounts of money in the form of asset buying"}, {"note": "Q53细节定位：more people 对应 general public，greater concern 对应 more people worry about。", "option": "Deflation", "original": "more people worry about the opposite, deflation"}, {"note": "Q54反义推理替换：认为过去监管过于宽松（too slack）且不认同自我监管 -> 将收紧（tighten）金融监管。", "option": "Tighten financial regulation", "original": "not one to buy into the finance industry's argument that it should be left alone to regulate itself. She knows all along the Fed has been too slack on regulation"}, {"note": "Q55词性转换替换：动词 persuade 转化为名词短语 persuasive power。", "option": "She possesses strong persuasive power", "original": "She can persuade without creating hostility"}, {"note": "高频习语替换：walk a fine line 表示在两难之间如履薄冰、谨慎维持平衡。", "option": "strike a delicate balance when gradually withdrawing stimulus", "original": "walk a fine line in slowly ending the stimulus"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2023-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2023", "examSet": "2023 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2023 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "美国公立学校气候变化教育之争", "subtitle": "教育政策与科学共识 · 气候变化课程的意识形态博弈", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 418, "paragraphs": ["The weather in Texas may have cooled since the recent extreme heat, but the temperature will be high at the State Board of Education meeting in Austin this month as officials debate how climate change is taught in Texas schools.", "Pat Hardy, who sympathized with views of the energy sector, is resisting the proposed change to science standards for pre-teen pupils. These would emphasise the primacy of human activity in recent climate change and encourage discussion of mitigation measures.", "Most scientists and experts sharply dispute Hardy's views. \"They casually dismiss the career work of scholars and scientists as just another misguided opinion.\" says Dan Quinn, senior communications strategist at the Texas Freedom Network, a non-profit group that monitors public education, \"What millions of Texas kids learn in their public schools is determined too often by the political ideology of partisan board members, rather than facts and sound scholarship.\"", "Such debate reflects fierce discussions across the US and around the world, as researchers, policymakers, teachers and students step up demands for a greater focus on teaching about the facts of climate change in schools.", "A study last year by the National Center for Science Education, a non-profit group of scientists and teachers, looking at how state public schools across the country address climate change in science classes, gave barely half of US states a grade B + or higher. Among the 10 worst performers were some of the most populous states, including Texas, which was given the lowest grade (F) and has a disproportionate influence because its textbooks are widely sold elsewhere.", "Glenn Branch, the centre's deputy director, cautions that setting state-level science standards is only one limited benchmark in a country that decentralises decisions to local school boards. Even if a state is considered a high performer in its science standards, \"that does not mean it will be taught\", he says.", "Another issue is that while climate change is well integrated into some subjects and at some ages — such as earth and space sciences in high schools — it is not as well represented in curricula for younger children and in subjects that are more widely taught, such as biology and chemistry. It is also less prominent in many social studies courses.", "Branch points out that, even if a growing number of official guidelines and textbooks reflect scientific consensus on climate change, unofficial educational materials that convey more slanted perspectives are being distributed to teachers. They include materials sponsored by libertarian think-tanks and energy industry associations."], "translations": ["尽管自近期极端高温以来得克萨斯州的天气有所转凉，但本月在奥斯汀举行的州教育委员会会议上依然会“热火朝天”，因为官员们正就得州学校应如何教授气候变化展开辩论。", "倾向于支持能源行业观点的帕特·哈迪正在抵制针对低龄学生的科学课程标准修订提案。这些提案将强调人类活动在近期气候变化中的主导作用，并鼓励探讨减缓措施。", "大多数科学家和专家都强烈反驳哈迪的观点。“他们随意将学者和科学家的毕生研究当作又一种误入歧途的意见而一笔抹杀，”监测公共教育的非营利组织“得克萨斯自由网络”的高级传播策略师丹·奎因说，“数百万得州公立学校学生所学到的内容，往往过多地由带有党派立场的委员会成员的政治意识形态决定，而非事实和严谨的学术研究。”", "随着研究人员、政策制定者、教师和学生纷纷加大呼吁，要求学校更加重视教授气候变化事实，这场争论折射出全美乃至世界各地的激烈讨论。", "去年，由科学家和教师组成的非营利组织“全国科学教育中心”开展了一项研究，考察全美各州公立学校如何在科学课上讲授气候变化，结果仅勉强一半的州获得了 B+ 或更高的评级。在表现最差的 10 个州中，不乏一些人口最多的州，其中包括得克萨斯州——它不仅获得了最低等级（F），而且由于其教材广泛销往外地而具有举足轻重的影响。", "该中心副主任格伦·布兰奇提醒说，在一个将决策权下放给地方学校委员会的国家里，制定州级科学标准仅仅是一个有限的基准。他表示，即使一个州在科学标准方面表现优异，“也并不意味着这些内容就会被教授”。", "另一个问题是，尽管气候变化内容在一些学科和某些年龄段——如高中的地球与空间科学——中融入得很好，但在低龄儿童的课程以及普及度更高的学科（如生物和化学）中却体现不足，在许多社会科学课程中也同样不那么突出。", "布兰奇指出，即使越来越多的官方指南和教材反映了关于气候变化的科学共识，传递更具倾向性观点的非官方教学材料却仍在分发给教师，其中包括由自由意志主义智库和能源行业协会赞助的材料。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "例证题", "stem": "In paragraph 1, the weather in Texas is mentioned to", "options": ["forecast a policy shift in Texas schools", "stress the consequences of climate change", "indicate the atmosphere at the board meeting", "draw the public's attention to energy shortages"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The weather in Texas may have cooled since the recent extreme heat, but the temperature will be high at the State Board of Education meeting in Austin this month as officials debate how climate change is taught in Texas schools.", "explanation": "本题定位第一段首句。作者首先指出得州近期极端高温后天气转凉，随后用转折词 but 引出本月奥斯汀州教育委员会会议上“气温将依然很高（the temperature will be high）”，官员们将就学校如何教授气候变化展开辩论。此处以“天气转凉”与“会议高温”形成双关对比，temperature 指代会议气氛的激烈紧张。选项 C 中的 indicate the atmosphere at the board meeting 精准同义替换了“会议现场气氛紧张”的隐喻含义。", "trapNote": "A 项“预测政策转变”属无中生有，首段仅提及会议将辩论教学方式；B 项“强调气候变化后果”是将首句字面天气与后文气候议题混为一谈，属于望文生义。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does Quinn think of Hardy?", "options": ["She exaggerates the existing panic.", "She denies the value of scientific work.", "She shows no concern for pre-teens.", "She expresses self-contradictory views."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "\"They casually dismiss the career work of scholars and scientists as just another misguided opinion.\" says Dan Quinn, senior communications strategist at the Texas Freedom Network, a non-profit group that monitors public education", "explanation": "本题定位第三段 Dan Quinn 的言论。第二段提到 Pat Hardy 反对修订针对青少年的科学课程标准，第三段首句指出多数科学家和专家强烈反对 Hardy 的观点，随后引用 Quinn 的批评：“他们随意将学者和科学家的毕生心血（career work）当作又一种误入歧途的观点予以否定（casually dismiss）”。其中 dismiss...as... 对应选项 B 的 denies the value of（否定……的价值），career work of scholars and scientists 对应 scientific work，故选 B。", "trapNote": "A 项“夸大现有恐慌”文中未提及；C 项“不关心青少年”是对第二段 pre-teen pupils 的过度推理；D 项“观点自相矛盾”在文中毫无依据，均属无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The study mentioned in Paragraph 5 indicates that", "options": ["climate education is insufficient at state public schools", "policy makers have little drive for science education", "Texas is reluctant to rewrite its science textbooks", "environmental teaching in some states lacks supervision"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "A study last year by the National Center for Science Education, a non-profit group of scientists and teachers, looking at how state public schools across the country address climate change in science classes, gave barely half of US states a grade B + or higher.", "explanation": "本题定位第五段第一句。该段指出，全国科学教育中心去年的一项研究考察了全美各州公立学校在科学课上如何教授气候变化，结果“仅有勉强一半（barely half）的美国州获得了 B+ 或更高的评级”，而表现最差的 10 个州中包含得克萨斯州等人口大州（仅获最低等级 F）。由此可见，各州公立学校的气候变化教育整体存在明显不足，选项 A 中的 insufficient 准确概括了这一调查结果。", "trapNote": "B 项“政策制定者缺乏推动科学教育的动力”与第四段“政策制定者加大呼吁”不符且属过度泛化；C 项“得州不愿重写教材”偷换概念，原文只说得州教材销往他处且该州评级为 F。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Branch, state-level science standards in the US", "options": ["call for regular revision", "require urgent application", "have limited influence", "cater to local needs"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Glenn Branch, the centre's deputy director, cautions that setting state-level science standards is only one limited benchmark in a country that decentralises decisions to local school boards.", "explanation": "本题定位第六段第一句。中心副主任 Glenn Branch 提醒道，在一个将决策权下放给地方学校委员会的国家里，制定州级科学标准“仅仅是一个有限的基准（only one limited benchmark）”。紧接着他又补充说明，即便某个州在科学标准上表现优异，也“并不意味着这些内容就会被真正教授”。选项 C 中的 have limited influence 精准对应 limited benchmark 及其无法强制地方落实的局限性。", "trapNote": "A 项“呼吁定期修订”与 B 项“需要紧急应用”在第六段均未提及，属于无中生有；D 项“迎合地方需求”将原文的“决策权下放给地方委员会”偷换为州级标准主动迎合地方。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It is implied in the last paragraph that climate change teaching in some schools", "options": ["agree to major public demands", "reflects teachers' personal bias", "may misrepresent the energy sector", "can be swayed by external forces"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "unofficial educational materials that convey more slanted perspectives are being distributed to teachers. They include materials sponsored by libertarian think-tanks and energy industry associations.", "explanation": "本题定位最后一段。Branch 指出，尽管越来越多的官方指南和教材反映了关于气候变化的科学共识，但一些传递“更具倾向性观点（more slanted perspectives）”的非官方教育材料正在被分发给教师，其中包括由自由意志主义智库和能源行业协会赞助的材料。由此可推知，部分学校的气候变化教学可能会受到外部势力的左右，选项 D 中的 swayed by external forces 恰当概括了上述非官方外部赞助材料的影响。", "trapNote": "B 项“反映教师个人偏见”属于偷换概念，偏见来自外部发放的倾向性材料而非教师个人；C 项“可能歪曲能源行业”属于正反颠倒，材料正是由能源行业协会赞助的。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "同情；赞同", "note": "考研常考搭配 sympathize with，表示“赞成、支持（某种观点或立场）”，而非仅指“怜悯”。", "word": "sympathize"}, {"gloss": "主导地位；首要性", "note": "名词，源自 prime/primary；文中 primacy of human activity 指人类活动的主导作用。", "word": "primacy"}, {"gloss": "缓解；减轻（措施）", "note": "高频环保与政策词汇，mitigation measures 指“减缓气候变化的应对措施”。", "word": "mitigation"}, {"gloss": "反驳；质疑；争论", "note": "可作动词或名词；文中 sharply dispute 意为“强烈质疑/驳斥”，注意区别于 argue。", "word": "dispute"}, {"gloss": "不成比例的；过大的", "note": "常考词汇，由 dis- + proportionate 构成，文中指得州因教材销量大而拥有“与其单个州身份不相称的巨大影响”。", "word": "disproportionate"}, {"gloss": "有倾向性的；有偏见的", "note": "熟词僻义：slant 原意为“倾斜”，引申为“带偏见地歪曲/倾向性报道”，slanted perspectives 即“带有偏见的视角”。", "word": "slanted"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "\"What millions of Texas kids learn in their public schools is determined too often by the political ideology of partisan board members, rather than facts and sound scholarship.\"", "point": "主语从句 + 被动语态 + rather than 对比结构，常用于揭示“表面原因与深层决定因素”的对立。", "structure": "What 引导主语从句（What millions of Texas kids learn...）作主语；主句谓语为 is determined；by... rather than... 构成方式状语对比。", "zh": "“数百万得克萨斯州公立学校学生所学到的内容，往往过多地由带有党派偏见的委员会成员的政治意识形态所决定，而非事实和严谨的学术研究。”"}, {"en": "A study last year by the National Center for Science Education, a non-profit group of scientists and teachers, looking at how state public schools across the country address climate change in science classes, gave barely half of US states a grade B + or higher.", "point": "识别同位语与现在分词短语作后置定语的叠加，先抓主干“A study gave barely half of US states a grade B+ or higher”。", "structure": "主语为 A study，a non-profit group... 为插入同位语，looking at... 为现在分词短语作定语修饰 A study（内含 how 引导的宾语从句），主句谓语为 gave。", "zh": "去年，由科学家和教师组成的非营利组织“全国科学教育中心”开展了一项研究，考察全国各地公立学校在科学课上如何教授气候变化，结果显示仅勉强有一半的美国州获得了 B+ 或更高的评级。"}, {"en": "Another issue is that while climate change is well integrated into some subjects and at some ages — such as earth and space sciences in high schools — it is not as well represented in curricula for younger children and in subjects that are more widely taught, such as biology and chemistry.", "point": "表语从句中嵌套 while 引导的让步状语从句，注意破折号内的举例补充不影响主句连贯阅读。", "structure": "主系表结构 Another issue is that...；表语从句内部由 while 引导让步状语从句，破折号之间为举例插入语，后半句包含定语从句 that are more widely taught。", "zh": "另一个问题是，尽管气候变化内容在一些学科和某些年龄段——比如高中的地球与空间科学课程——融入得很好，但在面向低龄儿童的课程以及普及度更高的学科（如生物和化学）中却未能得到充分体现。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "动词短语与名词化表达的同义替换，体现“贬低、否定”。", "option": "denies the value of scientific work", "original": "casually dismiss the career work of scholars and scientists"}, {"note": "通过具体数据（勉强半数及格）概括出宏观评价“教育不足”。", "option": "climate education is insufficient at state public schools", "original": "gave barely half of US states a grade B + or higher"}, {"note": "“有限的基准”且未必被执行，同义替换为“影响力有限”。", "option": "have limited influence", "original": "only one limited benchmark... \"that does not mean it will be taught\""}, {"note": "被动表达“受外部势力影响”高度概括了“智库和行业协会赞助的倾向性材料”。", "option": "can be swayed by external forces", "original": "unofficial educational materials that convey more slanted perspectives... sponsored by libertarian think-tanks and energy industry associations"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2023-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2023", "examSet": "2023 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2023 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "美国短租监管与住房危机之争", "subtitle": "住房市场与公共政策 · 短租监管与保障性住房供需平衡", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 507, "paragraphs": ["Communities throughout the region have been attempting to regulate short-term rentals since sites like Airbnb took off in the 2010s. Now, with record-high home prices and historically low inventory, there's an increased urgency in such regulation, particularly among those who worry that developers will come in and buy up swaths of housing to flip for a fortune on the short-term rental market.", "In New Hampshire, where the rental vacancy rate has dropped below 1 percent, housing advocates fear unchecked short-term rentals will put further pressure on an already strained market. The state Legislature recently voted against a bill that would've made it illegal for towns to create legislation restricting short-term rentals.", "\"We are at a crisis level on the supply of rental housing, so anytime you're taking the tool out of the toolkit for communities to address this, you're potentially taking supply off the market that's already incredibly stressed,\" said Nick Taylor, executive director of the Workforce Housing Coalition of the Greater Seacoast. Without enough affordable housing in southern New Hampshire towns, \"employers are having a hard time attracting employees, and workers are having a hard time finding a place to live,\" Taylor said.", "However, short-term rentals also provide housing for tourists, a crucial part of the economies in places like Nantucket, Cape Cod, or the towns that make up New Hampshire's Seacoast and Lakes Region, pointed out Ryan Castle, CEO of the Cape Cod & Islands Association of Realtors. \"A lot of workers are servicing the tourist industry, and the tourism industry is serviced by those people coming in short term,\" Castle said, \"and so it's a cyclical effect.\"", "Short-term rentals themselves are not the crux of the issue, said Keren Horn, an affordable housing policy expert at the University of Massachusetts Boston. \"I think individuals being able to rent out their second home is a good thing. If it's their vacation home anyway, and it's just empty, why can't you make money off it?\" Horn said. Issues arise, however, when developers attempt to create large-scale short-term rental facilities — de facto hotels — to bypass taxes and regulations. \"I think the question is, shouldn't a developer who's really building a hotel, but disguising it as not a hotel, be treated and taxed and regulated like a hotel?\" Horn said.", "At the end of 2018, Governor Charlie Baker signed a bill to rein in those potential investor-buyers. \"The bill requires every rental host to register with the state, mandates they carry insurance, and opens the potential for local taxes on top of a new state levy,\" the Globe reported. Boston took things even further, limiting who is authorized to rent out their home, and requiring renters to register with the city's Inspectional Services Department.", "Horn said similar registration requirements could benefit other struggling cities and towns. The only way to solve the issue, however, is by creating more housing. \"If we want to make a change in the housing market, the main one is we have to build a lot more.\""], "translations": ["自 2010 年代爱彼迎（Airbnb）等网站兴起以来，该地区各地社区一直在试图规范短期租赁。如今，面对创历史新高的房价和处于历史低位的房源库存，实施此类监管变得愈发迫切，尤其是对于那些担心开发商涌入并大量购置住房、继而在短租市场上转手牟取暴利的人而言。", "在出租屋空置率已跌破 1% 的新罕布什尔州，住房倡导者担心不受约束的短租会给本已紧张的市场带来更大压力。该州立法机构最近投票否决了一项本会禁止各城镇立法限制短租的法案。", "“我们在租赁住房供应方面已处于危机水平，因此每当你剥夺社区应对这一问题的工具时，你都可能从本已极其紧张的市场上撤走房源供应，”大海岸劳动力住房联盟执行董事尼克·泰勒说。泰勒还表示，由于新罕布什尔州南部城镇缺乏足够的可负担住房，“雇主很难招到员工，而工人也很难找到住所”。", "不过，科德角与群岛房地产经纪人协会首席执行官瑞安·卡斯尔指出，短租也为游客提供了住宿，而旅游业是楠塔基特岛、科德角以及构成新罕布什尔州海岸与湖泊地区各城镇经济的重要支柱。“大量工人服务于旅游业，而旅游业又由那些短期前来的人所支撑，”卡斯尔说，“因此这形成了一种循环效应。”", "马萨诸塞大学波士顿分校的保障性住房政策专家凯伦·霍恩表示，短租本身并不是问题的症结所在。“我认为个人能够出租自己的第二套住房是件好事。既然反正是他们的度假屋，平时又空着，为什么不能借此赚点钱呢？”霍恩说。然而，当开发商试图建造大型短租设施——即事实上的酒店——来规避税收和监管时，问题就出现了。“我认为问题在于，一个明明在建酒店却伪装成非酒店的开发商，难道不应该像酒店那样被对待、征税和监管吗？”霍恩说道。", "2018 年底，州长查理·贝克签署了一项旨在约束这些潜在投资买家的法案。《环球报》报道称：“该法案要求每位出租屋主向州政府登记，强制他们购买保险，并为在新的州税之外再征收地方税提供了可能。”波士顿更是更进一步，限制有资格出租房屋的人群，并要求出租人向该市检查服务部登记。", "霍恩说，类似的登记要求可能会让其他陷入困境的城镇受益。然而，解决这个问题的唯一办法是建造更多的住房。“如果我们想改变住房市场，最主要的一点就是我们必须建造多得多的房子。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is true of New England?", "options": ["Its housing supply is at a very low level.", "Its communities are in need of funding.", "Its rental vacancy rate is going up slowly", "Its home prices are under strict control."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Now, with record-high home prices and historically low inventory, there's an increased urgency in such regulation", "explanation": "本题考察对新英格兰地区（文中提及新罕布什尔州、科德角、波士顿等地均属该地区）整体住房状况的理解，重点定位第一至三段。第一段指出，当前房价创历史新高且“房源库存处于历史低位（historically low inventory）”；第二段提到新罕布什尔州出租屋空置率已跌破 1%；第三段引用 Taylor 的话称“租赁住房供应处于危机水平”。综上可知该地区住房供应极度短缺，与选项 A 完全一致。", "trapNote": "C 项“出租屋空置率缓慢上升”与第二段 dropped below 1 percent 正反颠倒；D 项“房价受严格控制”与第一段 record-high home prices 明显相悖。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The bill mentioned in the Paragraph 2 was intended to", "options": ["curb short-term rental speculation.", "ensure the supply of cheap housing.", "punish illegal dealings in housing.", "allow a free short-term rental market."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The state Legislature recently voted against a bill that would've made it illegal for towns to create legislation restricting short-term rentals.", "explanation": "本题定位第二段第二句。原文指出，州立法机构最近投票否决了一项法案，该法案“本会使得城镇制定限制短期租赁的法规成为非法（would've made it illegal for towns to create legislation restricting short-term rentals）”。也就是说，如果该法案通过，地方政府就无权限制短租，从而相当于允许一个不受限制的自由短租市场，这与选项 D 的 allow a free short-term rental market 完全吻合。", "trapNote": "A 项“遏制短租投机”是反对该法案的社区所希望做的，而非该法案本身的目的，属于正反颠倒；C 项“惩罚住房非法交易”曲解了原文中的 illegal（指禁止地方立法）。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Compared with Castle, Taylor is more likely to support", "options": ["further investment in local tourism.", "an increase in affordable housing.", "strict management of real estate agents.", "a favorable policy for short-term workers."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Without enough affordable housing in southern New Hampshire towns, \"employers are having a hard time attracting employees, and workers are having a hard time finding a place to live,\" Taylor said.", "explanation": "本题对比第四段的 Castle 与第三段的 Taylor。第四段中 Castle 强调短租为游客提供住宿，支撑着当地旅游业与从业人员的良性循环；而第三段中 Taylor 指出当前租赁住房供应已处于危机水平，并担忧由于“没有足够的可负担住房（Without enough affordable housing）”，雇主难以招工、工人难以安家。由此可见，与重视旅游业的 Castle 相比，Taylor 显然更倾向于支持增加可负担住房，故选 B。", "trapNote": "A 项“进一步投资当地旅游业”与 D 项“优惠短租从业者的政策”更贴近第四段 Castle 的立场，属于张冠李戴；C 项“严格管理房产中介”在文中并未提及。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does Horn emphasize in paragraph 5", "options": ["The urgency to upgrade short-term rental facilities.", "The efficient operation of the local housing market.", "The necessity to stop developers from evading taxes.", "The proper procedures for renting out spare houses."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Issues arise, however, when developers attempt to create large-scale short-term rental facilities — de facto hotels — to bypass taxes and regulations.", "explanation": "本题定位第五段。Horn 首先表示个人出租闲置度假屋并非问题核心，随后用 however 转折引出关键：当开发商试图建造大规模短租设施——即“事实上的酒店（de facto hotels）”——以“逃避税收和监管（to bypass taxes and regulations）”时，问题就出现了，并反问此类开发商难道不应该像酒店一样被征税和监管吗。因此她强调必须阻止开发商逃税避规，选项 C 中的 stop developers from evading taxes 精准对应原文。", "trapNote": "A 项“升级短租设施的紧迫性”曲解了原文对“大型短租设施”的批评，属正反颠倒；D 项“出租闲置房屋的规范程序”以偏概全，Horn 对个人出租第二套房仅表示认可而非强调程序。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "Horn holds that imposing registration requirements is", "options": ["an irrational decision.", "an unfeasible proposal.", "an unnecessary measure.", "an inadequate solution."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "Horn said similar registration requirements could benefit other struggling cities and towns. The only way to solve the issue, however, is by creating more housing.", "explanation": "本题定位最后一段（第七段）。第六段提及州长签署法案并要求短租房东向州政府登记，第七段首句中 Horn 表示“类似的登记要求可能有益于其他陷入困境的城镇”，紧接着用 however 转折强调“解决这一问题的唯一途径是建造更多住房（The only way to solve the issue, however, is by creating more housing）”。这表明在她看来，登记制度虽有帮助但治标不治本，是一个“不充分的解决方案（an inadequate solution）”，故选 D。", "trapNote": "A 项“非理性决定”、B 项“不可行提议”和 C 项“不必要措施”均全盘否定了登记制度的作用，忽视了 Horn 明确提到的 could benefit other struggling cities and towns，属程度失当或正反颠倒。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "房源库存；存货", "note": "商业/地产常用词，historically low inventory 指“处于历史最低水平的待售/待租房源量”。", "word": "inventory"}, {"gloss": "倒买倒卖；快速转手获利", "note": "熟词僻义：flip 原意为“翻转、轻抛”，在房地产与投资语境中指“低买高卖以迅速套利”。", "word": "flip"}, {"gloss": "未受限制的；放任的", "note": "由 un- + checked（抑制、约束）构成，unchecked short-term rentals 指“缺乏监管的短租”。", "word": "unchecked"}, {"gloss": "绕过；规避", "note": "动词，常考搭配 bypass taxes and regulations 意为“规避税收与监管”。", "word": "bypass"}, {"gloss": "控制；约束；限制", "note": "短语动词，rein 原意为“缰绳”，rein in 比喻“勒紧缰绳加以管束、控制”，常接潜在风险或投资者。", "word": "rein in"}, {"gloss": "征收；税款", "note": "可作名词或动词，文中 a new state levy 指“州政府新征收的税项”。", "word": "levy"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Now, with record-high home prices and historically low inventory, there's an increased urgency in such regulation, particularly among those who worry that developers will come in and buy up swaths of housing to flip for a fortune on the short-term rental market.", "point": "with 伴随状语 + there be 主句 + 介词短语中的定语从句（嵌套宾语从句），层次清晰但修饰链较长。", "structure": "with 短语作背景状语；主句为 there's an increased urgency...；particularly among those 后接 who 引导的定语从句修饰 those，worry 后接 that 引导的宾语从句。", "zh": "如今，面对创历史新高的房价和处于历史低位的房源库存，实施此类监管变得愈发迫切，尤其是对于那些担心开发商涌入并大量购置住房、继而在短租市场上转手暴利的人而言。"}, {"en": "\"We are at a crisis level on the supply of rental housing, so anytime you're taking the tool out of the toolkit for communities to address this, you're potentially taking supply off the market that's already incredibly stressed,\" said Nick Taylor, executive director of the Workforce Housing Coalition of the Greater Seacoast.", "point": "直接引语内部为 so 连接的因果并列句，注意比喻表达 take the tool out of the toolkit（剥夺解决手段）。", "structure": "引语前半句为主系表结构；so 引出结果分句，其中 anytime 引导时间/条件状语从句，主句为 you're potentially taking supply off the market，末尾 that 引导定语从句修饰 the market。", "zh": "“我们在租赁住房供应方面已处于危机水平，因此每当你剥夺社区应对这一问题的工具时，你都可能从本已极其紧张的市场上撤走房源供应，”大海岸劳动力住房联盟执行董事尼克·泰勒说道。"}, {"en": "\"The bill requires every rental host to register with the state, mandates they carry insurance, and opens the potential for local taxes on top of a new state levy,\" the Globe reported.", "point": "同一主语带三个并列谓语动词（requires... mandates... opens...），注意 on top of（除……之外还……）的叠加逻辑。", "structure": "主语为 The bill，后接三个并列谓语动词短语 requires...、mandates...（省去 that 的宾语从句）和 opens...。", "zh": "《环球报》报道称：“该法案要求每位出租屋主向州政府登记，强制他们购买保险，并为在新的州税之外再征收地方税提供了可能。”"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“历史最低库存”对应“住房供应处于极低水平”。", "option": "Its housing supply is at a very low level.", "original": "historically low inventory / at a crisis level on the supply of rental housing"}, {"note": "双重否定结构：投票反对“禁止城镇限制短租的法案”，该法案本意即“放开自由短租市场”。", "option": "allow a free short-term rental market", "original": "made it illegal for towns to create legislation restricting short-term rentals"}, {"note": "通过比较 Castle 与 Taylor 各自的关切点，推断 Taylor 支持增加可负担住房。", "option": "an increase in affordable housing", "original": "Without enough affordable housing... workers are having a hard time finding a place to live"}, {"note": "bypass taxes 同义替换为 evade taxes（逃税）。", "option": "stop developers from evading taxes", "original": "when developers attempt to create large-scale short-term rental facilities... to bypass taxes and regulations"}, {"note": "肯定登记有益，但紧接着用 the only way to solve... 转折，表明登记并非充分解决方案。", "option": "an inadequate solution", "original": "could benefit other struggling cities and towns. The only way to solve the issue, however, is by creating more housing."}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2023-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2023", "examSet": "2023 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2023 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "出版商与书店争端及行业并购隐忧", "subtitle": "商业博弈 · 出版业并购与多样性危机", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 508, "paragraphs": ["If you're heading for your nearest branch of Waterstones in search of the Duchess of Sussex's new children's book The Bench, you might have to be prepared to hunt around a bit; the same may be true of The President's Daughter, the new thriller by Bill Clinton and James Patterson. Both of these books are published next week by Penguin Random House, a company currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones.", "The problem began late last year, when Penguin Random House confirmed that it had introduced a credit limit with Waterstones \"at a very significant level\". The trade magazine The Bookseller reported that Waterstones branch managers were being told to remove PRH books from prominent areas such as tables, display spaces and windows, and were \"quietly retiring them to their relevant sections\".", "PRH declined to comment on the issue, but a spokesperson for Waterstones told me: \"Waterstones are currently operating with reduced credit terms from PRH, the only publisher in the UK to place any limitations on our ability to trade. We are not boycotting PRH titles but we are doing our utmost to ensure that availability for customers remains good despite the lower overall levels of stock. We do this generally by giving their titles less prominent positioning within our bookshops. \"We are hopeful with our shops now open again that normality will return and that we will be allowed to buy appropriately. Certainly, our shops are exceptionally busy and book sales are very strong. The sales for our May Books of the Month surpassed any month since 2018.\"", "In the meantime, PRH authors have been the losers - as have customers, who might expect the new titles from the country's biggest publisher to be prominently displayed by its biggest book retailer. Big-name PRH authors may suffer a bit, but it's those mid-list authors, who normally rely on Waterstones staff's passion for promoting books by lesser-known writers, who will be praying for an end to the dispute.", "It comes at a time when authors are already worried about the consequences of the proposed merger between PRH and another big publisher, Simon & Schuster - the reduction in the number of unaligned UK publishers is likely to lead to fewer bidding wars, lower advances, and more conformity in terms of what is published. And one wonders if PRH would have been confident enough to deal with Waterstones in the way it has if it weren't quite such a big company (it was formed with the merger of Penguin and Random House in 2013) and likely to get bigger.", "\"This is all part of a wider change towards concentration of power and cartels. Literary agencies are getting bigger to have the clout to negotiate better terms with publishers, publishers consolidating to deal with Amazon,\" says Lownie. \"The publishing industry talks about diversity in terms of authors and staff but it also needs a plurality of ways of delivering intellectual contact, choice and different voices. After all, many of the most interesting books in recent years have come from small publishers.\""], "translations": ["如果你正准备前往最近的水石书店分店寻找苏塞克斯公爵夫人的新童书《长椅》，你可能得做好多番寻觅的准备；比尔·克林顿与詹姆斯·帕特森合著的新惊悚小说《总统的女儿》或许也是如此。这两本书都将由企鹅兰登书屋于下周出版，而该公司目前正与水石书店陷入僵持。", "问题始于去年年底，当时企鹅兰登书屋证实已对水石书店设定了“力度非常大”的信用额度限制。行业杂志《书商》报道称，水石书店各分店经理接到通知，将企鹅兰登书屋的图书从展台、展示区和橱窗等显眼位置撤下，并“悄然将它们退回到各自的分类书区”。", "企鹅兰登书屋拒绝就此事置评，但水石书店的一位发言人向我表示：“水石书店目前正在企鹅兰登书屋缩减的信用条件下运营，这也是英国唯一对我们交易能力施加任何限制的出版商。我们并没有抵制企鹅兰登书屋的图书，而是在尽最大努力确保尽管总体库存水平较低，顾客依然能够顺利买到书籍。我们通常的做法是在书店内给予其图书不那么显眼的陈列位置。”“随着门店重新营业，我们希望一切能恢复正常，我们也能获准进行适当采购。当然，我们的门店目前格外忙碌，图书销量非常强劲。我们五月‘每月精选图书’的销量超过了2018年以来的任何一个月。”", "在此期间，企鹅兰登书屋的作者们成了输家——顾客也是如此，他们原本可能指望英国最大出版商的新书能由英国最大的图书零售商在显眼位置陈列。企鹅兰登书屋的大牌作家或许只是略受影响，但真正祈祷这场争端早日结束的，是那些二三线作家，他们平时往往依赖水石书店员工满怀热情地推广不太知名作家的作品。", "此事正值作家们本就对企鹅兰登书屋与另一家大型出版商西蒙与舒斯特拟议合并的后果忧心忡忡之际——独立英国出版商数量的减少很可能导致竞价争夺减少、预付稿酬降低，以及出版内容趋于雷同。而且人们不禁会想，如果企鹅兰登书屋不是这样一家大公司（它由企鹅与兰登书屋于2013年合并而成）且规模还可能进一步扩大，它是否会有足够底气以这种方式应对水石书店。", "“这一切都是权力集中和卡特尔化这一更广泛变革的一部分。文学代理机构正不断壮大，以获得与出版商谈判更优条件的筹码；出版商也在通过整合来应对亚马逊。”劳尼说道，“出版业口头上谈论作者和员工的多样性，但它同样需要多元化的途径来传递思想交流、提供选择和发出不同的声音。毕竟，近年来许多最有趣的书籍都出自小出版商之手。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "例证题", "stem": "The author mentions two books in the paragraph 1 to present", "options": ["an ongoing conflict", "an intellectual concept", "a prevailing sentiment", "a literary phenomenon"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Both of these books are published next week by Penguin Random House, a company currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones.", "explanation": "本题为例证题。第一段先列举梅根王妃的新童书和克林顿与帕特森合著的新惊悚小说，随后点明两本书均由企鹅兰登书屋出版，而该公司“currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones”（正与水石书店陷入僵持）。作者提及这两本书是为了引出并具体呈现出版商与书店之间正在发生的商业冲突。A项“一场持续的冲突”中ongoing conflict与currently involved in a stand-off构成同义替换，故正确。", "trapNote": "B项“智力概念”和C项“普遍情绪”均属无中生有；D项“文学现象”停留在两本新书的表面话题，忽略了后句点明的商业对峙主旨，属于偏离例证目的的常见干扰。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Why did Waterstones shops retire PRH books to their relevant sections?", "options": ["To make them easily noticeable.", "To comply with PRH's requirement.", "To respond to PRH's business move.", "To arrange them in a systematic way."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The problem began late last year, when Penguin Random House confirmed that it had introduced a credit limit with Waterstones \"at a very significant level\".", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位至第二段。前句指出问题的起因是企鹅兰登书屋对水石书店实施了“力度极大”的信用额度限制（credit limit）；紧接着第二句指出水石书店各分店经理接到通知，将PRH的图书从展台、橱窗等显眼位置撤下并放回各自所属书区。可见书店撤架并非主动配合，而是对PRH收紧信用额度这一商业举措的直接反制与回应。C项精准概括了这一因果逻辑，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“使其更易被注意”与原文“撤出显眼区域”正反颠倒；B项“遵守PRH的要求”曲解因果，限贷才是PRH所为，撤架是水石的反击；D项“系统整理”属过度臆测。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What message did the spokesman of Waterstones seem to convey?", "options": ["Their customers remain loyal.", "The credit limit will be removed.", "Their stock is underestimated.", "The book market is rather slack."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Certainly, our shops are exceptionally busy and book sales are very strong. The sales for our May Books of the Month surpassed any month since 2018.", "explanation": "本题为推断题，定位至第三段水石书店发言人的表态。发言人一方面指出受PRH缩减信用条件影响，书店库存总体减少；另一方面强调门店客流极旺、图书销量非常强劲，五月“每月精选”销量创下2018年以来的单月新高。由此可推断，尽管PRH供货受限、展位减少，顾客依然大力支持水石书店，即顾客依然忠诚（remain loyal）。A项符合文意，故正确。", "trapNote": "B项“信用额度将被取消”将发言人的主观希望（hopeful）偷换为必然事实；C项“库存被低估”曲解lower overall levels of stock；D项“市场低迷”与销量强劲正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What can be one consequence of current dispute?", "options": ["Sales of books by mid-list PRH writers fall off considerably.", "Lesser-known PRH writers become the target of criticism.", "Waterstones staff hesitate to promote big-name author's books.", "Waterstones branches suffer a severe reduction in revenue."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Big-name PRH authors may suffer a bit, but it's those mid-list authors, who normally rely on Waterstones staff's passion for promoting books by lesser-known writers, who will be praying for an end to the dispute.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位至第四段。段首指出PRH的作者和读者都是这场争端的输家；随后对比指出，大牌作家或许只受轻微影响，但那些二三线作家（mid-list authors）平时高度依赖水石书店员工热情推介冷门作品，如今最迫切祈祷争端结束。由于图书被撤出显眼展位且失去重点推介，二三线PRH作家的书籍销量势必大幅下滑。A项中fall off considerably精准对应其惨重损失，故正确。", "trapNote": "B项“成为批评对象”属无中生有；C项把“不太知名的二三线作家”偷换为“大牌作家（big-name）”；D项“分店收入严重下滑”与第三段门店销量强劲相悖。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "Which of the following statements best represents Lownie's view?", "options": ["Small publishers ought to stick together.", "Big publishers will lose their dominance.", "The publishing industry is having a hard time.", "The merger of publishers is a worrying trend."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "\"This is all part of a wider change towards concentration of power and cartels. Literary agencies are getting bigger to have the clout to negotiate better terms with publishers, publishers consolidating to deal with Amazon,\" says Lownie.", "explanation": "本题为态度题，定位至第六段Lownie的发言。他指出当前局面源于权力集中与行业卡特尔化的趋势：文学代理机构不断做大，出版商也通过合并（consolidating）来抗衡亚马逊；而他紧接着强调出版业不仅需要作者和员工的多样性，也需要多元化的传播渠道、选择和不同声音，并肯定小出版商近年贡献了大量佳作。由此可见，Lownie对出版商合并趋势深感担忧，D项准确概括了其核心观点。", "trapNote": "A项“小出版商应团结”在文中未提及，属过度推理；B项“大出版商将失去主导权”与“权力集中”正反颠倒；C项“出版业处境艰难”过于笼统，未点出并购与集中这一核心靶点。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "对峙，僵持", "note": "熟词/合成词；由动词短语stand off转化而来，常用于商业或政治争端，对应conflict/dispute", "word": "stand-off"}, {"gloss": "撤回，退回（书架）", "note": "熟词僻义；日常义为“退休”，文中retire A to B指把图书从醒目展位撤回到原属分类书架", "word": "retire"}, {"gloss": "抵制，联合拒绝购买", "note": "高频考点词；可作名词或动词，指因抗议或施压而拒绝交易、购买或参与", "word": "boycott"}, {"gloss": "非结盟的，独立的（未合并的）", "note": "构词法：un-（未）+ aligned（结盟的），文中指未并入大型出版集团的独立出版商", "word": "unaligned"}, {"gloss": "影响力，话语权", "note": "核心词；原指“猛击”，在商业与政治语境中常指议价实力或政治影响力", "word": "clout"}, {"gloss": "（企业）合并，整合", "note": "高频词；与merger构成同义替换，在经济类阅读中常涉及市场集中（concentration）话题", "word": "consolidate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Big-name PRH authors may suffer a bit, but it's those mid-list authors, who normally rely on Waterstones staff's passion for promoting books by lesser-known writers, who will be praying for an end to the dispute.", "point": "强调整句型与定语从句嵌套（it's...who...中间插入非限定性定语从句）", "structure": "前分句让步；后分句为it's...who...强调句型，被强调部分those mid-list authors后接who引导的非限定性定语从句对其进行补充说明。", "zh": "企鹅兰登书屋的知名作家或许会受一点影响，但真正祈祷这场争端早日结束的，是那些二三线作家——他们平时有赖于水石书店员工热情推介不太知名作家的作品。"}, {"en": "And one wonders if PRH would have been confident enough to deal with Waterstones in the way it has if it weren't quite such a big company (it was formed with the merger of Penguin and Random House in 2013) and likely to get bigger.", "point": "混合虚拟语气（对过去/已发生行为的虚拟与对现在状态的假设结合）", "structure": "if引导宾语从句，从句内部含混合虚拟语气：主句谓语would have been...针对已经采取的强硬做法，条件句if it weren't...针对PRH目前的庞大规模。", "zh": "而且人们不禁会想，如果PRH不是这样一家大公司（它由企鹅出版集团与兰登书屋于2013年合并而成）且规模还可能进一步扩大，它当初是否会有足够底气以这种方式应对水石书店。"}, {"en": "The publishing industry talks about diversity in terms of authors and staff but it also needs a plurality of ways of delivering intellectual contact, choice and different voices.", "point": "but转折递进与并列宾语结构", "structure": "but连接前后对比转折；delivering后接三个并列名词短语（intellectual contact, choice and different voices）作宾语。", "zh": "出版业口头上谈论作者和员工层面的多样性，但它同样需要多元化的途径来传递思想交流、提供选择以及发出不同的声音。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "名词stand-off（僵持）与ongoing conflict（持续冲突）同义替换", "option": "an ongoing conflict", "original": "currently involved in a stand-off"}, {"note": "实施严格信用额度属于商业举措，书店撤架是对其的直接应对", "option": "To respond to PRH's business move", "original": "introduced a credit limit ... remove PRH books from prominent areas"}, {"note": "门店极其忙碌、销量强劲且创2018年以来新高，间接体现顾客依然忠诚", "option": "Their customers remain loyal", "original": "our shops are exceptionally busy and book sales are very strong"}, {"note": "二三线作家依赖书店推荐，失去展位导致其迫切祈祷停火，即销量大幅下滑", "option": "Sales of books by mid-list PRH writers fall off considerably", "original": "those mid-list authors ... will be praying for an end to the dispute"}, {"note": "权力集中、卡特尔化及出版商整合趋势对应令人担忧的并购趋势", "option": "The merger of publishers is a worrying trend", "original": "concentration of power and cartels ... publishers consolidating"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2023-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2023", "examSet": "2023 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2023 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "学术论文引用操纵与掠夺性期刊乱象", "subtitle": "学术伦理 · 引用卡特尔与科研评价异化", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 438, "paragraphs": ["Scientific papers are the recordkeepers of progress in research. Each year researchers publish millions of papers in more than 30,000 journals. The scientific community measures the quality of those papers in a number of ways, including the perceived quality of the journal (as reflected by the title's impact factor) and the number of citations a specific paper accumulates. The careers of scientists and the reputation of their institutions depend on the number and prestige of the papers they produce, but even more so on the citations attracted by these papers.", "Citation cartels, where journals, authors, and institutions conspire to inflate citation numbers, have existed for a long time. In 2016, researchers developed an algorithm to recognize suspicious citation patterns, including groups of authors that disproportionately cite one another and groups of journals that cite each other frequently to increase the impact factors of their publications. Recently, another expression of this predatory behavior has emerged: so-called support service consultancies that provide language and other editorial support to individual authors and to journals sometimes advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles.", "The advent of electronic publishing and authors' need to find outlets for their papers resulted in thousands of new journals. The birth of predatory journals wasn't far behind. These journals can act as milk cows where every single article in an issue may cite a specific paper or a series of papers. In some instances, there is absolutely no relationship between the content of the article and the citations. The peculiar part is that the journal that the editor is supposedly working for is not profiting at all—it is just providing citations to other journals. Such practices can lead an article to accrue more than 150 citations in the same year that it was published.", "How insidious is this type of citation manipulation? In one example, an individual-acting as author, editor, and consultant - was able to use at least 15 journals as citation providers to articles published by five scientists at three universities. The problem is rampant in Scopus, a citation database, which includes a high number of the new \"international\" journals. In fact, a listing in Scopus seems to be a criterion to be targeted in this type of citation manipulation.", "Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice. Red flags include a large number of citations to an article within the first year. And for authors who wish to steer clear of citation cartel activities: when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal."], "translations": ["科学论文是研究进展的记录者。每年研究人员在三万多种期刊上发表数百万篇论文。科学界通过多种方式衡量这些论文的质量，包括期刊的公认质量（由刊物的影响因子体现）以及某篇论文积累的引用次数。科学家的职业生涯及其所属机构的声誉，取决于他们所产出论文的数量和声望，但更取决于这些论文所吸引的引用量。", "期刊、作者与机构合谋虚增引用次数的“引用卡特尔”早已存在。2016年，研究人员开发了一种算法来识别可疑的引用模式，包括不成比例地相互引用的作者群体，以及为了提高各自出版物影响因子而频繁互引的期刊群体。最近，这种掠夺性行为又出现了另一种表现形式：那些为个人作者和期刊提供语言及其他编辑支持的所谓服务咨询机构，有时会建议投稿人在自己的文章中添加若干引用。", "电子出版的兴起以及作者寻找论文发表渠道的需求，催生了数千种新期刊。掠夺性期刊的诞生也紧随其后。这些期刊可以充当“奶牛”——在一期期刊中，每一篇文章都可能引用某篇特定论文或某一系列论文。在某些情况下，文章内容与所引文献之间完全没有任何关联。奇特之处在于，该编辑名义上效力的期刊本身根本不从中获利——它只是在向其他期刊输送引用。此类做法可使一篇文章在发表当年就积累超过150次引用。", "这种引用操纵行为究竟有多隐蔽且危害深重？在一个案例中，某个人同时身兼作者、编辑和顾问三重身份，竟能利用至少15种期刊，为三所大学的五位科学家发表的论文提供引用。这一问题在引文数据库Scopus中尤为猖獗，该数据库收录了大量新兴的“国际”期刊。事实上，被Scopus收录似乎成了此类引用操纵所瞄准的一个标准。", "Scopus自身拥有检测这种学术不端行为所需的全部数据。危险信号包括一篇文章在发表后第一年内就获得大量引用。而对于那些希望远离“引用卡特尔”活动的作者而言：当编辑、审稿人或支持服务机构要求你添加不恰当的参考文献时，切勿照办，并且务必向期刊举报这一要求。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 1, the careers of scientists can be determined by", "options": ["how many citations their papers contain", "how many times their papers are cited", "the prestige of the people they work with", "the status they have in scientific circles"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The careers of scientists and the reputation of their institutions depend on the number and prestige of the papers they produce, but even more so on the citations attracted by these papers.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位至第一段末句。该句明确指出，科学家的职业发展（careers）及其所属机构的声誉，既取决于他们发表论文的数量与影响力，更取决于这些论文所吸引的引用次数（the citations attracted by these papers）。B项“他们的论文被引用的次数”中how many times their papers are cited是对citations attracted by these papers的精准同义转述，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项将“论文被他人引用的次数”偷换为“论文自身包含的参考文献数量（contain）”；C项“共事者的声望”偷换原文“论文的声望”；D项“学术圈地位”属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The support service consultancies tend to", "options": ["recommend journals to their clients", "list citations patterns for their clients", "ask authors to include extra citations", "advise contributors to cite each other"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "so-called support service consultancies that provide language and other editorial support to individual authors and to journals sometimes advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位至第二段末句。文中指出，近年来这种掠夺性引用行为出现了新的表现形式：那些为个人作者和期刊提供语言及其他编辑支持的服务咨询机构（support service consultancies），有时会建议投稿人在文章中额外增加一些引用（advise contributors to add a number of citations）。C项中的ask authors to include extra citations与原文构成准确对应，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“向客户推荐期刊”和B项“为客户列出引用模式”在原文中均未提及，属无中生有；D项“建议投稿人互相引用”混淆了上句算法识别的“作者群体互引”与咨询机构的行为。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The function of the \"milk cow\" journals is to", "options": ["boost citation counts for certain authors", "help scholars publish articles at low cost", "instruct first-time contributors in citation", "increase the readership of new journals"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "These journals can act as milk cows where every single article in an issue may cite a specific paper or a series of papers.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位至第三段。文中将部分掠夺性期刊比作“奶牛”（milk cows），具体表现是同一期里的每一篇文章都可能引用某篇或某系列特定论文，甚至文章内容与引用毫无关联，且这些期刊本身并不从中获利，只是为其他期刊输送引用，使目标论文当年即可积累逾150次引用；第四段也印证其服务于特定科学家。可见“奶牛期刊”的作用就是为特定作者刷高引用量，A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“低成本发表文章”、C项“指导首次投稿者引用”和D项“提高新期刊读者量”原文均未提及，均属于无中生有；且原文强调此类期刊“自身并不获利”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What can be learned about Scopus from the last two paragraphs?", "options": ["It fosters competition among citation providers.", "It has the capability to identify suspicious citations.", "It hinders the growth of international journals.", "It is established to prevent citation manipulation."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice. Red flags include a large number of citations to an article within the first year.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位至第四、五段关于Scopus的内容。第四段提到引用操纵问题在收录了大量新兴“国际”期刊的Scopus数据库中十分猖獗；而第五段开篇随即转折指出，Scopus自身拥有识别此类学术不端行为所需的全部数据（all the data necessary to detect this malpractice），例如第一年内引用量激增等危险信号。由此可知，Scopus具备识别可疑引用的能力，B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“促进引用提供者竞争”和C项“阻碍国际期刊发展”属无中生有；D项“建立目的是防止引用操纵”将Scopus作为引文数据库的性质与其具备的检测数据偷换为建库初衷。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What should an author do to deal with citation manipulation?", "options": ["Take legal action.", "Demand an apology.", "Seek professional advice.", "Reveal their misconduct."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位至第五段末句。作者针对希望远离“引用卡特尔”活动的学者给出明确建议：当编辑、审稿人或支持服务机构要求你在论文中添加不恰当的参考文献时，务必拒绝配合（do not oblige），并且一定要向期刊举报该请求（do report the request to the journal）。D项“揭发他们的不当行为”中的reveal their misconduct精准同义转述了report the request，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“采取法律行动”、B项“要求道歉”和C项“寻求专业建议”均超出原文“向期刊举报（report...to the journal）”的范围，属于无中生有或过度推理。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "合谋，密谋", "note": "负向高频动词；常接不定式conspire to do sth，表示“串通一气做坏事”", "word": "conspire"}, {"gloss": "掠夺性的，剥削性的", "note": "学术高频词；predatory journals（掠夺性期刊）指以敛财或刷指标为目的、缺乏严格同行评审的期刊", "word": "predatory"}, {"gloss": "发表途径，发布平台", "note": "熟词僻义；日常指“出口、折扣店”，文中find outlets for their papers指寻找发表论文的渠道/期刊", "word": "outlet"}, {"gloss": "积累，自然增加", "note": "高频动词；同段前文用accumulate，此处用accrue表示引用量随时间累积，构成同义替换", "word": "accrue"}, {"gloss": "隐蔽而有害的，潜伏的", "note": "阅读态度词；带有强烈的贬义色彩，常用来修饰蔓延却不易察觉的问题或操纵行为", "word": "insidious"}, {"gloss": "答应，顺从（要求）", "note": "熟词僻义；常用义为“迫使（be obliged to）”，文中do not oblige作不及物动词表示“不要顺从、不要照办”", "word": "oblige"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In 2016, researchers developed an algorithm to recognize suspicious citation patterns, including groups of authors that disproportionately cite one another and groups of journals that cite each other frequently to increase the impact factors of their publications.", "point": "including引出并列结构与双重定语从句", "structure": "主句为researchers developed an algorithm to recognize...；including引出两个由and连接的并列同位说明成分，分别由that引导定语从句修饰groups of authors和groups of journals。", "zh": "2016年，研究人员开发出一种算法来识别可疑的引用模式，包括不成比例地相互引用的作者群体，以及为提高各自刊物影响因子而频繁互引的期刊群体。"}, {"en": "Recently, another expression of this predatory behavior has emerged: so-called support service consultancies that provide language and other editorial support to individual authors and to journals sometimes advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles.", "point": "冒号解释说明+长定语从句修饰主语", "structure": "冒号前为主句；冒号后进一步阐释this predatory behavior，其中主语consultancies后接that引导的长定语从句，谓语动词为advise。", "zh": "最近，这种掠夺性行为出现了另一种表现形式：那些为个人作者和期刊提供语言及其他编辑支持的所谓服务咨询机构，有时会建议投稿人在其文章中额外添加若干引用。"}, {"en": "And for authors who wish to steer clear of citation cartel activities: when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal.", "point": "前置介词短语+when时间状语从句+强调助动词do祈使句", "structure": "for authors...为引出对象的介词短语（内含who定语从句）；冒号后由when引导时间状语从句，主句为两个并列祈使句，其中do report中do表强调。", "zh": "而对于那些希望远离“引用卡特尔”活动的作者而言：当编辑、审稿人或支持服务机构要求你添加不恰当的参考文献时，切勿照办，并且务必向期刊举报这一要求。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "citations attracted by these papers（论文吸引的引用）同义替换为how many times their papers are cited（论文被引次数）", "option": "how many times their papers are cited", "original": "the citations attracted by these papers"}, {"note": "advise contributors to add a number of citations（建议投稿人增加引用）同义替换为ask authors to include extra citations", "option": "ask authors to include extra citations", "original": "advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles"}, {"note": "为特定论文集中输送引用、使文章一年内积攒逾150次引用，即帮特定作者刷高引用量", "option": "boost citation counts for certain authors", "original": "cite a specific paper or a series of papers ... accrue more than 150 citations"}, {"note": "has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice（拥有检测违规所需的全部数据）对应具备识别可疑引用的能力", "option": "It has the capability to identify suspicious citations", "original": "has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice"}, {"note": "do report the request to the journal（向期刊举报请求）同义替换为Reveal their misconduct（揭发其不当行为）", "option": "Reveal their misconduct", "original": "do report the request to the journal"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2022-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2022", "examSet": "2022 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2022 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "塑料艺术品与文物的保护难题", "subtitle": "文化艺术 · 博物馆塑料制品老化与保存困境", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 438, "paragraphs": ["People often complain that plastics are too durable. Water bottles, shopping bags, and other trash litter the planet, from Mount Everest to the Mariana Trench, because plastics are everywhere and don't break down easily. But some plastic materials change over time. They crack and frizzle. They \"weep\" out additives. They melt into sludge. All of which creates huge headaches for institutions, such as museums, trying to preserve culturally important objects. The variety of plastic objects at risk is dizzying: early radios, avant-garde sculptures, celluloid animation stills from Disney films, the first artificial heart.", "Certain artifacts are especially vulnerable because some pioneers in plastic art didn't always know how to mix ingredients properly, says Thea van Oosten, a polymer chemist who, until retiring a few years ago, worked for decades at the Cultural Heritage Agency of the Netherlands. \"It's like baking a cake: If you don't have exact amounts, it goes wrong,\" she says. \"The object you make is already a time bomb.\"", "And sometimes, it's not the artist's fault. In the 1960s, the Italian artist Piero Gilardi began to create hundreds of bright, colorful foam pieces. Those pieces included small beds of roses and other items as well as a few dozen \"nature carpets\"-large rectangles decorated with foam pumpkins, cabbages, and watermelons. He wanted viewers to walk around on the carpets-which meant they had to be durable.", "Unfortunately, the polyurethane foam he used is inherently unstable. It's especially vulnerable to light damage, and by the mid-1990s, Gilardi's pumpkins, roses, and other figures were splitting and crumbling. Museums locked some of them away in the dark.", "So van Oosten and her colleagues worked to preserve Gilardi's sculptures. They infused some with stabilizing and consolidating chemicals. Van Oosten calls those chemicals \"sunscreens\" because their goal was to prevent further light damage and rebuild worn polymer fibers. She is proud that several sculptures have even gone on display again, albeit sometimes beneath protective cases.", "Despite success stories like van Oosten's, preservation of plastics will likely get harder. Old objects continue to deteriorate. Worse, biodegradable plastics designed to disintegrate, are increasingly common.", "And more is at stake here than individual objects. Joana Lia Ferreira, an assistant professor of conservation and restoration at the NOVA School of Science and Technology, notes that archaeologists first defined the great material ages of human history-Stone Age, Iron Age, and so on-after examining artifacts in museums. We now live in an age of plastic, she says, “and what we decide to collect today, what we decide to preserve...will have a strong impact on how in the future we'll be seen.”"], "translations": ["人们常常抱怨塑料太过耐用。从珠穆朗玛峰到马里亚纳海沟，水瓶、购物袋和其他垃圾遍布地球，因为塑料无处不在且不易分解。但有些塑料材料会随时间推移而发生变化。它们会开裂、卷曲，会“渗出”添加剂，还会融化成泥状物。所有这一切都给试图保存具有重要文化意义物品的机构（如博物馆）带来了极大的麻烦。处于危险之中的塑料物品种类繁多，令人目眩：早期的收音机、前卫雕塑、迪士尼电影的赛璐珞动画静帧，以及第一颗人工心脏。", "高分子化学家Thea van Oosten在几年前退休前曾在荷兰文化遗产局工作了几十年，她说，某些艺术品尤其脆弱，因为一些塑料艺术先驱并不总是懂得如何正确混合原料。“这就像烤蛋糕：如果你没有精确的用量，就会出错，”她说，“你做出来的物品本身就已经是一颗定时炸弹。”", "而有时，这并不是艺术家的错。20世纪60年代，意大利艺术家Piero Gilardi开始创作数百件色彩鲜艳的泡沫塑料作品。这些作品包括小型玫瑰花坛等物件，以及几十块“自然地毯”——装饰着泡沫塑料南瓜、卷心菜和西瓜的大块矩形地毯。他希望观众能在这些地毯上走来走去——这意味着它们必须经久耐用。", "遗憾的是，他所使用的聚氨酯泡沫本身就不稳定。它尤其容易受到光线损伤，到了20世纪90年代中期，Gilardi的南瓜、玫瑰花和其他造型都出现了开裂和碎裂。博物馆只得将其中一些锁在黑暗的库房里。", "于是van Oosten和她的同事们致力于保护Gilardi的雕塑。他们向部分雕塑中注入了稳定和加固化学药剂。Van Oosten称这些化学物质为“防晒霜”，因为它们的目标是防止进一步的光线损伤并重建受损的高分子纤维。令她感到自豪的是，有几件雕塑甚至已经重新公开展出，尽管有时需要放在保护罩下。", "尽管有像van Oosten这样的成功案例，塑料的保存工作仍可能会变得越来越困难。老旧物件在持续老化变质。更糟糕的是，设计用于自行分解的可生物降解塑料正变得越来越普遍。", "而且这里利害攸关的远不止单个物品。NOVA科学技术学院保护与修复学助理教授Joana Lia Ferreira指出，考古学家正是通过考察博物馆里的文物，才首先界定了人类历史上的重大物质时代——石器时代、铁器时代等等。她说，我们如今生活在一个塑料时代，“而我们今天决定收藏什么、决定保存什么……将会对未来世人如何看待我们产生重大影响。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 1, museums are faced with difficulties in ______.", "options": ["maintaining their plastic items.", "obtaining durable plastic artifacts.", "handling outdated plastic exhibits.", "classifying their plastic collections."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "All of which creates huge headaches for institutions, such as museums, trying to preserve culturally important objects.", "explanation": "定位于第一段倒数第二句。原文指出塑料会开裂、渗出添加剂或融化成泥状，这些变化“给试图保存具有重要文化意义物品的机构（如博物馆）带来了巨大麻烦”。题干问博物馆面临何种困难，A项“maintaining their plastic items（维护其塑料藏品）”是对原文“preserve culturally important objects”及前文“plastic materials”的精准同义转述，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项“获取耐用塑料文物”属无中生有，首段未提及获取困难；C项“处理过时塑料展品”偷换概念，原文指塑料老化变质而非展品过时；D项“分类藏品”在文中并无依据。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Van Oosten believes that certain plastic objects are ______.", "options": ["immune to decay.", "improperly shaped.", "inherently flawed.", "complex in structure."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Certain artifacts are especially vulnerable because some pioneers in plastic art didn't always know how to mix ingredients properly", "explanation": "定位于第二段首句及末句。Van Oosten指出，某些艺术品格外脆弱，因为一些塑料艺术先驱并不总懂得如何正确混合原料，就像烤蛋糕没掌握精确配比一样，“做出来的物品本身就是一颗定时炸弹”。C项“inherently flawed（存在固有缺陷）”精准概括了原料配比不当导致的先天脆弱性，其中flawed对应didn't mix ingredients properly与time bomb，故正确。", "trapNote": "A项“免疫腐朽”与原文“especially vulnerable”正反颠倒；B项“形状不当”偷换概念，原文指原料混合比例不当而非造型问题；D项“结构复杂”属无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Museums stopped exhibiting some of Gilardi's artworks to ______.", "options": ["keep them from hurting visitors.", "duplicate them for future display.", "have their ingredients analyzed.", "prevent them from further damage."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "It's especially vulnerable to light damage, and by the mid-1990s, Gilardi's pumpkins, roses, and other figures were splitting and crumbling. Museums locked some of them away in the dark.", "explanation": "定位于第四段第二、三句。前文介绍Gilardi用聚氨酯泡沫创作了作品，本段指出该泡沫极易受光线损伤，到20世纪90年代中期作品出现开裂和碎裂，因此“博物馆将其中一些锁进黑暗之处”。第五段也印证修复旨在“prevent further light damage（防止进一步光损伤）”。D项“prevent them from further damage（防止其进一步受损）”准确转述了避光封存的目的，为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“避免伤害参观者”属无中生有，第三段仅提及作者希望观众在毯子上走动；B项“复制以供未来展示”及C项“分析其成分”均未在博物馆封存原因中提及。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author thinks that preservation of plastics is ______.", "options": ["costly.", "unworthy.", "unpopular.", "challenging."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Despite success stories like van Oosten's, preservation of plastics will likely get harder.", "explanation": "定位于第六段首句。作者先肯定了van Oosten的成功案例，随后用Despite转折，明确指出“塑料的保存可能会变得更困难（will likely get harder）”，并补充两点原因：旧物继续老化，且旨在自行分解的可生物降解塑料日益普及。D项“challenging（具有挑战性的）”精准对应“get harder”，体现了作者认为塑料保护工作艰难的判断。", "trapNote": "A项“昂贵的”与C项“不受欢迎的”均属无中生有，文中未讨论保存成本或公众喜好；B项“不值得的”与末段强调保护具有重要意义的态度正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "In Ferreira's opinion, preservation of plastic artifacts ______.", "options": ["will inspire future scientific research.", "has profound historical significance.", "will help us separate the material ages.", "has an impact on today's cultural life."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "We now live in an age of plastic, she says, “and what we decide to collect today, what we decide to preserve...will have a strong impact on how in the future we'll be seen.”", "explanation": "定位于第七段。Ferreira指出考古学家正是通过研究博物馆文物才定义了石器时代、铁器时代等人类历史上的重大物质时代；如今我们处于塑料时代，“今天决定收藏和保存什么，将对未来世人如何看待我们产生重大影响”。B项“has profound historical significance（具有深远的历史意义）”准确概括了塑料文物保存对界定时代和影响后世认知的价值。", "trapNote": "A项“启发未来科学研究”偷换概念，原文指影响未来如何看待当代社会，而非科研启发；C项“帮助我们划分物质时代”混淆主语，是考古学家过去定义时代；D项“影响当今文化生活”把未来偷换为今天。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "渗出；排出", "note": "熟词僻义：常见意为“哭泣”，此处加引号形象指塑料内部添加剂“渗出、析出”。", "word": "weep"}, {"gloss": "保存，保护（文物等）", "note": "高频核心词，名词为preservation；注意与reserve（预订/保留）区分。", "word": "preserve"}, {"gloss": "固有的，内在的", "note": "考研高频副词，常与unstable/flawed等词搭配，是细节题常见同义替换源。", "word": "inherently"}, {"gloss": "恶化，变质", "note": "表示物品随时间腐朽、退化，同义词有decline/decay/degrade。", "word": "deteriorate"}, {"gloss": "碎裂，解体", "note": "由dis-（分开）+ integrate（整合）构成，指可降解塑料“分解、瓦解”。", "word": "disintegrate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "All of which creates huge headaches for institutions, such as museums, trying to preserve culturally important objects.", "point": "由“介词+关系代词（All of which）”引导的非限定性定语从句，指代前文塑料老化现象整体；现在分词短语trying to...作后置定语修饰institutions。", "structure": "主句（All of which creates huge headaches for institutions）+ 插入语（such as museums）+ 后置定语（trying to preserve culturally important objects）", "zh": "所有这一切都给试图保存具有重要文化意义物品的机构（如博物馆）带来了极大的麻烦。"}, {"en": "Certain artifacts are especially vulnerable because some pioneers in plastic art didn't always know how to mix ingredients properly, says Thea van Oosten, a polymer chemist who, until retiring a few years ago, worked for decades at the Cultural Heritage Agency of the Netherlands.", "point": "引语倒装结构（...says Thea van Oosten）搭配同位语（a polymer chemist）和多层嵌套的who定语从句，阅读时可先抓主干“某些文物很脆弱，因为先驱不懂配料”。", "structure": "直接引语内容（主句 + because原因状语从句）+ 说话人（says Thea van Oosten）+ 同位语（a polymer chemist）+ who引导的定语从句（内含until时间状语）", "zh": "高分子化学家Thea van Oosten在几年前退休前曾在荷兰文化遗产局工作了几十年，她说，某些艺术品尤其脆弱，因为一些塑料艺术先驱并不总是懂得如何正确混合原料。"}, {"en": "We now live in an age of plastic, she says, “and what we decide to collect today, what we decide to preserve...will have a strong impact on how in the future we'll be seen.”", "point": "两个并列的what引导主语从句作主语，意为“我们今天决定收藏什么、保存什么”，宾语从句how in the future we'll be seen中含时间状语倒装提前。", "structure": "主句 + 插入语（she says）+ 并列主语从句（what we decide...）+ 谓语（will have a strong impact on）+ 宾语从句（how... we'll be seen）", "zh": "她说，我们如今生活在一个塑料时代，“我们今天决定收藏什么、决定保存什么……将会对未来世人如何看待我们产生深远影响。”"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "preserve与maintain同义替换，culturally important objects对应文中plastic items。", "option": "maintaining their plastic items", "original": "preserve culturally important objects"}, {"note": "原料配比不当如同一颗定时炸弹，等价于物品存在“固有缺陷”。", "option": "inherently flawed", "original": "didn't always know how to mix ingredients properly... already a time bomb"}, {"note": "把作品锁在黑暗环境中，目的是防止光线造成进一步损害。", "option": "prevent them from further damage", "original": "locked some of them away in the dark / prevent further light damage"}, {"note": "保存工作“可能会变得更困难”，直接对应态度评价词challenging。", "option": "challenging", "original": "will likely get harder"}, {"note": "决定未来世人如何看待我们的时代，概括为“具有深远的历史意义”。", "option": "has profound historical significance", "original": "defined the great material ages of human history... strong impact on how in the future we'll be seen"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2022-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2022", "examSet": "2022 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2022 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "Z世代与大学学位的价值重估", "subtitle": "教育就业 · 学位贬值与终身学习趋势", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 419, "paragraphs": ["As the latest crop of students pen their undergraduate application form and weigh up their options, it may be worth considering just how the point, purpose and value of a degree has changed and what Generation Z need to consider as they start the third stage of their educational journey.", "Millennials were told that if you did well in school, got a decent degree, you would be set up for life. But that promise has been found wanting. As degrees became universal, they became devalued. Education was no longer a secure route of social mobility. Today, 28 per cent of graduates in the UK are in non-graduate roles, a percentage which is double the average among OECD countries.", "This is not to say that there is no point in getting a degree, but rather stress that a degree is not for everyone, that the switch from classroom to lecture hall is not an inevitable one and that other options are available.", "Thankfully, there are signs that this is already happening, with Generation Z seeking to learn from their millennial predecessors, even if parents and teachers tend to be still set in the degree mindset. Employers have long seen the advantages of hiring school leavers who often prove themselves to be more committed and loyal employees than graduates. Many too are seeing the advantages of scrapping a degree requirement for certain roles.", "For those for whom a degree is the desired route, consider that this may well be the first of many. In this age of generalists, it pays to have specific knowledge or skills. Postgraduates now earn 40 per cent more than graduates. When more and more of us have a degree, it makes sense to have two.", "It is unlikely that Generation Z will be done with education at 18 or 21; they will need to be constantly up-skilling throughout their career to stay employable. It has been estimated that this generation, due to the pressures of technology, the wish for personal fulfilment and desire for diversity, will work for 17 different employers over the course of their working life and have five different careers. Education, and not just knowledge gained on campus, will be a core part of Generation Z's career trajectory.", "Older generations often talk about their degree in the present and personal tense: I am a geographer or 'I am a classist.' Their sons or daughters would never say such a thing; it's as if they already know that their degree won't define them in the same way."], "translations": ["随着最新一批学生动笔填写本科申请表并权衡各种选择，或许值得思考的是：学位的意义、目的和价值究竟发生了怎样的变化，以及Z世代在开启他们求学旅程的第三阶段时需要考虑些什么。", "千禧一代曾被告知，只要你在学校表现出色、拿到一个体面的学位，就能一辈子衣食无忧。但这一承诺已被证明难以兑现。随着大学学位变得普及，它们也随之贬值。教育不再是通往社会阶层流动的可靠途径。如今，英国28%的大学毕业生从事的是无需本科学位的岗位，这一比例是经合组织国家平均水平的两倍。", "这并不是说拿学位毫无意义，而是想强调学位并非适合所有人，从中学教室走进大学礼堂并不是唯一必然的道路，还有其他选择可供考虑。", "值得庆幸的是，有迹象表明这种变化正在发生，Z世代正试图从千禧一代前辈的经历中吸取教训，尽管父母和老师往往仍固守着“唯学位论”的思维定式。雇主们早就看到了雇佣中学毕业生的优势，这些员工往往比大学毕业生表现出更强的敬业度和忠诚度。许多雇主也开始意识到取消某些职位学位要求的好处。", "对于那些仍把攻读学位作为理想路径的人来说，请考虑这很可能只是诸多学位中的第一个。在这个通才盛行的时代，拥有特定知识或技能会带来丰厚回报。如今研究生的收入比本科生高出40%。当越来越多的人都拥有一个学位时，再多拿一个学位就显得合情合理了。", "Z世代不太可能在18岁或21岁就结束教育；为了保持就业竞争力，他们需要在整个职业生涯中不断提升技能。据估计，由于技术压力、对个人成就感的追求以及对多样性的渴望，这一代人在职业生涯中将为17个不同的雇主工作，并从事5种不同的职业。教育——而不仅仅是在校园里学到的知识——将成为Z世代职业轨迹的核心组成部分。", "老一辈人谈起自己的学位时，常常使用一般现在时和带有个人身份认同的表达：“我是地理学家”或“我是古典学者”。他们的儿女绝不会这么说；就好像他们早已明白，学位不会以同样的方式定义他们。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "the author suggests that Generation Z should ______.", "options": ["be careful in choosing a college", "be diligent at each educational stage", "reassess the necessity of college education", "postpone their undergraduate application"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "it may be worth considering just how the point, purpose and value of a degree has changed and what Generation Z need to consider as they start the third stage of their educational journey.", "explanation": "定位于第一段及第三段。第一段作者建议Z世代在开启高等教育阶段时，值得思考“学位的意义、目的和价值发生了怎样的变化”；第三段进一步明确指出，“并不是每个人非得拿学位不可，从中学教室走进大学礼堂并非必然选择，还有其他选择”。C项“reassess the necessity of college education（重新评估大学教育的必要性）”精准概括了作者对Z世代的建议。", "trapNote": "A项“谨慎选择大学”以偏概全，原文讨论的是是否一定要读大学而非选哪所学校；B项“在每个教育阶段勤奋学习”及D项“推迟本科申请”均属无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "The percentage of UK graduates in non-graduate roles reflect ______.", "options": ["Millennial's opinions about work", "the shrinking value of a degree", "public discontent with education", "the desired route of social mobility"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "As degrees became universal, they became devalued. Education was no longer a secure route of social mobility. Today, 28 per cent of graduates in the UK are in non-graduate roles, a percentage which is double the average among OECD countries.", "explanation": "定位于第二段第三至五句。该段先指出“随着学位普及，学位贬值了（became devalued），教育不再是通往社会流动的可靠路径”，紧接着用英国28%的大学毕业生从事非学位要求岗位这一数据来佐证上述论断。B项“the shrinking value of a degree（学位价值的缩水）”直接对应“devalued”，是该数据所反映的核心问题。", "trapNote": "A项“千禧一代对工作的看法”偷换概念，数据反映的是就业现实而非主观观点；C项“公众对教育的不满”属无中生有；D项“社会流动的理想途径”与原文“no longer a secure route”正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The author considers it a good sign that ______.", "options": ["Generation Z are seeking to earn a decent degree.", "School leavers are willing to be skilled workers.", "Employers are taking a realistic attitude to degrees", "Parents are changing their minds about education."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Employers have long seen the advantages of hiring school leavers who often prove themselves to be more committed and loyal employees than graduates. Many too are seeing the advantages of scrapping a degree requirement for certain roles.", "explanation": "定位于第四段。作者以“Thankfully（值得庆幸的是）”引出积极迹象，随后指出雇主早已看到雇佣中学毕业生的优势，且“许多雇主也看到了取消某些职位学位要求的好处”。C项“Employers are taking a realistic attitude to degrees（雇主对学位采取了务实的态度）”准确概括了雇主不再唯学历论、根据岗位实际需求选人的变化。", "trapNote": "A项“Z世代寻求获得体面学位”偷换概念，第二段说千禧一代被灌输拿体面学位，而Z世代正汲取教训；B项“中学毕业生愿当技术工人”无中生有；D项“父母改变看法”与原文“still set in the degree mindset”正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It is advised in Paragraph 5 that those with one degree should ______.", "options": ["make an early decision on their career", "attend on the job training programs", "team up with high-paid postgraduates", "further their studies in a specific field"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "In this age of generalists, it pays to have specific knowledge or skills. Postgraduates now earn 40 per cent more than graduates. When more and more of us have a degree, it makes sense to have two.", "explanation": "定位于第五段第二至四句。作者针对决定攻读学位的人指出，“在这个通才盛行的时代，拥有特定知识或技能会带来回报”，接着说明研究生比本科生收入高40%，并总结“当越来越多的人拥有一个学位时，拥有两个学位是明智的”。D项“further their studies in a specific field（在特定领域深造）”精准对应“specific knowledge or skills”和攻读第二个学位，故正确。", "trapNote": "A项“尽早决定职业”与B项“参加在职培训项目”均未在第五段提及，属于无中生有（第六段才提到持续提升技能）；C项“与高薪研究生组队”属于对“earn 40 per cent more”的曲解。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can be concluded about Generation Z from the last two paragraphs?", "options": ["Lifelong learning will define them", "They will make qualified educators.", "Degrees will no longer appeal them.", "They will have a limited choice of jobs"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "It is unlikely that Generation Z will be done with education at 18 or 21; they will need to be constantly up-skilling throughout their career to stay employable.", "explanation": "定位于第六、七段。第六段指出Z世代不会在18或21岁就结束教育，他们需要在整个职业生涯中“不断提升技能（constantly up-skilling）”，教育将成为其职业轨迹的核心部分；第七段指出他们不会被某一个学位所定义。综合两段可知，A项“Lifelong learning will define them（终身学习将定义他们）”准确提炼了Z世代持续学习与身份认同的新特征。", "trapNote": "B项“他们将成为合格的教育者”属于对“Education... will be a core part”的曲解；C项“学位不再吸引他们”过度推理，文中仅说学位不再以同样方式定义他们；D项“工作选择有限”与“five different careers”正反颠倒。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "（发现某事物）有欠缺，不足", "note": "熟词僻义：常见意为“想要”，此处作形容词指承诺“被证明不尽如人意、落空”。", "word": "wanting"}, {"gloss": "废除，取消（制度、要求）", "note": "熟词僻义：常见名词意为“废品、碎片”，作动词常考“取消、摒弃（规定/标准）”。", "word": "scrap"}, {"gloss": "提升技能，进修", "note": "复合动词，职场与教育话题高频词，对应“终身学习”。", "word": "up-skill"}, {"gloss": "社会流动（阶层跃升）", "note": "考研社会学与教育类文章核心搭配，常讨论教育能否促进阶层流动。", "word": "social mobility"}, {"gloss": "有回报的，划算的", "note": "熟词僻义：it pays to do sth. 固定句型，意为“做某事是有益的、值得的”。", "word": "pay"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "This is not to say that there is no point in getting a degree, but rather stress that a degree is not for everyone, that the switch from classroom to lecture hall is not an inevitable one and that other options are available.", "point": "not to say... but rather... 构成“并非否定……而是强调……”的平衡论证；but rather后由三个并列的that宾语从句构成排比，梳理作者核心立场。", "structure": "主句（This is not to say... but rather stress...）+ 三个并列that宾语从句（that a degree... / that the switch... / that other options...）", "zh": "这并不是说拿学位毫无意义，而是想强调学位并非适合所有人，从中学教室走进大学礼堂并不是唯一必然的道路，还有其他选择可供考虑。"}, {"en": "Thankfully, there are signs that this is already happening, with Generation Z seeking to learn from their millennial predecessors, even if parents and teachers tend to be still set in the degree mindset.", "point": "there are signs that... 引导同位语从句；with复合结构作伴随状语说明Z世代的行动；even if让步状语从句形成代际观念对比。", "structure": "主句（there are signs）+ 同位语从句（that this is already happening）+ with伴随状语 + even if让步状语从句", "zh": "值得庆幸的是，有迹象表明这种变化正在发生，Z世代正试图从千禧一代前辈的经历中吸取教训，尽管父母和老师往往仍固守着“唯学位论”的思维定式。"}, {"en": "It has been estimated that this generation, due to the pressures of technology, the wish for personal fulfilment and desire for diversity, will work for 17 different employers over the course of their working life and have five different careers.", "point": "It has been estimated that... 形式主语结构；that从句内部插入由due to引导的三个并列原因短语，阅读时可先跳过插入部分抓主谓“will work... and have...”。", "structure": "形式主语（It has been estimated）+ that主语从句（主语this generation + 插入语due to... + 并列谓语will work... and have...）", "zh": "据估计，由于技术压力、对个人成就感的追求以及对多样性的渴望，这一代人在职业生涯中将为17个不同的雇主工作，并从事5种不同的职业。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "重新思考学位的意义与是否适合所有人，对应“重新评估大学教育的必要性”。", "option": "reassess the necessity of college education", "original": "considering just how the point, purpose and value of a degree has changed / a degree is not for everyone"}, {"note": "学位贬值（devalued）同义替换为“学位价值缩水（shrinking value）”。", "option": "the shrinking value of a degree", "original": "As degrees became universal, they became devalued"}, {"note": "雇佣中学毕业生并取消部分岗位学位要求，体现“对学位采取务实态度”。", "option": "taking a realistic attitude to degrees", "original": "advantages of hiring school leavers / scrapping a degree requirement for certain roles"}, {"note": "拥有特定知识技能且多拿一个学位，对应“在特定领域深造”。", "option": "further their studies in a specific field", "original": "have specific knowledge or skills / makes sense to have two"}, {"note": "在整个职业生涯不断提升技能且不被单一学位定义，概括为“终身学习将定义他们”。", "option": "Lifelong learning will define them", "original": "constantly up-skilling throughout their career / their degree won't define them in the same way"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2022-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2022", "examSet": "2022 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2022 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "科学与艺术的双向跨界合作", "subtitle": "跨学科合作 · 科普传播与双向共创", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 425, "paragraphs": ["Enlightening, challenging, stimulating, fun. These were some of the words that Nature readers used to describe their experience of art-science collaborations in a series of articles on partnerships between artists and researchers. Nearly 40% of the roughly 350 people who responded to an accompanying poll said, they had collaborated with artists; and almost all said they would consider doing so in future.", "Such an encouraging result is not surprising. Scientists are increasingly seeking out visual artists to help them communicate their work to new audiences. \"Artists help scientists reach a broader audience and make emotional connections that enhance learning.\" One respondent said.", "One example of how artists and scientists have together rocked the scenes came last month when the Sydney Symphony Orchestra performed a reworked version of Antonio Vivaldi's The Four Seasons. They reimagined the 300-year-old score by injecting the latest climate prediction data for each season-provided by Monash University's Climate Change Communication Research Hub. The performance was a creative call to action ahead of November's United Nations Climate Change Conference in Glasgow, UK.", "But a genuine partnership must be a two-way street. Fewer artists than scientists responded to the Nature poll, however, several respondents noted that artists do not simply assist scientists with their communication requirements. Nor should their work be considered only as an object of study. The alliances are most valuable when scientists and artists have a shared stake in a project, are able to jointly design it and can critique each other's work. Such an approach can both prompt new research as well as result in powerful art.", "More than half a century ago, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology opened its Center for Advanced Visual Studies (CAVS) to explore the role of technology in culture. The founders deliberately focused their projects around light-hence the \"visual studies\" in the name. Light was something that both artists and scientists had an interest in, and therefore could form the basis of collaboration. As science and technology progressed, and divided into more sub-disciplines, the centre was simultaneously looking to a time when leading researchers could also be artists, writers and poets, and vice versa.", "Nature's poll findings suggest that this trend is as strong as ever, but, to make a collaboration work, both sides need to invest time, and embrace surprise and challenge. The reach of art-science tie-ups needs to go beyond the necessary purpose of research communication, and participants. Artists and scientists alike are immersed in discovery and invention, and challenge and critique are core to both, too."], "translations": ["启迪人心、富有挑战、激发灵感、充满乐趣。这些词是《自然》杂志读者在一系列探讨艺术家与研究者合作关系的文章中，用来形容自己参与艺科合作经历的词汇。在大约350名参与配套民意调查的受访者中，近40%的人表示曾与艺术家合作过；几乎所有人都表示未来会考虑这样做。", "出现如此令人鼓舞的结果并不意外。科学家们正越来越多地寻找视觉艺术家，帮助他们将自己的研究成果传播给新的受众。“艺术家能帮助科学家触达更广泛的受众，并建立有助于增进学习的情感联结。”一位受访者说道。", "艺术家与科学家携手惊艳现场的一个例子发生在去年，当时悉尼交响乐团演奏了改编版的安东尼奥·维瓦尔第名作《四季》。他们将莫纳什大学气候变化传播研究中心提供的各季节最新气候预测数据注入这部已有300年历史的乐谱中，对其进行了重新演绎。这场演出是在11月英国格拉斯哥联合国气候变化大会前夕发起的一场极具创意的行动呼吁。", "但真正的合作必须是双向的。尽管参与《自然》杂志民意调查的艺术家人数少于科学家，但多位受访者指出，艺术家并不仅仅是协助科学家满足其传播需求，他们的作品也不应仅仅被视为被研究的对象。当科学家与艺术家在项目中拥有共同利益、能够共同设计项目并且能够彼此评判对方的作品时，这种合作联盟才最具价值。这样的方式既能催生新的研究，也能造就震撼人心的艺术作品。", "半个多世纪前，麻省理工学院成立了高级视觉研究中心（CAVS），以探索技术在文化中所扮演的角色。创始人们刻意将项目聚焦于“光”——中心名称中的“视觉研究”也由此而来。光既是艺术家也是科学家共同感兴趣的事物，因此能够成为双方合作的基础。随着科学技术不断进步并分化出更多子学科，该中心同时也在展望这样一个时代：顶尖研究人员也可以同时是艺术家、作家和诗人，反之亦然。", "《自然》杂志的民意调查结果表明，这一趋势一如既往地强劲；但要让合作取得成效，双方都需要投入时间，并欣然接纳惊喜与挑战。艺科合作的影响范围需要超越科研传播这一必要目的，以及参与者本身（的局限）。无论是艺术家还是科学家，都沉浸在发现与创造之中，而挑战与评判同样是两者共同的核心。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to paragraph 1, art-science collaborations have .", "options": ["caught the attention of critics", "received favorable responses", "promoted academic publishing", "sparked heated public disputes"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Enlightening, challenging, stimulating, fun. These were some of the words that Nature readers used to describe their experience of art-science collaborations", "explanation": "定位第一段。首句列举了《自然》杂志读者描述艺术与科学合作体验的四个正向形容词（启迪人心的、富有挑战的、激发灵感的、有趣的），随后民调数据显示近40%的受访者曾与艺术家合作，且几乎所有人都表示未来会考虑这样做。由此可知，艺术与科学合作收获了积极正面的反馈，对应B项 received favorable responses，该选项高度概括了首段正向评价词及“未来愿意继续合作”的态度。", "trapNote": "A项“引起评论家关注”属偷换概念，原文是读者而非评论家；D项“引发激烈争论”属正反颠倒，原文反馈正面；C项“促进学术出版”纯属无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "例证题", "stem": "The reworked version of The Four Seasons is mentioned to show that .", "options": ["art can offer audiences easy access to science", "science can help with the expression of emotions", "public participation in science has a promising future", "art is effective in facilitating scientific innovations"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Scientists are increasingly seeking out visual artists to help them communicate their work to new audiences.", "explanation": "本题为例证题，需回到第三段事例之前寻找其所论证的观点。第二段明确指出，科学家正日益寻求视觉艺术家的帮助，以便向新受众传播科研成果，并引用受访者的话说明艺术家能帮助科学家触达更广泛的受众、建立情感联结从而增进理解。第三段紧接着以悉尼交响乐团将气候预测数据融入《四季》乐谱为例，正是为了说明艺术能够让公众更轻松地接触并理解科学，对应A项 art can offer audiences easy access to science。", "trapNote": "B项“科学有助于情感表达”属正反颠倒，原文是艺术借助情感联结促进科学学习；C项“公众参与科学前景光明”属无中生有；D项“艺术促进科学创新”属过度推理。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Some artists seem to worry about in the art-science partnership", "options": ["their role may be underestimated", "their reputation may be impaired", "their creativity may be inhibited", "their work may be misguided"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "several respondents noted that artists do not simply assist scientists with their communication requirements. Nor should their work be considered only as an object of study.", "explanation": "定位第四段。该段首句指出真正的合作必须是双向的，接着提到尽管回应民调的艺术家人数少于科学家，但多位受访者强调：艺术家不只是协助科学家满足传播需求，其作品也不应仅仅被视为被研究的对象。言下之意，部分艺术家担心自己在合作中的角色被矮化或低估。A项 their role may be underestimated 精准概括了“仅作辅助或研究对象”的担忧，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项“声誉受损”、C项“创造力受抑”和D项“作品被误导”在第四段均未提及，属于典型的无中生有；原文仅聚焦于艺术家担心合作地位不对等、自身角色被片面化。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What does the author say about CAVS?", "options": ["It was headed alternately by artists and scientists", "It exemplified valuable art-science alliances", "Its projects aimed at advancing visual studies", "Its founders sought to raise the status of artists"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Light was something that both artists and scientists had an interest in, and therefore could form the basis of collaboration.", "explanation": "定位第四段末与第五段。第四段提出，当科学家和艺术家在项目中拥有共同利益、能够共同设计并互相评判作品时，这种联盟最具价值。第五段随即以麻省理工学院的 CAVS 为例，指出创始人刻意围绕艺术家和科学家共同感兴趣的“光”开展项目，使其成为合作基础，且期待研究者兼任艺术家（反之亦然）。由此可见，CAVS 体现了有价值的艺科合作联盟，对应B项 exemplified valuable art-science alliances。", "trapNote": "A项“由艺术家和科学家轮流领导”属无中生有；C项“旨在推进视觉研究”属偷换概念，CAVS 意在探索科技在文化中的作用，“光”才是名称由来；D项“提高艺术家地位”原文未提。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "In the last paragraph, the author holds that art-science collaborations", "options": ["are likely to go beyond public expectations", "will intensify interdisciplinary competition", "should do more than communicating science", "are becoming more popular than before"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "The reach of art-science tie-ups needs to go beyond the necessary purpose of research communication", "explanation": "定位最后一段。作者在末段指出，为了让合作真正奏效，双方都需要投入时间并拥抱惊喜与挑战，随后明确提出核心观点：艺科合作（art-science tie-ups）的影响范围不能止步于科研传播这一必要目的（needs to go beyond the necessary purpose of research communication）。C项 should do more than communicating science 正是 go beyond... research communication 的同义转述。", "trapNote": "A项“超出公众预期”与B项“加剧跨学科竞争”在末段均无依据，属无中生有；D项“比以往更受欢迎”是对首句 this trend is as strong as ever 的过度推理。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "启迪人心的，富有启发性的", "note": "常考正向态度形容词，动词 enlighten 意为“启发、开导”。", "word": "enlightening"}, {"gloss": "重新构想，重新演绎", "note": "前缀 re- + imagine，阅读中常指对经典作品或方案的创新改编。", "word": "reimagine"}, {"gloss": "（共享的）利益，利害关系", "note": "熟词僻义：除“木桩、赌注”外，have a stake in 表示“与……有利害关系/共同利益”。", "word": "stake"}, {"gloss": "评论，批判性地评价", "note": "考研高频词，作动词或名词均侧重“客观评判、审视”，而非单纯指责。", "word": "critique"}, {"gloss": "合作，联姻，联系", "note": "常用复数 tie-ups，与 collaboration / partnership / alliance 构成同义替换链。", "word": "tie-up"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "These were some of the words that Nature readers used to describe their experience of art-science collaborations in a series of articles on partnerships between artists and researchers.", "point": "识别定语从句修饰先行词 words，并理清多层介词短语（of / in / on / between）对中心概念的限定。", "structure": "主句（These were some of the words）+ 定语从句（that Nature readers used to describe...）+ 介词短语状语/定语（in a series of articles on partnerships between...）。", "zh": "这些词是《自然》杂志读者在一系列探讨艺术家与研究者合作关系的文章中，用来形容自己参与艺科合作经历的词汇。"}, {"en": "The alliances are most valuable when scientists and artists have a shared stake in a project, are able to jointly design it and can critique each other's work.", "point": "注意 when 引导的时间/条件状语从句内部的三个并列谓语结构（have... / are able to... / can critique...）。", "structure": "主句（The alliances are most valuable）+ when 引导的状语从句（内部由三个并列谓语动词短语构成）。", "zh": "当科学家与艺术家在项目中拥有共同利益、能够共同设计项目并且能够彼此评判对方的作品时，这种合作联盟才最具价值。"}, {"en": "As science and technology progressed, and divided into more sub-disciplines, the centre was simultaneously looking to a time when leading researchers could also be artists, writers and poets, and vice versa.", "point": "掌握 look to a time when... 结构以及句尾习语 vice versa（反之亦然）的指代关系。", "structure": "As 引导的时间状语从句 + 主句（the centre was... looking to a time）+ when 引导的定语从句修饰 a time。", "zh": "随着科学技术不断进步并分化出更多子学科，该中心同时也在展望这样一个时代：顶尖研究人员也可以同时是艺术家、作家和诗人，反之亦然。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "首段多个正向评价词与第二段“令人鼓舞的结果”在选项中高度概括为“收到积极反馈”。", "option": "received favorable responses", "original": "Enlightening, challenging, stimulating, fun... Such an encouraging result"}, {"note": "communicate... to new audiences 与 reach a broader audience 对应“让受众轻松接触科学”。", "option": "offer audiences easy access to science", "original": "communicate their work to new audiences / reach a broader audience"}, {"note": "“不仅仅是协助传播或被当成研究对象”被抽象概括为“角色被低估”。", "option": "their role may be underestimated", "original": "do not simply assist... Nor should their work be considered only as an object of study"}, {"note": "上文“最具价值的联盟”与下文 CAVS 作为“合作基础”的案例形成例证照应。", "option": "exemplified valuable art-science alliances", "original": "The alliances are most valuable... could form the basis of collaboration"}, {"note": "go beyond 的字面意义在选项中转化为 should do more than，精准传达作者倡导的超越单向传播的立场。", "option": "should do more than communicating science", "original": "needs to go beyond the necessary purpose of research communication"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2022-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2022", "examSet": "2022 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2022 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "雇佣保护法与企业效率悖论", "subtitle": "劳动法规 · 雇佣保护与企业生产力", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 409, "paragraphs": ["The personal grievance provisions of New Zealand's Employment Relations Act 2000 (ERA) prevent an employer from firing an employee without good cause. Instead, dismissals must be justified. Employers must both show cause and act in a procedurally fair way.", "Personal grievances were designed to guard the jobs of ordinary workers from \"unjustified dismissals\". The premise was that the common law of contract lacked sufficient safeguards for workers against arbitrary conduct by management. Long gone are the days when a boss could simply give an employee contractual notice.", "But these provisions create difficulties for businesses when applied to highly paid managers and executives. As countless boards and business owners will attest, constraining firms from firing poorly performing, high-earning managers is a handbrake on boosting productivity and overall performance. The difference between C-grade and A-grade managers may very well be the difference between business success or failure. Between preserving the jobs of ordinary workers or losing them. Yet mediocrity is no longer enough to justify a dismissal.", "Consequently -and paradoxically-laws introduced to protect the jobs of ordinary workers may be placing those jobs at risk.", "If not placing jobs at risk, to the extent employment protection laws constrain business owners from dismissing under-performing managers, those laws act as a constraint on firm productivity and therefore on workers' wages. Indeed, in \"An International Perspective on New Zealand's Productivity Paradox\" (2014), the Productivity Commission singled out the low quality of managerial capabilities as a cause of the country's poor productivity growth record.", "Nor are highly paid managers themselves immune from the harm caused by the ERA's unjustified dismissal procedures. Because employment protection laws make it costlier to fire an employee, employers are more cautious about hiring new staff. This makes it harder for the marginal manager to gain employment. And firms pay staff less because firms carry the burden of the employment arrangement going wrong.", "Society also suffers from excessive employment protections. Stringent job dismissal regulations adversely affect productivity growth and hamper both prosperity and overall well-being.", "Across the Tasman Sea, Australia deals with the unjustified dismissal paradox by excluding employees earning above a specified \"high-income threshold\" from the protection of its unfair dismissal laws. In New Zealand, a 2016 private members' Bill tried to permit firms and high-income employees to contract out of the unjustified dismissal regime. However, the mechanisms proposed were unwieldy and the Bill was voted down following the change in government later that year."], "translations": ["新西兰《2000年雇佣关系法》（ERA）中的个人申诉条款禁止雇主在没有正当理由的情况下解雇员工。相反，解雇必须具有正当性。雇主必须既说明正当理由，又在程序上做到公平公正。", "个人申诉条款旨在保护普通工人的工作免受“无理辞退”。其前提假设是，普通合同法缺乏足够的保障机制来保护工人免受管理层武断行为的侵害。老板只需给员工发一份合同终止通知即可辞退员工的时代早已一去不复返。", "然而，当这些条款应用于高薪经理和高管时，却给企业带来了困难。正如无数董事会和企业主所证明的那样，限制企业解雇表现不佳的高薪高管，会成为阻碍生产力和整体绩效提升的“手刹”。C级管理者与A级管理者之间的差距，很可能就是企业成功与失败、保住普通工人饭碗与失去这些工作之间的差距。然而，仅仅因为表现平庸已不足以成为解雇的正当理由。", "因此——极具讽刺意味的是——本为保护普通工人工作而引入的法律，反而可能正在把这些工作置于风险之中。", "即使没有把工作置于险境，只要雇佣保护法在某种程度上限制了企业主解雇表现不佳的管理者，这些法律就会制约企业生产力，进而限制工人的工资。事实上，在《新西兰生产力悖论的国际视角》（2014年）一书中，生产力委员会就将管理能力低下单列为该国生产力增长记录不佳的原因之一。", "高薪管理者自身也无法幸免于《雇佣关系法》无理解雇程序所带来的伤害。因为雇佣保护法提高了辞退员工的成本，雇主在招聘新员工时会更加谨慎。这使得边缘管理者更难获得就业机会。而且由于雇佣关系一旦出错，负担由企业承担，企业给员工开出的薪酬也会更低。", "整个社会同样因过度的雇佣保护而受损。严苛的解雇法规会对生产力增长产生负面影响，阻碍经济繁荣与整体福祉。", "在塔斯曼海对岸，澳大利亚通过设定一个具体的“高收入门槛”，将收入高于该门槛的雇员排除在不公平解雇法的保护之外，从而破解这一无理解雇悖论。在新西兰，2016年的一项私人议员法案曾试图允许企业和高收入雇员通过协议选择退出无理解雇保护制度。然而，该法案所提议的机制过于笨拙繁琐，并在当年晚些时候政府换届后被投票否决。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The personal grievance provisions of the ERA are intended to", "options": ["punish dubious corporate practices", "improve traditional hiring procedures", "exempt employers from certain duties", "protect the rights of ordinary workers"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Personal grievances were designed to guard the jobs of ordinary workers from \"unjustified dismissals\".", "explanation": "定位第二段首句。题目询问《雇佣关系法》（ERA）中“个人申诉条款”的设立意图。第二段明确指出，该条款旨在保护普通工人的工作免受“无理辞退”（guard the jobs of ordinary workers from \"unjustified dismissals\"），因为普通合同法缺乏足够机制防止管理层的武断行为。D项 protect the rights of ordinary workers 中 protect 对应 guard，精准复现了条款的设计初衷。", "trapNote": "A项“惩罚可疑企业行为”属过度推理，原文强调保护工人而非直接惩罚企业；B项“改善传统招聘流程”属偷换概念，原文讨论的是解雇而非招聘；C项“免除雇主某些责任”与原文加重雇主举证责任完全正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be learned from paragraph 3 that the provisions may", "options": ["hinder business development", "undermine managers' authority", "affect the public image of the firms", "worsen labor-management relations"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "constraining firms from firing poorly performing, high-earning managers is a handbrake on boosting productivity and overall performance.", "explanation": "定位第三段。本段转折指出该条款在应用于高薪高管时给企业带来了困难：限制企业解雇表现不佳的高薪高管，会成为提升生产力和整体绩效的“手刹”（handbrake），而平庸与优秀高管之差甚至决定企业成败。A项 hinder business development 准确概括了“阻碍生产力与绩效提升、影响企业成败”的含义，其中 hinder 对应 constraining / is a handbrake on。", "trapNote": "B项“削弱管理者权威”属无中生有，限制解雇高管反而束缚了企业老板而非削弱高管权威；C项“影响企业公众形象”与D项“恶化劳资关系”在第三段中均未提及，属于主观臆断。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Which of the following measures would the Productivity Commission support?", "options": ["Imposing reasonable wage restraints.", "Enforcing employment protection laws.", "Limiting the powers of business owners.", "Dismissing poorly performing managers."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "the Productivity Commission singled out the low quality of managerial capabilities as a cause of the country's poor productivity growth record.", "explanation": "定位第五段。该段先指出雇佣保护法限制企业解雇表现不佳的管理者，从而抑制企业生产力与员工工资；接着引述生产力委员会（Productivity Commission）的报告，指出该机构将“管理能力低下”单列为新西兰生产力增长记录不佳的原因。由此可推断，生产力委员会会支持解雇表现不佳的管理者以改善管理质量，对应D项 Dismissing poorly performing managers。", "trapNote": "B项“严格执行雇佣保护法”与该机构批判低效管理阻碍生产力的立场正反颠倒；A项“合理限制工资”和C项“限制企业主权力”均属于曲解文意或无中生有，工资下降是法案的负面后果而非主张。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What might be an effect of ERA's unjustified dismissal procedures?", "options": ["Highly paid managers lose their jobs.", "Employees suffer from salary cuts.", "Society sees a rise in overall well-being.", "Employers need to hire new staff."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "And firms pay staff less because firms carry the burden of the employment arrangement going wrong.", "explanation": "定位第五、六段。第五段提到雇佣保护法限制了企业生产力并进而限制工人薪资；第六段进一步说明 ERA 无理解雇程序的负面影响：因为雇佣关系出错的风险由企业承担，企业支付给员工的薪酬会减少（firms pay staff less）。B项 Employees suffer from salary cuts 正是 pay staff less 及 constraint on workers' wages 的同义转述，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项“高薪高管失业”属偷换概念，原文指边际高管更难获聘而非已雇者失业；C项“整体福祉上升”与第七段 hamper well-being 正反颠倒；D项“雇主需招新员工”与第六段谨慎招聘相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be inferred that the \"high-income threshold\" in Australia", "options": ["has secured managers' earnings", "has produced undesired results", "is beneficial to business owners", "is difficult to put into practice"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "Australia deals with the unjustified dismissal paradox by excluding employees earning above a specified \"high-income threshold\" from the protection of its unfair dismissal laws.", "explanation": "定位第八段。前文反复论证无理解雇保护条款覆盖高薪高管时，会束缚企业解雇不称职高管的手脚、拖累生产力并损害企业利益。第八段指出，澳大利亚通过设定“高收入门槛”，将收入超过该标准的雇员排除在不公平解雇法的保护之外，从而破解这一悖论。由此可推知，这一举措解除了企业对高薪员工解雇受限的困扰，对企业主是有利的，对应C项 is beneficial to business owners。", "trapNote": "A项“保障高管收入”属正反颠倒，该门槛使高薪者不再受解雇法保护；B项“产生不良后果”无中生有；D项“难以实施”属张冠李戴，机制笨拙指的是新西兰2016年未通过的法案。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "申诉，委屈，不满", "note": "法律与职场高频词，personal grievance 指“个人劳动申诉”。", "word": "grievance"}, {"gloss": "武断的，专横的，任意的", "note": "与 justified（正当的、有理有据的）在文中形成反义对照。", "word": "arbitrary"}, {"gloss": "平庸，表现平平", "note": "源自形容词 mediocre（平庸的），第三段用其指工作表现“勉强及格但远非优秀”。", "word": "mediocrity"}, {"gloss": "免受……影响的，豁免的", "note": "熟词僻义：除“免疫的”外，be immune from/to 意为“不受……损害或影响”。", "word": "immune"}, {"gloss": "笨拙的，难以运作的，繁琐的", "note": "带有明显贬义，用于形容法规、机制或方案设计复杂、缺乏可操作性。", "word": "unwieldy"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "As countless boards and business owners will attest, constraining firms from firing poorly performing, high-earning managers is a handbrake on boosting productivity and overall performance.", "point": "识别动名词短语（constraining firms from...）作主语及暗喻词 handbrake（阻力、掣肘）的表达效果。", "structure": "As 引导的非限制性定语从句（作插入语）+ 主句（动名词短语作主语 + is a handbrake on...）。", "zh": "正如无数董事会和企业主所证明的那样，限制企业解雇表现不佳的高薪高管，会成为阻碍生产力和整体绩效提升的“手刹”。"}, {"en": "If not placing jobs at risk, to the extent employment protection laws constrain business owners from dismissing under-performing managers, those laws act as a constraint on firm productivity and therefore on workers' wages.", "point": "理清让步省略结构（If not placing...）及程度状语从句 to the extent (that)... 的逻辑层次。", "structure": "条件/让步状语省略（If not placing...）+ to the extent 引导的状语从句 + 主句（those laws act as a constraint on...）。", "zh": "即使没有把工作置于险境，只要雇佣保护法在某种程度上限制了企业主解雇表现不佳的管理者，这些法律就会制约企业生产力，进而限制工人的工资。"}, {"en": "Across the Tasman Sea, Australia deals with the unjustified dismissal paradox by excluding employees earning above a specified \"high-income threshold\" from the protection of its unfair dismissal laws.", "point": "掌握 exclude A from B（将A排除在B之外）结构，以及现在分词短语 earning above... 作后置定语。", "structure": "地点状语 + 主句（Australia deals with...）+ by 引导的方式状语（内部含现在分词后置定语 earning above...）。", "zh": "在塔斯曼海对岸，澳大利亚通过设定一个具体的“高收入门槛”，将收入高于该门槛的雇员排除在不公平解雇法的保护之外，从而破解这一无理解雇悖论。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "guard... from 与 protect 同义替换，ordinary workers 原词复现。", "option": "protect the rights of ordinary workers", "original": "guard the jobs of ordinary workers from \"unjustified dismissals\""}, {"note": "动词 constrain 与名词 handbrake 形象表达“阻碍、妨碍”，在选项中抽象为 hinder。", "option": "hinder business development", "original": "constraining firms... is a handbrake on boosting productivity and overall performance"}, {"note": "poorly performing 与文中的 under-performing 互为同义词组。", "option": "Dismissing poorly performing managers", "original": "dismissing under-performing managers"}, {"note": "“给员工付更少的钱”及“限制工人工资”同义替换为“遭受减薪”。", "option": "Employees suffer from salary cuts", "original": "constraint... on workers' wages / firms pay staff less"}, {"note": "将高收入者排除出解雇保护范围，旨在解决限制企业解雇低效高管的问题，因而“对企业主有利”。", "option": "is beneficial to business owners", "original": "deals with the unjustified dismissal paradox by excluding employees earning above a specified \"high-income threshold\""}]}}, {"difficulty": "L3", "exam": "kaoyan1", "id": "ky1-2021-t1", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["How can the train operators possibly justify yet another increase to rail passenger fares? It has become a grimly reliable annual ritual: every January the cost of travelling by train rises, imposing a significant extra burden on those who have no option but to use the rail network to get to work or otherwise. This year's rise, an average of 2.7 per cent, may be a fraction lower than last year's, but it is still well above the official Consumer Price Index (CPI) measure of inflation.", "Successive governments have permitted such increases on the grounds that the cost of investing in and running the rail network should be borne by those who use it, rather than the general taxpayer. Why, the argument goes, should a car-driving pensioner from Lincolnshire have to subsidise the daily commute of a stockbroker from Surrey? Equally, there is a sense that the travails of commuters in the South East, many of whom will face among the biggest rises, have received too much attention compared to those who must endure the relatively poor infrastructure of the Midlands and the North.", "However, over the past 12 months, those commuters have also experienced some of the worst rail strikes in years. It is all very well train operators trumpeting the improvements they are making to the network, but passengers should be able to expect a basic level of service for the substantial sums they are now paying to travel. The responsibility for the latest wave of strikes rests on the unions. However, there is a strong case that those who have been worst affected by industrial action should receive compensation for the disruption they have suffered.", "The Government has pledged to change the law to introduce a minimum service requirement so that, even when strikes occur, services can continue to operate. This should form part of a wider package of measures to address the long-running problems on Britain's railways. Yes, more investment is needed, but passengers will not be willing to pay more indefinitely if they must also endure cramped, unreliable services, punctuated by regular chaos when timetables are changed, or planned maintenance is managed incompetently. The threat of nationalisation may have been seen off for now, but it will return with a vengeance if the justified anger of passengers is not addressed in short order."], "questions": [{"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "How can the train operators possibly justify yet another increase to rail passenger fares?", "explanation": "定位第一段。首句以反问“铁路运营商怎么可能为又一次涨价找到正当理由”开篇，直接表达了作者对涨价合理性的否定态度（justify 对应 C 项的 unreasonable measure）；第三句进一步补充今年 2.7% 的涨幅仍远超官方 CPI 通胀率，由此可知涨价依然是不合理的举措。", "no": 21, "options": ["has kept pace with inflation.", "is a big surprise to commuters.", "remains an unreasonable measure.", "will ease train operators' burden."], "stem": "The author holds that this year's increase in rail passenger fares", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 属于正反颠倒，原文明确指出涨幅远高于通胀率（well above... inflation），而非与通胀“保持同步”。", "type": "态度题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "those who use it, rather than the general taxpayer. Why, the argument goes, should a car-driving pensioner from Lincolnshire have to subsidise the daily commute of a stockbroker", "explanation": "定位第二段前两句。首句指出铁路投资与运营成本应由“铁路使用者（those who use it）”而非“普通纳税人（the general taxpayer）”承担；第二句紧接着以“开车的退休老人补贴每天通勤的股票经纪人”为例进行类比，可见 stockbroker 在此代表乘坐火车通勤的旅客（rail travelers）。", "no": 22, "options": ["car drivers.", "rail travelers.", "local investors.", "ordinary taxpayers."], "stem": "The stockbroker in Paragraph 2 is used to stand for", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 和 D 属于张冠李戴，把类比中被要求补贴铁路的“开车老人/普通纳税人”错配给了“股票经纪人”；C 则属于脱离语境的望文生义。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "train operators trumpeting the improvements they are making to the network, but passengers should be able to expect a basic level of service", "explanation": "定位第三段第二句。该句使用“It is all very well..., but...”的让步转折句式，指出运营商虽大肆宣扬网络改进，但乘客支付高昂票价后理应能享受到基本服务水平。由此可推断，铁路运营商实际上未能提供足够的基本服务（failed to provide an adequate service）。", "no": 23, "options": ["are offering compensation to commuters.", "are trying to repair relations with the unions.", "have failed to provide an adequate service.", "have suffered huge losses owing to the strikes."], "stem": "It is indicated in Paragraph 3 that train operators", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 属于未然偷换为已然，末句说的是受罢工影响最严重者“理应获得赔偿（should receive compensation）”，而非运营商“正在提供赔偿”。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The threat of nationalisation may have been seen off for now, but it will return with a vengeance if the justified anger of passengers is not addressed in short order.", "explanation": "定位第四段末句。条件从句“if the justified anger of passengers is not addressed in short order”与题干“If unable to calm down passengers”构成同义替换；主句明确指出，若不及时平息乘客怒火，国有化（nationalisation）的威胁将卷土重来，而国有化意味着铁路所有权的变更（a change of ownership）。", "no": 24, "options": ["the loss of investment.", "the collapse of operations.", "a reduction of revenue.", "a change of ownership."], "stem": "If unable to calm down passengers, the railways may have to face", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 属于定位错位，前句提及乘客“不愿无休止地多付钱”的前提是服务持续拥挤混乱，并非末句“无法平息乘客愤怒”的直接后果。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "passengers will not be willing to pay more indefinitely if they must also endure cramped, unreliable services", "explanation": "综合全文并定位第四段核心句。文章开篇质疑铁路票价连年高于通胀的上涨，中间剖析了高票价与低质量服务、频发罢工之间的矛盾，末段明确指出乘客不会无休止地接受涨价（will not be willing to pay more indefinitely）。D 项“不断上涨的票价不可持续”精准概括了全文主旨。", "no": 25, "options": ["Who Are to Blame for the Strikes?", "Constant Complaining Doesn't Work", "Can Nationalisation Bring Hope?", "Ever-rising Fares Aren't Sustainable"], "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the text?", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 和 C 均属以偏概全，分别只截取了第三段的“罢工责任”或第四段结尾的“国有化威胁”等局部内容作为全文标题。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "2021 考研英语一真题", "subtitle": "英国铁路票价与运营争议（Q21–25）", "timeLimitMin": 18, "title": "Text 1", "year": "2021", "wordCount": 388, "examSet": "2021 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "translations": ["铁路运营商怎么可能为又一次上调铁路客运票价找到正当理由呢？这已经成了一项冷酷而准时的年度惯例：每年一月，乘火车出行的费用都会上涨，给那些别无选择、只能依靠铁路网通勤或出行的人增添沉重的额外负担。今年的涨幅平均为2.7%，或许比去年略低一点，但仍远高于官方以消费者物价指数（CPI）衡量的通胀率。", "历届政府都允许此类涨价，理由是投资和运营铁路网的成本理应由使用者而非普通纳税人来承担。按照这种说法，为什么林肯郡一名开车的退休老人要为萨里郡一名股票经纪人的日常通勤提供补贴呢？同样，人们也认为，与中部和北部地区那些不得不忍受相对落后的基础设施的乘客相比，东南部通勤者（其中许多人将面临最大幅度的涨价）的艰辛受到了过多的关注。", "然而，在过去12个月里，这些通勤者也经历了多年来最严重的几次铁路罢工。铁路运营商大肆吹嘘自己正在对路网进行的改进固然没错，但乘客付出如今这么高昂的出行费用，理应能指望获得最基本的服务水平。最新一轮罢工的责任在于工会。不过，完全有理由认为，受劳资行动影响最严重的群体应当因其遭受的出行中断而获得赔偿。", "政府已承诺修改法律，引入最低服务保障要求，以便即便发生罢工，铁路服务仍能继续运营。这应当成为解决英国铁路长期问题的一揽子更广泛措施的一部分。诚然，铁路需要更多投资，但如果乘客还不得不忍受拥挤、不可靠的服务——而且每逢时刻表调整或计划内维护管理不善时就频繁陷入混乱——他们就不会愿意无休止地多付钱。国有化的威胁眼下或许暂时被击退了，但如果乘客合情合理的愤怒未能迅速得到平息，这一威胁必将卷土重来、变本加厉。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "证明……正当，为……辩护", "note": "考研阅读高频态度动词，常出现在质疑某项政策或行为合理性的语境中，名词为 justification。", "word": "justify"}, {"gloss": "少量，一点儿", "note": "熟词僻义重点词：常见义为“分数/部分”，但在 a fraction lower/faster 等比较结构中意为“略微、一点儿”。", "word": "fraction"}, {"gloss": "承担，负担", "note": "高频搭配 bear the cost（承担费用）；其过去分词 borne（本文中 should be borne by）极易与出生的 born 混淆。", "word": "bear"}, {"gloss": "大肆宣扬，吹嘘", "note": "熟词僻义：名词本义为“喇叭、小号”，作及物动词时意为“大肆吹嘘、鼓吹”，常含轻微贬义。", "word": "trumpet"}, {"gloss": "不时打断，穿插于", "note": "熟词僻义：本义为“加标点符号”，在阅读中常作动词表示“不时被……打断、反复穿插”。", "word": "punctuate"}, {"gloss": "拥挤狭小的", "note": "考研高频形容词，源于动词 cramp（限制/束缚），常用来形容居住空间狭小或公共交通拥挤。", "word": "cramped"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "It has become a grimly reliable annual ritual: every January the cost of travelling by train rises, imposing a significant extra burden on those who have no option but to use the rail network to get to work or otherwise.", "point": "现在分词短语作结果状语 + who 引导的定语从句 + 固定搭配 have no option but to do", "structure": "冒号前主干：It has become a grimly reliable annual ritual；冒号后解释说明主干：every January the cost of travelling by train rises；现在分词短语作结果状语：imposing a significant extra burden on those...；定语从句：who have no option but to use the rail network... 修饰先行词 those（其中 have no option but to do 意为“别无选择只能做……”）。", "zh": "这已经成了一项冷酷而准时的年度惯例：每年一月乘火车出行的费用都会上涨，给那些别无选择只能依靠铁路网通勤或出行的人施加了沉重的额外负担。"}, {"en": "Equally, there is a sense that the travails of commuters in the South East, many of whom will face among the biggest rises, have received too much attention compared to those who must endure the relatively poor infrastructure of the Midlands and the North.", "point": "that 引导的同位语从句 + “代词 + of + whom”引导的非限制性定语从句 + 指示代词 those 指代前文名词", "structure": "主干：there is a sense that...；同位语从句：that the travails of commuters ... have received too much attention... 解释 sense 的内容；非限制性定语从句：many of whom will face among the biggest rises 插入修饰 commuters；过去分词短语作比较状语：compared to those...（其中 those 指代 commuters in the Midlands and the North，后接定语从句 who must endure...）。", "zh": "同样，人们也认为，与不得不忍受中部和北部地区相对落后基础设施的通勤者相比，东南部通勤者（其中许多人将面临最大幅度的涨价）的艰辛受到了过多的关注。"}, {"en": "Yes, more investment is needed, but passengers will not be willing to pay more indefinitely if they must also endure cramped, unreliable services, punctuated by regular chaos when timetables are changed, or planned maintenance is managed incompetently.", "point": "转折并列句 + 条件状语从句嵌套时间状语从句 + 过去分词短语作后置定语", "structure": "转折并列句主干：more investment is needed, but passengers will not be willing to pay more indefinitely；条件状语从句：if they must also endure cramped, unreliable services；过去分词短语作后置定语：punctuated by regular chaos 修饰 services；时间状语从句：when timetables are changed, or planned maintenance is managed incompetently 修饰 chaos。", "zh": "诚然，铁路需要更多投资，但如果乘客还必须忍受拥挤且不可靠的服务，甚至每逢时刻表调整或计划维护管理不善时就频繁陷入混乱，他们就不会愿意无休止地多付钱。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第21题态度转换：反问句“怎么可能为涨价找到正当理由”表明作者认为涨价“仍然是不合理的举措”。", "option": "remains an unreasonable measure.", "original": "How can the train operators possibly justify yet another increase"}, {"note": "第22题例证题替换：文中的股票经纪人是“乘坐铁路出行的人（those who use it）”的具体例证，与普通纳税人形成对比。", "option": "rail travelers.", "original": "the cost ... should be borne by those who use it ... subsidise the daily commute of a stockbroker"}, {"note": "第23题细节推断：作者强调乘客理应得到基本服务水平，反衬出铁路运营商“未能提供充足/合格的服务”。", "option": "have failed to provide an adequate service.", "original": "passengers should be able to expect a basic level of service"}, {"note": "第24题同义替换：“国有化（nationalisation）”即铁路所有权由私营转为国家所有，对应“所有权的变更”。", "option": "a change of ownership.", "original": "The threat of nationalisation ... will return with a vengeance"}, {"note": "第25题主旨概括：全文围绕车费连年上涨而服务低劣展开，最终指出乘客不会无限期买单，对应“不断上涨的票价不可持续”。", "option": "Ever-rising Fares Aren't Sustainable", "original": "passengers will not be willing to pay more indefinitely if they must also endure cramped, unreliable services"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L3", "exam": "kaoyan1", "id": "ky1-2021-t2", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["Last year marked the third year in a row of when Indonesia's bleak rate of deforestation has slowed pace. One reason for the turnaround may be the country's antipoverty program.", "In 2007, Indonesia started phasing in a program that gives money to its poorest residents under certain conditions, such as requiring people to keep kids in school or get regular medical care. Called conditional cash transfers or CCTs, these social assistance programs are designed to reduce inequality and break the cycle of poverty. They're already used in dozens of countries worldwide. In Indonesia, the program has provided enough food and medicine to substantially reduce severe growth problems among children.", "But CCT programs don't generally consider effects on the environment. In fact, poverty alleviation and environmental protection are often viewed as conflicting goals, says Paul Ferraro, an economist at Johns Hopkins University.", "That's because economic growth can be correlated with environmental degradation, while protecting the environment is sometimes correlated with greater poverty. However, those correlations don't prove cause and effect. The only previous study analyzing causality, based on an area in Mexico that had instituted CCTs, supported the traditional view. There, as people got more money, some of them may have more cleared land for cattle to raise for meat, Ferraro says.", "Such programs do not have to negatively affect the environment, though. Ferraro wanted to see if Indonesia's poverty-alleviation program was affecting deforestation. Indonesia has the third-largest area of tropical forest in the world and one of the highest deforestation rates.", "Ferraro analyzed satellite data showing annual forest loss from 2008 to 2012-including during Indonesia's phase-in of the antipoverty program-in 7,468 forested villages across 15 provinces. \"We see that the program is associated with a 30 percent reduction in deforestation,\" Ferraro says.", "That's likely because the rural poor are using the money as makeshift insurance policies against inclement weather, Ferraro says. Typically, if rains are delayed, people may clear land to plant more rice to supplement their harvests.", "Whether this research translates elsewhere is anybody's guess. Ferraro suggests the results may transfer to other parts of Asia, due to commonalities such as the importance of growing rice and market access. And regardless of transferability, the study shows that what's good for people may also be good for the environment. Even if this program didn't reduce poverty, Ferraro says, \"the value of the avoided deforestation just for carbon dioxide emissions alone is more than the program costs.\""], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Called conditional cash transfers or CCTs, these social assistance programs are designed to reduce inequality and break the cycle of poverty.", "explanation": "定位第一、二段，核心句在第二段第二句。该句明确指出 CCT 这类社会援助项目的设立目的（are designed to）是“减少不平等并打破贫困循环（reduce inequality and break the cycle of poverty）”。这与选项 B 中的“帮助贫困家庭改善经济状况（help poor families get better off）”构成同义替换。", "no": 26, "options": ["facilitate healthcare reform.", "help poor families get better off.", "improve local education systems.", "lower deforestation rates."], "stem": "According to the first two paragraphs, CCT programs aim to", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 和 C 属于条件与目的混淆，让孩子上学和定期体检只是领取现金的前提条件（under certain conditions），而非项目旨在推进教育或医疗改革。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The only previous study analyzing causality, based on an area in Mexico that had instituted CCTs, supported the traditional view.", "explanation": "定位第四段第三句，例证题需把握论据所支撑的观点。该研究“支持了传统观点（supported the traditional view）”，而这一传统观点在第三段指“减贫与环保相冲突”，并在第四段首句具体阐述为“经济增长往往与环境恶化相关（economic growth can be correlated with environmental degradation）”。D 项正是对该传统观点的同义改写。", "no": 27, "options": ["cattle raising has been a major means of livelihood for the poor.", "CCT programs have helped preserve traditional lifestyles.", "antipoverty efforts require the participation of local farmers.", "economic growth tends to cause environmental degradation."], "stem": "The study based on an area in Mexico is cited to show that", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 属于就事论事且过度夸大，误把例子中“有人毁林养牛”的具体细节当作论点，并擅自添加了“主要生计来源（major means of livelihood）”的绝对表述。", "type": "例证题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Ferraro wanted to see if Indonesia's poverty-alleviation program was affecting deforestation.", "explanation": "定位第五段第二句。该句直接点明 Ferraro 开展研究的目的（wanted to see 对应 intends to find out），即探究印尼的减贫项目（poverty-alleviation program，即 CCTs）是否对森林砍伐产生了影响（was affecting deforestation）。C 项“CCT 项目与其森林流失的关系”为精准同义替换。", "no": 28, "options": ["its acceptance level of CCTs.", "its annual rate of poverty alleviation.", "the relation of CCTs to its forest loss.", "the role of its forests in climate change."], "stem": "In his study about Indonesia, Ferraro intends to find out", "trapNote": "干扰项 D 属于偷换研究目的，碳排放价值只是末段评价项目附带生态价值时提及的维度，并非 Ferraro 开展印尼研究的初衷。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "Even if this program didn't reduce poverty, Ferraro says, \"the value of the avoided deforestation just for carbon dioxide emissions alone is more than the program costs.\"", "explanation": "定位第八段末两句。前句点明“对人类有益的事也可能有益于环境”，末句 Ferraro 进一步强调，即便该项目没有减少贫困，仅避免毁林（avoided deforestation）在减少二氧化碳排放方面的价值就已超过项目成本。由此可知，该项目的重大价值在于能够保护环境（protect the environment）。", "no": 29, "options": ["it will benefit other Asian countries.", "it will reduce regional inequality.", "it can protect the environment.", "it can benefit grain production."], "stem": "According to Ferraro, the CCT program in Indonesia is most valuable in that", "trapNote": "干扰项 A 属于或然变必然且主次倒置，原文表述为研究结果“或许（may）”适用于其他亚洲地区，且以“regardless of transferability”弱化了推广性的地位。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "And regardless of transferability, the study shows that what's good for people may also be good for the environment.", "explanation": "通读全文并定位第八段第三句的总结句。文章第一、二段介绍印尼 CCT 反贫困项目及其脱贫、助医的效果，第三至八段重点探讨该项目在减缓毁林方面的生态效应，并在末段点出“对人类有益的举措也可能造福环境”。因此，全文围绕“一个项目（CCT）的效果（The effects of a program）”展开。", "no": 30, "options": ["The effects of a program.", "The debates over a program.", "The process of a study.", "The transferability of a study."], "stem": "What is the text centered on?", "trapNote": "干扰项 C 和 D 均属以偏概全，分别只覆盖了第六段的数据分析过程与第八段开头的成果推广性讨论，无法概括全文核心。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "2021 考研英语一真题", "subtitle": "印尼条件现金转移项目研究（Q26–30）", "timeLimitMin": 18, "title": "Text 2", "year": "2021", "wordCount": 405, "examSet": "2021 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "translations": ["去年已是印度尼西亚惨淡的森林砍伐率连续第三年放缓增速。这一局面好转的原因之一，或许正是该国的扶贫计划。", "2007年，印度尼西亚开始逐步推行一项计划，在特定条件下向最贫困的居民发放补贴，例如要求居民让孩子坚持上学或定期接受医疗检查。这种被称为“有条件现金转移支付”（CCT）的社会救助项目，旨在减少不平等并打破贫困的恶性循环。这类项目已在全球数十个国家得到应用。在印度尼西亚，该项目提供了充足的食物和药品，显著减少了儿童中的严重发育障碍问题。", "但“有条件现金转移支付”项目通常并不考虑对环境的影响。约翰·霍普金斯大学的经济学家保罗·费拉罗表示，事实上，减贫与环境保护常被视为相互冲突的目标。", "这是因为经济增长可能与环境恶化相关，而保护环境有时又与更严重的贫困相伴。然而，这些相关性并不能证明因果关系。此前唯一一项分析因果关系的研究（以墨西哥一个实施了“有条件现金转移支付”的地区为研究对象）支持了传统观点。费拉罗说，在那里，随着人们手头资金增加，部分人可能会开垦更多土地来养牛以获取肉类。", "不过，这类项目未必会对环境造成负面影响。费拉罗想看看印度尼西亚的扶贫计划是否正在影响森林砍伐。印度尼西亚拥有世界第三大热带森林面积，同时也是森林砍伐率最高的国家之一。", "费拉罗分析了2008年至2012年（包括印度尼西亚逐步推行扶贫计划期间）覆盖15个省份7,468个森林村庄的年度森林损失卫星数据。费拉罗表示：“我们发现，该计划与森林砍伐率下降30%存在关联。”", "费拉罗认为，这很可能是因为农村贫困人口把这笔补贴当作抵御恶劣天气的临时保险。通常情况下，一旦雨水推迟，人们就会开垦土地种植更多水稻，以弥补收成不足。", "这项研究结果能否推广到其他地区，谁也说不准。费拉罗指出，由于存在水稻种植的重要性以及市场准入条件等共性，这一结果或许可以推广至亚洲其他地区。无论能否推广，这项研究都表明，造福人类之举同样可能有益于环境。费拉罗表示，即使这项计划没有减少贫困，“仅就二氧化碳排放而言，避免毁林所带来的价值就已经超过了该计划本身的成本。”"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "逐渐停止，缓和；减慢（速度）", "note": "高频动词短语：slow pace 表示“放慢脚步/放缓速度”；此外 phase in（逐步推行）也是本文高频短语。", "word": "slow"}, {"gloss": "缓解，减轻（痛苦、贫困等）", "note": "考研高频词，常与 poverty 搭配构成 poverty alleviation（扶贫）。名词形式 alleviation，形容词 alleviative。", "word": "alleviate"}, {"gloss": "建立，制定，实行（制度、政策等）", "note": "熟词僻义：作名词意为“研究所/学院”，作动词在社会科学语境中常考“建立、实行（政策或项目）”。", "word": "institute"}, {"gloss": "权宜之计的，临时的；代用品", "note": "高频词/熟词僻义：作形容词意为“临时的、权宜的”（makeshift insurance policies 临时保险单），作名词意为“权宜之计”。", "word": "makeshift"}, {"gloss": "（气候）恶劣的，严酷的", "note": "书面高频词：常搭配 inclement weather（恶劣天气），注意与 clement（温和的）对比记忆。", "word": "inclement"}, {"gloss": "（结果、方法等）可推广，适用，转化", "note": "熟词僻义：除“翻译”外，在科研实验类文章中高频考查“（研究结果）适用于他处、转化应用”。", "word": "translate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In 2007, Indonesia started phasing in a program that gives money to its poorest residents under certain conditions, such as requiring people to keep kids in school or get regular medical care.", "point": "that 引导定语从句 + 动词短语 phase in（逐步推行）+ 介词短语作条件状语", "structure": "主干：Indonesia started phasing in a program；定语从句：that gives money to its poorest residents under certain conditions（修饰 program）；举例状语：such as requiring people to keep kids in school or get regular medical care（具体说明 certain conditions）。", "zh": "2007年，印度尼西亚开始逐步推行一项计划，在特定条件下向最贫困的居民发放补贴，例如要求居民让孩子坚持上学或定期接受医疗检查。"}, {"en": "The only previous study analyzing causality, based on an area in Mexico that had instituted CCTs, supported the traditional view.", "point": "现在分词短语作后置定语 + 过去分词短语作插入状语/定语 + that 引导定语从句", "structure": "主干：The only previous study supported the traditional view；后置定语：analyzing causality（修饰 study）；插入修饰成分：based on an area in Mexico（修饰 study，说明研究基础）；嵌套定语从句：that had instituted CCTs（修饰 an area in Mexico）。", "zh": "此前唯一一项分析因果关系的研究（以墨西哥一个实施了“有条件现金转移支付”的地区为研究对象）支持了传统观点。"}, {"en": "Even if this program didn't reduce poverty, Ferraro says, \"the value of the avoided deforestation just for carbon dioxide emissions alone is more than the program costs.\"", "point": "even if 引导让步状语从句 + 过去分词前置定语（avoided deforestation）+ 主谓宾基本结构与比较表达", "structure": "让步状语从句：Even if this program didn't reduce poverty；主句插入语：Ferraro says；引语主干：the value (of the avoided deforestation) is more than the program costs；状语修饰：just for carbon dioxide emissions alone（仅就二氧化碳排放而言）。", "zh": "费拉罗表示，即使这项计划没有减少贫困，“仅就二氧化碳排放而言，避免毁林所带来的价值就已经超过了该计划本身的成本。”"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第26题同义改写：原文“减少不平等并打破贫困恶性循环”对应选项“帮助贫困家庭改善生活条件”。", "option": "help poor families get better off", "original": "reduce inequality and break the cycle of poverty"}, {"note": "第27题同义改写：墨西哥地区案例支持“传统观点”，即前文提到的“经济增长往往导致环境恶化”。", "option": "economic growth tends to cause environmental degradation", "original": "supported the traditional view (economic growth can be correlated with environmental degradation)"}, {"note": "第28题同义改写：affecting deforestation 对应“与森林减少之间的关系”。", "option": "the relation of CCTs to its forest loss", "original": "if Indonesia's poverty-alleviation program was affecting deforestation"}, {"note": "第29题同义改写：避免毁林、减少碳排放的价值超过项目成本，说明项目能有效保护环境。", "option": "it can protect the environment", "original": "the value of the avoided deforestation just for carbon dioxide emissions alone is more than the program costs"}, {"note": "第30题主旨概括：全文围绕印度尼西亚扶贫计划（CCT）对减贫和森林保护的双重影响展开。", "option": "The effects of a program", "original": "what's good for people may also be good for the environment"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L3", "exam": "kaoyan1", "id": "ky1-2021-t3", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["As a historian who's always searching for the text or the image that makes us re-evaluate the past, I've become preoccupied with looking for photographs that show our Victorian ancestors smiling (what better way to shatter the image of 19th-century prudery?). I've found quite a few, and—since I started posting them on Twitter—they have been causing quite a stir. People have been surprised to see evidence that Victorians had fun and could, and did, laugh. They are noting that the Victorians suddenly seem to become more human as the hundred-or-so years that separate us fade away through our common experience of laughter.", "Of course, I need to concede that my collection of 'Smiling Victorians' makes up only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue of photographic portraiture created between 1840 and 1900, the majority of which show sitters posing miserably and stiffly in front of painted backdrops, or staring absently into the middle distance. How do we explain this trend?", "During the 1840s and 1850s, in the early days of photography, exposure times were notoriously long: the daguerreotype photographic method (producing an image on a silvered copper plate) could take several minutes to complete, resulting in blurred images as sitters shifted position or adjusted their limbs. The thought of holding a fixed grin as the camera performed its magical duties was too much to contemplate, and so a non-committal blank stare became the norm.", "But exposure times were much quicker by the 1880s, and the introduction of the Box Brownie and other portable cameras meant that, though slow by today's digital standards, the exposure was almost instantaneous. Spontaneous smiles were relatively easy to capture by the 1890s, so we must look elsewhere for an explanation of why Victorians still hesitated to smile.", "One explanation might be the loss of dignity displayed through a cheesy grin. \"Nature gave us lips to conceal our teeth,\" ran one popular Victorian maxim, alluding to the fact that before the birth of proper dentistry, mouths were often in a shocking state of hygiene. A flashing set of healthy and clean, regular 'pearly whites' was a rare sight in Victorian society, the preserve of the super-rich (and even then, dental hygiene was not guaranteed).", "A toothy grin (especially when there were gaps or blackened gnashers) lacked class: drunks, tramps, and music hall performers might gum and grin with a smile as wide as Lewis Carroll's gum-exposing Cheshire Cat, but it was not a becoming look for properly bred persons. Even Mark Twain, a man who enjoyed a hearty laugh, said that when it came to photographic portraits there could be \"nothing more damning than a silly, foolish smile fixed forever\"."], "questions": [{"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "since I started posting them on Twitter—they have been causing quite a stir. People have been surprised to see evidence that Victorians had fun and could, and did, laugh.", "explanation": "题干定位第1段。作者在Twitter发布维多利亚时代人物微笑的照片后引起轰动，人们惊讶地发现维多利亚时代的人也能开怀大笑，并觉得他们“突然显得更有人情味了”，打破了过去对19世纪拘谨刻板的认知，与A项“changed people's impression of the Victorians”构成同义替换。", "no": 31, "options": ["changed people's impression of the Victorians.", "highlighted social media's role in Victorian studies.", "re-evaluated the Victorian's notion of public image.", "illustrated the development of Victorian photography."], "stem": "According to Paragraph 1, the author's posts on Twitter", "trapNote": "C项属于偷换概念与原词复现陷阱，第1段开头说的是历史图像“让我们重新评估过去”，而非重新评估维多利亚时代人的公众形象观念。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "my collection of 'Smiling Victorians' makes up only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue of photographic portraiture created between 1840 and 1900", "explanation": "题干定位第2段。作者坦言自己收集的“微笑的维多利亚人”照片只占1840年至1900年间庞大人像摄影目录中极小的比例（only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue），与B项“rare among photographs of that age”精准对应。", "no": 32, "options": ["They are in popular use among historians.", "They are rare among photographs of that age.", "They mirror 19th-century social conventions.", "They show effects of different exposure times."], "stem": "What does the author say about the Victorian portraits he has collected?", "trapNote": "C项属于张冠李戴，反映当时社会礼仪规训的是占绝大多数的严肃僵硬肖像，而非作者收集的少数微笑照片。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "ran one popular Victorian maxim, alluding to the fact that before the birth of proper dentistry, mouths were often in a shocking state of hygiene.", "explanation": "题干定位第4段和第5段。第4段指出到19世纪90年代曝光速度已很快，必须另寻不爱微笑的原因；第5段随即解释道，在现代牙科诞生前人们口腔卫生状况极差（a shocking state of hygiene），咧嘴露齿有失体面，对应D项“unhealthy dental condition”。", "no": 33, "options": ["Their inherent social sensitiveness.", "Their tension before the camera.", "Their distrust of new inventions.", "Their unhealthy dental condition."], "stem": "What might have kept the Victorians from smiling for pictures in the 1890s?", "trapNote": "B项属于时间错位与偷换原因，面对相机长久保持僵硬表情的困扰发生在19世纪四五十年代长曝光时期，并非90年代的原因。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Even Mark Twain, a man who enjoyed a hearty laugh, said that when it came to photographic portraits there could be \"nothing more damning than a silly, foolish smile fixed forever\"", "explanation": "题干定位第6段末尾。前文刚提到露齿笑在当时被视为缺乏教养，随后用“Even Mark Twain”引出连平日爱开怀大笑的马克·吐温也痛斥肖像照上固定着傻笑，以此强有力地证明拍照时不赞成露齿微笑在当时是一种根深蒂固的观念（a deep-root belief）。", "no": 34, "options": ["a deep-root belief.", "a misguided attitude.", "a controversial view.", "a thought-provoking idea."], "stem": "Mark Twain is quoted to show that the disapproval of smiles in pictures was", "trapNote": "B项与C项均属态度误判与无中生有，作者客观剖析维多利亚时代拒绝露齿笑的社会成因，并未批驳马克·吐温的观点“被误导”或称其“存在争议”。", "type": "例证题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "the majority of which show sitters posing miserably and stiffly in front of painted backdrops, or staring absently into the middle distance. How do we explain this trend?", "explanation": "第2段结尾明确提出核心设问“How do we explain this trend?”（指绝大多数人像显得痛苦僵硬、眼神木然），第3至6段围绕该问题分别从长曝光技术局限和口腔卫生与礼仪观念展开解答。因此全文主要回答了“为何大多数维多利亚时代人在照片中表情严肃”，即A项。", "no": 35, "options": ["Why did most Victorians look stern in photographs?", "Why did the Victorians start to view photographs?", "What made photography develop in the Victorian period?", "How did smiling in photographs become a post-Victorian norm?"], "stem": "Which of the following questions does the text answer?", "trapNote": "C项属于以偏概全，第3、4段提及银版照相法与便携相机的发展只是为了说明曝光时间变化对拍照表情的影响，并非探讨摄影发展的动因。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "2021 考研英语一真题", "subtitle": "Text 3 · 维多利亚时代肖像照中的微笑之谜", "timeLimitMin": 18, "title": "Why Victorians Rarely Smiled in Photographs", "year": "2021", "wordCount": 451, "examSet": "2021 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "translations": ["作为一名总在搜寻能让我们重新审视过去的文字或图像的历史学家，我一直热衷于寻找能够展现维多利亚时代先辈微笑的照片（还有什么比这更能打破19世纪人们古板拘谨的形象呢？）。我已经找到了不少这样的照片，而且自从我开始在推特上发布这些照片以来，它们引起了不小的轰动。人们惊讶地看到证据表明，维多利亚时代的人也懂得享乐，能够而且确实会开怀大笑。人们还注意到，随着我们共同的欢笑体验抹平了相隔百余年的岁月距离，维多利亚时代的人突然间显得更加富有“人情味”了。", "当然，我必须承认，我收集的“微笑的维多利亚人”在1840年至1900年间创作的庞大肖像摄影集里仅占极小一部分，其中绝大多数照片上的被摄者要么在手绘背景幕布前愁苦僵硬地摆拍，要么眼神空洞地望向中远景。我们该如何解释这一趋势呢？", "在19世纪40至50年代的摄影早期，曝光时间长得令人发指：达盖尔银版摄影法（在镀银铜板上成像）可能需要几分钟才能完成，一旦被摄者挪动位置或调整四肢姿势，就会导致画面模糊。在相机履行其神奇职责的过程中一直保持固定微笑，这种想法实在让人难以想象，于是毫无表情、不置可否的凝视便成了常态。", "但到了19世纪80年代，曝光时间大幅缩短，“布朗尼盒式相机”及其他便携相机的问世意味着，尽管按今天的数码标准来看仍然偏慢，但曝光几乎已经是瞬时完成的。到19世纪90年代，抓拍自然流露的微笑已相对容易，因此我们必须从其他方面寻找维多利亚时代的人依然不愿微笑的原因。", "一种解释可能是，刻意露齿的笑容会有损体面。“大自然赐予我们嘴唇，正是为了遮住牙齿，”维多利亚时代的一句流行格言这样写道——这暗指在正规牙科诞生之前，人们的口腔卫生状况往往令人触目惊心。一口闪亮、健康、洁净整齐的“珍珠白牙”在维多利亚社会实属罕见，几乎是超级富豪的专属（即便如此，口腔卫生也未必能得到保障）。", "露齿而笑（尤其是牙齿有缺口或发黑时）显得有失身份：醉汉、流浪汉和音乐厅艺人或许会像刘易斯·卡罗尔笔下露出牙龈的柴郡猫那样咧开大嘴露龈傻笑，但对有教养的体面人而言，这绝非得体的仪表。就连平时喜欢放声大笑的马克·吐温也曾说过，在肖像照中，“没有什么比永远定格在画面上的愚蠢傻笑更毁形象的了”。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "使全神贯注；使着迷，迷住", "note": "高频搭配：become/be preoccupied with... 表示“全神贯注于/执着于某事”，在人物经历或学术兴趣类语境中常见。", "word": "preoccupy"}, {"gloss": "（勉强）承认，让步", "note": "议论文核心态度词：concede that... 意为“（虽不情愿但）承认……”，常用来引出让步后的转折反驳。", "word": "concede"}, {"gloss": "（在相机前）摆好姿势拍照的人；模特", "note": "熟词僻义：由 sit 派生，在摄影或绘画语境中特指“坐在那里让人拍照/画像的人”。", "word": "sitter"}, {"gloss": "不表态的，模糊的；毫无表情的", "note": "高频派生词：non-committal blank stare 指“不置可否/面无表情的凝视”，常考态度辨析与细节理解。", "word": "non-committal"}, {"gloss": "隐约提及，暗指，影射", "note": "高频动词短语：allude to sth. 意为“暗指、影射或顺带提及某事”，同义替换常考 imply 或 refer to indirectly。", "word": "allude"}, {"gloss": "（言行举止）毁灭性的，招致批评的，极不利的", "note": "熟词僻义：日常意为“该死的”，在正式或评论语境中（如马克·吐温引语）表示“令人难堪的、招致诟病的、毁形象的”。", "word": "damning"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "As a historian who's always searching for the text or the image that makes us re-evaluate the past, I've become preoccupied with looking for photographs that show our Victorian ancestors smiling (what better way to shatter the image of 19th-century prudery?).", "point": "多层定语从句嵌套 + 插入反问句 + 动名词作宾语补足语（show sb. doing）", "structure": "方式/身份状语：As a historian（后接定语从句 who's always searching for... 及嵌套定语从句 that makes us re-evaluate the past）；主句主干：I've become preoccupied with looking for photographs；定语从句：that show our Victorian ancestors smiling（修饰 photographs）；括号补充反问：what better way to shatter the image of 19th-century prudery?", "zh": "作为一名总在搜寻能让我们重新审视过去的文字或图像的历史学家，我一直热衷于寻找能够展现维多利亚时代先辈微笑的照片（还有什么比这更能打破19世纪人们古板拘谨的形象呢？）。"}, {"en": "Of course, I need to concede that my collection of 'Smiling Victorians' makes up only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue of photographic portraiture created between 1840 and 1900, the majority of which show sitters posing miserably and stiffly in front of painted backdrops, or staring absently into the middle distance.", "point": "that 引导宾语从句 + 过去分词作后置定语 + “介词+关系代词（the majority of which）”引导非限制性定语从句", "structure": "主干：I need to concede that...；宾语从句主干：my collection makes up only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue...；后置定语：created between 1840 and 1900（修饰 photographic portraiture）；非限制性定语从句：the majority of which show sitters posing... or staring...（which 指代 photographic portraiture/catalogue）。", "zh": "当然，我必须承认，我收集的“微笑的维多利亚人”在1840年至1900年间创作的庞大肖像摄影集里仅占极小一部分，其中绝大多数照片上的被摄者要么在手绘背景幕布前愁苦僵硬地摆拍，要么眼神空洞地望向中远景。"}, {"en": "\"Nature gave us lips to conceal our teeth,\" ran one popular Victorian maxim, alluding to the fact that before the birth of proper dentistry, mouths were often in a shocking state of hygiene.", "point": "直接引语倒装结构（ran one popular Victorian maxim）+ 现在分词作伴随状语 + that 引导同位语从句", "structure": "主干（倒装）：\"...\" ran one popular Victorian maxim（= one popular Victorian maxim ran \"...\"）；伴随状语：alluding to the fact；同位语从句：that before the birth of proper dentistry, mouths were often in a shocking state of hygiene（解释说明 the fact）。", "zh": "“大自然赐予我们嘴唇，正是为了遮住牙齿，”维多利亚时代的一句流行格言这样写道——这暗指在正规牙科诞生之前，人们的口腔卫生状况往往令人触目惊心。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第31题同义改写：推文引发轰动、人们惊讶地发现维多利亚人也会笑且更有烟火气，即“改变了人们对维多利亚人的印象”。", "option": "changed people's impression of the Victorians", "original": "they have been causing quite a stir. People have been surprised to see evidence that Victorians had fun and could, and did, laugh"}, {"note": "第32题同义改写：只占庞大肖像摄影集里“极小一部分”，对应在同时代照片中“十分罕见”。", "option": "They are rare among photographs of that age", "original": "makes up only a tiny percentage of the vast catalogue of photographic portraiture created between 1840 and 1900"}, {"note": "第33题同义改写：19世纪90年代快门已足够快，此时不笑源于口腔卫生差、牙齿不健康。", "option": "Their unhealthy dental condition", "original": "before the birth of proper dentistry, mouths were often in a shocking state of hygiene"}, {"note": "第34题同义改写：连平时爱开怀大笑的马克·吐温都认为照片里露齿傻笑很毁形象，说明这种偏见是“根深蒂固的观念”。", "option": "a deep-root belief", "original": "Even Mark Twain, a man who enjoyed a hearty laugh, said that when it came to photographic portraits there could be \"nothing more damning than a silly, foolish smile fixed forever\""}, {"note": "第35题主旨概括：全文围绕“为什么维多利亚时代的照片里人们很少微笑/显得严肃”及其原因（早期曝光时间长、后期顾忌牙齿与体面）展开。", "option": "Why did most Victorians look stern in photographs?", "original": "show sitters posing miserably and stiffly... How do we explain this trend?"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L3", "exam": "kaoyan1", "id": "ky1-2021-t4", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["From the early days of broadband, advocates for consumers and web-based companies worried that the cable and phone companies selling broadband connections had the power and incentive to favor affiliated websites over their rivals'. That's why there has been such a strong demand for rules that would prevent broadband providers from picking winners and losers online, preserving the freedom and innovation that have been the lifeblood of the Internet.", "Yet that demand has been almost impossible to fill—in part because of pushback from broadband providers, anti-regulatory conservatives and the courts. A federal appeals court weighed in again Tuesday, but instead of providing a badly needed resolution, it only prolonged the fight. At issue before the U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit was the latest take of the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) on net neutrality, adopted on a party-line vote in 2017. The Republican-penned order not only eliminated the strict net neutrality rules the FCC had adopted when it had a Democratic majority in 2015, but rejected the commission's authority to require broadband providers to do much of anything. The order also declared that state and local governments couldn't regulate broadband providers either.", "The commission argued that other agencies would protect against anti-competitive behavior, such as a broadband-providing conglomerate like AT&T favoring its own video-streaming service at the expense of Netflix and Apple TV. Yet the FCC also ended the investigations of broadband providers that imposed data caps on their rivals' streaming services but not their own.", "On Tuesday, the appeals court unanimously upheld the 2017 order deregulating broadband providers, citing a Supreme Court ruling from 2005 that upheld a similarly deregulatory move. But Judge Patricia Millett rightly argued in a concurring opinion that \"the result is unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service,\" and said Congress or the Supreme Court could intervene to \"avoid trapping Internet regulation in technological anachronism.\"", "In the meantime, the court threw out the FCC's attempt to block all state rules on net neutrality, while preserving the commission's power to preempt individual state laws that undermine its order. That means more battles like the one now going on between the Justice Department and California, which enacted a tough net neutrality law in the wake of the FCC's abdication.", "The endless legal battles and back-and-forth at the FCC cry out for Congress to act. It needs to give the commission explicit authority once and for all to bar broadband providers from meddling in the traffic on their network and to create clear rules protecting openness and innovation online."], "questions": [{"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "worried that the cable and phone companies selling broadband connections had the power and incentive to favor affiliated websites over their rivals'.", "explanation": "题干定位第1段。消费者与网络企业倡导者长期担忧宽带服务商有能力且有动机“偏袒旗下关联网站而打压竞争对手”（favor affiliated websites over their rivals'），防止其在线上“挑选赢家与输家”，与C项“show partiality in treating clients（在对待客户时偏心袒护）”形成同义替换。", "no": 36, "options": ["bring web-based firms under control.", "slow down the traffic on their network.", "show partiality in treating clients.", "intensify competition with their rivals."], "stem": "There has long been concern that broadband providers would", "trapNote": "A项属于过度推理，偏袒关联网站并不等同于将所有网络企业置于自身控制之下；B项“减慢网络流量”也属扩大化偷换概念。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "not only eliminated the strict net neutrality rules the FCC had adopted when it had a Democratic majority in 2015, but rejected the commission's authority", "explanation": "题干定位第2段。面对制定网络中立规则的强烈呼声，FCC在2017年通过的命令不仅废除了2015年的严格网络中立规则，还否定了自身的监管权力并禁止州和地方政府进行监管，明确体现了其反监管立场（anti-regulatory stance），对应B项。", "no": 37, "options": ["sticks to an out-of-date order.", "takes an anti-regulatory stance.", "has issued a special resolution.", "has allowed the states to intervene."], "stem": "Faced with the demand for net neutrality rules, the FCC", "trapNote": "D项属于正反颠倒，2017年FCC的命令明确禁止州和地方政府监管宽带商，第5段也表明是上诉法院推翻了FCC阻挠各州立法的企图，并非FCC允许各州介入。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "anti-competitive behavior, such as a broadband-providing conglomerate like AT&T favoring its own video-streaming service at the expense of Netflix and Apple TV.", "explanation": "题干定位第3段。FCC声称其他机构能防范反竞争行为，并紧接着以AT&T为例说明这种行为——即宽带巨头以牺牲Netflix和Apple TV的利益为代价偏袒自家视频流媒体服务，由此可推知AT&T存在反竞争做法（engages in anti-competitive practices），对应B项。", "no": 38, "options": ["It protects against unfair competition.", "It engages in anti-competitive practices.", "It is under the FCC's investigation.", "It is in pursuit of quality service."], "stem": "What can be learned about AT&T from Paragraph 3?", "trapNote": "C项属于正反颠倒，第3段末句明确指出FCC已经“终止了（ended）”对相关宽带商的调查，而非“正在接受调查”；A项则偷换了“other agencies”的主语。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "But Judge Patricia Millett rightly argued in a concurring opinion that \"the result is unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service,\"", "explanation": "题干定位第4段。帕特里夏·米莱特法官在协同意见中明确指出，上诉法院的判决结果“与现代宽带服务的现实脱节”（unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service），其中“unhinged from the realities”与D项“is out of touch with reality”构成精准同义替换。", "no": 39, "options": ["focus on trivialities.", "conveys an ambiguous message.", "is at odds with its earlier rulings.", "is out of touch with reality."], "stem": "Judge Patricia Millett argues that the appeals court's decision", "trapNote": "C项属于正反颠倒，上诉法院正是援引了2005年最高法院同样支持放松监管的裁决才维持了2017年命令，并非与早期判决相矛盾。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "cry out for Congress to act. It needs to give the commission explicit authority once and for all to bar broadband providers from meddling in the traffic on their network", "explanation": "题干定位最后一段（第6段）。作者指出FCC的无休止法律争端与摇摆不定“迫切呼吁国会采取行动”（cry out for Congress to act），要求国会明确授权委员会彻底禁止宽带商干预网络流量并制定清晰规则以保障网络开放与创新，与A项完全吻合。", "no": 40, "options": ["Congress needs to take action to ensure net neutrality.", "The FCC should be put under strict supervision.", "Rules need to be set to diversify online services.", "Broadband providers' rights should be protected."], "stem": "What does the author argue in the last paragraph?", "trapNote": "B项属于偷换概念与曲解文意，第6段主张国会应给予FCC“明确授权（explicit authority）”去监管宽带商，而非将FCC置于严格监督之下；D项则与作者反对宽带商干预流量的立场正反颠倒。", "type": "细节题"}], "sourceLabel": "2021 考研英语一真题", "subtitle": "Text 4 · 美国宽带监管与网络中立性之争", "timeLimitMin": 18, "title": "The Battle Over Net Neutrality Regulation", "year": "2021", "wordCount": 434, "examSet": "2021 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "translations": ["从宽带兴起之初，消费者和网络公司的倡导者就担忧，销售宽带连接服务的有线电视和电话公司既有能力也有动机偏袒其关联网站，而非竞争对手的网站。正因如此，人们强烈呼吁制定规则，防止宽带服务商在网络上人为决定赢家和输家，从而维护作为互联网生命线的自由与创新。", "然而，这一诉求几乎难以实现——部分原因在于宽带服务商、反监管保守派以及法院的阻挠。本周二，一家联邦上诉法院再次介入此事，但非但没有提供亟需的解决方案，反而延长了这场争端。此次提交给美国哥伦比亚特区巡回上诉法院审理的争议焦点，是联邦通信委员会（FCC）于2017年按党派划线投票通过的最新网络中立性立场。这份由共和党人起草的政令不仅废除了FCC在2015年由民主党占多数时通过的严格网络中立规则，还否定了该委员会要求宽带服务商采取几乎任何举措的权力。该政令还宣布，州政府和地方政府同样无权对宽带服务商进行监管。", "该委员会辩称，其他机构将防范反竞争行为，例如像AT&T这样提供宽带服务的大型企业集团以牺牲网飞（Netflix）和苹果电视（Apple TV）的利益为代价来偏袒自家的视频流媒体服务。然而，FCC同时也终止了对那些仅对竞争对手的流媒体服务设置流量上限、却不对自家服务设限的宽带服务商的调查。", "周二，该上诉法院援引2005年最高法院支持类似放松管制举措的一项裁决，一致维持了2017年取消对宽带服务商管制的政令。但帕特里夏·米利特法官在一份协同意见书中中肯地指出，“这一结果脱离了现代宽带服务的现实”，并表示国会或最高法院可以介入，“避免将互联网监管困在技术过时的窘境之中”。", "与此同时，法院驳回了FCC试图封杀所有州级网络中立法规的企图，但保留了该委员会优先废止削弱其政令的个别州法律的权力。这意味着未来将出现更多类似于目前美国司法部与加利福尼亚州之间的争斗——加州在FCC放弃监管职责后颁布了一项严厉的网络中立法律。", "无休止的法律诉讼以及FCC的政策反复亟需国会采取行动。国会需要一劳永逸地赋予该委员会明确权力，禁止宽带服务商干涉其网络流量，并制定明确规则以保护网络的开放性与创新性。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "看法，观点，立场", "note": "熟词僻义：常用作动词表“拿、带”，在考研阅读中作名词常表示“对某事的看法、解读”（the latest take on...）。", "word": "take"}, {"gloss": "满足（需求、要求）", "note": "熟词僻义：常规义为“填满”，高频搭配 fill a demand/need 表示“满足需求”，等效于 meet/satisfy。", "word": "fill"}, {"gloss": "撰写，起草", "note": "词性活用：名词意为“钢笔”，作动词表示“撰写、写下”，如文中 Republican-penned order（共和党人起草的政令）。", "word": "pen"}, {"gloss": "优先取代，使失效；先发制人", "note": "高频学术/法律词：在政治与法律语境中常指上级法规“优先取代并废止”下级法规。", "word": "preempt"}, {"gloss": "放弃（职责或权力），退位", "note": "高频派生词：由 abdicate（退位，放弃权力）派生，文中指机构放弃自身监管职责（FCC's abdication）。", "word": "abdication"}, {"gloss": "过时的事物，时代错误", "note": "进阶词汇：由 ana-（向后）+ chron-（时间）构成，指“不合时代潮流的现象或做法”。", "word": "anachronism"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "From the early days of broadband, advocates for consumers and web-based companies worried that the cable and phone companies selling broadband connections had the power and incentive to favor affiliated websites over their rivals'.", "point": "现在分词短语作后置定语 + 宾语从句 + 不定式作抽象名词后置定语 + 所有格省略", "structure": "时间状语(From...) + 主语(advocates for...) + 谓语(worried) + 宾语从句(that the cable and phone companies [selling broadband connections 现在分词作后置定语] had the power and incentive [to favor affiliated websites over their rivals' 不定式作后置定语])。rivals' 后省略了 websites。", "zh": "从宽带兴起之初，消费者和网络公司的倡导者就担忧，销售宽带连接服务的有线电视和电话公司既有能力也有动机偏袒其关联网站，而非竞争对手的网站。"}, {"en": "At issue before the U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit was the latest take of the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) on net neutrality, adopted on a party-line vote in 2017.", "point": "介词短语置于句首引起的全部倒装 + 熟词僻义(take) + 过去分词短语作定语", "structure": "全部倒装句：表语介词短语(At issue before...) + 系动词(was) + 主语(the latest take of... on net neutrality) + 过去分词短语作后置修饰(adopted on a party-line vote in 2017)。正常语序为 The latest take... was at issue before...。", "zh": "此次提交给美国哥伦比亚特区巡回上诉法院审理的争议焦点，是联邦通信委员会（FCC）于2017年按党派划线投票通过的最新网络中立性立场。"}, {"en": "In the meantime, the court threw out the FCC's attempt to block all state rules on net neutrality, while preserving the commission's power to preempt individual state laws that undermine its order.", "point": "while + 现在分词作状语 + 不定式作定语 + that引导的定语从句", "structure": "主句(the court threw out the FCC's attempt [to block... 不定式作定语]) + 让步/并列状语(while preserving the commission's power [to preempt individual state laws {that undermine its order 定语从句}])。", "zh": "与此同时，法院驳回了FCC试图封杀所有州级网络中立法规的企图，但保留了该委员会优先废止削弱其政令的个别州法律的权力。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "Q36同义替换：favor A over B（偏袒A胜过B）替换为 show partiality（表现出偏袒）。", "option": "show partiality in treating clients", "original": "favor affiliated websites over their rivals'"}, {"note": "Q37概括替换：废除严格规则并否定自身监管权限，体现反监管（anti-regulatory）立场。", "option": "takes an anti-regulatory stance", "original": "not only eliminated the strict net neutrality rules... but rejected the commission's authority"}, {"note": "Q38微调替换：behavior 替换为 practices，点明AT&T存在反竞争行为。", "option": "engages in anti-competitive practices", "original": "anti-competitive behavior, such as a broadband-providing conglomerate like AT&T favoring its own video-streaming service"}, {"note": "Q39同义替换：be unhinged from the realities 替换为 be out of touch with reality（脱离现实）。", "option": "is out of touch with reality", "original": "is unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service"}, {"note": "Q40同义替换：cry out for sb. to act（迫切需要某人行动）替换为 need to take action。", "option": "Congress needs to take action to ensure net neutrality", "original": "cry out for Congress to act"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2020-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2020", "examSet": "2020 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2020 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "英国“文化名镇”奖的设想与反思", "subtitle": "社会文化 · 城市文化品牌建设与地方发展", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 425, "paragraphs": ["A group of labour MPs, among them Yvette Cooper, are bringing in the new year with a call to institute a UK \"town of culture\" award. The proposal is that it should sit alongside the existing city of culture title, which was held by Hull in 2017 and has been awarded to Coventry for 2021. Cooper and her colleagues argue that the success of the crown for Hull, where it brought in £220m of investment and an avalanche of arts, ought not to be confined to cities. Britain's towns, it is true, are not prevented from applying, but they generally lack the resources to put together a bid to beat their bigger competitors. A town of culture award could, it is argued, become an annual event, attracting funding and creating jobs.", "Some might see the proposal as a booby prize for the fact that Britain is no longer able to apply for the much more prestigious title of European capital of culture, a sought-after award bagged by Glasgow in 1990 and Liverpool in 2008. A cynic might speculate that the UK is on the verge of disappearing into an endless fever of self-celebration in its desperation to reinvent itself for the post-Brexit world: after town of culture, who knows what will follow—village of culture? Suburb of culture? Hamlet of culture?", "It is also wise to recall that such titles are not a cure-all. A badly run \"year of culture\" washes in and out of a place like the tide, bringing prominence for a spell but leaving no lasting benefits to the community. The really successful holders of such titles are those that do a great deal more than fill hotel bedrooms and bring in high-profile arts events and good press for a year. They transform the aspirations of the people who live there; they nudge the self-image of the city into a bolder and more optimistic light. It is hard to get right, and requires a remarkable degree of vision, as well as cooperation between city authorities, the private sector, community groups and cultural organisations. But it can be done: Glasgow's year as European capital of culture can certainly be seen as one of a complex series of factors that have turned the city into the power of art, music and theatre that it remains today.", "A \"town of culture\" could be not just about the arts but about honouring a town's peculiarities-helping sustain its high street, supporting local facilities and above all celebrating its people and turn it into action."], "translations": ["以伊薇特·库珀为首的一批工党议员在新的一年伊始发出呼吁，倡议设立英国“文化名镇”奖。该提案建议将其与现有的“文化之城”头衔并行——赫尔市曾于2017年获此头衔，考文垂则已获选为2021年文化之城。库珀及其同事认为，赫尔市摘得该桂冠所取得的成功——带来了2.2亿英镑投资和丰富的艺术活动——不应仅局限于大城市。诚然，英国的小镇并未被禁止参与申办，但它们通常缺乏资源来组织一场足以击败更大竞争对手的申办活动。有人主张，“文化名镇”奖可以成为一项年度盛事，既能吸引资金，又能创造就业岗位。", "有些人可能会将这一提案视作一种安慰奖，因为英国再也无法申请声望高得多的“欧洲文化之都”头衔——这一备受追捧的奖项曾于1990年被格拉斯哥、2008年被利物浦收入囊中。持犬儒态度的人甚至会揣测，英国在脱欧后急于重塑自我，正濒临陷入一场无休止的自我吹捧狂热之中：继“文化名镇”之后，谁知道接下来还会冒出什么——“文化名村”？“文化郊区”？还是“文化小村落”？", "我们同样应当清醒地记得，这类头衔并非包治百病的灵丹妙药。一场运作拙劣的“文化年”只会像潮水般在当地涌来又退去，虽能带来一时的显赫声名，却无法给社区留下持久的收益。真正成功的头衔持有者，绝不仅仅满足于在一年内填满酒店客房、举办几场高规格艺术活动和收获媒体好评。它们会重塑当地居民的抱负；它们将城市的自我形象推向更自信、更乐观的境界。这很难做到，需要非凡的远见卓识，以及市政当局、私营部门、社区团体和文化机构之间的通力协作。但这并非无法实现：格拉斯哥担任“欧洲文化之都”的那一年，无疑可以被视为一系列复杂因素之一，正是这些因素将这座城市塑造成为了如今依然稳固的艺术、音乐与戏剧重镇。", "“文化名镇”可以不仅仅局限于艺术领域，它还能礼赞小镇的独特风貌——助力维系当地商业街的生机、扶持本地公共设施，而最重要的是歌颂当地人民并将其转化为切实的行动。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Cooper and her colleagues argue that a \"town of culture\" award could", "options": ["consolidate the town-city ties in Britain.", "promote cooperation among Britain's towns.", "increase the economic strength of Britain's towns.", "focus Britain's limited resources on cultural events."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "A town of culture award could, it is argued, become an annual event, attracting funding and creating jobs.", "explanation": "定位第一段第三至五句。库珀及其同事先以赫尔市为例，指出“文化之城”头衔带来了2.2亿英镑的投资和丰富的艺术活动，随后进一步说明“文化名镇”奖可以成为年度盛事，吸引资金（attracting funding）并创造就业机会（creating jobs）。这些都直接指向带动地方经济增长，对应C项“增强英国小镇的经济实力（increase the economic strength of Britain's towns）”。", "trapNote": "D项为强干扰项：将原文“小镇通常缺乏资源去击败大城市竞争对手（lack the resources）”偷换为“将有限资源集中于文化活动”，属于偷换概念；A、B两项提到的“城乡联系”“小镇间合作”在第一段均未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, the proposal might be regarded by some as", "options": ["a sensible compromise.", "a self-deceiving attempt.", "an eye-catching bonus.", "an inaccessible target."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "A cynic might speculate that the UK is on the verge of disappearing into an endless fever of self-celebration in its desperation to reinvent itself for the post-Brexit world: after town of culture, who knows what will follow—village of culture? Suburb of culture? Hamlet of culture?", "explanation": "定位第二段。首先提到有人将该提案视作英国无法再角逐更具声望的“欧洲文化之都”后的安慰奖（booby prize）；接着指出愤世嫉俗者推测英国急于在脱欧后重塑自我，正陷入一场无休止的自我吹捧狂热（endless fever of self-celebration），甚至讽刺接下来还会有“文化名村”“文化郊区”。这体现了部分人认为该提案不过是自欺欺人的举动，对应B项“a self-deceiving attempt”。", "trapNote": "A项“明智的妥协”与原文贬义色彩（booby prize、self-celebration）正反颠倒；C项“引人注目的额外奖励”篡改了booby prize（安慰奖/末名奖）的嘲讽意味；D项“遥不可及的目标”把前文无法再申请的欧洲文化之都张冠李戴到了新提案上。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "The author suggests that a title holder is successful only if it", "options": ["endeavours to maintain its image.", "meets the aspirations of its people.", "brings its local arts to prominence.", "commits to its long-term growth."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "A badly run \"year of culture\" washes in and out of a place like the tide, bringing prominence for a spell but leaving no lasting benefits to the community. The really successful holders of such titles are those that do a great deal more than fill hotel bedrooms and bring in high-profile arts events and good press for a year.", "explanation": "定位第三段第二至六句。作者通过正反对比指出，运作糟糕的头衔只能带来短暂关注，无法给社区留下持久收益（leaving no lasting benefits）；而真正成功的头衔获得者绝不仅仅满足于一年的游客入住、高规格艺术活动和正面宣传，它们能改变当地居民的抱负与自我形象，并像格拉斯哥那样依靠远见与各方合作实现绵延至今的持久蜕变。可见成功的关键在于致力于长远发展，对应D项。", "trapNote": "A项“维持形象”与原文“nudge the self-image... into a bolder and more optimistic light（推动自我形象向更大胆乐观转变）”相悖；B项“满足民意”偷换了原文“transform the aspirations（重塑/提升居民抱负）”；C项“凸显本地艺术”仅对应“短暂关注”，以偏概全。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Glasgow is mentioned in Paragraph 3 to present", "options": ["a contrasting case.", "a supporting example.", "a background story.", "a related topic."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "But it can be done: Glasgow's year as European capital of culture can certainly be seen as one of a complex series of factors that have turned the city into the power of art, music and theatre that it remains today.", "explanation": "定位第三段末句。前一句作者指出要真正做好文化头衔很难，需要非凡的远见以及市政府、私营部门、社区团体和文化机构之间的通力合作；紧接着以冒号前的“But it can be done（但这是可以做到的）”引出格拉斯哥作为1990年“欧洲文化之都”成功转型为艺术、音乐与戏剧强市的实例。由此可知，提及格拉斯哥是为了给作者的观点提供正面佐证，对应B项“a supporting example”。", "trapNote": "A项“对比案例”误判了逻辑关系，格拉斯哥正是“可以做到”的正面例证，而非与前文构成反例对比；C项“背景故事”和D项“相关话题”均未准确把握例证服务于“But it can be done”这一核心论点的功能。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "What is the author's attitude towards the proposal?", "options": ["Skeptical", "Objective", "Favourable", "Critical"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "A \"town of culture\" could be not just about the arts but about honouring a town's peculiarities-helping sustain its high street, supporting local facilities and above all celebrating its people and turn it into action.", "explanation": "综观全文，作者态度呈现“先抑后扬、总体支持”的特点：第一段介绍提案的经济与社会益处；第二段虽引用批评者与讽刺者的负面看法，但明确标明为“Some”“A cynic”的观点；第三段先提醒头衔并非万能，随即用“But it can be done”肯定长期价值；第四段更明确畅想“文化名镇”不仅关乎艺术，更能维系商业街、扶持本地设施、礼赞当地民众并化为实际行动，流露出明确的赞许与支持，故选C项。", "trapNote": "A项“怀疑的”和D项“批判的”容易受第二段“booby prize”“self-celebration”干扰，但那些属于他人（Some、A cynic）的观点，并非作者立场；B项“客观的”忽略了作者在第三段末与第四段中对提案积极意义的明确赞赏。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "设立，制定（制度、奖项等）", "note": "熟词僻义：作动词考法高频，意为“建立、实行”，非名词“机构/学院”。", "word": "institute"}, {"gloss": "令人向往的，抢手的", "note": "合成形容词，考研阅读高频评价词，相当于popular / in high demand。", "word": "sought-after"}, {"gloss": "一阵，一段短暂时期", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“拼写；魔咒”，此处意为“一段时间”，与lasting对比。", "word": "spell"}, {"gloss": "轻轻推动，促进，逐步引导", "note": "地道动词，常考于社会政策与心理引导语境，此处指逐渐提升城市自我认知。", "word": "nudge"}, {"gloss": "独特性，地方特色", "note": "由peculiar派生，此处非贬义“古怪”，而是褒义“小镇独特风貌/特质”。", "word": "peculiarity"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Cooper and her colleagues argue that the success of the crown for Hull, where it brought in £220m of investment and an avalanche of arts, ought not to be confined to cities.", "point": "主句谓语argue后接that宾语从句，从句中嵌入where引导的非限制性定语从句修饰Hull；注意crown此处指代“文化之城”桂冠，an avalanche of形象表达“大量涌现”。", "structure": "主语(Cooper and her colleagues) + 谓语(argue) + that宾语从句[主语(the success...) + where非限定从 + 谓语(ought not to be confined to cities)]", "zh": "库珀和她的同事们认为，赫尔市摘得该桂冠所取得的成功——吸引了2.2亿英镑投资并催生了大量艺术活动——不应仅限于城市。"}, {"en": "Some might see the proposal as a booby prize for the fact that Britain is no longer able to apply for the much more prestigious title of European capital of culture, a sought-after award bagged by Glasgow in 1990 and Liverpool in 2008.", "point": "that引导同位语从句解释说明the fact；句末名词短语a sought-after award作European capital of culture的同位语，其中过去分词短语bagged by...作后置定语。", "structure": "主句(Some might see... as a booby prize for the fact) + that同位语从句 + 同位语(a sought-after award) + 过去分词后置定语(bagged by...)", "zh": "有些人可能会把这一提议视作一种安慰奖，因为英国再也无法申请声望高得多的“欧洲文化之都”头衔——格拉斯哥曾在1990年、利物浦曾在2008年斩获这一备受追捧的奖项。"}, {"en": "Glasgow's year as European capital of culture can certainly be seen as one of a complex series of factors that have turned the city into the power of art, music and theatre that it remains today.", "point": "包含两层定语从句：第一个that引导定语从句修饰factors；第二个that引导定语从句修饰the power，且that在从句中作remains的表语，意为“它至今仍是那样的重镇”。", "structure": "主语(Glasgow's year...) + 谓语(can certainly be seen as) + 宾语(one of... factors) + 定语从句1(that have turned...) + 定语从句2(that it remains today)", "zh": "格拉斯哥担任“欧洲文化之都”的那一年，无疑可以被视为一系列复杂因素之一，正是这些因素将该市塑造成为了它至今依然保持的艺术、音乐与戏剧重镇。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "吸引资金并创造就业 → 增强英国小镇的经济实力（具体措施概括为经济效果）", "option": "increase the economic strength of Britain's towns", "original": "attracting funding and creating jobs"}, {"note": "陷入自我吹捧的狂热以重塑自我 → 自欺欺人的尝试（态度概括）", "option": "a self-deceiving attempt", "original": "disappearing into an endless fever of self-celebration in its desperation to reinvent itself"}, {"note": "留下持久收益、远不止一年的短期效益 → 致力于长远发展", "option": "commits to its long-term growth", "original": "leaving no lasting benefits... do a great deal more than... for a year"}, {"note": "格拉斯哥的例子证明“这是可以做到的” → 作为支持观点的正面例证", "option": "a supporting example", "original": "But it can be done: Glasgow's year as European capital of culture..."}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2020-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2020", "examSet": "2020 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2020 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "学术出版暴利模式与开放获取困境", "subtitle": "科技商业 · 学术期刊垄断、Sci-Hub 与出版改革", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 428, "paragraphs": ["Scientific publishing has long been a licence to print money. Scientists need journals in which to publish their research, so they will supply the articles without monetary reward. Other scientists perform the specialised work of peer review also for free, because it is a central element in the acquisition of status and the production of scientific knowledge.", "With the content of papers secured for free, the publisher needs only find a market for its journal. Until this century, university libraries were not very price sensitive. Scientific publishers routinely report profit margins approaching 40% on their operations, at a time when the rest of the publishing industry is in an existential crisis.", "The Dutch giant Elsevier, which claims to publish 25% of the scientific papers produced in the world, made profits of more than £900m last year, while UK universities alone spent more than £210m in 2016 to enable researchers to access their own publicly funded research: both figures seem to rise unstoppably despite increasingly desperate efforts to change them.", "The most drastic, and thoroughly illegal, reaction has been the emergence of Sci-Hub, a kind of global photocopier for scientific papers, set up in 2012, which now claims to offer access to every paywalled article published since 2015. The success of Sci-Hub, which relies on researchers passing on copies they have themselves legally accessed, shows the legal ecosystem has lost legitimacy among its users and must be transformed so that it works for all participants.", "In Britain the move towards open access publishing has been driven by funding bodies. In some ways it has been very successful. More than half of all British scientific research is now published under open access terms: either freely available from the moment of publication, or paywalled for a year or more so that the publishers can make a profit before being placed on general release.", "Yet the new system has not worked out any cheaper for the universities. Publishers have responded to the demand that they make their product free to readers by charging their writers fees to cover the costs of preparing an article. These range from around £500 to $5,000. A report last year pointed out that the costs both of subscriptions and of these \"article preparation costs\" had been steadily rising at a rate above inflation. In some ways the scientific publishing model resembles the economy of the social internet: labour is provided free in exchange for the hope of status, while huge profits are made by a few big firms who run the market places. In both cases, we need a rebalancing of power."], "translations": ["长期以来，学术出版一直如同“印钞许可证”。科学家需要期刊来发表他们的研究成果，因此他们会毫无金钱报酬地提供文章。其他科学家也会免费完成同行评审这项专业工作，因为这是获取学术地位和产出科学知识的核心环节。", "在免费获得论文内容后，出版商只需为旗下期刊寻找市场即可。直到本世纪之前，大学图书馆对价格都不怎么敏感。当出版业的其他领域正陷入生存危机之时，学术出版商却照例报告其运营利润率接近40%。", "声称发表了全球25%科学论文的荷兰巨头爱思唯尔去年获利超过9亿英镑，而仅英国各大学在2016年就花费了超过2.1亿英镑，只为让研究人员能够阅读他们自己由公共资金资助的研究成果：尽管人们越来越迫切地努力想要改变这一局面，这两个数字似乎仍在不可阻挡地攀升。", "最极端也彻底违法的反击，便是2012年创立的Sci-Hub的出现——它就像一个全球性的科学论文复印机，如今声称能提供2015年以来所有设付费墙论文的访问通道。依赖研究人员转发自己合法获取的论文副本而运作的Sci-Hub之所以能成功，表明合法的学术出版生态系统已在其用户群中丧失了公信力，必须加以改革，从而服务于所有参与者。", "在英国，向开放获取出版模式的推进一直由科研资助机构主导。在某些方面，这一举措非常成功。如今，英国半数以上的科学研究都依据开放获取条款发表：要么一经出版即可免费阅读，要么先设置一年或更长时间的付费墙，以便出版商在向公众全面开放前赚取利润。", "然而，新体系对大学而言并没有变得更便宜。面对读者免费获取产品的要求，出版商的应对之道是向作者收取费用，以弥补文章的编审制作成本。这些费用从约500英镑到5000美元不等。去年的一份报告指出，期刊订阅费和这类“文章处理费”都在以高于通胀的速度稳步上涨。在某些方面，学术出版模式与社交互联网经济颇为相似：人们无偿提供劳动以期换取地位，而运营交易平台的少数大公司却赚取巨额利润。在这两种情况下，我们都需要重新平衡权力。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Scientific publishing is seen as “a licence to print money” partly because", "options": ["its content acquisition costs nothing.", "its marketing strategy has been successful.", "its payment for peer review is reduced.", "its funding has enjoyed a steady increase."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Scientists need journals in which to publish their research, so they will supply the articles without monetary reward. Other scientists perform the specialised work of peer review also for free, because it is a central element in the acquisition of status and the production of scientific knowledge.", "explanation": "定位第一段。首句提出学术出版长期以来如同“印钞许可证”（暴利行业），紧接着两句阐明原因：科学家为了发表研究而无偿提供论文（supply the articles without monetary reward），其他科学家也免费承担同行评审工作（for free）。第二段首句进一步总结为“论文内容免费获取（the content of papers secured for free）”。由此可知其暴利原因之一在于内容获取零成本，对应A项。", "trapNote": "C项“同行评审费用降低了”偷换原文“also for free（完全免费）”，将“零报酬”弱化为“费用减少”；B项“营销策略成功”曲解第二段“只需要找市场”；D项“资助稳步增长”无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraphs 2 and 3, scientific publishers Elsevier have", "options": ["financed researchers generously.", "gone through an existential crisis.", "revived the publishing industry.", "thrive mainly on university libraries."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The Dutch giant Elsevier, which claims to publish 25% of the scientific papers produced in the world, made profits of more than £900m last year, while UK universities alone spent more than £210m in 2016 to enable researchers to access their own publicly funded research: both figures seem to rise unstoppably despite increasingly desperate efforts to change them.", "explanation": "定位第二、三段。第二段指出直至本世纪大学图书馆对价格都不太敏感（not very price sensitive），使得学术出版商的运营利润率接近40%；第三段以荷兰出版巨头爱思唯尔（Elsevier）为例，指出其去年利润超9亿英镑，而仅英国大学在2016年就花费逾2.1亿英镑购买自己公费资助研究成果的访问权。两段共同表明，爱思唯尔等学术出版商主要依靠大学图书馆的巨额订阅费蓬勃发展，对应D项。", "trapNote": "B项“经历了生存危机”张冠李戴，第二段明确指出处于生存危机的是“the rest of the publishing industry（出版业的其他领域）”，而非学术出版商；A、C两项在文中毫无依据，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "态度题", "stem": "How does the author feel about the success of Sci-Hub?", "options": ["Relieved.", "Concerned.", "Puzzled.", "Encouraged."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The success of Sci-Hub, which relies on researchers passing on copies they have themselves legally accessed, shows the legal ecosystem has lost legitimacy among its users and must be transformed so that it works for all participants.", "explanation": "定位第四段。作者开篇将Sci-Hub的出现定性为“最极端且完全非法的反应（most drastic, and thoroughly illegal, reaction）”，并紧接着分析其成功所折射出的严峻问题：合法的学术出版生态系统已在用户群中丧失公信力/合法性（lost legitimacy among its users），必须加以变革以兼顾所有参与者的利益。可见作者对Sci-Hub的成功并不乐观或赞许，而是对其背后反映的生态危机感到担忧，对应B项“Concerned”。", "trapNote": "A项“宽慰的”和D项“受到鼓舞的”与作者定性其“thoroughly illegal”及呼吁“must be transformed”的严肃忧虑相悖（正反颠倒）；C项“困惑的”无中生有，作者对其产生原因和后果分析得十分清晰。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It can be learned from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that open access terms", "options": ["free universities from financial burdens.", "render publishing much easier for scientists.", "reduce the cost of publication substantially.", "allow publishers some room to make money."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "More than half of all British scientific research is now published under open access terms: either freely available from the moment of publication, or paywalled for a year or more so that the publishers can make a profit before being placed on general release.", "explanation": "定位第五、六段。第五段末句指出开放获取条款的两种形式：要么一经发表即可免费阅读，要么先设置一年及以上的付费墙，让出版商在公开发布前赚取利润（so that the publishers can make a profit）；第六段补充指出，即便面向读者免费，出版商也转而向作者收取高达500英镑至5000美元的“文章处理费”。可见开放获取依然给出版商留出了盈利空间，对应D项。", "trapNote": "A项“减轻大学财务负担”和C项“大幅降低出版成本”均与第六段首句“has not worked out any cheaper for the universities”及费用高于通胀速率上涨的事实正反颠倒；B项“使发表更容易”属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Which of the following characterises the scientific publishing model?", "options": ["Trial subscription is offered.", "Labour triumphs over status.", "The few feed on the many.", "Costs are well controlled."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "In some ways the scientific publishing model resembles the economy of the social internet: labour is provided free in exchange for the hope of status, while huge profits are made by a few big firms who run the market places.", "explanation": "定位第六段倒数第二句。作者将学术出版模式比作社交互联网经济：大量科研人员无偿提供劳动以期换取学术声望（labour is provided free in exchange for the hope of status），而经营市场的少数几家大公司却从中攫取巨额利润（huge profits are made by a few big firms）。C项“少数人靠多数人牟利（The few feed on the many）”精炼概括了这一不对等的利益分配机制。", "trapNote": "B项“劳动胜过声望”曲解了“labour is provided free in exchange for the hope of status（用免费劳动换取声望的希望）”；D项“成本控制良好”与“rising at a rate above inflation”正反颠倒；A项无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "（合法）特许，摇钱树，生财之道", "note": "熟词僻义及习语：a licence to print money为地道表达，指“稳赚不赔的暴利买卖”。", "word": "licence"}, {"gloss": "存亡攸关的，生死存亡的", "note": "考研高频词，existential crisis指“生存危机”，注意区别于“存在主义的”。", "word": "existential"}, {"gloss": "合法性，正统性，公信力", "note": "由legitimate派生，此处不仅指法律层面，更指制度被用户认可的合理性。", "word": "legitimacy"}, {"gloss": "设付费墙的（需付费才能阅读的）", "note": "新闻与数字出版高频词，作动词或形容词使用，对应open access（开放获取）。", "word": "paywalled"}, {"gloss": "利润率，幅度，边缘", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“页边空白/边缘”，商业语境profit margin必考“利润率”。", "word": "margin"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The Dutch giant Elsevier, which claims to publish 25% of the scientific papers produced in the world, made profits of more than £900m last year, while UK universities alone spent more than £210m in 2016 to enable researchers to access their own publicly funded research: both figures seem to rise unstoppably despite increasingly desperate efforts to change them.", "point": "主句由while连接两个对比分句，前分句含which引导的非限制性定语从句及过去分词短语produced in the world作后置定语；冒号后为总结性独立分句，despite引出让步状语。", "structure": "主分句1(The Dutch giant Elsevier + which定从 + made profits...) + while对比连词 + 主分句2(UK universities... spent... to enable...) : 总结分句(both figures seem to rise... despite...)", "zh": "声称发表了全球25%科学论文的荷兰出版巨头爱思唯尔去年获利超过9亿英镑，而仅英国的大学在2016年就花费了超过2.1亿英镑，只为让研究人员能够查阅由公共资金资助的他们自己的研究成果：尽管人们越来越迫切地试图改变现状，这两个数字似乎仍在不可阻挡地攀升。"}, {"en": "The success of Sci-Hub, which relies on researchers passing on copies they have themselves legally accessed, shows the legal ecosystem has lost legitimacy among its users and must be transformed so that it works for all participants.", "point": "主语后紧跟which引导的非限制性定语从句，其中passing on copies后带省略关系代词that的定语从句they have themselves legally accessed；shows后接省略that的宾语从句，包含并列谓语has lost和must be transformed及so that引导的目的状语从句。", "structure": "主语(The success of Sci-Hub) + which非限定从(含动名词复合结构与省略that的定从) + 谓语(shows) + 宾语从句(the legal ecosystem has lost... and must be transformed + so that目的状语从句)", "zh": "依赖研究人员传递自己合法获取的论文副本而运作的Sci-Hub之所以能够成功，表明合法的学术出版生态系统已在其用户中丧失了公信力，必须进行彻底改革，以使其惠及所有参与者。"}, {"en": "In some ways the scientific publishing model resembles the economy of the social internet: labour is provided free in exchange for the hope of status, while huge profits are made by a few big firms who run the market places.", "point": "冒号后具体解释科学出版模式与社交互联网经济的相似之处：while对比前后两种截然不同的主体处境，who引导定语从句修饰a few big firms。", "structure": "总起句(the scientific publishing model resembles...) : 解释分句1(labour is provided free...) + while对比 + 解释分句2(huge profits are made by a few big firms + who定从)", "zh": "在某些方面，学术出版模式类似于社交互联网经济：人们无偿提供劳动以期换取地位与声望，而掌控市场的少数大公司却赚取了巨额利润。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "免费供稿与免费审稿 / 内容免费获取 → 内容获取零成本", "option": "its content acquisition costs nothing", "original": "supply the articles without monetary reward... for free / content of papers secured for free"}, {"note": "先设付费墙一年或更久以便出版商盈利 → 给出版商留出盈利空间", "option": "allow publishers some room to make money", "original": "paywalled for a year or more so that the publishers can make a profit"}, {"note": "合法生态在用户中丧失公信力、必须变革 → 作者对Sci-Hub成功的忧虑态度", "option": "Concerned", "original": "shows the legal ecosystem has lost legitimacy among its users and must be transformed"}, {"note": "多数人免费劳动换声望，少数大公司攫取暴利 → 少数人靠多数人牟利", "option": "The few feed on the many", "original": "labour is provided free... while huge profits are made by a few big firms"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2020-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2020", "examSet": "2020 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2020 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "董事会性别配额政策反思", "subtitle": "社会政策 · 性别平等与企业治理", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 412, "paragraphs": ["Progressives often support diversity mandates as a path to equality and a way to level the playing field. But all too often such policies are an insincere form of virtue-signaling that benefits only the most privileged and does little to help average people.", "A pair of bills sponsored by Massachusetts state Senator Jason Lewis and House Speaker Pro Tempore Patricia Haddad, to ensure \"gender parity\" on boards and commissions, provide a case in point.", "Haddad and Lewis are concerned that more than half the state-government boards are less than 40 percent female. In order to ensure that elite women have more such opportunities, they have proposed imposing government quotas. If the bills become law, state boards and commissions will be required to set aside 50 percent of board seats for women by 2022.", "The bills are similar to a measure recently adopted in California, which last year became the first state to require gender quotas for private companies. In signing the measure, California Governor Jerry Brown admitted that the law, which expressly classifies people on the basis of sex, is probably unconstitutional.", "The US Supreme Court frowns on sex-based classifications unless they are designed to address an \"important\" policy interest. Because the California law applies to all boards, even where there is no history of prior discrimination, courts are likely to rule that the law violates the constitutional guarantee of \"equal protection\".", "But are such government mandates even necessary? Female participation on corporate boards may not currently mirror the percentage of women in the general population, but so what?", "The number of women on corporate boards has been steadily increasing without government interference. According to a study by Catalyst, between 2010 and 2015 the share of women on the boards of global corporations increased by 54 percent.", "Requiring companies to make gender the primary qualification for board membership will inevitably lead to less experienced private sector boards. That is exactly what happened when Norway adopted a nationwide corporate gender quota.", "Writing in The New Republic, Alice Lee notes that increasing the number of opportunities for board membership without increasing the pool of qualified women to serve on such boards has led to a \"golden skirt\" phenomenon, where the same elite women scoop up multiple seats on a variety of boards.", "Next time somebody pushes corporate quotas as a way to promote gender equity, remember that such policies are largely self-serving measures that make their sponsors feel good but do little to help average women."], "translations": ["进步派人士通常支持多元化强制指令，将其视为通往平等与营造公平竞争环境的途径。但此类政策往往只是一种虚伪的道德作秀，仅仅惠及最特权阶层，对普通民众却毫无助益。", "由马萨诸塞州参议员杰森·刘易斯和众议院临时议长帕特里夏·哈达德联名发起的两项旨在确保董事会及委员会“性别均等”的法案，便是明证。", "哈达德和刘易斯担心，超过半数的州政府委员会中女性占比不足40%。为了确保精英女性获得更多此类机会，他们提议实行政府配额制。一旦法案生效，州属董事会和委员会将被要求在2022年前为女性预留50%的席位。", "这两项法案与加利福尼亚州近期通过的一项举措类似——加州去年成为全美首个要求私营企业实行性别配额的州。在签署该法案时，加州州长杰里·布朗承认，这项明确按性别对人进行分类的法律很可能是违宪的。", "美国最高法院向来不赞成基于性别的分类，除非其旨在解决某项“重大”政策利益。由于加州法律适用于所有董事会，哪怕毫无先前歧视记录的企业也不例外，法院很可能裁定该法违反了宪法所保障的“平等保护”原则。", "但此类政府强制指令真的有必要吗？企业董事会中的女性参与度目前或许未能镜像反映女性在总人口中的比例，可那又如何呢？", "在没有政府干预的情况下，企业董事会中的女性人数一直在稳步增长。根据Catalyst的一项研究，2010年至2015年间，全球企业董事会中女性所占比例增长了54%。", "要求企业将性别作为董事会成员的首要资格，必然会导致私营部门董事会经验匮乏。这正是挪威实行全国性企业性别配额制度后发生的情况。", "爱丽丝·李在《新共和》撰文指出，只增加董事会成员的机会数量，却不扩大有资格担任董事的女性人才储备库，这导致了“金裙子”现象——同一批精英女性同时包揽了多家公司的多个董事席位。", "下次再有人把企业配额当作促进性别平等的手段来推行时，请记住，此类政策很大程度上只是自私的举措，只能让倡导者自我感觉良好，对普通女性却几乎毫无帮助。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The author believes that the bills sponsored by Lewis and Haddad will", "options": ["help little to reduce gender bias.", "pose a threat to the state government.", "raise women's position in politics.", "greatly broaden career options."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "But all too often such policies are an insincere form of virtue-signaling that benefits only the most privileged and does little to help average people.", "explanation": "定位第1、2段。第1段指出，旨在促进平等的多元化强制措施往往只是虚伪的道德作秀，仅惠及特权阶层而对普通人帮助甚微；第2段紧接着以刘易斯和哈达德发起的旨在确保董事会“性别均等”的两项法案为例（a case in point）来印证该观点。选项A“对减少性别偏见作用甚微”正是对原文“does little to help average people”的合理概括。", "trapNote": "B项“对州政府构成威胁”无中生有；C项“提高女性政治地位”和D项“极大拓宽职业选择”与作者认为该法案“收效甚微、只利好少数精英”的批判态度正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is true of the California measure?", "options": ["It has irritated private business owners.", "It is welcomed by the Supreme Court.", "It may go against the Constitution.", "It will settle the prior controversies."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Because the California law applies to all boards, even where there is no history of prior discrimination, courts are likely to rule that the law violates the constitutional guarantee of \"equal protection\".", "explanation": "定位第4、5段。第4段提到加州州长杰里·布朗签署该法案时承认，按性别对人进行明确分类的法律“可能违宪”（probably unconstitutional）。第5段进一步指出，最高法院通常反对基于性别的分类，由于该法案适用于所有董事会，法院很可能裁定其违反宪法中的“平等保护”条款。选项C“它可能违背宪法”精准同义转述原文。", "trapNote": "B项“受最高法院欢迎”与第5段“frowns on”（不赞成）正反颠倒；D项“解决先前的争议”偷换了原文“no history of prior discrimination”的概念；A项“激怒私营企业主”属无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "例证题", "stem": "The author mentions the study by Catalyst to illustrate", "options": ["the harm from arbitrary board decision.", "the importance of constitutional guarantees.", "the pressure on women in global corporations.", "the needlessness of government interventions."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "The number of women on corporate boards has been steadily increasing without government interference.", "explanation": "定位第6、7段。第6段以设问句提出核心论点：“但这类政府强制指令真的有必要吗？”第7段随即指出，在没有政府干预（without government interference）的情况下，企业董事会中的女性人数一直在稳步增长，并引用Catalyst的研究数据（2010至2015年间增长54%）加以佐证。可见引用该研究旨在说明政府干预毫无必要，对应D项。", "trapNote": "A项“任意董事会决定的危害”、B项“宪法保障的重要性”和C项“跨国企业女性面临的压力”在第7段均未提及，属于脱离例证服务论点的无中生有或跨段拼凑。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Norway's adoption of a nationwide corporate gender quota has led to", "options": ["the underestimation of elite women's role.", "the objection to female participation on boards.", "the entry of unqualified candidates into the board.", "the growing tension between labor and management."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "Requiring companies to make gender the primary qualification for board membership will inevitably lead to less experienced private sector boards. That is exactly what happened when Norway adopted a nationwide corporate gender quota.", "explanation": "定位第8、9段。第8段指出，要求企业将性别作为董事会成员的首要资格，必然导致私营部门董事会缺乏经验，而这正是挪威实施全国性企业性别配额后发生的情况。第9段补充道，在未扩大合格女性人才库的情况下增加董事会名额，导致了“金裙子”现象。选项C“不合格候选人进入董事会”对应原文“less experienced”及“without increasing the pool of qualified women”。", "trapNote": "A项“低估精英女性的作用”与第9段精英女性身兼多职的描述不符，属正反颠倒；B项“反对女性进入董事会”和D项“劳资关系紧张”在原文中均未体现，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from the text?", "options": ["Women's need in employment should be considered.", "Feasibility should be a prime concern in policymaking.", "Everyone should try hard to promote social justice.", "Major social issues should be the focus of legislation."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 10, "evidenceQuote": "Next time somebody pushes corporate quotas as a way to promote gender equity, remember that such policies are largely self-serving measures that make their sponsors feel good but do little to help average women.", "explanation": "本题为全文推理题，需综合全篇论点。作者从法律和现实两方面质疑性别配额政策：第4-5段指出其可能违宪，第6-7段指出其多此一举，第8-9段指出其因合格女性人才库不足而导致董事会经验匮乏与“金裙子”现象，第10段总结其只让发起者自我感觉良好却难助普通女性。由此可推知，制定政策时应将可行性作为首要考量，对应B项。", "trapNote": "A项“应考虑女性的就业需求”属于以偏概全且偏离作者对政策可操作性的批判；C项“每个人都应努力促进社会正义”和D项“重大社会问题应成为立法重点”均为过度推理与泛化。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "强制指令，法定要求", "note": "考法：高频政经词，常与impose/support搭配，文中指多样性/性别配额强制令。", "word": "mandate"}, {"gloss": "（道德）作秀，表态标榜", "note": "熟词僻义：由virtue（美德）+ signaling（发信号）构成，贬义，指空喊口号以彰显道德高尚。", "word": "virtue-signaling"}, {"gloss": "（数量、地位等的）均等，平等", "note": "考法：常用于gender parity（性别均等）或purchasing power parity（购买力平价）。", "word": "parity"}, {"gloss": "不赞成，反对（后接on）", "note": "熟词僻义：本义“皱眉”，作动词短语frown on sth.表示“不赞成、反对某事”。", "word": "frown on"}, {"gloss": "（政策等）自私自利的，利己的", "note": "考法：文中与virtue-signaling呼应，揭露配额倡导者只为自我标榜的本质。", "word": "self-serving"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "But all too often such policies are an insincere form of virtue-signaling that benefits only the most privileged and does little to help average people.", "point": "that引导的定语从句修饰virtue-signaling，其中由and连接两个并列谓语benefits和does little to help，注意the most privileged指“最特权阶层”。", "structure": "主句（such policies are...）+ that引导的定语从句（并列谓语：benefits... and does little to help...）", "zh": "但此类政策往往只是一种虚伪的道德作秀，仅仅惠及最特权阶层，对普通民众却毫无助益。"}, {"en": "Writing in The New Republic, Alice Lee notes that increasing the number of opportunities for board membership without increasing the pool of qualified women to serve on such boards has led to a \"golden skirt\" phenomenon, where the same elite women scoop up multiple seats on a variety of boards.", "point": "动名词短语increasing...作宾语从句主语，后接介词短语without increasing...作条件状语，句末where引导非限制性定语从句解释“金裙子”现象。", "structure": "现在分词短语作状语（Writing...）+ 主句（Alice Lee notes...）+ that引导的宾语从句 + where引导的定语从句", "zh": "爱丽丝·李在《新共和》撰文指出，只增加董事会成员的机会数量，却不扩大有资格担任董事的女性人才储备库，这导致了“金裙子”现象——同一批精英女性同时包揽了多家公司的多个董事席位。"}, {"en": "Next time somebody pushes corporate quotas as a way to promote gender equity, remember that such policies are largely self-serving measures that make their sponsors feel good but do little to help average women.", "point": "Next time引导时间状语从句，主句为祈使句remember that...；从句中又嵌套由that引导的定语从句，通过but形成强烈对比。", "structure": "Next time引导时间状语从句 + 祈使句主句（remember）+ that引导的宾语从句 + that引导的定语从句", "zh": "下次再有人把企业配额当作促进性别平等的手段来推行时，请记住，此类政策很大程度上只是自私的举措，只能让倡导者自我感觉良好，对普通女性却几乎毫无帮助。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "态度转化：原文批判法案对普通人几乎无益，选项概括为对减少性别偏见作用甚微。", "option": "help little to reduce gender bias", "original": "does little to help average people"}, {"note": "同义改写：原文“可能违宪”在选项中转为“可能违背宪法”。", "option": "go against the Constitution", "original": "is probably unconstitutional / violates the constitutional guarantee"}, {"note": "反向概括：无政府干预下女性占比稳步上升，例证旨在说明政府干预没有必要。", "option": "the needlessness of government interventions", "original": "are such government mandates even necessary? ... steadily increasing without government interference"}, {"note": "语义对应：未扩大合格女性人才库且导致董事会缺乏经验，对应不合格候选人进入董事会。", "option": "the entry of unqualified candidates into the board", "original": "less experienced private sector boards / without increasing the pool of qualified women"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2020-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2020", "examSet": "2020 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2020 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "法国数字服务税与国际税改", "subtitle": "国际经济 · 数字税博弈与全球税制改革", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 434, "paragraphs": ["Last Thursday, the French Senate passed a digital services tax, which would impose an entirely new tax on large multinationals that provide digital services to consumers or users in France. Digital services include everything from providing a platform for selling goods and services online to targeting advertising based on user data, and the tax applies to gross revenue from such services. Many French politicians and media outlets have referred to this as a \"GAFA tax,\" meaning that it is designed to apply primarily to companies such as Google, Apple, Facebook and Amazon—in other words, multinational tech companies based in the United States.", "The digital services tax now awaits the signature of President Emmanuel Macron, who has expressed support for the measure, and it could go into effect within the next few weeks. But it has already sparked significant controversy, with the United States trade representative opening an investigation into whether the tax discriminates against American companies, which in turn could lead to trade sanctions against France.", "The French tax is not just a unilateral move by one country in need of revenue. Instead, the digital services tax is part of a much larger trend, with countries over the past few years proposing or putting in place an alphabet soup of new international tax provisions. These have included Britain's DPT (diverted profits tax), Australia's MAAL (multinational antiavoidance law), and India's SEP (significant economic presence) test, to name but a few. At the same time, the European Union, Spain, Britain and several other countries have all seriously contemplated digital services taxes.", "These unilateral developments differ in their specifics, but they are all designed to tax multinationals on income and revenue that countries believe they should have a right to tax, even if international tax rules do not grant them that right. In other words, they all share a view that the international tax system has failed to keep up with the current economy.", "In response to these many unilateral measures, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD) is currently working with 131 countries to reach a consensus by the end of 2020 on an international solution. Both France and the United States are involved in the organization's work, but France's digital services tax and the American response raise questions about what the future holds for the international tax system.", "France's planned tax is a clear warning: Unless a broad consensus can be reached on reforming the international tax system, other nations are likely to follow suit, and American companies will face a cascade of different taxes from dozens of nations that will prove burdensome and costly."], "translations": ["上周四，法国参议院通过了一项数字服务税法案，将对向法国消费者或用户提供数字服务的大型跨国公司征收一种全新的税种。数字服务涵盖范围广泛，从提供在线商品与服务交易平台，到基于用户数据精准投放广告，该税种将按此类服务的总营收征收。许多法国政界人士和媒体将其称为“GAFA税”，意即该税主要针对谷歌、苹果、脸书和亚马逊等公司——换言之，即总部位于美国的跨国科技公司。", "该数字服务税目前正等待总统埃马纽埃尔·马克龙的签署，他已对该举措表示支持，法案可能在未来几周内生效。但它已经引发了巨大争议，美国贸易代表已就该税种是否歧视美国公司展开调查，而这进而可能导致针对法国的贸易制裁。", "法国的这项税收并不仅仅是一个急需财政收入的国家采取的单边行动。相反，数字服务税是一股更大潮流的组成部分——过去几年间，各国纷纷提出或实施了名目繁多的新型国际税收条款。其中包括英国的“转移利润税”（DPT）、澳大利亚的“跨国反避税法”（MAAL）以及印度的“显著经济存在”（SEP）测试等，不一而足。与此同时，欧盟、西班牙、英国以及其他几个国家都在认真考虑推出数字服务税。", "这些单边举措在具体细节上各有不同，但其目的都是对跨国公司的所得和营收征税——各国认为即便现行国际税收规则未赋予它们这种权利，它们也应当拥有征税权。换言之，它们都秉持着同一个观点：现行国际税收体系已未能跟上当前经济的发展步伐。", "为应对这些众多的单边措施，经济合作与发展组织（OECD）目前正与131个国家合作，力争在2020年底前就一项国际解决方案达成共识。法国和美国都参与了该组织的工作，但法国的数字服务税以及美方的回应，让人对国际税收体系的未来走向产生了疑问。", "法国计划征收的这项税费发出了一个明确的警告：除非各方能就改革国际税收体系达成广泛共识，否则其他国家很可能会纷纷效仿，美国公司也将面临来自数十个国家接踵而至的各类税费，这将会带来沉重且高昂的负担。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The French Senate has passed a bill to", "options": ["regulate digital services platforms.", "protect French companies' interests.", "impose a levy on tech multinationals.", "curb the influence of advertising."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Last Thursday, the French Senate passed a digital services tax, which would impose an entirely new tax on large multinationals that provide digital services to consumers or users in France.", "explanation": "定位第1段。首句指出法国参议院通过了一项数字服务税法案，将对在法提供数字服务的大型跨国公司征收全新税种；末句进一步说明该税主要针对总部位于美国的跨国科技公司（multinational tech companies，如谷歌、苹果等）。选项C“对跨国科技公司征税”中impose a levy对应impose an entirely new tax，精准匹配原文。", "trapNote": "A项“监管数字服务平台”和D项“遏制广告影响”将征税目的曲解为行业监管，属于偷换概念；B项“保护法国企业利益”在首段并未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It can be learned from Paragraph 2 that the digital services tax", "options": ["may trigger countermeasures against France.", "is apt to arouse criticism at home and abroad.", "aims to ease international trade tensions.", "will prompt the tech giants to quit France."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But it has already sparked significant controversy, with the United States trade representative opening an investigation into whether the tax discriminates against American companies, which in turn could lead to trade sanctions against France.", "explanation": "定位第2段。第二句指出，该法案已引发巨大争议，美国贸易代表已启动调查，审查该税种是否歧视美国企业，而这进而可能导致针对法国的贸易制裁（trade sanctions against France）。选项A“可能引发针对法国的反制措施”中countermeasures精准同义替换了trade sanctions，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项“易引起国内外批评”中的“国内批评”与前句马克龙总统支持该举措不符，属以偏概全；C项“旨在缓解国际贸易紧张”与文意正反颠倒；D项“促使科技巨头退出法国”属过度推理。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The countries adopting the unilateral measures share the opinion that", "options": ["redistribution of tech giants' revenue must be ensured.", "the current international tax system needs upgrading.", "tech multinationals' monopoly should be prevented.", "all countries ought to enjoy equal taxing rights."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "In other words, they all share a view that the international tax system has failed to keep up with the current economy.", "explanation": "定位第4段。段首提到这些单边举措（unilateral developments）虽具体细节不同，但都旨在对各国认为有权征税的跨国公司收入征税；末句以“In other words”点明其共识：它们一致认为现行国际税收体系未能跟上当前经济发展（failed to keep up with the current economy）。选项B“现行国际税制需要升级”高度契合该核心观点。", "trapNote": "A项“必须确保科技巨头收入再分配”、C项“应防止跨国科技公司垄断”和D项“所有国家应享有平等征税权”均偏离第4段聚焦的“税制滞后于经济”这一共识，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be learned from Para 5 that the OECD's current work", "options": ["is being resisted by US companies.", "needs to be readjusted immediately.", "is faced with uncertain prospects.", "needs to involve more countries."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Both France and the United States are involved in the organization's work, but France's digital services tax and the American response raise questions about what the future holds for the international tax system.", "explanation": "定位第5段。本段指出经合组织（OECD）正与131个国家合作，力争在2020年底前就国际解决方案达成共识。但转折句指出，尽管法美两国都参与了该组织的工作，法国的数字税及美方的回应却让人对国际税制的未来走向产生疑问（raise questions about what the future holds）。由此推断OECD当前的工作前景尚不明朗，对应C项。", "trapNote": "A项“正遭到美国企业抵制”将美方政府回应偷换为企业抵制；B项“需立即重新调整”属过度推理；D项“需要更多国家参与”与原文已与131国合作的表述相悖，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following might be the best title for this text?", "options": ["France Is Confronted with Trade Sanctions", "France leads the charge on Digital Tax", "France Says \"NO\" to Tech Multinationals", "France Demands a Role in the Digital Economy"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The French tax is not just a unilateral move by one country in need of revenue. Instead, the digital services tax is part of a much larger trend, with countries over the past few years proposing or putting in place an alphabet soup of new international tax provisions.", "explanation": "本题为主旨标题题，需把握全文脉络。第1-2段介绍法国参议院率先通过数字服务税及美方制裁威胁；第3-4段指出法国举措并非孤例，而是顺应各国改革滞后税制的潮流；第5-6段警告若无法达成国际共识，其他国家将纷纷效仿。全文以法国率先征收数字税为切入点并贯穿始终，B项“法国领衔推进数字税”最能全面概括全文主旨。", "trapNote": "A项“法国面临贸易制裁”仅对应第2段细节，以偏概全；C项“法国对跨国科技公司说不”片面曲解征税意图；D项“法国要求在数字经济中扮演角色”属无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "单边的，单方面的", "note": "考法：常与multilateral（多边的）构成反义对比，用于国际关系与贸易语境。", "word": "unilateral"}, {"gloss": "五花八门的缩写，杂乱无章的一堆（条款）", "note": "熟词僻义：本义“字母汤”，在政经新闻中喻指“名目繁多的缩写词、政策或法规汇编”。", "word": "alphabet soup"}, {"gloss": "慎重考虑，打算", "note": "考法：常见考点词，不要误译为“冥想”，在政策类文章中多指“仔细斟酌、拟议推行”。", "word": "contemplate"}, {"gloss": "效仿，照着做", "note": "考法：真题高频固定搭配，源自扑克牌用语“出同花色牌”，引申为“跟风、效仿”。", "word": "follow suit"}, {"gloss": "一连串，接踵而至的（税费等）", "note": "熟词僻义：本义“小瀑布”，作名词短语a cascade of sth.意为“一连串、大量的”。", "word": "cascade"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "But it has already sparked significant controversy, with the United States trade representative opening an investigation into whether the tax discriminates against American companies, which in turn could lead to trade sanctions against France.", "point": "with+名词+现在分词复合结构作伴随状语，其中嵌套whether引导的宾语从句；句末which引导非限制性定语从句修饰前面整个调查事件。", "structure": "主句（it has sparked...）+ with复合结构（opening an investigation into whether...）+ which引导的非限制性定语从句", "zh": "但它已经引发了巨大争议，美国贸易代表已就该税种是否歧视美国公司展开调查，而这进而可能导致针对法国的贸易制裁。"}, {"en": "These unilateral developments differ in their specifics, but they are all designed to tax multinationals on income and revenue that countries believe they should have a right to tax, even if international tax rules do not grant them that right.", "point": "that引导定语从句修饰income and revenue，其中countries believe为插入语；句末even if引导让步状语从句。", "structure": "并列主句（differ... but are designed to...）+ that引导的定语从句（含插入语）+ even if引导的让步状语从句", "zh": "这些单边举措在具体细节上各有不同，但其目的都是对跨国公司的所得和营收征税——各国认为即便现行国际税收规则未赋予它们这种权利，它们也应当拥有征税权。"}, {"en": "Unless a broad consensus can be reached on reforming the international tax system, other nations are likely to follow suit, and American companies will face a cascade of different taxes from dozens of nations that will prove burdensome and costly.", "point": "Unless引导条件状语从句；主句由and连接两个并列分句，末尾that引导定语从句修饰a cascade of different taxes。", "structure": "Unless引导的条件状语从句 + 并列主句（other nations... and American companies...）+ that引导的定语从句", "zh": "除非各方能就改革国际税收体系达成广泛共识，否则其他国家很可能会纷纷效仿，美国公司也将面临来自数十个国家接踵而至的各类税费，这将会带来沉重且高昂的负担。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "精准替换：impose a levy（征收税款）对应impose an entirely new tax，tech multinationals概括大型跨国科技公司。", "option": "impose a levy on tech multinationals", "original": "impose an entirely new tax on large multinationals... multinational tech companies"}, {"note": "同义转述：countermeasures（反制措施）对应trade sanctions（贸易制裁），may trigger对应could lead to。", "option": "may trigger countermeasures against France", "original": "could lead to trade sanctions against France"}, {"note": "因果转化：税制未能跟上当前经济发展，意味着现行国际税制需要更新升级。", "option": "the current international tax system needs upgrading", "original": "the international tax system has failed to keep up with the current economy"}, {"note": "推理概括：对国际税制的未来提出疑问，直接推导出其前景充满不确定性。", "option": "is faced with uncertain prospects", "original": "raise questions about what the future holds for the international tax system"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2019-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2019", "examSet": "2019 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2019 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "金融监管新规与遏制企业短视", "subtitle": "经济与商业 · 金融监管与公司治理中的“长期主义”", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 424, "paragraphs": ["Financial regulators in Britain have imposed a rather unusual rule on the bosses of big banks. Starting next year, any guaranteed bonus of top executives could be delayed 10 years if their banks are under investigation for wrongdoing. The main purpose of this “clawback” rule is to hold bankers accountable for harmful risk-taking and to restore public trust in financial institutions. Yet officials also hope for a much larger benefit: more long-term decision-making, not only by banks but by all corporations, to build a stronger economy for future generations.", "“Short-termism” or the desire for quick profits, has worsened in publicly traded companies, says the Bank of England’s top economist, Andrew Haldane. He quotes a giant of classical economics, Alfred Marshall, in describing this financial impatience as acting like “children who pick the plums out of their pudding to eat them at once” rather than putting them aside to be eaten last.", "The average time for holding a stock in both the United States and Britain, he notes, has dropped from seven years to seven months in recent decades. Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty. This has been dubbed “quarterly capitalism.”", "In addition, new digital technologies have allowed more rapid trading of equities, quicker use of information, and thus shorter attention spans in financial markets. “There seems to be a predominance of short-term thinking at the expense of long-term investing,” said Commissioner Daniel Gallagher of the US Securities and Exchange Commission in a speech this week.", "In the US, the Sarbanes-Oxley Act of 2002 has pushed most public companies to defer performance bonuses for senior executives by about a year, slightly helping reduce “short-termism.” In its latest survey of CEO pay, The Wall Street Journal finds that “a substantial part” of executive pay is now tied to performance.", "Much more could be done to encourage “long-termism,” such as changes in the tax code and quicker disclosure of stock acquisitions. In France, shareholders who hold onto a company investment for at least two years can sometimes earn more voting rights in a company.", "Within companies, the right compensation design can provide incentives for executives to think beyond their own time at the company and on behalf of all stakeholders. Britain’s new rule is a reminder to bankers that society has an interest in their performance, not just for the short term but for the long term."], "translations": ["英国金融监管机构对大型银行的高管施加了一项颇为不寻常的规定。从明年起，如果银行因不当行为正在接受调查，高层管理人员的任何保障性奖金都可能被延迟十年发放。这项“追回”规定的主要目的，是让银行家为有害的冒险行为负责，并恢复公众对金融机构的信任。然而，官员们还寄望于收获更大益处：不仅是银行，所有企业都能开展更多长期决策，从而为子孙后代建设更强大的经济。", "英格兰银行首席经济学家安德鲁·霍尔丹表示，上市公司中的“短视主义”——即对快钱的渴求——已经恶化。他引用古典经济学泰斗阿尔弗雷德·马歇尔的话，将这种金融急躁心态比作“把布丁里的李子挑出来立刻吃掉，而不是留到最后再吃”的孩子。", "他指出，近几十年来，美国和英国持有股票的平均时间已从七年骤降至七个月。要求企业交出高额季度利润的短期投资者，可能会阻碍企业在长期研发或培养客户忠诚度方面的投入。这种现象被称为“季度资本主义”。", "此外，新的数字技术使得股票交易更加迅速、信息利用更加快捷，从而缩短了金融市场的注意力持续时间。美国证券交易委员会委员丹尼尔·加拉格尔在本周的一次演讲中表示：“人们似乎普遍倾向于短期思维，而牺牲了长期投资。”", "在美国，2002年的《萨班斯-奥克斯利法案》促使大多数上市公司将高管绩效奖金推迟约一年发放，这在一定程度上有助于减少“短视主义”。《华尔街日报》在最新的首席执行官薪酬调查中发现，“相当大一部分”高管薪酬如今已与绩效挂钩。", "要鼓励“长期主义”还可以采取更多举措，例如修改税法以及加快股票收购的披露。在法国，持有公司投资至少两年的股东有时可以在公司中获得更多投票权。", "在公司内部，恰当的薪酬设计能够激励高管超越自身在公司的任期限制，代表全体利益相关者去思考问题。英国的新规是在提醒银行家：社会对他们的业绩抱有利益关切，这不仅着眼于短期，更着眼于长期。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 1, one motive in imposing the new rule is to", "options": ["enhance bankers’ sense of responsibility", "help corporations achieve larger profits", "build a new system of financial regulation", "guarantee the bonuses of top executives"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The main purpose of this “clawback” rule is to hold bankers accountable for harmful risk-taking and to restore public trust in financial institutions.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，题干问第一段中实施新规的动机之一。定位第一段第三句“The main purpose of this ‘clawback’ rule is to hold bankers accountable for harmful risk-taking...”。其中“hold bankers accountable”意为“让银行家对有害冒险行为负责”，与A项“enhance bankers’ sense of responsibility”（增强银行家的责任感）构成精准同义替换，故选A。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：B项偷换概念，末句说的是促进长期决策以建设更强经济，而非帮企业赚取更大利润；D项正反颠倒，原文是若银行受查，高管保障奖金可被延迟10年发放，并非保障奖金。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Alfred Marshall is quoted to indicate", "options": ["the conditions for generating quick profits.", "governments’ impatience in decision-making.", "the solid structure of publicly traded companies.", "“short-termism” in economic activities."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "He quotes a giant of classical economics, Alfred Marshall, in describing this financial impatience as acting like “children who pick the plums out of their pudding to eat them at once” rather than putting them aside to be eaten last.", "explanation": "本题为例证题，考查引用古典经济学泰斗马歇尔名言的意图。第二段首句指出上市公司中“短视主义”（即追逐快钱的欲望）恶化，随后第二句用马歇尔的比喻形容这种“financial impatience”（金融急躁心态）就像迫不及待挑出布丁里的李子吃掉的孩子。可见该引语正是为了说明经济活动中的“短视主义”现象，与D项完全吻合，故选D。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：A项无中生有，引语重在批判急功近利的心态而非赚快钱的条件；B项偷换主语，原文批评的是上市公司及金融市场，并非“政府”在决策中的急躁。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It is argued that the influence of transient investment on public companies can be", "options": ["indirect.", "adverse.", "minimal.", "temporary."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，题干询问短期投资对上市公司的影响。定位第三段第二句“Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty.”。句中“hinder”（阻碍、妨碍）表明短期投资者会阻碍企业的长期研发与客户忠诚度建设，即带来不利影响，与B项“adverse”（不利的、负面的）形成同义替换，故选B。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：D项利用词汇表层联想设陷，看到原文“Transient investors”（短期投资者）易误选“temporary”（暂时的），但原文说的是影响具有阻碍性而非影响本身是暂时的；A、C项均属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "例证题", "stem": "The US and France examples are used to illustrate", "options": ["the obstacles to preventing “short-termism”.", "the significance of long-term thinking.", "the approaches to promoting “long-termism”.", "the prevalence of short-term thinking."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Much more could be done to encourage “long-termism,” such as changes in the tax code and quicker disclosure of stock acquisitions. In France, shareholders who hold onto a company investment for at least two years can sometimes earn more voting rights in a company.", "explanation": "本题为例证题，考查第五、六段举出美国和法国例子的目的。第五段指出美国《萨班斯-奥克斯利法案》促使上市公司推迟高管绩效奖金发放，有助于减少“短视主义”；第六段紧接着提出可以采取更多措施鼓励“长期主义”，并以法国赋予长期持股股东更多投票权为例。两例均旨在说明促进“长期主义”的具体做法与途径，对应C项“the approaches to promoting ‘long-termism’”，故选C。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：A项正反颠倒，美法措施是在缓解短视而非制造障碍；D项张冠李戴，前文已论述短视的普遍性，美法例子处于对策段，旨在给出解决方案而非重申现状。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the text?", "options": ["Failure of Quarterly Capitalism", "Patience as a Corporate Virtue", "Decisiveness Required of Top Executives", "Frustration of Risk-taking Bankers"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "Britain’s new rule is a reminder to bankers that society has an interest in their performance, not just for the short term but for the long term.", "explanation": "本题为主旨题，考查全文最佳标题。文章从英国延迟发放银行高管奖金的新规切入，剖析了当下金融市场“短视主义”和“季度资本主义”的弊端，进而列举美、法两国及公司薪酬设计等措施来倡导企业与高管的“长期主义”，末段点明社会关注的是长期表现而非短期利益。B项“Patience as a Corporate Virtue”（耐心作为企业的美德）高度契合“戒除短视、立足长远”的全文主旨，故选B。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：A项以偏概全，“季度资本主义”仅在第三段提及，无法涵盖后半篇的应对方案与“长期主义”核心；D项无中生有，全文并未聚焦银行家的挫败感，而是强调监管引导长期决策。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "追究……的责任；使……负责", "note": "核心搭配 hold sb. accountable for sth.，常替换题干中的 responsibility / duty。", "word": "accountable"}, {"gloss": "短视主义；只顾眼前利益的行为", "note": "构词法 short-term + -ism，与文中 long-termism（长期主义）构成反义对照。", "word": "short-termism"}, {"gloss": "暂时的，短期的；流动的", "note": "文中修饰 investors，指频繁进出、只看季度回报的短期投资者，注意不要与影响“暂时的”混淆。", "word": "transient"}, {"gloss": "推迟，延期（发放）", "note": "文中 defer performance bonuses 与第一段 delay 10 years 构成同义复现。", "word": "defer"}, {"gloss": "利益相关者，利益攸关方", "note": "区别于 shareholder（股东），指受企业决策影响的所有群体（员工、客户、社会等）。", "word": "stakeholder"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The average time for holding a stock in both the United States and Britain, he notes, has dropped from seven years to seven months in recent decades.", "point": "插入语识别与数据对比：识别 he notes，准确把握主句从 seven years 降至 seven months 的下降趋势，体现金融市场短期化。", "structure": "主语（The average time for holding a stock in both the United States and Britain）+ 插入语（he notes）+ 谓语（has dropped）+ 状语（from seven years to seven months in recent decades）。", "zh": "他指出，近几十年来，美国和英国持有股票的平均时间已从七年骤降至七个月。"}, {"en": "Within companies, the right compensation design can provide incentives for executives to think beyond their own time at the company and on behalf of all stakeholders.", "point": "介词短语并列：beyond their own time... 与 on behalf of... 共同修饰 think，点出合理薪酬机制如何引导长期治理。", "structure": "状语（Within companies）+ 主语（the right compensation design）+ 谓语（can provide）+ 宾语（incentives）+ 宾补/定语（for executives to think [beyond their own time at the company] and [on behalf of all stakeholders]）。", "zh": "在公司内部，恰当的薪酬设计能够激励高管超越自身在公司的任期限制，代表全体利益相关者去思考问题。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "动词短语转换为名词短语，高频考察责任与义务表达。", "option": "enhance bankers’ sense of responsibility", "original": "hold bankers accountable"}, {"note": "金融急躁心态即前句定义的“短视主义”。", "option": "“short-termism” in economic activities", "original": "this financial impatience"}, {"note": "“阻碍努力”对应“不利的”定性评价。", "option": "adverse", "original": "hinder a firm’s efforts"}, {"note": "措施列举与“减少短视、鼓励长期”合指促进长期主义的路径。", "option": "the approaches to promoting “long-termism”", "original": "encourage “long-termism,” such as..."}, {"note": "“立足长远、不求急功近利”在标题中凝练为企业“耐心”。", "option": "Patience as a Corporate Virtue", "original": "not just for the short term but for the long term"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2019-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2019", "examSet": "2019 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2019 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "高校“分数宽恕”与成绩膨胀", "subtitle": "教育与社会 · 高等教育消费化背景下的成绩膨胀现象", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 411, "paragraphs": ["Grade inflation—the gradual increase in average GPAs (grade-point averages) over the past few decades—is often considered a product of a consumer era in higher education, in which students are treated like customers to be pleased. But another, related force—a policy often buried deep in course catalogs called “grade forgiveness”— is helping raise GPAs.", "Grade forgiveness allows students to retake a course in which they received a low grade, and the most recent grade or the highest grade is the only one that counts in calculating a student’s overall GPA.", "The use of this little-known practice has accelerated in recent years, as colleges continue to do their utmost to keep students in school (and paying tuition) and improve their graduation rates. When this practice first started decades ago, it was usually limited to freshmen, to give them a second chance to take a class in their first year if they struggled in their transition to college-level courses. But now most colleges, save for many selective campuses, allow all undergraduates, and even graduate students, to get their low grades forgiven.", "College officials tend to emphasize that the goal of grade forgiveness is less about the grade itself and more about encouraging students to retake courses critical to their degree program and graduation without incurring a big penalty. “Ultimately,” said Jack Miner, Ohio State University’s registrar, “we see students achieve more success because they retake a course and do better in subsequent contents or master the content that allows them to graduate on time.”", "That said, there is a way in which grade forgiveness satisfies colleges’ own needs as well. For public institutions, state funds are sometimes tied partly to their success on metrics such as graduation rates and student retention—so better grades can, by boosting figures like those, mean more money. And anything that raises GPAs will likely make students—who, at the end of the day, are paying the bill—feel they’ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another big concern for colleges.", "Indeed, grade forgiveness is just another way that universities are responding to consumers’ expectations for higher education. Since students and parents expect a college degree to lead to a job, it is in the best interest of a school to turn out graduates who are as qualified as possible—or at least appear to be. On this, students’ and colleges’ incentives seem to be aligned."], "translations": ["成绩膨胀——即过去几十年间平均绩点的逐步攀升——通常被视为高等教育消费时代的产物，在这个时代里，学生被当作需要取悦的顾客来对待。但另一股相关力量——一项常常深藏在课程目录中、被称为“分数宽恕”的政策——也在推高平均绩点。", "“分数宽恕”允许学生重修曾获低分的课程，在计算学生总绩点时，仅计入最新一次成绩或最高成绩。", "近年来，这种鲜为人知的做法加速普及，因为高校正竭尽全力留住学生（让他们继续缴纳学费）并提高毕业率。几十年前这项做法刚起步时，通常仅限于大一新生，以便他们在大一适应大学水平课程的过渡期内遇到困难时能有第二次机会。但如今，除了许多录取严苛的名校之外，大多数高校都允许所有本科生甚至研究生洗掉低分记录。", "高校官员往往强调，“分数宽恕”的目的与其说是分数本身，不如说是鼓励学生重修对其学位项目和毕业至关重要的课程，而不致遭受沉重的成绩惩罚。“归根结底，”俄亥俄州立大学教务长杰克·迈纳说，“我们看到学生取得了更大成功，因为他们重修一门课后，在后续课程中表现更好，或者掌握了能让他们按时毕业的知识内容。”", "话虽如此，“分数宽恕”在某种程度上也满足了高校自身的需求。对于公立院校而言，州政府拨款有时部分与毕业率和学生保留率等指标的成绩挂钩——因此，更高的成绩通过推高这类数据，也就意味着更多的资金。而且，任何能提高绩点的做法，都很可能让归根结底在掏钱买单的学生觉得自己的学费更值，而这正是高校关心的另一大问题。", "事实上，“分数宽恕”只是高校回应消费者对高等教育期待的又一种方式。既然学生和家长都期望大学学位能带来一份工作，那么培养出尽可能合格——或者至少看起来合格——的毕业生就最符合学校的利益。在这一点上，学生和高校的动机似乎高度一致。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is commonly regarded as the cause of grade inflation?", "options": ["The change of course catalogs.", "Students’ indifference to GPAs.", "Colleges’ neglect of GPAs.", "The influence of consumer culture."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Grade inflation—the gradual increase in average GPAs (grade-point averages) over the past few decades—is often considered a product of a consumer era in higher education, in which students are treated like customers to be pleased.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，询问人们普遍认为的“成绩膨胀”成因。第一段首句指出，过去几十年平均绩点逐步上升的“成绩膨胀”现象“is often considered a product of a consumer era in higher education”，即高等教育消费时代的产物（学生被当作需要取悦的顾客）。D项“The influence of consumer culture”（消费文化的影响）准确对应“product of a consumer era”，故选D。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：A项偷换概念，课程目录中只是隐藏着“分数宽恕”这一另一推力，并非目录本身的变化导致成绩膨胀；B、C项均与文中师生看重GPA的事实正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What was the original purpose of grade forgiveness?", "options": ["To help freshmen adapt to college learning.", "To maintain colleges’ graduation rates.", "To prepare graduates for a challenging future.", "To increase universities’ income from tuition."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "When this practice first started decades ago, it was usually limited to freshmen, to give them a second chance to take a class in their first year if they struggled in their transition to college-level courses.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，考查“分数宽恕”政策最初的目的。定位第三段第二句“When this practice first started decades ago, it was usually limited to freshmen, to give them a second chance to take a class in their first year if they struggled in their transition to college-level courses.”。句中“in their transition to college-level courses”指大一新生向大学水平课程过渡时的适应过程，对应A项“help freshmen adapt to college learning”，故选A。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：B、D项属时空错位（偷换时间），维持毕业率与留住学生交学费是“近年来（in recent years）”加速推行该做法的原因，而非几十年前最初创立时的目的。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to", "options": ["obtain more financial support.", "boost their student enrollments.", "improve their teaching quality.", "meet local governments’ needs."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "For public institutions, state funds are sometimes tied partly to their success on metrics such as graduation rates and student retention—so better grades can, by boosting figures like those, mean more money.", "explanation": "本题为细节题，定位第五段。第二句指出，对于公立院校而言，州政府拨款有时部分与毕业率和学生保留率等指标挂钩，因此更好的成绩通过推高这些数据就能“mean more money”（带来更多资金）。这说明“分数宽恕”有助于高校获得更多财政支持，与A项“obtain more financial support”直接对应，故选A。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：B项偷换概念，原文提及的是 student retention（学生保留率，即不退学），而非扩大招生规模（enrollments）；D项过度推理，是州拨款依据这些指标，并非满足地方政府需求。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "词义题", "stem": "What does the phrase “to be aligned”(Line 5, Para. 6) most probably mean?", "options": ["To counterbalance each other.", "To complement each other.", "To be identical with each other.", "To be contradictory to each other."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Since students and parents expect a college degree to lead to a job, it is in the best interest of a school to turn out graduates who are as qualified as possible—or at least appear to be. On this, students’ and colleges’ incentives seem to be aligned.", "explanation": "本题为词义题，考查第六段中“to be aligned”的含义。前句指出学生和家长希望大学学位能带来好工作，而培养看起来尽可能合格的毕业生也最符合学校自身利益（in the best interest of a school）。“On this”（在这一点上）承接前文，说明学生与高校的动机方向完全一致、利益吻合。C项“To be identical with each other”（彼此一致）最贴合语境，故选C。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：B项“相互补充”极具迷惑性，但前文说的是双方共同追求“毕业生显得合格”这一相同目标，强调诉求重合而非互补；A“相互制衡”与D“相互矛盾”均与文意正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "The author examines the practice of grade forgiveness by", "options": ["assessing its feasibility.", "analyzing the causes behind it.", "comparing different views on it.", "listing its long-run effects."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "That said, there is a way in which grade forgiveness satisfies colleges’ own needs as well.", "explanation": "本题为主旨题（写作手法题），考查作者剖析“分数宽恕”的方式。全文首先定义该政策（第二段），接着探讨近年来该做法普及的原因（第三段：留住学生交学费、提高毕业率），第四段呈现校方官方解释（鼓励重修关键课程），第五、六段进一步揭示深层动因（满足公立拨款指标、迎合学生学费性价比诉求及就业期待）。可见全篇重在剖析其背后的多重原因，故选B。", "trapNote": "干扰项分析：C项以偏概全，文章虽提及校方说法与深层动因的差异，但本质上是挖掘驱动该政策普及的多重原因，而非对比各方观点；A项“评估可行性”和D项“列举长期影响”均非文章主线。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "（成绩）膨胀；通货膨胀", "note": "文中 grade inflation 指高校平均绩点普遍虚高，与第四段 incur a penalty（受罚）等评价性表达呼应。", "word": "inflation"}, {"gloss": "保留，留存（率）", "note": "文中 student retention 指学生继续留校就读而不退学的比率，切勿与 enrollment（招生）混淆。", "word": "retention"}, {"gloss": "除了……之外（表排除）", "note": "熟词僻义：save 作介词相当于 except，如 save for many selective campuses（除许多挑剔的精英大学外）。", "word": "save"}, {"gloss": "招致，遭受（惩罚、损失等）", "note": "常与 penalty、cost、debt 搭配，文中 without incurring a big penalty 意为“不致遭受严厉扣分惩罚”。", "word": "incur"}, {"gloss": "（使）一致，对齐；结盟", "note": "第六段核心词，熟词常考“利益/动机保持一致”。", "word": "align"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Grade inflation—the gradual increase in average GPAs (grade-point averages) over the past few decades—is often considered a product of a consumer era in higher education, in which students are treated like customers to be pleased.", "point": "破折号同位语与非限制性定语从句：双破折号解释核心概念 grade inflation，in which 引导定语从句揭示“消费时代”的具体内涵。", "structure": "主语（Grade inflation）+ 插入同位语（—the gradual increase...—）+ 谓语（is often considered）+ 宾补（a product of a consumer era in higher education）+ 定语从句（in which students are treated like customers to be pleased）。", "zh": "成绩膨胀——即过去几十年间平均绩点的逐步攀升——通常被视为高等教育消费时代的产物，在这个时代里，学生被当作需要取悦的顾客来对待。"}, {"en": "And anything that raises GPAs will likely make students—who, at the end of the day, are paying the bill—feel they’ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another big concern for colleges.", "point": "多层嵌套结构：make sb. do 复合结构中夹杂定语从句插入语（who...），句末 which 指代“让学生觉得学费物有所值”这一整件事。", "structure": "主语（anything that raises GPAs）+ 谓语（will likely make）+ 宾语（students）+ 插入定语从句（—who, at the end of the day, are paying the bill—）+ 宾补（feel they’ve gotten...）+ 非限制性定语从句（which is another big concern for colleges）。", "zh": "任何能提高绩点的做法，都很可能让归根结底在掏钱买单的学生觉得自己的学费更值，而这正是高校关心的另一大问题。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“消费时代的产物”在选项中凝练为“消费文化的影响”。", "option": "The influence of consumer culture", "original": "a product of a consumer era"}, {"note": "“适应大学课程过渡期”即“适应大学学习”。", "option": "adapt to college learning", "original": "transition to college-level courses"}, {"note": "“意味着更多资金”同义替换为“获得更多财政支持”。", "option": "obtain more financial support", "original": "mean more money"}, {"note": "双方利益与目标方向重合即“彼此一致”。", "option": "To be identical with each other", "original": "to be aligned"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2019-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2019", "examSet": "2019 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2019 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "AI 伦理困境：复杂但必然的探索", "subtitle": "科技伦理 · 人工智能的意识难题与全球治理规制", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 440, "paragraphs": ["This year marks exactly two centuries since the publication of “Frankenstein; or, The Modern Prometheus,” by Mary Shelley. Even before the invention of the electric light bulb, the author produced a remarkable work of speculative fiction that would foreshadow many ethical questions to be raised by technologies yet to come.", "Today the rapid growth of artificial intelligence (AI) raises fundamental questions: “What is intelligence, identity, or consciousness? What makes humans humans?”", "What is being called artificial general intelligence, machines that would imitate the way humans think, continues to evade scientists. Yet humans remain fascinated by the idea of robots that would look, move, and respond like humans, similar to those recently depicted on popular sci-fi TV series such as “Westworld” and “Humans”.", "Just how people think is still far too complex to be understood, let alone reproduced, says David Eagleman, a Stanford University neuroscientist. “We are just in a situation where there are no good theories explaining what consciousness actually is and how you could ever build a machine to get there.”", "But that doesn’t mean crucial ethical issues involving AI aren’t at hand. The coming use of autonomous vehicles, for example, poses thorny ethical questions. Human drivers sometimes must make split-second decisions. Their reactions may be a complex combination of instant reflexes, input from past driving experiences, and what their eyes and ears tell them in that moment. AI “vision” today is not nearly as sophisticated as that of humans. And to anticipate every imaginable driving situation is a difficult programming problem.", "Whenever decisions are based on masses of data, “you quickly get into a lot of ethical questions,” notes Tan Kiat How, chief executive of a Singapore-based agency that is helping the government develop a voluntary code for the ethical use of AI. Along with Singapore, other governments and mega-corporations are beginning to establish their own guidelines. Britain is setting up a data ethics center. India released its AI ethics strategy this spring.", "On June 7 Google pledged not to “design or deploy AI” that would cause “overall harm,” or to develop AI-directed weapons or use AI for surveillance that would violate international norms. It also pledged not to deploy AI whose use would violate international laws or human rights.", "While the statement is vague, it represents one starting point. So does the idea that decisions made by AI systems should be explainable, transparent, and fair.", "To put it another way: How can we make sure that the thinking of intelligent machines reflects humanity’s highest values? Only then will they be useful servants and not Frankenstein’s out-of-control monster."], "translations": ["今年距离玛丽·雪莱出版《弗兰肯斯坦：或现代普罗米修斯》恰好整整两个世纪。甚至在电灯泡发明之前，这位作者就创作出了一部非凡的推理科幻作品，预示了未来技术将引发的诸多伦理问题。", "如今，人工智能（AI）的迅速发展引发了一些根本性的问题：“什么是智能、身份或意识？是什么让人类成为人类？”", "所谓的通用人工智能——即模仿人类思维方式的机器——仍然让科学家们束手无策。然而，人类依然对能够像人一样外观、行动和回应的机器人着迷，就像近期热门科幻剧集《西部世界》和《真实的人类》中所描绘的那样。", "斯坦福大学神经科学家大卫·伊格尔曼表示，人类究竟如何思考至今仍过于复杂而无法理解，更不用说复制了。“我们正处于这样一种境地：目前还没有良好的理论能够解释意识究竟是什么，以及究竟如何制造一台机器来达到那种境界。”", "但这并不意味着涉及人工智能的紧迫伦理问题尚未摆在眼前。例如，即将投入使用的自动驾驶汽车就带来了棘手的伦理问题。人类驾驶员有时必须在一瞬间做出决定，他们的反应可能是即时反射、过往驾驶经验以及当时眼耳所获信息的复杂结合。如今人工智能的“视觉”远不如人类精密，而且要预判每一种可能想象得到的驾驶场景，是一个十分困难的编程难题。", "每当决策基于海量数据时，“你很快就会陷入大量的伦理问题之中，”陈杰豪指出。他是新加坡一家机构的首席执行官，该机构正协助政府制定一份合乎伦理使用人工智能的自愿准则。除新加坡外，其他国家政府和大型跨国企业也开始制定各自的指导方针。英国正在设立一个数据伦理中心，印度也在今年春季发布了其人工智能伦理战略。", "6月7日，谷歌承诺不会“设计或部署”会造成“整体伤害”的人工智能，也不会研发人工智能制导武器或将人工智能用于违反国际准则的监控活动。它还承诺不会部署其用途违反国际法或人权的人工智能。", "尽管这份声明尚显含糊，但它代表了一个起点；正如“人工智能系统做出的决策应当具有可解释性、透明度和公平性”这一理念一样。", "换言之：我们如何才能确保智能机器的思考能够反映人类最崇高的价值观？唯有如此，它们才会成为有用的仆人，而不是弗兰肯斯坦手下那头失控的怪物。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Mary Shelley’s novel Frankenstein is mentioned because it", "options": ["fascinates AI scientists all over the world.", "has remained popular for as long as 200 years.", "involves some concerns raised by AI today.", "has sparked serious ethical controversies"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Even before the invention of the electric light bulb, the author produced a remarkable work of speculative fiction that would foreshadow many ethical questions to be raised by technologies yet to come.", "explanation": "题干询问首段提及小说《弗兰肯斯坦》的原因，属于典型的例证/写作目的题。首段指出该小说预示了未来科技将引发的诸多伦理问题（foreshadow many ethical questions to be raised by technologies yet to come），紧接着第二段即点出当今人工智能（AI）的快速发展正引发此类根本性问题。C项“它涉及当今人工智能引发的一些担忧”准确概括了例子的引入作用，其中concerns对应ethical questions。", "trapNote": "A项“令全球AI科学家着迷”将第三段人们对类人机器人的着迷偷换给小说；B项“畅销两百年”是对首句出版两百周年的过度推理；D项“引发激烈伦理争议”在文中无依据，小说只是“预示”问题而非引发争议。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "In David Eagleman’s opinion, our current knowledge of consciousness", "options": ["helps explain artificial intelligence.", "can be misleading to robot making.", "inspires popular sci-fi TV series.", "is too limited for us to reproduce it"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Just how people think is still far too complex to be understood, let alone reproduced, says David Eagleman, a Stanford University neuroscientist.", "explanation": "定位至第四段斯坦福大学神经科学家David Eagleman的观点。原文指出人类如何思考仍太过复杂而难以被理解，更不用说去复制它（far too complex to be understood, let alone reproduced），且目前缺乏解释意识本质及如何制造机器来获得意识的理论。D项“过于有限以至于我们无法复制它”精准对应原文“难以理解、更遑论复制”的语义，属于同义转述。", "trapNote": "A项“有助于解释AI”与原文“没有好理论能解释意识本质”正反颠倒；B项“误导机器人制造”属于无中生有；C项“启发热门科幻剧”张冠李戴，科幻剧出现在第三段且与Eagleman无关。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "The solution to the ethical issues brought by autonomous vehicles", "options": ["can hardly ever be found.", "is still beyond our capacity.", "causes little public concern.", "has aroused much curiosity."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "AI “vision” today is not nearly as sophisticated as that of humans. And to anticipate every imaginable driving situation is a difficult programming problem.", "explanation": "定位至第五段自动驾驶汽车（autonomous vehicles）的例子。原文先指出其带来了棘手的伦理问题，随后解释原因：人类驾驶员依靠瞬间反应、驾驶经验和感官综合做出毫秒级决策，而如今AI的“视觉”远不如人类精密，且预判所有可能的驾驶场景是一个困难的编程难题。由此可推知，目前解决此类伦理问题仍超出我们的技术能力范围，对应B项。", "trapNote": "A项“几乎永远无法找到”过于绝对，原文只说目前AI技术不足且编程困难，并非永久无解，属于过度推理；C项“很少引起公众关注”与crucial ethical issues相悖；D项“引发强烈好奇”偷换了第三段人们对人形机器人的好奇。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author’s attitude toward Google’s pledges is one of", "options": ["affirmation", "skepticism.", "contempt", "respect."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "While the statement is vague, it represents one starting point.", "explanation": "第七段介绍了谷歌承诺不设计或部署造成总体伤害或违反国际法与人权的AI，第八段直接给出作者的评价：“虽然该声明尚显含糊，但它代表了一个起点”（While the statement is vague, it represents one starting point）。由while引导的让步状语从句可知，作者重点肯定了谷歌此举作为“起点”的积极意义，因此态度是肯定的（affirmation），对应A项。", "trapNote": "B项“怀疑”只片面抓住了让步从句中的vague，忽略了主句的正面肯定，属于以偏概全；C项“轻蔑”明显偏离作者温和客观的基调；D项“尊敬”感情色彩过重，作者只是客观认可其作为起点的积极作用，并非表达敬意。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the text?", "options": ["AI’s Future: In the Hands of Tech Giants", "Frankenstein, the Novel Predicting the Age of AI", "The Conscience of AI: Complex But Inevitable", "AI Shall Be Killers Once Out of Control"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 9, "evidenceQuote": "How can we make sure that the thinking of intelligent machines reflects humanity’s highest values?", "explanation": "本题考查全文主旨。文章以《弗兰肯斯坦》开篇引出科技伦理议题，接着指出人类对意识与通用AI尚难企及，但自动驾驶等领域的AI伦理问题迫在眉睫；后半部分讲述新加坡、英国、印度及谷歌等政府与巨头着手制定AI伦理准则，末段再次强调必须确保智能机器反映人类最高价值。C项“AI的良知：复杂但不可回避”全面概括了“复杂性”与“制定伦理的必然性”，为最佳标题。", "trapNote": "A项“AI未来掌握在科技巨头手中”仅片面提及谷歌等企业，忽视了多国政府及伦理核心，属于以偏概全；B项“预言AI时代的小说”只是首段引入手段；D项“AI一旦失控将成为杀手”属于极端化表述，与末段呼吁规制的主旨不符。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "预示，成为……的先兆", "note": "熟词高频：由fore-（预先）+shadow（影子）构成，常用于引出后文历史或现实话题的铺垫句中。", "word": "foreshadow"}, {"gloss": "躲避，使……困惑；难倒", "note": "考研核心词：文中continues to evade scientists指通用人工智能“依然让科学家束手无策/难以实现”。", "word": "evade"}, {"gloss": "（时间）极短的，一刹那的", "note": "复合形容词：split-second decisions意为“毫秒级/瞬间做出的决定”，常修饰决定、反应等名词。", "word": "split-second"}, {"gloss": "棘手的，令人苦恼的", "note": "熟词僻义：本义为“多刺的”，考研阅读中常引申为“（问题等）棘手的、复杂的”，如thorny ethical questions。", "word": "thorny"}, {"gloss": "自愿的，自觉遵守的", "note": "语境辨析：文中a voluntary code指非强制性的“自律准则”，与后文法律形成对比。", "word": "voluntary"}, {"gloss": "承诺，保证；誓言", "note": "一词多义：文中作动词表示“郑重承诺”（pledged not to），也可作名词表示“承诺、誓言”。", "word": "pledge"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Even before the invention of the electric light bulb, the author produced a remarkable work of speculative fiction that would foreshadow many ethical questions to be raised by technologies yet to come.", "point": "由that引导的定语从句嵌套过去分词短语作后置定语，其中yet to come表示“尚未到来/未来的”。", "structure": "时间状语 + 主句(the author produced a remarkable work...) + that定语从句(修饰work) + 不定式被动结构to be raised作后置定语(修饰questions)", "zh": "甚至在电灯泡发明之前，这位作者就创作出了一部非凡的推理科幻作品，预示了未来技术将引发的诸多伦理问题。"}, {"en": "Whenever decisions are based on masses of data, “you quickly get into a lot of ethical questions,” notes Tan Kiat How, chief executive of a Singapore-based agency that is helping the government develop a voluntary code for the ethical use of AI.", "point": "注意“引语前置+倒装主句+同位语+定语从句”的典型外刊新闻报道句式，需快速剥离主干notes Tan Kiat How。", "structure": "时间状语从句(Whenever...) + 宾语引语 + 倒装主句(notes Tan Kiat How) + 同位语(chief executive...) + that定语从句(修饰agency)", "zh": "陈杰豪指出，每当决策基于海量数据时，“你很快就会陷入大量的伦理问题之中”；他是新加坡一家机构的首席执行官，该机构正协助政府制定一份合乎伦理使用人工智能的自愿准则。"}, {"en": "On June 7 Google pledged not to “design or deploy AI” that would cause “overall harm,” or to develop AI-directed weapons or use AI for surveillance that would violate international norms.", "point": "识别not to do A or to do B or do C的并列不定式结构，同时区分两个that定语从句各自的先行词（AI与surveillance）。", "structure": "时间状语 + 主谓(Google pledged) + 并列不定式宾语(not to design/deploy... or to develop... or use...) + 两个that定语从句", "zh": "6月7日，谷歌承诺不会“设计或部署”会造成“整体伤害”的人工智能，也不会研发人工智能制导武器或将人工智能用于违反国际准则的监控活动。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "原文以“预兆未来的伦理问题”引出下文AI议题，选项用concerns（担忧）替换ethical questions。", "option": "involves some concerns raised by AI today", "original": "foreshadow many ethical questions to be raised by technologies yet to come"}, {"note": "“太复杂以至于无法理解，更不用说复制”精准转述为“知识过于有限而无法复制”。", "option": "is too limited for us to reproduce it", "original": "is still far too complex to be understood, let alone reproduced"}, {"note": "AI视觉不如人类精密且编程困难，等价于问题解决“仍超出当前能力”。", "option": "is still beyond our capacity", "original": "not nearly as sophisticated as that of humans... difficult programming problem"}, {"note": "作者在让步后强调谷歌声明“代表了一个起点”，体现出对其做法的肯定（affirmation）。", "option": "affirmation", "original": "represents one starting point"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2019-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2019", "examSet": "2019 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2019 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "美国网购销售税新政与市场博弈", "subtitle": "司法与经济 · 美国最高法院网购征税新政及多方博弈", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 459, "paragraphs": ["States will be able to force more people to pay sales tax when they make online purchases under a Supreme Court decision Thursday that will leave shoppers with lighter wallets but is a big financial win for states.", "The Supreme Court’s opinion Thursday overruled a pair of decades-old decisions that states said cost them billions of dollars in lost revenue annually. The decisions made it more difficult for states to collect sales tax on certain online purchases.", "The cases the court overturned said that if a business was shipping a customer’s purchase to a state where the business didn’t have a physical presence such as a warehouse or office, the business didn’t have to collect sales tax for the state. Customers were generally responsible for paying the sales tax to the state themselves if they weren’t charged it, but most didn’t realize they owed it and few paid.", "Justice Anthony Kennedy wrote that the previous decisions were flawed. “Each year the physical presence rule becomes further removed from economic reality and results in significant revenue losses to the States,” he wrote in an opinion joined by four other justices. Kennedy wrote that the rule “limited states’ ability to seek long-term prosperity and has prevented market participants from competing on an even playing field.”", "The ruling is a victory for big chains with a presence in many states, since they usually collect sales tax on online purchases already. Now, rivals will be charging sales tax where they hadn’t before. Big chains have been collecting sales tax nationwide because they typically have physical stores in whatever state a purchase is being shipped to. Amazon.com, with its network of warehouses, also collects sales tax in every state that charges it, though third-party sellers who use the site don’t have to.", "Until now, many sellers that have a physical presence in only a single state or a few states have been able to avoid charging sales taxes when they ship to addresses outside those states. Sellers that use eBay and Etsy, which provide platforms for smaller sellers, also haven’t been collecting sales tax nationwide. Under the ruling Thursday, states can pass laws requiring out-of-state sellers to collect the state’s sales tax from customers and send it to the state.", "Retail trade groups praised the ruling, saying it levels the playing field for local and online businesses. The losers, said retail analyst Neil Saunders, are online-only retailers, especially smaller ones. Those retailers may face headaches complying with various state sales tax laws. The Small Business & Entrepreneurship Council advocacy group said in a statement, “Small businesses and internet entrepreneurs are not well served at all by this decision.”"], "translations": ["根据最高法院周四做出的一项裁决，各州将能够强制更多人在网购时缴纳销售税；这一裁决会让消费者的钱包缩水，但对各州而言却是一场重大的财政胜利。", "最高法院周四的裁决意见推翻了两项存在了数十年的旧判例，各州曾表示这些判例每年给它们造成了数十亿美元的税收损失。那些判例使得各州更难对某些网购交易征收销售税。", "法院推翻的那些先例曾规定，如果一家企业将顾客购买的商品运往该企业没有仓库或办公室等实体存在的州，该企业就不必为该州代收销售税。如果企业未向顾客收取，顾客通常有责任自行向所在州缴纳销售税，但大多数人并未意识到自己有此纳税义务，真正缴纳的人寥寥无几。", "大法官安东尼·肯尼迪撰文指出，先前的判例存在缺陷。“每一年，‘实体存在规则’都进一步脱离经济现实，并给各州带来巨额财政收入损失，”他在一份获得另外四位大法官赞同的意见书中写道。肯尼迪还写道，该规则“限制了各州寻求长期繁荣的能力，并阻碍了市场参与者在公平的环境下开展竞争。”", "这项裁决对于在多个州设有实体门店的大型连锁企业而言是一场胜利，因为它们通常已经在对网购商品代收销售税了。如今，其竞争对手也将在此前未征税的地区开始代收销售税。大型连锁企业一直在全美范围内代收销售税，因为不管商品运往哪个州，它们通常都在当地设有实体店。拥有庞大仓库网络的亚马逊公司也在每一个开征销售税的州代收税款，不过使用该网站的第三方卖家此前不必这么做。", "在此之前，许多仅在单个州或少数几个州设有实体机构的卖家，在向这些州以外的地址发货时，一直能够避开征收销售税。使用eBay和Etsy等为小卖家提供交易平台的商家，此前也未在全美范围内代收销售税。根据周四的裁决，各州可以立法要求州外卖家向顾客代收该州的销售税并上缴给州政府。", "零售业贸易团体对这一裁决表示赞赏，称它为实体零售商和在线商家拉平了竞争环境。零售业分析师尼尔·桑德斯表示，输家则是纯线上零售商，尤其是小型网店。这些零售商在遵守各州不同的销售税法方面可能会面临令人头疼的难题。小企业与创业委员会这一倡议团体在一份声明中称：“这项裁决对小企业和互联网创业者来说极其不利。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The Supreme Court decision Thursday will", "options": ["better business’ relations with states.", "put most online business in a dilemma.", "make more online shoppers pay sales tax.", "force some states to cut sales tax."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "States will be able to force more people to pay sales tax when they make online purchases under a Supreme Court decision Thursday that will leave shoppers with lighter wallets but is a big financial win for states.", "explanation": "题干询问最高法院周四裁决的影响，直接定位第一段首句。原文明确指出，根据最高法院周四的裁决，各州将能够强制更多人在网购时缴纳销售税（force more people to pay sales tax when they make online purchases），这将使消费者荷包变瘪但让各州获得巨大的财政收益。C项“让更多网购者缴纳销售税”是对原文核心信息的直接复现与精炼转述。", "trapNote": "A项“改善企业与各州的关系”在文中未提及，裁决反而让跨州小商家面临合规麻烦；B项“使大多数电商陷入困境”将末段“纯网店尤其是小商家”偷换为“大多数”；D项“迫使各州减税”与各州扩大征税权正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be learned from paragraphs 2 and 3 that the overruled decisions", "options": ["have led to the dominance of e-commerce.", "have cost consumers a lot over the years.", "were widely criticized by online purchasers.", "were considered unfavorable by states."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The Supreme Court’s opinion Thursday overruled a pair of decades-old decisions that states said cost them billions of dollars in lost revenue annually.", "explanation": "定位至第二段和第三段。第二段提到，最高法院推翻了两项延续数十年的旧裁决，各州表示这些旧裁决每年给它们造成了数十亿美元的税收损失（cost them billions of dollars in lost revenue annually），并使各州更难对某些网购征收销售税。第三段进一步解释消费者很少主动补缴。由此可推断，各州认为这些被推翻的旧裁决对其非常不利，对应D项。", "trapNote": "A项“导致电商占主导地位”属于过度推理，原文未提及电商主导地位；B项“多年来让消费者付出高昂代价”与原文相反，消费者过去大多没交税从而省了钱；C项“遭到网购者广泛批评”属于无中生有且与常理相悖。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Justice Anthony Kennedy, the physical presence rule has", "options": ["hindered economic development.", "brought prosperity to the country.", "harmed fair market competition.", "boosted growth in states’ revenue."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Kennedy wrote that the rule “limited states’ ability to seek long-term prosperity and has prevented market participants from competing on an even playing field.”", "explanation": "定位至第四段安东尼·肯尼迪大法官的观点。原文指出“实体存在规则”限制了各州寻求长期繁荣的能力，并且阻碍了市场参与者在一个公平的竞争环境中开展竞争（prevented market participants from competing on an even playing field）。C项“损害了公平的市场竞争”精准对应“阻止市场参与者在公平环境中竞争”，属于高频同义替换。", "trapNote": "A项“阻碍经济发展”范围过大，原文限定为“限制各州寻求长期繁荣的能力”，属于概念偷换与扩大；B项“带来国家繁荣”及D项“促进各州税收增长”均与原文“税收损失”和“限制繁荣”正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Who are most likely to welcome the Supreme Court ruling?", "options": ["Internet entrepreneurs.", "Big-chain owners.", "Third-party sellers.", "Small retailers."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The ruling is a victory for big chains with a presence in many states, since they usually collect sales tax on online purchases already.", "explanation": "定位至第五段。原文开篇即点明，这项裁决对在多州设有实体店的大型连锁企业而言是一场胜利（The ruling is a victory for big chains with a presence in many states），因为它们通常已经在代收网购销售税，如今竞争对手也必须开始征税。因此大型连锁企业主最可能欢迎该裁决，B项“大型连锁店老板”完全符合文意。", "trapNote": "A项“互联网创业者”和D项“小零售商”在第七段均被明确列为裁决的“输家”或利益受损者；C项“第三方卖家”在第五段末与第六段指出此前无需全国征税，新政后将面临纳税合规压力，不会欢迎此裁决。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "In dealing with the Supreme Court decision Thursday, the author", "options": ["gives a factual account of it and discusses its consequences.", "describes the long and complicated process of its making.", "presents its main points with conflicting views on them.", "cites some cases related to it and analyzes their implications."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "States will be able to force more people to pay sales tax when they make online purchases under a Supreme Court decision Thursday that will leave shoppers with lighter wallets but is a big financial win for states.", "explanation": "本题考查文章行文结构与写作手法。首段客观陈述周四最高法院裁决的内容及直接影响；二至四段交代被推翻的旧判例背景及大法官肯尼迪的意见；五至七段具体分析该裁决对大型连锁、电商平台、小零售商及消费者等不同市场主体的后果。全文客观中立，既如实报道裁决内容又剖析其各方影响，对应A项。", "trapNote": "B项“描述其漫长复杂的制定过程”无中生有，全文未写裁决诞生过程；C项“呈现实质要点及矛盾观点”不准确，文中主要呈现各利益方的得失后果而非针锋相对的法理辩论；D项“援引相关案例”以偏概全，只在前文背景提及被推翻的旧案。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "推翻，驳回（上级法院或权威裁决）", "note": "法律高频词：常用于司法语境，文中overruled a pair of decisions与第三段的overturned构成同义替换。", "word": "overrule"}, {"gloss": "有缺陷的，有错误的", "note": "阅读高频评价词：flawed意为“有瑕疵的”，表明大法官对旧判例的否定态度。", "word": "flawed"}, {"gloss": "使……处于同等地位；拉平（竞争环境）", "note": "熟词僻义：level作动词表示“使平坦、拉平”，level the playing field为高频习语，意为“营造公平的竞争环境”。", "word": "level"}, {"gloss": "遵守，顺从（法规、要求等）", "note": "固定搭配：comply with常用于商业和法律语篇，文中complying with various state sales tax laws指“遵守各州不同的销售税法”。", "word": "comply"}, {"gloss": "利益倡导组织，游说团体", "note": "外刊高频词：advocacy group指代表特定群体发声并游说立法的组织，文中指中小企业权益倡导组织。", "word": "advocacy group"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "States will be able to force more people to pay sales tax when they make online purchases under a Supreme Court decision Thursday that will leave shoppers with lighter wallets but is a big financial win for states.", "point": "注意定语从句修饰decision，其中but连接两个并列谓语，形象地用lighter wallets比喻消费者支出增加。", "structure": "主句(States will be able to force...) + 时间状语从句(when...) + 方式状语(under a Supreme Court decision) + that定语从句(修饰decision)", "zh": "根据最高法院周四做出的一项裁决，各州将能够强制更多人在网购时缴纳销售税；这一裁决会让消费者的钱包缩水，但对各州而言却是一场重大的财政胜利。"}, {"en": "The cases the court overturned said that if a business was shipping a customer’s purchase to a state where the business didn’t have a physical presence such as a warehouse or office, the business didn’t have to collect sales tax for the state.", "point": "多层嵌套结构：省略关系代词的定语从句修饰cases，宾语从句中又嵌套if条件从句与where地点定语从句。", "structure": "主语(The cases) + 省略that的定语从句(the court overturned) + 谓语(said) + that宾语从句[if条件从句(包含where定语从句) + 从句主干]", "zh": "法院推翻的那些先例曾规定，如果一家企业将顾客购买的商品运往该企业没有仓库或办公室等实体存在的州，该企业就不必为该州代收销售税。"}, {"en": "Until now, many sellers that have a physical presence in only a single state or a few states have been able to avoid charging sales taxes when they ship to addresses outside those states.", "point": "长主语包含that定语从句修饰sellers，谓语采用现在完成时体现截止目前一直持续的状态，后接when时间状语从句。", "structure": "时间状语(Until now) + 主语(many sellers) + that定语从句 + 谓语(have been able to avoid...) + when时间状语从句", "zh": "在此之前，许多仅在单个州或少数几个州设有实体机构的卖家，在向这些州以外的地址发货时，一直能够避开征收销售税。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“实体存在规则阻止市场参与者在公平环境中竞争”直接转述为“损害了公平的市场竞争”。", "option": "harmed fair market competition", "original": "prevented market participants from competing on an even playing field"}, {"note": "“在多州设有实体店的大型连锁企业”转述为选项中的“大型连锁店老板”。", "option": "Big-chain owners", "original": "big chains with a presence in many states"}, {"note": "“各州称旧裁决每年令其损失数十亿美元税收”表明各州认为旧裁决对其不利。", "option": "were considered unfavorable by states", "original": "states said cost them billions of dollars in lost revenue annually"}, {"note": "“使更多人网购时被迫缴纳销售税”精炼概括为“让更多网购者缴纳销售税”。", "option": "make more online shoppers pay sales tax", "original": "force more people to pay sales tax when they make online purchases"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2018-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2018", "examSet": "2018 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2018 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "自动化冲击中产就业与应对之策", "subtitle": "科技变革 · 中产岗位替代 · 教育与财税应对", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 453, "paragraphs": ["Among the annoying challenges facing the middle class is one that will probably go unmentioned in the next presidential campaign: What happens when the robots come for their jobs?", "Don't dismiss that possibility entirely. About half of U.S. jobs are at high risk of being automated, according to a University of Oxford study, with the middle class disproportionately squeezed. Lower-income jobs like gardening or day care don't appeal to robots. But many middle-class occupations — trucking, financial advice, software engineering — have aroused their interest, or soon will. The rich own the robots, so they will be fine.", "This isn't to be alarmist. Optimists point out that technological upheaval has benefited workers in the past. The Industrial Revolution didn't go so well for Luddites whose jobs were displaced by mechanized looms, but it eventually raised living standards and created more jobs than it destroyed. Likewise, automation should eventually boost productivity, stimulate demand by driving down prices, and free workers from hard, boring work. But in the medium term, middle-class workers may need a lot of help adjusting.", "The first step, as Erik Brynjolfsson and Andrew McAfee argue in The Second Machine Age, should be rethinking education and job training. Curriculums — from grammar school to college — should evolve to focus less on memorizing facts and more on creativity and complex communication. Vocational schools should do a better job of fostering problem-solving skills and helping students work alongside robots. Online education can supplement the traditional kind. It could make extra training and instruction affordable. Professionals trying to acquire new skills will be able to do so without going into debt.", "The challenge of coping with automation underlines the need for the U.S. to revive its fading business dynamism: Starting new companies must be made easier. In previous eras of drastic technological change, entrepreneurs smoothed the transition by dreaming up ways to combine labor and machines. The best uses of 3D printers and virtual reality haven't been invented yet. The U.S. needs the new companies that will invent them.", "Finally, because automation threatens to widen the gap between capital income and labor income, taxes and the safety net will have to be rethought. Taxes on low-wage labor need to be cut, and wage subsidies such as the earned income tax credit should be expanded: This would boost incomes, encourage work, reward companies for job creation, and reduce inequality.", "Technology will improve society in ways big and small over the next few years, yet this will be little comfort to those who find their lives and careers upended by automation. Destroying the machines that are coming for our jobs would be nuts. But policies to help workers adapt will be indispensable."], "translations": ["在中产阶级面临的诸多棘手挑战中，有一个问题在下届总统大选中可能会被只字不提：当机器人来抢走他们的饭碗时，会发生什么？", "千万别完全排除这种可能性。牛津大学的一项研究表明，美国约半数工作面临高度自动化的风险，其中中产阶级受到的挤压尤为严重。园艺或日托这类低收入工作对机器人没什么吸引力。但卡车运输、金融顾问、软件工程等许多中产阶级职业已经引起了机器人的“兴趣”，或者很快就会如此。富人拥有机器人，所以他们将安然无恙。", "这并非危言耸听。乐观主义者指出，过去的技术变革曾让劳动者受益。对于那些工作被机械化织布机取代的“卢德分子”而言，工业革命的滋味并不好受，但它最终提高了生活水平，创造的工作岗位比消灭的还要多。同样，自动化最终也应会提高生产率、通过压低价格刺激需求，并将劳动者从繁重枯燥的工作中解放出来。但从中期来看，中产阶级劳动者可能需要大量帮助才能适应这种变化。", "正如埃里克·布林约尔松和安德鲁·麦卡菲在《第二次机器时代》中所主张的，第一步应当是重新思考教育与职业培训。从小学到大学的课程设置都应当不断演进，减少对死记硬背事实的关注，将重心更多地放在创造力和复杂沟通能力上。职业院校应当更好地培养解决问题的能力，并帮助学生学会与机器人协同工作。在线教育可以补充传统教育，使额外的培训和指导变得经济实惠。试图掌握新技能的职场人士无需背负债务就能实现自我提升。", "应对自动化的挑战凸显了美国重振其日渐衰退的商业活力的必要性：必须让创办新企业变得更加容易。在以往技术剧变的时代，企业家通过构思将劳动力与机器结合的方式，使转型过程更为平稳。3D打印和虚拟现实的最佳用途尚未被发明出来，美国需要能够发明这些用途的新公司。", "最后，由于自动化有可能扩大资本收入与劳动收入之间的差距，税收和社会保障网也必须重新审视。需要削减对低薪劳动的征税，并扩大诸如劳动所得税抵免之类的工资补贴：这将提高收入、鼓励工作、奖励创造就业的企业，并减少不平等现象。", "未来几年，技术将在方方面面改善社会，但对于那些生活和事业被自动化彻底颠覆的人而言，这几乎算不上什么安慰。摧毁即将抢走我们工作的机器是愚蠢的做法，但帮助劳动者适应变革的政策将不可或缺。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Who will be most threatened by automation?", "options": ["Leading politicians.", "Low-wage laborers.", "Robot owners.", "Middle-class workers."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "About half of U.S. jobs are at high risk of being automated, according to a University of Oxford study, with the middle class disproportionately squeezed.", "explanation": "题干询问自动化对谁的威胁最大。定位第二段第二句，牛津大学研究指出美国约半数工作面临高度自动化风险，而中产阶级受到的挤压尤为严重（disproportionately squeezed）；下文进一步对比说明低收入体力工作不易被取代，富人拥有机器人因而安然无恙，唯独卡车运输、金融顾问等众多中产职业正引起机器人的“兴趣”。可见受威胁最大的是中产阶级劳动者，对应D项。", "trapNote": "A项将第一段“下届总统大选可能只字不提”偷换为政客受威胁；B项和C项均为正反颠倒，第二段明确指出低收入工作和机器人拥有者不受影响。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "态度题", "stem": "Which of the following best represent the author’s view?", "options": ["Worries about automation are in fact groundless.", "Optimists' opinions on new tech find little support.", "Issues arising from automation need to be tackled", "Negative consequences of new tech can be avoided"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "But policies to help workers adapt will be indispensable.", "explanation": "题干询问哪一项最能代表作者的观点。定位末段末句，作者指出帮助劳动者适应变革的政策将不可或缺（indispensable），与第三段末句“中期来看中产劳动者需要大量帮助以适应变化”相呼应，且第四至六段具体提出教育、创业与税收等应对举措。选项C中“issues arising from automation need to be tackled”精准概括了作者主张积极应对的核心立场。", "trapNote": "A项正反颠倒，作者并非认为担忧毫无根据；B项偷换立场，作者认可乐观派的长期判断，仅强调中期需应对；D项“负面后果可以避免”属过度推理。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Education in the age of automation should put more emphasis on", "options": ["creative potential.", "job-hunting skills.", "individual needs.", "cooperative spirit."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Curriculums — from grammar school to college — should evolve to focus less on memorizing facts and more on creativity and complex communication.", "explanation": "题干询问自动化时代的教育应更侧重什么。定位第四段第二句，文章指出从小学到大学的课程设置都应当改革，减少对死记硬背事实的关注，转而更重视创造力和复杂沟通能力（focus less on memorizing facts and more on creativity and complex communication）。选项A中的creative potential正是原文creativity的同义替换，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项将后文的job training和acquiring new skills偷换为“求职技巧”；C项“个人需求”与D项“合作精神”在第四段均未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The author suggests that tax policies be aimed at", "options": ["encouraging the development of automation.", "increasing the return on capital investment.", "easing the hostility between rich and poor.", "preventing the income gap from widening."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Finally, because automation threatens to widen the gap between capital income and labor income, taxes and the safety net will have to be rethought.", "explanation": "题干询问作者建议税收政策应针对什么目标。定位第六段首句，作者指出由于自动化可能扩大资本收入与劳动收入之间的差距，税收与社会保障网必须重新审视；随后进一步提出削减低薪劳动税、扩大劳动所得税抵免，最终实现reduce inequality（减少不平等）。选项D“防止收入差距扩大”正是对threatens to widen the gap的反向精准概括。", "trapNote": "A项“鼓励自动化发展”与B项“提高资本投资回报”均属于无中生有且与缩小资本/劳动收入差距的意图相反；C项“缓和贫富敌意”属过度推理。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "In this text, the author presents a problem with", "options": ["opposing views on it.", "possible solutions to it.", "its alarming impacts.", "its major variations."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The first step, as Erik Brynjolfsson and Andrew McAfee argue in The Second Machine Age, should be rethinking education and job training.", "explanation": "题干考查全文的行文结构与核心主旨。文章第一、二段提出“自动化威胁中产阶级就业”这一社会问题；第三段过渡并指出中产阶级需要帮助来适应变革；随后第四至六段通过The first step、underlines the need、Finally等逻辑标志词，逐层给出教育培训、激发商业活力与改革财税保障这三项应对方案，末段总结政策不可或缺。故本文先提出问题再给出可能方案，对应B项。", "trapNote": "A项“对立观点”仅在第三段提及乐观派看法，属以偏概全；C项“令人震惊的影响”和D项“主要变体”未能涵盖占据后半篇幅的对策主体。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "挤压，压榨；使经济拮据", "note": "考研高频熟词僻义：除“挤榨”外，在经济语境中常指“紧缩、使（某群体）处境艰难”", "word": "squeeze"}, {"gloss": "取代，替代；迫使……离开原位", "note": "常与replace构成同义替换；文中指机械化织布机淘汰手工岗位", "word": "displace"}, {"gloss": "危言耸听者；大惊小怪的", "note": "由alarm加-ist派生；not to be alarmist为常见议论文让步缓和表达", "word": "alarmist"}, {"gloss": "活力，生机，进取精神", "note": "business dynamism指“商业活力”，注意区分dynamic（动态的/有活力的）", "word": "dynamism"}, {"gloss": "颠覆，使彻底改观；使倒置", "note": "upend = up + end，形象表示“把……弄得底朝天”，真题常用于科技或危机对生活的影响", "word": "upend"}, {"gloss": "不可或缺的，必需的", "note": "表示作者强烈肯定态度的高频核心词，等效于essential / vital", "word": "indispensable"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "About half of U.S. jobs are at high risk of being automated, according to a University of Oxford study, with the middle class disproportionately squeezed.", "point": "with复合结构作伴随状语，disproportionately表示“不成比例地、尤为严重地”。", "structure": "主句 (About half of U.S. jobs are at high risk...) + 插入语 (according to...) + with复合结构 (with + 名词 + 过去分词)", "zh": "牛津大学的一项研究表明，美国约半数工作面临高度自动化的风险，其中中产阶级受到的挤压尤为严重。"}, {"en": "In previous eras of drastic technological change, entrepreneurs smoothed the transition by dreaming up ways to combine labor and machines.", "point": "by + 动名词短语作方式状语；dream up意为“想出，构思出（新点子）”。", "structure": "时间状语 + 主句 (entrepreneurs smoothed the transition) + 方式状语 (by dreaming up ways to...)", "zh": "在以往技术剧变的时代，企业家通过构思将劳动力与机器结合的方式，使转型过程更为平稳。"}, {"en": "Technology will improve society in ways big and small over the next few years, yet this will be little comfort to those who find their lives and careers upended by automation.", "point": "yet引导转折分句；find + 宾语 + 过去分词（upended）作宾语补足语。", "structure": "分句1 + 转折连词yet + 分句2 (those + who定语从句含find复合宾语结构)", "zh": "未来几年，技术将在方方面面改善社会，但对于那些生活和事业被自动化彻底颠覆的人而言，这几乎算不上什么安慰。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "受威胁最大的群体对应受挤压尤为严重的群体", "option": "Middle-class workers (Q1)", "original": "with the middle class disproportionately squeezed (Para. 2)"}, {"note": "需要适应帮助与政策不可或缺对应需要解决相关问题", "option": "Issues arising from automation need to be tackled (Q2)", "original": "policies to help workers adapt will be indispensable (Para. 7)"}, {"note": "“创造潜力”直接对应原文中的“创造力”", "option": "creative potential (Q3)", "original": "more on creativity and complex communication (Para. 4)"}, {"note": "“防止收入差距扩大”对应反向消除“扩大收入差距的威胁”", "option": "preventing the income gap from widening (Q4)", "original": "threatens to widen the gap between capital income and labor income (Para. 6)"}, {"note": "三项政策建议的顺序展开对应“可能的解决方案”", "option": "possible solutions to it (Q5)", "original": "The first step... / underlines the need... / Finally... (Paras. 4-6)"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2018-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2018", "examSet": "2018 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2018 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "社交媒体假新闻与青年媒介素养", "subtitle": "社会调查 · 假新闻治理 · 青年媒介批判素养", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 410, "paragraphs": ["A new survey by Harvard University finds more than two-thirds of young Americans disapprove of President Trump’s use of Twitter. The implication is that Millennials prefer news from the White House to be filtered through other sources, not a president’s social media platform.", "Most Americans rely on social media to check daily headlines. Yet as distrust has risen toward all media, people may be starting to beef up their media literacy skills. Such a trend is badly needed. During the 2016 presidential campaign, nearly a quarter of web content shared by Twitter users in the politically critical state of Michigan was fake news, according to the University of Oxford. And a survey conducted for BuzzFeed News found 44 percent of Facebook users rarely or never trust news from the media giant.", "Young people who are digital natives are indeed becoming more skillful at separating fact from fiction in cyberspace. A Knight Foundation focus-group survey of young people between ages 14 and 24 found they use “distributed trust” to verify stories. They cross-check sources and prefer news from different perspectives—especially those that are open about any bias. “Many young people assume a great deal of personal responsibility for educating themselves and actively seeking out opposing viewpoints,” the survey concluded.", "Such active research can have another effect. A 2014 survey conducted in Australia, Britain, and the United States by the University of Wisconsin-Madison found that young people’s reliance on social media led to greater political engagement.", "Social media allows users to experience news events more intimately and immediately while also permitting them to re-share news as a projection of their values and interests. This forces users to be more conscious of their role in passing along information. A survey by Barna research group found the top reason given by Americans for the fake news phenomenon is “reader error,” more so than made-up stories or factual mistakes in reporting. About a third say the problem of fake news lies in “misinterpretation or exaggeration of actual news” via social media. In other words, the choice to share news on social media may be the heart of the issue. “This indicates there is a real personal responsibility in counteracting this problem,” says Roxanne Stone, editor in chief at Barna Group.", "So when young people are critical of an over-tweeting president, they reveal a mental discipline in thinking skills – and in their choices on when to share on social media."], "translations": ["哈佛大学的一项新调查发现，超过三分之二的美国年轻人不赞成特朗普总统使用推特。这意味着千禧一代更希望来自白宫的新闻经过其他渠道的过滤，而不是通过总统的社交媒体平台直接发布。", "大多数美国人依赖社交媒体浏览每日头条。然而，随着人们对所有媒体的不信任感上升，民众可能正在开始提升自己的媒介素养技能。这种趋势正是当下迫切需要的。牛津大学数据显示，在2016年总统竞选期间，密歇根州这个政治关键州的推特用户分享的网络内容中，近四分之一是假新闻。而为BuzzFeed新闻网进行的一项调查发现，44%的脸书用户极少或从不信任这家媒体巨头发布的新闻。", "作为“数字原住民”的年轻一代，在网络空间分辨事实与虚构方面确实变得越来越娴熟。奈特基金会针对14至24岁年轻人的一项焦点小组调查发现，他们利用“分布式信任”来核实新闻报道。他们会交叉核对信息来源，并更青睐来自不同视角的新闻——尤其是那些坦承自身存在偏见的媒体。该调查总结道：“许多年轻人承担起极大的个人责任，自我学习并积极寻找相反的观点。”", "这种主动探究还会产生另一种影响。威斯康星大学麦迪逊分校2014年在澳大利亚、英国和美国进行的一项调查发现，年轻人对社交媒体的依赖带来了更高的政治参与度。", "社交媒体让用户能够更亲密、更即时地体验新闻事件，同时也允许他们转发新闻，以此作为个人价值观和兴趣的投射。这促使用户在传递信息时更加意识到自身所扮演的角色。巴纳研究小组的一项调查发现，美国人认为假新闻现象的首要原因是“读者失误”，远高于新闻报道中的捏造故事或事实差错。约三分之一的人表示，假新闻的问题在于通过社交媒体对真实新闻进行“误读或夸大”。换言之，在社交媒体上选择分享新闻的决定或许才是问题的核心。“这表明在应对这一问题上存在切实的个人责任，”巴纳集团主编罗克珊·斯通说道。", "因此，当年轻人批评一位过度发推的总统时，他们展现出的是思考能力上的心智自律——以及在何时于社交媒体分享新闻上的审慎抉择。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the Paragraphs 1 and 2, many young Americans cast doubts on", "options": ["the justification of the news-filtering practice.", "people’s preference for social media platforms.", "the administration’s ability to handle information.", "social media as a reliable source of news."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "And a survey conducted for BuzzFeed News found 44 percent of Facebook users rarely or never trust news from the media giant.", "explanation": "题干要求根据第一、二段判断许多美国年轻人对什么持怀疑态度。第一段指出超过三分之二的美国年轻人不赞成特朗普使用推特发布消息，更希望白宫新闻经由其他渠道过滤而非总统的社交平台；第二段紧接着补充对各类媒体的不信任感上升，推特分享的大量内容为假新闻，且44%的脸书用户几乎不信任该平台的新闻。综合两段可知，他们怀疑社交媒体作为可靠新闻来源的可信度，对应D项。", "trapNote": "A项正反颠倒，年轻人恰恰赞成新闻过滤机制而非怀疑其合理性；B项和C项偏离两段核心，第一段未怀疑民众偏好，也未质疑政府处理信息的能力。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The phrase “beef up” (Line 2, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to", "options": ["sharpen", "define", "boast", "share"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Yet as distrust has risen toward all media, people may be starting to beef up their media literacy skills.", "explanation": "题干考查第二段第二句中短语beef up的词义。该句构成转折：尽管大多数美国人依赖社交媒体获取每日头条，但随着对所有媒体的不信任上升，人们正开始“beef up”其媒介素养技能，下句指出“这种趋势迫切需要”，第三段进一步说明年轻人在分辨网络真假方面变得更有技巧。由此语境可推断beef up意为“加强、提升”，选项A sharpen（提高、使敏锐）最为贴近。", "trapNote": "B项“界定”、C项“吹嘘”与D项“分享”均不符合“提升媒介素养以应对假新闻”的上下文语义逻辑，其中D项是受前后文share一词干扰而设。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the Knight Foundation survey, young people", "options": ["tend to voice their opinions in cyberspace.", "verify news by referring to diverse resources.", "have a strong sense of responsibility.", "like to exchange views on “distributed trust”"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "They cross-check sources and prefer news from different perspectives—especially those that are open about any bias.", "explanation": "题干定位第三段中的奈特基金会（Knight Foundation）调查。该段第二、三句指出，14至24岁的年轻人利用“分布式信任”核实新闻故事，他们交叉核对信息来源（cross-check sources），并偏好来自不同视角（different perspectives）的新闻。选项B中verify news对应verify stories，referring to diverse resources对应交叉核对多种不同视角的信息源，故为正解。", "trapNote": "A项“倾向于在网络发声”在调查中未提及，属无中生有；C项以偏概全，原文强调的是对自我教育和寻求不同观点的个人责任；D项曲解了“使用分布式信任”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The Barna survey found that a main cause for the fake news problem is", "options": ["readers’ outdated values.", "journalists’ biased reporting", "readers’ misinterpretation", "journalists’ made-up stories."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "About a third say the problem of fake news lies in “misinterpretation or exaggeration of actual news” via social media.", "explanation": "题干询问巴纳（Barna）调查发现的假新闻问题的主要成因。定位第五段第三、四句，该调查显示美国人认为假新闻现象的首要原因是“读者失误”（reader error），而非捏造报道或事实差错；约三分之一受访者指出问题在于社交媒体上对真实新闻的“误读或夸大”（misinterpretation or exaggeration）。选项C“读者的误读”直接命中原文核心表述。", "trapNote": "B项与D项均与原文“more so than made-up stories or factual mistakes in reporting”相悖，属于正反颠倒；A项将values与error混为一谈，属偷换概念。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the text?", "options": ["A Rise in Critical Skills for Sharing News Online", "A Counteraction Against the Over-tweeting Trend", "The Accumulation of Mutual Trust on Social Media.", "The Platforms for Projection of Personal Interests."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "So when young people are critical of an over-tweeting president, they reveal a mental discipline in thinking skills – and in their choices on when to share on social media.", "explanation": "题干考查全文最佳标题。文章开篇由年轻人批评总统过度发推引出话题，第二至四段重点论述在假新闻泛滥与媒介信任危机下，人们尤其是年轻人正在提升媒介素养与批判性核查能力；第五段点明用户在社交媒体分享新闻时的个人责任；末段总结指出，年轻人展现出的正是思维技能与分享抉择上的心智自律。选项A“在线分享新闻批判技能的提升”全面概括了文章主旨。", "trapNote": "B项和D项分别仅抓住了首段“反对过度发推”和第五段“投射个人兴趣”的局部细节，属于以偏概全；C项“积累互信”与第二段“不信任上升”正反颠倒。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "不赞成，反对", "note": "固定搭配disapprove of，态度题中常表达否定态度，等效于object to", "word": "disapprove"}, {"gloss": "媒介素养，读写能力", "note": "media literacy为现代社会话题核心词；literacy原意“识字、读写能力”，引申为“某领域的素养”", "word": "literacy"}, {"gloss": "核实，查证", "note": "阅读真题高频动词，常与cross-check（交叉核对）在同义替换中呼应", "word": "verify"}, {"gloss": "投射，反映，显现", "note": "考研熟词僻义：除“投影、预测”外，文中a projection of their values指“价值观的外在体现/投射”", "word": "projection"}, {"gloss": "抵消，对抗，中和", "note": "counter-（相反）+ act（行动）= 对抗/抵消（不良影响）", "word": "counteract"}, {"gloss": "纪律，自律，训练有素", "note": "熟词僻义：除“学科、惩罚”外，mental discipline在文中指“心智自律、思维约束力”", "word": "discipline"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "During the 2016 presidential campaign, nearly a quarter of web content shared by Twitter users in the politically critical state of Michigan was fake news, according to the University of Oxford.", "point": "过去分词短语shared by Twitter users作后置定语修饰web content，主干为nearly a quarter of web content was fake news。", "structure": "时间状语 + 主语 (nearly a quarter of web content + 过去分词定语) + 系表结构 (was fake news) + 状语 (according to...)", "zh": "牛津大学数据显示，在2016年总统竞选期间，密歇根州这个政治关键州的推特用户分享的网络内容中，近四分之一是假新闻。"}, {"en": "“Many young people assume a great deal of personal responsibility for educating themselves and actively seeking out opposing viewpoints,” the survey concluded.", "point": "assume responsibility for...为高频固定搭配，意为“承担……的责任”；educating和seeking out作介词for的并列宾语。", "structure": "直接引语 (主语 + 谓语assume + 宾语responsibility + 介词短语for...) + 报道主句 (the survey concluded)", "zh": "该调查总结道：“许多年轻人承担起极大的个人责任，自我学习并积极寻找相反的观点。”"}, {"en": "Social media allows users to experience news events more intimately and immediately while also permitting them to re-share news as a projection of their values and interests.", "point": "while引导并列对比/同时发生的情况，其后省略了主语，直接用分词permitting与主句allows呼应。", "structure": "主句 (Social media allows users to...) + 伴随/并列状语 (while also permitting them to...)", "zh": "社交媒体让用户能够更亲密、更即时地体验新闻事件，同时也允许他们转发新闻，以此作为个人价值观和兴趣的投射。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "“不赞成总统推特”与“极少或从不信任平台新闻”共同指向怀疑其新闻可靠性", "option": "cast doubts on social media as a reliable source of news (Q1)", "original": "disapprove of President Trump’s use of Twitter / rarely or never trust news from the media giant (Paras. 1-2)"}, {"note": "beef up在提升技能语境中与sharpen（磨砺、提高）同义", "option": "sharpen (Q2)", "original": "beef up (Para. 2)"}, {"note": "“核实新闻故事”与“交叉核对不同视角的来源”对应“参考多元信息源核实新闻”", "option": "verify news by referring to diverse resources (Q3)", "original": "verify stories / cross-check sources and prefer news from different perspectives (Para. 3)"}, {"note": "调查中的“读者失误”及“误读或夸大”直接对应“读者的误读”", "option": "readers’ misinterpretation (Q4)", "original": "“reader error” / “misinterpretation or exaggeration of actual news” (Para. 5)"}, {"note": "“提升媒介素养”“分开事实与虚构”“思考与分享的心智自律”概括出批判技能提升的主题", "option": "A Rise in Critical Skills for Sharing News Online (Q5)", "original": "beef up their media literacy skills / reveal a mental discipline in thinking skills – and in their choices on when to share (Paras. 2, 6)"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2018-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2018", "examSet": "2018 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2018 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "医疗AI合作与数据垄断隐忧", "subtitle": "医疗AI · 数据隐私与科技巨头垄断", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 429, "paragraphs": ["Any fair-minded assessment of the dangers of the deal between Britain's National Health Service (NHS) and DeepMind must start by acknowledging that both sides mean well. DeepMind is one of the leading artificial intelligence (AI) companies in the world. The potential of this work applied to healthcare is very great, but it could also lead to further concentration of power in the tech giants. It is against that background that the information commissioner, Elizabeth Denham, has issued her damning verdict against the Royal Free hospital trust under the NHS, which handed over to DeepMind the records of 1.6 million patients in 2015 on the basis of a vague agreement which took far too little account of the patients' rights and their expectations of privacy.", "DeepMind has almost apologized. The NHS trust has mended its ways. Further arrangements—and there may be many—between the NHS and DeepMind will be carefully scrutinised to ensure that all necessary permissions have been asked of patients and all unnecessary data has been cleaned. There are lessons about informed patient consent to learn. But privacy is not the only angle in this case and not even the most important. Ms Denham chose to concentrate the blame on the NHS trust, since under existing law it “controlled” the data and DeepMind merely “processed” it. But this distinction misses the point that it is processing and aggregation, not the mere possession of bits, that gives the data value.", "The great question is who should benefit from the analysis of all the data that our lives now generate. Privacy law builds on the concept of damage to an individual from identifiable knowledge about them. That misses the way the surveillance economy works. The data of an individual there gains its value only when it is compared with the data of countless millions more.", "The use of privacy law to curb the tech giants in this instance feels slightly maladapted. This practice does not address the real worry. It is not enough to say that the algorithms DeepMind develops will benefit patients and save lives. What matters is that they will belong to a private monopoly which developed them using public resources. If software promises to save lives on the scale that drugs now can, big data may be expected to behave as a big pharma has done. We are still at the beginning of this revolution and small choices now may turn out to have gigantic consequences later. A long struggle will be needed to avoid a future of digital feudalism. Ms Denham's report is a welcome start."], "translations": ["对英国国家医疗服务体系（NHS）与DeepMind之间这项协议潜在危险的任何公正评估，都必须首先承认双方均怀有良好初衷。DeepMind是全球领先的人工智能（AI）公司之一。将这项工作应用于医疗保健的潜力非常巨大，但它也可能导致权力进一步向科技巨头集中。正是在这一背景下，信息专员伊丽莎白·丹纳姆对NHS下属的皇家自由医院信托基金作出了严厉裁决；该基金于2015年依据一份模糊的协议，将160万名患者的病历移交给了DeepMind，而该协议对患者的权利及其隐私期望考虑得远远不够。", "DeepMind几乎已经道歉，NHS信托基金也已痛改前非。NHS与DeepMind之间未来的进一步安排——而且可能还有许多——都将受到严格审查，以确保已向患者征得所有必要许可，并已清除所有不必要的数据。在患者知情同意方面确实有教训需要吸取。但隐私并非此案的唯一角度，甚至不是最重要的角度。丹纳姆女士选择将指责集中于NHS信托基金，因为根据现行法律，是它“控制”着数据，而DeepMind只是“处理”数据。但这种区分忽略了一个关键点，即赋予数据价值的正是对数据的处理与聚合，而不仅仅是对零散比特数据的占有。", "真正的大问题是：究竟谁应当从对我们当下生活所生成的全部数据的分析中获益。隐私法建立在“可识别的个人身份信息会给个人带来损害”这一概念之上。这忽略了监控经济的运作方式。在那种经济模式下，个人的数据只有与成百上千万其他人的数据加以比对时，才会产生价值。", "在这起事件中动用隐私法来遏制科技巨头，让人感觉有些水土不服。这种做法并未解决真正的担忧。仅仅说DeepMind开发的算法将造福患者、拯救生命是不够的。真正重要的是，这些算法将归属于一家利用公共资源开发出它们的私人垄断企业。如果软件有望像如今的药物一样大规模挽救生命，那么大数据就很可能会像大型药企那样行事。我们仍处于这场变革的开端，当下微小的选择日后可能会产生巨大的后果。要避免“数字封建主义”的未来，就需要经历一场漫长的斗争。丹纳姆女士的报告是一个受欢迎的开端。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is true of the agreement between the NHS and DeepMind?", "options": ["It caused conflicts among tech giants.", "It failed to pay due attention to patient’s rights.", "It fell short of the latter's expectations", "It put both sides into a dangerous situation."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "which handed over to DeepMind the records of 1.6 million patients in 2015 on the basis of a vague agreement which took far too little account of the patients' rights and their expectations of privacy.", "explanation": "定位至第一段末句。题干询问NHS与DeepMind协议的真相。原文指出皇家自由医院信托基金依据一份“模糊协议”向DeepMind移交了160万份患者记录，该协议“对患者的权利及其隐私期望考虑得远远不够”（took far too little account of the patients' rights）。B项中的failed to pay due attention to精准同义替换了took far too little account of，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "D项属无中生有，首段首句仅提及双方初衷良善及合作可能带来权力集中的危险，并未称协议使双方陷入危险境地；C项属偷换概念，原文指协议未充分顾及患者的隐私期望，而非未达DeepMind的期望。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The NHS trust responded to Denham's verdict with", "options": ["empty promises.", "tough resistance.", "necessary adjustments.", "sincere apologies."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The NHS trust has mended its ways. Further arrangements—and there may be many—between the NHS and DeepMind will be carefully scrutinised to ensure that all necessary permissions have been asked of patients and all unnecessary data has been cleaned.", "explanation": "定位至第二段前两句。针对丹纳姆（Denham）的严厉裁决，原文明确指出“The NHS trust has mended its ways”（NHS信托基金已痛改前非），随后具体说明未来双方协议将受到严格审查，以确保征得患者必要许可并清除多余数据。C项necessary adjustments（必要调整）精准概括了mended its ways及后续整改措施，故正确。", "trapNote": "D项属张冠李戴，第二段首句说的是“DeepMind has almost apologized”（DeepMind几乎已道歉），而非NHS信托基金致以真诚道歉；A、B两项均与原文积极整改的态度正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The author argues in Paragraph 2 that", "options": ["privacy protection must be secured at all costs.", "leaking patients' data is worse than selling it.", "making profits from patients' data is illegal.", "the value of data comes from the processing of it"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But this distinction misses the point that it is processing and aggregation, not the mere possession of bits, that gives the data value.", "explanation": "定位至第二段末句。作者在评价丹纳姆将责任集中于“控制”数据的NHS而非仅“处理”数据的DeepMind时指出，这种区分抓错了重点，“赋予数据价值的正是处理和聚合（processing and aggregation），而非仅仅持有字节”。D项the value of data comes from the processing of it与该强调句核心观点完全吻合，故选D。", "trapNote": "A项属过度推理且与作者立场不符，第二段强调“隐私并非本案唯一甚至最重要的角度”，作者并未主张不惜一切代价保护隐私；B、C两项提及的内容在第二段均未出现，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the last paragraph, the real worry arising from this deal is", "options": ["the vicious rivalry among big pharmas.", "the ineffective enforcement of privacy law.", "the uncontrolled use of new software.", "the monopoly of big data by tech giants."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "This practice does not address the real worry. It is not enough to say that the algorithms DeepMind develops will benefit patients and save lives. What matters is that they will belong to a private monopoly which developed them using public resources.", "explanation": "定位至第四段第二至四句。作者首先指出运用隐私法限制科技巨头“并未解决真正的担忧（the real worry）”，接着通过What matters is引出核心关切：DeepMind利用公共资源开发的算法最终将归属于一家私人垄断企业，随后还提到大数据可能像大型药企一样行事并导致“数字封建主义”。D项“科技巨头对大数据的垄断”准确概括了这一真正担忧，故选D。", "trapNote": "B项属以偏概全，末段首句称以隐私法遏制巨头“略显不适切”（slightly maladapted），问题在于法律思路不对症而非“执法不力”；A项“大型药企间的恶性竞争”是对big pharma类比的无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author's attitude toward the application of AI to healthcare is", "options": ["ambiguous.", "cautious.", "appreciative.", "contemptuous."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "We are still at the beginning of this revolution and small choices now may turn out to have gigantic consequences later. A long struggle will be needed to avoid a future of digital feudalism.", "explanation": "考查作者态度。第一段作者肯定了AI应用于医疗的巨大潜力（very great），但同时警示这可能加剧科技巨头的权力集中；第四段进一步指出我们仍处于这场变革的开端，当下微小的选择日后可能产生巨大后果，需要长期斗争来避免“数字封建主义”。可见作者既认可潜力又保持高度警惕，态度是审慎的（cautious），而非一味赞美或轻蔑，故选B。", "trapNote": "C项appreciative（赞赏的）属以偏概全，作者虽承认AI医疗潜力巨大，但全文重心在于警示数据垄断风险；A项ambiguous（模棱两可的）和D项contemptuous（轻蔑的）均与作者批判性审慎立场不符。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "严厉批评的，毁灭性的", "note": "考研高频评价词，常见搭配 damning verdict（严厉裁决/谴责性结论），源自动词 damn（谴责）。", "word": "damning"}, {"gloss": "仔细检查，详查", "note": "词义与 examine closely 相当，常考被动语态 be carefully scrutinised，注意英式拼写 scrutinise / 美式 scrutinize。", "word": "scrutinise"}, {"gloss": "聚集，聚合，总计", "note": "名词与动词同形（重音有别），文中指数据的“汇聚整合”，与 processing 并列说明数据价值的来源。", "word": "aggregation"}, {"gloss": "不适应的，不适切的", "note": "前缀 mal-（坏、不当）+ adapted（适应的），指“隐私法在应对监控经济和巨头垄断时显得水土不服”。", "word": "maladapted"}, {"gloss": "遏制，抑制，控制", "note": "熟词僻义：作名词常见义为“路缘”，作动词在考研经济与社会类文章中高频表示“抑制、约束（权力、通胀等）”。", "word": "curb"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "It is against that background that the information commissioner, Elizabeth Denham, has issued her damning verdict against the Royal Free hospital trust under the NHS, which handed over to DeepMind the records of 1.6 million patients in 2015 on the basis of a vague agreement which took far too little account of the patients' rights and their expectations of privacy.", "point": "强调句与多层定语从句嵌套（which 修饰 trust，第二个 which 修饰 agreement），阅读时先抓主干“信息专员裁决皇家自由医院信托基金”。", "structure": "It is ... that ... 强调句型 + 同位语 Elizabeth Denham + 两个依次嵌套的 which 定语从句", "zh": "正是在这一背景下，信息专员伊丽莎白·丹纳姆对英国国家医疗服务体系下属的皇家自由医院信托基金作出了严厉裁决；该基金于2015年依据一份模糊的协议，将160万名患者的病历移交给了DeepMind，而该协议对患者的权利及其隐私期望考虑得远远不够。"}, {"en": "But this distinction misses the point that it is processing and aggregation, not the mere possession of bits, that gives the data value.", "point": "that 引导同位语从句解释 the point，从句内部再嵌一个“It is ... that ...”强调句型，突出“处理与聚合”而非“单纯占有数据”才是关键。", "structure": "the point + that 同位语从句（内含 It is A, not B, that ... 强调句）", "zh": "但这种区分忽略了一个关键点，即赋予数据价值的正是对数据的处理与聚合，而不仅仅是对零散比特数据的占有。"}, {"en": "What matters is that they will belong to a private monopoly which developed them using public resources.", "point": "主语从句 + 表语从句 + 定语从句的紧凑组合，其中 using public resources 为现在分词短语作方式状语，点明“公器私用”的垄断实质。", "structure": "What matters（主语从句）+ is + that 表语从句 + which 定语从句", "zh": "真正重要的是，这些算法将归属于一家利用公共资源开发出它们的私人垄断企业。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "动词短语与否定表达同义替换：take far too little account of（对……考虑远远不够）= fail to pay due attention to（未能给予应有重视）。", "option": "failed to pay due attention to patient’s rights", "original": "took far too little account of the patients' rights"}, {"note": "习语及具体举措概括替换：mend one's ways（痛改前非）及后续审查、清理数据 = necessary adjustments（必要调整）。", "option": "necessary adjustments", "original": "The NHS trust has mended its ways. ... will be carefully scrutinised ... all unnecessary data has been cleaned."}, {"note": "句式转换与核心词汇对应：it is processing and aggregation ... that gives the data value 改写为因果主动表达。", "option": "the value of data comes from the processing of it", "original": "it is processing and aggregation, not the mere possession of bits, that gives the data value"}, {"note": "核心概念对应：belong to a private monopoly（归属私人垄断企业）结合 tech giants 与 big data，概括为“科技巨头垄断大数据”。", "option": "the monopoly of big data by tech giants", "original": "belong to a private monopoly which developed them using public resources"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2018-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2018", "examSet": "2018 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2018 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "美国邮政局改革困局与治本之策", "subtitle": "公共治理 · 美国邮政局财政危机与改革", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 412, "paragraphs": ["The U.S. Postal Service (USPS) continues to bleed red ink. It reported a net loss of 5.6 billion for fiscal 2016, the 10th straight year its expenses have exceeded revenue. Meanwhile, it has more than 120 billion in unfunded liabilities, mostly for employee health and retirement costs. There are many bankruptcies. Fundamentally, the USPS is in a historic squeeze between technological change that has permanently decreased demand for its bread-and-butter product, first-class mail, and a regulatory structure that denies management the flexibility to adjust its operations to the new reality.", "And interest groups ranging from postal unions to greeting-card makers exert self-interested pressure on the USPS’s ultimate overseer-Congress-insisting that whatever else happens to the Postal Service, aspects of the status quo they depend on get protected. This is why repeated attempts at reform legislation have failed in recent years, leaving the Postal Service unable to pay its bills except by deferring vital modernization.", "Now comes word that everyone involved—Democrats, Republicans, the Postal Service, the unions and the system's heaviest users—has finally agreed on a plan to fix the system. Legislation is moving through the House that would save USPS an estimated $28.6 billion over five years, which could help pay for new vehicles, among other survival measures. Most of the money would come from a penny-per-letter permanent rate increase and from shifting postal retirees into Medicare. The latter step would largely offset the financial burden of annually pre-funding retiree health care, thus addressing a long-standing complaint by the USPS and its union.", "If it clears the House, this measure would still have to get through the Senate – where someone is bound to point out that it amounts to the bare, bare minimum necessary to keep the Postal Service afloat, not comprehensive reform. There’s no change to collective bargaining at the USPS, a major omission considering that personnel accounts for 80 percent of the agency’s costs. Also missing is any discussion of eliminating Saturday letter delivery. That common-sense change enjoys wide public support and would save the USPS $2 billion per year. But postal special-interest groups seem to have killed it, at least in the House. The emerging consensus around the bill is a sign that legislators are getting frightened about a politically embarrassing short-term collapse at the USPS. It is not, however, a sign that they’re getting serious about transforming the postal system for the 21st century."], "translations": ["美国邮政局（USPS）仍在持续严重亏损。据其报告，2016财年净亏损达56亿美元，这是其连续第10年支出超过收入。与此同时，它还背负着超过1200亿美元的未备资金债务，其中大部分是员工医疗和退休金费用。破产案例比比皆是。从根本上说，美国邮政局正处于历史性的双重挤压之中：一方面是技术变革永久性地降低了人们对其支柱业务——一类邮件的需求，另一方面则是监管体制剥夺了管理层根据新现实调整运营的灵活性。", "而且，从邮政工会到贺卡制造商等各类利益集团都在向美国邮政局的最高监管者——国会——施加自私的压力，坚持认为无论邮政局发生什么其他变化，他们所依赖的现状的方方面面都必须得到保护。这就是近年来改革立法屡次受挫的原因，迫使美国邮政局只能通过推迟关键的现代化改造来勉强支付账单。", "如今传来消息，各方参与者——包括民主党人、共和党人、邮政局、工会以及该系统最大的用户——终于就整顿该系统的方案达成一致。众议院正在推进一项立法，预计在五年内为美国邮政局节省286亿美元，这笔资金除了用于其他维持生存的措施外，还能帮助支付购买新车的费用。大部分资金将来自每封信件永久提价一美分，以及将邮政退休人员转入联邦医疗保险计划（Medicare）。后一项举措将在很大程度上抵消每年预付退休人员医疗保健费用的财政负担，从而解决美国邮政局及其工会长期以来的不满。", "即便该法案在众议院获得通过，仍须过参议院这一关——在那里，肯定会有人指出，这项措施充其量只是让邮政局勉强维持运转的最低限度之举，而非全面改革。考虑到人力成本占该机构总成本的80%，法案却丝毫未触及美国邮政局的集体谈判制度，这无疑是一大重大遗漏。同样缺失的还有关于取消周六信件投递的讨论。这一合乎常理的改革享有广泛的公众支持，每年可为美国邮政局节省20亿美元。但邮政特殊利益集团似乎至少已在众议院扼杀了这一提议。围绕该法案逐渐形成的共识表明，立法者正对美国邮政局短期内可能出现令其在政治上难堪的崩溃感到恐慌。然而，这并不意味着他们正认真地为21世纪改造邮政系统。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The financial problem with the USPS is caused partly by", "options": ["its unbalanced budget.", "its rigid management.", "the cost for technical upgrading.", "the withdrawal of bank support."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Fundamentally, the USPS is in a historic squeeze between technological change that has permanently decreased demand for its bread-and-butter product, first-class mail, and a regulatory structure that denies management the flexibility to adjust its operations to the new reality.", "explanation": "定位至第一段末句。该段指出USPS连续十年入不敷出并背负巨额债务，随后点明其财务困境的两大根本原因：一是技术变革导致核心业务（一类邮件）需求永久性下降，二是监管体制“剥夺了管理层根据新现实调整运营的灵活性”（denies management the flexibility）。B项its rigid management（僵化的管理）精准同义替换了缺乏调整灵活性的管理体制，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项“预算不平衡”属于财务困境的表面结果而非原因（因果倒置），第一段第二句提到的“支出连续十年超过收入”正是财政问题的表现；C、D两项在首段均无依据，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, the USPS fails to modernize itself due to", "options": ["the interference from interest groups.", "the inadequate funding from Congress.", "the shrinking demand for postal service.", "the incompetence of postal unions."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "And interest groups ranging from postal unions to greeting-card makers exert self-interested pressure on the USPS’s ultimate overseer-Congress-insisting that whatever else happens to the Postal Service, aspects of the status quo they depend on get protected. This is why repeated attempts at reform legislation have failed in recent years, leaving the Postal Service unable to pay its bills except by deferring vital modernization.", "explanation": "定位至第二段全段。首句指出从邮政工会到贺卡制造商等各类利益集团向国会施加自私的压力（exert self-interested pressure），坚持要求保护其赖以生存的现状。次句用This is why总结因果：这正是改革立法屡屡受挫的原因，迫使USPS只能通过推迟关键的现代化改造（deferring vital modernization）来应付账单。A项“利益集团的干涉”与原文完全一致，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项“国会资金不足”属无中生有，第二段指出国会是受利益集团施压的最高监管者，未提及拨款不足；C项是第一段提及的财务困境原因之一，并非第二段解释无法实现现代化的原因。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The long-standing complaint by the USPS and its unions can be addressed by", "options": ["removing its burden of retiree health care.", "making more investment in new vehicles.", "adopting a new rate-increase mechanism.", "attracting more first-class mail users."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Most of the money would come from a penny-per-letter permanent rate increase and from shifting postal retirees into Medicare. The latter step would largely offset the financial burden of annually pre-funding retiree health care, thus addressing a long-standing complaint by the USPS and its union.", "explanation": "定位至第三段末句。前文提到众议院法案中的资金来源主要有两项：每封信永久涨价一美分，以及将邮政退休人员转入联邦医疗保险（Medicare）。末句明确指出“后一项举措（The latter step）将很大程度上抵消每年预付退休人员医疗保健费用的财务负担，从而解决USPS及其工会长期以来的不满”。A项精准对应“消除退休人员医保负担”，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项“加大新车投资”和C项“采用新涨价机制”均属张冠李戴，前者是法案省钱后的用途之一，后者对应前文涨价措施而非解决长期不满的“后一项举措”；D项属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "态度题", "stem": "In the last paragraph, the author seems to view legislators with", "options": ["respect.", "tolerance.", "discontent.", "gratitude."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The emerging consensus around the bill is a sign that legislators are getting frightened about a politically embarrassing short-term collapse at the USPS. It is not, however, a sign that they’re getting serious about transforming the postal system for the 21st century.", "explanation": "定位至第四段末两句。作者评价该法案只是让邮政局勉强维持运转的“最低限度措施”（bare, bare minimum），而非全面改革，且回避了集体谈判和取消周六派送等关键议题。最后作者直言：立法者达成共识只是因为害怕短期崩溃带来政治尴尬，而非“真正认真地为21世纪改造邮政系统”。由此可见作者对立法者持不满态度（discontent），故选C。", "trapNote": "B项tolerance（宽容）属于态度误判，末段通篇批评法案流于表面、向特殊利益集团妥协，毫无宽容之意；A项respect（尊重）和D项gratitude（感激）与作者对立法者的批判正反颠倒。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the text?", "options": ["The USPS Starts to Miss Its Good Old Days", "The Postal Service: Keep Away from My Cheese", "The USPS: Chronic Illness Requires a Quick Cure", "The Postal Service Needs More than a Band-Aid"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "If it clears the House, this measure would still have to get through the Senate – where someone is bound to point out that it amounts to the bare, bare minimum necessary to keep the Postal Service afloat, not comprehensive reform.", "explanation": "考查主旨大意。全文前三段剖析USPS深陷财政亏损、受制于僵化体制与利益集团阻挠，以及众议院近期推出权宜法案的背景；第四段点明主旨：该法案只是维持其不破产的最低限度措施，既未触及人事成本也未推动全面改革，立法者并未真正着手重塑21世纪邮政体系。D项“邮政局需要的不仅是一块创可贴（权宜之计）”生动准确地概括了全文核心论点，故为最佳标题。", "trapNote": "C项“慢性病需要速效药（quick cure）”属正反颠倒，作者恰恰反对只顾应付短期政治尴尬的“权宜之计”，呼吁全面深层改革；B项“别动我的奶酪”仅对应第二段利益集团护短的局部信息，属以偏概全。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "（财务上）持续亏损，流血不止", "note": "熟词僻义：red ink 在财务语境中指“赤字、亏损”（因传统记账亏损用红墨水书写），bleed red ink 形象指“严重亏损”。", "word": "bleed red ink"}, {"gloss": "核心产品，主要收入来源", "note": "复合形容词，直译“黄油面包”，在商业和经济类真题中常比喻“最基本、最主要的生计或支柱业务”。", "word": "bread-and-butter"}, {"gloss": "（使）维持运营，不倒闭，漂浮", "note": "常见搭配 keep ... afloat，原意“使不沉没”，在经济报道中高频引申为“使企业/机构免于破产、勉强维持运转”。", "word": "afloat"}, {"gloss": "推迟，延缓", "note": "及物动词，注意区分 defer（推迟）与 differ（不同）；文中 leaving ... except by deferring vital modernization 意为“只能靠推迟现代化来勉强支付账单”。", "word": "defer"}, {"gloss": "抵消，弥补", "note": "熟词僻义/高频经济词：既可作动词也可作名词，文中 offset the financial burden 表示“抵消财政负担”。", "word": "offset"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Fundamentally, the USPS is in a historic squeeze between technological change that has permanently decreased demand for its bread-and-butter product, first-class mail, and a regulatory structure that denies management the flexibility to adjust its operations to the new reality.", "point": "between A and B 并列结构分别带两个长定语从句，清晰拆解USPS面临“市场需求萎缩”和“监管僵化”的双重挤压。", "structure": "between A (technological change + that定语从句) and B (regulatory structure + that定语从句)", "zh": "从根本上说，美国邮政局正处于历史性的双重挤压之中：一方面是技术变革永久性地降低了人们对其支柱业务——一类邮件的需求，另一方面则是监管体制剥夺了管理层根据新现实调整运营的灵活性。"}, {"en": "And interest groups ranging from postal unions to greeting-card makers exert self-interested pressure on the USPS’s ultimate overseer-Congress-insisting that whatever else happens to the Postal Service, aspects of the status quo they depend on get protected.", "point": "ranging from ... to ... 作后置定语，insisting that ... 作伴随状语，从句内含 whatever 引导的让步状语从句及虚拟语气（get protected 省略 should）。", "structure": "主句 + 现在分词伴随状语 insisting that（内含 whatever 让步状语从句 + 省略定语从句 they depend on）", "zh": "而且，从邮政工会到贺卡制造商等各类利益集团都在向美国邮政局的最高监管者——国会——施加自私的压力，坚持认为无论邮政局发生什么其他变化，他们所依赖的现状的方方面面都必须得到保护。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "逆向正反同义替换：denies management the flexibility（剥夺管理灵活性）= rigid management（僵化的管理）。", "option": "its rigid management", "original": "a regulatory structure that denies management the flexibility to adjust its operations"}, {"note": "概括替换：interest groups exert self-interested pressure ... reform legislation have failed（利益集团施压致改革受挫）= the interference from interest groups（利益集团的干涉）。", "option": "the interference from interest groups", "original": "interest groups ... exert self-interested pressure ... This is why repeated attempts at reform legislation have failed"}, {"note": "短语精确对应：offset the financial burden of ... retiree health care（抵消退休人员医保负担）= removing its burden of retiree health care（消除退休人员医保负担）。", "option": "removing its burden of retiree health care", "original": "offset the financial burden of annually pre-funding retiree health care"}, {"note": "隐喻与主旨归纳：bare, bare minimum ... not comprehensive reform（最低限度措施，而非全面改革）对应形象比喻 Needs More than a Band-Aid（需要的不仅是一块创可贴）。", "option": "The Postal Service Needs More than a Band-Aid", "original": "amounts to the bare, bare minimum necessary to keep the Postal Service afloat, not comprehensive reform"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L3", "exam": "kaoyan1", "id": "ky1-2017-t1", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["First two hours, now three hours—this is how far in advance authorities are recommending people show up to catch a domestic flight, at least at some major U.S. airports with increasingly massive security lines.", "Americans are willing to tolerate time-consuming security procedures in return for increased safety. The crash of EgyptAir Flight 804, which terrorists may have downed over the Mediterranean Sea, provides another tragic reminder of why. But demanding too much of air travelers or providing too little security in return undermines public support for the process. And it should: Wasted time is a drag on Americans’ economic and private lives, not to mention infuriating.", "Last year, the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) found in a secret check that undercover investigators were able to sneak weapons—both fake and real—past airport security nearly every time they tried. Enhanced security measures since then, combined with a rise in airline travel due to the improving economy and low oil prices, have resulted in long waits at major airports such as Chicago’s O’Hare International. It is not yet clear how much more effective airline security has become—but the lines are obvious.", "Part of the issue is that the government did not anticipate the steep increase in airline travel, so the TSA is now rushing to get new screeners on the line. Part of the issue is that airports have only so much room for screening lanes. Another factor may be that more people are trying to overpack their carry-on bags to avoid checked-baggage fees, though the airlines strongly dispute this.", "There is one step the TSA could take that would not require remodeling airports or rushing to hire: Enroll more people in the PreCheck program. PreCheck is supposed to be a win-win for travelers and the TSA. Passengers who pass a background check are eligible to use expedited screening lanes. This allows the TSA to focus on travelers who are higher risk, saving time for everyone involved. The TSA wants to enroll 25 million people in PreCheck.", "It has not gotten anywhere close to that, and one big reason is sticker shock: Passengers must pay $85 every five years to process their background checks. Since the beginning, this price tag has been PreCheck’s fatal flaw. Upcoming reforms might bring the price to a more reasonable level. But Congress should look into doing so directly, by helping to finance PreCheck enrollment or to cut costs in other ways.", "The TSA cannot continue diverting resources into underused PreCheck lanes while most of the traveling public suffers in unnecessary lines. It is long past time to make the program work."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "in return for increased safety. The crash of EgyptAir Flight 804, which terrorists may have downed over the Mediterranean Sea, provides another tragic reminder of why.", "explanation": "定位第2段第1、2句。首句指出美国人愿意为提高安全性而容忍耗时的安检程序，第2句紧接着指出埃及航空804号班机坠毁事件提供了“为何如此（why）”的又一悲痛提醒。因此，文中提及该空难正是为了解释美国人容忍现行安检的原因（tolerate对应tolerance，security procedures对应security checks）。", "no": 21, "options": ["stress the urgency to strengthen security worldwide", "explain Americans’ tolerance of current security checks", "highlight the necessity of upgrading major U.S. airports", "emphasize the importance of privacy protection"], "stem": "The crash of EgyptAir Flight 804 is mentioned to ____.", "trapNote": "A项属于过度推理与偷换概念，原文仅借空难解释美国民众容忍国内安检的原因，并未借此强调在全球（worldwide）范围内加强安检的紧迫性；D项则误将后文“private lives（私人生活）”曲解为“privacy protection（隐私保护）”。", "type": "例证题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Enhanced security measures since then, combined with a rise in airline travel due to the improving economy and low oil prices, have resulted in long waits at major airports", "explanation": "定位第3段第2句与第4段首句。第3段明确指出，加强安检措施与经济增长、低油价带动的航空出行增长（a rise in airline travel）共同造成了主要机场的长时间排队（long waits）。C项中的“An increase in the number of travelers”是对“a rise in airline travel”及第4段“the steep increase in airline travel”的同义替换。", "no": 22, "options": ["New restrictions on carry-on bags.", "The declining efficiency of the TSA.", "An increase in the number of travelers.", "Frequent unexpected secret checks."], "stem": "Which of the following contributes to long waits at major airports?", "trapNote": "A项属于偷换概念，第4段指出的潜在原因是乘客为省去托运费而过度装满随身行李（overpack their carry-on bags），而非机场针对随身行李出台了“新限制（new restrictions）”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "eligible to use expedited screening lanes. This allows the TSA to focus on travelers who are higher risk, saving time for everyone involved.", "explanation": "定位第5段第3、4句。前句说明通过背景审查的乘客可使用“expedited”安检通道，紧接着下句点明这能使TSA集中排查高风险旅客，从而“为所有人节省时间（saving time for everyone involved）”。结合前文缓解安检排长队的语境，可知expedited意为“加速的、更快的”，与D项faster含义最接近。", "no": 23, "options": ["quieter", "cheaper", "wider", "faster"], "stem": "The word “expedited” (Para 5) is closest in meaning to ____.", "trapNote": "B项“cheaper”属于跨段干扰，受到第6段讨论PreCheck收费85美元的干扰，但第5段语境讨论的是分流通道的通行效率与时间成本，与价格高低无关。", "type": "词义题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Passengers must pay $85 every five years to process their background checks. Since the beginning, this price tag has been PreCheck’s fatal flaw.", "explanation": "定位第6段第1至3句。该段指出PreCheck注册人数远未达到目标，关键原因在于令旅客望而却步的高价（sticker shock）：每五年需支付85美元背景审查费，而“自始至终，这一标价都是PreCheck的致命缺陷（fatal flaw）”，后续改革有望将其降至“更合理的水平（a more reasonable level）”。由此可知，PreCheck存在的问题是注册定价不合理（an unreasonable price for enrollment）。", "no": 24, "options": ["a dramatic reduction of its scale", "its wrongly-directed implementation", "the government’s reluctance to back it", "an unreasonable price for enrollment"], "stem": "One problem with the PreCheck program is ____.", "trapNote": "B项“实施方向有误”是对末段“diverting resources into underused PreCheck lanes”的曲解，项目受阻的原因在于高昂定价导致注册人数少，而非其分流实施方向本身错误。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "The TSA cannot continue diverting resources into underused PreCheck lanes while most of the traveling public suffers in unnecessary lines.", "explanation": "文章第1至4段详述美国主要机场安检长队（massive security lines / long waits）的现状与成因，第5至7段分析PreCheck方案本可缓解排队却因收费过高遇冷，导致多数旅客仍在“不必要的排长队中煎熬（suffers in unnecessary lines）”。全文始终围绕“机场安检排长队困局”展开，C项“受困于安检长队（Getting Stuck in Security Lines）”最能凝练全篇核心主题。", "no": 25, "options": ["Less Screening for More Safety", "PreCheck—a Belated Solution", "Getting Stuck in Security Lines", "Underused PreCheck Lanes"], "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the test?", "trapNote": "D项“使用率低的PreCheck通道”属于以偏概全，该表述仅出现在最后一段且前四段完全未提PreCheck；B项“迟来的解决方案”则曲解了末段“long past time to make the program work”，原文意指早该让既有项目真正运转起来，而非该方案本身提出太迟。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "2017 考研英语一真题", "subtitle": "2017年考研英语一 阅读理解 Part A · Text 1", "timeLimitMin": 18, "title": "Text 1: Airport Security Lines and PreCheck", "year": "2017", "wordCount": 442, "examSet": "2017 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "translations": ["起初是提前两小时，如今变成了三小时——至少在部分安检排起惊人长队的美国大型机场，这是有关部门建议旅客搭乘国内航班时应提前到场的时间。", "为了换取更高的安全性，美国人愿意忍受耗时的安检程序。埃及航空804号航班在地中海上空坠毁——极可能是遭恐怖分子击落——这一事件再次以悲剧的方式提醒人们个中缘由。但是，对航空旅客提出过多要求，或作为回报提供的安全保障过少，都会削弱公众对安检流程的支持。而且理当如此：浪费时间不仅令人生厌，更会拖累美国人的经济生活与私人生活。", "去年，美国运输安全管理局（TSA）在一次秘密抽查中发现，卧底调查人员几乎每次尝试都能将武器——既有仿真的也有真家伙——偷带过机场安检。自那时起加强的安保措施，再加上经济好转与低油价带动的航空出行增长，共同导致芝加哥奥黑尔国际机场等大型机场排起了漫长的队伍。目前尚不清楚航空安保究竟变得多有效——但排起的长队却显而易见。", "部分原因在于政府未能预见到航空出行的激增，因此TSA眼下正急着调派新的安检员上岗。另一部分原因在于机场用来设置安检通道的空间本就有限。还有一个因素可能是，越来越多的人为了省下行李托运费而把随身行李箱塞得过满，不过航空公司对此予以强烈反驳。", "美国运输安全管理局有一项举措既无需改建机场，也无需仓促招人，那便是：让更多人加入“预检”（PreCheck）项目。该项目本应实现旅客与TSA的双赢。通过背景审查的旅客便有资格使用快速安检通道。这使得TSA能够集中精力排查风险较高的旅客，从而为各方节省时间。TSA希望能吸引2500万人加入“预检”项目。", "但实际参与人数远未达到这一目标，其中一大原因便是高昂的费用令人望而却步：旅客每五年必须支付85美元用于处理背景审查。从一开始，这一价格标签就是“预检”项目的致命缺陷。即将出台的改革或许能将价格降至更合理的水平。但国会应当考虑直接出手解决这一问题，比如为“预检”注册提供资金补贴，或通过其他方式削减成本。", "美国运输安全管理局不能再继续把资源分流到使用率低下的“预检”通道上，而让大多数乘机出行的大众在毫无必要的长队中苦苦煎熬。早该让这个项目真正发挥作用了。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 击落，使坠落", "note": "熟词僻义：常用作副词或介词“向下”，本文用作及物动词，指恐怖分子“击落”客机。", "word": "down"}, {"gloss": "n. 拖累，负担，障碍", "note": "熟词僻义：作动词常指“拖、拉”，本文用作名词，构成 a drag on...，意为“对……的拖累”。", "word": "drag"}, {"gloss": "v. 加速，加快处理", "note": "考研核心词，其过去分词 expedited 作前置定语意为“加急的、快速的”，真题直接考查词义替换 faster。", "word": "expedite"}, {"gloss": "n. 标价震惊，高价惊吓", "note": "常见文化及经济类表达，指消费者面对远超预期的商品或服务标价时产生的震惊感。", "word": "sticker shock"}, {"gloss": "v. 转移，分流；使改道", "note": "高频核心词，常与 into / from / to 搭配，表示“将（资源、资金、注意力）转移到……”。", "word": "divert"}, {"gloss": "v. 逐渐削弱，破坏", "note": "考研阅读高频动词，多指从根基上“削弱（公众支持、信心、权威等）”，常与 weaken / erode 互换。", "word": "undermine"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Enhanced security measures since then, combined with a rise in airline travel due to the improving economy and low oil prices, have resulted in long waits at major airports such as Chicago’s O’Hare International.", "point": "过去分词短语作插入语（非主语成分，谓语单复数由中心主语决定） + 多重介词短语作原因状语", "structure": "主干：Enhanced security measures since then... have resulted in long waits at major airports...；插入修饰语：combined with a rise in airline travel（不改变主语复数性质）；原因状语：due to the improving economy and low oil prices；举例定语：such as Chicago’s O’Hare International。", "zh": "自那时起加强的安保措施，再加上经济好转与低油价带动的航空出行增长，共同导致芝加哥奥黑尔国际机场等大型机场排起了漫长的队伍。"}, {"en": "There is one step the TSA could take that would not require remodeling airports or rushing to hire: Enroll more people in the PreCheck program.", "point": "双重限制性定语从句修饰同一先行词（前省关系代词，后为分隔式定语从句） + 冒号引出同位说明", "structure": "主干：There is one step；定语从句1：(that) the TSA could take（修饰 one step）；定语从句2：that would not require remodeling airports or rushing to hire（同样修饰 one step，形成分隔定语从句）；冒号后：Enroll more people in the PreCheck program（具体解释 one step 的内容）。", "zh": "美国运输安全管理局有一项举措既无需改建机场，也无需仓促招人，那便是：让更多人加入“预检”（PreCheck）项目。"}, {"en": "The TSA cannot continue diverting resources into underused PreCheck lanes while most of the traveling public suffers in unnecessary lines.", "point": "动名词短语作宾语 + while 引导对比状语从句 + 集合名词作主语的谓语单数一致", "structure": "主干：The TSA cannot continue diverting resources into underused PreCheck lanes；对比状语从句：while most of the traveling public suffers in unnecessary lines（the traveling public 整体视为单数，故用 suffers）。", "zh": "美国运输安全管理局不能再继续把资源分流到使用率低下的“预检”通道上，而让大多数乘机出行的大众在毫无必要的长队中苦苦煎熬。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第21题例证题：以坠机事件作为悲剧性提醒，解释为何民众愿忍受耗时安检。", "option": "explain Americans’ tolerance of current security checks", "original": "tolerate time-consuming security procedures in return for increased safety... provides another tragic reminder of why"}, {"note": "第22题细节题：航空出行增加即“旅客人数增长”。", "option": "An increase in the number of travelers.", "original": "a rise in airline travel"}, {"note": "第23题词义题：expedited（加急的、快速的）同义替换为 faster。", "option": "faster", "original": "expedited"}, {"note": "第24题细节题：85美元的价签被称为“致命缺陷”，即注册费用定价不合理。", "option": "an unreasonable price for enrollment", "original": "this price tag has been PreCheck’s fatal flaw"}, {"note": "第25题主旨标题题：全文聚焦机场大排长龙、旅客陷入安检队伍的困境。", "option": "Getting Stuck in Security Lines", "original": "increasingly massive security lines... suffers in unnecessary lines"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L3", "exam": "kaoyan1", "id": "ky1-2017-t2", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["“The ancient Hawaiians were astronomers,” wrote Queen Liliuokalani, Hawaii’s last reigning monarch, in 1897. Star watchers were among the most esteemed members of Hawaiian society. Sadly, all is not well with astronomy in Hawaii today. Protests have erupted over construction of the Thirty Meter Telescope (TMT), a giant observatory that promises to revolutionize humanity’s view of the cosmos.", "At issue is the TMT’s planned location on Mauna Kea, a dormant volcano worshiped by some Hawaiians as the piko, that connects the Hawaiian Islands to the heavens. But Mauna Kea is also home to some of the world’s most powerful telescopes. Rested in the Pacific Ocean, Mauna Kea’s peak rises above the bulk of our planet’s dense atmosphere, where conditions allow telescopes to obtain images of unsurpassed clarity.", "Opposition to telescopes on Mauna Kea is nothing new. A small but vocal group of Hawaiians and environmentalists have long viewed their presence as disrespect for sacred land and a painful reminder of the occupation of what was once a sovereign nation.", "Some blame for the current controversy belongs to astronomers. In their eagerness to build bigger telescopes, they forgot that science is not the only way of understanding the world. They did not always prioritize the protection of Mauna Kea’s fragile ecosystems or its holiness to the islands’ inhabitants. Hawaiian culture is not a relic of the past; it is a living culture undergoing a renaissance today.", "Yet science has a cultural history, too, with roots going back to the dawn of civilization. The same curiosity to find what lies beyond the horizon that first brought early Polynesians to Hawaii’s shores inspires astronomers today to explore the heavens. Calls to disassemble all telescopes on Mauna Kea or to ban future development there ignore the reality that astronomy and Hawaiian culture both seek to answer big questions about who we are, where we come from and where we are going. Perhaps that is why we explore the starry skies, as if answering a primal calling to know ourselves and our true ancestral homes.", "The astronomy community is making compromises to change its use of Mauna Kea. The TMT site was chosen to minimize the telescope’s visibility around the island and to avoid archaeological and environmental impact. To limit the number of telescopes on Mauna Kea, old ones will be removed at the end of their lifetimes and their sites returned to a natural state. There is no reason why everyone cannot be welcomed on Mauna Kea to embrace their cultural heritage and to study the stars."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "“The ancient Hawaiians were astronomers,” wrote Queen Liliuokalani, Hawaii’s last reigning monarch, in 1897. Star watchers were among the most esteemed members of Hawaiian society.", "explanation": "定位第1段前两句。作者引用利留卡拉尼女王的话指出“古代夏威夷人是天文学家”，并在下句紧接着阐明观星者（star watchers）在夏威夷社会中处于最受尊崇的地位（among the most esteemed members）。由此可推断，女王的话体现了天文学在古代夏威夷社会中的重要性（importance）。", "no": 26, "options": ["her conservative view on the historical role of astronomy", "the importance of astronomy in ancient Hawaiian society", "the regrettable decline of astronomy in ancient times", "her appreciation of star watchers’ feats in her time"], "stem": "Queen Liliuokalani’s remark in Paragraph 1 indicates ____.", "trapNote": "D项存在时间偷换陷阱，女王1897年发表该言论赞誉的是“ancient Hawaiians（古代夏威夷人）”，而非“in her time（她所处时代）”的观星者功绩。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Rested in the Pacific Ocean, Mauna Kea’s peak rises above the bulk of our planet’s dense atmosphere, where conditions allow telescopes to obtain images of unsurpassed clarity.", "explanation": "定位第2段第3句。该句指出莫纳克亚山位于太平洋之中（Rested in the Pacific Ocean），山峰高出地球绝大部分稠密大气层（rises above the bulk of our planet’s dense atmosphere），从而让望远镜拍出极其清晰的图像。A项“its geographical features（其地理特征）”准确概括了这一海岛位置与高海拔地形特征。", "no": 27, "options": ["its geographical features", "its protective surroundings", "its religious implications", "its existing infrastructure"], "stem": "Mauna Kea is deemed as an ideal astronomical site due to ____.", "trapNote": "C项属于因果错位，该山作为宗教圣地（piko）的意义是当地部分民众“反对”在此建造望远镜的理由，而非其成为理想天文台选址的原因。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "have long viewed their presence as disrespect for sacred land and a painful reminder of the occupation of what was once a sovereign nation.", "explanation": "定位第3段第2句。文中指出，一小群声音响亮的夏威夷人与环保人士长期把山上的望远镜看作对圣地的不敬，且是“对一个曾为主权国家被占领的痛苦提醒（a painful reminder of the occupation of what was once a sovereign nation）”。B项中的“reminds them of a humiliating history”正是对此痛苦历史记忆的同义替换。", "no": 28, "options": ["it may risk ruining their intellectual life", "it reminds them of a humiliating history", "their culture will lose a chance of revival", "they fear losing control of Mauna Kea"], "stem": "The construction of the TMT is opposed by some locals partly because ____.", "trapNote": "C项属于正反颠倒，第4段末句明确指出夏威夷文化并非过去遗迹，而是“如今正经历复兴的活文化（undergoing a renaissance today）”，并非将失去复兴机会。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The same curiosity to find what lies beyond the horizon that first brought early Polynesians to Hawaii’s shores inspires astronomers today to explore the heavens.", "explanation": "定位第5段第2至4句。该段强调最早驱使早期波利尼西亚人（古代夏威夷先民）来到夏威夷的“探索地平线之外的好奇心”，如今同样激励着当代天文学家探索苍穹；天文学与夏威夷文化都在追问人类从何而来等终极问题，探索星空仿佛回应着认识自我与祖先家园的“原始呼唤（primal calling）”。由此可推知，当今的天文学进步正实现着古代夏威夷人的梦想与追求。", "no": 29, "options": ["is fulfilling the dreams of ancient Hawaiians", "helps spread Hawaiian culture across the world", "may uncover the origin of Hawaiian culture", "will eventually soften Hawaiians’ hostility"], "stem": "It can be inferred from Paragraph 5 that progress in today’s astronomy ____.", "trapNote": "C项属于偷换概念，第5段说的是天文学与夏威夷文化“共同寻求解答人类从何而来（where we come from）的宏大问题”，而非天文学能揭开“夏威夷文化本身的起源（the origin of Hawaiian culture）”。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "There is no reason why everyone cannot be welcomed on Mauna Kea to embrace their cultural heritage and to study the stars.", "explanation": "定位第5段第3句与第6段全段。作者先是否定了禁止未来在莫纳克亚山进行天文开发的呼声，接着在第6段列举天文学界为减少视觉、考古与生态影响所采取的让步举措，并在末句明确表示“没有任何理由不能欢迎大家在莫纳克亚山拥抱文化遗产并研究星空”。这清晰地表达了作者对选址莫纳克亚山建造TMT的完全赞同（full approval）。", "no": 30, "options": ["severe criticism", "passive acceptance", "slight hesitancy", "full approval"], "stem": "The author’s attitude toward choosing Mauna Kea as the TMT site is one of ____.", "trapNote": "B项“被动接受”与C项“轻微犹豫”均曲解了作者态度，末段末句“There is no reason why... cannot...”以双重否定句式展现了非常明确且充分的肯定立场。", "type": "态度题"}], "sourceLabel": "2017 考研英语一真题", "subtitle": "2017年考研英语一 阅读理解 Part A · Text 2", "timeLimitMin": 18, "title": "Text 2: Astronomy and Cultural Heritage on Mauna Kea", "year": "2017", "wordCount": 431, "examSet": "2017 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "translations": ["“古代夏威夷人就是天文学家。”夏威夷最后一位在位君主利留卡拉尼女王在1897年这样写道。观星者曾是夏威夷社会中最受尊敬的成员之一。遗憾的是，如今夏威夷的天文学发展并不顺利。围绕着有望彻底改变人类宇宙观的巨型天文台——30米望远镜（TMT）的建设，抗议活动已经爆发。", "争议的焦点在于30米望远镜选址于莫纳克亚山——这是一座被部分夏威夷人尊奉为“脐带”（piko）的休眠火山，象征着夏威夷群岛与苍穹的连接。但莫纳克亚山同时也是世界上一些最强大望远镜的所在地。它坐落于太平洋之中，山峰高耸于地球浓密大气层的主体之上，那里的环境条件使望远镜能够获取清晰度无与伦比的图像。", "对莫纳克亚山上建造望远镜的反对声音并非新鲜事。一小群但态度坚决的夏威夷民众与环保人士长期以来一直认为，望远镜的存在是对圣地的不敬，也是对这片曾经的主权国家领土遭侵占的痛苦提醒。", "引发当前这场争议，天文学家自身也有一定责任。他们急于建造更大的望远镜，却忘记了科学并非理解世界的唯一方式。他们并不总是将保护莫纳克亚山脆弱的生态系统或尊重其对岛上居民的神圣意义放在首位。夏威夷文化并非过去的遗迹，而是一种在当代正经历复兴的活态文化。", "然而，科学同样拥有文化历史，其根源可追溯至人类文明的黎明时期。当年驱使早期波利尼西亚人驶向夏威夷海岸、去探寻地平线之外未知世界的同一种好奇心，如今也在激励着天文学家探索苍穹。要求拆除莫纳克亚山上所有望远镜或禁止未来在当地开展建设的呼声，忽视了这样一个现实：天文学与夏威夷文化都在试图回答关于“我们是谁、我们从哪里来、我们要到哪里去”的宏大问题。或许正因如此，我们才仰望并探索星空，仿佛在回应一种原始的召唤，去认识自我以及我们真正的祖先家园。", "天文学界正在做出妥协，以改变其对莫纳克亚山的使用方式。30米望远镜的选址旨在最大限度减少其在全岛范围内的可见度，并避免对考古遗迹和生态环境造成影响。为了控制莫纳克亚山上的望远镜数量，老旧望远镜将在使用寿命到期后被拆除，其所在地也将恢复至自然状态。没有任何理由不能让所有人都在莫纳克亚山上受到欢迎，共同拥抱自己的文化遗产并研究星辰。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "受尊敬的，敬重的", "note": "高频正态度形容词，源于动词 esteem（尊重/认为），考研阅读常用于评价社会地位或人物声望。", "word": "esteemed"}, {"gloss": "休眠的，蛰伏的", "note": "常见于科普与文化类阅读（如 dormant volcano 休眠火山），引申义为“暂不活动的、潜在的”。", "word": "dormant"}, {"gloss": "优先考虑，给予……优先权", "note": "阅读与写作高频动词，常与 protect/safety 等搭配，对应名词为 priority（优先事项）。", "word": "prioritize"}, {"gloss": "拆开，拆卸", "note": "构词法高频词：dis-（分离）+ assemble（组装）= 拆卸、拆除；反义词为 assemble。", "word": "disassemble"}, {"gloss": "无与伦比的，未被超越的", "note": "构词法词：un-（未）+ surpass（超越）+ -ed = 卓越的、无出其右的，常作极高评价词。", "word": "unsurpassed"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "At issue is the TMT’s planned location on Mauna Kea, a dormant volcano worshiped by some Hawaiians as the piko, that connects the Hawaiian Islands to the heavens.", "point": "表语前置引起的全部倒装 + 名词同位语 + 过去分词短语作后置定语", "structure": "倒装主干：The TMT’s planned location on Mauna Kea is at issue（表语 At issue 置于句首构成全部倒装）；同位语：a dormant volcano... 补充说明 Mauna Kea；过去分词短语作后置定语：worshiped by some Hawaiians as the piko 修饰 volcano；定语从句：that connects the Hawaiian Islands to the heavens 修饰 the piko。", "zh": "争议的焦点在于30米望远镜选址于莫纳克亚山——这是一座被部分夏威夷人尊奉为“脐带”（piko）、将夏威夷群岛与苍穹连接起来的休眠火山。"}, {"en": "The same curiosity to find what lies beyond the horizon that first brought early Polynesians to Hawaii’s shores inspires astronomers today to explore the heavens.", "point": "不定式短语与定语从句共同修饰同一先行词 + what 引导的宾语从句", "structure": "主干：The same curiosity inspires astronomers today to explore the heavens；不定式短语作后置定语：to find what lies beyond the horizon 修饰 curiosity（内含宾语从句 what lies beyond the horizon）；定语从句：that first brought early Polynesians to Hawaii’s shores 同样修饰先行词 The same curiosity。", "zh": "当年首次将早期波利尼西亚人带到夏威夷海岸、驱使他们去探寻地平线之外奥秘的同一种好奇心，如今也在激励着天文学家探索宇宙苍穹。"}, {"en": "Calls to disassemble all telescopes on Mauna Kea or to ban future development there ignore the reality that astronomy and Hawaiian culture both seek to answer big questions about who we are, where we come from and where we are going.", "point": "that 引导的同位语从句 + 并列不定式作后置定语 + 并列宾语从句", "structure": "主干：Calls ... ignore the reality；并列不定式作后置定语：to disassemble ... or to ban ... 修饰 Calls；同位语从句：that astronomy and Hawaiian culture both seek to answer big questions... 解释说明 the reality；介词宾语从句：who we are, where we come from and where we are going 并列作 about 的宾语。", "zh": "要求拆除莫纳克亚山上所有望远镜或禁止未来在当地进行建设的呼声，忽视了这样一个现实：天文学和夏威夷文化都在试图回答关于我们是谁、从何而来以及去往何方的重大问题。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第26题同义替换：原文“最受尊敬的成员之一”对应选项“天文学在古夏威夷社会中的重要性”。", "option": "the importance of astronomy in ancient Hawaiian society", "original": "among the most esteemed members of Hawaiian society"}, {"note": "第27题高度概括：原文描述海拔高于浓密大气层等自然条件，选项概括为“其地理特征”。", "option": "its geographical features", "original": "rises above the bulk of our planet’s dense atmosphere"}, {"note": "第28题同义替换：原文“对昔日主权国家遭侵占的痛苦提醒”对应选项“让他们想起屈辱的历史”。", "option": "it reminds them of a humiliating history", "original": "a painful reminder of the occupation of what was once a sovereign nation"}, {"note": "第29题推理引申：当代天文学受同一种探索未知的好奇心驱使，意在延续并实现古代夏威夷先民的探索梦想。", "option": "is fulfilling the dreams of ancient Hawaiians", "original": "The same curiosity ... that first brought early Polynesians ... inspires astronomers today"}, {"note": "第30题态度判断：双重否定“没有理由不欢迎……”表达作者对在莫纳克亚山建望远镜并与文化共存持“完全赞同”的态度。", "option": "full approval", "original": "There is no reason why everyone cannot be welcomed on Mauna Kea"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2017-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2017", "examSet": "2017 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2017 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "GDP与国民幸福：英国脱欧的反思", "subtitle": "2017 考研英语一 Text 3 · 经济指标与社会福祉", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 429, "paragraphs": ["Robert F. Kennedy once said that a country’s GDP measures “everything except that which makes life worthwhile.” With Britain voting to leave the European Union, and GDP already predicted to slow as a result, it is now a timely moment to assess what he was referring to.", "The question of GDP and its usefulness has annoyed policymakers for over half a century. Many argue that it is a flawed concept. It measures things that do not matter and misses things that do. By most recent measures, the UK’s GDP has been the envy of the Western world, with record low unemployment and high growth figures. If everything was going so well, then why did over 17 million people vote for Brexit, despite the warnings about what it could do to their country’s economic prospects?", "A recent annual study of countries and their ability to convert growth into well-being sheds some light on that question. Across the 163 countries measured, the UK is one of the poorest performers in ensuring that economic growth is translated into meaningful improvements for its citizens. Rather than just focusing on GDP, over 40 different sets of criteria from health, education and civil society engagement have been measured to get a more rounded assessment of how countries are performing.", "While all of these countries face their own challenges, there are a number of consistent themes. Yes, there has been a budding economic recovery since the 2008 global crash, but in key indicators in areas such as health and education, major economies have continued to decline. Yet this isn’t the case with all countries. Some relatively poor European countries have seen huge improvements across measures including civil society, income equality and environment.", "This is a lesson that rich countries can learn: When GDP is no longer regarded as the sole measure of a country’s success, the world looks very different.", "So, what Kennedy was referring to was that while GDP has been the most common method for measuring the economic activity of nations, as a measure, it is no longer enough. It does not include important factors such as environmental quality or education outcomes – all things that contribute to a person’s sense of well-being.", "The sharp hit to growth predicted around the world and in the UK could lead to a decline in the everyday services we depend on for our well-being and for growth. But policymakers who refocus efforts on improving well-being rather than simply worrying about GDP figures could avoid the forecasted doom and may even see progress."], "translations": ["罗伯特·F·肯尼迪曾说过，一个国家的GDP衡量了“除让生命有价值之物外的一切”。随着英国投票决定脱离欧盟，且GDP预计也将因此放缓，现在正是评估他所指含义的适当时机。", "GDP及其有用性的问题已经困扰了政策制定者半个多世纪。许多人认为这是一个有缺陷的概念：它衡量了无关紧要的事物，却遗漏了真正重要的东西。按最近的大多数标准来看，英国的GDP一直是西方世界羡慕的对象，其失业率创历史新低，增长数据强劲。但如果一切都进展得如此顺利，为何仍有超过1700万人不顾关于此举可能损害国家经济前景的警告而投票支持脱欧呢？", "最近一项关于各国及其将经济增长转化为国民福祉能力的年度研究为这个问题提供了一些启发。在受评估的163个国家中，英国在确保将经济增长转化为民众切实改善方面的表现是最差的国家之一。为了更全面地评估各国的表现，该研究没有仅仅关注GDP，而是衡量了涵盖健康、教育和公民社会参与等领域的40多套不同标准。", "尽管所有这些国家都面临各自的挑战，但其中存在一些一贯的趋势。诚然，自2008年全球金融危机以来，经济出现了复苏萌芽，但在健康和教育等领域的 key（关键）指标上，主要经济体却在持续下滑。然而，并非所有国家都是如此。一些相对贫穷的欧洲国家在公民社会、收入平等和环境等指标上都取得了巨大进步。", "这是富裕国家可以吸取的一个教训：当GDP不再被视为衡量国家成功的唯一标准时，世界看起来会大不相同。", "因此，肯尼迪所指的是：尽管GDP一直是衡量各国经济活动最常用的方法，但作为一种衡量标准，它已经不再足够。它没有包括环境质量或教育成果等重要因素——而所有这些都构成了人们的幸福感。", "预计全球和英国经济增长将遭遇急剧冲击，这可能导致我们赖以维系福祉和增长的日常服务出现滑坡。但政策制定者若能将工作重心重新聚焦于改善国民福祉，而不是一味担忧GDP数字，就能避免预测中的厄运，甚至可能看到进步。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Robert F. Kennedy is cited because he", "options": ["praised the UK for its GDP.", "identified GDP with happiness.", "misinterpreted the role of GDP.", "had a low opinion of GDP."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Robert F. Kennedy once said that a country’s GDP measures “everything except that which makes life worthwhile.”", "explanation": "定位第一段首句。文章开篇引用罗伯特·F·肯尼迪的名言：一个国家的GDP衡量了“除让生命有价值之物外的一切”。紧接着作者指出，随着英国公投脱欧且GDP预计放缓，现在正是评估他所指含义的适当时机。这表明肯尼迪认为GDP遗漏了真正重要的东西，即他对GDP持批评或轻视态度（had a low opinion of GDP），故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“赞扬英国GDP”与原文引用肯尼迪批评GDP的立场正反颠倒；B项“将GDP等同于幸福”与“除让生命有价值之物外”恰好相反；C项“误解GDP作用”属于无中生有，作者对其观点持肯定态度。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be inferred from Paragraph 2 that", "options": ["the UK is reluctant to remold its economic pattern.", "GDP as the measure of success is widely defied in the UK.", "the UK will contribute less to the world economy.", "policymakers in the UK are paying less attention to GDP."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "If everything was going so well, then why did over 17 million people vote for Brexit, despite the warnings about what it could do to their country’s economic prospects?", "explanation": "定位第二段末句。前文提到按近期标准，英国GDP增速高、失业率创纪录新低，曾是西方羡慕的对象；但随后作者反问：既然一切看似向好，为何仍有超过1700万英国人无视对其经济前景的警告而投票支持脱欧？由此可推知，在英国，人们并不完全买账将GDP作为衡量国家成功的标准（is widely defied），故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“英国不愿重塑经济模式”和C项“英国对世界经济贡献将减少”在第二段均未提及，属无中生有；D项“英国决策者越来越不重视GDP”偷换概念，挑战GDP至上的是投票民众而非决策者。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is true about the recent annual study?", "options": ["It is sponsored by 163 countries.", "It excludes GDP as an indicator.", "Its criteria are questionable.", "Its results are enlightening."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "A recent annual study of countries and their ability to convert growth into well-being sheds some light on that question.", "explanation": "定位第三段第一句。针对第二段提出的“高GDP与脱欧投票的矛盾”，第三段指出，近期一项关于各国将经济增长转化为国民福祉能力的年度研究“为这一问题提供了一些启发（sheds some light on that question）”。题干中enlightening（富有启发的）正是sheds some light on的同义替换，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“由163个国家赞助”属于偷换概念，原文Across the 163 countries measured指“被评估的163个国家”，并非赞助方；B项“排除GDP指标”与原文“不仅仅关注GDP”相悖。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "In the last two paragraphs, the author suggests that", "options": ["the UK is preparing for an economic boom.", "high GDP foreshadows an economic decline.", "it is essential to consider factors beyond GDP.", "it requires caution to handle economic issues."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "It does not include important factors such as environmental quality or education outcomes – all things that contribute to a person’s sense of well-being.", "explanation": "定位最后两段。第六段指出GDP作为衡量指标“已不再足够（no longer enough）”，因为它未包含环境质量、教育成果等提升幸福感的重要因素；第七段进一步提出，政策制定者若将重心转向提升福祉而非单纯担忧GDP数字，就能避免危机甚至取得进展。综合两段可知作者建议必须考虑GDP之外的因素，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“英国正准备迎接经济繁荣”与第七段“预测全球和英国经济增长将受重创”正反颠倒；B项“高GDP预示经济衰退”属强加因果与过度推理；D项“处理经济问题需谨慎”偏离核心主旨。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following is the best title for the text?", "options": ["High GDP But Inadequate Well-being, a UK Lesson", "GDP Figures, a Window on Global Economic Health", "Robert F. Kennedy, a Terminator of GDP", "Brexit, the UK’s Gateway to Well-being"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "This is a lesson that rich countries can learn: When GDP is no longer regarded as the sole measure of a country’s success, the world looks very different.", "explanation": "纵观全文，第一至三段以英国为例，指出其GDP表现亮眼却在“将增长转化为福祉”上垫底，这也是民众选择脱欧的原因之一；第四至七段借年度研究和肯尼迪名言指出，不应再把GDP当成唯一标准，而要关注环境、教育等福祉因素，这正是“发达国家（尤其是英国）可汲取的教训”。A项精准概括全文主旨与英国例证，故正确。", "trapNote": "B项“GDP数字是全球经济健康的窗口”与全文批判GDP局限性的基调正反颠倒；C项“肯尼迪是GDP终结者”以偏概全且过度夸张；D项“脱欧是英国通往福祉之门”属于无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "有缺陷的，不完善的", "note": "flaw（缺陷）的形容词形式；常修饰概念、体系或论证，等同于defective/imperfect。", "word": "flawed"}, {"gloss": "反抗，蔑视，公然无视", "note": "熟词僻义/高频核心动词；Q32正确选项出现is widely defied，表示“遭到广泛质疑/公然挑战”。", "word": "defy"}, {"gloss": "转变，转化", "note": "常与into搭配（convert A into B），第三段与translate...into...构成同义复现。", "word": "convert"}, {"gloss": "全面的，圆润丰满的", "note": "熟词僻义；a more rounded assessment意为“更全面的评估”，而非字面的“圆形的”。", "word": "rounded"}, {"gloss": "萌芽的，初露端倪的", "note": "由bud（花蕾/萌芽）转化而来；a budding economic recovery指“刚刚起步的经济复苏”。", "word": "budding"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "With Britain voting to leave the European Union, and GDP already predicted to slow as a result, it is now a timely moment to assess what he was referring to.", "point": "with独立主格结构（with + 名词 + 分词短语）作伴随状语，后接形式主语it句型。", "structure": "With + 复合宾语（Britain voting..., and GDP predicted...）作状语 + 主句（it作形式主语，to assess...作真正主语，what引导宾语从句）。", "zh": "随着英国投票决定脱离欧盟，且GDP预计也将因此放缓，现在正是评估他所指含义的适当时机。"}, {"en": "Across the 163 countries measured, the UK is one of the poorest performers in ensuring that economic growth is translated into meaningful improvements for its citizens.", "point": "过去分词measured作后置定语，in ensuring后接that引导的宾语从句，注意be translated into意为“转化为”。", "structure": "地点/范围状语（Across the 163 countries measured） + 主系表（the UK is one of the poorest performers） + 介词短语（in ensuring + that宾语从句）。", "zh": "在受评估的163个国家中，英国在确保将经济增长转化为民众切实改善方面的表现是最差的国家之一。"}, {"en": "So, what Kennedy was referring to was that while GDP has been the most common method for measuring the economic activity of nations, as a measure, it is no longer enough.", "point": "what引导的主语从句配that引导的表语从句，表语从句内部嵌套while引导的让步状语从句。", "structure": "主语从句（what Kennedy was referring to） + 系动词（was） + 表语从句（that [while让步状语从句], it is no longer enough）。", "zh": "因此，肯尼迪所指的是：尽管GDP一直是衡量各国经济活动最常用的方法，但作为一种衡量标准，它已经不再足够。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "引文中的否定排除表达转化为对肯尼迪个人态度的评价。", "option": "had a low opinion of GDP", "original": "measures “everything except that which makes life worthwhile.”"}, {"note": "用隐喻习语“照亮/揭示某问题”同义替换为“具有启发性的”。", "option": "enlightening", "original": "sheds some light on that question"}, {"note": "由“已不再足够且忽略重要幸福要素”概括为“必须考虑GDP之外的因素”。", "option": "consider factors beyond GDP", "original": "it is no longer enough. It does not include important factors..."}, {"note": "将经济增长转化为民众生活改善的能力，高度凝练为“转化增长为福祉”。", "option": "inadequate well-being", "original": "one of the poorest performers in ensuring that economic growth is translated into meaningful improvements"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2017-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2017", "examSet": "2017 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2017 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "美国最高法院推翻前州长受贿案裁决", "subtitle": "2017 考研英语一 Text 4 · 司法裁决与廉政透明", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 404, "paragraphs": ["In a rare unanimous ruling, the U.S. Supreme Court has overturned the corruption conviction of a former Virginia governor, Robert McDonnell. But it did so while holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct, which included accepting gifts such as a Rolex watch and a Ferrari Automobile from a company seeking access to government.", "The high court’s decision said the judge in Mr. McDonnell’s trial failed to tell a jury that it must look only at his “official acts,” or the former governor’s decisions on “specific” and “unsettled” issues related to his duties.", "Merely helping a gift-giver gain access to other officials, unless done with clear intent to pressure those officials, is not corruption, the justices found.", "The court did suggest that accepting favors in return for opening doors is “distasteful” and “nasty.” But under anti-bribery laws, proof must be made of concrete benefits, such as approval of a contract or regulation. Simply arranging a meeting, making a phone call, or hosting an event is not an “official act”.", "The court’s ruling is legally sound in defining a kind of favoritism that is not criminal. Elected leaders must be allowed to help supporters deal with bureaucratic problems without fear of prosecution of bribery. “The basic compact underlying representative government,” wrote Chief Justice John Roberts for the court, “assumes that public officials will hear from their constituents and act on their concerns.”", "But the ruling reinforces the need for citizens and their elected representatives, not the courts, to ensure equality of access to government. Officials must not be allowed to play favorites in providing information or in arranging meetings simply because an individual or group provides a campaign donation or a personal gift. This type of integrity requires well-enforced laws in government transparency, such as records of official meetings, rules on lobbying, and information about each elected leader’s source of wealth.", "Favoritism in official access can fan public perceptions of corruption. But it is not always corruption. Rather officials must avoid double standards, or different types of access for average people and the wealthy. If connections can be bought, a basic premise of democratic society—that all are equal in treatment by government—is undermined. Good governance rests on an understanding of the inherent worth of each individual.", "The court’s ruling is a step forward in the struggle against both corruption and official favoritism."], "translations": ["在一次罕见的一致裁决中，美国最高法院推翻了前弗吉尼亚州州长罗伯特·麦克唐纳的腐败定罪。但法院在作出这一裁决的同时，对他行为的道德操守深表厌恶——这些行为包括收受一家试图接近政府部门的公司赠送的劳力士手表和法拉利跑车等礼物。", "最高法院的裁决指出，审理麦克唐纳一案的法官未能告知陪审团，其只能审视他的“公务行为”，即这位前州长就与其职责相关的“具体”且“尚未解决”的事务作出的决定。", "大法官们认定，仅仅帮助送礼者获得接触其他官员的机会，除非明确意图向这些官员施压，否则并不构成腐败。", "法院确实表示，收受好处作为打通关系门的回报是“令人作呕”和“卑劣”的。但根据反贿赂法，必须证明存在具体的利益，例如批准某项合同或法规。仅仅安排一次会面、打一个电话或主办一场活动，并不属于“公务行为”。", "法院的裁决在界定一种不构成犯罪的偏袒行为方面在法律上是站得住脚的。必须允许民选领导人帮助支持者解决官僚体制带来的问题，而不必担心遭到受贿起诉。首席大法官约翰·罗伯茨代表法院写道：“代议制政府的基本契约假定公职人员会倾听选民的诉求，并对其关切采取行动。”", "但这项裁决也强化了一个必要性：应当由公民及其民选代表——而不是法院——来确保平等接触政府的机会。绝不能允许官员仅仅因为某个个人或团体提供了竞选捐款或私人礼物，就在提供信息或安排会面时偏袒一方。这种廉洁性需要严格执行的政府透明法来保障，例如官方会议记录、游说规定以及每位民选领导人的财富来源信息。", "在官方接触中搞偏袒会助长公众对腐败的看法，但这并不总是腐败。相反，官员必须避免双重标准，即对普通民众和富人提供不同规格的接触机会。如果关系可以用钱买到，那么民主社会的一个基本前提——所有人在受到政府对待时一律平等——就会遭到破坏。良政建立在对每个人内在价值的理解之上。", "最高法院的这项裁决是在打击腐败与官方偏袒的斗争中迈出的向前一步。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The underlined sentence (Para.1) most probably shows that the court", "options": ["avoided defining the extent of McDonnell’s duties.", "made no compromise in convicting McDonnell.", "was contemptuous of McDonnell’s conduct.", "refused to comment on McDonnell’s ethics."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "But it did so while holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct, which included accepting gifts such as a Rolex watch and a Ferrari Automobile from a company seeking access to government.", "explanation": "定位第一段第二句。美国最高法院推翻了前弗吉尼亚州长麦克唐纳的腐败定罪，但“did so while holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct”。英文习语hold one’s nose字面意为“捏住鼻子”，引申为“掩鼻而过、对……深感厌恶/鄙视”。结合第四段“distasteful”和“nasty”的评价，可知法院对其行为持鄙夷态度，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "D项“拒绝评论其道德操守”最易误选，但“捏住鼻子”本身就是强烈的负面态度表达，并非拒绝评论，属正反颠倒；B项“在定罪上毫不妥协”与首句“推翻定罪”直接矛盾。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 4, an official act is deemed corruptive only if it involves", "options": ["leaking secrets intentionally.", "sizable gains in the form of gifts.", "concrete returns for gift-givers.", "breaking contracts officially."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "But under anti-bribery laws, proof must be made of concrete benefits, such as approval of a contract or regulation.", "explanation": "定位第四段第二句。题干询问根据第四段，公务行为在何种情况下才会被认定为腐败。原文明确指出，依据反贿赂法，“必须证明存在具体的利益回报（proof must be made of concrete benefits），例如批准某项合同或法规”。选项C中的concrete returns for gift-givers与原文concrete benefits形成同义替换，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“以礼物形式获得可观收益”偷换概念，礼物体现的是送礼者给官员的好处，而法院要求证明官员为送礼者提供“具体利益回报”；A、D项均属无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The court’s ruling is based on the assumption that public officials are", "options": ["justified in addressing the needs of their constituents.", "qualified to deal independently with bureaucratic issues.", "allowed to focus on the concerns of their supporters.", "exempt from conviction on the charge of favoritism."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "“The basic compact underlying representative government,” wrote Chief Justice John Roberts for the court, “assumes that public officials will hear from their constituents and act on their concerns.”", "explanation": "定位第五段最后一句。首席大法官约翰·罗伯茨在代表法院撰写的意见中指出，代议制政府的基本契约“假定公职人员会倾听选民诉求并对其关切采取行动（hear from their constituents and act on their concerns）”。A项中的addressing the needs of their constituents精准对应原文，且前文也说明应允许民选官员帮支持者解决官僚问题，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "C项“只准关注支持者的诉求”极具迷惑性，但大法官强调的是面向全体选民（constituents），而非仅仅支持者（supporters），属于偷换范围；B项“独立处理”和D项“免予偏袒指控”均属无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Well-enforced laws in government transparency are needed to", "options": ["awaken the conscience of officials.", "guarantee fair play in official access.", "allow for certain kinds of lobbying.", "inspire hopes in average people."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "This type of integrity requires well-enforced laws in government transparency, such as records of official meetings, rules on lobbying, and information about each elected leader’s source of wealth.", "explanation": "定位第六段第三句。该段首句提出需确保公民“平等接触政府的权利（equality of access to government）”，第二句强调官员不得因捐款或礼物而在提供信息、安排会面上“偏袒特定人士（play favorites）”，随后指出“这种廉洁需要严格执行的政府透明法来保障”。可见透明法的目的是保证接触政府渠道的公平（fair play），故B项正确。", "trapNote": "C项“允许某些游说活动”误解了原文rules on lobbying（对游说的规范监管），属正反颠倒；A项“唤醒官员良知”与D项“激发普通民众希望”在第六段均未提及，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author’s attitude toward the court’s ruling is", "options": ["sarcastic.", "tolerant.", "skeptical.", "supportive."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 8, "evidenceQuote": "The court’s ruling is a step forward in the struggle against both corruption and official favoritism.", "explanation": "定位第五段与第八段。第五段首句作者明确评价该裁决“在界定一种不构成犯罪的偏袒行为方面在法律上是站得住脚的（legally sound）”；文章结尾第八段进一步总结称，“最高法院的这项裁决是在打击腐败与官方偏袒的斗争中迈出的向前一步（a step forward）”。由此可见作者对法院裁决持明确的肯定和支持态度，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“宽容的”往往带有对原本不认同之事勉强接受的意味，而作者直接称其legally sound和a step forward，属正面赞赏而非宽容；A项“讽刺的”和C项“怀疑的”均与原文立场相反。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "推翻，撤销（判决等）", "note": "法律阅读高频词；也可表示“打翻”。文中overturn the corruption conviction意为“推翻腐败定罪”。", "word": "overturn"}, {"gloss": "偏袒，徇私", "note": "派生自favorite，后文play favorites（偏袒、搞特殊）为其动词短语同义表达。", "word": "favoritism"}, {"gloss": "选区居民，选民", "note": "常考政治/法律类词汇；也可指“组成部分”（作形容词意为“组成的”）。注意与supporters（支持者）区分。", "word": "constituent"}, {"gloss": "煽动，激起", "note": "熟词僻义；作名词是“扇子”，作动词在文中fan public perceptions of corruption意为“助长/煽动公众对腐败的看法”。", "word": "fan"}, {"gloss": "契约，协定", "note": "熟词僻义；作形容词意为“紧凑的、小巧的”，作名词在法律语境中指“契约、协议”（the basic compact）。", "word": "compact"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "But it did so while holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct, which included accepting gifts such as a Rolex watch and a Ferrari Automobile from a company seeking access to government.", "point": "did so指代前句的overturned the corruption conviction；while引导时间/伴随状语从句省略，which引导非限制性定语从句修饰conduct。", "structure": "主句（it did so） + 状语（while holding its nose at...） + 非限制性定语从句（which included...） + 现在分词短语作后置定语（seeking access to government）。", "zh": "但最高法院在作出这一裁决的同时，对他行为的道德操守深表厌恶——这些行为包括收受一家试图接触政府部门的公司赠送的劳力士手表和法拉利跑车等礼物。"}, {"en": "The high court’s decision said the judge in Mr. McDonnell’s trial failed to tell a jury that it must look only at his “official acts,” or the former governor’s decisions on “specific” and “unsettled” issues related to his duties.", "point": "多层宾语从句嵌套，or在此处不是“或者”，而是引导同位语对official acts进行解释说明。", "structure": "主句（The high court’s decision said） + 宾语从句1（the judge... failed to tell a jury） + 宾语从句2（that it must look only at...） + or引出的同位语解释。", "zh": "最高法院的裁决指出，审理麦克唐纳一案的法官未能告知陪审团，其只能审视他的“公务行为”，即这位前州长就与其职责相关的“具体”且“尚未解决”的事务作出的决定。"}, {"en": "If connections can be bought, a basic premise of democratic society—that all are equal in treatment by government—is undermined.", "point": "两个破折号之间是that引导的同位语从句，解释说明a basic premise；主句采用被动语态is undermined。", "structure": "If条件状语从句（If connections can be bought） + 主句主语（a basic premise...） + 同位语从句（—that all are equal...—） + 主句谓语（is undermined）。", "zh": "如果关系可以用钱买到，那么民主社会的一个基本前提——所有人在受到政府对待时一律平等——就会遭到破坏。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "习语“捏住鼻子”表达厌恶/鄙视，与选项中“鄙夷的”构成情感同义替换。", "option": "was contemptuous of McDonnell’s conduct", "original": "holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct"}, {"note": "“具体利益”在给送礼者回报的语境下直接对应“给送礼者的具体回报”。", "option": "concrete returns for gift-givers", "original": "concrete benefits, such as approval of a contract or regulation"}, {"note": "“倾听选民诉求并采取行动”同义替换为“合法合理地解决选民需求”。", "option": "justified in addressing the needs of their constituents", "original": "hear from their constituents and act on their concerns"}, {"note": "“确保接触政府渠道的平等、不偏袒”同义替换为“保障官方接触中的公平竞争”。", "option": "guarantee fair play in official access", "original": "ensure equality of access to government... must not be allowed to play favorites"}, {"note": "结尾段肯定裁决为“向前一步”，直接体现作者“支持”的立场。", "option": "supportive", "original": "a step forward in the struggle against both corruption and official favoritism"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2016-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2016", "examSet": "2016 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2016 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "挑战时尚业身材审美标准的不同路径", "subtitle": "对比法国立法重罚与丹麦行业自律，探讨审美标准之重塑", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 427, "paragraphs": ["France, which prides itself as the global innovator of fashion, has decided its fashion industry has lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women. Its lawmakers gave preliminary approval last week to a law that would make it a crime to employ ultra-thin models on runways. The parliament also agreed to ban websites that \"incite excessive thinness\" by promoting extreme dieting.", "Such measures have a couple of uplifting motives. They suggest beauty should not be defined by looks that end up impinging on health. That's a start. And the ban on ultra-thin models seems to go beyond protecting models from starving themselves to death - as some have done. It tells the fashion industry that it must take responsibility for the signal it sends women, especially teenage girls, about the social tape-measure they must use to determine their individual worth. The bans, if fully enforced, would suggest to women (and many men) that they should not let others be arbiters of their beauty. And perhaps faintly, they hint that people should look to intangible qualities like character and intellect rather than dieting their way to size zero or wasp-waist physiques.", "The French measures, however, rely too much on severe punishment to change a culture that still regards beauty as skin-deep - and bone-showing. Under the law, using a fashion model that does not meet a government-defined index of body mass could result in a $85,000 fine and six months in prison. The fashion industry knows it has an inherent problem in focusing on material adornment and idealized body types. In Denmark, the United States, and a few other countries, it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images that rely more on peer pressure for enforcement.", "In contrast to France's actions, Denmark's fashion industry agreed last month on rules and sanctions regarding the age, health, and other characteristics of models. The newly revised Danish Fashion Ethical Charter clearly states: \"We are aware of and take responsibility for the impact the fashion industry has on body ideals, especially on young people.\" The charter's main tool of enforcement is to deny access for designers and modeling agencies to Copenhagen Fashion Week (CFW), which is run by the Danish Fashion Institute. But in general it relies on a name-and-shame method of compliance.", "Relying on ethical persuasion rather than law to address the misuse of body ideals may be the best step. Even better would be to help elevate notions of beauty beyond the material standards of a particular industry."], "translations": ["自诩为全球时尚创新者的法国已认定，其时尚产业不再拥有为女性定义形体美的绝对权力。上周，法国议员初步批准了一项法案，将雇用过瘦模特走秀定为犯罪。议会还同意取缔那些通过鼓吹极端节食来“煽动过度消瘦”的网站。", "此类措施背后有几个令人振奋的动机。它们表明，美不应由最终会损害健康的容貌体态来定义。这是一个良好的开端。而且，对过瘦模特的禁令似乎不仅是为了保护模特免于饿死——过去确有模特因此丧命。它还告诫时尚业必须为其向女性——尤其是少女——发出的信号负责，即她们必须用什么样的社会“量尺”来衡量自身价值。这些禁令如果得到全面执行，将向女性（以及许多男性）传达这样的信息：他们不应让他人成为自己美的评判者。或许，这些禁令还隐约暗示人们应当看重品格和才智等无形品质，而不是通过节食追求零号身材或蜂腰体型。", "然而，法国的措施过于依赖严厉惩罚来改变一种仍将美视为“肤浅表面”——甚至“瘦骨嶙峋”——的文化。根据该法律，使用不符合政府规定身体质量指数的时装模特，可能会被处以8.5万美元罚款和6个月监禁。时尚业深知自身在过度关注物质修饰和理想化体型方面存在固有问题。在丹麦、美国和少数其他国家，该行业正试图为模特和时尚形象制定更依赖同行压力来执行的自愿标准。", "与法国的举措不同，丹麦时尚业上个月就模特的年龄、健康和其他特征达成了规则与制裁协议。新修订的《丹麦时尚道德宪章》明确指出：“我们意识到时尚业对身材理想——尤其是对年轻人——产生的影响，并对此承担责任。”该宪章的主要执行手段是拒绝设计师和模特经纪公司参加由丹麦时尚协会主办的哥本哈根时装周（CFW）。不过总的来说，它依赖的是一种“点名羞辱”的守规机制。", "依靠道德劝说而非法律手段来解决身材理想被滥用的问题，或许是最佳的一步。而更好的一步，则是帮助提升美的观念，使其超越某一特定行业的物质标准。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the first paragraph, what would happen in France?", "options": ["Physical beauty would be redefined.", "New runways would be constructed.", "Websites about dieting would thrive.", "The fashion industry would decline."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "France, which prides itself as the global innovator of fashion, has decided its fashion industry has lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women.", "explanation": "定位至第1段首句。原文指出，以全球时尚创新者自居的法国已经认定，其时尚产业失去了“为女性定义形体美的绝对权力”（lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women）。随后议会初步通过法案禁止雇用过瘦模特及宣传极端节食的网站。由此可知女性形体美的定义权不再由时尚业独占，将会被重新定义，对应A项。", "trapNote": "B项“修建新T台”和C项“节食网站兴盛”均与原文禁用过瘦模特、取缔极端节食网站相反；D项“时尚业衰退”属于过度推断，原文并未提及产业衰落。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The phrase \"impinging on\" (Line 2, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to", "options": ["indicating the state of.", "heightening the value of.", "losing faith in.", "doing harm to."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "They suggest beauty should not be defined by looks that end up impinging on health.", "explanation": "词义题定位至第2段第2句：beauty should not be defined by looks that end up impinging on health。前一句说这些措施具有积极动机（uplifting motives），后文又提到保护模特免于“饿死”（starving themselves to death），因此用极端外貌定义美最终会“损害”健康。D项doing harm to（对……造成伤害）最贴合语境。", "trapNote": "A项“表明……状态”和B项“提高……价值”均未体现极端瘦身对健康的负面冲击，B项更是与上下文保护健康的情感态度完全背离。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is true of the fashion industry?", "options": ["The French measures have already failed.", "Its inherent problems are getting worse.", "Models are no longer under peer pressure.", "New standards are being set in Denmark."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "In Denmark, the United States, and a few other countries, it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images that rely more on peer pressure for enforcement.", "explanation": "定位至第3段末句与第4段。第3段指出在丹麦、美国等国，时尚业正尝试制定依赖同行压力执行的自愿标准（set voluntary standards）；第4段紧接着说明丹麦时尚业上月就模特年龄、健康等准则与制裁达成一致，修订了《丹麦时尚道德宪章》。D项New standards are being set in Denmark精准概括了这两处的事实信息。", "trapNote": "A项“法国措施已经失败”过于绝对且与第1段“初步批准”不符；C项将原文rely more on peer pressure（更依赖同行压力）反向篡改为不再受其制约。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "A designer is most likely to be rejected by CFW for", "options": ["pursuing perfect physical conditions.", "caring too much about models' character.", "showing little concern for health factors.", "setting a high age threshold for models."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "The charter's main tool of enforcement is to deny access for designers and modeling agencies to Copenhagen Fashion Week (CFW), which is run by the Danish Fashion Institute.", "explanation": "定位至第4段。原文第1句说明丹麦时尚业就模特的年龄、健康（health）等特征达成了规则与制裁；第3句指出《宪章》的主要执行手段是拒绝不符合标准的设计师和模特机构参加哥本哈根时装周（deny access...to CFW）。由此可推知，若设计师对模特健康因素缺乏关注（showing little concern for health factors），最可能被CFW拒之门外，选C。", "trapNote": "A项“追求完美身体状态”和B项“过于关心模特品格”与原文鼓励关注健康和内在品质（第2段）导向相反；D项“设置高年龄门槛”并非违规原因。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following may be the best title of the text?", "options": ["The Great Threats to the Fashion Industry", "Just Another Round of Struggle for Beauty", "A Dilemma for the Starving Models in France", "A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Relying on ethical persuasion rather than law to address the misuse of body ideals may be the best step.", "explanation": "全文围绕时尚界对女性身材审美标准的定义权展开：第1-2段肯定法国立法禁用过瘦模特的积极动机，第3-4段对比法国严厉惩罚与丹麦道德宪章自律的做法，第5段总结提出应依靠道德劝说超越单一行业的物质审美标准。全篇主线即对时尚业畸形身材审美标准的挑战与反思，D项准确概括全文主旨。", "trapNote": "A项“对时尚业的巨大威胁”夸大其词且偏离审美主题；C项“法国饥饿模特的困境”仅涉及局部细节，无法涵盖后半部分关于丹麦自律和道德劝说的内容。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "影响，侵犯，损害", "note": "常与介词on连用（impinge on），表示对健康、权利或界限造成不良影响或侵犯。", "word": "impinge"}, {"gloss": "鼓舞人心的，令人振奋的", "note": "由up（向上）+lift（举起）派生，文中uplifting motives指立法背后积极向善的初衷。", "word": "uplifting"}, {"gloss": "仲裁者，决定者，权威人士", "note": "注意拼写与名词含义：arbiters of beauty意为“美的评判者/决定权归属者”，与第1段define physical beauty呼应。", "word": "arbiter"}, {"gloss": "无形的，触摸不到的；难以言喻的", "note": "in-（否定）+ tang（接触）+ -ible，文中intangible qualities（如品格和才智）与外在物质身材形成对比。", "word": "intangible"}, {"gloss": "装饰，点缀，修饰", "note": "名词，动词为adorn，文中material adornment指时尚业对外在物质修饰的过度聚焦。", "word": "adornment"}, {"gloss": "遵守，顺从，遵从", "note": "动词为comply（with），文中method of compliance指促使行业遵守道德规范的手段。", "word": "compliance"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "It tells the fashion industry that it must take responsibility for the signal it sends women, especially teenage girls, about the social tape-measure they must use to determine their individual worth.", "point": "多层定语从句省略关系代词（that/which）后的句子结构切分，以及隐喻词汇tape-measure的语义理解。", "structure": "主干为It tells the fashion industry that...（that引导宾语从句）；宾语从句中signal后省略了关系代词引导定语从句it sends women...；介词短语about the social tape-measure后又省略关系代词引导定语从句they must use to determine...。", "zh": "它告诫时尚业必须为其向女性——尤其是少女——发出的信号负责，即她们必须用什么样的社会“量尺”来衡量自身的价值。"}, {"en": "And perhaps faintly, they hint that people should look to intangible qualities like character and intellect rather than dieting their way to size zero or wasp-waist physiques.", "point": "rather than连接的对比结构，以及dieting one's way to...（通过节食达到……）的动词化习惯表达。", "structure": "主干为they hint that...；宾语从句中包含rather than连接的平行比较成分：look to intangible qualities与dieting their way to...；介词like引出举例说明。", "zh": "或许，这些禁令还隐约暗示人们应当看重品格和才智等无形品质，而不是通过节食追求零号身材或蜂腰体型。"}, {"en": "The charter's main tool of enforcement is to deny access for designers and modeling agencies to Copenhagen Fashion Week (CFW), which is run by the Danish Fashion Institute.", "point": "固定搭配deny access for sb. to sth.（拒绝某人参与/进入……）以及which引导的非限制性定语从句。", "structure": "主语为The charter's main tool of enforcement，系动词is后接不定式短语to deny access...to CFW作表语；句末which引导非限制性定语从句，补充说明CFW的运营主体。", "zh": "该宪章的主要执行手段，是拒绝设计师和模特经纪公司参加由丹麦时尚协会主办的哥本哈根时装周（CFW）。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "时尚业失去了定义美的绝对权力，意味着美的定义权不再固定，对应“形体美将被重新定义”。", "option": "Physical beauty would be redefined.", "original": "its fashion industry has lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women"}, {"note": "结合语境中过度追求骨感导致健康受损与模特饿死，impinging on即“对……造成伤害（doing harm to）”。", "option": "doing harm to", "original": "impinging on"}, {"note": "将原文在丹麦等地尝试制定自愿标准、达成模特年龄与健康规则，概括为“丹麦正在制定新标准”。", "option": "New standards are being set in Denmark.", "original": "In Denmark... it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images"}, {"note": "宪章就健康等因素设限并对违规者拒绝准入，反推出设计师若忽视健康因素最可能被CFW拒之门外。", "option": "showing little concern for health factors", "original": "rules and sanctions regarding the age, health, and other characteristics of models... deny access... to Copenhagen Fashion Week"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2016-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2016", "examSet": "2016 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2016 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "英国乡村保护与城乡规划之争", "subtitle": "乡村保护的政治困境与合理规划", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["For the first time in history more people live in towns than in the country. In Britain this has had a curious result. While polls show Britons rate \"the countryside\" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support. A century ago Octavia Hill launched the National Trust not to rescue stylish houses but to save \"the beauty of natural places for everyone forever.\" It was specifically to provide city dwellers with spaces for leisure where they could experience \"a refreshing air.\" Hill's pressure later led to the creation of national parks and green belts. They don't make countryside any more, and every year concrete consumes more of it. It needs constant guardianship.", "At the next election none of the big parties seem likely to endorse this sentiment. The Conservatives' planning reform explicitly gives rural development priority over conservation, even authorising \"off-plan\" building where local people might object. The concept of sustainable development has been defined as profitable. Labour likewise wants to discontinue local planning where councils oppose development. The Liberal Democrats are silent. Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land. Its Campaign to Protect Rural England struck terror into many local Conservative parties.", "The sensible place to build new houses, factories and offices is where people are, in cities and towns where infrastructure is in place. The London agents Stirling Ackroyd recently identified enough sites for half a million houses in the London area alone, with no intrusion on green belt. What is true of London is even truer of the provinces.", "The idea that \"housing crisis\" equals \"concreted meadows\" is pure lobby talk. The issue is not the need for more houses but, as always, where to put them. Under lobby pressure, George Osborne favours rural new-build against urban renovation and renewal. He favours out-of-town shopping sites against high streets. This is not a free market but a biased one. Rural towns and villages have grown and will always grow. They do so best where building sticks to their edges and respects their character. We do not ruin urban conservation areas. Why ruin rural ones? Development should be planned, not let rip. After the Netherlands, Britain is Europe's most crowded country. Half a century of town and country planning has enabled it to retain an enviable rural coherence, while still permitting low-density urban living. There is no doubt of the alternative - the corrupted landscapes of southern Portugal, Spain or Ireland. Avoiding this rather than promoting it should unite the left and right of the political spectrum."], "translations": ["历史上第一次出现城镇人口多于乡村人口的情况。在英国，这产生了一个奇特的结果。虽然民调显示，英国人将“乡村”与王室、莎士比亚以及国民医疗服务体系（NHS）并列，视作最令他们为国家感到自豪的事物，但这一点在政治上得到的支持却十分有限。一个世纪前，奥克塔维亚·希尔创立“国民信托”，并非为了拯救时尚华丽的宅邸，而是为了“永远为所有人留存自然之地的美景”。此举专门旨在为城市居民提供休闲空间，让他们能够体验“清新的空气”。希尔的呼吁后来促成了国家公园和绿带的建立。然而，人们已无法再造出更多的乡村，混凝土每年都在吞噬更多的乡村土地，它需要持续不断的守护。", "在下届大选中，似乎没有哪个主要政党愿意支持这一情怀。保守党的规划改革明确将乡村开发置于保护之上，甚至在当地民众可能反对的情况下仍批准“规划外”建设。“可持续发展”的概念已被定义为“有利可图”。同样，工党也希望在地方议会反对开发时中止地方规划。自由民主党对此保持沉默。唯有英国独立党敏锐地抓住了机会，站到了呼吁更审慎使用绿地的人群一边。其发起的“保护英国乡村运动”令许多地方保守党人惊恐不已。", "建造新住宅、工厂和办公室的明智之地是人口聚集的地方，即基础设施已然完备的城镇。伦敦房地产代理商斯特林·阿克罗伊德最近仅在伦敦地区就找到了足够建造50万套住房的地块，且完全不会侵占绿带。伦敦如此，外省地区更是如此。", "将“住房危机”等同于“铺满混凝土的草地”，纯属游说集团的话术。问题并不在于需要更多住房，而一如既往地在于把住房建在哪里。在游说压力下，乔治·奥斯本更青睐在乡村新建住宅，而非进行城市翻新和改造；他更青睐城外购物中心，而非城市商业街。这并非自由市场，而是有失偏颇的市场。乡村市镇和村庄过去在发展，今后也将继续发展。只要建设紧贴其边缘并尊重其自身风貌，就能实现最好的发展。我们尚且不会毁掉城市保护区，又为何要毁掉乡村保护区呢？开发应当有规划，而不应任其泛滥。英国是欧洲人口密度仅次于荷兰的国家。半个世纪的城乡规划使其得以保留令人艳羡的乡村整体风貌，同时仍允许低密度的城市生活。另一种选择的结果毫无疑问——就像葡萄牙南部、西班牙或爱尔兰遭到破坏的景观那样。政治光谱的左右两翼应当团结起来，共同避免而非助长这种局面。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Britain's public sentiment about the countryside", "options": ["is not well reflected in politics.", "is fully backed by the royal family.", "didn't start till the Shakespearean age.", "has brought much benefit to the NHS."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "While polls show Britons rate \"the countryside\" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support.", "explanation": "定位第1段第3句。文中指出，虽然民调显示英国民众将“乡村”与王室、莎士比亚及NHS并列，视作最令自己为国家感到自豪的事物，但这种民众情感得到的政治支持却很有限（this has limited political support）。A项中的not well reflected in politics与limited political support形成同义替换，准确概括了公众情感未能在政治中得到充分体现这一事实，故选A。", "trapNote": "B、C、D三项均将原文与“乡村”并列作为英国人自豪来源的“王室”“莎士比亚”和“NHS”进行了强行关联，属于典型的张冠李戴，原文并未提及相互间的支持、起源或受益关系。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, the achievements of the National Trust are now being", "options": ["largely overshadowed.", "properly protected.", "effectively reinforced.", "gradually destroyed."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "They don't make countryside any more, and every year concrete consumes more of it.", "explanation": "本题题干中的Paragraph 2对应合并后文本第1段后半部分。该段指出奥克塔维亚·希尔创立国民信托是为了保护自然美景，其努力促成了国家公园与绿带的建立；紧接着转折指出乡村不可再生，且每年混凝土都在吞噬更多乡村土地（every year concrete consumes more of it），可见其保护成果正遭受破坏。D项gradually destroyed（逐渐被毁坏）精准对应此意，故选D。", "trapNote": "B项“得到妥善保护”和C项“得到有效巩固”与原文中“混凝土每年吞噬更多乡村土地、需要持续守护”的现状完全相反；A项“很大程度上黯然失色”在文中并无体现，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from Paragraph 3?", "options": ["Labour is under attack for opposing development.", "The Conservatives may abandon \"off-plan\" building.", "Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation.", "The Liberal Democrats are losing political influence."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land.", "explanation": "题干中的Paragraph 3对应合并后文本第2段。该段指出在大选前，保守党、工党倾向于开发而忽视保护，自由民主党保持沉默，唯有英国独立党（Ukip）敏锐地抓住了机会（sensing its chance），站在呼吁审慎利用绿地的一方，其运动甚至让许多地方保守党人感到恐慌。由此可合理推断，独立党有望凭借支持乡村保护而获益，C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项与原文“工党希望在地方议会反对开发时中止地方规划”意思相反；B项无中生有，原文仅说保守党批准“规划外”建设；D项属于过度推断，原文只说自由民主党保持沉默，未提其失去影响力。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The author holds that George Osborne's preference", "options": ["shows his disregard for the character of rural areas.", "stresses the necessity of easing the housing crisis.", "highlights his firm stand against lobby pressure.", "reveals a strong prejudice against urban areas."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Under lobby pressure, George Osborne favours rural new-build against urban renovation and renewal.", "explanation": "定位第4段第3—7句。文中指出在游说集团的压力下，乔治·奥斯本偏好乡村新建项目而忽视城市翻新改造，偏好城外购物点而忽视商业街。作者紧接着指出，乡村发展最理想的方式是紧贴边缘并尊重自身风貌（respects their character），随后反问“为何要毁掉乡村保护区”，表明奥斯本的偏好忽视了乡村的特色与风貌，对应A项disregard for the character of rural areas。", "trapNote": "B项受首句“housing crisis”干扰，但作者明确称其为“纯属游说话术”；C项与“Under lobby pressure”事实相反；D项“强烈偏见”属偷换概念，奥斯本只是在游说压力下偏向乡村新建，并非反城市。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "In the last paragraph, the author shows his appreciation of", "options": ["the size of population in Britain.", "the enviable urban lifestyle in Britain.", "the town-and-country planning in Britain.", "the political life in today's Britain."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Half a century of town and country planning has enabled it to retain an enviable rural coherence, while still permitting low-density urban living.", "explanation": "定位末段倒数第3句。作者指出英国是欧洲人口密度第二高的国家，但半个世纪以来的城乡规划使其既保留了令人艳羡的乡村整体风貌（enviable rural coherence），又实现了低密度城市生活，随后更以南欧、爱尔兰遭破坏的景观作反衬。由此可见作者对英国的城乡规划持赞赏态度，C项the town-and-country planning in Britain准确契合原文，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项“人口规模”与原文“crowded country”所体现的担忧不符；B项张冠李戴，原文“enviable”修饰的是“rural coherence”而非城市生活方式；D项“当今英国政治生活”在末段未体现赞赏。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 赞同，支持，认可", "note": "本文第2段指政党是否愿意支持乡村保护情怀", "word": "endorse"}, {"gloss": "v. 中止，停止，废除", "note": "前缀dis-+continue，第2段指工党欲中止地方规划", "word": "discontinue"}, {"gloss": "n. 侵占，闯入，干扰", "note": "动词为intrude，第3段指不侵占绿带（no intrusion on green belt）", "word": "intrusion"}, {"gloss": "n. 翻新，修复，整修", "note": "第4段与rural new-build对比，指城市旧区翻新", "word": "renovation"}, {"gloss": "n. 整体性，连贯性，协调性", "note": "第4段enviable rural coherence指令人艳羡的乡村整体风貌", "word": "coherence"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "While polls show Britons rate \"the countryside\" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support.", "point": "while表让步（“虽然”）；rate A alongside B as...意为“把A与B并列视作……”", "structure": "While引导让步状语从句，从句中show后接宾语从句，what引导宾语从句作介词as的宾语；主句为this has limited political support。", "zh": "虽然民调显示，英国人将“乡村”与王室、莎士比亚以及国民医疗服务体系（NHS）并列，视作最令他们为国家感到自豪的事物，但这一点在政治上得到的支持却十分有限。"}, {"en": "The Conservatives' planning reform explicitly gives rural development priority over conservation, even authorising \"off-plan\" building where local people might object.", "point": "give A priority over B（将A置于B之上/优先考虑A）；where引导地点状语从句", "structure": "主句主干为The Conservatives' planning reform gives rural development priority over conservation；现在分词短语even authorising...作伴随状语，其中where引导地点状语从句。", "zh": "保守党的规划改革明确将乡村开发置于保护之上，甚至在当地民众可能反对的情况下仍批准“规划外”建设。"}, {"en": "Half a century of town and country planning has enabled it to retain an enviable rural coherence, while still permitting low-density urban living.", "point": "enable sb./sth. to do sth.（使……能够做某事）；while+分词表同时伴随", "structure": "主句为Half a century of... has enabled it to retain...；while still permitting...为“连词+现在分词”结构作伴随/对比状语。", "zh": "半个世纪的城乡规划使其得以保留令人艳羡的乡村整体风貌，同时仍允许低密度的城市生活。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "有限的政治支持 → 未在政治中充分体现", "option": "is not well reflected in politics", "original": "this has limited political support"}, {"note": "混凝土每年吞噬更多乡村土地 → 逐渐遭到破坏", "option": "gradually destroyed", "original": "every year concrete consumes more of it"}, {"note": "敏锐抓住机会并支持审慎保护绿地 → 借此获益", "option": "may gain from its support for rural conservation", "original": "sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach"}, {"note": "偏好乡村新建且不顾其风貌 → 忽视乡村风貌特征", "option": "shows his disregard for the character of rural areas", "original": "favours rural new-build... Why ruin rural ones?"}, {"note": "“令人艳羡”体现作者对城乡规划成果的赞赏", "option": "shows his appreciation of the town-and-country planning", "original": "retain an enviable rural coherence"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2016-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2016", "examSet": "2016 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2016 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "企业社会责任与光环效应", "subtitle": "CSR如何通过光环效应为企业减轻法律惩罚", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 427, "paragraphs": ["\"There is one and only one social responsibility of business,\" wrote Milton Friedman, a Nobel prize-winning economist, \"That is, to use its resources and engage in activities designed to increase its profits.\" But even if you accept Friedman's premise and regard corporate social responsibility (CSR) policies as a waste of shareholders' money, things may not be absolutely clear-cut. New research suggests that CSR may create monetary value for companies - at least when they are prosecuted for corruption.", "The largest firms in America and Britain together spend more than $15 billion a year on CSR, according to an estimate by EPG, a consulting firm. This could add value to their businesses in three ways. First, consumers may take CSR spending as a \"signal\" that a company's products are of high quality. Second, customers may be willing to buy a company's products as an indirect way to donate to the good causes it helps. And third, through a more diffuse \"halo effect,\" whereby its good deeds earn it greater consideration from consumers and others. Previous studies on CSR have had trouble differentiating these effects because consumers can be affected by all three. A recent study attempts to separate them by looking at bribery prosecutions under America's Foreign Corrupt Practices Act (FCPA). It argues that since prosecutors do not consume a company's products as part of their investigations, they could be influenced only by the halo effect. The study found that, among prosecuted firms, those with the most comprehensive CSR programmes tended to get more lenient penalties. Their analysis ruled out the possibility that it was firms' political influence, rather than their CSR stand, that accounted for the leniency: Companies that contributed more to political campaigns did not receive lower fines.", "In all, the study concludes that whereas prosecutors should only evaluate a case based on its merits, they do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR. \"We estimate that either eliminating a substantial labour-rights concern, such as child labour, or increasing corporate giving by about 20% results in fines that generally are 40% lower than the typical punishment for bribing foreign officials,\" says one researcher.", "Researchers admit that their study does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR. Nor does it reveal how much companies are banking on the halo effect, rather than the other possible benefits, when they decide their do-gooding policies. But at least they have demonstrated that when companies get into trouble with the law, evidence of good character can win them a less costly punishment."], "translations": ["“企业的社会责任有且仅有一项，”诺贝尔经济学奖得主米尔顿·弗里德曼写道，“那就是利用其资源并从事旨在增加利润的活动。”但即便你接受弗里德曼的前提，认为企业社会责任（CSR）政策是在浪费股东的钱，事情也未必非黑即白。新研究表明，CSR或许能为企业创造金钱价值——至少在它们因腐败被起诉时是如此。", "据咨询公司EPG估算，美英两国最大的企业每年在CSR上的支出合计超过150亿美元。这可以通过三种方式为企业增添价值。第一，消费者可能将CSR支出视为公司产品质量上乘的“信号”；第二，顾客可能愿意购买该公司的产品，将其作为向其所扶持的公益事业捐款的间接方式；第三，通过一种更为弥散的“光环效应”，企业的善举能为其赢得来自消费者及其他方面的更多体谅。以往关于CSR的研究一直难以区分这三种效应，因为消费者可能同时受到这三种效应的影响。最近的一项研究试图通过考察美国《反海外腐败法》（FCPA）下的贿赂起诉案件来将它们剥离开来。该研究认为，由于检察官在调查过程中并不消费该公司的产品，他们可能只受光环效应的影响。研究发现，在被起诉的企业中，拥有最完善CSR项目的企业往往会得到更宽大的处罚。他们的分析排除了宽大处理源于企业政治影响力而非其CSR立场的可能性：向政治竞选捐款更多的企业并未获得更低的罚款。", "总之，该研究得出结论：尽管检察官本应仅依据案情本身来评估案件，但他们似乎确实会受到企业CSR记录的影响。“我们估计，无论是消除诸如童工之类的重大劳工权益隐患，还是将企业捐赠提高约20%，都能使罚款金额通常比贿赂外国官员的常规处罚低40%。”一位研究人员说道。", "研究人员承认，他们的研究并未回答企业应当在CSR上花费多少的问题，也未揭示企业在制定行善政策时究竟在多大程度上指望“光环效应”而非其他潜在收益。但至少他们已经证明，当企业惹上官司时，品行良好的证据能够为其赢得代价更低的惩罚。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author views Milton Friedman's statement about CSR with", "options": ["tolerance.", "skepticism.", "approval.", "uncertainty."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "But even if you accept Friedman's premise and regard corporate social responsibility (CSR) policies as a waste of shareholders' money, things may not be absolutely clear-cut.", "explanation": "定位第1段第2—3句。首句引述弗里德曼的观点（企业唯一责任是逐利），紧接着作者用But转折，指出即使接受弗里德曼的前提并将CSR视为浪费股东钱财，事情也未必那么绝对（not be absolutely clear-cut），随后引出新研究说明CSR在企业面临腐败起诉时能创造金钱价值。由此可见作者对弗里德曼的论断持怀疑态度，对应B项skepticism，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项“容忍”、C项“赞成”均与“But”引导的转折及后文反例相悖；D项“不确定”具有一定迷惑性，但作者用新研究直接反驳“CSR纯粹浪费钱”的观点，态度是明确质疑而非犹豫不定。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, CSR helps a company by", "options": ["guarding it against malpractices.", "protecting it from being defamed.", "winning trust from consumers.", "raising the quality of its products."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "First, consumers may take CSR spending as a \"signal\" that a company's products are of high quality.", "explanation": "定位第2段第3句。该段介绍了CSR为企业增值的三种途径：其一，消费者可能将CSR支出视为产品质量上乘的信号；其二，顾客愿意购买其产品以间接行善；其三，善举通过光环效应为企业赢得消费者及他人的更多体谅。这三条均表明CSR帮助企业赢得了消费者的信任与认可，C项winning trust from consumers最符合文意，故选C。", "trapNote": "D项偷换概念，原文只是说消费者将CSR视作产品高质量的“信号”，而非CSR能直接提高产品质量；A项“防范不当行为”与B项“免遭诽谤”在文中均未提及，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The expression \"more lenient\" (Para.4) is closest in meaning to", "options": ["less controversial.", "more effective.", "more lasting.", "less severe."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The study found that, among prosecuted firms, those with the most comprehensive CSR programmes tended to get more lenient penalties.", "explanation": "本题题干标注的Para.4对应本篇合并后文本的第2段。该段倒数第2句指出，拥有最完善CSR项目的被起诉企业往往会获得more lenient penalties；紧接着末句将其与向政治竞选捐款的企业未获“lower fines（更低罚款）”对比，且后文亦提到罚款降低40%及“less costly punishment”。由此推断more lenient意为“更宽大的、更轻的”，与D项less severe同义。", "trapNote": "A项“较少争议”、B项“更有效”及C项“更持久”均脱离了“对涉腐企业进行罚款处罚”的司法语境，无法与后文的“lower fines”和“less costly punishment”形成语义呼应。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "When prosecutors evaluate a case, a company's CSR record", "options": ["has an impact on their decision.", "comes across as reliable evidence.", "increases the chance of being penalized.", "constitutes part of the investigation."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "In all, the study concludes that whereas prosecutors should only evaluate a case based on its merits, they do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR.", "explanation": "定位第3段第1句。研究总结指出，尽管检察官本应仅凭案件事实本身进行评估，但他们似乎确实受到了企业CSR记录的影响（do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR）。A项中的has an impact on their decision与be influenced by形成直接同义替换，准确表述了CSR记录对检察官量刑决定的影响，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项过度拔高，原文仅说CSR记录影响了检察官的判断，并未称其本身作为“可靠证据”；C项与“罚款降低40%”相反；D项把第2段“调查时不消费产品”偷换为CSR构成调查本身。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is true of CSR, according to the last paragraph?", "options": ["Its negative effects on businesses are often overlooked.", "The necessary amount of companies' spending on it is unknown.", "Companies' financial capacity for it has been overestimated.", "It has brought much benefit to the banking industry."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Researchers admit that their study does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR.", "explanation": "定位末段首句。研究人员坦承，他们的研究并未回答企业究竟应当在CSR上花费多少这一问题（does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR）。B项中的The necessary amount... is unknown精准对应了“未回答应当投入多少”，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项“负面影响常被忽视”与C项“财务承受力被高估”在末段均无提及；D项属典型熟词僻义陷阱，把原文第2句中的动词短语“banking on（指望、依赖）”误解为名词“银行业（banking industry）”。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 起诉，检控", "note": "名词prosecutor意为“检察官”，本文围绕企业腐败被起诉展开", "word": "prosecute"}, {"gloss": "adj. 弥散的，广泛的；v. 扩散", "note": "第2段a more diffuse \"halo effect\"指作用范围更泛化的光环效应", "word": "diffuse"}, {"gloss": "adj. 宽大的，宽容的，从轻的", "note": "名词为leniency，第2段高频考点词，指量刑从宽", "word": "lenient"}, {"gloss": "n. 案情是非曲直；优点，价值", "note": "第3段based on its merits为法律固定表达，指“依据案情本身”", "word": "merit"}, {"gloss": "v. 指望，依赖（常与on连用）", "note": "熟词僻义，末段banking on意为“指望”，真题高频陷阱词", "word": "bank"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Their analysis ruled out the possibility that it was firms' political influence, rather than their CSR stand, that accounted for the leniency: Companies that contributed more to political campaigns did not receive lower fines.", "point": "rule out（排除）；that同位语从句+强调句；account for（解释，是……的原因）", "structure": "主句为Their analysis ruled out the possibility，后接that引导的同位语从句解释possibility，其中包含it was... that...强调句型；冒号后为that引导定语从句的解释分句。", "zh": "他们的分析排除了宽大处理源于企业政治影响力而非其CSR立场的可能性：向政治竞选捐款更多的企业并未获得更低的罚款。"}, {"en": "We estimate that either eliminating a substantial labour-rights concern, such as child labour, or increasing corporate giving by about 20% results in fines that generally are 40% lower than the typical punishment for bribing foreign officials,", "point": "either A or B作主语遵循就近原则；result in（导致）；be X% lower than", "structure": "estimate后接that引导宾语从句，从句主语为either eliminating... or increasing...两个并列动名词短语，谓语动词为单数results in，宾语fines后接that引导的定语从句。", "zh": "我们估计，无论是消除诸如童工之类的重大劳工权益隐患，还是将企业捐赠提高约20%，都能使罚款金额通常比贿赂外国官员的常规处罚低40%。"}, {"en": "Nor does it reveal how much companies are banking on the halo effect, rather than the other possible benefits, when they decide their do-gooding policies.", "point": "Nor置于句首的部分倒装；bank on（指望、依赖，熟词僻义）", "structure": "否定副词Nor置于句首引起部分倒装（does it reveal）；how much引导宾语从句，末尾when引导时间状语从句。", "zh": "它也未揭示企业在制定行善政策时究竟在多大程度上指望“光环效应”而非其他潜在收益。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "否定“非黑即白”的论断 → 对弗里德曼观点持怀疑态度", "option": "views... with skepticism", "original": "things may not be absolutely clear-cut"}, {"note": "视作高质量信号及赢得体谅 → 赢得消费者信任", "option": "winning trust from consumers", "original": "take CSR spending as a \"signal\"... greater consideration from consumers"}, {"note": "与“更低罚款”呼应，指处罚更轻、更宽大", "option": "less severe", "original": "more lenient penalties... lower fines"}, {"note": "受到企业CSR记录影响 → 对其裁决产生影响", "option": "has an impact on their decision", "original": "do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR"}, {"note": "未回答该花多少 → 必要支出金额尚不明确", "option": "The necessary amount... is unknown", "original": "does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2016-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2016", "examSet": "2016 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2016 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "纸媒转型：《纽约时报》印刷版的定位策略", "subtitle": "探讨数字时代纸质报刊如何通过提价与服务忠实读者实现战略转型", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 433, "paragraphs": ["There will eventually come a day when The New York Times ceases to publish stories on newsprint. Exactly when that day will be is a matter of debate. \"Sometime in the future,\" the paper's publisher said back in 2010.", "Nostalgia for ink on paper and the rustle of pages aside, there's plenty of incentive to ditch print. The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper - printing presses, delivery trucks - isn't just expensive; it's excessive at a time when online-only competitors don't have the same set of financial constraints. Readers are migrating away from print anyway. And though print ad sales still dwarf their online and mobile counterparts, revenue from print is still declining. Overhead may be high and circulation lower, but rushing to eliminate its print edition would be a mistake, says BuzzFeed CEO Jonah Peretti.", "Peretti says the Times shouldn't waste time getting out of the print business, but only if they go about doing it the right way. \"Figuring out a way to accelerate that transition would make sense for them,\" he said, \"but if you discontinue it, you're going to have your most loyal customers really upset with you.\"", "Sometimes that's worth making a change anyway. Peretti gives the example of Netflix discontinuing its DVD-mailing service to focus on streaming. \"It was seen as a blunder,\" he said. The move turned out to be foresighted. And if Peretti were in charge at the Times? \"I wouldn't pick a year to end print,\" he said. \"I would raise prices and make it into more of a legacy product.\"", "The most loyal customers would still get the product they favor, the idea goes, and they'd feel like they were helping sustain the quality of something they believe in. \"So if you're overpaying for print, you could feel like you were helping,\" Peretti said. \"Then increase it at a higher rate each year and essentially try to generate additional revenue.\" In other words, if you're going to make a print product, make it for the people who are already obsessed with it. Which may be what the Times is doing already. Getting the print edition seven days a week costs nearly $500 a year - more than twice as much as a digital-only subscription. \"It's a really hard thing to do and it's a tremendous luxury that BuzzFeed doesn't have a legacy business,\" Peretti remarked. \"But we're going to have questions like that where we have things we're doing that don't make sense when the market changes and the world changes. In those situations, it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive.\""], "translations": ["《纽约时报》终有一天会停止在新闻纸上刊印报道。究竟这一天何时到来尚无定论。“在未来的某个时候，”该报出版人早在2010年就曾如此表示。", "抛开对纸墨质感与翻页沙沙声的怀旧情结不谈，放弃印刷版其实有诸多动因。制作实体报纸所需的基础设施——印刷机、送货卡车——不仅成本高昂，在纯网络竞争对手不受同等财务约束的当下，更显得过于冗余。况且读者本就在从纸媒向外流失。尽管印刷版广告销售额仍远超网络及移动端广告，但印刷业务的营收仍在持续下滑。不过，BuzzFeed首席执行官乔纳·佩雷蒂表示，即便运营费用高企、发行量走低，急于取消印刷版仍是一个错误。", "佩雷蒂认为，《纽约时报》应当抓紧时间退出印刷业务，但前提是采取正确的方式。“想办法加速这一转型对他们来说是合理的，”他说道，“但如果你直接停刊，就会让你最忠实的读者感到非常不满。”", "有时即便如此，变革也值得一试。佩雷蒂举了奈飞（Netflix）停掉DVD邮寄服务以专注于流媒体的例子。“当时这被视为一大败笔，”他说，但事实证明此举颇具远见。那么如果由佩雷蒂来掌管《纽约时报》呢？“我不会设定一个停印的年份，”他表示，“我会提高售价，把它打造成更偏向高端传承的产品。”", "按这一设想，最忠实的读者仍能得到他们青睐的产品，而且他们会觉得自己正在助力维系所信赖之物的品质。“因此，即便你为纸质版支付了高额溢价，你也会觉得自己是在提供支持，”佩雷蒂说，“然后每年以更高的幅度提价，本质上是试图创造额外收入。”换言之，如果你要继续做印刷产品，就要为那些已经对其痴迷的人而做。这或许正是《纽约时报》眼下在做的事情。每周七天订阅纸质版的费用高达近500美元一年——是纯数字版订阅价格的两倍多。“这是一件非常艰难的事，而BuzzFeed没有传统业务可谓莫大的幸运，”佩雷蒂评论道，“但我们也会遇到类似问题：当市场和世界发生变化时，我们原本在做的事情不再合理。在这种情况下，更激进些比不够激进要好。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The New York Times is considering ending its print edition partly due to", "options": ["the high cost of operation.", "the increasing online ad sales.", "the pressure from its investors.", "the complaints from its readers."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper - printing presses, delivery trucks - isn't just expensive; it's excessive at a time when online-only competitors don't have the same set of financial constraints.", "explanation": "定位至第2段。该段指出放弃印刷版的诸多动因，其中提到制作实体报纸所需的基础设施（印刷机、送货卡车）不仅昂贵，而且在纯网络竞争对手不受同等财务约束的当下显得过于冗余，后文也提到管理费用高企（Overhead may be high）。选项A“高昂的运营成本”正是对基础设施昂贵与管理成本高的高度概括，符合题意。", "trapNote": "B项曲解文意，第2段仅指出印刷广告收入仍远超网络及移动端且自身在下滑，未提及网络广告增长是停印原因；D项无中生有，文中仅说读者正在流失，并非读者投诉所致。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Peretti suggests that, in face of the present situation, the Times should", "options": ["end the print edition for good.", "make strategic adjustments.", "seek new sources of readership.", "aim for efficient management."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Peretti says the Times shouldn't waste time getting out of the print business, but only if they go about doing it the right way.", "explanation": "定位至第3段及第4段。第3段指出佩雷蒂认为《纽约时报》应抓紧退出印刷业务，但前提是采取正确的方式（the right way），即想办法加速转型而非贸然停刊以免激怒最忠实的读者；第4段进一步给出“提价并打造为传承产品”的具体方案。可见他建议《纽约时报》进行策略性调整，对应选项B。", "trapNote": "A项“彻底停印”与原文第2段“急于取消印刷版是错误的”及第4段“不会设定停印年份”直接相悖；C项“寻找新读者群”与D项“追求高效管理”在文中均未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be inferred from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that a \"legacy product\"", "options": ["helps restore the glory of former times.", "is meant for the most loyal customers.", "will have the cost of printing reduced.", "expands the popularity of the paper."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The most loyal customers would still get the product they favor, the idea goes, and they'd feel like they were helping sustain the quality of something they believe in.", "explanation": "定位至第5段（对应原题第5至6段）。该段紧承第4段提出的“legacy product”，解释称此举能让最忠实的读者继续买到心仪产品并感到自己在维系信赖之物的品质；随后明确指出“换言之，如果要做印刷产品，就要为那些已经对其痴迷的人而做”。由此可推知“传承产品”专为最忠实读者打造，对应选项B。", "trapNote": "A项“重现往日辉煌”属于望文生义，将legacy曲解为恢复昔日荣光；C项“降低印刷成本”与文意相反，文中强调的是提高售价而非降本；D项“扩大报纸普及度”误解了受众定位。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Peretti believes that, in a changing world,", "options": ["traditional luxuries can stay unaffected.", "cautiousness facilitates problem-solving.", "aggressiveness better meets challenges.", "legacy businesses are becoming outdated."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "But we're going to have questions like that where we have things we're doing that don't make sense when the market changes and the world changes. In those situations, it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive.", "explanation": "定位至第5段末句。佩雷蒂在结尾指出，当市场和世界发生变化时，人们会面临现有做法不再合理的问题；在这种局势下，“更激进比不够激进要好”（it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive）。选项C中的aggressiveness better meets challenges正是对该句核心观点的同义转述。", "trapNote": "A项偷换概念，原文luxury指BuzzFeed没有传统业务的“奢侈优势”，而非传统奢侈品不受影响；B项“谨慎有助于解决问题”与“更激进更好”意思完全相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title of the text?", "options": ["Shift to Online Newspapers All at Once", "Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good", "Keep Your Newspapers Forever in Fashion", "Cherish the Newspaper Still in Your Hand"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "I would raise prices and make it into more of a legacy product.", "explanation": "主旨题需贯通全文核心脉络。文章第1至2段指出《纽约时报》印刷版面临成本高企与收入下滑的困境，但又不宜急于停印；第3至5段借佩雷蒂的观点提出核心对策——通过大幅提价将印刷版打造成专供忠实读者的“传承型高端产品”，并列举《纽约时报》年费近500美元的现状作证。B项准确凝练了全文中心，故为最佳标题。", "trapNote": "A项“立即全面转向网络报刊”与文中反对贸然取消印刷版的立场相悖；C项“让报纸永远流行”违背第1段纸媒终将停刊的趋势；D项“珍惜手中报纸”偏离商业转型主旨。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 怀旧，留恋", "note": "第2段“Nostalgia for ink on paper”，指对纸墨触感的怀旧情结。", "word": "nostalgia"}, {"gloss": "adj. 过度的，过分的", "note": "第2段描述实体报纸基础设施在数字竞争时代显得“过度冗余”。", "word": "excessive"}, {"gloss": "v. 使相形见绌，远超", "note": "第2段熟词僻义，“print ad sales still dwarf their online... counterparts”指纸媒广告仍远超网络端。", "word": "dwarf"}, {"gloss": "n. 经常性管理费用，运营成本", "note": "第2段“Overhead may be high”，商业阅读高频词，对应题干中的cost of operation。", "word": "overhead"}, {"gloss": "adj. 有远见的，深谋远虑的", "note": "第4段评价Netflix停止邮寄DVD转攻流媒体的决策最终证明“有远见”。", "word": "foresighted"}, {"gloss": "v. 维持，支撑", "note": "第5段“sustain the quality of something they believe in”，意为维系品质。", "word": "sustain"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper - printing presses, delivery trucks - isn't just expensive; it's excessive at a time when online-only competitors don't have the same set of financial constraints.", "point": "过去分词短语作后置定语、破折号同位解释及when引导定语从句修饰time。", "structure": "主语(The infrastructure) + 后置定语(required to make...) + 破折号插入解释 + 并列分句(isn't just...; it's excessive...) + 时间状语(at a time when...)", "zh": "制作实体报纸所需的基础设施——印刷机和送货卡车——不仅价格高昂，而且在纯网络竞争对手不受同等财务约束的当下，更显得过于冗余。"}, {"en": "And though print ad sales still dwarf their online and mobile counterparts, revenue from print is still declining.", "point": "though引导让步状语从句，注意熟词僻义dwarf作动词意为“使相形见绌、远超”。", "structure": "让步状语从句(though print ad sales still dwarf...) + 主句(revenue from print is still declining)", "zh": "尽管纸媒广告销售额仍远超网络及移动端广告，但印刷业务的营收仍在持续下滑。"}, {"en": "The most loyal customers would still get the product they favor, the idea goes, and they'd feel like they were helping sustain the quality of something they believe in.", "point": "插入语the idea goes（按这种想法）及两个省略关系词的定语从句嵌套。", "structure": "分句1(customers would still get the product) + 定语从句(they favor) + 插入语(the idea goes) + 并列分句2(they'd feel like...) + 宾语从句 + 定语从句(they believe in)", "zh": "按这一设想，最忠实的读者仍能获得他们青睐的产品，同时他们会觉得自己在协助维持所信赖之物的品质。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将实体报刊基础设施昂贵与管理费用高企概括为“高昂的运营成本”。", "option": "the high cost of operation", "original": "The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper ... isn't just expensive / Overhead may be high"}, {"note": "把采取正确方式加速转型、提价并打造传承产品归纳为“做出战略调整”。", "option": "make strategic adjustments", "original": "go about doing it the right way / accelerate that transition"}, {"note": "“专为对其痴迷的群体打造”同义对应“面向最忠实的读者”。", "option": "is meant for the most loyal customers", "original": "make it for the people who are already obsessed with it"}, {"note": "将“更激进比不那么激进更好”名物化转述为“积极进取更能应对挑战”。", "option": "aggressiveness better meets challenges", "original": "it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive"}, {"note": "把大幅提价并服务核心铁粉的策略形象化概括为“把纸质报纸打造成奢侈品”。", "option": "Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good", "original": "raise prices and make it into more of a legacy product"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2015-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2015", "examSet": "2015 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2015 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "欧洲王室的存续危机与君主制反思", "subtitle": "社会政治 · 欧洲君主制现状与英国王室隐忧", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 422, "paragraphs": ["King Juan Carlos of Spain once insisted “kings don’t abdicate, they die in their sleep.” But embarrassing scandals and the popularity of the republican left in the recent Euro-elections have forced him to eat his words and stand down. So, does the Spanish crisis suggest that monarchy is seeing its last days? Does that mean the writing is on the wall for all European royals, with their magnificent uniforms and majestic lifestyle?", "The Spanish case provides arguments both for and against monarchy. When public opinion is particularly polarised, as it was following the end of the Franco regime, monarchs can rise above “mere” politics and “embody” a spirit of national unity.", "It is this apparent transcendence of politics that explains monarchs’ continuing popularity. And also, the Middle East excepted, Europe is the most monarch-infested region in the world, with 10 kingdoms (not counting Vatican City and Andorra). But unlike their absolutist counterparts in the Gulf and Asia, most royal families have survived because they allow voters to avoid the difficult search for a non-controversial but respected public figure.", "Even so, kings and queens undoubtedly have a downside. Symbolic of national unity as they claim to be, their very history—and sometimes the way they behave today – embodies outdated and indefensible privileges and inequalities. At a time when Thomas Piketty and other economists are warning of rising inequality and the increasing power of inherited wealth, it is bizarre that wealthy aristocratic families should still be the symbolic heart of modern democratic states.", "The most successful monarchies strive to abandon or hide their old aristocratic ways. Princes and princesses have day-jobs and ride bicycles, not horses (or helicopters). Even so, these are wealthy families who party with the international 1%, and media intrusiveness makes it increasingly difficult to maintain the right image.", "While Europe’s monarchies will no doubt be smart enough to survive for some time to come, it is the British royals who have most to fear from the Spanish example.", "It is only the Queen who has preserved the monarchy’s reputation with her rather ordinary (if well-heeled) granny style. The danger will come with Charles, who has both an expensive taste of lifestyle and a pretty hierarchical view of the world. He has failed to understand that monarchies have largely survived because they provide a service – as non-controversial and non-political heads of state. Charles ought to know that as English history shows, it is kings, not republicans, who are the monarchy’s worst enemies."], "translations": ["西班牙国王胡安·卡洛斯曾坚称：“国王不会退位，只会在睡梦中驾崩。”但令人尴尬的丑闻以及左翼共和派在近期欧洲议会选举中的高人气，迫使他食言退位。那么，西班牙的危机是否意味着君主制已走入暮年？这是否意味着身着华丽制服、过着尊贵生活的所有欧洲王室已大势已去？", "西班牙的案例为支持和反对君主制两方都提供了论据。当公众舆论像佛朗哥政权倒台后那样出现严重两极分化时，君主可以超脱于“单纯的”政治之上，并“体现”出一种民族团结的精神。", "正是这种看似超脱政治的特质，解释了君主制为何依然受到欢迎。此外，除中东外，欧洲是世界上君主国最密集的地区，共有10个王国（梵蒂冈和安道尔不计在内）。但与海湾地区和亚洲的专制君主同行不同，欧洲大多数王室得以存续，是因为他们让选民免去了艰难寻找一位毫无争议而又受人尊敬的公众人物的麻烦。", "即便如此，国王和王后无疑也有其负面影响。尽管他们声称自己象征着国家团结，但他们的历史本身——有时还包括他们如今的行事方式——却体现着过时且毫无道理的特权与不平等。在托马斯·皮凯蒂等经济学家正就日益加剧的不平等及世袭财富日益膨胀的权力发出警告之际，富裕的贵族家庭竟然仍是现代民主国家的象征核心，这实在令人匪夷所思。", "最成功的君主制国家都在竭力摒弃或掩饰其古老的贵族做派。王子和公主们都有日常工作，骑自行车而非骑马（或乘直升机）。即便如此，这些仍是与全球最顶尖1%富豪一起派对的富裕家庭，而媒体的无孔不入让他们越来越难以维持恰当的公众形象。", "尽管欧洲的君主制无疑会聪明到足以再存续一段时间，但最应当对西班牙先例感到恐惧的却是英国王室。", "全靠女王以其相当普通（尽管颇为富有）的老奶奶风格才保住了王室的声誉。危险将随查尔斯而来，他既偏爱奢华的生活方式，又有着相当强烈的等级观念。他未能理解，君主制之所以能够大体存续，是因为它们提供了一项服务——充当毫无争议、非政治性的国家元首。查尔斯本应明白，正如英国历史所表明的那样，君主制最大的敌人是国王自己，而非共和派。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the first two Paragraphs, King Juan Carlos of Spain", "options": ["used to enjoy high public support", "was unpopular among European royals", "eased his relationship with his rivals", "ended his reign in embarrassment"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "But embarrassing scandals and the popularity of the republican left in the recent Euro-elections have forced him to eat his words and stand down.", "explanation": "定位第一段第二句。胡安·卡洛斯一世曾宣称国王不会退位，但“令人尴尬的丑闻（embarrassing scandals）”以及左翼共和派在近期欧洲议会选举中的高人气迫使他收回前言并退位（stand down）。由此可知，他是在尴尬的丑闻中结束了自己的统治，“ended his reign in embarrassment”正是对“embarrassing scandals”和“stand down”的精准同义改写，故选D。", "trapNote": "A项“过去曾享高公众支持”无中生有，前两段未提他过去支持率高；C项“缓和与对手的关系”正反颠倒，文中指左翼共和派崛起逼宫而非关系缓和。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Monarchs are kept as heads of state in Europe mostly", "options": ["owing to their undoubted and respectable status", "to achieve a balance between tradition and reality", "to give voters more public figures to look up to", "due to their everlasting political embodiment"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "But unlike their absolutist counterparts in the Gulf and Asia, most royal families have survived because they allow voters to avoid the difficult search for a non-controversial but respected public figure.", "explanation": "定位第三段末句。欧洲多数王室得以延续，是因为他们让选民免去了艰难寻找“毫无争议且受人尊敬的公众人物（a non-controversial but respected public figure）”的麻烦。A项“owing to their undoubted and respectable status”中undoubted对应non-controversial，respectable对应respected，高度契合原文因果，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项“平衡传统与现实”属于无中生有；C项“给选民提供更多可仰慕的公众人物”曲解原文，王室是替选民省去寻找这类人物的麻烦，并非提供更多选择。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is shown to be odd, according to Paragraph 4?", "options": ["Aristocrats’ excessive reliance on inherited wealth", "The role of the nobility in modern democracies", "The simple lifestyle of the aristocratic families", "The nobility’s adherence to their privileges"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "At a time when Thomas Piketty and other economists are warning of rising inequality and the increasing power of inherited wealth, it is bizarre that wealthy aristocratic families should still be the symbolic heart of modern democratic states.", "explanation": "题干中的odd对应第四段末句的bizarre（怪异的、奇特的）。该句指出，在经济学家警示不平等加剧和世袭财富力量膨胀的当下，富裕的贵族家庭竟然仍是“现代民主国家的象征性核心（the symbolic heart of modern democratic states）”，这十分荒诞。B项“贵族在现代民主国家中的角色”正是对这一现象的准确概括，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项“过度依赖世袭财富”和D项“贵族坚持自身特权”均在第四段有所涉及，但均非作者用“bizarre”明确指出的怪异核心；C项“简朴生活方式”与第五段及本段语义相反。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The British royals “have most to fear” because Charles", "options": ["takes a rough line on political issues", "fails to change his lifestyle as advised", "takes republicans as his potential allies", "fails to adapt himself to his future role"], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "He has failed to understand that monarchies have largely survived because they provide a service – as non-controversial and non-political heads of state.", "explanation": "第六段提出英国王室最应担忧，第七段具体阐释原因：女王凭亲民作风保住了王室声誉，但危机将在查尔斯继位后到来。他生活奢靡且等级观念强，“未能理解君主制得以留存主要是因为它们提供了一项服务——充当无争议、非政治的国家元首”，即他未能让自己适应未来作为君主应扮演的角色，D项“fails to adapt himself to his future role”精准概括该原因。", "trapNote": "B项“未按建议改变生活方式”属过度推理，文中仅提他品味奢华，未提有人劝他改变；A项“在政治问题上态度强硬”及C项“视共和派为潜在盟友”均属无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following is the best title of the text?", "options": ["Carlos, Glory and Disgrace Combined", "Charles, Anxious to Succeed to the Throne", "Carlos, a Lesson for All European Monarchs", "Charles, Slow to React to the Coming Threats"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "So, does the Spanish crisis suggest that monarchy is seeing its last days? Does that mean the writing is on the wall for all European royals, with their magnificent uniforms and majestic lifestyle?", "explanation": "文章首段由西班牙国王卡洛斯因丑闻退位引出核心议题：这是否意味着所有欧洲王室都将走向没落？随后第二至五段分析欧洲君主制的存续逻辑与固有弊端，第六至七段以英国王室为例发出警示，指出王室自身的所作所为才是最大威胁。全文以卡洛斯为切入点探讨对全体欧洲君主的警示，C项“卡洛斯：给所有欧洲君主的一课”最贴合主旨。", "trapNote": "A项仅聚焦卡洛斯个人荣辱，以偏概全且偏离后文对欧洲及英国王室的探讨；B、D项均只抓住末段查尔斯这一个局部细节，无法概括全文核心。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "退位，放弃权力", "note": "首段高频核心政治词汇，注意搭配 abdicate the throne。", "word": "abdicate"}, {"gloss": "超越，超出（……的局限）", "note": "第三段名词形式 transcendence 表“超脱性”，指王室超越党派政治。", "word": "transcendence"}, {"gloss": "不可辩护的，站不住脚的", "note": "否定前缀 in- + defensible，形容王室过时的特权与不平等。", "word": "indefensible"}, {"gloss": "侵入的，打扰的", "note": "media intrusiveness 意为“媒体的步步紧逼/隐私刺探”，源于动词 intrude。", "word": "intrusive"}, {"gloss": "富有的，阔绰的", "note": "熟词僻义：well-heeled 并非“鞋跟好”，而是“富裕的、手头宽裕的”。", "word": "well-heeled"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "But unlike their absolutist counterparts in the Gulf and Asia, most royal families have survived because they allow voters to avoid the difficult search for a non-controversial but respected public figure.", "point": "主句+原因状语从句+介词对比短语；注意 counterparts 指代“同类人/对应方”。", "structure": "[对比状语] Unlike..., [主句] most royal families have survived [原因状语从句] because they allow voters to avoid...", "zh": "但与海湾地区和亚洲的专制君主同行不同，欧洲大多数王室得以存续，是因为他们让选民免去了艰难寻找一位毫无争议而又受人尊敬的公众人物的麻烦。"}, {"en": "Symbolic of national unity as they claim to be, their very history—and sometimes the way they behave today – embodies outdated and indefensible privileges and inequalities.", "point": "as 引导倒装让步状语从句（表语前置）；破折号间为插入补充的主语成分。", "structure": "[让步状语从句] Symbolic of national unity as they claim to be, [主语] their very history (—and... today–) [谓语] embodies [宾语] outdated... inequalities.", "zh": "尽管他们声称自己象征着国家团结，但他们的历史本身——有时还包括他们如今的行事方式——却体现着过时且毫无道理的特权与不平等。"}, {"en": "At a time when Thomas Piketty and other economists are warning of rising inequality and the increasing power of inherited wealth, it is bizarre that wealthy aristocratic families should still be the symbolic heart of modern democratic states.", "point": "when 引导时间状语从句修饰 time；it 作形式主语，that 引导真正的主语从句（含虚拟/感叹语气 should）。", "structure": "[时间状语] At a time when..., [形式主语主句] it is bizarre [主语从句] that wealthy aristocratic families should still be...", "zh": "在托马斯·皮凯蒂等经济学家正就日益加剧的不平等及世袭财富日益膨胀的权力发出警告之际，富裕的贵族家庭竟然仍是现代民主国家的象征核心，这实在令人匪夷所思。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "21题同义替换：因丑闻被迫下台对应“在尴尬中结束统治”。", "option": "ended his reign in embarrassment", "original": "embarrassing scandals... forced him to eat his words and stand down"}, {"note": "22题同义替换：毫无争议且受人尊敬的形象对应“无可置疑且令人敬重的地位”。", "option": "undoubted and respectable status", "original": "a non-controversial but respected public figure"}, {"note": "23题同义替换：形容“荒诞、奇特”，bizarre 替换为 odd。", "option": "odd", "original": "bizarre"}, {"note": "23题同义替换：贵族家庭充当现代民主国家的象征核心即“贵族在现代民主国家中的角色”。", "option": "The role of the nobility in modern democracies", "original": "wealthy aristocratic families should still be the symbolic heart of modern democratic states"}, {"note": "24题同义替换：查尔斯未能理解王室非政治元首的定位，即未适应未来君主角色。", "option": "fails to adapt himself to his future role", "original": "failed to understand that monarchies have largely survived because they provide a service – as non-controversial and non-political heads of state"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2015-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2015", "examSet": "2015 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2015 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "数字时代隐私权与宪法第四修正案", "subtitle": "法律科技 · 手机搜查权与数字隐私边界", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 453, "paragraphs": ["Just how much does the Constitution protect your digital data? The Supreme Court will now consider whether police can search the contents of a mobile phone without a warrant if the phone is on or around a person during an arrest.", "California has asked the justices to refrain from a sweeping ruling particularly one that upsets the old assumption that authorities may search through the possessions of suspects at the time of their arrest. It is hard, the state argues, for judges to assess the implications of new and rapidly changing technologies.", "The court would be recklessly modest if it followed California’s advice. Enough of the implications are discernable, even obvious, so that the justices can and should provide updated guidelines to police, lawyers and defendants.", "They should start by discarding California’s lame argument that exploring the contents of a smart phone — a vast storehouse of digital information — is similar to, say, rifling through a suspect’s purse. The court has ruled that police don’t violate the Fourth Amendment when they sift through the wallet or pocketbook of an arrestee without a warrant. But exploring one’s smart phone is more like entering his or her home. A smart phone may contain an arrestee’s reading history, financial history, medical history and comprehensive records of recent correspondence. The development of “cloud computing,” meanwhile, has made that exploration so much the easier.", "Americans should take steps to protect their digital privacy. But keeping sensitive information on these devices is increasingly a requirement of normal life. Citizens still have a right to expect private documents to remain private and protected by the Constitution’s prohibition on unreasonable searches.", "As so often is the case, stating that principle doesn’t ease the challenge of line-drawing. In many cases, it would not be overly onerous for authorities to obtain a warrant to search through phone contents. They could still invalidate Fourth Amendment protections when facing severe, urgent circumstances, and they could take reasonable measures to ensure that phone data are not erased or altered while a warrant is pending. The court, though, may want to allow room for police to cite situations where they are entitled to more freedom.", "But the justices should not swallow California’s argument whole. New, disruptive technology sometimes demands novel applications of the Constitution’s protections. Orin Kerr, a law professor, compares the explosion and accessibility of digital information in the 21st century with the establishment of automobile use as a virtual necessity of life in the 20th: The justices had to specify novel rules for the new personal domain of the passenger car then; they must sort out how the Fourth Amendment applies to digital information now."], "translations": ["宪法究竟在多大程度上保护你的数字数据？最高法院现将审议：在实施逮捕期间，如果手机在嫌犯身上或其身边，警方是否可以在没有搜查令的情况下搜查手机内容。", "加利福尼亚州已请求大法官避免做出全面裁决，尤其是不要做出会推翻“当局在逮捕嫌犯时可搜查其随身财物”这一旧有假定的裁决。该州辩称，法官很难评估不断快速变化的各类新技术的潜在影响。", "如果最高法院听从加州的建议，那将是鲁莽的过度谦逊。足够多的影响已经清晰可见，甚至显而易见，因此大法官能够而且应当向警方、律师和被告提供更新后的指导准则。", "他们应当首先摒弃加州站不住脚的论点——该论点认为搜查智能手机（一个庞大的数字信息库）的内容，就好比翻查嫌犯的钱包。法院曾裁定，警方在没有搜查令的情况下翻查被捕者的钱包或手提包并不违反宪法第四修正案。但搜查某人的智能手机更像是进入他或她的家。智能手机中可能包含被捕者的阅读记录、财务记录、医疗记录以及近期通讯的全面记录。与此同时，“云计算”的发展让这种搜查变得更加容易。", "美国人应当采取措施保护自己的数字隐私。但将敏感信息保存在这些设备上正越来越成为正常生活的必要条件。公民仍有权期望私人文件保持私密，并受到宪法中禁止无理搜查条款的保护。", "一如既往，仅仅陈述这一原则并不能降低划定界限的难度。在许多案件中，当局获取搜查手机内容的搜查令并不算过于繁重。在面对严重、紧急情况时，他们仍可使第四修正案的保护条款暂不生效，并可采取合理措施，确保在等待搜查令期间手机数据不被擦除或篡改。不过，法院或许希望留出余地，允许警方援引其有权获得更大自由的特定情形。", "但大法官不应全盘接受加州的论点。颠覆性的新技术有时需要以全新方式运用宪法保护条款。法学教授奥林·克尔将21世纪数字信息的爆发和易获取性，与20世纪汽车作为实质上的生活必需品普及相提并论：当时的大法官必须为乘用车这一新的私人领域制定新规则；如今他们也必须理清第四修正案如何适用于数字信息。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The Supreme Court will work out whether, during an arrest, it is legitimate to", "options": ["prevent suspects from deleting their phone contents.", "search for suspects’ mobile phones without a warrant.", "check suspects’ phone contents without being authorized.", "prohibit suspects from using their mobile phones."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The Supreme Court will now consider whether police can search the contents of a mobile phone without a warrant if the phone is on or around a person during an arrest.", "explanation": "定位第一段第二句。最高法院将审议的问题是：在实施逮捕期间，如果嫌犯随身或身边有手机，警方是否可以“在没有搜查令的情况下搜查手机内容（search the contents of a mobile phone without a warrant）”。C项中check对应search，phone contents对应contents of a mobile phone，without being authorized对应without a warrant，完美对应，故选C。", "trapNote": "B项“无令搜寻嫌犯手机”偷换概念，原文是搜查手机“内容（contents）”而非搜寻手机本身；A项“阻止删除内容”与第六段警方采取措施保数据混淆，非最高法院审理核心。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author’s attitude toward California’s argument is one of", "options": ["disapproval.", "indifference.", "tolerance.", "cautiousness."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "The court would be recklessly modest if it followed California’s advice.", "explanation": "定位第三段首句及第四段首句。面对加州提出的不做全面裁决的请求，作者直言若采纳加州的建议，法院将是“鲁莽地过度谦逊（recklessly modest）”，并在第四段直接将其论点斥为“站不住脚的论点（California’s lame argument）”，建议予以摒弃（discarding）。可见作者对加州的观点持明确的不赞成、反对态度，故选A（disapproval）。", "trapNote": "D项“cautiousness（谨慎）”易误选，但文中明确使用recklessly modest和lame等强烈贬义词否定加州观点，并非谨慎观望；B项“漠不关心”与C项“宽容”均与作者态度相反。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The author believes that exploring one’s phone contents is comparable to", "options": ["getting into one’s residence.", "handling one’s historical records.", "scanning one’s correspondences.", "going through one’s wallet."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "But exploring one’s smart phone is more like entering his or her home.", "explanation": "定位第四段第三句。加州政府将搜查智能手机类比为翻看嫌犯的钱包或手提包，而作者反驳称智能手机包含阅读、财务、医疗及近期通讯等海量记录，“搜查智能手机更像是进入他或她的家（entering his or her home）”。A项“getting into one’s residence”中getting into对应entering，residence对应home，为精准同义替换，故选A。", "trapNote": "D项“翻看钱包”是加州方面提出的错误类比，也是作者明确反对的观点，属正反颠倒；B、C项只是手机内含信息类型，并非作者用来类比搜查手机行为的对应物。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "In Paragraph 5 and 6, the author shows his concern that", "options": ["principles are hard to be clearly expressed.", "the court is giving police less room for action.", "citizens’ privacy is not effectively protected.", "phones are used to store sensitive information."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Citizens still have a right to expect private documents to remain private and protected by the Constitution’s prohibition on unreasonable searches.", "explanation": "综合第五、六段来看，第五段指出在手机上保存敏感信息已成为正常生活的必需，公民仍有权期望私人文件受到宪法对无理搜查禁令的保护；第六段接着指出确立原则容易，但划定界限（line-drawing）充满挑战，警方在紧急情况下仍可能使第四修正案的保护失效，法院也可能给警方留有余地。作者的深层担忧在于公民数字隐私能否得到切实保护，故选C。", "trapNote": "A项“原则难以清晰表达”偷换概念，第六段首句说的是“说明原则并不能缓解划定界限的难度”；B项“给警方更少行动空间”正反颠倒，原文说法院可能给警方更多自由空间。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Orin Kerr’s comparison is quoted to indicate that", "options": ["the Constitution should be implemented flexibly.", "new technology requires reinterpretation of the Constitution.", "California’s argument violates principles of the Constitution.", "principles of the Constitution should never be altered"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "New, disruptive technology sometimes demands novel applications of the Constitution’s protections.", "explanation": "定位第七段。作者先提出论点：“颠覆性的新技术有时需要以全新方式运用宪法保护条款（novel applications of the Constitution’s protections）”，紧接着引用法学教授Orin Kerr的对比：正如20世纪汽车普及促使大法官为私人乘用车领域制定新规则一样，21世纪数字信息的爆发要求法院重新明确第四修正案如何适用于数字信息。B项“新技术要求重新诠释宪法”准确概括该例证目的，故选B。", "trapNote": "A项“宪法应被灵活执行”过于宽泛，未点明“新技术”这一核心条件；C项在例证中未体现；D项“宪法原则绝不应被改变”与原文强调的novel rules及novel applications意思相反。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "搜查令，授权令", "note": "法律高频词，without a warrant 意为“无搜查令”；作动词可表“使合理，成为……的依据”。", "word": "warrant"}, {"gloss": "站不住脚的，无说服力的", "note": "熟词僻义：本义为“跛的”，在议论文中常引申为“拙劣的、站不住脚的”（lame argument）。", "word": "lame"}, {"gloss": "翻找，搜寻", "note": "rifle through 与 sift through 同为“翻检、搜查”之意，注意与名词“步枪”区分。", "word": "rifle"}, {"gloss": "繁重的，费力的", "note": "第六段出现 overly onerous，指警方获取搜查令的程序“并不算过于繁琐沉重”。", "word": "onerous"}, {"gloss": "使无效，使作废", "note": "词根 valid（有效的）+ 否定前缀 in-，文中指紧急情况下宪法第四修正案保护可暂不适用。", "word": "invalidate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "California has asked the justices to refrain from a sweeping ruling particularly one that upsets the old assumption that authorities may search through the possessions of suspects at the time of their arrest.", "point": "one 作为 sweeping ruling 的同位语；第一个 that 引导定语从句修饰 one，第二个 that 引导同位语从句解释 assumption。", "structure": "[主句] California has asked the justices to refrain from a sweeping ruling, [同位语] particularly one [定语从句] that upsets the old assumption [同位语从句] that authorities may search...", "zh": "加利福尼亚州已请求大法官避免做出全面裁决，尤其是不要做出会推翻“当局在逮捕嫌犯时可搜查其随身财物”这一旧有假定的裁决。"}, {"en": "They should start by discarding California’s lame argument that exploring the contents of a smart phone — a vast storehouse of digital information — is similar to, say, rifling through a suspect’s purse.", "point": "that 引导同位语从句解释 argument；破折号间为 smart phone 的同位语；say 在句中作插入语，意为“比方说”。", "structure": "[主句] They should start by discarding California’s lame argument [同位语从句] that exploring the contents of a smart phone (...) is similar to... rifling through a suspect’s purse.", "zh": "他们应当首先摒弃加州站不住脚的论点——该论点认为搜查智能手机（一个庞大的数字信息库）的内容，就好比翻查嫌犯的钱包。"}, {"en": "They could still invalidate Fourth Amendment protections when facing severe, urgent circumstances, and they could take reasonable measures to ensure that phone data are not erased or altered while a warrant is pending.", "point": "and 连接两个并列分句；when facing... 为省略了主语和 be 动词的时间状语从句；pending 表“待审、尚待签发”。", "structure": "[分句1] They could still invalidate... [时间状语] when facing..., and [分句2] they could take reasonable measures to ensure [宾语从句] that phone data are not erased... [时间状语从句] while a warrant is pending.", "zh": "在面对严重、紧急情况时，他们仍可使第四修正案的保护条款暂不生效，并可采取合理措施，确保在等待搜查令期间手机数据不被擦除或篡改。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "26题同义替换：无搜查令（without a warrant）即未获授权（without being authorized）。", "option": "check suspects’ phone contents without being authorized", "original": "search the contents of a mobile phone without a warrant"}, {"note": "27题态度判定：recklessly modest 与 lame argument 共同指向作者的不赞成态度。", "option": "disapproval", "original": "recklessly modest / discarding California’s lame argument"}, {"note": "28题同义替换：进入住宅（getting into one’s residence）对应原文进入家中（entering his or her home）。", "option": "getting into one’s residence", "original": "entering his or her home"}, {"note": "30题同义替换：新技术需要宪法保护的全新应用即“新技术要求重新诠释宪法”。", "option": "new technology requires reinterpretation of the Constitution", "original": "New, disruptive technology sometimes demands novel applications of the Constitution’s protections"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2015-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2015", "examSet": "2015 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2015 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "《科学》期刊强化论文统计审查", "subtitle": "学术出版与科研可重复性", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 438, "paragraphs": ["The journal Science is adding an extra round of statistical checks to its peer-review process, editor-in-chief Marcia McNutt announced today. The policy follows similar efforts from other journals, after widespread concern that basic mistakes in data analysis are contributing to the irreproducibility of many published research findings.", "“Readers must have confidence in the conclusions published in our journal,” writes McNutt in an editorial. Working with the American Statistical Association, the journal has appointed seven experts to a statistics board of reviewing editors (SBoRE). Manuscripts will be flagged up for additional scrutiny by the journal’s internal editors, or by its existing Board of Reviewing Editors or by outside peer reviewers. The SBoRE panel will then find external statisticians to review these manuscripts.", "Asked whether any particular papers had impelled the change, McNutt said: “The creation of the ‘statistics board’ was motivated by concerns broadly with the application of statistics and data analysis in scientific research and is part of Science’s overall drive to increase reproducibility in the research we publish.”", "Giovanni Parmigiani, a biostatistician at the Harvard School of Public Health, a member of the SBoRE group. He says he expects the board to “play primarily an advisory role.” He agreed to join because he “found the foresight behind the establishment of the SBoRE to be novel, unique and likely to have a lasting impact. This impact will not only be through the publications in Science itself, but hopefully through a larger group of publishing places that may want to model their approach after Science.”", "John Ioannidis, a physician who studies research methodology, says that the policy is “a most welcome step forward” and “long overdue.” “Most journals are weak in statistical review, and this damages the quality of what they publish. I think that, for the majority of scientific papers nowadays, statistical review is more essential than expert review,” he says. But he noted that biomedical journals such as Annals of Internal Medicine, the Journal of the American Medical Association and The Lancet pay strong attention to statistical review.", "Professional scientists are expected to know how to analyze data, but statistical errors are alarmingly common in published research, according to David Vaux, a cell biologist. Researchers should improve their standards, he wrote in 2021, but journals should also take a tougher line, “engaging reviewers who are statistically literate and editors who can verify the process”. Vaux says that Science’s idea to pass some papers to statisticians “has some merit, but a weakness is that it relies on the board of reviewing editors to identify ‘the papers that need scrutiny’ in the first place”."], "translations": ["《科学》杂志主编玛西娅·麦克纳特今日宣布，该期刊将在同行评审流程中增加一轮额外的统计学核查。由于人们普遍担忧数据分析中的基本错误正导致许多已发表的研究成果无法复现，该政策紧随其他期刊的类似举措之后出台。", "“读者必须对我们期刊发表的结论抱有信心，”麦克纳特在一篇社论中写道。该期刊与美国统计协会合作，已任命七位专家组成统计学审稿编辑委员会（SBoRE）。稿件将由期刊内部编辑、现有审稿编委会或外部同行评审员标记出来，以接受额外审查。随后，SBoRE小组将寻找外部统计学家来评审这些稿件。", "当被问及是否有某些特定论文促使了这一改革时，麦克纳特表示：“设立‘统计学委员会’的初衷，源于人们对科学研究中统计学及数据分析应用问题的广泛担忧，这也是《科学》杂志致力于提高所发表研究可重复性的整体举措的一部分。”", "哈佛大学公共卫生学院的生物统计学家乔瓦尼·帕尔米贾尼是SBoRE小组的成员之一。他表示，自己预计该委员会将“主要发挥咨询顾问的作用”。他之所以同意加入，是因为他“认为成立SBoRE背后的远见卓识具有新颖性和独特性，并可能产生持久影响。这种影响不仅将通过《科学》杂志自身发表的文章体现出来，而且有望惠及更多可能效仿《科学》做法的出版机构。”", "研究方法论的医师约翰·约阿尼迪斯表示，这项政策是“最受欢迎的前进举措”且“早该实行”。“大多数期刊在统计学审查方面都很薄弱，这损害了它们所发表文章的质量。我认为，对于如今的大多数科学论文而言，统计学审查比专家评审更为重要，”他说道。但他也指出，诸如《内科学年鉴》《美国医学会杂志》和《柳叶刀》等生物医学期刊对统计学审查给予了高度重视。", "细胞生物学家戴维·沃克斯指出，人们理应期望专业科学家懂得如何分析数据，但已发表研究中的统计错误却多得惊人。他在2021年撰文称，研究人员应当提高自身标准，但期刊也应采取更强硬的态度，“聘请具备统计学素养的审稿人以及能够核验流程的编辑”。沃克斯表示，《科学》杂志将部分论文交由统计学家审阅的想法“有一定价值，但一个弱点在于最初需要依赖审稿编委会来识别‘需要严格审查的论文’”。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It can be learned from Paragraph 1 that", "options": ["Science intends to simplify their peer-review process.", "journals are strengthening their statistical checks.", "few journals are blamed for mistakes in data analysis.", "lack of data analysis is common in research projects."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The journal Science is adding an extra round of statistical checks to its peer-review process, editor-in-chief Marcia McNutt announced today. The policy follows similar efforts from other journals, after widespread concern that basic mistakes in data analysis are contributing to the irreproducibility of many published research findings.", "explanation": "【定位】第1段首句与第二句。【解析】第1段指出《科学》杂志正在其同行评审流程中增加一轮额外的统计核查（adding an extra round of statistical checks），且这一政策效仿了其他期刊的类似举措（follows similar efforts from other journals），起因是人们普遍担忧数据分析中的基本错误导致许多已发表研究成果无法复现。选项B“各期刊正在加强统计学核查”正是对上述内容的同义转述，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】A项“简化同行评审”与原文“增加额外一轮核查”正反颠倒；C项“很少期刊受指责”及D项“普遍缺乏数据分析”均属偷换概念与无中生有，原文强调的是“数据分析中的基本错误”而非缺乏分析。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The phrase “flagged up” (Para. 2) is the closest in meaning to", "options": ["found.", "marked.", "revised.", "stored."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Manuscripts will be flagged up for additional scrutiny by the journal’s internal editors, or by its existing Board of Reviewing Editors or by outside peer reviewers.", "explanation": "【定位】第2段第三句。【解析】第2段提到，期刊内部编辑、现有审稿编委会或外部同行评审员会“flag up”需要额外审查（additional scrutiny）的稿件，随后统计学审稿编辑委员会（SBoRE）再指派外部统计学家进行审核。结合语境“挑选出需要额外审查的稿件”，可知“flagged up”意为“标记、标出”。选项B“marked（标记）”与该词义及上下文逻辑最贴合，故正确。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】A项“发现”、C项“修改”和D项“储存”均不符合后续“交由外部统计学家审查”的衔接逻辑；评审前需要先“标记筛选”问题稿件，选A或C属于望文生义。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Giovanni Parmigiani believes that the establishment of the SBoRE may", "options": ["pose a threat to all its peers.", "meet with strong opposition.", "increase Science’s circulation.", "set an example for other journals."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "This impact will not only be through the publications in Science itself, but hopefully through a larger group of publishing places that may want to model their approach after Science.", "explanation": "【定位】第4段末句。【解析】第4段引述SBoRE成员Giovanni Parmigiani的观点，他认为该委员会将产生持久影响，这种影响不仅体现在《科学》杂志自身的出版物上，而且有望惠及更多“可能效仿《科学》做法的出版机构”（a larger group of publishing places that may want to model their approach after Science）。“model... after”对应D项“为其他期刊树立榜样（set an example）”。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】A项“对同行构成威胁”、B项“遭遇强烈反对”以及C项“增加《科学》发行量”在文中均无依据，属于典型的无中生有；原文强调的是其他出版机构“效仿其做法”的积极示范效应。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "David Vaux holds that what Science is doing now", "options": ["adds to researchers’ workload.", "diminishes the role of reviewers.", "has room for further improvement.", "is to fail in the foreseeable future"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Vaux says that Science’s idea to pass some papers to statisticians “has some merit, but a weakness is that it relies on the board of reviewing editors to identify ‘the papers that need scrutiny’ in the first place”.", "explanation": "【定位】第6段末句。【解析】第6段中细胞生物学家David Vaux对《科学》的做法做出了评价：将部分论文交由统计学家审核的想法“有一定价值（has some merit）”，但存在弱点（a weakness），即最初仍需依赖审稿编委会来识别“需要严格审查的论文”。这表明他认为《科学》目前的举措虽有可取之处但仍存不足，即“还有进一步改进的空间（has room for further improvement）”，对应选项C。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】A项“增加研究人员工作量”与B项“削弱审稿人作用”文中未提及，属无中生有；D项“在可预见的未来必将失败”过于绝对，属于过度推理，Vaux实际肯定了该做法“有一定价值”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following is the best title of the text?", "options": ["Science Joins Push to Screen Statistics in Papers.", "Professional Statisticians Deserve More Respect", "Data Analysis Finds Its Way onto Editors’ Desks", "Statisticians Are Coming Back with Science"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The journal Science is adding an extra round of statistical checks to its peer-review process, editor-in-chief Marcia McNutt announced today. The policy follows similar efforts from other journals, after widespread concern that basic mistakes in data analysis are contributing to the irreproducibility of many published research findings.", "explanation": "【定位】第1段首句及全文主线。【解析】文章开篇点明核心事件：《科学》杂志效仿其他期刊，在同行评审中增设统计学核查；第2至4段介绍SBoRE委员会的设立及预期示范效应；第5至6段引述学者对该举措的肯定与完善建议。全文围绕《科学》加入强化论文统计学审查行列展开。选项A“《科学》加入论文统计筛查推动行列”高度概括全文主旨，“joins push”精准对应第1段“follows similar efforts”。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】B项“专业统计学家应获更多尊重”偏离主题，属无中生有；C项未突出核心主体《科学》杂志且将范围泛化为“数据分析”；D项“统计学家的回归”属于曲解文意与以偏概全。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "不可复现性，不可重复性", "note": "由前缀ir-（否定）+reproducibility构成；高频学术科研词汇，常见于实验与数据科学语境。", "word": "irreproducibility"}, {"gloss": "标记，标出（引起注意）", "note": "考研高频短语动词；此处指审稿人将有疑点的稿件标记出来以便进一步审查。", "word": "flag up"}, {"gloss": "促使，推动，迫使", "note": "熟词僻义及写作高分替换词，相当于force或drive，注意区分impel（促使）与compel（强迫）。", "word": "impel"}, {"gloss": "远远不够的，早该实行的", "note": "常用作“过期的（overdue bills）”，本文引申为某项合理政策“姗姗来迟、早该实施”。", "word": "overdue"}, {"gloss": "懂统计学的，具备统计素养的", "note": "literate常见义为“识字的”，在“statistically literate”中表“精通某领域知识、有……素养的”。", "word": "literate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The policy follows similar efforts from other journals, after widespread concern that basic mistakes in data analysis are contributing to the irreproducibility of many published research findings.", "point": "主句后接时间状语短语，其中that引导同位语从句解释concern的具体内容。", "structure": "主句（The policy follows...） + 介词短语作时间状语（after widespread concern） + that引导的同位语从句（说明concern的内容）。", "zh": "由于人们普遍担忧数据分析中的基本错误正导致许多已发表的研究成果无法复现，该政策紧随其他期刊的类似举措之后出台。"}, {"en": "Vaux says that Science’s idea to pass some papers to statisticians “has some merit, but a weakness is that it relies on the board of reviewing editors to identify ‘the papers that need scrutiny’ in the first place”.", "point": "不定式短语作后置定语修饰idea，同时包含but连接的转折分句及that引导的表语从句。", "structure": "主句（Vaux says） + that引导的宾语从句（含不定式to pass...作idea的后置定语，以及but连接的并列转折句，其中that引导表语从句）。", "zh": "沃克斯表示，《科学》杂志将部分论文交由统计学家审阅的想法“有一定价值，但一个弱点在于最初需要依赖审稿编委会来识别‘需要严格审查的论文’”。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将具体行为“增加统计核查”与“效仿其他期刊”高度概括为各期刊都在强化统计审查。", "option": "journals are strengthening their statistical checks", "original": "adding an extra round of statistical checks ... follows similar efforts from other journals"}, {"note": "词义题直接对应，根据上下文“挑出稿件接受额外审查”推出“标记”含义。", "option": "marked", "original": "flagged up"}, {"note": "“以《科学》的做法为模板/效仿《科学》”转述为“为其他期刊树立榜样”。", "option": "set an example for other journals", "original": "model their approach after Science"}, {"note": "“有一定价值但存在弱点”客观概括为“仍有进一步改进的空间”。", "option": "has room for further improvement", "original": "has some merit, but a weakness is that..."}, {"note": "主旨题标题转述，用“joins push to screen”生动概括“紧随其他期刊增设统计检查”。", "option": "Science Joins Push to Screen Statistics in Papers", "original": "Science is adding an extra round of statistical checks ... follows similar efforts from other journals"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2015-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2015", "examSet": "2015 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2015 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "窃听丑闻背后的商业道德缺失", "subtitle": "媒体伦理与商业利益反思", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 447, "paragraphs": ["Two years ago, Rupert Murdoch’s daughter, Elisabeth, spoke of the “unsettling dearth of integrity across so many of our institutions.” Integrity had collapsed, she argued, because of a collective acceptance that the only “sorting mechanism” in society should be profit and the market. But “it’s us, human beings, we the people who create the society we want, not profit.”", "Driving her point home, she continued: “It’s increasingly apparent that the absence of purpose, of a moral language within government, media or business could become one of the most dangerous foes for capitalism and freedom.” This same absence of moral purpose was wounding companies such as News International, she thought, making it more likely that it would lose its way as it had with widespread illegal telephone hacking.", "As the hacking trial concludes – finding guilty ex-editor of the News of the World, Andy Coulson, for conspiring to hack phones, and finding his predecessor, Rebekah Brooks, innocent of the same charge – the wider issue of dearth of integrity still stands. Journalists are known to have hacked the phones of up to 5,500 people. This is hacking on an industrial scale, as was acknowledged by Glenn Mulcaire, the man hired by the News of the World in 2001 to be the point person for phone hacking. Others await trial. This long story still unfolds.", "In many respects, the dearth of moral purpose frames not only the fact of such widespread phone hacking but the terms on which the trial took place. One of the astonishing revelations was how little Rebekah Brooks knew of what went on in her newsroom, how little she thought to ask and the fact that she never inquired how the stories arrived. The core of her successful defence was that she knew nothing.", "In today’s world, it has become normal that well-paid executives should not be accountable for what happens in the organizations that they run. Perhaps we should not be so surprised. For a generation, the collective doctrine has been that the sorting mechanism of society should be profit. The words that have mattered are efficiency, flexibility, shareholder value, business-friendly, wealth generation, sales, impact and, in newspapers, circulation. Words degraded to the margin have been justice, fairness, tolerance, proportionality and accountability.", "The purpose of editing the News of the World was not to promote reader understanding, to be fair in what was written or to betray any common humanity. It was to ruin lives in the quest for circulation and impact. Ms Brooks may or may not have had suspicions about how her journalists got their stories, but she asked no questions, gave no instructions—nor received traceable, recorded answers."], "translations": ["两年前，鲁珀特·默多克的女儿伊丽莎白曾谈及“我们众多机构中令人不安的诚信匮乏”。她认为，诚信之所以崩溃，是因为社会普遍接受了利润和市场应当成为唯一的“筛选机制”。但她强调：“创造我们想要之社会的是我们自己，是人类，是我们人民，而不是利润。”", "为了把观点阐述透彻，她继续说道：“越来越明显的是，政府、媒体或商界缺乏宗旨和道德语言，可能会成为资本主义与自由最危险的敌人之一。”她认为，正是这种道德宗旨的缺失正在损害新闻国际等公司，使其更有可能像在大规模非法电话窃听事件中那样迷失方向。", "随着窃听案审理落下帷幕——判决《世界新闻报》前编辑安迪·库尔森共谋窃听电话罪名成立，而裁定其前任丽贝卡·布鲁克斯在同一指控下无罪——诚信匮乏这一更广泛的问题依然存在。众所周知，记者曾窃听了多达5500人的电话。正如2001年受雇于《世界新闻报》担任窃听事件核心负责人的格伦·马尔凯尔所承认的那样，这是工业化规模的窃听。其他人仍在等待受审。这一漫长的事件仍在持续发酵。", "在许多方面，道德宗旨的匮乏不仅决定了如此大规模窃听事件的发生，也左右了此次审判的展开方式。其中一项令人震惊的揭露是，丽贝卡·布鲁克斯对编辑部里发生的事情知之甚少、几乎从不曾想过过问，并且从未打听过这些新闻报道是如何得来的。她成功脱罪的核心辩护理由便是她对此一无所知。", "在当今世界，拿高薪的高管不必为自己所管理机构内部发生的事情负责，这已变得司空见惯。或许我们本不该对此感到如此惊讶。整整一代人以来，集体的信条一直是把利润作为社会的筛选机制。真正重要的词汇是效率、灵活性、股东价值、亲商、财富创造、销售额、影响力，而在报纸行业则是发行量。被贬低到边缘地带的词汇则是正义、公平、宽容、适度与问责。", "主编《世界新闻报》的目的并非增进读者理解、保证报道公正或流露出起码的普世人情；它的目的是在追逐发行量与影响力的过程中毁掉他人的人生。布鲁克斯女士或许曾对记者如何获取报道心存疑虑，或许没有，但她既不发问，也不下达指示——更未收到任何可追溯、有记录的答复。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the first two paragraphs, Elisabeth was upset by", "options": ["the consequences of the current sorting mechanism", "companies’ financial loss due to immoral practices.", "governmental ineffectiveness on moral issues.", "the wide misuse of integrity among institutions."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Integrity had collapsed, she argued, because of a collective acceptance that the only “sorting mechanism” in society should be profit and the market.", "explanation": "【定位】第1段第二句及第2段。【解析】第1段指出伊丽莎白认为诚信之所以崩溃，是因为社会普遍接受利润和市场是唯一的“筛选机制”（sorting mechanism）；第2段进一步指出，缺乏道德宗旨和道德语言会成为资本主义与自由最危险的敌人，且正损害新闻国际等公司，使其更容易在窃听等违法事件中迷失方向。可见令她感到不安的正是当前“利润筛选机制”所带来的不良后果，对应选项A。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】B项“公司因不道德行为造成的经济损失”属无中生有，文中“wounding”指道德层面的迷失与损害；C项“政府在道德问题上低效”及D项“诚信的广泛滥用”均属偷换概念，原文说的是诚信“匮乏（dearth）”。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be inferred from Paragraph 3 that", "options": ["Glenn Mulcaire may deny phone hacking as a crime", "more journalists may be found guilty of phone hacking.", "Andy Coulson should be held innocent of the charge.", "phone hacking will be accepted on certain occasions."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Others await trial. This long story still unfolds.", "explanation": "【定位】第3段最后两句。【解析】第3段先说明《世界新闻报》前编辑Andy Coulson因共谋窃听电话被判有罪，随后指出记者窃听人数高达5500人，属于工业化规模的窃听，最后提到“其他人正等待受审，这一漫长事件仍在继续（Others await trial. This long story still unfolds.）”。由此可合理推断，后续还会有更多涉案记者被判定犯有窃听罪，选项B正确。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】A项“否认窃听是犯罪”与文中“acknowledged（承认）”相悖，属正反颠倒；C项“Coulson应被判无罪”及D项“窃听在某些场合将被接受”均与原文事实及批判立场相反，属于主观臆断。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author believes the Rebekah Brooks’s defence", "options": ["revealed a cunning personality", "centered on trivial issues", "was hardly convincing", "was part of a conspiracy"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "One of the astonishing revelations was how little Rebekah Brooks knew of what went on in her newsroom, how little she thought to ask and the fact that she never inquired how the stories arrived. The core of her successful defence was that she knew nothing.", "explanation": "【定位】第4段第二、三句及第6段末句。【解析】第4段先用“astonishing revelations（令人震惊的揭露）”描述Rebekah Brooks对编辑部发生的事知之甚少、从未过问报道来源，且她成功脱罪的核心正是“自己一无所知”；第5段对此现象予以讽刺；第6段更指出她或许怀疑过报道来源，却故意不问、不指示、不留书面记录。由此可见，作者认为她的辩护词根本难以令人信服（hardly convincing），故C正确。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】A项“暴露了狡猾的性格”属于过度推理，作者批判的是高管不担责的制度文化与敷衍辩词；B项“聚焦于琐碎问题”与原文“核心是她一无所知”不符；D项“属于共谋的一部分”与判决结果及文意不符。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The author holds that the current collective doctrine shows", "options": ["generally distorted values", "unfair wealth distribution", "a marginalized lifestyle", "a rigid moral code"], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The words that have mattered are efficiency, flexibility, shareholder value, business-friendly, wealth generation, sales, impact and, in newspapers, circulation. Words degraded to the margin have been justice, fairness, tolerance, proportionality and accountability.", "explanation": "【定位】第5段第三至五句。【解析】第5段指出，一代人以来的集体信条（collective doctrine）一直将“利润”作为社会的筛选机制，受追捧的是效率、股东价值、销量和发行量等商业词汇，而被边缘化（degraded to the margin）的却是正义、公平、宽容、适度与问责等道德准则。这种重利轻义的倾向表明当前集体信条反映出普遍扭曲的价值观（generally distorted values），选项A最为精准。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】B项“财富分配不公”与C项“被边缘化的生活方式”均为偷换概念（原文边缘化的是“正义、公平等词汇/准则”而非生活方式）；D项“僵化的道德准则”与原文“缺乏道德语言与问责”正好相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Which of the following is suggested in the last paragraph?", "options": ["The quality of writing is of primary importance.", "Common humanity is central to news reporting.", "Moral awareness matters in editing a newspaper.", "Journalists need stricter industrial regulations."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "The purpose of editing the News of the World was not to promote reader understanding, to be fair in what was written or to betray any common humanity. It was to ruin lives in the quest for circulation and impact.", "explanation": "【定位】第6段首句与第二句。【解析】末段指出，主编《世界新闻报》的目的并非增进读者理解、保证报道公正或流露普世人情（common humanity），而是为了追求发行量与影响力不惜毁掉他人生活；紧接着批评Brooks作为主编对下属获取新闻的手段不闻不问。由此可见，作者意在强调办报编辑时道德意识与职业伦理至关重要（Moral awareness matters in editing a newspaper），对应选项C。", "trapNote": "【干扰排除】A项“写作质量最重要”属无中生有；B项“人情是新闻报道的核心”把反面批判的缺失当成客观事实，属偷换概念；D项“需要更严厉的行业法规”在末段并未提及，属过度推理。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "缺乏，匮乏", "note": "考研高频书面名词，相当于lack或shortage，常与of连用，如dearth of integrity（诚信缺失）。", "word": "dearth"}, {"gloss": "应承担责任的，负有责任的", "note": "社会伦理与商业管理话题核心词，常用搭配be accountable for（对……负责）。", "word": "accountable"}, {"gloss": "（使）降级，贬低，边缘化", "note": "常考义为“使恶化、降级”；文中“degraded to the margin”意为“被贬低至边缘地位”。", "word": "degrade"}, {"gloss": "流露，显露（情感或特质）", "note": "超级重点熟词僻义！常见义为“背叛、出卖”，在“betray any common humanity”中意为“流露出起码的人性”。", "word": "betray"}, {"gloss": "适度，相称性，均衡性", "note": "由proportion派生，法律与媒体伦理中指报道或惩罚的“分寸感、适度原则”。", "word": "proportionality"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "This same absence of moral purpose was wounding companies such as News International, she thought, making it more likely that it would lose its way as it had with widespread illegal telephone hacking.", "point": "she thought作插入语，现在分词making...作结果状语，其中that引导真正宾语从句，as引导方式状语从句。", "structure": "主句（This same absence... was wounding companies...） + 插入语（she thought） + 分词结果状语（making it more likely that...） + 方式状语从句（as it had...）。", "zh": "她认为，正是这种道德宗旨的缺失正在损害新闻国际等公司，使其更有可能像在大规模非法电话窃听事件中那样迷失方向。"}, {"en": "One of the astonishing revelations was how little Rebekah Brooks knew of what went on in her newsroom, how little she thought to ask and the fact that she never inquired how the stories arrived.", "point": "三个并列成分共同构成表语，包含两个how little引导的表语从句及由that引导的同位语从句。", "structure": "主语（One of the astonishing revelations） + 系动词（was） + 三个并列表语（how little... / how little... / the fact that...，内含what及how引导的宾语从句）。", "zh": "其中一项令人震惊的揭露是，丽贝卡·布鲁克斯对编辑部里发生的事情知之甚少、几乎从不曾想过过问，并且从未打听过这些新闻报道是如何得来的。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将“认为……是唯一筛选机制，且缺乏道德语言正损害公司并导致迷失”概括为对现有筛选机制后果的不安。", "option": "the consequences of the current sorting mechanism", "original": "Integrity had collapsed... because of a collective acceptance that the only “sorting mechanism” in society should be profit... wounding companies"}, {"note": "“其他人正在等待受审，故事仍在继续”合理推导出更多涉案记者将被定罪。", "option": "more journalists may be found guilty of phone hacking", "original": "Others await trial. This long story still unfolds."}, {"note": "用否定评价概括“不知情”借口在作者眼中的荒诞与不可信。", "option": "was hardly convincing", "original": "astonishing revelations... The core of her successful defence was that she knew nothing... asked no questions"}, {"note": "将商业词汇受捧、正义与问责被边缘化的现象概括为“普遍扭曲的价值观”。", "option": "generally distorted values", "original": "words that have mattered are efficiency... Words degraded to the margin have been justice, fairness..."}, {"note": "由《世界新闻报》只顾发行量而不顾公正人性，反推出办报时道德意识的重要性。", "option": "Moral awareness matters in editing a newspaper", "original": "purpose of editing the News of the World was not to promote reader understanding, to be fair... or to betray any common humanity"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2014-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2014", "examSet": "2014 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2014 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "英国失业救济改革与福利原则之争", "subtitle": "评英国财政大臣推行的求职前置福利改革", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 424, "paragraphs": ["In order to \"change lives for the better\" and reduce \"dependency\", George Osborne, Chancellor of the Exchequer, introduced the \"upfront work search\" scheme. Only if the jobless arrive at the jobcentre with a CV, register for online job search, and start looking for work will they be eligible for benefit - and then they should report weekly rather than fortnightly. What could be more reasonable? More apparent reasonableness followed. There will now be a seven-day wait for the jobseeker's allowance. \"Those first few days should be spent looking for work, not looking to sign on,\" he claimed. \"We're doing these things because we know they help people stay off benefits and help those on benefits get into work faster.\" Help? Really? On first hearing, this was the socially concerned chancellor, trying to change lives for the better, complete with \"reforms\" to an obviously indulgent system that demands too little effort from the newly unemployed to find work, and subsidises laziness. What motivated him, we were to understand, was his zeal for \"fundamental fairness\" - protecting the taxpayer, controlling spending and ensuring that only the most deserving claimants received their benefits. Losing a job is hurting: you don't skip down to the jobcentre with a song in your heart, delighted at the prospect of doubling your income from the generous state. It is financially terrifying, psychologically embarrassing and you know that support is minimal and extraordinarily hard to get. You are now not wanted; you are now excluded from the work environment that offers purpose and structure in your life. Worse, the crucial income to feed yourself and your family and pay the bills has disappeared. Ask anyone newly unemployed what they want and the answer is always: a job.", "But in Osborneland, your first instinct is to fall into dependency - permanent dependency if you can get it - supported by a state only too ready to indulge your falsehood. It is as though 20 years of ever-tougher reforms of the job search and benefit administration system never happened. The principle of British welfare is no longer that you can insure yourself against the risk of unemployment and receive unconditional payments if the disaster happens. Even the very phrase \"jobseeker's allowance\" is about redefining the unemployed as a \"jobseeker\" who had no fundamental right to a benefit he or she has earned through making national insurance contributions. Instead, the claimant receives a time-limited \"allowance,\" conditional on actively seeking a job; no entitlement and no insurance, at £71.70 a week, one of the least generous in the EU."], "translations": ["为了“让生活变得更美好”并减少“依赖性”，英国财政大臣乔治·奥斯本推出了“求职前置”方案。只有当失业者带着简历来到就业中心、注册线上求职并开始找工作时，他们才有资格领取救济金——而且之后他们必须每周而非每两周汇报一次。还有什么比这更合理的呢？看似合理的措施接踵而至。如今领取“求职者津贴”还要先等七天。“最初几天应该用来找工作，而不是急着去登记领救济，”他声称，“我们这样做是因为我们知道，这能帮助人们远离救济金，并帮助正在领救济的人更快找到工作。”有帮助？真的吗？乍一听，这是一位关心社会民生的财政大臣，正试图让人们的生活变得更美好，并对一个明显纵容惰性的制度进行“改革”——该制度对新失业者找工作的要求太低，反倒助长了懒惰。照此说法，促使他采取行动的，是他对“基本公平”的热忱——保护纳税人、控制支出并确保只有最应得的申领人才能拿到救济。失去工作是痛苦的：你绝不会哼着小曲蹦蹦跳跳地去就业中心，为慷慨的国家能让你的收入翻倍而欣喜若狂。失业在经济上令人恐惧，在心理上令人窘迫，而且你清楚自己能得到的支持微乎其微、极难获取。你不再被需要了；你被排除在能够赋予生活目标与秩序的工作环境之外。更糟糕的是，用来养活自己和家人、支付账单的关键收入消失了。问问任何一位新失业的人他们想要什么，答案永远只有一个：一份工作。", "然而在“奥斯本的世界”里，人的第一本能却是陷入依赖——如果可以的话甚至变成永久依赖——并由一个极其乐意纵容你弄虚作假的国家来供养。仿佛过去20年来对求职和救济管理制度愈发严苛的改革从未发生过一样。英国福利制度的原则不再是你可以通过参保来抵御失业风险，并在灾难降临时获得无条件的赔付。甚至连“求职者津贴”这一说法本身，也是为了把失业者重新定义为“求职者”——此人对通过缴纳国民保险费而挣得的救济金并不享有基本权利。相反，申领人拿到的是一种有时限的“津贴”，且以积极找工作为前提；没有应享权利，也没有保险保障，每周只有71.70英镑，属于欧盟中最不慷慨的水平之一。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "George Osborne's scheme was intended to", "options": ["encourage jobseekers' active engagement in job seeking.", "provide the unemployed with easier access to benefits.", "guarantee jobseekers' legitimate right to benefits.", "motivate the unemployed to report voluntarily."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Only if the jobless arrive at the jobcentre with a CV, register for online job search, and start looking for work will they be eligible for benefit - and then they should report weekly rather than fortnightly.", "explanation": "定位第1段前两句。财政大臣奥斯本推出“求职前置”方案，要求失业者必须携带简历到就业中心、注册线上求职并开始找工作才有资格领取救济金，且须每周而非每两周汇报一次；随后他还提到前几天应专注于找工作。这些措施旨在督促求职者更积极地投入求职，对应选项A“encourage jobseekers' active engagement in job seeking”，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“让失业者更容易获得救济金”和C项“保障合法领取救济的权利”均与方案提高申领门槛的事实完全相反；D项“促使失业者自愿汇报”错在“voluntarily”，原文是强制规定。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The phrase \"to sign on\" (Line 3, Para. 2) most probably means", "options": ["to check on the availability of jobs at the jobcentre.", "to accept the government's restrictions on the allowance.", "to register for an allowance from the government.", "to attend a governmental job-training program."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "There will now be a seven-day wait for the jobseeker's allowance. \"Those first few days should be spent looking for work, not looking to sign on,\" he claimed.", "explanation": "定位第1段“sign on”所在句及前一句。前文刚指出领取“求职者津贴（jobseeker's allowance）”需等待七天，紧接着奥斯本称“最初几天应该用来找工作，而不是急着去 sign on”。结合语境对比，此处“looking for work”与“looking to sign on”形成对照，且后文提及“stay off benefits”，可见“sign on”意为登记申领政府救济金，对应选项C，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“去就业中心查看岗位空缺”混淆了前文的“looking for work”；B项“接受政府对津贴的限制”和D项“参加政府职业培训项目”均脱离了等待期申领津贴的上下文语境。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What prompted the chancellor to develop his scheme?", "options": ["A desire to secure a better life for all.", "An eagerness to protect the unemployed.", "An urge to be generous to the claimants.", "A passion to ensure fairness for taxpayers."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "What motivated him, we were to understand, was his zeal for \"fundamental fairness\" - protecting the taxpayer, controlling spending and ensuring that only the most deserving claimants received their benefits.", "explanation": "定位第1段中“What motivated him...”一句。题干中“prompted”同义替换原文“motivated”。原文明确指出，推动奥斯本制定该方案的动力是他对“基本公平”的热忱——即保护纳税人利益、控制财政支出并确保只有最应得的申领人才能获得救济。选项D“A passion to ensure fairness for taxpayers”以“passion”对应“zeal”，精准匹配原文，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“为所有人确保更好生活”属过度扩大范围；B项“急于保护失业者”和C项“渴望对申领人慷慨”均与奥斯本收紧福利、保护纳税人的真实动机背道而驰。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 3, being unemployed makes one feel", "options": ["uneasy.", "insulted.", "enraged.", "guilty."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "It is financially terrifying, psychologically embarrassing and you know that support is minimal and extraordinarily hard to get.", "explanation": "定位第1段后半部分作者对失业的真实描述。作者指出失业令人感到痛苦，在经济上令人恐惧（financially terrifying），在心理上令人难堪窘迫（psychologically embarrassing），同时让人感到自己不再被需要、被排除在工作环境之外并失去基本收入。这些强烈的不安、焦虑与窘迫感对应选项A“uneasy（不安的、局促的）”，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“受到侮辱”、C项“暴怒”与D项“内疚”均曲解了原文情绪；“embarrassing”强调陷入困境后的尴尬窘迫与忐忑不安，并非他人蓄意侮辱或自身愤怒愧疚。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "To which of the following would the author most probably agree?", "options": ["Unemployment benefits should not be made conditional.", "The British welfare system indulges jobseekers' laziness.", "The jobseekers' allowance has met their actual needs.", "Osborne's reforms will reduce the risk of unemployment."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The principle of British welfare is no longer that you can insure yourself against the risk of unemployment and receive unconditional payments if the disaster happens.", "explanation": "定位第2段。作者在末段讽刺了奥斯本的福利观，批评英国福利原则已背离过去“通过缴纳国民保险应对失业风险、遭遇灾难时即可获得无条件救济”的传统，转而将失业者重新定义为只有积极求职才能获得有条件、限时“津贴”的人，且失去了基本权利与保险保障。由此可见作者认同失业救济金不应附加条件，对应选项A，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“英国福利制度纵容求职者懒惰”是奥斯本而非作者的观点，属于张冠李戴；C项“津贴满足了实际需求”与末尾“欧盟中最不慷慨之一”相悖；D项“改革将降低失业风险”属无中生有。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "有资格的，合格的", "note": "常用搭配 be eligible for sth.，意为“有资格获得某物（如津贴、职位）”。", "word": "eligible"}, {"gloss": "纵容的，宽容的；放纵的", "note": "动词为 indulge，文中用 indulgent system 讽刺政客眼中“纵容懒惰的福利制度”。", "word": "indulgent"}, {"gloss": "热忱，狂热，热情", "note": "带有强烈的感情色彩，文中与 zeal for \"fundamental fairness\" 搭配，后在Q3中同义替换为 passion。", "word": "zeal"}, {"gloss": "申领人，索赔人", "note": "由 claim + -ant 构成，特指申请救济金、保险理赔或权益的人。", "word": "claimant"}, {"gloss": "应享的权利；津贴，福利保障", "note": "文中与 allowance 形成鲜明对比，揭示失业救济从“应得权利”降格为“有条件的施舍”。", "word": "entitlement"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Only if the jobless arrive at the jobcentre with a CV, register for online job search, and start looking for work will they be eligible for benefit - and then they should report weekly rather than fortnightly.", "point": "Only if 引导的条件状语从句置于句首，主句（will they be eligible...）采用部分倒装结构。", "structure": "Only if 引导的条件状语从句（含三个并列谓语）+ 部分倒装主句 + 破折号后并列分句。", "zh": "只有当失业者带着简历来到就业中心、注册线上求职并开始找工作时，他们才有资格领取救济金——而且之后他们必须每周汇报一次，而不是每两周一次。"}, {"en": "On first hearing, this was the socially concerned chancellor, trying to change lives for the better, complete with \"reforms\" to an obviously indulgent system that demands too little effort from the newly unemployed to find work, and subsidises laziness.", "point": "trying to... 作现在分词短语修饰 chancellor；complete with... 为形容词短语作伴随状语；that 引导定语从句修饰 system。", "structure": "时间状语 + 主系表结构 + 现在分词短语作定语 + 形容词短语（complete with...）+ that 引导的定语从句（含并列谓语 demands...and subsidises...）。", "zh": "乍一听，这是一位关心社会民生的财政大臣，正试图让人们的生活变得更美好，并对一个明显纵容惰性的制度进行“改革”——该制度对新失业者找工作的要求太低，反倒助长了懒惰。"}, {"en": "Even the very phrase \"jobseeker's allowance\" is about redefining the unemployed as a \"jobseeker\" who had no fundamental right to a benefit he or she has earned through making national insurance contributions.", "point": "who 引导定语从句修饰 jobseeker；benefit 后接省略关系代词 that/which 的定语从句，说明福利是通过缴费挣得的。", "structure": "主谓表结构（is about redefining...as...）+ who 引导的定语从句 + 省略关系词的定语从句（修饰 benefit）。", "zh": "甚至“求职者津贴”这一措辞本身，也是在将失业者重新定义为“求职者”——他们对自己通过缴纳国民保险费而挣得的救济金并不享有基本权利。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第1段“注册线上求职并开始找工作”对应Q1正确选项A“鼓励求职者积极参与求职”。", "option": "encourage jobseekers' active engagement in job seeking", "original": "register for online job search, and start looking for work"}, {"note": "第1段“等待七天、不要急着 sign on”对应Q2正确选项C“登记申领政府津贴”。", "option": "to register for an allowance from the government", "original": "seven-day wait for the jobseeker's allowance...looking to sign on"}, {"note": "第1段“对基本公平的热忱——保护纳税人”对应Q3正确选项D“确保对纳税人公平的热情”。", "option": "A passion to ensure fairness for taxpayers", "original": "his zeal for \"fundamental fairness\" - protecting the taxpayer"}, {"note": "第1段“经济上恐惧、心理上尴尬窘迫”在Q4中概括为正确选项A“不安的”。", "option": "uneasy", "original": "financially terrifying, psychologically embarrassing"}, {"note": "第2段批评英国福利原则不再“无条件支付”，对应Q5正确选项A“失业救济金不应附带条件”。", "option": "Unemployment benefits should not be made conditional", "original": "no longer that you can insure yourself against the risk of unemployment and receive unconditional payments"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2014-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2014", "examSet": "2014 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2014 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "美国法律行业的高成本与改革出路", "subtitle": "剖析美国法律教育高昂成本与律所僵化所有制的问题及改革方向", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 429, "paragraphs": ["All around the world, lawyers generate more hostility than the members of any other profession - with the possible exception of journalism. But there are few places where clients have more grounds for complaint than America. During the decade before the economic crisis, spending on legal services in America grew twice as fast as inflation. The best lawyers made skyscrapers-full of money, tempting ever more students to pile into law schools. But most law graduates never get a big-firm job. Many of them instead become the kind of nuisance-lawsuit filer that makes the tort system a costly nightmare. There are many reasons for this. One is the excessive costs of a legal education. There is just one path for a lawyer in most American states: a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject, then a three-year law degree at one of 200 law schools authorized by the American Bar Association and an expensive preparation for the bar exam. This leaves today's average law-school graduate with $100,000 of debt on top of undergraduate debts. Law-school debt means that they have to work fearsomely hard.", "Reforming the system would help both lawyers and their customers. Sensible ideas have been around for a long time, but the state-level bodies that govern the profession have been too conservative to implement them. One idea is to allow people to study law as an undergraduate degree. Another is to let students sit for the bar after only two years of law school. If the bar exam is truly a stern enough test for a would be lawyer, those who can sit it earlier should be allowed to do so. Students who do not need the extra training could cut their debt mountain by a third. The other reason why costs are so high is the restrictive guild-like ownership structure of the business. Except in the District of Columbia, non-lawyers may not own any share of a law firm. This keeps fees high and innovation slow. There is pressure for change from within the profession, but opponents of change among the regulators insist that keeping outsiders out of a law firm isolates lawyers from the pressure to make money rather than serve clients ethically.", "In fact, allowing non-lawyers to own shares in law firms would reduce costs and improve services to customers, by encouraging law firms to use technology and to employ professional managers to focus on improving firms' efficiency. After all, other countries, such as Australia and Britain, have started liberalizing their legal professions. America should follow."], "translations": ["在世界各地，律师招致的敌意比其他任何行业的从业者都要多——新闻业或许是个例外。但很少有地方的客户像美国这样有如此充足的抱怨理由。在经济危机前的十年里，美国在法律服务上的支出增长速度是通货膨胀率的两倍。最顶尖的律师赚得盆满钵满，这诱使越来越多的学生涌入法学院。但大多数法学院毕业生永远也进不了大型律所工作。相反，他们中的许多人成了专门提起恶意诉讼的律师，使侵权法体系沦为一场代价高昂的噩梦。造成这种情况的原因有很多，其中之一便是法律教育过高的成本。在美国大多数州，成为律师只有一条路径：先花四年攻读某个无关专业的本科学位，然后在美国律师协会认可的200所法学院之一攻读三年制法学学位，还要花大价钱准备律师资格考试。这使得如今普通法学院毕业生在本科债务之外又背负了10万美元的债务。法学院债务意味着他们必须拼命工作。", "改革这一体系将对律师及其客户双方都有利。明智的改革构想早已存在，但监管该行业的州级机构过于保守，迟迟未能付诸实施。一个构想是允许人们在本科阶段就攻读法学学位；另一个构想是允许学生在法学院学习两年后就参加律师资格考试。如果律师资格考试对于未来的律师而言确实足够严格，那么能够提前通过的人就应该被允许提前参考。不需要额外培训的学生可以将他们堆积如山的债务减少三分之一。成本居高不下的另一个原因是该行业带有行会色彩的限制性所有权结构。除哥伦比亚特区外，非律师人士不得持有律师事务所的任何股份。这导致律师费用居高不下，行业创新步履维艰。行业内部已存在变革的压力，但监管机构中的反对者坚称，将局外人排除在律所之外，能使律师免受逐利压力的影响，从而坚守职业道德为客户服务。", "事实上，允许非律师人士持有律师事务所的股份，能够鼓励律所采用新技术并聘请职业经理人专注于提升事务所效率，从而降低成本、改善客户服务。毕竟，澳大利亚和英国等其他国家已经开始放开对法律行业的管制。美国也应当效仿。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "A lot of students take up law as their profession due to", "options": ["the growing demand from clients.", "the increasing pressure of inflation.", "the prospect of working in big firms.", "the attraction of financial rewards."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The best lawyers made skyscrapers-full of money, tempting ever more students to pile into law schools.", "explanation": "本题定位第1段第4句。原文指出，最顶尖的律师赚得巨额财富（made skyscrapers-full of money），诱使越来越多的学生涌入法学院（pile into law schools）。选项D中的the attraction of financial rewards（丰厚经济回报的吸引力）正是对skyscrapers-full of money和tempting的同义转述，因果关系明确，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项“客户需求增长”文中未提及；B项将文中“法律服务支出增速是通胀两倍”偷换为“通胀压力增大”；C项属于反向干扰，后文明确说明大多数毕业生进不了大律所，并非吸引入学的原因。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following adds to the costs of legal education in most American states?", "options": ["Higher tuition fees for undergraduate studies.", "Receiving training by professional associations.", "Admissions approval from the bar association.", "Pursuing a bachelor's degree in another major."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "There is just one path for a lawyer in most American states: a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject, then a three-year law degree at one of 200 law schools authorized by the American Bar Association and an expensive preparation for the bar exam.", "explanation": "本题定位第1段倒数第3句。文中说明法律教育成本过高的表现之一是成为律师路径单一且耗时费钱：必须先在无关专业攻读四年制本科学位（a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject），之后再读三年法学院并备考。选项D中的Pursuing a bachelor's degree in another major（攻读另一专业的学士学位）与原文高度对应，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项“本科学费上涨”属于无中生有，文中只强调多读四年无关本科增加总体成本；B项将“律师协会认可的法学院”曲解为“由专业协会提供培训”；C项“律师协会的入学批准”偷换概念。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Hindrance to the reform of the legal system originates from", "options": ["the rigid bodies governing the profession.", "lawyers' and clients' strong resistance.", "the stern exam for would-be lawyers.", "non-professionals' sharp criticism."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Sensible ideas have been around for a long time, but the state-level bodies that govern the profession have been too conservative to implement them.", "explanation": "本题定位第2段第2句。原文指出，合理的改革构想由来已久，但管理该行业的州级机构（the state-level bodies that govern the profession）过于保守而不愿实施（too conservative to implement them）。选项A中the rigid bodies governing the profession的rigid精准对应conservative，故A正确。", "trapNote": "B项与文意相反，第2段明确指出行业内部存在变革压力，改革对律师和客户都有利；C项“严格考试”是允许提前参考的前提而非改革阻力；D项“非专业人士的尖锐批评”文中未提及。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The guild-like ownership structure is considered \"restrictive\" partly because it", "options": ["prevents lawyers from gaining due profits.", "bans outsiders' involvement in the profession.", "aggravates the ethical situation in the trade.", "keeps lawyers from holding law-firm shares."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Except in the District of Columbia, non-lawyers may not own any share of a law firm.", "explanation": "本题定位第2段第8句。前文提到高成本的另一原因是限制性行会式所有权结构（restrictive guild-like ownership structure），紧接着解释除哥伦比亚特区外，非律师人士不得持有律所任何股份（non-lawyers may not own any share of a law firm）。B项bans outsiders' involvement（禁止局外人参与）正是对non-lawyers与outsiders的同义替换，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项与原文“该结构使费用居高不下”及“逐利压力”表述不符；C项将监管者担心的伦理问题曲解为该结构“恶化了道德状况”；D项把限制对象non-lawyers偷换为lawyers。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "In this text, the author mainly discusses", "options": ["the factors that help make a successful lawyer in America.", "a problem in America's legal profession and solutions to it.", "the role of undergraduate studies in America's legal education.", "flawed ownership of America's law firms and its causes."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Reforming the system would help both lawyers and their customers.", "explanation": "本文呈“提出问题—分析原因—给出对策”结构。第1段指出美国法律行业广受诟病且教育成本过高；第2段首句提出改革体系对双方都有利，并剖析州级监管保守与行会式所有权两大症结；第3段进一步论证放开非律师持股等解决方案的益处并呼吁美国效仿英澳。B项“美国法律行业的问题及其解决方案”全面概括全文主旨，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项“成为成功律师的因素”和C项“本科教育的作用”均属以偏概全；D项只提及“律所所有权缺陷及其成因”，遗漏了教育成本问题及全文核心的改革对策部分。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 敌意；抵触情绪", "note": "文中指律师在全球范围内普遍招致公众的敌意，常见搭配 generate hostility。", "word": "hostility"}, {"gloss": "n. 【律】侵权（行为）", "note": "tort system 指“侵权法体系”，nuisance-lawsuit filer 指滥诉者。", "word": "tort"}, {"gloss": "adj. 过度的；过分的", "note": "文中 excessive costs 指高得过分的法律教育成本，名词形式为 excess。", "word": "excessive"}, {"gloss": "n. 行会；同业公会", "note": "文中 guild-like ownership structure 形象形容律所排外、封闭的行会式所有权结构。", "word": "guild"}, {"gloss": "v. 放开管制；使自由化", "note": "文中 liberalizing their legal professions 指英澳两国放宽对法律行业的准入与持股限制。", "word": "liberalize"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "There is just one path for a lawyer in most American states: a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject, then a three-year law degree at one of 200 law schools authorized by the American Bar Association and an expensive preparation for the bar exam.", "point": "冒号后的长列举与过去分词短语作后置定语", "structure": "There be 句型作主干 + 冒号后三个并列名词短语（a four-year undergraduate degree..., then a three-year law degree..., and an expensive preparation...）作 path 的同位语；过去分词短语 authorized by... 作后置定语修饰 200 law schools。", "zh": "在美国大多数州，成为律师只有一条路径：先花四年攻读某个无关专业的本科学位，然后在美国律师协会认可的200所法学院之一攻读三年制法学学位，还要花大价钱准备律师资格考试。"}, {"en": "There is pressure for change from within the profession, but opponents of change among the regulators insist that keeping outsiders out of a law firm isolates lawyers from the pressure to make money rather than serve clients ethically.", "point": "动名词短语作主语与 rather than 连接的并列不定式", "structure": "but 连接的并列复合句；后半句中 insist 后接 that 引导的宾语从句，从句主语为动名词短语 keeping outsiders out of a law firm，谓语为 isolates...from...，不定式短语 to make money rather than serve clients ethically 作 pressure 的后置定语。", "zh": "行业内部已存在变革的压力，但监管机构中的反对者坚称，将局外人排除在律所之外，能使律师免受逐利而非恪守职业道德服务客户的压力。"}, {"en": "In fact, allowing non-lawyers to own shares in law firms would reduce costs and improve services to customers, by encouraging law firms to use technology and to employ professional managers to focus on improving firms' efficiency.", "point": "动名词作主语与 by 引出的方式状语嵌套并列不定式", "structure": "主语为动名词短语 allowing non-lawyers to own shares in law firms，谓语为并列结构 would reduce... and improve...，方式状语 by encouraging... 后接两个并列的不定式短语 to use technology 和 to employ professional managers... 作宾语补足语。", "zh": "事实上，允许非律师人士持有律所股份，能够通过鼓励律所运用技术以及聘用职业经理人专注于提升律所效率，从而降低成本并改善对客户的服务。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "比喻手法“赚得摩天大楼般多的钱”对应选项中的“经济回报”", "option": "financial rewards", "original": "made skyscrapers-full of money"}, {"note": "“在某个无关专业攻读四年制本科学位”同义转述为“在另一专业攻读学士学位”", "option": "Pursuing a bachelor's degree in another major", "original": "a four-year undergraduate degree in some unrelated subject"}, {"note": "定语从句变为现在分词短语作后置定语，too conservative 对应 rigid", "option": "the rigid bodies governing the profession", "original": "bodies that govern the profession have been too conservative"}, {"note": "non-lawyers 对应后文及选项中的 outsiders，may not own 对应 bans", "option": "bans outsiders' involvement in the profession", "original": "non-lawyers may not own any share of a law firm"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2014-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2014", "examSet": "2014 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2014 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "科学大奖争议与学术界态度", "subtitle": "探讨互联网企业家设立高额科学奖项引发的争议及学者应持的态度", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 440, "paragraphs": ["The US$3-million Fundamental Physics Prize is indeed an interesting experiment, as Alexander Polyakov said when he accepted this year's award in March. And it is far from the only one of its type. As a News Feature article in Nature discusses, a string of lucrative awards for researchers have joined the Nobel Prizes in recent years. Many, like the Fundamental Physics Prize, are funded from the telephone-number-sized bank accounts of Internet entrepreneurs. These benefactors have succeeded in their chosen fields, they say, and they want to use their wealth to draw attention to those who have succeeded in science. What's not to like? Quite a lot, according to a handful of scientists quoted in the News Feature. You cannot buy class, as the old saying goes, and these upstart entrepreneurs cannot buy their prizes the prestige of the Nobels. The new awards are an exercise in self-promotion for those behind them, say scientists. They could distort the achievement-based system of peer-review-led research. They could cement the status quo of peer-reviewed research. They do not fund peer-reviewed research. They perpetuate the myth of the lone genius.", "The goals of the prize-givers seem as scattered as the criticism. Some want to shock, others to draw people into science, or to better reward those who have made their careers in research.", "As Nature has pointed out before, there are some legitimate concerns about how science prizes - both new and old - are distributed. The Breakthrough Prize in Life Sciences, launched this year, takes an unrepresentative view of what the life sciences include. But the Nobel Foundation's limit of three recipients per prize, each of whom must still be living, has long been outgrown by the collaborative nature of modern research - as will be demonstrated by the inevitable row over who is ignored when it comes to acknowledging the discovery of the Higgs boson. The Nobels were, of course, themselves set up by a very rich individual who had decided what he wanted to do with his own money. Time, rather than intention, has given them legitimacy.", "As much as some scientists may complain about the new awards, two things seem clear. First, most researchers would accept such a prize if they were offered one. Second, it is surely a good thing that the money and attention come to science rather than go elsewhere. It is fair to criticize and question the mechanism - that is the culture of research, after all - but it is the prize-givers' money to do with as they please. It is wise to take such gifts with gratitude and grace."], "translations": ["正如亚历山大·波利亚科夫今年三月领奖时所说，奖金高达300万美元的“基础物理学奖”的确是一项有趣的实验。而且这绝非唯一此类奖项。正如《自然》杂志一篇新闻特写所探讨的，近年来一系列面向科研人员的丰厚奖项加入了诺贝尔奖的行列。其中许多奖项与基础物理学奖一样，由互联网企业家宛如电话号码般庞大的银行账户出资设立。这些资助者表示，他们在各自选择的领域取得了成功，希望利用自己的财富来吸引人们关注那些在科学界取得成功的人。这有什么不好的呢？据该新闻特写援引的少数科学家的说法，问题还真不少。俗话说，格调是买不来的，这些暴发户企业家也买不来诺贝尔奖的声望。科学家们称，这些新奖项是幕后出资人的自我宣传之举。它们可能会扭曲以同行评议研究为主导的成就体系，可能会固化同行评议研究的现状，却并不资助同行评议研究本身，并且延续了“孤胆天才”的神话。", "设奖者的目的似乎和外界的批评一样众说纷纭。有人想制造轰动，也有人想吸引大众投身科学，或者更好地奖励那些以科研为事业的人。", "正如《自然》杂志此前指出的，关于新老科学奖项的分配方式确实存在一些合理担忧。今年设立的“生命科学突破奖”对生命科学所涵盖领域的界定缺乏代表性。然而，诺贝尔基金会对每个奖项最多三名在世获奖者的限制，早已落后于现代科研的协作本质——这一点从希格斯玻色子发现成果确认过程中因谁被忽略而必然引发的争吵中便可见一斑。当然，诺贝尔奖本身也是由一位极其富有的个人设立的，他当时只是决定用自己的钱做想做的事。赋予诺贝尔奖合法性的，是时间，而非初衷。", "尽管一些科学家可能对新奖项有所抱怨，但有两点似乎显而易见。首先，如果获得此类奖项，大多数科研人员都会接受。其次，资金和关注度流向科学界总比流向别处要好。批评和质疑其评选机制是合理的——毕竟这就是科研文化的一部分——但这终究是设奖者自己的钱，他们有权自行支配。怀着感恩与风度接受这样的馈赠才是明智之举。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The Fundamental Physics Prize is seen as", "options": ["a symbol of the entrepreneurs' wealth.", "a handsome reward for researchers.", "a possible replacement of the Nobel Prizes.", "an example of bankers' investments."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "As a News Feature article in Nature discusses, a string of lucrative awards for researchers have joined the Nobel Prizes in recent years.", "explanation": "本题定位第1段第1至4句。开头提及基础物理学奖奖金高达300万美元，第3句随后将其归为一类“面向科研人员的丰厚奖项”（a string of lucrative awards for researchers）。选项B中的a handsome reward for researchers精准转述了US$3-million及lucrative awards for researchers，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项“企业家财富的象征”偏离句意，文中说的是企业家借此吸引大众关注科学界成功人士；C项“可能取代诺贝尔奖”和D项“银行家投资”均属曲解与无中生有，出资人是互联网企业家而非银行家。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The critics think that the new awards will most benefit", "options": ["the profit-oriented scientists.", "the achievement-based system.", "the founders of the new awards.", "peer-review-led research."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The new awards are an exercise in self-promotion for those behind them, say scientists.", "explanation": "本题定位第1段第9句。针对这些新奖项，批评的科学家指出，它们是幕后出资人的一场自我宣传（an exercise in self-promotion for those behind them）。句中的those behind them正是指新奖项的设立者，即选项C中的the founders of the new awards，故C正确。", "trapNote": "A项“逐利科学家”原文未提；B项“成就体系”与D项“同行评议主导的研究”在原文第1段末句均被批评者认为会受新奖项扭曲或得不到资助，并非最大受益方。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "例证题", "stem": "The discovery of the Higgs boson is a typical case which involves", "options": ["legitimate concerns over the new prizes.", "controversies over the recipients' status.", "the joint effort of modern researchers.", "the demonstration of research findings."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "But the Nobel Foundation's limit of three recipients per prize, each of whom must still be living, has long been outgrown by the collaborative nature of modern research - as will be demonstrated by the inevitable row over who is ignored when it comes to acknowledging the discovery of the Higgs boson.", "explanation": "本题为第3段第3句的例证题。句中破折号后提到“确认希格斯玻色子发现时因谁被忽略而引发的必然争执”，正是用来佐证破折号前的主句观点：现代科研具有协作性本质（the collaborative nature of modern research），已远远超出诺贝尔奖每项最多三人的限制。选项C中的joint effort完美对应collaborative nature，故C正确。", "trapNote": "A项将诺贝尔奖的旧制问题误作“对新奖项的担忧”；B项“获奖者地位争议”偷换概念，原文争吵焦点是多人协作下谁被忽略；D项“研究成果展示”属于望文生义，误解了demonstrated。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 4, which of the following is true of the Nobels?", "options": ["History has never cast doubt on them.", "Their endurance has done justice to them.", "They are the most representative honor.", "Their legitimacy has long been in dispute."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Time, rather than intention, has given them legitimacy.", "explanation": "本题定位第3段末尾（对应原卷第4段）。原文指出，诺贝尔奖最初也是由一位富豪凭个人意愿用自己的钱设立的，赋予它们合法性的是时间而非初衷（Time, rather than intention, has given them legitimacy）。选项B“时间的积淀证明了其合理性”（Their endurance has done justice to them）精准对应Time...given them legitimacy，故B正确。", "trapNote": "A项“历史从未质疑过诺奖”与第3段指出诺奖三人上限不合时宜的事实相悖；C项“最具代表性”和D项“合法性长期存疑”均与原文赋予其合法性的表述相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author believes that the new awards are", "options": ["unworthy of public attention.", "subject to undesirable changes.", "harmful to the culture of research.", "acceptable despite the criticism."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "It is fair to criticize and question the mechanism - that is the culture of research, after all - but it is the prize-givers' money to do with as they please. It is wise to take such gifts with gratitude and grace.", "explanation": "本题定位第4段末两句。作者先表明两点：多数科研人员会接受奖项，且资金与关注流入科学界是好事；接着指出尽管批评和质疑评选机制合情合理，但归根结底是设奖者自愿出资，怀着感恩与风度接受这些馈赠才是明智之举。可见作者认为尽管存在批评，新奖项仍是可接受的，故D正确。", "trapNote": "A项“不值得公众关注”与第4段“关注度流向科学是好事”相反；B项“面临不良变动”原文未提；C项将“质疑机制本身就是科研文化”曲解为新奖项“损害科研文化”。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 赚大钱的；报酬丰厚的", "note": "文中指基础物理学奖等奖金数额巨大的科研奖项。", "word": "lucrative"}, {"gloss": "n./adj. 暴发户（的）；新贵（的）", "note": "文中 upstart entrepreneurs 带有一丝批评或调侃意味，指靠互联网骤富的企业家。", "word": "upstart"}, {"gloss": "v. 使永久存在；延续", "note": "文中 perpetuate the myth of the lone genius 指使“孤胆天才”的错误观念长期延续下去。", "word": "perpetuate"}, {"gloss": "v. 发展超出…的限制；比…长得更大", "note": "文中用被动语态说明诺奖三人限制早已跟不上现代科研协作发展的步伐。", "word": "outgrow"}, {"gloss": "n. 合法性；合理性；正当性", "note": "文中指经过时间沉淀赋予诺贝尔奖的公信力与正当性，形容词为 legitimate。", "word": "legitimacy"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "But the Nobel Foundation's limit of three recipients per prize, each of whom must still be living, has long been outgrown by the collaborative nature of modern research - as will be demonstrated by the inevitable row over who is ignored when it comes to acknowledging the discovery of the Higgs boson.", "point": "“each of whom”非限制性定语从句与 as 引导的定语从句", "structure": "主语 the Nobel Foundation's limit... 后接“不定代词 + of + 关系代词”构成的定语从句 each of whom must still be living；破折号后为 as 引导的非限制性定语从句，其中包含 who 引导的宾语从句及 when it comes to... 时间状语从句。", "zh": "然而，诺贝尔基金会对每个奖项最多三名在世获奖者的限制，早已落后于现代科研的协作本质——这一点从确认希格斯玻色子发现时因谁被忽略而必然引发的争吵中便可见一斑。"}, {"en": "The Nobels were, of course, themselves set up by a very rich individual who had decided what he wanted to do with his own money.", "point": "被动语态中插入语分隔及定语从句嵌套宾语从句", "structure": "主干为被动语态 The Nobels were... set up by a very rich individual，插入语 of course 隔开助动词与过去分词；who 引导定语从句修饰 individual，其中包含 what 引导的宾语从句。", "zh": "当然，诺贝尔奖本身也是由一位极其富有的个人设立的，他当时只是决定用自己的钱做他想做的事。"}, {"en": "It is fair to criticize and question the mechanism - that is the culture of research, after all - but it is the prize-givers' money to do with as they please.", "point": "形式主语 It 句型与破折号插入语", "structure": "but 连接的并列句；前半句为形式主语结构 It is fair to do...，破折号内为插入语解释原因；后半句中不定式短语 to do with（省略逻辑宾语 money）作后置定语，as they please 为方式状语从句。", "zh": "批评和质疑其机制是合理的——毕竟这就是科研文化的一部分——但这终究是设奖者自己的钱，他们可以随心所欲地处置。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "lucrative（利润丰厚的、报酬高的）同义替换为 handsome（数量可观的、丰厚的）", "option": "a handsome reward for researchers", "original": "a string of lucrative awards for researchers"}, {"note": "self-promotion（自我宣传）表明最大受益方是奖项幕后的出资创立者（those behind them）", "option": "most benefit the founders of the new awards", "original": "an exercise in self-promotion for those behind them"}, {"note": "collaborative nature（协作本质）与 joint effort（共同努力）精准对应", "option": "the joint effort of modern researchers", "original": "the collaborative nature of modern research"}, {"note": "Time 与 endurance（持久度）对应，given them legitimacy 对应 done justice to them", "option": "Their endurance has done justice to them", "original": "Time, rather than intention, has given them legitimacy"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2014-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2014", "examSet": "2014 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2014 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "通识教育报告偏离本质与学术偏见", "subtitle": "评美国艺术与科学院人文社科报告对自由教育真实危机的回避", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 430, "paragraphs": ["\"The Heart of the Matter,\" the just-released report by the American Academy of Arts and Sciences (AAAS), deserves praise for affirming the importance of the humanities and social sciences to the prosperity and security of liberal democracy in America. Regrettably, however, the report's failure to address the true nature of the crisis facing liberal education may cause more harm than good. In 2010, leading congressional Democrats and Republicans sent letters to the AAAS asking that it identify actions that could be taken by \"federal, state and local governments, universities, foundations, educators, individual benefactors and others\" to \"maintain national excellence in humanities and social scientific scholarship and education.\" In response, the American Academy formed the Commission on the Humanities and Social Sciences. Among the commission's 51 members are top-tier-university presidents, scholars, lawyers, judges, and business executives, as well as prominent figures from diplomacy, filmmaking, music and journalism. The goals identified in the report are generally admirable. Because representative government presupposes an informed citizenry, the report supports full literacy; stresses the study of history and government, particularly American history and American government; and encourages the use of new digital technologies. To encourage innovation and competition, the report calls for increased investment in research, the crafting of coherent curricula that improve students' ability to solve problems and communicate effectively in the 21st century, increased funding for teachers and the encouragement of scholars to bring their learning to bear on the great challenges of the day. The report also advocates greater study of foreign languages, international affairs and the expansion of study abroad programs. Unfortunately, despite 2½ years in the making, \"The Heart of the Matter\" never gets to the heart of the matter: the illiberal nature of liberal education at our leading colleges and universities. The commission ignores that for several decades America's colleges and universities have produced graduates who don't know the content and character of liberal education and are thus deprived of its benefits. Sadly, the spirit of inquiry once at home on campus has been replaced by the use of the humanities and social sciences as vehicles for publicizing \"progressive,\" or left liberal propaganda.", "Today, professors routinely treat the progressive interpretation of history and progressive public policy as the proper subject of study while portraying conservative or classical liberal ideas - such as free markets and self-reliance - as falling outside the boundaries of routine, and sometimes legitimate, intellectual investigation. The AAAS displays great enthusiasm for liberal education. Yet its report may well set back reform by obscuring the depth and breadth of the challenge that Congress asked it to illuminate."], "translations": ["美国艺术与科学院（AAAS）刚刚发布的报告《核心问题》肯定了人文和社会科学对美国自由民主繁荣与安全的重要性，这一点值得赞扬。然而令人遗憾的是，该报告未能触及自由教育所面临危机的真正本质，这可能会弊大于利。2010年，美国国会两党的重要议员致信AAAS，要求其明确“联邦、州及地方政府、大学、基金会、教育工作者、个人资助者及其他各方”可采取的行动，以“保持美国在人文与社会科学学术研究和教育领域的国家卓越地位”。作为回应，美国艺术与科学院成立了人文与社会科学委员会。该委员会的51名成员中包括顶尖大学校长、学者、律师、法官和企业高管，以及外交界、电影界、音乐界和新闻界的知名人士。报告确定的目标总体上令人钦佩。鉴于代议制政府以有识公民为前提，该报告支持全面普及读写能力；强调对历史和政治学的研究，尤其是美国历史和美国政治；并鼓励使用新的数字技术。为鼓励创新与竞争，报告呼吁增加研究投资，制定连贯的课程体系以提高学生在21世纪解决问题的能力和有效沟通的能力，增加对教师的资助，并鼓励学者将其所学运用于应对当今时代的重大挑战。报告还倡导加强对外语和国际事务的研究，并扩大海外留学项目。不幸的是，尽管耗时两年半才完成，《核心问题》却始终未触及问题的核心：我国顶尖高校中自由教育的“非自由化”本质。该委员会忽视了这样一个事实：几十年来，美国的高校培养出的毕业生并不了解自由教育的内涵与品格，因而被剥夺了从中获益的机会。可悲的是，曾经在校园里蔚然成风的探索精神，如今已被利用人文和社会科学作为宣传“进步主义”或左翼自由派舆论的工具所取代。", "如今，教授们习以为常地将对历史的进步主义解读以及进步主义公共政策视为正当的研究课题，同时却把自由市场和自力更生等保守派或古典自由主义思想描绘成超出常规——有时甚至超出合法——学术探究边界之外的内容。AAAS对自由教育表现出了极大的热情。然而，其报告却因掩盖了国会要求其阐明之挑战的深度和广度，很可能会阻碍改革的推进。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "态度题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 1, what is the author's attitude toward the AAAS's report?", "options": ["Critical.", "Appreciative.", "Contemptuous.", "Tolerant."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Regrettably, however, the report's failure to address the true nature of the crisis facing liberal education may cause more harm than good.", "explanation": "第1段首句先肯定AAAS报告的价值，但第二句紧接着用Regrettably, however转折，指出该报告未能触及自由教育危机的本质，可能“弊大于利”（cause more harm than good）。下文又用Unfortunately、never gets to the heart of the matter和Sadly进一步批判。可见作者整体持批判态度，对应A项Critical。", "trapNote": "B项（赞赏的）只看到首句的deserves praise和后文的admirable，忽略了however后的核心批判；D项（宽容的）与作者尖锐指责不符。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Influential figures in the Congress required that the AAAS report on how to", "options": ["define the government's role in education.", "safeguard individuals' rights to education.", "retain people's interest in liberal education.", "keep a leading position in liberal education."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "In 2010, leading congressional Democrats and Republicans sent letters to the AAAS asking that it identify actions that could be taken by \"federal, state and local governments, universities, foundations, educators, individual benefactors and others\" to \"maintain national excellence in humanities and social scientific scholarship and education.\"", "explanation": "定位至第1段第3句。2010年国会两党重要人物致信AAAS，要求其明确各方可采取的行动，以“维持美国在人文与社会科学学术及教育方面的国家卓越地位”（maintain national excellence...）。D项keep a leading position in liberal education精准同义替换了maintain national excellence，故选D。", "trapNote": "A项将信中“各级政府应采取的行动”偷换为“界定政府在教育中的角色”；C项“保持人们对自由教育的兴趣”属于无中生有，原文强调的是卓越地位而非兴趣。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 3, the report suggests", "options": ["an exclusive study of American history.", "a greater emphasis on theoretical subjects.", "the application of emerging technologies.", "funding for the study of foreign languages."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Because representative government presupposes an informed citizenry, the report supports full literacy; stresses the study of history and government, particularly American history and American government; and encourages the use of new digital technologies.", "explanation": "题目对应第1段中段关于报告目标的论述（原卷第3段内容）。原文指出报告“鼓励使用新的数字技术”（encourages the use of new digital technologies），C项the application of emerging technologies中application对应use，emerging technologies对应new digital technologies，为原词同义复现，故正确。", "trapNote": "A项exclusive（排他的）属绝对化偷换，原文是“尤其（particularly）强调美国历史”，并非唯一；D项把“加大对教师的资助”张冠李戴为“资助外语学习”。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "The author implies in Paragraph 5 that professors are", "options": ["supportive of free markets.", "conservative about public policy.", "biased against classical liberal ideas.", "cautious about intellectual investigation."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Today, professors routinely treat the progressive interpretation of history and progressive public policy as the proper subject of study while portraying conservative or classical liberal ideas - such as free markets and self-reliance - as falling outside the boundaries of routine, and sometimes legitimate, intellectual investigation.", "explanation": "定位至第2段第1句（原卷第5段内容）。作者指出，如今大学教授常把“进步主义”史观和公共政策视为正当研究对象，却将保守派或古典自由主义思想（如自由市场和自力更生）描绘成超出常规乃至合法学术探究边界之外的内容（falling outside the boundaries...）。由此可推知教授对古典自由主义思想抱有偏见，对应C项biased against。", "trapNote": "A项与原文完全相反，教授排斥free markets；B项将教授推崇的progressive public policy偷换为conservative，属于反向干扰。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the text?", "options": ["Ways to Grasp \"The Heart of the Matter\"", "Illiberal Education and \"The Heart of the Matter\"", "The AAAS's Contribution to Liberal Education", "Progressive Policy vs. Liberal Education"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Unfortunately, despite 2½ years in the making, \"The Heart of the Matter\" never gets to the heart of the matter: the illiberal nature of liberal education at our leading colleges and universities.", "explanation": "文章第1段点出AAAS报告虽提出诸多良好目标，却未能触及自由教育危机的真正本质——高校教育本身的“非自由化”（the illiberal nature of liberal education）；第2段进一步说明教授们用左翼进步派宣传取代学术探究，使报告反而阻碍改革。B项同时涵盖核心议题“非自由化教育”与报告书名，最契合主旨。", "trapNote": "A项“掌握‘核心问题’的方法”偏离批判主题；C项只停留在文章开头和结尾表面提到的AAAS贡献与热情，未能概括作者对“非自由化”教育现状的批判。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "（教育）自由开放的；通识的；自由派的", "note": "注意一词多义与反义词illiberal：文中liberal education指自由教育/通识教育，liberal democracy指自由民主，left liberal指左翼自由派，而illiberal则指“心胸狭隘的、不宽容的、非自由化的”。", "word": "liberal"}, {"gloss": "以……为前提；假定", "note": "由pre-（预先）+ suppose（假设）构成，常用于议论文逻辑起点推导，如文中representative government presupposes an informed citizenry。", "word": "presuppose"}, {"gloss": "工具，媒介，载体", "note": "熟词僻义：本义为“车辆”，在学术议论文中常引申为传播思想或观点的“载体/工具”（vehicles for publicizing...）。", "word": "vehicle"}, {"gloss": "使模糊，掩盖，遮蔽", "note": "作动词表示“掩盖事实真相或问题的严重性”，与下文要求“阐明（illuminate）”形成鲜明反义对比。", "word": "obscure"}, {"gloss": "阐明，照亮，启发", "note": "词根lumin（光）+ate，此处指国会要求报告“揭示、阐明”自由教育面临挑战的深度与广度。", "word": "illuminate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In 2010, leading congressional Democrats and Republicans sent letters to the AAAS asking that it identify actions that could be taken by \"federal, state and local governments, universities, foundations, educators, individual benefactors and others\" to \"maintain national excellence in humanities and social scientific scholarship and education.\"", "point": "多层嵌套结构分析：分词短语作伴随状语+ask虚拟语气宾语从句+关系代词that引导定语从句+不定式目的状语。", "structure": "主句为leading congressional Democrats and Republicans sent letters to the AAAS；现在分词短语asking that...作伴随状语，其中that引导宾语从句（ask后用动词原形identify表虚拟语气）；第二个that引导定语从句修饰actions；最后不定式短语to maintain...作目的状语。", "zh": "2010年，国会两党的资深参众议员致信美国艺术与科学院，要求其明确“联邦、州和地方政府、大学、基金会、教育工作者、个人资助者及其他各方”可采取的行动，以“保持美国在人文和社会科学学术研究及教育领域的国家卓越地位”。"}, {"en": "To encourage innovation and competition, the report calls for increased investment in research, the crafting of coherent curricula that improve students' ability to solve problems and communicate effectively in the 21st century, increased funding for teachers and the encouragement of scholars to bring their learning to bear on the great challenges of the day.", "point": "长并列宾语识别，以及短语bring sth. to bear on sth.（把……运用于/对……产生影响）的准确理解。", "structure": "句首不定式To encourage...作目的状语；主句calls for后接四个并列名词短语作宾语：increased investment..., the crafting of coherent curricula（后接that引导的定语从句）, increased funding..., 和the encouragement of scholars...（含不定式复合结构to bring their learning to bear on...）。", "zh": "为鼓励创新与竞争，该报告呼吁增加研究投入，制定连贯的课程体系以提升学生在21世纪解决问题的能力和有效沟通的能力，增加教师资助，并鼓励学者将其所学运用于应对当今时代的重大挑战。"}, {"en": "Today, professors routinely treat the progressive interpretation of history and progressive public policy as the proper subject of study while portraying conservative or classical liberal ideas - such as free markets and self-reliance - as falling outside the boundaries of routine, and sometimes legitimate, intellectual investigation.", "point": "while引导对比状语及两个并行搭配：treat A as B 与 portray A as B 的结构对称。", "structure": "主干为professors routinely treat...as the proper subject of study；while表对比，引导现在分词短语portraying...as falling outside...；双破折号之间的such as...为插入语，举例说明classical liberal ideas。", "zh": "如今，教授们习以为常地将对历史的进步主义解读以及进步主义公共政策视为正当的研究课题，同时却把自由市场、自力更生等保守派或古典自由主义思想描绘成超出常规、有时甚至超出合法学术探究边界之外的内容。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "题干keep a leading position（保持领先地位）同义替换原文maintain national excellence（维持国家卓越水平）。", "option": "keep a leading position in liberal education", "original": "maintain national excellence in humanities and social scientific scholarship and education"}, {"note": "application对应use，emerging technologies对应new digital technologies，属典型词性转换与近义改写。", "option": "the application of emerging technologies", "original": "encourages the use of new digital technologies"}, {"note": "将“把……描摹为超出常规乃至合法研究边界”提炼为对古典自由主义思想“抱有偏见（biased against）”。", "option": "biased against classical liberal ideas", "original": "portraying conservative or classical liberal ideas... as falling outside the boundaries of routine, and sometimes legitimate, intellectual investigation"}, {"note": "fail to address the true nature与cause more harm than good直接体现作者对报告的“批判（critical）”态度。", "option": "Critical.", "original": "failure to address the true nature of the crisis... may cause more harm than good"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2013-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2013", "examSet": "2013 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2013 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "快时尚产业的崛起与隐忧", "subtitle": "剖析快时尚对传统时尚周期的颠覆、环境劳工代价及消费反思", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 427, "paragraphs": ["In the 2006 film version of The Devil Wears Prada, Miranda Priestly, played by Meryl Streep, scolds her unattractive assistant for imagining that high fashion doesn't affect her. Priestly explains how the deep blue color of the assistant's sweater descended over the years from fashion shows to department stores and to the bargain bin in which the poor girl doubtless found her garment.", "This top-down conception of the fashion business couldn't be more out of date or at odds with the feverish world described in Overdressed, Elizabeth Cline's three-year indictment of \"fast fashion\". In the last decade or so, advances in technology have allowed mass-market labels such as Zara, H&M, and Uniqlo to react to trends more quickly and anticipate demand more precisely. Quicker turnarounds mean less wasted inventory, more frequent releases, and more profit. These labels encourage style-conscious consumers to see clothes as disposable - meant to last only a wash or two, although they don't advertise that - and to renew their wardrobe every few weeks. By offering on-trend items at dirt-cheap prices, Cline argues, these brands have hijacked fashion cycles, shaking an industry long accustomed to a seasonal pace. The victims of this revolution, of course, are not limited to designers. For H&M to offer a $5.95 knit miniskirt in all its 2,300-plus stores around the world, it must rely on low-wage overseas labor, order in volumes that strain natural resources, and use massive amounts of harmful chemicals.", "Overdressed is the fashion world's answer to consumer-activist bestsellers like Michael Pollan's The Omnivore's Dilemma. \"Mass-produced clothing, like fast food, fills a hunger and need, yet is non-durable and wasteful,\" Cline argues. Americans, she finds, buy roughly 20 billion garments a year - about 64 items per person - and no matter how much they give away, this excess leads to waste.", "Towards the end of Overdressed, Cline introduced her ideal, a Brooklyn woman named Sarah Kate Beaumont, who since 2008 has made all of her own clothes - and beautifully. But as Cline is the first to note, it took Beaumont decades to perfect her craft; her example can't be knocked off.", "Though several fast-fashion companies have made efforts to curb their impact on labor and the environment - including H&M, with its green Conscious Collection line - Cline believes lasting change can only be effected by the customer. She exhibits the idealism common to many advocates of sustainability, be it in food or in energy. Vanity is a constant; people will only start shopping more sustainably when they can't afford not to."], "translations": ["在2006年电影版《穿普拉达的女王》中，梅丽尔·斯特里普饰演的米兰达·普里斯特利训斥她那位毫无魅力的助理，因为对方竟以为高端时尚不会影响到自己。普里斯特利解释说，助理身上那件毛衣的深蓝色，是如何历经多年，从时装秀场流转到百货商店，最终落入这个可怜女孩无疑淘到这件衣服的特价清仓箱里的。", "这种自上而下的时尚业观念，与伊丽莎白·克莱恩耗时三年撰写的批判“快时尚”之作《过度着装》中所描绘的狂热世界可谓大相径庭、彻底过时。大约在过去十年间，技术的进步让Zara、H&M和优衣库等大众市场品牌能够更迅速地对潮流做出反应，并更精准地预测需求。更快的周转意味着更少的库存积压、更频繁的新品发布以及更高的利润。这些品牌鼓励注重时尚的消费者把衣服看作一次性用品——只经得起洗一两次，尽管它们不会公开宣传这一点——并每隔几周就更新一次衣橱。克莱恩认为，通过以极低的价格提供紧跟潮流的单品，这些品牌劫持了时尚周期，动摇了一个长期习惯于按季节更替节奏运转的行业。当然，这场变革的受害者并不仅限于设计师。H&M要在其全球2300多家门店同时供应一条售价5.95美元的针织迷你裙，就必须依赖低薪的海外劳动力，以给自然资源造成重负的体量下订单，并使用大量有害化学物质。", "《过度着装》是时尚界对迈克尔·波伦的《杂食者的两难》等消费者维权畅销书的回应。“大规模生产的服装就像快餐一样，能满足一时的饥渴与需求，但却不耐穿且造成浪费，”克莱恩指出。她发现，美国人每年大约购买200亿件衣物——人均约64件——而且无论他们捐出多少，这种过度消费最终都会导致浪费。", "在《过度着装》一书接近尾声时，克莱恩介绍了她的理想典范——一位名叫萨拉·凯特·博蒙特的布鲁克林女性，她自2008年以来一直自己亲手制作所有衣物，而且做工精美。但正如克莱恩自己率先指出的那样，博蒙特花费了数十年才将这门手艺打磨至臻；她的榜样无法被轻易复制。", "尽管包括H&M推出绿色环保“自觉行动”系列在内的多家快时尚公司已做出努力，试图遏制自身对劳工和环境的影响，但克莱恩认为，持久的改变只能由消费者来实现。她身上流露出许多可持续发展倡导者共有的理想主义，无论是在食品领域还是能源领域皆然。虚荣心是永恒的人性；人们只有在不这么做就负担不起的时候，才会开始以更可持续的方式购物。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Priestly criticizes her assistant for her", "options": ["insensitivity to fashion.", "obsession with high fashion.", "poor bargaining skill.", "lack of imagination."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "In the 2006 film version of The Devil Wears Prada, Miranda Priestly, played by Meryl Streep, scolds her unattractive assistant for imagining that high fashion doesn't affect her.", "explanation": "定位第一段第一句。普里斯特利训斥（scolds，对应题干criticizes）她的助理，是因为助理以为高端时尚与自己无关（imagining that high fashion doesn't affect her），随后普里斯特利解释连助理特价淘来的深蓝毛衣颜色都源自高端秀场。可见助理对时尚潮流的传导毫无察觉，即对时尚缺乏敏感度，对应A项insensitivity to fashion。", "trapNote": "C项利用文中bargain bin（特价清仓箱）进行字面词汇干扰，并非批评砍价能力差；D项利用imagining一词偷换概念，把“误以为不受影响”歪曲为“缺乏想象力”。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Cline, mass-market labels urge consumers to", "options": ["combat unnecessary waste.", "shop for their garments more frequently.", "resist the influence of advertisements.", "shut out the feverish fashion world."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "These labels encourage style-conscious consumers to see clothes as disposable - meant to last only a wash or two, although they don't advertise that - and to renew their wardrobe every few weeks.", "explanation": "定位第二段第四句。题干中的mass-market labels urge consumers to对应原文These labels encourage style-conscious consumers to...。原文明确指出这些品牌鼓励消费者把衣服视为一次性用品，并且每隔几周就更新一次衣橱（renew their wardrobe every few weeks），即促使消费者更频繁地购买衣物，这与B项shop for their garments more frequently完全吻合。", "trapNote": "A项“对抗不必要浪费”与快时尚品牌诱导消费、加剧浪费的做法正好相反；C项利用although they don't advertise that作词汇拼凑，原文只是说品牌不会宣传衣服不耐洗，并非呼吁抵制广告。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The word \"indictment\" (Line 3, Para.2) is closest in meaning to", "options": ["tolerance.", "indifference.", "enthusiasm.", "accusation."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "This top-down conception of the fashion business couldn't be more out of date or at odds with the feverish world described in Overdressed, Elizabeth Cline's three-year indictment of \"fast fashion\".", "explanation": "定位第二段第一句中的indictment一词。其后内容揭露快时尚品牌鼓动一次性消费、劫持时尚周期，并指出其依赖低薪海外劳工、耗费自然资源及使用大量有害化学物质；第三段还将其比作消费者维权畅销书，批评大众服饰不耐穿且造成浪费。由此可见该书是对快时尚的强烈批判与控诉，故indictment意为“控告、指责”，与D项accusation（指控、谴责）同义。", "trapNote": "A项“容忍”、B项“冷漠”和C项“热情”均与下文Cline对快时尚负面代价的尖锐揭露完全背离，属于情感色彩明显相反的干扰项，可通过上下文正负态度迅速排除。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from the last paragraph?", "options": ["Vanity has more often been found in idealists.", "The fast-fashion industry ignores sustainability.", "Pricing is vital to environment-friendly purchasing.", "People are more interested in unaffordable garments."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Vanity is a constant; people will only start shopping more sustainably when they can't afford not to.", "explanation": "定位最后一段末句。作者在评价克莱恩对消费者的理想主义期待后指出，虚荣心是永恒的人性，人们只有在不这么做就负担不起的时候（when they can't afford not to），才会开始以更可持续的方式购物。换言之，只有当不环保消费的价格代价高到难以承受时，人们才会转向环保购物，由此可推知价格因素对环保购买行为至关重要，对应C项。", "trapNote": "B项以偏概全，末段首句明确提到多家快时尚公司已采取措施（如H&M推出绿色系列）减少影响，并非完全忽视；D项曲解can't afford not to的双重否定，误读为人们偏爱买不起的衣服。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "What is the subject of the text?", "options": ["Satire on an extravagant lifestyle.", "Challenge to a high-fashion myth.", "Criticism of the fast-fashion industry.", "Exposure of a mass-market secret."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "This top-down conception of the fashion business couldn't be more out of date or at odds with the feverish world described in Overdressed, Elizabeth Cline's three-year indictment of \"fast fashion\".", "explanation": "纵观全文，第一段以电影《穿普拉达的女王》引出传统的时尚传播观念，第二段随即指出该观念已过时，并借《过度着装》一书展开全文核心——批判快时尚产业在劳工剥削、资源消耗和化学污染方面的恶果；第三、四段分析快时尚引发的过度消费浪费及手工替代的局限性；第五段探讨解决之道。全篇紧扣对快时尚产业的批判与反思，故C项最能概括主题。", "trapNote": "A项“讽刺奢靡生活方式”无中生有，快时尚主打廉价而非奢靡；B项仅概括第一、二段引出话题的高端时尚旧观念，属于局部细节充当主旨。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 控告，起诉书；强烈谴责", "note": "第二段指《过度着装》一书是对快时尚产业历时三年的深刻批判与控诉", "word": "indictment"}, {"gloss": "adj. 一次性的，用完即弃的", "note": "第二段指快时尚品牌诱导消费者将衣物视为只洗一两次即可丢弃的消耗品", "word": "disposable"}, {"gloss": "v. 劫持，强行控制，篡改", "note": "第二段have hijacked fashion cycles生动形容快时尚打破并主导了传统换季节奏", "word": "hijack"}, {"gloss": "phr. 仿制，抄袭，轻易复制", "note": "第四段can't be knocked off一语双关，既指服装界的“山寨仿制”，也指她的手艺无法轻易复制", "word": "knock off"}, {"gloss": "v. 控制，抑制，约束", "note": "第五段curb their impact指快时尚企业试图减少自身对劳工和环境的不良影响", "word": "curb"}, {"gloss": "v. 使产生，实现，促成", "note": "第五段熟词僻义作动词，can only be effected by the customer意为“只能由消费者促成”", "word": "effect"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "These labels encourage style-conscious consumers to see clothes as disposable - meant to last only a wash or two, although they don't advertise that - and to renew their wardrobe every few weeks.", "point": "encourage sb. to see... and to renew...构成并列不定式宾补结构；中间破折号插入过去分词短语meant to...补充说明一次性用品的质量真相。", "structure": "主句(These labels encourage consumers to see... and to renew...) + 插入破折号补充说明disposable(meant to last..., 含although让步状语从句)", "zh": "这些品牌鼓励注重时尚的消费者把衣服看作一次性用品——只经得起洗一两次，尽管它们不会公开宣传这一点——并每隔几周就更新一次衣橱。"}, {"en": "For H&M to offer a $5.95 knit miniskirt in all its 2,300-plus stores around the world, it must rely on low-wage overseas labor, order in volumes that strain natural resources, and use massive amounts of harmful chemicals.", "point": "句首For H&M to offer...作目的状语，引出低价快时尚背后的三重代价；rely on、order、use三者并列构成谓语，揭示廉价背后的严峻成本。", "structure": "For...to...不定式复合结构作目的状语 + 主句(it must rely on..., order..., and use...三个并列谓语，含that定语从句修饰volumes)", "zh": "H&M要在其全球2300多家门店同时供应一条售价5.95美元的针织迷你裙，就必须依赖低薪的海外劳动力，以给自然资源造成重负的体量下订单，并使用大量有害化学物质。"}, {"en": "Though several fast-fashion companies have made efforts to curb their impact on labor and the environment - including H&M, with its green Conscious Collection line - Cline believes lasting change can only be effected by the customer.", "point": "though让步从句承认行业已做出的局部改善，转而突出主句的核心观点；注意effect在此作动词，意为“实现，促成”。", "structure": "Though引导的让步状语从句(含破折号举例补充) + 主句(Cline believes + 省略that的宾语从句)", "zh": "尽管包括H&M推出绿色环保“自觉行动”系列在内的多家快时尚公司已做出努力，试图遏制自身对劳工和环境的影响，但克莱恩认为，持久的改变只能由消费者来实现。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "误以为高端时尚与己无关，体现出对时尚影响的迟钝与不敏感", "option": "insensitivity to fashion", "original": "imagining that high fashion doesn't affect her"}, {"note": "“每隔几周更新衣橱”直接同义转述为“更频繁地购买衣物”", "option": "shop for their garments more frequently", "original": "renew their wardrobe every few weeks"}, {"note": "由后文对低薪劳工、资源和污染的揭露可知indictment意为“控诉、指责”", "option": "accusation", "original": "indictment of \"fast fashion\""}, {"note": "“负担不起不环保的代价才会环保购物”推断出定价对环保消费至关重要", "option": "Pricing is vital to environment-friendly purchasing", "original": "when they can't afford not to"}, {"note": "全篇围绕快时尚的负面社会、劳工及环境后果展开批判", "option": "Criticism of the fast-fashion industry", "original": "hijacked fashion cycles... low-wage overseas labor... excess leads to waste"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2013-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2013", "examSet": "2013 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2013 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "微软默认“禁止追踪”引发广告争议", "subtitle": "网络行为定向广告与浏览器默认隐私设置之争", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 431, "paragraphs": ["An old saying has it that half of all advertising budgets are wasted - the trouble is, no one knows which half. In the internet age, at least in theory, this fraction can be much reduced. By watching what people search for, click on and say online, companies can aim \"behavioural\" ads at those most likely to buy.", "In the past couple of weeks a quarrel has illustrated the value to advertisers of such fine-grained information: Should advertisers assume that people are happy to be tracked and sent behavioural ads? Or should they have explicit permission? In December 2010 America's Federal Trade Commission (FTC) proposed adding a \"do not track\" (DNT) option to internet browsers, so that users could tell advertisers that they did not want to be followed. Microsoft's Internet Explorer and Apple's Safari both offer DNT; Google's Chrome is due to do so this year. In February the FTC and the Digital Advertising Alliance (DAA) agreed that the industry would get cracking on responding to DNT requests.", "On May 31st Microsoft set off the row. It said that Internet Explorer 10, the version due to appear with Windows 8, would have DNT as a default. Advertisers are horrified. Human nature being what it is, most people stick with default settings. Few switch DNT on now, but if tracking is off it will stay off. Bob Liodice, the chief executive of the Association of National Advertisers, says consumers will be worse off if the industry cannot collect information about their preferences. People will not get fewer ads, he says. \"They'll get less meaningful, less targeted ads.\"", "It is not yet clear how advertisers will respond. Getting a DNT signal does not oblige anyone to stop tracking, although some companies have promised to do so. Unable to tell whether someone really objects to behavioural ads or whether they are sticking with Microsoft's default, some may ignore a DNT signal and press on anyway.", "Also unclear is why Microsoft has gone it alone. After all, it has an ad business too, which it says will comply with DNT requests, though it is still working out how. If it is trying to upset Google, which relies almost wholly on advertising, it has chosen an indirect method: there is no guarantee that DNT by default will become the norm. DNT does not seem an obviously huge selling point for windows 8 - though the firm has compared some of its other products favourably with Google's on that count before. Brendon Lynch, Microsoft's chief privacy officer, blogged: \"We believe consumers should have more control.\" Could it really be that simple?"], "translations": ["俗话说，广告预算有一半都打了水漂——问题在于，没人知道到底是哪一半。在互联网时代，至少在理论上，这一浪费比例可以大幅降低。通过观察人们在网上的搜索、点击和言论内容，企业能够向最有可能购买商品的人群精准投放“行为定向”广告。", "最近几周的一场争论凸显了这种精细化信息对广告商的价值：广告商是否应该假定人们乐意被追踪并接收行为定向广告？还是必须征得用户的明确同意？2010年12月，美国联邦贸易委员会（FTC）提议在网络浏览器中增加“禁止追踪”（DNT）选项，以便用户告知广告商自己不愿被追踪。微软的 Internet Explorer 和苹果的 Safari 均已提供 DNT 功能，谷歌的 Chrome 浏览器也将于今年推出该功能。今年2月，联邦贸易委员会与数字广告联盟（DAA）达成协议，行业将着手积极响应用户的 DNT 请求。", "5月31日，微软引发了这场风波。该公司宣布，随 Windows 8 一同推出的 Internet Explorer 10 将把 DNT 设为默认选项。广告商对此大为震惊。人之常情大抵如此，大多数用户都会沿用默认设置。如今很少有人主动开启 DNT，但如果默认关闭追踪，它就会一直保持关闭状态。全美广告商协会首席执行官鲍勃·利奥迪斯表示，如果行业无法收集用户的偏好信息，消费者的处境反而会更糟。他说，人们并不会因此少看广告，“他们只会收到更无意义、针对性更差的广告。”", "目前尚不清楚广告商将如何应对。收到 DNT 信号并不意味着任何一方有义务停止追踪，尽管一些公司已承诺会这样做。由于无法判断用户是真正反对行为定向广告，还是仅仅沿用了微软的默认设置，部分广告商可能会无视 DNT 信号并继续照常追踪。", "同样不清楚的是微软为何要独自采取这一行动。毕竟，微软自己也有广告业务；该公司表示其广告业务将遵守 DNT 请求，但目前仍在研究具体如何落实。如果微软此举意在给几乎完全依赖广告的谷歌添堵，那它选择的手段也颇为迂回：目前并不能保证默认开启 DNT 会成为行业常态。DNT 似乎也不算 Windows 8 的显著卖点——尽管微软此前确实曾在这方面将自家其他产品与谷歌产品作过有利对比。微软首席隐私官布伦登·林奇在博客中写道：“我们认为消费者应当拥有更多控制权。”事情真的会如此简单吗？"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It is suggested in Paragraph 1 that \"behavioural\" ads help advertisers to", "options": ["provide better online services.", "ease competition among themselves.", "avoid complaints from consumers.", "lower their operational costs."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "In the internet age, at least in theory, this fraction can be much reduced. By watching what people search for, click on and say online, companies can aim \"behavioural\" ads at those most likely to buy.", "explanation": "定位第1段。段首提到传统广告预算有一半被浪费（half of all advertising budgets are wasted），随后指出在互联网时代这一比例（this fraction）至少在理论上能大幅降低，企业通过追踪用户在线搜索、点击和言论，可将“行为定向”广告精准投向最可能购买的人群。减少广告预算浪费即降低了企业投放广告的运营成本，与D项“lower their operational costs”构成同义改写。", "trapNote": "A项“提供更好的在线服务”与C项“避免消费者投诉”在第一段均无依据，属于无中生有；B项“缓和同行竞争”原文未提及公司间的竞争关系。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "词义题", "stem": "\"the industry\" (Line 5, Para.3) refers to", "options": ["internet browser developers.", "digital information analysts.", "e-commerce conductors.", "online advertisers."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Microsoft's Internet Explorer and Apple's Safari both offer DNT; Google's Chrome is due to do so this year. In February the FTC and the Digital Advertising Alliance (DAA) agreed that the industry would get cracking on responding to DNT requests.", "explanation": "定位第2段末尾（对应原卷第3段第5行）。前文指出美国联邦贸易委员会（FTC）提议在网络浏览器中增加DNT选项，紧接着列举微软IE、苹果Safari均已提供DNT，谷歌Chrome也将于今年跟进；末句随后指出FTC与数字广告联盟达成协议，该行业将着手响应DNT请求。结合紧邻列举的IE、Safari和Chrome，官方解析将其指代锁定为A项“网络浏览器开发商”。", "trapNote": "D项“在线广告商”极具干扰性，因末句出现了Digital Advertising Alliance，但紧接前句的主语是三大浏览器，按就近指代与官方答案应选A；B、C两项文中未提及。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Bob Liodice holds that setting DNT as a default", "options": ["may cut the number of junk ads.", "fails to affect the ad industry.", "will not benefit consumers.", "goes against human nature."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Bob Liodice, the chief executive of the Association of National Advertisers, says consumers will be worse off if the industry cannot collect information about their preferences. People will not get fewer ads, he says. \"They'll get less meaningful, less targeted ads.\"", "explanation": "定位第3段后半部分。Bob Liodice明确指出，如果广告行业无法收集用户偏好信息，消费者的处境会变得更糟（consumers will be worse off），他们收到的广告数量不会减少，反而会变成更无意义、针对性更差的广告。“consumers will be worse off”意为“对消费者不利”，与C项“will not benefit consumers”形成精准反义/同义转换，故C为正确答案。", "trapNote": "A项错把“less meaningful”偷换为“减少垃圾广告数量”，而原文明确说“will not get fewer ads”；D项“违背人性”与前文“大多数人沿用默认设置符合人性”的意思恰好相反。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Which of the following is true according to Paragraph 6?", "options": ["Advertisers are willing to implement DNT.", "DNT may not serve its intended purpose.", "DNT is losing its popularity among consumers.", "Advertisers are obliged to offer behavioural ads."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Getting a DNT signal does not oblige anyone to stop tracking, although some companies have promised to do so. Unable to tell whether someone really objects to behavioural ads or whether they are sticking with Microsoft's default, some may ignore a DNT signal and press on anyway.", "explanation": "定位第4段（对应原卷第6段）。段中指出，收到DNT信号并不强制任何广告商停止追踪，且由于无法分辨用户是真心拒绝行为广告还是仅仅沿用了微软默认设置，部分广告商可能会无视DNT信号继续照常追踪。由此可见，即便开启了DNT，也未必能真正阻止追踪，即B项“DNT可能无法达到其预期目的”。", "trapNote": "A项错在以偏概全，原文仅说“some companies”承诺停止追踪，但广告商总体震惊且部分会无视；D项将“not oblige anyone to stop tracking”反说成“有义务提供行为广告”。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author's attitude towards what Brendon Lynch said in his blog is one of", "options": ["indulgence.", "understanding.", "appreciation.", "skepticism."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Brendon Lynch, Microsoft's chief privacy officer, blogged: \"We believe consumers should have more control.\" Could it really be that simple?", "explanation": "定位第5段末尾。针对微软首席隐私官Brendon Lynch在博客中宣称“我们认为消费者应当拥有更多控制权”这一冠冕堂皇的理由，作者紧接着用反问句“Could it really be that simple?”（事情真的会如此简单吗？）作结。全段前文还在探讨微软此举是否意在打击谷歌的广告业务，因此该反问明确表达了作者对其说辞的质疑态度，对应D项“skepticism”。", "trapNote": "A项“纵容”、B项“理解”与C项“赞赏”均属于正面或偏宽容态度，忽略了篇末反问句“Could it really be that simple?”所流露出的明显怀疑与审视语气。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "精细化的，细粒度的", "note": "文中指广告商通过追踪用户点击与搜索获得的高度细化的个人偏好信息。", "word": "fine-grained"}, {"gloss": "默认设置，预设", "note": "固定搭配 as a default（作为默认设置）、stick with default settings（沿用默认设置）。", "word": "default"}, {"gloss": "迫使，使负有义务", "note": "句型 oblige sb. to do sth.（强制某人做某事），文中指收到DNT信号并不具有法律强制力。", "word": "oblige"}, {"gloss": "遵守，顺从", "note": "常与 with 连用，comply with DNT requests 表示“遵守禁止追踪请求”。", "word": "comply"}, {"gloss": "明确的，明示的", "note": "文中 explicit permission 指用户“明确表示的同意”，与假定同意相对。", "word": "explicit"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In December 2010 America's Federal Trade Commission (FTC) proposed adding a \"do not track\" (DNT) option to internet browsers, so that users could tell advertisers that they did not want to be followed.", "point": "propose doing sth.（提议做某事）；so that引导目的状语从句；tell sb. that...结构及被动不定式to be followed。", "structure": "主句(America's FTC proposed adding...) + 目的状语从句(so that users could tell advertisers...) + 宾语从句(that they did not want to be followed)", "zh": "2010年12月，美国联邦贸易委员会（FTC）提议在网络浏览器中增加“禁止追踪”（DNT）选项，以便用户告知广告商自己不愿被追踪。"}, {"en": "Unable to tell whether someone really objects to behavioural ads or whether they are sticking with Microsoft's default, some may ignore a DNT signal and press on anyway.", "point": "形容词短语Unable to tell...前置作原因状语；whether...or whether...引导并列宾语从句；stick with（坚持/沿用）与press on（继续进行）。", "structure": "形容词短语作原因状语(Unable to tell whether... or whether...) + 主句(some may ignore... and press on anyway)", "zh": "由于无法判断用户是真正反对行为定向广告，还是仅仅沿用了微软的默认设置，部分广告商可能会无视DNT信号并继续照常追踪。"}, {"en": "If it is trying to upset Google, which relies almost wholly on advertising, it has chosen an indirect method: there is no guarantee that DNT by default will become the norm.", "point": "which引导非限制性定语从句修饰Google；冒号后的句子解释indirect method；that引导同位语从句说明guarantee的具体内容。", "structure": "条件状语从句(If it is trying to upset Google, + 非限制性定语从句which...) + 主句(it has chosen an indirect method) + 冒号解释同位语从句(there is no guarantee that...)", "zh": "如果微软此举意在给几乎完全依赖广告的谷歌添堵，那它选择的手段也颇为迂回：目前并不能保证默认开启DNT会成为行业常态。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "减少广告预算的浪费即降低企业的广告运营成本。", "option": "lower their operational costs", "original": "half of all advertising budgets are wasted ... this fraction can be much reduced"}, {"note": "worse off（处境更糟）同义转化为will not benefit（不会使……受益）。", "option": "will not benefit consumers", "original": "consumers will be worse off"}, {"note": "广告商无视DNT信号继续追踪，说明DNT可能无法实现预期保护隐私的目的。", "option": "DNT may not serve its intended purpose", "original": "some may ignore a DNT signal and press on anyway"}, {"note": "反问句“事情真有那么简单吗”体现作者对微软官方说辞的怀疑（skepticism）。", "option": "skepticism", "original": "Could it really be that simple?"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2013-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2013", "examSet": "2013 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2013 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "长远视角下的人类光明前景", "subtitle": "从长尺度与历史规律看待人类的生存与未来", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 420, "paragraphs": ["Up until a few decades ago, our visions of the future were largely - though by no means uniformly - glowingly positive. Science and technology would cure all the ills of humanity, leading to lives of fulfilment and opportunity for all. Now utopia has grown unfashionable, as we have gained a deeper appreciation of the range of threats facing us, from asteroid strike to epidemic flu and to climate change. You might even be tempted to assume that humanity has little future to look forward to.", "But such gloominess is misplaced. The fossil record shows that many species have endured for millions of years - so why shouldn't we? Take a broader look at our species' place in the universe, and it becomes clear that we have an excellent chance of surviving for tens, if not hundreds, of thousands of years. Look up Homo sapiens in the \"Red List\" of threatened species of the International Union for the Conservation of Nature (IUCN) and you will read: \"Listed as Least Concern as the species is very widely distributed, adaptable, currently increasing, and there are no major threats resulting in an overall population decline.\"", "So what does our deep future hold? A growing number of researchers and organisations are now thinking seriously about that question. For example, the Long Now Foundation has as its flagship project a mechanical clock that is designed to still be marking time thousands of years hence.", "Perhaps willfully, it may be easier to think about such lengthy timescales than about the more immediate future. The potential evolution of today's technology, and its social consequences, is dazzlingly complicated, and it's perhaps best left to science fiction writers and futurologists to explore the many possibilities we can envisage. That's one reason why we have launched Arc, a new publication dedicated to the near future.", "But take a longer view and there is a surprising amount that we can say with considerable assurance. As so often, the past holds the key to the future: we have now identified enough of the long-term patterns shaping the history of the planet, and our species, to make evidence-based forecasts about the situations in which our descendants will find themselves.", "This long perspective makes the pessimistic view of our prospects seem more likely to be a passing fad. To be sure, the future is not all rosy. But we are now knowledgeable enough to reduce many of the risks that threatened the existence of earlier humans, and to improve the lot of those to come."], "translations": ["直到几十年前，我们对未来的展望在很大程度上——尽管绝非毫无例外——都洋溢着乐观色彩。人们曾认为科学技术将治愈人类的一切痼疾，为所有人带来充实且充满机遇的生活。如今，乌托邦式的愿景已不再流行，因为我们对自身面临的种种威胁有了更深刻的认识，从小行星撞击、流行性感冒到气候变化皆在其列。你甚至可能会忍不住认为，人类几乎没有什么未来可言。", "但这种悲观情绪其实找错了方向。化石记录表明，许多物种都已存续了数百万年——那我们又何尝不能呢？从更宏大的视角审视人类在宇宙中的位置，就会清楚地看到，我们极有可能存续数万年，甚至数十万年。在世界自然保护联盟（IUCN）的濒危物种“红色名录”中查阅“智人”（Homo sapiens），你会读到这样的描述：“被列为无危物种，因为该物种分布极其广泛、适应力强、目前数量仍在增长，且不存在导致总体种群数量下降的重大威胁。”", "那么，人类遥远的未来究竟会怎样？越来越多的研究人员和机构如今正严肃思考这一问题。例如，“今日长存基金会”（Long Now Foundation）的旗舰项目便是一座机械钟，它被设计成在数千年后依然能够精准走时。", "或许是出于主观意愿，思考如此漫长的时间尺度，反而比设想更为迫近的未来要容易些。当今技术的潜在演变及其社会后果令人眼花缭乱地复杂，探索我们所能设想的种种可能性，或许最好留给科幻作家和未来学家。这正是我们创办专注于近未来领域的新刊物《Arc》的原因之一。", "但若将眼光放长远，我们其实能以相当大的把握断言许多事情，这着实令人惊讶。正如以往屡次印证的那样，过去掌握着通往未来的钥匙：我们已经识别出足够多塑造地球和人类历史的长期规律，从而能够基于证据，对后代将要置身的处境作出预测。", "这种长远的视角使得对人类前景的悲观论调看起来更像是一时的风尚。诚然，未来并非一片美好。但我们如今已具备足够的知识，能够降低诸多曾威胁早期人类生存的风险，并改善后世人类的境遇。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Our vision of the future used to be inspired by", "options": ["our desire for lives of fulfillment.", "our faith in science and technology.", "our awareness of potential risks.", "our belief in equal opportunity."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Up until a few decades ago, our visions of the future were largely - though by no means uniformly - glowingly positive. Science and technology would cure all the ills of humanity, leading to lives of fulfilment and opportunity for all.", "explanation": "定位第1段前两句。文中指出，直到几十年前，人们对未来的展望在很大程度上都无比乐观，其原因紧接着在第二句点明：人们相信科学技术将治愈人类的一切痼疾，从而带来充实而充满机遇的生活。可见过去乐观的未来愿景源自对科技力量的信赖，对应B项“our faith in science and technology”。", "trapNote": "A项“对充实生活的渴望”与D项“对平等机会的信念”把“科学技术带来的结果”（leading to lives of fulfilment and opportunity for all）误当成了愿景的起因；C项是如今乌托邦不再流行的原因。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The IUCN's \"Red List\" suggests that human beings are", "options": ["a sustained species.", "the world's dominant power.", "a threat to the environment.", "a misplaced race."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Listed as Least Concern as the species is very widely distributed, adaptable, currently increasing, and there are no major threats resulting in an overall population decline.", "explanation": "定位第2段末尾对IUCN“红色名录”的引文。名录将智人列为“无危（Least Concern）”物种，理由是人类分布广泛、适应性强、数量仍在增长，且不存在导致总体种群数量下降的重大威胁。这说明人类能够长久存续下去，与A项“a sustained species（可持续存续的物种）”意思高度契合，故选A。", "trapNote": "B项“世界主宰力量”和C项“对环境的威胁”在IUCN名录引文中均未提及；D项“找错位置的种族”系偷换本段首句“such gloominess is misplaced（这种悲观找错了方向）”的用词。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is true according to Paragraph 5?", "options": ["The interest in science fiction is on the rise.", "Arc helps limit the scope of futurological studies.", "Technology offers solutions to social problems.", "Our immediate future is hard to conceive."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Perhaps willfully, it may be easier to think about such lengthy timescales than about the more immediate future. The potential evolution of today's technology, and its social consequences, is dazzlingly complicated, and it's perhaps best left to science fiction writers and futurologists to explore the many possibilities we can envisage.", "explanation": "定位第4段（对应原卷第5段）。段首指出，思考遥远的时间尺度或许比思考更为迫近的未来（the more immediate future）还要容易；接着解释原因：当今技术的潜在演变及其社会后果极其复杂（dazzlingly complicated），或许最好留给科幻作家和未来学家去探索。由此可知近未来很难构想预测，对应D项“Our immediate future is hard to conceive”。", "trapNote": "A项“科幻兴趣上升”属无中生有；B项与末句“创办专注于近未来的新刊物《Arc》”意思相悖，并非限制研究范围；C项把“技术的社会后果复杂”曲解为技术能解决社会问题。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "To ensure the future of mankind, it is crucial to", "options": ["adopt an optimistic view of the world.", "draw on our experience from the past.", "explore our planet's abundant resources.", "curb our ambition to reshape history."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "As so often, the past holds the key to the future: we have now identified enough of the long-term patterns shaping the history of the planet, and our species, to make evidence-based forecasts about the situations in which our descendants will find themselves.", "explanation": "定位第5段。段中明确指出“过去掌握着通往未来的钥匙（the past holds the key to the future）”，并进一步说明人类已经识别出诸多塑造地球及人类历史的长期规律，从而能对后代的处境做出有据可依的预测，再结合第6段降低早期人类面临过的风险，可知借鉴过往经验对保障人类未来至关重要，对应B项“draw on our experience from the past”。", "trapNote": "A项“采取乐观世界观”在文中并未作为保障未来的关键举措，第6段也指出未来并非一片美好；C项“开发丰富资源”和D项“遏制重塑历史的野心”均属无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the text?", "options": ["The Ever-bright Prospects of Mankind.", "Science, Technology and Humanity.", "Evolution of the Human Species.", "Uncertainty about Our Future."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "This long perspective makes the pessimistic view of our prospects seem more likely to be a passing fad. To be sure, the future is not all rosy. But we are now knowledgeable enough to reduce many of the risks that threatened the existence of earlier humans, and to improve the lot of those to come.", "explanation": "定位第6段并结合全文脉络。第1段引出当下对未来的悲观论调后，第2段立即以“But such gloominess is misplaced”转折，论证人类可长期存续；第3至5段从长远视角与历史规律论证未来可期；末段总结指出长远视角让悲观论更像一时风尚，人类已有足够知识降低风险并改善后代境遇。全文基调积极，故A项“人类光明的前景”最适合作标题。", "trapNote": "D项“未来的不确定性”与作者反驳悲观论、强调有依据预测长远未来的中心主旨相悖；B项“科技与人文”与C项“人类物种的进化”仅涵盖局部信息，片面且偏离中心。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "找错方向的，不合时宜的", "note": "文中形容gloominess（悲观情绪），表示这种悲观是没有道理、放错地方的。", "word": "misplaced"}, {"gloss": "存续，持久，忍受", "note": "文中指许多物种在地球上“存续、延续”了数百万年（have endured for millions of years）。", "word": "endure"}, {"gloss": "设想，想象，展望", "note": "常见考研高阶词，文中指“我们所能设想的种种可能性”（possibilities we can envisage）。", "word": "envisage"}, {"gloss": "把握，确信，保证", "note": "短语 with considerable assurance 表示“有相当大的把握”。", "word": "assurance"}, {"gloss": "一时的风尚，短暂的狂热", "note": "文中 a passing fad 指对人类前景的悲观论调不过是“昙花一现的流行看法”。", "word": "fad"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Now utopia has grown unfashionable, as we have gained a deeper appreciation of the range of threats facing us, from asteroid strike to epidemic flu and to climate change.", "point": "appreciation此处意为“认识，理解”；现在分词短语facing us作后置定语修饰threats；from...to...and to...列举具体威胁。", "structure": "主句(Now utopia has grown unfashionable) + 原因状语从句(as we have gained a deeper appreciation of... + 后置定语facing us + 举例介词短语from... to... and to...)", "zh": "如今，乌托邦式的愿景已不再流行，因为我们对自身面临的种种威胁有了更深刻的认识，从小行星撞击、流行性感冒到气候变化皆在其列。"}, {"en": "The potential evolution of today's technology, and its social consequences, is dazzlingly complicated, and it's perhaps best left to science fiction writers and futurologists to explore the many possibilities we can envisage.", "point": "it作形式主语替代不定式to explore...；leave sth. to sb. to do（把某事留给某人去做）；we can envisage作定语修饰possibilities。", "structure": "并列复合句：前分句(主语+系动词is+表语dazzlingly complicated) + and + 后分句(形式主语it + be left to sb. + 真正主语不定式to explore... + 省略that的定语从句we can envisage)", "zh": "当今技术的潜在演变及其社会后果令人眼花缭乱地复杂，探索我们所能设想的种种可能性，或许最好留给科幻作家和未来学家。"}, {"en": "we have now identified enough of the long-term patterns shaping the history of the planet, and our species, to make evidence-based forecasts about the situations in which our descendants will find themselves.", "point": "enough... to do sth.结构；shaping...作后置定语修饰patterns；in which引导定语从句修饰situations，对应find oneself in a situation。", "structure": "主句(we have now identified enough of the long-term patterns...) + 分词定语(shaping the history...) + 目的/结果不定式(to make evidence-based forecasts...) + 介词+关系代词定语从句(in which our descendants will find themselves)", "zh": "我们已经识别出足够多塑造地球和人类历史的长期规律，从而能够基于证据，对后代将要置身的处境作出预测。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "认为科技能治愈人类一切病痛，体现过去人们对科学技术的坚定信仰。", "option": "our faith in science and technology", "original": "Science and technology would cure all the ills of humanity"}, {"note": "分布广、适应强、数量增长且无重大衰退威胁，概括为能够长久存续的物种（sustained species）。", "option": "a sustained species", "original": "very widely distributed, adaptable, currently increasing, and there are no major threats resulting in an overall population decline"}, {"note": "思考近未来比漫长尺度更难且极其复杂，同义改写为近未来难以构想（hard to conceive）。", "option": "Our immediate future is hard to conceive", "original": "easier to think about such lengthy timescales than about the more immediate future ... dazzlingly complicated"}, {"note": "过去掌握通往未来的钥匙，即需借鉴过往经验与长期历史规律。", "option": "draw on our experience from the past", "original": "the past holds the key to the future"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2013-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2013", "examSet": "2013 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2013 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "亚利桑那移民法与联邦州权之争", "subtitle": "联邦最高法院界定移民执法中的联邦与州权限", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 412, "paragraphs": ["On a five to three vote, the Supreme Court knocked out much of Arizona's immigration law Monday - a modest policy victory for the Obama Administration. But on the more important matter of the Constitution, the decision was an 8-0 defeat for the Administration's effort to upset the balance of power between the federal government and the states.", "In Arizona v. United States, the majority overturned three of the four contested provisions of Arizona's controversial plan to have state and local police enforce federal immigration law. The Constitutional principles that Washington alone has the power to \"establish a uniform Rule of Naturalization\" and that federal laws precede state laws are noncontroversial. Arizona had attempted to fashion state policies that ran parallel to the existing federal ones.", "Justice Anthony Kennedy, joined by Chief Justice John Roberts and the Court's liberals, ruled that the state flew too close to the federal sun. On the overturned provisions the majority held Congress had deliberately \"occupied the field\" and Arizona had thus intruded on the federal's privileged powers.", "However, the Justices said that Arizona police would be allowed to verify the legal status of people who come in contact with law enforcement. That's because Congress has always envisioned joint federal-state immigration enforcement and explicitly encourages state officers to share information and cooperate with federal colleagues.", "Two of the three objecting Justices - Samuel Alito and Clarence Thomas - agreed with this Constitutional logic but disagreed about which Arizona rules conflicted with the federal statute. The only major objection came from Justice Antonin Scalia, who offered an even more robust defense of state privileges going back to the Alien and Sedition Acts.", "The 8-0 objection to President Obama turns on what Justice Samuel Alito describes in his objection as \"a shocking assertion of federal executive power\". The White House argued that Arizona's laws conflicted with its enforcement priorities, even if state laws complied with federal statutes to the letter. In effect, the White House claimed that it could invalidate any otherwise legitimate state law that it disagrees with.", "Some powers do belong exclusively to the federal government, and control of citizenship and the borders is among them. But if Congress wanted to prevent states from using their own resources to check immigration status, it could. It never did so. The Administration was in essence asserting that because it didn't want to carry out Congress's immigration wishes, no state should be allowed to do so either. Every Justice rightly rejected this remarkable claim."], "translations": ["周一，最高法院以五比三的投票结果废除了亚利桑那州移民法的大部分条款——这对奥巴马政府而言是一场温和的政策胜利。但在更为重要的宪法层面上，这一裁决却是行政当局试图打破联邦政府与各州之间权力平衡之举的八比零惨败。", "在“亚利桑那州诉合众国案”中，多数派大法官推翻了亚利桑那州这项备受争议的计划中四项受质疑条款中的三项，该计划旨在让州和地方警察执行联邦移民法。唯有华盛顿拥有“制定统一归化规则”的权力以及联邦法律优先于州法律这两项宪法原则是毫无争议的。亚利桑那州曾试图制定与现行联邦政策并行不悖的州政策。", "大法官安东尼·肯尼迪在首席大法官约翰·罗伯茨及最高法院自由派大法官的附议下裁定，该州“飞得太靠近联邦的太阳”了（越界了）。关于被推翻的条款，多数派大法官认为国会已刻意“占领该领域”，因此亚利桑那州侵犯了联邦的特权。", "不过，大法官们表示，亚利桑那州警察将被允许核实与执法人员接触者的合法身份。这是因为国会一直设想由联邦和州联合开展移民执法，并明确鼓励州执法人员与联邦同僚共享信息、通力合作。", "三位持反对意见的大法官中有两位——塞缪尔·阿利托和克拉伦斯·托马斯——认同这一宪法逻辑，但对亚利桑那州的哪些规定与联邦法规相冲突持有不同看法。唯一重大的异议来自大法官安东宁·斯卡利亚，他为州特权进行了更为有力的辩护，并将依据追溯至《客籍法与惩治叛乱法》。", "以八比零否定奥巴马总统的裁决，核心在于大法官塞缪尔·阿利托在其异议书中所称的“对联邦行政权力的令人震惊的主张”。白宫辩称，亚利桑那州的法律与其执法优先事项相冲突，即便该州法律在字面上完全遵守了联邦法规。实际上，白宫声称自己可以废除任何其不认同的、原本合法的州法律。", "某些权力确实专属于联邦政府，对公民身份和边境的控制权便位列其中。但如果国会想阻止各州动用自身资源来核查移民身份，它本可以这么做，但它从未这样做过。行政当局实质上是在宣称，因为自己不想执行国会的移民意愿，所以也不应允许任何州这样做。每一位大法官都理所当然地驳回了这一荒谬的主张。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Three provisions of Arizona's plan were overturned because they", "options": ["disturbed the power balance between different states.", "overstepped the authority of federal immigration law.", "deprived the federal police of Constitutional powers.", "contradicted both the federal and state policies."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "On the overturned provisions the majority held Congress had deliberately \"occupied the field\" and Arizona had thus intruded on the federal's privileged powers.", "explanation": "定位第3段第2句。针对被推翻的三项条款，多数派大法官指出国会已刻意“占领该领域”，而亚利桑那州由此侵犯了联邦政府的特权。选项B中“overstepped the authority of federal immigration law（越过了联邦移民法的权限）”精准同义转述了原文的“intruded on the federal's privileged powers”，并结合第2段提到的州警察执行联邦移民法越界，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项将“联邦与州之间的权力平衡”偷换为“不同州之间的权力平衡”；C项中的“剥夺联邦警察的宪法权力”与D项中“同时违背联邦和州政策”均属于无中生有，原文仅提及州法越权。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "On which of the following did the Justices agree, according to Paragraph 4?", "options": ["Congress's intervention in immigration enforcement.", "Federal officers' duty to withhold immigrants' information.", "States' legitimate role in immigration enforcement.", "States' independence from federal immigration law."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "However, the Justices said that Arizona police would be allowed to verify the legal status of people who come in contact with law enforcement. That's because Congress has always envisioned joint federal-state immigration enforcement and explicitly encourages state officers to share information and cooperate with federal colleagues.", "explanation": "定位第4段。大法官们一致认为亚利桑那州警察有权核实与执法人员接触者的合法身份，因为国会一直设想由联邦与州联合进行移民执法，并明确鼓励州执法人员与联邦同僚共享信息、开展合作。选项C“States' legitimate role in immigration enforcement（州在移民执法中的合法角色）”概括了州警察在联邦框架下依法参与核查与配合执法的合法地位，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“国会干预移民执法”偏离第4段强调州执法合法性的主旨；B项将“鼓励共享信息”反向歪曲为“隐瞒移民信息”；D项“独立于联邦移民法”与原文“联合执法与合作”完全相悖。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be inferred from Paragraph 5 that the Alien and Sedition Acts", "options": ["stood in favor of the states.", "supported the federal statute.", "undermined the states' interests.", "violated the Constitution."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "The only major objection came from Justice Antonin Scalia, who offered an even more robust defense of state privileges going back to the Alien and Sedition Acts.", "explanation": "定位第5段第2句。斯卡利亚大法官提出了唯一的主要异议，他为州特权进行了更为有力的辩护，并将依据追溯至《客籍法与惩治叛乱法》。既然该法案被大法官用来作为捍卫“state privileges（州特权）”的历史依据，由此可合理推断该法案是支持州权的，对应选项A“stood in favor of the states（站在支持州的一方）”，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“支持联邦法规”与斯卡利亚捍卫州特权的立场相反；C项“损害州利益”属于反向干扰；D项“违反宪法”在文中并无提及，属于脱离文本的过度主观臆断。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The White House claims that its power of enforcement", "options": ["is dependent on the states' support.", "is established by federal statutes.", "outweighs that held by the states.", "rarely goes against state laws."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "In effect, the White House claimed that it could invalidate any otherwise legitimate state law that it disagrees with.", "explanation": "定位第6段第2、3句。白宫辩称，即使州法律严格遵守联邦法规，只要与白宫的执法优先事项相冲突，白宫就能宣布其无效——实际上白宫声称自己可以废除任何其不认同的原本合法的州法律。这表明白宫认为自身的行政执法权凌驾于州权之上，选项C“outweighs that held by the states（重于州所持有的权力）”精准转述了这一主张，故C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“依赖州的支持”与白宫压制州法的态度相反；B项“由联邦法规确立”偏离核心，白宫强调的是行政执法优先权而非遵循法规；D项“很少违背州法”同样与原文语义相悖。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can be learned from the last paragraph?", "options": ["Immigration issues are usually decided by Congress.", "The Administration is dominant over immigration issues.", "Justices wanted to strengthen its coordination with Congress.", "Justices intended to check the power of the Administration."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 7, "evidenceQuote": "The Administration was in essence asserting that because it didn't want to carry out Congress's immigration wishes, no state should be allowed to do so either. Every Justice rightly rejected this remarkable claim.", "explanation": "定位末段最后两句。行政当局实质上是在宣称，由于自己不想执行国会的移民意愿，任何州也不应被允许这样做。对此，每一位大法官都理所当然地驳回了这一荒谬主张（即前文第1、6段所指的8比0一致否定）。由此可知，大法官们意在制衡、限制行政当局过度膨胀的行政权力，对应选项D“Justices intended to check the power of the Administration”，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项和B项均把部分前提或行政当局的企图当成全段结论，忽视了末句大法官集体驳回的核心动作；C项“大法官想加强与国会的协调”属无中生有，文中并未提及司法与国会的协调意愿。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "推翻，废除（法律、裁决等）", "note": "法律类阅读高频词，文中指最高法院推翻亚利桑那州移民法中的三项条款。", "word": "overturn"}, {"gloss": "侵入，侵犯（权力、领地）", "note": "常与介词 on 搭配，intrude on sth. 表示“侵占/干涉某事物”。", "word": "intrude"}, {"gloss": "核实，查证", "note": "指州警察核实相关人员的合法身份（verify the legal status）。", "word": "verify"}, {"gloss": "宣布无效，使作废", "note": "由 in- + valid + -ate 构成，文中指白宫声称有权废除其不认同的州法律。", "word": "invalidate"}, {"gloss": "声称，主张；维护（权利）", "note": "名词形式为 assertion，文中多次出现以揭示行政当局对权力的强硬主张。", "word": "assert"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In Arizona v. United States, the majority overturned three of the four contested provisions of Arizona's controversial plan to have state and local police enforce federal immigration law.", "point": "不定式短语 to have...enforce 作后置定语修饰 plan，内含使役结构 have sb. do sth.。", "structure": "介词短语作地点/案件状语 + 主句（the majority overturned...contested provisions）+ 介词短语修饰 provisions + 不定式短语作后置定语修饰 plan。", "zh": "在“亚利桑那州诉合众国案”中，多数派大法官推翻了亚利桑那州这项备受争议的计划中的四项受质疑条款中的三项，该计划旨在让州和地方警察执行联邦移民法。"}, {"en": "Two of the three objecting Justices - Samuel Alito and Clarence Thomas - agreed with this Constitutional logic but disagreed about which Arizona rules conflicted with the federal statute.", "point": "破折号插入同位语补充人名；which 引导的宾语从句作介词 about 的宾语。", "structure": "主语（Two of the three objecting Justices）+ 破折号插入语（同位语）+ 并列谓语（agreed with...but disagreed about...）+ which 引导的宾语从句。", "zh": "三位持反对意见的大法官中有两位——塞缪尔·阿利托和克拉伦斯·托马斯——认同这一宪法逻辑，但在亚利桑那州的哪些规定与联邦法规相冲突这一问题上存在分歧。"}, {"en": "The Administration was in essence asserting that because it didn't want to carry out Congress's immigration wishes, no state should be allowed to do so either.", "point": "asserting 后接 that 宾语从句，从句中嵌套 because 原因状语从句，do so 指代前文的 carry out Congress's immigration wishes。", "structure": "主句（The Administration was asserting）+ 状语（in essence）+ that 引导的宾语从句（内含 because 引导的原因状语从句）。", "zh": "行政当局实质上是在主张，因为自己不想贯彻国会在移民问题上的意愿，所以也不应允许任何州这样做。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第3段“侵犯联邦特权”对应Q1正确选项B的“超越联邦移民法权限”。", "option": "overstepped the authority of federal immigration law", "original": "intruded on the federal's privileged powers"}, {"note": "第4段“允许州警核查并鼓励联合执法”高度概括为Q2正确选项C。", "option": "States' legitimate role in immigration enforcement", "original": "Arizona police would be allowed to verify the legal status...envisioned joint federal-state immigration enforcement"}, {"note": "第5段“对州特权的更有力辩护”在Q3中推断为“支持州方”。", "option": "stood in favor of the states", "original": "defense of state privileges"}, {"note": "第6段“白宫声称可废除其不认同的州法”对应Q4正确选项C“其执法权凌驾于州之上”。", "option": "outweighs that held by the states", "original": "invalidate any otherwise legitimate state law that it disagrees with"}, {"note": "第7段大法官一致驳回行政当局的主张，对应Q5正确选项D“意在制约行政权力”。", "option": "check the power of the Administration", "original": "Every Justice rightly rejected this remarkable claim"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2012-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2012", "examSet": "2012 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2012 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "同伴压力与“社会疗法”的局限", "subtitle": "评析蒂娜·罗森伯格《加入俱乐部》中同伴压力的积极作用及外部干预的局限性", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 438, "paragraphs": ["Come on - Everybody's doing it. That whispered message, half invitation and half forcing, is what most of us think of when we hear the words peer pressure. It usually leads to no good - drinking, drugs and casual sex. But in her new book Join the Club, Tina Rosenberg contends that peer pressure can also be a positive force through what she calls the social cure, in which organizations and officials use the power of group dynamics to help individuals improve their lives and possibly the world.", "Rosenberg, the recipient of a Pulitzer Prize, offers a host of examples of the social cure in action: In South Carolina, a state-sponsored antismoking program called Rage Against the Haze sets out to make cigarettes uncool. In South Africa, an HIV-prevention initiative known as loveLife recruits young people to promote safe sex among their peers.", "The idea seems promising, and Rosenberg is a perceptive observer. Her critique of the lameness of many public-health campaigns is spot-on: they fail to mobilize peer pressure for healthy habits, and they demonstrate a seriously flawed understanding of psychology. \"Dare to be different, please don't smoke!\" pleads one billboard campaign aimed at reducing smoking among teenagers - teenagers, who desire nothing more than fitting in. Rosenberg argues convincingly that public-health advocates ought to take a page from advertisers, so skilled at applying peer pressure. But on the general effectiveness of the social cure, Rosenberg is less persuasive. Join the Club is filled with too much irrelevant detail and not enough exploration of the social and biological factors that make peer pressure so powerful. The most glaring flaw of the social cure as it's presented here is that it doesn't work very well for very long. Rage Against the Haze failed once state funding was cut. Evidence that the loveLife program produces lasting changes is limited and mixed. There's no doubt that our peer groups exert enormous influence on our behavior. An emerging body of research shows that positive health habits - as well as negative ones - spread through networks of friends via social communication. This is a subtle form of peer pressure: we unconsciously imitate the behavior we see every day. Far less certain, however, is how successfully experts and bureaucrats can select our peer groups and steer their activities in virtuous directions. It's like the teacher who breaks up the troublemakers in the back row by pairing them with better-behaved classmates. The tactic never really works. And that's the problem with a social cure engineered from the outside: in the real world, as in school, we insist on choosing our own friends."], "translations": ["“来吧——大家都在这么做呢。”这句半是邀请、半是强迫的低语，正是大多数人听到“同伴压力”一词时首先想到的画面。它通常不会带来什么好结果——往往导致酗酒、吸毒和随意性行为。但在其新书《加入俱乐部》中，蒂娜·罗森伯格主张，通过她所谓的“社会疗法”，同伴压力也可以成为一种积极力量——在这一疗法中，机构和官员利用群体动力的力量帮助个体改善自身生活，乃至改善世界。", "曾获普利策奖的罗森伯格列举了大量正在实践中的“社会疗法”案例：在南卡罗来纳州，一项由政府资助的反吸烟项目“向烟雾宣战”致力于让吸烟显得不再酷炫；在南非，一项名为“爱与生命”的艾滋病预防倡议招募年轻人，在同龄人中推广安全性行为。", "这一想法看起来颇具前景，罗森伯格也是一位敏锐的观察者。她对许多公共卫生宣传活动乏力之处的批评可谓一针见血：这些活动未能调动同伴压力来培养健康习惯，且暴露出对心理学存在严重误解。“敢于与众不同，请勿吸烟！”——一则旨在减少青少年吸烟的广告牌这样恳求道，而青少年最渴望的恰恰是融入群体。罗森伯格令人信服地指出，公共卫生倡导者应当向极其擅长运用同伴压力的广告商学习。然而，谈及“社会疗法”的普遍有效性时，罗森伯格的论述就显得不那么有说服力了。《加入俱乐部》充斥着过多无关细节，却对使同伴压力如此强大的社会和生物因素缺乏足够探讨。书中呈现的“社会疗法”最明显的缺陷在于它难以持久奏效。一旦政府资金被削减，“向烟雾宣战”项目便宣告失败；而证明“爱与生命”项目能带来持久改变的证据也十分有限且结论不一。毫无疑问，同伴群体对我们的行为有着巨大影响。一项新兴研究表明，无论是积极的健康习惯还是消极习惯，都会通过社交互动在朋友圈中传播。这是一种微妙的同伴压力：我们会不知不觉地模仿每天看到的行为。然而，远不确定的是，专家和官僚能在多大程度上成功挑选我们的同伴群体，并将其活动引导向有益的方向。这就好比老师把后排的捣蛋鬼拆散，让他们与表现较好的同学坐在一起——这种策略从未真正奏效。而这正是从外部强加“社会疗法”的问题所在：在现实生活中，正如在学校里一样，我们总是坚持自己选择朋友。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the first paragraph, peer pressure often emerges as", "options": ["a supplement to the social cure.", "a stimulus to group dynamics.", "an obstacle to social progress.", "a cause of undesirable behaviors."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "It usually leads to no good - drinking, drugs and casual sex.", "explanation": "定位第1段第3句。当大多数人听到“同伴压力”一词时，首先想到的就是它通常不会带来好结果，具体表现为酗酒、吸毒和随意性行为。其中“leads to no good”对应选项D中的“a cause of undesirable behaviors（不良行为的诱因）”，同义替换精准，因此D项正确。作者随后虽用But引出罗森伯格对其积极面的探讨，但题干问的是同伴压力常以何种面貌出现（即大众通常认知），故锁定转折前内容。", "trapNote": "A项将后文“social cure”拼凑进来，属无中生有；B项“group dynamics”是组织利用同伴压力的方式，并非同伴压力通常表现出的本质；C项“社会进步的障碍”属于过度夸大。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Rosenberg holds that public-health advocates should", "options": ["recruit professional advertisers.", "learn from advertisers' experience.", "stay away from commercial advertisers.", "recognize the limitations of advertisements."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Rosenberg argues convincingly that public-health advocates ought to take a page from advertisers, so skilled at applying peer pressure.", "explanation": "定位第3段第4句。罗森伯格令人信服地指出，公共卫生倡导者应当向广告商学习（take a page from advertisers），因为广告商非常擅长运用同伴压力。习语“take a page from sb.”意为“向某人学习/借鉴经验”，与B项“learn from advertisers' experience”构成精准同义替换，且“ought to”对应题干“should”，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“雇佣专业广告商”属于偷换动作，“向其借鉴”并非“雇佣”；C项“远离商业广告商”与原文态度完全相反；D项“认识到广告的局限性”原文未提及，原文实为肯定广告商的技巧。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "In the author's view, Rosenberg's book fails to", "options": ["adequately probe social and biological factors.", "effectively evade the flaws of the social cure.", "illustrate the functions of state funding.", "produce a long-lasting social effect."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Join the Club is filled with too much irrelevant detail and not enough exploration of the social and biological factors that make peer pressure so powerful.", "explanation": "定位第3段第6句。作者在肯定罗森伯格观察力的同时转折指出，其著作《加入俱乐部》充斥过多无关细节，却对使同伴压力如此强大的社会和生物因素缺乏足够探讨。“not enough exploration of the social and biological factors”与A项“adequately probe social and biological factors（充分探究社会和生物因素）”在题干“fails to”的否定语境下完全吻合，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“有效规避社会疗法的缺陷”与原文不符，作者批评的是书中未充分探讨原因而非要求书籍规避缺陷；D项“产生持久社会效果”是“社会疗法”本身的问题，而非该书写作上的不足，属张冠李戴。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Paragraph 5 shows that our imitation of behaviors", "options": ["is harmful to our networks of friends.", "will mislead behavioral studies.", "occurs without our realizing it.", "can produce negative health habits."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "This is a subtle form of peer pressure: we unconsciously imitate the behavior we see every day.", "explanation": "定位第3段中“This is a subtle form of peer pressure: we unconsciously imitate the behavior we see every day.”（对应原真题第5段）。句中指出这是一种微妙的同伴压力：我们会不知不觉地模仿每天看到的行为。副词“unconsciously（无意识地）”与C项“without our realizing it（在我们未察觉的情况下）”形成直接同义替换，因此C项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“对交友网络有害”曲解文意，原文说健康习惯和不良习惯都会通过社交网络传播；D项“会产生不良健康习惯”属于因果倒置且片面，原文仅说好坏习惯都会经由社交传播，并非模仿行为本身必然产生坏习惯。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "The author suggests in the last paragraph that the effect of peer pressure is", "options": ["harmful.", "desirable.", "profound.", "questionable."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Far less certain, however, is how successfully experts and bureaucrats can select our peer groups and steer their activities in virtuous directions.", "explanation": "定位第3段末尾（对应原真题末段）。作者用“Far less certain”明确指出，专家和官僚能否成功挑选同伴群体并引导其向善是“远不确定的”；随后用老师拆散后排捣蛋鬼的比喻说明这种做法“never really works（从未真正奏效）”，因为人们坚持自己选择朋友。由此可推断，作者认为外部引导下的同伴压力效果是存疑的，“Far less certain”对应D项“questionable”，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“令人满意的”与作者质疑外部干预的态度相悖；C项“深远的”虽在段首提及同伴影响巨大，但末段核心转折强调的是人为施加同伴压力的效果并不确定，非主旨所在；A项“有害的”过于绝对。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 声称，主张，认为", "note": "常接that从句引出作者或学者观点，在考研阅读中高频出现。", "word": "contend"}, {"gloss": "n. 接受者，获得者", "note": "文中指普利策奖获得者（recipient of a Pulitzer Prize），动词词根为receive。", "word": "recipient"}, {"gloss": "n. 笨拙，无力，缺乏说服力", "note": "由形容词lame（站不住脚的、无说服力的）派生，文中批评公共卫生宣传效果不佳。", "word": "lameness"}, {"gloss": "adj. 十分准确的，切中要害的", "note": "用于评价批评或观察“一针见血、正中靶心”，体现作者对该部分内容的肯定。", "word": "spot-on"}, {"gloss": "adj. 明显的，显眼的，耀眼的", "note": "文中“the most glaring flaw”指“最显而易见的缺陷”，强调用词色彩。", "word": "glaring"}, {"gloss": "v. 引导，驾驶，控制方向", "note": "文中指“引导同伴群体的活动走向有益的方向”（steer... in virtuous directions）。", "word": "steer"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "But in her new book Join the Club, Tina Rosenberg contends that peer pressure can also be a positive force through what she calls the social cure, in which organizations and officials use the power of group dynamics to help individuals improve their lives and possibly the world.", "point": "宾语从句嵌套what引导的介词宾语从句及in which引导的非限制性定语从句，理清“social cure”的定义是理解全文核心概念的关键。", "structure": "主干为Tina Rosenberg contends that...；that引导宾语从句，其中包含what she calls the social cure作through的宾语；in which引导非限制性定语从句修饰the social cure。", "zh": "但在其新书《加入俱乐部》中，蒂娜·罗森伯格主张，通过她所谓的“社会疗法”，同伴压力也可以成为一种积极力量——在这一疗法中，机构和官员利用群体动力的力量帮助个体改善自身生活，乃至改善世界。"}, {"en": "Her critique of the lameness of many public-health campaigns is spot-on: they fail to mobilize peer pressure for healthy habits, and they demonstrate a seriously flawed understanding of psychology.", "point": "冒号后为两个并列分句，具体解释前文“critique of the lameness”的内容，需注意flawed understanding的精准译法。", "structure": "主系表结构Her critique... is spot-on；冒号起解释说明作用，后接由and连接的两个并列分句具体阐明批评内容。", "zh": "她对许多公共卫生宣传活动乏力之处的批评可谓一针见血：这些活动未能调动同伴压力来培养健康习惯，且暴露出对心理学存在严重误解。"}, {"en": "Far less certain, however, is how successfully experts and bureaucrats can select our peer groups and steer their activities in virtuous directions.", "point": "表语前置引起的完全倒装句，正常语序为“How successfully experts... is far less certain”。倒装旨在突出“Far less certain”，标志作者态度转折。", "structure": "表语Far less certain置于句首构成完全倒装；主语为how引导的主语从句，系动词为is，副词however作插入语表示转折。", "zh": "然而，远不确定的是，专家和官僚能在多大程度上成功挑选我们的同伴群体，并将其活动引导向有益的方向。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "常见行为结果的负向概括与名词短语替换", "option": "a cause of undesirable behaviors", "original": "leads to no good - drinking, drugs and casual sex"}, {"note": "习语“take a page from sb.”向某人借鉴经验的同义改写", "option": "learn from advertisers' experience", "original": "take a page from advertisers"}, {"note": "“未充分探讨”在否定语境下的反义/正话反说转换", "option": "adequately probe social and biological factors", "original": "not enough exploration of the social and biological factors"}, {"note": "副词“unconsciously”与介词短语“without our realizing it”精准互换", "option": "occurs without our realizing it", "original": "unconsciously imitate"}, {"note": "程度不确定表达“Far less certain”与形容词“questionable”的态度的直接对应", "option": "questionable", "original": "Far less certain"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L3", "exam": "kaoyan1", "id": "ky1-2012-t2", "origin": "official", "paragraphs": ["A deal is a deal—except, apparently, when Entergy is involved. The company, a major energy supplier in New England, provoked justified outrage in Vermont last week when it announced it was reneging on a longstanding commitment to abide by the state’s strict nuclear regulations.", "Instead, the company has done precisely what it had long promised it would not: challenge the constitutionality of Vermont’s rules in the federal court, as part of a desperate effort to keep its Vermont Yankee nuclear power plant running. It’s a stunning move.", "The conflict has been surfacing since 2002, when the corporation bought Vermont’s only nuclear power plant, an aging reactor in Vernon. As a condition of receiving state approval for the sale, the company agreed to seek permission from state regulators to operate past 2012. In 2006, the state went a step further, requiring that any extension of the plant’s license be subject to the Vermont legislature’s approval. Then, too, the company went along.", "Either Entergy never really intended to live by those commitments, or it simply didn’t foresee what would happen next. A string of accidents, including the partial collapse of a cooling tower in 2007 and the discovery of an underground pipe system leakage, raised serious questions about both Vermont Yankee’s safety and Entergy’s management—especially after the company made misleading statements about the pipe. Enraged by Entergy’s behavior, the Vermont Senate voted 26 to 4 last year against allowing an extension.", "Now the company is suddenly claiming that the 2002 agreement is invalid because of the 2006 legislation, and that only the federal government has regulatory power over nuclear issues. The legal issues in the case are obscure: whereas the Supreme Court has ruled that states do have some regulatory authority over nuclear power, legal scholars say the Vermont case will offer a precedent-setting test of how far those powers extend. Certainly, there are valid concerns about the patchwork regulations that could result if every state sets its own rules. But had Entergy kept its word, that debate would be beside the point.", "The company seems to have concluded that its reputation in Vermont is already so damaged that it has nothing left to lose by going to war with the state. But there should be consequences. Permission to run a nuclear plant is a public trust. Entergy runs 11 other reactors in the United States, including Pilgrim Nuclear station in Plymouth. Pledging to run Pilgrim safely, the company has applied for federal permission to keep it open for another 20 years. But as the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) reviews the company’s application, it should keep in mind what promises from Entergy are worth."], "questions": [{"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "provoked justified outrage in Vermont last week when it announced it was reneging on a longstanding commitment to abide by the state’s strict nuclear regulations.", "explanation": "定位到第 1 段第 2 句并结合第 2 段语境。第 1 段指出 Entergy 宣布对“遵守该州严格核能规定的长期承诺”采取 reneging on 的做法并引发正当愤慨，第 2 段紧接着点明公司恰恰做了长期承诺绝不会做的事（在联邦法院挑战法规合宪性），可见其违背了先前的承诺。C 项 dishonoring（违背、不履行）与“违背承诺”构成准确同义替换。", "no": 26, "options": ["condemning", "reaffirming", "dishonoring", "securing"], "stem": "The phrase “reneging on” (Line 3, Para.1) is closest in meaning to______.", "trapNote": "最迷惑干扰项为 A（condemning，谴责），它利用后文公司挑战州法规的举动诱导考生望文生义，偷换了“背弃自身承诺”与“谴责对方规定”这两个不同动作；B、D 则与原文违背承诺的语义正反颠倒。", "type": "词义题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "since 2002, when the corporation bought Vermont’s only nuclear power plant, an aging reactor in Vernon. As a condition of receiving state approval for the sale", "explanation": "定位到第 3 段前两句。第 1 句说明公司于 2002 年买下（bought）佛蒙特州唯一的核电站，第 2 句紧接着交代“作为获得州政府批准该笔收购交易（receiving state approval for the sale）的条件”，公司才同意未来申请延期运营许可。由此可知，签署 2002 年协议的直接目的是获得购买核电站的批准，D 项中 get permission 对应 receiving state approval，purchase a power plant 对应 bought...nuclear power plant 与 the sale。", "no": 27, "options": ["obtain protection from Vermont regulators", "seek favor from the federal legislature", "acquire an extension of its business license", "get permission to purchase a power plant"], "stem": "By entering into the 2002 agreement, Entergy intended to______.", "trapNote": "最迷惑干扰项为 C（acquire an extension of its business license），它把“为获准收购而答应日后申请运营延期的条件”偷换为签署协议的目的，且将“核电站运行许可”偷换概念为泛化的“营业执照（business license）”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "raised serious questions about both Vermont Yankee’s safety and Entergy’s management—especially after the company made misleading statements about the pipe.", "explanation": "定位到第 4 段第 2 句。一系列安全事故以及公司针对管道泄漏作出的误导性陈述（misleading statements），使外界对核电站安全性及 Entergy 的管理（Entergy’s management）产生严重质疑。A 项中的 managerial practices（管理做法）是对 Entergy’s management 及事故应对失当的同义替换，have problems with 对应 raised serious questions about。", "no": 28, "options": ["managerial practices", "technical innovativeness", "financial goals", "business vision"], "stem": "According to Paragraph 4, Entergy seems to have problems with its______.", "trapNote": "最迷惑干扰项为 D（business vision，商业远见），它断章取义地利用段首的 didn’t foresee（未能预见）进行过度推理，把具体的安全事故与信息披露管理失误偷换为企业的长期商业战略远见问题。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "states do have some regulatory authority over nuclear power, legal scholars say the Vermont case will offer a precedent-setting test of how far those powers extend.", "explanation": "定位到第 5 段第 2 句。作者转述法律学者的观点指出，最高法院已裁定各州对核能拥有一定监管权，而佛蒙特州一案将开创性地检验“这些权力能延伸到何种程度（how far those powers extend）”，其中 those powers 回指前文各州的核能监管权。D 项中 the limits of states' power over nuclear issues 正是对 how far those powers extend 的同义替换，作者虽在段末批评企业失信，但并未否定该法律判断。", "no": 29, "options": ["Entergy's capacity to fulfill all its promises", "the nature of states' patchwork regulations", "the federal authority over nuclear issues", "the limits of states' power over nuclear issues"], "stem": "In the author's view, the Vermont case will test______.", "trapNote": "最迷惑干扰项为 A（Entergy's capacity to fulfill all its promises），它混淆了作者在段末对企业失信的道德批评与案件本身的法律检验对象，属于偷换概念且带有 all 的绝对化错误；C 则将“州监管权”张冠李戴为“联邦权威”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "But as the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) reviews the company’s application, it should keep in mind what promises from Entergy are worth.", "explanation": "定位到第 6 段。作者用“But there should be consequences”引出后果，指出 Entergy 在全美还运营着 11 座反应堆并已为普利茅斯的 Pilgrim 核电站申请继续运营 20 年，最后呼吁核管会（NRC）在审查该申请时牢记 Entergy 的承诺究竟值多少信任。由此可合理推断，该公司在佛蒙特州的失信行为可能会波及（might be affected）其在其他地区的业务审批，A 项中 might 准确体现了推论的克制语气。", "no": 30, "options": ["Entergy's business elsewhere might be affected", "the authority of the NRC will be defied", "Entergy will withdraw its Plymouth application", "Vermont's reputation might be damaged"], "stem": "It can be inferred from the last paragraph that______.", "trapNote": "最迷惑干扰项为 C（Entergy will withdraw its Plymouth application），它将监管机构在审批时应审慎考量企业信用过度推理为“公司将主动撤回申请”；D 项则将公司自身受损的声誉张冠李戴给了佛蒙特州。", "type": "推断题"}], "sourceLabel": "2012 考研英语一 Text 2", "subtitle": "2012 年考研英语一 Reading Comprehension Text 2", "timeLimitMin": 18, "title": "Entergy and Vermont's Nuclear Power Dispute", "year": "2012", "wordCount": 446, "translations": ["协议就是协议——但凡涉及安特吉公司（Entergy），情况似乎就另当别论了。作为新英格兰地区的主要能源供应商，该公司上周宣布将违背遵守佛蒙特州严格核监管规定的长期承诺，此举在当地引发了合情合理的公愤。", "相反，该公司恰恰做出了它长期以来承诺绝不会做的事情：在联邦法院质疑佛蒙特州法规的合宪性，以此作为孤注一掷的手段，企图让旗下的佛蒙特扬基核电站继续运营。这一举动令人震惊。", "这场冲突自2002年起便已开始显现，当时该公司买下了佛蒙特州唯一的核电站——一座位于弗农的老旧反应堆。作为获得州政府批准此次收购的条件，该公司同意在2012年后继续运营需向州监管机构申请许可。2006年，该州更进一步，要求该核电站运营许可的任何延期都必须经过佛蒙特州议会的批准。当时，该公司也顺从了这一要求。", "要么安特吉公司从未真正打算信守这些承诺，要么它根本没有预料到接下来会发生什么。一系列事故——包括2007年一座冷却塔的部分坍塌以及地下管道系统泄漏的发现——引发了人们对佛蒙特扬基核电站安全性及安特吉公司管理能力的严重质疑，尤其是在该公司就管道问题发表了误导性声明之后。由于对安特吉公司的行为感到愤怒，佛蒙特州参议院去年以26比4的投票结果否决了允许其延期的提案。", "如今，该公司突然声称2002年的协议因2006年的立法而失效，并且只有联邦政府才对核事务拥有监管权。本案涉及的法律问题相当模糊：尽管最高法院曾裁定各州对核能确实拥有一定的监管权，但法律学者指出，佛蒙特州一案将成为一个开创先例的试金石，用以检验这些权力的界限究竟能延伸到何种程度。诚然，如果每个州都自行制定规则，可能会产生拼凑杂乱的监管体系，这种担忧不无道理。但如果安特吉公司信守了诺言，那场争论原本就无从谈起。", "该公司似乎已经认定，自己在佛蒙特州的声誉已经受损殆尽，即便与该州开战也已无所顾忌。但这样做理应付出代价。获准运营核电站承载着公众的信任。安特吉公司在美国还运营着另外11座反应堆，其中包括位于普利茅斯的朝圣者核电站。该公司承诺将安全运营朝圣者核电站，并已向联邦政府申请许可，希望让其再继续运行20年。然而，当核管理委员会（NRC）审查该公司的申请时，应当牢记安特吉公司的承诺究竟有几分分量。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 违背，食言", "note": "高频难点词，常与 on 搭配表示“违背（承诺、协议等）”，真题直接考查其同义替换 dishonor。", "word": "renege"}, {"gloss": "v. 遵守，信守", "note": "常以固定搭配 abide by 出现，意为“遵守（规定、法律、承诺）”，相当于 comply with / adhere to。", "word": "abide"}, {"gloss": "v. 浮现，显露，公开", "note": "熟词僻义：作名词意为“表面”，本文用作不及物动词，指冲突或问题“浮出水面、显露”。", "word": "surface"}, {"gloss": "adj. 须经……批准的，受……支配的", "note": "熟词僻义及高频考点：be subject to 在本文指“须经……批准”，另有“易受……影响的”之意。", "word": "subject"}, {"gloss": "adj. 模糊不清的，晦涩难懂的", "note": "考研核心词，常形容法律条文、依据“含糊不清、难以界定”，也可指人“默默无闻的”。", "word": "obscure"}, {"gloss": "n. 杂乱拼凑的东西", "note": "原意为“拼布”，在政治与法律类阅读中常喻指“零散拼凑、缺乏统一性的（法规、政策）”。", "word": "patchwork"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "The company, a major energy supplier in New England, provoked justified outrage in Vermont last week when it announced it was reneging on a longstanding commitment to abide by the state’s strict nuclear regulations.", "point": "同位语插入 + 时间状语从句 + 省略引导词的宾语从句 + 不定式作后置定语", "structure": "主干：The company provoked justified outrage in Vermont last week；同位语：a major energy supplier in New England（补充说明主语）；时间状语从句：when it announced (that) it was reneging on a longstanding commitment；后置定语：to abide by the state’s strict nuclear regulations（修饰 commitment）。", "zh": "作为新英格兰地区的主要能源供应商，该公司上周宣布将违背遵守佛蒙特州严格核监管规定的长期承诺，此举在当地引发了合情合理的公愤。"}, {"en": "In 2006, the state went a step further, requiring that any extension of the plant’s license be subject to the Vermont legislature’s approval.", "point": "现在分词短语作伴随状语 + require 后宾语从句的虚拟语气（省 should）", "structure": "主干：the state went a step further；伴随状语：requiring that...；宾语从句：any extension of the plant’s license (should) be subject to the Vermont legislature’s approval（动词原形 be 体现虚拟语气）。", "zh": "2006年，该州更进一步，要求该核电站运营许可的任何延期都必须经过佛蒙特州议会的批准。"}, {"en": "The legal issues in the case are obscure: whereas the Supreme Court has ruled that states do have some regulatory authority over nuclear power, legal scholars say the Vermont case will offer a precedent-setting test of how far those powers extend.", "point": "冒号解释说明 + whereas 引导让步/对比状语从句 + 助动词 do 表强调 + 宾语从句嵌套", "structure": "前半句主干：The legal issues in the case are obscure；冒号后具体阐释：whereas 引导对比/让步从句（the Supreme Court has ruled that states do have...，其中 do 强调谓语 have）；主句：legal scholars say (that) the Vermont case will offer a precedent-setting test of how far those powers extend（of 后接 how far 引导的宾语从句作后置定语）。", "zh": "本案涉及的法律问题相当模糊：尽管最高法院曾裁定各州对核能确实拥有一定的监管权，但法律学者指出，佛蒙特州一案将成为一个开创先例的试金石，用以检验这些权力的界限究竟能延伸到何种程度。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第26题词义猜词：违背承诺即“不履行、背弃”。", "option": "dishonoring", "original": "reneging on"}, {"note": "第27题细节推断：获得州政府对收购的批准 = 获准购买发电厂。", "option": "get permission to purchase a power plant", "original": "bought Vermont’s only nuclear power plant... receiving state approval for the sale"}, {"note": "第28题细节理解：对公司管理及误导性陈述的质疑 = 管理做法存在问题。", "option": "managerial practices", "original": "Entergy’s management—especially after the company made misleading statements"}, {"note": "第29题观点态度：检验这些权力延伸多远 = 检验各州在核问题上的权力限度。", "option": "the limits of states' power over nuclear issues", "original": "offer a precedent-setting test of how far those powers extend"}, {"note": "第30题推理判断：暗示核管会审查新申请时应看清其信誉，即其在别处的业务恐受牵连。", "option": "Entergy's business elsewhere might be affected", "original": "reviews the company’s application, it should keep in mind what promises from Entergy are worth"}]}, "examSet": "2012 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）"}, {"id": "ky1-2012-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2012", "examSet": "2012 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2012 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "科学发现中的可信度建构过程", "subtitle": "探讨科学发现如何从个人主张通过科学共同体的集体审查转化为可信知识", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 445, "paragraphs": ["In the idealized version of how science is done, facts about the world are waiting to be observed and collected by objective researchers who use the scientific method to carry out their work. But in the everyday practice of science, discovery frequently follows an ambiguous and complicated route. We aim to be objective, but we cannot escape the context of our unique life experiences. Prior knowledge and interests influence what we experience, what we think our experiences mean, and the subsequent actions we take. Opportunities for misinterpretation, error, and self deception abound.", "Consequently, discovery claims should be thought of as protoscience. Similar to newly staked mining claims, they are full of potential. But it takes collective scrutiny and acceptance to transform a discovery claim into a mature discovery. This is the credibility process, through which the individual researcher's me, here, now becomes the community's anyone, anywhere, anytime. Objective knowledge is the goal, not the starting point.", "Once a discovery claim becomes public, the discoverer receives intellectual credit. But, unlike with mining claims, the community takes control of what happens next. Within the complex social structure of the scientific community, researchers make discoveries; editors and reviewers act as gatekeepers by controlling the publication process; other scientists use the new finding to suit their own purposes; and finally, the public (including other scientists) receives the new discovery and possibly accompanying technology. As a discovery claim works its way through the community, the interaction and confrontation between shared and competing beliefs about the science and the technology involved transforms an individual's discovery claim into the community's credible discovery.", "Two paradoxes exist throughout this credibility process. First, scientific work tends to focus on some aspect of prevailing knowledge that is viewed as incomplete or incorrect. Little reward accompanies duplication and confirmation of what is already known and believed. The goal is new-search, not re-search. Not surprisingly, newly published discovery claims and credible discoveries that appear to be important and convincing will always be open to challenge and potential modification or refutation by future researchers. Second, novelty itself frequently provokes disbelief. Nobel Laureate and physiologist Albert Szent-Gyorgyi once described discovery as \"seeing what everybody has seen and thinking what nobody has thought.\" But thinking what nobody else has thought and telling others what they have missed may not change their views. Sometimes years are required for truly novel discovery claims to be accepted and appreciated.", "In the end, credibility \"happens\" to a discovery claim - a process that corresponds to what philosopher Annette Baier has described as the commons of the mind. \"We reason together, challenge, revise, and complete each other's reasoning and each other's conceptions of reason.\""], "translations": ["在科学研究如何开展的理想化图景中，关于世界的事实正静待客观的研究者去观察和收集，而这些研究者会运用科学方法来开展工作。但在日常的科学实践中，发现往往遵循着一条模糊而复杂的路径。我们力求客观，却无法摆脱各自独特人生经历的语境。先前的知识与兴趣会影响我们的所见所感、我们对经历意义的解读，以及我们随后采取的行动。误读、出错与自欺的机会比比皆是。", "因此，发现主张应当被视为一种前科学。与新划定的采矿权主张相似，它们充满了潜力。但要将一项发现主张转化为成熟的科学发现，还需要集体的审查与接纳。这便是可信度建构过程，通过这一过程，个体研究者“此时此地的我”得以转化为科学共同体“任何地、任何时的任何人”。客观知识是终点目标，而非起点。", "一旦某项发现主张公之于众，发现者便会获得智力荣誉。但与采矿权主张不同的是，科学共同体将接管接下来发生的一切。在科学共同体复杂的社会结构中，研究者做出发现；编辑与审稿人通过把控发表流程充当守门人；其他科学家按各自目的运用这项新成果；最终，公众（包括其他科学家）接收这项新发现及可能伴随的新技术。当一项发现主张在科学共同体中逐步流转时，围绕所涉科学与技术的共享信念及竞争信念之间的互动与交锋，便会将个人的发现主张转化为科学共同体认可的可信发现。", "这一可信度建构过程自始至终伴随着两个悖论。首先，科学研究往往聚焦于主流知识中被视为不完整或不正确的某些方面。重复并印证已知且已被相信的内容几乎得不到什么回报。科学的目标是求新（new-search），而非重复（re-search）。不足为奇的是，那些新近发表的、看似重要且令人信服的发现主张与可信发现，永远都要接受未来研究者的挑战，并可能面临修改或推翻。其次，新颖性本身往往会招致怀疑。诺贝尔奖得主、生理学家阿尔伯特·圣捷尔吉曾将科学发现描述为“看见众人所见之物，思考无人所想之事”。然而，思考无人所想之事并告诉他人其所忽略之处，未必能改变他们的看法。真正新颖的发现主张有时需要数年时间才能得到接纳与赏识。", "归根结底，可信度是“发生”在发现主张之上的——这一过程正契合哲学家安妮特·拜尔所描述的“心灵公地”：“我们共同推理，互相质疑、修正并完善彼此的推理以及各自对理性的理解。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the first paragraph, the process of discovery is characterized by its", "options": ["uncertainty and complexity.", "misconception and deceptiveness.", "logicality and objectivity.", "systematicness and regularity."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "But in the everyday practice of science, discovery frequently follows an ambiguous and complicated route.", "explanation": "定位第1段第2句。第1句先描述了理想化的科学研究模式（客观研究者按科学方法收集事实），紧接着第2句用“But”转折，指出在日常科学实践中，发现过程往往遵循一条“ambiguous and complicated route（模糊且复杂的路径）”。其中“ambiguous”对应A项“uncertainty（不确定性）”，“complicated”对应“complexity（复杂性）”，精准同义替换，故A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“误解与欺骗性”是对末句“misinterpretation, error, and self deception”的曲解，原文说的是研究者自身存在误判与自欺的可能，并非发现过程本身具有欺骗性；C、D两项符合理想化版本，与日常实际相反。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be inferred from Paragraph 2 that credibility process requires", "options": ["strict inspection.", "shared efforts.", "individual wisdom.", "persistent innovation."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "But it takes collective scrutiny and acceptance to transform a discovery claim into a mature discovery.", "explanation": "定位第2段第3、4句。原文指出，将一项发现主张转化为成熟发现需要“collective scrutiny and acceptance（集体的审查与接受）”，这正是可信度建构过程——将个人研究者“此时此地”的主张转化为科学共同体“任何人、任何地、任何时”的共识。其中“collective（集体的）”与B项“shared efforts（共同努力）”精准呼应，由此可推知该过程需要众人协作，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“严格审查”看似对应“scrutiny”，但遗漏了核心修饰词“collective（集体的）”，未能体现由“个人”向“群体”转化的本质，属于片面干扰；C项“个人智慧”与原文“collective”及从“me”到“anyone”的转化完全相反。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Paragraph 3 shows that a discovery claim becomes credible after it", "options": ["has attracted the attention of the general public.", "has been examined by the scientific community.", "has received recognition from editors and reviewers.", "has been frequently quoted by peer scientists."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "As a discovery claim works its way through the community, the interaction and confrontation between shared and competing beliefs about the science and the technology involved transforms an individual's discovery claim into the community's credible discovery.", "explanation": "定位第3段末句。前文先列举了科学共同体内部不同角色的互动（研究者、编辑审稿人、其他科学家、公众），末句总结道：当发现主张在共同体中流转时，共享信念与竞争信念之间的互动与碰撞，才将其转化为共同体的可信发现。这说明发现主张变可信的前提是经过了整个科学共同体的检验与磨合，对应B项“has been examined by the scientific community”，故B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“吸引公众注意”和C项“获得编辑与审稿人认可”均只是科学共同体内部运转的局部环节，以偏概全；D项“被同行频繁引用”在原文中未提及，属于无中生有。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Albert Szent-Gyorgyi would most likely agree that", "options": ["scientific claims will survive challenges.", "discoveries today inspire future research.", "efforts to make discoveries are justified.", "scientific work calls for a critical mind."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Nobel Laureate and physiologist Albert Szent-Gyorgyi once described discovery as \"seeing what everybody has seen and thinking what nobody has thought.\"", "explanation": "定位第4段第6句。诺贝尔奖得主阿尔伯特·圣捷尔吉将科学发现描述为“看见众人所见之物，思考无人所想之事”。第4段首句亦指出科学研究往往聚焦于主流知识中被视为“不完整或不正确”的方面，这说明发现者不能盲从既有认知，而应具备独立思考、敢于质疑与批判的精神。“thinking what nobody has thought”与D项“calls for a critical mind（需要批判性思维）”高度契合，故D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“科学主张能经受住挑战”与本段“always be open to challenge and potential modification or refutation”相悖；B、C两项均为过度引申，并非圣捷尔吉名言所表达的核心思想。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title of the text?", "options": ["Novelty as an Engine of Scientific Development.", "Collective Scrutiny in Scientific Discovery.", "Evolution of Credibility in Doing Science.", "Challenge to Credibility at the Gate to Science."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "This is the credibility process, through which the individual researcher's me, here, now becomes the community's anyone, anywhere, anytime.", "explanation": "主旨题需通览全篇脉络。第1段指出日常科学发现充满不确定性；第2段核心提出“credibility process（可信度建构过程）”，即个人主张转化为共同体共识；第3段阐述该过程在科学共同体中的具体运作；第4段分析其中的两个悖论；第5段总结可信度是如何在共同体理性碰撞中“发生”的。可见全文围绕“科学研究中可信度的演变/确立过程”展开，C项最能概括主旨。", "trapNote": "A项“新颖性作为科学发展的引擎”仅对应第4段第二个悖论，属局部细节；B项“集体审查”主要出现在第2、3段，未能涵盖第4段悖论与全文“可信度演变”的中心词；D项“科学门槛处对可信度的挑战”偏离文意。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 模棱两可的，不明确的，含糊的", "note": "形容日常科学发现的路线并非单一明确，对应选项中的uncertainty。", "word": "ambiguous"}, {"gloss": "n. 前科学，原科学（尚未成熟确立的科学主张）", "note": "前缀proto-表示“原始的、初步的”，指尚未经过共同体检验的初步发现主张。", "word": "protoscience"}, {"gloss": "n. 仔细审查，详细检验", "note": "文中“collective scrutiny”指科学共同体的集体审查，是确立可信度的必要步骤。", "word": "scrutiny"}, {"gloss": "n. 冲突，对抗，交锋", "note": "文中指共享信念与竞争信念之间的碰撞交锋，动词为confront。", "word": "confrontation"}, {"gloss": "n. 悖论，自相矛盾的情况", "note": "第4段总起句核心词，统领后文“求新反遭质疑”等两个科学传播中的矛盾现象。", "word": "paradox"}, {"gloss": "n. 反驳，驳斥，推翻", "note": "动词为refute，文中指未来的研究者可能会修改甚至推翻看似已具可信度的发现。", "word": "refutation"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In the idealized version of how science is done, facts about the world are waiting to be observed and collected by objective researchers who use the scientific method to carry out their work.", "point": "介词短语作状语引出“理想化模式”，与后文But引出的日常实际形成对比，定语从句修饰researchers。", "structure": "In the idealized version of...为介词短语作状语，其中包含how引导的宾语从句；主干为facts... are waiting to be observed and collected by objective researchers；who引导定语从句修饰researchers。", "zh": "在科学研究如何开展的理想化图景中，关于世界的事实正静待客观的研究者去观察和收集，而这些研究者会运用科学方法来开展工作。"}, {"en": "As a discovery claim works its way through the community, the interaction and confrontation between shared and competing beliefs about the science and the technology involved transforms an individual's discovery claim into the community's credible discovery.", "point": "主语较长（由interaction and confrontation构成并列中心词后接长介词短语），注意谓语动词transforms的搭配“transform A into B”。", "structure": "As引导时间状语从句；主句主语为the interaction and confrontation，between...为后置定语，involved为过去分词作后置定语；谓语为transforms，宾语为an individual's discovery claim，into...为介词短语作补足成分。", "zh": "当一项发现主张在科学共同体中逐步流转时，围绕所涉科学与技术的共享信念及竞争信念之间的互动与交锋，便会将个人的发现主张转化为科学共同体认可的可信发现。"}, {"en": "Not surprisingly, newly published discovery claims and credible discoveries that appear to be important and convincing will always be open to challenge and potential modification or refutation by future researchers.", "point": "注意that定语从句同时修饰并列名词短语，且“be open to...”在此处意为“易于遭受、随时面临（挑战、修改或推翻）”。", "structure": "副词Not surprisingly作句首状语；主语为newly published discovery claims and credible discoveries，后接that引导的定语从句；谓语为will always be open to...。", "zh": "不足为奇的是，那些新近发表的、看似重要且令人信服的发现主张与可信发现，永远都要接受未来研究者的挑战，并可能面临修改或推翻。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "两个并列形容词与对应的抽象名词短语精准置换", "option": "uncertainty and complexity", "original": "an ambiguous and complicated route"}, {"note": "“集体的”审查与“共同努力”的同义概念对应", "option": "shared efforts", "original": "collective scrutiny and acceptance"}, {"note": "主从句描述共同体内部磨合过程，概括为“经科学共同体检验”", "option": "has been examined by the scientific community", "original": "works its way through the community... interaction and confrontation"}, {"note": "“思考无人所想之事”体现突破常规的批判性思维", "option": "calls for a critical mind", "original": "thinking what nobody has thought"}, {"note": "全文中心概念“可信度建构过程”在标题中的升华表述", "option": "Evolution of Credibility in Doing Science", "original": "the credibility process"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2012-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2012", "examSet": "2012 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2012 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "公共部门工会的崛起与制度困境", "subtitle": "解析美英公共部门工会扩张原因、巨大影响力及现行体制弊端", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 442, "paragraphs": ["If the trade unionist Jimmy Hoffa were alive today, he would probably represent civil servants. When Hoffa's Teamsters were in their prime in 1960, only one in ten American government workers belonged to a union; now 36% do. In 2009 the number of unionists in America's public sector passed that of their fellow members in the private sector. In Britain, more than half of public-sector workers but only about 15% of private-sector ones are unionized.", "There are three reasons for the public-sector unions' thriving. First, they can shut things down without suffering much in the way of consequences. Second, they are mostly bright and well-educated. A quarter of America's public-sector workers have a university degree. Third, they now dominate left-of-centre politics. Some of their ties go back a long way. Britain's Labor Party, as its name implies, has long been associated with trade unionism. Its current leader, Ed Miliband, owes his position to votes from public-sector unions.", "At the state level their influence can be even more fearsome. Mark Baldassare of the Public Policy Institute of California points out that much of the state's budget is patrolled by unions. The teachers' unions keep an eye on schools, the CCPOA on prisons and a variety of labor groups on health care.", "In many rich countries average wages in the state sector are higher than in the private one. But the real gains come in benefits and work practices. Politicians have repeatedly \"backloaded\" public-sector pay deals, keeping the pay increases modest but adding to holidays and especially pensions that are already generous. Reform has been vigorously opposed, perhaps most notoriously in education, where charter schools, academies and merit pay all faced drawn-out battles. Even though there is plenty of evidence that the quality of the teachers is the most important variable, teachers' unions have fought against getting rid of bad ones and promoting good ones.", "As the cost to everyone else has become clearer, politicians have begun to clamp down. In Wisconsin the unions have rallied thousands of supporters against Scott Walker, the hardline Republican governor. But many within the public sector suffer under the current system, too.", "John Donahue at Harvard's Kennedy School points out that the norms of culture in Western civil services suit those who want to stay put but is bad for high achievers. The only American public-sector workers who earn well above $250,000 a year are university sports coaches and the president of the United States. Bankers' fat pay packets have attracted much criticism, but a public-sector system that does not reward high achievers may be a much bigger problem for America."], "translations": ["如果工会活动家吉米·霍法今天还活着，他很可能会代表公务员群体。1960年霍法的卡车司机工会处于鼎盛时期时，每十名美国政府雇员中只有一人加入工会；如今这一比例已达36%。2009年，美国公共部门的工会成员人数超过了私营部门的同行。在英国，超过半数的公共部门雇员加入了工会，而私营部门雇员的入会比例仅为15%左右。", "公共部门工会之所以蓬勃发展，原因有三。首先，他们可以让公共服务陷入停摆，却无需承担多少后果。其次，其成员大多聪明且受过良好教育。四分之一的美国公共部门雇员拥有大学学位。第三，他们如今主导着中左翼政坛。他们与政党的部分渊源由来已久。正如其名称所暗示的，英国工党长期以来一直与工会主义紧密相连。其现任领袖埃德·米利班德能坐上这一位置，正得益于公共部门工会的选票。", "在州一级层面，他们的影响力可能更加令人生畏。加州公共政策研究所的马克·巴尔达萨雷指出，该州的大部分预算都处于工会的严密监督之下。教师工会紧盯着学校，加州狱警工会（CCPOA）盯着监狱，而各类劳工团体则盯着医疗保健领域。", "在许多富裕国家，公共部门的平均工资高于私营部门。但真正的收益来自福利和工作惯例。政客们一再对公共部门的薪酬协议采取“后置支付”策略，使账面加薪幅度保持温和，却不断增加本已优厚的假期，尤其是养老金福利。改革遭到了激烈反对，其中或许以教育领域最为臭名昭著，特许学校、学院制学校和绩效工资制都面临着旷日持久的争斗。尽管有充分证据表明教师质量是最重要的变量，但教师工会一直反对辞退不合格教师和提拔优秀教师。", "随着其他人为此付出的代价变得越来越清晰，政客们已开始采取强硬措施加以限制。在威斯康星州，工会聚集了成千上万名支持者，反对强硬派共和党州长斯科特·沃克。但公共部门内部的许多人也同样在现行体制下饱受其苦。", "哈佛大学肯尼迪学院的约翰·多纳休指出，西方公务员体系的文化规范适合那些想安于现状的人，但对高成就者却十分不利。美国公共部门中年薪远超25万美元的雇员，只有大学体育教练和美国总统。银行家丰厚的薪酬包招致了诸多批评，但一个不奖励高成就者的公共部门体制对美国而言或许是一个大得多的问题。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It can be learned from the first paragraph that", "options": ["Teamsters still have a large body of members.", "Jimmy Hoffa used to work as a civil servant.", "unions have enlarged their public-sector membership.", "the government has improved its relationship with unionists."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "When Hoffa's Teamsters were in their prime in 1960, only one in ten American government workers belonged to a union; now 36% do. In 2009 the number of unionists in America's public sector passed that of their fellow members in the private sector.", "explanation": "定位第一段第二、三句。1960年美国政府雇员加入工会的比例仅为十分之一，如今已上升到36%，且2009年美国公共部门工会成员总数超过了私营部门；紧接着还补充英国公共部门入会率超半数。这组时间对比和数据增长直接表明，工会在公共部门的成员规模不断扩大，对应C项中enlarged their public-sector membership的同义转述。", "trapNote": "A项将1960年Teamsters处于鼎盛时期偷换为“如今依然成员庞大”，属于时态错位；B项曲解虚拟语气，原文仅假设霍法若在世可能代表公务员，并非曾任公务员。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is true of Paragraph 2?", "options": ["Public-sector unions are prudent in taking actions.", "Education is required for public-sector union membership.", "Labor Party has long been fighting against public-sector unions.", "Public-sector unions seldom get in trouble for their actions."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "First, they can shut things down without suffering much in the way of consequences.", "explanation": "定位第二段第二句，文章阐述公共部门工会蓬勃发展的第一条原因时指出，他们能够让事务停摆却无需承受太多后果（without suffering much in the way of consequences）。其中without suffering much...consequences同义替换为D项的seldom get in trouble for their actions，说明其行动很少给自己招致麻烦。", "trapNote": "B项把“成员大多受过良好教育、四分之一拥有大学学位”绝对化为“入会门槛”；C项正反混淆，原文指出工党长期与工会主义紧密相连且领袖依赖工会选票，而非与之对抗。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It can be learned from Paragraph 4 that the income in the state sector is", "options": ["illegally secured.", "indirectly augmented.", "excessively increased.", "fairly adjusted."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Politicians have repeatedly \"backloaded\" public-sector pay deals, keeping the pay increases modest but adding to holidays and especially pensions that are already generous.", "explanation": "定位第四段第二、三句。作者指出公共部门真正的收益在于福利和工作惯例（real gains come in benefits），政客屡次对薪酬协议采取“后置支付”，即保持明面加薪温和，却不断增加本已优厚的假期尤其是养老金。这种不直接涨基本工资、而通过福利和养老金变相提高待遇的做法，正是B项indirectly augmented（间接增加）的精准概括。", "trapNote": "A项“非法获取”无中生有，政客妥协的薪酬协议虽不合理但合法；C项易受“工资高于私营部门”误导，但原文明确指出账面加薪幅度保持温和（modest），并非单纯过度涨薪。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "例证题", "stem": "The example of the unions in Wisconsin shows that unions", "options": ["often run against the current political system.", "can change people's political attitudes.", "may be a barrier to public-sector reforms.", "are dominant in the government."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "As the cost to everyone else has become clearer, politicians have begun to clamp down. In Wisconsin the unions have rallied thousands of supporters against Scott Walker, the hardline Republican governor.", "explanation": "本题为例证题，需结合第四段末尾及第五段首句论点作答。第四段指出工会激烈反对教育等领域的改革，第五段首句进而说明随着代价愈发明显，政客开始出手限制（clamp down），紧接着便举出威斯康星州工会集结数千名支持者抗议强硬派州长斯科特·沃克的例子。该例证意在说明工会往往会抵制并阻碍公共部门改革的推进，对应C项。", "trapNote": "A项将反对州长的限制措施过度拔高为“对抗现行政治体制”；D项把第二段“主导中左翼政坛”与州预算受监督偷换为“在政府中占主导”，且威斯康星州案例正体现双方的对抗而非统治。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "John Donahue's attitude towards the public-sector system is one of", "options": ["disapproval.", "appreciation.", "tolerance.", "indifference."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "John Donahue at Harvard's Kennedy School points out that the norms of culture in Western civil services suit those who want to stay put but is bad for high achievers.", "explanation": "定位第六段第一句及段末总结。约翰·多纳休明确指出，西方公务员体系的文化规范只适合安于现状者，却对高成就者十分不利（is bad for high achievers），随后指出美国公共部门极少有高薪岗位，无法激励拔尖人才可能是一个大得多的问题。其中bad for与bigger problem直接传达出多纳休对现行公共部门体制的不满与反对态度，故选A项disapproval。", "trapNote": "C项tolerance（容忍）和D项indifference（漠不关心）属于考研态度题常见的弱干扰或无关项，学者在文中明确使用负面评价词指出体制弊端，并未保持中立或容忍。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 组织工会；加入工会", "note": "第一段are unionized表示“加入了工会”，派生自union（工会）", "word": "unionize"}, {"gloss": "v. 巡逻；严密监督，把守", "note": "第三段is patrolled by unions形象地表示州预算被工会严密盯防把控", "word": "patrol"}, {"gloss": "v. 后置支付，延迟兑现（薪酬福利）", "note": "第四段指压低当前明面工资涨幅，而将丰厚回报转入日后养老金等福利", "word": "backload"}, {"gloss": "adj. 持久的，拖延的，漫长的", "note": "第四段drawn-out battles形容围绕教育改革展开的旷日持久的拉锯战", "word": "drawn-out"}, {"gloss": "v. 镇压，取缔，严加限制", "note": "第五段politicians have begun to clamp down指政客开始出手遏制工会势力", "word": "clamp down"}, {"gloss": "phr. 原地不动，安于现状", "note": "第六段those who want to stay put指在公务员体系中安稳混日子、不求冒尖的人", "word": "stay put"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Politicians have repeatedly \"backloaded\" public-sector pay deals, keeping the pay increases modest but adding to holidays and especially pensions that are already generous.", "point": "分词短语keeping...but adding to...具体解释前文backloaded的含义；注意that引导的定语从句修饰pensions（及holidays）。", "structure": "主句(Politicians have repeatedly \"backloaded\"...) + 现在分词短语作伴随状语(keeping...but adding to...) + that引导的定语从句修饰holidays and especially pensions", "zh": "政客们一再对公共部门的薪酬协议采取“后置支付”策略，使账面加薪幅度保持温和，却不断增加本已优厚的假期，尤其是养老金福利。"}, {"en": "Even though there is plenty of evidence that the quality of the teachers is the most important variable, teachers' unions have fought against getting rid of bad ones and promoting good ones.", "point": "evidence后接that同位语从句解释具体证据内容；against后接两个并列动名词短语getting rid of...和promoting...作宾语。", "structure": "Even though引导的让步状语从句(含that引导的同位语从句修饰evidence) + 主句(teachers' unions have fought against...)", "zh": "尽管有充分证据表明教师质量是最重要的变量，但教师工会一直反对辞退不合格教师和提拔优秀教师。"}, {"en": "Bankers' fat pay packets have attracted much criticism, but a public-sector system that does not reward high achievers may be a much bigger problem for America.", "point": "通过与银行家高薪的对比形成转折，that定语从句界定公共部门体制的核心缺陷，点明全文收尾主旨。", "structure": "分句1(Bankers' fat pay packets...) + but转折分句2(a public-sector system [that does not reward high achievers] may be...)", "zh": "银行家丰厚的薪酬包招致了诸多批评，但一个不奖励高成就者的公共部门体制对美国而言或许是一个大得多的问题。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "比例上升与人数超越具体体现了公共部门工会成员规模的扩大", "option": "enlarged their public-sector membership", "original": "now 36% do... the number of unionists in America's public sector passed that of their fellow members in the private sector"}, {"note": "“无需承担多少后果”同义转述为“很少因行动惹上麻烦”", "option": "seldom get in trouble for their actions", "original": "without suffering much in the way of consequences"}, {"note": "明面加薪有限而增加隐性福利，对应“间接增加”收入", "option": "indirectly augmented", "original": "keeping the pay increases modest but adding to holidays and especially pensions"}, {"note": "集结支持者反对强硬派州长削减福利，例证工会阻挠公共部门改革", "option": "a barrier to public-sector reforms", "original": "rallied thousands of supporters against Scott Walker"}, {"note": "负向评价词is bad for直接体现不赞成（disapproval）的态度", "option": "disapproval", "original": "is bad for high achievers"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2011-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2011", "examSet": "2011 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2011 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "纽约爱乐新任指挥与古典乐坛危机", "subtitle": "由艾伦·吉尔伯特履新探讨现场古典音乐会在唱片时代面临的挑战与出路", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 423, "paragraphs": ["The decision of the New York Philharmonic to hire Alan Gilbert as its next music director has been the talk of the classical-music world ever since the sudden announcement of his appointment in 2009. For the most part, the response has been favorable, to say the least. \"Hooray! At last!\" wrote Anthony Tommasini, a sober sided classical-music critic.", "One of the reasons why the appointment came as such a surprise, however, is that Gilbert is comparatively little known. Even Tommasini, who had advocated Gilbert's appointment in the Times, calls him \"an unpretentious musician with no air of the formidable conductor about him.\" As a description of the next music director of an orchestra that has hitherto been led by musicians like Gustav Mahler and Pierre Boulez, that seems likely to have struck at least some Times readers as faint praise. For my part, I have no idea whether Gilbert is a great conductor or even a good one. To be sure, he performs an impressive variety of interesting compositions, but it is not necessary for me to visit Avery Fisher Hall, or anywhere else, to hear interesting orchestral music. All I have to do is to go to my CD shelf, or boot up my computer and download still more recorded music from iTunes.", "Devoted concertgoers who reply that recordings are no substitute for live performance are missing the point. For the time, attention, and money of the art loving public, classical instrumentalists must compete not only with opera houses, dance troupes, theater companies, and museums, but also with the recorded performances of the great classical musicians of the 20th century. These recordings are cheap, available everywhere, and very often much higher in artistic quality than today's live performances; moreover, they can be \"consumed\" at a time and place of the listener's choosing. The widespread availability of such recordings has thus brought about a crisis in the institution of the traditional classical concert. One possible response is for classical performers to program attractive new music that is not yet available on record. Gilbert's own interest in new music has been widely noted: Alex Ross, a classical-music critic, has described him as a man who is capable of turning the Philharmonic into \"a markedly different, more vibrant organization.\" But what will be the nature of that difference? Merely expanding the orchestra's repertoire will not be enough. If Gilbert and the Philharmonic are to succeed, they must first change the relationship between America's oldest orchestra and the new audience it hopes to attract."], "translations": ["纽约爱乐乐团决定聘请艾伦·吉尔伯特担任下一任音乐总监，自2009年这一任命突然宣布以来，此事一直是古典音乐界热议的话题。在很大程度上，外界的反应至少可以说是积极的。“太好了！终于等到了！”一向冷静克制的古典音乐评论家安东尼·托马西尼写道。", "然而，这一任命之所以如此出人意料，原因之一在于吉尔伯特的知名度相对较低。就连曾在《泰晤士报》上力主任命吉尔伯特的托马西尼，也称他为“一位毫无架子、没有大牌指挥家派头的音乐家”。对于一个此前曾由古斯塔夫·马勒和皮埃尔·布列兹等音乐大师执棒的乐团而言，用这样的话来形容下一任音乐总监，似乎很可能让至少一部分《泰晤士报》读者觉得这只是勉强夸赞。就我个人而言，我不知道吉尔伯特算不算一位伟大的指挥家，甚至不知道他算不算一位优秀的指挥家。诚然，他演出过种类丰富、令人印象深刻的有趣曲目，但我完全没有必要去艾弗里·费舍尔音乐厅或任何其他地方欣赏有趣的管弦乐。我只需要走到我的CD架前，或者启动电脑从iTunes下载更多录制的音乐就行了。", "那些反驳说录音无法替代现场演出的忠实音乐会听众，并没有抓住重点。为了争夺热爱艺术的公众的时间、关注度和金钱，古典器乐演奏家不仅要与歌剧院、舞蹈团、剧团和博物馆竞争，还必须与20世纪伟大古典音乐家录制的演奏唱片竞争。这些唱片价格低廉、随处可得，而且在艺术水准上往往远高于如今的现场演出；此外，听众还可以自由选择时间与地点来“消费”这些录音。因此，此类唱片的广泛普及给传统古典音乐会这一形式带来了危机。一种可能的应对之道，是古典音乐演奏者安排尚未录制发行的新颖动听曲目。吉尔伯特本人对新音乐的兴趣已广受关注：古典音乐评论家亚历克斯·罗斯曾形容他是一个有能力将纽约爱乐乐团变成“一个截然不同、更具活力的团体”的人。但这种改变的本质究竟会是什么？仅仅扩大乐团的曲目库是不够的。如果吉尔伯特和纽约爱乐乐团想要取得成功，他们首先必须改变这个美国历史最悠久的乐团与其希望吸引的新听众之间的关系。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "We learn from Paragraph 1 that Gilbert's appointment has", "options": ["incurred criticism.", "raised suspicion.", "received acclaim.", "aroused curiosity."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "For the most part, the response has been favorable, to say the least. \"Hooray! At last!\" wrote Anthony Tommasini, a sober sided classical-music critic.", "explanation": "定位至第一段第二、三句。文中指出，对于纽约爱乐乐团任命吉尔伯特为下任音乐总监一事，外界反应“在很大程度上至少可以说是积极的”（favorable, to say the least），随后引用评论家托马西尼“太好了！终于等到了！”的欢呼作为佐证。选项C中的received acclaim（受到赞扬/好评）正是对response has been favorable的同义改写，故选C。", "trapNote": "A（招致批评）与原文favorable表意完全相反；D（引起好奇）偷换概念，第一段提及此事是业界热议话题（talk of the world），但重点强调的是积极赞许而非单纯的好奇。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Tommasini regards Gilbert as an artist who is", "options": ["influential.", "modest.", "respectable.", "talented."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Even Tommasini, who had advocated Gilbert's appointment in the Times, calls him \"an unpretentious musician with no air of the formidable conductor about him.\"", "explanation": "定位至第二段第二句。题干询问托马西尼对吉尔伯特的评价。原文引用他在《泰晤士报》上的话，称吉尔伯特是一位“不炫耀、没有大牌指挥家派头的音乐家”（an unpretentious musician with no air of the formidable conductor about him）。其中unpretentious意为“谦逊的、不摆架子的”，与选项B中的modest（谦虚的）构成精准同义替换，故选B。", "trapNote": "A（有影响力的）与第一段中提及吉尔伯特“知名度相对较低（comparatively little known）”相悖；C（值得尊敬的）和D（有才华的）均未体现unpretentious所指的“谦逊不张扬”核心特征。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "The author believes that the devoted concertgoers", "options": ["ignore the expenses of live performances.", "reject most kinds of recorded performances.", "exaggerate the variety of live performances.", "overestimate the value of live performances."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Devoted concertgoers who reply that recordings are no substitute for live performance are missing the point.", "explanation": "定位至第三段第一至三句。忠实音乐会听众认为“录音无法替代现场演出”，但作者直言他们“没有抓住重点”（missing the point），并随即指出唱片价格低廉且艺术水准往往“远高于如今的现场演出”（much higher in artistic quality than today's live performances）。由此可知，作者认为这些听众高估了现场演出的价值，对应D项overestimate the value of live performances。", "trapNote": "A（忽视现场演出费用）属于无中生有，文中虽提到唱片cheap，但未说明听众忽视现场票价；B（排斥大多数录音）过度绝对，听众只是认为录音不能替代现场，并非全盘排斥。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to the text, which of the following is true of recordings?", "options": ["They are often inferior to live concerts in quality.", "They are easily accessible to the general public.", "They help improve the quality of music.", "They have only covered masterpieces."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "These recordings are cheap, available everywhere, and very often much higher in artistic quality than today's live performances; moreover, they can be \"consumed\" at a time and place of the listener's choosing.", "explanation": "定位至第三段第三句。原文明确描述古典音乐录音具有价格便宜、随处可得（available everywhere）的特点，且听众可以随时随地欣赏（at a time and place of the listener's choosing），紧接着下一句又提到此类唱片的“广泛普及”（widespread availability）。选项B中的easily accessible to the general public（大众很容易获取）精准对应available everywhere，故选B。", "trapNote": "A（质量常不如现场音乐会）与原文“often much higher in artistic quality”完全相反；C（有助于提升音乐品质）与D（只收录杰作）在文中均未提及，属于典型的无中生有。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "Regarding Gilbert's role in revitalizing the Philharmonic, the author feels", "options": ["doubtful.", "enthusiastic.", "confident.", "puzzled."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "But what will be the nature of that difference? Merely expanding the orchestra's repertoire will not be enough.", "explanation": "定位至第三段末尾及第二段后半部分。第二段作者先表明不知道吉尔伯特是否算优秀指挥家；第三段虽引用评论家称其能让乐团焕发活力，但随即以转折词But设问“这种改变的本质究竟会是什么？”，并指出仅仅扩大曲目库还不够，必须先改变乐团与新听众的关系。可见作者对其能否真正振兴纽约爱乐乐团持怀疑与审慎态度，对应A项doubtful。", "trapNote": "B（热情的）和C（自信的）与文中作者质疑性的反问及“will not be enough”的保留态度相悖；D（困惑的）曲解了反问句的修辞功能，作者是在质疑而非感到迷茫。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "n. 任命，委派", "note": "文中指艾伦·吉尔伯特出任纽约爱乐乐团音乐总监的任命（announce his appointment）。", "word": "appointment"}, {"gloss": "adj. 谦逊的，不炫耀的，朴实的", "note": "由前缀un-+pretentious（炫耀的）构成，文中托马西尼用来形容吉尔伯特毫无名家架子。", "word": "unpretentious"}, {"gloss": "adv. 迄今为止，到目前为止", "note": "正式书面语副词，文中指该乐团此前一直由马勒、布列兹等大师执棒。", "word": "hitherto"}, {"gloss": "adj. 忠实的，热衷的，献身的", "note": "devoted concertgoers指热爱并忠实于现场音乐会的听众。", "word": "devoted"}, {"gloss": "n. 全部保留曲目，演奏曲目库", "note": "指乐团或演奏家准备演出的全部曲目集合，文中指仅靠扩充新曲目库不足以解决危机。", "word": "repertoire"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "As a description of the next music director of an orchestra that has hitherto been led by musicians like Gustav Mahler and Pierre Boulez, that seems likely to have struck at least some Times readers as faint praise.", "point": "注意that seems likely to have struck...中不定式完成式to have struck表示对过去产生影响的推测；faint praise意为“勉强/冷淡的夸赞”。", "structure": "介词短语As a description of...作状语（内含that引导的定语从句修饰orchestra） + 主句that seems likely to have struck...（strike sb. as...意为“给某人留下……印象”）", "zh": "对于一个此前曾由古斯塔夫·马勒和皮埃尔·布列兹等音乐大师执棒的乐团而言，用这样的话来形容下一任音乐总监，似乎很可能让至少一部分《泰晤士报》读者觉得这只是勉强夸赞。"}, {"en": "For the time, attention, and money of the art loving public, classical instrumentalists must compete not only with opera houses, dance troupes, theater companies, and museums, but also with the recorded performances of the great classical musicians of the 20th century.", "point": "把握not only with...but also with...的并列结构，理解古典音乐现场演出面临的“外部艺术形式”与“历史经典录音”双重竞争。", "structure": "介词短语For...作目的状语 + 主句classical instrumentalists must compete + not only with...but also with...并列介词短语作状语", "zh": "为了争夺热爱艺术的公众的时间、关注度和金钱，古典器乐演奏家不仅要与歌剧院、舞蹈团、剧团和博物馆竞争，还必须与20世纪伟大古典音乐家录制的演奏唱片竞争。"}, {"en": "Gilbert's own interest in new music has been widely noted: Alex Ross, a classical-music critic, has described him as a man who is capable of turning the Philharmonic into \"a markedly different, more vibrant organization.\"", "point": "注意冒号后的内容是对前句的举例阐释，同时turn...into...结构体现了评论家对吉尔伯特改革潜力的期待。", "structure": "主句Gilbert's own interest... + 冒号后解释说明句（含同位语a classical-music critic与who引导的定语从句修饰a man）", "zh": "吉尔伯特本人对新音乐的兴趣已广受关注：古典音乐评论家亚历克斯·罗斯曾形容他是一个有能力将纽约爱乐乐团变成“一个截然不同、更具活力的团体”的人。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "反应是积极肯定的 → 受到赞扬/好评", "option": "received acclaim", "original": "the response has been favorable"}, {"note": "不炫耀、没有架子 → 谦逊的", "option": "modest", "original": "an unpretentious musician with no air of the formidable conductor"}, {"note": "只看重现场演出而忽视高水准录音 → 高估了现场演出的价值", "option": "overestimate the value of live performances", "original": "recordings are no substitute for live performance are missing the point... much higher in artistic quality"}, {"note": "随处可得 → 大众很容易获取", "option": "easily accessible to the general public", "original": "available everywhere"}, {"note": "以反问和条件不足质疑举措效果 → 持怀疑态度", "option": "doubtful", "original": "what will be the nature of that difference? Merely expanding... will not be enough."}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2011-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2011", "examSet": "2011 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2011 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "企业高管“裸辞”潮与职场新法则", "subtitle": "分析越来越多公司高管不再“骑驴找马”而是辞职追寻CEO职位的原因与趋势", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 437, "paragraphs": ["When Liam McGee departed as president of Bank of America in August, his explanation was surprisingly straight up. Rather than cloaking his exit in the usual vague excuses, he came right out and said he was leaving \"to pursue my goal of running a company.\" Broadcasting his ambition was \"very much my decision,\" McGee says. Within two weeks, he was talking for the first time with the board of Hartford Financial Services Group, which named him CEO and chairman on September 29.", "McGee says leaving without a position lined up gave him time to reflect on what kind of company he wanted to run. It also sent a clear message to the outside world about his aspirations. And McGee isn't alone. In recent weeks the No.2 executives at Avon and American Express quit with the explanation that they were looking for a CEO post. As boards scrutinize succession plans in response to shareholder pressure, executives who don't get the nod also may wish to move on. A turbulent business environment also has senior managers cautious of letting vague pronouncements cloud their reputations.", "As the first signs of recovery begin to take hold, deputy chiefs may be more willing to make the jump without a net. In the third quarter, CEO turnover was down 23% from a year ago as nervous boards stuck with the leaders they had, according to Liberum Research. As the economy picks up, opportunities will abound for aspiring leaders.", "The decision to quit a senior position to look for a better one is unconventional. For years executives and headhunters have adhered to the rule that the most attractive CEO candidates are the ones who must be poached. Says Korn/Ferry senior partner Dennis Carey: \"I can't think of a single search I've done where a board has not instructed me to look at sitting CEOs first.\"", "Those who jumped without a job haven't always landed in top positions quickly. Ellen Marram quit as chief of Tropicana a decade ago, saying she wanted to be a CEO. It was a year before she became head of a tiny Internet-based commodities exchange. Robert Willumstad left Citigroup in 2005 with ambitions to be a CEO. He finally took that post at a major financial institution three years later.", "Many recruiters say the old disgrace is fading for top performers. The financial crisis has made it more acceptable to be between jobs or to leave a bad one. \"The traditional rule was it's safer to stay where you are, but that's been fundamentally inverted,\" says one headhunter. \"The people who've been hurt the worst are those who've stayed too long.\""], "translations": ["当利亚姆·麦基在8月辞去美国银行总裁一职时，他的解释直白得令人意外。他没有用通常那种含糊其辞的借口来掩饰自己的离开，而是直截了当地表示，他离职是“为了追求自己执掌一家公司的目标”。麦基表示，公开表达自己的抱负“完全是我个人的决定”。不到两周后，他便首次与哈特福德金融服务集团董事会展开洽谈，该集团于9月29日任命他为首席执行官兼董事长。", "麦基说，在还没有找好下家时就离职，让他有时间思考自己究竟想执掌什么样的公司。这也向外界明确传递了关于他职业抱负的信号。而且麦基并非孤例。近几周，雅芳公司和美国运通公司的二把手纷纷辞职，理由是他们正在寻找首席执行官的职位。随着董事会在股东压力下严格审视继任计划，那些未能获得青睐的高管或许也想另谋高就。动荡的商业环境也让高级管理人员担心，含糊不清的声明会损害自己的声誉。", "随着经济复苏的初步迹象开始显现，副手们或许更愿意冒着没有退路的风险跳槽。据利伯姆研究公司的数据，第三季度首席执行官的离职率同比下降了23%，原因是焦虑的董事会选择继续留用现有的领导者。随着经济好转，有抱负的领导者将迎来大量机会。", "辞去高级职位去寻找更好职位的决定并不符合常规。多年来，高管和猎头一直信奉这样一条准则：最具吸引力的首席执行官人选必须是那些需要去“挖角”的在职高管。光辉国际高级合伙人丹尼斯·凯里说：“在我经手的所有招聘中，我想不出有哪一次董事会没有指示我优先物色在任的首席执行官。”", "那些没有找好下家就辞职的人，并不总能迅速坐上最高职位。十年前，埃伦·马拉姆辞去了纯果乐公司首席执行官的职务，并表示自己想成为另一家公司的首席执行官。结果一年后，她才成为一家小型互联网大宗商品交易所的负责人。罗伯特·威勒姆斯塔德于2005年怀揣成为首席执行官的抱负离开了花旗集团。三年后，他终于在一家大型金融机构担任了这一职务。", "许多招聘人员表示，对于顶尖人才而言，过去那种“失业即丢脸”的观念正在消退。金融危机使得处于待业状态或离开一家糟糕的公司变得更容易被接受。“过去的传统法则是留在原位更安全，但如今这一法则已经彻底颠倒了，”一位猎头说，“受到伤害最深的，反而是那些在同一职位上待得太久的人。”"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "When McGee announced his departure, his manner can best be described as being", "options": ["arrogant.", "frank.", "self-centered.", "impulsive."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "When Liam McGee departed as president of Bank of America in August, his explanation was surprisingly straight up. Rather than cloaking his exit in the usual vague excuses, he came right out and said he was leaving \"to pursue my goal of running a company.\"", "explanation": "定位至第一段第一、二句。文中指出，麦基在辞去美国银行总裁一职时，他的解释“直白得令人意外”（surprisingly straight up），没有用惯常的含糊借口遮掩，而是“直截了当地说出”（came right out and said）离职是为了追求执掌公司的目标。选项B中的frank（坦率的、直白的）正是对straight up和came right out的同义替换，故选B。", "trapNote": "A（傲慢的）和C（以自我为中心的）均属于过度负面解读，原文仅客观描述他坦诚说明职业规划；D（冲动的）与原文不符，公开表达抱负是他的慎重决定。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, senior executives' quitting may be spurred by", "options": ["their expectation of better financial status.", "their need to reflect on their private life.", "their strained relations with the boards.", "their pursuit of new career goals."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "In recent weeks the No.2 executives at Avon and American Express quit with the explanation that they were looking for a CEO post. As boards scrutinize succession plans in response to shareholder pressure, executives who don't get the nod also may wish to move on.", "explanation": "定位至第二段第四、五句。文中先以麦基为例说明辞职给了他反思想执掌何种公司的机会并传递抱负信号，随后指出雅芳与美国运通的二把手辞职是因为“正在寻找CEO职位”，而在继任计划中未获董事会青睐（don't get the nod）的高管也可能想另谋高就（move on）。这都说明高管辞职是受追求新职业目标所驱使，对应D项their pursuit of new career goals。", "trapNote": "A（期待更好的财务状况）文中未提及薪酬待遇；B（反思私人生活）偷换概念，原文是反思想经营什么公司；C（与董事会关系紧张）过度推断，未获继任提名不等于关系紧张。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The word \"poached\" (Line 3, Paragraph 4) most probably means", "options": ["approved of.", "attended to.", "hunted for.", "guarded against."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "For years executives and headhunters have adhered to the rule that the most attractive CEO candidates are the ones who must be poached. Says Korn/Ferry senior partner Dennis Carey: \"I can't think of a single search I've done where a board has not instructed me to look at sitting CEOs first.\"", "explanation": "定位至第四段第二、三句。上文提到高管辞去现有高位去寻找更好职位是不合常规的（unconventional），因为长期以来高管和猎头遵循的准则是最具吸引力的CEO候选人必须是“在职且需要被挖角”的人；下文凯里的话进一步印证，董事会总是要求先物色在任CEO（look at sitting CEOs first）。因此poached在此指“从别处挖来、搜寻物色”，与C项hunted for（猎取、物色）同义。", "trapNote": "A（赞成）、B（照料/关注）和D（提防）均无法体现“主动从原公司把在任高管挖过来”这一猎头招聘语境，且与下文search和look at sitting CEOs的语义线索不符。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It can be inferred from the last paragraph that", "options": ["top performers used to cling to their posts.", "loyalty of top performers is getting out-dated.", "top performers care more about reputations.", "it's safer to stick to the traditional rules."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "\"The traditional rule was it's safer to stay where you are, but that's been fundamentally inverted,\" says one headhunter. \"The people who've been hurt the worst are those who've stayed too long.\"", "explanation": "定位至最后一段第三、四句。文中一位猎头指出：“过去的传统法则是留在原位更安全（it's safer to stay where you are），但如今这一法则已经彻底颠倒了”，而且受伤害最深的是“在原位待得太久的人（stayed too long）”。由此可以合理推断，过去那些顶尖人才往往会坚守并恋栈自己的原有职位，对应A项top performers used to cling to their posts。", "trapNote": "B（顶尖人才的忠诚正在过时）偷换概念，文中谈论的是“留在原位求稳”还是“主动离职谋求新机会”，而非道德层面的忠诚；D（坚持传统法则更安全）与“fundamentally inverted”完全相反。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following is the best title for the text?", "options": ["CEOs: Where to Go?", "CEOs: All the Way Up?", "Top Managers Jump without a Net", "The Only Way Out for Top Performers"], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "As the first signs of recovery begin to take hold, deputy chiefs may be more willing to make the jump without a net.", "explanation": "通读全文，文章开篇以麦基未找好下家便辞去美国银行总裁为例，继而分析二把手和高管们纷纷选择“无保护伞跳槽（裸辞）”的原因，再对比传统“只挖在职高管”的法则，最后指出金融危机后待业羞耻感消退、“留守反而受损”的新趋势。第三段中的make the jump without a net高度概括了全文核心现象，对应C项Top Managers Jump without a Net，作标题最贴切。", "trapNote": "A和B将主体限定为CEOs，而文中辞职寻找机会的多数是总裁、二把手（deputy chiefs）等高管；D中的The Only Way Out（唯一出路）过于绝对，原文并未将“裸辞”说成唯一选择。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 掩饰，遮掩（n. 斗篷）", "note": "文中用于cloak his exit in the usual vague excuses，形象地表示用借口掩盖真实离职原因。", "word": "cloak"}, {"gloss": "v. 仔细检查，严格审视", "note": "文中指董事会在股东压力下严格审视高管继任计划（succession plans）。", "word": "scrutinize"}, {"gloss": "adj. 非常规的，打破常规的", "note": "由un-+conventional构成，形容辞去高级职位再去寻找更好职位的“裸辞”做法。", "word": "unconventional"}, {"gloss": "v. 挖角，挖走（人才）；偷猎", "note": "原义为偷猎，职场语境中常指猎头或企业从竞争对手处挖走优秀高管。", "word": "poach"}, {"gloss": "v. 使颠倒，使倒置", "note": "文中指“留在原位更安全”这一传统职场法则已被彻底颠倒（fundamentally inverted）。", "word": "invert"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Rather than cloaking his exit in the usual vague excuses, he came right out and said he was leaving \"to pursue my goal of running a company.\"", "point": "cloak...in...意为“用……掩饰……”；came right out and said表达“开门见山地直接说出”，与前句straight up呼应。", "structure": "介词短语Rather than cloaking...作状语 + 主句he came right out and said + 省略that的宾语从句（含不定式作目的状语）", "zh": "他没有用通常那种含糊其辞的借口来掩饰自己的离开，而是直截了当地表示，他离职是“为了追求自己执掌一家公司的目标”。"}, {"en": "As boards scrutinize succession plans in response to shareholder pressure, executives who don't get the nod also may wish to move on.", "point": "get the nod是地道习语，意为“得到批准/认可/提名”；move on在此指离开现任岗位另谋发展。", "structure": "As引导的时间/原因状语从句 + 主句executives（含who引导的定语从句）+ may wish to move on", "zh": "随着董事会在股东压力下严格审视继任计划，那些未能获得青睐的高管或许也想另谋高就。"}, {"en": "For years executives and headhunters have adhered to the rule that the most attractive CEO candidates are the ones who must be poached.", "point": "adhere to意为“坚持、信奉”；that引导同位语从句解释说明the rule的具体内容，在从句中不作成分。", "structure": "时间状语For years + 主句executives and headhunters have adhered to the rule + that引导的同位语从句（内含who引导的定语从句）", "zh": "多年来，高管和猎头一直信奉这样一条准则：最具吸引力的首席执行官人选必须是那些需要去“挖角”的在职高管。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "直白且开门见山 → 坦率的", "option": "frank", "original": "his explanation was surprisingly straight up... came right out and said"}, {"note": "寻找CEO职位或另谋高就 → 追求新的职业目标", "option": "their pursuit of new career goals", "original": "looking for a CEO post... executives who don't get the nod also may wish to move on"}, {"note": "从别处挖角在职人员 → 猎取、物色", "option": "hunted for", "original": "the ones who must be poached... look at sitting CEOs first"}, {"note": "传统认为留在原位更安全 → 顶尖人才过去常恋栈原有职位", "option": "top performers used to cling to their posts", "original": "The traditional rule was it's safer to stay where you are"}, {"note": "副手们愿意没有退路地跳槽 → 高管“裸辞”跳槽", "option": "Top Managers Jump without a Net", "original": "deputy chiefs may be more willing to make the jump without a net"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2011-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2011", "examSet": "2011 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2011 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "超越付费媒体的多元营销新格局", "subtitle": "解析赢得媒体、自有媒体、售出媒体与被劫持媒体对当代营销的影响", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 447, "paragraphs": ["The rough guide to marketing success used to be that you got what you paid for. No longer. While traditional \"paid\" media - such as television commercials and print advertisements - still play a major role, companies today can exploit many alternative forms of media. Consumers passionate about a product may create \"earned\" media by willingly promoting it to friends, and a company may leverage \"owned\" media by sending e-mail alerts about products and sales to customers registered with its Web site. The way consumers now approach the process of making purchase decisions means that marketing's impact stems from a broad range of factors beyond conventional paid media.", "Paid and owned media are controlled by marketers promoting their own products. For earned media, such marketers act as the initiator for users' responses. But in some cases, one marketer's owned media become another marketer's paid media - for instance, when an e-commerce retailer sells ad space on its Web site. We define such sold media as owned media whose traffic is so strong that other organizations place their content or e-commerce engines within that environment. This trend, which we believe is still in its infancy, effectively began with retailers and travel providers such as airlines and hotels and will no doubt go further. Johnson & Johnson, for example, has created BabyCenter, a stand-alone media property that promotes complementary and even competitive products. Besides generating income, the presence of other marketers makes the site seem objective, gives companies opportunities to learn valuable information about the appeal of other companies' marketing, and may help expand user traffic for all companies concerned.", "The same dramatic technological changes that have provided marketers with more (and more diverse) communications choices have also increased the risk that passionate consumers will voice their opinions in quicker, more visible, and much more damaging ways. Such hijacked media are the opposite of earned media: an asset or campaign becomes hostage to consumers, other stakeholders, or activists who make negative allegations about a brand or product. Members of social networks, for instance, are learning that they can hijack media to apply pressure on the businesses that originally created them.", "If that happens, passionate consumers would try to persuade others to boycott products, putting the reputation of the target company at risk. In such a case, the company's response may not be sufficiently quick or thoughtful, and the learning curve has been steep. Toyota Motor, for example, alleviated some of the damage from its recall crisis earlier this year with a relatively quick and well-orchestrated social media response campaign, which included efforts to engage with consumers directly on sites such as Twitter and the social-news site Digg."], "translations": ["关于营销成功的粗略准则过去曾是“一分钱一分货”，但如今已不再如此。尽管电视商业广告和平面广告等传统“付费”媒体依然扮演着重要角色，如今的企业却可以利用许多替代性的媒体形式。对某款产品充满热情的消费者可能会通过主动向朋友推荐该产品来创造“赢得”媒体；而企业也可以通过向在其网站上注册的客户发送产品及促销邮件提醒来利用“自有”媒体。消费者如今处理购买决策的方式，意味着营销的影响力源于传统付费媒体之外的广泛因素。", "付费媒体和自有媒体都由推广自身产品的营销人员所控制。对于赢得媒体而言，这类营销人员则充当用户反应的发起者。但在某些情况下，一家营销人员的自有媒体会变成另一家营销人员的付费媒体——例如，当一家电子商务零售商在其网站上出售广告位时。我们将这种“售出媒体”定义为：自身流量极其庞大，以至于其他机构将自己的内容或电商引擎植入该环境中的自有媒体。我们认为这一趋势仍处于起步阶段，它实际上始于零售商以及航空公司、酒店等旅游服务提供商，而且无疑还将进一步发展。例如，强生公司创建了“宝宝中心”（BabyCenter），这是一个独立的媒体平台，用于推广互补性甚至竞争性的产品。除了创造收入外，其他营销商的入驻还使该网站显得客观，让企业有机会了解其他公司营销手段吸引力的宝贵信息，并可能有助于扩大所有相关企业的用户流量。", "同样是那些为营销人员提供了更多（也更多元）传播选择的剧烈技术变革，也增加了充满激情的消费者以更迅速、更显眼且更具破坏性的方式表达意见的风险。这种“被劫持”媒体恰恰是赢得媒体的反面：某项品牌资产或营销活动沦为消费者、其他利益相关者或活动人士的人质，这些人会对某一品牌或产品提出负面指控。例如，社交网络的成员正在逐渐意识到，他们可以劫持媒体，向最初创建这些媒体的企业施加压力。", "一旦发生这种情况，充满激情的消费者就会试图说服他人抵制相关产品，从而将目标企业的声誉置于危险境地。在此类情况下，企业的回应可能不够迅速或周全，而且学习适应的过程一直十分陡峭。例如，丰田汽车今年早些时候通过一场相对迅速且精心策划的社交媒体回应活动，减轻了召回危机带来的部分损失，其中包括在推特和社交新闻网站Digg等平台上直接与消费者互动的举措。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Consumers may create \"earned\" media when they are", "options": ["obsessed with online shopping at certain Web sites.", "inspired by product-promoting e-mails sent to them.", "eager to help their friends promote quality products.", "enthusiastic about recommending their favorite products."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Consumers passionate about a product may create \"earned\" media by willingly promoting it to friends", "explanation": "定位至第1段第3句。原文指出，对产品充满热情的消费者通过自愿向朋友推广来创造“赢得媒体”，从而影响购买决策。D项中的“热衷于推荐心仪产品”与原文中passionate及willingly promoting形成精准的同义对应，符合“赢得媒体”的产生条件。其余选项分别混淆了网购沉迷、企业邮件促销或帮助朋友，故D正确。", "trapNote": "B项“受促销邮件启发”对应的是紧随其后的“自有媒体”（owned media），属于张冠李戴；C项“急于帮朋友推广优质产品”偷换了主客体与动机，原文强调消费者因喜爱产品而向朋友推荐。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, sold media feature", "options": ["a safe business environment.", "random competition.", "strong user traffic.", "flexibility in organization."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "We define such sold media as owned media whose traffic is so strong that other organizations place their content or e-commerce engines within that environment.", "explanation": "定位至第2段第4句。作者将“售出媒体”定义为：自身的流量（traffic）极其庞大，以至于其他机构愿意将内容或电商引擎植入其中的“自有媒体”。由此可知，售出媒体的核心特征在于拥有强大的用户流量，即C项的strong user traffic。第2段虽提到零售商和旅游服务商，但并未将其特征归结为安全环境、随机竞争或组织灵活性。", "trapNote": "A项将原文中的“that environment”（指代自有媒体平台）曲解为“安全的商业环境”；D项则属于无中生有，文中仅提及在平台内植入电商引擎，未涉及“组织灵活性”。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "The author indicates in Paragraph 3 that earned media", "options": ["invite constant conflicts with passionate consumers.", "can be used to produce negative effects in marketing.", "may be responsible for fiercer competition.", "deserve all the negative comments about them."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Such hijacked media are the opposite of earned media: an asset or campaign becomes hostage to consumers, other stakeholders, or activists who make negative allegations about a brand or product.", "explanation": "定位至第3段。作者先指出技术变革为营销提供了更多传播选择，同时也增加了消费者迅速且更具破坏性地发声的风险；接着指出“被劫持媒体”正是“赢得媒体”的反面，即品牌资产受制于做出负面指控的消费者或活动人士。由此可推知，如同赢得媒体依托消费者自发传播一样，这种传播机制也能在营销中产生负面效应，B项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“招致与热情消费者的持续冲突”过于绝对且曲解文意；D项“活该受到所有负面评论”属于主观臆断，原文强调的是传播渠道被劫持带来的声誉风险，并未认为商家理应受责。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "例证题", "stem": "Toyota Motor's experience is cited as an example of", "options": ["responding effectively to hijacked media.", "persuading customers into boycotting products.", "cooperating with supportive consumers.", "taking advantage of hijacked media."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Toyota Motor, for example, alleviated some of the damage from its recall crisis earlier this year with a relatively quick and well-orchestrated social media response campaign, which included efforts to engage with consumers directly on sites such as Twitter and the social-news site Digg.", "explanation": "定位至第4段第3句。第3、4段指出当发生“被劫持媒体”事件、消费者号召抵制产品时，企业往往难以快速应对；随后第4段末句以Toyota Motor为例，说明其在召回危机中通过相对迅速且精心策划的社交媒体回应活动，直接与消费者互动从而减轻了部分损失。可见该例子旨在证明有效应对被劫持媒体的方法，A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项将前文消费者“劝说他人抵制产品”的行为张冠李戴到丰田身上；D项“利用被劫持媒体”曲解了事例意图，丰田是借官方社交媒体积极回应危机，而非利用负面舆论本身。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following is the text mainly about?", "options": ["Alternatives to conventional paid media.", "Conflict between hijacked and earned media.", "Dominance of hijacked media.", "Popularity of owned media."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "While traditional \"paid\" media - such as television commercials and print advertisements - still play a major role, companies today can exploit many alternative forms of media.", "explanation": "文章首段即点明主旨：虽然传统“付费媒体”仍发挥重要作用，但如今企业可以利用许多替代性的媒体形式，消费者的购买决策受传统付费媒体之外的多种因素影响。随后各段依次探讨了赢得媒体、自有媒体、售出媒体以及被劫持媒体这几类新型媒体的运作模式与风险。全文围绕传统付费媒体的替代方案展开，故A项最准确概括主旨。", "trapNote": "B、C项仅聚焦第3、4段提及的“被劫持媒体”，D项仅涉及“自有媒体”，均属于以偏概全的局部信息干扰，无法涵盖全篇对多种新型媒体的系统介绍。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 充分利用；开发", "note": "文中意为“充分利用（替代性媒体形式）”，并非贬义的“剥削”", "word": "exploit"}, {"gloss": "n. 发起者；创始人", "note": "由动词 initiate 派生，文中指营销人员在赢得媒体中扮演“发起者”角色", "word": "initiator"}, {"gloss": "adj. 互补的；补充的", "note": "注意区分形近词 complimentary（赞美的、免费的），文中与 competitive 并列", "word": "complementary"}, {"gloss": "n. （无证据的）指责，指控", "note": "常用于负面语境，文中指消费者或活动人士对品牌做出的负面指控", "word": "allegation"}, {"gloss": "v. 减轻，缓和", "note": "高频考研动词，常见搭配 alleviate damage / pain / pressure", "word": "alleviate"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "We define such sold media as owned media whose traffic is so strong that other organizations place their content or e-commerce engines within that environment.", "point": "定语从句套结果状语从句（whose ... so ... that ...）", "structure": "主干：We define such sold media as owned media；whose引导定语从句修饰owned media，其中包含so...that...引导的结果状语从句。", "zh": "我们将这种“售出媒体”定义为：自身流量极其庞大，以至于其他机构将自己的内容或电商引擎植入该环境中的自有媒体。"}, {"en": "The same dramatic technological changes that have provided marketers with more (and more diverse) communications choices have also increased the risk that passionate consumers will voice their opinions in quicker, more visible, and much more damaging ways.", "point": "插入语与定语从句、同位语从句的嵌套识别", "structure": "主干：The same dramatic technological changes have also increased the risk；that have provided...为定语从句修饰changes；risk后接that引导的同位语从句。", "zh": "同样是那些为营销人员提供了更多（也更多元）传播选择的剧烈技术变革，也增加了充满激情的消费者以更迅速、更显眼且更具破坏性的方式表达意见的风险。"}, {"en": "Toyota Motor, for example, alleviated some of the damage from its recall crisis earlier this year with a relatively quick and well-orchestrated social media response campaign, which included efforts to engage with consumers directly on sites such as Twitter and the social-news site Digg.", "point": "长介词短语作状语及which引导的非限制性定语从句", "structure": "主干：Toyota Motor alleviated some of the damage with a ... campaign；which引导非限制性定语从句补充说明campaign的具体内容。", "zh": "例如，丰田汽车今年早些时候通过一场相对迅速且精心策划的社交媒体回应活动，减轻了召回危机带来的部分损失，其中包括在推特和社交新闻网站Digg等平台上直接与消费者互动的举措。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "passionate 对应 enthusiastic；willingly promoting 对应 recommending", "option": "enthusiastic about recommending their favorite products", "original": "passionate about a product ... willingly promoting it to friends"}, {"note": "名词短语替换定语从句的核心语义", "option": "strong user traffic", "original": "owned media whose traffic is so strong"}, {"note": "具体破坏性行为抽象概括为“产生负面影响”", "option": "produce negative effects in marketing", "original": "voice their opinions in quicker, more visible, and much more damaging ways"}, {"note": "具体危机公关措施概括为“有效回应被劫持媒体”", "option": "responding effectively to hijacked media", "original": "alleviated some of the damage ... with a relatively quick and well-orchestrated social media response campaign"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2011-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2011", "examSet": "2011 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2011 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "育儿幸福感与名人母亲形象误导", "subtitle": "剖析养育子女的真实感受、社会生育文化与名人杂志营造的虚假育儿观", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 464, "paragraphs": ["It's no surprise that Jennifer Senior's insightful, provocative magazine cover story, \"I love My Children, I Hate My Life,\" is arousing much chatter - nothing gets people talking like the suggestion that child rearing is anything less than a completely fulfilling, life-enriching experience. Rather than concluding that children make parents either happy or miserable, Senior suggests we need to redefine happiness: instead of thinking of it as something that can be measured by moment-to-moment joy, we should consider being happy as a past-tense condition. Even though the day-to-day experience of raising kids can be soul-crushingly hard, Senior writes that \"the very things that in the moment dampen our moods can later be sources of intense gratification and delight.\"", "The magazine cover showing an attractive mother holding a cute baby is hardly the only Madonna-and-child image on newsstands this week. There are also stories about newly adoptive - and newly single - mom Sandra Bullock, as well as the usual \"Jennifer Aniston is pregnant\" news. Practically every week features at least one celebrity mom, or mom-to-be, smiling on the newsstands.", "In a society that so persistently celebrates procreation, is it any wonder that admitting you regret having children is equivalent to admitting you support kitten killing? It doesn't seem quite fair, then, to compare the regrets of parents to the regrets of the childless. Unhappy parents rarely are provoked to wonder if they shouldn't have had kids, but unhappy childless folks are bothered with the message that children are the single most important thing in the world: obviously their misery must be a direct result of the gaping baby-size holes in their lives.", "Of course, the image of parenthood that celebrity magazines like Us Weekly and People present is hugely unrealistic, especially when the parents are single mothers like Bullock. According to several studies concluding that parents are less happy than childless couples, single parents are the least happy of all. No shock there, considering how much work it is to raise a kid without a partner to lean on; yet to hear Sandra and Britney tell it, raising a kid on their \"own\" (read: with round-the-clock help) is a piece of cake.", "It's hard to imagine that many people are dumb enough to want children just because Reese and Angelina make it look so glamorous: most adults understand that a baby is not a haircut. But it's interesting to wonder if the images we see every week of stress-free, happiness-enhancing parenthood aren't in some small, subconscious way contributing to our own dissatisfactions with the actual experience, in the same way that a small part of us hoped getting \"the Rachel\" might make us look just a little bit like Jennifer Aniston."], "translations": ["詹妮弗·西尼尔那篇富有洞察力且发人深省的杂志封面报道《我爱我的孩子，我恨我的生活》引发了大量热议，这并不令人意外——没有什么比暗示育儿并非完全令人满足、充实人生的经历更能引起人们的讨论了。西尼尔并没有得出孩子会让父母要么快乐要么痛苦的结论，而是建议我们需要重新定义幸福：与其把幸福看作可以用时时刻刻的愉悦来衡量的东西，不如把感到幸福视作一种过去时态的状态。尽管日复一日的育儿体验可能会让人筋疲力尽，但西尼尔写道：“那些在当下令我们情绪低落的事情，日后却可能成为强烈满足感和喜悦的源泉。”", "本周报刊亭上展示一位迷人母亲抱着可爱婴儿的杂志封面，绝非唯一的“圣母圣子”式画面。此外还有关于新近收养孩子——且新近单身——的妈妈桑德拉·布洛克的报道，以及常见的“詹妮弗·安妮斯顿怀孕了”之类的新闻。几乎每周的报刊亭上，至少都会有一位名人妈妈或准妈妈在封面微笑。", "在一个如此执着地赞颂生育的社会里，承认自己后悔生孩子就等同于承认自己支持杀害小猫，这又有什么好奇怪的呢？那么，把父母的后悔与无子女者的遗憾相提并论，似乎并不太公平。不快乐的父母很少被质问自己是否当初就不该生孩子，但不快乐的无子女者却常常受到这样一种论调的困扰——孩子是世界上唯一最重要的东西，显然他们的痛苦必定是生活中缺少孩子所留下的巨大空洞直接导致的。", "当然，像《我们周刊》和《人物》这类名人杂志所呈现的为人父母形象极度不真实，尤其是当家长是像布洛克这样的单亲妈妈时。根据几项得出“父母不如无子女夫妇快乐”结论的研究，单亲父母是所有群体中最不快乐的。考虑到在没有伴侣依靠的情况下独自抚养孩子有多么辛苦，这毫不令人惊讶；然而听桑德拉和布兰妮讲起来，似乎“独自”（实为：在全天候帮手的协助下）养育一个孩子简直轻而易举。", "很难想象会有多少人愚蠢到仅仅因为瑞茜和安吉丽娜让养孩子看起来光鲜亮丽就想要孩子：大多数成年人都明白，孩子可不是剪个新发型那么简单。但值得玩味的是，我们每周看到的那些毫无压力、增添幸福感的育儿画面，难道没有以某种微小而潜意识的方式，助长了我们对自身真实育儿体验的不满吗——就像我们内心深处曾有那么一丝希望，剪个“瑞秋头”或许能让自己看起来有那么一点像詹妮弗·安妮斯顿一样。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Jennifer Senior suggests in her article that raising a child can bring", "options": ["temporary delight.", "enjoyment in progress.", "happiness in retrospect.", "lasting reward."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "instead of thinking of it as something that can be measured by moment-to-moment joy, we should consider being happy as a past-tense condition.", "explanation": "定位至第1段第2、3句。Jennifer Senior提出我们需要重新定义幸福：不应将其视为以时时刻刻的快乐来衡量的东西，而应把幸福看作一种“过去时态”（a past-tense condition），那些当下令人沮丧的育儿经历日后反而会成为强烈满足与喜悦的源泉。C项中的in retrospect（回想起来）精准对应“过去时态”与“日后”之意。", "trapNote": "A项“暂时的愉悦”和B项“过程中的享受”均与原文“日常育儿极其艰辛、幸福并非当下即时快乐”的表述直接相悖；D项“持久回报”未体现“事后追忆”的时间维度。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "We learn from Paragraph 2 that", "options": ["celebrity moms are a permanent source for gossip.", "single mothers with babies deserve greater attention.", "news about pregnant celebrities is entertaining.", "having children is highly valued by the public."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Practically every week features at least one celebrity mom, or mom-to-be, smiling on the newsstands.", "explanation": "定位至第2段。该段指出每周报刊亭上几乎都会出现至少一位面带微笑的名人妈妈或准妈妈封面，并列举了桑德拉·布洛克和詹妮弗·安妮斯顿的相关报道。媒体如此高频且正面地展示名人母亲与孕育形象，结合第3段首句“社会一贯赞颂生育”的语境，可推知生儿育女在公众眼中备受推崇与重视，即D项所表达的含义。", "trapNote": "A项“永久的八卦来源”与C项“孕期名人新闻具有娱乐性”均未抓住名人封面高频出现的深层社会意义；B项“单亲妈妈值得更多关注”属于脱离段落主旨的过度引申。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "It is suggested in Paragraph 3 that childless folks", "options": ["are constantly exposed to criticism.", "are largely ignored by the media.", "fail to fulfill their social responsibilities.", "are less likely to be satisfied with their life."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "but unhappy childless folks are bothered with the message that children are the single most important thing in the world: obviously their misery must be a direct result of the gaping baby-size holes in their lives.", "explanation": "定位至第3段末句。在这样一个持续推崇生育的社会里，不快乐的父母很少被质疑是否该生孩子，但“不快乐的无子女群体”（unhappy childless folks）却常被这样一种论调困扰：孩子是世上最重要的东西，他们的痛苦显然直接源于生活中缺少孩子留下的巨大空洞。可见无子女者经常面临来自社会的指责与批评，A项正确。", "trapNote": "B项“被媒体忽视”与第2、3段语境相反；D项“更难对生活满意”偷换概念，原文对比的是“不快乐的父母”与“不快乐的无子女者”所承受的社会归因压力，而非满意度高低。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 4, the message conveyed by celebrity magazines is", "options": ["soothing.", "ambiguous.", "compensatory.", "misleading."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Of course, the image of parenthood that celebrity magazines like Us Weekly and People present is hugely unrealistic, especially when the parents are single mothers like Bullock.", "explanation": "定位至第4段。段首直接指出名人杂志所呈现的育儿形象“极度不真实”（hugely unrealistic），随后用研究数据反驳：单亲父母其实最不快乐，没有伴侣分担非常辛苦，但名人杂志却把她们在全天候保姆协助下的育儿生活描绘得轻而易举（a piece of cake）。由此可知，这些杂志传达的信息具有误导性，D项正确。", "trapNote": "A项“抚慰人心的”和C项“补偿性的”在文中毫无依据；B项“模棱两可的”与原文不符，杂志呈现的单一乐观形象并非含糊不清，而是脱离现实、刻意美化从而误导受众。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "推断题", "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from the last paragraph?", "options": ["Having children contributes little to the glamour of celebrity moms.", "Celebrity moms have influenced our attitude towards child rearing.", "Having children intensifies our dissatisfaction with life.", "We sometimes neglect the happiness from child rearing."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "But it's interesting to wonder if the images we see every week of stress-free, happiness-enhancing parenthood aren't in some small, subconscious way contributing to our own dissatisfactions with the actual experience", "explanation": "定位至末段第2句。作者提出耐人寻味的疑问：我们每周看到的那些毫无压力、增添幸福感的名人育儿图景，难道没有以某种微小而潜意识的方式，助长了我们对自己真实育儿体验的不满吗？这恰如我们内心深处曾希望剪个“瑞秋头”就能像安妮斯顿一样迷人。由此可推知，名人母亲的形象潜移默化地影响了我们对育儿的态度，B项正确。", "trapNote": "C项“生孩子加剧对生活的不满”错在因果倒置，加剧不满的是名人杂志营造的虚幻对比而非生育本身；D项“忽略育儿快乐”偏离末段聚焦名人形象心理影响的论证核心。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "adj. 挑衅的，煽动性的；发人深省的", "note": "文中指封面故事观点犀利、引人热议", "word": "provocative"}, {"gloss": "n. 满足，喜悦", "note": "动词为 gratify，文中与 delight 并列强调事后的强烈满足感", "word": "gratification"}, {"gloss": "n. 生殖，生育", "note": "源自动词 procreate，第3段核心词，指社会推崇的生儿育女行为", "word": "procreation"}, {"gloss": "adj. 等价的，等同的", "note": "常考搭配 be equivalent to + 名词/动名词", "word": "equivalent"}, {"gloss": "adj. 潜意识的，下意识的", "note": "前缀 sub-（在……之下）+ conscious（有意识的）", "word": "subconscious"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Rather than concluding that children make parents either happy or miserable, Senior suggests we need to redefine happiness: instead of thinking of it as something that can be measured by moment-to-moment joy, we should consider being happy as a past-tense condition.", "point": "Rather than与instead of双重对比结构及冒号解释说明", "structure": "介词短语Rather than...作状语；主干：Senior suggests (that) we need to redefine happiness；冒号后解释redefine的具体内容，其中instead of引导对比结构，包含that引导的定语从句。", "zh": "西尼尔并没有得出孩子会让父母要么快乐要么痛苦的结论，而是建议我们需要重新定义幸福：与其把幸福看作可以用时时刻刻的愉悦来衡量的东西，不如把感到幸福视作一种过去时态的状态。"}, {"en": "In a society that so persistently celebrates procreation, is it any wonder that admitting you regret having children is equivalent to admitting you support kitten killing?", "point": "修辞性反问句（is it any wonder that...）表达强烈肯定语气", "structure": "In a society...为地点/背景状语，其中that引导定语从句；主句为形式主语反问句is it any wonder that...，真正主语是that引导的主语从句。", "zh": "在一个如此执着地赞颂生育的社会里，承认自己后悔生孩子就等同于承认自己支持杀害小猫，这又有什么好奇怪的呢？"}, {"en": "But it's interesting to wonder if the images we see every week of stress-free, happiness-enhancing parenthood aren't in some small, subconscious way contributing to our own dissatisfactions with the actual experience, in the same way that a small part of us hoped getting \"the Rachel\" might make us look just a little bit like Jennifer Aniston.", "point": "否定疑问形式宾语从句（wonder if ... aren't）与定语从句分隔修饰", "structure": "主干：it's interesting to wonder if...；if引导宾语从句，其中we see every week为省略关系代词的定语从句修饰images，of stress-free...为后置定语；后半句in the same way that...作方式状语，内含宾语从句。", "zh": "但值得玩味的是，我们每周看到的那些毫无压力、增添幸福感的育儿画面，难道没有以某种微小而潜意识的方式，助长了我们对自身真实育儿体验的不满吗——就像我们内心深处曾有那么一丝希望，剪个“瑞秋头”或许能让自己看起来有那么一点像詹妮弗·安妮斯顿一样。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "将“过去时态”和“事后回味”的隐喻替换为地道短语 in retrospect（回想起来）", "option": "happiness in retrospect", "original": "consider being happy as a past-tense condition"}, {"note": "通过媒体高频展示名人母亲的现象归纳出公众对生育的高度推崇", "option": "having children is highly valued by the public", "original": "Practically every week features at least one celebrity mom ... smiling on the newsstands"}, {"note": "社会将无子女者的痛苦归因于未生育的论调，概括为持续面临批评", "option": "are constantly exposed to criticism", "original": "unhappy childless folks are bothered with the message that ... their misery must be a direct result of the gaping baby-size holes"}, {"note": "“极度不真实”且将保姆协助说成“轻而易举”，实为具有“误导性”", "option": "misleading", "original": "the image of parenthood that celebrity magazines ... present is hugely unrealistic"}, {"note": "潜意识中助长对育儿体验的不满，概括为“影响了我们对育儿的态度”", "option": "have influenced our attitude towards child rearing", "original": "subconscious way contributing to our own dissatisfactions"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2010-t1", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2010", "examSet": "2010 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2010 考研英语一真题 Text 1", "title": "英媒艺术评论的往昔辉煌与衰落", "subtitle": "从日常报刊的深度艺评到当代严肃批评的式微", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 435, "paragraphs": ["Of all the changes that have taken place in English-language newspapers during the past quarter-century, perhaps the most far-reaching has been the inexorable decline in the scope and seriousness of their arts coverage.", "It is difficult to the point of impossibility for the average reader under the age of forty to imagine a time when high-quality arts criticism could be found in most big city newspapers. Yet a considerable number of the most significant collections of criticism published in the 20th century consisted in large part of newspaper reviews. To read such books today is to marvel at the fact that their learned contents were once deemed suitable for publication in general-circulation dailies.", "We are even farther removed from the unfocused newspaper reviews published in England between the turn of the 20th century and the eve of World War II, at a time when newsprint was dirt-cheap and stylish arts criticism was considered an ornament to the publications in which it appeared. In those far-off days, it was taken for granted that the critics of major papers would write in detail and at length about the events they covered. Theirs was a serious business, and even those reviewers who wore their learning lightly, like George Bernard Shaw and Ernest Newman, could be trusted to know what they were about. These men believed in journalism as a calling, and were proud to be published in the daily press. \"So few authors have brains enough or literary gift enough to keep their own end up in journalism,\" Newman wrote, \"that I am tempted to define 'journalism' as 'a term of contempt applied by writers who are not read to writers who are'.\"", "Unfortunately, these critics are virtually forgotten. Neville Cardus, who wrote for the Manchester Guardian from 1917 until shortly before his death in 1975, is now known solely as a writer of essays on the game of cricket. During his lifetime, though, he was also one of England's foremost classical-music critics, and a stylist so widely admired that his Autobiography (1947) became a best-seller. He was knighted in 1967, the first music critic to be so honored. Yet only one of his books is now in print, and his vast body of writings on music is unknown save to specialists.", "Is there any chance that Cardus's criticism will enjoy a revival? The prospect seems remote. Journalistic tastes had changed long before his death, and postmodern readers have little use for the richly upholstered Vicwardian prose in which he specialized. Moreover, the amateur tradition in music criticism has been in headlong retreat."], "translations": ["在过去25年英文报纸发生的所有变化中，影响最为深远的，或许莫过于报纸在艺术报道的广度与严肃性上不可阻挡的衰退。", "对于40岁以下的普通读者而言，几乎无法想象大多数大城市报纸上曾经随处可见高质量艺术评论的时代。然而，20世纪出版的最具分量的批评文集中，有相当大一部分主要是由报纸评论文章汇编而成的。如今重读这些书籍，人们不禁会惊叹：如此博学深邃的内容，当年竟被认为适合刊登在面向大众发行的日报上。", "我们更难以企及的是20世纪初至二战前夕发表在英国报纸上的那些题材宽泛的评论——当时新闻纸极其廉价，文风考究的艺术批评被视作刊物的一大装点。在那个遥远的年代，各大报社的评论家对所报道的活动撰写详尽长文是理所当然的事。他们干的是一份严肃的事业；即便是像萧伯纳和欧内斯特·纽曼这样举重若轻、不显山露水的评论家，也能让人信赖他们对本行了如指掌。这些人把新闻工作视为天职，并能以在日报上发表文章为荣。纽曼曾写道：“很少有作家拥有足够的头脑或文学天赋在新闻界站稳脚跟，以至于我忍不住想把‘新闻写作’定义为‘无人问津的作家用来轻蔑受读者欢迎的作家的词’。”", "遗憾的是，这些评论家如今几乎已被遗忘。内维尔·卡达斯从1917年起一直为《曼彻斯特卫报》撰稿，直至1975年逝世前不久才停笔，如今人们只知道他是一位写板球评论的随笔作家。然而在他在世时，他还是英国最顶尖的古典音乐评论家之一，且文风广受推崇，其1947年出版的《自传》曾成为畅销书。1967年他获封爵士，是第一位获此殊荣的音乐评论家。但如今他的著作仅有一本仍在印行，而他浩如烟海的音乐评论文集，除专业研究者外已无人知晓。", "卡达斯的评论还有可能迎来复兴吗？前景似乎十分渺茫。早在卡达斯去世前，新闻界的审美趣味便已改变，而后现代读者对他所擅长的华丽繁复的维多利亚-爱德华时期散文风格已毫无兴趣。此外，音乐批评中的业余传统也正在全线溃退。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "推断题", "stem": "It is indicated in Paragraphs 1 and 2 that", "options": ["arts criticism has disappeared from big-city newspapers.", "English-language newspapers used to carry more arts reviews.", "high-quality newspapers retain a large body of readers.", "young readers doubt the suitability of criticism on dailies."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "It is difficult to the point of impossibility for the average reader under the age of forty to imagine a time when high-quality arts criticism could be found in most big city newspapers.", "explanation": "定位第1、2段。第1段指出过去25年英文报纸艺术报道的广度和严肃性持续下滑；第2段进一步说明40岁以下读者已难以想象多数大城市报纸曾刊登高质量艺评，且20世纪许多重要批评文集很大一部分源自报纸评论。由此可知，英文报纸过去刊载过更多艺术评论，B项准确概括了这两段的对比，其中used to carry more对应过去的繁荣与如今的衰落。", "trapNote": "A项“已彻底消失”把decline（衰落）偷换为绝对化的disappeared；C项“保留大量读者”和D项“怀疑适宜性”均曲解第2段内容，文中是现代人对昔日风气感到惊叹而非质疑。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Newspaper reviews in England before World War II were characterized by", "options": ["free themes.", "casual style.", "elaborate layout.", "radical viewpoints."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "We are even farther removed from the unfocused newspaper reviews published in England between the turn of the 20th century and the eve of World War II, at a time when newsprint was dirt-cheap and stylish arts criticism was considered an ornament to the publications in which it appeared.", "explanation": "定位第3段首句。题干询问二战前英国报纸评论的特点，对应文中between the turn of the 20th century and the eve of World War II这一时期。原文用unfocused（不拘一格的、主题宽泛不设限的）修饰newspaper reviews，并提到当时新闻纸极其廉价、评论文章篇幅详尽。A项free themes（题材自由）精准同义替换了unfocused，故为正确答案。", "trapNote": "B项casual style（随意文风）与文中stylish（讲究文采的）和serious business相悖；C项“精心排版”及D项“激进观点”在原文均无提及，属无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following would Shaw and Newman most probably agree on?", "options": ["It is writers' duty to fulfill journalistic goals.", "It is contemptible for writers to be journalists.", "Writers are likely to be tempted into journalism.", "Not all writers are capable of journalistic writing."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "\"So few authors have brains enough or literary gift enough to keep their own end up in journalism,\" Newman wrote, \"that I am tempted to define 'journalism' as 'a term of contempt applied by writers who are not read to writers who are'.\"", "explanation": "定位第3段后半段。原文先指出萧伯纳和纽曼这类评论家虽举重若轻却深谙本行、将新闻写作视为使命，随后直接引用纽曼的话：很少有作家具备足够的才智或文学天赋去胜任新闻写作（keep their own end up in journalism），反倒是无人问津的作家借“新闻业”一词贬损受读者欢迎的作家。D项“并非所有作家都能胜任新闻写作”正是对该句的同义转述。", "trapNote": "A项“实现新闻目标是作家的义务”属过度拔高，原文仅指少数评论家视其为天职；B项与纽曼反讽“贬低记者的言论”完全相反；C项误读了I am tempted to的语义。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "What can be learned about Cardus according to the last two paragraphs?", "options": ["His music criticism may not appeal to readers today.", "His reputation as a music critic has long been in dispute.", "His style caters largely to modern specialists.", "His writings fail to follow the amateur tradition."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Journalistic tastes had changed long before his death, and postmodern readers have little use for the richly upholstered Vicwardian prose in which he specialized.", "explanation": "定位第4、5段。第4段指出卡达斯的音乐评论如今除专业人士外几乎无人问津，仅有一本书仍在印行；第5段分析其作品难获复兴的原因：新闻品味早已改变，后现代读者对他擅长的华丽繁复的维多利亚-爱德华风格散文毫无兴趣（have little use for）。A项“他的音乐评论如今可能难以吸引当代读者”准确归纳了两段的核心信息，故正确。", "trapNote": "B项“声誉长期存疑”与第4段生前广受赞誉并受封爵位矛盾；C项迎合现代专家曲解了unknown save to specialists；D项与原文“业余传统大撤退”不符。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "What would be the best title for the text?", "options": ["Newspapers of the Good Old Days", "The Lost Horizon in Newspapers", "Mournful Decline of Journalism", "Prominent Critics in Memory"], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Of all the changes that have taken place in English-language newspapers during the past quarter-century, perhaps the most far-reaching has been the inexorable decline in the scope and seriousness of their arts coverage.", "explanation": "纵观全文，首段点明过去25年英文报纸艺术报道在广度与严肃性上的不可逆衰退；第2、3段追忆20世纪及二战前高质量报纸艺评的黄金时代；第4、5段以名家卡达斯被遗忘为例，感叹昔日严谨艺评传统一去不返。B项The Lost Horizon in Newspapers（报纸上失落的地平线/逝去的艺术视野）以比喻手法精准概括“报刊深度艺评沦丧”的全文主旨。", "trapNote": "A项“美好旧时光的报纸”仅涵盖追忆部分，未体现衰落；C项将局部“艺术评论衰落”扩大为整个“新闻业衰落”；D项只突出第3、4段评论家人物，以偏概全。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "不可阻挡的，无法改变的", "note": "常修饰decline、trend等名词，考研高频形容词", "word": "inexorable"}, {"gloss": "认为，视作", "note": "常用于被动语态 be deemed suitable/necessary，等价于consider", "word": "deem"}, {"gloss": "装饰品，点缀", "note": "既可作名词也可作动词；文中指报纸的“门面点缀”", "word": "ornament"}, {"gloss": "天职，使命感；职业", "note": "熟词僻义重点词，文中指“新闻写作是一份神圣使命”", "word": "calling"}, {"gloss": "复兴，重振", "note": "动词为revive，常考enjoy a revival（重获生机）", "word": "revival"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "We are even farther removed from the unfocused newspaper reviews published in England between the turn of the 20th century and the eve of World War II, at a time when newsprint was dirt-cheap and stylish arts criticism was considered an ornament to the publications in which it appeared.", "point": "把握“farther removed from...”表时代隔膜，以及多重定语从句对背景的补充说明", "structure": "主句为We are even farther removed from the unfocused newspaper reviews；过去分词短语published in England...作后置定语；at a time后接when引导的定语从句，包含and连接的两个并列分句，其中in which it appeared修饰publications。", "zh": "我们更难以企及的是20世纪初至二战前夕发表在英国报纸上的那些题材宽泛的评论——当时新闻纸极其廉价，文风考究的艺术批评被视作刊物的一大装点。"}, {"en": "\"So few authors have brains enough or literary gift enough to keep their own end up in journalism,\" Newman wrote, \"that I am tempted to define 'journalism' as 'a term of contempt applied by writers who are not read to writers who are'.\"", "point": "识别so...that...结果状语从句及结尾省略成分（who are [read]）的对应关系", "structure": "插入语Newman wrote隔开了so...that...引导的结果状语从句；so few...that...结构中，applied by...to...为过去分词短语作后置定语修饰term；句末writers who are后承前省略了read。", "zh": "纽曼写道：“很少有作家能有足够的头脑或文学天赋在新闻界站稳脚跟，以至于我忍不住想把‘新闻写作’定义为‘无人问津的作家用来轻蔑受读者欢迎的作家的词’。”"}, {"en": "Journalistic tastes had changed long before his death, and postmodern readers have little use for the richly upholstered Vicwardian prose in which he specialized.", "point": "理解have little use for（对……毫无兴趣/不屑一顾）及“介词+which”定语从句", "structure": "and连接的并列句；后半句主干为postmodern readers have little use for the...prose，in which he specialized为定语从句修饰prose。", "zh": "早在卡达斯去世前，新闻界的审美趣味便已改变，而后现代读者对他所擅长的华丽繁复的维多利亚-爱德华时期散文风格已毫无兴趣。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "第2段今昔对比核心：40岁以下读者无法想象大报曾满是高质量艺评，对应“过去曾刊载更多”", "option": "used to carry more arts reviews", "original": "a time when high-quality arts criticism could be found in most big city newspapers"}, {"note": "unfocused在文中指不受主题限制、自由挥洒的评论特点，精准对应free themes", "option": "free themes", "original": "unfocused newspaper reviews"}, {"note": "keep one's own end up意为“跟上、胜任、不掉队”，否定含义转述为not all...are capable of", "option": "Not all writers are capable of journalistic writing", "original": "So few authors have brains enough or literary gift enough to keep their own end up in journalism"}, {"note": "have little use for为固定搭配，意为“对……不需要/不感兴趣”，对应may not appeal to", "option": "may not appeal to readers today", "original": "postmodern readers have little use for the richly upholstered Vicwardian prose"}, {"note": "文章主旨通过对比往昔与如今的艺术报道衰退，凝练为“失落的报刊视野”", "option": "The Lost Horizon in Newspapers", "original": "inexorable decline in the scope and seriousness of their arts coverage"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2010-t2", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2010", "examSet": "2010 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2010 考研英语一真题 Text 2", "title": "商业方法专利面临全面缩紧", "subtitle": "美联邦巡回上诉法院拟重审商业方法专利的合法性", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 437, "paragraphs": ["Over the past decade, thousands of patents have been granted for what are called business methods. Amazon.com received one for its \"one-click\" online payment system. Merrill Lynch got legal protection for an asset allocation strategy. One inventor patented a technique for lifting a box.", "Now the nation's top patent court appears completely ready to scale back on business-method patents, which have been controversial ever since they were first authorized 10 years ago. In a move that has intellectual-property lawyers abuzz, the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit said it would use a particular case to conduct a broad review of business-method patents. In re Bilski, as the case is known, is \"a very big deal,\" says Dennis D. Crouch of the University of Missouri School of Law. It \"has the potential to eliminate an entire class of patents.\" Curbs on business-method claims would be a dramatic about-face, because it was the Federal Circuit itself that introduced such patents with its 1998 decision in the so-called State Street Bank case, approving a patent on a way of pooling mutual-fund assets. That ruling produced an explosion in business-method patent filings, initially by emerging Internet companies trying to stake out exclusive rights to specific types of online transactions. Later, more established companies raced to add such patents to their files, if only as a defensive move against rivals that might beat them to the punch. In 2005, IBM noted in a court filing that it had been issued more than 300 business-method patents, despite the fact that it questioned the legal basis for granting them. Similarly, some Wall Street investment firms armed themselves with patents for financial products, even as they took positions in court cases opposing the practice.", "The Bilski case involves a claimed patent on a method for hedging risk in the energy market. The Federal Circuit issued an unusual order stating that the case would be heard by all 12 of the court's judges, rather than a typical panel of three, and that one issue it wants to evaluate is whether it should \"reconsider\" its State Street Bank ruling.", "The Federal Circuit's action comes in the wake of a series of recent decisions by the Supreme Court that has narrowed the scope of protections for patent holders. Last April, for example, the justices signaled that too many patents were being upheld for \"inventions\" that are obvious. The judges on the Federal Circuit are \"reacting to the anti-patent trend at the Supreme Court,\" says Harold C. Wegner, a patent attorney and professor at George Washington University Law School."], "translations": ["过去十年间，数以千计的所谓“商业方法”获得了专利授权。亚马逊公司为其“一键”在线支付系统获得了专利；美林证券为其资产配置策略取得了法律保护；甚至还有一位发明者为一种搬起箱子的技巧申请了专利。", "如今，美国最高专利法院似乎已完全准备好缩减商业方法专利的规模——自10年前首次获批以来，这类专利就一直争议不断。美国联邦巡回上诉法院宣布将借一桩具体案件对商业方法专利展开全面审查，此举令知识产权律师们议论纷纷。密苏里大学法学院的丹尼斯·D·克劳奇表示，被称为“比尔斯基案”（In re Bilski）的这起案件“事关重大”，它“有可能彻底取消整整一类专利”。对商业方法专利申请加以限制将是一次戏剧性的立场大逆转，因为正是联邦巡回上诉法院自己在1998年所谓的“道富银行案”裁决中引入了此类专利，当时批准了一项关于汇集共同基金资产方法的专利。那项裁决引发了商业方法专利申请的井喷：起初是新兴互联网公司试图抢占特定类型在线交易的独家权利；随后，实力更雄厚的成熟企业也竞相将这些专利收入囊中，哪怕只是为了采取防御举措，防止竞争对手抢先占得先机。2005年，IBM在一份法庭文件中指出，尽管其对授予此类专利的法律依据存疑，但公司仍已获批超过300项商业方法专利。同样，华尔街的一些投资公司也用金融产品专利武装自己，即便它们同时在法庭诉讼中持反对这一做法的立场。", "比尔斯基案涉及一项关于能源市场风险对冲方法的专利申请。联邦巡回上诉法院发布了一项罕见的命令，声明该案将由法院全部12名法官共同审理，而非通常的三人合议庭，并且其希望评估的一个问题是是否应当“重新审视”此前的道富银行案裁决。", "联邦巡回上诉法院的此番举措，紧随美国最高法院近期一系列缩窄专利持有人保护范围的裁决之后。例如，去年4月，大法官们就释放出信号，指出有太多本属显而易见的“发明”获得了专利维持。乔治·华盛顿大学法学院教授、专利律师哈罗德·C·韦格纳表示，联邦巡回上诉法院的法官们“正在对最高法院的反专利趋势做出回应”。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Business-method patents have recently aroused concern because of", "options": ["their limited value to businesses.", "their connection with asset allocation.", "the possible restriction on their granting.", "the controversy over their authorization."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Now the nation's top patent court appears completely ready to scale back on business-method patents, which have been controversial ever since they were first authorized 10 years ago.", "explanation": "定位第2段开头。首句指出美国最高专利法院似乎已完全准备好缩减（scale back on）商业方法专利；次句进一步说明美国联邦巡回上诉法院宣布将借具体案件对商业方法专利展开全面审查，此举令知识产权律师们议论纷纷（abuzz）。可见近期引发广泛关注的直接原因是法院可能对授予此类专利加以限制，C项restriction对应原文scale back和curbs。", "trapNote": "D项“关于其授权的争议”是10年前获批以来一直存在的背景（ever since），并非recently（近期）引发关注的新原因；A、B项均以第1段细节拼凑。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Which of the following is true of the Bilski case?", "options": ["Its ruling complies with the court decisions.", "It involves a very big business transaction.", "It has been dismissed by the Federal Circuit.", "It may change the legal practices in the U.S."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "It \"has the potential to eliminate an entire class of patents.\"", "explanation": "定位第2、3段关于Bilski案的论述。第2段引用丹尼斯·克劳奇的话指出，该案“是一件大事”，有可能取消一整类专利（eliminate an entire class of patents），紧接着称限制商业方法专利将是戏剧性的态度逆转；第3段补充该案将破例由全体12名法官共同审理，重估此前确立该专利的先例。D项“它可能改变美国的司法实践”准确概括了该案的潜在颠覆性影响。", "trapNote": "A项“裁决符合法院既往决定”与reconsider推翻先例的意图相反；B项把法学教授评价案件是a very big deal偷换为“涉及巨额商业交易”；C项“已被驳回”无中生有。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The word \"about-face\" (Line 1, Para. 3) most probably means", "options": ["loss of goodwill.", "increase of hostility.", "change of attitude.", "enhancement of dignity."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Curbs on business-method claims would be a dramatic about-face, because it was the Federal Circuit itself that introduced such patents with its 1998 decision in the so-called State Street Bank case, approving a patent on a way of pooling mutual-fund assets.", "explanation": "定位第2段中段（题干标注原卷Para. 3首句即此处）。前文指出法院准备限制商业方法专利，随后用because解释“限制商业方法专利申请将是一次戏剧性的about-face，因为正是联邦巡回上诉法院自己在1998年State Street Bank案中首次批准并引入了此类专利”。由前后“先批准引入、今拟限制取消”的强烈对比可知，about-face意为“态度/立场的彻底转变”，即C项change of attitude。", "trapNote": "A项“失去商誉”、B项“敌意增加”与D项“尊严提升”均未能结合because后面的因果对比逻辑，属于脱离语境的主观猜测。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "推断题", "stem": "We learn from the last two paragraphs that business-method patents", "options": ["are immune to legal challenges.", "are often unnecessarily issued.", "lower the esteem for patent holders.", "increase the incidence of risks."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Last April, for example, the justices signaled that too many patents were being upheld for \"inventions\" that are obvious.", "explanation": "定位最后两段。第3段说明联邦巡回法院全体12名法官罕见介入以决定是否重审1998年的判例；第4段指出此举紧随美国最高法院一系列缩窄专利保护范围的裁决之后，例如大法官们去年4月明确表示，过多本属显而易见的“发明”获得了专利维持（too many patents were being upheld for \"inventions\" that are obvious）。由此可推知商业方法专利经常被不必要地授予，对应B项。", "trapNote": "A项“免受法律挑战”与全文法院重审并限制专利的基调完全相反；C项“降低对专利持有人的尊重”及D项“增加风险发生率”均曲解了第3、4段细节。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "主旨题", "stem": "Which of the following would be the subject of the text?", "options": ["A looming threat to business-method patents.", "Protection for business-method patent holders.", "A legal case regarding business-method patents.", "A prevailing trend against business-method patents."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "In re Bilski, as the case is known, is \"a very big deal,\" says Dennis D. Crouch of the University of Missouri School of Law. It \"has the potential to eliminate an entire class of patents.\"", "explanation": "纵观全文，第1段引出商业方法专利在过去十年的泛滥；第2、3段核心阐述美国联邦巡回上诉法院拟借Bilski案全面审查并可能废除整类商业方法专利；第4段点明其背后的最高法院反专利大背景。全文聚焦商业方法专利正面临被司法收紧甚至取消的紧迫危机，A项“迫在眉睫的威胁”最贴合文章核心主题。", "trapNote": "B项“对专利持有人的保护”与第4段narrowed the scope of protections相反；C项只提到单个案件，未点出威胁；D项把“反专利趋势（仅限背景）”扩大为唯一主体，忽略了核心对象所受的威胁。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "缩减，按比例减少", "note": "常接on，文中表示法院“缩减”商业方法专利规模", "word": "scale back"}, {"gloss": "限制，约束；抑制", "note": "可作名词或动词，文中Curbs on...对应题目中的restriction", "word": "curb"}, {"gloss": "（风险）对冲，规避风险", "note": "金融法律高频词，常见短语hedge risk（对冲风险）", "word": "hedge"}, {"gloss": "维持（原判或专利），支持", "note": "法律语境核心动词，过去分词为upheld，常见uphold a patent/ruling", "word": "uphold"}, {"gloss": "紧随……之后", "note": "固定介词短语，等同于following，表示事件紧接在另一事件后发生", "word": "in the wake of"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Curbs on business-method claims would be a dramatic about-face, because it was the Federal Circuit itself that introduced such patents with its 1998 decision in the so-called State Street Bank case, approving a patent on a way of pooling mutual-fund assets.", "point": "辨析it was...that...强调句及分词短语approving...对1998年裁决的补充说明", "structure": "主句为Curbs...would be a dramatic about-face；because引导原因状语从句，内部嵌套it was the Federal Circuit itself that...强调句型；句末现在分词短语approving a patent...作状语说明1998年判决的内容。", "zh": "对商业方法专利申请加以限制将是一次戏剧性的立场大逆转，因为正是联邦巡回上诉法院自己在1998年所谓的“道富银行案”裁决中引入了此类专利，当时批准了一项关于汇集共同基金资产方法的专利。"}, {"en": "The Federal Circuit issued an unusual order stating that the case would be heard by all 12 of the court's judges, rather than a typical panel of three, and that one issue it wants to evaluate is whether it should \"reconsider\" its State Street Bank ruling.", "point": "理清stating引导的两个并列宾语从句that...and that...及表语从句whether...", "structure": "主句为The Federal Circuit issued an unusual order；现在分词stating作后置定语修饰order，后接两个由and连接的并列that宾语从句；第二个that从句中it wants to evaluate修饰issue，whether引导表语从句。", "zh": "联邦巡回上诉法院发布了一项罕见的命令，声明该案将由法院全部12名法官共同审理，而非通常的三人合议庭，并且其希望评估的一个问题是是否应当“重新审视”此前的道富银行案裁决。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "scale back（缩减）与curbs（限制）共同指向对商业方法专利授予的restriction", "option": "the possible restriction on their granting", "original": "completely ready to scale back on business-method patents"}, {"note": "前文由法院先批准、今欲限制并重审先例，故about-face意为“态度的彻底转变”", "option": "change of attitude", "original": "Curbs on business-method claims would be a dramatic about-face"}, {"note": "取消一整类专利并重审确立该类专利的先例，即“可能改变美国的司法实践”", "option": "It may change the legal practices in the U.S.", "original": "It \"has the potential to eliminate an entire class of patents.\""}, {"note": "为显而易见的“发明”维持过多专利，同义转述为“经常被不必要地授予”", "option": "are often unnecessarily issued", "original": "too many patents were being upheld for \"inventions\" that are obvious"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2010-t3", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2010", "examSet": "2010 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2010 考研英语一真题 Text 3", "title": "少数意见领袖并非社会流行潮的主导", "subtitle": "质疑“二级传播”理论，揭示大众易受影响倾向在信息传播中的核心作用", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 450, "paragraphs": ["In his book The Tipping Point, Malcolm Gladwell argues that \"social epidemics\" are driven in large part by the actions of a tiny minority of special individuals, often called influentials, who are unusually informed, persuasive, or well connected. The idea is intuitively compelling, but it doesn't explain how ideas actually spread. The supposed importance of influentials derives from a plausible-sounding but largely untested theory called the \"two-step flow of communication\": Information flows from the media to the influentials and from them to everyone else. Marketers have embraced the two-step flow because it suggests that if they can just find and influence the influentials, those select people will do most of the work for them. The theory also seems to explain the sudden and unexpected popularity of certain looks, brands, or neighborhoods. In many such cases, a cursory search for causes finds that some small group of people was wearing, promoting, or developing whatever it is before anyone else paid attention. Anecdotal evidence of this kind fits nicely with the idea that only certain special people can drive trends.", "In their recent work, however, some researchers have come up with the finding that influentials have far less impact on social epidemics than is generally supposed. In fact, they don't seem to be required at all.", "The researchers' argument stems from a simple observation about social influence: With the exception of a few celebrities like Oprah Winfrey - whose outsize presence is primarily a function of media, not interpersonal, influence - even the most influential members of a population simply don't interact with that many others. Yet it is precisely these non-celebrity influentials who, according to the two-step-flow theory, are supposed to drive social epidemics, by influencing their friends and colleagues directly. For a social epidemic to occur, however, each person so affected must then influence his or her own acquaintances, who must in turn influence theirs, and so on; and just how many others pay attention to each of these people has little to do with the initial influential. If people in the network just two degrees removed from the initial influential prove resistant, for example, the cascade of change won't propagate very far or affect many people.", "Building on this basic truth about interpersonal influence, the researchers studied the dynamics of social influence by conducting thousands of computer simulations of populations, manipulating a number of variables relating to people's ability to influence others and their tendency to be influenced. They found that the principal requirement for what is called \"global cascades\" - the widespread propagation of influence through networks - is the presence not of a few influentials but, rather, of a critical mass of easily influenced people."], "translations": ["马尔科姆·格拉德威尔在其著作《引爆点》中指出，“社会流行潮”在很大程度上是由极少数通常被称为“意见领袖”的特殊个体的行为所推动的，这些人往往消息格外灵通、极具说服力或人脉广博。这一观点直观上颇具说服力，但它并未解释思想究竟是如何传播的。所谓意见领袖的重要性源于一种听起来合理却基本未经检验的理论，即“信息二级传播理论”：信息从媒体流向意见领袖，再由他们流向其他人。营销人员欣然接纳了这一理论，因为它意味着只要能找到并影响这些意见领袖，这些精挑细选的人就会替他们完成大部分推广工作。该理论似乎还能解释某些造型、品牌或街区突然且出人意料的走红。在许多这类案例中，粗略追根溯源便会发现，在其他人关注之前，就有一小群人在穿戴、推广或开发该事物。此类轶事证据恰好契合了“只有某些特殊人物才能引领潮流”的想法。", "然而，一些研究人员在近期研究中却得出了这样的发现：意见领袖对社会流行潮的影响远比人们通常认为的要小得多。事实上，他们似乎根本不是必需的。", "研究人员的论点源于对社会影响的一个简单观察：除了像奥普拉·温弗瑞这样的少数名人——她们的巨大影响力主要源于媒体作用而非人际影响——即便是人群中最具影响力的成员，实际上也并不会与那么多其他人产生互动。然而，根据二级传播理论，恰恰是这些非名人的意见领袖应当通过直接影响朋友和同事来推动社会流行潮。但要形成社会流行潮，每个受此影响的人都必须再去影响自己的熟人，而这些熟人又必须接着影响他们的熟人，以此类推；究竟有多少人会关注其中的每一个人，其实与最初的意见领袖几乎毫无关系。例如，如果在社交网络中与初始意见领袖仅相隔两层关系的人表现出抵触情绪，变化的连锁反应就无法传播得很远，也难以影响多少人。", "基于这一关于人际影响的基本事实，研究人员通过对人群进行数千次计算机模拟来研究社会影响的动态机制，在模拟中调控了与人们影响他人的能力以及受他人影响的倾向相关的多个变量。他们发现，所谓“全球级联”——即影响力在网络中的广泛传播——的首要条件并非少数意见领袖的存在，而是存在足够数量的容易受影响的人群。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "例证题", "stem": "By citing the book The Tipping Point, the author intends to", "options": ["analyze the consequences of social epidemics.", "discuss influentials' function in spreading ideas.", "exemplify people's intuitive response to social epidemics.", "describe the essential characteristics of influentials."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "In his book The Tipping Point, Malcolm Gladwell argues that \"social epidemics\" are driven in large part by the actions of a tiny minority of special individuals, often called influentials, who are unusually informed, persuasive, or well connected. The idea is intuitively compelling, but it doesn't explain how ideas actually spread.", "explanation": "第1段首句引用《引爆点》指出，社会流行潮很大程度上由少数极具影响力的特殊个体推动，随后转折指出该观点虽直观却未能解释思想究竟如何传播，从而引出全文对“意见领袖”作用的探讨。B项中discuss influentials' function in spreading ideas精准对应作者引用该书旨在讨论意见领袖在传播思想中的作用这一写作意图。", "trapNote": "C项偷换概念，将原文对“该观点直观上令人信服(intuitively compelling)”的评价歪曲为“人们对社会流行潮的直觉反应”；D项以偏概全，仅对应定语从句中的局部修饰信息，并非引用目的。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "The author suggests that the \"two-step-flow theory\"", "options": ["serves as a solution to marketing problems.", "has helped explain certain prevalent trends.", "has won support from influentials.", "requires solid evidence for its validity."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "The supposed importance of influentials derives from a plausible-sounding but largely untested theory called the \"two-step flow of communication\": Information flows from the media to the influentials and from them to everyone else.", "explanation": "定位第1段第3句。作者将该理论定性为plausible-sounding but largely untested，后文又指出其支持证据仅属于anecdotal evidence（轶事证据），且第2段指出最新研究发现意见领袖远不如人们想象的那样有影响力。由此可合理推断，“二级传播理论”缺乏充分检验，其有效性尚需扎实证据支撑，对应D项requires solid evidence for its validity。", "trapNote": "A项过度绝对，原文仅说营销人员接纳该理论，未说其能解决营销问题；B项与原文矛盾，原文用seems to explain表示“似乎能解释”某些流行趋势，实则作者对此持怀疑态度。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What the researchers have observed recently shows that", "options": ["the power of influence goes with social interactions.", "interpersonal links can be enhanced through the media.", "influentials have more channels to reach the public.", "most celebrities enjoy wide media attention."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "With the exception of a few celebrities like Oprah Winfrey - whose outsize presence is primarily a function of media, not interpersonal, influence - even the most influential members of a population simply don't interact with that many others.", "explanation": "定位第3段首句。研究人员指出，除少数依靠媒体而非人际传播的名人外，即便最具影响力的普通成员也并不与那么多人互动，而社交流行潮却依赖人际间的直接及链式互动。这说明影响力的大小与社交互动直接相关。A项the power of influence goes with social interactions准确概括了研究人员关于人际影响依赖于社交互动的观察结论。", "trapNote": "B项无中生有，原文将媒体影响与人际影响区分开，未提及媒体能增强人际联系；C项与原文相反，非名人“意见领袖”并未拥有更多接触公众的渠道，反而互动人数有限。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "词义题", "stem": "The underlined phrase \"these people\" in Paragraph 4 refers to the ones who", "options": ["stay outside the network of social influence.", "have little contact with the source of influence.", "are influenced and then influence others.", "are influenced by the initial influential."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "For a social epidemic to occur, however, each person so affected must then influence his or her own acquaintances, who must in turn influence theirs, and so on; and just how many others pay attention to each of these people has little to do with the initial influential.", "explanation": "题干所指“these people”位于所供文本第3段第3句（原真题分段中为第4段）。根据指代就近与语义衔接原则，前文提到each person so affected must then influence his or her own acquaintances, who must in turn influence theirs，即“先被影响、继而再去影响熟人的每一环成员”。C项are influenced and then influence others完整还原了这种链式传递身份。", "trapNote": "D项以偏概全，仅涵盖“被初始意见领袖影响的人”，忽略了后面“再去影响各自熟人”的链条延续；B项误读了句末的has little to do with，其主语是“关注人数”，而非接触程度。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "细节题", "stem": "What is the essential element in the dynamics of social influence?", "options": ["The eagerness to be accepted.", "The impulse to influence others.", "The readiness to be influenced.", "The inclination to rely on others."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "They found that the principal requirement for what is called \"global cascades\" - the widespread propagation of influence through networks - is the presence not of a few influentials but, rather, of a critical mass of easily influenced people.", "explanation": "定位第4段末句。题干中的essential element同义替换原文中的principal requirement，问社交影响动态中的关键要素。原文明确指出，推动“全球级联”（即影响力在网络中广泛传播）的首要条件并非少数意见领袖，而是存在大量“容易被影响的人群”(a critical mass of easily influenced people)。C项The readiness to be influenced精准对应easily influenced。", "trapNote": "B项偷换概念，将“容易被影响”反向曲解为“去影响他人的冲动”；A项“渴望被接纳”与D项“依赖他人的倾向”均属无中生有，将“易受影响”过度引申为心理依赖或社交迎合。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "流行病；（思想、风尚等的）流行潮", "note": "本文中加引号的 social epidemics 指思想、风尚等在人群中的大规模传播现象。", "word": "epidemic"}, {"gloss": "看似合理的，貌似有理的", "note": "常含“表面合理但未必经得起推敲”的评价色彩，常与 untested 等负面限定词连用。", "word": "plausible"}, {"gloss": "粗略的，草率的，敷衍的", "note": "cursory search 指粗略探寻原因，暗示结论缺乏深入严谨的实证。", "word": "cursory"}, {"gloss": "传播，扩散，繁衍", "note": "本文中指社会变革或影响力在社交网络中的链式传播，与 spread 同义。", "word": "propagate"}, {"gloss": "级联，连续传递，倾泻", "note": "global cascades 指影响力通过网络节点逐级放大的全局性传播效应。", "word": "cascade"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "In his book The Tipping Point, Malcolm Gladwell argues that \"social epidemics\" are driven in large part by the actions of a tiny minority of special individuals, often called influentials, who are unusually informed, persuasive, or well connected.", "point": "识别过去分词短语作同位语补充说明及非限制性定语从句对特殊个体特征的界定，理解首段立靶点。", "structure": "主句 (Malcolm Gladwell argues) + that 引导的宾语从句；从句中 often called influentials 为过去分词短语作后置定语，who 引导非限制性定语从句修饰 individuals。", "zh": "马尔科姆·格拉德威尔在其著作《引爆点》中认为，“社会流行潮”在很大程度上是由极少数通常被称为“意见领袖”的特殊个体的行为所推动的，这些人往往消息格外灵通、极具说服力或人脉广博。"}, {"en": "With the exception of a few celebrities like Oprah Winfrey - whose outsize presence is primarily a function of media, not interpersonal, influence - even the most influential members of a population simply don't interact with that many others.", "point": "把握双破折号插入语中的对比结构（media, not interpersonal）及 a function of（……的结果/作用），理清主句核心让步含义。", "structure": "With the exception of... 作状语；破折号内为 whose 引导的定语从句修饰 celebrities；主句主干为 even the most influential members... don't interact with that many others。", "zh": "除了少数像奥普拉·温弗瑞这样的名人——她们的巨大影响力主要源于媒体传播而非人际影响——即便是人群中最具影响力的成员，实际上也并不会与那么多其他人发生互动。"}, {"en": "Building on this basic truth about interpersonal influence, the researchers studied the dynamics of social influence by conducting thousands of computer simulations of populations, manipulating a number of variables relating to people's ability to influence others and their tendency to be influenced.", "point": "理清多个现在分词短语在句首、句尾分别作状语（基础、伴随动作）和后置定语（relating to...）的层次关系。", "structure": "句首 Building on... 为现在分词短语作方式/基础状语；主干为 the researchers studied... by conducting...；句尾 manipulating... 为伴随状语，其中 relating to... 修饰 variables。", "zh": "基于这一关于人际影响的基本事实，研究人员通过对人群进行数千次计算机模拟来研究社会影响的动态机制，在模拟中调控了与人们影响他人的能力及受他人影响的倾向有关的多个变量。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "由“未经检验”结合上下文的“轶事证据”合理推断出“需要扎实证据验证”。", "option": "requires solid evidence for its validity", "original": "largely untested theory"}, {"note": "用抽象名词 function 概括“意见领袖通过自身行动推动传播”的作用。", "option": "influentials' function in spreading ideas", "original": "driven in large part by the actions of a tiny minority of special individuals, often called influentials"}, {"note": "将“不与那么多人互动”的负面限制概括为“影响力与社交互动相伴相生”。", "option": "the power of influence goes with social interactions", "original": "even the most influential members of a population simply don't interact with that many others"}, {"note": "主被动结合的链式动作同义改写，还原“被影响后再影响熟人”的传递链。", "option": "are influenced and then influence others", "original": "each person so affected must then influence his or her own acquaintances"}, {"note": "readiness to do 精确改写形容词 easily influenced 所体现的“乐于/易于接受影响的状态”。", "option": "the readiness to be influenced", "original": "a critical mass of easily influenced people"}]}}, {"id": "ky1-2010-t4", "exam": "考研英语一", "difficulty": "L3", "origin": "official", "year": "2010", "examSet": "2010 考研英语一真题（4篇全套）", "sourceLabel": "2010 考研英语一真题 Text 4", "title": "会计准则制定机构独立性面临妥协危机", "subtitle": "银行游说施压会计准则制定机构放宽资产估值标准及其引发的独立性危机", "timeLimitMin": 18, "wordCount": 433, "paragraphs": ["Bankers have been blaming themselves for their troubles in public. Behind the scenes, they have been taking aim at someone else: the accounting standard-setters. Their rules, moan the banks, have forced them to report enormous losses, and it's just not fair. These rules say they must value some assets at the price a third party would pay, not the price managers and regulators would like them to fetch.", "Unfortunately, banks' lobbying now seems to be working. The details may be unknowable, but the independence of standard-setters, essential to the proper functioning of capital markets, is being compromised. And, unless banks carry toxic assets at prices that attract buyers, reviving the banking system will be difficult. After a bruising encounter with Congress, America's Financial Accounting Standards Board (FASB) rushed through rule changes. These gave banks more freedom to use models to value illiquid assets and more flexibility in recognizing losses on long-term assets in their income statements. Bob Herz, the FASB's chairman, cried out against those who \"question our motives.\" Yet bank shares rose and the changes enhance what one lobbying group politely calls \"the use of judgment by management.\" European ministers instantly demanded that the International Accounting Standards Board (IASB) do likewise. The IASB says it does not want to act without overall planning, but the pressure to fold when it completes its reconstruction of rules later this year is strong. Charlie McCreevy, a European commissioner, warned the IASB that it did \"not live in a political vacuum\" but \"in the real world\" and that Europe could yet develop different rules.", "It was banks that were on the wrong planet, with accounts that vastly overvalued assets. Today they argue that market prices overstate losses, because they largely reflect the temporary illiquidity of markets, not the likely extent of bad debts. The truth will not be known for years. But banks' shares trade below their book value, suggesting that investors are skeptical. And dead markets partly reflect the paralysis of banks which will not sell assets for fear of booking losses, yet are reluctant to buy all those supposed bargains.", "To get the system working again, losses must be recognized and dealt with. America's new plan to buy up toxic assets will not work unless banks mark assets to levels which buyers find attractive. Successful markets require independent and even combative standard-setters. The FASB and IASB have been exactly that, cleaning up rules on stock options and pensions, for example, against hostility from special interests. But by giving in to critics now they are inviting pressure to make more concessions."], "translations": ["银行家们一直在公开场合为自己的困境自责。而在幕后，他们却一直将矛头指向另一批人：会计准则制定者。银行抱怨称，这些人的规则迫使它们报告巨额亏损，这实在太不公平了。这些规则要求银行必须按第三方愿意支付的价格——而非银行管理层和监管机构希望卖出的价格——来为部分资产估值。", "不幸的是，银行的游说如今似乎正在奏效。具体细节或许无从知晓，但对资本市场正常运转至关重要的准则制定机构的独立性正在受到损害。而且，除非银行以能够吸引买家的价格在账面列示有毒资产，否则银行业的复苏将十分困难。在与国会经历了一场激烈交锋后，美国财务会计准则委员会（FASB）仓促通过了规则修改。这些修改赋予银行更大的自由去使用模型为流动性差的资产估值，并在损益表中确认长期资产亏损时享有更大的灵活性。FASB主席鲍勃·赫茨对那些“质疑我们动机”的人表示愤慨。然而银行股却应声上涨，且这些修改扩大了一个游说团体委婉称之为“管理层运用主观判断”的空间。欧洲各国部长随即要求国际会计准则理事会（IASB）效仿此举。IASB表示不愿在缺乏整体规划的情况下贸然行动，但当它在今年晚些时候完成规则重构时，迫使其屈服的压力将十分巨大。欧盟委员查理·麦克里维警告IASB，它“并非生活在政治真空中”，而是生活在“现实世界里”，欧洲完全有可能自行制定不同的规则。", "真正脱离现实的是银行，它们的账目严重高估了资产价值。如今银行辩称市场价格夸大了亏损，因为这些价格主要反映的是市场暂时的流动性不足，而非坏账的可能规模。真相在多年之内都无从知晓。但银行股价的交易价格低于其账面价值，这表明投资者对此持怀疑态度。而市场的死气沉沉在一定程度上反映了银行的瘫痪状态——它们因害怕在账面上确认亏损而不愿出售资产，却又不情愿买入所有那些所谓的低价资产。", "要让金融体系重新运转起来，就必须承认并处理亏损。除非银行将资产减记至买家认为有吸引力的水平，否则美国收购有毒资产的新计划将无法奏效。成功的市场需要独立乃至敢于抗争的准则制定机构。FASB和IASB过去正是如此，例如它们曾顶住特殊利益集团的敌意，清理了有关股票期权和养老金的规则。但如今向批评者让步，它们正招致外界施加更多要求妥协的压力。"], "questions": [{"no": 1, "type": "细节题", "stem": "Bankers complained that they were forced to", "options": ["follow unfavorable asset evaluation rules.", "collect payments from third parties.", "cooperate with the price managers.", "reevaluate some of their assets."], "answer": 0, "evidencePara": 1, "evidenceQuote": "Their rules, moan the banks, have forced them to report enormous losses, and it's just not fair. These rules say they must value some assets at the price a third party would pay, not the price managers and regulators would like them to fetch.", "explanation": "定位第1段第3至4句。题干中complained同义替换moan，forced to直接对应原词。银行抱怨会计准则制定机构的规定迫使它们报告巨额亏损，且要求按第三方愿意支付的市场价格而非管理者或监管者期望的价格对资产进行估值。这说明银行认为现行资产估值规则对其不利，A项follow unfavorable asset evaluation rules准确概括了这一抱怨内容。", "trapNote": "B项望文生义，将“按第三方愿意支付的价格估值”曲解为“向第三方收款”；C项误读并列结构，原文为managers and regulators（管理者和监管者），并非price managers。"}, {"no": 2, "type": "推断题", "stem": "According to the author, the rule changes of the FASB may result in", "options": ["the diminishing role of management.", "the revival of the banking system.", "the banks' long-term asset losses.", "the weakening of its independence."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The details may be unknowable, but the independence of standard-setters, essential to the proper functioning of capital markets, is being compromised. And, unless banks carry toxic assets at prices that attract buyers, reviving the banking system will be difficult. After a bruising encounter with Congress, America's Financial Accounting Standards Board (FASB) rushed through rule changes.", "explanation": "定位第2段第2至4句。作者首先指出银行游说正在奏效，这对资本市场正常运作至关重要的准则制定机构的独立性正在受损(independence... is being compromised)；随后紧接着以美国财务会计准则委员会(FASB)在国会施压后仓促修改规则为例加以印证。由此可见，FASB修改规则会导致其独立性削弱，对应D项the weakening of its independence。", "trapNote": "A项与原文相反，修改规则恰恰扩大了管理层的自由裁量权(the use of judgment by management)；B项亦与原文逻辑相悖，作者认为若不按吸引买家的价格计价，银行业将难以复苏。"}, {"no": 3, "type": "推断题", "stem": "According to Paragraph 4, McCreevy objects to the IASB's attempt to", "options": ["keep away from political influences.", "evade the pressure from their peers.", "act on their own in rule-setting.", "take gradual measures in reform."], "answer": 2, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "The IASB says it does not want to act without overall planning, but the pressure to fold when it completes its reconstruction of rules later this year is strong. Charlie McCreevy, a European commissioner, warned the IASB that it did \"not live in a political vacuum\" but \"in the real world\" and that Europe could yet develop different rules.", "explanation": "定位所供文本第2段末两句（原真题分段中为第4段）。IASB表示不愿仓促跟进，而欧盟委员McCreevy警告称IASB并非生活在政治真空中，且“欧洲完全可能自行制定不同规则”。他意在施压IASB顺应欧洲政治与银行诉求，反对IASB在规则制定上不顾欧洲立场而独自行动。C项act on their own in rule-setting准确揭示了其反对态度。", "trapNote": "A项极具迷惑性，但“not live in a political vacuum”是McCreevy用于威慑的理由，而非IASB“企图远离政治影响”的行为本身；IASB此前强调的是按自身整体规划推进，拒绝外部强压下的跟随。"}, {"no": 4, "type": "细节题", "stem": "The author thinks the banks were \"on the wrong planet\" in that they", "options": ["misinterpreted market price indicators.", "exaggerated the real value of their assets.", "neglected the likely existence of bad debts.", "denied booking losses in their sale of assets."], "answer": 1, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "It was banks that were on the wrong planet, with accounts that vastly overvalued assets.", "explanation": "定位第3段首句。作者以“脱离现实（on the wrong planet）”反驳银行对准则制定者的指责，并在后面的with伴随状语中直接给出原因：银行账目严重高估了资产价值（vastly overvalued assets）。B项exaggerated the real value of their assets与vastly overvalued assets构成精准同义改写，直接说明了银行“活在错误星球”的原因。", "trapNote": "A项和C项均混淆了后文银行当前的辩解（声称市场价格反映暂时流动性不足而非坏账），并非作者指责银行脱离现实的原因；D项曲解了末句，银行是不愿因出售资产而确认亏损，并非否认记账亏损。"}, {"no": 5, "type": "态度题", "stem": "The author's attitude towards standard-setters is one of", "options": ["satisfaction.", "skepticism.", "objectiveness.", "sympathy."], "answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Successful markets require independent and even combative standard-setters. The FASB and IASB have been exactly that, cleaning up rules on stock options and pensions, for example, against hostility from special interests. But by giving in to critics now they are inviting pressure to make more concessions.", "explanation": "定位第4段及第2段相关表述。作者认为成功的市场需要独立乃至敢于抗争的准则制定机构，充分肯定FASB和IASB过去顶住特殊利益集团敌意清理期权和养老金规则的作为，同时对其当前在国会与欧洲政治压力下被迫妥协表示担忧与惋惜（第2段首句即用Unfortunately表明态度）。综合而言，作者对准则制定机构抱有支持与同情，对应D项sympathy。", "trapNote": "A项satisfaction（满意）不准确，作者对其目前向批评者让步的做法明确表示遗憾和担忧；C项objectiveness（客观）虽常见但弱化了作者鲜明站在准则制定者一边、谴责银行游说施压的立场。"}], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "损害，削弱，妥协", "note": "在“independence... is being compromised”中表示“独立性受损/受到损害”，而非“达成妥协”。", "word": "compromise"}, {"gloss": "流动性差的，难以变现的", "note": "由否定前缀 il- + liquid（流动的/易变现的）构成；illiquid assets 指难以迅速按公允价格售出的资产。", "word": "illiquid"}, {"gloss": "屈服，让步，认输", "note": "在商业与政治语境中，pressure to fold 指迫于压力而屈服、妥协。", "word": "fold"}, {"gloss": "怀疑的，持怀疑态度的", "note": "在考研阅读态度题和观点题中高频出现，也可拼写为 sceptical。", "word": "skeptical"}, {"gloss": "好斗的，敢于抗争的", "note": "文中用于褒义，形容准则制定机构不惧利益集团压力、立场坚定。", "word": "combative"}, {"gloss": "让步，妥协", "note": "make concessions 为固定搭配，表示“做出让步”。", "word": "concession"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "These gave banks more freedom to use models to value illiquid assets and more flexibility in recognizing losses on long-term assets in their income statements.", "point": "看清并列宾语 more freedom... and more flexibility... 及其各自的修饰限定成分，理解FASB新规对银行的松绑方式。", "structure": "主干为 These gave banks more freedom and more flexibility；不定式 to use models to value... 修饰 freedom，介词短语 in recognizing... 修饰 flexibility。", "zh": "这些新规赋予银行更大的自由去使用模型为流动性差的资产估值，并在损益表中确认长期资产亏损时享有更大的灵活性。"}, {"en": "The IASB says it does not want to act without overall planning, but the pressure to fold when it completes its reconstruction of rules later this year is strong.", "point": "把握转折连词 but 前后的博弈关系，注意 the pressure to fold 被较长的 when 时间状语从句隔开后的主系表结构（the pressure... is strong）。", "structure": "but 连接两个并列分句；后半句主语为 the pressure，不定式 to fold 作定语，when 引导时间状语从句，谓语为 is strong。", "zh": "国际会计准则理事会表示不愿在缺乏整体规划的情况下贸然行动，但当它在今年晚些时候完成规则重构时，迫使其屈服的压力将十分巨大。"}, {"en": "And dead markets partly reflect the paralysis of banks which will not sell assets for fear of booking losses, yet are reluctant to buy all those supposed bargains.", "point": "理解 which 定语从句内部由 yet 连接的银行矛盾行为（既不敢卖又不敢买），把握市场陷入僵局的双重根源。", "structure": "主干为 dead markets partly reflect the paralysis of banks；which 引导定语从句修饰 banks，从句内部包含 will not sell... yet are reluctant to buy... 两个并列谓语。", "zh": "而市场的死气沉沉在一定程度上反映了银行的瘫痪状态——它们因害怕在账面上确认亏损而不愿出售资产，却又不情愿买入所有那些所谓的低价资产。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "verb moan（抱怨、哀叹）直接对应题干中的 complained。", "option": "Bankers complained", "original": "moan the banks"}, {"note": "将“按第三方买价估值而非管理层期望价格”的规则概括为对银行不利的资产估值规则。", "option": "follow unfavorable asset evaluation rules", "original": "value some assets at the price a third party would pay, not the price managers and regulators would like them to fetch"}, {"note": "weakening 与 is being compromised 均表达“独立性遭到削弱/损害”。", "option": "the weakening of its independence", "original": "the independence of standard-setters... is being compromised"}, {"note": "exaggerated the real value 精准同义替换 vastly overvalued（严重高估）。", "option": "exaggerated the real value of their assets", "original": "vastly overvalued assets"}, {"note": "警告“不生活在政治真空中且欧洲可能另立规则”，实质是反对对方按自身规划独自制定规则。", "option": "act on their own in rule-setting", "original": "does not want to act without overall planning / not live in a political vacuum"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L4", "exam": "advanced", "id": "adv-l4-p1", "origin": "curated", "paragraphs": ["Municipal governments increasingly enlist machine-learning models to triage welfare claims, prioritize inspections, and inform bail rulings, tasks once reserved for fallible human discretion. Proponents credit such tools with curbing overt prejudice while taxing municipal budgets far less heavily than conventional casework. Yet beneath the veneer of mathematical neutrality lies a disquieting civic dilemma: when an automated verdict denies housing or flags a citizen for audit, who answers for the error?", "In response to mounting outcry over opaque \"black-box\" algorithms, lawmakers from Brussels to Sacramento have championed transparency mandates as a panacea. Open the proprietary code to public inspection, the prevailing wisdom holds, and accountability will naturally follow. That faith, however, misconstrues both the mechanics of contemporary artificial intelligence and the sociology of bureaucratic power. Inspecting millions of shifting statistical weights in a deep neural network yields little intelligible rationale, much less a legal basis for appeal.", "Worse still, forced disclosure can ironically compromise the very oversight it purports to advance. Software vendors frequently invoke trade-secret protections to shield core architectures, leaving regulators with sanitized technical summaries that register compliance on paper while obscuring bias in practice. Even where source code is freely published, agencies rarely possess the technical fluency to audit it independently, and an overload of raw documentation can act as a smokescreen, drowning watchdogs in data rather than illuminating decisions.", "Consider the cautionary episode of a regional benefits-fraud scoring tool abandoned after investigative journalists obtained its technical manual. Far from exposing deliberate malice, the released blueprints revealed how routine administrative shortcuts—such as treating unstable employment as a proxy for deception—had quietly entrenched socioeconomic penalties. Transparency arrived only after years of litigation, and only because external reporters, rather than statutory auditors, knew which assumptions to interrogate.", "To bridge this accountability gap, scholars of administrative law increasingly urge a shift from mere visibility to contestability. Instead of demanding full algorithmic disclosure—a standard that often shields vendors behind intellectual-property claims or overwhelms the public—governments should mandate clear, individual explanations of adverse outcomes alongside accessible channels for human review. Equally vital is empowering independent oversight bodies to conduct adversarial audits of training data and error rates before deployment, rather than waiting for harm to surface in court.", "Algorithms need not be banished from civic life, yet democratic legitimacy demands that automation remain subordinate to public judgment. Until institutions pair technical rigor with enforceable rights of redress, the promise of transparent governance will remain an empty gesture, visible on paper yet elusive where citizens need it most."], "questions": [{"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Inspecting millions of shifting statistical weights in a deep neural network yields little intelligible rationale, much less a legal basis for appeal.", "explanation": "定位至第2段末句。该句指出，审查深度神经网络中数以百万计不断变化的统计权重，既得不出清晰易懂的决策依据（little intelligible rationale），更谈不上构成上诉的法律基础（a legal basis for appeal）。D项中的“cannot be readily translated into legally actionable explanations”正是对这一技术黑箱与法律救济脱节现象的精准同义替换。", "no": 1, "options": ["Lawmakers deliberately prioritize technical complexity over citizens' legal rights.", "Deep neural networks are inherently incompatible with administrative governance.", "Public inspection alters statistical weights before citizens can lodge an appeal.", "Raw algorithmic parameters cannot be readily translated into legally actionable explanations."], "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, why do lawmakers' transparency mandates fall short of ensuring accountability?", "trapNote": "C项属于张冠李戴与词义误读，将原文描述神经网络自身参数动态特征的“shifting statistical weights”曲解为“公众审查会导致权重改变”。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "shield core architectures, leaving regulators with sanitized technical summaries that register compliance on paper while obscuring bias in practice.", "explanation": "定位至第3段第2句。上文提到软件供应商以商业秘密为由隐匿核心架构（shield core architectures），后文转折指出技术摘要表面合规实则掩盖偏见（register compliance on paper while obscuring bias in practice）。由此推断，sanitized在此处取熟词僻义，指经过“刻意删减、粉饰敏感缺陷的”，与C项“selectively scrubbed”完美对应。", "no": 2, "options": ["officially certified", "exhaustively detailed", "selectively scrubbed", "maliciously fabricated"], "stem": "The word \"sanitized\" (Paragraph 3) most probably means _____.", "trapNote": "D项属于过度推理，原文强调供应商借摘要隐藏偏见与核心架构，但第4段也明确指出偏见未必源于恶意伪造（deliberate malice），故“maliciously fabricated”言过其实。", "type": "词义题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Transparency arrived only after years of litigation, and only because external reporters, rather than statutory auditors, knew which assumptions to interrogate.", "explanation": "定位至第4段例证及其末句主旨落脚点。该案例承接第3段对“形式化公开”的批判，指出即便技术手册最终公开，透明问责也经历了漫长诉讼，且仅因外部记者（而非法定审计员）懂得质询其中隐藏的行政预设才得以实现。B项将“external reporters... knew which assumptions to interrogate”概括为“公开文件须辅以批判性审视方能产生问责效力”，切中例证核心。", "no": 3, "options": ["deliberate programmer malice is the primary driver of automated discrimination", "disclosing technical documents creates accountability only when paired with critical scrutiny", "investigative journalists are better equipped than judges to redesign welfare systems", "automated scoring tools should be outlawed whenever employment histories are analyzed"], "stem": "The author cites the regional benefits-fraud scoring tool in Paragraph 4 primarily to show that _____.", "trapNote": "A项属于正反颠倒，第4段明确以“Far from exposing deliberate malice”否定系统性惩罚源自开发者刻意恶意，而将其归因于例行行政捷径。", "type": "例证题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "governments should mandate clear, individual explanations of adverse outcomes alongside accessible channels for human review.", "explanation": "定位至第5段提出的治理转向方案。该段主张放弃往往沦为挡箭牌或信息过载的“全面算法公开”，转而要求政府对不利结果提供清晰的个体化解释、畅通的人工复核渠道，并在部署前开展对抗性审计（rather than waiting for harm to surface in court）。据此可合理推断，可争辩性原则把可操作的公民救济保障与事前主动审计置于全盘代码公开之上（A项）。", "no": 4, "options": ["It favors actionable citizen safeguards and proactive audits over exhaustive code release.", "It resolves intellectual-property disputes by banning proprietary software in public agencies.", "It shifts primary oversight responsibility from independent regulators to judicial courts.", "It replaces algorithmic scoring with manual human review for all routine public decisions."], "stem": "What can be inferred from Paragraph 5 about the proposed shift toward \"contestability\"?", "trapNote": "D项属于以偏概全，原文主张的是为“不利结果（adverse outcomes）”提供人工复核渠道，而非用人工审查取代所有常规公共决策中的算法。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Algorithms need not be banished from civic life, yet democratic legitimacy demands that automation remain subordinate to public judgment.", "explanation": "定位至第6段首句并结合第1、5段立场。作者既在第1段肯定算法有助于节省市政预算与遏制显性偏见，又在末段强调“算法不必被逐出公共生活（need not be banished）”，但紧接着以yet转折指出民主合法性要求自动化必须服从公共判断并配有可执行的救济权利。由此可见，作者对公共治理中的算法持“审慎接纳但坚持制度约束”的辩证态度（C项）。", "no": 5, "options": ["Dismissive of their potential to ease administrative burdens", "Optimistic that voluntary industry disclosure will correct bias", "Measured in acceptance yet insistent on institutional checks", "Skeptical that public oversight bodies can ever evaluate technical risks"], "stem": "What is the author's attitude toward algorithmic tools in public governance?", "trapNote": "D项属于过度推理与以偏概全，第3段虽指出监管机构目前往往缺乏技术流利度，但第5段明确主张通过赋权独立监管机构开展事前对抗性审计来弥补，并非认为监管永远无法评估技术风险。", "type": "态度题"}], "sourceLabel": "外刊同源拔高（L4 压轴训练）", "subtitle": "科技伦理与算法透明度：公共治理中的黑箱问责困境", "timeLimitMin": 20, "title": "When the Code Decides: The Paradox of Algorithmic Transparency", "year": "外刊同源", "wordCount": 423, "translations": ["市政当局越来越多地采用机器学习模型来分流福利申请、排定检查优先级以及为保释裁决提供参考——这些任务曾专属于容易出错的人类自由裁量。支持者认为，这类工具在遏制明显偏见的同时，对市政预算造成的负担也远低于传统人工个案处理。然而，在数学中立的表象之下，隐藏着一个令人不安的公共治理困境：当自动裁决拒绝提供住房或将某位公民标记为审查对象时，谁来为其中的错误负责？", "面对针对不透明“黑箱”算法日益高涨的批评声浪，从布鲁塞尔到萨克拉门托的立法者纷纷将强制透明法案吹捧为万能灵药。主流观点认为，只要将专有代码向公众开放审查，问责机制便会水到渠成。然而，这种信念既误解了当代人工智能的运作机制，也误判了官僚权力的社会学规律。检视深度神经网络中数百万个不断变化的统计权重，几乎无法得出可理解的推理依据，更遑论为上诉提供法律基础。", "更糟糕的是，强制披露具有讽刺意味地反而会削弱它声称要推进的监管。软件供应商经常援引商业秘密保护条款来屏蔽核心架构，只留给监管机构经过删节润色的技术摘要——这些文件在纸面上显示合规，在实践中却掩盖了偏见。即便源代码免费公开，监管机构也鲜少具备独立审计的技术能力；而过载的原始文档还会起到烟幕弹的作用，将监督者淹没在数据海洋中，而非阐明决策逻辑。", "不妨看看一个具有警示意义的案例：一款地区性福利欺诈评分工具在调查记者获取其技术手册后被废止。公开的蓝图远未揭露蓄意作恶，反而显示出诸如将不稳定就业视为欺诈替代指标等常规行政捷径，是如何悄然固化社会经济惩罚的。透明是在经过多年诉讼后才得以实现的，而且仅仅是因为外部记者——而非法定审计人员——知道应当质疑哪些预设前提。", "为了弥合这一问责鸿沟，行政法学者越来越主张从单纯的“可见性”转向“可质疑性”。政府不应一味要求全面公开算法——这一标准往往让供应商得以躲在知识产权主张背后，或令公众不堪重负——而应当强制要求针对不利结果提供清晰的个性化解释，并配套便捷的人工复核渠道。同样至关重要的是，应当授权独立监管机构在算法部署前对训练数据和错误率开展对抗性审计，而不是坐等损害发生后再诉诸法庭。", "算法不必被逐出公共生活，但民主合法性要求自动化始终服从于公众评判。除非各机构将技术严谨性与可强制执行的救济权结合起来，否则透明治理的承诺仍将是一纸空文——在文件上清晰可见，在公民最需要的地方却遥不可及。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "使负重担，消耗，考验", "note": "熟词僻义：名词常考“税”，作动词在阅读中常表“使负担过重、消耗（精力/预算）”，如文中 taxing municipal budgets。", "word": "tax"}, {"gloss": "显示出，记录，流露", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“注册、登记”，此处意为“（在文件/表面上）显现出、记录下”，如 register compliance on paper。", "word": "register"}, {"gloss": "删节修饰（以掩盖不利信息）；给……消毒", "note": "熟词僻义：原意“消毒、净化”，在政治与商业语境中常引申为“对报告或文本进行删节清洗以掩盖敏感问题”。", "word": "sanitize"}, {"gloss": "采用，借助，征募", "note": "高频词熟义延伸：原指“应征入伍”，在科技与社会语境中常表示“采用、利用（工具、模型或人员协助）”。", "word": "enlist"}, {"gloss": "替代指标，代理人", "note": "高频学术词：除“代理人、委托书”外，在数据科学与社科语境中常指“替代变量/衡量指标”（a proxy for deception）。", "word": "proxy"}, {"gloss": "使根深蒂固，使长期固化", "note": "高频考词：常用于指偏见、制度或不利处境被长期固化，如 entrench socioeconomic penalties。", "word": "entrench"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Yet beneath the veneer of mathematical neutrality lies a disquieting civic dilemma: when an automated verdict denies housing or flags a citizen for audit, who answers for the error?", "point": "地点介词短语置于句首引起的全部倒装 + 冒号引出具体阐释", "structure": "全部倒装主句(beneath the veneer of mathematical neutrality [前置状语] + lies [谓语] + a disquieting civic dilemma [主语]) + 冒号后的解释说明(when引导时间状语从句 + who引导特殊疑问句)。", "zh": "然而，在数学中立的表象之下，隐藏着一个令人不安的公共治理困境：当自动裁决拒绝提供住房或将某位公民标记为审查对象时，谁来为其中的错误负责？"}, {"en": "Software vendors frequently invoke trade-secret protections to shield core architectures, leaving regulators with sanitized technical summaries that register compliance on paper while obscuring bias in practice.", "point": "现在分词短语作结果状语 + 定语从句嵌套while分词结构 + 熟词僻义(sanitized/register)", "structure": "主句(Software vendors frequently invoke... to shield...) + 现在分词短语作结果状语(leaving regulators with sanitized technical summaries) + that引导的定语从句(that register compliance on paper while obscuring bias in practice，内含while+现在分词作对比状语)。", "zh": "软件供应商经常援引商业秘密保护条款来屏蔽核心架构，只留给监管机构经过删节润色的技术摘要——这些文件在纸面上显示合规，在实践中却掩盖了偏见。"}, {"en": "Far from exposing deliberate malice, the released blueprints revealed how routine administrative shortcuts—such as treating unstable employment as a proxy for deception—had quietly entrenched socioeconomic penalties.", "point": "far from + 动名词短语作状语 + 双破折号插入语 + how引导宾语从句", "structure": "状语(Far from exposing deliberate malice) + 主句(the released blueprints revealed) + 宾语从句(how routine administrative shortcuts [双破折号插入语举例说明 such as...] had quietly entrenched socioeconomic penalties)。", "zh": "公开的蓝图远未揭露蓄意作恶，反而显示出诸如将不稳定就业视为欺诈替代指标等常规行政捷径，是如何悄然固化社会经济惩罚的。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "Q1同义转换：statistical weights 对应 algorithmic parameters，yields little intelligible rationale... legal basis for appeal 对应 cannot be readily translated into legally actionable explanations。", "option": "Raw algorithmic parameters cannot be readily translated into legally actionable explanations", "original": "Inspecting millions of shifting statistical weights in a deep neural network yields little intelligible rationale, much less a legal basis for appeal"}, {"note": "Q2词义猜测：结合后文“纸面合规却在实践中掩盖偏见”的语境，sanitized 在此指“经过选择性删节清洗的”。", "option": "selectively scrubbed", "original": "sanitized technical summaries that register compliance on paper while obscuring bias in practice"}, {"note": "Q3归纳替换：knew which assumptions to interrogate（知道质疑哪些预设）对应 critical scrutiny（批判性审视）。", "option": "disclosing technical documents creates accountability only when paired with critical scrutiny", "original": "only because external reporters, rather than statutory auditors, knew which assumptions to interrogate"}, {"note": "Q4概括替换：个性化解释、人工复核渠道与部署前审计分别对应 citizen safeguards 与 proactive audits，优于单纯的全面代码公开。", "option": "favors actionable citizen safeguards and proactive audits over exhaustive code release", "original": "mandate clear, individual explanations of adverse outcomes alongside accessible channels for human review... conduct adversarial audits... before deployment"}, {"note": "Q5态度题归纳：need not be banished 体现有节制地接纳（measured in acceptance），demands... subordinate to public judgment 体现坚持制度制衡（insistent on institutional checks）。", "option": "Measured in acceptance yet insistent on institutional checks", "original": "Algorithms need not be banished from civic life, yet democratic legitimacy demands that automation remain subordinate to public judgment"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L4", "exam": "advanced", "id": "adv-l4-p2", "origin": "curated", "paragraphs": ["As lethal heatwaves test the endurance of metropolitan grids, city planners have turned eagerly to \"green infrastructure\"—street trees, bioswales, and vegetated roofs—to blunt the urban heat island effect. Dark asphalt and dense masonry trap solar radiation, pushing downtown temperatures several degrees above surrounding countryside and spiking peak electricity demand. Because foliage cools neighborhoods through shading and evapotranspiration while simultaneously absorbing storm runoff, urban forestry is routinely pitched as a rare fiscal bargain that pays ecological and economic dividends alike.", "Yet ecological economists warn that celebratory cost-benefit appraisals often flatter green interventions by discounting mundane operational realities. Planting a sapling costs a fraction of maintaining it to maturity, particularly in compacted urban soils laced with utility lines and road salt. In arid cities, sustaining lush tree canopies can tax scarce municipal water supplies, pitting summer cooling against drought resilience. Even vegetated roofs, widely touted for lowering indoor cooling loads, demand structural reinforcement whose upfront capital expense can eclipse energy savings for decades.", "The spatial distribution of cooling benefits introduces an equally vexing equity wrinkle. Empirical audits across major cities show that canopy cover tracks property values closely, leaving low-income industrial districts markedly hotter than leafy affluent suburbs. When municipalities subsequently install pocket parks or shaded corridors in neglected neighborhoods, however, they risk triggering \"ecological gentrification.\" Rising amenity values frequently invite speculative redevelopment, pushing up rents and displacing the very heat-vulnerable residents whom public funds were intended to shield.", "Consider a recent comparative modeling study of mid-sized European cities evaluating cooling strategies per euro spent. High-albedo \"cool pavements\" and reflective roof coatings delivered faster, cheaper surface temperature drops in dense commercial cores where underground cables precluded deep tree pits. Yet reflective surfaces merely bounced radiation back onto pedestrians at street level when poorly sited, and failed to capture the mental-health, air-filtration, and flood-buffering gains that greenery provides, illustrating why narrow engineering metrics can distort policy choices.", "Rather than treating vegetation as an all-purpose panacea or dismissing it as an expensive luxury, urban planners should embrace portfolio thinking. Pairing targeted drought-tolerant plantings with reflective surfaces, permeable paving, and tenant-protection ordinances allows cities to match remedies to local microclimates while containing displacement. Crucially, municipal accounting must credit multi-decade public-health savings, such as fewer heatstroke hospitalizations, rather than fixating on annual upkeep, lest tight fiscal cycles starve projects whose returns compound slowly.", "Urban cooling, ultimately, is less a horticultural makeover than an exercise in political economy. Trees and reflective roofs alike deliver enduring value only when planners reckon honestly with maintenance costs, spatial trade-offs, and who bears the bill."], "questions": [{"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "celebratory cost-benefit appraisals often flatter green interventions by discounting mundane operational realities.", "explanation": "定位至第2段首句及后续展开论述。生态经济学家指出，乐观的成本收益评估常通过低估日常运营现实来美化绿色干预措施（flatter green interventions by discounting mundane operational realities），具体包括树木成活前的管护成本、地下管线与压实土壤的限制、干旱城市的水资源消耗以及绿色屋顶漫长的结构加固回本期。A项精准概括了“忽视持续维护成本与因地制宜的物理限制”。", "no": 1, "options": ["They overlook ongoing upkeep expenses and site-specific physical constraints.", "They exaggerate foliage's capacity to reduce peak electricity consumption.", "They assume green roofs can repay upfront structural costs within a few years.", "They ignore the biodiversity losses triggered by compacted urban soils."], "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, why do cost-benefit appraisals often overstate the economic appeal of green infrastructure?", "trapNote": "B项属于偷换概念与无中生有，第1段说明植被降温可削减峰值用电需求，第2段并未质疑这一物理机制，而是指出财政评估忽视了维护与前置投入。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "Rising amenity values frequently invite speculative redevelopment, pushing up rents and displacing the very heat-vulnerable residents whom public funds were intended to shield.", "explanation": "定位至第3段后两句。前句提出在被忽视街区兴建袖珍公园或林荫道会引发“ecological gentrification”，紧接着下句阐明其具体机制：环境便利设施价值上升吸引投机性再开发，推高房租并迫使原本最易受高温侵害的低收入居民搬离。C项“环境改善推高地产价值并挤走弱势本地居民”与该句同义高度吻合。", "no": 2, "options": ["wealthy residents abandon older suburbs for newly planted downtown corridors", "private developers demolish neighborhood parks to construct high-density housing", "environmental upgrades raise property values and price out vulnerable locals", "municipalities redirect cooling funds from industrial districts to affluent suburbs"], "stem": "The term \"ecological gentrification\" (Paragraph 3) most likely refers to a process in which _____.", "trapNote": "D项属于逻辑倒置与偷换概念，原文指出政府资金原本正是为了保护弱势居民（whom public funds were intended to shield），只是市场租金反馈导致了意外排挤，而非政府主动把资金转移给富人区。", "type": "词义题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "failed to capture the mental-health, air-filtration, and flood-buffering gains that greenery provides, illustrating why narrow engineering metrics can distort policy choices.", "explanation": "定位至第4段对比研究及其末句结论。虽然在地下管线密集的商业核心区，高反照率涂层在“每欧元降温幅度”上更快更便宜，但若选址不当会将辐射反射给行人，且无法计入绿植在心理健康、空气过滤与防洪缓冲方面的附带收益，由此说明“狭隘的工程指标会扭曲政策选择”。D项准确点出该研究旨在批判仅以直接降温与单项成本衡量方案的片面性。", "no": 3, "options": ["To demonstrate that reflective coatings outperform urban greenery across all climate zones", "To argue that underground utility cables render tree planting futile in modern cities", "To warn that cool pavements inevitably raise street-level heat exposure for pedestrians", "To show that judging cooling options solely by direct temperature and cost figures is misleading"], "stem": "Why does the author cite the European comparative modeling study in Paragraph 4?", "trapNote": "C项属于过度推理与绝对化，原文限定反射面仅在“选址不当（when poorly sited）”时才会将辐射反弹给街面行人，并非必然恶化行人热暴露。", "type": "例证题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "municipal accounting must credit multi-decade public-health savings, such as fewer heatstroke hospitalizations, rather than fixating on annual upkeep", "explanation": "定位至第5段末句。该句指出市政会计必须把跨越数十年的公共卫生节省（如减少中暑住院）纳入考量，而非死盯年度维护开支，以免紧缩的财政周期让那些回报缓慢复利增长的项目陷入资金断流（lest tight fiscal cycles starve projects whose returns compound slowly）。由此可推断，短期财政视角往往会不利于回报逐步累积的长期投资（B项）。", "no": 4, "options": ["Tenant-protection laws can substitute for matching cooling measures to local climates.", "Short-term fiscal horizons tend to penalize investments whose payoffs accumulate gradually.", "Public-health agencies should take over routine tree maintenance from municipal utilities.", "Drought-tolerant plantings generate immediate financial returns that offset annual upkeep."], "stem": "What can be inferred from Paragraph 5 about municipal budgeting for urban cooling?", "trapNote": "D项属于正反颠倒，原文明确强调相关生态项目的收益是“缓慢复利积累的（returns compound slowly）”，并非能立竿见影抵消年度管护费的短期回报。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Trees and reflective roofs alike deliver enduring value only when planners reckon honestly with maintenance costs, spatial trade-offs, and who bears the bill.", "explanation": "定位至第6段全文总结句，并纵贯前五段论证。文章先破除“绿色基建稳赚不赔”的单一神话，剖析维护成本（第2段）、生态绅士化与公平悖论（第3段）及单一工程指标的局限（第4段），进而倡导“组合思维”、租户保护与长周期公共卫生核算（第5段），最后点明城市降温归根结底是政治经济学命题（第6段）。A项完整囊括“多元物理方案组合”“务实成本核算”与“社会公平”三大支柱。", "no": 5, "options": ["Effective urban cooling requires pairing diverse physical remedies with realistic accounting and social equity.", "Urban forestry has proven too resource-intensive to serve as a viable strategy against heatwaves.", "Reflective engineering surfaces provide a fairer and cheaper alternative to urban green spaces.", "Rising energy prices have compelled European planners to abandon green infrastructure projects."], "stem": "Which of the following best summarizes the central argument of the passage?", "trapNote": "B项属于过度推理与正反颠倒，作者批判的是盲目美化绿色基建的评估方式，而非全盘否定城市林业的可行性，第5段恰恰主张将其纳入组合方案。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "外刊同源拔高（L4 压轴训练）", "subtitle": "生态经济与城市降温：城市热岛效应与绿色基础设施的成本收益之争", "timeLimitMin": 20, "title": "Shade at a Price: Rethinking the Economics of Urban Cooling", "year": "外刊同源", "wordCount": 440, "translations": ["随着致命热浪不断考验大都市电网的承受极限，城市规划者纷纷热切求助于“绿色基础设施”——即行道树、生态植草沟和植被屋顶——以缓解城市热岛效应。深色沥青和密集的砖石建筑会蓄积太阳辐射，使市中心气温比周边乡村高出数度，并推高用电高峰期的电力需求。由于绿植既能通过遮荫和蒸腾作用为街区降温，又能同时吸纳暴雨径流，城市林业常被吹捧为一种兼顾生态与经济双重红利的罕见财政划算买卖。", "然而生态经济学家警告称，赞歌式的成本效益评估往往因忽视平淡琐碎的运营现实，而过度美化了绿色干预措施。种下一株树苗的成本仅占将其养护至成材所需费用的九牛一毛，在布满地下管线和融雪盐的板结城市土壤中更是如此。在干旱城市中，维持茂密的树冠可能会消耗本就稀缺的市政水资源，使夏季降温与抗旱韧性陷入两难。即便是因降低室内制冷负荷而广受吹捧的植被屋顶，也需要对建筑结构进行加固，而这笔前期资本开支在数十年内都可能远超其节省的能源费用。", "降温收益的空间分布还带来了同样棘手的公平性难题。各大城市的实证审计表明，树冠覆盖率与房产价值高度正相关，导致低收入工业区比绿树成荫的富裕郊区明显更热。然而，当市政当局随后在被忽视的街区修建口袋公园或林荫走廊时，却又面临引发“生态绅士化”的风险。环境宜居度的提升往往会招致投机性再开发，推高房租并挤走那些公共资金原本旨在保护的高温脆弱居民。", "不妨思考近期一项针对欧洲中等规模城市、评估每欧元投入对应降温成效的对比建模研究。在地下电缆密布、无法挖掘深树坑的密集商业核心区，高反射率的“清凉路面”和反光屋顶涂层实现了更快、更廉价的地表降温。然而，反光表面一旦选址不当，只会将太阳辐射重新反射到街道行人的身上，且无法实现绿植所能提供的心理健康改善、空气过滤和雨水滞蓄等收益，这充分说明了狭隘的工程指标为何会扭曲政策选择。", "城市规划者与其将植被奉为包治百病的灵丹妙药，或将其贬为昂贵的奢侈品，不如采取投资组合式的思维。将有针对性的耐旱植物种植与反光表面、透水铺装以及租户保护条例相结合，能使城市在遏制居民流离失所的同时，因地制宜地为局地微气候匹配解决方案。至关重要的是，市政会计核算必须将数十年间节省的公共卫生开支（例如中暑住院人数的减少）计入收益，而非紧盯年度维护费用，以免捉襟见肘的财政周期断送了那些回报缓慢累积的长期项目。", "归根结底，城市降温与其说是一场园艺改造，不如说是一场政治经济学的考验。唯有当规划者诚实直面维护成本、空间权衡以及“由谁买单”的问题时，树木与反光屋顶才能真正释放持久的价值。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 低估，忽视，不予考虑", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“打折”，在考研/四六级学术阅读中常作动词表示“轻视、不考虑、认为……不重要”（文中指忽略日常运营现实）。", "word": "discount"}, {"gloss": "v. 使相形见绌，超过，遮蔽", "note": "熟词僻义：名词常指“日食/月食”，作动词在经济与比较语境中常表“使黯然失色、远超”（文中指前期成本远超节能收益）。", "word": "eclipse"}, {"gloss": "v. 使负重担，消耗，使吃力", "note": "熟词僻义：作名词意为“税”，作动词除“征税”外，高频考查“使……承受重压、过度消耗（资源或精力）”。", "word": "tax"}, {"gloss": "v. 把……记入（账目），认可，归功于", "note": "熟词僻义：除名词“信用/学分”外，作动词在财政会计语境中表“将……计入收益/纳入核算”。", "word": "credit"}, {"gloss": "adj. 令人烦恼的，棘手的", "note": "高频问题描述词：常用于引出政策制定或现实分析中的复杂难题与矛盾（如 equity wrinkle）。", "word": "vexing"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "Even vegetated roofs, widely touted for lowering indoor cooling loads, demand structural reinforcement whose upfront capital expense can eclipse energy savings for decades.", "point": "过去分词短语作后置定语（widely touted...）+ whose 引导的定语从句（修饰 reinforcement）", "structure": "主干：Even vegetated roofs demand structural reinforcement；插入修饰：widely touted for lowering indoor cooling loads（过去分词短语作非限制性定语修饰 roofs）；定语从句：whose upfront capital expense can eclipse energy savings for decades（whose 在从句中作定语，指代 reinforcement 的）。", "zh": "即便是因降低室内制冷负荷而广受吹捧的植被屋顶，也需要对建筑结构进行加固，而这笔前期资本开支在数十年内都可能远超其节省的能源费用。"}, {"en": "Yet reflective surfaces merely bounced radiation back onto pedestrians at street level when poorly sited, and failed to capture the mental-health, air-filtration, and flood-buffering gains that greenery provides, illustrating why narrow engineering metrics can distort policy choices.", "point": "状语从句的省略（when poorly sited）+ 并列谓语（bounced... and failed...）+ 现在分词短语作结果/伴随状语（illustrating...）+ why 引导的宾语从句", "structure": "主干：reflective surfaces bounced radiation back... and failed to capture the gains；时间状语省略：when (they were) poorly sited；定语从句：that greenery provides（修饰 gains）；结果状语：illustrating why narrow engineering metrics can distort policy choices（其中 why 从句作 illustrating 的宾语）。", "zh": "然而，反光表面一旦选址不当，只会将太阳辐射重新反射到街道行人的身上，且无法实现绿植所能提供的心理健康改善、空气过滤和雨水滞蓄等收益，这充分说明了狭隘的工程指标为何会扭曲政策选择。"}, {"en": "Crucially, municipal accounting must credit multi-decade public-health savings, such as fewer heatstroke hospitalizations, rather than fixating on annual upkeep, lest tight fiscal cycles starve projects whose returns compound slowly.", "point": "rather than 连接并列对比结构 + lest 引导的否定目的状语从句（接动词原形构成虚拟语气）+ whose 引导的定语从句", "structure": "主干：municipal accounting must credit multi-decade public-health savings；举例插入：such as fewer heatstroke hospitalizations；对比结构：rather than fixating on annual upkeep；目的状语从句：lest tight fiscal cycles starve projects（lest 意为“以免”，后接虚拟语气动词原形 starve）；定语从句：whose returns compound slowly（修饰 projects）。", "zh": "至关重要的是，市政会计核算必须将数十年间节省的公共卫生开支（例如中暑住院人数的减少）计入收益，而非紧盯年度维护费用，以免捉襟见肘的财政周期断送了那些回报缓慢累积的长期项目。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "discount 熟词僻义作“忽视、低估”，同义替换为 overlook；mundane operational realities 具象化为日常维护开销与场地物理限制。", "option": "overlook ongoing upkeep expenses and site-specific physical constraints", "original": "discounting mundane operational realities"}, {"note": "push up rents 对应 raise property values，displace（迫使流离）精准替换为 price out（因涨价将原住民挤出）。", "option": "raise property values and price out vulnerable locals", "original": "pushing up rents and displacing the very heat-vulnerable residents"}, {"note": "narrow engineering metrics 概括为“仅看直接的温控与成本数据”，distort policy choices 替换为 is misleading。", "option": "judging cooling options solely by direct temperature and cost figures is misleading", "original": "illustrating why narrow engineering metrics can distort policy choices"}, {"note": "annual upkeep / tight fiscal cycles 对应 short-term fiscal horizons；starve 隐喻替换为 penalize；returns compound slowly 对应 payoffs accumulate gradually。", "option": "Short-term fiscal horizons tend to penalize investments whose payoffs accumulate gradually", "original": "fixating on annual upkeep, lest tight fiscal cycles starve projects whose returns compound slowly"}, {"note": "reckon honestly with maintenance costs 对应 realistic accounting，spatial trade-offs, and who bears the bill 对应 social equity。", "option": "pairing diverse physical remedies with realistic accounting and social equity", "original": "reckon honestly with maintenance costs, spatial trade-offs, and who bears the bill"}]}}, {"difficulty": "L4", "exam": "advanced", "id": "adv-l4-p3", "origin": "curated", "paragraphs": ["Every era of media upheaval has provoked predictions that new tools would ruin the human mind, from Socrates' misgivings about writing to nineteenth-century alarms over penny newspapers. Yet cognitive psychologists argue that today's attention economy—engineered around algorithmic feeds, rapid notifications, and bite-sized clips—differs in both velocity and design. Rather than merely redistributing what people know, continuous partial attention may be quietly altering how the brain regulates effortful inquiry.", "At the heart of this transformation lies a habit known as cognitive offloading: delegating memory storage and synthesis to external search engines and summarized feeds. In small doses, offloading frees scarce working memory for creative problem-solving. When platforms constantly pre-digest complexity into frictionless takeaways, however, users lose practice in building durable mental models. Critical thinking is not a discrete skill; it depends on a reservoir of structured knowledge against which new claims can be weighed and contested.", "Fragmented reading habits exact a subtler toll on patience for ambiguity. Eye-tracking experiments reveal that readers accustomed to rapid feed-scrolling adopt an \"F-shaped\" scanning pattern—sampling headlines and opening lines before darting away—even when confronting dense, print-based arguments. Because nuanced reasoning unfolds recursively, requiring readers to hold competing premises in mind before resolution arrives, skimming systematically favors punchy certainty over qualified evidence. Over time, intellectual stamina atrophies, and ideas that resist instant compression begin to register as tedious rather than rigorous.", "To test whether superficial confidence accompanies this shift, researchers recently asked volunteers to read identical policy debates either in uninterrupted long-form essays or in curated social-media threads. Although thread readers scored markedly lower on tests requiring them to synthesize counterarguments, they rated their own grasp of the topic higher than essay readers did. Depleted by constant context-switching, it appears, minds mistake fluency of retrieval for genuine comprehension—an illusion amplified by algorithms calibrated to reward outrage and consensus rather than hesitation.", "Still, blaming digital architecture alone risks lapsing into technological determinism. Human cognition remains plastic across adulthood, and the connectivity that fractures focus also democratizes access to scholarship once locked behind elite gatekeepers. Experimental interventions—from \"friction-rich\" reading interfaces that strip away hyperlinked distractions to university seminars banning devices during primary-text debates—consistently show that sustained analytical capacity rebounds when environments protect cognitive stillness.", "The central challenge, then, is neither to retreat into Luddite nostalgia nor to confuse rapid information access with wisdom. Deep critical thought survives not by accident, but through deliberate cultural and pedagogical scaffolding that treats slow, arduous attention as a civic virtue worth defending."], "questions": [{"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 2, "evidenceQuote": "Critical thinking is not a discrete skill; it depends on a reservoir of structured knowledge against which new claims can be weighed and contested.", "explanation": "定位至第2段后两句。当平台持续把复杂内容预消化为无摩擦要点时，用户就失去了构建持久心智模型的训练（lose practice in building durable mental models），而批判性思维并非孤立技能，它高度依赖可供权衡、质疑新论断的结构化知识储备（reservoir of structured knowledge）。B项以“weakens the structured knowledge base needed to test unfamiliar arguments”精准对应这一机制。", "no": 1, "options": ["It depletes scarce working memory required for creative problem-solving.", "It weakens the structured knowledge base needed to test unfamiliar arguments.", "It encourages search engines to oversimplify verified scientific findings.", "It transforms analytical inquiry into an effortless mechanical routine."], "stem": "According to Paragraph 2, how does habitual cognitive offloading undermine critical thinking?", "trapNote": "A项属于正反颠倒，第2段明确指出适度的认知卸载反而能够解放有限的工作记忆（frees scarce working memory）以用于创造性问题解决。", "type": "细节题"}, {"answer": 2, "evidencePara": 3, "evidenceQuote": "requiring readers to hold competing premises in mind before resolution arrives, skimming systematically favors punchy certainty over qualified evidence.", "explanation": "定位至第3段第3句的对比结构。该句指出细微推理需要读者在得出结论前同时兼顾相互竞争的前提（competing premises），而跳读习惯会系统性地偏爱短平快的确定性结论，冷落“qualified evidence”。此处qualified取熟词僻义，与“punchy certainty”形成反义对照，意为“有分寸的、附带限定条件的”（C项）。", "no": 2, "options": ["authoritatively certified", "emotionally provocative", "measured and conditional", "empirically outdated"], "stem": "The word \"qualified\" (Paragraph 3) most probably means _____.", "trapNote": "A项属于望文生义，误将qualified套用为常见义“合格的、经权威认证的”，忽略了语境中与武断结论（punchy certainty）构成的审慎限定对比。", "type": "词义题"}, {"answer": 0, "evidencePara": 4, "evidenceQuote": "Although thread readers scored markedly lower on tests requiring them to synthesize counterarguments, they rated their own grasp of the topic higher than essay readers did.", "explanation": "定位至第4段实验结果及其认知解释。阅读社交媒体串文的受试者在整合反方论点测试中得分明显更低，但对自身掌握程度的自评却高于长文读者；后句进一步点出，持续语境切换使大脑将提取流畅度误认为真正理解。由此可推断，碎片化阅读在削弱真实综合能力的同时，反而制造了虚高的自信（A项）。", "no": 3, "options": ["Fragmented reading can deflate real synthesis while inflating perceived mastery.", "Social-media threads expose readers to counterarguments more efficiently than essays.", "Context-switching impairs learning only when algorithms promote polarized consensus.", "Long-form essay readers underestimate their grasp of complex policy debates."], "stem": "What can be inferred from the volunteer experiment in Paragraph 4?", "trapNote": "D项属于无中生有与逻辑推演过度，文中仅说串文读者自评高于长文读者，并未说明长文读者“低估”了自己的理解水平。", "type": "推断题"}, {"answer": 3, "evidencePara": 5, "evidenceQuote": "Human cognition remains plastic across adulthood, and the connectivity that fractures focus also democratizes access to scholarship once locked behind elite gatekeepers.", "explanation": "定位至第5段全段态度脉络。作者首先否定将责任全推给数字架构的技术决定论，随后既承认网络联结会撕裂注意力（fractures focus），又肯定其打破精英壁垒、普及学术资源的积极面，并援引“高摩擦”界面与无设备课堂实验表明分析能力在受保护的环境中能够回弹（rebounds）。可见作者持兼顾利弊且对认知可塑性抱有审慎乐观的立场（D项）。", "no": 4, "options": ["Fatalistic about the irreversible erosion of adult analytical stamina", "Uncritically enthusiastic about its democratizing effect on scholarship", "Skeptical of classroom policies that restrict digital devices", "Balanced and cautiously optimistic about the mind's capacity to recover"], "stem": "What is the author's attitude toward the cognitive impact of digital connectivity in Paragraph 5?", "trapNote": "A项属于正反颠倒，第5段明确指出人类认知在成年期仍具可塑性（remains plastic），且专注分析能力在适宜环境下能够恢复，并非不可逆转地衰退。", "type": "态度题"}, {"answer": 1, "evidencePara": 6, "evidenceQuote": "Deep critical thought survives not by accident, but through deliberate cultural and pedagogical scaffolding that treats slow, arduous attention as a civic virtue", "explanation": "定位至第6段主旨总结句并统筹全文结构。文章先揭示注意力经济在速率与设计上的独特性（第1段），继而剖析认知卸载（第2段）、浅层跳读（第3段）与理解错觉（第4段）对批判思维的侵蚀，最后以认知可塑性与环境干预破除决定论（第5段），呼吁以文化和教育支架捍卫慢速深度注意力（第6段）。B项完整概括了“浅层浏览之困”与“以静修护深度思维”的核心议题。", "no": 5, "options": ["Why Search Engines Are Eroding Human Creativity", "Skimming vs. Stillness: Defending Deep Thought in the Attention Economy", "From Socrates to Smartphones: Why Media Panics Always Prove Groundless", "Disconnecting Entirely: The Only Remedy for Fractured Attention"], "stem": "Which of the following would be the best title for the passage?", "trapNote": "C项属于正反颠倒，第1段提及苏格拉底与廉价报纸的历史担忧仅作为引子，紧接着以Yet转折指出当代注意力经济与以往存在本质差异，并非认为当代担忧毫无根据。", "type": "主旨题"}], "sourceLabel": "外刊同源拔高（L4 压轴训练）", "subtitle": "认知心理学与注意力经济：碎片化消费对深度批判思维的重塑", "timeLimitMin": 20, "title": "Skimming the Surface: Cognitive Offloading in the Attention Economy", "year": "外刊同源", "wordCount": 430, "translations": ["每一次媒介剧变的时代，都会引发新工具将摧毁人类心智的预言——从苏格拉底对书写的疑虑，到十九世纪人们对廉价报纸的恐慌，莫不如是。然而认知心理学家认为，如今围绕算法推送、即时通知和碎片化短视频构建的注意力经济，在传播速度与产品设计上都截然不同。持续性的“部分注意力”或许不只是在重新分配人们所知的内容，更在悄然改变大脑调控高耗能深度探究的方式。", "这一转变的核心在于一种被称为“认知卸载”的习惯：即将记忆存储与信息整合的任务外包给外部搜索引擎和摘要信息流。在适度范围内，认知卸载能释放稀缺的工作记忆，用于创造性的问题解决。然而，当平台不断将复杂问题预先消化成毫无阻力的现成结论时，用户便失去了构建持久心智模型的训练机会。批判性思维并非孤立存在的技能，它依赖于一个结构化的知识储备库，唯有借助这一知识库，新的主张才能被权衡与质询。", "碎片化的阅读习惯还对人们容忍模糊性的耐心造成了更隐蔽的消耗。眼动追踪实验显示，习惯了快速刷屏的读者即便面对结构严密的纸质论证，也会采取“F型”扫描模式——先浏览标题和开头几行，随即跳离。由于细致入微的推理往往呈递归式展开，要求读者在结论水落石出前在脑海中同时权衡相互竞争的前提，扫读习惯便会系统性地偏爱冲击力十足的武断结论，而排斥审慎克制的论据。假以时日，智识耐力逐渐萎缩，那些抗拒即时压缩的思想便开始让人觉得冗长乏味，而非严谨深刻。", "为了检验肤浅的自信是否伴随着这种转变，研究人员近期让志愿者分别以不间断的长篇文章或精选的社交媒体串文形式，阅读内容完全相同的政策辩论。尽管串文读者在要求综合反方论点的测试中得分明显更低，他们对自己掌握该议题程度的自评却高于长文读者。看来，在频繁切换语境的消耗下，大脑将提取信息的流畅感误认作了真正的理解——而迎合愤怒情绪与浅层共识、而非鼓励犹豫思索的算法，更放大了这种错觉。", "尽管如此，把问题全盘归咎于数字架构，难免有陷入技术决定论之嫌。人类认知在整个成年期依然保持着可塑性，而且分散注意力的互联网络，同时也将曾经被精英把关人垄断的学术资源推向了大众。各类实验性干预——从剔除超链接干扰的“高阻力”阅读界面，到在原典辩论期间禁用电子设备的大学研讨课——均一致表明，当环境能够守护认知的沉静时，持久的分析能力便会回升。", "因此，核心挑战既不是退回到拒绝新技术的“卢德主义”怀旧情绪中，也不是将快速获取信息与智慧混为一谈。深度批判性思维的存续并非偶然，而是有赖于有意识的文化与教育制度支撑——将缓慢而艰辛的专注力视为一种值得捍卫的公民美德。"], "studyPack": {"keyVocab": [{"gloss": "v. 造成（代价/损害），索取，强加", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为形容词“精确的”，作动词时在阅读中高频出现搭配 exact a toll (on)，意为“对……造成隐性伤害/代价”。", "word": "exact"}, {"gloss": "adj. 有限定条件的，有保留的，适度的", "note": "熟词僻义：常考义为“有资格的、胜任的”，在学术论证语境中常与 certainty 相对，意为“审慎限定的、非绝对的”。", "word": "qualified"}, {"gloss": "v. 在脑海中留下印象，被感知，显得", "note": "熟词僻义：常见义为“登记、注册”，作不及物动词后接 as 时表“被感受为、在主观上显得”（如 register as tedious）。", "word": "register"}, {"gloss": "adj. 可塑的，能适应并改变的", "note": "熟词僻义：名词指“塑料”，作形容词在神经科学与认知语境中高频指“具有可塑性的”（cognition remains plastic）。", "word": "plastic"}, {"gloss": "n. 支撑机制，培育框架（原指脚手架）", "note": "高频学术隐喻词：由建筑“脚手架”引申为教育、文化或制度层面的“支撑体系、脚手架式扶持”（pedagogical scaffolding）。", "word": "scaffolding"}], "longSentences": [{"en": "At the heart of this transformation lies a habit known as cognitive offloading: delegating memory storage and synthesis to external search engines and summarized feeds.", "point": "地点状语前置引发的完全倒装（At the heart... lies a habit）+ 过去分词作后置定语（known as...）+ 冒号同位语解释", "structure": "倒装主干：a habit known as cognitive offloading lies at the heart of this transformation（因主语较长且强调地点状语而倒装）；后置定语：known as cognitive offloading；冒号后为动名词短语 delegating... 作 habit 的同位语解释。", "zh": "这一转变的核心在于一种被称为“认知卸载”的习惯：即将记忆存储与信息整合的任务外包给外部搜索引擎和摘要信息流。"}, {"en": "Because nuanced reasoning unfolds recursively, requiring readers to hold competing premises in mind before resolution arrives, skimming systematically favors punchy certainty over qualified evidence.", "point": "原因状语从句 + 现在分词短语作伴随状语（requiring...）+ 固定搭配 favor A over B（偏爱 A 胜过 B）", "structure": "原因状语从句：Because nuanced reasoning unfolds recursively；伴随状语：requiring readers to hold competing premises in mind before resolution arrives（内嵌 before 时间状语从句）；主句：skimming systematically favors punchy certainty over qualified evidence。", "zh": "由于细致入微的推理往往呈递归式展开，要求读者在结论水落石出前在脑海中同时权衡相互竞争的前提，扫读习惯便会系统性地偏爱冲击力十足的武断结论，而排斥审慎克制的论据。"}, {"en": "Experimental interventions—from \"friction-rich\" reading interfaces that strip away hyperlinked distractions to university seminars banning devices during primary-text debates—consistently show that sustained analytical capacity rebounds when environments protect cognitive stillness.", "point": "破折号插入语（from... to... 含定语从句与现在分词后置定语）+ that 引导的宾语从句 + when 引导的时间状语从句", "structure": "主干：Experimental interventions consistently show that...；破折号插入例证：from \"friction-rich\" reading interfaces（后接 that 定语从句）to university seminars（后接 banning... 现在分词短语作后置定语）；宾语从句：that sustained analytical capacity rebounds when environments protect cognitive stillness。", "zh": "各类实验性干预——从剔除超链接干扰的“高阻力”阅读界面，到在原典辩论期间禁用电子设备的大学研讨课——均一致表明，当环境能够守护认知的沉静时，持久的分析能力便会回升。"}], "paraphrases": [{"note": "reservoir of structured knowledge 对应 structured knowledge base，against which new claims can be weighed and contested 替换为 test unfamiliar arguments。", "option": "weakens the structured knowledge base needed to test unfamiliar arguments", "original": "reservoir of structured knowledge against which new claims can be weighed and contested"}, {"note": "词义猜测题：前文 punchy certainty（铿锵武断的确定性）与 qualified evidence 形成对比，因此 qualified 意为“有保留的、有条件限定的”。", "option": "measured and conditional", "original": "favors punchy certainty over qualified evidence"}, {"note": "scored markedly lower 对应 deflate real synthesis，rated their own grasp higher 对应 inflating perceived mastery，精准提炼“实际能力下降与主观自信膨胀”的反差。", "option": "deflate real synthesis while inflating perceived mastery", "original": "scored markedly lower on tests requiring them to synthesize counterarguments, they rated their own grasp of the topic higher"}, {"note": "also democratizes access 体现平衡客观视角，analytical capacity rebounds 体现对人类心智恢复力的审慎乐观。", "option": "Balanced and cautiously optimistic about the mind's capacity to recover", "original": "Human cognition remains plastic across adulthood, and the connectivity that fractures focus also democratizes access to scholarship"}, {"note": "主旨标题题：紧扣标题与全文核心冲突（扫读文化 vs 认知沉静）以及结尾呼吁的“捍卫深度思考”。", "option": "Skimming vs. Stillness: Defending Deep Thought in the Attention Economy", "original": "treats slow, arduous attention as a civic virtue worth defending"}]}}]};
